\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Speaker Johnson says decision coming \u8216\'20\'18very soon\u8217\'20\'19 on Biden impeachment - as it happened\b0\par\par\uc2 Chris Stein \par \uc2 5,109 \uc2 words\par \uc2 2 November 2023\par 20:04 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 This live blog is now closed.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.01pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Closing summary\par \par \uc2 The Republican speaker of the House, Mike Johnson, says the party {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/nov/02/george-santos-vote-joe-biden-trump-israel-latest-us-politics-news?filterKeyEvents=false&page=with:block-6543c8618f08af73b5ca7114#block-6543c8618f08af73b5ca7114"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 will soon decide}}}\uc2  on whether to continue its impeachment inquiry into \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 , but {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/nov/02/george-santos-vote-joe-biden-trump-israel-latest-us-politics-news?page=with:block-6543cf4d8f08d1827a66aab0#block-6543cf4d8f08d1827a66aab0"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 all indications}}}\uc2  point to the GOP pressing on. Republicans have been showing off evidence they say proves the president received money from a Chinese company, but the White House says Biden merely received a loan repayment from his brother during the period when he was out of office. Elsewhere in the House, George Santos {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/nov/02/george-santos-vote-joe-biden-trump-israel-latest-us-politics-news?page=with:block-6543b3898f08293ffae51797#block-6543b3898f08293ffae51797"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 survived}}}\uc2  a removal attempt, while \uc2 Marjorie Taylor Greene{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/nov/02/george-santos-vote-joe-biden-trump-israel-latest-us-politics-news?page=with:block-6543b7d48f08af73b5ca6f79#block-6543b7d48f08af73b5ca6f79"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 is furious}}}\uc2  at some of her Republican colleagues for refusing to support her resolution to censure progressive Democrat \uc2 Rashida Tlaib\uc2 , which died on the House floor last night.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s what else happened:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The White House{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/nov/02/george-santos-vote-joe-biden-trump-israel-latest-us-politics-news?page=with:block-6543f0fb8f08d1827a66ac83#block-6543f0fb8f08d1827a66ac83"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 said}}}\uc2  Biden would veto the House GOP\u8217\'20\'19s proposal to send Israel security assistances while slashing funding to the \uc2 IRS\uc2 , and Senate leader Chuck Schumer{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/nov/02/george-santos-vote-joe-biden-trump-israel-latest-us-politics-news?page=with:block-6543f5ad8f08293ffae51bfe#block-6543f5ad8f08293ffae51bfe"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 said}}}\uc2  he would not bring the bill up for a vote anyway.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Jamie Raskin\uc2 , a Democrat who voted against expelling Santos, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/nov/02/george-santos-vote-joe-biden-trump-israel-latest-us-politics-news?page=with:block-6543abc68f08af73b5ca6eab#block-6543abc68f08af73b5ca6eab"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 said}}}\uc2  he did so over concerns for due process.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Biden{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/nov/02/george-santos-vote-joe-biden-trump-israel-latest-us-politics-news?page=with:block-6543c1f58f08af73b5ca7035#block-6543c1f58f08af73b5ca7035"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 appeared}}}\uc2  to endorse \u8220\'20\'1Ca pause\u8221\'20\'1D in Israel\u8217\'20\'19s invasion of Gaza.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The Minnesota supreme court{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/nov/02/george-santos-vote-joe-biden-trump-israel-latest-us-politics-news?page=with:block-6543ba268f08293ffae51822#block-6543ba268f08293ffae51822"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 began hearing a case}}}\uc2  in which voters want to keep \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  off the ballot for his involvement in an insurrection.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Indiana\u8217\'20\'19s supreme court{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/nov/02/george-santos-vote-joe-biden-trump-israel-latest-us-politics-news?page=with:block-6543f9348f08af73b5ca7395#block-6543f9348f08af73b5ca7395"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 found}}}\uc2  that the state\u8217\'20\'19s Republican attorney general, \uc2 Todd Rokita\uc2 , \u8220\'20\'1Cengaged in attorney misconduct\u8221\'20\'1D for comments he made about an obstetrician-gynecologist who performed an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  for a 10-year-old rape survivor.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 8.04pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.43pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Indiana\u8217\'20\'19s supreme court has found that the state\u8217\'20\'19s Republican attorney general, \uc2 Todd Rokita\uc2 , \u8220\'20\'1Cengaged in attorney misconduct\u8221\'20\'1D for comments he made to Fox News about a doctor in the state who performed an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  on a 10-year-old girl who had traveled from Ohio, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.indystar.com/story/news/politics/2023/11/02/todd-rokita-indiana-attorney-general-reprimand-supreme-court-abortion-caitlin-bernard/71421463007/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the Indianapolis Star reports}}}\uc2 .\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/jul/03/ohio-indiana-abortion-rape-victim"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 The incident}}}\uc2  was one of the first high-profile examples of the fallout from the supreme court decision in June 2022 to overturn Roe v Wade and allow states to ban \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  entirely. In Ohio, a state law immediately went into effect that cut off access to the procedure after six weeks of pregnancy, but it was {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.aclu.org/press-releases/ohio-lower-court-blocks-six-week-abortion-ban-restoring-reproductive-rights-across"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 later halted}}}\uc2  by a court ruling.\par \par \uc2 The Indiana supreme court took issue with Rokita\u8217\'20\'19s description of Caitlin Bernard, an obstetrician-gynecologist, as an \u8220\'20\'1C\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  activist acting as a doctor \u8211\'20\'13 with a history of failing to report\u8221\'20\'1D in a Fox News interview in July 2022. In September, the supreme court\u8217\'20\'19s disciplinary commission filed charges against Rokita, saying he violated professional conduct rules, and three of the state\u8217\'20\'19s five supreme court justices agreed in today\u8217\'20\'19s ruling. The court has ordered that Rokita receive a public reprimand and pay a $250 fine, though the two justices who dissented said the punishment was too lenient.\par \par \uc2 Ohio voters will next week decide on a ballot measure to enshrine \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access in the state\u8217\'20\'19s constitution. Here\u8217\'20\'19s the latest on that, from the Guardian\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/carter-sherman"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Carter Sherman}}}\uc2  :\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2023/sep/19/ohio-abortion-rights-referendum-language"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Ohio \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  rights activists suffer blow in suit over referendum language}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 7.59pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.18pm GMT\par \par \uc2 The Senate\u8217\'20\'19s Democratic leader, \uc2 Chuck Schumer\uc2 , now says the House GOP\u8217\'20\'19s Israel aid proposal will not be put up for a vote in his chamber:\par \par \uc2 enltrLet me be clear: The Senate will not take up the House GOP's deeply flawed proposal\par \par \uc2 Instead we will work on our own bipartisan emergency aid package that includes funding for aid to Israel, Ukraine, humanitarian aid including for Gaza, and competition with the Chinese Government\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 \uc2 Chuck Schumer\uc2  (@SenSchumer) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/SenSchumer/status/1720134873841623374?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 November 2, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 That means that even if the House approves the bill, the Senate will not send it to \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s desk \u8211\'20\'13 whose administration said he will veto it anyway.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 7.20pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.01pm GMT\par \par \uc2 White House threatens to veto Republican bill to help Israel while excluding Ukraine, border security\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  would veto a proposal by House Republicans to send military aid to Israel while slashing funding for the \uc2 IRS\uc2  tax authority, White House national security council spokesman John Kirby told reporters at today\u8217\'20\'19s briefing.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe president would veto an only Israel bill. I think we\u8217\'20\'19ve made that clear,\u8221\'20\'1D Kirby said.\par \par \uc2 Biden last month requested a $106b security measure to help Israel respond to \uc2 Hamas\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s terrorist attack, shore up Ukraine\u8217\'20\'19s defenses against Russia\u8217\'20\'19s invasion and improve border security. Led by speaker Mike Johnson, House Republicans responded by offering to approve Israeli security assistance, while considering funding for Ukraine and the southern border at a later date. Johnson has billed cutting the \uc2 IRS\uc2  as a way to pay for the cost of the foreign assistance, but an analysis from the nonpartisan \uc2 Congressional Budget Office\uc2  yesterday found it would actually cost the government money because it would lower tax revenues.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.37pm GMT\par \par \uc2 The White House national security spokes person John Kirby said that a call by \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  on Wednesday evening {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/nov/02/biden-pause-ceasefire-israel-hamas-war-minnesota"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 for a pause}}}\uc2  in fire by both Israel and \uc2 Hamas\uc2  in Gaza \u8220\'20\'1Cdoes not mean we are calling for a general ceasefire \u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 At the daily press briefing from the west wing, Kirby asked rhetorically whether the White House thought a strategic and temporary \u8220\'20\'1Cpause by both sides\u8221\'20\'1D was a good idea to help facilitate the delivery of humanitarian aid into Gaza and the evacuation of foreign citizens and hostages taken by \uc2 Hamas\uc2  from southern Israel on 7 October. Kirby answered himself: \u8220\'20\'1CYou betcha we do.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 He went on to explain why the US is willing to accept Qatar\u8217\'20\'19s assistance with the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/nov/02/george-santos-vote-joe-biden-trump-israel-latest-us-politics-news?page=with:block-6543d7848f08af73b5ca720e#block-6543d7848f08af73b5ca720e"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 passage of Americans}}}\uc2  and hostages out of Gaza, despite the small Arab country\u8217\'20\'19s harboring of \uc2 Hamas\uc2  members, including the leader \uc2 Ismail Haniyeh\uc2 . Reporters questioned Kirby about this at the daily briefing at the White House moments ago.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CQatar has lines of communication with \uc2 Hamas\uc2  that almost no-one else has,\u8221\'20\'1D Kirby said.\par \par \uc2 A reporter asked why the US was not asking Qatar to hand over the \uc2 Hamas\uc2  chief. Kirby said the US was busy working with Qatar on evacuations \u8220\'20\'1Cand we are also helping Israel go after \uc2 Hamas\uc2 \u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Kirby also said the US supports pauses in hostilities, not just a single pause. This is a point he\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/CNNThisMorning/status/1718971722316067143"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 made before}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 enltrJUST IN: White House's John Kirby says, "We're really not just talking about like one pause, what we're trying to do is explore the idea of as many pauses as might be necessary." {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/d9hO8cuFH5"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/d9hO8cuFH5}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Simon Ateba (@simonateba) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/simonateba/status/1720140212003623353?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 November 2, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 Kirby said the White House \u8220\'20\'1Chas not seen evidence that \uc2 Hezbollah\uc2  is ready to go full force\u8221\'20\'1D. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/hezbollah"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Hezbollah}}}\uc2 , the Lebanese Shia militant group, said it {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2023/nov/02/tension-escalates-on-lebanese-frontier-amid-hamas-and-hezbollah-barrages"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 had attacked}}}\uc2  19 positions in Israel on Thursday evening in the latest escalation on Israel\u8217\'20\'19s northern border. \uc2 The Guardian\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s report is {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2023/nov/02/tension-escalates-on-lebanese-frontier-amid-hamas-and-hezbollah-barrages"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 here}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The Guardian\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s global live blog with all the details on the crisis in Gaza and the Israel-\uc2 Hamas\uc2  war is {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/live/2023/nov/02/israel-hamas-war-live-updates-gaza-jabalia-refugee-camp-strikes-today-latest-news#top-of-blog"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 here}}}\uc2  .\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 6.49pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.53pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Antony Blinken\uc2  has urged Russia to hold to its commitment not to resume nuclear weapons testing, Reuters reports.\par \par \uc2 The secretary of state said the US is deeply concerned by Moscow\u8217\'20\'19s planned action to withdraw its ratification of the \uc2 comprehensive test ban treaty\uc2  (CTBT).\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CUnfortunately, it represents a significant step in the wrong direction,\u8221\'20\'1D Blinken said in a statement released by the state department.\par \par \uc2 The latest {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2023/oct/06/nuclear-watchdog-russia-putin-testing-treaty"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 development happened}}}\uc2  this last month, when, the Guardian\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/julianborger"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Julian Borger}}}\uc2  reported, a senior Russian diplomat said that Moscow will revoke its ratification of the CTBT, in a move Washington denounced as jeopardising the \u8220\'20\'1Cglobal norm\u8221\'20\'1D against nuclear test blasts.\par \par \uc2 Mikhail Ulyanov\uc2 , the Russian representative to the international nuclear agencies in Vienna, was speaking after {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/vladimir-putin"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Vladimir Putin}}}\uc2  suggested Moscow might resuming testing for the first time in 33 years, signalling another downward turn in relations between the world\u8217\'20\'19s two biggest nuclear powers.\par \par \uc2 Ulyanov said on X, formerly known as \uc2 Twitter\uc2 : \u8220\'20\'1CRussia plans to revoke ratification (which took place in the year 2000) of the Comprehensive Nuclear-Test-Ban Treaty.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe aim is to be on equal footing with the #US who signed the Treaty, but didn\u8217\'20\'19t ratify it. Revocation doesn\u8217\'20\'19t mean the intention to resume nuclear tests.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The US signed the CTBT in 1996 but the Senate did not ratify the treaty. Successive US administrations however have observed a moratorium on testing nuclear weapons.\par \par \uc2 Any Russian nuclear test would be the first since 1990, the last conducted by the Soviet Union. Renewed testing by a nuclear superpower would undo one of the principal advances in non-proliferation since the cold war.\par \par \uc2 Since the all-out invasion of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/ukraine"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Ukraine}}}\uc2  in February 2022, Putin and other Russian officials have frequently drawn attention to the country\u8217\'20\'19s nuclear arsenal, the biggest in the world, in an attempt to deter other countries from helping Ukraine resist the invasion.\par \par \uc2 Antony Blinken\uc2  is quizzed by reporters before departing the US for Israel again on 2 November. Photograph: Jonathan Ernst/Reuters\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 6.11pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.25pm GMT\par \par \uc2 US says 74 dual citizens have been allowed to leave Gaza\par \par \uc2 The US has been able to get 74 Americans with dual citizenship out of Gaza, \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  said at the White House a little earlier, one day after evacuees {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2023/nov/01/israel-hamas-war-gaza-injured-egypt-rafah-crossing"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 began crossing}}}\uc2  into Egypt, Reuters reported.\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile the US secretary of state, \uc2 Antony Blinken\uc2 , talked to reporters before leaving Washington for a flight to Israel and said the US is determined to prevent escalation of the war there on all fronts, including southern Lebanon, the West Bank or elsewhere in the region.\par \par \uc2 He will be talking to the Israeli government \u8220\'20\'1Cand partners\u8221\'20\'1D in the region, he said.\par \par \uc2 You can follow more details on all the developments in the crisis in Gaza and the Israel-\uc2 Hamas\uc2  war in our global live blog, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/live/2023/nov/02/israel-hamas-war-live-updates-gaza-jabalia-refugee-camp-strikes-today-latest-news#top-of-blog"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 here}}}\uc2  .\par \par \uc2 This post was updated at 2.56pm ET to reflect a clarifying detail in a later wire piece by Reuters to specify that the 74 dual citizens Biden referred to were Americans with dual citizenship.\par \par \uc2 Antony Blinken\uc2  talks to reporters at Joint Base Andrews in Maryland, on his way to the Middle East and Asia on 2 November. Photograph: Jonathan Ernst/AFP/Getty Images\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 5.57pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.56pm GMT\par \par \uc2 The day so far\par \par \uc2 The Republican speaker of the House, Mike Johnson, says the party {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/nov/02/george-santos-vote-joe-biden-trump-israel-latest-us-politics-news?filterKeyEvents=false&page=with:block-6543c8618f08af73b5ca7114#block-6543c8618f08af73b5ca7114"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 will soon decide}}}\uc2  on whether to continue their impeachment inquiry into \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 , but {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/nov/02/george-santos-vote-joe-biden-trump-israel-latest-us-politics-news?page=with:block-6543cf4d8f08d1827a66aab0#block-6543cf4d8f08d1827a66aab0"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 all indications}}}\uc2  point to them pressing on. The GOP has been showing off evidence it says proves the president received money from a Chinese company, but the White House says the president merely received a loan repayment from his brother during the period when he was out of office. Elsewhere in the House, George Santos {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/nov/02/george-santos-vote-joe-biden-trump-israel-latest-us-politics-news?page=with:block-6543b3898f08293ffae51797#block-6543b3898f08293ffae51797"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 survived}}}\uc2  a removal attempt, while \uc2 Marjorie Taylor Greene{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/nov/02/george-santos-vote-joe-biden-trump-israel-latest-us-politics-news?page=with:block-6543b7d48f08af73b5ca6f79#block-6543b7d48f08af73b5ca6f79"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 is furious}}}\uc2  at some of her Republican colleagues for refusing to support her resolution to censure progressive Democrat \uc2 Rashida Tlaib\uc2 , which died on the House floor last night.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s what else is going on:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Jamie Raskin\uc2 , a Democrat who voted against expelling Santos, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/nov/02/george-santos-vote-joe-biden-trump-israel-latest-us-politics-news?page=with:block-6543abc68f08af73b5ca6eab#block-6543abc68f08af73b5ca6eab"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 said}}}\uc2  he did so over concerns for due process.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Biden{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/nov/02/george-santos-vote-joe-biden-trump-israel-latest-us-politics-news?page=with:block-6543c1f58f08af73b5ca7035#block-6543c1f58f08af73b5ca7035"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 appeared}}}\uc2  to endorse \u8220\'20\'1Ca pause\u8221\'20\'1D in Israel\u8217\'20\'19s invasion of Gaza.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The Minnesota supreme court{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/nov/02/george-santos-vote-joe-biden-trump-israel-latest-us-politics-news?page=with:block-6543ba268f08293ffae51822#block-6543ba268f08293ffae51822"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 began hearing a case}}}\uc2  in which voters want to keep \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  off the ballot for his involvement in an insurrection.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 5.00pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.37pm GMT\par \par \uc2 All signs point to the House GOP continuing its impeachment inquiry into \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Yesterday, the oversight committee, one of three bodies tasked with handling the effort, published an infographic purporting to show how the president received money from a Chinese company that was funneled through his family members:\par \par \uc2 zxxltr {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/WKwuRzmYUy"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/WKwuRzmYUy}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Oversight Committee (@GOPoversight) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/GOPoversight/status/1719715832337424586?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 November 1, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 They even have an image of the check:\par \par \uc2 zxxltr {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/UGKwRHMxNP"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/UGKwRHMxNP}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Oversight Committee (@GOPoversight) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/GOPoversight/status/1719715754218520921?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 November 1, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 The White House replied by saying that the money was a loan repayment to Biden from his brother, James, and it all took place in the period after Biden concluded his term as vice-president, and before he returned to the White House in 2021.\par \par \uc2 As Ian Sams, the Biden administration spokesman handling the GOP\u8217\'20\'19s inquiries, put it:\par \par \uc2 zxxltr {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/Lo3f4WYxrj"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/Lo3f4WYxrj}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/9sbqHeMf9E"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/9sbqHeMf9E}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Ian Sams (@IanSams46) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/IanSams46/status/1719716656744661349?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 November 1, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 This post has been corrected to say Biden received the loan repayment from his brother James.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 4.59pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.11pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Republican House speaker Johnson says decision will come \u8216\'20\'18very soon\u8217\'20\'19 on Biden impeachment\par \par \uc2 The Republican speaker of the House Mike Johnson said a decision will be made \u8220\'20\'1Cvery soon\u8221\'20\'1D on whether to push forward with the effort to impeach \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 His predecessor Kevin McCarthy announced the inquiry into the president\u8217\'20\'19s conduct in September, weeks before rightwing Republicans and Democrats removed him from the speaker\u8217\'20\'19s post. The investigation centers on allegations of corruption surrounding the president and his family, particularly his son \uc2 Hunter Biden\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Republicans held a single committee hearing into the matter, which was widely seen as a flop after their witnesses said the investigation had merit but {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/sep/28/biden-impeachment-hearing-house-republicans"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 there was still no evidence}}}\uc2  the president broke the law. Another blow to the effort came when \uc2 Ken Buck\uc2 , a conservative Republican who yesterday announced he would not seek re-election in 2024, wrote {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.washingtonpost.com/opinions/2023/09/15/congressman-ken-buck-biden-impeachment/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a column in the Washington Post}}}\uc2  to argue that impeaching Biden was a bad idea.\par \par \uc2 The investigation was put on pause for weeks while the House grappled with McCarthy\u8217\'20\'19s ouster, and whether and how to continue it is one of the major issues Johnson has to decide. Here\u8217\'20\'19s what the speaker had to say when asked about it at a press conference today:\par \par \uc2 enltrSpeaker Mike Johnson (R-LA), when asked if there's enough evidence for the House to draft articles of impeachment against President Biden:\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CAs we stand here today, I'm not predetermined that, but I do believe that very soon we are coming to a point of decision on it.\u8221\'20\'1D {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/LZSvatxBA1"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/LZSvatxBA1}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 The Recount (@therecount) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/therecount/status/1720093783784829011?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 November 2, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 4.14pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.53pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Israel\u8217\'20\'19s conflict with \uc2 Hamas\uc2  continues as its troops push deeper into the Gaza Strip.\par \par \uc2 We have a separate live blog covering it, and you can read it here:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/live/2023/nov/02/israel-hamas-war-live-updates-gaza-jabalia-refugee-camp-strikes-today-latest-news"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Israel-Hamas war live: Israeli troops operating inside and surrounding Gaza City, IDF says}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.38pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  was in Minnesota yesterday, where he appeared to call for a \u8220\'20\'1Cpause\u8221\'20\'1D in Israel\u8217\'20\'19s attack against \uc2 Hamas\uc2  in the Gaza Strip. Here\u8217\'20\'19s more on that from the Guardian\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/martin-pengelly"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Martin Pengelly}}}\uc2  :\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  called for a \u8220\'20\'1Cpause\u8221\'20\'1D in the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/israel-hamas-war"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Israel-Hamas war}}}\uc2  on Wednesday, in response to a call from the crowd during remarks in Minneapolis.\par \par \uc2 A rabbi, who later identified herself as Jessica Rosenberg, called out: \u8220\'20\'1CMr President, if you care about Jewish people, as a rabbi, I need you to call for a ceasefire.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Biden said: \u8220\'20\'1CI think we need a pause. A pause means giv[ing] time to get the prisoners out.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Israel says more than 1,400 people were killed, and more than 5,400 injured, after \uc2 Hamas\uc2  launched surprise attacks on 7 October. More than 240 hostages were taken.\par \par \uc2 Israeli strikes in response, predominantly in Gaza but also in the West Bank, have killed more than 9,000, according to the Gaza health ministry, which is run by \uc2 Hamas\uc2 . The same source says nearly 24,000 Palestinians have been injured.\par \par \uc2 Israel says 16 of its soldiers have been killed.\par \par \uc2 Biden has been under pressure to call for a ceasefire or a meaningful humanitarian pause in Israel\u8217\'20\'19s campaign.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/nov/02/biden-pause-ceasefire-israel-hamas-war-minnesota"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Biden calls for \u8216\'20\'18pause\u8217\'20\'19 in Israel-Hamas war during Minnesota event}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.43pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.18pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Speaking of insurrections, the Minnesota supreme court is today hearing a case in which voters want \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  removed from the state\u8217\'20\'19s ballots for participating in an insurrection \u8211\'20\'13 which would be the January 6 attack on the Capitol, and the broader effort to overturn the 2020 election. A similar case was heard in Colorado earlier this week, and legal experts believe the \uc2 US supreme court\uc2  may eventually have to decide the issue. Here\u8217\'20\'19s the Guardian\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/rachel-leingang"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Rachel Leingang}}}\uc2  with the latest on the Minnesota effort:\par \par \uc2 Attorneys at the Minnesota supreme court will argue on Thursday that former President {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/donaldtrump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Donald Trump}}}\uc2  should not be allowed to appear on the state\u8217\'20\'19s ballots for president because of his efforts to overturn the 2020 election and role in the insurrection.\par \par \uc2 A group of voters wants the courts to weigh a clause in the 14th amendment, which disqualifies an \u8220\'20\'1Cofficer of the United States\u8221\'20\'1D who has taken an oath to defend the constitution from holding office if they have \u8220\'20\'1Cengaged in insurrection or rebellion\u8221\'20\'1D against the country. In dozens of pages in their {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.mncourts.gov/mncourtsgov/media/High-Profile-Cases/A23-1354/Petition-pursuant-to-Minn-Stat-204B-44-to-Challenge-Placement-of-Donald-J-Trump-on-the-2024-Primary-and-General-Election-Ballots.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 initial court filing}}}\uc2 , they cite examples of Trump\u8217\'20\'19s election interference, from the fake electors scheme to his comments to rioters on 6 January 2021.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CDespite having sworn an oath to support the Constitution of the United States, Trump \u8216\'20\'18engaged in insurrection or rebellion against the same, or [gave] aid or comfort to the enemies thereof,\u8217\'20\'19\u8221\'20\'1D the voters argue.\par \par \uc2 The lawsuit is one of several the former president faces in his bid to return to the White House, not to mention the various criminal and civil actions he is currently defending against. A similar petition is the subject of a trial in Colorado this week. Legal experts {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/aug/20/trump-disqualified-constitution-section-3-14th-amendment"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 say}}}\uc2  the Reconstruction-era clause is ripe for the courts, though it has never been used to forestall a presidential candidate in this way.\par \par \uc2 Free Speech for People, a left-leaning group, represents the voters in the case, who include the former {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/minnesota"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Minnesota}}}\uc2  secretary of state Joan Growe and the former Minnesota supreme court justice Paul H Anderson.\par \par \uc2 Trump\u8217\'20\'19s attorneys and the Republican party have fought back against the suit, claiming the matter is a political question instead of a legal one. Trump\u8217\'20\'19s campaign also claims there\u8217\'20\'19s \u8220\'20\'1Cno evidence that President Trump intended or supported any violent or unlawful activity seeking to overthrow the government of the United States, either on January 6 or at any other time.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThis request is manifestly inappropriate,\u8221\'20\'1D Trump\u8217\'20\'19s team wrote in a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.mncourts.gov/mncourtsgov/media/High-Profile-Cases/A23-1354/Response-Petition_3.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 brief}}}\uc2 . \u8220\'20\'1CBoth the federal Constitution and Minnesota law place the resolution of this political issue where it belongs: the democratic process, in the hands of either Congress or the people of the United States.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/nov/02/minnesota-supreme-court-case-trump-2024-ballot-eligibility"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Minnesota supreme court to hear case challenging Trump\u8217\'20\'19s 2024 eligibility}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.02pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Majorie Taylor Greene is having quite the morning.\par \par \uc2 Last night, 23 Republicans voted with the Democrats to block a motion the rightwing Georgia lawmaker proposed to censure \uc2 Rashida Tlaib\uc2 , a progressive Democrat who is the only Palestinian American in the House. In return, Democrat Becca Balint pulled a separate resolution to censure Greene.\par \par \uc2 At this point, one could imagine a scenario where Greene calls a truce, realizing the chamber isn\u8217\'20\'19t in the mood to censure lawmakers {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/oct/25/mike-johnson-republican-house-speaker-vote"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 after weeks of chaos}}}\uc2  following Kevin McCarthy \u8217\'20\'19s removal as speaker. But Greene isn\u8217\'20\'19t interested.\par \par \uc2 She\u8217\'20\'19s been raging on X (formally known as \uc2 Twitter\uc2 ) all morning, with much of her ire directed at the Republicans who voted against her effort:\par \par \uc2 enltrOur country is in the worst crisis in it\u8217\'20\'19s history in every category and the Democrats are full blown communists and Republicans can\u8217\'20\'19t even censure \uc2 Rashida Tlaib\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Conservatives on this list hide behind excuses with their white wigs on and quote the constitution.\par \par \uc2 ??1/11 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/Z2hCB6nUw5"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/Z2hCB6nUw5}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Rep. \uc2 Marjorie Taylor Greene\uc2 ???? (@RepMTG) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/RepMTG/status/1720041312349561228?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 November 2, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 She is particularly upset at Chip Roy, a fellow conservative who voted against her motion because, he said, it accused Tlaib of participating in an \u8220\'20\'1Cinsurrection\u8221\'20\'1D, when she had done no such thing:\par \par \uc2 enltrYou voted to kick me out of the freedom caucus, but keep CNN wannabe \uc2 Ken Buck\uc2  and vaping groping \uc2 Lauren Boebert\uc2  and you voted with the Democrats to protect Terrorist Tlaib.\par \par \uc2 You hate Trump, certified Biden\u8217\'20\'19s election, and could care less about J6 defendants being persecuted. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/OIgUvndXek"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/OIgUvndXek}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Rep. \uc2 Marjorie Taylor Greene\uc2 ???? (@RepMTG) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/RepMTG/status/1720050983596642492?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 November 2, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 The insults grew more creative as the morning wore on:\par \par \uc2 enltrOh shut up Colonel Sanders, you\u8217\'20\'19re not even from Texas, more like the DMV.\par \par \uc2 Chip Roy\u8217\'20\'19s career exist of working for politicians, working for campaigns for politicians, and being a politician himself.\par \par \uc2 Unity Party all the way!\par \par \uc2 Which is why you will never hold anyone accountable. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/RejH3yDqdM"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/RejH3yDqdM}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Rep. \uc2 Marjorie Taylor Greene\uc2 ???? (@RepMTG) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/RepMTG/status/1720072501009732041?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 November 2, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 If you are wondering what Roy means by \u8220\'20\'1CJewish space lasers\u8221\'20\'1D, you will find the answer in this article:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/sep/25/marjorie-taylor-greene-yom-kippur-hanukah-menorah"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Far-right Marjorie Taylor Greene ridiculed for Yom Kippur error}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.38pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Here are some scenes from the House floor last night, as the chamber considered whether to expel George Santos.\par \par \uc2 The effort to boot him was introduced by five Republican lawmakers from New York, four of which occupy seats vulnerable to being taken by Democrats next year. Mike Lawler is among that group, and used his time on the floor to remind lawmakers that Santos {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/jan/22/george-santos-lies-republican-party-future"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 lied about}}}\uc2  his mother dying in the 9-11 terrorist attacks, when she in fact died years later:\par \par \uc2 enltrRep. Mike Lawler (R-NY), a key leader of the effort to expel Rep. George Santos (R-NY), slams Santos' lies about 9/11:\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CAll of us being from New York remember that day precisely \u8230\'20\'26 This is not something you joke about, you lie about! It is unfit.\u8221\'20\'1D {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/BFJRdtlazJ"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/BFJRdtlazJ}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 The Recount (@therecount) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/therecount/status/1719831951886954963?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 November 1, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 When it was Santos\u8217\'20\'19s turn to speak, he warned lawmakers that expelling him would set a \u8220\'20\'1Cdangerous precedent\u8221\'20\'1D:\par \par \uc2 enltr\u8220\'20\'1CNow is not the time to set dangerous precedent... The last time a member of Congress was expelled was in 2002, following a criminal conviction.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Rep. George Santos (R-NY) pans the resolution to expel him from Congress, saying the move would circumvent his due process rights {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/X6VApgAIZq"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/X6VApgAIZq}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 The Recount (@therecount) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/therecount/status/1719835961385746670?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 November 1, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 Strangely, Santos opted to yield some of his time to Dan Goldman, a New York Democrat who spoke in favor of expelling him:\par \par \uc2 enltrRep. George Santos (R-NY) yields time to Rep. Dan Goldman (D-NY):\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThank you very much, Mr. Santos. *2 seconds later* I rise today in support of this resolution to expel George Santos from Congress.\u8221\'20\'1D {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/xvqKsMwQUt"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/xvqKsMwQUt}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 The Recount (@therecount) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/therecount/status/1719828964510757371?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 November 1, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.23pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Who else was talking about due process last night? George Santos himself!\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s what he tweeted last night after surviving yet another brush with congressional death, figuratively speaking:\par \par \uc2 enltrTonight was a victory for due process not me.\par \par \uc2 This was never about me, and I\u8217\'20\'19ll never let it become about me.\par \par \uc2 We all have rights under this great Constitutional Republic and I\u8217\'20\'19ll fight for our right to uphold them till my last dying breath.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 George Santos (@MrSantosNY) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/MrSantosNY/status/1719895433151983900?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 November 2, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.06pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Among the lawmakers who voted against removing George Santos from Congress was \uc2 Jamie Raskin\uc2 , a Maryland Democrat who served on the January 6 committee.\par \par \uc2 After the vote, Raskin released a statement that articulated what are essentially due process concerns over removing Santos from his seat. While the New York Republican has admitted to telling an impressive number of lies to win his seat in Congress, Raskin argues that because Santos has not yet been convicted of any crime, expelling him would be premature and, could come back to haunt Democrats in the future.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s Raskin\u8217\'20\'19s statement, in full:\par \par \uc2 I\u8217\'20\'19m a Constitution guy. The House has expelled five people in our history, three for joining the Confederacy as traitors to the Union and two after they were convicted of serious criminal offenses. Santos has not been criminally convicted yet of any of the offenses he has been indicted for that were cited in the Resolution nor has he been found guilty of ethics offenses in the House internal process.\par \par \uc2 This would be a terrible precedent to set, expelling people who have not been convicted of a crime and without internal due process. If and when Santos is convicted of these serious criminal offenses or ethics charges, I will certainly vote to expel him. Until then, it\u8217\'20\'19s a very risky road to go down and we have to stick by due process and the rule of law, as obvious as the eventual result seems. In these times of war, chaos, insurrection, division and lawlessness, the rule of law is a lifeline for us.\par \par \uc2 I can think of four or five Democratic Members the Republicans would like to expel without any criminal conviction or adverse ethics findings tomorrow simply because they hate their politics. Indeed, the same New York Republicans who want to expel Santos now because he is a complete political albatross for them acted to vigorously defend him in the spring because they wanted his vote for their party on the floor. If Members are not going to be expelled for purely political reasons, we need to stick to due process and the rule of law.\par \par \uc2 Back in the spring, the Republicans promised action within 60 days on the sprawling Santos ethics investigation, but nothing has happened since then. Now, they are promising action by November 17. Good, it\u8217\'20\'19s about time.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.45pm GMT\par \par \uc2 From Reuters, here\u8217\'20\'19s the write-up of last night\u8217\'20\'19s vote over whether to expel George Santos, where a diverse group of Democratic and Republicans lawmakers rejected booting the New York congressman and big-time liar from his job:\par \par \uc2 A vote to expel Republican lawmaker George Santos from the US {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/house-of-representatives"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 House of Representatives}}}\uc2  failed on Wednesday when fewer than two-thirds of the chamber supported the resolution, preserving Republicans\u8217\'20\'19 narrow 221-212 majority.\par \par \uc2 Santos on Friday pleaded not guilty to a 23-count federal indictment accusing him of crimes including laundering funds to pay for his personal expenses, illegally receiving unemployment benefits and charging donors\u8217\'20\'19 credit cards without their consent.\par \par \uc2 Santos, who represents a small slice of New York City and parts of its eastern suburbs, would have been just the sixth to be expelled from the House in US history. Three of the five congressmen have been voted out for fighting against the US in the civil war.\par \par \uc2 Republican lawmakers from Santos\u8217\'20\'19 state of New York said last month they would introduce a resolution to expel Santos, but the move was delayed by weeks when the House was leaderless following the ouster of Kevin McCarthy as speaker.\par \par \uc2 Republicans on 25 October elected Mike Johnson, who has said he does not support expelling Santos for being charged with a crime, to succeed McCarthy.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/nov/01/us-house-vote-republican-george-santos-expel-new-york"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 US House vote fails to expel Republican George Santos after 23 federal charges}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.30pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Focus now on ethics committee after Santos survives expulsion vote\par \par \uc2 That George Santos survived a vote to expel him from the House is not hugely surprising. The motion needed a massive two-thirds majority of lawmakers to pass, and Republicans were always unlikely to do anything to further reduce their mere four-seat majority in Congress\u8217\'20\'19s lower chamber.\par \par \uc2 It is still possible that Santos leaves the House early, perhaps if he admits to any of the 23 federal crimes he is charged with as part of a plea deal. If that doesn\u8217\'20\'19t occur, it\u8217\'20\'19s hard to imagine Santos winning re-election in his suburban New York City district next year.\par \par \uc2 But before any of that happens, we should expect to hear from the ethics committee, which earlier this year opened an investigation into the New York congressman. On the eve of yesterday\u8217\'20\'19s expulsion vote against Santos, the panel made an unusual public statement, where they promised a public update on their inquiry by 17 November. That\u8217\'20\'19ll be something to look out for.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.08pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Santos survives expulsion vote, Greene rages after effort to censure progressive Democrat Tlaib rejected\par \par \uc2 Good morning, US politics blog readers. As evening arrived yesterday, lawmakers in the House of Representatives were presented with the opportunity to expel admitted fabulist George Santos, and censure both progressive Democrat \uc2 Rashida Tlaib\uc2  and rightwing Republican Marjorie Taylore Greene. But none of those things ended up happening. Despite the fact that Santos is facing {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/oct/27/george-santos-pleads-not-guilty-fraud-charges-new-york"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 23 federal fraud charges}}}\uc2 , and lied about most his qualifications for the job, an ideologically mixed group of Democrats and Republicans voted against removing him from his seat. Many argued doing so would set a bad precedent since he has not been convicted of a crime \u8211\'20\'13 the usual bar for booting a lawmaker.\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, several of Greene\u8217\'20\'19s fellow Republicans joined with Democrats to oppose her resolution against Tlaib, which led Becca Balint, the Democratic sponsor of the measure to censure Greene, to withdraw her resolution. But that wasn\u8217\'20\'19t enough for the Georgia lawmaker, who is spending her morning {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/RepMTG/status/1720050983596642492"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 tweeting in fury}}}\uc2  at GOP colleagues she feels betrayed her. They may no longer be fighting over {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/oct/25/mike-johnson-republican-house-speaker-vote#:~:text=Republican%20Mike%20Johnson%20elected%20House%20speaker%20after%20weeks%20of%20chaos"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 who their speaker should be}}}\uc2 , but the episode makes plain the House Republican conference remains a fractious place.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s what else is going on today:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Minnesota\u8217\'20\'19s supreme court will {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/nov/02/minnesota-supreme-court-case-trump-2024-ballot-eligibility"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 begin considering}}}\uc2  whether to remove \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  from its presidential ballot for taking part in an insurrection.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Senators will vote on three high-ranking military officers whose promotions have been blocked for months by Republican Tommy Tuberville in protest of the Pentagon\u8217\'20\'19s \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  policy.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 White House Press Secretary \uc2 Karine Jean-Pierre\uc2  and reporters meet at 1.30pm eastern time. National security council spokesman John Kirby will attend as well, and likely speak about the conflict in the Gaza Strip.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020231102ejb2001me\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
