\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 \u8216\'20\'18It\u8217\'20\'19s cruel\u8217\'20\'19: the last southern refuge for  \highlight22\uc2 abortion \highlight\uc2  rights might soon fall\b0\par\par\uc2 Carter Sherman in Charlottesville, Virginia \par \uc2 2,041 \uc2 words\par \uc2 31 October 2023\par 17:22 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Virginia is the only southern state that hasn\u8217\'20\'19t restricted \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  post-Roe. Is that about to change?\par \par \uc2 By the time Chasity Dunans learned about her pregnancy, she had already lost the right to end it.\par \par \uc2 She had gotten her period in July, but towards the end of the month the 23-year-old mother of one started to have heartburn and wrenching stomach pains. She told herself: you\u8217\'20\'19re not pregnant, you\u8217\'20\'19re just sick. When the pain didn\u8217\'20\'19t stop, she gave in and saw a doctor.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CHe was like, \u8216\'20\'18Oh, yeah, you\u8217\'20\'19re six, seven weeks pregnant,\u8217\'20\'19\u8221\'20\'1D Dunans recalled. Then, she says, he added: \u8220\'20\'1CI don\u8217\'20\'19t know what your guys\u8217\'20\'19 plans are, but I do have to let you know that in Georgia, [if it\u8217\'20\'19s] six weeks with a heartbeat, you cannot terminate the pregnancy here.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 In the year since the supreme court overturned Roe v Wade, nearly all states in the US south, including Georgia, have banned almost all abortions. Only one southern state has not restricted \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 : Virginia.\par \par \uc2 That\u8217\'20\'19s why, on a recent Tuesday in October, Dunans and her boyfriend, Jayvonta Stone, drove eight hours from their home in Georgia to a house on a sleepy street in Charlottesville, Virginia. Other than the small sign out front and a couple of quiet protesters who lingered on the sidewalk, there was little to suggest that the house was home to an outpost of a national network of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  clinics, Whole Woman\u8217\'20\'19s Health.\par \par \uc2 You should have that choice to determine how your life should go, especially if you cannot handle a child\par \par \uc2 Chasity Dunans\par \par \uc2 There, after waiting all day, Dunans was finally able to get an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , exactly 14 weeks into her pregnancy.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThere are situations where some people are not ready, and why is it fair to bring a child into that situation? Some people, in the moment, have sex, and boom: \u8216\'20\'18Oh, no, we\u8217\'20\'19re pregnant,\u8217\'20\'19\u8221\'20\'1D Dunans said, as she sipped tea a few minutes after her procedure. \u8220\'20\'1CThat doesn\u8217\'20\'19t mean it\u8217\'20\'19s planned, doesn\u8217\'20\'19t mean it\u8217\'20\'19s wanted. It\u8217\'20\'19s unexpected. So you should have that choice to determine how your life should go, especially if you cannot handle a child.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Virginia\u8217\'20\'19s status as a haven of southern \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access is at risk. On 7 November, the state will hold elections for the state legislature. Republicans, who already hold a majority in the house of delegates, need to win only a handful of seats to take control of the senate.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  is at the center of the election. Not only is it one of the top issues for voters, according to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.umw.edu/news/2023/09/27/virginians-closely-divided-over-2023-legislative-elections-in-statewide-survey/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 multiple}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cnu.edu/wasoncenter/surveys/archive/2023-10-17.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 polls}}}\uc2 , but Virginia\u8217\'20\'19s governor, the Republican Glenn Youngkin, has made his support for a 15-week ban the centerpiece of his campaign to help Republicans retake the state legislature.\par \par \uc2 Democrats and Republicans have spent the last decade trading control of both chambers of Virginia\u8217\'20\'19s state legislature and the governor\u8217\'20\'19s mansion, with Democrats winning all three in 2019 only to lose the house of delegates and the governorship just two years later. The November elections are set to be extremely close: a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cnu.edu/wasoncenter/surveys/archive/2023-10-17.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 mid-October poll found}}}\uc2  that 42% of voters plan to support the local Democratic candidate, while 41% will support the Republican.\par \par \uc2 If such a ban were to take effect in Virginia, many \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  clinics outside the state would likely feel the effects. In the year after Roe\u8217\'20\'19s demise, the rate of abortions in Virginia surged. Clinics in the state performed, on average, roughly 550 more abortions each month compared with the months before Roe disintegrated, according to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2023/oct/24/us-abortion-rates-post-roe-v-wade"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 research}}}\uc2  from the Society of Family Planning. An \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban could force many of those patients to flee even farther north, to clinics that are already overwhelmed.\par \par \uc2 Republican proponents of a 15-week ban argue that it\u8217\'20\'19s a reasonable compromise on a contentious issue \u8211\'20\'13 the vast majority of US abortions take place in the first trimester of pregnancy. But \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  providers and their allies say they are increasingly seeing patients later on in pregnancy, due to the cascade of post-Roe restrictions that make it harder to get abortions quickly. People with low incomes, people of color and minors all are more likely to get abortions later in pregnancy.\par \par \uc2 \u8216\'20\'18I think it\u8217\'20\'19s cruel\u8217\'20\'19\par \par \uc2 A 20-year-old woman who got an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  at Whole Woman\u8217\'20\'19s Health the same day as Dunans said that, although an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  fund helped cover half the cost of her \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , she and her partner struggled to pool the remaining $700.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19m still at home and don\u8217\'20\'19t feel like I could give the child the best life right now,\u8221\'20\'1D she said. The woman, who asked to speak anonymously, wants to go to college and get a real estate license.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI would always say if I did something stupid, I would have a baby, but now I\u8217\'20\'19m at the point where I did something stupid,\u8221\'20\'1D the woman said, as she snacked on chocolate pudding and a Slim Jim while waiting for the procedure. \u8220\'20\'1CWell, not stupid. I had sex and I got pregnant.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The woman, who said she has identified as \u8220\'20\'1Cpro-choice\u8221\'20\'1D all her life, wants to move out of her conservative hometown in Virginia, especially if the state restricts \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 . Right now, she can\u8217\'20\'19t afford to leave.\par \par \uc2 After Dunans and Stone discovered Dunans was pregnant, the couple took a few weeks to decide what to do. Having been together since they met on the school bus seven years ago, they are already parents to a one-year-old. They want to have a second child one day, but decided they just can\u8217\'20\'19t afford another right now. Stone does maintenance; Dunans raises their child.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI don\u8217\'20\'19t think I would be able to stay afloat with two children at this time,\u8221\'20\'1D Dunans said. Becoming a parent is exhausting, she continued: \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s mentally draining. It\u8217\'20\'19s emotionally draining. It\u8217\'20\'19s physically draining. And there\u8217\'20\'19s a lot of people who don\u8217\'20\'19t have that strength to do so. So I\u8217\'20\'19m always pro-choice. Your body, your choice.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Since Georgia bans \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  past roughly six weeks of pregnancy, Dunans booked an appointment at an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  clinic in North Carolina for the first week of October. The drive took five hours and cost $80 in gas. Once she and Stone arrived, they learned Dunans was past 12 weeks of pregnancy. Due to a law enacted on 1 July, North Carolina clinics can\u8217\'20\'19t perform abortions after that point.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CMy jaw dropped,\u8221\'20\'1D Dunans said. \u8220\'20\'1CWe don\u8217\'20\'19t have the luxury of wasting money like that, not in this time in our lives. So every penny counts. And to get that information \u8211\'20\'13 it was crushing.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 After the 12-week ban took effect in North Carolina, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2023/oct/10/abortion-ban-north-carolina-decrease#:~:text=Abortion-,Abortions%20in%20North%20Carolina%20drop%20by%2030%25%20in,of%20new%20restrictions%2C%20data%20shows&text=Abortions%20in%20North%20Carolina%20fell,by%20the%20Guttmacher%20Institute%20shows."}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 abortions in the state plunged}}}\uc2  by more than 30%, according to recent research by the \uc2 Guttmacher Institute\uc2 , which tracks \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  restrictions.\par \par \uc2 On the day Dunans and Stone visited Whole Woman\u8217\'20\'19s Health, about a week after their trip to North Carolina, 18 people showed up for abortions. At least two patients came from North Carolina \u8211\'20\'13 two from Georgia and one from West Virginia, according to a doctor who performed abortions that day.\par \par \uc2 Due to the volume of patients that day, the doctors worked late into the evening, well past the clinic\u8217\'20\'19s normal closing time. Because many patients had brought loved ones \u8211\'20\'13 their boyfriends, their mothers \u8211\'20\'13 to the appointment, the clinic was a full house. People waited in a converted living room, complete with fireplace and brochures for birth control, and listened to a soundtrack of relaxing muzak, waves and birdsong as doctors bustled around upstairs.\par \par \uc2 Almost everybody was dressed for comfort, with many in sweats and Crocs. Few people spoke; several couples held hands and cuddled. One man appeared to fall asleep as he and his partner waited for her turn.\par \par \uc2 The clinic\u8217\'20\'19s purple walls were peppered with quotes from famous women and inspirational posters. \u8220\'20\'1CYou got this,\u8221\'20\'1D one read. \u8220\'20\'1CBe your own hero,\u8221\'20\'1D another declared. One wall in a back room featured a quote attributed to Heather Heyer, the woman killed in the infamous 2017 Unite the Right rally in Charlottesville. \u8220\'20\'1CIf you are not outraged, you are not paying attention,\u8221\'20\'1D it read.\par \par \uc2 Amy Hagstrom Miller\uc2 , the CEO of Whole Woman\u8217\'20\'19s Health, bought the clinic in 2017 from a retiring \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  provider, whose version of security was a back door that played the song Jingle Bells whenever someone walked in. Now, a receptionist keeps an eye on several cameras pointed at the clinic\u8217\'20\'19s exterior \u8211\'20\'13 one of the few visible reminders that \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , and the people who provide it, are under threat. A list of anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  extremists, including their pictures, hangs in a back hallway, away from patients\u8217\'20\'19 eyes.\par \par \uc2 Currently, the clinic performs abortions up until 16 weeks of pregnancy. Hagstrom Miller wants to expand to 18 weeks by the end of the year and eventually go as late as 24 weeks.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CMore and more people are being pushed into the second trimester because they\u8217\'20\'19re being denied \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  in Alabama or in Georgia or South Carolina or West Virginia or Tennessee, and so they have to figure out how to travel to another state and get childcare and get time off work,\u8221\'20\'1D she said. \u8220\'20\'1CIt just pushes them further into the pregnancy \u8211\'20\'13 not because they\u8217\'20\'19re just like sitting around, saying, \u8216\'20\'18Oh, I\u8217\'20\'19m gonna wait until the second trimester \u8217\'20\'19cause that sounds like a better kind of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\u8217\'20\'19 I think it\u8217\'20\'19s cruel.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 My \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  literally saved my life\par \par \uc2 Whole Woman\u8217\'20\'19s Health patient advocate Avantae\par \par \uc2 Avantae, who asked to be identified only by her first name, works as a patient advocate at Whole Woman\u8217\'20\'19s Health, counseling patients as they navigate the process. She had an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  when she was nearly 14 weeks into her pregnancy. She only realized she was pregnant at 13 weeks, when she was a single mother of one and, she said, \u8220\'20\'1Cat a really unhealthy and low place\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 If she had been unable to get an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , Avantae is not sure if she would still be alive.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CEven the child that I had, who I love and adore, was not enough to keep me here,\u8221\'20\'1D Avantae said. \u8220\'20\'1CMy \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  literally saved my life.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Most \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  patients in the United States are in their 20s, have already given birth at least once before, and have low incomes. Avantae talks to patients who don\u8217\'20\'19t have phones, cars or computers; they have to scramble to take time off work, find childcare and scrape together hundreds of dollars to pay for an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 All of these problems can delay getting care.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CFifteen weeks, from start to finish, is a seemingly good amount of time, but in the scope of pregnancy and making this type of decision, it\u8217\'20\'19s not enough time,\u8221\'20\'1D Avantae said.\par \par \uc2 If Virginia outlaws \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  past 15 weeks or earlier, southern \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  seekers will likely stream into clinics closest to the Mason-Dixon line, in places like Maryland or Washington DC. Those clinics are already facing an increase in patients.\par \par \uc2 Hagstrom Miller, well aware that the coming election may torpedo her plans to expand the kinds of abortions her clinic offers, doesn\u8217\'20\'19t trust that Republicans would stop at a 15-week ban. She\u8217\'20\'19s not alone. A {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.dataforprogress.org/blog/2023/10/11/va-voters-in-competitive-districts-do-not-trust-youngkin-or-republicans-when-learning-about-candidates-positions-on-abortion"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 September poll from Data for Progress}}}\uc2 , a progressive polling firm, found that more than half of likely Virginia voters in competitive districts have little trust in Republicans when it comes to their positions on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  and reproductive healthcare.\par \par \uc2 After all, the case that overturned Roe v Wade, Dobbs v Jackson Women\u8217\'20\'19s Health Organization, technically turned on the constitutionality of a 15-week \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban in Mississippi. Since then, 16 states have banned almost all abortions.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThey start with a 15-week ban,\u8221\'20\'1D Hagstrom Miller said. \u8220\'20\'1CAnd then they push to a six-week ban, and then they push to a total ban.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 This article was amended on 31 October 2023 to correctly identify the lower chamber of Virginia\u8217\'20\'19s legislature.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020231031ejav0018j\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
