\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Special counsel accuses Trump of threatening \uc2 Mark Meadows\uc2  after he testified in election case - as it happened\b0\par\par\uc2 Chris Stein \par \uc2 6,337 \uc2 words\par \uc2 26 October 2023\par 20:03 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 This live blog is now closed. For more on Trump, read our latest report:Trump accused of witness threats after Meadows reportedly granted immunity\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.00pm BST\par \par \uc2 Closing summary\par \par \uc2 Washington is adjusting to the new reality presented by Mike Johnson \u8217\'20\'19s ascension to the speaker\u8217\'20\'19s podium in the House of Representatives. The Louisiana lawmaker is {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/oct/26/mike-johnson-speaker-house-election-denial-democrats-biden-2024-campaign-latest?page=with:block-653a63488f08a94db5838e9e#block-653a63488f08a94db5838e9e"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a staunch but low-profile conservative}}}\uc2  who wants \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  banned, doubts the scientific consensus regarding climate change and has promoted \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s baseless fraud claims over the 2020 election. But as much as they are likely to seize on those positions next year to argue Republicans are too extreme to govern, Democrats must first work with Johnson and his party on legislative business. In remarks on the Senate floor, Democratic leader \uc2 Chuck Schumer{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/oct/26/mike-johnson-speaker-house-election-denial-democrats-biden-2024-campaign-latest?page=with:block-653a800c8f08fea9e14db0c1#block-653a800c8f08fea9e14db0c1"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 urged}}}\uc2  the new speaker to embrace bipartisanship and avoid \u8220\'20\'1Cthe Maga road\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s what else happened today:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Federal prosecutors{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/oct/26/mike-johnson-speaker-house-election-denial-democrats-biden-2024-campaign-latest?page=with:block-653aac748f0880c2481900a3#block-653aac748f0880c2481900a3"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 accused}}}\uc2 Donald Trump of threatening \uc2 Mark Meadows\uc2 , his former White House chief of staff who spoke to them about the ex-president\u8217\'20\'19s efforts to overturn the 2020 election.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  and Johnson {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/oct/26/mike-johnson-speaker-house-election-denial-democrats-biden-2024-campaign-latest?page=with:block-653abc378f0837aa4c22b4c2#block-653abc378f0837aa4c22b4c2"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 met at the White House}}}\uc2  to discuss the president\u8217\'20\'19s request for more aid to Israel and Ukraine.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 A federal judge{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/oct/26/mike-johnson-speaker-house-election-denial-democrats-biden-2024-campaign-latest?page=with:block-653a93f48f08fea9e14db1db#block-653a93f48f08fea9e14db1db"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 ordered}}}\uc2  Georgia\u8217\'20\'19s Republican-dominated legislature to draw new congressional maps with another majority Black district, potentially offering Democrats an opportunity to gain a seat in the US House.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The president{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/oct/26/mike-johnson-speaker-house-election-denial-democrats-biden-2024-campaign-latest?page=with:block-653a71b98f08a94db5838fdf#block-653a71b98f08a94db5838fdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 cheered}}}\uc2  better-than-expected economic growth data that undercut forecasts of a looming US recession, and warned Republicans against sparking a government shutdown.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Patrick McHenry{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/oct/26/mike-johnson-speaker-house-election-denial-democrats-biden-2024-campaign-latest?page=with:block-653a991e8f08b48bad7c238c#block-653a991e8f08b48bad7c238c"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 dished}}}\uc2  on what it was like to be acting speaker of the House for three weeks.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.43pm BST\par \par \uc2 It\u8217\'20\'19s still too soon to say what kind of speaker of the House Mike Johnson will be, but the Guardian\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/carter-sherman"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Carter Sherman}}}\uc2  reports all signs point to him acting zealously in trying to roll back \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access:\par \par \uc2 The day after the \uc2 US supreme court\uc2  overturned Roe v Wade in June last year, Mike Johnson of Louisiana celebrated his home state\u8217\'20\'19s new penalties for \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  providers. \u8220\'20\'1CThe right to life has now been RESTORED!\u8221\'20\'1D the Republican {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/RepMikeJohnson/status/1540730281010860032"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 crowed}}}\uc2  on X, formerly known as \uc2 Twitter\uc2 , on 25 June. \u8220\'20\'1CPerform an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  and get imprisoned at hard labor for 1-10 yrs & fined $10K-$100K.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Opposition to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  is virtually a job requirement for {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/republicans"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Republicans}}}\uc2  these days. But Johnson, the newly minted speaker of the House, is a committed \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  opponent even by the standards of his fellow conservative colleagues.\par \par \uc2 Johnson ascended to the speakership after the sudden ouster of Kevin McCarthy, a California Republican, and weeks of tumult in the House. A member of the House since 2016, Johnson is a loyal supporter of \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  \u8211\'20\'13 to the point that {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/oct/25/who-is-mike-johnson-republican-2020-election"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 he served on Trump\u8217\'20\'19s legal defense team}}}\uc2  during Trump\u8217\'20\'19s first impeachment \u8211\'20\'13 and a social conservative {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nola.com/news/politics/rep-mike-johnson-of-benton-may-run-for-house-speaker/article_9cdb32b6-6d19-11ee-853c-6bdfaac9ccfa.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 fueled by his evangelical Christian faith}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 And, at a time when many Republicans in Congress are trying to quietly ignore \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , wary of the backlash from their constituents over proliferating \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  bans, Johnson has continued to champion an array of anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  bills.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/oct/26/republican-speaker-mike-johnson-roe-v-wade"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 New House speaker pushed for \u8216\'20\'18hard labor\u8217\'20\'19 for \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  providers after fall of Roe}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.25pm BST\par \par \uc2 Republican House speaker Mike Johnson meets Biden at White House on Ukraine, Israel aid\par \par \uc2 At her briefing today, White House press secretary \uc2 Karine Jean-Pierre\uc2  said \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  had invited Mike Johnson to meet shortly after he won election as House speaker last night.\par \par \uc2 She said the Louisiana Republican was with the president for \u8220\'20\'1Ca bipartisan briefing with leadership and relevant committee chairs and ranking members on the president\u8217\'20\'19s supplemental national security package\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 In a primetime television address from the Oval Office last week, Biden called on Congress to approve billions of dollars in aid to Israel and Ukraine. While the former is a popular cause with both parties, a growing number of Republicans is against further funding Kyiv\u8217\'20\'19s defense against the Russian invasion. Here\u8217\'20\'19s more on that:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/oct/20/biden-israel-ukraine-gaza-aid-request-congress"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Biden sends $106bn aid request to Congress for Israel, Ukraine and Gaza}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.01pm BST\par \par \uc2 We are learning more about Mike Johnson, the new speaker of the House who \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s press secretary \uc2 Karine Jean-Pierre\uc2  just said is currently attending a meeting at the White House. As the Guardian\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/roberttait"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Robert Tait}}}\uc2  reports, he has a history of channeling taxpayer funding to conservative Christian causes:\par \par \uc2 Mike Johnson, the newly-elected Republican speaker of the US House, won taxpayer funding for a Noah\u8217\'20\'19s Ark amusement park while working as a lawyer, in a graphic illustration of his uncompromising rightwing Christian beliefs.\par \par \uc2 Working for Freedom Guard, a non-profit proclaiming a commitment to defending religious liberty, Johnson was hired by Answers in Genesis, a creationist ministry, in 2015, after the state of Kentucky rescinded an offer of tourism tax incentives for the project in Williamstown, citing discrimination against non-Christian believers.\par \par \uc2 The state retracted an offer of tax breaks after the then-governor, Steve Beshear, said the ministry reneged on a commitment to refrain from hiring based on religious belief.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt has become clear that they do intend to use religious beliefs as a litmus test for hiring decisions,\u8221\'20\'1D Beshear said.\par \par \uc2 Johnson, who would win a seat in Congress from Louisiana in 2016, was among a team of attorneys engaged to press a federal lawsuit described by the Answers in Genesis president and chief executive, Ken Ham, as involving \u8220\'20\'1Cfreedom of religion, free exercise of religion, freedom of speech in this great nation of America\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Johnson accused the state of \u8220\'20\'1Cviewpoint discrimination\u8221\'20\'1D, adding: \u8220\'20\'1CThey have decided to exclude this organisation from a tax rebate programme that\u8217\'20\'19s offered to all applications across the state.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/oct/26/mike-johnson-noah-arc-amusement-park-tax-money"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 House speaker once won taxpayer funds for Noah\u8217\'20\'19s Ark park accused of discrimination}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.40pm BST\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s more from the Guardian\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/hugo-lowell"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Hugo Lowell}}}\uc2  on the news that former White House chief of staff \uc2 Mark Meadows\uc2  had spoken to special counsel Jack Smith as part of their investigation into \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s attempt to overturn the 2020 election:\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s former White House chief of staff {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/mark-meadows"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Mark Meadows}}}\uc2  testified to a federal grand jury earlier this year about efforts by the former president to overturn the 2020 election results pursuant to a court order that granted him limited immunity, according to two people familiar with the matter.\par \par \uc2 The immunity \u8211\'20\'13 which forces witnesses to testify on the promise that they will not be charged on their statements or information derived from their statements \u8211\'20\'13 came after a legal battle in March with special counsel prosecutors, who had subpoenaed Meadows.\par \par \uc2 Trump\u8217\'20\'19s lawyers attempted to block Meadows\u8217\'20\'19 testimony partially on executive privilege grounds. However, the outgoing chief US district judge \uc2 Beryl Howell\uc2  ruled that executive privilege was inapplicable and compelled Meadows to appear before the grand jury in Washington, the people said.\par \par \uc2 The precise details of what happened next are unclear, but prosecutors sought and received an order from the incoming chief judge \uc2 James Boasberg\uc2  granting limited-use immunity to Meadows to overcome his concerns about self-incrimination, the people familiar with the matter said.\par \par \uc2 That Meadows testified pursuant to a court order suggests prosecutors in the office of special counsel Jack Smith were determined to learn what information he was afraid to share because of self-incrimination concerns \u8211\'20\'13 but it does not mean he became a cooperator.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/oct/24/trump-chief-of-staff-mark-meadows-2020-election-case-immunity"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Trump chief Mark Meadows testified in 2020 election case after immunity order}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.20pm BST\par \par \uc2 Special counsel accuses Trump of threatening ex-chief of staff who testified in election case - report\par \par \uc2 Jack Smith, the special counsel prosecuting \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  for his attempt to overturn the 2020 election, accused the former president of threatening his former chief of staff after he spoke to investigators, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://abcnews.go.com/US/special-counsel-accuses-trump-threatening-chief-staff-mark/story?id=104348706"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 ABC News reports}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Smith\u8217\'20\'19s team cited posts Trump made on Truth Social after {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/oct/24/trump-chief-of-staff-mark-meadows-2020-election-case-immunity"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reports emerged}}}\uc2  that \uc2 Mark Meadows\uc2 , his chief of staff in the final months of his presidency, spoke to investigators about his attempts to stop \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s election victory.\par \par \uc2 Trump\u8217\'20\'19s comments \u8220\'20\'1Csend an unmistakable and threatening message to a foreseeable witness in this case,\u8221\'20\'1D Smith\u8217\'20\'19s team wrote in a Wednesday filing.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s more from ABC:\par \par \uc2 In a filing Wednesday night to the judge presiding over Trump\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://abcnews.go.com/US/timeline-special-counsels-probe-trumps-efforts-overturn-2020/story?id=101537003"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 federal election interference}}}\uc2  case in Washington, Smith\u8217\'20\'19s team said Trump\u8217\'20\'19s \u8220\'20\'1Charmful\u8221\'20\'1D post on Truth Social was trying to \u8220\'20\'1Csend an unmistakable and threatening message to a foreseeable witness in this case.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Smith\u8217\'20\'19s team argued to U.S. District Court Judge \uc2 Tanya Chutkan\uc2  that the alleged threat is just one more example of why a limited gag order in the case is needed as soon as possible.\par \par \uc2 Chutkan had issued such a gag order early last week but then {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://abcnews.go.com/US/judge-temporarily-halts-trumps-limited-gag-order-federal/story?id=104186855"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 temporarily suspended it}}}\uc2  after the former president\u8217\'20\'19s legal team appealed the judge\u8217\'20\'19s order to a higher court.\par \par \uc2 \u8230\'20\'26\par \par \uc2 In their filing Wednesday, Smith\u8217\'20\'19s team argued that Trump is now trying to \u8220\'20\'1Cuse external influences to distort the trial in his favor,\u8221\'20\'1D and that \u8220\'20\'1CThese actions, particularly when directed against witnesses and trial participants, pose a grave threat to the very notion of a fair trial based on the facts and the law.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Trump has a \u8220\'20\'1Clong and well-documented history of using his public platform to target disparaging and inflammatory comments at perceived adversaries,\u8221\'20\'1D and \u8220\'20\'1CWhen the defendant does so, harassment, threats, and intimidation foreseeably and predictably follow,\u8221\'20\'1D Smith\u8217\'20\'19s team wrote.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.04pm BST\par \par \uc2 Sam Levine, our dedicated voting rights reporter, has more on the federal {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.democracydocket.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/12/2023-10-26-Order-dckt-286_03.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 ruling}}}\uc2  today which says Georgia Republicans must redraw congressional and state legislative maps to give Black voters a fair shot at electing the candidate of their choice, a decision that could result in an additional Democratic seat in Congress.\par \par \uc2 When Georgia Republicans drew the state\u8217\'20\'19s 14 congressional districts last year, they placed the lines in such a way that they weakened the influence of Black voters in the west metro-Atlanta area, violating Section 2 of the Voting Rights Act, US district judge Steve Jones ruled on Thursday.\par \par \uc2 Jones gave Georgia lawmakers until 8 December to draw an additional majority-Black district in the west metro-Atlanta area, and said the court would draw a map if the legislature could not come up with a new plan by then.\par \par \uc2 Georgia is likely to appeal the ruling and to try and drag out the redrawing process as long as possible. A lengthy legal dispute is to the state\u8217\'20\'19s advantage because federal courts have been hesitant to intervene when elections are close.\par \par \uc2 Republicans currently have a 9-5 advantage in Georgia\u8217\'20\'19s congressional delegation. Since voting in the south of the US is often racially polarized, any district that gives Black voters a chance to elect the candidate of their choosing is likely to favor Democrats.\par \par \uc2 Republicans also have a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://ballotpedia.org/Georgia_House_of_Representatives"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 102-78 advantage}}}\uc2  in the state House of Representatives, where Jones ordered the addition of five majority-Black seats. They also have 33-23 advantage in the state senate, where Jones ordered two additional majority-Black seats.\par \par \uc2 Georgia gained an additional seat in Congress last year after significant population growth over the last decade. Almost all of that growth was due to a surging minority population in the state, Jones noted in a 516-page opinion, but the number of majority-Black congressional and legislative districts remained the same. Jones wrote:\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe court reiterates that Georgia has made great strides since 1965 towards equality in voting. However, the evidence before this court shows that Georgia has not reached the point where the political process has equal openness and equal opportunity for everyone.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The ruling is the latest in a series from federal courts in recent months finding that Republicans, who dominate state legislatures in the south and control the redistricting process, discriminated against Black voters when they drew district lines.\par \par \uc2 Judges have also ordered Republicans in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://viewer.gutools.co.uk/us-news/2023/sep/26/supreme-court-alabama-reject-map-black-voters"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Alabama}}}\uc2  and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://viewer.gutools.co.uk/law/2023/oct/19/black-voters-louisiana-us-supreme-court"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Louisiana}}}\uc2  to reconfigure their maps to add districts that give Black voters adequate power. There is also ongoing litigation in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://viewer.gutools.co.uk/us-news/2023/oct/11/supreme-court-south-carolina-congressional-map-case"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 South Carolina}}}\uc2  and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.usatoday.com/story/news/politics/elections/2023/09/04/florida-judge-strikes-down-ron-desantis-redistricting-map/70761229007/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Florida}}}\uc2  claiming district lines illegally minimize the influence of Black voters.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.45pm BST\par \par \uc2 Our columnist Margaret Sullivan thinks the installation of the Republican Mike Johnson as House speaker bodes ill not just for Democrats \u8211\'20\'13 but perhaps for democracy, in the sense of the prospects of a more peaceful election next year than in 2020, when the Louisianan was at \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s side as he attempted to cling onto power\u8230\'20\'26\par \par \uc2 The process was appalling, and the outcome even more so, as Republicans in the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/house-of-representatives"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 House of Representatives}}}\uc2  finally found someone they could more or less agree on.\par \par \uc2 That agreement, though, may be more accurately described as simple exhaustion after three weeks of embarrassing misfires.\par \par \uc2 And who is it they have managed to elect speaker of the US House, the person in line to lead the nation just after the president and vice-president?\par \par \uc2 It\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/mike-johnson"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Mike Johnson}}}\uc2  of Louisiana who, as one example of his profound unsuitability, brags that he doesn\u8217\'20\'19t believe that human beings cause the climate crisis, though his home state has been ravaged by it. He is against \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , voted against aid to Ukraine and stridently opposes LGBTQ+ rights.\par \par \uc2 Perhaps most notably, Johnson had a leading role in trying to overturn he 2020 election.\par \par \uc2 That means that the official second in line to the presidency \u8220\'20\'1Cviolated his oath to the constitution and tried to disenfranchise four states\u8221\'20\'1D, as the writer Marcy Wheeler neatly put it.\par \par \uc2 Johnson certainly has his Trumpian bona fides in order. In 2020, he helped lead a legal effort to reverse the results of the election in Georgia, Michigan, Pennsylvania and Wisconsin, and he hawked Trump\u8217\'20\'19s lies that the election had been rigged.\par \par \uc2 Whatever his shortcomings, we know that Johnson excels at one thing: pleasing {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/donaldtrump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Donald Trump}}}\uc2 , the autocrat wannabe and Republican party leader who loves nothing more than a good yes man.\par \par \uc2 Read on\u8230\'20\'26\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/commentisfree/2023/oct/26/mike-johnson-house-speaker-trump-2020-election"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Trumpist Mike Johnson is the House speaker. There\u8217\'20\'19s plenty to fear | Margaret Sullivan}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.22pm BST\par \par \uc2 Before the new Republican House speaker, Mike Johnson, won election to Congress in 2016, he worked as an attorney for rightwing Christian groups. Here, Robert Tait reports on events in Kentucky in 2015, when Johnson successfully fought the corner of builders of a Noah\u8217\'20\'19s Ark-themed amusement park, who were seeking government support despite the separation of church and state outlined in the US consitution\u8230\'20\'26\par \par \uc2 Mike Johnson, the newly-elected Republican speaker of the US House, won taxpayer funding for a Noah\u8217\'20\'19s Ark amusement park while working as a lawyer, in a graphic illustration of his uncompromising rightwing Christian beliefs.\par \par \uc2 Working for Freedom Guard, a nonprofit proclaiming a commitment to defending religious liberty, Johnson was hired by Answers in Genesis, a creationist ministry, in 2015, after the state of Kentucky rescinded an offer of tourism tax incentives for the project in Williamstown, citing discrimination against non-Christian believers.\par \par \uc2 The state retracted an offer of tax breaks after the-then governor, Steve Beshear, said the ministry reneged on a commitment to refrain from hiring based on religious belief.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt has become clear that they do intend to use religious beliefs as a litmus test for hiring decisions,\u8221\'20\'1D Beshear said.\par \par \uc2 Johnson, who would win a seat in Congress from Louisiana in 2016, was among a team of attorneys engaged to press a federal lawsuit described by the Answers in Genesis president and chief executive, Ken Ham, as involving \u8220\'20\'1Cfreedom of religion, free exercise of religion, freedom of speech in this great nation of America\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s more on Johnson\u8217\'20\'19s own beliefs and previous work\u8230\'20\'26\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/oct/26/republican-speaker-mike-johnson-roe-v-wade"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 New House speaker pushed for \u8216\'20\'18hard labor\u8217\'20\'19 for \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  providers after fall of Roe}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 6.22pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.03pm BST\par \par \uc2 The day so far\par \par \uc2 Washington is adjusting to the new reality presented by Mike Johnson \u8217\'20\'19s ascension to the speaker\u8217\'20\'19s podium in the House of Representatives. The Louisiana lawmaker is {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/oct/26/mike-johnson-speaker-house-election-denial-democrats-biden-2024-campaign-latest?page=with:block-653a63488f08a94db5838e9e#block-653a63488f08a94db5838e9e"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a staunch but low-profile conservative}}}\uc2  who wants \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  banned, doubts the scientific consensus regarding climate change and has promoted \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s baseless fraud claims over the 2020 election. But as much as they are likely to seize on those positions next year to argue Republicans are too extreme to govern, Democrats also have to work with Johnson and his party on legislative business. In remarks on the Senate floor, Democratic leader \uc2 Chuck Schumer{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/oct/26/mike-johnson-speaker-house-election-denial-democrats-biden-2024-campaign-latest?page=with:block-653a800c8f08fea9e14db0c1#block-653a800c8f08fea9e14db0c1"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 urged}}}\uc2  the new speaker to embrace bipartisanship and avoid \u8220\'20\'1Cthe Maga road\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s what else has happened today so far:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/oct/26/mike-johnson-speaker-house-election-denial-democrats-biden-2024-campaign-latest?page=with:block-653a71b98f08a94db5838fdf#block-653a71b98f08a94db5838fdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 cheered}}}\uc2  better-than-expected economic growth data that undercut forecasts of a looming US recession, and warned Republicans against sparking a government shutdown.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 A federal judge{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/oct/26/mike-johnson-speaker-house-election-denial-democrats-biden-2024-campaign-latest?page=with:block-653a93f48f08fea9e14db1db#block-653a93f48f08fea9e14db1db"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 ordered}}}\uc2  Georgia\u8217\'20\'19s Republican-dominated legislature to draw new congressional maps with another majority Black district, potentially offering Democrats an opportunity to gain a seat in the US House.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Patrick McHenry{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/oct/26/mike-johnson-speaker-house-election-denial-democrats-biden-2024-campaign-latest?page=with:block-653a991e8f08b48bad7c238c#block-653a991e8f08b48bad7c238c"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 dished}}}\uc2  on what it was like to be acting speaker of the House for three weeks.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.55pm BST\par \par \uc2 Back in the House, \uc2 Patrick McHenry\uc2 , who was the acting speaker for three weeks during the Republican civil war over finding a replacement for Kevin McCarthy, shared some details of his brief term leading the chamber.\par \par \uc2 The Associated Press reports that McHenry was given advance notice that McCarthy had named him as a temporary replacement before the then speaker was removed from office:\par \par \uc2 enltr????New: Former Speaker Pro Tem Patrick McHenry tells us that he was first alerted that he was first on McCarthy\u8217\'20\'19s list as temporary replacement two weeks (!!) before Gaetz filed his resolution to oust McCarthy. He faced immense pressure from GOP to take on more powers in the 3\u8230\'20\'26\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Farnoush Amiri (@FarnoushAmiri) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/FarnoushAmiri/status/1717584541362098670?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 October 26, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 McHenry also made a point of noting his continued ill feelings towards those who removed McCarthy:\par \par \uc2 enltrPatrick McHenry telling us what he really thinks: calls the last month \u8220\'20\'1Cperhaps the dumbest set of politics or decision making a majority party in this institution can make\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Jonathan Tamari (@JonathanTamari) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/JonathanTamari/status/1717579097277141183?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 October 26, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 6.03pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.33pm BST\par \par \uc2 Judge orders Georgia to draw another majority-Black congressional district, in potential boost for Democrats\par \par \uc2 A federal judge {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.documentcloud.org/documents/24087324/10-26-23-redistricting-order.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 has ordered}}}\uc2  Georgia\u8217\'20\'19s Republican-dominated legislature to draw another majority-Black congressional district, arguing that the state\u8217\'20\'19s current lines violate the Voting Rights Act.\par \par \uc2 The Atlanta-Journal Constitution reports the legislature will have to convene for a special session to make a new map, which could present Democrats an opportunity to pick up another House seat from the state, since African American voters tend to support the party:\par \par \uc2 enltrJust in: A federal judge has struck down Georgia\u8217\'20\'19s congressional and legislative maps, ruling that they violate Section 2 of the Voting Rights Act. Georgia lawmakers have until Dec. 8 to draw new lines, setting up a special legislative session. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/hashtag/gapol?src=hash&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 #gapol}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/aK5Hkoh8C5"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/aK5Hkoh8C5}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Greg Bluestein (@bluestein) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/bluestein/status/1717572744059957732?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 October 26, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 enltrThe ruling is a victory for Democrats and their allies who challenged the maps, contending they illegally diluted the voting power of Black Georgians. And some Democrats were already lining up to run in GOP-leaning districts that could be redrawn. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/hashtag/gapol?src=hash&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 #gapol}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/vLZo1FoP8k"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/vLZo1FoP8k}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Greg Bluestein (@bluestein) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/bluestein/status/1717573639418085816?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 October 26, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 enltrThe decision could result in the election of additional Black representatives next year, with Democrats hoping to gain a seat in the U.S. House, where Republicans currently hold a narrow majority, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/markniesse?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @markniesse}}}\uc2  reports. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/hashtag/gapol?src=hash&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 #gapol}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/Xa6JGxJRTG"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/Xa6JGxJRTG}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Greg Bluestein (@bluestein) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/bluestein/status/1717575369417539738?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 October 26, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 5.38pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.13pm BST\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, Democratic congressman \uc2 Jamaal Bowman\uc2  insisted he was not trying to disrupt Congress last month when he pulled a Capitol complex fire alarm amid fervent negotiations aimed at passing a government spending bill:\par \par \uc2 enltr\u8220\'20\'1CThey weaponize any opportunity they can... just so we don\u8217\'20\'19t focus on their own dysfunction.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 As he pleads guilty to a misdemeanor for pulling a fire alarm at the Capitol last month, Rep. \uc2 Jamaal Bowman\uc2  (D-NY) reacts to Republicans comparing him to a Jan. 6 insurrectionist {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/kMe9oDMIpk"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/kMe9oDMIpk}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 The Recount (@therecount) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/therecount/status/1717566216938615237?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 October 26, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 The New York lawmaker is moving to resolve the issue today by entering a not guilty plea to a misdemeanor charge and paying a fine. Here\u8217\'20\'19s more on that:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/oct/26/jamaal-bowman-fire-alarm-fine"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Jamaal Bowman to plead guilty and pay fine for pulling House fire alarm }}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 5.17pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.53pm BST\par \par \uc2 Rightwing congresswoman \uc2 Marjorie Taylor Greene\uc2  moves to censure progressive \uc2 Rashida Tlaib\uc2  for alleged antisemitism\par \par \uc2 Marjorie Taylore Greene, one of the most outspoken far-right Republicans in the House, has proposed a resolution to censure Democrat \uc2 Rashida Tlaib\uc2  on claims of antisemitism.\par \par \uc2 The Michigan lawmaker is one of two Muslims in the House and has been outspoken against Israel\u8217\'20\'19s conduct in its bombing campaign against the Gaza Strip following the 7 October terrorist attack. Greene\u8217\'20\'19s censure resolution makes a number of far-fetched and dubious claims, including that Tlaib engaged in \u8220\'20\'1Cinsurrection\u8221\'20\'1D earlier this month when protesters entered a House office building and staged a noisy protest that ended with many arrests.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s Greene on the House floor announcing the censure resolution:\par \par \uc2 enltrRep. \uc2 Marjorie Taylor Greene\uc2  (R-GA) on resolution to censure Rep. \uc2 Rashida Tlaib\uc2  (D-MI): "A resolution censuring representative \uc2 Rashida Tlaib\uc2  for anti-Semitic activity, sympathizing with terrorist organization and leading an insurrection at the United States Capitol complex." {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/Cp0MH9XXke"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/Cp0MH9XXke}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 CSPAN (@cspan) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/cspan/status/1717556253617262663?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 October 26, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 Politico managed to get their hands on a copy of the resolution, which you can read below:\par \par \uc2 enltrHere\u8217\'20\'19s the resolution {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/8fDziixzkA"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/8fDziixzkA}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Olivia Beavers (@Olivia_Beavers) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/Olivia_Beavers/status/1717551598916731044?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 October 26, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.28pm BST\par \par \uc2 Biden condemns Maine mass shooting, calls for GOP to support ban on assault weapons, high-capacity magazines\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  has released a statement calling yesterday\u8217\'20\'19s mass shooting in Lewiston, Maine, that left 18 people dead \u8220\'20\'1Csenseless and tragic\u8221\'20\'1D, and urging Republicans to support tightening access to firearms.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1COnce again, our nation is in mourning after yet another senseless and tragic mass shooting. Today, Jill and I are praying for the Americans who\u8217\'20\'19ve lost their lives, for those still in critical care, and for the families, survivors and community members enduring shock and grief,\u8221\'20\'1D the president said.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CToday, in the wake of yet another tragedy, I urge Republican lawmakers in Congress to fulfill their duty to protect the American people. Work with us to pass a bill banning assault weapons and high-capacity magazines, to enact universal background checks, to require safe storage of guns and end immunity from liability for gun manufacturers. This is the very least we owe every American who will now bear the scars \u8211\'20\'13 physical and mental \u8211\'20\'13 of this latest attack.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 For more on this developing story, follow our live blog:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/oct/26/maine-shooting-lewiston-deaths-us-latest-updates"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Maine shootings: 18 killed and suspected gunman still at large, police say \u8211\'20\'13 latest updates}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 4.33pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.08pm BST\par \par \uc2 Senate Democratic leader \uc2 Chuck Schumer\uc2  says Johnson \u8216\'20\'18will fail\u8217\'20\'19 as speaker if he shuns bipartisanship\par \par \uc2 In remarks on the Senate floor, Democratic majority leader \uc2 Chuck Schumer\uc2  urged the newly elected Republican House speaker to embrace bipartisanship, and warned him against tumbling down \u8220\'20\'1Cthe Maga road\u8221\'20\'1D:\par \par \uc2 enltr\u8220\'20\'1CIf Speaker Johnson lives up to the label that Congressman Gaetz has given him, \u8216\'20\'18MAGA Mike,\u8217\'20\'19 he will fail as the previous Speakers have\u8230\'20\'26 I look forward to working constructively\u8230\'20\'26and congratulate him on his election.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Majority Leader \uc2 Chuck Schumer\uc2  (D-NY) on the Senate floor {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/sAZTR3vuw1"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/sAZTR3vuw1}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 The Recount (@therecount) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/therecount/status/1717555809503035894?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 October 26, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 Anything the GOP-dominated House passes must be approved by the Democratic-controlled Senate, and vice versa \u8211\'20\'13 including legislation to fund the government beyond 17 November. That is expected to be Congress\u8217\'20\'19s top priority in the weeks to come.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 4.11pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.44pm BST\par \par \uc2 On the topic of government shutdowns, there appears to be a resolution at hand to address the strange incident of Democratic congressman \uc2 Jamaal Bowman\uc2  pulling a fire alarm last month during a tense moment in spending negotiations, the Guardian\u8217\'20\'19s Martin Pengelly reports:\par \par \uc2 The Democratic New York congressman \uc2 Jamaal Bowman\uc2  said he would plead guilty to a misdemeanour charge and pay a fine for {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/sep/30/democrat-jamaal-bowman-fire-alarm-house"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pulling a fire alarm}}}\uc2  in a congressional building as a crucial vote neared last month.\par \par \uc2 In a statement, Bowman {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/RepBowman/status/1717297618491953308/photo/1"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 said}}}\uc2  : \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19m thankful for the quick resolution from the District of Columbia attorney general\u8217\'20\'19s office on this issue and grateful that the United States Capitol police general counsel\u8217\'20\'19s office agreed I did not obstruct nor intend to obstruct any House vote of proceedings.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI am responsible for activating a fire alarm, I will be paying the fine issued, and look forward to these charges ultimately being dropped.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 On Saturday, 30 September, Bowman was {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/sep/30/democrat-jamaal-bowman-fire-alarm-house"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 captured on camera}}}\uc2  pulling the alarm in the Cannon office building as a vote on a stopgap funding measure, which ultimately staved off a government shutdown, drew near.\par \par \uc2 Republicans accused him of seeking to delay the vote. He denied it.\par \par \uc2 He said: \u8220\'20\'1CToday, as I was rushing to make a vote, I came to a door that is usually open for votes but today was not open. I am embarrassed to admit that I activated the fire alarm, mistakenly thinking it would open the door. I regret this and sincerely apologise for any confusion this caused.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/oct/26/jamaal-bowman-fire-alarm-fine"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Jamaal Bowman to plead guilty and pay fine for pulling House fire alarm }}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 4.03pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.28pm BST\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s more from Reuters on today\u8217\'20\'19s economic growth data. Among the conclusions that can be drawn from it is that the United States is not in a recession, despite the predictions of some economists as well as \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s Republican adversaries:\par \par \uc2 The {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/business/useconomy"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 US economy}}}\uc2  grew at its fastest pace in nearly two years in the third quarter as higher wages from a tight labor market helped to power consumer spending, again defying dire warnings of a recession that have lingered since 2022.\par \par \uc2 Gross domestic product increased at a 4.9% annualized rate last quarter, the fastest since the fourth quarter of 2021, the \uc2 Commerce Department\u8217\'20\'19s Bureau of Economic Analysis\uc2  said in its advance estimate of third-quarter GDP growth. Economists polled by Reuters had forecast GDP rising at a 4.3% rate.\par \par \uc2 Estimates ranged from as low as a 2.5% rate to as high as a 6.0% pace, a wide margin reflecting that some of the input data, including September durable goods orders, goods trade deficit, wholesale and retail inventory numbers were published at the same time as the GDP report.\par \par \uc2 The economy grew at a 2.1% pace in the April-June quarter and is expanding at a rate well above what Fed officials regard as the non-inflationary growth rate of around 1.8%.\par \par \uc2 While the robust growth pace notched last quarter is unlikely sustainable, it was testament to the economy\u8217\'20\'19s resilience despite aggressive interest rate hikes from the \uc2 Federal Reserve\uc2 . Growth could slow in the fourth quarter because of the \uc2 United Auto Workers\uc2  strikes and the resumption of student loan repayments by millions of Americans.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/business/2023/oct/26/us-economy-growth-gdp-2023-q3"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 US economy grows at fastest pace in nearly two years in third quarter of 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.08pm BST\par \par \uc2 Biden hails economic growth, warns Republicans against government shutdown\par \par \uc2 In a just-released statement, \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  cheered {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/business/2023/oct/26/us-economy-growth-gdp-2023-q3"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 today\u8217\'20\'19s commerce department data}}}\uc2  showing the US economy grew at its fastest pace in nearly two years in the third quarter, while warning Republicans against shutting down the government.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI always say it is a mistake to bet against the American people, and just today we learned the economy grew 4.9% in the third quarter. I never believed we would need a recession to bring inflation down \u8211\'20\'13 and today we saw again that the American economy continues to grow even as inflation has come down. It is a testament to the resilience of American consumers and American workers, supported by Bidenomics \u8211\'20\'13 my plan to grow the economy by growing the middle class,\u8221\'20\'1D the president said, using the term his administration coined to describe his economic policies.\par \par \uc2 Congress is in the midst of a protracted fight over government spending, which has returned as the biggest issue on lawmakers\u8217\'20\'19 plates after the House yesterday elected Mike Johnson speaker, allowing the lower chamber to pass legislation again. The federal government will exhaust its ability to spend money after 17 November, at which point it will have to halt or dramatically curtail services. In his statement, Biden warned that could have a disastrous effect on the economy.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI hope Republicans in Congress will join me in working to build on this progress, rather than putting our economy at risk with reckless threats of a shutdown or proposals to cut taxes for the wealthy and large corporations, while slashing programs that are essential for hard-working families and seniors,\u8221\'20\'1D the president said.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.12pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.45pm BST\par \par \uc2 Or take it from \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  himself.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s the former president yesterday taking credit for getting Mike Johnson elected as speaker of the House. Trump was speaking outside his ongoing civil fraud trial in New York City:\par \par \uc2 enltrDonald Trump congratulates Speaker Mike Johnson (R-LA) and takes credit for him being elected:\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe were very happy to help \u8230\'20\'26 At this time yesterday, nobody was thinking of Mike, and then we put out the word and now he's the Speaker of the House.\u8221\'20\'1D {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/ytSQMNGP6l"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/ytSQMNGP6l}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 The Recount (@therecount) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/therecount/status/1717280735499878636?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 October 25, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 Just the day prior, Republicans had nominated their third-highest-ranking lawmaker in the House, \uc2 Tom Emmer\uc2 , for the leadership post, only to see him quickly drop out of contention, in part due to opposition from Trump.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.49pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.26pm BST\par \par \uc2 Affirmation of Mike Johnson\u8217\'20\'19s Trumpian bona fides came yesterday from none other than \uc2 Matt Gaetz\uc2 , the rightwing lawmaker who successfully ousted Kevin McCarthy from the speaker\u8217\'20\'19s post earlier this month, kicking off three weeks of crisis in the House. Here\u8217\'20\'19s what Gaetz had to say about the chamber\u8217\'20\'19s new leader, from the Guardian\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/martin-pengelly"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Martin Pengelly}}}\uc2  :\par \par \uc2 Mike Johnson\u8217\'20\'19s ascent to be speaker of the \uc2 US House of Representatives\uc2  proves \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  dominates the Republican party and \u8220\'20\'1CMaga is ascendant\u8221\'20\'1D, the Florida congressman \uc2 Matt Gaetz{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/atrupar/status/1717198721178357949"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 said}}}\uc2 , using an acronym for Trump\u8217\'20\'19s campaign slogan, \u8220\'20\'1CMake America great again\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe swamp is on the run, Maga is ascendant and if you don\u8217\'20\'19t think that moving from Kevin McCarthy to Maga Mike Johnson shows the ascendance of this movement, and where the power of the Republican party truly lies, then you\u8217\'20\'19re not paying attention,\u8221\'20\'1D Gaetz {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/atrupar/status/1717198721178357949"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 told}}}\uc2  the former Trump campaign chair and White House strategist \uc2 Steve Bannon\uc2  on his podcast on Wednesday.\par \par \uc2 Gaetz precipitated three weeks of leaderless chaos inside the Republican party, and therefore the House, when he triggered the removal of McCarthy this month. Seven other {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/republicans"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Republicans}}}\uc2  voted to make McCarthy the first speaker ever ejected by his own party but Gaetz orchestrated the move.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/oct/26/mike-johnson-speaker-matt-gaetz-maga-ascendant"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Mike Johnson as speaker shows \u8216\'20\'18Maga is ascendant\u8217\'20\'19 in Congress, Matt Gaetz says}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.38pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.08pm BST\par \par \uc2 At one point in the chaotic three weeks it took Republicans to elect a new speaker of the House, the party nominated conservative firebrand Jim Jordan for the post, only to see him lose the election and drop out after more lawmakers objected to his embrace of rightwing causes. But as the Guardian\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/martin-pengelly"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Martin Pengelly}}}\uc2  and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/sam-levine"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Sam Levine}}}\uc2  made clear yesterday, Mike Johnson believes in many of the same things \u8211\'20\'13 and now, he\u8217\'20\'19s the leader of the chamber. Here\u8217\'20\'19s more on what they found:\par \par \uc2 Mike Johnson\u8217\'20\'19s emergence as the new speaker of the US {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/house-of-representatives"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 House of Representatives}}}\uc2  has earned the relatively little-known Louisiana Republican a turn in the national spotlight.\par \par \uc2 That spotlight has illuminated positions and remarks many deem extreme.\par \par \uc2 He tried to overturn the 2020 election\par \par \uc2 In the modern Republican party, supporting \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s lie about the role of voter fraud in his defeat by \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  is hardly an outlandish position. But Johnson took it further.\par \par \uc2 After the election, he voiced {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://nymag.com/intelligencer/2023/10/house-speaker-republican-mike-johnson-january-6-mastermind-trump-election-2020.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 support}}}\uc2  for Trump\u8217\'20\'19s conspiracy theory that voting machines were rigged. Later, he was one of 147 Republicans to object to results in key states, even after a pro-Trump mob attacked Congress on 6 January 2021, a riot now linked to nine deaths and hundreds of convictions.\par \par \uc2 Johnson also authored {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.supremecourt.gov/DocketPDF/22/22O155/163550/20201211132250339_Texas%20v.%20Pennsylvania%20Amicus%20Brief%20of%20126%20Representatives%20--%20corrected.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 an amicus brief}}}\uc2  filed to the supreme court in a case in which Texas sought to have swing-state results thrown out. According {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/2022/10/03/us/politics/republican-election-objectors.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 to the New York Times}}}\uc2 , a House Republican lawyer said Johnson\u8217\'20\'19s brief was unconstitutional. Nonetheless, he persuaded 125 colleagues to sign it, using tactics some thought heavy-handed.\par \par \uc2 The supreme court refused to take the case. On Tuesday, Johnson refused to take a question about his work on Trump\u8217\'20\'19s behalf \u8211\'20\'13 smiling as fellow Republicans {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/oct/25/house-speaker-mike-johnson-republican-heckle-abc-reporter-trump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 booed and jeered}}}\uc2  the reporter.\par \par \uc2 He was a spokesperson for a \u8216\'20\'18hate group\u8217\'20\'19\par \par \uc2 Before entering politics, Johnson worked for the \uc2 Alliance Defending Freedom\uc2  \u8211\'20\'13 designated a hate group by the Southern Law Poverty Center, which tracks US extremists.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.splcenter.org/fighting-hate/extremist-files/group/alliance-defending-freedom"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 According to the SPLC}}}\uc2 , the \uc2 ADF\uc2  has \u8220\'20\'1Csupported the recriminalisation of sexual acts between consenting LGBTQ+ adults in the US and criminalisation abroad; defended state-sanctioned sterilisation of trans people abroad; contended that LGBTQ+ people are more likely to engage in paedophilia; and claimed that a \u8216\'20\'18homosexual agenda\u8217\'20\'19 will destroy Christianity and society\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 On Wednesday, the \uc2 ADF\uc2  senior counsel, \uc2 Jeremy Tedesco\uc2 , denied the organisation was a hate group and attacked the \uc2 SPLC\uc2  designation as partisan.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe truth is, \uc2 Alliance Defending Freedom\uc2  is among the largest and most effective legal advocacy organizations dedicated to protecting the religious freedom and free speech rights of all Americans,\u8221\'20\'1D he said.\par \par \uc2 He opposes LGBTQ+ rights\par \par \uc2 In state politics and at the national level, Johnson has worked to claw back gains made by LGBTQ+ Americans in their fight for equality.\par \par \uc2 In 2016, as he ran for Congress, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.baptistmessage.com/mike-johnson-faith-family-freedom-motivate-run-seat-u-s-congress/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 he told the Louisiana Baptist Message}}}\uc2  he had \u8220\'20\'1Cbeen out on the front lines of the \u8216\'20\'18culture war\u8217\'20\'19 defending religious freedom, the sanctity of human life and biblical values, including the defense of traditional marriage, and other ideals like these when they\u8217\'20\'19ve been under assault\u8221\'20\'1D. He has since led efforts for a national \u8220\'20\'1C {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://lailluminator.com/2022/10/25/u-s-rep-mike-johnson-introduces-dont-say-gay-bill/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 don\u8217\'20\'19t say gay}}}\uc2  \u8221\'20\'1D bill, regarding the teaching of LGBTQ+ issues in schools, and is also {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://lailluminator.com/2023/07/27/parents-have-no-right-to-allow-their-childrens-gender-transition-republicans-say/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 opposed}}}\uc2  to gender-affirming care for children.\par \par \uc2 On Wednesday, the Rev Jasmine Beach-Ferrara, executive director of the Campaign for Southern Equality, said: \u8220\'20\'1CJohnson has made a career out of attacking the LGBTQ+ community at every turn. His positions are out of touch with the clear majority support for LGBTQ+ equality in our country. His new leadership role is just further proof of the dangerous priorities of the GOP and the critical stakes for our democracy \u8211\'20\'13 and for LGBTQ+ Americans \u8211\'20\'13 in 2024.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/oct/25/who-is-mike-johnson-house-speaker-election-denier-climate-anti-abortion"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Election denier, climate skeptic, anti-\b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22 : seven beliefs of new US House speaker Mike Johnson}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.12pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.46pm BST\par \par \uc2 Democrats gear up to put House speaker Johnson\u8217\'20\'19s rightwing leaning at center of 2024 campaign\par \par \uc2 Good morning, US politics blog readers. With Mike Johnson \u8217\'20\'19s election as speaker of the House of Representatives yesterday, the chamber can finally get back to work \u8211\'20\'13 and so can the Democratic strategists who are sure to use {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/oct/25/who-is-mike-johnson-house-speaker-election-denier-climate-anti-abortion"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 his rightwing beliefs}}}\uc2  as evidence that the GOP is too extreme to rule. The Louisiana lawmaker was an enthusiastic supporter of \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s attempt to disrupt his 2020 election loss, opposes abortions and LGBTQ+ rights, and rejects the scientific consensus on climate change. The GOP has only a four-seat majority in the chamber, and Democrats are keen to topple some of the 18 Republicans representing districts \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  won in 2020 and retake the majority next year \u8211\'20\'13 a campaign Johnson seems to be at the center of.\par \par \uc2 One of the first orders of business before Johnson will be finding agreement on a measure to fund the government beyond mid-November, when its current authorization expires. He\u8217\'20\'19ll have to choose between insisting on deep cuts in spending that could alienate voters and potentially his own fellow lawmakers, or a more moderate proposal meant to keep the lights on while longer-term spending is negotiated. That\u8217\'20\'19s a story that will play out in the weeks to come, but one thing is assured: Democrats will be watching.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s what else is happening today:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  has no public events planned today, after staying up late yesterday for a state dinner with the Australian prime minister, Anthony Albanese. The usual press briefing takes place at 1pm eastern time.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 A manhunt is under way in Maine after a gunman killed 16 people. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/oct/26/maine-shooting-lewiston-deaths-us-latest-updates"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Follow our live blog}}}\uc2  for the latest on this developing story.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Nancy Pelosi\uc2 , the former Democratic speaker of the House, will address first-year students at Georgetown Law School this afternoon \u8211\'20\'13 and perhaps weigh in on Johnson\u8217\'20\'19s emergence.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 1.51pm BST\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020231026ejaq001xp\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
