\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 New House speaker pushed for \u8216\'20\'18hard labor\u8217\'20\'19 for  \highlight22\uc2 abortion \highlight\uc2  providers after fall of Roe\b0\par\par\uc2 Carter Sherman \par \uc2 702 \uc2 words\par \uc2 26 October 2023\par 16:07 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Mike Johnson of Louisiana has continued to champion anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  bills even as some in his party beware US voter backlash\par \par \uc2 The day after the \uc2 US supreme court\uc2  overturned Roe v Wade in June last year, Mike Johnson of Louisiana celebrated his home state\u8217\'20\'19s new penalties for \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  providers. \u8220\'20\'1CThe right to life has now been RESTORED!\u8221\'20\'1D the Republican {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/RepMikeJohnson/status/1540730281010860032"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 crowed}}}\uc2  on X, formerly known as \uc2 Twitter\uc2 , on 25 June. \u8220\'20\'1CPerform an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  and get imprisoned at hard labor for 1-10 yrs & fined $10K-$100K.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Opposition to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  is virtually a job requirement for Republicans these days. But Johnson, the newly minted speaker of the House, is a committed \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  opponent even by the standards of his fellow conservative colleagues.\par \par \uc2 Johnson ascended to the speakership after the sudden ouster of Kevin McCarthy, a California Republican, and weeks of tumult in the House. A member of the House since 2016, Johnson is a loyal supporter of Donald Trump \u8211\'20\'13 to the point that {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/oct/25/who-is-mike-johnson-republican-2020-election"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 he served on Trump\u8217\'20\'19s legal defense team}}}\uc2  during Trump\u8217\'20\'19s first impeachment \u8211\'20\'13 and a social conservative {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nola.com/news/politics/rep-mike-johnson-of-benton-may-run-for-house-speaker/article_9cdb32b6-6d19-11ee-853c-6bdfaac9ccfa.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 fueled by his evangelical Christian faith}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 And, at a time when many Republicans in Congress are trying to quietly ignore \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , wary of the backlash from their constituents over proliferating \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  bans, Johnson has continued to champion an array of anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  bills.\par \par \uc2 Since Roe v Wade\u8217\'20\'19s demise, Johnson has co-sponsored a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.congress.gov/bill/117th-congress/house-bill/8814?s=2&r=30&q=%7B%22search%22%3A%22abortion+abortion+abortion%22%7D"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 national 15-week \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  ban}}}\uc2  as well as a ban on the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.congress.gov/bill/118th-congress/house-bill/862?q=%7B%22search%22%3A%22abortion+abortion+abortion%22%7D&s=2&r=6"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 most common second-trimester \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  method}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 He also co-sponsored bills to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.congress.gov/bill/118th-congress/house-bill/371?q=%7B%22search%22%3A%22abortion+abortion%22%7D&s=1&r=13"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 strip Planned Parenthood of federal funding}}}\uc2 , to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.congress.gov/bill/118th-congress/house-bill/983?q=%7B%22search%22%3A%22abortion+abortion%22%7D&s=1&r=5"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 force providers to tell women}}}\uc2  that they may be able to \u8220\'20\'1Creverse\u8221\'20\'1D their abortions \u8211\'20\'13 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/carter-sherman"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a claim unproven by science}}}\uc2  \u8211\'20\'13 and to make it a federal crime to transport a minor across state lines for a legal \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  without telling that minor\u8217\'20\'19s parents.\par \par \uc2 Johnson backed a bill that would have {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.congress.gov/bill/118th-congress/house-bill/431?q=%7B%22search%22%3A%22abortion+abortion%22%7D&s=1&r=9"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 established that life begins at conception}}}\uc2  and redefined fetuses as human beings. So-called \u8220\'20\'1Cpersonhood\u8221\'20\'1D bills could upend vast swaths of US law. For example, Georgia\u8217\'20\'19s six-week \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban, which includes personhood language, lets people claim fetuses as tax dependents.\par \par \uc2 In 2021, Johnson even co-sponsored a bill that would have {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.congress.gov/bill/117th-congress/house-bill/705?s=3&r=2&q=%7B%22search%22%3A%22abortion+abortion+heartbeat+abortion+abortion+heartbeat%22%7D"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 nationally banned abortions past roughly six weeks}}}\uc2  of pregnancy. The bill would have allowed abortions in cases where a woman\u8217\'20\'19s life is endangered due to a physical condition, but not due to a psychological one.\par \par \uc2 Before arriving at the House, Johnson worked as an attorney for the \uc2 Alliance Defending Freedom\uc2 , a powerhouse of a Christian law firm and the organization behind much of the modern anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  movement\u8217\'20\'19s legal strategy. The group drafted model legislation that led to a 15-week \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban in Mississippi, which, ultimately, was at the heart of the case used to overturn Roe.\par \par \uc2 Democrats are {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/BidenHQ/status/1717177186086465983"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 circulating}}}\uc2  footage of Johnson on social media, where Johnson can be seen speaking at a House hearing linking the availability of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  to the health of the economy.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CRoe v Wade gave constitutional cover to the elective killing of unborn children in America, period,\u8221\'20\'1D Johnson said in the clip. \u8220\'20\'1CYou think about the implications of that on the economy. We\u8217\'20\'19re all struggling here to cover the bases of social security and Medicare and Medicaid and all the rest. If we had all those able-bodied workers in the economy, we wouldn\u8217\'20\'19t be going upside down and toppling over like this.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Susan B Anthony\uc2  Pro-Life America, a powerful anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  organization, has given Johnson an \u8220\'20\'1CA+\u8221\'20\'1D for his record in Congress.\par \par \uc2 On Wednesday, the group\u8217\'20\'19s president, Marjorie Dannenfelser, quickly congratulated Johnson.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe are thrilled by the election of Speaker Johnson and look forward to working closely with him to advance national protections for unborn babies, serve mothers, and grow the pro-life House majority in 2024,\u8221\'20\'1D she said in a statement.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CHe has boldly championed life as an activist, litigator, state legislator, and as a member of Congress. These strong credentials will help him lead the pro-life movement in this exciting and challenging new era as speaker of the House.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020231026ejaq002e6\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
