\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Conservative Mike Johnson wins House vote to become next speaker - as it happened\b0\par\par\uc2 Maanvi Singh (now); Maya Yang and Gloria Oladipo (earlier) \par \uc2 5,193 \uc2 words\par \uc2 25 October 2023\par 21:28 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 This live blog is now closed. For the latest on the new House speaker, read our latest report:Republican Mike Johnson elected House speaker after weeks of chaos\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.23pm BST\par \par \uc2 Today's recap\par \par \uc2 After weeks of political in fighting and unsuccessful speaker nominations, the Louisiana Republican representative Mike Johnson has become House speaker.\par \par \uc2 The vote came out to 220-209 with every House Republican voting for him. The vote marks a breakthrough in a three-week limbo after House Republicans voted to oust Kevin McCarthy from the seat earlier this month.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Johnson has {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/oct/25/house-speaker-mike-johnson-republican-heckle-abc-reporter-trump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 already faced questions}}}\uc2  over his history of supporting Trump\u8217\'20\'19s efforts to overturn the results of the 2020 presidential election\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Groups advocating for human rights, including LGBTQ+ and womens\u8217\'20\'19 rights have said that Johnson\u8217\'20\'19s speakership is a threat, condemning his far-right views and voting record.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Democrats believe Johnson\u8217\'20\'19s central role in refuting the 2020 election results and his conservative views on many social issues could help them win back the House next year.\par \par \uc2 \u8211\'20\'13 Chris Stein, Joan E Greve, Maanvi Singh\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/oct/25/mike-johnson-republican-house-speaker-vote"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Republican Mike Johnson elected House speaker after weeks of chaos}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 10.28pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.33pm BST\par \par \uc2 Now that the House has a speaker, it\u8217\'20\'19s right onto business. Once the speaker is sworn in, the House will consider a resolution to stand with Israel.\par \par \uc2 The broad resolution affirms Israel\u8217\'20\'19s right to defend itself against \uc2 Hamas\uc2 . It also calls for sanctions and aid. It will be interesting to see how Johnson and other Republicans land on the issue.\par \par \uc2 Last month, Johnson was among 93 Republicans who supported an amendment to cut off military assistance to Ukraine, proposed by hard-right congressman \uc2 Matt Gaetz\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 9.52pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.13pm BST\par \par \uc2 The progressive advocacy organization Stand Up America has called Johnson\u8217\'20\'19s speakership \u8220\'20\'1Ca threat to our democracy \u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Following Johnson\u8217\'20\'19s win, Stand Up America\u8217\'20\'19s founder and president Sean Eldridge said:\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CToday is a dark day for American democracy. Mike Johnson\u8217\'20\'19s record of election denial and his attempts to overturn the will of the people make him totally unfit to be second in line to the presidency. Those who have spent years trying to undermine our democracy cannot be trusted to lead it.\par \par \uc2 Entrusting the House of Representatives to a man the \uc2 New York Times\uc2  called \u8216\'20\'18 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://click.agilitypr.delivery/ls/click?upn=DgEyPVbrCGEPHBNWwTp0iQiwDG5KuQtLcwz-2FDdB7G-2F4XD4DBqvTmMoRHuTU2gmZY5SsNl7zIDFWxMIF8BG-2BE7e2FKSDCNWFiQrESGMnv6QSHaNQIvUgrfxDPk-2F61tdeHAI1n_YxCxpoge33FNHhRVcK23dztoAT9Kx65j-2FLzJh3gs46qWBHX491YTlrqXDe8-2FdwfcZMRSfTMenxOMJ6EQQJJmv6FEgn5H0jnReiSZLgmtVoaIgVEKsYXfJzkC-2F-2BnpHKnLSEzIOjmEgCGr0PNvPfADWLNRwY1VUsVrSQacoj-2B434RM98C0bTiglejsYl7MdfWKvJiV-2F8cVoAucAtd7MZ28hKNx33YYepxcwT5hH9uu9i5RjJM-2B4vH1C84UELyrJZbGco9JofXboHFN36fyYsmvkKImVGVt9dnEphZMtsxlvFJrzG32U-2Fom67jEbHKCRbdJ0U6PNcGfiusR1GLUUHCIfqKxBpOFhUhdpxxyA09ZxDLRdT6hcE53tnZsBiQzeTBEZE3mEyDPFgKBAioIncKhaNtj7hm-2F-2BiENiEanma-2BSeqCsmvQyOJplwGXd86Ls1WCAb2Xj-2BStB9lmUet4wP0pPhg-3D-3D"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the most important architect of the electoral college objections}}}\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19 is proof of House Republicans\u8217\'20\'19 contempt for our freedom to vote. The American people deserve a speaker who will stand up for our democracy and our fundamental freedoms, but sadly, House Republicans have embraced Maga extremism instead.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 9.53pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.01pm BST\par \par \uc2 The Democratic Women\u8217\'20\'19s Caucus has also condemned Mike Johnson\u8217\'20\'19s win, citing his history of supporting legislation that targeted women\u8217\'20\'19s rights including the 2022 \uc2 US supreme court\uc2  overturning of Roe v Wade.\par \par \uc2 House Republicans\u8217\'20\'19 new speaker of the House, Rep. Mike Johnson, is a MAGA extremist through and through. While Democrats have worked to lower costs for working women, Mike Johnson has opposed efforts to make child care more affordable, and wants to cut Medicare and Social Security and ban \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  nationwide,\u8221\'20\'1D the caucus said.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe Democratic Women\u8217\'20\'19s Caucus unanimously voted no \u8211\'20\'13 because a vote for speaker Johnson was a vote against women,\u8221\'20\'1D it added.\par \par \uc2 Johnson has previously voted against the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://clerk.house.gov/evs/2021/roll143.xml"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Pregnant Workers Fairness Act }}}\uc2  and the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://clerk.house.gov/Votes/2021331"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Pump for Nursing Mothers Act}}}\uc2 , bipartisan legislations that offered to give expecting and new mothers increased workplace protections.\par \par \uc2 He also voted against bipartisan legislation to protect victims of sexual assault and harassment, including the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://clerk.house.gov/Votes/2022480"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Speak Out Act }}}\uc2  and the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://clerk.house.gov/Votes/202233"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Ending Forced Arbitration of Sexual Assault and Sexual Harrassment Act}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 9.54pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.43pm BST\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 Human Rights Campaign\uc2 , the country\u8217\'20\'19s largest LGBTQ+ advocacy group, has condemned Mike Johnson\u8217\'20\'19s new House speakership position.\par \par \uc2 In a statement released on Wednesday, the president of \uc2 HRC\uc2 , Kelley Robinson, said:\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe Maga House majority has selected the most anti-equality speaker in US history by elevating Mike Johnson \u8211\'20\'13 this is a choice that will be a stain on the record of everyone who voted for him.\par \par \uc2 Johnson is someone who doesn\u8217\'20\'19t hesitate to express his disdain for the LGTBQ+ community from the rooftops and then introduces legislation that seeks to erase us from society. Just like Jim Jordan, Mike Johnson is an election-denying, anti-LGBTQ+ extremist, and the lawmakers who appeared to stand on principle in opposing Jordan\u8217\'20\'19s bid have revealed themselves to be just as out-of-touch as their new leader.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 8.45pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.21pm BST\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  on Mike Johnson's House speaker win: 'This is a time for all of us to act responsibly'\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  has congratulated Mike Johnson on becoming the House\u8217\'20\'19s newest speaker and called for lawmakers across the aisle to move quickly to address national security needs.\par \par \uc2 In a statement released on Wednesday, Biden said:\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CJill and I congratulate Speaker Johnson on his election.\par \par \uc2 As I said when this process began, whoever the Speaker is, I will seek to work with them in good faith on behalf of the American people \u8230\'20\'26\par \par \uc2 We need to move swiftly to address our national security needs and to avoid a shutdown in 22 days.\par \par \uc2 Even though we have real disagreements about important issues, there should be mutual effort to find common ground wherever we can.\par \par \uc2 This is a time for all of us to act responsibly, and to put the good of the American people and the everyday priorities of American families above any partisanship.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 8.44pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.07pm BST\par \par \uc2 In other news, Minnesota representative \uc2 Dean Phillips\uc2  is expected to launch a 2024 Democratic presidential primary challenge against \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Phillips, 54, will reportedly launch his campaign on Friday, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.foxnews.com/politics/rep-dean-phillips-to-launch-2024-democratic-primary-challenge-against-biden"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Fox News reported}}}\uc2 , citing people familiar with his campaign.\par \par \uc2 From there, Phillips will travel to New Hampshire and file his name for the state\u8217\'20\'19s primary ballot.\par \par \uc2 Several Democrats have discouraged Phillips from running, in response to the expected announcement.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CHe ought to go home to Minnesota,\u8221\'20\'1D Democratic senator Peter Welch {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.huffpost.com/entry/dean-phillips-joe-biden-2024_n_65382d10e4b011a9cf7b8250"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 said to the Huffington Post}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s a distraction and he\u8217\'20\'19s going to be hounding on the president not because of policies \u8211\'20\'13 the Democrats support the policies and accomplishments of Biden \u8211\'20\'13 so he\u8217\'20\'19s going to try to unravel that. It\u8217\'20\'19s not helpful,\u8221\'20\'1D Welch added.\par \par \uc2 The Massachusetts senator Elizabeth Warren told the Post that she also disapproves of Phillips\u8217\'20\'19s run.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt just doesn\u8217\'20\'19t make sense,\u8221\'20\'1D Warren said to the Post. \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19m all for President Biden getting re-elected. He has delivered for America\u8217\'20\'19s middle class and he\u8217\'20\'19s going to win.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Despite the ire, Phillips\u8217\'20\'19s campaign seems all the ready to launch. A tour bus for \uc2 Dean Phillips\uc2  was spotted in Ohio, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cbsnews.com/minnesota/news/dean-phillips-for-president-bus-spotted-in-ohio/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 CBS News reported}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The bus reading, \u8220\'20\'1C\uc2 Dean Phillips\uc2  For President\u8221\'20\'1D, was seen driving through Ohio on Tuesday, presumably headed towards New Hampshire. The bus also featured Phillips\u8217\'20\'19s slogan: \u8220\'20\'1CMake America Affordable Again\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 8.10pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.50pm BST\par \par \uc2 Johnson is now delivering remarks in his first speech to the House after being elected as the 56th House speaker on Wednesday.\par \par \uc2 After walking up to the podium, Johnson and the House minority leader, \uc2 Hakeem Jeffries\uc2 , hugged as Jeffries handed Johnson the House speaker gavel.\par \par \uc2 During his speech, Johnson vowed to decentralize power in the House and have members more involved in the process, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://thehill.com/homenews/house/4274127-house-republicans-speaker-mike-johnson-live-coverage/#97800"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the Hill reported}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe owe that to the people,\u8221\'20\'1D he said.\par \par \uc2 Johnson has also said that the first bill he will bring to the floor on Wednesday is a resolution in support of Israel.\par \par \uc2 From Punchbowl News\u8217\'20\'19 Mica Soellner:\par \par \uc2 enltrJOHNSON said the first bill he plans to bring the floor as speaker today is a pro-Israel resolution later today.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Mica Soellner (@MicaSoellnerDC) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/MicaSoellnerDC/status/1717248723221119214?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 October 25, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 7.53pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.22pm BST\par \par \uc2 More reactions are pouring in after Mike Johnson becomes the 56th House speaker, following weeks of House electoral chaos.\par \par \uc2 The Congressional Integrity Project (CIP), a liberal activist group, said those who supported Johnson \u8220\'20\'1Cvoted For Election Denial and Radical Extremism\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CAll of the House Republicans who supported Mike Johnson for Speaker voted for election denial, a national \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban, and gutting Social Security and Medicare,\u8221\'20\'1D CIP said in a statement.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CJohnson will use the Speaker\u8217\'20\'19s power to continue to undermine our democracy, restore Trump to power, and pursue a Maga Republican agenda that throws working families under the bus,\u8221\'20\'1D the group said.\par \par \uc2 CIP was {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.politico.com/news/2022/11/16/democratic-strategists-launch-war-room-00065498"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 relaunched by Democrats in 2022}}}\uc2  as a counterpoint to House Republicans, particularly following the January 6 insurrection and the belief in the Republican party that the 2020 election results were falsified.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 7.25pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.09pm BST\par \par \uc2 Mike Johnson has published a statement to social media following his win as the House\u8217\'20\'19s newest speaker.\par \par \uc2 In a statement posted to X, Johnson acknowledged the \u8220\'20\'1Carduous\u8221\'20\'1D House speaker election process that has dominated the Republican party for weeks.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt has been an arduous few weeks, and a reminder that the House is as complicated and diverse as the people we represent,\u8221\'20\'1D Johnson said.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe urgency of this moment demands bold, decisive action to restore trust, advance our legislative priorities, and demonstrate good governance,\u8221\'20\'1D he said.\par \par \uc2 Johnson further said that, as House speaker, he will work to restore \u8220\'20\'1Ctrust\u8221\'20\'1D in the House and \u8220\'20\'1Csanity\u8221\'20\'1D within the government more broadly.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe will restore trust in this body. We will advance a comprehensive conservative policy agenda, combat the harmful policies of the Biden Administration, and support our allies abroad,\u8221\'20\'1D Johnson added.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CAnd we will restore sanity to a government desperately in need of it. Let\u8217\'20\'19s get back to work,\u8221\'20\'1D he said.\par \par \uc2 enltrIt is the honor of a lifetime to have been elected the 56th Speaker of the House.\par \par \uc2 Thank you to my colleagues, friends, staff, and family for the unmatched support throughout this process.\par \par \uc2 It has been an arduous few weeks, and a reminder that the House is as complicated and\u8230\'20\'26\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Rep. Mike Johnson (@RepMikeJohnson) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/RepMikeJohnson/status/1717239282795000280?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 October 25, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.59pm BST\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 Republican National Committee\uc2  has congratulated Mike Johnson as the House\u8217\'20\'19s newest speaker.\par \par \uc2 In a statement released following the House vote, \uc2 RNC\uc2  chairwoman \uc2 Ronna McDaniel\uc2  said:\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CCongratulations to the new speaker of the House, Mike Johnson! In eight months, the Republican House majority passed bills to lower energy costs, secure the border, defend parents\u8217\'20\'19 rights, improve public safety, and more. When Republicans come together, we deliver results, and that\u8217\'20\'19s what we need to showcase ahead of 2024. We delivered this majority to bring solutions to the American people. It\u8217\'20\'19s time for Republicans to unite behind speaker Johnson and get back to work.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 7.01pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.54pm BST\par \par \uc2 Mike Johnson wins House vote to become next speaker\par \par \uc2 House Republicans have voted for Mike Johnson to be the newest speaker.\par \par \uc2 The vote came out to 220-209 with every House Republican voting for him.\par \par \uc2 The vote marks a breakthrough in a three-week limbo after House Republicans voted to oust Kevin McCarthy from the seat earlier this month.\par \par \uc2 Following the vote, House Republicans erupted into cheers and applause as the Louisiana representative was elevated to one of the highest offices in the \uc2 US government\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 7.33pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.42pm BST\par \par \uc2 Steve Scalise, once a top contender of the House speaker race only to then drop out, has voted for Mike Johnson.\par \par \uc2 As with Kevin McCarthy and \uc2 Patrick McHenry\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s votes for Johnson, Republicans stood up and applauded the Louisiana Republican for his vote.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 6.44pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.36pm BST\par \par \uc2 Patrick McHenry\uc2 , the House speaker pro tempore, has cast his vote for Mike Johnson as the next House speaker.\par \par \uc2 Republicans stood and applauded the North Carolina Republican representative.\par \par \uc2 enltrSpeaker Pro Temp \uc2 Patrick McHenry\uc2  from the chair votes for Mike Johnson for Speaker. Republicans stand and applaud. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/40Hd2Lu5n1"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/40Hd2Lu5n1}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Craig Caplan (@CraigCaplan) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/CraigCaplan/status/1717233032200180005?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 October 25, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.32pm BST\par \par \uc2 Former House speaker Kevin McCarthy has voted for Mike Johnson as the next House speaker.\par \par \uc2 In response, House Republicans stood up around him and clapped.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.29pm BST\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 Democratic National Committee\uc2  has criticized Mike Johnson\u8217\'20\'19s House speaker nomination, calling the Louisiana representative the \u8220\'20\'1Cnew Maga speaker-designate \u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 In a statement released on Wednesday, a DNC spokesperson, Sarafina Chitika said:\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CMany Americans are waking up this morning wondering \u8211\'20\'13 who is Mike Johnson? We\u8217\'20\'19re here to help: Maga Republicans\u8217\'20\'19 new speaker-designate supports extreme nationwide \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  bans. He led the charge for \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  denying president Biden\u8217\'20\'19s legitimate election win and tried to overthrow the votes of 81 million Americans.\par \par \uc2 He\u8217\'20\'19s a leading proponent of slashing Social Security and Medicare. Mike Johnson is a carbon-copy of the Maga extremism that is deeply unpopular with Americans across the country. House Republicans will have to answer for their support for their new Maga speaker next November. Make no mistake: the American people will hold them accountable for this choice.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 6.31pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.20pm BST\par \par \uc2 The Minnesota Democratic representative \uc2 Angie Craig\uc2  voiced her vote for \uc2 Hakeem Jeffries\uc2  by saying, \u8220\'20\'1CHappy wedding anniversary to my wife \u8211\'20\'13 \uc2 Hakeem Jeffries\uc2 !\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Democrats stood up and applauded Craig, the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://lgbthistorymonth.com/sites/default/files/icon_multimedia_pdfs/2020/Craig-LGBTHM2020-Bio%203.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 first }}}\uc2  openly lesbian mother elected to Congress and first openly gay person elected to Congress from Minnesota.\par \par \uc2 Mike Johnson, the Republican speaker nominee, has been a long-standing opponent of same-sex marriages.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 6.25pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.09pm BST\par \par \uc2 House vote under way for Mike Johnson as speaker\par \par \uc2 The House has started voting in the first ballot on Mike Johnson\u8217\'20\'19s speakership nomination.\par \par \uc2 This marks the fourth round of voting in the House for a new speaker.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 6.13pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.55pm BST\par \par \uc2 Punchbowl News reports that for the first time, there was unanimous applause for a House speaker candidate on the GOP side.\par \par \uc2 enltrFor the first time, unanimous applause for a speaker candidate on the GOP side.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Jake Sherman (@JakeSherman) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/JakeSherman/status/1717222732247548168?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 October 25, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 Today\u8217\'20\'19s House attendance is 429. That means 215 votes are required for Johnson to win the gavel if everyone votes for a person by name, Punchbowl News reports.\par \par \uc2 enltrHOUSE ATTENDANCE TODAY: 429\par \par \uc2 215 for Johnson to win, if everyone votes for a person by name\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Jake Sherman (@JakeSherman) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/JakeSherman/status/1717222091223621771?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 October 25, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 6.02pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.47pm BST\par \par \uc2 Ahead of a floor vote on Mike Johnson\u8217\'20\'19s candidacy to be the next speaker of the House, the House Democratic leader, \uc2 Hakeem Jeffries\uc2 , warned that Republicans were poised to elevate a political extremist who voted to overturn the US election and supports a nationwide ban on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 During an interview at a conference hosted by the left-leaning Washington thinktank, \uc2 Center for American Progress\uc2 , Jeffries said Johnson \u8220\'20\'1Chas a very pleasant demeanor in terms of how he communicates, but his voting record is as extreme as the most extreme members of their conference, with very few exceptions\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 He added: \u8220\'20\'1CMike Johnson, probably more so than almost any other member of the House Republican conference, wants to criminalize \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  care and impose a nationwide ban.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Jeffries said his caucus would \u8220\'20\'1Cforcefully push back\u8221\'20\'1D on Republican \u8220\'20\'1Cextremism\u8221\'20\'1D. He also called on the would-be speaker to bring legislation to the floor that would secure additional aid for both Ukraine and Israel, rather than split the bills to appease what Jeffries called the \u8220\'20\'1Cpro-Putin caucus\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 In the friendly interview, the MSNBC host Ari Melber pressed Jeffries: \u8220\'20\'1CIt sort of sounds like you\u8217\'20\'19re saying Congressman Johnson is just a less stylistically annoying Jim Jordan?\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1COne could say that,\u8221\'20\'1D Jeffries said to laughs in the audience.\par \par \uc2 But the Democratic leader added that Johnson, more so than Republicans\u8217\'20\'19 previous candidates for speaker, has a working relationship with members of the House judiciary committee that could be the foundation for bipartisan work. He also noted Johnson\u8217\'20\'19s vote for two Trump-era bills that won broad bipartisan support: the US-Mexico-Canada trade agreement and on a criminal justice overhaul bill.\par \par \uc2 Still, Jeffries has no intention of backing Johnson to be speaker. Before heading back to Capitol Hill to vote, he vowed: \u8220\'20\'1CLater on today, we\u8217\'20\'19ll make clear that we will continue to forcefully push back against that extremism and lay out what the stakes are for the American people.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 5.50pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.30pm BST\par \par \uc2 The former New Jersey governor and 2024 Republican presidential candidate \uc2 Chris Christie\uc2  said that he thinks Mike Johnson is the \u8220\'20\'1Clucky beneficiary of [Republicans\u8217\'20\'19] exhaustion and their embarassment \u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 In response to a question on whether he thinks House Republicans will have to make some sort of compromise with Democrats to elect a speaker if Johnson is unable to secure the necessary votes, Christie said;\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI don\u8217\'20\'19t know \u8230\'20\'26 They seemed pretty unified last night. I think they\u8217\'20\'19ve all been beaten into submission and it appears Mike Johnson turns out to be the lucky beneficiary of their exhaustion and their embarrassment. If it doesn\u8217\'20\'19t happen today, then I\u8217\'20\'19m a total loss as to what they do next.\par \par \uc2 Folks in that caucus are going to have to have a reckoning now. Mike Johnson, if he wins, I hope understands that he is the definition of a compromise candidate and that he needs to act in the way that represents the interest of everybody in the caucus, not just one group in particular.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 enltr\u8220\'20\'1CI think they\u8217\'20\'19ve all been beaten into submission and it appears Mike Johnson turns out to be the lucky beneficiary of their exhaustion and their embarrassment.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 2024 GOP presidential candidate \uc2 Chris Christie\uc2  in New Hampshire weighs in on the GOP House Speaker race {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/VwgQQwLfOY"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/VwgQQwLfOY}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 The Recount (@therecount) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/therecount/status/1717202833508835392?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 October 25, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 5.34pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.13pm BST\par \par \uc2 Mike Johnson says he believes he will win 'on the first vote'\par \par \uc2 Mike Johnson said that he will win \u8220\'20\'1Con the first vote \u8221\'20\'1D, CNN\u8217\'20\'19s Manu Raju reports.\par \par \uc2 enltrMike Johnson told {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/AnnieGrayerCNN?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @AnnieGrayerCNN}}}\uc2  that he will win "on the first vote."\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Manu Raju (@mkraju) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/mkraju/status/1717211542813299127?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 October 25, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 Punchbowl News reports that the House is moving into a quorum call.\par \par \uc2 enltrThe House is now moving into a quorum call.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Jake Sherman (@JakeSherman) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/JakeSherman/status/1717210813381869702?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 October 25, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 5.56pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.04pm BST\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  throws support behind Mike Johnson: 'He's respected by all'\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  has hailed Mike Johnson as the House speaker nominee, saying:\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI think Mike Johnson is doing very well. He\u8217\'20\'19s a tremendous congressman, respected by everybody. I hear it looks like it\u8217\'20\'19s really good. I haven\u8217\'20\'19t had one negative comment about him. Everybody likes him. He\u8217\'20\'19s respected by all.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 enltr\u8220\'20\'1CI think Mike Johnson is doing very well. He's a tremendous congressman, respected by everybody. I hear it looks like it\u8217\'20\'19s really good. I haven\u8217\'20\'19t had one negative comment about him. Everybody likes him. He\u8217\'20\'19s respected by all.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Trump on House GOP's latest nominee for Speaker {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/rZA5dOiZ56"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/rZA5dOiZ56}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 The Recount (@therecount) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/therecount/status/1717184130239054064?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 October 25, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 5.56pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.50pm BST\par \par \uc2 The Texas Republican representative Tony Gonzales hailed Mike Johnson\u8217\'20\'19s speakership nomination, tweeting on Wednesday:\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI look forward to working with him to help SECURE the southern border as OUR next Speaker of the US House.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 enltrMike Johnson and I both represent two of the poorest districts in the country, but the richest in the values held by the great people of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/hashtag/TX23?src=hash&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 #TX23}}}\uc2  & {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/hashtag/LA04?src=hash&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 #LA04}}}\uc2 . I look forward to working with him to help SECURE the southern border as OUR next Speaker of the US House. ???? {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/WTvi6JpSvj"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/WTvi6JpSvj}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Tony Gonzales (@TonyGonzales4TX) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/TonyGonzales4TX/status/1717179239856799872?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 October 25, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 4.54pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.35pm BST\par \par \uc2 With the House set to convene at noon, House speaker nominee Mike Johnson has tweeted the following:\par \par \uc2 zxxltr {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/fZaHhBMliz"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/fZaHhBMliz}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Rep. Mike Johnson (@RepMikeJohnson) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/RepMikeJohnson/status/1717194879116148974?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 October 25, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 Johnson said he will pass the energy and water appropriations bill this week, Punchbowl News reports.\par \par \uc2 On Monday, Johnson laid out an ambitious House schedule surrounding bills which did not mention any aid to Israel or Ukraine.\par \par \uc2 enltrNEW -- MIKE JOHNSON, who is likely to win the speakership today, says he will pass the Energy and Water approps bill THIS WEEK {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/VqxCRS7UnE"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/VqxCRS7UnE}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Jake Sherman (@JakeSherman) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/JakeSherman/status/1717201849525194845?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 October 25, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.16pm BST\par \par \uc2 Democrats reportedly call Mike Johnson 'Jordan in a coat'\par \par \uc2 Punchbowl News is reporting some descriptions of Mike Johnson coming out of the Democrat whips meeting.\par \par \uc2 enltrSome interesting descriptions for speaker-designate Mike Johnson coming out of the Dem whips meeting:\par \par \uc2 -He's "Jordan in a coat"\par \par \uc2 -Johnson is "different waiter, same menu"\par \par \uc2 W {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/maxpcohen?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @maxpcohen}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Heather Caygle (@heatherscope) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/heatherscope/status/1717193896478802377?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 October 25, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 5.56pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.58pm BST\par \par \uc2 The Senate foreign relations committee has approved Jack Lew\u8217\'20\'19s nomination to serve as the US ambassador to Israel, Punchbowl News reports.\par \par \uc2 The Biden pick was approved with a 12-9 vote, with Kentucky\u8217\'20\'19s Republican senator \uc2 Rand Paul\uc2  voting alongside Democrats in support of Lew.\par \par \uc2 enltrNEWS \u8212\'20\'14 Senate Foreign Relations Committee approves Jack Lew\u8217\'20\'19s nomination to serve as U.S. ambassador to Israel, 12-9.\par \par \uc2 Sen. RAND PAUL (R-Ky.) joined all Dems in voting for Lew. All other Republicans voted against.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Andrew Desiderio (@AndrewDesiderio) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/AndrewDesiderio/status/1717186357431345370?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 October 25, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 4.00pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.41pm BST\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  has assured \uc2 Evan Gershkovich\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s family that the US will bring the detained Wall Street Journal reporter home from Russia.\par \par \uc2 The Guardian\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s Ramon Antonio Vargas reports:\par \par \uc2 As the Wall Street Journal\u8217\'20\'19s \uc2 Evan Gershkovich\uc2  prepared to spend his 32nd birthday on Thursday in a Moscow lockup, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/joebiden"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Joe Biden}}}\uc2  has assured the reporter\u8217\'20\'19s family that the White House will ultimately get him back to the US from Russia, the journalist\u8217\'20\'19s sister said.\par \par \uc2 Danielle Gershkovich remarked on Tuesday in an interview on {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://x.com/NEWSMAX/status/1716853848164250111?s=20"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Newsmax}}}\uc2  that the president \u8220\'20\'1Cpromised our family personally that he\u8217\'20\'19s going to get Evan home\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CHis friends and family \u8211\'20\'13 we just want him to get back to doing what he loves the most,\u8221\'20\'1D Danielle Gershkovich said in reference to her brother\u8217\'20\'19s reporting as she appeared on several cable news networks across the political spectrum. \u8220\'20\'1CEvan\u8217\'20\'19s not here yet \u8211\'20\'13 the job isn\u8217\'20\'19t done, and we\u8217\'20\'19re waiting to see him home.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Gershkovich in late March became the first American journalist to be held in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/russia"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Russia}}}\uc2  on spying charges since the end of the cold war. He was at the end of a work trip when he was detained in Ekaterinburg.\par \par \uc2 For the full story, click here:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/oct/25/evan-gershkovich-journalist-russia-biden-latest"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 US will bring detained journalist home from Russia, Biden assures family}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.26pm BST\par \par \uc2 Several House Republicans have told Punchbowl News that they think Mike Johnson could win the speakership on the first ballot today.\par \par \uc2 enltrSeveral House Republicans tell me they think Mike Johnson could win the speakership on the first ballot.\par \par \uc2 House gavels in at noon.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Jake Sherman (@JakeSherman) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/JakeSherman/status/1717183384659673597?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 October 25, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.10pm BST\par \par \uc2 Here are some images from the newswires last night following Mike Johnson\u8217\'20\'19s House speaker nomination:\par \par \uc2 Mike Johnson is applauded after receiving the Republican nomination for speaker of the House of Representatives at Capitol Hill, in Washington DC on 24 October. Photograph: Saul Loeb/AFP/Getty Images Mike Johnson is surrounded by fellow members after speaking to reporters after securing the nomination. Photograph: Jonathan Ernst/Reuters House Republicans bow their heads in prayer after electing Johnson their next nominee for House speaker. Photograph: Jonathan Ernst/Reuters Johnson speaks to reporters after securing the nomination for House speaker from the Republican conference. Photograph: Jonathan Ernst/Reuters\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.17pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.55pm BST\par \par \uc2 The Republican senator for Maine \uc2 Susan Collins\uc2  said she will \uc2 Google\uc2  who Mike Johnson is, CNN\u8217\'20\'19s Lauren Fox reports.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI asked \uc2 Susan Collins\uc2  what it would be like to work with Johnson on spending issues and she said she doesn\u8217\'20\'19t know him, but was going to \uc2 Google\uc2  him this morning,\u8221\'20\'1D Fox tweeted on Wednesday.\par \par \uc2 enltrI asked \uc2 Susan Collins\uc2  what it would be like to work with Johnson on spending issues and she said she doesn't know him, but was going to \uc2 Google\uc2  him this morning\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Lauren Fox (@FoxReports) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/FoxReports/status/1717169079071494175?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 October 25, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.57pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.41pm BST\par \par \uc2 Nearly one in four Americans believe that political violence is justified to \u8220\'20\'1Csave\u8221\'20\'1D the country, a new report shows.\par \par \uc2 The Guardian\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s David Smith reports:\par \par \uc2 The 14th annual American Values Survey, carried out by the non-profit {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.prri.org/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Public Religion Research Institute}}}\uc2  (PRRI) in partnership with the \uc2 Brookings Institution\uc2  thinktank, offers a snapshot of America\u8217\'20\'19s deepening polarisation and willingness to contemplate taking up arms.\par \par \uc2 Even as \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  has sought to lower the temperature, support for political violence has increased over the past two years, the survey shows. Today about 23% of Americans agree that \u8220\'20\'1Cbecause things have gotten so far off track, true American patriots may have to resort to violence in order to save our country\u8221\'20\'1D \u8211\'20\'13 up from 15% in 2021.\par \par \uc2 The PRRI has asked this question in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/nov/01/republicans-violence-save-us-poll"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 eight separate surveys}}}\uc2  since March 2021 but this is the first time that support for political violence has risen above 20% in the general population.\par \par \uc2 One in three Republicans believe that \u8220\'20\'1Ctrue American patriots\u8221\'20\'1D may have to resort to violence to save the country, compared with 22% of independents and 13% of Democrats \u8211\'20\'13 all representing increases since 2021. Almost one in three white evangelical Protestants believe that patriots may have to resort to political violence to save the country, markedly higher than any other religious group.\par \par \uc2 For the full story, click here:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/oct/25/us-political-violence-justified-survey"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Nearly one in four Americans believe political violence justified to \u8216\'20\'18save\u8217\'20\'19 US}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.26pm BST\par \par \uc2 The White House has cancelled its plans to have the American new wave band B-52s perform at Wednesday\u8217\'20\'19s state dinner for the Australian prime minister.\par \par \uc2 The Associated Press {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://apnews.com/article/biden-white-house-state-dinner-australia-3e689d8d95297d98847d1cd1fb3b0f50"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reports}}}\uc2  the first lady, Jill Biden, saying the performance would be inappropriate at a time when \u8220\'20\'1Cso many are facing sorrow and pain\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe made a few adjustments to the entertainment portion of the evening,\u8221\'20\'1D she said, without directly referring to the ongoing war between Israel and \uc2 Hamas\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CNurturing our partnerships and relationships with our allies is critically important, especially in these tumultuous times,\u8221\'20\'1D Jill Biden added. \u8220\'20\'1CFood is comforting, reassuring and healing, and we hope that this dinner provides a little of that as well.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Members of the band will instead be guests at the state dinner.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.30pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.14pm BST\par \par \uc2 House Republicans booed a reporter after she appeared to ask Mike Johnson, who {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/RepMikeJohnson/status/1336679860861886467?s=20"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 led}}}\uc2  an amicus brief that urged supreme court justices to overturn 2020 electoral votes from key swing states, about his involvement.\par \par \uc2 In response to the question, \u8220\'20\'1CYou help lead the effort to overturn the 2020 election results, do you\u8211\'20\'13,\u8221\'20\'1D a group of House Republicans standing behind Johnson immediately started booing, with one saying, \u8220\'20\'1CShut up!\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Johnson meanwhile shook his head, smiled and said, \u8220\'20\'1CNext question.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 enltrReporter: You help lead the effort to overturn the 2020 election results, do you\u8212\'20\'14\par \par \uc2 Republicans: *boo* shut up {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/L7R5fwhpIi"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/L7R5fwhpIi}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Acyn (@Acyn) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/Acyn/status/1717013355775545630?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 October 25, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.23pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.03pm BST\par \par \uc2 Mike Johnson: 'This House Republican majority is united'\par \par \uc2 Speaking about his nomination, Mike Johnson said, \u8220\'20\'1CThis is leadership\u8221\'20\'1D and maintained that the House Republican conference is united.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe\u8217\'20\'19re going to restore your trust in what we do here. You\u8217\'20\'19re going to see a new form of government and we\u8217\'20\'19re going to move this quickly. This group here is ready to govern and we\u8217\'20\'19re going to govern well,\u8221\'20\'1D said Johnson.\par \par \uc2 He added, \u8220\'20\'1CYou\u8217\'20\'19re going to see this group working like a well-oiled machine.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 enltrRep. Mike Johnson after being nominated for Speaker: \u8220\'20\'1CDemocracy is messy sometimes, but it is our system. This conference that you see, this House Republican majority, is united.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/4ycz7eSWZl"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/4ycz7eSWZl}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Benny Johnson (@bennyjohnson) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/bennyjohnson/status/1717013755958059374?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 October 25, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.11pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.54pm BST\par \par \uc2 Mike Johnson becomes latest nominee with support unclear\par \par \uc2 Good morning,\par \par \uc2 After weeks of political infighting and unsucesseful speaker nominations, the Louisiana Republican representative Mike Johnson has become the GOP\u8217\'20\'19s latest nominee for the House speaker\u8217\'20\'19s chair last night.\par \par \uc2 Johnson\u8217\'20\'19s nomination came just hours after \uc2 Tom Emmer\uc2 , a Minnesota representative, withdrew his speaker bid due to opposition from hard-right Republicans.\par \par \uc2 Johnson is now the fourth nominee to attempt to secure 217 votes needed to win the gavel, following Emmer, as well as Ohio\u8217\'20\'19s Jim Jordan and Louisiana\u8217\'20\'19s Steve Scalise.\par \par \uc2 Speaking to reporters following his nomination, Johnson {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=EIKgD2u46F0&ab_channel=AssociatedPress"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 said}}}\uc2  : \u8220\'20\'1CDemocracy is messy sometimes but it is our system \u8230\'20\'26 This House Republican majority is united.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 With no speaker since Republicans ousted Kevin McCarthy from the seat earlier this month, the House has been left in a limbo and unable to pass legislation needed to respond to the ongoing conflict in the Middle East and Ukraine.\par \par \uc2 With the House set to meet at noon, it remains to be seen whether Johnson will be able to overcome the political divisions that the previous candidates faced.\par \par \uc2 Here are other developments:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  and \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  will welcome the Australian prime minister, Anthony Albanese, and his partner, Jodie Haydon, to the White House today.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Mark Meadows\uc2 , Donald Tump\u8217\'20\'19s former White House chief of staff,{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/oct/24/trump-chief-of-staff-mark-meadows-2020-election-case-immunity"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 testified}}}\uc2  in the 2020 election case after being granted limited immunity.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Nearly one in four Americans believe political violence is justified to \u8220\'20\'1Csave\u8221\'20\'1D the country, according to a new {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/oct/25/us-political-violence-justified-survey"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 report}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.08pm BST\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020231025ejap001mm\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
