\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 First Thing: Biden condemns \uc2 Hamas\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s \u8216\'20\'18sheer evil\u8217\'20\'19 as Israeli death toll rises to 1,200\b0\par\par\uc2 Nicola Slawson \par \uc2 1,662 \uc2 words\par \uc2 11 October 2023\par 10:56 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 President says \uc2 Hamas\uc2  does not represent \u8216\'20\'18legitimate aspirations\u8217\'20\'19 of Palestinian people and says US \u8216\'20\'18stands with\u8217\'20\'19 Israel. Plus, the Chinese women shaking off taboos around divorceDon\u8217\'20\'19t already get First Thing in your inbox? Sign up here\par \par \uc2 Good morning.\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden has pledged {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/oct/10/biden-hamas-hostages-israel-gaza"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 unflinching support for Israel}}}\uc2 , calling the assault by \uc2 Hamas\uc2  that left nearly 1,000 people dead an \u8220\'20\'1Cact of sheer evil\u8221\'20\'1D, as reports emerge of a massacre at a kibbutz.\par \par \uc2 Yesterday, journalists were allowed into the Kfar Aza kibbutz, on the border with Gaza, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2023/oct/11/hamas-attack-kfar-aza-kibbutz-massacre-israel"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 where people were killed after Hamas broke through the border on Saturday}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CMothers, fathers, babies, young families killed in their beds, in the protection room, in the dining room, in their garden,\u8221\'20\'1D Maj Gen Itai Veruv, of the \uc2 Israel Defence Forces\uc2 , told the BBC as his troops searched homes for bodies of victims. \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s not a war, it\u8217\'20\'19s not a battlefield. It\u8217\'20\'19s a massacre.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Rampaging fighters armed with assault rifles, rocket-propelled grenades and hand grenades gunned down dozens of residents and mutilated some of the bodies, Veruv and other soldiers said.\par \par \uc2 In a televised speech from the White House, Biden said at least 14 Americans were killed in the weekend\u8217\'20\'19s attack by \uc2 Hamas\uc2 , the Palestinian group that controls Gaza, and an as yet unknown number of Americans were being held hostage.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 What\u8217\'20\'19s happening in Gaza? More than 900 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2023/oct/10/830-dead-in-gaza-since-saturday-as-shelling-hits-school-hospitals-and-homes"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 people in Gaza have been killed}}}\uc2  in retaliatory Israeli airstrikes, and Israel is enforcing a blockade that has sealed off the besieged territory of 2.3 million people from food, fuel and other supplies. Frightened residents of Gaza have described bombardments striking residential buildings, hospitals and schools, while humanitarian workers have said nowhere is safe.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 What has the US said about Gaza? The US is discussing the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2023/oct/11/gaza-attacks-hamas-israel-war-us-holds-talks-on-safe-passage-civilians"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 possibility of creating a safe passage for Gaza\u8217\'20\'19s civilians}}}\uc2  as Israel\u8217\'20\'19s air force continued to pound the enclave. The US national security adviser Jake Sullivan said on Tuesday that talks on safe passage were being held with Israel and Egypt.\par \par \uc2 Abortions in North Carolina drop by 30% in wake of new restrictions\par \par \uc2 Abortions in North Carolina {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2023/oct/10/abortion-ban-north-carolina-decrease"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 fell by more than 30%}}}\uc2  after the state enacted new \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  restrictions on 1 July, including a 12-week \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban, data released today by the \uc2 Guttmacher Institute\uc2  shows.\par \par \uc2 North Carolina \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  clinics performed more than 4,200 abortions in June and 2,920 abortions in July. Nearby states did not see a comparable surge in abortions, suggesting that patients denied abortions in North Carolina had to self-manage their own \u8211\'20\'13 or went without.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CHaving to turn away patients over and over again is truly just soul-crushing,\u8221\'20\'1D said Calla Hales, who runs A Preferred Women\u8217\'20\'19s Health Center, a network of clinics with two locations in North Carolina and two in Georgia, which has a six-week \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe\u8217\'20\'19re having to try our best to help patients but they\u8217\'20\'19re going through incredible financial and logistical difficulties to get here. And then there\u8217\'20\'19s the patients who just can\u8217\'20\'19t make it, or have to be turned away because they\u8217\'20\'19re just too far, or have some other condition that isn\u8217\'20\'19t compatible with doing a non-hospital \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 . It weighs a person down.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 What else does the new law say? The 12-week ban included a requirement that \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  patients show up for an in-person consultation at an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  clinic at least 72 hours before their \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 . That requirement was devastating for patients and providers, Hales said. It confused patients and left providers scrambling to schedule patients twice at already crowded clinics. This rule is a huge obstacle for out-of-state residents who either have to take two trips or find accommodation to stay multiple days.\par \par \uc2 Two US House Republicans make their bid for the speaker\u8217\'20\'19s gavel\par \par \uc2 The prominent Republican party members Steve Scalise and Jim Jordan made their pitches {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/oct/11/two-us-house-republicans-make-their-bid-for-the-speakers-gavel"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 for the powerful role of speaker of the US House of Representatives}}}\uc2  yesterday amid mounting pressure from a war in the Middle East and another looming government shutdown.\par \par \uc2 Lawmakers exiting a closed-door forum said neither Scalise, the House majority leader, nor Jordan, who chairs the judiciary committee, would have a clear advantage when Republicans begin to vote for a nominee by secret ballot on Wednesday. \u8220\'20\'1CWe\u8217\'20\'19ve got two good leaders within our party, with good perspectives on where the party needs to go and an understanding and an emphasis on reuniting the party,\u8221\'20\'1D Mike Garcia told reporters.\par \par \uc2 Before voting for a candidate today, Republicans will have to decide whether to keep internal disagreements behind closed doors by requiring any nominee to win 217 Republican votes, enough to elect the next speaker on the House floor over Democratic opposition. Current rules require only a simple majority.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe first order of business is figuring out a rules change that works for the conference,\u8221\'20\'1D said the congresswoman Kat Cammack.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 What does the Republicans\u8217\'20\'19 narrow majority mean for the vote? The narrowly divided caucus \u8211\'20\'13 Republicans hold a 221-212 majority in the House \u8211\'20\'13 raised some worries that neither candidate would be able to win enough support to be elected speaker in the first round of voting. In January this narrow majority made it possible for a fraction of their members to force Kevin McCarthy to endure 15 grueling floor votes to become speaker. He was ousted last week.\par \par \uc2 In other news \u8230\'20\'26\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Federal prosecutors added major allegations to the indictment charging the House Republican George Santos with fraud and lying about his campaign finance disclosures, presenting {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/oct/10/george-santos-indictment-stealing-fraud-credit-cards"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 evidence that he stole donors\u8217\'20\'19 identities}}}\uc2  and charged thousands of dollars to their credit cards without their knowledge.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The\par \par \uc2 supreme court is\par \par \uc2 to review whether the South Carolina map, which was redrawn by Republicans, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/oct/11/supreme-court-south-carolina-congressional-map-case"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 discriminated against Black voters}}}\uc2 . The court will hear the redistricting case after a panel ruled that Republicans had undertaken an \u8220\'20\'1Ceffective bleaching\u8221\'20\'1D in redrawing the state\u8217\'20\'19s seven congressional districts after the 2020 census.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Kari Lake, the Republican candidate who lost the race for Arizona governor but never conceded her loss, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/oct/10/kari-lake-senate-bid-arizona-announcement"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 announced a run for US Senate}}}\uc2  in the western state yesterday. A former TV news anchor, Lake made her move into politics by making repeated false claims about elections.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 California has become the first state to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/oct/10/california-police-brutality-excited-delirium-ban-cause-death-newsom"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 ban the use of \u8220\'20\'1Cexcited delirium\u8221\'20\'1D}}}\uc2  in recording a cause of death, prohibiting the pseudoscientific diagnosis that authorities have frequently cited to justify killings at the hands of law enforcement. Excited delirium suggests that people can develop superhuman strength due to drug use.\par \par \uc2 Stat of the day: Thousands bought \u8216\'20\'18golden passports\u8217\'20\'19 through Dominica\u8217\'20\'19s $1bn scheme\par \par \uc2 The Caribbean state of Dominica has sold citizenship to thousands of individuals including a former Afghan spymaster, a Turkish millionaire convicted of fraud and a former Libyan colonel under \uc2 Muammar Gaddafi\uc2 , the first detailed examination of the country\u8217\'20\'19s controversial \u8220\'20\'1Cgolden passports\u8221\'20\'1D scheme has found. The findings are from Dominica: Passports of the Caribbean, an investigation by the Guardian and 14 other international news organizations in partnership with the Organized Crime and Corruption Reporting Project (OCCRP). According to official declarations, Dominica\u8217\'20\'19s golden passports scheme \u8211\'20\'13 one of the world\u8217\'20\'19s biggest \u8211\'20\'13 has {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2023/oct/11/golden-passports-dominica-citizenship-by-investment-cbi-scheme"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 raised more than $1bn}}}\uc2  (\u163\'00\'A3822m) since 2009.\par \par \uc2 Don\u8217\'20\'19t miss this: \u8216\'20\'18Happy rebirth!\u8217\'20\'19 \u8211\'20\'13 Chinese women shake off taboos around divorce to celebrate freedom\par \par \uc2 In a karaoke room filled with balloons, confetti and cake, a 34-year-old woman dances with a dozen friends celebrating her \u8220\'20\'1Crebirth of the past\u8221\'20\'1D. The woman, who posts on Chinese social media under the name Sushi, had just ended her four-year marriage. Shaking off social stereotypes around divorce that suggest she should feel shame and failure, she decided to throw a party with all of her girlfriends. \u8220\'20\'1CIf I had known divorce would be so happy, I would have done it a long time ago!\u8221\'20\'1D she wrote on social media.\par \par \uc2 As the divorce rate in China rises and attitudes to separations change, divorce parties and inspiring content about the lives of newly single women are {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2023/oct/11/china-divorce-rate-rise"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 gaining thousands of likes}}}\uc2  on \uc2 Xiaohongshu\uc2 , a Chinese video-sharing social media app.\par \par \uc2 Climate check: Human emissions made deadly South American heat 100 times more likely\par \par \uc2 The deadly heat in central South America over the past two months was made {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/environment/2023/oct/10/human-emissions-made-deadly-south-american-heat-100-times-more-likely"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 100 times more likely by human emissions}}}\uc2  that disrupted the climate, scientists have shown. Temperatures have exceeded 40C in late winter and early spring in the southern hemisphere, affecting millions and leading to heat-related deaths. This year\u8217\'20\'19s El Ni\u241\'00\'F1o has been partly to blame, but a rapid study by researchers at World Weather Attribution revealed that the human-made climate crisis was by far the main cause of the unseasonable warmth. If global heating rises to 2C above pre-industrial levels, similar heatwaves will be expected every five or six years. The world has now heated by about 1.2C.\par \par \uc2 Last Thing: Female frogs appear to fake death to avoid unwanted advances, study shows\par \par \uc2 When it comes to avoiding unwanted male attention, researchers have found that some frogs take drastic action: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/science/2023/oct/11/female-frogs-fake-death-unwanted-advances-study"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 they appear to feign death}}}\uc2 . Researchers say the findings shed new light on the European common frog, suggesting females do not simply put up with the male scramble for mates \u8211\'20\'13 a situation in which several males can end up clinging to a female, sometimes fatally. \u8220\'20\'1CIt was previously thought that females were unable to choose or defend themselves against this male coercion,\u8221\'20\'1D said Dr Carolin Dittrich, the first author of the study from the Natural History Museum of Berlin. But the research suggests females are not passive as previously thought, she said.\par \par \uc2 Sign up\par \par \uc2 First Thing is delivered to thousands of inboxes every weekday. If you\u8217\'20\'19re not already signed up, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/info/2018/sep/17/guardian-us-morning-briefing-sign-up-to-stay-informed"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 subscribe now}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Get in touch\par \par \uc2 If you have any questions or comments about any of our newsletters, please email {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "mailto:newsletters@theguardian.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 newsletters@theguardian.com}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020231011ejab001h5\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
