\par\par \uc2 Global development\par \b \uc2 US Aids fund: What is the Pepfar fight and what does it mean for Africa?\b0\par\par\uc2 Joan van Dyk \par \uc2 1,114 \uc2 words\par \uc2 10 October 2023\par 15:35 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 The emergency plan for Aids relief has become caught up in the politics of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights, with far-reaching implications\par \par \uc2 What is Pepfar and why is it in the news?\par \par \uc2 Pepfar is an acronym for the US \u8220\'20\'1Cpresident\u8217\'20\'19s emergency plan for Aids relief\u8221\'20\'1D. It was set up {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.state.gov/pepfar-celebrates-20-years-of-unprecedented-global-impact-in-the-fight-to-end-hiv-aids/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 two decades ago}}}\uc2  by \uc2 George W Bush\uc2  to address the HIV epidemic.\par \par \uc2 It\u8217\'20\'19s the biggest government-run fund of its kind. Since 2003, the project has donated about {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://datawrapper.dwcdn.net/fB21b/2/#"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 $110bn (\u163\'00\'A390.5bn) }}}\uc2  to governments, universities and nonprofits in 50 countries, either directly or through agencies such as \uc2 USAid\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Until now Pepfar has been funded in five-year cycles. In the past the programme has had virtually unanimous support from Republicans and Democrats. But the next funding cycle (from 2023 to 2028) became ensnared in US \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  politics and the fallout contributed to Congress missing the 30 September deadline to allow another five-year funding cycle for the initiative.\par \par \uc2 What\u8217\'20\'19s the link between Pepfar and \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 ?\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.kff.org/global-health-policy/fact-sheet/the-u-s-government-and-international-family-planning-reproductive-health-statutory-requirements-and-policies/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 US laws}}}\uc2  already prevent Pepfar (or any state agencies) from paying for \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  services, according to the California-based policy research group, \uc2 Kaiser Family Foundation\uc2  (KFF). But in May, a coalition of conservative {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.heritage.org/budget-and-spending/report/reassessing-americas-30-billion-global-aids-relief-program"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 thinktanks}}}\uc2  and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.foxnews.com/politics/biden-administration-hijacking-george-bush-aids-program-to-push-abortion-in-africa-gop-rep"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 lawmakers}}}\uc2  began to make waves with arguments that \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s administration has \u8220\'20\'1Chijacked\u8221\'20\'1D Pepfar to promote \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  instead of treating and preventing HIV.\par \par \uc2 That\u8217\'20\'19s where the risk to Pepfar\u8217\'20\'19s five-year budget emerged \u8211\'20\'13 because the Republican lawmakers then refused to sign off on a spending bill for Pepfar if there weren\u8217\'20\'19t stricter rules in place to stop Pepfar funds from overlapping with \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  services in any way.\par \par \uc2 According to Brian Honermann, deputy director of public policy at the US-based \uc2 Foundation for Aids Research\uc2 , the allegations that Pepfar has been usurped to push a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.heritage.org/budget-and-spending/report/reassessing-americas-30-billion-global-aids-relief-program"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1Cradical social agenda}}}\uc2  \u8221\'20\'1D overseas are \u8220\'20\'1Cbaseless\u8221\'20\'1D and \u8220\'20\'1Cstitched together from unrelated policy speeches, documents and assertions about how those apply to Pepfar\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 What will happen to Pepfar now?\par \par \uc2 The multibillion-dollar health programme is a permanent part of US law. That means Pepfar funding will continue, but it will lose its favoured position of receiving five years of funding at a time.\par \par \uc2 The failure to reauthorise Pepfar will mean some of its built-in rules will expire, including a guideline that requires 10% of Pepfar money to go to orphans and children in need.\par \par \uc2 Will organisations and governments lose their Pepfar grants?\par \par \uc2 The fund has enough money to pay governments and civil society organisations until September 2024 (about {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://datawrapper.dwcdn.net/fB21b/2/#"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 $6.8bn}}}\uc2  ), but a state department spokesperson warns that Pepfar won\u8217\'20\'19t escape unscathed in the long term.\par \par \uc2 Moreover, getting funding for only one year at a time will make it harder for Pepfar to plan ahead and to source crucial HIV tools, such as condoms or medicine, at the best prices. This could ultimately imperil the people that rely on the fund\u8217\'20\'19s support, the spokesperson warned.\par \par \uc2 The symbolic power of a five-year commitment will also be lost, says Honermann. \u8220\'20\'1CIt shows partner countries that the US is invested for a significant period of time and that Pepfar won\u8217\'20\'19t just disappear.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The threat of a permanent \u8216\'20\'18gag rule\u8217\'20\'19\par \par \uc2 Another factor has swirled around Pepfar\u8217\'20\'19s funding drama: some lawmakers have said they\u8217\'20\'19ll only agree to restart the five-year funding regime if the fund is once again subject to the \u8220\'20\'1CMexico City policy\u8221\'20\'1D, also called the \u8220\'20\'1C {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.kff.org/global-health-policy/fact-sheet/mexico-city-policy-explainer/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 gag rule}}}\uc2  \u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 The gag rule bans organisations and governments from providing or promoting termination of pregnancy services regardless of whose money they\u8217\'20\'19re using to do it. It was expanded to apply to Pepfar for the first time in 2017. It is only ever enforced when there\u8217\'20\'19s a Republican president in the White House, so is not currently in effect.\par \par \uc2 And while there is no finalised legislation that would make a permanent gag rule a reality (and Honermann argues it would be unlikely to get past the Democrats), the threat of it may already have done some damage.\par \par \uc2 Research conducted by {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://fosfeminista.org/wp-content/uploads/2023/06/The-Global-Impact-of-the-Dobbs_Preliminary-Findings-Fact-Sheet-1.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 F\u242\'00\'F2s Feminista}}}\uc2 , a global alliance that advocates for sexual and reproductive rights, found that the 2022 decision to roll back the national right to an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the US had a contagious impact in a number of countries. In Nigeria, for instance, respondents told {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://fosfeminista.org/wp-content/uploads/2023/06/The-Global-Impact-of-the-Dobbs_Preliminary-Findings-Fact-Sheet-1.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 F\u242\'00\'F2s Feminista}}}\uc2  that local lawmakers were using the change in US \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  laws to push back on a more liberal law in their country. Terminations are {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.guttmacher.org/fact-sheet/abortion-nigeria"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 legal in Nigeria only }}}\uc2  if carrying the foetus to term threatens the mother\u8217\'20\'19s life.\par \par \uc2 Recipients of \uc2 US government\uc2  funding are often so worried about losing it that they enforce \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  laws more harshly than is necessary. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://fosfeminista.org/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Research}}}\uc2  shows that confusion about whether the gag rule had been revoked at the start of the Biden administration resulted in the policy \u8211\'20\'13 and its harms \u8211\'20\'13 being in place for much longer in practice.\par \par \uc2 And the Pepfar wrangling and attendant media coverage has already resulted in mixed messages reaching health advocates in Africa. Some South African activists told the Guardian they were concerned that the news would be calamitous for civil society in the country. Such organisations receive the most Pepfar dollars (44%) in South Africa {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://copsdata.amfar.org/s/South%20Africa"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 according to 2020 tracking data.}}}\uc2  The government gets just under 1.5% of the money.\par \par \uc2 Honermann says that there is an intentional political strategy to keep communication about the changes in restrictions vague. \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s a way to encourage over-enforcement for fear of falling on the wrong side of this.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 He adds: \u8220\'20\'1CFor now, Pepfar will continue as long as funding is made available. But these political threats to the programme are ultimately playing with the lives of millions of people worldwide who rely on this programme.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 What has the reaction been in Africa?\par \par \uc2 Dave Clark is the chief operating officer at the Aurum Institute, a non-profit that works on HIV and tuberculosis (TB) projects in South Africa, Mozambique, Ghana, Lesotho and Eswatini.\par \par \uc2 Aurum is a partner for Pepfar\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.usaid.gov/global-health/health-areas/hiv-and-aids/technical-areas/dreams"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Dreams}}}\uc2  project which works towards an Aids-free future for girls and women aged 10 to 24 by providing HIV services, contraception and violence prevention support for women, adolescents and their sexual partners.\par \par \uc2 One of the major strengths of Pepfar, Clark says, is that it\u8217\'20\'19s a sure-fire source of carefully planned funding for global health in a world that is often more talk than action.\par \par \uc2 He explains: \u8220\'20\'1CThe debate in America should not throw us off saving lives. Pepfar is what it says on the label: president\u8217\'20\'19s emergency plan for Aids relief. That\u8217\'20\'19s its extraordinary power and legacy.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020231006eja6001bm\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
