\par\par \uc2 Global development\par \b \uc2 \u8216\'20\'18We are fighting for the girls who come after us\u8217\'20\'19:  \highlight22\uc2 abortion \highlight\uc2  rights at risk in Argentina election\b0\par\par\uc2 Harriet Barber in Buenos Aires \par \uc2 812 \uc2 words\par \uc2 9 October 2023\par 15:43 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Argentina\u8217\'20\'19s presidential frontrunner, Javier Milei, is threatening to outlaw the \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights only won three years ago\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe are fighting against the presidential candidates who threaten the rights of women,\u8221\'20\'1D says Marilyna, 28, standing hand in hand with her friend outside Argentina\u8217\'20\'19s National Congress last Thursday evening.\par \par \uc2 Argentina is three weeks away from a national election in which the rights of women and \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  have been put on the ballot, just three years after elective terminations were legalised. Marilyna is one of thousands of women, men and children protesting on the streets of Buenos Aires.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe are afraid of the \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  referendum proposal and of the destructive policies that are being suggested in this election campaign. But we are fighting,\u8221\'20\'1D she says.\par \par \uc2 Behind her, elderly women wave green handkerchiefs, teenagers set off purple flares, and mothers march to the beat of steel drums with toddlers strapped to their backs.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  was {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2020/dec/30/argentina-legalises-abortion-in-landmark-moment-for-womens-rights"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 legalised in Argentina in 2020}}}\uc2  after sweeping protests known as the \u8220\'20\'1C {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/global-development/2020/dec/09/argentina-legalize-abortion-bill-congress-vote"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 green wave\u8221\'20\'1D movement}}}\uc2 . Previously, abortions were only permitted in cases of rape or if the woman\u8217\'20\'19s health was at risk.\par \par \uc2 But now women fear that those hard-won rights could be under threat.\par \par \uc2 On 22 October, the country heads to the polls in a highly contested election, in which the frontrunner Javier Milei has described \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  as murder.\par \par \uc2 In a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://buenosairesherald.com/politics/milei-says-hed-do-a-referendum-on-abortion-law-if-elected-president#:~:text=Abortion%20is%20legal%20in%20Argentina%20for%20pregnancies%20of%20up%20to%2014%20weeks&text=Libertarian%20presidential%20candidate%20Javier%20Milei,to%20keep%20it%20or%20not."}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 recent interview}}}\uc2 , Milei, a 52-year-old far-right candidate and political outsider, reportedly said that those who support \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights are \u8220\'20\'1Cbrainwashed by a homicidal policy\u8221\'20\'1D. He vowed to launch a referendum to overturn the \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  law if he takes the presidency.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CLife starts at the moment of fertilisation. Three weeks after that, your mother decides to kill you because you are not alive yet. How come?\u8221\'20\'1D Milei said in August.\par \par \uc2 The former economist and TV pundit has also pledged to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://en.mercopress.com/2022/05/19/gomez-alcorta-talks-back-at-milei-s-promise-to-shut-down-women-s-ministry"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 close the Ministry for Women, Gender and Diversity}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Partly in response to such rhetoric, the Ni Una Menos feminist movement organised protests across the South American country on {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.who.int/news-room/events/detail/2023/09/28/default-calendar/international-safe-abortion-day"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 International Safe \b  \highlight22Abortion\b0 \highlight22  Day}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Among those who gathered in the capital was 69-year-old Sandra Olue.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe are here because we want to preserve the rights of women and \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 ,\u8221\'20\'1D Olue says. \u8220\'20\'1CWe fought for a long time, and are afraid this potential new president might cut our rights. We will not allow it.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Cecilia Benitez marched holding her six-year-old daughter on her hip. \u8220\'20\'1CThe far right is organising itself in Latin America, specifically Javier Milei and his henchmen, who are trying to undo our laws,\u8221\'20\'1D she says.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CHe is organising his force like Donald Trump, and, like Trump, his proposals go against us, against women and LGBT people.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The government {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.batimes.com.ar/news/argentina/a-year-on-from-passage-of-argentinas-abortion-law-change-remains-slow.phtml"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 estimates}}}\uc2  that 3,000 women died between 1983 and 2020, before the legalisation, due to clandestine abortions. Officials {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/world-latin-america-64784660"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 have said}}}\uc2  that maternal deaths have decreased by more than 40% since the law was enacted.\par \par \uc2 Despite such progress, \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  remains a fraught and divisive issue in the majority Roman Catholic country, even among health workers.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThere is still a lot of resistance to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 ,\u8221\'20\'1D says Soledad Deza, a lawyer and president of women\u8217\'20\'19s group Fundaci\u243\'00\'F3n Mujeres x Mujeres. \u8220\'20\'1CThere are entire public and private institutions that do not guarantee abortions because all their staff are objectors.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThen there is \u8216\'20\'18covert\u8217\'20\'19 conscientious objection, which is perhaps more dangerous. Health personnel, instead of openly denying the service, mask it and carry out more harmful actions: they provide false information, and provide medication in insufficient doses.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Doctors who perform abortions have also reportedly been targeted with {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://amnistia.org.ar/sobreseyeron-a-miranda-ruiz-la-medica-injustamente-criminalizada-por-haber-garantizado-un-aborto-legal-en-salta-dara-una-conferencia-de-prensa/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 spurious legal complaints}}}\uc2 . In August 2021, one doctor in Salta, a city in north-western Argentina, was detained following an accusation that she had performed an \u8220\'20\'1Cillegal \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 \u8221\'20\'1D. She faced almost two years of criminal proceedings before she was acquitted.\par \par \uc2 Mexico\u8217\'20\'19s supreme court {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2023/sep/06/mexico-decriminalizes-abortion"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 recently ruled}}}\uc2  that state laws prohibiting \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  are unconstitutional and violate women\u8217\'20\'19s rights, but despite the region\u8217\'20\'19s green wave movement, the only other Latin American countries where elective \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  is legal are Colombia, Cuba, Guyana and Uruguay. In neighbouring Brazil, the supreme court is currently voting on whether to decriminalise \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the first 12 weeks of a pregnancy.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWomen\u8217\'20\'19s rights have never been fully accepted in Latin America. There is a very strong presence of religions in public spaces and a very powerful network of political neoconservatism,\u8221\'20\'1D says Diaz. \u8220\'20\'1CThe green wave does not stop, because we have to fight for our rights and defend them all the time.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CPeople gave their lives for these rights and we have to defend against a terrible enemy,\u8221\'20\'1D says Ali Gondret, aged 64. \u8220\'20\'1CWe are fighting for the girls who come after us, because what comes next may be very bad.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020231009eja9002bs\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
