\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Trump rails against fraud trial as it appears legal team did not submit request for jury \u8211\'20\'13 as it happened\b0\par\par\uc2 L\u233\'00\'E9onie Chao-Fong (now) and Chris Stein (earlier) \par \uc2 7,243 \uc2 words\par \uc2 2 October 2023\par 22:10 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 This live blog has now closed. You can read our full report on the trial below:Trump attacks New York court on day one of fraud trialSign up to the free Trump on Trial newsletter\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.00pm BST\par \par \uc2 Closing summary\par \par \uc2 It\u8217\'20\'19s 6pm in Washington. Here\u8217\'20\'19s a recap of today\u8217\'20\'19s developments:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  attacked the judge and New York prosecutors who have charged him with orchestrating a years-long fraud for the first day of a civil trial that could see the former president and his family business paying hundreds of millions of dollars in damages and that has already threatened to end his business career in the city where it started.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The former president, speaking in front of cameras during the first day of his fraud trial, said his financial statements were \u8220\'20\'1Cphenomenal\u8221\'20\'1D, and called New York attorney general, Letitia James, who is Black, a \u8220\'20\'1Cracist\u8221\'20\'1D and a \u8220\'20\'1Chorror show\u8221\'20\'1D and said the case was being overseen by a \u8220\'20\'1Crogue judge\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Congressman \uc2 Matt Gaetz\uc2  continued to attack Kevin McCarthy over the House Republican speaker\u8217\'20\'19s successful efforts to avoid a government shutdown, even as other hard-right lawmakers came to McCarthy\u8217\'20\'19s defense. Speaking on the House floor on Monday, Gaetz railed against McCarthy, accusing the speaker of cutting \u8220\'20\'1Ca secret side deal\u8221\'20\'1D with \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  to provide additional funding to Ukraine.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Gavin Newsom\uc2 , the California governor, has named Laphonza Butler to fill the Senate seat held by \uc2 Dianne Feinstein\uc2 , who died on Thursday. Butler, a Democratic strategist and former labor leader, will be {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/oct/02/laphonza-butler-to-fill-dianne-feinsteins-vacant-senate-seat-newsom-office-says"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the only Black woman serving in the US senate,}}}\uc2  and the first openly LGBTQ+ person to represent California in the chamber.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 A federal judge has scheduled the trial of US senator \uc2 Bob Menendez\uc2  on bribery and corruption charges to begin 6 May 2024. Under the indictment unsealed last month, Menendez and his wife, Nadine Menendez, were a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/oct/02/trump-trial-mccarthy-house-speaker-shutdown-republicans-politics-live-updates?page=with:block-651b26bb8f08b90f4edd655d#block-651b26bb8f08b90f4edd655d"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 ccused of using his seat in the Senate, }}}\uc2  as chair of the foreign relations committee, to benefit the government of Egypt.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 A state senator from North Dakota, Doug Larsen, his wife and their two young children died when the small plane they were traveling in crashed in Utah, a senate leader {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/oct/02/north-dakota-state-senator-killed-plane-crash-doug-larsen"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  said.}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.50pm BST\par \par \uc2 Congressman \uc2 Jamaal Bowman\uc2  attempted to distance himself from a memo released by his office that referred to some Republican extremists as Nazis.\par \par \uc2 In a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.politico.com/live-updates/2023/10/02/congress/bowmans-damage-control-00119493"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  memo}}}\uc2  obtained by Politico, Bowman\u8217\'20\'19s office suggested several talking points his Democratic colleagues could use to defend him amid a GOP push to punish the New York congressman {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/oct/02/trump-trial-mccarthy-house-speaker-shutdown-republicans-politics-live-updates?page=with:block-651b16e18f08b90f4edd64ee#block-651b16e18f08b90f4edd64ee"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  after he set off a House fire alarm }}}\uc2  during Saturday\u8217\'20\'19s spending vote.\par \par \uc2 One suggested response from Bowman\u8217\'20\'19s office to questions about the incident:\par \par \uc2 I believe Congressman Bowman when he says this was an accident. Republicans need to instead focus their energy on the Nazi members of their party before anything else.\par \par \uc2 Posting on X, formerly known as \uc2 Twitter\uc2 , Bowman condemned the use of the word \u8220\'20\'1CNazi\u8221\'20\'1D, calling it \u8220\'20\'1Cinappropriate\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 enltrI just became aware that in our messaging guidance, there was inappropriate use of the term Nazi without my consent. I condemn the use of the term Nazi out of its precise definition. It is important to specify the term Nazi to refer to members of the Nazi party & neo-Nazis. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/DUi92VpUia"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/DUi92VpUia}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Congressman \uc2 Jamaal Bowman\uc2  (@RepBowman) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/RepBowman/status/1708925626407674238?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 October 2, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.26pm BST\par \par \uc2 Trump says he has done 'nothing wrong' in remarks at the end of first trial day\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , speaking after leaving the courtroom during the first day of his fraud trial, accused New York attorney general Letitia James of being a \u8220\'20\'1Cdisgrace\u8221\'20\'1D who \u8220\'20\'1Cshould focus on all of the violent crime and murders going on\u8221\'20\'1D in the state rather than on him.\par \par \uc2 The former president insisted he has done \u8220\'20\'1Cnothing wrong\u8221\'20\'1D and that the lawsuit was part of an effort to interfere with the 2024 election, NBC reported.\par \par \uc2 He also complained that his time spent at trial was keeping him off the campaign trail.\par \par \uc2 I\u8217\'20\'19ve been sitting in a courthouse all day long instead of being in Iowa, New Hampshire, South Carolina or a lot of other places I could be at. This is a horrible situation for our country.\par \par \uc2 enltrTrump departs court in NYC by lobbing more insults at AG James {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/Yt4TfHUlWC"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/Yt4TfHUlWC}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Aaron Rupar (@atrupar) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/atrupar/status/1708944716761284983?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 October 2, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 10.29pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.09pm BST\par \par \uc2 New York City public hospitals will now offer \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  care via telehealth, placing them among the first public health systems in the US to do so.\par \par \uc2 The city\u8217\'20\'19s mayor, Eric Adams, a nnounced on Monday that \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  pill prescriptions would now be available by telephone or online, adding that such access can happen from \u8220\'20\'1Cthe comfort of your home\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 As a result of the move, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/new-york"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 New York}}}\uc2  City residents will now be able to connect with health practitioners for those prescriptions, building on previous legislations to protect abortions rights in New York.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIf you are clinically eligible, that provider will be able to prescribe \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  medication that would be delivered to your New York City address within days,\u8221\'20\'1D {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://x.com/NYCMayor/status/1708862010572657034?s=20"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Adams said}}}\uc2  during Monday\u8217\'20\'19s announcement.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe will not stand idly by as these attacks continue and the far-rights seeks to strip our citizens of their basic rights,\u8221\'20\'1D Adams added, referring to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  restrictions being legislated across the country.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights organizations celebrated Monday\u8217\'20\'19s announcement as an essential step to protect reproductive rights.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2023/oct/02/new-york-city-hospital-abortion-pill-mail-telehealth"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 New York City public hospitals to offer \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  care via telehealth}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.46pm BST\par \par \uc2 The first day of \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s fraud trial has concluded, with proceedings expected to resume tomorrow morning.\par \par \uc2 Judge \uc2 Arthur Engoron\uc2  heard testimony from the first witness in the trial, Trump\u8217\'20\'19s former longtime accountant Donald Bender.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.30pm BST\par \par \uc2 Criminal trial of Senator \uc2 Bob Menendez\uc2  set for 6 May\par \par \uc2 A federal judge has scheduled the trial of US senator \uc2 Bob Menendez\uc2  and his wife on bribery and corruption charges to begin 6 May 2024.\par \par \uc2 The New Jersey Democratic senator has pleaded not guilty and resisted calls for his resignation after he was indicted on charges of taking bribes from three New Jersey businessmen.\par \par \uc2 Under the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.justice.gov/usao-sdny/pr/us-senator-robert-menendez-his-wife-and-three-new-jersey-businessmen-charged-bribery"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 indictment}}}\uc2  unsealed last month, Menendez and his wife, Nadine Menendez, were accused of using his seat in the Senate, as chair of the foreign relations committee, to benefit the government of Egypt.\par \par \uc2 Prosecutors described how the large sums of cash were found at Menendez\u8217\'20\'19s New Jersey home, as well as actual gold bars. A \uc2 Mercedes-Benz\uc2  car is also at issue. Three businessmen have also been charged.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 9.33pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.12pm BST\par \par \uc2 Gavin Newsom\uc2 , the California governor, has named Laphonza Butler, a Democratic strategist and former labor leader, to fill the Senate seat held by {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/dianne-feinstein"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Dianne Feinstein}}}\uc2 , who died on Thursday.\par \par \uc2 The appointment fulfills Newsom\u8217\'20\'19s pledge to appoint a Black woman to the Senate, while shirking calls to name Barbara Lee, a Black Bay Area congresswoman who is already running for the position in 2024.\par \par \uc2 Butler, 44, will be the only Black woman serving in the US senate, and the first openly LGBTQ+ person to represent California in the chamber. She currently leads Emily\u8217\'20\'19s List, a national political organization dedicated to electing Democratic women who support reproductive rights. She has also served as a strategist and adviser to \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s presidential campaign and was a former labor leader of SEIU California, the state\u8217\'20\'19s largest union, representing more than 700,000 workers.\par \par \uc2 Butler currently lives in Maryland, according to her Emily\u8217\'20\'19s List biography, but she owns a house in California and will re-register to vote in the state before taking office, according to the Newsom administration. She could be sworn in as early as Tuesday evening when the Senate returns to session.\par \par \uc2 Democrats control the Senate 51-49, though Feinstein\u8217\'20\'19s seat is vacant. The quick appointment by Newsom will give the Democratic caucus more wiggle room on close votes, including nominations that Republicans uniformly oppose.\par \par \uc2 Laphonza Butler currently leads Emily\u8217\'20\'19s List, a political organization dedicated to electing Democratic women who support reproductive rights Photograph: Susan Walsh/AP\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.54pm BST\par \par \uc2 Trump gained $100m through inflating real estate value, NY state attorney says\par \par \uc2 At the opening of \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  and his family\u8217\'20\'19s civil fraud trial today, an attorney for New York state said the defendants gained more than $100m by inflating the value of their properties, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.reuters.com/world/us/donald-trumps-business-empire-peril-civil-fraud-trial-opens-new-york-2023-10-02/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Reuters reports}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The gains came through lower insurance premiums and better loan conditions, and in his opening statement, Kevin Wallace, an attorney for New York attorney general Letitia James, said the former president was \u8220\'20\'1Cmaterially inaccurate\u8221\'20\'1D when he would describe his business to insurers and lenders.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThis isn\u8217\'20\'19t business as usual, and this isn\u8217\'20\'19t how sophisticated parties deal with each other,\u8221\'20\'1D Wallace said. \u8220\'20\'1CThese are not victimless crimes.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 However, Trump\u8217\'20\'19s attorney Christopher Kise denied any wrongdoing.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt is one of the most highly successful brands in the world, and he has made a fortune literally being right about real estate investments,\u8221\'20\'1D Kise said in his opening statement. \u8220\'20\'1CThere was no intent to defraud, there was no illegality, there was no default, there was no breach, there was no reliance from the banks, there were no unjust profits, and there were no victims.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Kise also said that Trump\u8217\'20\'19s valuations of his properties were understood to be estimates, and that just because people disagree with them does not mean they are fraudulent.\par \par \uc2 But as evidence for his case, Wallace played from a deposition with Trump\u8217\'20\'19s former fixer \uc2 Michael Cohen\uc2 , where he said he was told \u8220\'20\'1Cto attain the number that Mr. Trump wanted.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Note: We first reported the figure as $1bn, citing Reuters. We have since corrected the figure to $100m.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 9.56pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.34pm BST\par \par \uc2 Axios reports that congressman \uc2 Jamaal Bowman\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s office is encouraging his fellow Democrats to step up and defend him after he pulled a fire alarm on Saturday:\par \par \uc2 enltrHere's the memo that Bowman's office sent to other House Democratic staff.\par \par \uc2 They closed the link 7 minutes later "as it was leaked to reporters," but offered to send messaging to those who reached out directly, per an email viewed by {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/axios?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @Axios}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/yrjD5HVhE1"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/yrjD5HVhE1}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Andrew Solender (@AndrewSolender) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/AndrewSolender/status/1708910965796864277?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 October 2, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, the \uc2 Capitol police\uc2  says they are investigating the incident, and released a statement {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.uscp.gov/media-center/press-releases/uscp-investigating-cannon-building-evacuation"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 recounting what happened}}}\uc2 . It reads, in part:\par \par \uc2 At approximately 12:05 p.m. on Saturday, September 30, a fire alarm sounded inside the Cannon Building. USCP officers evacuated people from the building, floor by floor, while DC Fire & EMS responded. The fire alarm only sounded in the Cannon Building, so that was the only building that was evacuated.\par \par \uc2 On security video, a man was seen trying to exit the door in the Cannon Building and then pulling the fire alarm that prompted the evacuation. USCP officers had previously placed signs with clear language that explained the door was secured and marked as an emergency exit only.\par \par \uc2 At approximately 1:30 p.m. the DC Fire Marshal determined there was not a fire and the building was safe.\par \par \uc2 The USCP will continue to keep the public updated on the status of the investigation.\par \par \uc2 Some House Republicans have already made up their mind, and will try to expel Bowman, Axios reports. However, expelling a House member requires the approval of two-thirds of the chamber, and has not been done since 2002:\par \par \uc2 enltrGOP Rep. \uc2 Nicole Malliotakis\uc2  says she is introducing her expulsion resolution with a dozen cosponsors and "will continue to add more throughout the day."\par \par \uc2 Co-sponsors: Greene, Collins, Scott (Ga.), Gonzales, Miller (Ill.), Palmer, Rosendale, Weber, Nehls, Brecheen, Moore (Ala.). {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/zPU0IYCLM9"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/zPU0IYCLM9}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Andrew Solender (@AndrewSolender) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/AndrewSolender/status/1708914743052828763?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 October 2, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.17pm BST\par \par \uc2 As lawmakers scrambled over the weekend in their surprisingly successful effort to avert a government shutdown, the show was almost disrupted when Democratic congressman \uc2 Jamaal Bowman\uc2  pulled the fire alarm in a House office building. There have been some new developments in that episode, but before we get into it, here\u8217\'20\'19s a recap of what happened, from the Guardian\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/maya-yang"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Maya Yang}}}\uc2  :\par \par \uc2 The New York Democratic congressman \uc2 Jamaal Bowman\uc2  denied that he pulled a fire alarm in a Capitol office building to delay a vote on the stopgap measure that ultimately stopped a government shutdown.\par \par \uc2 In a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://x.com/RepBowman/status/1708299648782262656?s=20"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  statement}}}\uc2  on Saturday evening, the New Yorker said he mistakenly thought the alarm, which prompted the Cannon House office building to be evacuated, would open a door.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CToday, as I was rushing to make a vote, I came to a door that is usually open for votes but today was not open. I am embarrassed to admit that I activated the fire alarm, mistakenly thinking it would open the door,\u8221\'20\'1D said Bowman.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI regret this and sincerely apologize for any confusion this caused.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 He dismissed accusations from {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/republicans"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Republicans}}}\uc2  that he pulled the alarm in an attempt to delay the vote.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI want to be very clear, this was not me, in any way, trying to delay any vote. It was the exact opposite \u8211\'20\'13 I was trying to urgently get a vote, which I ultimately did and joined my colleagues in a bipartisan effort to keep our government open,\u8221\'20\'1D he said.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/sep/30/democrat-jamaal-bowman-fire-alarm-house"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Democrat Jamaal Bowman denies pulling fire alarm to delay House vote}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.54pm BST\par \par \uc2 An update on \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s civil fraud trial, which has resumed in New York City.\par \par \uc2 As the Messenger reports, the first witness to take the stand in the damages phase of the trial is Trump\u8217\'20\'19s former accountant:\par \par \uc2 enltrNow\par \par \uc2 Witness testimony in NYAG v. Trump will begin with testimony by Donald Bender, his ex-accountant at \uc2 Mazars\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Adam Klasfeld (@KlasfeldReports) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/KlasfeldReports/status/1708914108542648684?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 October 2, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 Trump and his three children were named by their attorneys as witnesses, but that does not necessarily mean they will speak to the court.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.37pm BST\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s civil fraud trial isn\u8217\'20\'19t the only court news happening today. As the Guardian\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/edpilkington"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Ed Pilkington}}}\uc2  reports, the supreme court is starting a new term today, giving its conservative majority another opportunity to hand down decisions that could have major impacts on American life:\par \par \uc2 The {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/law/us-supreme-court"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 US supreme court}}}\uc2  will gather on Monday at the start of a new judicial term that has the potential to catastrophically disrupt the functioning of government, expand the assault on reproductive rights and unleash yet more gun violence on an already reeling America.\par \par \uc2 When the nine justices convene on Monday morning it will mark the start of the third full term in which the 6-3 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/books/2023/jun/04/the-supermajority-review-supreme-court-trump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 rightwing supermajority}}}\uc2  created by \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  is in command. Explosive rulings delivered over the past two terms have demonstrated the conservatives\u8217\'20\'19 newfound muscle, stripping millions of Americans of fundamental rights from {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2022/jun/24/roe-v-wade-overturned-abortion-summary-supreme-court"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22 }}}\uc2  to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/law/2023/jun/29/us-supreme-court-affirmative-action-harvard-unc-ruling"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 affirmative action}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Three significant cases before the court this term cut to the core of the functioning of the \uc2 US government\uc2  itself. According to the co-hosts of the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://crooked.com/podcast-series/strict-scrutiny/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Strict Scrutiny podcast}}}\uc2 , at stake is no less than \u8220\'20\'1Cthe future of government as we know it\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 On Tuesday the court will hear oral arguments in a case that poses the greatest threat to consumer protections for decades. Stephen Vladeck, an authority on constitutional law at the University of Texas law school, said that although {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.oyez.org/cases/2023/22-448"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 CFPB v CFSA}}}\uc2  is technical in its framing, it has the potential to \u8220\'20\'1Cbring down much of the American financial system\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/law/2023/oct/02/us-supreme-court-term-begins-abortion-gun-control-government"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \b  \highlight22Abortion\b0 \highlight22 , guns, democracy: US rights at stake as supreme court term begins}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.17pm BST\par \par \uc2 Trump attending fraud trial to 'watch this witch-hunt'\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , speaking in front of cameras during the break, said he attended the civil fraud trial against him so he could \u8220\'20\'1Cwatch this witch-hunt myself\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 He slammed the \u8220\'20\'1Cdisgraceful trial\u8221\'20\'1D put forward by the \u8220\'20\'1Ccorrupt\u8221\'20\'1D New York attorney general, Letitia James, accusing her of wasting time when there are \u8220\'20\'1Cmurderers and killers that are all over New York killing people\u8221\'20\'1D. He added:\par \par \uc2 We\u8217\'20\'19re going to be here for months with a judge that already made up his mind. It\u8217\'20\'19s ridiculous. He\u8217\'20\'19s a Democrat judge a and operative and it\u8217\'20\'19s ridiculous.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1COther than that, things went very well,\u8221\'20\'1D Trump added.\par \par \uc2 The former president also attacked Manhattan supreme court judge \uc2 Arthur Engoron\uc2 , who he said should be disbarred for \u8220\'20\'1Cinterfering with an election\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 enltr\u8220\'20\'1CHe\u8217\'20\'19s a Democrat judge \u8230\'20\'26 It\u8217\'20\'19s ridiculous.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  speaks after leaving the courtroom on day one of a civil fraud lawsuit trial filed against him in New York.\par \par \uc2 MORE: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/Fd9tspNnmA"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/Fd9tspNnmA}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/hashtag/NewsNationLive?src=hash&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 #NewsNationLive}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/qaTKhb2fUJ"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/qaTKhb2fUJ}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 NewsNation (@NewsNation) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/NewsNation/status/1708897632817492202?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 October 2, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 7.18pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.51pm BST\par \par \uc2 The White House press secretary, \uc2 Karine Jean-Pierre\uc2 , was asked about \uc2 Matt Gaetz\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s comments on the House floor {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/oct/02/trump-trial-mccarthy-house-speaker-shutdown-republicans-politics-live-updates?page=with:block-651af2358f087e532d8e0c8e#block-651af2358f087e532d8e0c8e"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  accusing Speaker}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/oct/02/trump-trial-mccarthy-house-speaker-shutdown-republicans-politics-live-updates?page=with:block-651af2358f087e532d8e0c8e#block-651af2358f087e532d8e0c8e"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  Kevin McCarthy }}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/oct/02/trump-trial-mccarthy-house-speaker-shutdown-republicans-politics-live-updates?page=with:block-651af2358f087e532d8e0c8e#block-651af2358f087e532d8e0c8e"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 of}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/oct/02/trump-trial-mccarthy-house-speaker-shutdown-republicans-politics-live-updates?page=with:block-651af2358f087e532d8e0c8e#block-651af2358f087e532d8e0c8e"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 making a secret side deal}}}\uc2  on Ukraine aid with \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Speaking to reporters, she replied:\par \par \uc2 What we know is that there is bipartisan support for this deal. Speaker McCarthy was on the air multiple times yesterday saying that he wants to continue support for Ukraine, to get the weapons that they need. So we are going to hold him to that.\par \par \uc2 enltrWH Press Sec. \uc2 Karine Jean-Pierre\uc2  doesn't expand upon or confirm Biden's claim he made a deal with Speaker McCarthy on Ukraine funding:\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWhat I'm saying is that there's been a bipartisan focus and agreement to continue the funding for Ukraine...That's what we're going to see.\u8221\'20\'1D {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/nwWQDURtyz"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/nwWQDURtyz}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 The Recount (@therecount) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/therecount/status/1708889559398854906?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 October 2, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.42pm BST\par \par \uc2 As we {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/oct/02/trump-trial-mccarthy-house-speaker-shutdown-republicans-politics-live-updates?page=with:block-651ad6f88f080714cd55f6f1#block-651ad6f88f080714cd55f6f1"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reported earlier,}}}\uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s civil fraud case is being tried without a jury reportedly because the former president\u8217\'20\'19s attorneys seemingly did not pay too close of attention to their paperwork.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CNobody asked for\u8221\'20\'1D a jury trial, Judge \uc2 Arthur Engoron\uc2  noted during Monday\u8217\'20\'19s trial. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://themessenger.com/politics/trump-new-york-civil-trial-jury-judge"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 According}}}\uc2  to the Messenger:\par \par \uc2 Earlier this year, New York Attorney Letitia James filed a form with a checkmark next to the field: \u8220\'20\'1C {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://iapps.courts.state.ny.us/fbem/DocumentDisplayServlet?documentId=Mh7T6YNL3ysJbWUq2rffTQ==&system=prod"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Trial without a jury}}}\uc2 .\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Trump\u8217\'20\'19s legal team didn\u8217\'20\'19t file a corresponding form, and the former president may have regretted his lawyer\u8217\'20\'19s inaction ever since.\par \par \uc2 enltrIt\u8217\'20\'19s incredibly easy to ask for a jury trial. You just check a box on a form. Hard to believe that Trump understood that his lawyers hadn\u8217\'20\'19t done it when he\u8217\'20\'19s been savaging the judge who is now the factfinder in his huge fraud trial. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/E2NlkIUBzX"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/E2NlkIUBzX}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Harry Litman (@harrylitman) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/harrylitman/status/1708862304182550716?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 October 2, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.31pm BST\par \par \uc2 In brief remarks as he arrived at the courthouse, \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  claimed his financial statements were \u8220\'20\'1Cphenomenal\u8221\'20\'1D, even though a judge last week determined he and his family had committed fraud over the course of a decade.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s a clip:\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.21pm BST\par \par \uc2 The day so far\par \par \uc2 The damages phase of \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s civil fraud trial opened in New York City, which the former president attended in person. Though he {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/oct/02/trump-trial-mccarthy-house-speaker-shutdown-republicans-politics-live-updates?page=with:block-651acd968f087e532d8e0a69#block-651acd968f087e532d8e0a69"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 blasted}}}\uc2  the case as politically motivated and insisted that his financial statements were {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/oct/02/trump-trial-mccarthy-house-speaker-shutdown-republicans-politics-live-updates?page=with:block-651acfe68f080714cd55f686#block-651acfe68f080714cd55f686"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1Cphenomenal\u8221\'20\'1D}}}\uc2 , despite already being found liable for fraud, he and his children are facing severe financial consequences, and could lose control of properties such as Trump Tower. Meanwhile, in Washington DC, Republican insurgent leader \uc2 Matt Gaetz\uc2  held off on formally attempting to remove Kevin McCarthy as speaker of the House. Gaetz {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/oct/02/trump-trial-mccarthy-house-speaker-shutdown-republicans-politics-live-updates?filterKeyEvents=false&page=with:block-651af2358f087e532d8e0c8e#block-651af2358f087e532d8e0c8e"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 demanded answers}}}\uc2  from his fellow Republican, accusing him of cutting a side deal with \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 . We\u8217\'20\'19ll see if he gets them.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s what else has happened today so far:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Gaetz{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/oct/02/trump-trial-mccarthy-house-speaker-shutdown-republicans-politics-live-updates?page=with:block-651af6b08f080714cd55f8ca#block-651af6b08f080714cd55f8ca"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 said}}}\uc2  he delayed formally introducing his motion to vacate because not enough lawmakers were in town yet.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Trump\u8217\'20\'19s legal team{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/oct/02/trump-trial-mccarthy-house-speaker-shutdown-republicans-politics-live-updates?page=with:block-651ad6f88f080714cd55f6f1#block-651ad6f88f080714cd55f6f1"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 did not ask}}}\uc2  for a jury to determine damages in the ex-president\u8217\'20\'19s civil fraud trial, meaning the decision will be left to judge \uc2 Arthur Engoron\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 New York attorney general Letitia James{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/oct/02/trump-trial-mccarthy-house-speaker-shutdown-republicans-politics-live-updates?page=with:block-651acbf18f08b90f4edd618a#block-651acbf18f08b90f4edd618a"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 said}}}\uc2  \u8220\'20\'1Cno one is above the law\u8221\'20\'1D just before Trump\u8217\'20\'19s fraud trial was about to get under way.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.08pm BST\par \par \uc2 The long-running feud between Republican House speaker Kevin McCarthy and rightwing insurgents from his own party, particularly congressman \uc2 Matt Gaetz\uc2 , hit a new peak on Sunday, when Gaetz announced he would move to hold a vote on whether McCarthy could keep his job. From the Guardian\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/richardluscombe"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Richard Luscombe}}}\uc2 , here\u8217\'20\'19s a look at how the two men came to be at loggerheads, and whether Democrats will come to the speaker\u8217\'20\'19s rescue:\par \par \uc2 Simmering hostility between Republicans over the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/sep/30/us-government-shutdown-congress-senate-kevin-mccarthy"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 bipartisan deal}}}\uc2  that averted a government shutdown descended into open political warfare on Sunday, a rightwing congressman saying he would move to oust Kevin McCarthy and the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/oct/01/kevin-mccarthy-us-government-shutdown-republican-speaker"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 embattled House speaker}}}\uc2  insisting he would survive.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe need to rip off the Bandaid. We need to move on with new leadership that can be trustworthy,\u8221\'20\'1D the Florida representative \uc2 Matt Gaetz\uc2  told CNN\u8217\'20\'19s State of the Union, saying he would file a \u8220\'20\'1Cmotion to vacate\u8221\'20\'1D in the next few days.\par \par \uc2 McCarthy, Gaetz said, lied about \u8220\'20\'1Ca secret deal\u8221\'20\'1D struck with Democrats to later pass money for Ukraine that was left out of the compromise agreement, and misled {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/republicans"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Republicans}}}\uc2  about working with the opposition at all.\par \par \uc2 The bill keeping the government funded for 47 days passed the House on Saturday night 335-91, 209 Democrats joining 126 Republicans in support. It cleared the Senate 88-9 and was signed by \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 In remarks at the White House on Sunday, Biden said the measure extending funding until 17 November, and including $16bn in disaster aid, prevented \u8220\'20\'1Ca needless crisis\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 But, Biden said: \u8220\'20\'1CThe truth is we shouldn\u8217\'20\'19t be here in the first place. It\u8217\'20\'19s time to end governing by crisis and keep your word when you give it in the Congress. I fully expect the speaker to keep his commitment to secure the passage of support needed to help Ukraine as they defend themselves against aggression.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Asked if he expected McCarthy to stand up to extremists, Biden replied: \u8220\'20\'1CI hope this experience for the speaker has been one of personal revelation.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/oct/01/matt-gaetz-kevin-mccarthy-house-speaker-shutdown-deal"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \u8216\'20\'18Let\u8217\'20\'19s have that fight\u8217\'20\'19: McCarthy and Gaetz go to war over shutdown deal }}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.59pm BST\par \par \uc2 Asked by reporters why he did not formally introduce his motion to vacate Kevin McCarthy from the speaker of the House\u8217\'20\'19s chair, \uc2 Matt Gaetz\uc2  said it was because not enough lawmakers were in town yet:\par \par \uc2 enltrCNN's {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/mkraju?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @mkraju}}}\uc2  : \u8220\'20\'1CWhy didn't you go forward right now and are you backing off of your plans to push [McCarthy] out of the speakership?\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Rep. \uc2 Matt Gaetz\uc2  (R-FL): \u8220\'20\'1CNo one is in town yet. It's Monday on a fly-in day at noon. I think we'll have more folks later this afternoon.\u8221\'20\'1D {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/dyfBoSL4J9"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/dyfBoSL4J9}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 The Recount (@therecount) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/therecount/status/1708884808359653423?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 October 2, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.47pm BST\par \par \uc2 Republican insurgent Gaetz demands answers from McCarthy, threatens removal vote\par \par \uc2 A day after announcing that he will propose removing Kevin McCarthy from his post as speaker of the House, \uc2 Matt Gaetz\uc2 , a leader of the far-right block of Republican insurgents in the chamber, demanded answers from the speaker but held off on formally introducing the motion.\par \par \uc2 In a speech on the House floor, Gaetz accused McCarthy of making a secret side deal on Ukraine aid with \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 , the Democratic president who far-right Republicans have warned the speaker against working with.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CMr. Speaker, just tell us \u8230\'20\'26 what was in the secret Ukraine side deal, what commitments were made to president Biden to continue the spending of president Biden, in exchange for doing things for president Biden,\u8221\'20\'1D Gaetz said. \u8220\'20\'1CIt is becoming increasingly clear who the speaker of the House already works for, and it\u8217\'20\'19s not the Republican conference.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 While Gaetz had announced yesterday he would make a motion to vacate the speaker\u8217\'20\'19s chair, he did not formally do so in his speech today, rather forecasting that he would do so in the coming days, if McCarthy did not answer his questions:\par \par \uc2 Mr. Speaker, I would ask that these questions be answered soon. Because there may be other votes coming today, or later this week, that could be implicated by the answers to these questions. Members of the Republican Party might vote differently on a motion to vacate if they heard what the speaker had to share with us about his secret side deal with \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  on Ukraine. I\u8217\'20\'19ll be listening. Stay tuned.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 5.48pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.22pm BST\par \par \uc2 From the Guardian\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/lauren-aratani"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Lauren Aratani}}}\uc2 , here\u8217\'20\'19s a recap of everything we know about \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s fraud trial in New York, and the potentially sizable damages he could be forced to pay:\par \par \uc2 The future of \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s New York real estate business will be decided in a Manhattan court case that starts on Monday.\par \par \uc2 The {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/new-york"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 New York}}}\uc2  attorney general, Letitia James, is taking Trump to court after a three-year investigation found that he and others within the \uc2 Trump Organization\uc2  repeatedly used false or misleading financial statements to broker deals, obtain favorable loans and bolster the appearance of his net worth.\par \par \uc2 The judge presiding over the trial, the New York supreme court justice \uc2 Arthur Engoron\uc2 , already {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/sep/26/trump-liable-fraud-new-york"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 found Trump guilty}}}\uc2  of financial fraud in a pre-trial judgment. The trial will be dedicated to determining whether, and how much, Trump will have to pay for the verdict.\par \par \uc2 James has argued that the \uc2 Trump Organization\uc2  should owe at least $250m for profiting off loans that were awarded based on false and misleading financial statements. Trump\u8217\'20\'19s lawyers have appealed the judgment, though it is unlikely to affect the trial\u8217\'20\'19s proceedings.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s what we know about Trump\u8217\'20\'19s upcoming fraud trial.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/oct/02/donald-trump-real-estate-verdict-guilty"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Trump real estate case: what to know before the fraud trial begins}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.01pm BST\par \par \uc2 Letitia James is the latest legal adversary to win in court against \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , and attract the former president\u8217\'20\'19s ire. Here\u8217\'20\'19s the Guardian\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/edwardhelmore"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Edward Helmore}}}\uc2  with a look at the New York attorney general\u8217\'20\'19s path to power, and to suing the Trump family:\par \par \uc2 New York attorney general Letitia James has never shied away from taking on powerful adversaries \u8211\'20\'13 from the \uc2 National Rifle Association\uc2  to former {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/new-york"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 New York}}}\uc2  governor \uc2 Andrew Cuomo\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 On Monday she will take on her biggest case yet: a fraud trial that threatens the very foundation of \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s New York real estate empire.\par \par \uc2 Critics have accused the 64-year-old career prosecutor of using her office, with 1,700 staff and over 700 assistant attorneys general, for political purposes. To others, the Democrat is a heroic figure: the first woman elected as New York\u8217\'20\'19s attorney general and the first Black person to serve in the role. A fearless prosecutor who has taken on cases others would walk away from.\par \par \uc2 Like Trump, \u8220\'20\'1CTish\u8221\'20\'1D James was born and raised in New York City. It\u8217\'20\'19s about the only thing they have in common. Raised with her seven siblings in Brooklyn, James attended public schools in the city before getting her law degree at \uc2 Howard University\uc2  in Washington DC.\par \par \uc2 She started her law career as a public defender before entering New York politics as a council member and then as public advocate, the first Black woman to hold the watchdog role. James\u8217\'20\'19 passions were clear from the start \u8211\'20\'13 she filed a record number of suits on behalf of tenants, seniors and people with disabilities. James became New York state attorney general in 2018.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/oct/02/letitia-james-new-york-attorney-general-trump-real-estate-trial"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Letitia James: the fearless attorney general threatening Trump\u8217\'20\'19s business}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.41pm BST\par \par \uc2 From the Guardian\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/lauren-aratani"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Lauren Aratani}}}\uc2 , here\u8217\'20\'19s a recap of what has happened so far today in \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s civil fraud trial:\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  arrived at a New York court just a few miles south of Trump Tower on Monday for the first day of a fraud trial that could see the former president and his family business paying hundreds of millions of dollars in damages and that has already threatened to end his business career in the city where it started.\par \par \uc2 The {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/new-york"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 New York}}}\uc2  attorney general, Letitia James, has accused Trump of using false and misleading financial statements from 2011 to 2021 to make himself and his businesses wealthier, helping him broker deals and obtain financing. Based on her office\u8217\'20\'19s three-year investigation, James is arguing that Trump owes at least $250m for committing fraud.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThis is a continuation of the single greatest witch-hunt of all time,\u8221\'20\'1D Trump said as he headed into court. He said his financial statements were \u8220\'20\'1Cphenomenal,\u8221\'20\'1D called James, who is Black, a \u8220\'20\'1Cracist\u8221\'20\'1D and a \u8220\'20\'1Chorror show\u8221\'20\'1D and said the case was being overseen by a \u8220\'20\'1Crogue judge\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CMy message is simple: No matter how powerful you are, no matter how much money you think you may have, no one is above the law,\u8221\'20\'1D James said outside the court.\par \par \uc2 During the three-year investigation, James found that Trump had exaggerated the value of 23 of his properties and assets to the tune of hundreds of millions or even billions of dollars. Trump used these financial statements to obtain favorable loans and make his net worth appear higher than it actually was.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/oct/02/trump-fraud-case-new-york"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Trump in New York court for fraud trial that threatens his business career}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.21pm BST\par \par \uc2 Today, \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  is in a New York City courtroom, but yesterday, he was having what can only be described as a weird one, the Guardian\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/michael-sainato"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Michael Sainato}}}\uc2  reports:\par \par \uc2 Faced with a litany of criminal charges, \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  on Sunday told a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=9UZePWtEnco&t=1030s"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 campaign rally}}}\uc2  in Iowa that he would prefer to die by electrocution rather than be eaten by a shark if he ever found himself on a rapidly sinking, electrically powered boat.\par \par \uc2 The former president and frontrunner for the 2024 Republican presidential nomination delivered the bizarre remarks during a speech in the community of Ottuma. He was pontificating over batteries for electric powered boats while recounting a conversation he claimed to have with a boat manufacturer in South Carolina.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIf I\u8217\'20\'19m sitting down and that boat is going down and I\u8217\'20\'19m on top of a battery and the water starts flooding in, I\u8217\'20\'19m getting concerned, but then I look 10 yards to my left and there\u8217\'20\'19s a shark over there, so I have a choice of electrocution and a shark, you know what I\u8217\'20\'19m going to take? Electrocution,\u8221\'20\'1D Trump said. \u8220\'20\'1CI will take electrocution every single time, do we agree?\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Trump then continued criticizing the prospect of any other sustainable energy technologies and claiming he would repeal the Joe Biden White House\u8217\'20\'19s electric vehicle mandate.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThese people are crazy,\u8221\'20\'1D Trump said.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/oct/02/donald-trump-electrocution-campaign-event-iowa"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Trump says he would prefer to die by electrocution in bizarre campaign rant}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.05pm BST\par \par \uc2 Judge \uc2 Arthur Engoron\uc2  will determine damages in civil fraud trial\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  started off his day by attacking \uc2 Arthur Engoron\uc2 , the New York supreme court judge who will begin determining damages after finding last week that the former president and his family committed fraud.\par \par \uc2 Engoron is now set to be the latest character in Trump\u8217\'20\'19s many legal dramas, and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://apnews.com/article/trump-engoron-letitia-james-fraud-new-york-9bd42690d327f6f63c9eb31c046f8426"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the Associated Press has a good profile}}}\uc2  of the 74-year-old judge:\par \par \uc2 He\u8217\'20\'19s driven a taxi cab, played in a band and protested the Vietnam War. As a New York City judge, \uc2 Arthur Engoron\uc2  has resolved hundreds of disputes, deciding everything from zoning and free speech issues to a custody fight over a dog named \u8220\'20\'1CStevie.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Now, in the twilight of a distinguished two-decade career on the bench, the erudite, Ivy League-educated judge is presiding over his biggest case yet: deciding the future of former President \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s real estate empire.\par \par \uc2 Last week, Engoron ruled that Trump committed years of fraud by exaggerating his wealth and the value of assets on financial statements he used to get loans and make deals. As punishment, the judge said he would dissolve some of Trump\u8217\'20\'19s companies \u8212\'20\'14 a decision that could cause him to lose control of marquee New York properties, like Trump Tower.\par \par \uc2 Starting Monday, Engoron will preside over a non-jury trial in Manhattan to resolve remaining claims in New York Attorney General Letitia James\u8217\'20\'19 lawsuit against Trump, his company and top executives. He will also decide on monetary damages. James\u8217\'20\'19 office is seeking $250 million.\par \par \uc2 Trump, who is listed as a potential witness and could end up face-to-face with Engoron in court, called the judge\u8217\'20\'19s fraud ruling \u8220\'20\'1Cthe corporate death penalty.\u8221\'20\'1D He referred to Engoron as a \u8220\'20\'1Cpolitical hack\u8221\'20\'1D and said his would appeal.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI have a Deranged, Trump Hating Judge, who RAILROADED this FAKE CASE through a NYS Court at a speed never before seen,\u8221\'20\'1D the 2024 Republican frontrunner wrote on his Truth Social platform.\par \par \uc2 Through a court spokesperson, Engoron has declined to comment on Trump\u8217\'20\'19s barbs. He is barred from commenting to the news media about the case.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 5.11pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.49pm BST\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  in court for the opening of the damages phase of his civil fraud trial:\par \par \uc2 The former president (center), looking not exactly stoked to be there. Photograph: Seth Wenig/AP\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.44pm BST\par \par \uc2 Trump legal team did not submit request for a jury\par \par \uc2 The damages in \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s fraud trial will be determined not by a jury, but by one man: supreme court judge \uc2 Arthur Engoron\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 As the Guardian\u8217\'20\'19s Hugo Lowell reports, that appears to be because the former president\u8217\'20\'19s attorneys did not pay too close of attention to their paperwork:\par \par \uc2 enltrTrump isn\u8217\'20\'19t getting a jury trial in his $250m civil fraud suit brought against him by New York AG James because one of his lawyers overlooked submitting the routine request/checking boxes on the form, per two people familiar {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/7zvUfytiEr"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/7zvUfytiEr}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Hugo Lowell (@hugolowell) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/hugolowell/status/1708851585869140399?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 October 2, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 5.12pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.28pm BST\par \par \uc2 We won\u8217\'20\'19t have much visibility into the damages phase of \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s civil fraud trial.\par \par \uc2 CNN reports that judge \uc2 Arthur Engoron\uc2  has turned down media outlets\u8217\'20\'19 request that cameras broadcast today\u8217\'20\'19s opening statements:\par \par \uc2 enltrAnd the judge overseeing Trump's civil fraud trial has just denied the request from media outlets to allow a camera in the courtroom for opening statements.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Kaitlan Collins (@kaitlancollins) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/kaitlancollins/status/1708849121388315087?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 October 2, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.15pm BST\par \par \uc2 Trump says financial statements 'phenomenal' despite being found liable for fraud\par \par \uc2 In brief remarks as he arrived at the courthouse, \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  said his financial statements were \u8220\'20\'1Cphenomenal\u8221\'20\'1D, even though a judge last week determined he and his family had committed fraud over the course of a decade:\par \par \uc2 enltr'We have a racist attorney general who\u8217\'20\'19s a horror show.'\par \par \uc2 A defiant \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  continued his claims of a 'witch-hunt' while speaking to reporters as his NY civil fraud trial is due to begin, saying his financial statements are in fact 'phenomenal.' {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/nSMjoZhWUk"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/nSMjoZhWUk}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 NowThis (@nowthisnews) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/nowthisnews/status/1708846630340837588?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 October 2, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 The trial opening today is expected to take several weeks, and determine the amount of damages the former president and his children will have to pay.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.07pm BST\par \par \uc2 In an all-caps post on his Truth social account containing at least one spelling error, \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  accused Letitia James of being \u8220\'20\'1CCORRUPT & RACIST\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 He also called the presiding supreme court judge \uc2 Arthur Engoron\uc2  \u8220\'20\'1CROGUE, OUT OF CONTROL\u8221\'20\'1D and \u8220\'20\'1CTRUMP HATING\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.01pm BST\par \par \uc2 Not a red carpet but a hallway of cameras is awaiting \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  at the courthouse in downtown Manhattan.\par \par \uc2 It\u8217\'20\'19s the first day of Trump\u8217\'20\'19s fraud trial, where a judge will determine how much the former president will have to pay for fudging financial statements over the course of a decade.\par \par \uc2 Trump late Sunday night announced that he would be making an appearance in court the following day, though it is unclear if or when he will ultimately take the witness stand.\par \par \uc2 New York attorney general Letitia James is in attendance for the first day of the trial. James\u8217\'20\'19 three-year investigation into Trump found that he inflated his net worth up by hundreds of millions of dollars and raised the value of his assets on financial statements. James is arguing that Trump should pay up at least $250m in fines.\par \par \uc2 Outside the courthouse early Monday morning, a small group of anti-Trump protestors stood in the middle of the street, chanting \u8220\'20\'1CTrump lies all the time\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 The trial is scheduled to start at 10 am ET.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.56pm BST\par \par \uc2 Attorney general Letitia James says 'no one is above the law'\par \par \uc2 Before stepping into the courthouse, attorney general Letitia James spoke briefly to reporters.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s what she had to say:\par \par \uc2 enltr"My message is simple: No matter how powerful you are, no matter how much money you think you may have, no one is above the law."\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 New York Attorney General Letitia James, outside the court where \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 's latest trial is set to begin {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/TyhJmd7Noz"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/TyhJmd7Noz}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 The Recount (@therecount) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/therecount/status/1708842382018355577?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 October 2, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.57pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.48pm BST\par \par \uc2 Trump arrives at New York courthouse for civil fraud trial\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  has arrived at the Manhattan courthouse where a New York supreme court judge will today open the damages phase of his and his family\u8217\'20\'19s civil fraud trial, the Associated Press reports.\par \par \uc2 The former president faces the prospect of significant penalties that could cost him control of some of his major real estate holdings, including Trump Tower in New York City.\par \par \uc2 Follow along here for more on the trial\u8217\'20\'19s opening day.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.45pm BST\par \par \uc2 New York attorney general Letitia James has arrived at the Manhattan courthouse where a judge will preside over the damages phase of \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  and his family\u8217\'20\'19s civil fraud trial:\par \par \uc2 New York attorney general Letitia James wades through the press. Photograph: Andrew Kelly/Reuters\par \par \uc2 The trial has also attracted the usual New York City protesters:\par \par \uc2 Protesters chant outside the New York Supreme Court ahead of former President \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 's civil business fraud trial. Photograph: Brittainy Newman/AP\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.31pm BST\par \par \uc2 Minutes ago, \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s presidential campaign sent out an email attacking Letitia James, the New York state attorney general who sued him and his family, alleging fraud.\par \par \uc2 A judge agreed with her last week, setting the stage for the trial opening today that will determine how much the Trump must pay for inflating their assets in order to secure better loan terms over a period of ten years.\par \par \uc2 In typical Trump form, the email is basically a list of attack on James, including calling her a \u8220\'20\'1CDemocratic activist\u8221\'20\'1D and accusing her of being \u8220\'20\'1Csoft on crime\u8221\'20\'1D and preventing \u8220\'20\'1CNew York\u8217\'20\'19s police officers from doing their jobs\u8221\'20\'1D. James is indeed a Democrat, and if she\u8217\'20\'19s been trying to frustrate the police, evidence suggests {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://pix11.com/news/morning/mayor-adams-calls-nyc-the-safest-big-city-in-america-as-statistics-show-crime-is-down/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 she hasn\u8217\'20\'19t been very good at it}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.11pm BST\par \par \uc2 From the Guardian\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/lauren-aratani"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Lauren Aratani}}}\uc2 , here\u8217\'20\'19s more about \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s civil fraud trial happening in New York City today, and why it could have major financial consequences for the ex-president and his family:\par \par \uc2 Just a few miles south of Trump Tower in New York City, a judge on Monday will hear allegations of fraud within the \uc2 Trump Organization\uc2  in a trial that could see {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/donaldtrump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Donald Trump}}}\uc2  and his family business paying hundreds of millions of dollars in damages and that has already threatened to end his business career in the city where it started.\par \par \uc2 The {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/new-york"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 New York}}}\uc2  attorney general, Letitia James, has accused Trump of using false and misleading financial statements from 2011 to 2021 to make himself and his businesses wealthier, helping him broker deals and obtain financing. Based on her office\u8217\'20\'19s three-year investigation, James is arguing that Trump owes at least $250m for committing fraud.\par \par \uc2 During the three-year investigation, James found that Trump had exaggerated the value of 23 of his properties and assets to the tune of hundreds of millions or even billions of dollars. Trump used these financial statements to obtain favorable loans and make his net worth appear higher than it actually was.\par \par \uc2 Trump said he will appear in court on Monday. \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19m going to Court tomorrow morning to fight for my name and reputation,\u8221\'20\'1D he said on his Truth Social account on Sunday.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/oct/02/trump-fraud-case-new-york"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Trump fraud civil suit starting Monday threatens to end his business career}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.55pm BST\par \par \uc2 Trump heads to New York for civil fraud trial that could see business empire dismantled\par \par \uc2 Good morning, US politics blog readers. All eyes will be on a New York City courtroom this morning, where \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  is expected to appear for the start of a trial that will determine the amount he and his children must pay after a judge last week determined {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/sep/26/trump-liable-fraud-new-york"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 they committed fraud}}}\uc2 . Presided over by New York supreme court justice \uc2 Arthur Engoron\uc2 , the trial is scheduled to last until 22 December and the former president is on the witness list, as are his children, meaning they could be called to the stand.\par \par \uc2 The trial is among the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/jul/28/donald-trump-investigations-criminal-charges-tracker"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 many legal entanglements}}}\uc2  Trump is involved in, none of which appear to have dented his large lead in the race for the Republican presidential nomination. But the implications for Trump could be damning. If the judge agrees with New York attorney general Letitia James, he could impose a large fine on the former president, and potentially do grievous damage to the business empire Trump used as the platform to launch the political career that brought him to the White House.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s what else is happening today:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Democrats are caught in the middle as far-right Republicans plan to attempt to remove Kevin McCarthy as speaker of the House of Representatives. Do they sign on to the effort, or use it as leverage to save McCarthy, in exchange for major concessions? We\u8217\'20\'19ll hear lots about this today.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 California has a new senator: Laphonza Butler, the president of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights group EMILY\u8217\'20\'19s list, who governor \uc2 Gavin Newsom\uc2  appointed to fill the seat \uc2 Dianne Feinstein\uc2  vacated when she died last week.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Karine Jean-Pierre\uc2  will brief the White House press corps at 12.30pm eastern time, and perhaps elaborate on what \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  thinks of all the drama in Congress.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020231002eja2001xp\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
