\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Republican debate: Trump attacked for being absent as reports say he will skip third one too \u8211\'20\'13 as it happened\b0\par\par\uc2 Chris Stein and Maanvi Singh \par \uc2 8,330 \uc2 words\par \uc2 28 September 2023\par 04:07 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 This blog is now closed. You can read our latest pieces on the Republican debate here:Full story: Trump accused of being \u8216\'20\'18missing in action\u8217\'20\'19Key takeaways: absent Trump and bad jokes\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.59am BST\par \par \uc2 Closing summary\par \par \uc2 For two hours, the seven Republican candidates gathered in California {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/sep/27/republican-second-debate-2023-desantis-trump-speech-uaw-live-updates?page=with:block-6514a3808f08e6e1e6635187#block-6514a3808f08e6e1e6635187"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 duked it out }}}\uc2  over everything from energy to immigration, all {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/sep/27/republican-second-debate-2023-desantis-trump-speech-uaw-live-updates?page=with:block-6514c7088f08e6e1e663524c#block-6514c7088f08e6e1e663524c"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 in the absence of  }}}\uc2  over everything from energy to immigration, all {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/sep/27/republican-second-debate-2023-desantis-trump-speech-uaw-live-updates?page=with:block-6514c7088f08e6e1e663524c#block-6514c7088f08e6e1e663524c"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Donald Trump }}}\uc2  , the far-and-away frontrunner for the GOP\u8217\'20\'19s presidential nomination. We\u8217\'20\'19ll see if anything that was said on the debate stage at the Ronald Reagan Presidential Library this evening changed the contours of the race, but one thing is now clear: none of these candidates will share the debate stage with Trump. He\u8217\'20\'19s opted to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/sep/27/republican-second-debate-2023-desantis-trump-speech-uaw-live-updates?page=with:block-6514f3818f08e6e1e6635378#block-6514f3818f08e6e1e6635378"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 skip the third debate }}}\uc2  set for Miami in November, and his campaign is calling for the Republican Party to cancel it altogether.\par \par \uc2 Here are some highlights from tonight\u8217\'20\'19s event:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Nikki Haley\uc2  and Tim Scott {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/sep/27/republican-second-debate-2023-desantis-trump-speech-uaw-live-updates?page=with:block-6514ea3e8f0844f4dfe54aed#block-6514ea3e8f0844f4dfe54aed"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 squabbled over curtains }}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Mike Pence{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/sep/27/republican-second-debate-2023-desantis-trump-speech-uaw-live-updates?page=with:block-6514e0d78f0844f4dfe54a97#block-6514e0d78f0844f4dfe54a97"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 shared aspects of his marriage }}}\uc2  we never expected him to discuss.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Chris Christie\uc2  continued to goad Trump, who he says he will now refer to as \u8220\'20\'1CDonald Duck\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Haley {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/sep/27/republican-second-debate-2023-desantis-trump-speech-uaw-live-updates?page=with:block-6514e3e98f08e6e1e6635313#block-6514e3e98f08e6e1e6635313"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 jumped on }}}\uc2  entreprenneur \uc2 Vivek Ramaswamy\uc2  for joining controversial social media app TikTok. He argues its the best way to reach young voters.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 There was lots of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/sep/27/republican-second-debate-2023-desantis-trump-speech-uaw-live-updates?page=with:block-6514dd328f08ea4e57fcbdbe#block-6514dd328f08ea4e57fcbdbe"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 cross-talk and chaos }}}\uc2 . One of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/sep/27/republican-second-debate-2023-desantis-trump-speech-uaw-live-updates?page=with:block-6514e2548f0844f4dfe54aa5#block-6514e2548f0844f4dfe54aa5"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the most prolific interrupters }}}\uc2  was North Dakota governor \uc2 Doug Burgum\uc2  , who complained the moderators weren\u8217\'20\'19t calling on him.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.47am BST\par \par \uc2 The reviews of the second Republican presidential debate are rolling in from political analysts and they are \u8230\'20\'26 not great.\par \par \uc2 Larry Sabato\uc2  of the University of Virginia\u8217\'20\'19s Center for Politics:\par \par \uc2 enltrTruly awful. The whole thing. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/hashtag/GOPDebate?src=hash&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 #GOPDebate }}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 \uc2 Larry Sabato\uc2  (@LarrySabato) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/LarrySabato/status/1707209025283318197?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 September 28, 2023 }}}\uc2  (@LarrySabato)\par \par \uc2 Fernand R. Amandi of public opinion research firm Bendixen & Amandi:\par \par \uc2 enltrThe {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/hashtag/GOPDebate?src=hash&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 #GOPDebate }}}\uc2  tonight was the worst debate of any kind at any level I have ever seen in life.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Fernand R. Amandi (@AmandiOnAir) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/AmandiOnAir/status/1707233681109078233?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 September 28, 2023 }}}\par \par \uc2 GOP pollster Frank Luntz, who thought \uc2 Nikki Haley\uc2  and Tim Scott \u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/sep/27/republican-second-debate-2023-desantis-trump-speech-uaw-live-updates?page=with:block-6514ea3e8f0844f4dfe54aed#block-6514ea3e8f0844f4dfe54aed"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 argument about curtains }}}\uc2  was a low point:\par \par \uc2 enltrFighting over curtains? Really? That is embarrassing.\par \par \uc2 We're about to have a government shutdown and they're wasting time over curtains. Ridiculous. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/hashtag/GOPDebate?src=hash&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 #GOPDebate }}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/1wNGSPrZGs"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/1wNGSPrZGs }}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Frank Luntz (@FrankLuntz) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/FrankLuntz/status/1707227900838392266?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 September 28, 2023 }}}\par \par \uc2 But did think \uc2 Chris Christie\uc2  handled questions about \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  in a way other Republicans could learn from:\par \par \uc2 enltrChris Christie showed real pathos on the pro-life question.\par \par \uc2 He shows a way for Republicans to navigate the \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  issue. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/hashtag/GOPDebate?src=hash&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 #GOPDebate }}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/xA59gukhQH"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/xA59gukhQH }}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Frank Luntz (@FrankLuntz) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/FrankLuntz/status/1707228785421271310?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 September 28, 2023 }}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.36am BST\par \par \uc2 Trump to skip third debate - report\par \par \uc2 Republican rivals hoping to face \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  on the debate stage won\u8217\'20\'19t get their chance. CBS News reports that the former president will skip the third and final debate of the primary process, set for November in Miami:\par \par \uc2 enltrNEWS: \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  won\u8217\'20\'19t attend the 3rd presidential debate in Miami in November, his senior aide Chris LaCavita tells {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/CBSNews?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @cbsnews }}}\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/finnygo?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @finnygo }}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Ed O'Keefe (@edokeefe) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/edokeefe/status/1707235195693490336?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 September 28, 2023 }}}\par \par \uc2 In fact, the Trump campaign is out with a statement calling on the \uc2 Republican National Committee\uc2  to cancel the third debate entirely. Here\u8217\'20\'19s the campaign\u8217\'20\'19s senior advisor Chris LaCivita:\par \par \uc2 Tonight\u8217\'20\'19s GOP debate was as boring and inconsequential as the first debate, and nothing that was said will change the dynamics of the primary contest being dominated by President Trump. President Trump has a 40- or 50-point lead in the primary election and a 10-point lead over \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  in the general election, and it\u8217\'20\'19s clear that President Trump alone can defeat Biden.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 RNC\uc2  should immediately put an end to any further primary debates so we can train our fire on Crooked \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  and quit wasting time and money that could be going to evicting Biden from the White House.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.21am BST\par \par \uc2 Fact check: Pence claim he and Trump cut immigration by 90% not really true\par \par \uc2 Mike Pence\uc2  claimed that during his and \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s administration, they \u8220\'20\'1Creduced illegal immigration and asylum abuse by 90%.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 That\u8217\'20\'19s not really true.\par \par \uc2 The number of Border Patrol {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cbp.gov/sites/default/files/assets/documents/2021-Aug/U.S.%20Border%20Patrol%20Total%20Apprehensions%20%28FY%201925%20-%20FY%202020%29%20%28508%29.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 apprehensions }}}\uc2  was higher during the Trump administration than during the last four years of \uc2 Barack Obama\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s administration. There was a change in how \uc2 US Customs and Border Protection\uc2  reports migrant encounters during the pandemic, complicating some of this data \u8211\'20\'13 pre-pandemic, the agency reported enforcement actions taken under immigration law, but after, it also began reporting actions taken under the Title 42 public health policy that authorized officers to immediately send most migrants at the border back to Mexico.\par \par \uc2 Analysis by {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.politifact.com/factchecks/2022/dec/06/mike-pence/pences-claim-about-a-90-drop-in-illegal-immigratio/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Politifact }}}\uc2  found that Pence\u8217\'20\'19s 90% reduction figure could be approximated by comparing enforcement data from May 2019, the month that saw the highest number of apprehensions, with data from April 2020 \u8211\'20\'13 right as governments around the world moved to severe restrict travel due to the Covid-19 pandemic.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThat\u8217\'20\'19s a severely cherry-picked period,\u8221\'20\'1D the fact-checking group writes.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 4.25am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.10am BST\par \par \uc2 It\u8217\'20\'19s worth noting that the moderators\u8217\'20\'19 attempts to spur even more conflict between the candidates was not particularly well received.\par \par \uc2 None of them were willing to name another to be voted off the stage, or the island, as it were:\par \par \uc2 enltrFox News debate moderator Dana Perino: \u8220\'20\'1CWhich one of you on stage tonight should be voted off the island? Please use your marker to write your choice on the notepad in front of you. 15 seconds.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Led by \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2  , the candidates refuse to participate in the exercise. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/9pQMINqxbA"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/9pQMINqxbA }}}\uc2 , the candidates refuse to participate in the exercise.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 The Recount (@therecount) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/therecount/status/1707230132224561324?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 September 28, 2023 }}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.06am BST\par \par \uc2 Second Republican debate concludes\par \par \uc2 The candidates are now leaving the stage after the moderators wrapped up the second Republican presidential debate with a question that, fittingly, invoked \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  .\par \par \uc2 In the debate\u8217\'20\'19s final moments, the candidates were asked by the moderators to write down which other candidate they would \u8211\'20\'13 in the style of pioneering reality TV program Survivor \u8211\'20\'13 vote off the stage. \uc2 Chris Christie\uc2  chose Trump, the frontrunner for the nomination who did not attend.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThis guy has not only divided our party, he divided families all over this country. He\u8217\'20\'19s divided friends all over this country,\u8221\'20\'1D Christie said. \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19ve spoken to people and I know everyone else has, who have sat at Thanksgiving dinner or at a birthday party and can\u8217\'20\'19t have a conversation anymore if they disagree with \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  . He needs to be off the island and taken out of this process.\par \par \uc2 Vivek Ramaswamy\uc2  disagreed. \u8220\'20\'1CI think Trump was an excellent president. But the America first agenda does not belong to one man. It does not belong to \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  . It doesn\u8217\'20\'19t belong to me. It belongs to you, the people of this country. And the question is who\u8217\'20\'19s going to unite this country and take the America first agenda to the next level?\u8221\'20\'1D he said.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe did not just hunger for a single man, we hungered for the unapologetic pursuit of excellence and yes, I will respect \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  and his legacy because it\u8217\'20\'19s the right thing to do.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 And with that, the debate was over.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 4.09am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.59am BST\par \par \uc2 Call it the Squabble in South Carolina.\par \par \uc2 While the debate may be taking place in Simi Valley, California, the two candidates hailing from the Palmetto state \u8211\'20\'13 Senator Tim Scott and \uc2 Nikki Haley\uc2 , the state\u8217\'20\'19s former governor \u8211\'20\'13 just got into it over gas taxes, curtains and several other things.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CAs the \uc2 UN\uc2  ambassador, you literally put $50,000 on curtains in a $15m subsidized location,\u8221\'20\'1D Scott said, while Haley defiantly interjected, \u8220\'20\'1Cbring it, man.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CYou got bad information,\u8221\'20\'1D Haley, who served as \uc2 UN\uc2  ambassador under \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  , replied. \u8220\'20\'1COn the curtains, do your homework, Tim, because Obama bought those curtains.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CDid you send them back?\u8221\'20\'1D the senator asked.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s the state department!\u8221\'20\'1D Haley shot back at Scott. \u8220\'20\'1CDid you send them back? You\u8217\'20\'19re the one that works in Congress \u8230\'20\'26 You are scrapping right now!\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe do not intend to go ahead like this,\u8221\'20\'1D the moderator, \uc2 Stuart Varney\uc2  , said, before sending us all, mercifully, to a commercial break.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 4.10am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.48am BST\par \par \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2  was asked about curriculum in Florida that said, ens laved people \u8220\'20\'1Cdevelop skills which in some instances, could be apply for their personal benefit \u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 DeSantis called this \u8220\'20\'1Ca hoax that was perpetrated by \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  \u8221\'20\'1D, mispronouncing the vice-president\u8217\'20\'19s name. In fact, the quoted bit is taken straight from Florida\u8217\'20\'19s African American history {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.fldoe.org/core/fileparse.php/20653/urlt/6-4.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 standards }}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 In an impassioned speech reacting to the standard, Harris {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/jul/21/kamala-harris-florida-schools-black-history-slavery"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 said }}}\uc2  : \u8220\'20\'1CThey insult us in an attempt to gaslight us and we will not stand for it.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 4.11am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.45am BST\par \par \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2  just won himself some applause with a well-timed interjection to tout his accomplishments as Florida governor.\par \par \uc2 Amid bickering over government spending between \uc2 Nikki Haley\uc2  and Tim Scott, DeSantis piped up.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19m the only one up here who\u8217\'20\'19s gotten in the big fights and has delivered big victories for the people of Florida. And that\u8217\'20\'19s what it\u8217\'20\'19s all about,\u8221\'20\'1D DeSantis said to cheers.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CYou can always talk but when when it gets hot in there, when they\u8217\'20\'19re shooting arrows at you, are you going to stand up for parents rights, keep the state free? Are you going to be able to do all those things? And in the state of Florida because of our success, the Democratic party lies in ruins. We have won the big fights. We have turned our state into a Republican state.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.54am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.41am BST\par \par \uc2 Doug Burgum\uc2  really wants to answer these questions, but the moderators aren\u8217\'20\'19t having it.\par \par \uc2 They asked \uc2 Nikki Haley\uc2  elaborate on her energy policies \u8211\'20\'13 but not Burgum. \u8220\'20\'1CAs the only leader of an energy state, can I answer?\u8221\'20\'1D interjected Burgum, whose state has a sizable oil industry. But the answer the North Dakota governor got was no.\par \par \uc2 He tried again after \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2  was asked the same question, but was rebuffed. \u8220\'20\'1CWe can\u8217\'20\'19t talk over each other. We must respect each other,\u8221\'20\'1D moderator \uc2 Stuart Varney\uc2  insisted.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.41am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.31am BST\par \par \uc2 Fact check: Republicans on trans healthcare\par \par \uc2 As candidates address trans rights on stage, here\u8217\'20\'19s a bit of context.\par \par \uc2 Vivek Ramaswamy\uc2  said: \u8220\'20\'1CTransgenderism, especially in kids is a mental health disorder.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 This is false. Major medical organizations, like the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://www.vox.com/2015/6/8/8748341/ama-transgender-soldiers"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 American Medical Association }}}\uc2  and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://www.dsm5.org/documents/gender%20dysphoria%20fact%20sheet.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 American Psychiatric Association }}}\uc2  (APA), say being transgender is not a mental disorder. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.psychiatry.org/patients-families/gender-dysphoria/what-is-gender-dysphoria"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Gender dysphoria  }}}\uc2  is recognized as a medical condition that doctors agree should be remedied by offering gender-affirming treatment.\par \par \uc2 From \uc2 Mike Pence\uc2  : \u8220\'20\'1CThe Linn-Marr community schools in Iowa had a policy where you could you had to have a permission slip from your parents to get a Tylenol but you could get a gender transition plan without notifying your parents.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 This is misleading. Linn-Marr\u8217\'20\'19s policy directed educators to use students\u8217\'20\'19 chosen names, without consulting with parents. That\u8217\'20\'19s a far reach from a \u8220\'20\'1Cgender transition plan\u8221\'20\'1D. Children under 17 seeking gender affirming care such as hormone replacement therapy or gender affirming surgery.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 4.00am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.28am BST\par \par \uc2 Haley to Ramaswamy: 'Every time I hear you, I feel a little bit dumber'\par \par \uc2 Vivek Ramaswamy\uc2  was the most pilloried candidate at the previous debate, and will likely win that dubious distinction after this debate.\par \par \uc2 He recently joined TikTok, the controversial social media app many GOP candidates want to ban over allegations that it\u8217\'20\'19s tied to the Chinese Communist party. Asked why he was on the app, Ramamswamy cited its popularity with young people, and said: \u8220\'20\'1CThe answer is, I have a radical idea for the Republican party. We need to win elections, and part of how we win elections is reaching the next generation of young Americans where they are.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Nikki Haley\uc2  did not like that response. \u8220\'20\'1CHonestly, every time I hear you, I feel a little bit dumber for what you say,\u8221\'20\'1D she said, before going on to outline a number of privacy and national security concerns about the app.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.47am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.20am BST\par \par \uc2 Mike Pence\uc2  wants to \u8220\'20\'1Crepeal the Green New Deal\u8221\'20\'1D. Too bad it\u8217\'20\'19s never passed Congress or been signed into law\u8230\'20\'26\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1C\uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s Green New Deal agenda is good for Beijing and bad for Detroit. We ought to repeal the Green New Deal,\u8221\'20\'1D the former vice president said. \u8220\'20\'1CWe ought to repeal the Green New Deal.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The Green New Deal is a climate legislation proposal that was never passed. \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  did sign into law the Inflation Reduction Act, which includes {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/aug/11/biden-climate-bill-inflation-reduction-act"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 key climate provisions  }}}\uc2  is different.\par \par \uc2 Although the IRA includes major investments in clean energy technologies \u8211\'20\'13 some of which have relied on critical minerals controlled by China. But the landmark climate investment is also considered a key step in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://foreignpolicy.com/2022/09/16/inflation-reduction-act-critical-mineral-chains-congress-biden/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reducing }}}\uc2  reliance on China for these minerals by increasing domestic supply. And while ramping up domestic extraction has raised new environmental concerns, Pence\u8217\'20\'19s assertion is notably misleading.\par \par \uc2 The IRA\u8217\'20\'19s tax credits for electric vehicles, for example, come with the caveat that the materials used to manufacture the veible come from the US or countries with which the US has free trade agreements. The law also incentivizes domestic manufacturing.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.19am BST\par \par \uc2 Doug Burgum\uc2  did it again.\par \par \uc2 The moderators didn\u8217\'20\'19t call on him for a contentious question about social media app TikTok, so he just started talking, keeping the moderators from moving on to \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2  .\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe will have to cut your mic and I don\u8217\'20\'19t want to do that,\u8221\'20\'1D warned moderator Dana Perino. Burgum piped down.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.16am BST\par \par \uc2 Mike Pence\uc2  discusses his marriage \u8212\'20\'14 for better or worse\par \par \uc2 Raise your hand if you expected \uc2 Mike Pence\uc2  to discuss his sex life at this debate.\par \par \uc2 Us neither. But discuss it he did. \uc2 Chris Christie\uc2  laid the groundwork while responding to a question about how he would close educational gaps with minorities, which he turned into an attack on teachers unions.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThis public school system is no longer run by the public. It is run by the teachers unions in this country,\u8221\'20\'1D Christie said. \u8220\'20\'1CAnd when you have the president of the United States sleeping with a member of the teachers union, there is no chance that you could take the stranglehold away from the teachers unions.\u8221\'20\'1D That line was a reference to Jill Biden, who has taught at community colleges and is a union member.\par \par \uc2 It got weird when the moderators, a few minutes later, called on \uc2 Mike Pence\uc2  . \u8220\'20\'1CBy way of full disclosure, Chris, you\u8217\'20\'19ve mentioned the president\u8217\'20\'19s situation,\u8221\'20\'1D Pence said. \u8220\'20\'1CMy wife isn\u8217\'20\'19t a member of the teachers union, but I gotta admit I\u8217\'20\'19ve been sleeping with a teacher for 38 years.\u8221\'20\'1D OK Mike.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 4.20am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.11am BST\par \par \uc2 Fact check: Republicans claim crime is rife \u8211\'20\'13 but murder rate down\par \par \uc2 The Guardian\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s Lois Beckett, who has extensively covered gun violence, offers this context on the candidate\u8217\'20\'19s rhetoric on crime \u8230\'20\'26\par \par \uc2 As Republicans talk about fears of crime and crime overrunning our cities, it\u8217\'20\'19s worth noting that the best data we have so far suggests that, after an increase in killings during the early pandemic, the number of murders across the country fell substantially last year, and that, as crime analyst Jeff Asher has noted, murders appear to be falling even more this year.\par \par \uc2 The 2023 drop in murders began early in the year, when Asher\u8217\'20\'19s analysis of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theatlantic.com/ideas/archive/2023/06/us-murder-rate-decline-crime-statistics/674290/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 early data suggested }}}\uc2  that \u8220\'20\'1CUnited States may be experiencing one of the largest annual percent changes in murder ever recorded.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 enltrMurder fell 5.1% last year for the 29 states with \uc2 FBI\uc2  data already available. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/Crimealytics?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @Crimealytics }}}\uc2  : {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/VqJC736K5L"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/VqJC736K5L }}}\uc2  : {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/MUkPQHYK6e"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/MUkPQHYK6e }}}\uc2  :\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Matt Cravens (@mattcravens) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/mattcravens/status/1705036801138733206?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 September 22, 2023 }}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.16am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.08am BST\par \par \uc2 Fact check: claims death penalty threat would deter mass shootings\par \par \uc2 Would the the threat of the death penalty deter people from committing mass shootings? Lois Beckett offers some context \u8230\'20\'26\par \par \uc2 Mike Pence\uc2  volunteered his plan for preventing the toll mass shootings in the United States: \u8220\'20\'1CA federal expedited death penalty for anyone involved in a mass shooting.\u8221\'20\'1D He said he was disgusted that the teenager who committed the Parkland school shooting did not get a death sentence.\par \par \uc2 According to the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theviolenceproject.org/mass-shooter-database/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Violence Project }}}\uc2 , \u8220\'20\'1CSeventy-two per cent of mass shooters were {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://projects.voanews.com/mass-shootings/#"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 suicidal }}}\uc2  either before or {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://projects.voanews.com/mass-shootings/#"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 at the time of the shooting }}}\uc2 .\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Data from the \uc2 FBI\uc2  on {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.fbi.gov/file-repository/active-shooter-incidents-in-the-us-2022-042623.pdf/view"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 active shooter incidents in 2021 and 2022 }}}\uc2  also showed that a third to nearly a half of perpetrators of these shootings either died by suicide or were killed by police or other citizens during the attack.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 4.01am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.08am BST\par \par \uc2 Ilia Calder\u243\'00\'F3n wanted \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2  to explain {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/jul/21/kamala-harris-florida-schools-black-history-slavery"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Florida\u8217\'20\'19s controversial school curriculum }}}\uc2  that teaches students slaves learned some useful skills from their bondage.\par \par \uc2 As DeSantis launched into his response, Tim Scott, the lone major Republican contender who is Black, could be heard saying: \u8220\'20\'1CTake the line out. Just take the line out.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 DeSantis then said:\par \par \uc2 First of all, that\u8217\'20\'19s a hoax that was perpetrated by \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  \u8230\'20\'26 second of all, that was written by descendants of slaves. These are great Black history scholars. So we need to stop playing these games.\par \par \uc2 Scott was then asked to elaborate on his objections.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThere is not a redeeming quality in slavery. He and Kamala should have just taken the one sentence out. America has suffered because of slavery. But we\u8217\'20\'19ve overcome that. We are the greatest nation on Earth because we faced our demons in the mirror and made a decision,\u8221\'20\'1D the senator said.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.09am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.03am BST\par \par \uc2 The debate started with questions about Americans\u8217\'20\'19 sentiments about the economy. Dominic Rushe unpacked this in our {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/sep/15/biden-economy-bidenomics-poll-republicans-democrats-independents"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  new series }}}\uc2  called Confidence Crisis, which is examining why consumers feel frustrated by finances, even as the data shows a relatively strong picture:\par \par \uc2 The US has roared back from the Covid recession by official measures. But two-thirds of Americans are unhappy about the economy despite consistent reports that inflation is easing and unemployment is close to a 50-year low. And the poll suggests many are unaware of or don\u8217\'20\'19t believe the positive economic news the government has reported.\par \par \uc2 The results illustrate a dramatic political split on economic views \u8211\'20\'13 with Republicans far more pessimistic than Democrats. But unhappiness about the economy is widespread.\par \par \uc2 Two-thirds of respondents (68%) reported it\u8217\'20\'19s difficult to be happy about positive economic news when they feel financially squeezed each month (Republicans: 69%, Democrats: 68%).\par \par \uc2 Two-thirds of Americans (65%) believe that the economy is worse than the media makes it out to be rather than better (35%).\par \par \uc2 In August the unemployment rate was 3.8%, close to a 50-year low. But the poll found that 51% wrongly believe that unemployment is nearing a 50-year high rather than those who believe it\u8217\'20\'19s actually low (49%).\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.00am BST\par \par \uc2 Tonights\u8217\'20\'19 GOP presidential hopefuls are debating at stage not far from \uc2 Ronald Reagan\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s actual grave, which is outside the Ronald Reagan Presidential Foundation overlooking the Pacific.\par \par \uc2 enltrTonight\u8217\'20\'19s GOP debate is taking place not far from \uc2 Ronald Reagan\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s grave, which is at the Reagan library, with a view overlooking the Pacific. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/urjXerK35S"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/urjXerK35S }}}\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s grave, which is at the Reagan library, with a view overlooking the Pacific.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Lois Beckett (@loisbeckett) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/loisbeckett/status/1707195960143892761?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 September 28, 2023 }}}\par \par \uc2 (At the moment, it\u8217\'20\'19s right next to the large overflow tent where journalists are watching the debate.)\par \par \uc2 As The Guardian\u8217\'20\'19s David Smith wrote earlier, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/sep/27/ronald-reagan-library-republican-presidential-debate"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Regan\u8217\'20\'19s legacy looms large }}}\uc2  over this current debate. And it\u8217\'20\'19s not clear how happy Reagan would be with this current version of the Republican party.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.58am BST\par \par \uc2 Debate lapses into occasional chaos as candidates jostle for airtime\par \par \uc2 The debate thus far has occasionally lapsed into chaos as candidates jostle for airtime.\par \par \uc2 An early interrupter was North Dakota governor \uc2 Doug Burgum\uc2  , who is {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://pro.morningconsult.com/trackers/2024-gop-primary-election-tracker"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 way down in the polls }}}\uc2  and clamored to answer questions in instances the moderators passed him over.\par \par \uc2 But the kings of cross-talk thus far are Tim Scott and \uc2 Vivek Ramaswamy\uc2  who, as the below clip shows, paralyzed the debate for about two minutes by refusing to individually shut up:\par \par \uc2 enltrRepublican presidential candidates Tim Scott and \uc2 Vivek Ramaswamy\uc2  talk over each other for almost two whole minutes.\par \par \uc2 A telling accidental line by Ramaswamy: \u8220\'20\'1CThank you for speaking while I'm interrupting.\u8221\'20\'1D {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/AJ42OMWtwo"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/AJ42OMWtwo }}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 The Recount (@therecount) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/therecount/status/1707208410050011547?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 September 28, 2023 }}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.00am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.55am BST\par \par \uc2 Mike Pence\uc2  had a unique proposal to curb mass shootings in the US .\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI am sick and tired of these mass shootings happening in the United States of America, and if I\u8217\'20\'19m president of the United States, I\u8217\'20\'19m going to go to the \uc2 Congress of the United States\uc2  , and we\u8217\'20\'19re going to pass a federal expedited death penalty for anyone involved in a mass shooting so that they do meet their fate in months, not years,\u8221\'20\'1D the former vice-president said.\par \par \uc2 He cited the case of \uc2 Nikolas Cruz\uc2  , who killed 17 people in the Parkland school shooting in Florida, but who {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/nov/02/parkland-school-shooter-sentencing-life-without-parole"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a jury decided should be sentenced to life in prison }}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 4.01am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.52am BST\par \par \uc2 The topic is now fentanyl, a serious public health crisis, where Republican candidates are competing with each other for whose response is more extreme and militaristic.\par \par \uc2 Vivek Ramaswamy\uc2  said we \u8220\'20\'1Chave to seal that southern border. Building the wall is not enough. They\u8217\'20\'19re building cartel-financed tunnels underneath that wall, semitrucks can drive through them. We have to use our own military to seal the Swiss cheese at the southern border.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2  called for using \u8220\'20\'1Cthe US military to go after the Mexican drug cartels. They are killing our people.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The Florida governor vowed that \u8220\'20\'1Cthis border is going to be a day one issue for me as president. We\u8217\'20\'19re going to declare a national emergency, yes, we\u8217\'20\'19ll build the wall, we\u8217\'20\'19ll do remain in Mexico.\u8221\'20\'1D The latter is a controversial policy that forces asylum seekers to stay in Mexico while waiting for their claims to be processed.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.45am BST\par \par \uc2 Writing from Simi Valley, the Guardians\u8217\'20\'19s Lois Beckett, who spent the last few months covering Hollywood\u8217\'20\'19s historic double strike, notes that the candidates were quick to dismiss the unions\u8217\'20\'19 actual reasons for striking\u8230\'20\'26\par \par \uc2 There\u8217\'20\'19s been a lot of talking over each other so far this debate. But it\u8217\'20\'19s fascinating to hear GOP candidates immediately jump in to contest the claims of \u8220\'20\'1Cunion leaders\u8221\'20\'1D and offer their own explanations for why workers across industries, from actors and screenwriters to autoworkers, have been going on strike.\par \par \uc2 Different candidates offered their own spin on the same explanation: the problem is Biden, and Bidenomics, not any more systematic problems with America\u8217\'20\'19s economic system.\par \par \uc2 Mike Pence\uc2  started this off: \u8220\'20\'1CWhile the union bosses are talking about class warfare and talking about disparities in wages, I really believe what\u8217\'20\'19s driving that is Bidenomics have failed,\u8221\'20\'1D the former president said.\par \par \uc2 Nikki Haley\uc2  blamed Biden\u8217\'20\'19s spending policies for causing inflation. North Dakota Gov. \uc2 Doug Burgum\uc2  , a little-known candidate, appeared to blame subsidies for electric cars for the auto worker strike.\par \par \uc2 Interested to hear back from workers on the picket lines about what they think about GOP presidential candidates blaming Biden for their situations.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.43am BST\par \par \uc2 'We're gonna call you Donald Duck': Christie says Trump too scared to attend\par \par \uc2 Chris Christie\uc2  turned a question about crime fighting into an attack on \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  , the frontrunner for the Republican nomination who has snubbed this debate.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CAnd I want to look at a camera right now to tell you, Donald, I know you\u8217\'20\'19re watching. You can\u8217\'20\'19t help yourself. I know you\u8217\'20\'19re watching, OK,\u8221\'20\'1D the former New Jersey governor said.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CAnd you\u8217\'20\'19re not here tonight. Not because of polls, and not because of your indictments. You\u8217\'20\'19re not here tonight because you\u8217\'20\'19re afraid of being on the stage and defending your record. You\u8217\'20\'19re ducking these things. And let me tell you what\u8217\'20\'19s going to happen. You keep doing that, no one up here is gonna call you \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  any more. We\u8217\'20\'19re gonna call you Donald Duck.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.59am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.41am BST\par \par \uc2 Mike Pence\uc2  turned a question about how he would handle the issue of Dreamers, as undocumented people who were brought the United States are minors are called, into an opportunity to attack \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2  and tout his economic proposals.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CYou know, Ron, you talk a really good game about cutting spending, but you\u8217\'20\'19ve increased spending in Florida by 30%. When I was a member of Congress in 2006, right after Hurricane Katrina, you remember it. We stood our ground. I led house conservatives, we cut $100 billion out of the federal budget,\u8221\'20\'1D Pence said.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt can be done but as I said in the last debate, I\u8217\'20\'19ll say again, this is no time for on the job training. I\u8217\'20\'19m going to be ready on day one.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.39am BST\par \par \uc2 Vivek Ramaswamy\uc2  , who was born in the US to two non-citizen parents, gaining his citizenship and right to become US president via birthright citizenship, is an ardent supporter of ending birthright citizenship.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CMilitarize the southern border, stop funding sanctuary cities and end foreign aid to Mexico and Central America to end the incentives to come across. But I do go a step further,\u8221\'20\'1D Ramaswamy said. \u8220\'20\'1C favor ending birthright citizenship for the kids of illegal immigrants in this country.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Ramaswamy was confident that stripping birthright citizenship from the children of undocumented immigrants wouldn\u8217\'20\'19t be an issue, but legal scholars disagree. Here\u8217\'20\'19s \uc2 University of Chicago\uc2  law School\u8217\'20\'19s Aziz Huq discussing why \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/2018/10/30/us/politics/trump-birthright-citizenship.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 proposal }}}\uc2  to end birthright citizenship was problematic. Here\u8217\'20\'19s another {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.newsweek.com/republicans-want-end-birthright-citizenship-they-cant-opinion-1828277"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 analysis }}}\uc2  by Georgia College & State University\u8217\'20\'19s Nicholas Creel.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.31am BST\par \par \uc2 Univision\u8217\'20\'19s Ilia Calder\u243\'00\'F3n wanted to hear more from \uc2 Vivek Ramaswamy\uc2  on his call to deport all undocumented immigrants, including their children born in the US, and who are therefore citizens.\par \par \uc2 Ramaswamy\u8217\'20\'19s immigration policy is an outlier for its extremity, and on the debate stage, he made clear he was not backing down:\par \par \uc2 The Republicans on the stage are on the right side of this issue: militarize the southern border, stop funding sanctuary cities and end foreign aid to Mexico and Central America to end the incentives to come across. But I do go a step further, you\u8217\'20\'19re right about that Ilia. I favor ending birthright citizenship for the kids of illegal immigrants in this country.\par \par \uc2 Now the left will howl about the Constitution and the 14th amendment. The difference between me and them is I\u8217\'20\'19ve actually read the 14th amendment. What it says is that all persons born or naturalized in the United States, and subject to the laws and jurisdiction thereof are citizens. So nobody believes that the kid of a Mexican diplomat in this country enjoys birthright citizenship \u8211\'20\'13 not a judge or legal scholar in this country will disagree with me on that. Well, if the kid of a Mexican diplomat doesn\u8217\'20\'19t enjoy birthright citizenship, then neither does the kid of an illegal migrant who broke the law to come here.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.32am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.25am BST\par \par \uc2 Tim Scott, who was the first to speak tonight on the question of whether striking autoworkers should be fired, actually had a labor complaint filed against him for suggesting that strikers be made redundant.\par \par \uc2 Shawn Fain, the president of \uc2 UAW\uc2  , filed a complaint with the \uc2 National Labor Relations Board\uc2  after Scott suggested that auto workers on strike should be fired. At a recent event, Scott said: \u8220\'20\'1CI think \uc2 Ronald Reagan\uc2  gave us a great example when federal employees decided they were going to strike. He said, you strike, you\u8217\'20\'19re fired. Simple concept to me... To the extent that we can use that once again, absolutely.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Tonight, Scott said the government couldn\u8217\'20\'19t fire workers \u8211\'20\'13 before swiftly transitioning to a discussion about the US border policy.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.32am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.20am BST\par \par \uc2 Christie attacks Trump for skipping debate\par \par \uc2 Citing a comment from \uc2 Mike Pence\uc2  who blamed politicians like \uc2 Vivek Ramaswamy\uc2  for dysfunction in the GOP, Univision\u8217\'20\'19s Ilia Calder\u243\'00\'F3n asked \uc2 Chris Christie\uc2  : \u8220\'20\'1CIf the government shuts down, should voters blame populist Republicans?\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Christie was a prolific hurler of insults in the last debate, but he didn\u8217\'20\'19t take the bait here. \u8220\'20\'1CEverybody who\u8217\'20\'19s in Washington DC, they get sent down there to do the job and they\u8217\'20\'19ve been failing at doing the job for a very long time,\u8221\'20\'1D Christie replied, faulting the Biden administration and the Trump administration for increasing the national debt and, in turn, increasing inflation. He went on to criticize \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  for hiding \u8220\'20\'1Cin his basement\u8221\'20\'1D, while \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  \u8220\'20\'1Chides behind the walls of his golf clubs\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CHe should be in this room to answer those questions for the people you talked about who are suffering,\u8221\'20\'1D said Christie, one of the few open Trump critics onstage.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.31am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.12am BST\par \par \uc2 Ramaswamy, again, calls to 'drill, frack, burn coal'\par \par \uc2 Vivek Ramaswamy\uc2  was up next for his thoughts on the \uc2 United Auto Workers\uc2  strike, and reiterated a call for the aggressive expansion of polluting energy sources that he\u8217\'20\'19d made in the previous debate.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIf I was giving advice to those workers, I would say go picket in front of the White House in Washington DC, that\u8217\'20\'19s really where the protest needs to be,\u8221\'20\'1D Ramaswamy said.\par \par \uc2 He continued:\par \par \uc2 What we need is to deliver economic growth in this country. Unlock American energy, drill, frack, burn coal, embrace nuclear energy, put people back to work by no longer paying them more money to stay at home, stabilize the US dollar itself and rescind a majority of those unconstitutional federal regulations that are hampering our economy. That is how we unleash American exceptionalism. And that\u8217\'20\'19s not a Democratic vision or a Republican vision, that is an American vision.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.13am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.08am BST\par \par \uc2 The debate\u8217\'20\'19s first question is to Tim Scott, who is asked if he would fire striking autoworkers.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CObviously, the president of United States cannot fire anybody in the private sector,\u8221\'20\'1D said Scott, showing a keen understanding of what the president can and cannot do. He then criticized the \uc2 United Auto Workers\uc2  demands, before shifting to a tried and true subject for Republicans: border security:\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  should not be on the picket line, he should be on the southern border, working to close our southern border because it is unsafe, wide open and insecure, leading to the deaths of 70,000 Americans in the last 12 months because of fentanyl. It is devastating. Every county in America is now a border county because fentanyl has devastated Americans in every single state.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.05am BST\par \par \uc2 The debate\u8217\'20\'19s moderators have started by introducing the candidates and themselves.\par \par \uc2 Onstage is South Carolina senator Tim Scott, former New Jersey governor \uc2 Chris Christie\uc2  , Florida governor \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2  , North Dakota governor \uc2 Doug Burgum\uc2  , former \uc2 UN\uc2  ambassador \uc2 Nikki Haley\uc2 , entrepreneur \uc2 Vivek Ramaswamy\uc2  and former vice-president \uc2 Mike Pence\uc2  .\par \par \uc2 Moderating the debate is \uc2 Fox Business Network\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s \uc2 Stuart Varney\uc2  , Fox News\u8217\'20\'19s Dana Perino and Univision\u8217\'20\'19s Ilia Calder\u243\'00\'F3n.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.22am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.00am BST\par \par \uc2 David Smith, who is at the debate in Simi Valley, writes:\par \par \uc2 Gavin Newsom\uc2  , the governor of California, has been holding court in the debate \u8220\'20\'1Cspin room\u8221\'20\'1D, looking very much like a man trying not to look like he is running for president.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI was asked by the vice-president and president of the United States to make a case for the Biden record,\u8221\'20\'1D he told reporters by way of explaining his presence.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe winner of tonight\u8217\'20\'19s debate is clear. It\u8217\'20\'19s \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  and it\u8217\'20\'19s the Biden presidency and the extraordinary job he\u8217\'20\'19s done in the last few years to take unemployment that was 14.7% down to 3.8%. To take inflation, a global phenomenon, from 9.1 to 3.7%.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Newsom exchanged warm greetings with Fox News host \uc2 Sean Hannity\uc2  , who will next month moderate a debate between the California governor and the Florida governor, \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2  .\par \par \uc2 Newsom told the media: \u8220\'20\'1C\uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2  is running for president of United States and he wants to, in the middle of his presidential campaign, debate a governor of California. Think about it: it\u8217\'20\'19s disqualifying. You can goat someone this easy? Can you imagine with Kim Jong-un?\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 And he said of the looming government shutdown: \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s like three blind mice. \uc2 Marjorie Taylor Greene\uc2  , Gaettz, McCarthy are walking us off a cliff. I mean, it\u8217\'20\'19s student government. In nearly 30 years there\u8217\'20\'19s been five shutdowns. They have one thing in common: five Republican speakers.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.08am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.54am BST\par \par \uc2 Republican candidates take stage for second presidential debate\par \par \uc2 The seven Republicans who have qualified for the second debate of the 2024 presidential primary are now on stage at the Ronald Reagan Presidential Library in Simi Valley, California.\par \par \uc2 The debating should start in a few minutes, and we\u8217\'20\'19ll follow it live here.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.53am BST\par \par \uc2 In Michigan, meanwhile, \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  is trying to position himself as an ally to striking blue-collar auto workers \u8211\'20\'13 against the cries of union leaders who have said a second term for the former president would be a \u8220\'20\'1Cdisaster\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 United Auto Workers\uc2  have witheld an endorsement in the presidential race, but leaders have repeatedly questioned Trump\u8217\'20\'19s record. Tonight, he\u8217\'20\'19ll be speaking at Drake Enterprises in Clinton Township, north of Detroit, a nonunion shop.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI find a pathetic irony that the former president is going to hold a rally for union members at a nonunion business,\u8221\'20\'1D said Shawn Fain, the president of the \uc2 UAW\uc2  .\par \par \uc2 enltrCNN\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/wolfblitzer?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @WolfBlitzer }}}\uc2  talks to \uc2 United Auto Workers\uc2  President Shawn Fain about former President \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s planned trip to Michigan and if he would be willing to meet with Trump. Hear his response on {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/CNNSitRoom?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @CNNSitRoom }}}\uc2 . {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/SHPVRsu8L2"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/SHPVRsu8L2 }}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 CNN (@CNN) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/CNN/status/1706801528260939853?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 September 26, 2023 }}}\par \par \uc2 Fain said he wouldn\u8217\'20\'19t meet with Trump during he visit.\par \par \uc2 Trump claimed there were thousands at the rally, though there appeared to be a few hundred in the crowd. Several of those who spoke with \uc2 The Guardian\uc2  said they are small business owners, or work for small businesses.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThat\u8217\'20\'19s the thing \u8211\'20\'13 there are people who are union, but there\u8217\'20\'19s also a whole bunch of us who are not and who work for small businesses, and we are more pro-Trump,\u8221\'20\'1D said Laura D, who lives in nearby Mt Clemens.\par \par \uc2 Tom Perkins contributed reporting\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.24am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.47am BST\par \par \uc2 From August, here\u8217\'20\'19s the Guardian\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/mary-yang"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Mary Yang }}}\uc2  with a look at where the Republican candidates stand on the issues. They probably haven\u8217\'20\'19t changed their minds much since then:\par \par \uc2 Republicans vying for the 2024 party nomination are set to take the stage in Milwaukee, Wisconsin, on Wednesday night for the first debate of the primary season.\par \par \uc2 The candidates will certainly throw punches at each other and at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/donaldtrump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Donald Trump }}}\uc2 , who has a significant lead in polls but is skipping the debate. But it\u8217\'20\'19s also a chance for each candidate to present their policy agenda and voice their stance on key voter issues such as \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  and aid to Ukraine.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s where each candidate in Wednesday\u8217\'20\'19s debate stands on issues such as \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , immigration, the economy and continued aid to Ukraine.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/aug/22/republican-candidate-views-debate-desantis-ramaswamy-christie"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 From \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  to January 6: where each Republican candidate in the debate stands on big issues }}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.37am BST\par \par \uc2 One presidential candidate you can expect to hear plenty from tonight, and about, is \uc2 Vivek Ramaswamy\uc2  . He took the stage in Milwaukee last month with the kind of no-compromises, no-concerns rhetoric that was straight out of the Trump playbook, and was in turn jumped on by pretty much everyone else on stage, who called him too inexperienced for the White House. Here\u8217\'20\'19s the Guardian\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/martin-pengelly"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Martin Pengelly }}}\uc2  with a look back at his inaugural debate appearance:\par \par \uc2 Vivek Ramaswamy\uc2  , the 38-year-old biotech entrepreneur running {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://projects.fivethirtyeight.com/polls/president-primary-r/2024/national/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 third in Republican polling }}}\uc2 , emerged in the absence of \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  as a surprise focus of the first debate of the Republican primary, showing scant respect for other candidates and drawing heavy fire in return.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe live in a dark moment,\u8221\'20\'1D Ramaswamy declaimed, in the distinctly Trumpian and conspiratorial fashion that has become a hallmark of his campaign.\par \par \uc2 Ramaswamy\u8217\'20\'19s bid for the Republican nomination has been hit by recent scandals over remarks that suggested sympathy for conspiracy theories around the 9/11 terrorist attacks and the January 6 assault on the Capitol. But he has sought to portray himself as a Trump-like outsider taking on the establishment with his extreme views.\par \par \uc2 All the other presidential candidates onstage in Milwaukee, Ramaswamy repeatedly said, were \u8220\'20\'1Cbought and paid for\u8221\'20\'1D by donors.\par \par \uc2 After all eight candidates declined to raise their hands when asked if they believed human behavior was causing the climate crisis, Ramaswamy jumped in, stridently rapping out: \u8220\'20\'1CUnlock American energy, drill, frack, burn coal, embrace nuclear.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/aug/23/vivek-ramaswamy-focus-republican-debate"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Combative Vivek Ramaswamy emerges as surprise focal point of GOP debate }}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.26am BST\par \par \uc2 First debate recap: lots of squabbling, no breakthroughs\par \par \uc2 About a month ago, Republican presidential candidates gathered in Milwaukee for the first debate of the presidential cycle. \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  opted to skip it, and the lineup of candidates was almost the same as it will be this evening. The lone candidate who qualified for the first debate but failed to make it to the second is the Arkansas governo,r Asa Hutchinson, whose low name recognition and steadfast opposition to Trump has few takers in the GOP.\par \par \uc2 The first parley of GOP candidates was characterized by a cross-fire squabbling and insults, much of it directed at \uc2 Vivek Ramaswamy\uc2  , the entrepreneur whose lack of political experience was seized on by the veterans of various elected offices onstage. Meanwhile, none of the eight candidates had the sort of breakthrough moment that represents the best-case scenario for a presidential debate appearance. If anything, the contours of the Republican primary were largely the same after the debate as they were before it: Trump remains the frontrunner in polls, and all the other candidates are essentially fighting for scraps. If there was a big loser, you might say it was Florida\u8217\'20\'19s governor, \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2  , who at the start of the year looked like he\u8217\'20\'19d run a strong challenge to Trump, but whose support has markedly flagged in recent polls.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s more from the Guardian\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/davidsmith"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 David Smith }}}\uc2  on what we learned from the first Republican presidential debate:\par \par \uc2 The winners of the first Republican presidential primary debate are \u8230\'20\'26 \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  and \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  .\par \par \uc2 Eight candidates who took the stage in Milwaukee tore pieces out of each other while failing to distinguish themselves. They revealed a party of chaos and discord that has veered right of the mainstream on issues such as \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , education, immigration and the climate crisis. It was a two-hour campaign ad for the Democrats broadcast by Fox News.\par \par \uc2 The Republican contenders also failed to dent Trump who, with a huge lead in opinion polls, skipped the event in favour of a prerecorded interview with the former Fox News host \uc2 Tucker Carlson\uc2  . He told Carlson he did not feel like being on stage to be \u8220\'20\'1Charassed by people that shouldn\u8217\'20\'19t even be running for president\u8221\'20\'1D \u8211\'20\'13 a decision that he will now feel was vindicated.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/aug/24/a-republican-debate-that-offered-no-alternative-to-trump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 A Republican debate that offered no alternative to Trump }}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.25am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.24am BST\par \par \uc2 Tom Perkins writes from Michigan:\par \par \uc2 The Republican frontrunner won\u8217\'20\'19t on the debate stage tonight.\par \par \uc2 Instead, \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  is an industrial park in Clinton Township, Michigan, preparing to make remarks at an auto supply shop\par \par \uc2 Hundreds of supporters lining the street erupted in cheers moments ago as the former president\u8217\'20\'19s motorcade pulled in. Trump\u8217\'20\'19s address today comes after {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/sep/26/uaw-strike-biden-visit-update-trump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Joe Biden joined }}}\uc2  striking \uc2 United Auto Workers\uc2  on the picket line in Wayne, Michigan yesterday.\par \par \uc2 The gathering has all the festive and sometimes surreal energy often part of Trump rallies. In one spot, supporters bang on drums, breaking to yell \u8220\'20\'1CFreedom!\u8221\'20\'1D, and drawing loud cheers from up and down the street. Many are draped in Trump 2024 fags, another flag shows Trump as a Rambo-life figure holding a grenade launcher. Another declares \u8220\'20\'1CMy governor is an idiot\u8221\'20\'1D, a reference to Michigan governor \uc2 Gretchen Whitmer\uc2  .\par \par \uc2 Trump has positioned himself as the champion of workers and unions, and Ed Sands, a 73-year-old retired auto supplier employee, buys it: Trump is \u8220\'20\'1Cthe only one who gives a shit about working people,\u8221\'20\'1D he said.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1C\uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  , \uc2 Hillary Clinton\uc2  , Obama \u8211\'20\'13 they were all terrible for Macomb County, jobs went to China, south, and you see all these people here today because Trump will bring them back,\u8221\'20\'1D Sands added.\par \par \uc2 The former president\u8217\'20\'19s return to office is all but guaranteed, Sands said. \u8220\'20\'1CLook around you, look at these people. Do you think he is going to lose? Do you?\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Christopher Demopolis, 35, who works in heating and cooling, echoed that sentiment, and said his \uc2 UAW\uc2  base will play a role.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI don\u8217\'20\'19t see why he won\u8217\'20\'19t Michigan next time around \u8211\'20\'13 a lot of this is going to determine it,\u8221\'20\'1D he said, motioning to the lively crowd. \u8220\'20\'1CTrump supports the workers, Biden supports the leaders.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.11am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.13am BST\par \par \uc2 Ronald Reagan\uc2  is a Republican icon, and his presidential library will play host to tonight\u8217\'20\'19s debate. But as the Guardian\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/davidsmith"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 David Smith }}}\uc2  reports, it is unlikely the late former president would think much of the direction his party has recently taken:\par \par \uc2 Tourists posed for photos beside the presidential seal, peered inside the cockpit, studied the nuclear football and gazed at a desk where a \u8220\'20\'1C\uc2 Ronald Reagan\uc2  \u8221\'20\'1D jacket slung over the chair, page of handwritten notes and jelly bean jar made it appear as if the 40th US president could saunter back at any moment.\par \par \uc2 Air Force One is the star attraction at the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.reaganlibrary.gov/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Ronald Reagan Presidential Library and Museum }}}\uc2  in Simi Valley, California. But on Wednesday it is competing for attention with a curving Starship Enterprise-style stage set featuring seven lecterns and microphones for the second {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.washingtonpost.com/elections/2023/09/26/reagan-gop-presidential-candidates/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Republican presidential primary debate }}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The Reagan library describes this as \u8220\'20\'1Cthe Super Bowl\u8221\'20\'1D of Republican debates, against the dramatic backdrop of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.reaganfoundation.org/library-museum/permanent-exhibitions/air-force-one/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the Boeing 707  }}}\uc2  that flew seven presidents and close to the granite gravesite where {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/news/2004/jun/07/guardianobituaries.past"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Reagan }}}\uc2  was buried in 2004, looking across a majestic valley towards the Pacific Ocean.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CAs a new field of Republicans make their case to be the next President, the legacy of \uc2 Ronald Reagan\uc2  looms larger than ever,\u8221\'20\'1D the Ronald Reagan Presidential Foundation and Institute, which sustains the library, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://view.reply.reaganfoundation.org/?qs=76482167301bedcc1721bdfd6dabbbbc63dea52dae26f7176688fda3b9c7f9f9ee0922fe42c679032b38001f09eacf08f1a29e7babf7d497adef03ec422a570524e9decae47af88fad13b1e3c19595719f63f22bf6ff2f45"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 said in an email }}}\uc2  statement that will be put to the test at 9pm ET. For there are some who argue that Reagan would no longer recognise a Republican party that now belongs to \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  .\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/sep/27/ronald-reagan-library-republican-presidential-debate"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \u8216\'20\'18Almost a troll of the legacy\u8217\'20\'19: Reagan\u8217\'20\'19s spirit looms over Republican debate }}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.10am BST\par \par \uc2 How to watch the debate\par \par \uc2 Tonight\u8217\'20\'19s debate at the Ronald Regan presidential library in Simi Valley, California begins at 9pm eastern time, and will be broadcast on Fox News and \uc2 Fox Business Network\uc2  . For Spanish-language viewers, it will be carried on Univision, according to the Associated Press.\par \par \uc2 It\u8217\'20\'19s expected to last two hours, and will be moderated by \uc2 Fox Business Network\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s \uc2 Stuart Varney\uc2  , Fox News\u8217\'20\'19s Dana Perino and Univision\u8217\'20\'19s Ilia Calder\u243\'00\'F3n.\par \par \uc2 And will, of course, be covering it live on this blog.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.08am BST\par \par \uc2 Where's Trump?\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  is skipping the second debate to visit Detroit auto workers instead.\par \par \uc2 He will attempt to position himself as an ally of working-class voters in Michigan \u8211\'20\'13 a Democratic-leaning swing state he carried in his upset 2016 election victory \u8211\'20\'13 by promising to raise wages and protect jobs if returned to the White House.\par \par \uc2 The former president is the clear frontrunner for the GOP\u8217\'20\'19s presidential nomination and will at 8pm eastern time, just before the debate starts, speak before a crowd of current and former \uc2 United Auto Workers (UAW)\uc2  members at Drake Enterprises, a nonunion manufacturer in Clinton Township, about a half-hour outside Detroit.\par \par \uc2 A Trump campaign radio ad released last week and airing in Detroit and Toledo, Ohio, praised autoworkers, and said the former president has \u8220\'20\'1Calways had their back\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 This is the second debate in a row Trump has skipped. Rather than attend the inaugural GOP debate in Milwaukee, Trump gave an interview to conservative commentator \uc2 Tucker Carlson\uc2  , which was posted on X, the social network owned by billionaire \uc2 Elon Musk\uc2  and formerly known as \uc2 Twitter\uc2  .\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.07am BST\par \par \uc2 Who qualified for the second Republican debate?\par \par \uc2 Seven candidates have qualified for the second Republican primary debate but former Arkansas governor \uc2 Asa Hutchinson\uc2  did not make the cut this time.\par \par \uc2 Taking part this time are Florida governor \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2  , South Carolina senator Tim Scott, former vice-president \uc2 Mike Pence\uc2  , former \uc2 UN\uc2  envoy \uc2 Nikki Haley\uc2 , entrepreneur \uc2 Vivek Ramaswamy\uc2  , former New Jersey governor \uc2 Chris Christie\uc2  and \uc2 Doug Burgum\uc2  .\par \par \uc2 Candidates needed at least 3% support in two national polls or 3% in one national poll and two polls from Iowa, New Hampshire, Nevada or South Carolina \u8211\'20\'13 all early-voting states.\par \par \uc2 The candidates also need at least 50,000 unique donors (200 of those need to come from 20 states or territories) and they had to sign a pledge promising to support the eventual nominee.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 1.07am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.00am BST\par \par \uc2 Republicans \u8212\'20\'14 but not Trump \u8212\'20\'14 to duke it out in second debate of presidential primary\par \par \uc2 Good evening, US politics blog readers, and thanks for joining us as the Guardian\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/maanvi-singh"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Maanvi Singh }}}\uc2  and I cover the second debate of Republican presidential candidates. This evening\u8217\'20\'19s face-off takes place at the \uc2 Ronald Reagan\uc2  presidential library in Simi Valley, California, but if you know only one thing about this debate, know this: \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  , who {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://projects.fivethirtyeight.com/polls/president-primary-r/2024/national/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 polls show has an overwhelming lead }}}\uc2  in the race for the GOP nomination, will not attend. The debate stage will instead feature seven candidates, including Florida\u8217\'20\'19s governor \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2  , Trump\u8217\'20\'19s former \uc2 UN\uc2  ambassador \uc2 Nikki Haley\uc2 , his ex-vice-president \uc2 Mike Pence\uc2  and South Carolina\u8217\'20\'19s senator Tim Scott. We\u8217\'20\'19ll tell you more about who else is there, and what Trump is doing instead, a little later.\par \par \uc2 That said, there\u8217\'20\'19s still plenty of news to be made at this debate. Here\u8217\'20\'19s what we\u8217\'20\'19ll be watching for:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The federal government is on the cusp of shutting down for the 11th time since 1980 due to a protracted dispute over spending among Republicans, mostly in the House. Will the candidates take sides in the spending battle? And if so, will they support speaker Kevin McCarthy and his attempts to placate all wings of his party, or the insurgent Republicans who disputes over spending, border security and parliamentary tactics may soon grind much of the government to a halt?\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Trump has {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/sep/17/trump-interview-democratic-principles-abortion-rights"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 warned his fellow Republicans }}}\uc2  against stringent \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  bans that keep the procedure off limits in cases of rape, incest or health complications. Will the candidates join his call, or back hardline restrictions \u8211\'20\'13 perhaps even a federal ban?\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  is the target of an impeachment inquiry launched by House Republicans, even though {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.washingtonpost.com/opinions/2023/09/15/congressman-ken-buck-biden-impeachment/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 some of their own lawmakers }}}\uc2  don\u8217\'20\'19t think there\u8217\'20\'19s enough of a case against the president. Do the candidates agree, or do they think House Republicans should press on, even though Democrats\u8217\'20\'19 control of the Senate means there\u8217\'20\'19s practically no chance Biden will be removed from office?\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020230928ej9s0005m\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
