\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Judge in 2020 election meddling trial rejects call to recuse - as it happened\b0\par\par\uc2 Chris Stein (now); L\u233\'00\'E9onie Chao-Fong and Maya Yang (earlier) \par \uc2 11,112 \uc2 words\par \uc2 28 September 2023\par 00:24 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 This live blog is now closed. We\u8217\'20\'19re covering the Republican second debate \u8211\'20\'13 once again minus Trump \u8211\'20\'13 in a standalone live blog, which you can follow here:Republican second debate \u8211\'20\'13 live updates\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.05am BST\par \par \uc2 Follow our debate blog!\par \par \uc2 We\u8217\'20\'19re about to close down the US politics live blog, but the evening\u8217\'20\'19s news is far from over. The second debate of the Republican presidential primary starts at 9pm eastern time at the \uc2 Ronald Reagan\uc2  presidential library in California, and we\u8217\'20\'19ll be covering it live on our new blog, which you can read below:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/sep/27/republican-second-debate-2023-desantis-trump-speech-uaw-live-updates"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Republican debate live: seven candidates \u8211\'20\'13 but not Trump \u8211\'20\'13 to face off in California}}}\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s a recap of what happened today:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Federal judge Tanya Chutkan{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/sep/27/trump-org-fraud-uaw-biden-government-shutdown-funding-politics-live?filterKeyEvents=false&page=with:block-6514a2918f08ea4e57fcbc31#block-6514a2918f08ea4e57fcbc31"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 declined to recuse herself}}}\uc2  from \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s trial on charges related to overturning the 2020 election.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The apparently impending government shutdown could disrupt air travel in the United States, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/sep/27/trump-org-fraud-uaw-biden-government-shutdown-funding-politics-live?page=with:block-651474ff8f08e6e1e6635047#block-651474ff8f08e6e1e6635047"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the Biden administration warned}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Senator Bob Menendez{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/sep/27/trump-org-fraud-uaw-biden-government-shutdown-funding-politics-live?page=with:block-651439338f08ea4e57fcb715#block-651439338f08ea4e57fcb715"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pleaded not guilty}}}\uc2  to corruption-related charges in his initial court appearance.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 United Auto Workers\uc2  president Shawn Fain{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/sep/27/trump-org-fraud-uaw-biden-government-shutdown-funding-politics-live?page=with:block-6514347a8f0844f4dfe543d3#block-6514347a8f0844f4dfe543d3"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 will not meet with Trump}}}\uc2  when he visits Michigan this evening. Fain, however, joined \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  yesterday, when the president appeared with striking union members on a picket line in the state.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 House speaker Kevin McCarthy{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/sep/27/trump-org-fraud-uaw-biden-government-shutdown-funding-politics-live?page=with:block-651451b98f08e6e1e6634e3c#block-651451b98f08e6e1e6634e3c"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 said he would not}}}\uc2  put a short-term funding measure passed by the Senate up for a vote, saying he doesn\u8217\'20\'19t see enough support for it among his Republicans. The development is an ominous sign for efforts to halt a shutdown.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 1.16am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.56am BST\par \par \uc2 Back in the Senate, Fox News reports that lawmakers have approved a dress code mandating men wear long pants, coats and ties \u8211\'20\'13 exactly the sort of thing Pennsylvania\u8217\'20\'19s freshman senator \uc2 John Fetterman\uc2  does not wear.\par \par \uc2 The changes came after the Senate\u8217\'20\'19s Democratic leader \uc2 Chuck Schumer\uc2  effectively {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/sep/19/fetterman-us-senate-dress-code"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 eliminated its dress code}}}\uc2  in what was seen as a way to allow Fetterman to wear his trademark hoodie and shorts when casting votes. But his fellow senators did not like that, and have thus codified a dress code requiring formal wear:\par \par \uc2 enltrSenate adopts dress code requring coats, ties and long pants for men on the floor. Dress code is specific to men. Here\u8217\'20\'19s the text of the resolution: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/P2pXajLVjW"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/P2pXajLVjW}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Chad Pergram (@ChadPergram) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/ChadPergram/status/1707179928649703609?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 September 27, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.30am BST\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s the Guardian\u8217\'20\'19s Joan E Greve with a preview of tonight\u8217\'20\'19s debate of Republican presidential contenders, which kicks off at 9pm eastern time but will not feature \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , the far and away frontrunner:\par \par \uc2 Seven Republican presidential contenders gathered in California on Wednesday night for the second primary debate of the 2024 election season, but the absence of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/donaldtrump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Donald Trump}}}\uc2 , the clear frontrunner in the race for the party\u8217\'20\'19s nomination, again loomed large over the event.\par \par \uc2 Seven candidates qualified for the second debate, held at the Ronald Reagan Presidential Foundation & Institute in Simi Valley, California. Those candidates were \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2 , the Florida governor, the former vice-president \uc2 Mike Pence\uc2 , the former \uc2 UN\uc2  ambassador and South Carolina governor Nikki Haley, Senator Tim Scott of South Carolina, the entrepreneur {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/vivek-ramaswamy"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Vivek Ramaswamy}}}\uc2 , the former New Jersey governor \uc2 Chris Christie\uc2 , and the North Dakota governor \uc2 Doug Burgum\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Asa Hutchinson\uc2 , the former Arkansas governor who participated in the first primary debate, did not appear on Wednesday because he failed to meet the heightened polling requirements outlined by the \uc2 Republican National Committee\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Trump skipped the event \u8211\'20\'13 as he skipped last month\u8217\'20\'19s debate \u8211\'20\'13 and instead delivered a speech in Michigan, where auto workers have gone on strike to demand pay increases. A day earlier, \uc2 Joe Biden{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/sep/26/biden-joins-uaw-strike-update-detroit"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 joined}}}\uc2  some of the striking workers on the picket line, and the back-to-back events provided an odd preview of the likely matchup in the 2024 general election.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/sep/27/republican-candidates-second-debate-polls-california-reagan-library"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Republican contenders gather for key debate with Trump again absent}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.17am BST\par \par \uc2 Here are more scenes from Simi Valley, California, where the Ronal Reagan Presidential Library will host this evening\u8217\'20\'19s debate between seven Republican presidential candidates:\par \par \uc2 Trump supporters gather near the entrance to the Ronald Reagan Presidential Library. Photograph: Frederic J Brown/AFP/Getty Images Attendees arrive ahead of the second Republican presidential primary debate at the Ronald Reagan Presidential Library. Photograph: Robyn Beck/AFP/Getty Images Police do a security sweep ahead of the second Republican presidential primary debate at the Ronald Reagan Presidential Library. Photograph: Robyn Beck/AFP/Getty Images\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.03am BST\par \par \uc2 Judge in 2020 election meddling case responds: 'Justice demands that judges not recuse without cause'\par \par \uc2 The federal judge presiding in \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s criminal case over his efforts to overturn the 2020 election results rejected his request that she recuse herself on Wednesday, ruling that the former president failed to show her previous comments about his role in the January 6 Capitol attack meant she could not be impartial.\par \par \uc2 The decision means the case remains with US district judge \uc2 Tanya Chutkan\uc2 , who was randomly assigned it after Trump was indicted last month on charges that he unlawfully conspired to obstruct the peaceful transfer of power, though Trump can appeal to the DC circuit for a special order known as a mandamus.\par \par \uc2 Trump has long complained that Chutkan was biased against him based on remarks she made about him during sentencing in other January 6 riot defendant cases. But he faced an uphill struggle in trying to get Chutkan to recuse because, to succeed, he needed to satisfy a particularly high evidentiary threshold.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CJustice \u8230\'20\'26 demands that judges not recuse without cause. \u8216\'20\'18In the wrong hands, a disqualification motion is a procedural weapon to harass opponents and delay proceedings,\u8221\'20\'1D Chutkan said in her ruling, a line with resonance given Trump has suggested his overarching legal strategy is to delay his cases beyond the 2024 election.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 12.05am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.51pm BST\par \par \uc2 A regular presence in the media tent at primary debates is {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://deanofstudents.umich.edu/profile/aaron-kall-0"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Aaron Kall}}}\uc2 , director of debate for the \uc2 University of Michigan\uc2  Debate Program.\par \par \uc2 He took his seat early in a media tent erected in the grounds of the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.reaganlibrary.gov/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Ronald Reagan Presidential Library and Museum}}}\uc2 , which is laid out in Spanish Mission architectural style with red tiled roof and central courtyard in sunny Simi Valley, California.\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  is staying away again but Kall will be looking out to see how much he features in tonight\u8217\'20\'19s contest. \u8220\'20\'1CIn {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/aug/24/a-republican-debate-that-offered-no-alternative-to-trump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the first debate in Milwaukee}}}\uc2 , there was only about 10 or 12 minutes where he was discussed,\u8221\'20\'1D he said, competing with the Fox Business channel booming from loudspeakers. \u8220\'20\'1CThere were solid performances \u8211\'20\'13 Ramaswamy, Haley, DeSantis all did well \u8211\'20\'13 but they didn\u8217\'20\'19t narrow the gap at all. In fact, Trump only increased his lead in the month since the Milwaukee debate.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CPart of that was because he really wasn\u8217\'20\'19t engaged by the candidates and the only time he was discussed were things that would help him: if he was criminally convicted, they would support him and maybe pardon him. So he\u8217\'20\'19s got to play a bigger role in the debate tonight, even if he\u8217\'20\'19s not here, for the candidates to have any chance of narrowing that gap at least a little bit to give them some momentum heading into future debates.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Asa Hutchinson\uc2 , the former governor of Arkansas, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nwahomepage.com/news/asa-hutchinson-fails-to-qualify-for-second-republican-presidential-debate/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 failed to qualify}}}\uc2  for the debate this time. For some candidates, Kall noted, tonight might be the last chance to stop Trump. \u8220\'20\'1CThe thresholds are only increasing so it\u8217\'20\'19s going to be much tougher to even qualify for the Miami debate in November. There are fewer debates this cycle and so it\u8217\'20\'19s really reaching a point of now or never for the inevitability of Trump as the nominee.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.30pm BST\par \par \uc2 Rather than attend this evening\u8217\'20\'19s debate of Republican presidential candidates, \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  will be in Michigan, addressing blue-collar workers in a state that will be crucial to his campaign to return to the White House.\par \par \uc2 His visit comes {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/sep/26/biden-joins-uaw-strike-update-detroit"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a day after }}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/sep/26/biden-joins-uaw-strike-update-detroit"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Joe Biden}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/sep/26/biden-joins-uaw-strike-update-detroit"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  walked the picket line}}}\uc2  with striking members of the \uc2 United Auto Workers union\uc2 , who are in the midst of a work stoppage brought on by a protracted contract dispute with Detroit\u8217\'20\'19s Big Three automakers.\par \par \uc2 Trump will appear at a non-union auto parts supplier in Clinton township, outside Detroit, and speak to a crowd that will include members of the \uc2 UAW\uc2  and other unions, as well as some non-union workers.\par \par \uc2 Ahead of Trump\u8217\'20\'19s visit, CNN reports that some in the region are giving him a cold reception:\par \par \uc2 enltrThere\u8217\'20\'19s a plane flying over the venue Trump is speaking at tonight in Clinton Township, Michigan with a sign that says \u8220\'20\'1CTrump sold us out - Trumphatesworkers.com\u8221\'20\'1D {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/Ed7AHW51wI"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/Ed7AHW51wI}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Kate Sullivan (@KateSullivanDC) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/KateSullivanDC/status/1707138973947342885?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 September 27, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.04pm BST\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s more from the Guardian\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/hugo-lowell"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Hugo Lowell}}}\uc2  on \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s attempts to get federal judge \uc2 Tanya Chutkan\uc2  to remove herself from his trial on charges related to trying to overturn the 2020 election \u8211\'20\'13 an effort that now appears to have failed:\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s legal team on Monday asked the federal judge overseeing the 2020 election interference prosecution against him to remove herself from the case, arguing that her previous public comments about the former president\u8217\'20\'19s culpability in the January 6 Capitol attack were disqualifying.\par \par \uc2 The recusal motion, filed to and against the US district judge \uc2 Tanya Chutkan\uc2 , faces major legal hurdles: to succeed, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/donaldtrump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Trump}}}\uc2  must show a \u8220\'20\'1Creasonable person\u8221\'20\'1D would conclude from just her remarks \u8211\'20\'13 but not any of her actual rulings \u8211\'20\'13 that she was unable to preside impartially.\par \par \uc2 Trump has long complained that the judge assigned to the case was biased against him because of her previous comments about Trump in other January 6 riot defendant cases and his legal team weighed filing the motion for weeks, according to two people familiar with deliberations.\par \par \uc2 The {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://storage.courtlistener.com/recap/gov.uscourts.dcd.258149/gov.uscourts.dcd.258149.50.0_4.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 nine-page motion}}}\uc2  identified two episodes where Chutkan remarked on her opinion about Trump\u8217\'20\'19s responsibility in instigating the Capitol attack, which Trump\u8217\'20\'19s lawyers argued gave rise to the appearance of potential bias or prejudice against the former president.\par \par \uc2 The first instance came in October 2022 when she said, referring to January 6: \u8220\'20\'1CAnd the people who mobbed that Capitol were there in fealty, in loyalty, to one man \u8230\'20\'26 It\u8217\'20\'19s a blind loyalty to one person who, by the way, remains free to this day.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Trump\u8217\'20\'19s lawyers argued that those remarks, which came during sentencing of a rioter who stormed the Capitol, suggested Chutkan believed Trump should have been prosecuted and jailed in a prejudgment of guilt that alone was disqualifying.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/sep/11/trump-2020-election-subversion-case-judge-tanya-chutkan"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Trump asks judge to recuse herself in federal 2020 election subversion case}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.49pm BST\par \par \uc2 Judge in Trump's 2020 election meddling trial rejects call to recuse\par \par \uc2 Tanya Chutkan\uc2 , the federal judge presiding over \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  trial on charges related to trying to overturn the 2020 election, has rejected an effort by the former president to remove her from the case, Politico reports:\par \par \uc2 enltrBREAKING: Judge CHUTKAN *denies* Trump's motion to recuse. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/N3O5MmeO2Z"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/N3O5MmeO2Z}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/Kt3mdsKgU8"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/Kt3mdsKgU8}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Kyle Cheney (@kyledcheney) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/kyledcheney/status/1707147522270023946?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 September 27, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 enltrCHUTKAN rejects the notion that some of her statements alluding to Trump were based on watching the news, rather than facts she was presented with by Jan. 6 defendants who pinned their conduct on Trump. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/EtKFH7taJH"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/EtKFH7taJH}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/idI7RuGEVm"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/idI7RuGEVm}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Kyle Cheney (@kyledcheney) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/kyledcheney/status/1707148661635846560?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 September 27, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 Trump\u8217\'20\'19s legal team earlier this month had filed the motion asking Chutkan to recuse herself from the case, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/sep/11/trump-2020-election-subversion-case-judge-tanya-chutkan"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 arguing}}}\uc2  previous statements she had made about his involvement in the January 6 insurrection were disqualifying.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.43pm BST\par \par \uc2 We\u8217\'20\'19re about three hours away from the start of the second Republican primary debate at the \uc2 Ronald Reagan\uc2  presidential library in Simi Valley, California.\par \par \uc2 The Guardian\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s \uc2 David Smith\uc2  is on the scene, and reports that the seven candidates who have qualified will have quite the view:\par \par \uc2 enltrRepublican candidates will be directly below the nose of Air Force One during the debate: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/EkYB4364lA"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/EkYB4364lA}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 \uc2 David Smith\uc2  (@SmithInAmerica) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/SmithInAmerica/status/1707126359234093497?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 September 27, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 zxxltr {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/MnGCqqs8iW"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/MnGCqqs8iW}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 \uc2 David Smith\uc2  (@SmithInAmerica) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/SmithInAmerica/status/1707128912084713801?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 September 27, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.21pm BST\par \par \uc2 The Republican-led House Ways and Means committee today held a press conference to discuss evidence related to \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s impeachment, but that was overshadowed by a testy exchange between its chair Jason Smith and a reporter for NBC News.\par \par \uc2 As this video shows, the reporter asked Smith, who chairs one of three committees involved in the impeachment effort, to explain some of the gaps in his evidence. Smith struggles to do so. You can watch more below:\par \par \uc2 enltrA heated exchange occurs between House Ways and Means Committee Chair Jason Smith (R-MO) and an NBC reporter during a news conference on the investigation into President Biden's family. The reporter presses Rep. Smith on the timeline of the evidence found against the Bidens. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/2hfbQXEsPh"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/2hfbQXEsPh}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 CSPAN (@cspan) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/cspan/status/1707126244662300691?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 September 27, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 Video clips like these play right into the hands of White House officials who argue the Republicans have no case. Here\u8217\'20\'19s Ian Sams, Biden\u8217\'20\'19s spokesman for oversight and investigations:\par \par \uc2 enltrWhen House Republicans staged this stunt to try to distract from them shutting down the government in 3 days, I don\u8217\'20\'19t think this is what they had in mind\u8230\'20\'26\par \par \uc2 Another total bust. Zero evidence of wrongdoing by \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 . And they can\u8217\'20\'19t even answer basic questions without snapping. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/UtKDQVVMon"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/UtKDQVVMon}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Ian Sams (@IanSams46) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/IanSams46/status/1707119137351164154?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 September 27, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.02pm BST\par \par \uc2 While the Senate\u8217\'20\'19s top Republican \uc2 Mitch McConnell\uc2  is not the type to engage in social media spats, he used his speaking time on the chamber\u8217\'20\'19s floor today to wag his finger at the House Republicans whose intransigence in approving spending may soon cause the government to shut down:\par \par \uc2 enltrSen. Min. Leader McConnell sends pointed message to House Speaker McCarthy:\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CA vote against a standard short-term funding measure is a vote against paying over $1 billion in salary for Border Patrol and ICE agents working to track down lethal fentanyl and tame our open borders.\u8221\'20\'1D {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/dz36nxHzlS"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/dz36nxHzlS}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 The Recount (@therecount) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/therecount/status/1707069338375594049?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 September 27, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.48pm BST\par \par \uc2 And here\u8217\'20\'19s another great example of the intraRepublican fingerpointing that\u8217\'20\'19s probably only going to get worse over the coming hours and days.\par \par \uc2 It\u8217\'20\'19s Montana congressman \uc2 Ryan Zinke\uc2 , who aligns with speaker Kevin McCarthy and House Republican leadership, squaring off against insurgent leader congressman \uc2 Matt Gaetz\uc2 . The point of contention is which wing of the House GOP was responsible for returning to \u8220\'20\'1Cregular order\u8221\'20\'1D in the chamber, which the nonpartisan \uc2 Congressional Research Service{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://sgp.fas.org/crs/misc/R46597.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 defines}}}\uc2  as \u8220\'20\'1Ca traditional, committee-centered process of lawmaking, very much in evidence during most of the 20th century.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 While it\u8217\'20\'19s somewhat in the weeds, the open social media bickering (yes, they really did this in front of everybody on \uc2 Twitter\uc2 /X) tells you a lot about how things are going in the House today:\par \par \uc2 enltrFunny, I recall you guys skipping the conference meetings in December where Republicans decided to restore regular order. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/fX3YWAs1vU"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/fX3YWAs1vU}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Rep \uc2 Ryan Zinke\uc2  (@RepRyanZinke) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/RepRyanZinke/status/1707090615228391651?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 September 27, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 enltrRiiiiiight, Ryan.\par \par \uc2 We are totally doing regular order in September (moments away from a shutdown) at 2am because you guys decided in December 22 that it was gonna be this way.\par \par \uc2 It wasn\u8217\'20\'19t that we forced this on Kevin by depriving him his preferred CR\u8230\'20\'26.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 \uc2 Matt Gaetz\uc2  (@mattgaetz) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/mattgaetz/status/1707095400513950101?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 September 27, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 enltrWe have 10 approps bills out of committee. One passed on the floor in July. For two weeks we tried to bring DOD approps forward and twice it was killed when a couple Rs voted with Ds. It stopped the process, backed up bills. That's why we were voting until 1:30am and you know it.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Rep \uc2 Ryan Zinke\uc2  (@RepRyanZinke) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/RepRyanZinke/status/1707096951978623427?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 September 27, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 They went on from there. Click on the tweets if you want to read more.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.30pm BST\par \par \uc2 As Washington shambles towards its {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Government_shutdowns_in_the_United_States"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 11th government shutdown since 1980}}}\uc2 , finger pointing is intensifying between lawmakers in Congress.\par \par \uc2 CNN heard from West Virginia\u8217\'20\'19s Republican senator \uc2 Shelley Moore Capito\uc2 , who pondered Kevin McCarthy could have averted the crisis that now looms if he had stuck to an agreement reached earlier this year that increased the government\u8217\'20\'19s borrowing limit and also provided a rough outline of future spending plans. Here\u8217\'20\'19s what she had to say:\par \par \uc2 enltrSen. \uc2 Shelley Moore Capito\uc2 , a member of the Senate GOP leadership, believes Speaker McCarthy should have stuck to the spending levels as part of the debt limit law, which he himself cut with the WH.\par \par \uc2 "If you make a deal, you've got to stick to the deal," she told me {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/fQnmVSmC9i"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/fQnmVSmC9i}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Manu Raju (@mkraju) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/mkraju/status/1707118956056543435?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 September 27, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.09pm BST\par \par \uc2 While \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  may not believe that anything is inevitable in politics, he struck a realistic note when reporters traveling with him in California pressed him on his ability to stop the federal government from shutting down.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIf I knew that, I would\u8217\'20\'19ve already done it,\u8221\'20\'1D the president replied, when asked what he could have done to stop the shutdown.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.52pm BST\par \par \uc2 X cuts half of election integrity team \u8211\'20\'13 report\par \par \uc2 Elon Musk\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s X, the platform formerly known as \uc2 Twitter\uc2 , has axed around half of its global team dedicated to tracking election disinformation, according to a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theinformation.com/articles/musks-x-cuts-half-of-election-integrity-team-after-promising-to-expand-it?utm_source=ti_app"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  report }}}\uc2  by the Information.\par \par \uc2 The cuts, which reportedly include the head of the Dublin-based team, come less than a month after the company said it would expand its safety and election teams.\par \par \uc2 X executives told the team last week that \u8220\'20\'1Chaving elections integrity employees based in Europe wasn\u8217\'20\'19t necessary,\u8221\'20\'1D according to the report. The team had about two dozen employees before Musk bought the platform, and is now down to less than half of that.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 8.58pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.40pm BST\par \par \uc2 Biden says government shutdown 'not inevitable'\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  said a government shutdown is not inevitable, but that if there is one, a lot of vital work could be impacted in science and health, Reuters reported.\par \par \uc2 The president, speaking to reporters after remarks to a group of science and technology advisers in San Francisco, was asked if he believed a government shutdown was inevitable. He replied:\par \par \uc2 I don\u8217\'20\'19t think anything is inevitable... in politics.\par \par \uc2 enltrReporter: \u8220\'20\'1CMr. President, do you think a government shutdown is inevitable at this point?\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 President Biden: \u8220\'20\'1CI don\u8217\'20\'19t think anything is inevitable... in politics.\u8221\'20\'1D {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/G8VKTJpX6F"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/G8VKTJpX6F}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 The Recount (@therecount) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/therecount/status/1707116112771514449?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 September 27, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.21pm BST\par \par \uc2 Moderate New York Republican Mike Lawler said members of the GOP blocking efforts to keep the federal government from going into shutdown before a Saturday deadline are \u8220\'20\'1Cstuck on stupid\u8221\'20\'1D in an interview with CNN.\par \par \uc2 Criticising members of his party, Lawler said:\par \par \uc2 Some of my colleagues have, frankly, been stuck on stupid and refused to do what we were elected to do, against the vast majority of the conference, who have been working to avoid a shutdown.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.14pm BST\par \par \uc2 Schumer says he was 'disappointed and disturbed' by Menendez indictment\par \par \uc2 The Senate majority leader, \uc2 Chuck Schumer\uc2 , said he was disappointed and disturbed by the indictment of fellow Democratic senator \uc2 Bob Menendez\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Schumer, speaking to reporters, said:\par \par \uc2 I\u8217\'20\'19ve known Senator Menendez a very long time, and it was truly, truly upsetting. We all know that for senators, there\u8217\'20\'19s a much, much higher standard. And clearly, when you read the indictment, Senator Menendez fell way, way below that standard.\par \par \uc2 But he stopped short of calling for the New Jersey senator\u8217\'20\'19s resignation, saying that \u8220\'20\'1Cwe\u8217\'20\'19ll see what will happen\u8221\'20\'1D after Menendez {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/sep/27/trump-org-fraud-uaw-biden-government-shutdown-funding-politics-live?page=with:block-65147bc88f08e6e1e6635077#block-65147bc88f08e6e1e6635077"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 addresses the Democratic caucus tomorrow. }}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.04pm BST\par \par \uc2 Embattled New Jersey senator \uc2 Bob Menendez\uc2  has asked to speak to the Senate Democratic caucus on Thursday as he faces growing calls to resign following his indictment on corruption and bribery charges.\par \par \uc2 Senator Mark Warner, chair of the Senate intelligence committee, said he would grant Menendez the \u8220\'20\'1Ccourtesy\u8221\'20\'1D of listening to what he had to say to the conference, the Hill {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://thehill.com/homenews/senate/4226029-menendez-to-address-senate-democrats-about-criminal-charges/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reported.}}}\par \par \uc2 A Senate aide confirmed that Democratic offices are aware of a special caucus meeting tomorrow, with no subject matter outlined, Politico {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.politico.com/live-updates/2023/09/27/congress/menendez-senate-resign-indictment-00118415"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  reported.}}}\par \par \uc2 Menendez {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/sep/27/trump-org-fraud-uaw-biden-government-shutdown-funding-politics-live?filterKeyEvents=false&page=with:block-65144d018f0844f4dfe54582#block-65144d018f0844f4dfe54582"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pleaded not guilty}}}\uc2  earlier today to charges of taking bribes from three New Jersey businessmen.\par \par \uc2 Senator \uc2 Bob Menendez\uc2  and his wife, Nadine Menendez, depart a Manhattan court after they were arraigned on federal bribery charges in New York. Photograph: Anadolu Agency/Getty Images\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.51pm BST\par \par \uc2 A majority of Black Americans say that their communities are unfairly depicted in news coverage, according to a sweeping new survey on Wednesday.\par \par \uc2 Nearly two-thirds of respondents observed that their community received more negative coverage than other racial and ethnic groups, the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.pewresearch.org/journalism/2023/09/26/views-on-how-black-people-are-covered-in-the-news/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Pew Research Center}}}\uc2  survey found. Roughly four in 10 surveyed said that the media not only stereotyped Black people but also felt that they saw racist and racially insensitive coverage sometimes or fairly often.\par \par \uc2 The center\u8217\'20\'19s findings reflect the shortfalls of a so-called racial reckoning that swept through newsrooms across the United States in 2020 following the murder of George Floyd, when news outlets focused on hiring for roles centering diversity and inclusion and reporters and editors focused on covering communities traditionally underrepresented in news coverage.\par \par \uc2 The latest survey indicates that the so-called reckoning inside newsrooms {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.niemanlab.org/2022/03/american-journalisms-racial-reckoning-still-has-lots-of-reckoning-to-do/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 has struggled}}}\uc2  to reach the communities that they are meant to serve, including as the news business continues to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.axios.com/2023/06/13/media-job-cuts-record"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 experience layoffs}}}\uc2 , and failed to change the way communities feel about the coverage they receive.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.39pm BST\par \par \uc2 Biden administration warns government shutdown could disrupt air travel\par \par \uc2 The US secretary of transportation, \uc2 Pete Buttigieg\uc2 , warned that a government shutdown could disrupt the nation\u8217\'20\'19s air travel system as he spoke to reporters just days before the deadline.\par \par \uc2 Even a short shutdown would jeopardize the work and the hiring and training of potentially thousands of air traffic controllers and other key department employees, he said in a news conference earlier today.\par \par \uc2 House Republicans who are \u8220\'20\'1Ccomfortable\u8221\'20\'1D with a government shutdown should \u8220\'20\'1Cexplain themselves directly to all of the nonpartisan civil servants who make sure that planes land safely, who inspect trucks and railroads and pipelines to prevent disasters, who will have to go without pay\u8221\'20\'1D, he said.\par \par \uc2 There is no good time for a government shutdown, but this is a particularly bad time for a government shutdown, especially when it comes to transportation.\par \par \uc2 The consequences of a shutdown would be \u8220\'20\'1Cdisruptive and dangerous\u8221\'20\'1D, he added.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 8.05pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.18pm BST\par \par \uc2 Trump\u8217\'20\'19s business empire could collapse \u8216\'20\'18like falling dominoes\u8217\'20\'19 after ruling\par \par \uc2 If appeals from \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s legal team are unsuccessful, the collapse of the Trump empire, upon which the former reality TV host {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/sep/27/scathing-court-ruling-on-donald-trumps-empire-is-a-bitter-blow-to-his-successful-tycoon-persona"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 staked his reputation}}}\uc2  as a successful business tycoon, could be imminent.\par \par \uc2 It would probably start with the sale of Trump\u8217\'20\'19s most prestigious real estate assets, experts say, including Trump Tower in New York, golf courses and resorts around the US, and possibly his prized Mar-a-Lago club in Florida, if it is determined to be a business operation instead of his primary residential home. In his post on Wednesday, Trump decried the judge\u8217\'20\'19s $18m valuation of Mar-a-Lago, claiming it was worth \u8220\'20\'1C100 times more than he values it\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 William Black, a white-collar criminologist, corporate fraud investigator and distinguished scholar in residence for financial regulation at the \uc2 University of Minnesota\uc2  law school, said:\par \par \uc2 In finance, once the dominoes start falling, it becomes basically impossible to save it. These properties are even more damaged goods today because of the success in demonstrating they are massively overvalued. The most likely thing, if you get an honest agent or receiver, they\u8217\'20\'19re going to sell the properties at a loss. And when you\u8217\'20\'19ve got a whole bunch of properties, with the first one you just desperately need to get some action and that gets discounted the most.\par \par \uc2 Black, who helped expose congressional wrongdoing in the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2014/apr/02/savings-and-loan-charles-keating-dies-aged-90"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Lincoln Savings and Loans scandal}}}\uc2  of the 1980s, in which the financier Charles Keating inflated his company\u8217\'20\'19s worth to bilk taxpayers for billions, called Engoron\u8217\'20\'19s ruling \u8220\'20\'1Cdevastating\u8221\'20\'1D. He believes Trump insiders and employees would have incentive to come forward with more information if he loses his wealth and influence.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 7.23pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.08pm BST\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s real estate empire could collapse \u8220\'20\'1Clike falling dominoes\u8221\'20\'1D, experts believe, following a New York judge\u8217\'20\'19s ruling that the former president\u8217\'20\'19s business fortune was built on {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/sep/26/trump-liable-fraud-new-york"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 rampant fraud and blatant lies}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 According to \uc2 Michael Cohen\uc2 , his former attorney and fixer, Trump is already effectively \u8220\'20\'1Cout of business\u8221\'20\'1D in New York after Judge \uc2 Arthur Engoron\uc2  on Tuesday {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/sep/26/donald-trump-new-york-financial-fraud-key-takeaways"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 rescinded the licenses}}}\uc2  of the \uc2 Trump Organization\uc2  and other companies owned by Trump and his adult sons, Eric and Don Jr. Cohen told CNN:\par \par \uc2 Those companies will end up being liquidated \u8230\'20\'26 the judge has already determined that the fraud existed.\par \par \uc2 On Wednesday morning, in a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/AndrewFeinberg/status/1707059937346560198/photo/1"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 confrontational post}}}\uc2  on his Truth Social website that branded the judge a \u8220\'20\'1Cpolitical hack\u8221\'20\'1D, Trump said Engoron \u8220\'20\'1Cmust be stopped\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Trump\u8217\'20\'19s lawyers said they would appeal the rescinding of the licenses, the appointment of receivers, and Engoron\u8217\'20\'19s assertion that Trump and executives lived in a \u8220\'20\'1Cfantasy world\u8221\'20\'1D of routinely, repeatedly and illegally overvaluing property values and his personal net worth to gain favorable loan terms and reduced insurance premiums.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.49pm BST\par \par \uc2 Ahead of tonight\u8217\'20\'19s second GOP primary debate, \uc2 Reproductive Freedom for All\uc2 , formerly Naral Pro-Choice America, warned that anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  Republican presidential candidates will try to \u8220\'20\'1Cmessage their way out of the electoral disaster \u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 The reproductive rights organization tweeted:\par \par \uc2 GOP presidential candidates can\u8217\'20\'19t message their way out of the electoral disaster their support for a national \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban poses, but during tonight\u8217\'20\'19s debate, they\u8217\'20\'19ll try to.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CNo matter how they spin it, bans are just that \u8211\'20\'13 bans. And voters will reject them every time,\u8221\'20\'1D it added.\par \par \uc2 enltrGOP presidential candidates can\u8217\'20\'19t message their way out of the electoral disaster their support for a national \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban poses, but during tonight's debate, they\u8217\'20\'19ll try to.\par \par \uc2 No matter how they spin it, bans are just that\u8212\'20\'14bans. And voters will reject them every time.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 \uc2 Reproductive Freedom for All\uc2  (@reproforall) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/reproforall/status/1707063555957112955?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 September 27, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 Key Republican presidential candidates including Florida\u8217\'20\'19s governor, \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2 , and former vice-president \uc2 Mike Pence\uc2  have all been vocal about their anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  stances.\par \par \uc2 In April, DeSantis {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2023/apr/13/florida-six-week-abortion-ban-republicans"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 approved}}}\uc2  of a six-week \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban in Florida while Pence previously {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://apnews.com/article/mike-pence-abortion-views-2024-election-e5b236c27bc9c86f77efedbeedb26520"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 said}}}\uc2  that he wants to ban abortions even during non-viable pregnancies.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 7.03pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.37pm BST\par \par \uc2 Jared Kushner\uc2  pressured the \uc2 Washington Post\uc2  to fire its editor over coverage of the Russia election interference investigation, a new book says.\par \par \uc2 The Guardian\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s Martin Pengelly reports:\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s son-in-law and senior White House adviser, \uc2 Jared Kushner\uc2 , tried to persuade the publisher of the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/media/washington-post"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Washington Post}}}\uc2  to fire its editor over coverage of the Russia investigation, that editor, Marty Baron, writes in a new book.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWith no delay and without pause during his four years as president,\u8221\'20\'1D Baron writes, \u8220\'20\'1CTrump and his team would go after the Post and everyone else in the media who didn\u8217\'20\'19t bend to his wishes.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIn December 2019, Kushner would lean on [Fred] Ryan to withdraw support for me and our Russia investigation.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1C\u8230\'20\'26 \u8216\'20\'18He aims to get me fired,\u8217\'20\'19 I told Ryan.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Baron\u8217\'20\'19s book, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.amazon.com/Collision-Power-Trump-Bezos-WASHINGTON-ebook/dp/B0BPQQB9B7"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Collision of Power: Trump, Bezos and the Washington Post}}}\uc2 , will be published next Tuesday. \uc2 The Guardian\uc2  obtained a copy.\par \par \uc2 For the full story, click here:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/books/2023/sep/27/jared-kushner-editor-washington-post-trump-russia-election-interference-2016"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Jared Kushner pressured Washington Post to fire editor over Russia, book says}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.22pm BST\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  approves Louisiana emergency declaration\par \par \uc2 President \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  has approved an emergency declaration in Louisiana due to the emergency conditions resulting from the seawater intrusion that began on September 20.\par \par \uc2 The White House announced in a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.whitehouse.gov/briefing-room/presidential-actions/2023/09/27/president-joseph-r-biden-jr-approves-louisiana-emergency-declaration-4/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 statement}}}\uc2  on Wednesday:\par \par \uc2 The President\u8217\'20\'19s action authorizes the \uc2 Department of Homeland Security\uc2 , \uc2 Federal Emergency Management Agency (FEMA)\uc2 , to coordinate all disaster relief efforts which have the purpose of alleviating the hardship and suffering caused by the emergency on the local population.\par \par \uc2 The declaration is also set to \u8220\'20\'1Cprovide appropriate assistance for required emergency measures, authorized under Title V of the Stafford Act, to save lives and to protect property and public health and safety, and to lessen or avert the threat of a catastrophe in the parishes of Jefferson, Orleans, Plaquemines, and St. Bernard\u8221\'20\'1D, it added.\par \par \uc2 Last Friday, New Orleans\u8217\'20\'19 mayor, \uc2 LaToya Cantrell\uc2 , {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/sep/22/louisiana-drought-drinking-water-mississippi-river-saltwater-new-orleans"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 signed}}}\uc2  an emergency declaration after saltwater from the Gulf of Mexico started seeping its way through the Mississippi River in Louisiana.\par \par \uc2 The concern comes as the saltwater makes its way into the drought-hit river as it could potentially affect thousands of residents\u8217\'20\'19 drinking water in the following weeks.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 6.26pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.07pm BST\par \par \uc2 Interim summary\par \par \uc2 It is slightly past 1pm in Washington DC. Here is where the day stands:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The speaker of the House, Kevin McCarthy, said he would not allow a vote on a bipartisan Senate stopgap funding bill that would avert a government shutdown. At a closed-door meeting this morning, McCarthy urged House GOP members to work together to approve their own temporary measure to keep the government open past the Saturday deadline.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 New Jersey senator \uc2 Bob Menendez\uc2  pleaded not guilty to charges of taking bribes from three New Jersey businessman as he {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/sep/27/trump-org-fraud-uaw-biden-government-shutdown-funding-politics-live?filterKeyEvents=false&page=with:block-651439338f08ea4e57fcb715#block-651439338f08ea4e57fcb715"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 appeared in a federal courthouse}}}\uc2  in New York on Wednesday. Menendez entered the plea at a hearing before US magistrate judge Ona Wang in Manhattan. His wife, Nadine Menendez, and co-defendants Jose Uribe and Fred Daibes also pleaded not guilty.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Senate majority leader \uc2 Chuck Schumer\uc2  urged House speaker Kevin McCarthy to use bipartisanship to avert a government shutdown that could force millions of federal employees to go without pay. NBC reported Schumer as saying: \u8220\'20\'1CThe only way out of a shutdown is bipartisanship, and by constantly adhering to what the hard right wants, you\u8217\'20\'19re aiming for a shutdown.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 A New York judge ruled on Tuesday that {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/donaldtrump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Donald Trump}}}\uc2  committed financial fraud by overstating the value of his assets to broker deals and obtain financing. The ruling is an acceleration of the case the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/new-york"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 New York}}}\uc2  attorney general, Letitia James, has been building against Trump since 2019.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 United Auto Workers\uc2  president, Shawn Fain, who appeared beside \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  at a picket line in Michigan on Tuesday, said he will not meet with {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/donaldtrump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Donald Trump}}}\uc2  during his upcoming visit to Detroit. In an interview with CNN on Tuesday evening, Fain said it was a \u8220\'20\'1Cpathetic irony\u8221\'20\'1D that Trump would hold a rally for union members at a non-union business.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 US soldier Travis King, who fled to North Korea in July, is in American custody after being expelled by Pyongyang into China, according to US officials. North Korea\u8217\'20\'19s KCNA state news agency said King had been expelled after he confessed to illegally entering the country.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 6.27pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.57pm BST\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  will attempt to woo blue-collar workers in Michigan in an intensifying political tug-of-war with \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  a day after the sitting {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/sep/26/biden-joins-uaw-strike-update-detroit"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 president visited a picket line}}}\uc2  to declare support for a trade union strike against the US\u8217\'20\'19s three flagship carmakers.\par \par \uc2 Targeting working-class voters in the key battleground, the former president will attempt to upstage Tuesday\u8217\'20\'19s appeal by Biden to union members on the frontline of the \uc2 United Auto Workers (UAW) \uc2 strike, which is turning into a proxy struggle for next year\u8217\'20\'19s presidential election.\par \par \uc2 Trump will address about 500 workers, including \uc2 UAW\uc2  members, at Drake Enterprises, a non-unionised car parts maker in Macomb county, a few miles from where Biden spoke to striking employees picketing a Ford facility.\par \par \uc2 Trump has emitted a sympathetic feeling towards workers striking against Ford, \uc2 General Motors\uc2  and \uc2 Stellantis\uc2  without explicitly endorsing their demands for a 40% pay rise, shorter working hours and better pensions \u8211\'20\'13 which polls show a majority of Americans support.\par \par \uc2 Instead, he has accused the \uc2 UAW\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s leadership of selling its members \u8220\'20\'1Cdown the river\u8221\'20\'1D and attacked Biden\u8217\'20\'19s clean energy policy of incentivizing the three car giants to convert to manufacturing electric vehicles.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 6.13pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.47pm BST\par \par \uc2 None of the series of tax revelations or reports about \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  seems likely to shake the Trump faithful ahead of next year\u8217\'20\'19s presidential election against \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Their instant assumption is that politically biased judges are trying to distract attention from Hunter Biden \u8217\'20\'19s troubles and that Trump is merely smarter than others when it comes to gaming the system.\par \par \uc2 At a campaign rally in Dubuque, Iowa, last week, Mathew Willis, 41, said:\par \par \uc2 I\u8217\'20\'19ve never seen him be anything but honest. During a debate at one point, they were like, \u8216\'20\'18Oh, you don\u8217\'20\'19t pay your taxes,\u8217\'20\'19 and he\u8217\'20\'19s like, \u8216\'20\'18Neither do you! I use the legal system to do what I do. The loopholes are there. They put them there for people like you and us. I\u8217\'20\'19m just working the system.\u8217\'20\'19 He\u8217\'20\'19s not doing anything illegal. What\u8217\'20\'19s wrong with that?\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 6.14pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.43pm BST\par \par \uc2 Letitia James, New York\u8217\'20\'19s attorney general, released a statement following the judge\u8217\'20\'19s ruling in her lawsuit against \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  on Tuesday.\par \par \uc2 The statement, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cnn.com/2023/09/26/politics/trump-organization-business-fraud/index.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reported}}}\uc2  by CNN, said:\par \par \uc2 Today, a judge ruled in our favor and found that \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  and the \uc2 Trump Organization\uc2  engaged in years of financial fraud. We look forward to presenting the rest of our case at trial.\par \par \uc2 Trump\u8217\'20\'19s attorney, Christopher Kise, called the ruling \u8220\'20\'1Ccompletely disconnected from the facts and governing law\u8221\'20\'1D, adding:\par \par \uc2 While the full impact of the decision remains unclear, what is clear is that President Trump and his family will seek all available appellate remedies to rectify this miscarriage of justice.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 5.46pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.29pm BST\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s son \uc2 Eric Trump\uc2  insisted his father\u8217\'20\'19s claims about the value of his Mar-a-Lago estate were correct, writing that the Palm Beach estate is \u8220\'20\'1Cspeculated to be worth well over a billion dollars making it arguably the most valuable residential property in the country\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Judge \uc2 Arthur Engoron\uc2 , ruling in a civil lawsuit brought by New York attorney general, Letitia James, found that the former president consistently overvalued Mar-a-Lago, inflating its value on one financial statement by as much as 2,300%.\par \par \uc2 Posting on X, formerly known as \uc2 Twitter\uc2 , \uc2 Eric Trump\uc2  called the ruling \u8220\'20\'1Can attempt to destroy my father and kick him out of New York\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 enltrIn an attempt to destroy my father and kick him out of New York, a Judge just ruled that Mar-a-Lago, in Palm Beach Florida, is only worth approximate \u8220\'20\'1C$18 Million dollars\u8221\'20\'1D\u8230\'20\'26 Mar-a-Lago is speculated to be worth we\u8217\'20\'19ll over a billion dollars making it arguably the most valuable\u8230\'20\'26 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/b0U6J5ykWJ"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/b0U6J5ykWJ}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 \uc2 Eric Trump\uc2  (@EricTrump) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/EricTrump/status/1706795629505114508?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 September 26, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 enltrWhile everyone can see that this case is egregious, the only thing worse than weaponizing the legal system against a political opponent is unfairly going after their family. Both the Attorney General and the Judge know I had absolutely NOTHING to do with this case. Every single\u8230\'20\'26\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 \uc2 Eric Trump\uc2  (@EricTrump) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/EricTrump/status/1706838028352688145?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 September 27, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 5.36pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.23pm BST\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  rallied against the ruling by a New York judge that he committed financial fraud by overstating the value of his assets to broker deals and obtain financing.\par \par \uc2 Writing on his Truth Social platform, Trump said the decision was \u8220\'20\'1Cun-American\u8221\'20\'1D and part of an ongoing plot to damage his campaign to return to the White House. He {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://truthsocial.com/@realDonaldTrump/posts/111134129680540625"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 wrote}}}\uc2  on Tuesday:\par \par \uc2 My Civil rights have been violated, and some Appellate Court, whether federal or state, must reverse this horrible, un-American decision.\par \par \uc2 He insisted his company had \u8220\'20\'1Cdone a magnificent job for New York State\u8221\'20\'1D and \u8220\'20\'1Cdone business perfectly\u8221\'20\'1D, calling it \u8220\'20\'1CA very sad Day for the New York State System of Justice!\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 5.37pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.12pm BST\par \par \uc2 McCarthy says he 'doesn't see the support' in House for Senate stopgap bill to avert shutdown\par \par \uc2 The speaker of the House, Kevin McCarthy, said he would not allow a vote on a bipartisan Senate stopgap funding bill that would avert a government shutdown.\par \par \uc2 At a closed-door meeting this morning, McCarthy urged House GOP members to work together to approve their own temporary measure to keep the government open past the Saturday deadline.\par \par \uc2 McCarthy set up a test vote on Friday, a day before the shutdown deadline, on a far-right bill, AP reported. It would slash federal spending by 8% from many agencies and toughen border security but has been rejected by \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 , Democrats and his own right-flank Republicans.\par \par \uc2 McCarthy, speaking to reporters after the meeting, rejected outright the Senate\u8217\'20\'19s bipartisan bill, which would fund the government to 17 November, adding $6bn for Ukraine and $6bn for US disaster relief while talks continue. He said he didn\u8217\'20\'19t \u8220\'20\'1Csee the support in the House\u8221\'20\'1D to pass the Senate\u8217\'20\'19s bill.\par \par \uc2 enltrSpeaker Kevin McCarthy says he had a \u8220\'20\'1Cgood conference\u8221\'20\'1D with House GOP, and hopes the House will pass 4 appropriation bills \u8220\'20\'1Cby Thursday.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe next 5, we\u8217\'20\'19re gonna need more time. So, we will pass a CR \u8212\'20\'14 bring that rule up hopefully on Friday \u8212\'20\'14 that would keep government open.\u8221\'20\'1D {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/XQIqTtgujC"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/XQIqTtgujC}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 The Recount (@therecount) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/therecount/status/1707065178880196643?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 September 27, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 5.15pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.54pm BST\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights supporters and foes will square off in the Ohio supreme court on Wednesday over whether the state should be allowed to ban \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  as early as six weeks into pregnancy, before many people even know they are pregnant.\par \par \uc2 Arguments in the case arrive just weeks before Ohio will become the only state in the United States to vote directly on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  in 2023. On 7 November, voters will have the chance to decide whether to enshrine \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights in the state\u8217\'20\'19s constitution.\par \par \uc2 If the Ohio supreme court rules to reinstate the state\u8217\'20\'19s six-week ban, which is currently paused, it could throw the election \u8211\'20\'13 and \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  providers across the midwest \u8211\'20\'13 into chaos.\par \par \uc2 First passed in 2019, before the \uc2 US supreme court\uc2  overturned Roe v Wade and abolished the national right to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the six-week ban was put on hold. But once Roe fell last year, the ban snapped into place.\par \par \uc2 In court documents, Ohio \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  providers spoke of encountering patients who could not get cancer treatments while pregnant, people who threatened suicide if they could not get abortions, and women whose pregnancies had fetal anomalies so serious that they would never result in healthy babies.\par \par \uc2 As the ban does not have exceptions for rape or incest, multiple children also had to flee the state for abortions after being raped, according to court records. One 10-year-old rape victim\u8217\'20\'19s case {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/sep/18/indiana-attorney-general-rokita-rape-abortion-lawsuit-iu"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 continues to make national headlines}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.42pm BST\par \par \uc2 Senator \uc2 Bob Menendez\uc2  pleads not guilty to corruption charges\par \par \uc2 New Jersey senator \uc2 Bob Menendez\uc2  pleaded not guilty to charges of taking bribes from three New Jersey businessman as he {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/sep/27/trump-org-fraud-uaw-biden-government-shutdown-funding-politics-live?filterKeyEvents=false&page=with:block-651439338f08ea4e57fcb715#block-651439338f08ea4e57fcb715"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 appeared in a federal courthouse }}}\uc2  in New York on Wednesday.\par \par \uc2 Menendez entered the plea at a hearing before US magistrate judge Ona Wang in Manhattan. His wife, Nadine Menendez, and co-defendants Jose Uribe, and Fred Daibes, also pleaded not guilty. A third businessman, Wael Hana, pleaded not guilty on Tuesday.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.40pm BST\par \par \uc2 Travis King, an American soldier who fled across the border from South Korea to North Korea in July, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/sep/27/trump-org-fraud-uaw-biden-government-shutdown-funding-politics-live?filterKeyEvents=false&page=with:block-651432328f08e6e1e6634bf7#block-651432328f08e6e1e6634bf7"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 is back in US custody, }}}\uc2  US officials have confirmed.\par \par \uc2 According to senior administration officials, King crossed the Chinese border on Wednesday, and Chinese authorities handed him to the US embassy, who then arranged for the army private to be flown to a US military base.\par \par \uc2 US officials briefing the press on Wednesday did not comment on his motivations but insisted he had returned willingly. A senior US official said:\par \par \uc2 We can confirm that Private King was very happy to be on his way home. That has been quite clear as we have resumed our contact with him, and he is very much looking forward to being reunited with his family.\par \par \uc2 On the issue of any legal or disciplinary action King might face on the return to the US, a US official said that would be considered after a medical and psychological assessment.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWhen he arrives on US soil, he will be evaluated by [a] very talented, experienced team that are going to guide him through a reintegration process,\u8221\'20\'1D the official said.\par \par \uc2 They\u8217\'20\'19ll address any medical and emotional concerns and ensure we get him in a good place to reunite with his family\u8230\'20\'26and we\u8217\'20\'19ll work through all those administrative status questions following completion of his reintegration.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.37pm BST\par \par \uc2 California congressman \uc2 Ted Lieu\uc2  accused House speaker Kevin McCarthy of having gone back on his word over the funding deal outlined in the Fiscal Responsibility Act, which passed the House and the Senate with bipartisan support earlier this year.\par \par \uc2 That agreement, brokered between \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  and McCarthy, suspended the debt ceiling and outlined modest spending cuts for fiscal year 2024, but those cuts were deemed insufficient by members of the hard-right House Freedom Caucus.\par \par \uc2 That deal \u8220\'20\'1Cwasn\u8217\'20\'19t just a handshake agreement,\u8221\'20\'1D Lieu said at a news conference with House Democratic leadership.\par \par \uc2 Democrats, Republicans disagree on many issues. We work together on various issues but in this town, your word still matters. How do we, the American people, trust Kevin McCarthy if he simply goes back on a deal that was put into law?\par \par \uc2 He urged the speaker to \u8220\'20\'1Csimply honour the deal that he made\u8221\'20\'1D and to \u8220\'20\'1Cstart taking steps to rebuild his integrity\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.21pm BST\par \par \uc2 Chuck Schumer\uc2  tells Kevin McCarthy 'you can stop it' as government shutdown looms\par \par \uc2 Senate majority leader \uc2 Chuck Schumer\uc2  urged House speaker Kevin McCarthy to use bipartisanship to avert a government shutdown that could force millions of federal employees to go without pay.\par \par \uc2 NBC reported Schumer, speaking on the chamber floor this morning, said:\par \par \uc2 The only way out of a shutdown is bipartisanship, and by constantly adhering to what the hard right wants, you\u8217\'20\'19re aiming for a shutdown. They want it, you know it, you can stop it.\par \par \uc2 House Republicans \u8220\'20\'1Chave tried everything but bipartisanship\u8221\'20\'1D, he said, adding that a shutdown would cause \u8220\'20\'1Cgrave harm\u8221\'20\'1D for communities across the country.\par \par \uc2 Last night, the Speaker twisted himself into pretzels yet again trying to avoid his responsibility of governing, but this is the truth, every bill House Republicans have pushed is partisan, every CR has been aimed at the hard right, and every path they\u8217\'20\'19ve pursued to date will inevitably lead to a shutdown.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.12pm BST\par \par \uc2 Pete Aguilar, chair of the House Democratic caucus, called for New Jersey senator \uc2 Bob Menendez\uc2  to resign during a news conference with House Democratic leadership.\par \par \uc2 Menendez has had \u8220\'20\'1Can incredible track record\u8221\'20\'1D of service to the people of New Jersey and of having \u8220\'20\'1Clifted up issues that the Latino community cares about\u8221\'20\'1D, Aguilar said.\par \par \uc2 It doesn\u8217\'20\'19t bring me or any of us joy to say that he should resign. But he should for the betterment of the Democratic party. For the people of New Jersey. It\u8217\'20\'19s better that he fights this trial outside of the halls of Congress.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 4.48pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.54pm BST\par \par \uc2 Senate majority leader \uc2 Chuck Schumer\uc2  celebrated {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/sep/27/trump-org-fraud-uaw-biden-government-shutdown-funding-politics-live?page=with:block-651440768f08ea4e57fcb7a3#block-651440768f08ea4e57fcb7a3"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the crafting of the bill}}}\uc2  as a bipartisan achievement that would buy lawmakers more time to make longer-term funding decisions, and he urged House Republicans to adopt a similar approach in their negotiations.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe worked together so hard and diligently over the weekend, and we produced a result, I think, that shows that bipartisanship can triumph over extremism,\u8221\'20\'1D Schumer said just before the vote.\par \par \uc2 It\u8217\'20\'19s a bridge towards cooperation and away from extremism, which will allow us to keep working to fully fund the federal government and spare families the pain of a shutdown.\par \par \uc2 The White House press secretary, \uc2 Karine Jean-Pierre\uc2 , echoed that message, saying in a statement:\par \par \uc2 The Senate\u8217\'20\'19s bipartisan continuing resolution will keep the government open, make a down payment on disaster relief, and is an important show of support for Ukraine. House Republicans should join the Senate in doing their job.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 4.01pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.51pm BST\par \par \uc2 The Senate took a significant step on Tuesday evening to extend government funding beyond the end of the month, with just days left to avoid a shutdown.\par \par \uc2 In a vote of 77 to 19, the Senate advanced a shell bill that will become a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.appropriations.senate.gov/imo/media/doc/230926_cr_legislative_text.PDF"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 stopgap measure}}}\uc2  to fund the government through 17 November while directing roughly $6bn toward Ukraine\u8217\'20\'19s war efforts and another $6bn toward disaster relief.\par \par \uc2 The Senate could give final approval to the bill in the coming days, but the proposal faces steep odds of passage in the Republican-controlled House, where hard-right members have denounced efforts to provide additional funding to Ukraine.\par \par \uc2 The disagreements have elevated the risk that Congress will fail to pass a short-term funding bill, known as a continuing resolution, before the 1 October deadline to avoid a government shutdown that could force millions of federal employees to go without pay.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.44pm BST\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s a list of Senate Democrats who have {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/sep/27/trump-org-fraud-uaw-biden-government-shutdown-funding-politics-live?page=with:block-65143b5c8f08ea4e57fcb732#block-65143b5c8f08ea4e57fcb732"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 called on}}}\uc2 Bob Menendez\uc2  to resign, as shared by NBC\u8217\'20\'19s Frank Thorp V.\par \par \uc2 enltr28 Senate Ds calling on Menendez to resign:\par \par \uc2 Fetterman\par \par \uc2 Brown\par \par \uc2 Welch\par \par \uc2 Baldwin\par \par \uc2 Tester\par \par \uc2 Casey\par \par \uc2 Rosen\par \par \uc2 Warren\par \par \uc2 Heinrich\par \par \uc2 Klobuchar\par \par \uc2 Bennet\par \par \uc2 Kelly\par \par \uc2 Booker\par \par \uc2 Gillibrand\par \par \uc2 Markey\par \par \uc2 Massan\par \par \uc2 Hirono\par \par \uc2 Warnock\par \par \uc2 Peters\par \par \uc2 Duckworth\par \par \uc2 Murphy\par \par \uc2 Blumenthal\par \par \uc2 Stabenow\par \par \uc2 Sanders\par \par \uc2 Ossof\par \par \uc2 Van Hollen\par \par \uc2 Hickenlooper\par \par \uc2 Durbin\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Frank Thorp V (@frankthorp) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/frankthorp/status/1707035604205150342?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 September 27, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.40pm BST\par \par \uc2 Key takeaways from \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s financial fraud case ruling\par \par \uc2 A New York judge ruled on Tuesday that \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  committed financial fraud by overstating the value of his assets to broker deals and obtain financing.\par \par \uc2 The ruling is an acceleration of the case the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/new-york"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 New York}}}\uc2  attorney general, Letitia James, has been building against Trump since 2019, that the former president fudged financial statements and inflated his net worth up to $2.2bn more than the actual figure.\par \par \uc2 In a dramatic step just days before the trial is set to start, New York supreme court justice \uc2 Arthur Engoron\uc2  issued a partial ruling largely agreeing with James. He also ordered the cancellation of New York business certificates of all companies related to Trump and his two sons, \uc2 Donald Trump Jr\uc2  and \uc2 Eric Trump\uc2 , making it difficult for Trump to continue running his real estate business in the state.\par \par \uc2 A trial is still set to start 2 October, in which Engoron will decide whether Trump, his allies and his companies will have to pay the $250m in monetary damages James is asking for. Trump\u8217\'20\'19s lawyers say they will appeal the judge\u8217\'20\'19s ruling.\par \par \uc2 My colleague Lauren Aratani reported {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/sep/26/donald-trump-new-york-financial-fraud-key-takeaways"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 five key takeaway\u8217\'20\'19s from Tuesday\u8217\'20\'19s ruling}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/sep/26/donald-trump-new-york-financial-fraud-key-takeaways"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Five key takeaways from Donald Trump\u8217\'20\'19s financial fraud case ruling}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.44pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.28pm BST\par \par \uc2 New Jersey senator \uc2 Cory Booker\uc2  on Tuesday joined calls for \uc2 Bob Menendez\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s resignation after days of silence on the matter.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe details of the allegations against Senator Menendez are of such a nature that the faith and trust of New Jerseyans as well as those he must work with in order to be effective have been shaken to the core,\u8221\'20\'1D Booker said in a statement.\par \par \uc2 I believe stepping down is best for those Senator Menendez has spent his life serving.\par \par \uc2 By early afternoon, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/sep/26/bob-menendez-resign-cory-booker-democrat"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 more than a dozen}}}\uc2  Democratic senators had called for Menendez to quit.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.31pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.21pm BST\par \par \uc2 Senator \uc2 Bob Menendez\uc2  arrives at court to answer to bribery case charges\par \par \uc2 New Jersey senator \uc2 Bob Menendez\uc2  arrived in a federal courthouse in Manhattan to face corruption charges, as he resisted growing calls among his fellow Democrats to resign.\par \par \uc2 Menendez and his wife, Nadine, who is also charged in the case, said nothing as they arrived at the lower Manhattan courthouse on Wednesday morning.\par \par \uc2 Under an {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.justice.gov/usao-sdny/pr/us-senator-robert-menendez-his-wife-and-three-new-jersey-businessmen-charged-bribery"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 indictment}}}\uc2  unsealed {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/sep/22/robert-menendez-wife-bribery-charges"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 last week}}}\uc2 , the couple were accused of using his seat in the Senate, as chair of the foreign relations committee, to benefit the government of Egypt. Prosecutors described how large sums of cash were found at Menendez\u8217\'20\'19s New Jersey home, as well as actual gold bars. A \uc2 Mercedes-Benz\uc2  car is also at issue. Three businessmen have also been charged.\par \par \uc2 Menendez his wife are scheduled to be arraigned in the morning. A third co-defendant, Wael Hana, was arraigned on Tuesday and pleaded not guilty.\par \par \uc2 New Jersey senator \uc2 Bob Menendez\uc2  and his wife, Nadine, arrive at the Manhattan federal court in New York. Photograph: Eduardo Mu\u241\'00\'F1oz/\uc2 EPA\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.32pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.15pm BST\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  has added at least two veteran attorneys to his criminal defense team as he faces 91 criminal charges under four indictments.\par \par \uc2 The legal team, organized by attorney Todd Blanche, now includes Emil Bove, a former federal prosecutor and co-chief of the national security unit at the Manhattan US attorney\u8217\'20\'19s office, and Kendra Wharton, a white-collar defense attorney, according to a Politico {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.politico.com/news/2023/09/26/trump-criminal-defense-team-prosecutor-00118258"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 report}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Bove and Wharton are expected to work on Trump\u8217\'20\'19s New York criminal case brought by the Manhattan district attorney, \uc2 Alvin Bragg\uc2 , and the federal cases filed by special counsel Jack Smith, according to the report.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.20pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.06pm BST\par \par \uc2 UAW\uc2  president Shawn Fain says he won't meet Trump during Detroit visit\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 United Auto Workers\uc2  president, Shawn Fain, who appeared beside \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  at a picket line in Michigan on Tuesday, said he will not meet with \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  during his upcoming visit to Detroit.\par \par \uc2 In an interview with CNN on Tuesday evening, Fain said it was a \u8220\'20\'1Cpathetic irony\u8221\'20\'1D that Trump would hold a rally for union members at a non-union business. He said:\par \par \uc2 I see no point in meeting with him because I don\u8217\'20\'19t think the man has any bit of care about what our workers stand for, what the working class stands for. He serves a billionaire class, and that\u8217\'20\'19s what\u8217\'20\'19s wrong with this country.\par \par \uc2 enltrCNN\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/wolfblitzer?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @WolfBlitzer}}}\uc2  talks to \uc2 United Auto Workers\uc2  President Shawn Fain about former President \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s planned trip to Michigan and if he would be willing to meet with Trump. Hear his response on {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/CNNSitRoom?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @CNNSitRoom}}}\uc2 . {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/SHPVRsu8L2"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/SHPVRsu8L2}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 CNN (@CNN) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/CNN/status/1706801528260939853?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 September 26, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.15pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.53pm BST\par \par \uc2 US soldier Travis King in American custody after expulsion from North Korea\par \par \uc2 US soldier Travis King, who fled to North Korea in July, is in American custody after being expelled by Pyongyang into China, according to US officials.\par \par \uc2 North Korea\u8217\'20\'19s KCNA state news agency said King had been expelled after he confessed to illegally entering the country. It said the soldier harboured ill feelings over inhumane treatment and racial discrimination within the US army.\par \par \uc2 A US official confirmed that King had been transferred to American custody in China, but did not offer further details.\par \par \uc2 Pte King entered North Korea on 18 July during a tour of the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2023/jul/18/us-citizen-crosses-border-from-south-korea-into-north-korea"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 border village of Panmunjom}}}\uc2 , US officials have said. He had served nearly two months in a South Korean prison for assault before being released to be sent home to Fort Bliss, Texas, where he faced possible additional military disciplinary actions and discharge from the service.\par \par \uc2 He is the first known American to be held in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/north-korea"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 North Korea}}}\uc2  in nearly five years.\par \par \uc2 A man walks past a television in Seoul, South Korea, showing a news item about the US soldier Travis King. Photograph: Anthony Wallace/AFP/Getty Images\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.04pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.44pm BST\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  bills himself as the most pro-union president in history, and his visit to the Michigan plant on Tuesday came a day before his expected 2024 Republican opponent, \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , was set to address workers in different industries in his own pitch for the strikers\u8217\'20\'19 support.\par \par \uc2 No other sitting president has joined a picket line, according to Nelson Lichtenstein, a longtime labor historian at the \uc2 University of California, Santa Barbara\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Lichtenstein {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/sep/26/why-biden-uaw-strike-visit"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 told the Guardian}}}\uc2  :\par \par \uc2 This is genuinely new \u8211\'20\'13 I don\u8217\'20\'19t think it\u8217\'20\'19s ever happened before, a president on a picket line. Candidates do it frequently and prominent senators, but not a president.\par \par \uc2 Trump won Michigan with the help of union members\u8217\'20\'19 support in his 2016 election victory over \uc2 Hillary Clinton\uc2  before losing it four years later in his defeat to Biden. He will need to regain significant union support if he is to prevail next year.\par \par \uc2 The former president has said workers are being betrayed by their leadership and also by Biden\u8217\'20\'19s environmentally friendly policy of encouraging the three American car giants to convert to making electric vehicles.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.48pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.37pm BST\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s visit to Detroit later today comes after \uc2 Joe Biden{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/sep/26/biden-joins-uaw-strike-update-detroit"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 joined a protest }}}\uc2  outside a Michigan car plant in solidarity with striking members of the \uc2 United Auto Workers (UAW) union\uc2 , becoming the first sitting president to appear on a picket line.\par \par \uc2 Addressing the cheering crowd through a bullhorn on Tuesday, Biden said:\par \par \uc2 The fact of the matter is you guys \u8211\'20\'13 the \uc2 UAW\uc2  \u8211\'20\'13 you saved the automobile industry back in 2008 and before. You made a lot of sacrifices, gave up a lot. The companies were in trouble. Now they are doing incredibly well and guess what? You should be doing incredibly well too.\par \par \uc2 The president, wearing a \uc2 UAW\uc2  baseball cap with the words \u8220\'20\'1CUnion Yes\u8221\'20\'1D on the side, added:\par \par \uc2 You deserve a significant raise and other benefits. Let\u8217\'20\'19s get back what we lost.\par \par \uc2 Biden was joined by the \uc2 UAW\uc2  president, Shawn Fain. The \uc2 UAW\uc2  has withheld an endorsement of Biden so far, but union leadership has been critical of \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , who has sought to capitalize on the strike and siphon support from the majority-Democratic unions.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.54pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.33pm BST\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  skips GOP debate to woo blue-collar Michigan workers\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  will skip the second Republican presidential debate on Wednesday and instead visit autoworkers in Detroit, where he will attempt to position himself as an ally of Michigan\u8217\'20\'19s working-class voters by promising to raise wages and protect jobs if elected to a second term.\par \par \uc2 Trump, the clear frontrunner for the GOP primary race, will speak before a crowd of current and former \uc2 United Auto Workers (UAW) \uc2 members at Drake Enterprises, a nonunion manufacturer in Clinton Township, about a half-hour outside Detroit.\par \par \uc2 A Trump campaign radio ad released last week in Detroit and Toledo, Ohio, praised autoworkers and said the former president has \u8220\'20\'1Calways had their back\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 5.31pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.18pm BST\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s persona as a successful tycoon was always more about illusion than reality.\par \par \uc2 In The Apprentice, he was effectively an actor reading from a script in a fantasy board room. In real life, it later transpired, he shied away from saying \u8220\'20\'1CYou\u8217\'20\'19re fired!\u8221\'20\'1D to anyone\u8217\'20\'19s face at the White House, preferring to delegate the unpleasant task.\par \par \uc2 Trump\u8217\'20\'19s origin story was told in his bestselling 1987 book The Art of the Deal. But the man who ghostwrote it, Tony Schwartz, describes him as an emperor with no clothes. He {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2020/oct/04/donald-trump-tony-schwartz-interview-art-of-the-deal"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 told the Guardian}}}\uc2  in 2020:\par \par \uc2 There\u8217\'20\'19s nothing more important to Trump than being seen as very, very rich, which is why he\u8217\'20\'19s expended so much effort in trying to claim a net worth far beyond what he actually was worth.\par \par \uc2 A series of tax revelations and reports have shown that Trump is not as rich as he would like everyone to believe. But the exaggerations are very on brand for a man who claimed to have the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2017/jan/22/trump-inauguration-crowd-sean-spicers-claims-versus-the-evidence"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 biggest inauguration crowd ever}}}\uc2 , that {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2020/nov/10/trump-and-republicans-escalate-election-claims-without-evidence"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 voter fraud is rampant}}}\uc2  and that Democrats are so pro-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/2019/02/26/health/abortion-bill-trump.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 they want to commit infanticide}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.24pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.09pm BST\par \par \uc2 Fraud ruling is a bitter blow to \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 's successful tycoon persona\par \par \uc2 For years \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  was the host of The Apprentice, a reality TV show in which contestants vied for a management job within his organisation and he would deliver the verdict: \u8220\'20\'1CYou\u8217\'20\'19re fired!\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 It cemented the image of Trump as an assertive chief executive who had conquered New York, an image that still proves seductive to millions of voters who want him to run the US like a business. But like much else about the 45th US president, it was all a lie.\par \par \uc2 On Tuesday a judge found that Trump\u8217\'20\'19s business empire was built, at least in part, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/sep/26/trump-liable-fraud-new-york"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 on rampant fraud}}}\uc2 . Noting that Trump\u8217\'20\'19s lawyers were effectively asking the court not to believe its own eyes, Engoron quoted the Marx brothers\u8217\'20\'19 film Duck Soup:\par \par \uc2 Well, who ya gonna believe, me or your own eyes?\par \par \uc2 The decision will make it easier for the New York state attorney general, Letitia James, to establish damages at a civil trial due to start next week; she is seeking a penalty of about $250m.\par \par \uc2 Engoron ordered the cancellation of certificates that let some of Trump\u8217\'20\'19s businesses, including the \uc2 Trump Organization\uc2 , operate in New York \u8211\'20\'13 just possibly the beginning of the end of his empire.\par \par \uc2 If the judge\u8217\'20\'19s scathing decision withstands an appeal from Trump\u8217\'20\'19s lawyers, it will be the first time a government investigation into the former president has resulted in punishment. It will also deal the biggest blow yet to his persona as a successful tycoon.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/sep/27/scathing-court-ruling-on-donald-trumps-empire-is-a-bitter-blow-to-his-successful-tycoon-persona"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Scathing court ruling on Donald Trump\u8217\'20\'19s empire is a bitter blow to his successful tycoon persona}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.14pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.04pm BST\par \par \uc2 Alina Habba, general counsel for \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , described the \uc2 Trump Organization\uc2  as \u8220\'20\'1Can American success story\u8221\'20\'1D and called the judge\u8217\'20\'19s ruling \u8220\'20\'1Cfundamentally flawed\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 In a statement after the judge\u8217\'20\'19s ruling on Tuesday, she said:\par \par \uc2 We intend to immediately appeal this decision because President Trump and his family, like every American business owner, is entitled to their day in court.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.59pm BST\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s legal team had previously asked the judge to dismiss the case against him, arguing New York\u8217\'20\'19s attorney general, Letitia James, lacked authority to file the lawsuit because there was no evidence the public was harmed by Trump\u8217\'20\'19s actions, and that many of the allegations were beyond the statute of limitations.\par \par \uc2 But Judge \uc2 Arthur Engoron\uc2  indicated last week he was not inclined to be sympathetic, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://abcnews.go.com/US/judge-hear-arguments-summary-judgment-new-york-ags/story?id=103347663"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 rebuking Trump\u8217\'20\'19s lawyers}}}\uc2  for making \u8220\'20\'1Cfrivolous arguments\u8221\'20\'1D and stating he was considering sanctions against them.\par \par \uc2 Chris Kise, who is also representing Trump in a federal indictment in Florida over the former president\u8217\'20\'19s handling of classified documents after leaving the White House, argued:\par \par \uc2 What is happening here is what happens every day in complex business transactions.\par \par \uc2 Engoron was not swayed. He said:\par \par \uc2 The fact that no one was hurt does not mean the case gets dismissed.\par \par \uc2 In his ruling on Tuesday, he granted a motion by James seeking sanctions against Trump\u8217\'20\'19s legal team for repeatedly making arguments already rejected, fining five attorneys $7,500 each.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.08pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.54pm BST\par \par \uc2 A New York judge ruled on Tuesday that \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  committed fraud for years while building the real estate empire that catapulted him to fame and the White House.\par \par \uc2 Judge \uc2 Arthur Engoron\uc2  found that Trump and executives from his company, including his sons Eric and Donald Jr, routinely and repeatedly deceived banks, insurers and others by massively overvaluing assets and exaggerating his net worth on paperwork.\par \par \uc2 His ruling came in a civil lawsuit brought by New York\u8217\'20\'19s attorney general, Letitia James, days before the start of a non-jury trial that will hear accusations that Trump, and the \uc2 Trump Organization\uc2 , lied for a decade about asset values and his net worth to get better terms on bank loans and insurance.\par \par \uc2 Engoron wrote:\par \par \uc2 The documents here clearly contain fraudulent valuations that defendants used in business.\par \par \uc2 James has said Trump had effectively engaged in a \u8220\'20\'1Cbait and switch\u8221\'20\'1D operation, inflating his net worth by as much as $2.23bn, and by one measure as much as $3.6bn, on annual financial statements given to banks and insurers. Assets whose values were inflated include Trump\u8217\'20\'19s Mar-a-Lago estate in Florida, his penthouse apartment in Manhattan\u8217\'20\'19s Trump Tower, and various office buildings and golf courses, James said in the lawsuit filed in September 2022.\par \par \uc2 In his ruling, the judge said James had established liability for false valuations of several properties, Mar-a-Lago and the penthouse. He wrote:\par \par \uc2 In defendants\u8217\'20\'19 world: rent regulated apartments are worth the same as unregulated apartments; restricted land is worth the same as unrestricted land; restrictions can evaporate into thin air; a disclaimer by one party casting responsibility on another party exonerates the other party\u8217\'20\'19s lies. That is a is a fantasy world, not the real world.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.13pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.46pm BST\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 's real estate empire under threat after New York fraud ruling\par \par \uc2 Good morning, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/us-politics"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 US politics}}}\uc2  blog readers. On Tuesday, a judge found that \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s business empire was built, at least in part, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/sep/26/trump-liable-fraud-new-york"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 on rampant fraud}}}\uc2 . Justice \uc2 Arthur Engoron\uc2  of the New York state court in Manhattan said Trump and his adult sons, Eric and Donald Jr, wildly inflated the value of his properties to hoodwink banks, insurers and others.\par \par \uc2 The ruling came in a civil lawsuit brought by Letitia James, New York\u8217\'20\'19s attorney general, days before the start of a non-jury trial that will hear accusations that Trump, and the \uc2 Trump Organization\uc2 , lied for a decade about asset values and his net worth to get better terms on bank loans and insurance.\par \par \uc2 James has said Trump had effectively engaged in a \u8220\'20\'1Cbait and switch\u8221\'20\'1D operation, inflating his net worth by as much as $2.23bn, and by one measure as much as $3.6bn, on annual financial statements given to banks and insurers.\par \par \uc2 Assets whose values were inflated include his office buildings and golf courses, his Mar-a-Lago estate in Florida and his penthouse apartment at Trump Tower in New York, which he claimed was 30,000 sq ft, nearly three times its actual size, resulting in an overvaluation of as much as $207m.\par \par \uc2 The decision will make it easier for James to establish damages at a civil trial due to start next week; she is seeking a penalty of about $250m. Engoron ordered the cancellation of certificates that let some of Trump\u8217\'20\'19s businesses, including the \uc2 Trump Organization\uc2 , operate in New York \u8211\'20\'13 just possibly the beginning of the end of his empire.\par \par \uc2 If the judge\u8217\'20\'19s scathing decision withstands an appeal from Trump\u8217\'20\'19s lawyers, it will be the first time a government investigation into the former president has resulted in punishment. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/sep/27/scathing-court-ruling-on-donald-trumps-empire-is-a-bitter-blow-to-his-successful-tycoon-persona"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 It will also deal the biggest blow yet to his persona as a successful tycoon.}}}\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, the former president is expected in Detroit today to address autoworkers. His visit comes a day after {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/sep/26/biden-joins-uaw-strike-update-detroit"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Biden made a rousing speech, telling striking workers they deserved higher pay}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s what else we\u8217\'20\'19re watching today:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 9am Eastern time: The House convenes. SEC chair \uc2 Gary Gensler\uc2  will testify before the financial services committee at 10am. The ways and means committee will meet in an executive session to discuss releasing new Hunter Biden/ IRS whistleblower info at 10.30am.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 10am: The Senate meets.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 1.30pm: \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  will convene a meeting with his advisers on science and tech in San Francisco.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 1.30pm: Republican senators \uc2 Lindsey Graham\uc2 , \uc2 John Kennedy\uc2 , \uc2 Thom Tillis\uc2 , \uc2 Marsha Blackburn\uc2 , Ted Cruz, Katie Britt and \uc2 John Cornyn\uc2  will hold a news conference about the border.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 2pm: Senate majority leader \uc2 Chuck Schumer\uc2  will hold his weekly news conference, where he may deliver remarks on embattled New Jersey senator \uc2 Bob Menendez\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s political future.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 8pm: \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  is expected to skip the second GOP primary debate and instead address striking auto workers in Michigan.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 9pm: Republicans will hold their second presidential debate at Ronald Reagan Presidential Library. Seven candidates are set to take part \u8211\'20\'13 Florida governor \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2 , former South Carolina governor Nikki Haley, South Carolina senator Tim Scott, entrepeneur \uc2 Vivek Ramaswamy\uc2 , former vice-president \uc2 Mike Pence\uc2 , former New Jersey governor \uc2 Chris Christie\uc2  and North Dakota governor \uc2 Doug Burgum\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.28pm BST\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020230927ej9r001ea\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
