\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Abortion \highlight\uc2  rights activists spend record amount in Pennsylvania race\b0\par\par\uc2 Ava Sasani \par \uc2 881 \uc2 words\par \uc2 21 September 2023\par 15:38 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Super Pac Planned Parenthood Votes launches seven-figure ad buy in the race for a seat on the state supreme court\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights advocates announced on Thursday record spending on this year\u8217\'20\'19s race for a seat on the Pennsylvania supreme court.\par \par \uc2 Planned Parenthood Votes, a Super Pac that supports \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access, launched a scathing television advertisement against the conservative candidate Carolyn Carluccio. The advertisement calls Carluccio \u8220\'20\'1Ca threat to our \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights\u8221\'20\'1D in Pennsylvania.\par \par \uc2 The seven-figure ad buy marks the Pac\u8217\'20\'19s largest investment in a state supreme court race.\par \par \uc2 The move by \uc2 Planned Parenthood\uc2  underscores the enduring importance of Pennsylvania as an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  safe haven for the surrounding region. A spokesperson for \uc2 Planned Parenthood\uc2  said Pennsylvania clinics saw an influx of out-of-state patients over the past year, as neighboring states like West Virginia enacted sweeping bans on the procedure.\par \par \uc2 Pennsylvania first emerged as a bitterly contested battleground on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  in last year\u8217\'20\'19s midterms, when supporters and opponents of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  vied for the governor\u8217\'20\'19s seat\u8211\'20\'13. Voters overwhelmingly opted for the Democratic candidate, \uc2 Josh Shapiro\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 At first glance, the stakes of this year\u8217\'20\'19s election appear far less dire for Pennsylvania voters who support \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 . The results of the November election will not shift the composition of the state\u8217\'20\'19s high court \u8211\'20\'13 four of the seven seats on the current bench are secured by Democrat-appointed justices.\par \par \uc2 But \uc2 Planned Parenthood\uc2  said it is looking ahead to the 2025 election, when three of those Democratic justices will appear on the ballot.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThis election is essential because, if we aren\u8217\'20\'19t able to continue a 5-2 majority, we\u8217\'20\'19re going to be up against a tougher race in 2025,\u8221\'20\'1D said Breana Ross, campaign director of \uc2 Planned Parenthood\uc2  Votes.\par \par \uc2 Even the 2025 judicial race is an unlikely subject of Pac interest. The three Democratic justices face a retention election in 2025, not a traditional race. In a retention year, justices do not face off against an opponent: voters simply select yes or no to decide if a justice should remain on the bench.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CNo one loses retention elections in Pennsylvania,\u8221\'20\'1D said David S Cohen, a law professor at \uc2 Drexel University\uc2 . \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s incumbency on steroids.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Only one justice has ever been ousted by Pennsylvania voters in a retention election.\par \par \uc2 Still, Cohen said \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights supporters and opponents alike are unwilling to take any risks about the composition of Pennsylvania\u8217\'20\'19s high court.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt doesn\u8217\'20\'19t matter if you already have six justices on your side, you want to make sure that every single one of those open seats is filled by someone that supports your position,\u8221\'20\'1D Cohen said.\par \par \uc2 After the \uc2 US supreme court\uc2  overturned Roe v Wade, \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights advocates \u8211\'20\'13\u8211\'20\'13 particularly in states where lawmakers are hostile to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  \u8211\'20\'13\u8211\'20\'13 have turned to the courts to safeguard access. Many state constitutions offer stronger privacy protections than the federal constitution.\par \par \uc2 But the strategy has brought uneven success for the \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights movement. \uc2 Planned Parenthood\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s South Carolina affiliate celebrated in January, when the state supreme court struck down a six-week ban on the procedure. Then in August, the court upheld a near-identical ban.\par \par \uc2 In the months between the two rulings, one justice retired and was replaced by a Republican appointee.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe South Carolina supreme court ruling reversed because one person changed,\u8221\'20\'1D Cohen said. \u8220\'20\'1CYou can\u8217\'20\'19t take any of these numbers for granted, every seat matters.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The seven-figure price tag of the new anti-Carluccio advertisement comes one month after the South Carolina supreme court\u8217\'20\'19s stunning reversal of precedent.\par \par \uc2 Ross said Thursday\u8217\'20\'19s legal landscape demanded a new strategy by \uc2 Planned Parenthood\uc2  \u8220\'20\'1Cto communicate with voters early and often around the impact that courts can have on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 In a statement announcing the new advertisement, \uc2 Planned Parenthood\uc2  Votes said Carluccio tried to \u8220\'20\'1Cto shade her views from the public eye, but she cannot pull one over on Pennsylvania voters\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 After winning the primary election in May, Carluccio removed information about her opposition to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  from her campaign website, according to a May report from {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://keystonenewsroom.com/story/republican-nominee-for-pennsylvania-supreme-court-wiped-anti-abortion-language-from-website/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the Keystone.}}}\par \par \uc2 In a February letter to the Pennsylvania Coalition for Civil Justice Reform, Carluccio {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://paforciviljusticereform.org/wp-content/uploads/2023/03/Carluccio-Questionnaire-Response.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 disclosed}}}\uc2  that her candidacy is endorsed by the Pennsylvania Pro-Life Federation.\par \par \uc2 During the primary race, Carluccio\u8217\'20\'19s campaign site said she would defend \u8220\'20\'1Call life under the law\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Positioning herself as an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  opponent helped Carluccio secure her party\u8217\'20\'19s nomination earlier this year. Republican voters in Pennsylvania have become more conservative since 2000, according to recent polling from {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.fandmpoll.org/poll-release-august-2023/?ref=franklin-marshall-college-poll-newsletter"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Franklin & Marshall College}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 But \uc2 Planned Parenthood\uc2  and other reproductive justice advocates hope Carluccio\u8217\'20\'19s opposition to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  will doom her campaign in November. Overall attitudes on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  have softened \u8211\'20\'13\u8211\'20\'13 64% of all Pennsylvania voters in the 2022 midterms said \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  should be legal in most or all cases, according to polling from {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://apnews.com/article/abortion-pennsylvania-supreme-court-274a476c66e2ea3f9dace25a4cff546a"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the Associated Press}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 As the November election nears, Carluccio\u8217\'20\'19s campaign has sidestepped questions about \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CJudges are often in the position of ruling on matters where passions, beliefs, and ideologies run deep,\u8221\'20\'1D Carluccio wrote in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.pennlive.com/opinion/2023/08/why-im-running-for-pennsylvania-supreme-court-opinion.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 an August op-ed}}}\uc2  about her candidacy. \u8220\'20\'1CI reject calls to rule based on partisan or ideological grounds and instead rule according to our laws.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020230921ej9l0020r\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
