\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 First Thing: Top carbon offset projects may not cut planet-heating emissions\b0\par\par\uc2 Nicola Slawson \par \uc2 1,617 \uc2 words\par \uc2 20 September 2023\par 10:30 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Majority of offset projects that have sold the most carbon credits are \u8216\'20\'18likely to be junk\u8217\'20\'19. Plus, how lucid dreams can make us fitter, more creative and less anxious\par \par \uc2 Good morning.\par \par \uc2 The vast majority of the environmental projects most frequently used to offset greenhouse gas emissions appear to have fundamental failings, suggesting they cannot be relied upon to cut planet-heating emissions, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/environment/2023/sep/19/do-carbon-credit-reduce-emissions-greenhouse-gases"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 according to an analysis}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The global, multibillion-dollar voluntary carbon trading industry has been embraced by governments, organisations and corporations including oil and gas companies, airlines, fast-food brands, fashion houses, tech firms, art galleries and universities as a way of claiming to reduce their greenhouse gas footprint.\par \par \uc2 It works by carbon offset credits being tradable \u8220\'20\'1Callowances\u8221\'20\'1D or certificates that allow the purchaser to compensate for 1 ton of carbon dioxide, or the equivalent in greenhouse gases, by investing in environmental projects that claim to reduce carbon emissions.\par \par \uc2 But there is growing evidence suggesting that many of these schemes exaggerate climate benefits and underestimate potential harms.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 What did the research find? A total of 39 of the top 50 emission offset projects, or 78%, were categorised as likely to be junk or worthless because of one or more fundamental failing that undermined its promised emission cuts. Overall, $1.16bn of carbon credits have been traded so far from the projects classified by the investigation as likely junk or worthless; a further $400m of credits bought and sold were potentially junk.\par \par \uc2 Ohio \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights activists suffer blow in suit over referendum language\par \par \uc2 In this year\u8217\'20\'19s only opportunity for US voters to directly weigh in on the right to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , an upcoming ballot referendum in Ohio will include language that describes a fetus as an \u8220\'20\'1Cunborn child\u8221\'20\'1D, in a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2023/sep/19/ohio-abortion-rights-referendum-language"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 disappointing loss for \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  rights activists}}}\uc2  in the state who had sued to stop voters from seeing language they say is misleading.\par \par \uc2 Ohioans are to vote on 7 November on a referendum to enshrine \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights into the state\u8217\'20\'19s constitution. The outcome could not only determine the future of Ohio\u8217\'20\'19s six-week \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban, which is frozen pending litigation, but also for the midwest. The state has become one of the few in the region to permit abortions since the \uc2 US supreme court\uc2  overturned Roe v Wade last year.\par \par \uc2 The Ohio referendum\u8217\'20\'19s journey to the ballot box has been a long one. In a special election in August, voters resoundingly rejected a GOP-backed ballot measure that would have required all constitutional amendments to garner 60% of the vote, rather than the simple majority currently required for passage. The measure was loudly denounced as an attempt to stymie the \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  referendum and keep it from passing.\par \par \uc2 Weeks after Republicans lost that election, the Ohio ballot board met to decide what language should show up on voters\u8217\'20\'19 ballots regarding Issue 1, the \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  referendum.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 What did campaigners want the text to say? Ohioans United for Reproductive Rights proposed using the text of the amendment, which includes guarantees that the state cannot interfere with the right to contraception, miscarriage care and \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  up until the point of viability, a benchmark that\u8217\'20\'19s generally pegged to about 24 weeks of pregnancy.\par \par \uc2 Olena Zelenska\par \par \uc2 calls for return of 19,000 \u8216\'20\'18abducted\u8217\'20\'19 children\par \par \uc2 Ukraine\u8217\'20\'19s first lady has urged world leaders to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/live/2023/sep/20/russia-ukraine-war-live-updates-olena-zelenska-child-abductions-moscow-drone-attacks-belgorod-oryol"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 help return Ukrainian children forcibly taken to Russia}}}\uc2 , where she says they are being indoctrinated and deprived of their national identity, the Agence France-Presse news agency reports.\par \par \uc2 Speaking on the sidelines of the \uc2 UN\uc2  general assembly on Tuesday, \uc2 Olena Zelenska\uc2  said more than 19,000 Ukrainian children had been transferred by force, or deported to Russia or occupied territories. So far, only 386 had been returned.\par \par \uc2 In Russia, \u8220\'20\'1Cthey were told that their parents don\u8217\'20\'19t need them, that their country doesn\u8217\'20\'19t need them, that nobody is waiting for them\u8221\'20\'1D, Zelenska said. \u8220\'20\'1CThe abducted children were told that they are no longer Ukrainian children, that they are Russian children.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Earlier, her husband, \uc2 Volodymyr Zelenskiy\uc2 , {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2023/sep/19/zelenskiy-russia-genocide-un-general-assembly"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 told the UN general assembly that Russia was committing genocide}}}\uc2  in Ukraine and urged world leaders to attend a peace summit to help stop the invasion and future wars of aggression.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 What\par \par \uc2 did \uc2 Joe Biden\par \par \uc2 say during the event? The US president said the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2023/sep/19/biden-putin-russia-weapons-un-general-assembly"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 UN gathering this week was \u8220\'20\'1Cdarkened by the shadow of war\u8221\'20\'1D}}}\uc2 , which he described as an \u8220\'20\'1Cillegal war of conquest without provocation by Russia\u8221\'20\'1D against Ukraine. \u8220\'20\'1CNo nation wants the war to end more than Ukraine,\u8221\'20\'1D he said, reiterating US support for Kyiv and its efforts to bring about \u8220\'20\'1Ca diplomatic resolution to a just and lasting peace\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 In other news \u8230\'20\'26\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Elon Musk\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s brain-implant startup, \uc2 Neuralink\uc2 , said it\par \par \uc2 had received approval from an independent review board to begin recruiting patients for its {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/technology/2023/sep/19/elon-musk-neuralink-human-trials-brain-implant"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 first human trial}}}\uc2 . The company is seeking people with paralysis to test its experimental device in a six-year study.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Iran\u8217\'20\'19s president,\par \par \uc2 Ebrahim Raisi\par \par \uc2 , in a lengthy speech to the \uc2 UN\uc2  general assembly, accused\par \par \uc2 the US of fanning the flames of violence in Ukraine, prompting protests from Israel\u8217\'20\'19s representative to the \uc2 UN\uc2 . Raisi claimed any Iranian-made drones hitting Ukrainian cities had been {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2023/sep/20/iran-un-speech-ebrahim-raisi-accuses-us-of-stoking-ukraine-war"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 sold before the war started}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 South Carolina has obtained a drug needed to carry out lethal injections and is ready to perform the state\u8217\'20\'19s first execution in\par \par \uc2 more than 12 years, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/sep/19/south-carolina-execution-drug-lethal-injection"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 officials have announced}}}\par \par \uc2 . The state\u8217\'20\'19s supply of drugs it used to kill inmates expired and pharmaceutical companies refused to sell them because they could be publicly identified.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 JoAnne A Epps\par \par \uc2 , the acting president of \uc2 Temple University\uc2 , died yesterday, shortly {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/sep/19/joanne-epps-president-temple-university-dies"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 after becoming ill on stage}}}\uc2  during a memorial service, officials said\par \par \uc2 . They described her loss as a \u8220\'20\'1Cgut punch\u8221\'20\'1D and fought back tears as they recalled her near four decades of service.\par \par \uc2 Stat of the day: \uc2 Rupert Murdoch\uc2  thought $787.5m Dominion suit would cost Fox $50m,\par \par \uc2 Michael Wolff\par \par \uc2 book says\par \par \uc2 In winter 2022, at a hideaway in St Barts, \uc2 Rupert Murdoch\uc2  directed \u8220\'20\'1Csudden fury\u8221\'20\'1D at \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , who he thought would lose the 2024 Republican presidential primary to \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2 , but who the media mogul also said was likely to cost him $50m, through a lawsuit regarding Trump\u8217\'20\'19s lies about the 2020 election.\par \par \uc2 The lawsuit was filed by \uc2 Dominion Voting Systems\uc2 , over Fox News\u8217\'20\'19s broadcast of Trump\u8217\'20\'19s lies. Settled this April, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/books/2023/sep/19/rupert-murdoch-dominion-suit-trump-fox-michael-wolff-book"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 it cost Murdoch considerably more than he predicted}}}\uc2  : $787.5m, to be precise. Murdoch\u8217\'20\'19s wildly off miscalculation and his anger at Trump \u8211\'20\'13 in conversation with friends at the idyllic Caribbean getaway \u8211\'20\'13 is described by the journalist Michael Wolff in his new book, which also details how {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/books/2023/sep/20/rupert-murdoch-wished-donald-trump-dead-michael-wolff-book"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Murdoch often wishes Trump dead}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Don\u8217\'20\'19t miss this: The sleep secret \u8211\'20\'13 how lucid dreams can make us fitter, more creative and less anxious\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CA lucid dream is a dream where you know that you\u8217\'20\'19re dreaming as the dream is happening,\u8221\'20\'1D says Charlie Morley, the author of Lucid Dreaming Made Easy. \u8220\'20\'1CSo, you\u8217\'20\'19re still sound asleep but in the dream and you are telling yourself: \u8216\'20\'18I know this is all a dream.\u8217\'20\'19 Most people have had a few. If you reckon you haven\u8217\'20\'19t, you might want to think about whether you have ever had a nightmare where you\u8217\'20\'19ve reassured yourself by saying: \u8216\'20\'18This isn\u8217\'20\'19t real \u8211\'20\'13 I have to wake up.\u8217\'20\'19 That\u8217\'20\'19s also a lucid dream.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Freud described dreams as windows into our repressed desires. Today, researchers are using them to boost athletic performance and help veterans with PTSD, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/lifeandstyle/2023/sep/20/the-sleep-secret-how-lucid-dreams-can-make-us-fitter-more-creative-and-less-anxious"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 unlocking huge benefits for us all}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Climate check: Global heating made Greece and Libya floods more likely, study says\par \par \uc2 Carbon pollution led to heavier rains and stronger floods in Greece and Libya this month but other human factors were responsible for \u8220\'20\'1Cturning the extreme weather into a humanitarian disaster\u8221\'20\'1D, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/environment/2023/sep/19/global-heating-made-mediterranean-floods-more-likely-study-says"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 scientists have said}}}\uc2 . Global heating made the levels of rainfall that devastated the Mediterranean in early September up to 50 times more likely in Libya and up to 10 times more likely in Greece, according to a study from World Weather Attribution that used established methods but had not yet been peer-reviewed. The network of scientists, who were racing to understand extreme weather events as soon as they happen, found people were made more vulnerable to the rain because of factors such as building homes on floodplains, chopping down trees and not maintaining dams.\par \par \uc2 Last Thing: \u8216\'20\'18He swam, hooking my arm with his penis\u8217\'20\'19 \u8211\'20\'13 inside the dolphin sex scandal that outraged a nation\par \par \uc2 When someone mentions the year 1990, you might think of the last days of \uc2 Margaret Thatcher\uc2 , The Satanic Verses, poll tax, recession and the IRA. Or, you just might think of a man in the north-east of England {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/tv-and-radio/2023/sep/19/dolphin-sex-scandal-hooked-on-freddie"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 getting arrested for masturbating a dolphin}}}\uc2 . The man in question was the animal rights campaigner Alan Cooper. The whole intriguing story has now been turned into a podcast series.\par \par \uc2 The podcast, Hooked on Freddie, revolves around one particular incident, during which a boatload of people watched Cooper swimming with Freddie in the harbour and reported an incident to the police. Cooper describes the event on his website as such: \u8220\'20\'1CFreddie was his usual self, sometimes hooking me with his penis to the leg or arm \u8211\'20\'13 it was all perfectly normal, to me at least. It was only later when I was provided with the police statements that I realised otherwise.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Sign up\par \par \uc2 First Thing is delivered to thousands of inboxes every weekday. If you\u8217\'20\'19re not already signed up, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/info/2018/sep/17/guardian-us-morning-briefing-sign-up-to-stay-informed"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 subscribe now}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Get in touch\par \par \uc2 If you have any questions or comments about any of our newsletters please email {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "mailto:newsletters@theguardian.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 newsletters@theguardian.com}}}\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020230920ej9k0018r\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
