\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Trump says Republicans \u8216\'20\'18speak very inarticulately\u8217\'20\'19 about  \highlight22\uc2 abortion \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 Edward Helmore \par \uc2 1,101 \uc2 words\par \uc2 17 September 2023\par 20:18 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Trump talks about democratic principles, ageing politicians and \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights in wide ranging NBC interview\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/donaldtrump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Donald Trump}}}\uc2  grappled with a wide range of contentious issues in an interview with NBC that generated criticism against the network, including his thoughts on democratic principles, \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights and ageing politicians.\par \par \uc2 He also confirmed his interest in choosing \uc2 Kristi Noem\uc2  to be his vice-presidential running mate if he wins the Republican presidential nomination in 2024 as he seeks a second term in the White House.\par \par \uc2 In an interview on Sunday with Kristen Welker during her debut as host of NBC\u8217\'20\'19s Meet the Press, the former president advised members of his party to abandon their hardline stance of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  bans with no exceptions.\par \par \uc2 He said Republicans \u8220\'20\'1C {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nbcnews.com/politics/donald-trump/trump-bring-country-together-abortion-meet-the-press-rcna105311"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 speak very inarticulately}}}\uc2  \u8221\'20\'1D about \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  and criticized those who push for \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  bans without exceptions in the cases of rape, incest and the health of the mother.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1COther than certain parts of the country, you can\u8217\'20\'19t \u8211\'20\'13 you\u8217\'20\'19re not going to win on this issue,\u8221\'20\'1D said Trump, who faces more than 90 pending criminal charges across four separate indictments, including for subversion of the 2020 election which he lost to \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CBut you will win on this issue when you come up with the right number of weeks.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Trump predicted that both sides would eventually come together on the issue after the \uc2 US supreme court\uc2  last year eliminated the federal \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights that had been put in place decades earlier by the Roe v Wade ruling. Three justices whom he appointed to the supreme court made the elimination of those rights a reality.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CFor the first time in \u8230\'20\'26 years, you\u8217\'20\'19ll have an issue that we can put behind us,\u8221\'20\'1D he said.\par \par \uc2 Trump said he is \u8220\'20\'1Call for\u8221\'20\'1D a presidency competency test, but the 77-year-old expressed his opposition to age limits.\par \par \uc2 He alluded to taking a mental competency test two or three years ago and boasted that he \u8220\'20\'1Caced it\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI get everything right,\u8221\'20\'1D Trump said during the interview conducted at his Bedminster, New Jersey, golf retreat. \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19m all for testing. I frankly think testing would be a good thing.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 In 2020, it was revealed that some of the early questions in that test involved Trump identifying an elephant and counting backward from 100.\par \par \uc2 Asked if it is time for a new generation of US leadership, Trump said: \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s always time for a new generation.\u8221\'20\'1D But he qualified his answer: \u8220\'20\'1CSome of the greatest world leaders have been in their 80s.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Those remarks from Trump came after retiring Republican US senator \uc2 Mitt Romney\uc2  of Utah called for a \u8220\'20\'1Cnew generation of leaders\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Trump notably defended Biden, his Democratic rival, on his age. A poll last month from the Associated Press and the Norc Center for Public Affairs showed 77% of Americans \u8211\'20\'13 including 69% of Democrats \u8211\'20\'13 think the 80-year-old Biden is too old to serve a second term.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI don\u8217\'20\'19t think Biden\u8217\'20\'19s too old,\u8221\'20\'1D Trump said to Welker. \u8220\'20\'1CBut I think he\u8217\'20\'19s incompetent, and that\u8217\'20\'19s a bigger problem. It\u8217\'20\'19s really a level of competency, not the age.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Two days before Trump attacked Biden\u8217\'20\'19s acuity, Trump told a summit in Washington that a \u8220\'20\'1Ccognitively impaired\u8221\'20\'1D Biden would lead the US into \u8220\'20\'1Cworld war two\u8221\'20\'1D, which already occurred between 1939 and 1945.\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, Trump said he \u8220\'20\'1Cliked the concept\u8221\'20\'1D of having a woman as his running mate if he wins the Republican nomination, adding that he had his eye on Noem, the South Dakota governor. \u8220\'20\'1CI think she\u8217\'20\'19s fantastic,\u8221\'20\'1D he said. \u8220\'20\'1CShe\u8217\'20\'19s been a great governor. She gave me a very full-throated endorsement, a beautiful endorsement actually. Certainly she\u8217\'20\'19d be one of the people I\u8217\'20\'19d consider.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Noem recently confirmed that she was a candidate for the position. \u8220\'20\'1COf course, I would consider it,\u8221\'20\'1D {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.foxnews.com/media/south-dakota-gov-kristi-noem-consider-trumps-vice-president-spot-asked"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 she told Fox News}}}\uc2 . But that was before the governor was splashed across the tabloid press for allegedly having an affair with former Trump aide \uc2 Corey Lewandowski\uc2  since at least 2019.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.dailymail.co.uk/news/article-12509093/Kristin-Noem-Corey-Lewandowski-secret-affair.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 The Daily Mail\u8217\'20\'19s}}}\uc2  reporting has not been denied, though Noem\u8217\'20\'19s spokesperson said it was \u8220\'20\'1Cso predictable\u8221\'20\'1D that the South Dakota governor would be attacked soon after she endorsed Trump for the Republican nomination.\par \par \uc2 Trump was asked if he still believes democracy is the most effective form of government. \u8220\'20\'1CI do \u8211\'20\'13 but it has to be a democracy that\u8217\'20\'19s fair,\u8221\'20\'1D he said. \u8220\'20\'1CThis democracy \u8211\'20\'13 I don\u8217\'20\'19t consider us to have much of a democracy right now.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 He went on to complain about the indictments against him, which also contain charges for allegedly mishandling classified documents and attempting to conceal hush money payments to adult film actor Stormy Daniels.\par \par \uc2 Those charges are separate from civil cases that include a $250m lawsuit by the New York attorney general about his business affairs as well as a defamation claim stemming from a rape accusation that a judge has deemed to be \u8220\'20\'1Csubstantially true\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 During the interview, Trump said he was not {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nbcnews.com/meet-the-press/meet-the-press/trump-doesnt-worry-going-jail-meet-the-press-rcna105312"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1Cconsumed}}}\uc2  \u8221\'20\'1D with the prospect of prison time.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI don\u8217\'20\'19t even think about it,\u8221\'20\'1D Trump said. \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19m built a little differently I guess, because I have had people come up to me and say, \u8216\'20\'18How do you do it, sir? How do you do it?\u8217\'20\'19 I don\u8217\'20\'19t even think about it.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI truly feel that, in the end, we\u8217\'20\'19re going to win.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Trump has maintained he would not pardon himself if he is re-elected, but he revealed to Welker that he had discussed pardoning himself in the dying days of his presidency \u8211\'20\'13 a sign that he and his legal team understood the legal peril he brought on to himself by challenging the election\u8217\'20\'19s results.\par \par \uc2 He said his failed election challenges eventually prompted him to ignore advice from his attorneys \u8220\'20\'1Cbecause I didn\u8217\'20\'19t respect them\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.mediaite.com/tv/sold-her-soul-boycottmeetthepress-trends-big-over-welkers-trump-interview/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Sunday\u8217\'20\'19s interview earned NBC criticism}}}\uc2  from many commentators who questioned the wisdom of giving such a soapbox to Trump after his alleged criminal misdeeds from before, during and after his presidency.\par \par \uc2 One question by Welker that some dismissed as a soft ball sought to discuss the contents of a message that Trump left for Biden when he left the White House.\par \par \uc2 Earlier this year, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/media/2023/may/10/donald-trump-cnn-town-hall-media-analysis"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 CNN was pilloried}}}\uc2  for giving Trump a town hall-style platform in New Hampshire that indirectly led to the dismissal of its programming architect, former morning TV producer and CNN chief Chris Licht.\par \par \uc2 NBC has said the network has also invited Biden to sit down for an interview with Welker.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020230917ej9h0015z\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
