\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Evangelical Christians need Republicans. Does the party need them?\b0\par\par\uc2 David Smith in Washington DC \par \uc2 1,727 \uc2 words\par \uc2 17 September 2023\par 11:51 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 The religious right is losing its grip as candidates respond to a voter majority that doesn\u8217\'20\'19t support a federal \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban\par \par \uc2 When \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  recalled how his three \uc2 US supreme court\uc2  justices {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/may/05/trump-abortion-supreme-court"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 helped repeal}}}\uc2  the nationwide right to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the audience rose to its feet and erupted in whistles, whoops and prolonged applause. But even as the former president basked in the religious right\u8217\'20\'19s moment of triumph, he went on to deliver a warning.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI will say politically, it\u8217\'20\'19s a very tough, it\u8217\'20\'19s a very tough decision for some people, but very, very hard on elections. Very, very hard,\u8221\'20\'1D {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://apnews.com/article/abortion-federal-ban-trump-gop-2024-20586bbb64a511030ef58290e98f99f0"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Trump told a gathering}}}\uc2  of Christian conservatives in the ballroom of a Washington hotel. \u8220\'20\'1CWe had midterms and this was an issue, you know.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 He added: \u8220\'20\'1CNow we can win elections on this issue but it\u8217\'20\'19s very delicate and explaining it properly is extremely important. Many politicians who are pro-life do not know how to properly discuss this topic, which is so important to the people in this room, so important to millions and millions of people in our country.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 It was a rare moment of sober reflection during an hour-long speech that otherwise had all the subtlety of a sledgehammer. It also offered a glimpse of the dilemma facing evangelicals as they push the Republican field to embrace their extremist agenda in next year\u8217\'20\'19s presidential election.\par \par \uc2 Other top Republican candidates for 2024 also trod carefully on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  at the \uc2 Family Research Council\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://prayvotestand.org/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Pray Vote Stand Summit}}}\uc2  on Friday. The tech entrepreneur \uc2 Vivek Ramaswamy\uc2  did not mention the word at all. \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2 , the governor of Florida, cited his state\u8217\'20\'19s six-week \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban in a single sentence. Only \uc2 Mike Pence\uc2 , the devout former vice-president, unambiguously committed to a 15-week \u8220\'20\'1Cnational standard\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 The caution signaled Republicans\u8217\'20\'19 awareness of how politically radioactive the issue has become, as evidenced by last year\u8217\'20\'19s midterm elections and other votes in states such as Kansas, Ohio and Wisconsin. A USA Today/\uc2 Suffolk University\uc2  poll in June found that 80% of Americans oppose a federal \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban, including 65% of Republicans and 83% of independents.\par \par \uc2 But the religious right looks to be making more headway on other issues. Trump, who got by far the most enthusiastic reception, declared: \u8220\'20\'1COn day one I will sign a new executive order to cut federal funding for any school pushing critical race theory, transgender insanity and other inappropriate racial, sexual or political content on our children.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Earlier, DeSantis, touting his war on \u8220\'20\'1Cwoke\u8221\'20\'1D, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://grabien.com/file/getmedia?id=2089363&key=1951323560b83f77925b00122534b70b&userid=18055"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 boasted that Florida}}}\uc2  has outlawed puberty blockers and gender surgeries, prohibited \u8220\'20\'1Cgender ideology\u8221\'20\'1D in schools and prevented teachers forcing students to identify their pronouns. \u8220\'20\'1CWe\u8217\'20\'19re not doing the pronoun Olympics in the state of Florida,\u8221\'20\'1D he told the conference.\par \par \uc2 Trailing Trump in opinion polls, DeSantis brought some attendees to their feet by barking: \u8220\'20\'1CDo not tell me that a man can become a woman. Do not tell me that a man can get pregnant and expect me to accept that.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 DeSantis\u8217\'20\'19s book {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/books/2023/feb/26/the-courage-to-be-free-review-ron-desantis-trump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 The Courage to Be Free}}}\uc2  was on sale at the conference venue, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.omnihotels.com/hotels/washington-dc-shoreham?utm_source=gmblisting&utm_medium=organic"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the Omni Shoreham Hotel}}}\uc2 , along with titles such as Busting the Barricades by Laura Ingraham, Tucker (about the rightwing host \uc2 Tucker Carlson\uc2 ) by Chadwick Moore, Blackout by \uc2 Candace Owens\uc2 , Woke Inc by \uc2 Vivek Ramaswamy\uc2 , The Art of the Deal by \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  and The Greatest Speeches of Donald J Trump.\par \par \uc2 Attendees wandered through an exhibition hall offering \u8220\'20\'1Cbiblically responsible retirement plans\u8221\'20\'1D, \u8220\'20\'1Cscience and statistics for the pro-life movement\u8221\'20\'1D and Christian-friendly children\u8217\'20\'19s books. A whiteboard asked people to write their favorite scripture while a lifesize cardboard cutout of \uc2 Ronald Reagan\uc2  had a speech bubble playing on one of 40th president\u8217\'20\'19s most famous lines with : \u8220\'20\'1CMr Gorbachev, tear down this hall!\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The backdrop helped imbue religious conservatives with confidence that the presidential contenders will keep their values front and centre.\par \par \uc2 Anita Stine, 84, a Trump supporter from Irvine, California, said: \u8220\'20\'1CI believe that the Republican candidates are going to pursue them strongly because they\u8217\'20\'19re biblical. Not take a life through \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , not try to claim that you\u8217\'20\'19re a man when you\u8217\'20\'19re a woman \u8211\'20\'13 the principles in the Bible are just put right there for us to read and to follow and God\u8217\'20\'19s word is truth.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 But many interviewed by the Guardian tempered such optimism with the hard-headed realism and patience that was rewarded with the fall of Roe v Wade after nearly {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2020/mar/04/us-abortion-rights-evangelical-campaign"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 50 years of striving}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Michael Case, 68, from Beltsville, Maryland, said: \u8220\'20\'1CI want the candidate that\u8217\'20\'19s going to win. I\u8217\'20\'19m very focused on winning this year. So if I had to pick right this second, I would pick Trump.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Case, who is retired from working at the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nrc.gov/about-nrc.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Nuclear Regulatory Commission}}}\uc2 , personally favors a federal \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban at six weeks or even less but acknowledged: \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19m still against \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  but you\u8217\'20\'19ve got to recognize that there are a lot of people who have a different view and so we need to turn their hearts and minds and that takes a little time. It\u8217\'20\'19s OK to be a little bit pragmatic and win.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Younger voters agree on the need for step-by-step expediency. Lily Tu, 19, a student from Stockton, California, praised Nikki Haley, the former governor of South Carolina, who during the first Republican primary debate pointed out that a national \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban would not pass the Senate and urged Americans to \u8220\'20\'1C {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/2023/09/09/us/politics/haley-abortion-2024-presidential-race.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 stop demonising}}}\uc2  \u8221\'20\'1D the issue.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI like Nikki Haley\u8217\'20\'19s approach because she seems really down to earth in the way that she was having realistic expectations,\u8221\'20\'1D she said. \u8220\'20\'1CIf they\u8217\'20\'19re promising immediate change, that\u8217\'20\'19s not really going to happen. But I trust in those who will take the smaller steps that will maybe lead towards that ultimate goal.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Jimmy Hammond, 74, a pastor from Lumberton, North Carolina, and a Vietnam war veteran, is adamantly opposed to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s not a political issue with me; it\u8217\'20\'19s a biblical issue,\u8221\'20\'1D he said. \u8220\'20\'1C\b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  is not right: it\u8217\'20\'19s killing the child and a woman don\u8217\'20\'19t have that right with her body because God gave her her body.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Hammond is sceptical that any of the candidates will take such a hard line on this or other religious right priorities. He said: \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19m not at all confident any of them would do what is right about it. They\u8217\'20\'19re going to do what\u8217\'20\'19s politically motivating them most of the time.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Trump, who bills himself as the \u8220\'20\'1Cmost pro-life president\u8221\'20\'1D in American history, has been deliberately vague on where the movement goes post-Roe. In June he said: \u8220\'20\'1CWhat I\u8217\'20\'19ll do is negotiate so people are happy.\u8221\'20\'1D His reluctance to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://apnews.com/article/abortion-federal-ban-trump-gop-2024-20586bbb64a511030ef58290e98f99f0"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 endorse a federal ban}}}\uc2  has exposed him to attacks from Susan B Anthony Pro-Life America, a major anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  group, and others on the right.\par \par \uc2 Pence told reporters on Friday: \u8220\'20\'1CHe promised to govern as a conservative in 2016 but what I want voters to know is he makes no such promise today. In fact, President Trump has actually {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.foxnews.com/politics/trump-blames-pro-life-republicans-midterm-loss"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 blamed election losses in 2022}}}\uc2  on overturning Roe versus Wade. He\u8217\'20\'19s joined other voices in this campaign trying to marginalize the right to life as a state-only issue.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Trump\u8217\'20\'19s circumspection may have cost him the vote of Ken Oliver, 59, from Williamsburg, Virginia, who said he prefers the clarity of DeSantis on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  and gender identity. \u8220\'20\'1CFormer president Trump, despite all the merits and many good things he did, is relatively weak in comparison to other candidates, and especially governor DeSantis, on these issues, which are core issues for social conservatives.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Oliver believes that a federal \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban can be achieved incrementally. \u8220\'20\'1CWe\u8217\'20\'19re not looking back. We\u8217\'20\'19re looking forward. We need to build a consensus around limitations to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , whether it\u8217\'20\'19s six weeks or 15 weeks or 20 weeks. Why shy away from that?\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Trump remains well ahead of every major Republican demographic in the race for the party nomination. He has a roughly 35 percentage-point lead over DeSantis and Ramaswamy among evangelical Christians, according to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.reuters.com/world/us/donald-trump-ron-desantis-converge-us-capital-court-evangelical-vote-2023-09-15/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a Reuters/Ipsos poll this week}}}\uc2 , despite him having been found liable for sexually abusing a New York woman in 1996 and indicted over hush-money payments to an adult film star.\par \par \uc2 Since early in Trump\u8217\'20\'19s presidency, some evangelicals have {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/2018/12/31/opinion/trump-evangelicals-cyrus-king.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 likened him to Cyrus the Great}}}\uc2 , the Persian king who, according to the Bible, enabled Jews to return to Israel from their exile in Babylon. From this perspective, Trump\u8217\'20\'19s own behavior and beliefs are less important than his identity as a vessel of God\u8217\'20\'19s will. Voters say they are choosing a president, not a pastor.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://960thepatriot.com/personality/elaine-beck"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Elaine Beck}}}\uc2 , 75, a Christian media personality from Tucson, Arizona, said she knows Trump personally and is confident he will pursue the religious right\u8217\'20\'19s goals in a second term: \u8220\'20\'1CIt has to be God\u8217\'20\'19s way or no way and I believe that God is working in President Trump\u8217\'20\'19s life to help him see that, just like he does you or me or anybody else.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 However, even as they push a hardline agenda, evangelical voters may find their leverage over Republican candidates waning. Ryan Burge, a political scientist at \uc2 Eastern Illinois University\uc2 , {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.politico.com/news/magazine/2023/09/12/republicans-church-trump-00113565"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 wrote on the Politico website}}}\uc2  that the religious right\u8217\'20\'19s grip on the party is weakening with every election cycle.\par \par \uc2 Trump can therefore afford some erosion of support among evangelicals, Burge argued: \u8220\'20\'1CThat\u8217\'20\'19s because Trump\u8217\'20\'19s real base of support in the 2016 primary contest came from a rising group in the GOP whose impact has been largely unnoticed: Republicans who hardly ever darken the door of a church, synagogue or mosque.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Pence, however, denies that the ground is shifting beneath his feet. He told the Guardian: \u8220\'20\'1CNo, I really believe that the majority of Republicans cherish faith, cherish freedom, cherish those conservative values.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CAs I travel around Iowa and travel around New Hampshire, the warm reception that we receive from almost everybody affirms to me \u8211\'20\'13 as someone who\u8217\'20\'19s been in the conservative movement as an evangelical Christian \u8211\'20\'13 that the support for our traditional values is alive and well in the GOP today.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020230917ej9h000ul\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
