\par\par \uc2 Opinion\par \b \uc2 The war on women who use  \highlight22\uc2 abortion \highlight\uc2  pills takes a terrifying new turn\b0\par\par\uc2 Arwa Mahdawi \par \uc2 1,100 \uc2 words\par \uc2 16 September 2023\par 13:45 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Researchers in Poland have developed tests that can detect if a woman has taken mifepristone. It\u8217\'20\'19s a chilling development\par \par \uc2 The war on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  pills takes a terrifying new turn\par \par \uc2 Have you ever come across a scientific study and immediately thought to yourself: why? What was the point of this work exactly? Why were resources and brainpower devoted to figuring this particular thing out?\par \par \uc2 Normally I have this thought when a study comes out about whether, for example, Viagra can help hamsters recover from jet lag ( {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/another-use-viagra-curing-hamster-jet-lag-180962613/#:~:text=The%20researchers%20found%20that%20the,guanosine%20monophosphate%20in%20the%20body."}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 it can!}}}\uc2  ) or whether mosquitoes like electronic dance music ( {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/playing-skrillex-may-help-ward-mosquito-bites-180971849/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 not really!).}}}\uc2  On this occasion, however, it was prompted by news that researchers in Poland have developed tests that can detect whether a woman has taken mifepristone and misoprostol, the drugs that are used in a medication \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  and colloquially known as \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  pills.\par \par \uc2 Why the desperate need to figure this out? According to the researchers, one of whom apparently identifies as pro-choice, it\u8217\'20\'19s because they were very worried about whether \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  pills on the black market posed a threat to public health. Which seems rather a strange explanation, since those drugs have been around for {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.france24.com/en/health/20230426-the-long-and-winding-history-of-the-war-on-abortion-drugs"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 decades}}}\uc2  and there is an overwhelming amount of evidence that they are safe and effective.\par \par \uc2 The real reason there was a state-funded study to try detect the use of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  pills is probably because Poland has draconian \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  laws \u8211\'20\'13 a near-ban on legal \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  was implemented in 2020 \u8211\'20\'13 and the government wants to crack down on any woman who dares to exercise autonomy over her own body. Under Polish law, you can\u8217\'20\'19t go to jail for taking \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  pills, but if you help someone else procure them you can be prosecuted. Last March, for example, a Polish human rights activist was sentenced to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/global-development/2023/mar/14/polish-court-convicts-activist-for-helping-woman-get-abortion-pills"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 eight months of community service}}}\uc2  for sending pills to a woman who was a victim of domestic violence.\par \par \uc2 In the past, trying to prove someone had taken \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  pills was tricky. It was impossible to tell whether a woman had experienced a miscarriage or had a medical \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 : the symptoms are the same and the technology didn\u8217\'20\'19t exist to find evidence mifepristone and misoprostol had been ingested. Now, however, a government intent on controlling women has chilling new tools at its disposal. And, according to a New York Times piece by {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/2023/09/14/opinion/abortion-pills-testing-poland.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Patrick Adams}}}\uc2 , it is using them: Polish authorities have already leveraged the new tests to investigate the outcomes of pregnancies.\par \par \uc2 While there is no evidence that these tests are being used anywhere else in the world I imagine that anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  activists in the US are champing at the bit to get their hands on them. Conservatives, after all, are already trying to clamp down on the availability of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  pills in the US: in August, a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/aug/16/restriction-abortion-pill-mifepristone-access-fda-court-decision"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 federal appeals court}}}\uc2  ruled that access to mifepristone should be limited. Extremists are going to continue trying to chip away at access to medication abortions; they are going to continue their calls for women who get abortions to be charged with murder. A small but frighteningly zealous group of lawmakers will not be happy until every woman who so much as thinks about \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  is thrown in jail. And once they\u8217\'20\'19ve outlawed all \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  they\u8217\'20\'19ll move on to birth control.\par \par \uc2 You think I\u8217\'20\'19m exaggerating? I wish I was. Daniel Cameron, the Republican candidate for governor in Kentucky, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://jessica.substack.com/p/abortion-every-day-91323"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 has said}}}\uc2  he believes hormonal birth control (ie the morning-after pill) is \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nbcnews.com/meet-the-press/meetthepressblog/kentucky-governor-hopeful-daniel-cameron-faces-heat-health-care-positi-rcna104659"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 should be criminalized}}}\uc2 . Last year, the Republican governor of Mississippi {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cnn.com/2022/05/08/politics/mississippi-abortion-contraception-roe-wade-cnntv/index.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 refused to rule}}}\uc2  out the possibility he might ban certain forms of contraception. Meanwhile, a number of states have passed \u8220\'20\'1Cpersonhood\u8221\'20\'1D laws, which state that life begins at the moment of fertilization \u8211\'20\'13 a position {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nbcnews.com/news/us-news/louisiana-lawmakers-advance-bill-classify-abortion-homicide-rcna27594"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 which paves the way}}}\uc2  for charging women who use emergency contraception with murder. No doubt all these lawmakers are watching Poland\u8217\'20\'19s development of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  pill testing methods with glee. It seems depressingly inevitable that technology like this is coming to a red state near you soon.\par \par \uc2 Young women in the US are afraid to get pregnant in a post-Roe world\par \par \uc2 Thirty-four per cent of women aged 18-39 questioned in a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.politico.com/news/magazine/2023/09/13/dobbs-pregnancy-maternal-health-00115561"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 new poll }}}\uc2  said they or someone they know personally has \u8220\'20\'1Cdecided not to get pregnant due to concerns about managing pregnancy-related medical emergencies \u8230\'20\'26 the Dobbs decision, it seems, has fundamentally altered how people feel about having families and the calculus for getting pregnant\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 DeSantis does not support criminalizing women who get abortions after all\par \par \uc2 The Florida governor {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/sep/14/ron-desantis-abortion-law-contradict-criminalize"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 recently insisted}}}\uc2  that it is only the doctors who perform the \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  that will be liable for fines and imprisonment under the extreme six-week \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban he signed the law. So that\u8217\'20\'19s OK, then!\par \par \uc2 Happiness of girls and young women at lowest level since 2009, shows UK poll\par \par \uc2 The biggest drop in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/society/2023/sep/13/happiness-of-girls-and-young-women-at-lowest-level-since-2009-shows-uk-poll"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 happiness is among seven- to 10-year-olds}}}\uc2 . Only 28% say they are happy compared with well over half in 2009.\par \par \uc2 Silicon Valley bros are having testosterone parties\par \par \uc2 Tickets to the \u8220\'20\'1CT parties\u8221\'20\'1D {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.businessinsider.com/testosterone-parties-silicon-valley-hormone-boosting-bio-hack-2023-9"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 cost between $100 and $400}}}\uc2 . According to founder Jeff Tang, guests can get blood tests to check their testosterone levels while discussing approaches to \u8220\'20\'1Coptimizing T naturally, endocrine disrupters, and supplements\u8221\'20\'1D while dining on \u8220\'20\'1Chome-made kefir, beef patties (heart, spleen, kidney) and pork loin (blood, liver), and delicious Colombian coffee\u8221\'20\'1D. Tang, by the way, is not a doctor or a scientist. \u8220\'20\'1CJust a guy who likes experimenting with his health and productivity.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Mahsa Amini and a year of brutality and courage in Iran\par \par \uc2 It\u8217\'20\'19s the first anniversary of the death in custody of 22-year-old Amini, who was allegedly detained for not wearing a headscarf. The Iranian illustrator Roshi Rouzbehani powerfully recaps a year of tumult {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/global-development/gallery/2023/sep/14/mahsa-amini-and-a-year-of-brutality-and-courage-in-iran-in-illustrations"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 for the Guardian}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Man accused of groping Spanish reporter live on air arrested\par \par \uc2 Journalist Isa Balado was just trying to do her job when a passerby groped her live on air. He\u8217\'20\'19s now been {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/video/2023/sep/14/man-arrested-after-apparently-groping-spanish-reporter-live-on-air-video-report"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 arrested for sexual assault}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The week in paw-triarchy\par \par \uc2 What happens to robot dogs when they get old? \uc2 Sony Japan\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s pack of digital canines are heading to a nursing home. Five years after releasing a reboot of the ERS-1000 Aibo robot dogs from the late 90s, \uc2 Sony\uc2  is launching an \u8220\'20\'1CAibo foster parent program\u8221\'20\'1D that lets owners who have cancelled their digital subscriptions send the dogs to nursing homes and medical facilities where they can {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theverge.com/2023/9/11/23867799/sony-launches-foster-care-program-aibo-robot-dog-sustainability"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 provide emotional support}}}\uc2  and spread paws-itivity.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020230916ej9g001p7\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
