\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 DeSantis contradicts own  \highlight22\uc2 abortion \highlight\uc2  law to claim woman will not be criminalized\b0\par\par\uc2 Ed Pilkington \par \uc2 676 \uc2 words\par \uc2 15 September 2023\par 14:51 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Florida six-week ban punishes anyone who \u8216\'20\'18actively participates\u8217\'20\'19 in termination but governor says only doctors criminally liable\par \par \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2  has contradicted the wording of the six-week \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban that he himself signed into law in April, insisting that women who terminate their pregnancies will not be criminalized under the prohibition.\par \par \uc2 The Florida governor and Republican White House hopeful told {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cbsnews.com/news/ron-desantis-abortion-florida-law-women-penalities/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 CBS Evening News}}}\uc2  that women would not be liable for fines and imprisonment under the ban. Only doctors who perform abortions would be targeted.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe have no criminal penalty. The penalties are for the physician,\u8221\'20\'1D he said.\par \par \uc2 Yet the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.flsenate.gov/Session/Bill/2023/300/BillText/er/HTML"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 wording of the law}}}\uc2  is written broadly enough that it could be interpreted as applying not only to doctors but also to pregnant women. It says that \u8220\'20\'1Cany person who willfully performs, or actively participates in a termination of pregnancy\u8221\'20\'1D in violation of the new law can be charged with a felony.\par \par \uc2 DeSantis was asked by CBS News whether a woman was not \u8220\'20\'1Cactively participating\u8221\'20\'1D in the termination of her pregnancy. He replied: \u8220\'20\'1CNo, because she\u8217\'20\'19s not a medical practitioner.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Florida\u8217\'20\'19s six-week \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban, which state Republicans refer to by the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2019/jun/07/abortion-the-guardian-style-guide"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 medically misleading}}}\uc2  title the \u8220\'20\'1CHeartbeat Protection Act\u8221\'20\'1D, is currently on hold as it faces a legal challenge before the state supreme court. While those legal proceedings are ongoing, an earlier 15-week \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban is in operation.\par \par \uc2 After this article was published, DeSantis\u8217\'20\'19s press secretary, Jeremy Redfern, contacted the Guardian to say that under existing Florida state law, pregnant women were safe from criminal penalties relating to abortions.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CFlorida supreme court precedent has affirmed the longstanding common law doctrine preventing a pregnant woman from being held criminally liable for receiving an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 . According to the court, the \u8216\'20\'18criminal laws were intended to protect, not punish her\u8217\'20\'19,\u8221\'20\'1D Redfern said.\par \par \uc2 DeSantis\u8217\'20\'19s protestation that women were safe under the pending ban speaks to the dual standards that many Republicans have applied to this issue. They strive to appear as tough on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  as possible, to appeal to the hard-right base of their party, while at the same time trying to appear moderate so as not to alienate the general voters, especially women.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1C\uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2  may try to pull the wool over voters\u8217\'20\'19 eyes, but Floridians know that he\u8217\'20\'19ll stop at nothing to ban \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  and punish the people who have them,\u8221\'20\'1D Laura Goodhue, executive director of the Florida Alliance of Planned Parenthood Affiliates, told the Guardian. \u8220\'20\'1CHe has signed two devastating \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  bans, and he did that without any thought of the consequences for Floridians and their families.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Goodhue added that while the \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban does not explicitly criminalize those seeking care, it has already created a dangerous climate for them.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CFloridians in need of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  have reported being afraid to seek help from their loved ones or to leave the state for care where it is legal,\u8221\'20\'1D she said.\par \par \uc2 The six-week prohibition, introduced in the wake of the \uc2 US supreme court\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s decision to overturn the right to an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  in its {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2022/jun/24/roe-v-wade-overturned-abortion-summary-supreme-court"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  Dobbs ruling}}}\uc2 , has been criticised as extreme because at that stage many women do not even know that they are pregnant. The bill contains {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2023/apr/13/florida-six-week-abortion-ban-republicans"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 very limited exceptions}}}\uc2 , including to save the woman\u8217\'20\'19s life.\par \par \uc2 Women wanting to terminate pregnancies resulting from rape or incest have until 15 weeks providing they can prove their claim with documentation.\par \par \uc2 The number of abortions performed in Florida in the first half of this year has increased compared with a similar period before Dobbs was introduced. The pattern is part of a significant nationwide uptick in \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  numbers compared with 2020, according to the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.guttmacher.org/monthly-abortion-provision-study"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Guttmacher Institute}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 DeSantis blamed the increase in the number of abortions in his state on \u8220\'20\'1C\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  tourism\u8221\'20\'1D. Were the six-week ban allowed by the courts to replace the current 15-week ban, it would \u8220\'20\'1Cprobably stop the whole \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  tourism thing. We don\u8217\'20\'19t want to be an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  tourism destination.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020230914ej9e002gx\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
