\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 McCarthy \u8216\'20\'18doing Trump\u8217\'20\'19s bidding\u8217\'20\'19 by backing impeachment inquiry, Biden campaign says \u8211\'20\'13 as it happened\b0\par\par\uc2 Maanvi Singh (now) and L\u233\'00\'E9onie Chao-Fong (earlier) \par \uc2 9,602 \uc2 words\par \uc2 13 September 2023\par 12:58 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 This live blog is now closed. You read our latest full report on House moves to impeach Biden below:House speaker McCarthy announces Biden impeachment inquiry\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.12pm BST\par \par \uc2 Today's recap\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The speaker of the House of Representatives, Kevin McCarthy, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/sep/12/trump-indictments-mccarthy-government-shutdown-biden-politics-live-updates?page=with:block-650086e28f0873945374ded9#block-650086e28f0873945374ded9"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 announced that}}}\uc2  Republicans would open an impeachment investigation into \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  over unproven allegations of corruption in his family\u8217\'20\'19s business dealings. House Republicans have so far have not produced hard evidence linking the business dealings of \uc2 Hunter Biden\uc2  and his father.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The announcement by McCarthy kicks off what are expected to be weeks of Republican-led hearings intended to convince Americans that the president profited from the business dealings of his son \uc2 Hunter Biden\uc2  and other family members. While impeachment can be the first step to removing a president from office, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/sep/12/trump-indictments-mccarthy-government-shutdown-biden-politics-live-updates?page=with:block-650082018f0873945374de6a#block-650082018f0873945374de6a"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 that appears unlikely to happen.}}}\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 A spokesperson for the Biden-Harris 2024 campaign said McCarthy has {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/sep/12/trump-indictments-mccarthy-government-shutdown-biden-politics-live-updates?page=with:block-6500accb8f0873945374e103#block-6500accb8f0873945374e103"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1Ccemented his role}}}\uc2  as the Trump campaign\u8217\'20\'19s super-surrogate by turning the House of Representatives into an arm of his presidential campaign\u8221\'20\'1D. \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  has been {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/sep/12/trump-indictments-mccarthy-government-shutdown-biden-politics-live-updates?page=with:block-6500bf2d8f08cf50e16136a7#block-6500bf2d8f08cf50e16136a7"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 weighing in behind the scenes}}}\uc2  in support of the House GOP push to impeach his successor, according to a report.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Ian Sams, the White House spokesperson for oversight and investigations, described McCarthy\u8217\'20\'19s announcement as {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/sep/12/trump-indictments-mccarthy-government-shutdown-biden-politics-live-updates?page=with:block-650092158f0893e8a8a018ff#block-650092158f0893e8a8a018ff"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1Cextreme politics at its worst\u8221\'20\'1D, }}}\uc2  adding that House GOP members had uncovered \u8220\'20\'1Cno evidence of wrongdoing\u8221\'20\'1D in the months-long investigation into \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 It is unclear if the GOP has the evidence to substantiate the long-running claims, or even the votes for impeachment. McCarthy plans to convene House GOP members behind closed doors this week to discuss the Biden impeachment.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 James Comer\uc2 , the chair of the House oversight committee leading the impeachment inquiry into Biden, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/sep/12/trump-indictments-mccarthy-government-shutdown-biden-politics-live-updates?page=with:block-65008af28f08cf50e1613446#block-65008af28f08cf50e1613446"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 spent \u8220\'20\'1Ceight months of abject failure\u8221\'20\'1D}}}\uc2  in trying to prove the president guilty of wrongdoing, a watchdog released earlier this week said. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/sep/12/trump-indictments-mccarthy-government-shutdown-biden-politics-live-updates?page=with:block-65007f7c8f08cf50e161336b#block-65007f7c8f08cf50e161336b"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 The report}}}\uc2  by the Congressional Integrity Project offers an anatomy of a fake scandal, detailing a series of exaggerated assertions that have shriveled under scrutiny.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Vladimir Putin\uc2  described the recent indictments of \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  as \u8220\'20\'1Cpolitical persecution\u8221\'20\'1D as the Russian leader {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2023/sep/12/putin-trump-political-persecution-claims"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 waded back into a US presidential campaign}}}\uc2  for the third consecutive election cycle. \u8220\'20\'1CI believe that everything happening at the moment is good. Because it demonstrates the rottenness of the American political system,\u8221\'20\'1D Putin remarked during an economic forum in the far eastern Russian city of Vladivostok.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The tech entrepreneur \uc2 Andrew Yang\uc2 , who ran for the Democratic presidential nomination in 2020, has \u8220\'20\'1Chad conversations\u8221\'20\'1D with No Labels, a group considering launching a third-party candidate in the 2024 election. Names linked to a No Labels candidacy have included Joe Manchin, the Democratic senator from West Virginia, and \uc2 Larry Hogan\uc2 , a former Republican governor of Maryland.\par \par \uc2 You can read the full report on the impeachment inquiry here:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/sep/12/biden-impeachment-kevin-mccarthy-announcement"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 House speaker Kevin McCarthy announces impeachment inquiry into Joe Biden}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.11pm BST\par \par \uc2 Almost all the Republicans running for the presidential nomination have endorsed the impeachment inquiry.\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  is notably the only one who\u8217\'20\'19s called impeachment outright. \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2 , Tim Scott, \uc2 Mike Pence\uc2 , Nikki Haley and \uc2 Vivek Ramaswamy\uc2  have all expressed support for the inquiry.\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, \uc2 Chris Christie\uc2  said he supports investigations, but noted, \u8220\'20\'1CI think we\u8217\'20\'19re cheapening impeachment by doing that kind of thing.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Will Hurd\uc2 , meanwhile said an investigation was warranted, but warned that if no evidence is found \u8220\'20\'1CI worry Republicans are walking into a political trap.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.36pm BST\par \par \uc2 Women challenge \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  bans in three states after emergency care denied\par \par \uc2 Women who say they were denied abortions in medical emergencies have taken legal action in Idaho, Oklahoma and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/tennessee"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Tennessee}}}\uc2 , in the latest attempt to challenge \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  bans that, \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  patients and doctors say, prevent people from getting care even when their health is in danger.\par \par \uc2 The lawsuits in Idaho and Tennessee, along with a federal complaint against a hospital in Oklahoma, were filed on Tuesday by the \uc2 Center for Reproductive Rights\uc2 , which filed a similar lawsuit on behalf of women in Texas earlier this year. Tuesday\u8217\'20\'19s filings were {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.washingtonpost.com/health/2023/09/12/abortion-rights-lawsuit-medical-care/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 first reported by the Washington Post}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI can\u8217\'20\'19t stop bad things from happening to people\u8217\'20\'19s pregnancies,\u8221\'20\'1D Jennifer Adkins, the lead plaintiff in the lawsuit filed in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/idaho"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Idaho}}}\uc2 , told the Post. \u8220\'20\'1CBut I want other Idahoans to feel safe and cared for.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 After the supreme court overturned Roe v Wade last year, states across the south and midwest enacted near-total \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  bans, many of which only allow abortions in cases of medical emergencies. However, doctors have repeatedly said that these bans, which contain non-medical language drafted by politicians, are too vague for medical providers to interpret. Instead, they are forced to wait until their patients get sick enough for them to intervene.\par \par \uc2 Read more:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2023/sep/12/women-denied-abortions-medical-emergencies-challenge-bans"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Women challenge \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  bans in three states after emergency care denied}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.00pm BST\par \par \uc2 Interim summary\par \par \uc2 It\u8217\'20\'19s been a busy Tuesday so far. Here\u8217\'20\'19s where things stand:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The speaker of the House of Representatives, Kevin McCarthy, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/sep/12/trump-indictments-mccarthy-government-shutdown-biden-politics-live-updates?page=with:block-650086e28f0873945374ded9#block-650086e28f0873945374ded9"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 announced that}}}\uc2  Republicans would open an impeachment investigation into \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  over unproven allegations of corruption in his family\u8217\'20\'19s business dealings. House Republicans have so far have not produced hard evidence linking the business dealings of \uc2 Hunter Biden\uc2  and his father.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The announcement by McCarthy kicks off what are expected to be weeks of Republican-led hearings intended to convince Americans that the president profited from the business dealings of his son \uc2 Hunter Biden\uc2  and other family members. While impeachment can be the first step to removing a president from office, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/sep/12/trump-indictments-mccarthy-government-shutdown-biden-politics-live-updates?page=with:block-650082018f0873945374de6a#block-650082018f0873945374de6a"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 that appears unlikely to happen.}}}\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 A spokesperson for the Biden-Harris 2024 campaign said McCarthy has {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/sep/12/trump-indictments-mccarthy-government-shutdown-biden-politics-live-updates?page=with:block-6500accb8f0873945374e103#block-6500accb8f0873945374e103"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1Ccemented his role}}}\uc2  as the Trump campaign\u8217\'20\'19s super-surrogate by turning the House of Representatives into an arm of his presidential campaign\u8221\'20\'1D. \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  has been {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/sep/12/trump-indictments-mccarthy-government-shutdown-biden-politics-live-updates?page=with:block-6500bf2d8f08cf50e16136a7#block-6500bf2d8f08cf50e16136a7"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 weighing in behind the scenes}}}\uc2  in support of the House GOP push to impeach his successor, according to a report.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Ian Sams, the White House spokesperson for oversight and investigations, described McCarthy\u8217\'20\'19s announcement as {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/sep/12/trump-indictments-mccarthy-government-shutdown-biden-politics-live-updates?page=with:block-650092158f0893e8a8a018ff#block-650092158f0893e8a8a018ff"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1Cextreme politics at its worst\u8221\'20\'1D, }}}\uc2  adding that House GOP members had uncovered \u8220\'20\'1Cno evidence of wrongdoing\u8221\'20\'1D in the months-long investigation into \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 It is unclear if the GOP has the evidence to substantiate the long-running claims, or even the votes for impeachment. McCarthy plans to convene House GOP members behind closed doors this week to discuss the Biden impeachment.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 James Comer\uc2 , the chair of the House oversight committee leading the impeachment inquiry into Biden, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/sep/12/trump-indictments-mccarthy-government-shutdown-biden-politics-live-updates?page=with:block-65008af28f08cf50e1613446#block-65008af28f08cf50e1613446"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 spent \u8220\'20\'1Ceight months of abject failure\u8221\'20\'1D}}}\uc2  in trying to prove the president guilty of wrongdoing, a watchdog released earlier this week said. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/sep/12/trump-indictments-mccarthy-government-shutdown-biden-politics-live-updates?page=with:block-65007f7c8f08cf50e161336b#block-65007f7c8f08cf50e161336b"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 The report}}}\uc2  by the Congressional Integrity Project offers an anatomy of a fake scandal, detailing a series of exaggerated assertions that have shriveled under scrutiny.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Vladimir Putin\uc2  described the recent indictments of \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  as \u8220\'20\'1Cpolitical persecution\u8221\'20\'1D as the Russian leader {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2023/sep/12/putin-trump-political-persecution-claims"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 waded back into a US presidential campaign}}}\uc2  for the third consecutive election cycle. \u8220\'20\'1CI believe that everything happening at the moment is good. Because it demonstrates the rottenness of the American political system,\u8221\'20\'1D Putin remarked during an economic forum in the far eastern Russian city of Vladivostok.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The tech entrepreneur \uc2 Andrew Yang\uc2 , who ran for the Democratic presidential nomination in 2020, has \u8220\'20\'1Chad conversations\u8221\'20\'1D with No Labels, a group considering launching a third-party candidate in the 2024 election. Names linked to a No Labels candidacy have included Joe Manchin, the Democratic senator from West Virginia, and \uc2 Larry Hogan\uc2 , a former Republican governor of Maryland.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.47pm BST\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  has been weighing in behind the scenes in support of the House GOP push to impeach \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 , including regularly speaking with a member of leadership in the lead up to Speaker Kevin McCarthy \u8217\'20\'19s announcement on Tuesday, according to a Politico {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.politico.com/news/2023/09/12/trump-privately-discussed-biden-impeachment-with-house-gopers-00115357"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 report. }}}\par \par \uc2 Trump has been speaking on a weekly basis with House GOP conference chair \uc2 Elise Stefanik\uc2 , who was the first member of Republican leadership to come out in support of impeachment, the report says.\par \par \uc2 The former president had dinner on Sunday night with the far-right congresswoman, \uc2 Marjorie Taylor Greene\uc2 , at his golf club in Bedminster, New Jersey, where the topic of impeachment was discussed, the report says.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.37pm BST\par \par \uc2 Two \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2  hats put up for auction at a Republican dinner in Florida at the weekend received precisely no bids, according to local party officials, suggesting his presidential campaign in his home state is going as badly as it is nationwide.\par \par \uc2 Details come in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.newsweek.com/photo-ron-desantis-unwanted-auction-items-goes-viral-1826082"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 this story by Newsweek}}}\uc2 , which says nobody signed up to bid on either of the red and white caps at the St Johns county GOP founders dinner in Ponte Vedra Beach on Saturday. St Johns is where the Florida governor was born.\par \par \uc2 enltrWow. Not a single person bid on the DeSantis hats at the St. Johns GOP meeting. St. Johns County, FL is literally his home county. Sad! {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/ENuNp2XKbW"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/ENuNp2XKbW}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Caroline Wren (@CarolineWren) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/CarolineWren/status/1700666064177156286?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 September 10, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 A photo of the barren sign-up sheets was posted to X, formerly \uc2 Twitter\uc2 , by Republican fundraiser Caroline Wren, the image taken two and a half hours after the event began.\par \par \uc2 Blake Paterson, chair of the county\u8217\'20\'19s Republican party, confirmed to Newsweek that the hats had attracted no bidders, though he characterized the event as a giveaway in exchange for donations rather than an auction.\par \par \uc2 Those in attendance at the dinner appeared to be overwhelmingly supporters of \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , DeSantis\u8217\'20\'19s rival for the 2024 Republican presidential nomination. They included Florida congressman Byron Donalds, a vocal Trump acolyte, and extremist conspiracy theorist Kari Lake, failed candidate for governor of Arizona in last year\u8217\'20\'19s election.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.33pm BST\par \par \uc2 Speaker Kevin McCarthy plans to convene House GOP members behind closed doors this week to discuss the Biden impeachment, amid uncertainty over whether he even has the support of rank-and-file Republicans behind him.\par \par \uc2 McCarthy is launching the impeachment inquiry on his own {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/sep/12/trump-indictments-mccarthy-government-shutdown-biden-politics-live-updates?page=with:block-650094d38f08cf50e16134fd#block-650094d38f08cf50e16134fd"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 and without a House floor vote, }}}\uc2  as he may not have enough support from his slim GOP majority, AP reported.\par \par \uc2 Senate Republican leader \uc2 Mitch McConnell\uc2  has warned House Republicans off the effort, but on Tuesday he said:\par \par \uc2 I don\u8217\'20\'19t think Speaker McCarthy needs advice from the Senate.\par \par \uc2 enltrSenate Minority Leader \uc2 Mitch McConnell\uc2  reacts to possible Biden impeachment inquiry:\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI don\u8217\'20\'19t have any advice to give to the House. They\u8217\'20\'19ve got a totally different set of challenges \u8230\'20\'26 So I think the best advice for the Senate is to do our job and we\u8217\'20\'19ll see how this plays out.\u8221\'20\'1D {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/lBzmvy6Yum"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/lBzmvy6Yum}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 The Recount (@therecount) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/therecount/status/1701673665442545952?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 September 12, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 Senate majority leader \uc2 Chuck Schumer\uc2  called the impeachment inquiry \u8220\'20\'1Cabsurd\u8221\'20\'1D. He told reporters:\par \par \uc2 The American people want us to do something that will make their lives better, not go off on these chases and witch hunts.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.21pm BST\par \par \uc2 House GOP members have found an \u8220\'20\'1Coverwhelming\u8221\'20\'1D amount of evidence showing \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  \u8220\'20\'1Clied to the American people about his knowledge and participation in his family\u8217\'20\'19s influence peddling schemes\u8221\'20\'1D, according to a joint statement by \uc2 James Comer\uc2 , Jim Jordan and Jason Smith.\par \par \uc2 Comer, Jordan and Smith chair the three committees expected to take the lead in the impeachment inquiry into the president. They are: the House committee on oversight and accountability, committee on the judiciary, and the committee on ways and means.\par \par \uc2 The statement says the investigation into Biden uncovered \u8220\'20\'1Cbank records, suspicious activity reports, emails, texts, and witness testimony\u8221\'20\'1D that showed the president \u8220\'20\'1Callowed his family to sell him as \u8216\'20\'18the brand\u8217\'20\'19 around the world\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Based on the evidence, we support the opening of an impeachment inquiry into President \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 . The House Committees on Oversight and Accountability, Judiciary, and Ways and Means, will continue to work to follow the facts to ensure President Biden is held accountable for abusing public office for his family\u8217\'20\'19s financial gain. The American people demand and deserve answers, transparency, and accountability for this blatant abuse of public office.\par \par \uc2 House Republicans have so far have not produced hard evidence linking the business dealings of \uc2 Hunter Biden\uc2  and the president.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 8.53pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.05pm BST\par \par \uc2 Senate Republicans are unhappy with House speaker Kevin McCarthy \u8217\'20\'19s decision to open an impeachment inquiry into \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  and concerned that it will backfire on the party, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://thehill.com/homenews/house/4200161-senate-gop-unhappy-with-mccarthy-on-impeachment-inquire-its-a-fools-errand/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 according}}}\uc2  to the Hill.\par \par \uc2 A Senate Republican, speaking on condition on anonymity, told the newspaper that even if the House did vote to impeach Biden after an inquiry, there is no way the Democrat-controlled Senate would vote to convict. Reports {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cnn.com/2023/08/28/politics/mccarthy-biden-impeachment-strategy/index.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 indicate}}}\uc2  McCarthy does not yet have enough votes in support of impeaching Biden.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s a waste of time. It\u8217\'20\'19s a fool\u8217\'20\'19s errand,\u8221\'20\'1D the GOP senator was quoted as saying.\par \par \uc2 We know how this is going to end. It just creates tumult within the conference. I can see it already how people are going to react when they send a message over if they go that far.\par \par \uc2 They noted that all the internal polling they had seen suggested GOP primary voters do not see impeachment as a priority. The senator added:\par \par \uc2 It seems like we\u8217\'20\'19re spending a lot of time on things that matter to them that don\u8217\'20\'19t matter to the people I want to have a positive opinion of Republicans next November \u8230\'20\'26 This is not driving [general election] turnout.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThey\u8217\'20\'19re all acting like children,\u8221\'20\'1D the GOP senator added.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.50pm BST\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s a statement from \uc2 Jamaal Bowman\uc2 , a Democratic congressman from New York, who accused House speaker Kevin McCarthy of announcing a \u8220\'20\'1Csham\u8221\'20\'1D impeachment inquiry into \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  in order to \u8220\'20\'1Cbring attention away from the failures of House Republicans to be able to pass a budget and avoid a government shutdown\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 The statement reads:\par \par \uc2 Speaker McCarthy and the dysfunctional Republican party are wasting time with their comical impeachment inquiry into President Biden instead of focusing on passing appropriations bills. We\u8217\'20\'19re just 3 weeks away from a government shutdown where millions of government employees won\u8217\'20\'19t get paid, small businesses won\u8217\'20\'19t be able to apply for federal loans, the \uc2 NIH\uc2  has to shut down most medical research, and more. We should be focused on doing our job by helping the American people & funding critical services, not forcing a shutdown & plotting baseless impeachment inquiries.\par \par \uc2 It goes on:\par \par \uc2 This is yet another example of Republican dysfunction and continues to show why many across the country do not want to trust or participate in our government.\par \par \uc2 enltrTo the supposed Speaker of the House Kevin McCarthy,\par \par \uc2 You are the worst coward, man.\par \par \uc2 You\u8217\'20\'19re opening an inquiry into President \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  for one reason only:\par \par \uc2 You are afraid of the extremists and terrified they will strip your power and you\u8217\'20\'19re trying to district Americans from\u8230\'20\'26 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/xGwRnbJOAB"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/xGwRnbJOAB}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Rep. \uc2 Jamaal Bowman Ed.D\uc2 . (@JamaalBowmanNY) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/JamaalBowmanNY/status/1701666479815459069?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 September 12, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 7.55pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.44pm BST\par \par \uc2 Ken Buck\uc2 , a Republican congressman for Colorado and House Freedom caucus member, has previously expressed skepticism about an impeachment inquiry into \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 On Sunday, Buck said any evidence linking the president to any high crime or misdemeanor \u8220\'20\'1Cdoesn\u8217\'20\'19t exist right now\u8221\'20\'1D. His recent comments against the House GOP\u8217\'20\'19s investigative efforts and track record of bucking his own party have put a target on his back, according to a CNN report.\par \par \uc2 A serious effort is now under way to find a candidate to mount a primary challenge against Buck in his eastern Colorado seat, the news channel reported, citing sources.\par \par \uc2 Marjorie Taylor Greene\uc2 , the far-right congresswoman from Georgia and ally of House speaker Kevin McCarthy, told the channel there is an \u8220\'20\'1Cunbelievable\u8221\'20\'1D level of frustration with Buck inside the House GOP. Greene added that she didn\u8217\'20\'19t think he should remain in his role on the House judiciary committee or the GOP whip\u8217\'20\'19s team.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThis is the same guy that wrote a book called \u8216\'20\'18Drain the Swamp\u8217\'20\'19, who is now arguing against an impeachment inquiry,\u8221\'20\'1D Greene said.\par \par \uc2 I really don\u8217\'20\'19t see how we can have a member on Judiciary that is flat out refusing to impeach \u8230\'20\'26 It seems like, can he even be trusted to do his job at this point?\par \par \uc2 Republican congressman for Colorado and House Freedom caucus member \uc2 Ken Buck\uc2 . Photograph: Anadolu Agency/Getty Images\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 7.46pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.30pm BST\par \par \uc2 Kevin McCarthy 'doing Trump's bidding' by calling for Biden impeachment inquiry, says Biden campaign\par \par \uc2 A spokesperson for the Biden-Harris 2024 campaign released a statement in response to House speaker Kevin McCarthy \u8217\'20\'19s announcement backing a formal impeachment inquiry into \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 McCarthy has \u8220\'20\'1Ccemented his role as the Trump campaign\u8217\'20\'19s super-surrogate by turning the House of Representatives into an arm of his presidential campaign\u8221\'20\'1D, the statement by Ammar Moussa reads.\par \par \uc2 11 days ago, McCarthy {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/sep/12/trump-indictments-mccarthy-government-shutdown-biden-politics-live-updates?page=with:block-65008f928f0873945374df99#block-65008f928f0873945374df99"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  unequivocally said}}}\uc2  he would not move forward with an impeachment inquiry without holding a vote on the House floor. What has changed since then?\par \par \uc2 The Biden-Harris campaign added:\par \par \uc2 Several members of the Speaker\u8217\'20\'19s own conference have come out and publicly panned impeachment as a political stunt, pointing out there is no evidence of wrongdoing by President Biden as Republicans litigate the same debunked conspiracy theories they\u8217\'20\'19ve investigated for over four years.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.19pm BST\par \par \uc2 A Virginia Democrat running in a closely contested legislative election has denounced reports that she and her husband engaged in sex acts livestreamed on an online platform in exchange for \u8220\'20\'1Ctips\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Susanna Gibson, a nurse practitioner and a first-time candidate seeking a seat in Virginia\u8217\'20\'19s house of delegates, shared the videos on a platform called Chaturbate.\par \par \uc2 The videos, which were first reported by the \uc2 Washington Post\uc2  and then confirmed by the Associated Press, show Gibson urging viewers to provide tips in the form of Chaturbate tokens in exchange for her performance of specific sex acts with her husband. The videos were archived in 2022, though it is unclear when the live streams occurred.\par \par \uc2 According to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.washingtonpost.com/dc-md-va/2023/09/11/susanna-gibson-sex-website-virginia-candidate/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the Post\u8217\'20\'19s report}}}\uc2 , a Republican operative first alerted the newspaper to the existence of the videos, which had been archived on another site. In a statement, Gibson denounced the report as a form of \u8220\'20\'1Cgutter politics\u8221\'20\'1D and \u8220\'20\'1Can illegal invasion of my privacy designed to humiliate me and my family\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt won\u8217\'20\'19t intimidate me and it won\u8217\'20\'19t silence me,\u8221\'20\'1D Gibson said.\par \par \uc2 My political opponents and their Republican allies have proven they\u8217\'20\'19re willing to commit a sex crime to attack me and my family because there\u8217\'20\'19s no line they won\u8217\'20\'19t cross to silence women when they speak up.\par \par \uc2 A lawyer representing Gibson, Daniel P Watkins, told the Post that the videos may have violated Virginia\u8217\'20\'19s revenge porn law, adding: \u8220\'20\'1CWe are working closely with state and federal law enforcement.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Gibson\u8217\'20\'19s district, located just north-west of Richmond, is considered one of just a handful of competitive seats in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/sep/09/virginia-election-abortion-rights"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the race to control}}}\uc2  Virginia\u8217\'20\'19s house of delegates. In the last legislative session, Republicans narrowly controlled the chamber, while Democrats maintained a slim majority in the state senate.\par \par \uc2 Susanna Gibson is a first-time candidate in the race. Photograph: Neil Smith/AP\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.07pm BST\par \par \uc2 Peter Navarro\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/sep/07/navarro-trial-guilty-contempt-congress-trump-adviser-january-6"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 contempt of Congress conviction}}}\uc2  has \u8220\'20\'1Ceverybody in that frigging White House\u8221\'20\'1D feeling as if they are grappling with \u8220\'20\'1Cmassive legal bills and \u8230\'20\'26 prison time\u8221\'20\'1D, the ex-\uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  administration official said on Monday.\par \par \uc2 Navarro\u8217\'20\'19s remarks came in an interview with the far-right media outlet \uc2 Newsmax\uc2  in which he used the term \u8220\'20\'1CSOBs\u8221\'20\'1D \u8211\'20\'13 short for sons of bitches \u8211\'20\'13 to refer to the US justice department prosecutors who secured a guilty verdict against him last week.\par \par \uc2 Lamenting that prosecutors had pushed to \u8220\'20\'1Cstick me in leg irons \u8230\'20\'26 [and] with half a million dollars of legal bills\u8221\'20\'1D, Navarro pledged to seek a reversal of his conviction from an appellate court. Navarro told the host Eric Bolling:\par \par \uc2 We\u8217\'20\'19re gonna win this fight \u8211\'20\'13 that\u8217\'20\'19s why God created the appeals court.\par \par \uc2 Navarro served as a senior trade adviser during {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/donaldtrump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Trump}}}\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s presidency, which ended in the Republican\u8217\'20\'19s defeat to \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  in the 2020 election. Congress subpoenaed him in February 2022 to answer questions about why Trump supporters attacked the US Capitol on 6 January 2021, temporarily delaying certification of Biden\u8217\'20\'19s electoral victory.\par \par \uc2 A House committee convened to investigate the attack suspected Navarro had more information about any connection between false claims of voter fraud in that election which Trump allies had pushed and the assault on the Capitol. But Navarro refused to testify while also declining to turn over any emails, reports or notes.\par \par \uc2 Navarro\u8217\'20\'19s attorney argued that the defendant asked the committee to talk to Trump to see what information he wanted protected under executive privilege, which never happened. Prosecutors countered that Navarro should have handed over the materials he had while labeling those he believed were privileged.\par \par \uc2 On Thursday, a jury convicted Navarro of two misdemeanor charges of contempt of Congress, each of which is punishable by between 30 days and a year in prison. His sentencing has tentatively been scheduled for 12 January.\par \par \uc2 Peter Navarro\uc2  speaks to the media outside a courthouse in Washington DC on 7 September. Photograph: Shawn Thew/\uc2 EPA\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 7.10pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.54pm BST\par \par \uc2 From the White House, Ian Sams, spokesperson for oversight and investigations, emails the statement he tweeted earlier.\par \par \uc2 Rather than recap it, as it is currently pinned above, I shall merely note that the Guardian style guide says \u8220\'20\'1Cflip-flopped\u8221\'20\'1D takes a hyphen. So it goes.\par \par \uc2 The White House also wants reporters to note quotes from six House Republicans who have said or indicated they are not convinced an impeachment inquiry is merited.\par \par \uc2 The group ranges from \uc2 Ken Buck\uc2  of Colorado, a strong conservative, to Mike Lawler of New York, the sort of blue-state relative moderate pollsters think might be endangered if voters do not take kindly to the move against Biden.\par \par \uc2 It\u8217\'20\'19s worth remembering of course that McCarthy only has {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.pewresearch.org/short-reads/2023/05/05/narrow-majorities-in-u-s-house-have-become-more-common-but-havent-always-led-to-gridlock/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a five-seat majority}}}\uc2  , pending any House vote to impeach the president.\par \par \uc2 The White House also sent a couple of recent quotes in which McCarthy said an inquiry should be the result of a vote, not \u8220\'20\'1Cthrough a declaration by one person\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 As {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.politico.com/newsletters/playbook/2023/08/30/the-house-gop-mulls-some-impeachment-hypocrisy-00113436?nname=playbook-pm&nid=0000015a-dd3e-d536-a37b-dd7fd8af0000&nrid=0000014e-f116-dd93-ad7f-f917ef350000&nlid=964328"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 described}}}\uc2  by Politico, the speaker has now performed \u8220\'20\'1Ca neat bit of hypocrisy after he excoriated then-Speaker \uc2 Nancy Pelosi\uc2  for pulling the same move against \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  in 2019\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 We should expect a lot more of this sort of thing to come, obviously.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.35pm BST\par \par \uc2 Republican reaction to House speaker Kevin McCarthy\u8217\'20\'19s endorsement of an impeachment inquiry continues to roll out \u8211\'20\'13 or click out? \u8211\'20\'13 of the corridors of Capitol Hill.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/ramsberry1/status/1701623672341999910"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 John Thune}}}\uc2  of South Dakota, the No 2 Republican in the Senate: \u8220\'20\'1CMy solution to changing things around here is to win elections. I think we ought to be focused on that, but [McCarthy] is under a lot of pressure over there from members of his caucus.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1COne thing I do know is I don\u8217\'20\'19t think it\u8217\'20\'19d be advantageous, obviously, if this thing went further [eg, to the Senate for trial], with all the other things that we have to do \u8230\'20\'26 I think you got to win elections. That\u8217\'20\'19s how, in my view, you change the direction of the country.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/sahilkapur/status/1701632333500051813"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Mitt Romney}}}\uc2  of Utah, 2012 Republican nominee for president and only senator to vote to convict \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  in both his impeachment trials: \u8220\'20\'1CThere\u8217\'20\'19s been no allegation of a high crime or misdemeanor that would meet the constitutional test. So that\u8217\'20\'19s a very different matter. We\u8217\'20\'19ll see if that arises.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 6.37pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.12pm BST\par \par \uc2 News that Kevin McCarthy had endorsed an impeachment inquiry into \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  landed while Wes Moore, the Democratic governor of Maryland, was speaking at an event in Washington DC, hosted by Semafor.\par \par \uc2 Wes Moore. Photograph: Barbara Haddock Taylor/AP\par \par \uc2 Moore, 44 and a combat veteran and Rhodes scholar who was elected last year as the first Black governor in the 246-year history of his state, is widely regarded as a potential candidate for the Democratic presidential nomination next time around, in 2028, or after.\par \par \uc2 That didn\u8217\'20\'19t stop the governor\u8217\'20\'19s host at the Gallup building on F Street, Semafor editor-at-large Steve Clemons, opening with: \u8220\'20\'1CDemocrats say, \u8216\'20\'18President Biden has set us up, given us a bad choice. Why don\u8217\'20\'19t you get Wes Moore to primary him?\u8217\'20\'19 Any interest in higher office?\par \par \uc2 To laughter, Moore said: \u8220\'20\'1CGood morning, everybody. And no, none.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Later, around the time McCarthy was speaking to the press at the Capitol, not too far to the east, Moore outlined why he supports Biden wholeheartedly for another term.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CYou are not going to find a more vocal support person like me,\u8221\'20\'1D he said. \u8220\'20\'1CAnd the reason I say this because I\u8217\'20\'19m on the ground. I see the work.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Detailing benefits to Maryland he said were owed to partnership with the Biden administration, Moore added: \u8220\'20\'1CSo frankly, I can get the arguments when people say, \u8216\'20\'18Well, we need to get excited because democracy is on the line.\u8217\'20\'19 And all that is very true. I mean, you don\u8217\'20\'19t need to look much further into what\u8217\'20\'19s going on right now. I understand that democracy actually is on the line. I get that.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CBut I\u8217\'20\'19m not excited to support President Biden because I\u8217\'20\'19m fearful about what the alternatives [might be]. I\u8217\'20\'19m excited to support President Biden because, look at the first nine months\u8221\'20\'1D of the Moore administration. \u8220\'20\'1CImagine if you give me four years.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1C\u8230\'20\'26 The president has been to our state, to multiple locations. That\u8217\'20\'19s the partner I want. And that\u8217\'20\'19s the partner that I need.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s some more on Moore, to the Guardian, before his election last year:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/oct/06/wes-moore-maryland-democrat-black-governor"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Wes Moore bids to become Maryland governor: \u8216\'20\'18I\u8217\'20\'19m running against an insurrectionist\u8217\'20\'19}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 6.17pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.52pm BST\par \par \uc2 Just over an hour before Speaker Kevin McCarthy announced he would direct his committees to open a formal impeachment inquiry into \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 , Senator \uc2 Lindsey Graham\uc2  reportedly told journalists:\par \par \uc2 The way to make inquiry legitimate is to have a vote as to whether or not you should have one at all, rather than just the leadership deciding.\par \par \uc2 From CBS News\u8217\'20\'19 Alan He:\par \par \uc2 enltrLindsey Graham to Senate reporters at 10am\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe way to make inquiry legitimate is to have a vote as to whether or not you should have one at all, rather than just the leadership deciding.\u8221\'20\'1D {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/sJFBohVavm"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/sJFBohVavm}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Alan He (@alanhe) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/alanhe/status/1701620373215756792?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 September 12, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.45pm BST\par \par \uc2 As we {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/sep/12/trump-indictments-mccarthy-government-shutdown-biden-politics-live-updates?page=with:block-65008f928f0873945374df99#block-65008f928f0873945374df99"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reported earlier,}}}\uc2  House speaker Kevin McCarthy said less than a fortnight ago that an impeachment inquiry against \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  would only move forward if there is a formal House vote.\par \par \uc2 In 2019, McCarthy posted a tweet warning his predecessor, \uc2 Nancy Pelosi\uc2 , that she could not call on an impeachment probe against \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  without a House vote. He wrote:\par \par \uc2 Speaker Pelosi can\u8217\'20\'19t decide on impeachment unilaterally. It requires a full vote of the House of Representatives.\par \par \uc2 enltrHere are the facts:\par \par \uc2 1. Speaker Pelosi can't decide on impeachment unilaterally. It requires a full vote of the House of Representatives.\par \par \uc2 2. The House has voted three times on articles of impeachment. Each vote failed.\par \par \uc2 3. For Dems, this is all about politics. Not about facts.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Kevin McCarthy (@SpeakerMcCarthy) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/SpeakerMcCarthy/status/1176637249435426816?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 September 24, 2019}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 5.46pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.33pm BST\par \par \uc2 White House spokesperson blasts McCarthy\u8217\'20\'19s move as 'extreme politics at its worst'\par \par \uc2 Ian Sams, the White House spokesperson for oversight and investigations, has also responded to Kevin McCarthy\u8217\'20\'19s announcement.\par \par \uc2 Posting to \uc2 Twitter\uc2 , Sams described the House speaker\u8217\'20\'19s move as \u8220\'20\'1Cextreme politics at its worst\u8221\'20\'1D, adding that House GOP members have uncovered \u8220\'20\'1Cno evidence of wrongdoing\u8221\'20\'1D in the months-long investigation into \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 enltrHouse Republicans have been investigating the President for 9 months, and they've turned up no evidence of wrongdoing\par \par \uc2 His own GOP members have said so\par \par \uc2 He vowed to hold a vote to open impeachment, now he flip flopped because he doesn't have support\par \par \uc2 Extreme politics at its worst\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Ian Sams (@IanSams46) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/IanSams46/status/1701619933283483848?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 September 12, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 5.34pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.27pm BST\par \par \uc2 John Fetterman\uc2 , the Democratic senator for Pennsylvania, was asked to respond to House speaker Kevin McCarthy \u8217\'20\'19s announcement.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s the clip from NBC\u8217\'20\'19s Liz Brown-Kaiser:\par \par \uc2 enltr. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/SenFettermanPA?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @SenFettermanPA}}}\uc2  reacts to Speaker McCarthy moving forward with a House impeachment inquiry into POTUS\u8230\'20\'26\par \par \uc2 (Just watch) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/jg3aeyDW7F"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/jg3aeyDW7F}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Liz Brown-Kaiser (@lizbrownkaiser) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/lizbrownkaiser/status/1701630833398821106?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 September 12, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 Fetterman had previously {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/sep/07/john-fetterman-impeach-biden-republicans"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  dared Republicans}}}\uc2  to impeach the president, saying that doing so could end up hurting the GOP.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 5.28pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.23pm BST\par \par \uc2 Just earlier this month, Speaker Kevin McCarthy said he wouldn\u8217\'20\'19t move forward with an impeachment inquiry into \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  without a floor vote.\par \par \uc2 In an {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.breitbart.com/politics/2023/09/01/mccarthy-details-impeachment-inquiry-process-if-we-move-forward-would-occur-vote-house-floor/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 interview }}}\uc2  with Breitbart published on 1 September, McCarthy made clear that the move would come not as an announcement from him or anyone else, but from a formal vote on the floor of the House. He said:\par \par \uc2 To open an impeachment inquiry is a serious matter, and House Republicans would not take it lightly or use it for political purposes. The American people deserve to be heard on this matter through their elected representatives.\par \par \uc2 That\u8217\'20\'19s why, if we move forward with an impeachment inquiry, it would occur through a vote on the floor of the People\u8217\'20\'19s House and not through a declaration by one person.\par \par \uc2 He now appears to have {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/sep/12/trump-indictments-mccarthy-government-shutdown-biden-politics-live-updates?page=with:block-65008df88f0873945374df6a#block-65008df88f0873945374df6a"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 changed his mind.}}}\par \par \uc2 Speaker of the House Kevin McCarthy at the Capitol on Tuesday. Photograph: Jacquelyn Martin/AP\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 5.25pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.13pm BST\par \par \uc2 A spokesperson for Speaker Kevin McCarthy said the House is not expected to vote on the impeachment inquiry into \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 , Reuters is reporting.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 5.18pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.05pm BST\par \par \uc2 Biden impeachment effort \u8216\'20\'18eight months of abject failure\u8217\'20\'19 \u8211\'20\'13 watchdog\par \par \uc2 James Comer\uc2 , the chair of the House of Representatives\u8217\'20\'19 oversight committee leading the Republican charge for an impeachment inquiry into \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 , spent \u8220\'20\'1Ceight months of abject failure\u8221\'20\'1D in trying to prove the US president guilty of wrongdoing, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/sep/11/biden-impeachment-inquiry-abject-failure-report"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 according to a watchdog report }}}\uc2  released on Monday.\par \par \uc2 In June, Comer and Senator \uc2 Chuck Grassley\uc2 , investigating \uc2 Hunter Biden\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s work for the Ukrainian energy company \uc2 Burisma\uc2 , began {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.grassley.senate.gov/news/remarks/grassley-fbi-redacted-references-to-recordings-in-biden-allegation-shared-with-congress"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 touting potential audio tapes}}}\uc2  supposedly proving that Biden accepted a $5m bribe from the energy firm during the Barack Obama administration. But Comer later admitted: \u8220\'20\'1CWe don\u8217\'20\'19t know if they are legit or not\u8221\'20\'1D during a \uc2 Newsmax\uc2  interview just five days later.\par \par \uc2 In July, after weeks of hype from Comer about \u8220\'20\'1Cbombshell testimony\u8221\'20\'1D, a business associate of \uc2 Hunter Biden\uc2  named Devon Archer appeared before the House oversight committee. But Archer {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://oversight.house.gov/release/comer-releases-devon-archers-transcribed-interview-transcript%EF%BF%BC/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 failed to offer any evidence}}}\uc2  of a conflict of interest between the president and his son\u8217\'20\'19s business ventures.\par \par \uc2 Comer made much of a portion of testimony by Archer suggesting that {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/aug/06/hunter-joe-biden-republican-legal-problem"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Biden joined Hunter on speakerphone}}}\uc2  while talking with business associates up to 20 times. The report says:\par \par \uc2 The reality, however, was that Archer\u8217\'20\'19s testimony referred to approximately 20 instances over the span of a decade in which Hunter indicated \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  was merely present; Archer did not testify that President Biden was directly involved in business discussions beyond \u8216\'20\'18the brand\u8217\'20\'19 \u8211\'20\'13 only that he held casual conversations about \u8216\'20\'18the weather\u8217\'20\'19 and \u8216\'20\'18fishing\u8217\'20\'19.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Comer himself was not even present for the testimony. One anonymous Republican source was quoted as saying:\par \par \uc2 It was like following a general into battle, but the general decided to stay home instead of fight.\par \par \uc2 In early August, \uc2 Comer\uc2  released a memo that attacked Biden for supposedly receiving bribes from foreign countries. It was widely derided by factcheckers. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.politico.com/minutes/congress/08-9-2023/comer-biden-push-continues/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 The Politico website reported}}}\uc2  :\par \par \uc2 But the memo, the third Comer has released so far this year, also doesn\u8217\'20\'19t show a direct payment to \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 5.08pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.53pm BST\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , who faces 91 criminal charges in four jurisdictions, has urged Republicans in Congress to impeach \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  or \u8220\'20\'1Cfade into oblivion\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 The former president, who was impeached twice himself, told Real America\u8217\'20\'19s Voice:\par \par \uc2 I don\u8217\'20\'19t know actually how a Republican could not do it. I think a Republican would be primaried and lose immediately, no matter what district you\u8217\'20\'19re in.\par \par \uc2 In a post on his Truth Social platform last month, Trump wrote:\par \par \uc2 Biden is a Stone Cold Crook \u8212\'20\'14 You don\u8217\'20\'19t need a long INQUIRY to prove it, it\u8217\'20\'19s already proven. These lowlifes Impeached me TWICE (I WON!), and Indicted me FOUR TIMES \u8211\'20\'13 For NOTHING! Either IMPEACH the BUM, or fade into OBLIVION. THEY DID IT TO US!\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.45pm BST\par \par \uc2 McCarthy vows to 'go wherever the evidence takes us' as he formally endorses Biden impeachment inquiry\par \par \uc2 McCarthy said his decision to direct a House committee to formally open a formal impeachment inquiry into \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  was not taken lightly.\par \par \uc2 The House speaker said he believed that the president \u8220\'20\'1Cwould want to answer these questions and allegations\u8221\'20\'1D and that this \u8220\'20\'1Cshould concern all Americans\u8221\'20\'1D regardless of who they voted for.\par \par \uc2 The American people deserve to know that the public offices are not for sale and that the federal government is not being used to cover up the actions of a politically associated family.\par \par \uc2 I would encourage the president and his team to fully cooperate with this investigation in the interests of transparency. We are committed to getting the answers for the American public \u8211\'20\'13 nothing more, nothing less. We will go wherever the evidence takes us.\par \par \uc2 enltr"These allegations paint a picture of a culture of corruption."\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Speaker Kevin McCarthy (R-CA) endorses a House GOP-led impeachment inquiry into President Biden. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/4VzUpq2UWQ"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/4VzUpq2UWQ}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 The Recount (@therecount) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/therecount/status/1701619565749248069?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 September 12, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 4.46pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.38pm BST\par \par \uc2 House investigation found a 'culture of corruption' around Biden family, says McCarthy\par \par \uc2 House speaker Kevin McCarthy said Republican-led investigations into \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  \u8220\'20\'1Cpaint a picture of a culture of corruption\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 He said:\par \par \uc2 Through our investigations we have found that President Biden did lie to American people about his own knowledge of his family\u8217\'20\'19s foreign business dealers. Eye witnesses have testified that the president joined on multiple phones and had multiple interactions, dinners that resulted in millions of dollars into his son and his son\u8217\'20\'19s business partners.\par \par \uc2 McCarthy claimed bank records showed nearly $20m in payments were directed to the Biden family members and associates \u8220\'20\'1Cthrough various shell companies\u8221\'20\'1D. He went on:\par \par \uc2 Despite the serious allegation, it appears that the president\u8217\'20\'19s family has been offered special treatment by Biden\u8217\'20\'19s own administration treatment that otherwise would not have received.\par \par \uc2 These are allegations of abuse of power, obstruction and corruption and they warrant further investigation by the House of Representatives.\par \par \uc2 He announced that he is directing the House committee to open a formal impeachment inquiry into the president, describing it as a \u8220\'20\'1Clogical next step\u8221\'20\'1D that will give the committees \u8220\'20\'1Cthe full power to gather all the facts and answers for the American public\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 4.41pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.28pm BST\par \par \uc2 Kevin McCarthy calls for Biden impeachment inquiry\par \par \uc2 House speaker Kevin McCarthy has called for an impeachment inquiry into Presiden t \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Speaking to reporters, he said:\par \par \uc2 I am directing our House committee to open a formal impeachment inquiry into President \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 More to follow.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 4.29pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.23pm BST\par \par \uc2 Impeachment would require a majority vote in the House \u8211\'20\'13 where Republicans have a slim advantage \u8211\'20\'13 to formally charge \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 , then a two-thirds vote in the Senate, which is controlled by Democrats, to convict him. It is therefore extremely unlikely to succeed.\par \par \uc2 Far-right Republicans in the House have agitated for impeaching the president but those who could face tough re-election battles next fall have been more skeptical.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CSo the question to me right now is: do the investigations \u8230\'20\'26 are they producing enough facts and evidence that warrant taking it to the next step?\u8221\'20\'1D Mike Lawler, a New York Republican in a highly competitive district, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nbcnews.com/politics/congress/vulnerable-republicans-arent-sold-impeaching-biden-rcna98638"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 told NBC News in August}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 I don\u8217\'20\'19t think it\u8217\'20\'19s there at the moment, but these committees are doing their job.\par \par \uc2 In the Senate, some more moderate Republicans have also expressed skepticism about impeachment. \uc2 Mitt Romney\uc2  of Utah {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.huffpost.com/entry/joe-biden-impeachment-john-fetterman_n_64f8df8de4b0d44852edd611"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 told HuffPost}}}\uc2  last week:\par \par \uc2 I haven\u8217\'20\'19t seen any evidence at this stage to suggest he\u8217\'20\'19s met the constitutional test for impeachment.\par \par \uc2 Even on the right of the Republican Senate caucus, enthusiasm for impeachment is scarce. Alabama senator Tommy Tuberville, a leading Trump ally, told reporters last week he was \u8220\'20\'1Cnot for going through another damn trial to be honest with you. [We] did that here with Trump.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.17pm BST\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/sep/12/trump-indictments-mccarthy-government-shutdown-biden-politics-live-updates?page=with:block-65007f7c8f08cf50e161336b#block-65007f7c8f08cf50e161336b"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 The report}}}\uc2  by the Congressional Integrity Project offers an anatomy of a fake scandal, detailing a series of exaggerated assertions that have shriveled under scrutiny.\par \par \uc2 They include \uc2 James Comer\uc2 , the chairman of the House of Representatives\u8217\'20\'19 oversight committee, saying at his first press conference that he had evidence of \u8220\'20\'1Cfederal crimes committed\u8221\'20\'1D, relentlessly invoking \u8220\'20\'1Cdeep state\u8221\'20\'1D conspiracy theories and claiming that his whistleblowers \u8220\'20\'1Cfear for their lives\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 The report states:\par \par \uc2 After months of political stunts, dozens of hearings, transcribed interviews, and memos, and despite hours on Fox peddling conspiracy theories, Comer and his Maga crew have failed to find a single shred of evidence linking President Biden to any of their lurid accusations.\par \par \uc2 In fact, Republicans have been forced to walk back claim after claim.\par \par \uc2 For months, the report says, \uc2 Comer\uc2  talked to the media about four individuals he claimed were \u8220\'20\'1Cwhistleblowers\u8221\'20\'1D, a term increasingly hijacked by the right. It adds:\par \par \uc2 Problem is \u8211\'20\'13 they weren\u8217\'20\'19t whistleblowers and there were only two people.\par \par \uc2 Comer was eventually factchecked by his own colleague on the House oversight committee. Democrat Jamie Raskin {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://oversightdemocrats.house.gov/sites/democrats.oversight.house.gov/files/2023-04-06.JBR%20to%20Comer%20re%20Laptop%20Witnesses%20FINAL.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 wrote to him}}}\uc2  :\par \par \uc2 The two individuals your staff specifically identified as the individuals they understood to have been referenced during your March 6 Fox News interview, are not whistleblowers \u8230\'20\'26 Your repeated statements about \u8216\'20\'18four people\u8217\'20\'19 suggest that either you have intentionally misrepresented the Committee\u8217\'20\'19s investigative progress to your conservative audience or that key investigative steps have been deliberately withheld from Committee Democrats.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.13pm BST\par \par \uc2 Kevin McCarthy and the GOP House leadership scheduled a closed-door session for Thursday morning so that members could get an update on the investigations by House judiciary committee chair Jim Jordan and House oversight committee chair \uc2 Jamie Comer\uc2 , according to the Punchbowl News {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://punchbowl.news/newsletter/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 report.}}}\par \par \uc2 On Monday, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/sep/11/biden-impeachment-inquiry-abject-failure-report"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  a report }}}\uc2  by the Congressional Integrity Project said Comer has spent \u8220\'20\'1Ceight months of abject failure\u8221\'20\'1D in trying to prove \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  guilty of wrongdoing. Comer has repeatedly overhyped allegations of bribery and corruption against Biden without once producing hard evidence, the report said.\par \par \uc2 Comer has been {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/may/15/joe-biden-compromised-house-committee-whistleblower"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 leading an aggressive investigation}}}\uc2  into unsubstantiated claims that Biden was involved in his son \uc2 Hunter Biden\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s foreign business affairs during his time as vice-president.\par \par \uc2 A CNN/SSRS poll this week found that 61% of Americans believe that Biden did play such a role, including 42% who think he acted illegally. But establishing the link between father and son has proved an elusive holy grail.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 4.14pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.09pm BST\par \par \uc2 We\u8217\'20\'19re currently waiting for House speaker Kevin McCarthy to deliver {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/sep/12/trump-indictments-mccarthy-government-shutdown-biden-politics-live-updates?page=with:block-65007afb8f0893e8a8a01756#block-65007afb8f0893e8a8a01756"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 an expected statement }}}\uc2  endorsing an impeachment inquiry into \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 McCarthy \u8220\'20\'1Chas been moving in the direction of an impeachment inquiry, calling it a \u8216\'20\'18natural step forward\u8217\'20\'19 for the House GOP to gather more facts", according to NBC News.\par \par \uc2 Yet this morning, Punchbowl News reported that McCarthy is set to tell House Republicans later this week that an impeachment inquiry is the \u8220\'20\'1Clogical next step\u8221\'20\'1D in the GOP\u8217\'20\'19s investigations into the president and his son, \uc2 Hunter Biden\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.55pm BST\par \par \uc2 Kevin McCarthy to give statement ahead of expected endorsement of Biden impeachment inquiry\par \par \uc2 House speaker Kevin McCarthy plans to tell Republicans that the House has enough evidence to justify impeachment proceedings against \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 , according to multiple reports.\par \par \uc2 McCarthy plans to tell his conference the impeachment inquiry is the \u8220\'20\'1Cthe logical next step\u8221\'20\'1D in order to obtain bank records and other documents from the president and his son, \uc2 Hunter Biden\uc2 , Punchbowl News {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://punchbowl.news/newsletter/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reported.}}}\par \par \uc2 In recent weeks, McCarthy has privately told Republicans he plans to pursue an impeachment inquiry into Biden and hopes to start the process by the end of September, sources {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cnn.com/2023/09/12/politics/biden-impeachment-house-gop/index.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 told}}}\uc2  CNN.\par \par \uc2 As \uc2 Donald Trump{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/jul/28/donald-trump-investigations-criminal-charges-tracker"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 faces four separate criminal cases}}}\uc2 , House Republicans have floated the impeachment of Biden as they investigate his son Hunter\u8217\'20\'19s business dealings. Republicans have been unable to substantiate wrongdoing by either Biden.\par \par \uc2 McCarthy suggested last month the House would pursue impeachment if it did not obtain access to certain documents, even though Republicans had never asked for some of the documents at issue, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://thehill.com/homenews/house/4165602-mccarthy-house-could-launch-impeachment-inquiry-when-we-come-back-into-session/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 according to the Hill}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 McCarthy is expected to give a press conference at 11am ET. We will be following it live here.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 4.19pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.42pm BST\par \par \uc2 Kevin McCarthy faces a 'perfect storm' as a shutdown looms\par \par \uc2 The House returns from its summer recess today as the speaker, Kevin McCarthy faces a collision course of difficult challenges \u8211\'20\'13 avoiding a costly government shutdown, and addressing growing calls on the right to launch an impeachment inquiry into \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 With just 12 legislative days left before the end of the fiscal year, the Republican-controlled House must quickly pass some kind of spending package to keep the federal government open after 30 September.\par \par \uc2 If it does not, the government will shut down for the first time in nearly five years, furloughing federal employees and stalling many crucial programs.\par \par \uc2 McCarthy has indicated his preference to pass a continuing resolution, but members of the hard-right House freedom caucus insist they will not back a continuing resolution unless the speaker agrees to several significant policy concessions, such as increased border security and an impeachment inquiry into Biden over the business dealings of the president\u8217\'20\'19s son, \uc2 Hunter Biden\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Given House Republicans\u8217\'20\'19 narrow majority and a new rule allowing any single member of the chamber to force a vote on removing the speaker, McCarthy\u8217\'20\'19s handling of this fraught situation could determine whether he loses his gavel after just eight months in power.\par \par \uc2 Ken Buck\uc2 , a Colorado Republican congressman, said in Sunday interview with MSNBC\u8217\'20\'19s \uc2 Jen Psaki\uc2 :\par \par \uc2 There\u8217\'20\'19s a perfect storm brewing in the House in the near future, in September.\par \par \uc2 He added:\par \par \uc2 On the one hand, we\u8217\'20\'19ve got to pass a [short-term funding bill]. And we also have the impeachment issue. And we also have members of the House, led by my good friend, Chip Roy, who are concerned about policy issues. So you take those three things put together, and Kevin McCarthy, the speaker, has made promises on each of those issues to different groups. And now it is all coming due at the same time.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.32pm BST\par \par \uc2 Former Democratic presidential candidate \uc2 Andrew Yang\uc2  remains listed as the co-chair for the Forward Party, which he launched after leaving the Democratic party to become an independent in 2021.\par \par \uc2 Yang slammed the idea of the 2024 presidential election shaping up to be a \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  vs \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  rematch in the Politico {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/sep/12/trump-indictments-mccarthy-government-shutdown-biden-politics-live-updates?page=with:block-650074168f0893e8a8a016e8#block-650074168f0893e8a8a016e8"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  interview}}}\uc2 , describing the situation as \u8220\'20\'1Cterribly unrepresentative and borderline ridiculous\u8221\'20\'1D and pointing to their ages.\par \par \uc2 I mean, you\u8217\'20\'19re talking about two guys whose combined age is 160. In a country of 330 million people, you would choose these two gentlemen at this stage? I mean, it makes zero sense.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.32pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.27pm BST\par \par \uc2 Andrew Yang\uc2  has \u8216\'20\'18had conversations\u8217\'20\'19 with third-party No Labels group\par \par \uc2 Andrew Yang\uc2 , the former Democratic presidential candidate, confirmed he has had \u8220\'20\'1Cconversations\u8221\'20\'1D with the centrist group No Labels about its third-party presidential bid.\par \par \uc2 Yang, in a Politico {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.politico.com/news/2023/09/11/andrew-yang-conversations-no-labels-00115126?nname=playbook&nid=0000014f-1646-d88f-a1cf-5f46b7bd0000&nrid=d66b2db2-0400-407f-afcc-3b1d45707d8e&nlid=630318"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  interview}}}\uc2  published yesterday evening, said:\par \par \uc2 I\u8217\'20\'19ve had conversations with various folks who are associated with No Labels.\par \par \uc2 He avoided directly answering if the group had specifically approached him about running as a possible presidential candidate, but said he and the group \u8220\'20\'1Chave a lot of friends and people in common\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Yang, who ran for the Democratic presidential nomination in 2020, said he is an \u8220\'20\'1Canyone-but-Trump guy\u8221\'20\'1D, adding:\par \par \uc2 I would not run for president, if I thought that my running would be counterproductive, or if it would increase the chances of someone like \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  becoming president again.\par \par \uc2 Andrew Yang\uc2 , who ran for the Democratic presidential nomination in 2020. Photograph: Marco Bello/Getty Images\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 4.03pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.13pm BST\par \par \uc2 Should the US district judge \uc2 Tanya Chutkan\uc2  decline to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/sep/12/trump-indictments-mccarthy-government-shutdown-biden-politics-live-updates?page=with:block-65006f1c8f0893e8a8a016ae#block-65006f1c8f0893e8a8a016ae"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 remove herself from the case}}}\uc2 , legal experts said \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  could seek to have the decision reviewed and petition the US court of appeals for the DC circuit for a writ of mandamus, a judicial order to a lower-court judge compelling an action such as recusal.\par \par \uc2 The appeal could be accompanied with a motion to stay Chutkan\u8217\'20\'19s rulings pending appeal, which could delay the pre-trial process and push back the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/aug/28/trump-trial-date-2020-election-tanya-chutkan"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 current trial date}}}\uc2  set for March 2024 while that litigation continues.\par \par \uc2 That kind of postponement would be beneficial to Trump, who has made clear that his overarching legal strategy for each of his criminal cases is to seek delay \u8211\'20\'13 preferably until after the 2024 presidential election as part of an effort to insulate himself from the charges.\par \par \uc2 The consequences of an extended delay could be far-reaching. If the case is not adjudicated until after the 2024 election and Trump is re-elected, he could try to pardon himself or direct the attorney general to have the justice department drop the case in its entirety.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.20pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.07pm BST\par \par \uc2 It was uncertain whether US district judge \uc2 Tanya Chutkan\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19 s two public statements would satisfy the high bar for removal from the 2020 election interference prosecution case.\par \par \uc2 Notably, the motion by \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s legal team did not complain about any of Chutkan\u8217\'20\'19s pre-trial rulings to date, perhaps because in a handful of instances, she has ruled against prosecutors.\par \par \uc2 The judge, an Obama appointee, came into the case with a reputation of being particularly tough in January 6-related prosecutions after she handed down sentences in some cases that were longer than had been requested by the justice department.\par \par \uc2 Still, Chutkan is far from the only federal judge in DC \u8211\'20\'13 or elsewhere in the country, for that matter \u8211\'20\'13 who has suggested Trump might have culpability for the Capitol attack during sentencing hearings.\par \par \uc2 Filing a recusal motion is not necessarily uncommon and federal judges tend not to take offense, former prosecutors and defense attorneys have said, even if Trump files them almost as a matter of routine. Recently, Trump sought to recuse the state court judge in his Manhattan criminal case, which was denied.\par \par \uc2 US District Judge \uc2 Tanya Chutkan\uc2 , who has been assigned to oversee the federal case against \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  for attempting to overturn the results of the 2020 election. Photograph: US Courts/Reuters\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.09pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.04pm BST\par \par \uc2 Trump asks judge to recuse herself in federal 2020 election subversion case\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s legal team on Monday asked the federal judge overseeing the 2020 election interference prosecution against him to remove herself from the case.\par \par \uc2 Lawyers for the former president argued that previous public comments by the US district judge \uc2 Tanya Chutkan\uc2  about the former president\u8217\'20\'19s culpability in the January 6 Capitol attack were disqualifying.\par \par \uc2 The recusal motion, filed to and against Chutkan, faces major legal hurdles: to succeed, Trump must show a \u8220\'20\'1Creasonable person\u8221\'20\'1D would conclude from just her remarks \u8211\'20\'13 but not any of her actual rulings \u8211\'20\'13 that she was unable to preside impartially.\par \par \uc2 Trump has long complained that the judge assigned to the case was biased against him because of her previous comments about Trump in other January 6 riot defendant cases and his legal team weighed filing the motion for weeks, two people familiar with deliberations {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/sep/11/trump-2020-election-subversion-case-judge-tanya-chutkan"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 told the Guardian.}}}\par \par \uc2 The {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://storage.courtlistener.com/recap/gov.uscourts.dcd.258149/gov.uscourts.dcd.258149.50.0_4.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 nine-page motion}}}\uc2  identified two episodes where Chutkan remarked on her opinion about Trump\u8217\'20\'19s responsibility in instigating the Capitol attack, which Trump\u8217\'20\'19s lawyers argued gave rise to the appearance of potential bias or prejudice against the former president.\par \par \uc2 The first instance came in October 2022 when she said, referring to January 6:\par \par \uc2 And the people who mobbed that Capitol were there in fealty, in loyalty, to one man \u8230\'20\'26 It\u8217\'20\'19s a blind loyalty to one person who, by the way, remains free to this day.\par \par \uc2 Trump\u8217\'20\'19s lawyers argued that those remarks, which came during sentencing of a rioter who stormed the Capitol, suggested Chutkan believed Trump should have been prosecuted and jailed in a pre-judgement of guilt that alone was disqualifying.\par \par \uc2 The second instance was when the judge told another January 6 rioter in December 2021:\par \par \uc2 The people who exhorted you and encouraged you and rallied you to go and take action and to fight have not been charged.\par \par \uc2 She added, \u8220\'20\'1CI have my opinions,\u8221\'20\'1D but that was out of her control.\par \par \uc2 Trump\u8217\'20\'19s lawyers argued that those remarks suggested Chutkan agreed with that rioter\u8217\'20\'19s defense attorney, who had said Trump had falsely convinced his supporters that the 2020 election was fraudulent and that they needed to take steps to stop the peaceful transition of power.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.06pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.47pm BST\par \par \uc2 US intelligence officials have accused \uc2 Vladimir Putin\uc2  of personally authorizing influence operations against Democratic candidates in support of \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  in both the 2016 and 2020 US presidential elections.\par \par \uc2 Yevgeny Prigozhin\uc2 , a former Putin ally who also managed online influence operations, admitted in November that he had interfered in the US elections. He said in the run-up to the US midterms:\par \par \uc2 Gentlemen, we interfered, we are interfering and we will interfere.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2023/aug/27/wagner-boss-yevgeny-prigozhin-killed-in-plane-crash-russia-investigative-committee-confirms"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Prigozhin was killed last month}}}\uc2  when his private jet crashed en route from Moscow to St Petersburg.\par \par \uc2 Putin made the remarks during an economic forum in the far eastern city of Vladivostok, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2023/sep/12/kim-jong-un-arrives-russia-vladivostok-vladimir-putin-meeting"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 where he is also due to hold meetings}}}\uc2  with Kim Jong-un, the North Korean leader, this week.\par \par \uc2 President Putin said in Vladivostok that even if \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  won next year\u8217\'20\'19s election the relationship between the two countries would not change. Photograph: Getty Images\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.32pm BST\par \par \uc2 Russian president \uc2 Vladimir Putin\uc2 , speaking earlier today, said significant changes in the US-Russia relationship were unlikely regardless of who wins next year\u8217\'20\'19s presidential election.\par \par \uc2 What to expect from the future, no matter who the president is, it\u8217\'20\'19s hard for us to say, but it\u8217\'20\'19s unlikely that anything will change radically.\par \par \uc2 He claimed the Biden administration was \u8220\'20\'1Chammering into people\u8217\'20\'19s heads\u8221\'20\'1D that Russia was an existential adversary and \u8221\'20\'1Dit will be very difficult for them to somehow turn this whole ship\u8221\'20\'1D in the other direction.\par \par \uc2 Speaking at an economic forum in Russia\u8217\'20\'19s far-eastern city of Vladivostok, Putin also discussed Moscow\u8217\'20\'19s \u8220\'20\'1Camazing\u8221\'20\'1D relations with Beijing and whether he would run for re-election in 2024. Please do follow {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/live/2023/sep/12/russia-ukraine-war-live-updates-kim-jong-un-putin-talks-weapons-ukraine-oil-rigs#top-of-blog"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 our Russia-Ukraine war live blog for more. }}}\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/live/2023/sep/12/russia-ukraine-war-live-updates-kim-jong-un-putin-talks-weapons-ukraine-oil-rigs"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Russia-Ukraine war live: Putin claims counteroffensive \u8216\'20\'18has not made progress\u8217\'20\'19; Sweden considers sending jets to Ukraine}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.19pm BST\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , in an interview with Fox Business last month, boasted about his relationship with \uc2 Vladimir Putin\uc2  and claimed the Russian leader would have never gone into Ukraine if he was US president because he was \u8220\'20\'1Cthe apple of his eye\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Trump said:\par \par \uc2 Putin would have never gone into Ukraine, but that was just on my relationship with him. My personality over his. [He] would have never gone in. I used to speak to him. I was the apple of his eye, but I said \u8216\'20\'18Don\u8217\'20\'19t ever do it.\u8217\'20\'19 It was tough stuff there, but he would have never done it.\par \par \uc2 enltrTrump says Putin "would have never gone into Ukraine" if he was still president, citing "my relationship with him" and because "I was the apple of his eye." {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/W8rPR8iPVp"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/W8rPR8iPVp}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Justin Baragona (@justinbaragona) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/justinbaragona/status/1692633948856394121?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 August 18, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 In a previous interview with Fox News, Trump claimed he had a plan to stop the war in Ukraine within 24 hours of taking back the White House.\par \par \uc2 Trump said he had a good relationship with both Ukraine\u8217\'20\'19s president, \uc2 Volodymyr Zelenskiy\uc2 , and Putin. He said:\par \par \uc2 I would tell Zelenskiy, no more. You got to make a deal. I would tell Putin, if you don\u8217\'20\'19t make a deal, we\u8217\'20\'19re going to give him a lot. We\u8217\'20\'19re going to [give Ukraine] more than they ever got if we have to. I will have the deal done in one day. One day.\par \par \uc2 Speaking earlier today in Vladivostok, the Russian leader said:\par \par \uc2 We hear that Mr Trump says that he will solve pressing problems in a few days, including the Ukrainian crisis. Well, this cannot but bring happiness. This is good.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.04pm BST\par \par \uc2 Putin: Trump's prosecution 'good for Russia'\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s a clip of Russia\u8217\'20\'19s president \uc2 Vladimir Putin\uc2  discussing the criminal cases against \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  while at a forum in Russia\u8217\'20\'19s far eastern city of Vladivostok.\par \par \uc2 Putin said the prosecution of the former US president was good from Russia\u8217\'20\'19s point of view. He said:\par \par \uc2 As for the prosecution of Trump, for us what is happening in today\u8217\'20\'19s conditions, in my opinion, is good because it shows the rottenness of the American political system, which cannot pretend to teach others democracy.\par \par \uc2 He continued:\par \par \uc2 In this sense, if they are trying to fight us in some way, it\u8217\'20\'19s good, because it shows who is fighting us. It shows, as they said back in Soviet times, \u8216\'20\'18the bestial face of American imperialism, the bestial grin\u8217\'20\'19.\par \par \uc2 enltrPutin speaks out about the cases against \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 :\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThis shows the whole rottenness of the American political system, which cannot claim to teach others about democracy. What\u8217\'20\'19s happening with Trump is a persecution of a political rival with political motives.\u8221\'20\'1D {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/oouu6rQwyQ"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/oouu6rQwyQ}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Matthew Luxmoore (@mjluxmoore) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/mjluxmoore/status/1701511140260430284?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 September 12, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.51pm BST\par \par \uc2 Putin claims Trump's criminal cases show 'rottenness' of US politics\par \par \uc2 Good morning, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/us-politics"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 US politics}}}\uc2  blog readers. Russian president \uc2 Vladimir Putin\uc2  waded into the debate over the criminal charges facing \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , saying that the cases against the former US president amount to political \u8220\'20\'1Cpersecution\u8221\'20\'1D that exposes the fundamental \u8220\'20\'1Crottenness\u8221\'20\'1D of the American political system.\par \par \uc2 Putin, speaking at an Eastern Economic Forum gathering in Russia\u8217\'20\'19s Pacific coast city of Vladivostok on Tuesday, said the prosecution of Trump was good for Russia \u8220\'20\'1Cbecause it shows the rottenness of the American political system, which cannot pretend to teach others democracy\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 The Russian leader added:\par \par \uc2 Everything that is happening with Trump is the persecution of a political rival for political reasons. That\u8217\'20\'19s what it is. And this is being done in front of the public of the United States and the whole world.\par \par \uc2 Trump currently faces a total of 91 charges across four criminal cases in Georgia, Florida, New York and Washington DC. Opinion polls indicate that he holds a commanding lead over his rivals to become the Republican party\u8217\'20\'19s candidate in the 2024 presidential election.\par \par \uc2 Both during and after his four-year term in the White House, Trump repeatedly touted having a friendly relationship with Putin. Trump has also claimed he could end {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/live/2023/sep/12/russia-ukraine-war-live-updates-kim-jong-un-putin-talks-weapons-ukraine-oil-rigs"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  the war in Ukraine}}}\uc2  in a matter of days if re-elected president.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s what else we\u8217\'20\'19re watching today:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 10am Eastern time. The Senate will meet and hold a confirmation for Tanya Bradsher\u8217\'20\'19s nomination as deputy veterans affairs secretary.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 12pm. The House will meet to take up various bills, including resolutions calling for the release of Paul Whelan and \uc2 Evan Gershkovich\uc2  in Russia.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 3pm. The House rules committee meets to prepare the annual defense spending bill for the floor.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 3pm. The House freedom caucus will hold a news conference on government funding.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.07pm BST\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020230912ej9c001h7\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
