\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Trump files for judge in federal election interference trial to be taken off case \u8211\'20\'13 as it happened\b0\par\par\uc2 Gabrielle Canon (now) and L\u233\'00\'E9onie Chao-Fong (earlier) \par \uc2 10,090 \uc2 words\par \uc2 11 September 2023\par 22:49 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Former US president files motion to recuse \uc2 Tanya Chutkan\uc2  over previous comments about his culpability\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.44pm BST\par \par \uc2 Today so far\par \par \uc2 Thank you for reading along with us during this busy news day. You can read more about Trump\u8217\'20\'19s recusal filing from \uc2 The Guardian\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s Hugo Lowell {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/sep/11/trump-2020-election-subversion-case-judge-tanya-chutkan"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 here}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s a rundown of what else we have covered:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 FDA\uc2  authorized updated Covid-19 vaccines that closely match the Omicron variants that are circulating, starting the process to deploy the shots this month.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Several people {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/sep/11/government-shutdown-trump-biden-911-anniversary-politics-live-updates?page=with:block-64ff33948f087658b6f99ea8#block-64ff33948f087658b6f99ea8"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 were arrested}}}\uc2  after entering the office of Kevin McCarthy, the speaker of the House, during a protest for HIV/Aids funding on Monday.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The Biden administration is close to approving the shipment of longer-range missiles packed with cluster bombs to Ukraine.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Five American prisoners being detained in Iran could soon be freed, thanks to a new deal the countries reached today. In exchange for the 5 US citizens, 5 Iranians held in the US will be released and the US will allow the transfer of $6bn in frozen Iranian funds from South Korea to Qatar without sanctions.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2023/sep/11/us-iran-sanctions-waiver-americans-detained-iran"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 US agrees to release $6bn in Iran funds as part of deal to free detained Americans}}}\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 President Biden marked the anniversary of 9/11 by speaking to service members, first responders, and their families in Anchorage, Alaska. Biden used the speech to highlight the battles the country is still fighting \u8211\'20\'13 deep-seated divisions that continue to threaten its future.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 In a court filing on Monday, former president {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/donaldtrump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Donald Trump}}}\uc2  moved to recuse federal judge \uc2 Tanya Chutkan\uc2 , who is overseeing the 2020 election subversion case, citing her previous comments about his culpability.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/aug/03/tanya-chutkan-trump-jan-6-case-judge"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Who is Tanya Chutkan, the judge assigned to Trump\u8217\'20\'19s January 6 case?}}}\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The filing is believed to be in response to the Trump team\u8217\'20\'19s disapproval of the date set for the trial on March 4th \u8211\'20\'13 the day before Super Tuesday. But analysts and experts are already highlighting the high unlikelihood that it will work.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.38pm BST\par \par \uc2 Chutkan is a highly respected federal judge, appointed by \uc2 Obama\uc2  and confirmed in 95-0 vote by the Senate in 2014. She also has been harsher than her colleagues in handing down sentences for rioters who attacked the Capitol on Jan 6.\par \par \uc2 As of July this year, all 38 defendants who came before her were given prison sentences, NPR reports, including 4 who weren\u8217\'20\'19t recommended for prison by prosecutors.\par \par \uc2 NPR {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.npr.org/2023/08/25/1195613760/trump-trial-judge-tanya-chulkan"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reports}}}\uc2  :\par \par \uc2 Chutkan has handed down tougher prison sentences than the government asked for in nearly 25% of her Jan. 6 cases. That is a notably higher rate than nearly all other judges handling these cases.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CShe was definitely on the high end of the range of those people,\u8221\'20\'1D said Bob Driscoll, a defense attorney at the McGlinchey Stafford firm in Washington. \u8220\'20\'1CShe was, in fact, still might be the only \u8212\'20\'14 if she\u8217\'20\'19s not the only she\u8217\'20\'19s one of the only \u8212\'20\'14 judges that has several times gone above the recommendation made by the government.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 With the trial date set for March 4, this case will be the first Trump will face against prosecutors and the special counsel Jack Smith \u8211\'20\'13 just as voters go to the polls for the primaries.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.05pm BST\par \par \uc2 Analysts believe the interesting timing of Trump\u8217\'20\'19s somewhat unsurprising attempt to get Chukan off the case came down to his frustration over scheduling.\par \par \uc2 Chukan set the date for the trial \u8211\'20\'13 which will examine the former president\u8217\'20\'19s efforts to overturn the 2020 election \u8211\'20\'13 to start on March 4. The start falls the day before Super Tuesday, when more than a dozen states will hold primaries.\par \par \uc2 Trump, who is attempting to retake the White House in 2024, pushed for a more than 2-year delay, asking for the trial to be held until April 2026. Chutkan rejected the request (opting for one about a month later than prosecutors initially argued for) and said Trump\u8217\'20\'19s legal time would have plenty of time to prepare.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CSetting a trial date does not depend and should not depend on the defendant\u8217\'20\'19s personal and professional obligations,\u8221\'20\'1D Chutkan said.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.54pm BST\par \par \uc2 Analysts and experts are beginning to weigh in on the filing for recusal, highlighting the high unlikelihood that it will work.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CJudge Chutkan\u8216\'20\'18s statements were made at January 6 sentencings, based on evidence in those proceedings,\u8221\'20\'1D lawyer Max Kennerly said in a social media post. \u8220\'20\'1CThe defendants argued they were following Trump\u8217\'20\'19s instructions, so Judge Chutkan addressed that. Thus, Liteky v US applies, and the bar for recusal is nearly insurmountable.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Adam Klasfeld, a senior legal correspondent at the Messenger, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://themessenger.com/politics/judges-tanya-chutkan-aileen-cannon-similar-rulings-trump-legal-troubles?utm_source=onsite&utm_medium=recombee_must_reads"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 highlighted how Trump has long-been critical of Chutkan}}}\uc2 , even though her rulings tend to align with Judge Aileen Cannon \u8211\'20\'13 who he appointed \u8211\'20\'13 and whose rulings he favors. Still, as Klasfeld highlights in a recent analysis, rebuking Chutkan will not likely help the former president.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI think that is to their great peril,\u8221\'20\'1D former federal prosecutor Mitchell Epner told Klasfeld, noting that treating the two judges differently was a poor legal strategy.\par \par \uc2 Keith Boykin, a national political commentator and author who served as a White House aide to President \uc2 Bill Clinton\uc2  framed the call as a more sinister tactic to discredit Chutkan.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CTrump trying to get Judge \uc2 Tanya Chutkan\uc2  to recuse herself is textbook Trump trying to smear a Black woman,\u8221\'20\'1D Boykin said in a post. \u8220\'20\'1CJudge Chutkan didn\u8217\'20\'19t indict Trump. A grand jury did. Judge Chutkan didn\u8217\'20\'19t bring the case. Jack Smith did. And Judge Chutkan won\u8217\'20\'19t decide his fate. A jury of his peers will.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 11.09pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.32pm BST\par \par \uc2 Though the filing only surfaced Monday, conservative calls for Chutkan to step down have been mounting in recent weeks. Republican congressman and Trump-loyalist \uc2 Matt Gaetz\uc2  filed a resolution to condemn and censure the federal judge for her comments in recent weeks.\par \par \uc2 Just last night, Mark Levin, a conservative pundit and Fox News show host, took aim at Judge Chutkan on his program.\par \par \uc2 Making the case that she is \u8220\'20\'1Cunqualified\u8221\'20\'1D to preside over the case against Trump, Levin cited an investigation on Real Clear Politics, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/2020/11/17/us/politics/real-clear-politics.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a right-leaning website largely funded by pro-Trump conservatives}}}\uc2 , that outlines many of the arguments used by the former president\u8217\'20\'19s legal team to call for Chutkan\u8217\'20\'19s recusal.\par \par \uc2 But for all the crying-foul coming from conservatives, it will be difficult for the Trump legal team to succeed in getting her off the case. As \uc2 New York University\uc2  professor of law Stephen Gillers told Real Clear Politics: \u8220\'20\'1CAlmost never will a judge be recused for opinions she forms as a judge \u8211\'20\'13 in hearing cases and motions. Judges are expected to form opinions based on these \u8216\'20\'18intrajudicial\u8217\'20\'19 sources. It\u8217\'20\'19s what judges do.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Ultimately, Chutkan will be the one to rule on whether she is too biased to preside over the case. If she denies the recusal, Trump\u8217\'20\'19s lawyers could petition an appeals court, but it\u8217\'20\'19s still a long shot.\par \par \uc2 This also isn\u8217\'20\'19t the first time Trump has tried to get a new judge. He previously failed to get a new judge to preside over his New York State court case and also attempted to get the case moved to federal court.\par \par \uc2 Trump has challenged the judge or jurisdiction in three of his four criminal cases this year, CBS News reports, excluding only Aileen Cannon \u8211\'20\'13 presiding over the 40 felony counts charged for \u8220\'20\'1Cwillful retention of national security information\u8221\'20\'1D \u8211\'20\'13 who he appointed.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 10.49pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.00pm BST\par \par \uc2 Trump moves to recuse Judge Chutkan\par \par \uc2 In a court filing on Monday, former president \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  moved to recuse federal judge \uc2 Tanya Chutkan\uc2 , who is overseeing the 2020 election subversion case, citing her previous comments about his culpability.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CJudge Chutkan has, in connection with other cases, suggested that President Trump should be prosecuted and imprisoned,\u8221\'20\'1D the motion for recusal reads. \u8220\'20\'1CSuch statements, made before this case began and without due process, are inherently disqualifying.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The filing includes a reference to a statement Chutkan made during cases in 2022 before the special counsel issued findings :\par \par \uc2 This was nothing less than an attempt to violently overthrow the government, the legally, lawfully, peacefully elected government by individuals who were mad that their guy lost. I see the videotapes. I see the footage of the flags and the signs that people were carrying and the hats they were wearing and the garb. And the people who mobbed that Capitol were there in fealty, in loyalty, to one man \u8211\'20\'13 not to the constitution, of which most of the people who come before me seem woefully ignorant; not to the ideals of this country; and not to the principles of democracy. It\u8217\'20\'19s a blind loyalty to one person who, by the way, remains free to this day.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CFairness and impartiality are the central tenets of our criminal justice system,\u8221\'20\'1D Trump\u8217\'20\'19s legal team wrote in the filing. \u8220\'20\'1CBoth a defendant and the public are entitled to a full hearing, on all relevant issues, by a Court that has not prejudged the guilt of the defendant, and whose neutrality cannot be reasonably questioned.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 10.13pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.47pm BST\par \par \uc2 Biden urges unity in his speech for 9/11\par \par \uc2 President Biden marked the anniversary of 9/11 by speaking to service members, first responders, and their families in Anchorage, Alaska.\par \par \uc2 Standing before an enormous American flag the president recounted memories of that tragic day while championing the acts of patriotism and courage performed in response.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThose terrorists could never touch the soul of America,\u8221\'20\'1D the President said resolutely. \u8220\'20\'1CHeroes, like all of you,\u8221\'20\'1D he added, \u8220\'20\'1Cnever faltered to defend our nation, our people an dour values in times of trial\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 He used the speech to tell the gathered troops that his administration is working to ensure broader support for service members when they return home. Outlining the ways in which the US has fought terrorist foes over the last two decades, and noting that \uc2 Osama Bin Laden\uc2  was sent \u8220\'20\'1Cto the gates of hell,\u8221\'20\'1D Biden turned toward the battles the country is still fighting \u8211\'20\'13 the deep-seated divisions that continue to threaten its future.\par \par \uc2 To drive home the point, the President ended with an anecdote about his late friend, Senator \uc2 John McCain\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CJohn and I were friends. Like a lot of us we had differences,\u8221\'20\'1D he said, adding that the two, \u8220\'20\'1Cdisagreed like hell,\u8221\'20\'1D on the Senate floor but would always find time to lunch afterward.\par \par \uc2 On their last meeting, Biden shared, McCain pulled him close, said he loved him, and asked Biden to perform his eulogy.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CHe put duty to country first,\u8221\'20\'1D Biden said. \u8220\'20\'1CAbove party, above politics, above his own person.\u8221\'20\'1D The president invoked the American people, including the military members in attendance, to reflect on that during this day of remembrance.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe must never lose that sense of national unity,\u8221\'20\'1D he said. \u8220\'20\'1CLet that be the common cause of our time.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 9.49pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.27pm BST\par \par \uc2 The US has reached a deal with Iran to swap prisoners\par \par \uc2 Five American prisoners being detained in Iran could soon be freed, thanks to a new deal the countries reached today. In exchange for the 5 US citizens, 5 Iranians held in the US will be released and the US will allow the transfer of $6bn in frozen Iranian funds from South Korea to Qatar without sanctions, the Associated Press {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://apnews.com/article/us-iran-prisoners-blinken-3e834df0a845ef2cc5c52af14598c66f"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reports}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Congress was notified of the deal today, after it was signed off by the Biden Administration late last week. AP reports that significant sum cleared for use by Iran was a key aspect to the deal, encouraging foreign banks to perform the transfer intended to be used to purchase humanitarian supplies. The cnetral bank of Qatar will hold the funds, which will be controlled by Qatar\u8217\'20\'19s government, to ensure its use is dedicated to aid, including medicine and food for the people of Iran.\par \par \uc2 The American prisoners have also been transferred out of Iranian jails and are now in house arrest.\par \par \uc2 The deal is the result of more than two years of negotiations between the two countries, according to the \uc2 The New York Times\uc2 , which {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/2023/08/10/us/politics/iran-us-prisoner-swap.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reported}}}\uc2  on the tentative agreement in August.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThis is just the beginning of a process that I hope and expect will lead to their return home to the United States,\u8221\'20\'1D Secretary of State \uc2 Antony J. Blinken\uc2  told reporters at the time. \u8220\'20\'1CThere\u8217\'20\'19s more work to be done to actually bring them home. My belief is that this is the beginning of the end of their nightmare.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.00pm BST\par \par \uc2 US close to approving long-range missiles armed with cluster bombs for Ukraine - report\par \par \uc2 The Biden administration is close to approving the shipment of longer-range missiles packed with cluster bombs to Ukraine, Reuters is reporting, citing four US officials.\par \par \uc2 The US is considering shipping either or both Army Tactical Missile Systems (ATACMS) that can fly up to 190 miles (306 km), or Guided Multiple Launch Rocket System (GMLRS) missiles with a 45-mile range packed with cluster bombs, the report says.\par \par \uc2 If approved, either option would be available for rapid shipment to Kyiv, giving Ukraine the ability to cause significant damage deeper within Russian-occupied territory.\par \par \uc2 The decision to send ATACMS or GMLRS, or both, is not final and could still fall through, according to the sources.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.54pm BST\par \par \uc2 The US has approved a series of Covid-19 booster vaccines amid rising cases of coronavirus around the country, the \uc2 Food and Drug Administration\uc2  said.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 FDA{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.fda.gov/news-events/press-announcements/fda-takes-action-updated-mrna-covid-19-vaccines-better-protect-against-currently-circulating"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 said}}}\uc2  it had approved \uc2 Moderna\uc2  and Pfizer-BioNTech vaccines, which can be administered even to people who never previously received a Covid-19 vaccination.\par \par \uc2 As with earlier vaccinations, the new round of shots are cleared for adults and children as young as age 6 months.\par \par \uc2 Starting at age five, most people can get a single dose even if they have never had a prior Covid-19 shot, per the \uc2 FDA\uc2 . Younger children might need additional doses depending on their history of Covid-19 infections and vaccinations.\par \par \uc2 Hospitalizations from Covid-19 have {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cdc.gov/coronavirus/2019-ncov/science/forecasting/hospitalizations-forecasts.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 crept up}}}\uc2  in recent weeks, although the rise is lower than the same time last year. In the week ending 26 August just over 17,400 people were hospitalized from Covid-19, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nbcnews.com/health/health-news/signs-point-rise-covid-rcna103439"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 NBC reported}}}\uc2 , up 16% from the week before.\par \par \uc2 In August, two hospitals in New York state re-introduced mandatory masking after an increase in Covid-19 cases, while the \uc2 Lionsgate\uc2  film studio {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/film/2023/aug/22/hollywood-lionsgate-mask-mandate-covid-eris-los-angeles"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reinstated}}}\uc2  a mask mandate for half its employees in its flagship Los Angeles offices.\par \par \uc2 That same month, the \uc2 US Centers for Disease Control and Prevention (CDC) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2023/aug/24/new-covid-variant-masking-high-risk-people"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 said}}}\uc2  that it had discovered a new Covid-19 variant and warned high-risk individuals to resume wearing masks.\par \par \uc2 The variant, BA 2.86, was detected during monitoring of wastewater, the CDC said. It said it was too soon to tell if BA 2.86 could lead to more severe illness than other variants, but reported \u8220\'20\'1Creassuring\u8221\'20\'1D results of early research which showed that existing antibodies work against the BA 2.86 variant.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.49pm BST\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  urged supporters they need to \u8220\'20\'1Cfight like hell\u8221\'20\'1D or risk losing their country during a speech at a South Dakota rally in which the former president used language resonant of the run-up to the January 6 US Capitol attack, according to a CNN {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cnn.com/2023/09/11/politics/trump-wild-rhetoric-2024/index.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 report. }}}\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI don\u8217\'20\'19t think there\u8217\'20\'19s ever been a darkness around our nation like there is now,\u8221\'20\'1D Trump said on Friday, as he accused Democrats of allowing an \u8220\'20\'1Cinvasion\u8221\'20\'1D of migrants over the southern border and of trying to restart Covid \u8220\'20\'1Chysteria\u8221\'20\'1D, the report says.\par \par \uc2 The Republican front-runner\u8217\'20\'19s stark speech raised the prospect of a second presidency that would be even more extreme and challenging to the rule of law than his first. His view that the Oval Office confers unfettered powers suggests Trump would indulge in similar conduct as that for which he is awaiting trial, including intimidating local officials in an alleged bid to overturn his 2020 defeat.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.37pm BST\par \par \uc2 Here are some images from the news wires of how the US has been marking the 22nd anniversary of the 9/11 terror attacks, which took the lives of nearly 3,000 people.\par \par \uc2 Honor guard rehearse before the 22nd Anniversary of 9/11 Commemoration Ceremony at the World Trade Center Memorial in New York. Photograph: Derek French/\uc2 Shutterstock\uc2  New York Governor \uc2 Kathy Hochul\uc2 , vice-president \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 , and New York City Mayor Eric Adams attend the commemoration ceremony. Photograph: Clutch Pockets Wambli/ZUMA Press Wire/Shutterstock US Secretary of Defense Lloyd Austin participates in a wreath laying ceremony to mark the 22nd anniversary of the September 11 terrorist attacks at the Pentagon in Arlington, Virginia near Washington, DC. Photograph: Bonnie Cash/UPI/Shutterstock Firefighters salute during a moment of silence (observance of time of the fall of the South Tower) at the World Trade Center Memorial in New York. Photograph: Derek French/\uc2 Shutterstock\uc2  Retired New York City firefighter Paul Matulis, right, and Austin firefighter Matthew Boyan of the Austin Fire Department Honor Guard pray during a 9/11 Memorial at the Buford Fire Tower in Austin, Texas. Photograph: Jay Janner/AP\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.19pm BST\par \par \uc2 Several people {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/sep/11/government-shutdown-trump-biden-911-anniversary-politics-live-updates?page=with:block-64ff33948f087658b6f99ea8#block-64ff33948f087658b6f99ea8"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 were arrested}}}\uc2  after entering the office of Kevin McCarthy, the speaker of the House, during a protest for HIV/Aids funding on Monday.\par \par \uc2 The US President\u8217\'20\'19s Emergency Plan for Aids Relief (Pepfar), a widely bipartisan program, has since been reauthorized three times, and \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  earlier this year indicated that he would work with Congress to extend it a fourth.\par \par \uc2 But the program\u8217\'20\'19s latest extension has been caught up in a partisan fight over \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  and is under threat amid Congress\u8217\'20\'19s negotiations over a government shutdown.\par \par \uc2 Some Republicans are opposing Pepfar\u8217\'20\'19s reauthorization, arguing that current restrictions do not sufficiently prevent the funds from being used to support abortions, according to an August {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://sgp.fas.org/crs/misc/IF12463.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 report}}}\uc2  by the \uc2 Federation of American Scientists\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 New Jersey Republican Representative Chris Smith, who chairs the House foreign affairs subcommittee, in a letter to colleagues in June:\par \par \uc2 Any multi-year PEPFAR reauthorizing legislation must ensure that Biden\u8217\'20\'19s hijacking of PEPFAR to promote \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  be halted.\par \par \uc2 The program was first established in 2003 by President \uc2 George W Bush\uc2  to prevent and treat HIV/Aids in developing countries worldwide, and it is overseen by the \uc2 US Department of State\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 About 20 million people depend on the program globally, according to a White House statement in January.\par \par \uc2 Smith was a co-sponsor of the 2018 bill extending Pepfar for five years but is now seeking to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.politico.com/news/2023/06/27/abortion-wars-pepfar-00103679"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 block its renewal}}}\uc2  after Biden in 2021 lifted Trump-era restrictions that barred Pepfar and other global programs receiving US funding from performing or promoting abortions.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.04pm BST\par \par \uc2 The Food and Drug Administration (\uc2 FDA\uc2 ) gave the green light to updated Covid-19 vaccine shots from \uc2 Moderna\uc2  and \uc2 Pfizer\uc2 /\uc2 BioNTech\uc2 , but it is the \uc2 Centers for Disease Control and Prevention\uc2  that recommends who should get the shot, according to a \uc2 Washington Post{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.washingtonpost.com/health/2023/09/11/covid-vaccine-new-booster/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 report. }}}\par \par \uc2 The CDC is leaning toward a broad recommendation that covers almost all ages, mirroring the \uc2 FDA\uc2  approach, the paper writes, citing federal officials.\par \par \uc2 But it is possible that some on the agency\u8217\'20\'19s panel of outside experts, the \uc2 Advisory Committee on Immunization Practices\uc2 , will push for a targeted recommendation focused on those at greatest risk \u8212\'20\'14 older Americans or people with weakened immune systems or other illnesses.\par \par \uc2 Experts interviewed by the paper said they would get the coronavirus shot as soon as possible amid a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/sep/11/government-shutdown-trump-biden-911-anniversary-politics-live-updates?page=with:block-64ff5d918f08571e8693b137#block-64ff5d918f08571e8693b137"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  late-summer uptick}}}\uc2  in Covid cases across the US\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.48pm BST\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/sep/11/government-shutdown-trump-biden-911-anniversary-politics-live-updates?page=with:block-64ff589f8f087658b6f9a044#block-64ff589f8f087658b6f9a044"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Updated}}}\uc2  Covid-19 vaccinations could begin later this week, and the US hopes to ramp up protection against the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/sep/11/government-shutdown-trump-biden-911-anniversary-politics-live-updates?page=with:block-64ff5d918f08571e8693b137#block-64ff5d918f08571e8693b137"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  latest coronavirus strains}}}\uc2  amid steadily increasing cases.\par \par \uc2 The newest shots target an omicron variant named XBB.1.5, replacing combination vaccines that mixed protection against the original coronavirus strain and even older omicron variants.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CVaccination remains critical to public health and continued protection against serious consequences of COVID-19, including hospitalization and death,\u8221\'20\'1D said Peter Marks, director of the \uc2 FDA\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s center for biologics evaluation and research.\par \par \uc2 The public can be assured that these updated vaccines have met the agency\u8217\'20\'19s rigorous scientific standards for safety, effectiveness, and manufacturing quality. We very much encourage those who are eligible to consider getting vaccinated.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.37pm BST\par \par \uc2 There has been a late-summer uptick in Covid cases across the US.\par \par \uc2 Experts are closely watching two new variants, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.yalemedicine.org/news/covid-eg5-eris-latest-coronavirus-strain#:~:text=This%20summer%2C%20that%20strain%20is,than%20any%20other%20single%20strain."}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 EG.5}}}\uc2 , now the dominant strain, and BA.2.86, which has attracted attention from scientists {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/article/covid-variant.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 because of its high number of mutations.}}}\par \par \uc2 Experts have said that the US is not facing a threat like it did in 2020 and 2021. \u8220\'20\'1CWe\u8217\'20\'19re in a different place,\u8221\'20\'1D Mandy Cohen, the head of the \uc2 Centers for Disease Control and Prevention\uc2 , {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nbcnews.com/health/health-news/covid-cases-are-ticking-not-time-panic-experts-say-rcna100380"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 told NBC News last month}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 I think we\u8217\'20\'19re the most prepared that we\u8217\'20\'19ve ever been.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.32pm BST\par \par \uc2 Updated Covid-19 vaccine {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/sep/11/government-shutdown-trump-biden-911-anniversary-politics-live-updates?page=with:block-64ff589f8f087658b6f9a044#block-64ff589f8f087658b6f9a044"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  shots }}}\uc2  made by \uc2 Pfizer\uc2  and \uc2 Moderna\uc2  are expected to be available in the coming days, according to \uc2 Moderna\uc2 . A third shot, by the vaccine maker \uc2 Novavax\uc2 , is still under review by the \uc2 FDA\uc2 , according to the company.\par \par \uc2 Advisers from the US centers for disease and protection (CDC) are due to meet on Tuesday to recommend who should receive the shot. An endorsement by the CDC\u8217\'20\'19s director should clear the way for millions of doses to be shipped nationwide within days.\par \par \uc2 As part of the \uc2 FDA\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s update, the original \uc2 Moderna\uc2  and \uc2 Pfizer\uc2 /\uc2 BioNTech\uc2  Covid-19 vaccines are no longer authorized for use in the US.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 7.44pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.16pm BST\par \par \uc2 FDA\uc2  authorizes updated Covid vaccines\par \par \uc2 The US health regulator on Monday authorized updated Covid-19 vaccines that closely match the Omicron variants that are circulating, starting the process to deploy the shots this month, Reuters reports.\par \par \uc2 The Food and Drug Administration authorized the shots, which target the XBB.1.5 subvariant, from manufacturers \uc2 Pfizer\uc2  and its German partner \uc2 BioNTech SE\uc2 , and US pharma company \uc2 Moderna\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 More details to follow.\par \par \uc2 Last year: Syringes with vaccines are prepared at the L.A. Care and \uc2 Blue Shield of California\uc2  Promise Health Plans' Community Resource Center where they were offering members and the public free flu and COVID-19 vaccines Oct. 28, 2022, in Lynwood, Calif. Updated COVID-19 vaccines are expected to be available in the US soon, following \uc2 FDA\uc2  approval of the latest version today. Photograph: Mark J Terrill/AP\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.08pm BST\par \par \uc2 A trial began Monday over a sweeping Texas voting law that sparked a 38-day {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/may/31/texas-democrats-late-night-walkout-republicans-restrict-voting-rights-bill-failure"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 walkout by Democrats}}}\uc2  in 2021 and were among the strictest changes passed by Republicans nationwide following former US president \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s false claims of a stolen election, the Associated Press reports.\par \par \uc2 The AP further notes:\par \par \uc2 The lawsuit was brought by a coalition of voting rights groups after Republican governor Greg Abbott signed the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/aug/27/texas-house-passes-sweeping-voting-restrictions-bill"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 changes into law}}}\uc2 . The trial in San Antonio federal court could last weeks and it is unclear when US district judge Xavier Rodriguez might rule. Potentially at stake are voting rules Texas will use for the 2024 elections, although any decision is likely to be appealed.\par \par \uc2 The challenge, from \uc2 the American Civil Liberties Union\uc2 , (\uc2 ACLU\uc2 ) the Mexican American Legal Defense Fund and others, has not stopped the measures from taking effect, including a ban on 24-hour polling places and drive-thru voting.\par \par \uc2 Many changes targeted Harris county, which includes Houston and is where a slate of Republican candidates {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://apnews.com/article/election-lawsuit-texas-harris-county-trial-0c9aef3291b0c0e5f07d9f6889e4f881"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 are challenging their defeats last year}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 During the hurried rollout of the law last year, more than 23,000 mail {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://apnews.com/article/2022-midterm-elections-elections-texas-voting-only-on-ap-45ba51fe9dd951a0f82015bd6bd9ff41"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 ballots in Texas were rejected}}}\uc2  during the March 2022 primary elections as voters struggled to navigate the new rules. By November\u8217\'20\'19s general election, the rejection rate fell significantly, but was still higher than what experts consider normal.\par \par \uc2 In August, Rodriguez separately struck {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://apnews.com/article/voting-rights-texas-georgia-republicans-restrictions-judges-7d90fd5f38a4ba1b613343213ec13547"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 down a requirement}}}\uc2  that mail voters provide the same identification number they used when they registered to vote.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.52pm BST\par \par \uc2 Interim summary\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  is up in the air literally and House Speaker Kevin McCarthy\u8217\'20\'19s future as House Speaker is likewise, but metaphorically. It\u8217\'20\'19s been a busy day in Vietnam for the US president post-G20, but he\u8217\'20\'19s now on his way back to the US and is due to address the public during a stopover in Alaska en route to Washington, DC.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s where things stand:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Mark Meadows\uc2 , the former Trump White House chief of staff, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/sep/11/government-shutdown-trump-biden-911-anniversary-politics-live-updates?page=with:block-64ff3a1f8f08571e8693afcf#block-64ff3a1f8f08571e8693afcf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 appealed}}}\uc2  a judge\u8217\'20\'19s ruling last Friday denying his bid to transfer his Georgia 2020 election interference case from state to federal court.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Jury {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/sep/11/government-shutdown-trump-biden-911-anniversary-politics-live-updates?page=with:block-64ff38008f082e414fc7095e#block-64ff38008f082e414fc7095e"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 deliberations}}}\uc2  for the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/sep/05/ken-paxton-impeachment-trial-texas-attorney-general"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 impeachment trial }}}\uc2  of the Texas attorney general, \uc2 Ken Paxton\uc2 , could start late Thursday or Friday, according to the presiding officer \uc2 Dan Patrick\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Kevin McCarthy, Speaker of the House, reportedly {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/sep/11/government-shutdown-trump-biden-911-anniversary-politics-live-updates?page=with:block-64ff306c8f082e414fc708db#block-64ff306c8f082e414fc708db"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 doesn\u8217\'20\'19t have}}}\uc2  the votes to move forward with an impeachment inquiry into \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  being clamored for by the right wing of his House caucus.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Ken Buck\uc2 , a Colorado Republican congressman, said that there was {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/sep/11/government-shutdown-trump-biden-911-anniversary-politics-live-updates?page=with:block-64ff1e1a8f08b298ac2fcef1#block-64ff1e1a8f08b298ac2fcef1"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a \u8220\'20\'1Cperfect storm\u8221\'20\'1D brewing}}}\uc2  in the House over government spending and on impeachment of the president that could pose a threat to Kevin McCarthy \u8217\'20\'19s speakership. More {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.politico.com/news/2023/09/11/kevin-mccarthy-government-shutdown-profile-00114028?nname=playbook&nid=0000014f-1646-d88f-a1cf-5f46b7bd0000&nrid=00000168-5c87-d6fb-a77d-fdb72f6a0000&nlid=630318"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 on this}}}\uc2  by Politico.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  will address the nation late on Monday afternoon on the 22nd anniversary of the terrorist attacks on the US on September 11, 2001. On Monday morning, US vice president \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  attended the annual memorial ceremony in New York at the spot where the al-Qaeda hijackers destroyed the twin towers of the World Trade Center.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.06pm BST\par \par \uc2 In the months before the supreme court handed down \uc2 Citizens United\uc2 , the 2010 ruling which unleashed a flood of dark money into American politics, the wife of a conservative justice worked with a prominent rightwing activist and a mega-donor closely linked to her husband to form a group to exploit the decision.\par \par \uc2 So said {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.politico.com/news/2023/09/10/ginni-thomas-leonard-leo-citizens-united-00108082"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a blockbuster report from Politico}}}\uc2 , detailing moves by Ginni Thomas \u8211\'20\'13 wife of Justice \uc2 Clarence Thomas\uc2  \u8211\'20\'13 and \uc2 Leonard Leo\uc2 , the \uc2 Federalist Society\uc2  chief who has worked to stock the court with rightwingers, leading to a series of epochal decisions, including the removal of the federal right to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Half a million dollars in seed money, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.politico.com/news/2023/09/10/ginni-thomas-leonard-leo-citizens-united-00108082"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Politico said}}}\uc2 , came from Harlan Crow, the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/apr/08/clarence-thomas-supreme-court-harlan-crow-hitler-memorabilia"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Nazi memorabilia-collecting}}}\uc2  billionaire whose extensive and mostly undeclared gifts to \uc2 Clarence Thomas\uc2  have fueled a spiraling supreme court ethics scandal.\par \par \uc2 Sheldon Whitehouse, a Democratic senator from Rhode Island and champion of ethics reform, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/SenWhitehouse/status/1700903582256504952"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 said}}}\uc2  the report laid out \u8220\'20\'1Cthe creepy intermingling of dark billionaire money, phoney front groups, far-right extremists and the United States supreme court\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Politico noted that the ruling in \uc2 Citizens United\uc2  was widely expected after justices \u8220\'20\'1Ctook the unusual step of asking for re-arguments based on a sweeping question \u8211\'20\'13 whether they should overrule prior decisions approving laws that limited spending on political campaigns\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.politico.com/news/2023/09/10/ginni-thomas-leonard-leo-citizens-united-00108082"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Noting}}}\uc2  that conservative groups moved to capitalise faster than others, the site {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.politico.com/news/2023/09/10/ginni-thomas-leonard-leo-citizens-united-00108082"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 quoted}}}\uc2  an anonymous source as saying Ginni Thomas \u8220\'20\'1Creally wanted to build an organisation and be a movement leader. Leonard was going to be the conduit of that.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Ginni Thomas on Capitol Hill on 29 September. Photograph: Anna Moneymaker/Getty Images\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/sep/11/ginni-thomas-leonard-leo-harlan-crow-citizens-united-dark-money"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  Ginni Thomas and rightwing activists exploited supreme court ruling \u8211\'20\'13 report}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.55pm BST\par \par \uc2 The justice department has dropped its five-year-old criminal case against \uc2 Bijan Rafiekian\uc2 , a one-time business partner of the former national security adviser \uc2 Michael Flynn\uc2  who had been charged with illegally lobbying for Turkey during the 2016 US presidential election.\par \par \uc2 Rafiekian, who also goes by the name \uc2 Bijan Kian\uc2 , was indicted in 2018 on charges including failing to register as a foreign agent. Prosecutors had accused Rafiekian of illegally lobbying to have the cleric Fethullah G\u252\'00\'FClen extradited from the US to Turkey.\par \par \uc2 The move wraps up a long-running tangent of the Mueller-era Russia investigation that originally had been used as leverage to pressure Flynn, CNN {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cnn.com/2023/09/11/politics/bijan-kian-charges-dropped/index.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reported. }}}\uc2  Prosecutors had planned on calling Flynn to testify against Rafiekian at his trial to solidify their evidence of a connection between Flynn\u8217\'20\'19s lobbying group and the government of Turkey.\par \par \uc2 In 2019, a jury convicted Rafiekian on charges of conspiracy and acting as a foreign agent. But the judge who presided over the trial later set aside the verdicts, citing insufficient evidence. The case then went into appeals, hanging in the criminal justice system for years.\par \par \uc2 In a court filing on Monday, the justice department said it sought to dismiss the charges against Rafiekian. Prosecutors wrote:\par \par \uc2 After carefully considering the Fourth Circuit\u8217\'20\'19s recent decision in this case and the principles of federal prosecution, the United States believes it is not in the public interest to pursue the case against defendant \uc2 Bijan Rafiekian\uc2  further.\par \par \uc2 Bijan Kian\uc2 , whose full name is \uc2 Bijan Rafiekian\uc2 , pictuerd in Washington, 17 December 2018. Photograph: Jacquelyn Martin/AP\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.36pm BST\par \par \uc2 After defending the integrity of US elections from an onslaught of threats over the last several years, secretaries of state across the US are now turning to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/aug/20/trump-disqualified-constitution-section-3-14th-amendment"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a new high-stakes question}}}\uc2  : is \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  eligible to run for president?\par \par \uc2 Several secretaries are already working with attorneys general in their states and studying whether Trump is disqualified under a provision of the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://constitution.congress.gov/browse/amendment-14/section-3/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 14th amendment }}}\uc2  that bars anyone from holding public office if they have previously taken an oath to the United States and then \u8220\'20\'1Cengaged in insurrection or rebellion against the same\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 That language clearly disqualifies Trump from running in 2024, William Baude and Michael Stokes Paulsen, two prominent conservative scholars, concluded in a lengthy forthcoming law review article. They write {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://papers.ssrn.com/sol3/papers.cfm?abstract_id=4532751"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 in the article}}}\uc2  :\par \par \uc2 If the public record is accurate, the case is not even close. He is no longer eligible to the office of Presidency, or any other state or federal office covered by the Constitution. All who are committed to the Constitution should take note and say so.\par \par \uc2 A flurry of challenges to Trump\u8217\'20\'19s candidacy are expected \u8211\'20\'13 one was filed in Colorado {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/sep/06/watchdog-group-sues-remove-trump-2024-election"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 on Wednesday}}}\uc2  \u8211\'20\'13 but the legal issues at play are largely untested. Never before has the provision been used to try to disqualify a presidential candidate from office and the issue is likely to quickly come to a head as soon as officials make their official certifications about who can appear on primary ballots.\par \par \uc2 Secretaries are studying who has the authority to remove Trump from the ballot and what process needs to occur before they do so. They also recognize that the issue is likely to be ultimately settled by the courts, including the \uc2 US supreme court\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Jocelyn Benson\uc2 , a Democrat in her second term as Michigan\u8217\'20\'19s secretary of state, said she had spoken with another secretary of state about the 14th amendment issue \u8220\'20\'1Cnearly every day\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 The north star for me is always: \u8216\'20\'18What is the law? What does the constitution require?\u8217\'20\'19 To keep politics and partisan considerations out of it. And simply just look at this from a sense of \u8216\'20\'18what does the 14th amendment say?\u8217\'20\'19 We\u8217\'20\'19re in unprecedented, uncharted territory.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/sep/11/us-elections-officials-trump-presidency-eligibility"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Read my colleague Sam Levin\u8217\'20\'19s full report.}}}\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/sep/11/us-elections-officials-trump-presidency-eligibility"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \u8216\'20\'18Uncharted territory\u8217\'20\'19: elections officials weigh Trump\u8217\'20\'19s presidency eligibility}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.24pm BST\par \par \uc2 Past government shutdowns prove the widespread upheaval caused by lapses in government funding.\par \par \uc2 During the last partial shutdown, which ended in January 2019, roughly 800,000 federal workers went without a paycheck.\par \par \uc2 The Trump administration tried to keep national parks open with limited staff, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.businessinsider.com/national-parks-damage-government-shutdown-2019-1"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 resulting in damage}}}\uc2  to the grounds. Loan programs overseen by the \uc2 Small Business Administration\uc2  and federally funded research projects were also halted or delayed.\par \par \uc2 David Reich, senior fellow at the left-leaning \uc2 Center on Budget and Policy Priorities\uc2 , said:\par \par \uc2 It\u8217\'20\'19s very disruptive. Federal agencies spend a whole lot of time trying to figure out what they\u8217\'20\'19re allowed to do and not allowed to do. It\u8217\'20\'19s a total waste of effort and energy.\par \par \uc2 Even though history shows the fallout of government shutdowns, Gordon Gray, vice-president for economic policy at the center-right thinktank American Action Forum, still anticipates a lapse in funding \u8211\'20\'13 if not in October then later this year.\par \par \uc2 I could envision a brief [continuing resolution] \u8211\'20\'13 like two weeks \u8211\'20\'13 with some disaster supplemental funding in it. My expectation is that we\u8217\'20\'19ll still have a shutdown this fall.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.07pm BST\par \par \uc2 Mark Meadows\uc2  files appeal to move Georgia case to federal court\par \par \uc2 Mark Meadows\uc2 , the former Trump White House chief of staff, appealed a judge\u8217\'20\'19s ruling denying his bid to transfer his Georgia 2020 election interference case from state to federal court, according to a court filing reported by Reuters.\par \par \uc2 US district judge Steve Jones {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/sep/08/mark-meadows-georgia-election-charges"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 denied Meadow\u8217\'20\'19s request }}}\uc2  on Friday, meaning the prosecution brought by the Fulton county district attorney \uc2 Fani Willis\uc2  stays in superior court in Atlanta, unless the US court of appeals for the 11th circuit approves Meadows\u8217\'20\'19 appeal.\par \par \uc2 Last month, the Atlanta-area grand jury handed up {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/aug/14/donald-trump-georgia-indictment-2020-election"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a sprawling 41-count indictment}}}\uc2  against \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  and 18 others, including Meadows, alleging that they violated Georgia\u8217\'20\'19s state Rico statute in their efforts to subvert the results of the 2020 election.\par \par \uc2 Meadows had sought to remove the case to federal court arguing that the sprawling racketeering charges related to his normal work undertaken as a White House chief of staff, which gave him immunity from prosecution and prevented him from being prosecuted at the state level.\par \par \uc2 But the judge rejected his arguments in a detailed 49-page decision, determining that Meadows did not meet his burden to show that he was acting within his job description when he undertook efforts to benefit Trump as a political candidate rather than Trump as president.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 5.07pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.00pm BST\par \par \uc2 Decision in Texas AG \uc2 Ken Paxton\uc2 's impeachment trial could come this week\par \par \uc2 Jury deliberations for the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/sep/05/ken-paxton-impeachment-trial-texas-attorney-general"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 impeachment trial }}}\uc2  of the Texas attorney general, \uc2 Ken Paxton\uc2 , could start late Thursday or Friday, according to the presiding officer \uc2 Dan Patrick\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Proceedings resumed this morning for the fifth day of Paxton\u8217\'20\'19s trial \u8211\'20\'13 the first impeachment trial in modern Texas history. The ultra-conservative attorney general has a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/jun/09/texas-republicans-ken-paxton-attorney-general"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 history}}}\uc2  of ethically questionable conduct that dates back to his first term in 2014, when he was fined by the Texas state securities board for violating financial laws.\par \par \uc2 The core of Paxton\u8217\'20\'19s alleged wrongdoing involves his relationship with the Austin real estate developer \uc2 Nate Paul\uc2 . Paxton has been accused of illegally using his office to benefit Paul, who in return gave Paxton\u8217\'20\'19s mistress, Laura Olsen, a job in his office. In early June, Paul was {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.texastribune.org/2023/06/09/nate-paul-federal-charges/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 arrested}}}\uc2  on eight charges of making false statements to financial institutions. Also being scrutinized are allegations that Paxton wrongly fired former employees who blew the whistle to the \uc2 FBI\uc2  and other agencies.\par \par \uc2 At the end of the trial, it will be known if Paxton will be removed from office and if he can ever hold office again. Paxton has pleaded not guilty.\par \par \uc2 Lt Gov Patrick, who is presiding over the proceedings, said each side has so far used about half its allotted time for arguments and that the case could go to the jury later this week, AP {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://apnews.com/article/ken-paxton-impeachment-texas-547f46284c7858905b067fefa2c48f0b"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reported}}}\uc2 . He also said there will be no more days off until the trial is resolved, raising the possibility that a decision could come over the weekend.\par \par \uc2 The Texas attorney general, \uc2 Ken Paxton\uc2 , is flanked by his attorneys as the articles of his impeachment are read in the senate chamber at the Texas capitol last week. Photograph: Eric Gay/AP\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 5.01pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.52pm BST\par \par \uc2 A pro-gun group is suing the New Mexico governor, \uc2 Michelle Lujan Grisham\uc2 , in an effort to block a 30-day emergency order suspending the right to carry firearms in public in Albuquerque\u8217\'20\'19s Bernalillo county issued last week after a spate of shootings.\par \par \uc2 The governor announced open and concealed carry restrictions on Friday in a public health order relating to gun violence after the fatal shootings of an 11-year-old boy on his way home from a minor league baseball game last week, as well as the fatal shooting of a four-year-old girl in her bed in a motor home and a 13-year-old girl in Taos county in August.\par \par \uc2 Lujan Grisham\uc2  said she expected someone to legally challenge her {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.governor.state.nm.us/wp-content/uploads/2023/09/Executive-Order-2023-130.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 executive order}}}\uc2 , adding that she welcomed \u8220\'20\'1Cthe debate and the fight about making New Mexicans safer\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 That challenge arrived on Saturday when the National Association for Gun Rights said it would file a lawsuit in federal court against the governor, citing 2021\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.supremecourt.gov/opinions/21pdf/20-843_7j80.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Bruen}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.supremecourt.gov/opinions/21pdf/20-843_7j80.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 US supreme court ruling}}}\uc2  easing gun restrictions.\par \par \uc2 The president of the pro-gun group, Dudley Brown, accused the governor of \u8220\'20\'1Cthrowing up a middle finger to the constitution and the supreme court\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Her executive order is in blatant disregard for Bruen. She needs to be held accountable for stripping the God-given rights of millions away with the stroke of a pen.\par \par \uc2 The order calls for monthly inspections of firearms dealers statewide to ensure compliance with gun laws and for the state health department to compile a report on gunshot victims at hospitals that includes age, race, gender and ethnicity, along with the brand and caliber of firearm involved, according to the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.santafenewmexican.com/ap/national/gun-rights-group-sues-lujan-grisham-over-emergency-order-banning-firearms-in-public/article_4acd75f0-f81e-5f37-b068-83d4e1c97d78.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Santa Fe New Mexican}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Lujan Graham said she issued the order to open up more resources to help New Mexico get the gun violence issue under control and called on the federal government for help.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThese are disgusting acts of violence that have no place in our communities,\u8221\'20\'1D \uc2 Lujan Grisham\uc2  said on Thursday, adding that Bernalillo county needed a \u8220\'20\'1Ccooling off period\u8221\'20\'1D during an epidemic of gun violence.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.42pm BST\par \par \uc2 Activists entered the speaker Kevin McCarthy \u8217\'20\'19s office in the US Capitol demanding the reauthorization of the law governing US global Aids funding, Politico\u8217\'20\'19s Alice Miranda Ollstein reports.\par \par \uc2 The President\u8217\'20\'19s Emergency Program for Aids Relief (Pepfar), which has {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/2023/07/28/us/politics/aids-relief-pepfar-abortion-republicans.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  saved 25 million lives }}}\uc2  and stands as one of the US\u8217\'20\'19 most successful foreign aid programs, is in danger of becoming a victim of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  politics as it reaches its expiration date at the end of the month.\par \par \uc2 enltrBREAKING: Activists are occupying {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/SpeakerMcCarthy?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @SpeakerMcCarthy}}}\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s office demanding a full 5 year reauthorization of PEPFAR, which some Rs are opposing. Background: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/nQVnCxPDE0"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/nQVnCxPDE0}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/wCZx4Z6wzu"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/wCZx4Z6wzu}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Alice Miranda Ollstein (@AliceOllstein) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/AliceOllstein/status/1701254337891119597?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 September 11, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 enltr6 activists are being arrested by \uc2 Capitol Police\uc2 , lined up against the wall and handcuffed {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/qgWCCcgsM2"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/qgWCCcgsM2}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Alice Miranda Ollstein (@AliceOllstein) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/AliceOllstein/status/1701256075381543233?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 September 11, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 5.17pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.32pm BST\par \par \uc2 McCarthy doesn't have votes to advance Biden impeachment inquiry, reports say\par \par \uc2 The speaker, Kevin McCarthy, doesn\u8217\'20\'19t have the votes to move forward with an impeachment inquiry into \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 , according to the CNN {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cnn.com/2023/09/11/politics/impeachment-government-shutdown-house-return/index.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  report.}}}\par \par \uc2 One moderate GOP lawmaker told the news channel there are as many as 30 Republicans who don\u8217\'20\'19t believe there\u8217\'20\'19s enough evidence yet for impeachment.\par \par \uc2 Republican congressman for South Dakota, \uc2 Dusty Johnson\uc2 , said:\par \par \uc2 There is a constitutional and legal test that you have to meet with evidence. I have not seen that evidence, but I guess I\u8217\'20\'19m not suggesting it doesn\u8217\'20\'19t exist. I do think the fact that the committees continue to ask for additional documents suggests that they don\u8217\'20\'19t think their evidentiary record is complete yet.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 5.18pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.18pm BST\par \par \uc2 Marjorie Taylor Greene\uc2 , the far-right congresswoman from Georgia, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cnn.com/2023/09/11/politics/impeachment-government-shutdown-house-return/index.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 told }}}\uc2  CNN she personally would like to see an impeachment inquiry into \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  happen this week.\par \par \uc2 Greene has made clear that her support for government funding is contingent upon the House GOP launching an impeachment inquiry into the president, among other things. She said:\par \par \uc2 Our conference needs to stop capitulating to the left, more members that are in blue districts. That\u8217\'20\'19s not what the donors are donating money for. And we need to stop allowing Biden-district Republicans to hold up our agenda.\par \par \uc2 She added:\par \par \uc2 Put the vote to the floor, even if it fails. I guarantee you, if you put it back, it\u8217\'20\'19ll pass because every single Republican that votes no to it will get destroyed by their districts.\par \par \uc2 Citing sources, the report says \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  is set to forcefully weigh in on the looming government shutdown, the White House\u8217\'20\'19s request for disaster relief and aid for Ukraine, and the growing calls on the right to impeach Biden.\par \par \uc2 The former president is likely to ramp up his calls to impeach Biden and come out strongly against Ukraine aid, further ratcheting up pressure on McCarthy as he plots his strategy for the treacherous month ahead.\par \par \uc2 All of this is expected to be discussed in a closed-door party meeting Wednesday, the first time House Republicans will huddle in person since before the six-week August recess. How McCarthy and his leadership team handles this critical month of governing will have major implications for both the country and his speakership.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 4.20pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.03pm BST\par \par \uc2 Republican senator \uc2 Bill Cassidy\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s comments follow increasing speculation surrounding the mental competence of Capitol Hill leaders, including 81-year-old Senate Republican leader \uc2 Mitch McConnell\uc2 , who appeared to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/aug/30/mcconnell-freezes-again-kentucky-press-conference"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 freeze up}}}\uc2  in front of reporters during two separate instances this summer. Meanwhile, in March, McConnell {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/mar/09/mitch-mcconnell-in-hospital-after-fall-in-washington-dc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 received}}}\uc2  treatment for a concussion after he tripped and fell at a Washington DC hotel during a private dinner.\par \par \uc2 The most recent freezing episode {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/aug/30/mcconnell-freezes-again-kentucky-press-conference"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 occurred}}}\uc2  less than two weeks earlier in Kentucky. McConnell appeared to freeze for more than 30 seconds before being eventually escorted away by staff members.\par \par \uc2 Afterwards, the congressional physician, Brian P Monahan, conducted several evaluations on McConnell, including brain MRI imaging, an EEG study and consultations with several neurologists for a \u8220\'20\'1Ccomprehensive neurology assessment\u8221\'20\'1D, he said in a letter. He added:\par \par \uc2 There is no evidence that you have a seizure disorder or that you experienced a stroke, TIA [transient ischaemic attack or mini-stroke] or movement disorder such as Parkinson\u8217\'20\'19s disease.\par \par \uc2 During Sunday\u8217\'20\'19s interview, Cassidy praised McConnell, saying he \u8220\'20\'1Chandled it perfectly\u8221\'20\'1D. \u8220\'20\'1CHis doctor is releasing not just the tests but the results of the tests,\u8221\'20\'1D Cassidy said.\par \par \uc2 And with that, there is a transparency that allows people to move beyond a number \u8211\'20\'13 how old is the person \u8211\'20\'13 into \u8216\'20\'18What is actually the kind of science, if you will, the medical science, of how to evaluate?\u8217\'20\'19 And I think that should be the standard that folks are held to, and I think he\u8217\'20\'19s responded.\par \par \uc2 Asked if he believed he had received enough information from McConnell, Cassidy said:\par \par \uc2 I do. The doctor is not lying.\par \par \uc2 Cassidy urged \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  to also release similar records, calling on the president to \u8220\'20\'1Cdo what Mitch just did\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Shouldn\u8217\'20\'19t President Biden, for example, release a full kind of neurologic evaluation of his cognitive ability and whomever else?\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.56pm BST\par \par \uc2 Republican senator says top federal officials should disclose medical records\par \par \uc2 Congress should have a rule requiring certain top federal officials to disclose medical records, the Republican senator \uc2 Bill Cassidy\uc2  said on Sunday.\par \par \uc2 Speaking on NBC\u8217\'20\'19s Meet the Press, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/aug/21/bill-cassidy-trump-drop-out-2024"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Cassidy}}}\uc2  \u8211\'20\'13 a gastroenterologist who was elected as a US senator for Louisiana in 2008 \u8211\'20\'13 said that it \u8220\'20\'1Cshould certainly be a House rule\u8221\'20\'1D for elected officials to disclose their medical records.\par \par \uc2 I think if you want to be the president of the United States, or a senator or House member, then there is a responsibility over and above that of just offering yourself. It has to be that you can show that you have clarity.\par \par \uc2 On his last show hosting Meet the Press, Chuck Todd went on to ask Cassidy whether it would be a good idea to standardize both the disclosure of tax returns and medical records. Cassidy replied:\par \par \uc2 Actually, I think that would be reasonable, too. Because if the voter is going to make a decision, we need to give her as much information as we possibly can.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.57pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.47pm BST\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 , in Hanoi earlier today, visited a memorial for his late friend and senator, \uc2 John McCain\uc2 , who was a prisoner of war during the Vietnam war.\par \par \uc2 Before departing Vietnam to return to the US, the president visited the \uc2 John Sidney McCain III\uc2  memorial near the site where a 31-year-old McCain was shot down and captured in 1967.\par \par \uc2 The harrowing incident began a more than five-year ordeal that became the defining moment for the future Republican senator from Arizona and two-time presidential candidate, according to AP.\par \par \uc2 enltrEarlier today, President Biden paid his respects to his friend \uc2 John McCain\uc2  at his memorial in Hanoi, Vietnam.\par \par \uc2 McCain was a POW in Hanoi during the Vietnam War from 1967 to 1973. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/Mps4mgSIWv"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/Mps4mgSIWv}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 The Recount (@therecount) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/therecount/status/1701212780047528218?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 September 11, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.30pm BST\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s national security tour of south-east Asia reached Hanoi, Vietnam, on Sunday, where the president {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/sep/10/joe-biden-south-east-asia-tour-us-china-relationship"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 called for stability}}}\uc2  in the US-China relationship against an increasingly complex diplomatic picture in the region for his country.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI don\u8217\'20\'19t want to contain China,\u8221\'20\'1D Biden said.\par \par \uc2 I just want to make sure that we have a relationship with China that is on the up and up, squared away, everybody knows what it\u8217\'20\'19s all about.\par \par \uc2 Biden also said that China\u8217\'20\'19s recent economic downturn may limit any inclination to invade Taiwan. He added that the country\u8217\'20\'19s economic woes had left President Xi Jinping with \u8220\'20\'1Chis hands full right now\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 The president\u8217\'20\'19s remarks came after a meeting with \uc2 Nguyen Phu Trong\uc2 , the general secretary of Vietnam\u8217\'20\'19s ruling Communist party, in the nation\u8217\'20\'19s capital designed to secure global supply chains of semiconductors and critical minerals, which would offer a strategic alternative to China.\par \par \uc2 The meeting came during a multi-front diplomatic push to shore up international support for Ukrainian resistance to Russia\u8217\'20\'19s invasion and enunciate a policy toward China that both encourages trade and reduces the potential for US-Chinese conflict.\par \par \uc2 President \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  attends a welcoming ceremony hosted by Vietnam\u8217\'20\'19s Communist party general secretary \uc2 Nguyen Phu Trong\uc2  at the Presidential Palace of Vietnam in Hanoi on Sunday. Photograph: VTV24/UPI/\uc2 Shutterstock\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/sep/10/joe-biden-south-east-asia-tour-us-china-relationship"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Joe Biden calls for stable US-China relationship during south-east Asia tour}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 5.19pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.19pm BST\par \par \uc2 \u8216\'20\'18Perfect storm\u8217\'20\'19 brewing in House over impeachment and spending, says GOP congressman\par \par \uc2 Ken Buck\uc2 , a Colorado Republican congressman, said on Sunday that there was a \u8220\'20\'1Cperfect storm\u8221\'20\'1D brewing in the House that could pose a threat to Kevin McCarthy \u8217\'20\'19s speakership.\par \par \uc2 In an interview with MSNBC\u8217\'20\'19s \uc2 Jen Psaki\uc2 , Buck said:\par \par \uc2 On the one hand, we\u8217\'20\'19ve got to pass a continuing resolution. We also have the impeachment issue. And we also have members of the House, led by my good friend, Chip Roy, who are concerned about policy issues. They want riders in the appropriations bills, amendments in the appropriations bills that guarantee some type of security on our Southern border.\par \par \uc2 McCarthy has \u8220\'20\'1Cmade promises\u8221\'20\'1D on those issues to different groups \u8220\'20\'1Cand now it is all coming due at the same time\u8221\'20\'1D, Buck said.\par \par \uc2 He added that the GOP\u8217\'20\'19s focus should be on issues like border security, crime and inflation, and warned against aggressively pursuing an impeachment inquiry of \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 . He added:\par \par \uc2 There is not a strong connection at this point between the evidence on \uc2 Hunter Biden\uc2  and any evidence connecting the president.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 4.15pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.06pm BST\par \par \uc2 In early May, \uc2 James Comer\uc2  and Senator \uc2 Chuck Grassley\uc2 , investigating \uc2 Hunter Biden\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s work for the Ukrainian energy company \uc2 Burisma\uc2 , {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://oversight.house.gov/release/grassley-comer-demand-fbi-record-alleging-criminal-scheme-involving-then-vp-biden/#:~:text=today%20are%20demanding%20the%20FBI,of%20money%20for%20policy%20decisions."}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 published an open letter}}}\uc2  to the \uc2 FBI\uc2  announcing subpoenas for an unclassified document supposedly describing an alleged \u8220\'20\'1Ccriminal scheme involving then-Vice President Biden and a foreign national relating to the exchange of money for policy decisions\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 But when Comer and Grassley obtained the document, form FD-1023, and publicly released a redacted version \u8211\'20\'13 against the advice of intelligence officials who feared it would \u8220\'20\'1Cunnecessarily risks the safety of a confidential source\u8221\'20\'1D \u8211\'20\'13 it turned out to be an uncorroborated \uc2 FBI\uc2  tip.\par \par \uc2 Also in May, \uc2 Comer\uc2  published a bank memo attacking Biden for his alleged foreign business ties but even the conservative Fox News network was unimpressed. Host Steve Doocy {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://sports.yahoo.com/fox-news-host-trashes-house-180135095.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 challenged Comer}}}\uc2  :\par \par \uc2 That\u8217\'20\'19s just your suggestion. You don\u8217\'20\'19t actually have any facts to that point. You\u8217\'20\'19ve got some circumstantial evidence. And the other thing is, of all those names, the one person who didn\u8217\'20\'19t profit is that \u8211\'20\'13 there\u8217\'20\'19s no evidence that \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  did anything illegally.\par \par \uc2 enltrFox & Friends host Steve Doocy brutally confronts Republican Congressman \uc2 James Comer\uc2  over his \u8220\'20\'1CBiden crime family\u8221\'20\'1D allegations: \u8220\'20\'1CYou don\u8217\'20\'19t actually have any facts...there\u8217\'20\'19s no evidence that \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  did anything illegally.\u8221\'20\'1D {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/FOLtFnvrlA"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/FOLtFnvrlA}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Republicans against Trump (@RpsAgainstTrump) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/RpsAgainstTrump/status/1656741216216571904?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 May 11, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 In June, \uc2 Comer\uc2  and Grassley began {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.grassley.senate.gov/news/remarks/grassley-fbi-redacted-references-to-recordings-in-biden-allegation-shared-with-congress"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 touting potential audio tapes}}}\uc2  supposedly proving that Biden accepted a $5m bribe from a Ukrainian energy company during the Barack \uc2 Obama\uc2  administration. But during a \uc2 Newsmax\uc2  interview just five days later, Comer admitted:\par \par \uc2 We don\u8217\'20\'19t know if they are legit or not.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.55pm BST\par \par \uc2 The threat of an abrupt ouster hovers over Kevin McCarthy \u8217\'20\'19s every move, as the speaker takes on an unusual and politically fraught undertaking of running a government funding process alongside an impeachment drive, AP {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://apnews.com/article/mccarthy-speaker-biden-impeachment-republicans-shutdown-4d8c314763252429a6f87e7d13ad2b43"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 writes}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 McCarthy has signaled an impeachment inquiry is coming but there is \u8220\'20\'1Cno date circled on the calendar\u8221\'20\'1D, according to a source.\par \par \uc2 Congress also has a pending request from the White House to provide an additional $40bn on three fronts \u8211\'20\'13 some $21bn in military and humanitarian relief for Ukraine as it battles the Russian invasion; $12bn to replenish federal disaster aids after floods, fires and other problems, including to curb the flow of deadly fentanyl at the southern US border with Mexico.\par \par \uc2 McCarthy has vowed there won\u8217\'20\'19t be any \u8220\'20\'1Cblank check\u8221\'20\'1D for Ukraine as he works to appease skeptical Republicans who want to end US involvement in overseas affairs, particularly involving Russia.\par \par \uc2 While the shutdown is the more pressing problem for McCarthy, the Biden impeachment inquiry is his bigger political gamble.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.34pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.47pm BST\par \par \uc2 Biden impeachment inquiry \u8216\'20\'18eight months of abject failure\u8217\'20\'19 \u8211\'20\'13 watchdog report\par \par \uc2 The man leading the Republican charge for an impeachment inquiry into \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  has endured \u8220\'20\'1Ceight months of abject failure\u8221\'20\'1D in trying to prove the US president guilty of wrongdoing, a watchdog report says.\par \par \uc2 James Comer\uc2 , the ambitious chairman of the House of Representatives\u8217\'20\'19 oversight committee, has repeatedly overhyped allegations of bribery and corruption against Biden without once producing hard evidence, according to the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://congressionalintegrity.org/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Congressional Integrity Project}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The lack of a case underlines the huge political risks facing House Republicans when they return to Capitol Hill on Tuesday. Some are threatening to force a government shutdown unless an impeachment inquiry is opened despite {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.axios.com/newsletters/axios-sneak-peek-d20b0734-69b3-4bfa-8795-99d4dc1717d8.html?chunk=0&utm_term=emshare#story0"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 objections from wary Republican colleagues}}}\uc2  in the Senate.\par \par \uc2 Comer has been {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/may/15/joe-biden-compromised-house-committee-whistleblower"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 leading an aggressive investigation}}}\uc2  into unsubstantiated claims that Biden was involved in his son \uc2 Hunter Biden\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s foreign business affairs during his time as vice-president. A CNN/SSRS poll this week found that 61% of Americans believe that Biden did play such a role, including 42% who think he acted illegally. But establishing the link between father and son has proved an elusive holy grail.\par \par \uc2 The report says:\par \par \uc2 After months of political stunts, dozens of hearings, transcribed interviews, and memos, and despite hours on Fox peddling conspiracy theories, Comer and his Maga crew have failed to find a single shred of evidence linking President Biden to any of their lurid accusations.\par \par \uc2 In fact, Republicans have been forced to walk back claim after claim.\par \par \uc2 The report offers an anatomy of a fake scandal, detailing a series of exaggerated assertions that have shriveled under scrutiny. They include Comer saying at his first press conference that he had evidence of \u8220\'20\'1Cfederal crimes committed\u8221\'20\'1D, relentlessly invoking \u8220\'20\'1Cdeep state\u8221\'20\'1D conspiracy theories and claiming that his whistleblowers \u8220\'20\'1Cfear for their lives\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 For months, the report says, \uc2 Comer\uc2  talked to the media about four individuals he claimed were \u8220\'20\'1Cwhistleblowers\u8221\'20\'1D, a term increasingly hijacked by the right. It adds:\par \par \uc2 Problem is \u8211\'20\'13 they weren\u8217\'20\'19t whistleblowers and there were only two people.\par \par \uc2 James Comer\uc2  has raised a substantial amount of money for his campaign coffers, yet offered no hard evidence of corruption on \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s part. Photograph: \uc2 Shutterstock\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.47pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.39pm BST\par \par \uc2 House freedom caucus member \uc2 Matt Rosendale{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.politico.com/news/2023/09/11/kevin-mccarthy-government-shutdown-profile-00114028?nname=playbook&nid=0000014f-1646-d88f-a1cf-5f46b7bd0000&nrid=d66b2db2-0400-407f-afcc-3b1d45707d8e&nlid=630318"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 told}}}\uc2  Politico he was displeased when the speaker, Kevin McCarthy, suggested a government shutdown would make it more difficult for Republicans to pursue an impeachment inquiry against \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Rosendale:\par \par \uc2 He\u8217\'20\'19s trying to intimidate us... It\u8217\'20\'19s called a distraction. And guess what? I will not be intimidated by such distractions.\par \par \uc2 If the speaker chooses a stopgap funding deal with help from Democrats, \u8220\'20\'1Cit would be very costly to him... it basically completely undermines his credibility\u8221\'20\'1D, Rosendale added.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.29pm BST\par \par \uc2 House Republicans are barreling toward an existential clash over this month\u8217\'20\'19s government funding talks, as Kevin McCarthy faces the greatest peril to his speakership since he began his role eight months ago, according to a Politico {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.politico.com/news/2023/09/11/kevin-mccarthy-government-shutdown-profile-00114028?nname=playbook&nid=0000014f-1646-d88f-a1cf-5f46b7bd0000&nrid=d66b2db2-0400-407f-afcc-3b1d45707d8e&nlid=630318"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 report.}}}\par \par \uc2 The report, based on interviews with GOP members and aides, writes that it would only take a few defectors to send the Republican party spiraling into a new period of chaos.\par \par \uc2 The last time a GOP speaker faced this intense level of fall spending pressure with a Democrat in the White House, it was September 2015. And while \uc2 John Boehner\uc2  avoided a shutdown, he didn\u8217\'20\'19t survive the month.\par \par \uc2 McCarthy has built a deeper well of goodwill with the right than Boehner ever did. Still, the Californian has other headaches too, from a party bitterly divided on Ukraine aid to the dicey politics of pushing his centrists into a Biden impeachment inquiry that many are leery of. And he\u8217\'20\'19s navigating a significantly smaller majority than his Ohio predecessor.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.13pm BST\par \par \uc2 Hard-right Republicans demand impeachment inquiry against Biden to avert government shutdown\par \par \uc2 Members of the House freedom caucus, who abhor the idea of extending funding at levels previously approved by a Democratic Congress, have already outlined a litany of demands in exchange for their support on a continuing resolution.\par \par \uc2 In a statement released late last month, the caucus said its members would only back a continuing resolution if it included a Republican proposal on border security and addressed \u8220\'20\'1Cthe unprecedented weaponization of the justice department and \uc2 FBI\uc2 \u8221\'20\'1D, an implicit reference to the four criminal cases against \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The caucus also demanded an end to the so-called \u8220\'20\'1Cwoke\u8221\'20\'1D policies at the department of defense, which has faced rightwing criticism for providing funding to servicemembers and their family members who need to travel to access \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  care.\par \par \uc2 Hard-right Republicans have now added another item to their list of demands: the launch of an impeachment inquiry against \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 . \uc2 Marjorie Taylor Greene\uc2 , a far-right Republican congresswoman from Georgia, said last week:\par \par \uc2 I\u8217\'20\'19ve already decided I will not vote to fund the government unless we have passed an impeachment inquiry on \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Another hard-right House member, \uc2 Matt Gaetz\uc2  of Florida, has warned that McCarthy\u8217\'20\'19s failure to act on impeaching Biden could cost him his speakership. \u8220\'20\'1CI worked very hard in January to develop a toolkit for House Republicans to use in a productive and positive way. I don\u8217\'20\'19t believe we\u8217\'20\'19ve used those tools as effectively as we should have,\u8221\'20\'1D Gaetz said on Tuesday.\par \par \uc2 We\u8217\'20\'19ve got to seize the initiative. That means forcing votes on impeachment. And if Speaker McCarthy stands in our way, he may not have the job long.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.06pm BST\par \par \uc2 The trouble for Kevin McCarthy started in the spring, after the House passed the compromise debt ceiling bill, known as the Fiscal Responsibility Act.\par \par \uc2 Seventy-one members of the House Republican conference opposed the legislation over concerns that it did not go far enough to reduce government spending, and they sharply criticized McCarthy for agreeing to the inadequate deal.\par \par \uc2 Gordon Gray, vice-president for economic policy at the center-right thinktank American Action Forum, said he had been bracing for a potential shutdown ever since the debt ceiling showdown concluded.\par \par \uc2 Since the debt limit grenade was diffused, there\u8217\'20\'19s a big chunk of House Republicans who just want to break something. That\u8217\'20\'19s just how some of these folks define governing. It\u8217\'20\'19s how their constituents define success.\par \par \uc2 Now House Republicans have reneged on the debt ceiling deal, instead choosing to advance appropriations bills with spending levels below those agreed to in the Fiscal Responsibility Act. Democrats warn that the proposed cuts could deal a devastating financial blow to early education programs, climate initiatives and housing assistance.\par \par \uc2 House Republicans\u8217\'20\'19 strategy in the spending talks has been met with exasperation in the Senate, which returned from its recess on Tuesday. Before the upper chamber adjourned at the end of July, the Senate appropriations committee advanced all 12 spending bills for fiscal year 2024 with bipartisan support.\par \par \uc2 The Democratic Senate majority leader, \uc2 Chuck Schumer\uc2 , has implored the House to take a similar approach to the budget process. Even the Senate Republican leader, \uc2 Mitch McConnell\uc2 , {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/sep/10/kevin-mccarthy-government-shutdown-far-right-republicans"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 offered a mild rebuke }}}\uc2  of his colleagues in the House when asked about the spending fight last week.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.58pm BST\par \par \uc2 US government\uc2  shutdown and Biden impeachment inquiry threats loom over House\u8217\'20\'19s return\par \par \uc2 Good morning, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/us-politics"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 US politics}}}\uc2  blog readers. The House returns from its summer recess this week, as the speaker, Kevin McCarthy faces a collision course of difficult challenges \u8211\'20\'13 avoiding a costly government shutdown, and addressing growing calls on the right to launch an impeachment inquiry into \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 With just 12 legislative days left before the end of the fiscal year, the Republican-controlled House must quickly pass some kind of spending package to keep the federal government open after 30 September. If it does not, the government will shut down for the first time in nearly five years, furloughing federal employees and stalling many crucial programs.\par \par \uc2 McCarthy has indicated his preference to pass a continuing resolution, but members of the hard-right House freedom caucus insist they will not back a continuing resolution unless the speaker agrees to several significant policy concessions, such as increased border security and an impeachment inquiry into Biden over the business dealings of the president\u8217\'20\'19s son, \uc2 Hunter Biden\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Given House Republicans\u8217\'20\'19 narrow majority and a new rule allowing any single member of the chamber to force a vote on removing the speaker, McCarthy\u8217\'20\'19s handling of this fraught situation could determine whether he loses his gavel after just eight months in power.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s what else we\u8217\'20\'19re watching today:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  has departed Hanoi, Vietnam for Anchorage, Alaska, where upon arrival he will deliver remarks to service members, first responders, and their families on the anniversary of 9/11.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The Senate will meet at 3pm ET to take up Tanya Bradsher\u8217\'20\'19s nomination as deputy veterans affairs secretary, with a cloture vote at 5.30pm.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The House is out.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020230911ej9b001b9\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
