\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Mark Meadows\uc2  loses bid to transfer Georgia election interference case to federal court \u8211\'20\'13 as it happened\b0\par\par\uc2 L\u233\'00\'E9onie Chao-Fong (now) and Chris Stein (US politics live blogger) \par \uc2 8,008 \uc2 words\par \uc2 8 September 2023\par 22:16 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Meadows faces two felony charges, including racketeering and solicitation of a violation of oath by a public officer\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.00pm BST\par \par \uc2 Closing summary\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s a recap of today\u8217\'20\'19s developments:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 A special purpose grand jury in Georgia that investigated \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/sep/07/donald-trump-georgia-election-charges-federal-court"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 efforts to overturn the 2020 election}}}\uc2  for nearly two years recommended bringing criminal charges against {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/sep/08/georgia-report-indictment-trump-expected-unsealed-biden-modi-g20-latest-news?page=with:block-64fb90f28f08addfe922406a#block-64fb90f28f08addfe922406a"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 21 people who ultimately were not charged, }}}\uc2  including the US senator \uc2 Lindsey Graham\uc2 , former senators \uc2 David Perdue\uc2  and Kelly Loeffler, as well as the influential conservative figure Cleta Mitchell.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Senator Graham said he {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/sep/08/georgia-report-indictment-trump-expected-unsealed-biden-modi-g20-latest-news?filterKeyEvents=false&page=with:block-64fb54e38f08b298ac2fb554#block-64fb54e38f08b298ac2fb554"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 was \u8220\'20\'1Ctotally surprised\u8221\'20\'1D}}}\uc2  to learn that a special grand jury {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/sep/08/georgia-report-indictment-trump-expected-unsealed-biden-modi-g20-latest-news?page=with:block-64fb2d518f08b298ac2fb230#block-64fb2d518f08b298ac2fb230"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 recommended he face charges}}}\uc2  in the Georgia election subversion case. Speaking after the special purpose grand jury\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/sep/08/lindsey-graham-criminal-charges-georgia-jury"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 final report was unsealed, }}}\uc2  Graham {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/sep/08/georgia-report-indictment-trump-expected-unsealed-biden-modi-g20-latest-news?page=with:block-64fb63728f08addfe9223e94#block-64fb63728f08addfe9223e94"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 defended his actions }}}\uc2  which he said were \u8220\'20\'1Cconsistent\u8221\'20\'1D with his job as a US senator.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Mark Meadows\uc2 , the former White House chief of staff, has {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/sep/08/georgia-report-indictment-trump-expected-unsealed-biden-modi-g20-latest-news?page=with:block-64fb95c48f08b298ac2fb7a6#block-64fb95c48f08b298ac2fb7a6"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 lost his bid}}}\uc2  to move his Georgia election interference case from state to federal court, according to a court filing. Meadows faces two felony charges, including racketeering and solicitation of a violation of oath by a public officer.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Former House of Representatives speaker Nancy Pelosi{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/sep/08/georgia-report-indictment-trump-expected-unsealed-biden-modi-g20-latest-news?page=with:block-64fb46178f08addfe9223cdf#block-64fb46178f08addfe9223cdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 announced that}}}\uc2  she will be seeking re-election in 2024. The 83-year-old Democrat\u8217\'20\'19s announcement comes amid several politically delicate moments on Capitol Hill, particularly as Democrats prepare to take back control of the House of Representatives.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The trial in the New York attorney general Letitia James\u8217\'20\'19 $250m civil fraud case against \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  and his family business {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/sep/08/georgia-report-indictment-trump-expected-unsealed-biden-modi-g20-latest-news?page=with:block-64fb8b0c8f08addfe9224046#block-64fb8b0c8f08addfe9224046"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 will last nearly three months,}}}\uc2  the judge presiding over the case said. Trump overstated his net worth {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/sep/08/georgia-report-indictment-trump-expected-unsealed-biden-modi-g20-latest-news?page=with:block-64fb67c18f08e39cdeca471a#block-64fb67c18f08e39cdeca471a"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 by as much as $3.6bn}}}\uc2  between 2011 and 2021, James said in a court filing on Friday.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Supreme court justice Samuel Alito{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/sep/08/georgia-report-indictment-trump-expected-unsealed-biden-modi-g20-latest-news?page=with:block-64fb81738f08addfe9223fde#block-64fb81738f08addfe9223fde"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 rejected calls}}}\uc2  by Senate Democrats to have him {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/aug/25/us-thinktank-billionaires-supreme-court-wealth-tax-lobbying"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 recuse from a tax case}}}\uc2  that involves an attorney who interviewed him for a newspaper article and helped him \u8220\'20\'1Cair his personal grievances\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 A federal appeals court stopped {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/sep/06/texas-buoys-rio-grande-migrants-mexico-border"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a lower court order}}}\uc2  that required Texas to remove a line of floating buoys that were placed in the middle of the Rio Grande to block migrants from crossing the US-Mexico border. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/sep/08/georgia-report-indictment-trump-expected-unsealed-biden-modi-g20-latest-news?page=with:block-64fb76f28f08e39cdeca47c7#block-64fb76f28f08e39cdeca47c7"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  The temporary stay}}}\uc2  puts on hold a ruling that would have required Texas to relocate the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/aug/04/like-traps-meant-for-animals-death-no-deterrent-at-the-rio-grande-river-barrier"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 controversial buoys}}}\uc2 , currently near the city of Eagle Pass, to an embankment on the Texas side of the river.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.56pm BST\par \par \uc2 US district judge Steve C Jones, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/sep/08/georgia-report-indictment-trump-expected-unsealed-biden-modi-g20-latest-news?page=with:block-64fb95c48f08b298ac2fb7a6#block-64fb95c48f08b298ac2fb7a6"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 rejecting}}}\uc2 Mark Meadows\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19 bid to move his Georgia election interference case to federal court, wrote:\par \par \uc2 This Order addresses a relatively narrow question: Has Meadows carried his burden of demonstrating that removal of the State of Georgia\u8217\'20\'19s criminal prosecution against him is proper under the federal officer removal statute, 28 U.S.C. \u167\'00\'A7 1442(a)?\par \par \uc2 Having considered the arguments and evidence, the Court concludes that Meadows has not met his burden.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 11.12pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.46pm BST\par \par \uc2 Judge rejects \uc2 Mark Meadows\uc2 ' bid to move Georgia election case to federal court\par \par \uc2 Mark Meadows\uc2 , the former White House chief of staff, has lost his bid to move his Georgia election interference case from state to federal court, according to a court filing.\par \par \uc2 Meadows faces two felony charges, including racketeering and solicitation of a violation of oath by a public officer. But he has argued that he acted in his capacity as a federal officer and thus is entitled to immunity \u8211\'20\'13 and that his case should be heard before a federal judge.\par \par \uc2 Meadows swiftly filed a motion to move his case to the federal US district court of northern Georgia after \uc2 Fani Willis\uc2 , the Fulton county district attorney, handed down her indictment last month.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.33pm BST\par \par \uc2 Georgia report reveals jury called for criminal charges against 39 people: who are they?\par \par \uc2 A special purpose grand jury in Georgia that investigated \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/sep/07/donald-trump-georgia-election-charges-federal-court"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 efforts to overturn the 2020 election}}}\uc2  for nearly two years recommended bringing criminal charges against 39 people in total.\par \par \uc2 Only 19 people were ultimately charged last month in Fulton county district attorney \uc2 Fani Willis\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19 indictment. They are:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Mark Meadows\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Rudy Giuliani\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 John Eastman\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Kenneth Chesebro\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Jeffrey Clark\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Jenna Ellis\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Sidney Powell\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Ray Smith\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Robert Cheeley\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 David Shafer\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Shawn Still\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Misty Hampton\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Cathy Latham\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Scott Hall\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Stephen Lee\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Trevian Kutti\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Harrison Floyd\par \par \uc2 In addition, Trump campaign official Mike Roman, who was not mentioned in the special grand jury report, was also charged.\par \par \uc2 The 21 people who the special purpose grand jury also recommended indicting but were not charged are:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 David Perdue\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Lindsey Graham\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Kelly Loeffler\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Cleta Mitchell\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Michael Flynn\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Boris Epshteyn\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Jacki Pick\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Burt Jones\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Lin Wood\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 William Ligon\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Kurt Hilbert\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Alex Kaufman\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Joseph Brannan\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Vikki Consiglio\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Carolyn Fisher\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Gloria Godwin\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Mark Hennessy\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Mark Hennessy\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 John Downey\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Brad Carver\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 CB Yadav\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.06pm BST\par \par \uc2 Trump civil fraud trial expected to take three months, says judge\par \par \uc2 The trial in the New York attorney general Letitia James\u8217\'20\'19 $250m civil fraud case against \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  and his family business will last nearly three months, the judge presiding over the case said.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe trial is scheduled to begin on October 2, 2023 and to end by December 22, 2023,\u8221\'20\'1D judge Arthur F Engoron wrote in an order on Friday.\par \par \uc2 In the civil fraud suit, James is suing Trump, his adult sons, \uc2 Donald Trump Jr\uc2  and \uc2 Eric Trump\uc2  and the \uc2 Trump Organization\uc2  alleging they had overstated their worth by billions in financial statements to banks and insurers. Trump\u8217\'20\'19s net worth was exaggerated by between $1.9bn and $3.6bn, James {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/sep/08/trump-net-worth-new-york-attorney-general"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 wrote in a filing.}}}\par \par \uc2 Earlier this week, Judge Engoron denied a Trump attempt to delay the trial which he {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cnbc.com/2023/09/06/trump-bid-to-delay-250-million-new-york-fraud-case-is-completely-without-merit-judge-says.html?recirc=taboolainternal&recirc=taboolainternal"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 said}}}\uc2  was \u8220\'20\'1Ccompletely without merit\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 10.08pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.52pm BST\par \par \uc2 Indicting US senators could have raised constitutional questions, said Anthony Michael Kreis, a law professor at \uc2 Georgia State University\uc2 . He wrote in an email:\par \par \uc2 Some of the legislators have constitutional immunity issues where they can\u8217\'20\'19t be tried for actions they took in their capacity as lawmakers. So, jurors might understandably think something they did was fishy but it doesn\u8217\'20\'19t rise to anything prosecutable.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CA second issue might be immunity deals or other cooperation negotiations that may have foreclosed an indictment,\u8221\'20\'1D he added.\par \par \uc2 And a third is practical: is there insufficient evidence or would indicting a 20th or 21st co-conspirator unnecessarily burden an efficient prosecution for little benefit in the interest of justice? Prosecutors always must use their discretion because resources and political capital are finite.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.39pm BST\par \par \uc2 J Tom Morgan, the former district attorney in DeKalb county, which neighbors Fulton county, said that in nearly 40 years of practicing law, he had never seen a grand jury report {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/sep/08/georgia-report-indictment-trump-expected-unsealed-biden-modi-g20-latest-news?filterKeyEvents=false&page=with:block-64fb2d518f08b298ac2fb230#block-64fb2d518f08b298ac2fb230"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 publicly released that recommended charges}}}\uc2  without an accompanying indictment.\par \par \uc2 He said in an interview:\par \par \uc2 It kind of puts the DA in a bind that she now has to justify why these people were not indicted. Could there be special plea deals or negotiations between some of these people that she\u8217\'20\'19s not ready to reveal?\par \par \uc2 Ultimately, it\u8217\'20\'19s her decision and her decision alone whether to go forward with any or all of those recommendations.\par \par \uc2 He added that he believes the names of those who were not ultimately indicted should have been redacted.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19m not commenting on whether or not these people should be indicted. That\u8217\'20\'19s for the DA to decide. But what you\u8217\'20\'19ve got is a report naming all these people who should be indicted and now they\u8217\'20\'19re not indicted and they have no way to defend themselves,\u8221\'20\'1D he added\par \par \uc2 You\u8217\'20\'19ve got a grand jury saying, \u8216\'20\'18Hey these people committed crimes. But since they\u8217\'20\'19re not indicted, they don\u8217\'20\'19t have a chance to prove their innocence in a court of law.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.20pm BST\par \par \uc2 Supreme court justice \uc2 Samuel Alito\uc2  rejected calls by Senate Democrats to have him {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/aug/25/us-thinktank-billionaires-supreme-court-wealth-tax-lobbying"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 recuse from a tax case}}}\uc2  that involves an attorney who interviewed him for a newspaper article and helped him \u8220\'20\'1Cair his personal grievances\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Alito, in a statement attached to a routine order issued by the court in the case, Moore v United States, said, \u8220\'20\'1CThere is no valid reason for my recusal in this case.\u8221\'20\'1D Individual justices make recusal decisions for themselves.\par \par \uc2 The Senate judiciary committee chairman, \uc2 Dick Durbin\uc2 , and nine other Democrats on the panel on 3 August sent a letter to Chief Justice \uc2 John Roberts\uc2  asking him to ensure Alito recuses in the case involving plaintiffs Charles and Kathleen Moore. One of the Moores\u8217\'20\'19 attorneys, David Rivkin Jr, helped interview Alito for articles that appeared in the Wall Street Journal\u8217\'20\'19s opinion section \u8211\'20\'13 including on 28 July when he said Congress lacks the power to regulate the court.\par \par \uc2 The senators stated:\par \par \uc2 Mr Rivkin\u8217\'20\'19s access to Justice Alito and efforts to help Justice Alito air his personal grievances could cast doubt on Justice Alito\u8217\'20\'19s ability to fairly discharge his duties in a case in which Mr Rivkin represents one of the parties.\par \par \uc2 Alito, one of six conservative justices on the court, said in his statement:\par \par \uc2 When Mr Rivkin participated in the interviews and co-authored the articles, he did so as a journalist, not an advocate. The case in which he is involved was never mentioned; nor did we discuss any issue in that case either directly or indirectly.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe have no control over the attorneys whom parties select to represent them,\u8221\'20\'1D he added.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/law/2023/sep/08/samuel-alito-supreme-court-recusal-tax-case"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Samuel Alito refuses to recuse himself from tax case before supreme court}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 10.09pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.56pm BST\par \par \uc2 Ex-Georgia senator Loeffler says 'no apologies' after report reveals grand jurors voted for her indictment\par \par \uc2 Georgia\u8217\'20\'19s Republican former senator Kelly Loeffler decried \u8220\'20\'1Ca two-tiered system of justice\u8221\'20\'1D after the special grand jury report released today showed a majority of those on the panel believed she should face charges for her involvement in \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s efforts to meddle in the state\u8217\'20\'19s elections three years ago.\par \par \uc2 According to the report, jurors believed the Loeffler broke the law over \u8220\'20\'1Cthe national effort to overturn the 2020 presidential election\u8221\'20\'1D, but the vote was somewhat close: 14 jurors thought she should face charges, six disagreed, and one abstained. The former senator was ultimately not among the 19 people Fulton county district attorney \uc2 Fani Willis\uc2  brought charges against last month.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s the statement from Loeffler, a close ally of Trump during her brief stint in the Senate, which ended after Georgia voters replaced her with Democrat \uc2 Raphael Warnock\uc2  the day before the January 6 insurrection:\par \par \uc2 enltrMy statement: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/vkVnV83g77"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/vkVnV83g77}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Kelly Loeffler (@KLoeffler) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/KLoeffler/status/1700228761805844627?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 September 8, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 Loeffler was also the co-owner of the Atlanta Dream WNBA, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/sport/2021/jan/06/wnba-kelly-loeffler-raphael-warnock"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 whose players actively campaigned for Warnock\u8217\'20\'19s victory}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 8.59pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.39pm BST\par \par \uc2 A federal appeals court stopped {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/sep/06/texas-buoys-rio-grande-migrants-mexico-border"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a lower court order}}}\uc2  that required Texas to remove a line of floating buoys that were placed in the middle of the Rio Grande to block migrants from crossing the US-Mexico border.\par \par \uc2 The temporary stay issued by the fifth circuit court of appeals puts on hold a ruling that would have required Texas to relocate the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/aug/04/like-traps-meant-for-animals-death-no-deterrent-at-the-rio-grande-river-barrier"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 controversial buoys}}}\uc2 , currently near the city of Eagle Pass, to an embankment on the Texas side of the river.\par \par \uc2 The Wednesday ruling by federal judge David Ezra had marked a tentative win for the Biden administration after the justice department sued the state. The Biden administration had argued in a legal challenge that the barrier illegally disrupts navigation and was installed without necessary permission from the US army corps of engineers.\par \par \uc2 The stay granted by the appeals court on Friday allows the barrier to remain in the water while the legal challenge continues.\par \par \uc2 A border patrol boat navigates alongside a string of buoys in the Rio Grande in Eagle Pass, Texas. Photograph: Suzanne Cordeiro/AFP/Getty Images\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 8.43pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.30pm BST\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  is seeking to move a Colorado lawsuit aimed at blocking his name from the 2024 presidential ballot in the state to federal court.\par \par \uc2 It comes after a watchdog group {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/sep/06/watchdog-group-sues-remove-trump-2024-election"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 earlier this week sued to remove Trump}}}\uc2  from the ballot, saying he violated the constitution and is disqualified from holding future office. The lawsuit claimed the former president violated section 3 of the 14th amendment, also known as the Disqualification Clause, with his involvement in the January 6 US Capitol attack.\par \par \uc2 In a response, lawyers for Trump argued the lawsuit relies on a federal law and therefore should be handled in federal court. The filing states:\par \par \uc2 This case arises under the 14th Amendment. Although Plaintiffs have drafted their Verified Petition in a manner that ostensibly relies on state claims, in fact every state claim \u8212\'20\'14 indeed every effort to bar Trump from running for President \u8212\'20\'14 relies solely on the application of U.S. Const. 14th Amend, Sec. 3.\par \par \uc2 The lawsuit by the watchdog group filed on Wednesday marks one of the strongest challenges to Trump\u8217\'20\'19s eligibility to seek re-election.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.03pm BST\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s allies are reportedly worrying over his lead in the key state of Iowa, and have called for a wake-up call for the former president\u8217\'20\'19s lagging operation as the stretch run to the Iowa caucuses begin.\par \par \uc2 Trump supporters are scrambling to fill roles in the campaign\u8217\'20\'19s Iowa operation with more experienced hires, as they prepare for months of battle against GOP presidential opponents who have built better machinery to find and secure votes, according to a NBC {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nbcnews.com/politics/2024-election/trump-allies-urge-wake-call-lagging-iowa-campaign-operation-rcna103556"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 report}}}\uc2 , which interviewed Trump campaign allies and state and local officials in Iowa.\par \par \uc2 One source claimed Trump\u8217\'20\'19s son, \uc2 Donald Trump Jr\uc2 , worried about a lack of experience on the campaign\u8217\'20\'19s Iowa team and said multiple times that they need \u8220\'20\'1Can adult in the room\u8221\'20\'1D in a phone call.\par \par \uc2 Trump Jr was concerned \u8220\'20\'1Cthat they were running from behind in getting things going, and that there was concern about that at the highest levels\u8221\'20\'1D, the report cited the source as saying.\par \par \uc2 A former Trump adviser in Iowa told the network the campaign\u8217\'20\'19s current efforts were cause for concern and may lead to problems down the line.\par \par \uc2 I know there\u8217\'20\'19s an operation. I\u8217\'20\'19m hearing that there\u8217\'20\'19s something going on. But it\u8217\'20\'19s hard to see it.\par \par \uc2 Trump holds significant and stable leads in the polls, both nationally and in key early-voting states, including Iowa. But his closest rival, Florida governor \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2 , has invested major resources and efforts in the state.\par \par \uc2 DeSantis has recruited organizing chairs in all 99 counties, which will be a force multiplier in the latter stages of the campaign, Iowa state senate president and DeSantis supporter, Amy Sinclair, told the report.\par \par \uc2 I think that former President Trump is not coming and mobilizing the people who support him. Will they even show up to a caucus? I think he\u8217\'20\'19s making a bad choice.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 8.17pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.44pm BST\par \par \uc2 Here are some images from the newswires of \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s visit to New Delhi, where he met with India\u8217\'20\'19s prime minister \uc2 Narendra Modi\uc2  after arriving in the capital today.\par \par \uc2 The two leaders held closed-door talks for nearly an hour at Modi\u8217\'20\'19s residence, Reuters reported.\par \par \uc2 Indian prime minister \uc2 Narendra Modi\uc2  receiving US President \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  in New Delhi. Photograph: Press Information Bureau Handout/EPA Biden watches a group of dancers with Vani Sarraju Rao, Joint Secretary in the Ministry of External Affairs, right, and Vijay Kumar Singh, Minister of State for Road Transport and Highways & Minister of State for Civil Aviation, at \uc2 Indira Gandhi International Airport\uc2 . Photograph: Evan Vucci/AP Biden and US delegates meet with Modi and Indian respresentatives in New Delhi, India. Photograph: India\u8217\'20\'19s PM Press Office/UPI/Shutterstock Biden with Modi ahead of the G20 summit. Photograph: India\u8217\'20\'19s PM Press Office/UPI/\uc2 Shutterstock\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.30pm BST\par \par \uc2 Trump overstated net worth by up to $3.6bn, says New York attorney general\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  overstated his net worth by as much as $3.6bn between 2011 and 2021, the attorney general of New York state said in a court filing \u8211\'20\'13 a $1.4bn increase on {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/aug/30/donald-trump-net-worth-inflated-2014-new-york-letitia-james"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a previous filing}}}\uc2  that put the top amount at $2.2bn.\par \par \uc2 In the new filing, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cnbc.com/2023/09/08/trump-overstated-net-worth-by-up-to-3point6-billion-per-year-ny-ag-alleges-in-new-filing.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 CNBC said}}}\uc2 , the attorney general, Letitia James, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cnbc.com/2023/09/08/trump-overstated-net-worth-by-up-to-3point6-billion-per-year-ny-ag-alleges-in-new-filing.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 said}}}\uc2  she was \u8220\'20\'1Cstill [making] a conservative estimate\u8221\'20\'1D about by how much Trump\u8217\'20\'19s net worth was overstated in annual financial statements.\par \par \uc2 Trump\u8217\'20\'19s net worth was exaggerated by between $1.9bn and $3.6bn, the filing said.\par \par \uc2 In the civil fraud suit, James is suing Trump, his adult sons, \uc2 Donald Trump Jr\uc2  and \uc2 Eric Trump\uc2 , and the \uc2 Trump Organization\uc2  for $250m. The state is also seeking stringent professional penalties. Trump\u8217\'20\'19s oldest daughter, \uc2 Ivanka Trump\uc2 , was dropped from the suit this year.\par \par \uc2 In the new filing on Friday, prosecutors said valuations experts arrived at the new figure for Trump\u8217\'20\'19s overestimations of his worth by applying financial methods \u8220\'20\'1Cmarket participants would consider when determining estimated current value\u8221\'20\'1D, ABC News {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://abcnews.go.com/Politics/trump-inflated-net-worth-36-billion-ny-attorney/story?id=103027458"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reported}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Prosecutors added:\par \par \uc2 After factoring in these and other fundamental considerations that any informed buyer and seller in the marketplace would take into account, Mr Trump\u8217\'20\'19s net worth would be further substantially reduced by between $1.9bn to $3.6bn per year, which is still a conservative estimate.\par \par \uc2 Denying wrongdoing, Trump claims political persecution by James, a Democrat. The trial is set to begin on 2 October.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 7.36pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.24pm BST\par \par \uc2 In a post on his Truth Social platform, \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  lashed out at the Fulton county district attorney, \uc2 Fani Willis\uc2 , after a Georgia grand jury report revealed it had recommended charges for several Trump allies, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/sep/08/georgia-report-indictment-trump-expected-unsealed-biden-modi-g20-latest-news?filterKeyEvents=false&page=with:block-64fb2d518f08b298ac2fb230#block-64fb2d518f08b298ac2fb230"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 including Senator Lindsey Graham.}}}\par \par \uc2 Trump wrote:\par \par \uc2 The Georgia Grand Jury report has just been released. It has ZERO credibility and badly taints \uc2 Fani Willis\uc2  and this whole political Witch Hunt. Essentially, they wanted to indict anybody who happened to be breathing at the time. It totally undermines the credibility of the findings, and badly hurts the Great State of Georgia, whose wonderful and patriotic people are not happy with this charade of an out of control \u8216\'20\'18prosecutor\u8217\'20\'19 doing the work of, and for, the DOJ. ELECTION INTERFERENCE!\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.17pm BST\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s more from South Carolina\u8217\'20\'19s Republican senator \uc2 Lindsey Graham\uc2 , who said he {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/sep/08/georgia-report-indictment-trump-expected-unsealed-biden-modi-g20-latest-news?filterKeyEvents=false&page=with:block-64fb54e38f08b298ac2fb554#block-64fb54e38f08b298ac2fb554"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 was \u8220\'20\'1Ctotally surprised\u8221\'20\'1D}}}\uc2  to learn that a special grand jury {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/sep/08/georgia-report-indictment-trump-expected-unsealed-biden-modi-g20-latest-news?page=with:block-64fb2d518f08b298ac2fb230#block-64fb2d518f08b298ac2fb230"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 recommended he face charges}}}\uc2  over the attempts by \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  and his allies to overturn Georgia\u8217\'20\'19s 2020 election result.\par \par \uc2 Speaking to reporters, Graham defended his actions which he said were \u8220\'20\'1Cconsistent\u8221\'20\'1D with his job as a US senator. He said:\par \par \uc2 This is troubling for the country. We can\u8217\'20\'19t criminalize senators doing their job when they have a constitutional requirement to do [\u8230\'20\'26] We\u8217\'20\'19re opening up Pandora\u8217\'20\'19s box here.\par \par \uc2 He added that he believed \u8220\'20\'1Cthe system in this country is getting off the rails. We have to be careful not to use the legal system as a political tool.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Graham said he continued to stand by Trump, who he described as being \u8220\'20\'1Ca handful at time, but I thought he was a good president\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 enltr\u8220\'20\'1CNothing happened. What I did was consistent with my job\u8230\'20\'26But it was just not me. 3 United States senators. We're opening up Pandora's Box.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Sen. \uc2 Lindsey Graham\uc2  (R-SC) reacts to a grand jury report that recommended he be charged for his role in Georgia election interference {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/AGoHPqgc9y"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/AGoHPqgc9y}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 The Recount (@therecount) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/therecount/status/1700200964395766181?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 September 8, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 7.17pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.00pm BST\par \par \uc2 While we\u8217\'20\'19re on {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/sep/08/georgia-report-indictment-trump-expected-unsealed-biden-modi-g20-latest-news?page=with:block-64fb5bf28f08addfe9223e3d#block-64fb5bf28f08addfe9223e3d"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the subject}}}\uc2  of \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2 , the Florida governor has reportedly been unhappy with a powerful operative at the center of his 2024 presidential effort.\par \par \uc2 DeSantis has privately complained about \uc2 Jeff Roe\uc2 , a lead strategist at his Super Pac Never Back Down, sources {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.washingtonpost.com/politics/2023/09/08/ron-desantis-super-pac-debate/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  told}}}\uc2  the \uc2 Washington Post\uc2  in a story published today.\par \par \uc2 The GOP presidential hopeful was also \u8220\'20\'1Capoplectic\u8221\'20\'1D after a pre-debate strategy memo {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/aug/17/ron-desantis-republican-debate-memos-presidential-campaign"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 was posted}}}\uc2  on a website of Roe\u8217\'20\'19s firm, \uc2 Axiom\uc2 , the report said. The memo, which was posted ahead of the first GOP primary debate last month, revealed DeSantis was advised to not attack \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  and to \u8220\'20\'1Ctake a sledgehammer\u8221\'20\'1D to \uc2 Vivek Ramaswamy\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The report goes on:\par \par \uc2 Top DeSantis aides have said they regret the extent of Roe\u8217\'20\'19s influence over DeSantis\u8217\'20\'19s 2024 operation, according to a person familiar with the comments, and several other people echoed that some campaign staff and donors have been upset with Roe, particularly after the debate memo and leaked recordings of a donor briefing by Roe and other super PAC officials held the day of the debate in Milwaukee.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.45pm BST\par \par \uc2 A Super Pac backing \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2  for the GOP presidential nomination used the Florida governor\u8217\'20\'19s controversial promise to leave suspected drug traffickers \u8220\'20\'1Cstone-cold dead\u8221\'20\'1D at the US-Mexico border in a new ad.\par \par \uc2 DeSantis has faced fierce criticism for using violent language about illegal immigration during his campaign, and in an August interview vowed \u8220\'20\'1Cto authorize the use of deadly force against the cartels\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 The new advert by DeSantis\u8217\'20\'19s Super Pac uses a clip from the Florida governor\u8217\'20\'19s talking points in which he discusses what his administration would do to suspected drug traffickers who cross the border:\par \par \uc2 We\u8217\'20\'19re going to use force and we\u8217\'20\'19re going to leave them stone cold dead, no excuses. We will get the job done.\par \par \uc2 enltra DeSantis PAC is now using his "stone cold dead" line in an ad {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/tnU735u48u"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/tnU735u48u}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Aaron Rupar (@atrupar) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/atrupar/status/1700151138148839759?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 September 8, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 6.46pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.27pm BST\par \par \uc2 The day so far\par \par \uc2 A report authored by the special grand jury tasked with investigating \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  and his allies\u8217\'20\'19 attempts to disrupt \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s election win in Georgia was released, and offered new details of the steps that led Fulton county district attorney \uc2 Fani Willis\uc2  to charge the ex-president and 18 others with racketeering-related crimes last month. In particular, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/sep/08/georgia-report-indictment-trump-expected-unsealed-biden-modi-g20-latest-news?filterKeyEvents=false&page=with:block-64fb2d518f08b298ac2fb230#block-64fb2d518f08b298ac2fb230"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the report revealed}}}\uc2  that the panel recommended charges against 20 additional people, including Georgia\u8217\'20\'19s former senators \uc2 David Perdue\uc2  and Kelly Loeffler, and the senator \uc2 Lindsey Graham\uc2 , who currently represents South Carolina. He commented briefly on the report, saying he was {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/sep/08/georgia-report-indictment-trump-expected-unsealed-biden-modi-g20-latest-news?page=with:block-64fb54e38f08b298ac2fb554#block-64fb54e38f08b298ac2fb554"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1Ctotally surprised\u8221\'20\'1D}}}\uc2  by their conclusion.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s what else has happened today so far:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Nancy Pelosi{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/sep/08/georgia-report-indictment-trump-expected-unsealed-biden-modi-g20-latest-news?page=with:block-64fb46178f08addfe9223cdf#block-64fb46178f08addfe9223cdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 said she will run}}}\uc2  for another two-year term in the House, ending speculation over whether the veteran San Francisco lawmaker would remain after stepping down as the chamber\u8217\'20\'19s top Democrat.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2  went out of his way {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/sep/08/georgia-report-indictment-trump-expected-unsealed-biden-modi-g20-latest-news?page=with:block-64fb25fc8f08addfe9223a7b#block-64fb25fc8f08addfe9223a7b"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 to insult an audience member}}}\uc2  who accused him of policies that put Black people at risk.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/sep/08/georgia-report-indictment-trump-expected-unsealed-biden-modi-g20-latest-news?page=with:block-64fb1c448f08addfe9223a0a#block-64fb1c448f08addfe9223a0a"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 toured the renovated White House situation room}}}\uc2  before heading to India to meet with the leaders of G20 countries.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 6.29pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.10pm BST\par \par \uc2 Graham says 'totally surprised' by special grand jury charging recommendation in Georgia election subversion case - report\par \par \uc2 South Carolina\u8217\'20\'19s Republican senator \uc2 Lindsey Graham\uc2  says he was \u8220\'20\'1Ctotally surprised\u8221\'20\'1D to learn that a special grand jury recommended he face charges over the attempts by \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  and his allies to overturn \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s election win in Georgia, HuffPost reports:\par \par \uc2 enltrGraham says he was "totally surprised" by grand jury recommendation he be charged in 2020 election case.\par \par \uc2 "It's over for me. You had 3 US senators caught up in this special grand jury, again, you gotta be careful where we go as a nation here," he says in SC\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Igor Bobic (@igorbobic) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/igorbobic/status/1700192625389707732?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 September 8, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 enltrGraham on call with Raffensberger: "I thought I made it pretty clear my phone call was about what I should be doing as a senator..I never said anything other than trying to find how the mail-in ballot system worked."\par \par \uc2 "I did my job, I wouldn't change anything I did"\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Igor Bobic (@igorbobic) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/igorbobic/status/1700192816368927108?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 September 8, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 Graham was ultimately not named when Fulton county district attorney \uc2 Fani Willis\uc2  last month unveiled a racketeering indictment against Trump and 18 co-defendants.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.56pm BST\par \par \uc2 Just yesterday, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.politico.com/news/magazine/2023/09/07/why-pelosi-might-run-again-00114342?nname=playbook&nid=0000014f-1646-d88f-a1cf-5f46b7bd0000&nrid=12069c7e-e346-405c-ad2c-71cb1a62e514&nlid=630318"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Politico published}}}\uc2  a lengthy article on \uc2 Nancy Pelosi\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s future, which opens with the House veteran and fixture of San Francisco politics dodging questions about whether they\u8217\'20\'19ll seek another term:\par \par \uc2 Speaker emerita \uc2 Nancy Pelosi\uc2  was riding through Chinatown here last month when she seemed to make the case for why she should run again and extend her emeritus status another term.\par \par \uc2 We were discussing her ailing colleague and Pacific Heights neighbor, Sen. \uc2 Dianne Feinstein\uc2  (D-Calif.), and how Feinstein\u8217\'20\'19s pending retirement would shape Pelosi\u8217\'20\'19s thinking \u8212\'20\'14 namely whether the ailing city they\u8217\'20\'19ve both represented for over three decades could afford for them to leave Congress at the same time.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI don\u8217\'20\'19t know,\u8221\'20\'1D Pelosi said with a chuckle, \u8220\'20\'1Ceverybody has an opinion, you can be sure.\u8221\'20\'1D Then she tried to change the subject, but unintentionally found a metaphor. \u8220\'20\'1CThere\u8217\'20\'19s Nancy\u8217\'20\'19s Fashion right there and it\u8217\'20\'19s closed,\u8221\'20\'1D she said, pointing out the window of her Capitol Police Suburban toward a once-familiar storefront on Stockton Street.\par \par \uc2 I tried again and seemed to have more success.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWell let\u8217\'20\'19s just go back about six years and we had Dianne, we had Barbara, we had Jackie Speier, now Jackie is gone, so we\u8217\'20\'19ll see,\u8221\'20\'1D Pelosi said, laying out the rationale for another run by invoking the three veteran Bay-area lawmakers who\u8217\'20\'19ve retired or are retiring: Feinstein, former Sen. Barbara Boxer, who stepped down in 2017, and former Rep. Jackie Speier, who left Congress at the start of this year.\par \par \uc2 It was a striking moment of candor, when the text of our conversation (\uc2 Nancy Pelosi\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s San Francisco) finally met the subtext of it (\uc2 Nancy Pelosi\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s future in San Francisco).\par \par \uc2 Yet it was only a moment. Pelosi grew characteristically elusive again \u8212\'20\'14 and harder to believe. \u8220\'20\'1CI haven\u8217\'20\'19t been thinking much about it \u8212\'20\'14 yet,\u8221\'20\'1D she said, \u8220\'20\'1Cbut I will. When I need to, I will.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Just over 24 hours after the piece was published, Pelosi announced that she would indeed run again.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.36pm BST\par \par \uc2 I just spoke with J Tom Morgan, a former district attorney in DeKalb county, Georgia, about the special purpose grand jury\u8217\'20\'19s report that was issued today.\par \par \uc2 He told me that in 40 years, he\u8217\'20\'19s never seen a publicly released special grand jury report like it, one that recommended charges without an indictment.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt kind of puts the DA in a bind that she now has to justify why these people were not indicted. Could there be special plea deals or negotiations between some of these people that she\u8217\'20\'19s not ready to reveal?,\u8221\'20\'1D he told me. \u8220\'20\'1CUltimately, it\u8217\'20\'19s her decision and her decision alone whether to go forward with any or all of those recommendations.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Morgan added that he believes the names of those who weren\u8217\'20\'19t ultimately indicted should have been redacted.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19m not commenting on whether or not these people should be indicted. That\u8217\'20\'19s for the DA to decide. But what you\u8217\'20\'19ve got is a report naming all these people who should be indicted and now they\u8217\'20\'19re not indicted and they have no way to defend themselves,\u8221\'20\'1D he added.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CYou\u8217\'20\'19ve got a grand jury saying \u8216\'20\'18hey these people committed crimes. But since they\u8217\'20\'19re not indicted, they don\u8217\'20\'19t have a chance to prove their innocence in a court of law.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 6.18pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.20pm BST\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s \uc2 Nancy Pelosi\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s tweet announcing her intention to stand for another two-year term in the House:\par \par \uc2 enltrNow more than ever our City needs us to advance San Francisco values and further our recovery. Our country needs America to show the world that our flag is still there, with liberty and justice for ALL. That is why I am running for reelection \u8212\'20\'14 and respectfully ask for your vote.\u8230\'20\'26\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 \uc2 Nancy Pelosi\uc2  (@TeamPelosi) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/TeamPelosi/status/1700177174542876754?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 September 8, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 Pelosi represents heavily Democratic San Francisco, and is unlikely to have any trouble winning the general election.\par \par \uc2 Democrats hope to retake control from the GOP in next year\u8217\'20\'19s election, where Republicans will be defending their slim control of the House. Pelosi, however, has handed over duties as her party\u8217\'20\'19s leader to New York\u8217\'20\'19s \uc2 Hakeem Jeffries\uc2  who, as minority leader, is positioned to be House speaker if the Democrats retake the majority.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.09pm BST\par \par \uc2 Pelosi says she will run for another term in House - reports\par \par \uc2 Democratic former speaker of the House \uc2 Nancy Pelosi\uc2  says she will stand for re-election in the House of Representatives, according to media reports.\par \par \uc2 enltrConfirmed: Former House Speaker \uc2 Nancy Pelosi\uc2  said today she\u8217\'20\'19s running for another term in Congress, her office tells {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/axios?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @Axios}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Andrew Solender (@AndrewSolender) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/AndrewSolender/status/1700177979085664434?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 September 8, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 Pelosi, 83, has represented San Francisco since 1987, and served as House speaker from 2007 to 2011, and from 2019 till the start of this year, the first woman ever to hold the position, which is second in line to the presidency.\par \par \uc2 She has remained in the chamber as speaker emerita after Kevin McCarthy and his Republican majority took office in January, and it had been unclear if she would seek another two-year term in the House.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.52pm BST\par \par \uc2 Back on the presidential campaign trail, \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2  has often dodged questions about \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , but as the Guardian\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/ava-sasani"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Ava Sasani}}}\uc2  reports, Florida\u8217\'20\'19s supreme court, dominated by judges he appointed, is hearing a case that could dramatically curtail access to the procedure in the state:\par \par \uc2 The {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/florida"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Florida}}}\uc2  supreme court on Friday will hear arguments in a case that could drastically limit \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access in the south-eastern United States.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  providers in Florida filed a lawsuit to block the state\u8217\'20\'19s ban on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  after 15 weeks of pregnancy.\par \par \uc2 If the state\u8217\'20\'19s high court upholds the 15-week ban, a separate, stricter law would take effect prohibiting \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  after six weeks, before most people know they are pregnant.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt would be devastating for providers to have to turn even more folks away under a six-week ban,\u8221\'20\'1D said Whitney White, a staff attorney with the \uc2 ACLU\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s Reproductive Freedom Project. \u8220\'20\'1CThey\u8217\'20\'19re already having to turn away patients under the current 15-week ban.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Friday\u8217\'20\'19s hearing is the culmination of Republican efforts to end Florida\u8217\'20\'19s legacy as a safe haven for \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  seekers in neighboring states. Five of the seven justices on the current state supreme court were selected by the conservative governor, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/ron-desantis"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Ron DeSantis}}}\uc2 , fueling the concerns of Floridians who support \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access.\par \par \uc2 After signing the six-week trigger ban into effect in April, Governor DeSantis said in a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.flgov.com/2023/04/13/governor-ron-desantis-signs-heartbeat-protection-act/#:~:text=%E2%80%94%20Today%2C%20Governor%20Ron%20DeSantis%20signed,%2C%E2%80%9D%20said%20Governor%20Ron%20DeSantis."}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 brief statement }}}\uc2  that he was \u8220\'20\'1Cproud to support life and family in the state of Florida\u8221\'20\'1D. The Florida governor has been hesitant to discuss \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  on the campaign trial.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2023/sep/08/florida-supreme-court-abortion-case-six-weeks"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Florida supreme court to hear \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  case that could drastically limit access}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.32pm BST\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s more from the Guardian\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/sam-levine"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Sam Levine}}}\uc2  on what we learned from the full report of the Georgia special grand jury tasked with investigating the attempt to overturn the state\u8217\'20\'19s 2020 election results:\par \par \uc2 A special purpose grand jury in Georgia that investigated \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/sep/07/donald-trump-georgia-election-charges-federal-court"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 efforts to overturn the 2020 election}}}\uc2  for nearly two years recommended bringing criminal charges against several people who ultimately were not charged, including US senator \uc2 Lindsey Graham\uc2 , former senators \uc2 David Perdue\uc2  and Kelly Loeffler, as well as the influential conservative figure Cleta Mitchell.\par \par \uc2 Those recommendations were revealed on Friday when the special purpose grand jury\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.fultonclerk.org/DocumentCenter/View/2165/2022-EX-000024-ORDER"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 final report was unsealed}}}\uc2 . A regular grand jury indicted Trump and 18 others over their efforts to overturn the 2020 election last month. Those charged include {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/sep/01/rudy-giuliani-not-guilty-georgia-election-racketeering-charges"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Rudy Giuliani}}}\uc2 , {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/sep/05/mark-meadows-pleads-not-guilty-trump-georgia-2020-election"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Mark Meadows}}}\uc2 , \uc2 Sidney Powell\uc2  and the former Georgia Republican party chairman David Shafer.\par \par \uc2 The special purpose grand jury recommended bringing charges against Graham, Perdue and Loeffler \u8220\'20\'1Cwith respect to the national effort to overturn the 2020 presidential election with efforts focused on {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/state-of-georgia"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Georgia}}}\uc2 , Arizona, Wisconsin, Michigan, Pennsylvania, and the District of Columbia\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Graham, a key Trump ally in the Senate, called Georgia secretary of state \uc2 Brad Raffensperger\uc2  after the election {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.washingtonpost.com/politics/brad-raffensperger-georgia-vote/2020/11/16/6b6cb2f4-283e-11eb-8fa2-06e7cbb145c0_story.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 and inquired}}}\uc2  about tossing aside legally cast mail-in ballots. Perdue {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.politico.com/news/magazine/2022/03/19/brian-kemp-david-perdue-donald-trump-2020-00018601"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reportedly pushed}}}\uc2  Georgia governor \uc2 Brian Kemp\uc2  to call a special session of the Georgia legislature in order to overturn the election results. Loeffler initially said she would vote against certification of Biden\u8217\'20\'19s win in the \uc2 US Senate\uc2  before {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://19thnews.org/2021/01/loeffler-reverses-course-and-certifies-bidens-election-victory/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reversing course}}}\uc2  after the January 6 riot and voting in favor of certification.\par \par \uc2 Mitchell, who remains an influential figure on the right today, was on the infamous January 2021 phone call in which Trump asked Raffensperger to find votes in his favor. The special purpose grand jury unanimously recommended indicting her under several Georgia statutes.\par \par \uc2 The special purpose grand jury also recommended indicting \uc2 Michael Flynn\uc2 , Trump\u8217\'20\'19s former national security adviser, and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/2023/03/14/us/politics/boris-epshteyn-trump-lawyer.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Boris Epshteyn}}}\uc2 , who remains a top Trump aide.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/sep/08/lindsey-graham-criminal-charges-georgia-jury"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Georgia report reveals jury called for criminal charges against Lindsey Graham and others}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 4.36pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.13pm BST\par \par \uc2 All told, the special grand jurors in Georgia recommended charges against 39 people for trying to overturn the state\u8217\'20\'19s elections, but Fulton county district attorney \uc2 Fani Willis\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s indictment only targeted 19 people, \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  among them.\par \par \uc2 Among those who were named in the report, but not charged:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Cleta Mitchell, a rightwing lawyer who {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/may/08/lawyer-trump-2020-election-attacks-college-student-voting"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 has lately been calling on Republicans}}}\uc2  to find ways to keep college students away from the polls and crack down on same-day voter registration and absentee voting.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Boris Epshteyn, who has {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/apr/19/trump-adviser-boris-epshteyn-interview-special-counsel"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 simultaneously been working}}}\uc2  as an attorney for Trump and an advisor to his campaign.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Michael Flynn\uc2 , a former national security advisor who is now spending his time {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/jul/07/sham-fears-over-trump-loyalists-election-integrity-drive"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 training rightwing poll workers}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.53pm BST\par \par \uc2 David Perdue\uc2  and Kelly Loeffler were Georgia\u8217\'20\'19s Republican senators, until both were ousted from office by the Democrats \uc2 Jon Ossoff\uc2  and \uc2 Raphael Warnock\uc2  in elections held the day before the January 6 insurrection.\par \par \uc2 The special grand jury in Fulton county recommended that Perdue be charged \u8220\'20\'1Cover the persistent, repeated communications directed to multiple Georgia officials and employees between November of 2020 and January of 2021\u8221\'20\'1D \u8211\'20\'13 the period when \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  was trying to overturn his election loss. The vote was 16 jurors in favor, one against, and one abstention.\par \par \uc2 The jurors also recommended charges against both Loeffler and Perdue for \u8220\'20\'1Cthe national effort to overturn the 2020 presidential election\u8221\'20\'1D. However there was more dissent on this count. For Perdue, the vote was 17 in favor and four against, while for Loeffler, the vote was 14 in favor, 6 against, and one abstention.\par \par \uc2 Fulton county district attorney \uc2 Fani Willis\uc2  ultimately did not indict either of the former lawmakers.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.55pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.33pm BST\par \par \uc2 Lindsey Graham\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s name appeared early as \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s attempts to stay in the White House began shortly after his re-election defeat in November 2020.\par \par \uc2 Georgia secretary of state \uc2 Brad Raffensperger\uc2  told the press that the South Carolina senator had called him to ask if it was possible to throw away mail-in ballots in counties crucial to \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s win in Georgia. From the Guardian\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/lauren-gambino"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Lauren Gambino}}}\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s report at the time:\par \par \uc2 Georgia\u8217\'20\'19s secretary of state, \uc2 Brad Raffensperger\uc2 , has said that Senator \uc2 Lindsey Graham\uc2  asked whether it was possible to invalidate legally cast ballots after \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  was narrowly defeated in the state.\par \par \uc2 In {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.washingtonpost.com/politics/brad-raffensperger-georgia-vote/2020/11/16/6b6cb2f4-283e-11eb-8fa2-06e7cbb145c0_story.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 an interview with the Washington Post}}}\uc2 , Raffensperger said that his fellow Republican, the chairman of the Senate judiciary committee, questioned him about the state\u8217\'20\'19s signature-matching law and asked whether political bias might have played a role in counties where poll workers accepted higher rates of mismatched signatures. According to Raffensperger, Graham then asked whether he had the authority to toss out all mail-in ballots in these counties.\par \par \uc2 Raffensperger was reportedly \u8220\'20\'1Cstunned\u8221\'20\'1D by the question, in which Graham appeared to suggest that he find a way to throw out legally cast absentee ballots.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt sure looked like he was wanting to go down that road,\u8221\'20\'1D he said.\par \par \uc2 Graham confirmed the conversation to reporters on Capitol Hill but said it was \u8220\'20\'1Cridiculous\u8221\'20\'1D to suggest that he pressured Raffensperger to throw out legally cast absentee ballots. According to Graham, he only wanted to learn more about the process for verifying signatures, because what happens in Georgia \u8220\'20\'1Caffects the whole nation\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI thought it was a good conversation,\u8221\'20\'1D Graham said on Monday after the interview was published. \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19m surprised to hear he characterized it that way.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Trump has refused to accept results showing \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  as the winner of the 2020 presidential election, falsely blaming rampant fraud and irregularities that election officials in both parties have dismissed as meritless.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.23pm BST\par \par \uc2 Georgia special grand jury recommended charging \uc2 Lindsey Graham\uc2  and former US senators\par \par \uc2 The special grand jury investigating the attempt to overturn Georgia\u8217\'20\'19s 2020 election results recommended bringing charges against the state\u8217\'20\'19s former senators David P erdue and Kelly Loeffler as well as the current South Carolina senator \uc2 Lindsey Graham\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 None of the three were named in the indictment Fulton county district attorney \uc2 Fani Willis\uc2  unveiled last month, which targeted \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  and 18 others with racketeering charges related to their attempt to stop \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  from collecting Georgia\u8217\'20\'19s electoral votes despite his victory there.\par \par \uc2 According to the report, the jurors recommended the three senators be charged over \u8220\'20\'1Cthe national effort to overturn the 2020 presidential election\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.26pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.14pm BST\par \par \uc2 Special grand jury's report in Georgia election subversion case released\par \par \uc2 The full report of the special grand jury whose investigation led to the indictment of \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  and 18 others for trying to overturn Georgia\u8217\'20\'19s 2020 election result has been released.\par \par \uc2 We\u8217\'20\'19re digging into it and will let you know what it says.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.12pm BST\par \par \uc2 The special grand jury report that was used in the indictment of \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  and 18 others in Georgia for trying to overturn the state\u8217\'20\'19s 2020 election results is expected to be released any minute now.\par \par \uc2 While parts of it have already been unsealed, we will finally be getting a look at the full report by the jurors empaneled by Fulton county district attorney \uc2 Fani Willis\uc2 . There are two main pieces of news expected from the report:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Whether the grand jurors recommended charges be brought against people who Willis ultimately opted not to pursue.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The vote counts for each person the jurors said should be indicted, and whether there were any significant splits within the panel.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.51pm BST\par \par \uc2 Yesterday, \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2  had a testy exchange with an audience member who accused the Republican governor of backing policies in Florida that enabled violence against Black people \u8211\'20\'13 such as {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/aug/30/florida-gun-laws-desantis-racist-jacksonville-shooting"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 last month\u8217\'20\'19s shooting by a racist gunman in Jacksonville}}}\uc2  :\par \par \uc2 enltr\u8220\'20\'1CYou have allowed people to hunt people like me\u8221\'20\'1D:\par \par \uc2 A Black audience member gets into a back and forth with Gov. \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2  (R-FL) at a Jacksonville news conference after questioning state policies he says have led to violence against Black people. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/7G99npsvZ8"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/7G99npsvZ8}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 The Recount (@therecount) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/therecount/status/1699805584403345499?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 September 7, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 Clearly smarting over the exchange, DeSantis later went on Fox News to call the questioner a \u8220\'20\'1Cnutjob\u8221\'20\'1D:\par \par \uc2 enltrGov. \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2  (R-FL) on critic at news conference who said his policies have led to violence against Black people:\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe can have disagreements on issues... be heated on issues. But to take some nutjob and to try to act like we were a part of that is absolutely absurd.\u8221\'20\'1D {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/M5wfO8gwLO"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/M5wfO8gwLO}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 The Recount (@therecount) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/therecount/status/1700141516973277290?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 September 8, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.51pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.32pm BST\par \par \uc2 While \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  is in India for a meeting of G20 leaders, Republicans angling to replace him next year are continuing their campaigns, including \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2  \u8211\'20\'13 who may have done himself more harm than good by skipping a meeting with the president after a hurricane struck Florida. Here\u8217\'20\'19s the story, from the Guardian\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/richardluscombe"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Richard Luscombe}}}\uc2  :\par \par \uc2 One reality of Florida politics is that a bad hurricane for the state traditionally blows good fortune for its governor. It was true for \uc2 Rick Scott\uc2 , elected a senator in November 2018, one month after guiding Florida through Category 5 Hurricane Michael; and again for {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/ron-desantis"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Ron DeSantis}}}\uc2 , whose landslide re-election last year followed his much-praised handling of the aftermath of Hurricane Ian.\par \par \uc2 This year, however, DeSantis is struggling to shake the dark clouds of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/hurricane-idalia"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Hurricane Idalia}}}\uc2 , as his return to the national stage to try to rescue his flailing presidential campaign after an 11-day break has been further scarred by his \u8220\'20\'1Cpetty and small\u8221\'20\'1D {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/sep/02/ron-desantis-snubs-joe-biden-hurricane-idalia"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 snub of Joe Biden\u8217\'20\'19s visit}}}\uc2  to Florida last weekend to survey the storm\u8217\'20\'19s damage.\par \par \uc2 Opponents seized on it as a partisan politicization of a climate disaster, contrasting the Republican Florida governor\u8217\'20\'19s approach to a year ago after Ian, when DeSantis and Biden {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/oct/09/ron-desantis-hurricane-ian-aftermath"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 put their differences aside}}}\uc2  to praise each other and tour the worst-affected areas with their respective first ladies.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CYour job as governor is to be the tour guide for the president, to make sure the president sees your people, sees the damage, sees the suffering, what\u8217\'20\'19s going on and what needs to be done to rebuild it,\u8221\'20\'1D \uc2 Chris Christie\uc2 , the former New Jersey governor, and a rival for the Republican presidential nomination, told Fox News Radio\u8217\'20\'19s Brian Kilmeade.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CYou\u8217\'20\'19re doing your job. And unfortunately, he put politics ahead of his job,\u8221\'20\'1D added Christie, who was applauded by Democrats and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.businessinsider.com/chris-christie-obama-sandy-new-jersey-damage-conservatives-drudge-2012-10"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 savaged by Republicans}}}\uc2  for {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2013/may/28/obama-christie-jersey-shore-sandy"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 working closely with Barack Obama}}}\uc2  after superstorm Sandy mauled his state in 2012.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/sep/08/ron-desantis-campaign-struggles-hurricane-idalia-biden-snub"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 DeSantis struggles to shake Hurricane Idalia\u8217\'20\'19s dark clouds after snub to Biden}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.11pm BST\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 Twitter\uc2 /X account of \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 , who is currently flying on Air Force One to New Delhi for a summit of G20 nations, just released video showing him touring the renovated situation room.\par \par \uc2 That\u8217\'20\'19s the space in the White House where the president goes to handle emergencies or highly sensitive operations:\par \par \uc2 enltrFolks, the newly renovated White House Situation Room is up and running.\par \par \uc2 My thanks to everyone who worked on this incredible facility. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/81sEvKV5Ma"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/81sEvKV5Ma}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 President Biden (@POTUS) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/POTUS/status/1700132068280209593?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 September 8, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 Perhaps the most famous appearance of a president in the situation room is \uc2 Barack Obama\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s from 1 May 2011, as he watched US soldiers kill \uc2 Osama bin Laden\uc2  in Pakistan. His photographer Pete Souza captured the scene:\par \par \uc2 Also in the photo: then-vice-president \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  (far left) and \uc2 Hillary Clinton\uc2  (lower right), who was at the time secretary of state. Photograph: Pete Souza/AP\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.44pm BST\par \par \uc2 Yesterday, \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  indicated he may ask that his trial in the Georgia election subversion case be moved to federal court, which the Guardian\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/hugo-lowell"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Hugo Lowell}}}\uc2  reported could have a number of advantages for the former president:\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s lead defense lawyer notified a judge in Fulton county on Thursday that he could soon seek to remove to federal court the racketeering prosecution charging him with attempting to overturn the results of the 2020 presidential election in the state of Georgia.\par \par \uc2 The unusual filing, submitted to the Fulton county superior court judge Scott McAfee, said only that {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/donaldtrump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the former president}}}\uc2  \u8220\'20\'1Cmay seek removal of his prosecution\u8221\'20\'1D, stopping short of submitting a formal motion to transfer the trial venue.\par \par \uc2 Trump has been weighing for weeks whether to seek removal to federal court and, according to two people familiar with deliberations, is expected to make a decision based on whether his former White House chief of staff \uc2 Mark Meadows\uc2  is successful in his own effort.\par \par \uc2 The idea with waiting on a decision in the Meadows case, the people said, is to use him as a test. If Meadows is successful in transferring to federal court, the Trump legal team is intending to repurpose the same arguments and follow a similar strategy.\par \par \uc2 To have the case moved to the US district court for the northern district of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/state-of-georgia"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Georgia}}}\uc2 , Trump would have to show that the criminal conduct alleged in the indictment involved his official duties as president \u8211\'20\'13 he was acting \u8220\'20\'1Cunder color of office\u8221\'20\'1D \u8211\'20\'13 and cannot be prosecuted at the state level.\par \par \uc2 The rationale to seek removal to federal court is seen as twofold: the jury pool would expand beyond just the Atlanta area \u8211\'20\'13 which skews heavily Democratic \u8211\'20\'13 and a federal judge might be less deferential to local prosecutors compared with judges in the Fulton county superior court.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/sep/07/donald-trump-georgia-election-charges-federal-court"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Trump may seek to transfer Georgia 2020 election charges to federal court}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.28pm BST\par \par \uc2 Report could offer more details of investigation that led to Trump's indictment in Georgia\par \par \uc2 The Georgia special grand jury report that is expected to be released at 10am ET today could reveal whether the investigative panel thought anyone else besides \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  and his 18 co-defendants should face charges for meddling in the state\u8217\'20\'19s election result three years ago.\par \par \uc2 Fulton county district attorney \uc2 Fani Willis\uc2  convened the panel and used its subpoena power to compel witness testimony, and portions of its final report have already been released. The special grand jury did not indict Trump \u8211\'20\'13 that was done by one of the regular grand juries she convened in August.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 1.36pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.05pm BST\par \par \uc2 Georgia grand jury report on election subversion case to be released\par \par \uc2 Good morning, US politics live blog readers. It\u8217\'20\'19s going to be another big Friday in one of the criminal cases against \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , while US president \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  is in India for G20 and a crucial bilateral with the prime minister, \uc2 Narendra Modi\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s some of what\u8217\'20\'19s ahead:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The report of the special grand jury in Georgia that investigated Trump in the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/sep/07/donald-trump-georgia-election-charges-federal-court"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 election subversion case}}}\uc2  \u8211\'20\'13 where the now-former president attempted to overturn the 2020 election in the swing state \u8211\'20\'13 is expected to be unsealed today.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Biden is due to touch down in New Delhi, India, in under two hours, a day before the start of the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/g20"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 G20}}}\uc2  summit there. He and Modi will hold a bilateral meeting shortly after the US president arrives. The specter of Russia\u8217\'20\'19s war in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/ukraine"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Ukraine}}}\uc2  looms over the event.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Speaking of criminal cases against former US presidents, on this day 49 years ago Republican president Gerald Ford granted a \u8220\'20\'1Cfull, free, and absolute pardon\u8221\'20\'1D to former president \uc2 Richard Nixon\uc2  covering his entire term in office, the AP notes.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Trump will attend a rally tonight in South Dakota and the state\u8217\'20\'19s rightwing governor \uc2 Kristi Noem\uc2  is expected to endorse his run for the 2024 Republican nomination for the White House. Noem is considered a vice-presidential {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.politico.com/news/2023/09/08/kristi-noem-veepstakes-00114586?nname=playbook&nid=0000014f-1646-d88f-a1cf-5f46b7bd0000&nrid=00000168-5c87-d6fb-a77d-fdb72f6a0000&nlid=630318"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 hopeful}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 1.36pm BST\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020230908ej980018p\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
