\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Florida supreme court signals openness to  \highlight22\uc2 abortion \highlight\uc2  ban that would slash access\b0\par\par\uc2 Carter Sherman and Ava Sasani \par \uc2 862 \uc2 words\par \uc2 8 September 2023\par 20:34 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Five of seven justices on court were selected by Governor \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2  and decision would have ramifications across south-east\par \par \uc2 In arguments in a case that could drastically limit \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access in the south-eastern United States, the Florida supreme court on Friday seemed open to arguments to uphold a law that bans \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  past 15 weeks of pregnancy.\par \par \uc2 If the state\u8217\'20\'19s high court upholds the 15-week ban under consideration, a separate, stricter law would take effect prohibiting \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  after six weeks, before many people know they are pregnant.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt would be devastating for providers to have to turn even more folks away under a six-week ban,\u8221\'20\'1D said Whitney White, a staff attorney with the \uc2 ACLU\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s Reproductive Freedom Project. \u8220\'20\'1CThey\u8217\'20\'19re already having to turn away patients under the current 15-week ban.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Friday\u8217\'20\'19s hearing is the culmination of Republican efforts to end Florida\u8217\'20\'19s legacy as a safe haven for \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  seekers in neighboring states. Five of the seven justices on the current state supreme court were selected by the conservative governor, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/ron-desantis"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Ron DeSantis}}}\uc2 , fueling the concerns of Floridians who support \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access.\par \par \uc2 Throughout the hearing, the justices peppered White and the attorney representing Florida, Henry Whitaker, with questions about whether Florida\u8217\'20\'19s constitutional right to privacy encompasses \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 At one point, Chief Justice Carlos Mu\u241\'00\'F1iz \u8211\'20\'13 a DeSantis appointee \u8211\'20\'13 suggested that Roe v Wade, the 1973 supreme court case that legalized \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  nationwide, was an \u8220\'20\'1Cabomination\u8221\'20\'1D. At another, he said that the fact that the \uc2 US supreme court\uc2  overturned Roe in 2022 revealed the right to an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  to be a \u8220\'20\'1Cmirage\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CYou\u8217\'20\'19re asking us to essentially take a whole class of human beings and put them outside of the protection of the law? Essentially, in the sense that \u8211\'20\'13 if the legislature wants to protect those human beings, they are precluded by the constitution of Florida from doing that?\u8221\'20\'1D Mu\u241\'00\'F1iz asked White, in an apparent reference to fetuses. \u8220\'20\'1CAnd at the end of the day, the argument as to why that would be right would be based based on a sort of legal meaning kind of understanding of the right of privacy?\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 During his time to speak, Whitaker said that the \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  providers who sued over the 15-week ban were reading Florida\u8217\'20\'19s privacy rights far too broadly.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThey do not provide a limiting principle to distinguish \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  from infanticide, from euthanasia, from spousal abuse,\u8221\'20\'1D Whitaker said. \u8220\'20\'1CThose are all involved, personal decisions that I suppose the government could be said to be interfering with, in some sense, when the legislature takes action to remedy choices that harm others.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Conflating \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  with infanticide has, in recent years, become a common anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  talking point. White told the justices that infanticide is already illegal and will remain so, no matter what the Florida supreme court rules in this case.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CFrankly, there\u8217\'20\'19s no reason for the court to be concerned about that,\u8221\'20\'1D White said. \u8220\'20\'1CThis is not a brave new world.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 After signing the six-week trigger ban into effect in April, Governor DeSantis said in a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.flgov.com/2023/04/13/governor-ron-desantis-signs-heartbeat-protection-act/#:~:text=%E2%80%94%20Today%2C%20Governor%20Ron%20DeSantis%20signed,%2C%E2%80%9D%20said%20Governor%20Ron%20DeSantis."}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 brief statement }}}\uc2  that he was \u8220\'20\'1Cproud to support life and family in the state of Florida\u8221\'20\'1D. The Florida governor has been hesitant to discuss \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  on the campaign trial.\par \par \uc2 A whopping 62% of American adults believe abortions should be legal in \u8220\'20\'1Call or most cases\u8221\'20\'1D, according to a 2022 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.pewresearch.org/politics/2022/07/06/majority-of-public-disapproves-of-supreme-courts-decision-to-overturn-roe-v-wade/#americans-views-of-abortion"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 report}}}\uc2  published by \uc2 Pew Research Center\uc2 . A {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.ipsos.com/sites/default/files/ct/news/documents/2020-11/topline_reuters_florida_state_poll_w6_11_02_2020_.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 2020 Ipsos/Reuters poll}}}\uc2  found that 56% of likely voters in Florida believe \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  should be legal in most cases. \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights supporters in Florida say the bans violate the explicit privacy protections found in the state constitution.\par \par \uc2 Florida {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/republicans"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Republicans}}}\uc2  passed the 15-week ban on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  in April 2022, months before the \uc2 US supreme court\uc2  ended the federal right to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 . That same month, a judge revived a 2015 state law that mandated patients wait 24 hours between getting an initial consultation for an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  and undergoing the procedure.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s been one restriction after another,\u8221\'20\'1D said Dr Kanthi Dhaduvai, a Jacksonville \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  provider with Physicians for Reproductive {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/society/health"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Health}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Ahead of the hearing, Dhaduvai felt \u8220\'20\'1Cnervous and frustrated,\u8221\'20\'1D fearing a court ruling that would make it impossible for her patients to receive \u8220\'20\'1Cwhat is often life-saving care\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Roughly half of Dhaduvai\u8217\'20\'19s patients come to Florida from states like Georgia, Louisiana, Mississippi, Alabama \u8211\'20\'13 even Texas.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI think a lot of people are not aware as to how dangerous this could be, not just for Florida, but the entire region,\u8221\'20\'1D she said. \u8220\'20\'1CFlorida has been a huge access point for people, we already have people traveling these great distances to get care.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 In the months after the \uc2 US supreme court\uc2  overturned Roe v Wade, Florida saw the greatest increase in the number of legal abortions performed per month, according to a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://societyfp.org/wp-content/uploads/2023/03/WeCountReport_April2023Release.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 report}}}\uc2  released this April from the Society of Family Planning. Florida performed more than 82,000 abortions in 2022.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19m still providing care and I\u8217\'20\'19m going to continue providing care, within legal limits, even after the decision,\u8221\'20\'1D Dhaduvai said.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020230908ej98001mk\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
