\par\par \uc2 World news\par \b \uc2 Mexico supreme court decriminalizes  \highlight22\uc2 abortion \highlight\uc2  across country\b0\par\par\uc2 Lillian Perlmutter in Mexico City \par \uc2 785 \uc2 words\par \uc2 7 September 2023\par 14:19 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par 27\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Decision to remove \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  from federal penal code comes amid trend in Latin America of loosening restrictions on procedure\par \par \uc2 Mexico\u8217\'20\'19s supreme court has unanimously ruled that state laws prohibiting \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  are unconstitutional and violate women\u8217\'20\'19s rights, in the latest in a series of victories for reproductive rights activists across Latin America.\par \par \uc2 Wednesday\u8217\'20\'19s ruling came two years after the court {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2021/sep/07/mexico-abortion-law-struck-down-supreme-court-penalties-unconstitutional"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 ordered the northern state of Coahuila}}}\uc2  to remove sanctions for \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  from its criminal code, a decision which prompted a tortuous state-by-state process of legal battles. So far 12 of Mexico\u8217\'20\'19s 31 states have decriminalized the procedure.\par \par \uc2 The court\u8217\'20\'19s decision marked a major victory for the GIRE, a reproductive rights organization based in Mexico City, which brought the test case against the Mexican state as part of a years-long campaign for reform.\par \par \uc2 Mexican women took to social media on Wednesday to celebrate, posting green heart emojis, in a reference to Latin America\u8217\'20\'19s burgeoning feminist movement.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt feels like a dream. Like I\u8217\'20\'19m the happiest person alive right now. If you don\u8217\'20\'19t have the ability to give birth, you can\u8217\'20\'19t tell me whether you think it\u8217\'20\'19s right or wrong,\u8221\'20\'1D said Andrea Hern\u225\'00\'E1ndez, a feminist activist in Mexico City.\par \par \uc2 But the ruling will not automatically make decriminalization the law of the land. Mexico\u8217\'20\'19s two congressional chambers will now need to come together to pass an accompanying law, eliminating \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  from the country\u8217\'20\'19s penal code.\par \par \uc2 This process could be fast, or it could take years, as happened with the court\u8217\'20\'19s ruling to decriminalize marijuana in 2018, which was not officially ratified by congress until 2021, leaving the possession and recreational consumption of the herb in a legal grey area for three years.\par \par \uc2 However, Wednesday\u8217\'20\'19s ruling will protect both women seeking abortions and healthcare workers involved in providing \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  care from criminal charges. Anyone with a uterus should also now be able to access abortions in federal health facilities across the country.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CNo woman or pregnant person, nor any health worker, will be punished for \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 ,\u8221\'20\'1D {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://gire.org.mx/blog/corte-despenaliza-el-aborto-a-nivel-federal/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 GIRE said in a statement}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Wednesday\u8217\'20\'19s decision is the latest victory for women\u8217\'20\'19s rights activists across Latin America, a region where the Catholic church remains a powerful influence, and where \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  is restricted or banned in many countries.\par \par \uc2 Nicaragua, Honduras, El Salvador, the Dominican Republic, Haiti and Suriname all have a complete ban on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 . But decades of organizing have brought major advances for pro-choice activists. Argentina {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2020/dec/30/argentina-legalises-abortion-in-landmark-moment-for-womens-rights"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 legalized the procedure in 2020 }}}\uc2  and Colombia, a highly conservative country, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/global-development/2022/feb/22/colombia-legalises-abortion-in-move-celebrated-as-historic-victory-by-campaigners"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 followed suit two years later.}}}\par \par \uc2 The Mexican ruling also represents a further separation between Mexico and its northern neighbor, the United States, where the supreme court voted last year to allow specific states to ban \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  and criminalize both women who seek to terminate pregnancies \u8211\'20\'13 even if the fetus is not viable \u8211\'20\'13 and medical professionals providing abortions.\par \par \uc2 Fifteen American states quickly passed laws banning abortions as early as at six weeks of gestation, when many women are not yet aware they are pregnant. In Texas, residents are now even offered cash bonuses should they turn a neighbor in to authorities for the crime of having an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Last year\u8217\'20\'19s US ruling led to the development of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2022/jun/10/mexico-abortion-access-americans"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a network of \u8220\'20\'1CJanes\u8221\'20\'1D }}}\uc2  who buy \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  pills over the counter in Mexico, and ship them to women and girls in need in the United States. It also prompted a rise in \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  tourism, both to other US states where the procedure is still legal, and to Mexico. Wednesday\u8217\'20\'19s Mexican ruling may entice more women from the American south to travel to Mexico for healthcare.\par \par \uc2 The court decision also marks an important milestone for Mexican feminists, who continue to protest against the country\u8217\'20\'19s catastrophic rates of femicide, sexual assault and domestic violence.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe\u8217\'20\'19ve seen rates of femicide rise since 2006 and even more since 2014 \u8211\'20\'13 and that\u8217\'20\'19s just one of the many difficult things Mexican women continue to face,\u8221\'20\'1D said Gina Jim\u233\'00\'E9nez, a researcher at Data C\u237\'00\'EDvica, an organization that compiles data on violence against women in Mexico.\par \par \uc2 Every year on International Women\u8217\'20\'19s Day, women\u8217\'20\'19s rights groups hold a march in Mexico City, attracting tens of thousands dressed in purple and green. This past year, several women held a banner asking the government for legal \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe\u8217\'20\'19re confident congress, whose legislation still provides obstacles to reproductive autonomy, will take account of the critiques of the highest court in the land, and will guarantee once and for all the right to choose,\u8221\'20\'1D GIRE said in a press release.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020230907ej970005o\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
