\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 First Thing: US pro-birth conference\u8217\'20\'19s links to far-right eugenicists revealed\b0\par\par\uc2 Nicola Slawson \par \uc2 1,814 \uc2 words\par \uc2 4 September 2023\par 11:13 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Natal conference, to be held in Austin in December, promoted on far-right podcast circuit and set to host self-described eugenicists. Plus, the age problem neither US political party wants to talk about\par \par \uc2 Good morning and happy Labor Day!\par \par \uc2 Due to an error, Friday\u8217\'20\'19s First Thing was not sent out. We apologize for the inconvenience.\par \par \uc2 A high-end hotel in the liberal Texan enclave of Austin is playing host to a conference whose theme is boosting global birthrates, but which will in fact {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/sep/04/natal-conference-austin-texas-eugenics"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 feature racist and eugenicist internet personalities and far-right media figures}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The Natal conference \u8211\'20\'13 whose website warns that \u8220\'20\'1Cby the end of the century, nearly every country on Earth will have a shrinking population, and economic systems dependent on reliable growth will collapse\u8221\'20\'1D \u8211\'20\'13 is scheduled to be held on 1 December at the Line hotel.\par \par \uc2 Natal\u8217\'20\'19s website claims the conference \u8220\'20\'1Chas no political or ideological goal other than a world in which our children can have grandchildren\u8221\'20\'1D, but the Guardian can reveal its organizer, Kevin Dolan, has been promoting the event on the far-right podcast circuit, and has explicitly linked the conference\u8217\'20\'19s \u8220\'20\'1Cpro-natalist\u8221\'20\'1D orientation to eugenics.\par \par \uc2 Dolan was at one time a social media influencer connected to the far-right Mormon \u8220\'20\'1CDeznat\u8221\'20\'1D or \u8220\'20\'1CDeseret nationalist\u8221\'20\'1D subculture and has himself linked the conference\u8217\'20\'19s theme with eugenics in interviews.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 What is eugenics? Broadly, eugenics is a group of beliefs and practices aimed at improving the genetic quality of a human population. It became the basis of a popular movement from the late 19th century, and led to governments around the world adopting policies such as forced sterilization of disabled and mentally ill people. The field was discredited after the second world war due to its association with racial policies in Nazi Germany, and many critics have attacked it as a pseudoscience.\par \par \uc2 Thousands donate to save Florida \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  clinic amid crippling state fines\par \par \uc2 Just a few weeks ago, one of the few \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  clinics left in Orlando, Florida, looked like it would have to close its doors. A government agency had ordered it to pay $193,000 in fines \u8211\'20\'13 enough to potentially bankrupt the clinic.\par \par \uc2 But supporters of the clinic, the Center of Orlando for Women, had an idea: they would crowdfund the money to keep it open. Within days, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/sep/04/florida-abortion-clinic-fundraiser-orlando"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 they succeeded}}}\uc2 . As of Friday, the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://givebutter.com/saveowc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 fundraiser}}}\uc2  had amassed more than $199,000 from roughly 5,500 donors. Many of the donations were less than $50.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19ll never forget how those protesters traumatized me as a scared teen making the hardest decision of my life,\u8221\'20\'1D wrote one donor who gave $5. \u8220\'20\'1CI one day hope to go back there and support women the way you do.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Had the Center of Orlando for Women gone dark, \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  patients across the south would have been affected. Because Florida is one of the few southern states that still permits \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , it had a greater increase in the number of patients seeking the procedure than any other state in the country after Roe v Wade collapsed last year, according to researchers from the Society of Family Planning.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 What does the future look like for the center? The future of the procedure in the state is decidedly uncertain. Although Florida already bans \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  past 15 weeks of pregnancy, \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2 , the governor, signed a six-week \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban into law earlier this year. (It is on hold pending a review by the state\u8217\'20\'19s supreme court of the 15-week ban.)\par \par \uc2 Officials investigate death at Burning Man as thousands stranded by floods\par \par \uc2 More than 70,000 attendees of the annual Burning Man festival in the Black Rock desert of Nevada are {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/culture/2023/sep/03/burning-man-nevada-festival-floods"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 stranded as the festival comes to a close}}}\uc2  today due to heavy rains that have cut off access to the site.\par \par \uc2 People have been ordered to shelter in place and to conserve food, water and fuel, although no shortages have been reported. A death that occurred at the festival is under investigation, but no details have been released, including the identity of the deceased or the suspected cause of death.\par \par \uc2 All traffic apart from emergency vehicles in and out of the festival site has been halted. More rain is forecast at the festival site on Sunday afternoon. Local officials said some attendees had been walking out of the site, but conditions remain too wet and muddy for vehicles to get out and could trap many people at the site for days.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe do not currently have an estimated time for the roads to be dry enough for RVs or vehicles to navigate safely. Monday late in the day would be possible if weather conditions are in our favor. We will let you know. It could be sooner, and it could be later,\u8221\'20\'1D said an update on the Burning Man website on Saturday evening.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Why else has the festival been in the news? The festival drew headlines from the start when climate activists attempted to blockade attendees from the site, blocking traffic for about an hour and clashing with attendees and local police in protest against the festival\u8217\'20\'19s carbon footprint. Rumors have also swirled around this year\u8217\'20\'19s festival, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.forbes.com/sites/mattnovak/2023/09/02/no-theres-not-an-ebola-outbreak-at-burning-man/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 including}}}\uc2  false rumors of an Ebola outbreak fueled by false social media posts about an evacuation due to a suspicious package at LAX airport in Los Angeles.\par \par \uc2 In other news \u8230\'20\'26\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Russia has launched its {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/live/2023/sep/04/russia-ukraine-war-live-updates-izmail-port-attack-putin-erdogan-talks-wheat?filterKeyEvents=false&page=with:block-64f55c6c8f083bb275c242ea#block-64f55c6c8f083bb275c242ea"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 second attack in two nights on Ukrainian ports}}}\uc2 , with Ukrainian officials warning residents of Izmail to remain in shelters in the early hours today. Oleg Kiper, the governor of Odesa, said Moscow launched an almost two-hour drone attack on the city.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 A judge in Florida has {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/sep/03/florida-judge-ron-desantis-voting-redistricting-map-unconstitutional"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 ruled in favor of voting rights groups}}}\uc2  that filed a lawsuit against a congressional redistricting map approved by \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2  in 2022. The groups had criticized the map for diluting political power in Black communities.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Algeria\u8217\'20\'19s defence ministry has said its {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2023/sep/03/algeria-says-its-coastguard-fired-warning-shots-before-killing-jetski-riders"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 coastguard fired warning shots}}}\uc2  before firing directly at a man on a jetski who entered Algerian waters, in an incident that a survivor said left two dead. The incident took place on Tuesday after five men strayed into Algerian waters on jetskis near the Moroccan coastal resort of Sa\u239\'00\'EFdia on Algeria\u8217\'20\'19s border.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The Democratic senator Tim Kaine of Virginia said\par \par \uc2 he believes there is a \u8220\'20\'1Cpowerful argument\u8221\'20\'1D to be made that {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/sep/03/trump-tim-kaine-donald-trump-2024"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Donald Trump can be disqualified from running in the 2024 presidential elections}}}\uc2  under the 14th amendment. Kaine says the clause on \u8220\'20\'1Cinsurrection against the constitution\u8221\'20\'1D could preclude the ex-president from running in next year\u8217\'20\'19s election.\par \par \uc2 Stat of the day: Native tribe to get back land 160 years after largest mass hanging in US history\par \par \uc2 Golden prairies and winding rivers of a Minnesota state park also hold the secret burial sites of Dakota people who died as the US failed to fulfill treaties with Native Americans {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/sep/03/native-tribe-upper-sioux-agency-us-dakota-war"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 more than a century ago}}}\uc2 . Now their descendants are getting the land back. The state is taking the rare step of transferring the park with a fraught history back to a Dakota tribe, trying to make amends for events that led to a war and the largest mass hanging in US history.\par \par \uc2 Decades of tension exploded into the US-Dakota war of 1862 between settler-colonists and a faction of Dakota people, according to the \uc2 Minnesota Historical Society\uc2 . After the US won the war, the government hanged more people than in any other execution in the country. A memorial honors the 38 Dakota men killed in Mankato, 110 miles (177km) from the park.\par \par \uc2 Don\u8217\'20\'19t miss this: Too old to govern? The age problem neither US party wants to talk about\par \par \uc2 The question was simple: what are your thoughts about running for re-election in 2026? \u8220\'20\'1COh,\u8221\'20\'1D said \uc2 Mitch McConnell\uc2  with a half chuckle, a mumble and then: silence. The most powerful Republican in the \uc2 US Senate\uc2  stared into space and said nothing for more than 30 seconds. It was the second time in little more than a month that 81-year-old McConnell had frozen while speaking to reporters. But there were few voices in the Democratic party calling on him to step down. The question of age is one that both party establishments in America have cause to avoid, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/sep/03/old-age-mcconnell-biden-trump-politics"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 writes David Smith}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The Democrat \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 , 80, is the oldest president in American history. The Republican \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , 77, is the second oldest and current frontrunner for the party nomination in 2024. The Senate, whose average age is 64, has one of the oldest memberships of any parliamentary body in the world. It is small wonder that dealing with America\u8217\'20\'19s drift into gerontocracy is not top of its agenda.\par \par \uc2 \u8230\'20\'26 Or this: Lonely in LA, I made a remarkable friendship with my older neighbour\par \par \uc2 If friendships are the real love stories of our lives, I can pinpoint the moment I knew Claudia was the one, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/lifeandstyle/2023/sep/03/lonely-in-la-i-made-a-remarkable-friendship-with-my-older-neighbour"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 writes Martha Hayes}}}\uc2 . It was the Saturday night I stood on her doorstep in my pyjamas. I had locked myself out of my house, while collecting a food delivery from the gate, with my two-year-old daughter, Maggie, alone inside. Claudia, who lives opposite me in Los Angeles, was calm and collected and made the necessary phone calls to help track down a spare set of keys.\par \par \uc2 My husband and I were in our late 30s when we relocated to Los Angeles in 2019, following a job offer. My mother died in 2017, and I was grieving and mentally unsettled. As a freelance writer with no driving licence, living in a city where everybody drives, the odds of making friends were stacked against me. What was I looking for? What was it that I was really lacking? I didn\u8217\'20\'19t know. Until I met Claudia who is 72 and my soulmate.\par \par \uc2 Climate check: Climate crisis poses greatest risk to people with respiratory illnesses, experts warn\par \par \uc2 The climate crisis may pose the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/environment/2023/sep/04/climate-crisis-poses-greatest-risk-to-people-with-respiratory-illnesses-experts-warn"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 greatest risks to people with respiratory illnesses}}}\uc2 , with high temperatures and changing weather patterns exacerbating lung health problems, experts have said. Air pollution is estimated to have killed 6.7 million people globally in 2019, with greenhouse gases and air pollution sharing many of the same sources.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CClimate change affects everyone\u8217\'20\'19s health, but arguably, respiratory patients are among the most vulnerable,\u8221\'20\'1D said Zorana Jovanovic Andersen, the author of the report. \u8220\'20\'1CThese are people who already experience breathing difficulties and they are far more sensitive to our changing climate. Their symptoms will become worse, and for some this will be fatal.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Sign up\par \par \uc2 First Thing is delivered to thousands of inboxes every weekday. If you\u8217\'20\'19re not already signed up, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/info/2018/sep/17/guardian-us-morning-briefing-sign-up-to-stay-informed"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 subscribe now}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Get in touch\par \par \uc2 If you have any questions or comments about any of our newsletters please email {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "mailto:newsletters@theguardian.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 newsletters@theguardian.com}}}\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020230904ej94001gu\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
