\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Proud Boys member receives 10-year prison sentence for US Capitol attack \u8211\'20\'13 as it happened\b0\par\par\uc2 Chris Stein US politics live blogger \par \uc2 6,332 \uc2 words\par \uc2 1 September 2023\par 20:17 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Dominic Pezzola\u8217\'20\'19s sentence is less than 20-year term prosecutors proposed while Ethan Nordean will also be sentenced. This blog is now closed\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.00pm BST\par \par \uc2 Closing summary\par \par \uc2 A federal judge ordered Proud Boys militia group member Dominic Pezzola {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/sep/01/proud-boys-jan-6-trump-trials-biden-politics-live-updates?page=with:block-64f212aa8f08a108316d5348#block-64f212aa8f08a108316d5348"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 to spend 10 years in prison}}}\uc2  for his violent actions on January 6, a sentence less than the 20-year term prosecutors requested. Ethan Nordean, a leader in the far-right group, is also scheduled to receive his sentence later today, and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/sep/01/proud-boys-jan-6-trump-trials-biden-politics-live-updates?page=with:block-64f1e3dd8f083bb275c22b35#block-64f1e3dd8f083bb275c22b35"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 prosecutors have asked}}}\uc2  that he be jailed for 27 years following his conviction on seditious conspiracy and other charges.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s what else happened today:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Georgia Republicans{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/sep/01/proud-boys-jan-6-trump-trials-biden-politics-live-updates?page=with:block-64f1e79a8f083bb275c22b55#block-64f1e79a8f083bb275c22b55"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 may decide to go after}}}\uc2 Fani Willis, the Democratic district attorney in the Atlanta area who last week indicted \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  and 18 others on election subversion charges.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 An effort by Trump foes to bar him from running from president because of his involvement in the January 6 insurrection {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/sep/01/proud-boys-jan-6-trump-trials-biden-politics-live-updates?page=with:block-64f227e98f08b9a6738ac7b5#block-64f227e98f08b9a6738ac7b5"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 was rejected by a federal judge}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 What does \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2  fear? A 15-year-old politics junky, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/sep/01/proud-boys-jan-6-trump-trials-biden-politics-live-updates?page=with:block-64f1fd128f08a108316d51d5#block-64f1fd128f08a108316d51d5"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 apparently}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 House Republicans{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/sep/01/proud-boys-jan-6-trump-trials-biden-politics-live-updates?page=with:block-64f239638f08b9a6738ac86d#block-64f239638f08b9a6738ac86d"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 will make security camera footage}}}\uc2  recorded on January 6 available to reporters, non-profit organizations, defendants in criminal cases and those injured in the attack. House speaker Kevin McCarthy earlier in the year gave conservative commentator \uc2 Tucker Carlson\uc2  access to the video, who used it to downplay the severity of the insurrection.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Dylan Quattrucci told police to \u8220\'20\'1Cgo hang yourself\u8221\'20\'1D on January 6. Now he works for the Trump campaign in New Hampshire, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/sep/01/proud-boys-jan-6-trump-trials-biden-politics-live-updates?page=with:block-64f1f44c8f083bb275c22c04#block-64f1f44c8f083bb275c22c04"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 according to a report}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.43pm BST\par \par \uc2 NBC News reports that 22-year-old January 6 defendant Jord Meacham has died:\par \par \uc2 enltrJan. 6 defendant Jord Meacham has died, according to a court filing. A funeral for the 22-year-old is scheduled for tomorrow, according to an obituary. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/UyW43TEdpJ"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/UyW43TEdpJ}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Ryan J. Reilly (@ryanjreilly) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/ryanjreilly/status/1697667132580913419?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 September 1, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 enltr"His passing has also been confirmed by Pretrial Services and defense counsel." {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/msyP7hasge"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/msyP7hasge}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Ryan J. Reilly (@ryanjreilly) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/ryanjreilly/status/1697667293604458855?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 September 1, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 Meacham was arrested recently, and facing relatively minor charges that usually have not resulted in jail time, NBC reports:\par \par \uc2 enltrNejourde Meacham was arrested less than a month ago, and faced the four basic misdemeanors that often result in plea deals and probationary sentences. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/gEz2yDfiki"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/gEz2yDfiki}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Ryan J. Reilly (@ryanjreilly) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/ryanjreilly/status/1697668210907124168?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 September 1, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.26pm BST\par \par \uc2 Earlier this year, Republican speaker of the House Kevin McCarthy provoked outrage by handing over footage from the January 6 insurrection recorded by Capitol security cameras to conservative commentator \uc2 Tucker Carlson\uc2  \u8211\'20\'13 who, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cnn.com/2023/03/09/politics/tucker-carlson-january-6-court-cases-us-capitol/index.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 predictably}}}\uc2 , used it to downplay the severity of the insurrection.\par \par \uc2 McCarthy later said the footage {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/mar/12/kevin-mccarthy-jan-6-footage-tucker-carlson-fox-news"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 would be \u8220\'20\'1Cslowly\u8221\'20\'1D released to networks}}}\uc2  other than Fox News, and today, Politico reports House Republicans have released the rules by which the footage can be accessed:\par \par \uc2 enltrNew: House GOP (through Loudermilk\u8217\'20\'19s Admin subcommittee) rolls out access policy for Jan. 6 Capitol security footage {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/yUHkfOz7T1"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/yUHkfOz7T1}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Jordain Carney (@jordainc) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/jordainc/status/1697686421417402710?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 September 1, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 Access is restricted to media organizations, non-profits, defendants in criminal cases related to the insurrection, their attorneys and people who were injured that day. People interested in the footage can view it on terminals set up in the Capitol complex, and request access to footage no longer than 10 minutes in length.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.07pm BST\par \par \uc2 The conservative-dominated supreme court surprised Democrats earlier this year when it ordered Alabama to draw a second majority-black congressional district. But as the Guardian\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/sam-levine"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Sam Levine}}}\uc2  and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/andrew-witherspoon"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Andrew Witherspoon}}}\uc2  report, the state\u8217\'20\'19s Republican lawmakers are doing everything they can not to obey the ruling:\par \par \uc2 Just a few months ago, the \uc2 US supreme court{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/law/2023/jun/08/supreme-court-voting-rights-decision-allen-milligan"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 issued one of its most surprising rulings}}}\uc2  in recent memory.\par \par \uc2 In a 5-4 decision in Allen v Milligan, the court {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/law/2023/jun/08/supreme-court-voting-rights-decision-allen-milligan"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 said Alabama\u8217\'20\'19s congressional map}}}\uc2  violated the 1965 Voting Rights Act because it diluted the influence of Black voters, who make up about a quarter of the state\u8217\'20\'19s population, but comprise a majority in just one of Alabama\u8217\'20\'19s congressional districts. The justices upheld a lower court\u8217\'20\'19s decision {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://redistricting.lls.edu/wp-content/uploads/AL-milligan-20220124-opinion-and-order-granting-PI.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 ordering Alabama to redraw its map}}}\uc2  \u8220\'20\'1Cto include two districts in which Black voters either comprise a voting-age majority or something quite close to it\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 It was widely seen as a major win for the Voting Rights Act, a statute that the \uc2 US supreme court\uc2  has significantly hollowed out over the last decade. It was a victory that was supposed to give the Black belt, a historically Black region in the state {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.al.com/news/2022/03/alabama-black-belts-struggle-with-poverty-a-chicken-and-egg-problem-but-there-are-solutions.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 that is among the poorest in the US}}}\uc2 , better representation in Washington.\par \par \uc2 The statute, a landmark of the civil rights movement, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.brennancenter.org/our-work/research-reports/use-section-2-secure-fair-representation"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 has been critical}}}\uc2  in increasing Black representation at all levels of government across the US.\par \par \uc2 But when Alabama\u8217\'20\'19s Republican-controlled legislature convened just a few weeks later, they ignored the mandate. Their new map still included just one majority Black district. It increased the percentage of Black voters in a second district to be around 41% Black, but continued to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.al.com/news/2017/08/what_is_the_black_belt_and_why.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 crack the Black belt}}}\uc2 , a historically Black region that stretches across the middle of Alabama, into multiple districts. Now, it is asking a federal court to approve that map and, if they don\u8217\'20\'19t, the case will probably return to the supreme court.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/sep/01/alabama-discrimination-black-voters-gerrymandering"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  How Alabama is defying the supreme court to discriminate against Black voters}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.50pm BST\par \par \uc2 When the supreme court overturned Roe v Wade last year, many conservatives welcomed the decision with the argument that \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access should be decided on a state-by-state basis. But as the Guardian\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/carter-sherman-is-a-reproductive-health-and-justice-reporter-at-guardian-us"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Carter Sherman}}}\uc2  reports, Texas Republicans are trying to override the will of local voters to ensure the procedure remains restricted throughout the country\u8217\'20\'19s second most-populous state:\par \par \uc2 After the supreme court overturned Roe v Wade last year, district attorneys from major counties in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/texas"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Texas}}}\uc2  vowed not to vigorously prosecute people under the state\u8217\'20\'19s anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  laws.\par \par \uc2 Now, Texas has a plan to punish them if they don\u8217\'20\'19t fall in line.\par \par \uc2 On Friday, Texas will enact Senate Bill 20, a law that forbids prosecutors from adopting a \u8220\'20\'1Cpolicy\u8221\'20\'1D of refusing to prosecute particular types of crimes, such as \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  cases. Under the new law, these policies constitute \u8220\'20\'1Cofficial misconduct\u8221\'20\'1D and could lead to prosecutors being removed from office.\par \par \uc2 This kind of legislation flies in the face of prosecutors\u8217\'20\'19 normal ability to choose whether and how to pursue cases, said Miriam Krinsky, executive director of Fair and Just Prosecution, an organization that works to support local prosecutors. Krinsky called the new law \u8220\'20\'1Cscare tactics\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThis is not about seeking to see enforcement of laws,\u8221\'20\'1D said Krinsky, a former federal prosecutor. \u8220\'20\'1CThis is about trying to erode the rights of individuals to make choices around their own personal healthcare. And that is incredibly sad, because the collateral damage of that political agenda is the erosion of democratic principles.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Laws like Senate Bill 20 are the latest volley in a long series of battles about the role of small government in regulating \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 . Before the supreme court overturned Roe and abolished national protections for \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights, opponents of the procedure had long argued that states should be allowed to write their own \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  laws. Now, however, some powerful anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  groups like Susan B Anthony Pro-Life America are calling for federal \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  restrictions, such as a 15-week ban.\par \par \uc2 Texas is far from the only state where prosecutors have said that they will refuse to go after people for violating \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  bans. Within days of Roe\u8217\'20\'19s overturning, 90 elected prosecutors released a statement \u8211\'20\'13 organized by Fair and Just Prosecution \u8211\'20\'13publicly announcing that they would \u8220\'20\'1Crefrain from prosecuting those who seek, provide, or support abortions\u8221\'20\'1D. (US \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  bans typically penalize individuals who provide abortions or help others get the procedure, rather than \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  patients.)\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/sep/01/texas-law-punish-prosecutors-abortion-cases"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Texas law aims to punish prosecutors who refuse to pursue \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  cases}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.35pm BST\par \par \uc2 The Guardian\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s Maya Yang{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2023/sep/01/canada-us-travel-warning-advisory-lgbtq"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reports}}}\uc2  on how Canadian LGBTQ+ rights and civil liberties organizations are speaking out about the rise in hostile laws and hate crimes in the United States.\par \par \uc2 Earlier this week, the \uc2 Canadian government\uc2  warned LGBTQ+ Canadian citizens about the risks of visiting the US due to a growing wave of anti-LGBTQ+ laws.\par \par \uc2 In an {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2023/aug/31/canada-travel-warning-lgbtq-residents-us"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 updated travel advisory}}}\uc2 , the government wrote that \u8220\'20\'1Csome states have enacted laws and politics that may affect [LBGTQ+] persons. Check relevant state and local laws.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 It {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://travel.gc.ca/travelling/health-safety/lgbt-travel"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 warned}}}\uc2  LGBTQ+ Canadians to \u8220\'20\'1Cwatch for laws that criminalise same-sex activities and relationships\u8221\'20\'1D, as well as laws that \u8220\'20\'1Ccriminalise people based on their sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, and sex characteristics\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.hrc.org/press-releases/roundup-of-anti-lgbtq-legislation-advancing-in-states-across-the-country"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 According to}}}\uc2  the \uc2 Human Rights Campaign\uc2 , the largest US LGBTQ+ advocacy group, as of May, more than 520 anti-LGBTQ+ bills had been introduced in state legislatures. More than 220 bills specifically targeted transgender and non-binary youth while a record 70 anti-LGBTQ+ laws had been officially enacted.\par \par \uc2 Speaking to the Guardian, Helen Kennedy, executive director of Egale Canada, one of the country\u8217\'20\'19s leading LGBTQ+ organizations, said: \u8220\'20\'1CWe\u8217\'20\'19re pleased that our government has issued this advisory. \u8220\'20\'1CI think it\u8217\'20\'19s important for members of our LGBTQ community here in Canada to understand the issue \u8230\'20\'26\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt is somewhat alarming when the neighbor is imposing and enacting these pieces of legislation. I would encourage people to be very aware of where they\u8217\'20\'19re going and what the laws are in those states. If they don\u8217\'20\'19t have to go, go somewhere else.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.14pm BST\par \par \uc2 A federal judge in Florida has dismissed a lawsuit seeking to rule \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  ineligible for a second term in the White House, for his role in the 6 January insurrection.\par \par \uc2 The district court judge Robin Rosenberg, an Obama appointee, said in a written ruling that the plaintiffs, including Florida attorney Lawrence Caplan, lacked standing to bring the suit, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.sun-sentinel.com/2023/09/01/federal-judge-dismisses-florida-lawsuit-seeking-to-have-trump-declared-ineligible-for-presidency/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 according to the Sun-Sentinel}}}\uc2  newspaper.\par \par \uc2 Caplan told the paper he was \u8220\'20\'1Cnot surprised\u8221\'20\'1D and didn\u8217\'20\'19t plan to appeal \u8220\'20\'1Cbecause that\u8217\'20\'19s not going to go anywhere\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 The suit, in district court in Palm Beach county, where Trump resides, said the 14th amendment to the US constitution barred those who had engaged in insurrection against the US from holding elected office.\par \par \uc2 Many legal scholars {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/aug/20/trump-disqualified-constitution-section-3-14th-amendment"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 say the argument is sound}}}\uc2 , though some believe it was implemented only to prevent Confederates on the losing side in the civil war from holding office again.\par \par \uc2 ABC News {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://abcnews.go.com/Politics/state-election-officials-prepare-efforts-disqualify-trump-14th/story?id=102833123"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reported on Friday}}}\uc2  that similar lawsuits are being prepared in several swing states, including Arizona, Michigan and New Hampshire.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.50pm BST\par \par \uc2 Richard Luscombe reports on the Proud Boys January 6 sentencing hearing in Washington today:\par \par \uc2 A member of the far-right Proud Boys militia group who took part in the 6 January 2021 attack on the US Capitol with the intention of keeping \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  in the White House was sentenced to a lengthy prison term on Friday, as another waited to learn his fate.\par \par \uc2 Dominic Pezzola, who attacked a police officer and was filmed using the officer\u8217\'20\'19s shield to smash a window, received 10 years from the federal judge Timothy Kelly in Washington DC, following his {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/may/04/proud-boys-convicted-seditious-conspiracy-capitol-attack"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 conviction in May}}}\uc2  for assault and obstructing an official proceeding. Prosecutors had sought a 20-year term.\par \par \uc2 Ethan Nordean, described by prosecutors as a leader of the extremist group, was to be sentenced later for crimes, including seditious conspiracy, committed when thousands of Trump supporters overran the Capitol building.\par \par \uc2 The pair, described by prosecutors as \u8220\'20\'1Cfoot soldiers of the right [who] aimed to keep their leader in power\u8221\'20\'1D, were part of a mob seeking to disrupt the certification by a joint session of Congress of \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s victory in the 2020 presidential election. Nine deaths have been linked to the riot, including law enforcement suicides.\par \par \uc2 Sentencing Pezzola, Kelly said: \u8220\'20\'1CYou were the one who smashed that window and let people begin to stream into that Capitol building and threaten the lives of our lawmakers. It\u8217\'20\'19s not something I would have ever dreamed I would have seen in our country.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Pezzola told the court he was \u8220\'20\'1Ca changed and humbled man\u8221\'20\'1D, his \u8220\'20\'1Csorrow and regret \u8230\'20\'26 unimaginable\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 His sentence was among the lengthiest handed down to those convicted of offences linked to the Capitol attack, in which 140 police officers were injured.\par \par \uc2 Pezzola, of Rochester, New York, posted to social media a profanity-laced video of himself inside the Capitol, smoking a cigar.\par \par \uc2 Prosecutors asked for a 27-year term for Nordean, of Auburn, Washington.\par \par \uc2 Read on:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/sep/01/proud-boys-dominic-pezzola-jan-6-attack"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Proud Boys member who smashed Capitol window given 10-year sentence}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.30pm BST\par \par \uc2 Some interesting nuggets \u8211\'20\'13 of news rather than reconstituted chicken \u8211\'20\'13 have emerged from an interview between \uc2 Tucker Carlson\uc2 , once of Fox News, and \uc2 Dave Portnoy\uc2 , still of another controversial rightwing outlet, \uc2 Barstool Sports\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Last week, Carlson\u8217\'20\'19s interview with \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  played as counter-programming to the first Republican presidential primary debate, in Milwaukee, Wisconsin. Trump has saluted the success of that gambit, and indeed remains miles ahead in the polls. But, it turns out, Carlson thinks both that Trump should have debated and that, at 77, the former president is too old to return to the White House.\par \par \uc2 Part of Carlson\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/TuckerCarlson/status/1697378139729539549"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 interview with Portnoy on X}}}\uc2 , the website formerly known as \uc2 Twitter\uc2 , now Carlson\u8217\'20\'19s home, went like this:\par \par \uc2 Portnoy: \u8220\'20\'1CTo me, if you\u8217\'20\'19re voting on the president you want to hear him debate. He\u8217\'20\'19s brilliant. He\u8217\'20\'19s the best to ever play the political game. So to become president, I think it was the right move not to do it. But for the betterment of country, I think you should be on it.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Carlson: \u8220\'20\'1CI kind of agree. I like the debates, personally.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Portnoy: \u8220\'20\'1CI mean, how else are people gonna decide?\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Carlson: \u8220\'20\'1CThe problem is that the news companies that host the debates\u8221\'20\'1D \u8211\'20\'13 Fox News hosted the first one, four months after letting Carlson go \u8211\'20\'13 \u8220\'20\'1Care so rotten and corrupt, and everybody knows it. The whole thing\u8217\'20\'19s wrong. The whole thing is rotten through.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Portnoy: \u8220\'20\'1C\u8230\'20\'26 I mean, to be honest, I think both Trump and Biden are too old \u8230\'20\'26 I don\u8217\'20\'19t think you should be able to be that old to be president.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Carlson: \u8220\'20\'1CI agree 100%.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 It\u8217\'20\'19s not quite at the level of the Carlson text messages that were revealed in the Dominion lawsuit over Fox News\u8217\'20\'19 broadcast of Trump\u8217\'20\'19s election lies \u8211\'20\'13 \u8220\'20\'1CWe are very, very close to being able to ignore Trump most nights,\u8221\'20\'1D {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/2023/03/08/business/media/tucker-carlson-trump.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the host wrote}}}\uc2 , \u8220\'20\'1CI truly can\u8217\'20\'19t wait. I hate him passionately\u8221\'20\'1D \u8211\'20\'13 but it might still land with a bit of a damp thud at Trump campaign HQ.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.05pm BST\par \par \uc2 The day so far\par \par \uc2 A federal judge has ordered Proud Boys militia group member Dominic Pezzola to spend 10 years in prison for his violent actions on January 6, a sentence less than the 20-year term prosecutors requested. Ethan Nordean, a leader in the far-right group, is scheduled to receive his sentence later today, and prosecutors have asked that he be jailed for 27 years following his conviction on seditious conspiracy and other charges.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s what else has happened today so far:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Georgia Republicans{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/sep/01/proud-boys-jan-6-trump-trials-biden-politics-live-updates?page=with:block-64f1e79a8f083bb275c22b55#block-64f1e79a8f083bb275c22b55"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 may decide to go after}}}\uc2 Fani Willis, the Democratic district attorney in the Atlanta area who last week indicted \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  and 18 others on election subversion charges.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 What does \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2  fear? A 15-year-old politics junky, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/sep/01/proud-boys-jan-6-trump-trials-biden-politics-live-updates?page=with:block-64f1fd128f08a108316d51d5#block-64f1fd128f08a108316d51d5"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 apparently}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Dylan Quattrucci told police to \u8220\'20\'1Cgo hang yourself\u8221\'20\'1D on January 6. Now he works for the Trump campaign in New Hampshire, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/sep/01/proud-boys-jan-6-trump-trials-biden-politics-live-updates?page=with:block-64f1f44c8f083bb275c22c04#block-64f1f44c8f083bb275c22c04"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 according to a report}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.54pm BST\par \par \uc2 After sentencing Dominic Pezzola to spend 10 years in prison for his actions on January 6, Politico reports federal judge Timothy Kelly took a moment to point out the difference between the attack on the Capitol and the violence {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2020/oct/31/americans-killed-protests-political-unrest-acled"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 that sometimes occurred}}}\uc2  during racial justice protests in the summer of 2020:\par \par \uc2 enltrKELLY briefly addresses comparison between Jan. 6 cases and other riot/protest cases such as BLM or Portland related cases.\par \par \uc2 He says comparisons are often inapt because Jan. 6 has a constitutional element \u8212\'20\'14 a fraught moment during transfer of power \u8212\'20\'14 that was unique.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Kyle Cheney (@kyledcheney) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/kyledcheney/status/1697651096984965424?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 September 1, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 Most of the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2020/jun/06/protests-george-floyd-black-lives-matter-saturday"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 protests that followed the death of }}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2020/jun/06/protests-george-floyd-black-lives-matter-saturday"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 George Floyd}}}\uc2  in May 2020 were peaceful. However, allies of \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  have often invoked instances of looting or fighting that occasionally happened during the nationwide demonstrations to downplay the severity of the attack on the Capitol months later.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 5.57pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.37pm BST\par \par \uc2 Proud Boys member Dominic Pezzola receives 10-year prison sentence - report\par \par \uc2 Federal judge Timothy Kelly has sentenced Proud Boys militia member Dominic Pezzola to spend 10 years in prison for his actions during the January 6 attack, Politico reports:\par \par \uc2 enltrKELLY sentences Pezzola to *10 years* in prison for his role on Jan. 6.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Kyle Cheney (@kyledcheney) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/kyledcheney/status/1697648872330342920?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 September 1, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 The sentence is less than the 20-year term prosecutors had proposed. During the insurrection, Pezzola was captured on video using a stolen police riot shield to break a window at the Capitol. He was convicted of several crimes, including assaulting a police officer and obstructing an official proceeding.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.34pm BST\par \par \uc2 Federal judge Timothy Kelly is now addressing Proud Boys member Dominic Pezzola at his sentencing hearing, Politico reports:\par \par \uc2 enltrKELLY: "That day broke our tradition of peacefully transferring power, which is among the most precious things we had as Americans. Notice I said \u8216\'20\'18had\u8217\'20\'19 because \u8230\'20\'26our tradition of unbroken peaceful transfers of power, that string has been broken."\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Kyle Cheney (@kyledcheney) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/kyledcheney/status/1697646965784293770?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 September 1, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 enltrKELLY: "You were the one who smashed that window and let people begin to stream, into that Capitol building and threaten the lives of our lawmakers. It\u8217\'20\'19s not something I would have ever dreamed I would have seen in our country.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Kyle Cheney (@kyledcheney) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/kyledcheney/status/1697647389727764629?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 September 1, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.19pm BST\par \par \uc2 Politico reports that Dominic Pezzola is addressing the court as a judge in Washington DC weighs how long he should spend in prison for his actions on January 6.\par \par \uc2 Pezzola was convicted of several crimes, including obstruction of an official proceeding and assaulting an officer, and prosecutors have recommended he receive a 20-year prison sentence.\par \par \uc2 As defendants in these case often do, Pezzola expressed remorse when addressing the judge:\par \par \uc2 enltrPEZZOLA now addressing Judge Kelly, says some of his remarks may be "tough to get through."\par \par \uc2 "I stand before you today as a changed and humbled man."\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Kyle Cheney (@kyledcheney) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/kyledcheney/status/1697640709891772611?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 September 1, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 enltrPEZZOLA now addressing his family, regretting missing his daughter's high school graduation, getting her driver's license.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CTo my beloved wife Lisa. I have broken this family and crushed your heart. My sorrow and regret is unimaginable.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Kyle Cheney (@kyledcheney) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/kyledcheney/status/1697641603546906887?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 September 1, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 enltrPEZZOLA acknowledges the dark stain on history that his actions helped cause, apologizes to the officer he assaulted, Mark Ode, and says "I never should have crossed the barrier at the Capitol that day."\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Kyle Cheney (@kyledcheney) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/kyledcheney/status/1697642294671732897?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 September 1, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 Assistant US attorney Erik Kenerson reminded the judge of Pezzola\u8217\'20\'19s actions during the attack, particularly how he broke into the Capitol with a stolen police riot shield, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cnn.com/2023/04/19/politics/dominic-pezzola-testimony/index.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a now-famous image}}}\uc2  from the insurrection:\par \par \uc2 enltrAUSA Kenerson says when Americans have anxiety during transfer of power in 2024, "The image of Mr. Pezzola breaking that window" will be among the ones "that many Americans think of when that wave of fear hits them."\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Kyle Cheney (@kyledcheney) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/kyledcheney/status/1697633366525305042?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 September 1, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.59pm BST\par \par \uc2 We\u8217\'20\'19re expecting \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  to soon speak about the government\u8217\'20\'19s August employment report that came out a few hours ago, which shows employment growth remaining steady in the world\u8217\'20\'19s largest economy, despite the sting of high interest rates, as the Guardian\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/lauren-aratani"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Lauren Aratani}}}\uc2  reports:\par \par \uc2 The US jobs market is holding steady as interest rates sit at a 22-year high, with US employers adding 187,000 jobs in August, according to the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.bls.gov/news.release/empsit.nr0.htm"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Bureau of Labor Statistics}}}\uc2  (\uc2 BLS\uc2 ).\par \par \uc2 The number of new jobs added in August is the same as the number of new jobs in July, showing that the labor market, down to levels seen before the pandemic, is resilient even with high interest rates.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 Federal Reserve\uc2  is closely monitoring the jobs market and other indicators that point to whether the economy is slowing down and inflation is dropping toward their target level. The Fed in July raised interest rates for the 11th time in under two years, bringing rates up to a range of 5.25% to 5.5%, making mortgage rates and other loans more expensive.\par \par \uc2 Even at the beginning of this year, employers were adding as many as 517,000 jobs a month, as seen in February. But over the last few months, the number of new jobs has started to slow.\par \par \uc2 In August, the unemployment rate was 3.8%, the highest it\u8217\'20\'19s been in over a year. The unemployment rate has been holding relatively steady over the last year, reaching a record low of 3.4% in February and then coming down again during the spring and summer.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://interactive.guim.co.uk/uploader/embed/2023/09/archive-zip/giv-13425uckNXYarDtcQ/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Interactive}}}\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/business/2023/sep/01/us-jobs-report-august-2023-inflation"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 US adds 187,000 jobs in August as market holds steady}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.39pm BST\par \par \uc2 As we await the sentencing of Proud Boys militia group member Dominic Pezzola, former Washington DC police office \uc2 Michael Fanone\uc2  shared his thoughts on the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/aug/31/joseph-biggs-sentenced-proud-boys-jan-6"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 prison terms handed down yesterday}}}\uc2  against two other members of the group.\par \par \uc2 Fanone was beaten by the mob on January 6 as he attempted to defend the Capitol, and has since become outspoken against \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  and his allies\u8217\'20\'19 efforts to downplay the insurrection. Here\u8217\'20\'19s what he had to say about yesterday\u8217\'20\'19s sentences, from CNN:\par \par \uc2 enltrOfficer Fanone weighs in after two leaders of the Proud Boys were sentenced to 17 and 15 years in prison today, some of the longest sentences stemming from the Capitol attack. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/rASACcevbR"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/rASACcevbR}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Kaitlan Collins (@kaitlancollins) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/kaitlancollins/status/1697429258006618563?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 September 1, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.16pm BST\par \par \uc2 DeSantis security followed, blocked questions from 15-year-old - report Quinn Mitchell asks \uc2 Chris Christie\uc2  a question in Concord, New Hampshire on 24 July 2023, as the former New Jersey governor campaigns for the Republican presidential nomination. Photograph: Cj Gunther/\uc2 EPA\par \par \uc2 Security guards for \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2  followed and physically blocked 15-year-old politics enthusiast Quinn Mitchell from speaking with the Florida governor during campaign events in New Hampshire, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.thedailybeast.com/republican-president-candidate-ron-desantis-is-afraid-of-questions-from-15-year-old-quinn-mitchell"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the Daily Beast reports}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Since 2019, Mitchell has shown up to presidential events in the Granite State to ask candidates questions, and has often received a positive response from politicians who admire his civic mindedness. But after asking DeSantis whether \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  \u8220\'20\'1Cviolated the peaceful transfer of power\u8221\'20\'1D \u8211\'20\'13 and getting a nonresponse in return from the governor \u8211\'20\'13 Mitchell says his security singled him out at campaign events:\par \par \uc2 Speaking about it for the first time in an interview with The Daily Beast, Mitchell says that he was grabbed and physically intimidated by DeSantis security at two subsequent campaign stops, where the candidate\u8217\'20\'19s staffers also monitored him in a way he perceived as hostile.\par \par \uc2 The experience, Mitchell said, was \u8220\'20\'1Chorrifying\u8221\'20\'1D and amounted to \u8220\'20\'1Cintimidation.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 At a Fourth of July parade DeSantis attended, Mitchell was swarmed by security and physically restrained after a brief interaction with the governor\u8212\'20\'14with his private security contractors even demanding Mitchell stay put until they said so.\par \par \uc2 With his mother alarmed, the situation escalated to such a degree that the candidate\u8217\'20\'19s wife, Casey, spoke directly with her\u8212\'20\'14but to suggest her son was being dishonest about what happened, according to Mitchell.\par \par \uc2 Then, at an August 19 event\u8212\'20\'14where Mitchell was tailed closely by two security guards\u8212\'20\'14an attendee told The Daily Beast they saw a staffer for DeSantis\u8217\'20\'19 super PAC, Never Back Down, take a photo of the teenager on Snapchat before typing out an ominous caption: \u8220\'20\'1CGot our kid.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Seven other sources corroborated Mitchell\u8217\'20\'19s version of events, either by sharing contemporaneous communications with the family or recounting what they witnessed in person at DeSantis events, including the Fourth of July parade. The teenager and his family say they have yet to receive any kind of apology from DeSantis.\par \par \uc2 The DeSantis campaign and Never Back Down did not return multiple requests for comment from The Daily Beast.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CReally stupid in a small state like New Hampshire,\u8221\'20\'1D Mitchell deadpanned about the guards\u8217\'20\'19 behavior. Indeed, the story has the potential to create an avoidable headache for DeSantis, whose campaign for the Republican presidential nomination is going far worse than expected. Despite early momentum and strong fundraising, most polls in the state and nationwide show the Florida governor in a very distant second place to Trump among GOP voters.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.49pm BST\par \par \uc2 The Guardian\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/martin-pengelly"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Martin Pengelly}}}\uc2  reports that former allies are turning their backs on \uc2 Rudy Giuliani\uc2 , the former New York City mayor and Republican presidential candidate who was last week indicted in Georgia for trying to overturn its 2020 election result:\par \par \uc2 As he attempts to meet mounting legal fees incurred in large part through his work for \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/rudygiuliani"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Rudy Giuliani}}}\uc2  will reportedly not get \u8220\'20\'1Ca nickel\u8221\'20\'1D from one billionaire who backed his campaign for the 2008 Republican presidential nomination \u8211\'20\'13 or, apparently, much from many other previously big donors.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI wouldn\u8217\'20\'19t give him a nickel,\u8221\'20\'1D the investor \uc2 Leon Cooperman{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cnbc.com/2023/08/31/giuliani-loses-financial-support-of-billionaires-langone-cooperman.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 told CNBC}}}\uc2 . \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19m very negative on \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 . It\u8217\'20\'19s an American tragedy. [Rudy] was \u8216\'20\'18America\u8217\'20\'19s mayor\u8217\'20\'19. He did a great job. And like everybody else who gets involved with Trump, it turns to shit.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Brian France, a former Nascar chief executive, was slightly more conciliatory. But he {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cnbc.com/2023/08/31/giuliani-loses-financial-support-of-billionaires-langone-cooperman.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 told the same outlet}}}\uc2  his wallet was staying shut: \u8220\'20\'1CI was a major supporter of Rudy in 2008 and at other times. I\u8217\'20\'19m not sure what happen[ed] but I miss the old Rudy. I\u8217\'20\'19m wishing him well.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  happened to Rudy.\par \par \uc2 Giuliani, now 79, was once a crusading US attorney who became New York mayor in 1993 and led the city on 9/11 and after. Capitalising on the resultant \u8220\'20\'1CAmerica\u8217\'20\'19s mayor\u8221\'20\'1D tag, he ran for the Republican nomination to succeed President \uc2 George W Bush\uc2 . Briefly leading the polls, he {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.opensecrets.org/pres08/summary.php?cycle=2008&cid=n00009908"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 raised $60m}}}\uc2  but {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2008/jan/30/usa.rudygiuliani"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 flamed out}}}\uc2  when the race got serious.\par \par \uc2 When Giuliani struggled with drink and depression, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/books/2022/aug/24/donald-trump-secret-mar-a-lago-stay-rudy-giuliani-drink-depression-wife-andrew-kirtzman-book"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 his former wife has said}}}\uc2 , Trump gave him shelter. When Trump himself entered presidential politics, in 2016, Giuliani became a vociferous surrogate. When Trump entered the White House, Giuliani {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2016/nov/25/trump-secretary-of-state-rudy-giuliani-mitt-romney"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 failed}}}\uc2  to be named secretary of state but did become the president\u8217\'20\'19s aide and attorney.\par \par \uc2 In that capacity his actions fueled Trump\u8217\'20\'19s first impeachment, over attempts to find dirt on opponents {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/jun/07/rudy-giuliani-ukraine-officials-audio-joe-biden"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 in Ukraine}}}\uc2 , and he helped drive the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2020/nov/19/rudy-giuliani-dye-my-cousin-vinny-press-conference"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 hapless attempt}}}\uc2  to overturn Trump\u8217\'20\'19s defeat by \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  in 2020, which has spawned numerous criminal charges.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/sep/01/rudy-giuliani-donor-trump-legal-fees"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \u8216\'20\'18I wouldn\u8217\'20\'19t give him a nickel\u8217\'20\'19: one-time Giuliani donors rule out legal aid}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.34pm BST\par \par \uc2 Republican politicians have a long record of claiming to be the party that supports the police, but {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nbcnews.com/politics/donald-trump/trump-aide-dylan-quattrucci-police-go-hang-jan-6-riot-rcna99437"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 as NBC News reports}}}\uc2 , a man who told officers to \u8220\'20\'1Cgo hang yourself\u8221\'20\'1D on January 6 is currently working for \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s presidential campaign.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIf you are a police officer and are going to abide by unconstitutional bulls---, I want you to do me a favor right now and go hang yourself, because you\u8217\'20\'19re a piece of s---,\u8221\'20\'1D said Dylan Quattrucci, the deputy state director of Trump\u8217\'20\'19s campaign in New Hampshire, in a video he recorded on January 6 near the Capitol. \u8220\'20\'1CGo f--- yourself.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Quattrucci\u8217\'20\'19s position makes him the number-two figure in Trump\u8217\'20\'19s campaign in the state, which is the second to vote in the GOP\u8217\'20\'19s nominating process. Trump is currently the frontrunner is most polls of Republican primary voters, both nationwide and in New Hampshire.\par \par \uc2 The video was first posted on \uc2 Twitter\uc2  by \u8220\'20\'1CSedition Hunters\u8221\'20\'1D, an online group focused on tracking down participants in the January 6 attack. NBC News reports there\u8217\'20\'19s no evidence Quattrucci entered the Capitol itself, though on his \uc2 Twitter\uc2  account, he does have a picture of himself posing with Trump at a New Hampshire campaign office.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.41pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.10pm BST\par \par \uc2 Sentencing begins for Proud Boy Dominic Pezzola\par \par \uc2 The sentencing hearing for Dominic Pezzola, a member of the Proud Boys militia group convicted of serious charges related to the January 6 insurrection, has begun in Washington DC, Politico reports:\par \par \uc2 enltrHAPPENING NOW: Proud Boy Dominic PEZZOLA, who committed one of the most memorable acts on Jan. 6 when he smashed a Senate window with a stolen police riot shield \u8212\'20\'14 and then lit up a victory cigar in the Capitol \u8212\'20\'14 is in the courtroom and prepared to face sentencing. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/oL7akLJxcp"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/oL7akLJxcp}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Kyle Cheney (@kyledcheney) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/kyledcheney/status/1697611074818757027?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 September 1, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 Prosecutors are requesting a 20-year prison sentence for Pezzola, which, if granted, would be the longest handed out to any defendant related to the attack on the Capitol.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.55pm BST\par \par \uc2 There\u8217\'20\'19s no telling how the state and federal cases against \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  and others for trying to overturn the 2020 polls will end, but as the Associated Press reports, the environment for election workers nationwide has grown much more hostile in recent years:\par \par \uc2 More than a dozen people nationally have been charged with threatening election workers by a justice department unit trying to stem the tide of violent and graphic threats against people who count and secure the vote.\par \par \uc2 Government employees are being {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/nov/01/us-election-workers-threats-violence"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 bombarded with threats}}}\uc2  even in normally quiet periods between elections, secretaries of state and experts warn. Some point to \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  and his allies repeatedly and falsely claiming the 2020 election was stolen and spreading conspiracy theories about election workers. Experts fear the 2024 election could be worse and want the justice department to do more to protect election workers.\par \par \uc2 The justice department had created the taskforce in 2021 led by its public integrity section, which investigates election crimes. John Keller, the unit\u8217\'20\'19s second in command, said in an interview with the Associated Press the department hoped its prosecutions would deter others from threatening election workers.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThis isn\u8217\'20\'19t going to be taken lightly. It\u8217\'20\'19s not going to be trivialized,\u8221\'20\'1D he said. \u8220\'20\'1CFederal judges, the courts are taking misconduct seriously and the punishments are going to be commensurate with the seriousness of the conduct.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 More people are expected to plead guilty on Thursday to threatening election workers in Arizona and Georgia.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/aug/31/election-workers-threat-justice-department-taskforce"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 More than a dozen people charged by US unit for threatening election workers}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.35pm BST\par \par \uc2 Georgia Republicans could target DA who indicted Trump for election subversion\par \par \uc2 Georgia\u8217\'20\'19s Republican governor \uc2 Brian Kemp{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/aug/31/donald-trump-net-worth-mitch-mcconnell-us-politics-live-updates?page=with:block-64f0b28e8f083bb275c21ff6#block-64f0b28e8f083bb275c21ff6"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 yesterday rejected a call}}}\uc2  from a handful of rightwing lawmakers to convene a special session of the state legislature with the intention of removing \uc2 Fani Willis\uc2 , the Fulton county district attorney who indicted \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  and 18 others for trying to overturn the state\u8217\'20\'19s elections three years ago.\par \par \uc2 But as the Guardian\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/jewel-wicker"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Jewel Wicker}}}\uc2  reports, Willis may not be out of the woods yet:\par \par \uc2 Republicans at the state and federal levels are calling for multiple tactics to unseat \uc2 Fani Willis\uc2 , the Fulton county district attorney, even if their legal standing is murky and they lack the support of Georgia\u8217\'20\'19s Republican governor.\par \par \uc2 Steve Gooch, the Georgia senate majority leader, and Clint Dixon, a state senator, have {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.ajc.com/politics/politics-blog/georgia-senate-leader-seeking-ways-to-sanction-tainted-willis-over-trump-charges/PP34EF3CS5B77F5XJ3WMTAW7KQ/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  said }}}\uc2  they plan to use a commission designed to discipline and potentially remove rogue prosecutors to investigate Willis following her indictment of \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  for attempting to reverse the results of the 2020 election.\par \par \uc2 In May, Governor \uc2 Brian Kemp{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/may/05/georgia-brian-kemp-bill-remove-local-prosecutors"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  signed a bill}}}\uc2 , SB92, that makes it easier to remove elected district attorneys. Under the law, a prosecuting attorneys qualifications commission has the power to investigate complaints and discipline or remove district attorneys whom the appointed commissioners believe are not properly enforcing the law.\par \par \uc2 Kemp on Thursday {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.ajc.com/politics/kemp-rejects-talk-of-special-session-warns-of-risks-of-punishing-fani-willis/I4JZYJIORNACFKY2COSFE3VCSI/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 dismissed talk }}}\uc2  of using the commission or the legislature to remove Willis from office, but said the decision was not his. \u8220\'20\'1CUp to this point, I have not seen any evidence that DA Willis\u8217\'20\'19s actions or lack thereof warrant action by the prosecuting attorney oversight commission, but that will ultimately be a decision that the commission will make,\u8221\'20\'1D the governor said.\par \par \uc2 The commission will begin receiving complaints on 1 October 2023, and earlier this month Burt Jones, the Republican lieutenant governor, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://ltgov.georgia.gov/press-releases/2023-08-04/lt-governor-jones-announces-appointments-prosecuting-attorneys"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 announced}}}\uc2  three appointments to the eight-member group. Jones, who served as one of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/aug/05/trump-fake-electors-georgia"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  Georgia\u8217\'20\'19s fake electors}}}\uc2  when he was a state senator in 2020, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.unionrecorder.com/news/lt-gov-burt-jones-says-he-wasn-t-surprised-by-trump-indictments/article_de1aa006-466b-11ee-bb0f-a3d78d366aa5.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  recently criticized}}}\uc2  Willis\u8217\'20\'19s prosecution of Trump and said her treatment of the defendants like criminals is \u8220\'20\'1Cvery disturbing\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/sep/01/georgia-republicans-fani-willis-unseat"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Republican state senators seek new path to unseating Georgia DA Fani Willis}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.16pm BST\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.reuters.com/legal/us-judge-sentence-two-more-proud-boys-jan-6-attack-capitol-2023-09-01/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 more from Reuters}}}\uc2  on the two Proud Boys who are being sentenced today, and what they were found guilty of:\par \par \uc2 The first Proud Boy to face sentencing on Friday morning, Dominic Pezzola, did not play a leadership role in the group and was the only defendant of five to be acquitted of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.reuters.com/legal/jury-convicts-proud-boys-members-seditious-conspiracy-us-capitol-attack-2023-05-04/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 seditious conspiracy}}}\uc2 . He was convicted of other felonies including obstructing an official proceeding and assaulting police.\par \par \uc2 The second defendant, Ethan Nordean, was a leader of the group who was convicted of seditious conspiracy and other crimes.\par \par \uc2 Thousands of Trump supporters attacked the Capitol following a speech in which the Republican falsely claimed that his November 2020 election defeat was the result of widespread fraud. Trump has continued to make those false claims even as he leads the Republican race for the 2024 nomination to challenge Democrat Biden.\par \par \uc2 Five people including a police officer died during or shortly after the riot and more than 140 police officers were injured. The Capitol suffered millions of dollars in damage.\par \par \uc2 The sentencing of Pezzola and Nordean follows U.S. District Judge Timothy Kelly on Thursday ordering two other former {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.reuters.com/legal/former-proud-boys-leaders-could-face-longest-sentences-yet-us-capitol-attack-2023-08-31/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Proud Boys}}}\uc2  leaders, Joseph Biggs and Zachary Rehl, to serve 17 years and 15 years in prison, respectively.\par \par \uc2 Biggs\u8217\'20\'19 term is just one year less than the 18 years former Oath Keepers founder Stewart Rhodes received earlier this year.\par \par \uc2 The sentences for Biggs and Rehl were far less than the 33-year and 30-year terms sought by federal prosecutors.\par \par \uc2 The government is seeking a 20-year prison term for Pezzola and a 27-year term for Nordean.\par \par \uc2 Although Pezzola was found not guilty of sedition, prosecutors said his assault on former Capitol Police Officer Mark Ode, in which he stole Ode\u8217\'20\'19s riot shield and used it to smash at a window at the Capitol, helps to justify a lengthy prison term.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CPezzola\u8217\'20\'19s actions and testimony leave no doubt that he intended to influence or affect the conduct of government by intimidation or coercion,\u8221\'20\'1D prosecutors wrote in their sentencing memo. \u8220\'20\'1CHe committed crimes of terrorism on January 6.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Pezzola\u8217\'20\'19s attorneys are asking for their client to be sentenced to around five years in prison, and said in their sentencing memo that he has already served about three years in jail awaiting trial.\par \par \uc2 Nordean\u8217\'20\'19s attorney, \uc2 Nick Smith\uc2 , plans to argue for a lower sentence within the range of 15-21 months.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CNordean walked in and out of the Capitol like hundreds of Class B misdemeanants,\u8221\'20\'1D Smith wrote. \u8220\'20\'1CWhen the government does distinguish Nordean\u8217\'20\'19s actions from any other January 6 defendant\u8217\'20\'19s, it relies on characterization, not facts.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.56pm BST\par \par \uc2 Two more Proud Boys face sentencing on January 6 charges\par \par \uc2 Good morning, US politics blog readers. Today, two more members of the Proud Boys militia group will be sentenced by a federal judge on charges related to the January 6 insurrection. Prosecutors are requesting a 27-year prison sentence for Ethan Nordean, a chapter president in the group, after his conviction for seditious conspiracy and other crimes, and a 20-year sentence for Dominic Pezzola, who was acquitted of that charge but convicted of other offenses related to the violent attack on the Capitol.\par \par \uc2 Yesterday, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/aug/31/joseph-biggs-sentenced-proud-boys-jan-6"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a judge sentenced}}}\uc2  former Proud Boys organizer Joseph Biggs to 17 years behind bars, and handed a 15-year sentence to Zachary Rehl, a leader of the group. Both men were convicted of seditious conspiracy, a civil war-era offense that is rarely brought. Their sentences were the second- and third-longest handed down from the attack on the Capitol, and two other members of the group, including its former leader, \uc2 Enrique Tarrio\uc2 , are scheduled to be sentenced next week.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s what else is happening today:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Just-released government data shows better-than-expect hiring in August but the unemployment rate ticking up to 3.8%. \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  will speak about the report at 11.15am eastern time.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 More defendants in the Georgia election subversion case may opt to skip next week\u8217\'20\'19s in-person arraignment and enter their pleas in writing. \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  did so yesterday, as did his former lawyer \uc2 Jenna Ellis\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The White House is asking Congress to allocate an additional $4b to the \uc2 Federal Emergency Management Agency\uc2  to pay for the response to recent disasters, including the wildfire that destroyed Lahaina in Maui and Hurricane Idalia in Florida and other southeastern states.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.00pm BST\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020230901ej91001mp\par 