\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Judge rules against \uc2 Rudy Giuliani\uc2  in Georgia election workers\u8217\'20\'19 defamation suit \u8211\'20\'13 as it happened\b0\par\par\uc2 Chris Stein US politics live blogger (now), and Maya Yang (earlier) \par \uc2 6,137 \uc2 words\par \uc2 30 August 2023\par 20:04 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Trump\u8217\'20\'19s former attorney ordered to pay attorneys\u8217\'20\'19 fees of $89,172.50 for Ruby Freeman and Shaye MossThis blog has closed. Read our latest report here: \u8226\'20\'22 \uc2 Rudy Giuliani\uc2  liable for defaming Georgia election workers, judge rules\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.00pm BST\par \par \uc2 Closing summary\par \par \uc2 A federal judge {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/aug/30/trump-georgia-arraignment-trials-biden-idalia-politics-live-updates?page=with:block-64ef56cb8f083bb275c21132#block-64ef56cb8f083bb275c21132"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 found }}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/aug/30/trump-georgia-arraignment-trials-biden-idalia-politics-live-updates?page=with:block-64ef56cb8f083bb275c21132#block-64ef56cb8f083bb275c21132"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Rudy Giuliani}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/aug/30/trump-georgia-arraignment-trials-biden-idalia-politics-live-updates?page=with:block-64ef56cb8f083bb275c21132#block-64ef56cb8f083bb275c21132"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  liable}}}\uc2  for defaming {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/aug/30/trump-georgia-arraignment-trials-biden-idalia-politics-live-updates?page=with:block-64ef64938f08b9a6738aa9f4#block-64ef64938f08b9a6738aa9f4"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 two Georgia election workers}}}\uc2  by spreading unfounded conspiracy theories about their work around the time of the 2020 election. While the exact monetary damages he will pay remain to be determined, the judge has already ordered Giuliani to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/aug/30/trump-georgia-arraignment-trials-biden-idalia-politics-live-updates?page=with:block-64ef5cad8f083bb275c21192#block-64ef5cad8f083bb275c21192"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 cough up tens of thousands of dollars in attorney fee reimbursements}}}\uc2  and penalties in the case. Separately, another judge {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/aug/30/trump-georgia-arraignment-trials-biden-idalia-politics-live-updates?page=with:block-64ef54208f08a108316d360e#block-64ef54208f08a108316d360e"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 rejected a key part}}}\uc2  of former \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  aide \uc2 Peter Navarro\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s defense against his indictment for contempt of Congress, and jury selection in his trial {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/aug/30/trump-georgia-arraignment-trials-biden-idalia-politics-live-updates?page=with:block-64ef61558f083bb275c211e8#block-64ef61558f083bb275c211e8"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 will begin next week}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s what else went on today:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Top Senate Republican Mitch McConnell{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/aug/30/trump-georgia-arraignment-trials-biden-idalia-politics-live-updates?page=with:block-64ef7b9c8f08b9a6738aab6d#block-64ef7b9c8f08b9a6738aab6d"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 froze up during a press conference}}}\uc2  today, his second public health scare in as many months. The 81-year-old had sustained a concussion earlier this year that kept him away from Capitol Hill for weeks.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Sentencing for members of the Proud Boys militia group{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/aug/30/trump-georgia-arraignment-trials-biden-idalia-politics-live-updates?page=with:block-64ef47ae8f083bb275c2105a#block-64ef47ae8f083bb275c2105a"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 was delayed}}}\uc2  after a judge fell ill. The five defendants convicted on charges related to the January 6 insurrection will now be sentenced {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/aug/30/trump-georgia-arraignment-trials-biden-idalia-politics-live-updates?page=with:block-64ef6e988f08a108316d37d2#block-64ef6e988f08a108316d37d2"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 starting tomorrow}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Was Giuliani drunk when he was advising Trump around the time of his 2020 election defeat? Federal prosecutors {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/aug/30/trump-georgia-arraignment-trials-biden-idalia-politics-live-updates?page=with:block-64ef6aa88f08b9a6738aaa67#block-64ef6aa88f08b9a6738aaa67"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reportedly want to know}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 A Texas judge {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/aug/30/trump-georgia-arraignment-trials-biden-idalia-politics-live-updates?page=with:block-64ef8f7c8f083bb275c214a5#block-64ef8f7c8f083bb275c214a5"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 blocked a law}}}\uc2  passed by its Republican-dominated state government that would have blocked a host of local ordinances, including those mandating water breaks for some workers.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Trump is considering skipping his arraignment in the Georgia election subversion case next week, and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/aug/30/trump-georgia-arraignment-trials-biden-idalia-politics-live-updates?page=with:block-64ef33e48f083bb275c20f71#block-64ef33e48f083bb275c20f71"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 instead opting}}}\uc2  to enter his plea in writing.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.43pm BST\par \par \uc2 Florida governor \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2  at the first debate of the Republican presidential primary in Milwaukee last week. Photograph: Brian Snyder/Reuters\par \par \uc2 At the first debate of the Republican primary process last week, Florida governor \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2  sidestepped a pointed question from the moderators about his stance on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  by telling the story of \u8220\'20\'1CPenny,\u8221\'20\'1D a woman who had survived an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CShe survived multiple \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  attempts. She was left discarded in a pan. Fortunately, her grandmother saved her and brought her to a different hospital,\u8221\'20\'1D said DeSantis, who is placing a distant second in most polls to \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  for the GOP\u8217\'20\'19s presidential nomination.\par \par \uc2 The governor did not provide more details on Penny\u8217\'20\'19s circumstances, but {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://apnews.com/article/desantis-abortion-story-survivor-florida-gop-debate-penny-9b2f9ac73710ca9e1ae78c13d4694670"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the Associated Press}}}\uc2  has partially unraveled the tale, which doesn\u8217\'20\'19t quite line up with DeSantis\u8217\'20\'19s recounting.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s more from their story:\par \par \uc2 The woman is 67-year-old Miriam \u8220\'20\'1CPenny\u8221\'20\'1D Hopper, a Florida resident who has been told that she survived multiple \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  attempts when she was in the womb. The first, she said in an interview, was by her parents at home and the second by a local doctor who instructed a nurse to discard her in a bedpan after inducing her birth at just 23 weeks gestation.\par \par \uc2 Hopper said she learned through her father that her parents tried to end the pregnancy at home. There were complications, and they went to the hospital. As the story goes, the doctor did not hear a heartbeat, gave her a shot and instructed the nurse to discard the baby \u8220\'20\'1Cdead or alive.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Hopper said she was born and made a squeaky noise but was put on the back porch of the hospital. She said her grandmother discovered her there alive the following day, wrapped in a towel, and she was rushed to another hospital. Hopper was told she stayed there for three-and-a-half months and survived with the help of an incubator. Nurses nicknamed her \u8220\'20\'1CPenny\u8221\'20\'1D because of her copper-red hair.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CMy parents had always told me all my life, \u8216\'20\'18You\u8217\'20\'19re a miracle to be alive,\u8217\'20\'19\u8221\'20\'1D she said.\par \par \uc2 Hopper has used her story to partner with anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  organizations nationwide. But doctors who reviewed the story said her birth did not appear to be an attempted \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  and questioned the accuracy of the presumed gestational age.\par \par \uc2 When Hopper was born in the 1950s, before major advances in care for premature infants, babies born at 23 weeks would have had {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://apnews.com/article/abortion-technology-science-health-birmingham-7fc806f3c06aeae94c5d6ed1b06a6461"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 very little chance}}}\uc2  of surviving. Even into the early part of this century, the generally accepted \u8220\'20\'1Cedge of viability\u8221\'20\'1D remained around 24 weeks. A pregnancy is {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.acog.org/clinical/clinical-guidance/committee-opinion/articles/2013/11/definition-of-term-pregnancy"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 considered full-term}}}\uc2  at 39 to 40 weeks.\par \par \uc2 Several OB-GYNs said it appears the case was treated as a stillbirth after a doctor was not able to detect a heartbeat. Because the fetus was presumed dead, the procedure performed in the hospital would not be considered an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , said Leilah Zahedi-Spung, a maternal fetal medicine physician in Colorado.\par \par \uc2 A newspaper article documenting Hopper\u8217\'20\'19s miraculous recovery in 1956, the year after her birth, also complicates the tale. The story in the Lakeland Ledger says doctors at a hospital in Wauchula \u8220\'20\'1Cput forth greater efforts\u8221\'20\'1D in keeping the 1 pound, 11 ounce baby alive before she was escorted by police to a larger hospital. She was admitted and placed in an incubator.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt sounds very much like they anticipated a stillbirth. And when she came out alive, they resuscitated that baby to the best of their abilities and then shipped her off to where she needed to be,\u8221\'20\'1D Zahedi-Spung said.\par \par \uc2 Another news article from The Tampa Tribune said \u8220\'20\'1Cdoctors advised incubation which was not available at Wauchula,\u8221\'20\'1D leading to her transfer.\par \par \uc2 Hopper disputes that doctors initially tried to save her: \u8220\'20\'1CI don\u8217\'20\'19t think there was any effort really put forth.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 OB-GYNs who reviewed the details also raised questions about Hopper\u8217\'20\'19s gestational age at birth, saying her recorded birth weight more likely matches a fetus several weeks further along, around 26 or 27 weeks. They said the lungs are not developed enough to breathe at 23 weeks without intense assistance, making it improbable such an infant could survive abandonment for hours outdoors.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.21pm BST\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s video of \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s brief remarks about \uc2 Mitch McConnell\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s health scare today:\par \par \uc2 enltrPresident Biden reacts to \uc2 Mitch McConnell\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s second freeze of the summer:\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CMitch is a friend, as you know. Not a joke. I know people don\u8217\'20\'19t believe that\u8217\'20\'19s the case... I\u8217\'20\'19m going to try and get in touch with him later this afternoon. I don\u8217\'20\'19t know enough.\u8221\'20\'1D {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/Lpr7i1jgqB"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/Lpr7i1jgqB}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 The Recount (@therecount) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/therecount/status/1696964922528198859?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 August 30, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.17pm BST\par \par \uc2 At his ongoing press conference addressing the federal government\u8217\'20\'19s response to Hurricane Idalia in Florida and the wildfire that destroyed Lahaina in Hawaii, \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  said he would reach out to \uc2 Mitch McConnell\uc2  after {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/aug/30/mcconnell-freezes-again-kentucky-press-conference"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 he appeared to freeze up}}}\uc2  while addressing reporters today.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CMitch is a friend, as you know,\u8221\'20\'1D said the president, who served a senator for decades. \u8220\'20\'1CPeople don\u8217\'20\'19t believe that\u8217\'20\'19s the case, we have disagreements politically, but he\u8217\'20\'19s a good friend. So I\u8217\'20\'19m going to try to get in touch with him later this afternoon.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Biden {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/jul/27/mitch-mcconnell-freeze-press-conference-fall-age"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 spoke to McConnell last month}}}\uc2  after the top Senate Republican suffered a similar health scare.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.05pm BST\par \par \uc2 Ted Goodman, a political adviser to \uc2 Rudy Giuliani\uc2 , has released a statement in response to today\u8217\'20\'19s federal court ruling that the former attorney for \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  is {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/aug/30/rudy-giuliani-liable-damages-election-2020"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 liable for defaming two Georgia election workers}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThis is a prime example of the weaponization of the justice system, where the process is the punishment. This decision should be reversed, as Mayor Giuliani is wrongly accused of not preserving electronic evidence that was seized and held by the \uc2 FBI\uc2 ,\u8221\'20\'1D Goodman said.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 8.13pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.57pm BST\par \par \uc2 Texas judge blocks state law that would curb workers' water breaks despite extreme heat\par \par \uc2 A judge in Texas has blocked a state law that would override a host of regulations passed by communities in the state \u8211\'20\'13 including {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/aug/02/texas-construction-worker-water-break-law-heat-exhaustion-abbott"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 ordinances in two cities that would mandate workers receive water breaks}}}\uc2  to protect them from worsening heatwaves.\par \par \uc2 The city of Houston had sued over the law, and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://news.bloomberglaw.com/daily-labor-report/judge-blocks-texas-death-star-local-ordinance-preemption-law"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 according to Bloomberg Law}}}\uc2 , Travis county district court judge Maya Guerra Gamble ruled it violated the state constitution and blocked its enforcement.\par \par \uc2 Should Texas\u8217\'20\'19s Republican-controlled government appeal, their petition would be considered by the state supreme court, where GOP justices control all nine seats.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s more from Bloomberg Law:\par \par \uc2 The law ( {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://aboutblaw.com/bagt"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 HB 2127}}}\uc2  ), which its opponents nicknamed the \u8220\'20\'1CDeath Star\u8221\'20\'1D for its potential to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://news.bloomberglaw.com/daily-labor-report/also-bigger-in-texas-the-states-preemption-of-local-ordinances"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 broadly kill off local regulations}}}\uc2 , attempts to override the local governing authority that the Texas Constitution gives to cities with more than 5,000 residents, the City of Houston argued in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://aboutblaw.com/9TN"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 its lawsuit challenging}}}\uc2  the measure. It would have been implemented starting Sept. 1.\par \par \uc2 Ruling from the bench following a Wednesday hearing, Judge Maya Guerra Gamble (D) of the Travis County District Court granted Houston\u8217\'20\'19s request for summary judgment and blocked the preemption law, also denying the state\u8217\'20\'19s motion to dismiss the case for lack of jurisdiction.\par \par \uc2 Republicans in the statehouse advanced the preemption measure earlier this year with support from business and industry groups, who said it would spare businesses from having to comply with a patchwork of local laws.\par \par \uc2 But it faced vocal opposition, including from worker advocates and LGBTQ+ rights groups. Its opponents said it would preempt safety protections such as Austin and Dallas laws requiring water breaks for outdoor workers as well as local nondiscrimination ordinances that prevent bias in employment, housing, and public accommodations.\par \par \uc2 The law creates a private enforcement mechanism, inviting businesses and individuals to sue cities to challenge ordinances they believe are preempted by state law. It bars local regulation in eight broadly defined policy areas unless specifically authorized by the state: agriculture, finance, insurance, labor, natural resources, property, business and commerce, and occupations.\par \par \uc2 Texas already specifically preempts cities from certain kinds of ordinances, such as minimum wages that apply to private businesses. Houston argued the Texas Constitution allows the state to preempt local regulations only where there\u8217\'20\'19s a clear conflict between the state and local law.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.35pm BST\par \par \uc2 Concerns have been mounting about the health of top Senate Republican \uc2 Mitch McConnell\uc2  over the past months.\par \par \uc2 In March, the 81-year-old {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/mar/09/mitch-mcconnell-in-hospital-after-fall-in-washington-dc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 fell and sustained a concussion}}}\uc2  which kept him away from Capitol hill for weeks. Last month, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/jul/27/mitch-mcconnell-freeze-press-conference-fall-age"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 he appeared to freeze up}}}\uc2  during a press conference, before being led away by other Republican senators.\par \par \uc2 After that episode, reports emerged that McConnell, who has represented Kentucky since 1985 and led the Senate when Republicans held the majority from 2015 to 2021, fell earlier in July while disembarking from a plane at the airport. Here\u8217\'20\'19s more on those episodes, from the Guardian\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/martin-pengelly"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Martin Pengelly}}}\uc2  :\par \par \uc2 Mitch McConnell\uc2 , the Republican leader in the \uc2 US Senate\uc2 , suffered an initially unreported fall earlier this month, before {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/jul/26/mitch-mcconnell-press-conference"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a very public health scare}}}\uc2  this week revived questions about his age and fitness.\par \par \uc2 On Wednesday, while speaking to reporters at the US Capitol, the 81-year-old appeared to freeze for nearly 20 seconds. Another Republican senator, \uc2 John Barrasso\uc2  of Wyoming, a doctor, then escorted his leader away from the cameras.\par \par \uc2 Only four months ago, McConnell, who suffered from polio as a child, affecting his gait, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/mar/09/mitch-mcconnell-in-hospital-after-fall-in-washington-dc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 fell and sustained a concussion}}}\uc2 , leading to a prolonged absence from Capitol Hill.\par \par \uc2 On Wednesday, he returned to work and told reporters he was \u8220\'20\'1Cfine\u8221\'20\'1D shortly after his incident. An aide told reporters McConnell \u8220\'20\'1Cfelt lightheaded and stepped away for a moment. He came back to handle Q and A.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 But NBC News then {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nbcnews.com/politics/congress/mcconnell-fell-recently-dc-airport-prior-wednesdays-freeze-rcna96568"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reported}}}\uc2  that McConnell also tripped and fell earlier this month, suffering a \u8220\'20\'1Cface plant\u8221\'20\'1D while disembarking a plane at Reagan airport, according to an anonymous witness.\par \par \uc2 Another source {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nbcnews.com/politics/congress/mcconnell-fell-recently-dc-airport-prior-wednesdays-freeze-rcna96568"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 told NBC}}}\uc2  McConnell now uses a wheelchair as a precaution in crowded airports. McConnell did not comment on the NBC report.\par \par \uc2 As {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/republicans"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Republicans}}}\uc2  relentlessly claim \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 , 80, is too old to be president, McConnell\u8217\'20\'19s freeze and news of another fall revived questions about his own age.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.17pm BST\par \par \uc2 Fox News has more details from top Senate Republican \uc2 Mitch McConnell\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s office on his apparent freezing up during a press conference this afternoon:\par \par \uc2 enltrMcConnell's office says the Leader "felt momentarily lightheaded and paused during his press conference today." A McConnell aide says that the Ldr feels fine. But will talk to his doctor before his next public event\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Chad Pergram (@ChadPergram) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/ChadPergram/status/1696948680333332929?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 August 30, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.06pm BST\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe are stopping the flow at the border,\u8221\'20\'1D White House press secretary \uc2 Karine Jean-Pierre\uc2  said in response to a question on New York City mayor Eric Adams\u8217\'20\'19 comments he made about \u8220\'20\'1Cany plan that does not include stopping the flow at the border is a failed plan.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWhat the president has been able to do on his own, without the help of Republicans in Congress, something that he had to do on his own again because Republicans refuse to give the funding necessary to deal with the situation, a broken immigration system that has been broken for decades.\par \par \uc2 What they choose to do is play politics,\u8221\'20\'1D Jean-Pierre said, referring to Republicans.\par \par \uc2 Earlier this week, Adams issued harsh words surrounding the increasing number of migrants in New York City, saying, \u8220\'20\'1CWe have no more room.\u8221\'20\'1D In recent months, Republican state leaders have been shuttling migrants to larger Democratic-led cities including Los Angeles and New York City in opposition to current border policies.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.50pm BST\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe should take politics out of any type of disaster we see that the American people are having to suffer or deal with \u8230\'20\'26 This is not about politics,\u8221\'20\'1D White House press secretary \uc2 Karine Jean-Pierre\uc2  said at a press briefing when asked about Hurricane Idalia.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1C[President \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 ] is going to be closely watching this, getting updated regularly to make sure that the people in Georgia, in South Carolina, in Florida are getting exactly what they need,\u8221\'20\'1D Jean-Pierre added.\par \par \uc2 Additional updates on Hurricane Idalia can be found at our separate live blog here:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/aug/30/hurricane-idalia-florida-latest-news-updates"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Hurricane Idalia: extreme flooding in Florida as storm moves into Georgia \u8211\'20\'13 live}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 6.59pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.35pm BST\par \par \uc2 Top Senate Republican McConnell again freezes up when addressing reporters\par \par \uc2 Senate Republican leader \uc2 Mitch McConnell\uc2  froze while speaking to reporters in Covington, Kentucky, on Wednesday.\par \par \uc2 McConnell, 81, stopped for over 30 seconds after he was asked whether he would seek re-election.\par \par \uc2 enltrBREAKING NEWS: Sen. \uc2 Mitch McConnell\uc2  appearing to have another scary episode in the media gaggle in Covington today. Aides had to step in to help him out and repeat questions. He was eventually lead away. We'll have the full video on {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/WLWT?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @WLWT}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/q9ex5MHxLV"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/q9ex5MHxLV}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Hannah Thomas (@HannahPThomas) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/HannahPThomas/status/1696936240040321474?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 August 30, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 At one point, an aide approached McConnell and asked, \u8220\'20\'1CDid you hear the question, senator?\u8221\'20\'1D McConnell continued to remain unresponsive before he appeared to re-engage again, only to have several questions repeated to him multiple times, NBC {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nbcnews.com/politics/congress/sen-mitch-mcconnell-appears-freeze-kentucky-event-rcna102583"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reports.}}}\par \par \uc2 Last month, McConnell froze for 19 seconds while speaking to reporters on Capitol Hill before being escorted away temporarily.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 7.29pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.24pm BST\par \par \uc2 Democratic representative \uc2 Ro Khanna\uc2  of California has said that court dates interferring with \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s campaign schedule is unfair.\par \par \uc2 In an interview with conservative radio host \uc2 Hugh Hewitt\uc2  on Tuesday, Khanna said:\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CMy instinct on all of this is they\u8217\'20\'19re not going to have trials in the middle of something that\u8217\'20\'19s going to compromise a candidate\u8217\'20\'19s ability to have a fair fight...\par \par \uc2 I just don\u8217\'20\'19t see that happening in our country\u8230\'20\'26\par \par \uc2 You can\u8217\'20\'19t just say OK, because someone was president or someone is a candidate, that you\u8217\'20\'19re above the law. Everyone is under the law, and that allegations, the evidence needs to be pursued. But what we\u8217\'20\'19re discussing is the timing.\par \par \uc2 Trump, who turned himself into Fulton county jail last week in Atlanta, Georgia is currently facing 91 criminal charges across four indictments over interference with the 2020 presidential election results, illegal retention of confidential documents from the White House and hush-money payments.\par \par \uc2 For the full story, click here:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/aug/30/trump-court-dates-2024-presidential-campaign-democrat-ro-khanna"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Democrat says court dates clashing with Trump\u8217\'20\'19s campaign schedule is unfair}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 6.25pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.09pm BST\par \par \uc2 The day so far\par \par \uc2 A federal judge has {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/aug/30/trump-georgia-arraignment-trials-biden-idalia-politics-live-updates?page=with:block-64ef56cb8f083bb275c21132#block-64ef56cb8f083bb275c21132"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 found }}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/aug/30/trump-georgia-arraignment-trials-biden-idalia-politics-live-updates?page=with:block-64ef56cb8f083bb275c21132#block-64ef56cb8f083bb275c21132"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Rudy Giuliani}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/aug/30/trump-georgia-arraignment-trials-biden-idalia-politics-live-updates?page=with:block-64ef56cb8f083bb275c21132#block-64ef56cb8f083bb275c21132"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  liable}}}\uc2  for defaming {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/aug/30/trump-georgia-arraignment-trials-biden-idalia-politics-live-updates?page=with:block-64ef64938f08b9a6738aa9f4#block-64ef64938f08b9a6738aa9f4"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 two Georgia election workers}}}\uc2  by reciting unfounded conspiracy theories about their work around the time of the 2020 election. While exact damages remain to be determined, the judge has already ordered Giuliani to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/aug/30/trump-georgia-arraignment-trials-biden-idalia-politics-live-updates?page=with:block-64ef5cad8f083bb275c21192#block-64ef5cad8f083bb275c21192"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pay tens of thousands of dollars in attorney fee reimbursements}}}\uc2  and penalties in the case. Separately, another judge {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/aug/30/trump-georgia-arraignment-trials-biden-idalia-politics-live-updates?page=with:block-64ef54208f08a108316d360e#block-64ef54208f08a108316d360e"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 rejected a key part}}}\uc2  of former \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  aide \uc2 Peter Navarro\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s defense against his indictment for contempt of Congress, and jury selection in his trial {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/aug/30/trump-georgia-arraignment-trials-biden-idalia-politics-live-updates?page=with:block-64ef61558f083bb275c211e8#block-64ef61558f083bb275c211e8"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 will begin next week}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s what else has gone on today:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Sentencing for members of the Proud Boys militia group{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/aug/30/trump-georgia-arraignment-trials-biden-idalia-politics-live-updates?page=with:block-64ef47ae8f083bb275c2105a#block-64ef47ae8f083bb275c2105a"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 was delayed}}}\uc2  after a judge fell ill. The five defendants convicted on charges related to the January 6 insurrection will now be sentenced {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/aug/30/trump-georgia-arraignment-trials-biden-idalia-politics-live-updates?page=with:block-64ef6e988f08a108316d37d2#block-64ef6e988f08a108316d37d2"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 starting tomorrow}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Was Giuliani drunk when he was advising Trump around the time of his 2020 election defeat? Federal prosecutors {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/aug/30/trump-georgia-arraignment-trials-biden-idalia-politics-live-updates?page=with:block-64ef6aa88f08b9a6738aaa67#block-64ef6aa88f08b9a6738aaa67"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reportedly want to know}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Trump is considering skipping his arraignment in the Georgia election subversion case next week, and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/aug/30/trump-georgia-arraignment-trials-biden-idalia-politics-live-updates?page=with:block-64ef33e48f083bb275c20f71#block-64ef33e48f083bb275c20f71"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 opting instead}}}\uc2  to enter his plea in writing.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.51pm BST\par \par \uc2 Trump vows to jail political enemies if returned to White House\par \par \uc2 In an interview with a conservative commentator yesterday, the Guardian\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/martin-pengelly"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Martin Pengelly}}}\uc2  reports that \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  made clear what he would do if he wins next year\u8217\'20\'19s presidential election:\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  says he will lock up his political enemies if he is president again.\par \par \uc2 In {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.mediaite.com/politics/you-have-no-choice-trump-tells-glenn-beck-he-will-absolutely-lock-people-up-if-returned-to-white-house/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 an interview on Tuesday}}}\uc2 , the rightwing broadcaster Glenn Beck raised Trump\u8217\'20\'19s famous campaign-trail vow to \u8220\'20\'1Clock up\u8221\'20\'1D \uc2 Hillary Clinton\uc2 , his opponent in 2016, a promise Trump did not fulfill in office.\par \par \uc2 Beck said: \u8220\'20\'1CDo you regret not locking [Clinton] up? And if you\u8217\'20\'19re president again, will you lock people up?\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Trump said: \u8220\'20\'1CThe answer is you have no choice, because they\u8217\'20\'19re doing it to us.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Trump has {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2020/oct/18/gretchen-whitmer-donald-trump-rally-lock-her-up-michigan"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 encouraged}}}\uc2  the \u8220\'20\'1Clock her up\u8221\'20\'1D chant against other opponents but he remains in considerable danger of being locked up himself.\par \par \uc2 Under four indictments, he faces 91 criminal charges related to election subversion, retention of classified information and hush-money payments to a adult film star. He denies wrongdoing and claims to be the victim of political persecution. Trials are scheduled next year.\par \par \uc2 Earlier this month, Politico {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.politico.com/news/2023/08/02/trump-prison-sentence-risk-00109544#:~:text=If%20Trump%20were%20convicted%20on,whopping%20641%20years%20in%20prison."}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 calculated}}}\uc2  that Trump faced a maximum of 641 years in jail. After the addition of 13 racketeering and conspiracy charges in Georgia, \uc2 Forbes{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.forbes.com/sites/alisondurkee/2023/08/16/trumps-total-charges-could-result-in-more-than-700-years-in-prison/?sh=62712074e963"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 upped}}}\uc2  the total to more than 717 years.\par \par \uc2 Trump is 77.\par \par \uc2 Both sites noted, however, that if convicted, the former president was unlikely to receive maximum sentences. Nor would convictions bar Trump from running for president or being elected. On that score, Trump dominates national and key state polling regarding the Republican presidential nomination.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/aug/30/trump-interview-jail-political-opponents-glenn-beck"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Donald Trump vows to lock up political enemies if he returns to White House}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.34pm BST\par \par \uc2 Politico has obtained the full schedule for the sentencing of the Proud Boys militia group members convicted of seditious conspiracy over their roles in the January 6 attack:\par \par \uc2 enltrNEW PROUD BOYS SENTENCING SCHEDULE:\par \par \uc2 Thursday\par \par \uc2 BIGGS: 10 am\par \par \uc2 REHL 2pm\par \par \uc2 Friday\par \par \uc2 Pezzola 10 am\par \par \uc2 Nordean 2pm\par \par \uc2 Tuesday (9/5)\par \par \uc2 Tarrio 2pm\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Kyle Cheney (@kyledcheney) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/kyledcheney/status/1696897747121475990?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 August 30, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 Enrique Tarrio\uc2 , the group\u8217\'20\'19s former leader, and Joseph Biggs, a self-described Proud Boys organizer, were to be sentenced today, but the hearing was called off when the judge fell ill, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://apnews.com/article/trump-sentencing-proud-boys-capitol-riot-1ab0567db6209a5a653beb4292ff6a91"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the Associated Press reports}}}\uc2 . Prosecutors are requesting some of the highest sentences yet in any of the January 6 prosecutions for members of the group:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/aug/18/enrique-tarrio-proud-boys-sentencing-jan-6"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  US government seeks 33 years for ex-Proud Boys leader over Capitol attack }}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.17pm BST\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.rollingstone.com/politics/politics-features/rudy-giuliani-jack-smith-donald-trump-jan6-1234814129/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Rolling Stone reports}}}\uc2  that prosecutors from special counsel Jack Smith\u8217\'20\'19s office have been asking witnesses if \uc2 Rudy Giuliani\uc2  was drinking while giving advice to \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  around the time of the 2020 election:\par \par \uc2 Special Counsel {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.rollingstone.com/politics/politics-features/donald-trump-jack-smith-indictment-jan6-justice-department-1234800968/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Jack Smith\u8217\'20\'19s office}}}\uc2  has repeatedly grilled witnesses about {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.rollingstone.com/politics/politics-features/rudy-giuliani-arizona-proseuctors-fake-elector-scheme-1234812075/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Rudy Giuliani}}}\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s drinking on and after election day, investigating whether {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.rollingstone.com/t/donald-trump/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Donald Trump}}}\uc2  was knowingly relying on an inebriated attorney while {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.rollingstone.com/politics/politics-features/donald-trump-jack-smith-coconspirators-rudy-giuliani-1234806292/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 trying to overturn a presidential election}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 In their questioning of multiple witnesses, Smith\u8217\'20\'19s team of federal investigators have asked questions about how seemingly intoxicated Giuliani was during the weeks he was giving Trump advice on how to cling to power, according to a source who\u8217\'20\'19s been in the room with Smith\u8217\'20\'19s team, one witness\u8217\'20\'19s attorney, and a third person familiar with the matter.\par \par \uc2 The special counsel\u8217\'20\'19s team has also asked these witnesses if Trump had ever gossiped with them about Giuliani\u8217\'20\'19s drinking habits, and if Trump had ever claimed Giuliani\u8217\'20\'19s drinking impacted his decision making or judgment. Federal investigators have inquired about whether the then-president was warned, including after Election Night 2020, about Giuliani\u8217\'20\'19s allegedly excessive drinking. They have also asked certain witnesses if Trump was told that the former New York mayor was giving him post-election legal and strategic advice while inebriated.\par \par \uc2 Stories {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/books/2022/aug/24/donald-trump-secret-mar-a-lago-stay-rudy-giuliani-drink-depression-wife-andrew-kirtzman-book"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 about}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/books/2022/sep/08/unhinged-giuliani-drank-ranted-islam-geoffrey-berman-book"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Giuliani\u8217\'20\'19s}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/books/2021/jul/13/rudy-giuliani-trump-book"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 drinking}}}\uc2  have circulated for a while, but as the \uc2 Rolling Stone\uc2  report makes clear, whether or not he was inebriated while advising Trump during the period when he sought to overturn his election defeat may prove crucial to the former president\u8217\'20\'19s ability to defend himself from {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/aug/01/trump-indicted-reaction-key-takeaways"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Smith\u8217\'20\'19s indictment}}}\uc2  :\par \par \uc2 Federal prosecutors often aren\u8217\'20\'19t interested in investigating mere alcohol consumption. But according to lawyers and witnesses who\u8217\'20\'19ve been in the room with special counsel investigators, Smith and his team are interested in this subject because it could help demonstrate that Trump was implementing the counsel of somebody he knew to be under the influence and perhaps not thinking clearly. If that were the case, it could add to federal prosecutors\u8217\'20\'19 argument that Trump behaved with willful recklessness in his attempts nullify the 2020 election \u8212\'20\'14 by relying heavily on a lawyer he believed to be working while inebriated, and another who he bashed for spouting \u8220\'20\'1C {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.rollingstone.com/politics/politics-features/donald-trump-jack-smith-election-lies-rudy-giuliani-1234796815/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 crazy}}}\uc2  \u8221\'20\'1D conspiracy theories that Trump ran with anyway.\par \par \uc2 And if federal prosecutors were to make this argument in court, it could undermine Trump and his legal team\u8217\'20\'19s \u8220\'20\'1Cadvice of counsel\u8221\'20\'1D defense. To avoid legal consequences or even possible prison time, the ex-president is already wielding this legal defense to try to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.rollingstone.com/politics/politics-features/donald-trump-jan6-jack-smith-rudy-giuliani-john-eastman-1234798826/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 scapegoat lawyers who advised him on overturning the election}}}\uc2  \u8212\'20\'14 even though these attorneys were only acting on Trump\u8217\'20\'19s behalf, or doing what Trump had instructed them to do.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIn order to rely upon an advice of counsel defense, the defendant has to, number one, have made full disclosure of all material facts to the attorney,\u8221\'20\'1D explains Mitchell Epner, a former Assistant United States Attorney for the District of New Jersey. \u8220\'20\'1CThat requires that the attorney understands what\u8217\'20\'19s being told to them. If you know that your attorney is drunk, that does not count as making full disclosure of all material facts.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.55pm BST\par \par \uc2 Wandrea \u8216\'20\'18Shaye\u8217\'20\'19 Moss, a former Georgia election worker, is comforted by her mother, Ruby Freeman, right, during a hearing of the January 6 committee on 21 June 2022. Photograph: Jacquelyn Martin/AP\par \par \uc2 In July, \uc2 Rudy Giuliani\uc2  admitted in a court filing that he had made false statements about Ruby Freeman and her daughter Wandrea \u8220\'20\'1CShaye\u8221\'20\'1D Moss, the two Georgia election workers who were suing him for defamation.\par \par \uc2 But as the Guardian\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/michael-sainato"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Michael Sainato}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/jun/23/georgia-election-worker-cleared-trump-giuliani-vote-2020"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reported at the time}}}\uc2 , an attorney for Giuliani said the admission was just part of their legal strategy.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CMayor \uc2 Rudy Giuliani\uc2  did not acknowledge that the statements were false but did not contest it in order to move on to the portion of the case that will permit a motion to dismiss,\u8221\'20\'1D Goodman said. \u8220\'20\'1CThis is a legal issue, not a factual issue. Those out to smear the mayor are ignoring the fact that this stipulation is designed to get to the legal issues of the case.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 That strategy appears to have backfired today, after a judge found Giuliani liable for defaming them and issued a summary judgment against him, which could result in the former \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  attorney paying substantial damages.\par \par \uc2 In a hearing before the January 6 committee last year, Moss and Freeman detailed how the campaign against them upended their lives. Here\u8217\'20\'19s the report from the Guardian\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/martin-pengelly"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Martin Pengelly}}}\uc2  on their testimony:\par \par \uc2 In powerful and emotional testimony about the sinister results of \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s attempt to overturn the 2020 election, a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.reuters.com/article/us-usa-election-threats-georgia-exclusiv-idCAKBN2IP0VZ"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 mother and daughter}}}\uc2  who were Georgia elections workers described how Trump and his allies upended their lives, fueling harassment and racist threats by claiming they were involved in voter fraud.\par \par \uc2 Testifying to the January 6 committee in Washington, Shaye Moss said she received \u8220\'20\'1Ca lot of threats. Wishing death upon me. Telling me that I\u8217\'20\'19ll be in jail with my mother and saying things like, \u8216\'20\'18Be glad it\u8217\'20\'19s 2020 and not 1920.\u8217\'20\'19\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 That was a reference to lynching, the violent extra-judicial fate of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2020/jun/15/lynchings-report-reconstruction-era-black-americans"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 thousands of Black men}}}\uc2  in the American south.\par \par \uc2 Moss also said her grandmother\u8217\'20\'19s home had been threatened by Trump supporters seeking to make \u8220\'20\'1Ccitizen\u8217\'20\'19s arrests\u8221\'20\'1D of the two poll workers.\par \par \uc2 No Democratic presidential candidate had won Georgia since 1992 but \uc2 Joe Biden{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.politico.com/2020-election/results/georgia/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 beat Trump}}}\uc2  by just under 12,000 votes, a result confirmed by recounts.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/jun/21/january-6-hearings-georgia-elections-workers-mother-daughter-testify"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \u8216\'20\'18There\u8217\'20\'19s nowhere I feel safe\u8217\'20\'19: Georgia election workers on how Trump upended their lives}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.35pm BST\par \par \uc2 Jury selection starts next week in ex-Trump aide's contempt of Congress trial\par \par \uc2 Jury selection will begin on 5 September in the contempt of Congress trial of \uc2 Peter Navarro\uc2 , a former White House aide to \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Navarro was indicted last year after failing to comply with two subpoenas from the bipartisan congressional committee investigating the January 6 attack. He attempted to argue that executive privilege concerns prevented him from cooperating with the panel, but a federal judge ruled against that defense today.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.19pm BST\par \par \uc2 In her ruling today, federal judge \uc2 Beryl Howell\uc2  ordered \uc2 Rudy Giuliani\uc2  to pay $89,172.50 to reimburse attorneys\u8217\'20\'19 fees for the two Georgia election workers who sued him.\par \par \uc2 Decisions are expected later on the exact damages the former lawyer for \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  will be expected to pay.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 4.30pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.55pm BST\par \par \uc2 Judge rules against \uc2 Rudy Giuliani\uc2  in defamation suit brought by Georgia election workers\par \par \uc2 A federal judge has granted a default judgment against former \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  attorney \uc2 Rudy Giuliani\uc2  in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/dec/24/ex-georgia-election-workers-sue-giuliani-oan-trump-conspiracy-theory"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a defamation lawsuit}}}\uc2  filed by Georgia election workers Ruby Freeman and her daughter Wandrea \u8220\'20\'1CShaye\u8221\'20\'1D Moss.\par \par \uc2 Judge \uc2 Beryl Howell\uc2  also granted a default judgment for punitive damage and attorneys\u8217\'20\'19 fees.\par \par \uc2 In their lawsuit filed in 2021 against Giuliani and the rightwing One America News Network, Moss and Freeman said they were the targets of unfounded conspiracies for their work during the election the year before, and \u8220\'20\'1Chave become the objects of vitriol, threats, and harassment\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.57pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.46pm BST\par \par \uc2 Federal judge rejects privilege claim by indicted ex-Trump adviser, clearing way for trial\par \par \uc2 A federal judge has rejected a crucial defense made by former \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  adviser \uc2 Peter Navarro\uc2 , clearing the way for his trial on contempt charges related to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/jun/03/peter-navarro-indicted-trump-adviser-capitol-attack-inquiry"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 defying a subpoena from the January 6 committee}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Navarro was indicted after declining two subpoenas from the bipartisan committee investigating the Capitol attack last year, one demanding documents and the other requiring him to sit for a deposition. In his criminal trial, Navarro argued that Trump had invoked executive privilege, which would prevent him from cooperating with the summons.\par \par \uc2 But in a hearing today to consider pre-trial motions in the case , federal judge \uc2 Amit Mehta\uc2  rejected that defense, which was seen as crucial to forestalling Navarro\u8217\'20\'19s conviction.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.24pm BST\par \par \uc2 Former Proud Boys leader's sentencing rescheduled to 5 September \u8211\'20\'13 report\par \par \uc2 Politico reports that former Proud Boys leader Enrique Tarrios \u8217\'20\'19s sentencing after he was found guilty of seditious conspiracy has been rescheduled to 5 September, due to unspecified logistical issues:\par \par \uc2 enltrUPDATE 3: There is *no* emergency, per a court spokesperson. Some logistical issues but all the Proud Boys sentencings are in the process of being rescheduled.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Kyle Cheney (@kyledcheney) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/kyledcheney/status/1696887287454310673?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 August 30, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 enltrUPDATE 4: TARRIO sentencing is rescheduled for Sept. 5 at 2 pm.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Kyle Cheney (@kyledcheney) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/kyledcheney/status/1696889932684402824?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 August 30, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 Tarrio was previously set to be sentenced today. Federal prosecutors have asked that he serve 33 years in jail, which would be longest sentence yet in relation to the January 6 attack.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.39pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.10pm BST\par \par \uc2 It\u8217\'20\'19s been just under a week since \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s trip to the Fulton county jail and subsequent mug shot release \u8211\'20\'13 unprecedented events which, as the Guardian\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/hugo-lowell"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Hugo Lowell}}}\uc2  reports, have not changed the basic contours of the presidential race:\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  extended his lead over his Republican nomination rivals in a series of polls conducted since the release of his mugshot in Fulton county after he surrendered on charges that he conspired to subvert the 2020 election in Georgia and his absence from the first GOP primary debate.\par \par \uc2 The {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/donaldtrump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 former US president}}}\uc2  held commanding advantages across the board in recent surveys done for the Trump campaign and for Morning Consult, leading his nearest challenger, Governor \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2  of Florida, in the overall race, in a head-to-head matchup, and in favorability ratings.\par \par \uc2 That outcome has been a trend for Trump who has seen polling and fundraising boosts with each indictment this year \u8211\'20\'13 in the hush-money case in New York, in the classified documents case in Florida, and in the federal 2020 election subversion case in Washington.\par \par \uc2 It also suggests that some of DeSantis\u8217\'20\'19s principal campaign arguments \u8211\'20\'13 that he is more electable than Trump \u8211\'20\'13 have failed to cut through with likely Republican voters even after he had the opportunity to establish himself last week in Trump\u8217\'20\'19s absence on the debate stage.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/aug/30/trump-lead-poll-mugshot-republican-presidential-primary"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Trump improves lead over Republican primary rivals after mugshot release}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.51pm BST\par \par \uc2 Sentencing unexpectedly called off for Proud Boys convicted on January 6 charges \u8211\'20\'13 report\par \par \uc2 The sentencing of two members of the Proud Boys militia group, including former leader \uc2 Enrique Tarrio\uc2 , was unexpectedly called off today, Politico reports:\par \par \uc2 enltrUPDATE: Both Tarrio and Biggs\u8217\'20\'19 sentences are canceled for the day. Still no explanation.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Kyle Cheney (@kyledcheney) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/kyledcheney/status/1696873959986212979?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 August 30, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 enltrUPDATE 2: DOJ says the Tarrio and Biggs sentencings are off \u8220\'20\'1Cdue to an emergency.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Kyle Cheney (@kyledcheney) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/kyledcheney/status/1696875194080440499?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 August 30, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 Tarrio and Joseph Biggs, a self-described Proud Boys organizer, were both found guilty of seditious conspiracy for their actions during the assault on the Capitol. Earlier this month, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/aug/18/enrique-tarrio-proud-boys-sentencing-jan-6"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 prosecutors asked for a 33-year jail sentence}}}\uc2  for both men, which, if granted, would be the longest sentence given in any of the prosecutions to emerge from January 6.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.09pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.32pm BST\par \par \uc2 Since the start of the year, \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  has appeared at arraignments in courthouses in New York City, Miami and Washington DC, but reportedly may decide to skip a court appearance in Georgia and enter his plea in writing.\par \par \uc2 Court access rules vary across the country, but Trump\u8217\'20\'19s previous arraignments have generated a variety of scenes \u8211\'20\'13 all of which are unprecedented, since no other former president has faced similar criminal charges.\par \par \uc2 Here are some of the images that emerged from his previous arraignments:\par \par \uc2 Trump next to attorneys Joe Tacopina and Boris Epshteyn (R) during his 4 April arraignment in Manhattan Criminal Court, where he faces charges related of falsifying business documents. Photograph: Getty Images Trump, as depicted in a courtroom sketch during his arraignment on charges related to trying to hide classified documents on 13 June, alongside his aide Walt Nauta (far left), and attorneys Chris Kise and Todd Blanche. Photograph: Jane Rosenberg/Reuters Trump sits between his attorneys Todd Blanche and John Lauro in this courtroom sketch from 4 August, when Trump was in Washington DC for his arraignment on federal charges related to trying to overturn the 2020 election. Photograph: Jane Rosenberg/Reuters\par \par \uc2 All that said, Trump\u8217\'20\'19s brief visit to the Fulton county jail last week to be formally arrested already produced its own iconic image:\par \par \uc2 Trump\u8217\'20\'19s 24 August mug shot, from his arrest at the Fulton county jail in Atlanta. Photograph: FULTON COUNTY SHERIFF'S OFFICE/AFP/Getty Images\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.09pm BST\par \par \uc2 Top Georgia Republican considering sanctioning Willis over Trump indictment \u8211\'20\'13 interview\par \par \uc2 Republicans in Congress have rallied to \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s defense as prosecutors at the state and federal level {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/jul/28/donald-trump-investigations-criminal-charges-tracker"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 brought charges against him}}}\uc2  this year, and the situation in Georgia is no different. The GOP controls the legislature in the Peach State, and in an interview with {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.ajc.com/politics/politics-blog/georgia-senate-leader-seeking-ways-to-sanction-tainted-willis-over-trump-charges/PP34EF3CS5B77F5XJ3WMTAW7KQ/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Atlanta Journal-Constitution published today}}}\uc2 , Steve Gooch, the majority leader in the Senate, said the party is considering whether to sanction Fulton county district attorney \uc2 Fani Willis\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe firmly believe that Willis\u8217\'20\'19 office is being used for political purposes, and that it\u8217\'20\'19s being weaponized against Republican candidates running for office,\u8221\'20\'1D Gooch said.\par \par \uc2 He continued:\par \par \uc2 There\u8217\'20\'19s a lot of angry people in this state on both sides of this issue. But there\u8217\'20\'19s still a majority of the Republican base who feel like there was fraud in the 2020 election, and they don\u8217\'20\'19t feel like it was completely vetted properly and investigated. And that\u8217\'20\'19s why a lot of these people are still upset today. They don\u8217\'20\'19t feel like they were heard.\par \par \uc2 The majority leader said the party was considering holding hearings where witnesses could testify about \u8220\'20\'1Chow the office is being run\u8221\'20\'1D. It\u8217\'20\'19s also possible Willis would face complaints under {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://apnews.com/article/georgia-district-attorney-prosecutor-misconduct-removal-acb1b9f667c193d4bee6bb8fdb99c975"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a newly enacted law set to take effect on 1 October}}}\uc2  creating a commission to discipline prosecutors, up to removal.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.23pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.49pm BST\par \par \uc2 Trump reportedly mulls skipping Georgia arraignment as prosecutor pushes for speedy trials\par \par \uc2 Good morning, US politics blog readers. Last week, \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  made a much-watched visit to the Fulton county jail in Atlanta to be formally arrested after his indictment in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/aug/14/donald-trump-georgia-indictment-2020-election"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the Georgia election rigging case}}}\uc2 . He was set to return to the city next week, when the defendants in the case will appear in a courtroom and plead to the charges brought against them by district attorney \uc2 Fani Willis\uc2 . But {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cbsnews.com/news/trump-arraignment-fulton-county-georgia/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 CBS News reports this morning}}}\uc2  that he is considering skipping the 6 September court date, as state law allows, and having his attorney enter his plea in writing. That would make Georgia the only one of the four criminal cases he\u8217\'20\'19s facing where he does not enter his plea in person.\par \par \uc2 Willis\u8217\'20\'19s case is still in its early stages, and Trump along with some of his 18 co-defendants have signaled they have no interest in seeing their proceedings resolved anytime soon. But Willis yesterday seized on a motion filed by indicted former Trump attorney Kenneth Chesebro to have his trial start on 23 October to ask a judge to start the other defendants\u8217\'20\'19 trials at the same time \u8211\'20\'13 unless they object. Expect plenty of them to do so, perhaps as soon as today.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s what else is going on:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Hurricane Idalia has made landfall in Florida, where Republican governor \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2  paused presidential campaigning to deal with its potentially catastrophic damage to the Gulf coast. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/aug/30/hurricane-idalia-florida-latest-news-updates"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Follow our live blog}}}\uc2  for the latest on the storm.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  will at 1.45 pm eastern time speak about the federal response to Idalia, and the deadly wildfire in Maui earlier this month.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Harrison Floyd, the only one of Trump\u8217\'20\'19s 18 co-defendants in Georgia who was not released following his arrest last week, left jail after posting a bond, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.ajc.com/news/last-of-trump-defendants-in-fulton-election-probe-gets-bond/7R3436UKGBBNFIB4KJ6VM42O2E/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 according to media reports}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020230830ej8u001bf\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
