\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Ohio Republicans accused of trying to mislead voters with  \highlight22\uc2 abortion \highlight\uc2  ballot wording\b0\par\par\uc2 Ava Sasani \par \uc2 655 \uc2 words\par \uc2 29 August 2023\par 20:15 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 New lawsuit accuses ballot board of presenting voters with a confusing summary on November ballot about access to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights advocates in Ohio filed a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.supremecourt.ohio.gov/clerk/ecms/#/caseinfo/2023/1088"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 lawsuit}}}\uc2  on Monday, claiming that state Republican leaders are trying to confuse voters on a ballot measure about access to reproductive healthcare.\par \par \uc2 Last week, the Ohio ballot board \u8211\'20\'13 led by the Republican secretary of state, \uc2 Frank LaRose\uc2  \u8211\'20\'13 approved the wording of Issue 1, a November ballot measure that will ask voters if the state constitution should guarantee a right to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , contraception, fertility treatment and miscarriage care.\par \par \uc2 The new lawsuit accuses the ballot board\u8217\'20\'19s Republican majority of presenting voters with a confusing summary of Issue 1 in an attempt \u8220\'20\'1Cto mislead Ohioans and persuade them to oppose the amendment\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 According to the lawsuit filed with the Ohio supreme court, the ballot board was asked to \u8220\'20\'1Cput the clear, simple 194-word text of the Amendment itself on the ballot, so that voters could see exactly what they were being asked to approve\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Instead, the board approved a summary of the amendment that is longer than the amendment itself, replacing the term \u8220\'20\'1Cfetus\u8221\'20\'1D with \u8220\'20\'1Cunborn child\u8221\'20\'1D. The summary also does not mention the other forms of reproductive healthcare guaranteed by the amendment, like access to contraception and fertility treatments.\par \par \uc2 The summary does not change the content of the constitutional amendment itself, but \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights advocates worry that it will mislead voters at the ballot box, dissuading Ohioans from supporting Issue 1.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe ballot board\u8217\'20\'19s members adopted politicized, distorted language for the amendment, exploiting their authority in a last-ditch effort to deceive and confuse Ohio voters ahead of the November vote on reproductive freedom,\u8221\'20\'1D said Lauren Blauvelt, a spokesperson for Ohioans United for Reproductive Rights, the \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights coalition leading the lawsuit.\par \par \uc2 The legal battle over the language of the Ohio ballot measure is the latest attempt to block voters from passing a state constitutional amendment on reproductive rights.\par \par \uc2 Earlier this month, Ohio Republicans held a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/aug/09/ohio-issue-1-abortion-rights-win"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 costly special election}}}\uc2  in an attempt to make it more difficult for voters to amend the state constitution. In a resounding failure for the Ohio GOP, voters overwhelmingly rejected the proposal, opting to keep the current method of passing citizen-led amendments.\par \par \uc2 A recent poll from {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.usatoday.com/story/news/politics/2023/07/24/ohioans-back-abortion-rights-amendment-a-test-case-for-other-states/70413318007/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 USA Today Network/Suffolk University}}}\uc2  showed rising support for a state constitutional amendment protecting the right to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 LaRose last week tweeted that the amendment was a move from {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/FrankLaRose/status/1694851056482627890"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1Cthe radical left\u8221\'20\'1D}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 In the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://ohiochannel.org/video/ohio-ballot-board-8-24-2023"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 ballot board meeting}}}\uc2 , LaRose told members that he thought his summary of the amendment was \u8220\'20\'1Cfair and accurate\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe tried to summarize that the best way we can and make it a clear statement here in the ballot language of what this amendment would actually do,\u8221\'20\'1D he said.\par \par \uc2 LaRose, an avowed \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  opponent, launched his campaign for \uc2 US Senate\uc2  last month.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://ohiocapitaljournal.com/2023/08/03/soft-money-group-raises-1-million-to-advance-frank-laroses-ohio-u-s-senate-bid/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 The Ohio Capital Journal}}}\uc2  revealed that LaRose\u8217\'20\'19s campaign received a $1m donation from a new soft-money group established by the conservative lawyer David Langson, who also funded at least two additional campaigns to block the passage of the reproductive rights amendment.\par \par \uc2 Other Ohio Republicans \u8211\'20\'13 like the state attorney general, \uc2 Dave Yost\uc2  \u8211\'20\'13 share LaRose\u8217\'20\'19s staunch opposition to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 But the lawsuit commended the attorney general for setting aside his personal views on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  to \u8220\'20\'1Clawfully and impartially\u8221\'20\'1D complete his \u8220\'20\'1Camendment-related duties\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 In March, Yost approved the summary language of the amendment submitted by \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights advocates, writing in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.ohioattorneygeneral.gov/getattachment/565d7148-689a-4cd2-90e7-d80e5841eb75/The-Right-to-Reproductive-Freedom-with-Protections-for-Health-and-Safety.aspx"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a certification letter}}}\uc2  that the language was a \u8220\'20\'1Cfair and truthful\u8221\'20\'1D explanation of the proposed changes to the Ohio constitution.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CMy personal views on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  are publicly known,\u8221\'20\'1D Yost wrote.\par \par \uc2 But the attorney general added that he could not \u8220\'20\'1Cuse the authority\u8221\'20\'1D of his office to unfairly influence state policy.\par \par \uc2 He added: \u8220\'20\'1CElected office is not a license to simply do what one wishes.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020230829ej8t0028n\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
