\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Trump vows to appeal after judge sets March 2024 trial date \u8211\'20\'13 as it happened\b0\par\par\uc2 L\u233\'00\'E9onie Chao-Fong (now) and Chris Stein US politics blogger (earlier) \par \uc2 7,480 \uc2 words\par \uc2 28 August 2023\par 22:28 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Experts say trial dates typically not subject to appeal as \uc2 Mark Meadows\uc2  attempts to move his case to federal courtGeorgia residents demand answers in Trump election plot\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.23pm BST\par \par \uc2 Summary\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s a recap of today\u8217\'20\'19s developments:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s criminal trial for his efforts to overturn the 2020 election results will take place on 4 March 2024, the federal judge presiding over the case in Washington {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/aug/28/trump-trial-date-2020-election-tanya-chutkan"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 ruled}}}\uc2 , marking a sharp repudiation of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/donaldtrump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the former president}}}\uc2  who had sought to delay the case for years.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The schedule set by US district court judge \uc2 Tanya Chutkan\uc2  means Trump\u8217\'20\'19s first trial defending himself against prosecutors and the special counsel Jack Smith will be the election subversion case \u8211\'20\'13 and it will come during the height of the 2024 Republican primary season.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Trump vowed to appeal Judge Chutkan\u8217\'20\'19s decision to start the proceedings on 4 March of next year. \u8220\'20\'1CToday a biased, Trump Hating Judge gave me only a two month extension, just what our corrupt government wanted, SUPER TUESDAY. I will APPEAL!\u8221\'20\'1D he wrote on Truth Social.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Mark Meadows\uc2 , the former White House chief of staff under \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , testified for nearly three hours in a hearing{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/aug/28/mark-meadows-trump-georgia-testimony-federal-court"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 to move}}}\uc2  his Georgia election interference case from state to federal court on Monday.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Former Trump campaign lawyer Ray Smith, one of the 19 defendants charged in Georgia as part of the sweeping indictment in connection with efforts to overturn the 2020 presidential election results, has waived his arraignment and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/aug/28/trump-trial-jan-6-georgia-biden-politics-live-updates?page=with:block-64ed0ffb8f08a1ac55464f08#block-64ed0ffb8f08a1ac55464f08"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 entered a plea of not guilty,}}}\uc2  according to a court filing.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The Florida governor, \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2 , has {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/aug/28/ron-desantis-florida-jacksonville-shooting-hbcu"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 announced $1m }}}\uc2  for heightened security at a historically Black college, a day after he was booed at a memorial gathering for victims of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/aug/27/florida-jacksonville-shooting-biden-desantis"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a deadly racist shooting}}}\uc2  in his state. DeSantis\u8217\'20\'19s funding measure comes as he faces criticism for {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/commentisfree/2023/jul/25/desantis-slavery-white-supremacy"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 limiting Black history education}}}\uc2  in Florida, a move that many have condemned as racist.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 More than three-quarters of respondents in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/aug/28/biden-voters-age"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a new US poll }}}\uc2  said \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  would be too old to be effective if re-elected president next year. But as many people in the survey said the 80-year-old Biden was \u8220\'20\'1Cold\u8221\'20\'1D and \u8220\'20\'1Cconfused\u8221\'20\'1D, so a similar number saw his 77-year-old likely challenger, \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , as \u8220\'20\'1Ccorrupt\u8221\'20\'1D and \u8220\'20\'1Cdishonest\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.58pm BST\par \par \uc2 Eminem sent a cease and desist letter to Republican presidential hopeful \uc2 Vivek Ramaswamy\uc2  asking him to stop using his music on the campaign trail.\par \par \uc2 In a letter {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.dailymail.co.uk/news/article-12453955/Im-REAL-Slim-Shady-Eminem-sends-skinny-Vivek-Ramaswamy-cease-desist-letter-demanding-stop-rapping-music-campaign-trail.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 obtained }}}\uc2  by the Daily Mail, music licenser BMI notified Ramaswamy\u8217\'20\'19s campaign that Marshall Mathers, AKA Eminem, \u8220\'20\'1Cobjecting to the \uc2 Vivek Ramaswamy\uc2  campaign\u8217\'20\'19s use of Eminem\u8217\'20\'19s musical compositions (the \u8220\'20\'1CEminem Works\u8221\'20\'1D) and requesting that BMI remove all Eminem Works from the Agreement.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The letter, dated 23 August, went on to say that the rapper\u8217\'20\'19s \u8220\'20\'1Cworks are excluded from the Agreement effective immediately\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 BMI will consider any performance of the Eminem Works by the Vivek 2024 campaign from this date forward to be a material breach of the Agreement for which BMI reserves all rights and remedies with respect thereto.\par \par \uc2 The letter comes after Ramaswamy rapped some of Eminem\u8217\'20\'19s song \u8220\'20\'1CLose Yourself\u8221\'20\'1D at the Iowa State Fair. In an interview with the \uc2 New York Times\uc2 , the biotech entrepreneur {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/2023/08/19/us/politics/vivek-ramaswamy-rap-eminem-republican-campaign.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 discussed}}}\uc2  his love of Eminem and said he used to perform under \u8220\'20\'1CDa Vek the Rapper\u8221\'20\'1D as an undergrad at \uc2 Harvard University\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 enltr2024 GOP candidate \uc2 Vivek Ramaswamy\uc2  raps Eminem\u8217\'20\'19s \u8220\'20\'1CLose Yourself\u8221\'20\'1D at the Iowa State Fair. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/xUxlxUf3TY"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/xUxlxUf3TY}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 The Recount (@therecount) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/therecount/status/1690386387395047424?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 August 12, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.46pm BST\par \par \uc2 An elected Democratic prosecutor whose removal \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2  boasted about during the first Republican presidential debate said the hard-right Florida governor and his allies ousted her because she was \u8220\'20\'1Cprosecuting their cops\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Law enforcement agencies in central Florida were \u8220\'20\'1Call working against me\u8221\'20\'1D, Monique Worrell {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.thedailybeast.com/the-real-story-behind-ron-desantis-newest-fired-prosecutor?ref=home?ref=home?ref=home"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 told the Daily Beast}}}\uc2 , \u8220\'20\'1Cbecause I was prosecuting their cops, the ones who used to do things and get away with them\u8221\'20\'1D. She added:\par \par \uc2 They thought that I was overly critical of law enforcement and didn\u8217\'20\'19t do anything against \u8216\'20\'18real criminals\u8217\'20\'19. Apparently there\u8217\'20\'19s a difference between citizens who commit crimes and cops who commit crimes.\par \par \uc2 In Florida, DeSantis has removed two elected Democratic prosecutors: Andrew Warren of Hillsborough county {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/aug/04/ron-desantis-suspends-andrew-warren-prosector-abortion-ban"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 in August 2022}}}\uc2  and Worrell {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/aug/09/desantis-suspends-orlando-democrat-prosecutor-monique-worrell"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 earlier this month}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Warren said {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/aug/04/ron-desantis-suspends-andrew-warren-prosector-abortion-ban"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 he would not enforce}}}\uc2  an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban signed by the governor. The prosecutor {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/sep/23/ron-desantis-andrew-warren-abortion-ban-lawsuit-trial"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 sued}}}\uc2  to regain his job but has so far failed, even though a judge found DeSantis to be in the wrong.\par \par \uc2 Worrell {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/aug/09/desantis-suspends-orlando-democrat-prosecutor-monique-worrell"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 previously}}}\uc2  responded to her removal by calling DeSantis a \u8220\'20\'1Cweak dictator\u8221\'20\'1D seeking to create a \u8220\'20\'1Csmokescreen for [a] failing and disastrous presidential campaign\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.27pm BST\par \par \uc2 First defendant in Trump Georgia election case pleads not guilty\par \par \uc2 Former Trump campaign lawyer Ray Smith, one of the 19 defendants charged in Georgia as part of the sweeping indictment in connection with efforts to overturn the 2020 presidential election results, has waived his arraignment and entered a plea of not guilty, according to a court filing.\par \par \uc2 The filing states:\par \par \uc2 It is counsel\u8217\'20\'19s understanding that by filing this waiver of arraignment, prior to the arraignment date, that Mr. Smith and the undersigned counsel are excused from appearing at the arraignment calendar on September 6, 2023.\par \par \uc2 From Atlanta\u8217\'20\'19s 11Alive News\u8217\'20\'19 Faith Jessie:\par \par \uc2 enltrNEW INFO: Attorney Ray Smith requests to waive his arraignment and enter a not guilty plea. His arraignment is currently scheduled for next Wednesday. He is the first of the 19 defendants in the Fulton County election interference case to make this move. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/hashtag/gapol?src=hash&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 #gapol}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/11Alive?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @11alive}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/AJXmqJorbT"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/AJXmqJorbT}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Faith Jessie (@FJessieTweets) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/FJessieTweets/status/1696271770460807500?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 August 28, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.03pm BST\par \par \uc2 The anti-Trump group, the Republican Accountability Project, is launching a six-figure ad campaign targeting \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  over his indictment in Georgia.\par \par \uc2 The group announced that it will run 60-second ads on Fox News in Phoenix, Milwaukee and Atlanta, focusing on the former president\u8217\'20\'19s four indictment, in which he was charged with 13 counts over his alleged efforts to overturn the 2020 election in Georgia.\par \par \uc2 As part of the campaign the group will be putting up a billboard in Times Square featuring Trump\u8217\'20\'19s mug shot with the 91 charges facing Trump scrolling by next to him.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.48pm BST\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 House Appropriations Committee\uc2  could consider amendments to a bill that would strip federal funding from prosecutors who are pursuing charges against \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 House Freedom Caucus member \uc2 Andrew Clyde\uc2 , a member of the committee, announced plans for two amendments to the Commerce, Justice, Science, and Related Agencies (CJS) fiscal 2024 appropriations bill that would \u8220\'20\'1Cprohibit the use of federal funding for the prosecution of any major presidential candidate prior to the upcoming presidential election on November 5th, 2024\u8221\'20\'1D, a press release said.\par \par \uc2 Clyde said he intends to \u8220\'20\'1Cdefund\u8221\'20\'1D the efforts by Manhattan district attorney \uc2 Alvin Bragg\uc2 , who charged Trump in relation to hush money payments to the adult film star Stormy Daniels, special counsel Jack Smith, who led dcharges against Trump over his alleged efforts to overturn the results of the 2020 presidential election, and Fulton county district attorney \uc2 Fani Willis\uc2 , who charged Trump in relation to his 2020 election subversion efforts in Georgia.\par \par \uc2 In a statement, the congressman from Georgia said:\par \par \uc2 Americans\u8217\'20\'19 hard-earned tax dollars have no place funding the radical Left\u8217\'20\'19s nefarious election interference efforts.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.24pm BST\par \par \uc2 Bryan Hughes\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/aug/28/trump-trial-jan-6-georgia-biden-politics-live-updates?page=with:block-64ecffcb8f08590bcc98fbc6#block-64ecffcb8f08590bcc98fbc6"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 support of HB 3058}}}\uc2  signals a new strategy by Republicans to insulate \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  bans from scrutiny by creating narrow exceptions for medical emergencies.\par \par \uc2 Mary Ziegler, a law professor at the \uc2 University of California, Davis\uc2 , said:\par \par \uc2 There\u8217\'20\'19s a feeling that \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights supporters are using those medical cases to delegitimize \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  bans altogether.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://capitol.texas.gov/tlodocs/88R/billtext/html/HB03058F.htm"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 HB 3058}}}\uc2  was first introduced in the aftermath of an explosive lawsuit in which five women denied abortions in Texas, along with two doctors, sued the state after {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2023/mar/07/texas-abortion-women-lawsuit-ban"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 they were refused care despite suffering severe complications}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2023/mar/07/texas-abortion-women-lawsuit-ban"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 with their pregnancies}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The horror stories that emerged from that lawsuit threatened public support of the Texas \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban.\par \par \uc2 Ziegler said:\par \par \uc2 Republicans can now point to these new exceptions and say, \u8216\'20\'18Look, that kind of thing doesn\u8217\'20\'19t happen any more\u8217\'20\'19.\par \par \uc2 State representative Ann Johnson said that Texas Republicans genuinely wanted to address the problems raised by the lawsuit \u8211\'20\'13 even staunch \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  opponents do not want the state\u8217\'20\'19s ban linked to dangerous delays in medical treatment. She said:\par \par \uc2 That\u8217\'20\'19s hard for people to politically justify.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.14pm BST\par \par \uc2 A Texas law about to take effect on Friday carves out exceptions to the state\u8217\'20\'19s \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban.\par \par \uc2 In June, the Republican governor, Greg Abbott, quietly signed {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://capitol.texas.gov/tlodocs/88R/billtext/html/HB03058F.htm"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 HB 3058}}}\uc2 , allowing doctors to provide \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  care when a patient\u8217\'20\'19s water breaks too early for the fetus to survive, or when a patient is suffering from an ectopic pregnancy.\par \par \uc2 Crafted by state representative Ann Johnson, HB 3058 appeared to be a rare bipartisan victory in a fiercely conservative state legislature. Johnson, a Democrat who supports \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access, found an unlikely ally in state senator \uc2 Bryan Hughes\uc2 , the Republican who crafted Texas\u8217\'20\'19s infamous \u8220\'20\'1Cbounty hunter\u8221\'20\'1D law, which allows citizens to sue \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  providers as well as anyone who \u8220\'20\'1Caids or abets\u8221\'20\'1D \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  care.\par \par \uc2 Johnson and her fellow Texas Democrats welcomed the bill\u8217\'20\'19s passage as a small but important compromise to improve reproductive health in the state.\par \par \uc2 But \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights advocates across the country said {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://capitol.texas.gov/tlodocs/88R/billtext/html/HB03058F.htm"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 HB 3058}}}\uc2  offers little help to Texas doctors treating high-risk pregnancies.\par \par \uc2 Mary Ziegler, a law professor at the \uc2 University of California, Davis\uc2 , said:\par \par \uc2 The exceptions in the bill are so narrow, and the penalties for violating the Texas ban are so high, that invariably, a lot of doctors are going to continue not to offer \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  in those situations because they don\u8217\'20\'19t want to get in trouble.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.01pm BST\par \par \uc2 The hearing that will determine whether the trial of \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s former chief of staff \uc2 Mark Meadows\uc2  in the Georgia election subversion case takes place in federal court is continuing today, with no decision yet made public. Here\u8217\'20\'19s a recap from the Guardian\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/mary-yang"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Mary Yang}}}\uc2  on today\u8217\'20\'19s events and why they\u8217\'20\'19re important, including the significance of Meadow\u8217\'20\'19s surprise decision to take the witness stand:\par \par \uc2 Mark Meadows\uc2 , the former White House chief of staff under {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/donaldtrump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Donald Trump}}}\uc2 , has testified for nearly three hours in a hearing to move his Georgia election interference case from state to federal court on Monday.\par \par \uc2 Meadows was charged alongside Trump and 17 other defendants for conspiring to subvert the 2020 election in a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/state-of-georgia"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Georgia}}}\uc2  superior court. He faces two felony charges, including racketeering and solicitation of a violation of oath by a public officer.\par \par \uc2 But Meadows is arguing that he acted in his capacity as a federal officer and thus is entitled to immunity \u8211\'20\'13 and that his case should be heard before a federal judge.\par \par \uc2 Meadows swiftly filed a motion to move his case to the federal US district court of northern Georgia after \uc2 Fani Willis\uc2 , the Fulton county district attorney, handed down her indictment.\par \par \uc2 According to the indictment, Meadows arranged the infamous call between Trump and \uc2 Brad Raffensperger\uc2 , the Georgia secretary of state, where the former president asked Raffensperger to \u8220\'20\'1Cfind\u8221\'20\'1D enough votes to block Biden\u8217\'20\'19s victory.\par \par \uc2 He also at one point instructed a White House aide to draft a strategy memo for \u8220\'20\'1Cdisrupting and delaying\u8221\'20\'1D the electoral certification process on 6 January 2021, according to the indictment. Yet Meadows denied doing that on Monday, calling it the \u8220\'20\'1Cbiggest surprise\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Meadows testified for about three hours on Monday, surprising legal experts who widely expected him to keep mum.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/aug/28/mark-meadows-trump-georgia-testimony-federal-court"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Mark Meadows testifies in bid to move Georgia election case to federal court}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.39pm BST\par \par \uc2 Trump says he'll appeal 4 March trial start\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , whose attorneys proposed holding his trial on federal charges related to overturning the 2020 election in 2026, today vowed to appeal a federal judge\u8217\'20\'19s decision to start the proceedings on 4 March of next year.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CToday a biased, Trump Hating Judge gave me only a two month extension, just what our corrupt government wanted, SUPER TUESDAY. I will APPEAL!\u8221\'20\'1D the former president wrote on {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://truthsocial.com/@realDonaldTrump/posts/110968692224160798"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 his Truth social account}}}\uc2 , referencing the multi-state Republican primary that will take place the day after his trial begins.\par \par \uc2 Citing legal experts, Reuters reports that trial dates are typically not subject to appeal.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 9.07pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.24pm BST\par \par \uc2 DeSantis speaks to Biden, puts campaigning on hold to deal with Florida shooting, hurricane\par \par \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2  has canceled some presidential campaign events and returned to Florida to deal with a racist shooting in Jacksonville and an approaching tropical storm that is expected to turn into a hurricane, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.politico.com/news/2023/08/27/desantis-pauses-campaigning-as-florida-faces-duel-crises-00113140?nname=playbook&nid=0000014f-1646-d88f-a1cf-5f46b7bd0000&nrid=12069c7e-e346-405c-ad2c-71cb1a62e514&nlid=630318"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Politico reports}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The Florida governor traveled to Jacksonville on Sunday, a day after a gunman who left behind manifestos peppered with racial slurs opened fire at a \uc2 Dollar General\uc2  store, killing three people. During an event in which DeSantis {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/aug/28/ron-desantis-florida-jacksonville-shooting-hbcu"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 was booed}}}\uc2 , the governor pledge $1m to help a historically Black college improve security, and $100,000 to a charity on behalf of the victim\u8217\'20\'19s families.\par \par \uc2 Politico reports that DeSantis plans to stay in the state as Idalia, a tropical storm that is expected to become a hurricane, moves closer to the Gulf coast:\par \par \uc2 enltr10 AM CDT 28Aug: Storm Surge, Hurricane & Tropical Storm warnings for {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/hashtag/Idalia?src=hash&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 #Idalia}}}\uc2  have been issued for portions of Florida. Residents in these areas should follow any advice given by local officials. Make sure to stay up to date with the latest information at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/tW4KeGe9uJ"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/tW4KeGe9uJ}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/R1uWF5Eu8f"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/R1uWF5Eu8f}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 National Hurricane Center (@NHC_Atlantic) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/NHC_Atlantic/status/1696181410741268676?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 August 28, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  said earlier today he has spoken to DeSantis, both to offer support for the expected storm damage, and condolences for the shooting victims. The two men are political rivals, but have in the past made appearances together in the Sunshine state in the aftermath of disasters:\par \par \uc2 enltrThis morning, I spoke with Governor DeSantis to inform him that we've approved the Emergency Declaration for Florida as they prepare for Hurricane Idalia, and FEMA has pre-deployed personnel and assets.\par \par \uc2 Florida has my full support as they prepare for Idalia and its aftermath.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 President Biden (@POTUS) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/POTUS/status/1696194874712682883?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 August 28, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 enltrI also reiterated my commitment to support the people of Jacksonville following the horrific shooting on Saturday.\par \par \uc2 My prayers continue to be with the victims and the families.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 President Biden (@POTUS) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/POTUS/status/1696194875895484540?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 August 28, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.59pm BST\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, Politico has obtained the schedule of \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s federal trial in Washington DC on charges related to overturning the 2020 election:\par \par \uc2 enltrUPDATE: We have the full trial schedule from Chutkan\par \par \uc2 Oct. 9: Pretrial motions\par \par \uc2 Dec. 4: 404b evidence\par \par \uc2 Dec. 11: Disclosure of expert witnesses\par \par \uc2 Dec. 18: Disclosure of exhibits\par \par \uc2 Dec. 27: Motions in limine\par \par \uc2 Jan. 15: Proposed voir dire questions/jury instructions {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/YxGJD0IuDo"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/YxGJD0IuDo}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/iBh4dRPmk2"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/iBh4dRPmk2}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Kyle Cheney (@kyledcheney) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/kyledcheney/status/1696219538059092113?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 August 28, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 The trial itself begins on 4 March 2024, per judge \uc2 Tanya Chutkan\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s ruling today.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.42pm BST\par \par \uc2 Atlanta\u8217\'20\'19s 11Alive News has published sketches from inside the courtroom as \uc2 Mark Meadows\uc2  testifies in his bid to be tried in federal court:\par \par \uc2 enltrJUST IN: New sketches are giving us a glimpse inside the federal courtroom where \uc2 Mark Meadows\uc2  is making his argument for the removal of his case to Federal court. The former Chief of Staff questioned for hours. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/hashtag/gapol?src=hash&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 #gapol}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/11AliveNews?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @11AliveNews}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/csATn9UWns"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/csATn9UWns}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Faith Jessie (@FJessieTweets) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/FJessieTweets/status/1696231315413115047?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 August 28, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 No electronic devices are permitted inside the courtroom, hence the employment of sketch artists.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.20pm BST\par \par \uc2 Meadows defends involvement in Georgia elections as part of White House job\par \par \uc2 In an ongoing hearing where a judge will determine whether to move his trial in the election subversion case to federal court, \uc2 Mark Meadows\uc2  has argued that he became involved in Georgia\u8217\'20\'19s 2020 polls in his capacity as White House chief of staff, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.ajc.com/politics/breaking-meadows-defends-actions-as-he-testifies-in-federal-court/YG3IFQBGGJA5BGAP5FNO74CIMI/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the Atlanta Journal-Constitution reports}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 In order to succeed in his bid to have the charges brought against him by the Fulton county district attorney, \uc2 Fani Willis\uc2 , tried in federal rather than state court, Meadows will need to convince a judge that he was acting in his capacity as a White House official when he traveled to Georgia and spoke with its leaders. Citing legal experts, the Journal-Constitution reports that is \u8220\'20\'1Ca fairly low threshold to clear if valid arguments can be made\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI don\u8217\'20\'19t know that I did anything that was outside my scope as chief of staff,\u8221\'20\'1D Meadows testified in an unexpected appearance on the witness stand during what has been called a \u8220\'20\'1Cmini-trial\u8221\'20\'1D in Judge Steve Jones \u8217\'20\'19s court today, who will decide whether to grant his request.\par \par \uc2 Cross examined by special prosecutor Anna Cross, the Journal-Constitution reports Meadows defended {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/oct/27/mark-meadows-georgia-grand-jury-testify-judge-orders"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 his conduct}}}\uc2  as part of his role as chief of staff, saying he wanted \u8220\'20\'1Cto make sure elections are accurate. I would assume that has a federal nexus.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Jones has not yet ruled.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 7.28pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.55pm BST\par \par \uc2 Mark Meadows\uc2  says Trump White House were 'challenging times'\par \par \uc2 Former White House chief of staff \uc2 Mark Meadows\uc2 , who has been {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/aug/28/trump-trial-jan-6-georgia-biden-politics-live-updates?page=with:block-64ecc5338f08a1ac55464cb2#block-64ecc5338f08a1ac55464cb2"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  testifying at his hearing to move his trial to federal court,}}}\uc2  described his time serving under \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  as \u8220\'20\'1Cchallenging\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 At the federal courthouse in Atlanta, Meadows described his duties as the former president\u8217\'20\'19s chief of staff, which included meeting with state officials. Meadows is arguing that his case should be moved and subsequently dismissed because he has immunity from prosecution for carrying out what he says were his duties as a federal official.\par \par \uc2 Speaking about his time at the White House, Meadows said:\par \par \uc2 Those were challenging times, bluntly.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI don\u8217\'20\'19t know if anyone was fully prepared for that type of job,\u8221\'20\'1D he added.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 7.06pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.45pm BST\par \par \uc2 On Sunday, \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2  was jeered while speaking at a memorial that drew a crowd of nearly 200 to remember the victims of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/aug/27/florida-jacksonville-shooting-biden-desantis"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the Dollar General shooting.}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CHe don\u8217\'20\'19t care,\u8221\'20\'1D an attendee shouted as DeSantis was being introduced, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://thehill.com/homenews/state-watch/4174426-desantis-booed-at-vigil-for-victims-of-racist-shooting-in-florida/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the Hill reported}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 At one point, a council member came to DeSantis\u8217\'20\'19s defense and attempted to quiet the crowd, but the booing continued.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt ain\u8217\'20\'19t about parties today,\u8221\'20\'1D said {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/jacksonville"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Jacksonville}}}\uc2  city councilwoman Ju\u8217\'20\'19Coby Pittman. \u8220\'20\'1CA bullet don\u8217\'20\'19t know a party.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 DeSantis referred to the shooter as a \u8220\'20\'1Cmajor-league scumbag\u8221\'20\'1D in his remarks, adding that Florida opposed racist violence.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWhat he did is totally unacceptable in the state of Florida,\u8221\'20\'1D DeSantis said. \u8220\'20\'1CWe are not going to let people be targeted based on their race.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.37pm BST\par \par \uc2 Florida governor \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2  has announced $1m for heightened security at a historically Black college, a day after he was booed at a memorial gathering for victims of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/aug/27/florida-jacksonville-shooting-biden-desantis"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a deadly racist shooting}}}\uc2  in his state.\par \par \uc2 DeSantis said his administration would give $1m to Edward Waters University to enhance its security after the gunman in this weekend\u8217\'20\'19s racist killings at a \uc2 Dollar General\uc2  store in Jacksonville tried to enter the historically Black college but was denied entry.\par \par \uc2 DeSantis said that an additional $100,000 would be given to a charity for the victims\u8217\'20\'19 families. \u8220\'20\'1CAs I\u8217\'20\'19ve said for the last couple of days, we are not going to allow our HBCUs to be targeted by these people,\u8221\'20\'1D DeSantis said. \u8220\'20\'1CWe\u8217\'20\'19re going to provide security help with them.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 DeSantis\u8217\'20\'19s funding measure comes as he faces criticism for {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/commentisfree/2023/jul/25/desantis-slavery-white-supremacy"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 limiting Black history education}}}\uc2  in Florida, a move that many have condemned as racist.\par \par \uc2 DeSantis has also come under renewed scrutiny for his support of expanded gun access in his state. The Florida governor signed legislation in April that allows resident {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://apnews.com/article/guns-desantis-florida-government-ac7adbc200cc4c1bb429ea84357f73be"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 to carry concealed guns}}}\uc2  without a permit.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 7.39pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.25pm BST\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  saw a slight drop in support among Republican primary voters after skipping the first GOP debate last week, according to a new poll.\par \par \uc2 The poll by Emerson College, which was conducted 25-26 August, found that 50% of GOP primary voters said they plan to vote for the former president, down from 56% in a pre-debate survey. Trump still maintains a huge 38% lead over his closest rival, Florida governor \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Former South Carolina governor Nikki Haley had the biggest post-debate gain, jumping from 2% to 7%. DeSantis gained two points to 12%.\par \par \uc2 Spencer Kimball, executive director of Emerson College Polling, said in a statement:\par \par \uc2 While Trump saw a slight dip in support, the question from this poll is whether this is a blip for Trump or if the other Republican candidates will be able to rally enough support to be competitive for the caucus and primary season.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.12pm BST\par \par \uc2 After four arrests in as many months, \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  has now been charged with 91 felony counts across criminal cases in New York, Florida, Washington and Georgia. The former president and current frontrunner in the 2024 Republican presidential primary faces the threat of prison time if he is convicted.\par \par \uc2 As Trump attempts to delay his criminal trials, civil lawsuits endanger the former president\u8217\'20\'19s financial and business prospects. A New York jury has already found Trump liable for sexually abusing and defaming E Jean Carroll, awarding her $5m in damages. A separate civil inquiry, led by New York attorney general Letitia James, seeks $250 million that the \uc2 Trump Organization\uc2  allegedly obtained through fraud.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/jul/28/donald-trump-investigations-criminal-charges-tracker"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s where each case against Trump stands}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/jul/28/donald-trump-investigations-criminal-charges-tracker"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  Donald Trump case tracker: where does each investigation stand?}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.01pm BST\par \par \uc2 Polls shows most voters think Biden too old for second term\par \par \uc2 An {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://apnorc.org/projects/bidens-age-is-a-significant-concern-for-voters/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Associated Press-NORC Center for Public Affairs Research poll}}}\uc2  released today brings bad news for \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  : most voters think the 80-year-old is too elderly to serve a second term. They do not feel quite the same way about \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , even though the former president is only four years Biden\u8217\'20\'19s junior:\par \par \uc2 enltr77% think \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  is too old to effectively serve as President, including 69% of Democrats. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/PDlUmWsmPA"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/PDlUmWsmPA}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/6v470MXZMk"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/6v470MXZMk}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 AP-NORC Center (@APNORC) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/APNORC/status/1696174346358661316?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 August 28, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 Biden is the oldest president ever to win the presidency, and would break records if elected to a second term next year. The poll finds voters are well aware of that, with 26% of respondents saying \u8220\'20\'1Cold\u8221\'20\'1D and its synonyms are the first things that come to mind when they think of Biden. When it comes to Trump, 15% say the first thing they think of is \u8220\'20\'1Ccorrupt\u8221\'20\'1D, \u8220\'20\'1Ccriminal\u8221\'20\'1D or \u8220\'20\'1Ccrooked\u8221\'20\'1D. \u8220\'20\'1CLiar\u8221\'20\'1D, \u8220\'20\'1Cdishonest\u8221\'20\'1D and \u8220\'20\'1Cuntrustworthy\u8221\'20\'1D come in second place at 8%. Biden does better here, with only 2% of respondents associating him with those terms.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.46pm BST\par \par \uc2 The day so far\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s trial on federal charges related to trying to overturn the 2020 election {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/aug/28/trump-trial-jan-6-georgia-biden-politics-live-updates?page=with:block-64ecbc408f08a1ac55464c53#block-64ecbc408f08a1ac55464c53"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 will begin on 4 March of next year}}}\uc2 , right in the middle of the Republican primary season, after judge \uc2 Tanya Chutkan{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/aug/28/trump-trial-jan-6-georgia-biden-politics-live-updates?page=with:block-64ecaab38f08a1ac55464b6f#block-64ecaab38f08a1ac55464b6f"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 turned down his attorneys\u8217\'20\'19 request}}}\uc2  for a 2026 start date. Meanwhile, we\u8217\'20\'19ll see the former president in court in Georgia {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/aug/28/trump-trial-jan-6-georgia-biden-politics-live-updates?filterKeyEvents=false&page=with:block-64eca7da8f081f06153fa3ce#block-64eca7da8f081f06153fa3ce"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 next week, where he will be arraigned}}}\uc2  along with everyone else accused by Fulton county district attorney \uc2 Fani Willis\uc2  of plotting to overturn the 2020 results in that state. Speaking of Georgia, Trump\u8217\'20\'19s former chief of staff \uc2 Mark Meadows\uc2  made {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/aug/28/trump-trial-jan-6-georgia-biden-politics-live-updates?page=with:block-64ecc5338f08a1ac55464cb2#block-64ecc5338f08a1ac55464cb2"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the surprise decision}}}\uc2  to take the stand as he argues to move his trial on Willis\u8217\'20\'19s charges to federal court from state court.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s what else has happened today:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Meadows \u8217\'20\'19s decision to undergo cross-examination in Georgia shows he may consider moving his case to federal court crucial to his defense, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/aug/28/trump-trial-jan-6-georgia-biden-politics-live-updates?page=with:block-64ecc9cc8f081f06153fa587#block-64ecc9cc8f081f06153fa587"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 an analyst says}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 A Trump spokeswoman{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/aug/28/trump-trial-jan-6-georgia-biden-politics-live-updates?page=with:block-64ec9a8f8f08a1ac55464a9a#block-64ec9a8f8f08a1ac55464a9a"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 fretted over the weekend}}}\uc2  that the trials in his four indictments would interfere with his campaigning for the White House.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The Georgia election meddling{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/aug/28/trump-trial-jan-6-georgia-biden-politics-live-updates?page=with:block-64eca0fe8f081f06153fa371#block-64eca0fe8f081f06153fa371"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 hangs over a rural county}}}\uc2  that found itself swept up in conspiracy theories.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.25pm BST\par \par \uc2 Per legal analyst Lisa Rubin, \uc2 Mark Meadows\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s appearance on the witness stand as he argues to move his case from Georgia state court to federal court was unexpected, and potentially a sign that he views winning the motion as crucial to his defense:\par \par \uc2 enltrThat a lawyer as experienced as former U.S. Attorney George Terwilliger allowed his client to take the stand tells you two things. First, Meadows and his team believe moving his case to federal court is so critical that it\u8217\'20\'19s worth the risk of his being cross-examined. 2/\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Lisa Rubin (@lawofruby) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/lawofruby/status/1696173703837454446?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 August 28, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 enltrSecond, Meadows\u8217\'20\'19s team concluded they had no other way of shouldering their burden of proof that he was acting as a federal officer beyond Meadows\u8217\'20\'19s own testimony. 3/\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Lisa Rubin (@lawofruby) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/lawofruby/status/1696174600265126034?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 August 28, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 enltrAnd that means either they were unable to convince any Meadows allies with firsthand knowledge of his activities and/or Trump\u8217\'20\'19s directives to take the stand for him\u8212\'20\'14or that because of the secrecy with which they operated, no such witnesses exist. Either one is not a good look. 4/\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Lisa Rubin (@lawofruby) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/lawofruby/status/1696174937323520329?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 August 28, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.05pm BST\par \par \uc2 Ex-Trump chief of staff takes stand as he argues for moving Georgia trial to federal court\par \par \uc2 CNN reports that \uc2 Mark Meadows\uc2 , \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s chief of staff during the period when he carried out a plan to overturn the 2020 based on unfounded claims of rigging, has taken the stand as he argues for his trial in Georgia to be argued at the federal level:\par \par \uc2 enltrMark Meadows is testifying at today's hearing where he's trying to move his case from state to federal court, per {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/KatelynPolantz?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @KatelynPolantz}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/MarshallCohen?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @MarshallCohen}}}\uc2  :\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThose were challenging times, bluntly,\u8221\'20\'1D Meadows said. \u8220\'20\'1CI don\u8217\'20\'19t know if anyone was fully prepared for that type of job."\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Jeremy Herb (@jeremyherb) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/jeremyherb/status/1696168120346402975?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 August 28, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 enltrMore from Meadows on the stand:\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI would get invited to almost every meeting that the president had,\u8221\'20\'1D Meadows testified, describing his close advisory role w/ Trump.\par \par \uc2 Sometimes people would meet with him so he could \u8220\'20\'1Cget in (Trump\u8217\'20\'19s) ear and pass along their message,\u8221\'20\'1D he said.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Jeremy Herb (@jeremyherb) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/jeremyherb/status/1696171934554202407?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 August 28, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.51pm BST\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s the Guardian\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/hugo-lowell"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Hugo Lowell}}}\uc2  with the full rundown of federal judge \uc2 Tanya Chutkan\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s decision to set a 4 March trial date for \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s election subversion trial:\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s criminal trial for his efforts to overturn the 2020 election results will take place in 4 March 2024, the federal judge presiding over the case in Washington ruled on Monday, marking a sharp repudiation of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/donaldtrump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the former president}}}\uc2  who had sought to delay the case for years.\par \par \uc2 The schedule set by US district court judge \uc2 Tanya Chutkan\uc2  means Trump\u8217\'20\'19s first trial defending himself against prosecutors and the special counsel Jack Smith will be the election subversion case \u8211\'20\'13 and it will come during the height of the 2024 Republican primary season.\par \par \uc2 Trump pleaded not guilty earlier this month to charges filed in federal district court in Washington that he conspired to defraud the United States, conspired to obstruct an official proceeding, obstructed an official proceeding and engaged in a conspiracy against rights.\par \par \uc2 The former president had asked ahead of the hearing for the trial to take place in April 2026, citing the supposed \u8220\'20\'1Cmedian time\u8221\'20\'1D of 29.2 months that it took to convict defendants in cases that involved the charge of conspiracy to obstruct an official proceeding.\par \par \uc2 But prosecutors {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/aug/21/trump-2020-election-indictment-trial-date"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 had argued in response}}}\uc2  that using the median time as a benchmark was misleading because it included the time it takes for jury selection, trial, verdict and several months of sentencing deliberation, rather than just the duration of pre-trial proceedings.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/aug/28/trump-trial-date-2020-election-tanya-chutkan"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Trump\u8217\'20\'19s federal trial in election subversion case set for March 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.42pm BST\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s federal trial on charges related to trying to overturn the 2020 election will start just before one of the biggest days in the Republican nominating process.\par \par \uc2 The trial\u8217\'20\'19s opening coincides with North Dakota\u8217\'20\'19s Republican caucus, but the real event will take place the next day, which is known as Super Tuesday for the sheer number of states that vote.\par \par \uc2 On 5 March, Republicans in Alabama, Alaska, Arkansas, California, Colorado, Maine, Massachusetts, Minnesota, North Carolina, Oklahoma, Tennessee, Texas, Utah, Vermont and Virginia will vote in primaries. With his trial kicking off the day before, the stage is set for Trump to once again be at the front of voters\u8217\'20\'19 minds when they head to the polls \u8211\'20\'13 for better or worse.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.33pm BST\par \par \uc2 In selecting 4 March as the date for \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s trial on charges of trying to overturn the 2020 election, \uc2 Tanya Chutkan\uc2  rejected the former president\u8217\'20\'19s request for a trial beginning in 2026, and gave prosecutors almost exactly what they wanted.\par \par \uc2 Special counsel Jack Smith \u8217\'20\'19s team had proposed starting in January, and the date Chutkan chose was only a few weeks off from that.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.26pm BST\par \par \uc2 Trump federal election subversion trial scheduled for 4 March 2024\par \par \uc2 Federal judge \uc2 Tanya Chutkan\uc2  has just set \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s trial date on charges of plotting to overturn the 2020 election for 4 March of next year.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 4.27pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.16pm BST\par \par \uc2 After about an hour and 15 minutes of arguments, judge \uc2 Tanya Chutkan\uc2  has called a recess in the hearing that will determine the date of \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s trial in the federal January 6 case.\par \par \uc2 She is expected to rule on the trial date when the hearing resumes.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.13pm BST\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s lawyer John Lauro is going back and forth with judge \uc2 Tanya Chutkan\uc2  on the date for the formal president\u8217\'20\'19s trial over trying to overturn the 2020 election.\par \par \uc2 Chutkan remains plainly skeptical of Lauro\u8217\'20\'19s request for a lengthy timeframe in the case. \u8220\'20\'1CI will say that, I don\u8217\'20\'19t doubt from it that you\u8217\'20\'19re working diligently, but I will say that you and I have a very, very different estimate of what of the time that\u8217\'20\'19s needed to prepare for this case,\u8221\'20\'1D the judge said.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.58pm BST\par \par \uc2 Ex-Trump chief of staff to face 'mini-trial' as he argues to move case to federal court\par \par \uc2 Attorneys for \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s former chief of staff \uc2 Mark Meadows\uc2  are today arguing in Georgia that his trial in the election subversion case should be moved to federal court from the state level, where Fulton county district attorney \uc2 Fani Willis\uc2  originally brought the charges.\par \par \uc2 The hearing was scheduled to start at 10 am, but attendees are not permitted to carry electronic devices while in the building, and so we are unlikely to know what\u8217\'20\'19s happening in the courtroom.\par \par \uc2 As {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.washingtonpost.com/national-security/2023/08/28/mark-meadows-federal-court-trump-georgia-election-case/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the Washington Post reports}}}\uc2 , having his case moved to federal court could bring several advantages to Meadows, one of which would be a potentially more conservative jury pool:\par \par \uc2 If Meadows is able to punt his case to federal court, it could benefit him when it comes time to choose a jury, experts said. The jury pool for a federal case would be composed of residents from across northern Georgia, which is more politically conservative than Fulton County and a potentially friendlier audience for the former Trump official and Republican congressman.\par \par \uc2 Today\u8217\'20\'19s hearing is seen as something of a \u8220\'20\'1Cmini-trial\u8221\'20\'1D, because Willis\u8217\'20\'19s prosecutors have subpoenaed four witnesses who dealt with Meadows in Georgia after the 2020 election and may testify. These include secretary of state \uc2 Brad Raffensperger\uc2 , subject of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/jan/04/trumps-phone-call-to-brad-raffensperger-five-key-points"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 an infamous phone call}}}\uc2  from the president following his defeat at the ballot box. But legal analyst Lisa Rubin notes that testimony from Frances Watson, an investigator for Raffensperger\u8217\'20\'19s office, may prove to be the most damning:\par \par \uc2 enltrMore than a week before Trump\u8217\'20\'19s purportedly \u8220\'20\'1Cperfect call\u8221\'20\'1D to Raffensperger, in which Meadows participated, Meadows went to GA to observe the Cobb County, GA signature audit. He even tried to get into the auditors\u8217\'20\'19 work space, only to be stopped by Watson and others. 3/\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Lisa Rubin (@lawofruby) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/lawofruby/status/1696164877046333794?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 August 28, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 enltrStill, while he was there, Meadows arranged a call between Watson and Trump for the next day, 12/23/30, that someone was wise enough to record. That call was a less formal, less pressured dress rehearsal for Trump\u8217\'20\'19s pressing Raffensperger on 1/2/21 to find him 11,780 votes. 4/\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Lisa Rubin (@lawofruby) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/lawofruby/status/1696166012842881358?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 August 28, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 enltrBut what matters most is that Watson had direct contact with Meadows first\u8212\'20\'14and at a time Trump likely didn\u8217\'20\'19t know she existed. To the extent anyone is well positioned to show how much freelance political work Meadows was doing, it\u8217\'20\'19s her. 5/\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Lisa Rubin (@lawofruby) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/lawofruby/status/1696166394918764590?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 August 28, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.45pm BST\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s attorney John Lauro just made an impassioned argument for delaying his trial to 2026, arguing his legal team needs years to investigate the evidence.\par \par \uc2 Judge \uc2 Tanya Chutkan\uc2  did not seem to buy it. \u8220\'20\'1CYou are not going to get two more years. This case is not going to trial in 2026,\u8221\'20\'1D she said.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.30pm BST\par \par \uc2 Judge \uc2 Tanya Chutkan\uc2  signals she disagrees with arguments made by \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s attorneys that, based on the \u8220\'20\'1Cmedian time\u8221\'20\'1D of similar cases, his trial should begin {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/aug/21/trump-2020-election-indictment-trial-date"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 in 2026}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 At the hearing, Chutkan said those numbers were misleading because they included the time from commencement to sentencing, not to trial.\par \par \uc2 The judge also noted that she is overseeing one of the cases cited by Trump\u8217\'20\'19s lawyers in their proposed timeframe, and the delays in that matter were because of Covid-19 and a superseding indictment \u8211\'20\'13 none of which applied to the former president.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.17pm BST\par \par \uc2 Federal judge \uc2 Tanya Chutkan\uc2  continues her opening remarks by stressing how the Speedy Trial Act exists to also benefit the public interest, and not just the defendant.\par \par \uc2 She adds that \u8220\'20\'1Ccounsel is not entitled to unlimited preparation time\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.15pm BST\par \par \uc2 Trump 'will have to make the trial date work' \u8212\'20\'14 federal judge\par \par \uc2 Federal judge \uc2 Tanya Chutkan\uc2  is giving opening remarks in the hearing to determine \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s trial date in the January 6 case.\par \par \uc2 She said she planned to question both the former president\u8217\'20\'19s attorneys and prosecutors from special counsel Jack Smith \u8217\'20\'19s team, and reiterated that Trump will have to yield to the criminal process \u8211\'20\'13 potentially bad new for his hopes to forestall the trial till after the 2024 election.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CSetting a trial date does not depend and should not depend on the defendant\u8217\'20\'19s personal and professional obligations. Mr Trump, like any defendant, will have to make the trial date work regardless of his schedule,\u8221\'20\'1D Chutkan said.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.02pm BST\par \par \uc2 Trump's arraignment in Georgia case set for 6 September - report\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  will be arraigned in the Georgia election subversion case at 9.30am on 6 September, Politico reports:\par \par \uc2 enltrARRAIGNMENT: \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 's arraignment in Fulton County, GA has been set for 9:30am on Sept. 6, per the court docket there.\par \par \uc2 The other 18 defendants also appear to be slated for arraignment that day in 15 minute increments.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Kyle Cheney (@kyledcheney) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/kyledcheney/status/1696156953200795878?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 August 28, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 His 18 co-defendants will also be arraigned the same day:\par \par \uc2 enltr9:30 Trump\par \par \uc2 9:45 Giuliani\par \par \uc2 10:00 Eastman\par \par \uc2 10:15 Powell\par \par \uc2 10:30 Meadows\par \par \uc2 10:45 Latham\par \par \uc2 11:00 Hall\par \par \uc2 11:15 Chesebro\par \par \uc2 11:30 Kutti\par \par \uc2 11:45 Floyd\par \par \uc2 1:00 Clark\par \par \uc2 1:15 Lee\par \par \uc2 1:30 Ellis\par \par \uc2 1:45 Still\par \par \uc2 2:00 Smith\par \par \uc2 2:15 Shafer\par \par \uc2 2:30 Roman\par \par \uc2 2:45 Cheeley\par \par \uc2 3:00 Hampton\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Kyle Cheney (@kyledcheney) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/kyledcheney/status/1696158716427374800?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 August 28, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 Trump and his co-defendants reported to the Fulton county jail last week in Atlanta to be processed and have their mug shots taken after being indicted by district attorney \uc2 Fani Willis\uc2  for trying to overturn the state\u8217\'20\'19s election result.\par \par \uc2 At his arraignment, Trump is expected {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/aug/14/donald-trump-georgia-indictment-2020-election"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 to enter pleas to the 13 charges}}}\uc2  he faces in the case.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.20pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.55pm BST\par \par \uc2 Trump's attorney arrive for hearing on January 6 trial date\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s lawyers have arrived at federal court in Washington DC for the hearing that will determine when his trial on charges related to trying to overturn the 2020 election and the January 6 insurrection will be held.\par \par \uc2 The former president is not expected to attend. Special prosecutor Jack Smith \u8217\'20\'19s team has asked that the trial begin in January, while Trump\u8217\'20\'19s attorneys have proposed starting in 2026. Federal judge \uc2 Tanya Chutkan\uc2 , an appointee of \uc2 Barack Obama\uc2 , is presiding over the hearing.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.33pm BST\par \par \uc2 In Georgia, \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  and 18 others are accused of a carrying out a sprawling plot aimed squarely at disrupting \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s election win. But as the Guardian\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/timothy-pratt"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Timothy Pratt}}}\uc2  reports, it also had real consequences for a rural county that found itself entangled in his campaign\u8217\'20\'19s unfounded allegations of vote rigging:\par \par \uc2 On Saturday afternoon, roughly 70 people gathered on folding chairs in a sweltering church meeting room in the small town of Douglas, about 200 miles (322km) south-east of Atlanta, Georgia. Less than a week earlier, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/donaldtrump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Donald Trump}}}\uc2  and 18 of his allies were indicted in Fulton county for efforts to overturn the 2020 election, including allegedly entering the Coffee county elections office less than a mile away and copying the state\u8217\'20\'19s voter software and other data.\par \par \uc2 County residents at the town hall raised concerns about the lack of accountability for those who played a role in copying software and other data, and said they felt insecure about the safety and integrity of future elections.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CPeople think, \u8216\'20\'18He\u8217\'20\'19s been indicted in Atlanta, so it\u8217\'20\'19s over,\u8217\'20\'19\u8221\'20\'1D 80-year-old county resident Jim Hudson said to the room, referring to Trump. \u8220\'20\'1C[But] how do we regroup? How do we become a county not referred to as \u8216\'20\'18Crooked Coffee\u8217\'20\'19?\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The Rev Bruce Francis read a message from Bishop Reginald T Jackson, who oversees 500 Black churches in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/state-of-georgia"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Georgia}}}\uc2 , referring to \u8220\'20\'1Ctroubling improprieties\u8221\'20\'1D that had brought this town of about 12,000 residents to the world\u8217\'20\'19s attention.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe nation is now aware of the travesty that happened in 2020,\u8221\'20\'1D he read. \u8220\'20\'1CWhat do we do to make sure it doesn\u8217\'20\'19t happen again?\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The \u8220\'20\'1Ctravesty\u8221\'20\'1D was what Marilyn Marks, the town hall\u8217\'20\'19s main speaker, called \u8220\'20\'1Cthe largest voting system breach in US history\u8221\'20\'1D. It happened in January 2021, when multiple people working on behalf of \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  allegedly entered the Coffee county elections office and copied software and other digital information from the agency\u8217\'20\'19s computers, gaining access to the entire elections system of the state of Georgia, home to about {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://sos.ga.gov/election-data-hub"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 7.9 million}}}\uc2  registered voters.\par \par \uc2 The digital information obtained is now in an unknown number of hands, meaning that future elections could be affected in Georgia and in other states that use \uc2 Dominion Voting Systems\uc2  and other equipment made by partner companies. The breach has been publicly reported for more than a year, but was launched into a global spotlight on 14 August, when the Fulton county district attorney, \uc2 Fani Willis\uc2 , issued indictments to Trump and 18 others. Several people were indicted for their direct role in the Coffee county breach, and nearly half the group had some kind of involvement in the incident, according to Marks.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/aug/28/bring-them-to-justice-georgia-town-residents-demand-answers-in-trump-election-plot"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \u8216\'20\'18Bring them to justice\u8217\'20\'19: Georgia town residents demand answers in Trump election plot}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.11pm BST\par \par \uc2 Trump ally fears trials will derail campaigning\par \par \uc2 Court cases are unpredictable, but with \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  facing four different criminal indictments spread over three states and Washington DC, it seems likely he\u8217\'20\'19ll be spending at least some of his time in courtrooms next year. The graphic below outlines what we know of his trials\u8217\'20\'19 schedule so far:\par \par \uc2 Timeline of Trump\u8217\'20\'19s potential trials. Illustration: Guardian Design\par \par \uc2 All that court time could conflict with his campaign to win back the White House in next year\u8217\'20\'19s election. Over the weekend, the Guardian\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/edpilkington"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Ed Pilkington}}}\uc2  reports that one of his allies said as much, and even went so far as to accuse prosecutors of conspiring to keep him away from his presidential run:\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s legal spokesperson has predicted that forthcoming early trial dates in the former president\u8217\'20\'19s four criminal cases will not hold, and that his multiple cases could clash with the final stages of the 2024 presidential election campaign and voting.\par \par \uc2 Alina Habba told the Fox News Sunday show that prosecutors\u8217\'20\'19 plans for fast turnarounds in Trump\u8217\'20\'19s two federal criminal cases and the state indictments in New York and Georgia amounted to \u8220\'20\'1Cunrealistic theatrics\u8221\'20\'1D. She said that each of the trials would last from four to six weeks, raising the threat of overlapping schedules.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CNo judge is going to say you can be in two trials in two different states, because a lot of these overlap. They are going to have to go into October, November of next year,\u8221\'20\'1D she said.\par \par \uc2 Habba, who acts as general counsel for the Trump-supporting political fundraising group Save America PAC, claimed that the possibility of extending the trials right up to election day, 5 November, next year, was \u8220\'20\'1Cby design\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 She claimed, without providing evidence, that \uc2 Fani Willis\uc2 , the district attorney of Fulton county in Georgia who is {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/aug/14/donald-trump-georgia-indictment-2020-election"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 leading the prosecution}}}\uc2  of Trump over his attempts to overturn the 2020 election result in Georgia, and Jack Smith, the special counsel who has spearheaded the two federal indictments, were engaged in a \u8220\'20\'1Ccoordinated effort\u8221\'20\'1D with partisan motive.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe know this is intentional \u8211\'20\'13 it\u8217\'20\'19s to tie [Trump] up, it\u8217\'20\'19s definitely political,\u8221\'20\'1D Habba said.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/aug/27/trump-legal-team-trial-timing-us-elections"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Trump legal team claims trial dates \u8216\'20\'18by design\u8217\'20\'19 clash with election campaign}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.51pm BST\par \par \uc2 Judge to decide date for Trump's January 6 trial in day of high-stakes court hearings\par \par \uc2 Good morning, US politics blog readers. \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  is expected to have a big day today in not one, but two courtrooms, where judges will consider matters that could have a great impact both on the criminal trials he is facing, and on the broader 2024 campaign. At 10 am eastern time in Washington DC, federal judge \uc2 Tanya Chutkan\uc2  will consider when to hold his trial on charges of trying to overturn the 2020 election. Special counsel Jack Smith \u8217\'20\'19s team wants it to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/aug/21/trump-2020-election-indictment-trial-date"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 begin in January}}}\uc2 , while Trump\u8217\'20\'19s attorneys have proposed holding off until 2026. If prosecutors get their way, it\u8217\'20\'19ll throw yet another wrench into his plans to spend next year campaigning for the White House.\par \par \uc2 At the same time in Atlanta, \uc2 Mark Meadows\uc2 , Trump\u8217\'20\'19s chief of staff during his final months in office, will be in federal court, arguing that his trial on charges of trying to disrupt \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s election win in Georgia three years ago should be held there, and not in its current state court venue. If Meadows prevails, it could aid his defense against the charges brought by Fulton county district attorney \uc2 Fani Willis\uc2 , and potentially apply to Trump and the 17 other co-defendants in the case. We\u8217\'20\'19ll be following both of these hearings as they happen.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s what else is going on today:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Today is the 60th anniversary of the March on Washington, a landmark moment in the civil rights struggle that Biden commemorated with {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.washingtonpost.com/opinions/2023/08/27/joe-biden-king-march-on-washington-jobs-freedom/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a piece in the Washington Post}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Vivek Ramaswamy\uc2  has {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theamericanconservative.com/a-viable-realism-and-revival-doctrine/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a piece in the American Conservative}}}\uc2  outlining his foreign policy doctrine, after he was attacked by his fellow Republican presidential contenders at last week\u8217\'20\'19s primary debate.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2  is taking a break from the campaign trail to return to Florida and deal with an approaching storm and the aftermath of a racist shooting in Jacksonville, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.politico.com/news/2023/08/27/desantis-pauses-campaigning-as-florida-faces-duel-crises-00113140?nname=playbook&nid=0000014f-1646-d88f-a1cf-5f46b7bd0000&nrid=12069c7e-e346-405c-ad2c-71cb1a62e514&nlid=630318"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Politico reports}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020230828ej8s0018l\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
