\par\par \uc2 World news\par \b \uc2 Texas carves out narrow exception to  \highlight22\uc2 abortion \highlight\uc2  ban in new Republican strategy\b0\par\par\uc2 Ava Sasani \par \uc2 1,177 \uc2 words\par \uc2 28 August 2023\par 10:08 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Law allows for termination if patient\u8217\'20\'19s water breaks too early or in cases of ectopic pregnancy, but critics say it is not enough\par \par \uc2 A Texas law about to take effect on Friday carves out exceptions to the state\u8217\'20\'19s \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban.\par \par \uc2 In June, the Republican governor, Greg Abbott, quietly signed {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://capitol.texas.gov/tlodocs/88R/billtext/html/HB03058F.htm"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 HB 3058}}}\uc2 , allowing doctors to provide \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  care when a patient\u8217\'20\'19s water breaks too early for the fetus to survive, or when a patient is suffering from an ectopic pregnancy.\par \par \uc2 Crafted by state representative Ann Johnson, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://capitol.texas.gov/tlodocs/88R/billtext/html/HB03058F.htm"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 HB 3058}}}\uc2  appeared to be a rare bipartisan victory in a fiercely conservative state legislature. Johnson, a Democrat who supports \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access, found an unlikely ally in state senator \uc2 Bryan Hughes\uc2 , the Republican who crafted Texas\u8217\'20\'19s infamous \u8220\'20\'1Cbounty hunter\u8221\'20\'1D law, which allows citizens to sue \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  providers as well as anyone who \u8220\'20\'1Caids or abets\u8221\'20\'1D \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  care.\par \par \uc2 Johnson and her fellow Texas Democrats welcomed the bill\u8217\'20\'19s passage as a small but important compromise to improve reproductive health in the state.\par \par \uc2 But \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights advocates across the country said {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://capitol.texas.gov/tlodocs/88R/billtext/html/HB03058F.htm"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 HB 3058}}}\uc2  offers little help to Texas doctors treating high-risk pregnancies.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe exceptions in the bill are so narrow, and the penalties for violating the Texas ban are so high, that invariably, a lot of doctors are going to continue not to offer \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  in those situations because they don\u8217\'20\'19t want to get in trouble,\u8221\'20\'1D said Mary Ziegler, a law professor at the \uc2 University of California, Davis\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Hughes\u8217\'20\'19 support of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://capitol.texas.gov/tlodocs/88R/billtext/html/HB03058F.htm"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 HB 3058}}}\uc2  signals a new strategy by Republicans to insulate \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  bans from scrutiny by creating narrow exceptions for medical emergencies.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThere\u8217\'20\'19s a feeling that \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights supporters are using those medical cases to delegitimize \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  bans altogether,\u8221\'20\'1D Ziegler said.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://capitol.texas.gov/tlodocs/88R/billtext/html/HB03058F.htm"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 HB 3058}}}\uc2  was first introduced in the aftermath of an explosive lawsuit in which five women denied abortions in Texas, along with two doctors, sued the state after {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2023/mar/07/texas-abortion-women-lawsuit-ban"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 they were refused care despite suffering severe complications}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2023/mar/07/texas-abortion-women-lawsuit-ban"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 with their pregnancies}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The horror stories that emerged from that lawsuit threatened public support of the Texas \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban.\par \par \uc2 Republicans can now point to these new exceptions and say, \u8216\'20\'18Look, that kind of thing doesn\u8217\'20\'19t happen any more'\par \par \uc2 Mary Ziegler of the \uc2 University of California, Davis\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CRepublicans can now point to these new exceptions and say, \u8216\'20\'18Look, that kind of thing doesn\u8217\'20\'19t happen any more,\u8217\'20\'19\u8221\'20\'1D said Ziegler.\par \par \uc2 Johnson said that Texas Republicans genuinely wanted to address the problems raised by the lawsuit \u8211\'20\'13 even staunch \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  opponents do not want the state\u8217\'20\'19s ban linked to dangerous delays in medical treatment.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThat\u8217\'20\'19s hard for people to politically justify,\u8221\'20\'1D she said.\par \par \uc2 Part of the problem seemed to arise from a misunderstanding of what constitutes an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 . If a doctor terminates an ectopic pregnancy, some Republicans did not consider that an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThere is a political terminology on the word \u8216\'20\'18\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19 that\u8217\'20\'19s different from the medical definition,\u8221\'20\'1D she said.\par \par \uc2 Johnson did not put the word \u8220\'20\'1C\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 \u8221\'20\'1D in HB 3058 in a bid for Republican votes, and her strategy seemed to succeed. In May, the Texas legislature overwhelmingly voted in favor of the bill.\par \par \uc2 Dr Katie McHugh, an Indiana OB-GYN and board member of the group Physicians for Reproductive Health, is skeptical of Republican motivations for supporting HB 3058.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThey are just now getting around to the treatment of ectopic pregnancies, more than two years after the first big restrictions went into effect?\u8221\'20\'1D McHugh said.\par \par \uc2 She added that Republicans have long known about the dire medical consequences of sweeping \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  restrictions.\par \par \uc2 Before the \uc2 US supreme court\uc2  struck down Roe v Wade last year, a study of Texas\u8217\'20\'19s existing \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  restrictions found that the \u8220\'20\'1Cbounty hunter\u8221\'20\'1D law left doctors afraid to care for patients whose water broke too early. The pregnant patients needed to be {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2022/jul/13/texas-abortion-ban-maternal-health-risk"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1Cat death\u8217\'20\'19s door\u8221\'20\'1D}}}\uc2  to receive pregnancy termination under the law.\par \par \uc2 In a June interview with the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nationalreview.com/2023/06/texas-democrats-and-republicans-find-common-ground-on-abortion/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 National Review}}}\uc2 , Hughes brushed off the suggestion that Texas\u8217\'20\'19s \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  restrictions are unclear.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CBut because some doctors and hospitals were not following the law,\u8221\'20\'1D Hughes told the publication, \u8220\'20\'1Cwe wanted to remove any doubt and remove any excuse for not giving the care that the moms need in these cases.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Texas doctors accused of violating the state\u8217\'20\'19s \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  law face up to $100,000 in fines or even life in prison.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CDoctors felt like their hands were tied behind their back \u8211\'20\'13 they could face financial ruin or lose their medical license,\u8221\'20\'1D said Johnson, who represents the district that is home to the Texas medical center.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  providers like McHugh warn that {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://capitol.texas.gov/tlodocs/88R/billtext/html/HB03058F.htm"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 HB 3058}}}\uc2  will not offer meaningful assurances to Texas OB-GYNs.\par \par \uc2 Everyone is afraid of the legal ramifications of crossing these legal boundaries, and writing in exception language is not going to change that\par \par \uc2 Dr Katie McHugh of Physicians for Reproductive Health\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CEveryone is afraid of the legal ramifications of crossing these legal boundaries, and writing in exception language is not going to change that,\u8221\'20\'1D she said.\par \par \uc2 McHugh said \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  bans create a chilling effect among doctors who are scared to misinterpret what constitutes a \u8220\'20\'1Cmedical emergency\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s this idea of having to prove how sick someone is before we can intervene,\u8221\'20\'1D she said. \u8220\'20\'1CYou can\u8217\'20\'19t always prove how life-threatening something is going to be.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Texas is the second state where \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  opponents approved new exceptions for medical emergencies.\par \par \uc2 Tennessee Republicans made similar concessions earlier this year, when the state \u8220\'20\'1Csoftened\u8221\'20\'1D its total ban in April. Tennessee previously had one of the harshest anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  laws in the country, one that did not make explicit exceptions to save the life of the pregnant person.\par \par \uc2 But Tennessee Republicans grew worried in February, when the Idaho supreme court temporarily blocked that state\u8217\'20\'19s \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban. Tennessee\u8217\'20\'19s attorney general, Jonathan Skrmetti, and Republican house speaker, Cameron Sexton, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://apnews.com/article/abortion-politics-idaho-tennessee-health-77e62ba129b6f2b8509b1e7dfc7412f9"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 raised concerns}}}\uc2  that a similar legal challenge could threaten the future of Tennessee\u8217\'20\'19s ban.\par \par \uc2 Sexton urged state lawmakers to add exceptions to the Tennessee law banning \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  at conception.\par \par \uc2 The next month, Tennessee\u8217\'20\'19s governor, \uc2 Bill Lee\uc2 , an avowed \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  opponent, signed a bill allowing doctors to offer the procedure when patients have an ectopic or molar pregnancy.\par \par \uc2 The Tennessee exceptions law is so narrowly tailored that it won the support of staunch \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  opponents.\par \par \uc2 In an April statement, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tnrtl.org/legislative_alerts"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Tennessee Right to Life}}}\uc2  praised the final version of the exceptions bill, saying it will \u8220\'20\'1Cnot allow for more unborn children to be aborted in our state\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Both the Texas and Tennessee laws are extremely limited in scope: ectopic pregnancies represent a small fraction of the medical emergencies that might require a doctor to terminate a pregnancy.\par \par \uc2 Still, Johnson welcomes any Republican concessions on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access.\par \par \uc2 The doctors in her district said the \u8220\'20\'1Cbulk of complications\u8221\'20\'1D they were struggling to treat involved a patient\u8217\'20\'19s water breaking too early, one of two medical conditions addressed by the new Texas law.\par \par \uc2 She added: \u8220\'20\'1CThere\u8217\'20\'19s a lot more we need to do.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020230828ej8s0010f\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
