\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Former US president surrenders at Fulton jail over election charges \u8211\'20\'13 as it happened\b0\par\par\uc2 Chris Stein US politics live blogger (now); Maya Yang and L\u233\'00\'E9onie Chao-Fong (earlier) \par \uc2 13,331 \uc2 words\par \uc2 25 August 2023\par 03:11 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 This blog has now closedFull report: Trump surrenders at Georgia jail on election chargesDonald Trump mugshot releasedAnalysis: Trump\u8217\'20\'19s jail spectacle is historic, but won\u8217\'20\'19t harm him politically\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.04am BST\par \par \uc2 Closing summary\par \par \uc2 In a lightning visit to Atlanta, \uc2 Donald Trump{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/aug/24/trump-georgia-fulton-rally-republican-debate-politics-live-updates?filterKeyEvents=false&page=with:block-64e7ea278f08a1ac55462946#block-64e7ea278f08a1ac55462946"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 was formally arrested}}}\uc2  after being indicted by Fulton county district attorney \uc2 Fani Willis\uc2  for trying to overturn the 2020 election, then released after posting a $200,000 bail bond. The visit to the county jail \u8211\'20\'13 a pilgrimage {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/aug/24/trump-georgia-fulton-rally-republican-debate-politics-live-updates?filterKeyEvents=false&page=with:block-64e7615a8f081f06153f7cba#block-64e7615a8f081f06153f7cba"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 many of his co-defendants}}}\uc2  made this week \u8211\'20\'13 produced an image that will no doubt endure in American politics: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/aug/24/trump-georgia-fulton-rally-republican-debate-politics-live-updates?page=with:block-64e7ef598f08590bcc98d725#block-64e7ef598f08590bcc98d725"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 his mug shot}}}\uc2 , the first ever taken of a former US president. Trump {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/aug/24/trump-georgia-fulton-rally-republican-debate-politics-live-updates?page=with:block-64e804a58f08a1ac554629ef#block-64e804a58f08a1ac554629ef"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 embraced the scowling portrait}}}\uc2 , even {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/aug/24/trump-georgia-fulton-rally-republican-debate-politics-live-updates?page=with:block-64e808478f081f06153f82e0#block-64e808478f081f06153f82e0"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 deploying it on Twitter}}}\uc2  in his first post since two days after the January 6 insurrection, when the platform {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/aug/24/trump-georgia-fulton-rally-republican-debate-politics-live-updates?page=with:block-64e808c38f081f06153f82e1#block-64e808c38f081f06153f82e1"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 temporarily}}}\uc2  booted him. That may be the biggest news of all. Trump used \uc2 Twitter\uc2  like no other politician during his successful White House run in 2016, and throughout his four years in office. We\u8217\'20\'19ll be watching to see if he tries to repeat the trick as he runs for president once again.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s what else happened today:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Willis{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/aug/24/trump-georgia-fulton-rally-republican-debate-politics-live-updates?page=with:block-64e78cc98f081f06153f7f87#block-64e78cc98f081f06153f7f87"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 asked a judge}}}\uc2  to start the trials in her case on 23 October \u8211\'20\'13 a speedy deadline that Trump is likely to fight.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 But Kenneth Chesebro, an attorney who assisted Trump as he looked for ways to prevent \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  from taking office, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/aug/24/trump-georgia-fulton-rally-republican-debate-politics-live-updates?page=with:block-64e7b9188f08590bcc98d5c9#block-64e7b9188f08590bcc98d5c9"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 will go to trial on 23 October}}}\uc2 , after he asked that his case be resolved quickly.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 House Republicans are running interference for Trump once again by {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/aug/24/trump-georgia-fulton-rally-republican-debate-politics-live-updates?page=with:block-64e773388f08590bcc98d2e8#block-64e773388f08590bcc98d2e8"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 announcing an investigation into Willis}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Mark Meadows\uc2 , who was Trump\u8217\'20\'19s chief of staff around the time of his election loss and was indicted in Georgia, wants his trial {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/aug/24/trump-georgia-fulton-rally-republican-debate-politics-live-updates?filterKeyEvents=false&page=with:block-64e7830a8f08590bcc98d3cf#block-64e7830a8f08590bcc98d3cf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 moved to federal court}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 One thing we learned from last night\u8217\'20\'19s Republican presidential debate (which Trump skipped): opinions on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/aug/24/trump-georgia-fulton-rally-republican-debate-politics-live-updates?page=with:block-64e7668c8f08a1ac55462456#block-64e7668c8f08a1ac55462456"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 range more than one might expect}}}\uc2  among the candidates.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 4.05am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.43am BST\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s campaign is putting his mug shot to use wherever they can, but Chris LaCivita, a senior advisor to his presidential campaign, is warning other parties against using it:\par \par \uc2 enltr??????????????????????\par \par \uc2 If you are a campaign, PAC , scammer and you try raising money off the mugshot of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/realDonaldTrump?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @realDonaldTrump}}}\uc2  and you have not received prior permission \u8230\'20\'26WE ARE COMING AFTER YOU you will NOT SCAM DONORS\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Chris LaCivita (@LaCivitaC) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/LaCivitaC/status/1694883551664115860?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 August 25, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.25am BST\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  is free to tweet his mug shot because he posted a $200,000 bond that will allow him to stay out of jail while his case in Georgia is resolved.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.washingtonpost.com/politics/2023/08/23/an-atlanta-bail-bondsman-explains-how-hed-handle-trump/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 The Washington Post interviewed}}}\uc2  a Georgia bail bondsman at a company called Red Eye Bail Bonds (who asked to stay anonymous, citing privacy concerns and the headaches that can come with weighing in on American politics). While the bond was in the \u8220\'20\'1Ctop tier\u8221\'20\'1D of what he deals with, the bondsman said Trump\u8217\'20\'19s case isn\u8217\'20\'19t as unusual as it may appear, at least from the perspective of a bondsman:\par \par \uc2 In general, the manager said, Red Eye requires that a client provide 10 percent of the total bond. If the person under arrest is deemed to be a higher risk, that percentage increases. If the risk is higher, the company also will do more on the front end to establish whether resources exist to recoup the full value of the bond. Does the client own a house? Things like this.\par \par \uc2 After all, while Red Eye requires only 10 percent, the county requires the whole thing. That doesn\u8217\'20\'19t mean that the firm has to put up $200,000 in cash. The whole point of involving a bondsman, after all, is that the firm serves as a proxy of trust on behalf of clients. There is a specialized power of attorney that is granted the firm, and when Red Eye decides to act as a guarantor for a client, a sum reflecting the total bond is frozen with the firm\u8217\'20\'19s insurer.\par \par \uc2 I asked whether Trump\u8217\'20\'19s $200,000 was unusually high. The manager thought about it for a moment before determining that it was in the \u8220\'20\'1Ctop tier\u8221\'20\'1D of what he usually sees. The midrange is about $100,000 or $110,000, he told me, but in cases involving more serious charges, costs could run higher.\par \par \uc2 He was also not fazed by the unique circumstances of Trump\u8217\'20\'19s situation. He often has clients who are facing more than one indictment; that shows up in the initial analysis of the case and factors into the consideration of the arrestee as a flight risk. It is also not unusual for one party to live out of state, as Trump does. (He used the example of a college kid getting arrested and his parents posting bond remotely.) This, too, would on other occasions give him pause.\par \par \uc2 But he wasn\u8217\'20\'19t really worried about Trump.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI wouldn\u8217\'20\'19t think he\u8217\'20\'19s just outright not going to show up in court,\u8221\'20\'1D he said. This wasn\u8217\'20\'19t just about Trump; in other \u8220\'20\'1Chigh-end cases like that, most likely or not the families are not going anywhere.\u8221\'20\'1D (I didn\u8217\'20\'19t mention Trump\u8217\'20\'19s recent social media post about moving to Russia.)\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.29am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.07am BST\par \par \uc2 Citing two sources, CNN has more details on why \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  opted to pose the way he did in his mug shot:\par \par \uc2 enltrTrump's team had discussed the former president's mug shot prior to him taking it at the Fulton County jail Thursday evening, two sources familiar with the discussions tell me. Trump ultimately decided he wanted to appear "defiant" in the shot, and purposefully chose not to smile\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Alayna Treene (@alaynatreene) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/alaynatreene/status/1694891058306429118?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 August 25, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.53am BST\par \par \uc2 Twitter\uc2  banned \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  two days after the January 6 attack, citing \u8220\'20\'1Cthe risk of further incitement of violence \u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 That all changed about a year-and-a-half later when, after a tortuous process that nearly went to court, billionaire \uc2 Elon Musk\uc2  bought the influential social media platform. Musk, who recently renamed the platform X, was already a prolific tweeter and after buying the site held a poll asking whether Trump should be let back on.\par \par \uc2 A slim majority said yes, and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/nov/20/twitter-lifts-donald-trump-ban-after-elon-musks-poll"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Trump\u8217\'20\'19s account was reinstated last November}}}\uc2 , but the former president did not use it \u8211\'20\'13 until today.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.54am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.49am BST\par \par \uc2 Trump tweets mug shot in first post since January 6 aftermath\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  has used his \uc2 Twitter\uc2  account for the first time since two days after the January 6 insurrection to share a photo of his newly taken mug shot:\par \par \uc2 zxxltr {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/MlIKklPSJT"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/MlIKklPSJT}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/Mcbf2xozsY"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/Mcbf2xozsY}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 \uc2 Donald J. Trump\uc2  (@realDonaldTrump) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/realDonaldTrump/status/1694886846050771321?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 August 25, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.54am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.34am BST\par \par \uc2 It seems \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  was happy with the mug shot authorities took at the Fulton county jail during his appearance there this evening.\par \par \uc2 It\u8217\'20\'19s on {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://secure.winred.com/save-america-joint-fundraising-committee/bf1d23bd52c25ba6?exitintent=true"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the front of his main fundraising page}}}\uc2 , and his campaign is {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://secure.winred.com/save-america-joint-fundraising-committee/storefront/never-surrender-white-premium-cotton-t-shirt/details"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 already selling t-shirts}}}\uc2  with the photo on the front and the words \u8220\'20\'1CNEVER SURRENDER!\u8221\'20\'1D on the back.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.37am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.18am BST\par \par \uc2 For all the spectacle the arrest of \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  and his co-defendants provided in Georgia, the Guardian\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/sam-levine"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Sam Levine}}}\uc2  reports that it is unlikely to change the basic dynamics of next year\u8217\'20\'19s presidential election:\par \par \uc2 One by one this week, they\u8217\'20\'19ve made their way to 901 Rice Street, the address of the notorious Fulton county jail. Lawyers, government officials, a former state party chair and others have all surrendered to authorities after being charged as part of an alleged criminal effort to overturn the 2020 election.\par \par \uc2 On Thursday, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/aug/14/donald-trump-georgia-indictment-2020-election"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the head}}}\uc2  of that enterprise, \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , himself surrendered, marking another historic moment for a president who has reshaped the rules of American politics. This is the closest that Trump has been to a jail cell to date and serves as a blunt reminder that no American or former president is above the law.\par \par \uc2 Like nearly everything Trump does, his surrender was orchestrated to be a spectacle. He {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/aug/22/donald-trump-surrender-fulton-county-jail-thursday-night"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 deliberately timed}}}\uc2  his surrender, 7.30pm, to maximize cable news coverage. Reporters camped outside the jail all day on Thursday as temperatures reached mid-90F and Trump supporters {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/BVKImages/status/1694764193537462466?s=20"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 gathered for a demonstration}}}\uc2 . There was wall-to-wall news coverage of Trump\u8217\'20\'19s motorcade and arrival at the jail. While politicians typically try and shift attention away from their criminal legal troubles, Trump has embraced it, feeding into the circuit by {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/bennyjohnson/status/1694782933863670218?s=20"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 advertising his surrender time}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/aug/24/trump-mugshot-jail-spectacle-political-meaning"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Trump\u8217\'20\'19s jail spectacle is historic, but it won\u8217\'20\'19t harm him politically}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.28am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.03am BST\par \par \uc2 Trump glares at camera in mugshot released by Fulton county jail\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s hostility shines through in the mug shot taken at the Fulton county jail as he was booked on charges of trying to steal the 2020 presidential election.\par \par \uc2 The former president turns his eyes up to glare toward the camera above him.\par \par \uc2 Dressed in a blue suit, white shirt and red tie, he makes no attempt to put on a smile like some of his co-accused in their booking photos. Instead, his mouth is taut and downturned.\par \par \uc2 The picture does not flatter, but it does convey the message many of Trump\u8217\'20\'19s supporters want to hear \u8211\'20\'13 one of belligerence.\par \par \uc2 The six-pointed star of the Fulton county sheriff\u8217\'20\'19s office badge and the name of the sheriff, Patrick Labat, sits in the top left-hand corner of the picture. But some will be disappointed that Trump is not seen in the classic pose holding a board in front of his chest with his name and date of arrest.\par \par \uc2 For all that, the former president\u8217\'20\'19s supporters are already embracing the booking photo as a badge of honour and defiance. It will be held up as evidence that their man will not give up the fight against a system his followers see as ever more determined to bring him down and prevent him returning to the White House. The mugshot\u8217\'20\'19s rapid appearance on T-shirts, posters and, well, mugs glorifying a martyred Trump can be expected.\par \par \uc2 The president\u8217\'20\'19s detractors, on the other hand, will see the booking photo as evidence that even a man who was once the most powerful person in the land cannot escape the might of the justice system.\par \par \uc2 Some will welcome anything that makes him look even a little bit more criminal as a confirmation that sooner or later he is going to prison. The accused may be innocent until a plea or a jury says otherwise, but mugshots can have a way of conveying guilt.\par \par \uc2 Trump\u8217\'20\'19s mugshot released by Fulton county officials. Photograph: Fulton County\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.38am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.48am BST\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s plane has now departed Atlanta, but the former president will undoubtedly be back.\par \par \uc2 The question is: when? Expect Trump\u8217\'20\'19s lawyers to do everything they can to delay his trial on the indictment brought by Fulton county district attorney \uc2 Fani Willis\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 For a taste of his likely strategy, take a look at the pre-trial motions in the federal case brought against him for trying to overturn the 2020 election, where Trump\u8217\'20\'19s lawyers have proposed a trial date {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/aug/21/trump-2020-election-indictment-trial-date"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 in 2026}}}\uc2 . A judge has yet to decide the matter.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.41am BST\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  mug shot released\par \par \uc2 Here is the mug shot of \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  that was taken when he was arrested at the Fulton county jail in Atlanta:\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  mugshot released today. Photograph: Fulton County Sheriff\u8217\'20\'19s Office/Reuters\par \par \uc2 No former US president has ever had his mug shot taken.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 1.53am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.28am BST\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s a video clip of \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s brief remarks to reporters before departing Atlanta:\par \par \uc2 enltrDonald Trump speaks after getting booked at Fulton County jail in the Georgia election interference case:\par \par \uc2 "When you, uh, have that great freedom to challenge, you have to be able to, otherwise you're gonna have very dishonest elections." {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/1XbW3rubsj"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/1XbW3rubsj}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 The Recount (@therecount) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/therecount/status/1694868732802171113?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 August 25, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.25am BST\par \par \uc2 Before boarding his plane at Atlanta\u8217\'20\'19s airport, \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  spoke briefly to reporters about his arrest.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWhat has taken place here is a travesty of justice. We did nothing wrong. I did nothing wrong, and everybody knows that,\u8221\'20\'1D Trump said, hewing to the line he has taken repeatedly as the investigations into his attempt to overturn his 2020 election defeat have unfolded.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWhat they\u8217\'20\'19re doing is election interference,\u8221\'20\'1D he added, in a nod to his ongoing campaign to return to the White House in the 2024 polls.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe did nothing wrong at all, and we have every right, every single right, to challenge an election that we think is dishonest.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 He declined to answer shouted questions from the press, including about whether he would pardon himself if he is again elected president.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.12am BST\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  is expected to speak at the Atlanta airport before he boards his private plane, CNN reports.\par \par \uc2 The former president made remarks from the tarmac in Washington DC earlier this month, after {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/aug/03/trump-court-indictment-jack-smith-jan-6"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 appearing in federal court}}}\uc2  to answer charges related to the plot to stop \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  from taking office and the January 6 insurrection.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.03am BST\par \par \uc2 Just before he arrived in Atlanta, \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  (or whoever writes his messages for him) sent an email to supporters that begins: \u8220\'20\'1CThis will be my last email to you before I enter the Fulton County Jail to be ARRESTED as an innocent man.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 It\u8217\'20\'19s a gripping opening line, and indeed, this was a big moment: Trump\u8217\'20\'19s trip to jail was something no former president has ever gone through.\par \par \uc2 The 250-plus words that follow are filled with dire proclamations. \u8220\'20\'1CThe people of our country will watch in shock and horror as a former President \u8211\'20\'13 and the LEADING OPPONENT to the current regime \u8211\'20\'13 gets WRONGFULLY ARRESTED in a notoriously violent jail at the hands of the ruling political party\u8221\'20\'1D, Trump protests in a typical line.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19m now about to enter Fulton County Jail. These are my last words to you before my sham arrest: I WILL NEVER SURRENDER OUR MISSION TO SAVE AMERICA\u8221\'20\'1D he continues.\par \par \uc2 And that\u8217\'20\'19s when the message\u8217\'20\'19s purpose becomes clear: \u8220\'20\'1CPlease make a contribution to peacefully defend our movement as the Deep State tries to JAIL me for life as an innocent man all because I put AMERICA first.\u8221\'20\'1D The text itself is actually a hyperlink that leads to a donation page run by WinRed \u8211\'20\'13 a fundraising platform with {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/apr/03/trump-money-bomb-scheme-republican-fundraising-2020"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a history of ripping off consumers}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Below that is a series of boxes beginning at $24 and going up to $250. Perhaps the goal is to cover the $20,000 he had to put down to bond out of the Fulton county jail.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.57am BST\par \par \uc2 Trump departs Fulton county jail after arrest\par \par \uc2 The motorcade carrying \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  has left the Fulton county jail, about 20 minutes after he arrived to be formally arrested following his indictment by district attorney \uc2 Fani Willis\uc2  on charges related to trying to overturn \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s election victory in the state.\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  seen through car window as he leaves. Photograph: Chandan Khanna/AFP/Getty Images\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 1.06am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.56am BST\par \par \uc2 Fulton county authorities took mugshot of Trump \u8211\'20\'13 report\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  had his mugshot taken during his processing into custody at the Fulton county jail in Atlanta, CNN reports, citing the county sheriff.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 12.58am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.55am BST\par \par \uc2 It\u8217\'20\'19s possible that \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  will have his mug shot taken when he is processed into custody in Fulton county \u8211\'20\'13 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/aug/23/trump-giuliani-georgia-fulton-republican-debate-politics-live-updates"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 as has been the case}}}\uc2  with the other co-defendants who have surrendered at the jail.\par \par \uc2 Outside the jail, rightwing Georgia congresswoman \uc2 Marjorie Taylor Greene\uc2 , who was not involved in the case but is nonetheless an enthusiastic supporter of the former president, announced she had made her own mugshot, and encouraged other Trump fans to do the same:\par \par \uc2 enltr\u8220\'20\'1CTo stand in solidarity with Pres. Trump, I made my own mug shot with the Fulton County Jail here logo and I changed it to my official photo on \uc2 Twitter\uc2 . So, I encourage everyone to make your own MAGA mug shot.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Rep. \uc2 Marjorie Taylor-Greene\uc2  (R-GA) outside the Fulton County Jail {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/mufFeGxxPv"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/mufFeGxxPv}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 The Recount (@therecount) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/therecount/status/1694855441023652254?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 August 24, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 She has indeed made the mugshot {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/RepMTG/photo"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 her Twitter (or X) profile picture}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 12.59am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.46am BST\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s booking details have been posted on {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://justice.fultoncountyga.gov/PAJailManager/JailingDetail.aspx?JailingID=1472740"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the Fulton county jail\u8217\'20\'19s website}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Besides listing the 13 charges the former president faces, the jail provides his identifying details: white male, 6ft 3in in height, 215lbs, blond or strawberry hair, blue eyes.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 12.47am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.41am BST\par \par \uc2 Trump surrenders at Fulton county jail\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  has been officially booked into the Fulton county jail after being indicted for trying to meddle in Georgia\u8217\'20\'19s elections three years ago, Reuters reports.\par \par \uc2 The former president plans to post a $200,000 bond that will allow him to avoid spending time behind bars before trial, but it is possible he will have his mugshot taken today \u8211\'20\'13 the first time this has happened in the four separate criminal cases he is now facing.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 1.31am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.34am BST\par \par \uc2 Trump arrives at Fulton county jail to be formally arrested in Georgia election case\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  has arrived at the Fulton county jail in Atlanta, where he will be formally arrested after his indictment by the district attorney \uc2 Fani Willis\uc2  on charges related to his efforts to overturn \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s 2020 election victory in the state.\par \par \uc2 The former president is not expected to spend time in jail, having reached an agreement to post a $200,000 bond that will guarantee his release as his case moves through the court system.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 12.35am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.32am BST\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s the scene outside the Fulton county jail in Atlanta, where \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  will soon arrive:\par \par \uc2 Supporters of \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  rest near the Fulton county jail. Photograph: Ben Gray/AP Rightwing Georgia congresswoman \uc2 Marjorie Taylor Greene\uc2  speaks to the media near the entrance of the jail. Photograph: Dustin Chambers/Reuters Sheriffs secure the area around the jail before Trump\u8217\'20\'19s arrival. Photograph: Erik S Lesser/\uc2 EPA\uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  supporters and their swag outside the county jail. Photograph: Brynn Anderson/AP\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.24am BST\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s video of the moment \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  disembarked in Atlanta:\par \par \uc2 enltrDonald Trump arrives in Atlanta, Georgia, to surrender to Fulton County authorities.\par \par \uc2 He stops and mouths, \u8220\'20\'1CThank you very much.\u8221\'20\'1D {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/CstAgs91d8"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/CstAgs91d8}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 The Recount (@therecount) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/therecount/status/1694851630850617388?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 August 24, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.16am BST\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  disembarked from his plane, flashing a thumbs up to a small group of reporters gathered below the boarding stairs.\par \par \uc2 He made no comments before getting into one of the many black SUVs that make up his motorcade.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.06am BST\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s a livestream of \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s plane, which is currently taxiing at Hartsfield-Jackson Atlanta international airport:\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 12.07am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.04am BST\par \par \uc2 Trump lands in Atlanta\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s plane has landed in Atlanta.\par \par \uc2 Next stop: the Fulton county jail, where the former president will be formally arrested, but is expected to be released after posting a $200,000 bond.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.54pm BST\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  has enlisted a local bonding company to secure his release from the Fulton county jail, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.ajc.com/news/lawrenceville-company-to-post-trumps-200k-bond/42RB75CEMRAZ3PJVXPOUDTKEDI/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the Atlanta Journal-Constitution reports}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe will be posting his bond when he arrives,\u8221\'20\'1D Charles Shaw, the CEO of Foster Bail Bonds LLC in Lawrenceville, an Atlanta suburb, told the paper.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://edition.cnn.com/politics/live-news/trump-georgia-surrender-indictment-08-24-23/h_850e98593c4f1a24ccc456c1ff4e8d34"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 According to CNN}}}\uc2 , Trump paid 10% of the $200,000 bond, which was one of the conditions for his release agreed to with the Fulton county district attorney \uc2 Fani Willis\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 11.56pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.36pm BST\par \par \uc2 When \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  arrives at the Fulton county jail, he\u8217\'20\'19ll have company.\par \par \uc2 Besides the Secret Service agents guarding him, CNN reports his newly retained lawyer will be there for his formal arrest:\par \par \uc2 enltrDonald Trump's newly-hired lawyer, Steven Sadow will accompany Trump to the Fulton County jail on Thursday, CNN has learned\par \par \uc2 Sadow is currently waiting at the airport in Atlanta and will ride in the former president's motorcade to the jail\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Alayna Treene (@alaynatreene) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/alaynatreene/status/1694824739359817742?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 August 24, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 Trump is not expected to spend time in jail, having posted a $200,000 bond as part of an agreement that will allow him to remain free while his case moves towards trial.\par \par \uc2 CNN reports that the rightwing Georgia congresswoman \uc2 Marjorie Taylor Greene\uc2  will also be waiting for Trump when he lands in Atlanta:\par \par \uc2 enltrRep. \uc2 Marjorie Taylor Greene\uc2  also stopped by the Atlanta airport where Trump is expected to arrive later this evening before she headed to the Fulton County jail where she plans to protest his indictment {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/MFQcajSApQ"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/MFQcajSApQ}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Alayna Treene (@alaynatreene) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/alaynatreene/status/1694839440630272049?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 August 24, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 The former president is currently in the air and expected to land at Hartsfield-Jackson Atlanta international airport shortly.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 11.39pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.21pm BST\par \par \uc2 Georgia is far from the only state grappling with the aftermath of \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s attempt to stay in the White House despite losing the 2020 election. As the Guardian\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/alice-herman"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Alice Herman}}}\uc2  reports, local officials in Michigan are outraged by the fake elector scandal that occurred there:\par \par \uc2 When the news broke in 2020 that 16 Republicans in Michigan had signed a certificate falsely claiming to be electors for {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/donaldtrump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Donald Trump}}}\uc2 , Rosemary Herweyer was dismayed to find a prominent local politician, Kent Vanderwood, listed among the signatories.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CHis willingness to sign a fake elector paper and try to send that in and negate Michigan\u8217\'20\'19s actual vote speaks to his integrity,\u8221\'20\'1D Herweyer said of Vanderwood, who was then a member of the Wyoming, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/michigan"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Michigan}}}\uc2 , city council. \u8220\'20\'1CHow can I trust anything he does?\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Vanderwood, who served on the city council for 16 years before being elected mayor of the city in 2022, now {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/jul/18/michigan-false-electors-charged"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 faces eight felony charges}}}\uc2  for his role as a false elector during the 2020 presidential election. Fifteen other Republicans, including the former co-chair of the Michigan GOP, have also been criminally charged.\par \par \uc2 Since Michigan\u8217\'20\'19s attorney general, Dana Nessel, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=FuwbYaBonjI"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 announced}}}\uc2  the charges on 18 July \u8211\'20\'13 making the state the first to prosecute a full slate of false electors involved in the seven-state scheme \u8211\'20\'13 voters and good government groups have begun a push for elected officials involved to resign. Across the state, a mayor, a school board member and a township clerk whose role includes administering elections have each been arraigned and have pleaded not guilty, and in each community, constituents are pushing for accountability.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1COver 2 million people voted for \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  in Michigan, and Stan Grot decided that our votes didn\u8217\'20\'19t matter,\u8221\'20\'1D said Alisa Diez, a Democratic party activist in Shelby Township, where Stanley Grot, one of the 16 false electors, currently serves as township clerk.\par \par \uc2 After Grot was charged, the state {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cbsnews.com/detroit/news/michigan-clerk-stripped-of-election-duties-after-being-charged-for-acting-as-fake-elector-in-2020-3/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 stripped him}}}\uc2  of his ability to administer elections, but he remains in office.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/aug/23/michigan-false-electors-trump-state-republicans"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Fury at Michigan officials charged in 2020 false electors scheme: \u8216\'20\'18This isn\u8217\'20\'19t who we are\u8217\'20\'19}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.00pm BST\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  will appear on \uc2 Newsmax\uc2  with host Greg Kelly at 9pm tonight following his surrender at the Fulton county jail in Atlanta, Georgia, the Guardian\u8217\'20\'19s Hugo Lowell reports.\par \par \uc2 enltrNew: Trump will be on \uc2 Newsmax\uc2  with Greg Kelly at 9pm tonight after his surrender at Fulton County jail, per notice\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Hugo Lowell (@hugolowell) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/hugolowell/status/1694829636440461592?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 August 24, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 Trump\u8217\'20\'19s \uc2 Newsmax\uc2  appearance later tonight will follow a post he made on his Truth Social account earlier today as he prepared to make his way from New Jersey to Georgia, which read:\par \par \uc2 I have to start getting ready to head down to Atlanta, Georgia, where Murder and other Violent Crimes have reached levels never seen before, to get ARRESTED by a Radical Left, Lowlife District Attorney, \uc2 Fani Willis\uc2 , for A PERFECT PHONE CALL, and having the audacity to challenge a RIGGED & STOLEN ELECTION. THE EVIDENCE IS IRREFUTABLE! ARREST TIME: 7:30 P.M.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 11.10pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.47pm BST\par \par \uc2 The Guardian\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s Hugo Lowell reports that a federal judge has set an 18 September hearing for former Donald Trump Department of Justice official Jeffrey Clark\u8217\'20\'19s request to remove his case to federal court.\par \par \uc2 Clark has been charged alongside Trump in a 41-count indictment over efforts to subvert the 2020 presidential elections in Georgia.\par \par \uc2 enltrNew: Federal judge sets Sep. 18 hearing for former Trump DOJ official Jeffrey Clark's request to remove his case to federal court. Clark has argued Fulton County charges involved actions within his official capacity as a DOJ official.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Hugo Lowell (@hugolowell) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/hugolowell/status/1694824443040636935?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 August 24, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 10.54pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.35pm BST\par \par \uc2 Republican presidential candidate \uc2 Chris Christie\uc2  appeared on Morning Joe following Wednesday evening\u8217\'20\'19s debate during which he refused to raise his hand when the presidential candidates were asked whether they would support \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  if he becomes the GOP nominee.\par \par \uc2 Christie spoke about the other candidates who raised their hands, saying: \u8220\'20\'1CI can only assume it\u8217\'20\'19s because they\u8217\'20\'19re auditioning for what they\u8217\'20\'19re praying to be a future vice-president nomination or cabinet bid in a Trump administration.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The problem for them is that \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  is never going to be president of the United States again \u8230\'20\'26 When someone says they\u8217\'20\'19re willing to suspend the constitution, that they took an oath to preserve, protect and defend. That\u8217\'20\'19s just wrong \u8230\'20\'26 It\u8217\'20\'19s not a hard answer for them either, but they\u8217\'20\'19re playing a political game.\par \par \uc2 enltr"When someone says they're willing to suspend the Constitution, that they took an oath to preserve, protect and defend. That's just wrong... It's not a hard answer for them either, but they're playing a political game."\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/GovChristie?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @GovChristie}}}\uc2  on GOP candidate's willingness to back Trump {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/m3KdwsmsYH"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/m3KdwsmsYH}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Morning Joe (@Morning_Joe) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/Morning_Joe/status/1694815974141104428?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 August 24, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 10.37pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.18pm BST\par \par \uc2 As \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  makes his way to Atlanta, Georgia, his former vice -president and current Republican opponent \uc2 Mike Pence\uc2  has urged him to join the other candidates in the next GOP debate.\par \par \uc2 Speaking to the Associated Press in a new interview after Wednesday night\u8217\'20\'19s debate, Pence said:\par \par \uc2 I believe that this country\u8217\'20\'19s in a lot of trouble and every man and woman who aspires to carry the banner of the Republican party owes it to the American people to get on that stage to answer the tough questions and to articulate their vision for the future of the country and let the voters decide.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 10.25pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.55pm BST\par \par \uc2 The legal gears continue to grind forward for the other people indicted in Georgia alongside \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , including Jeff Clark, the former justice department official who has asked to move his trial to federal court.\par \par \uc2 Politico reports that the judge handling his case will hold a hearing on 18 September on the matter:\par \par \uc2 enltrBREAKING: Judge Steve JONES has ordered a Sept. 18 hearing on Jeff CLARK's bid to remove his criminal charges to federal court. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/4vvAyjNHAY"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/4vvAyjNHAY}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/5TyneBbJ0b"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/5TyneBbJ0b}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Kyle Cheney (@kyledcheney) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/kyledcheney/status/1694808847339147393?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 August 24, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.42pm BST\par \par \uc2 This was the scene as the motorcade of \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  made its way from his resort in Bedminster, New Jersey, to the airport in Newark:\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s motorcade on its way to the airport in Newark, New Jersey. Photograph: Reuters\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 9.43pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.37pm BST\par \par \uc2 Squint through the gloomy Newark, New Jersey weather in this Sky News footage and you can see the flashing lights of what appears to be \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s motorcade arriving at the plane that will take him to Georgia:\par \par \uc2 enltrBREAKING: New pictures of Newark airport in New Jersey where Trump's motorcade has arrived ahead of his flight to Atlanta {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/PAiZ4D1jU3"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/PAiZ4D1jU3}}}\par \par \uc2 ?? Sky 501, Virgin 602, Freeview 233 and \uc2 YouTube{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/X8GGDyP6hq"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/X8GGDyP6hq}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Sky News (@SkyNews) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/SkyNews/status/1694810083861975461?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 August 24, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.34pm BST\par \par \uc2 Trump arrives at airport for flight to Georgia\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  has arrived at the airport in Newark, New Jersey, where he will board his flight to face arrest in Atlanta, CNN reports.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.27pm BST\par \par \uc2 In his order to begin Kenneth Chesebro\u8217\'20\'19s trial on 23 October, Judge Scott McAfee noted that the schedule does not apply to anyone else.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CAt this time, these deadlines do not apply to any co-defendant,\u8221\'20\'1D the judge wrote. That\u8217\'20\'19s good news for the 18 other people indicted by the Fulton county district attorney, \uc2 Fani Willis\uc2 , including \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , whose lawyers are currently {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/aug/17/trump-georgia-indictment-trial-move-federal-court"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 trying to get his case moved to federal court}}}\uc2 , which could delay it for months \u8211\'20\'13 potentially long enough for him to win his race for the White House.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 9.28pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.13pm BST\par \par \uc2 Judge sets 23 October trial date for Trump lawyer Kenneth Chesebro\par \par \uc2 Kenneth Chesebro, another of \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s attorneys who advised him on his plot to overturn his 2020 election loss, requested a speedy trial after being indicted in Georgia, and it appears his wish has been granted.\par \par \uc2 The Atlanta Journal-Constitution reports that the judge handling his case has said Chesebro\u8217\'20\'19s trial will begin on 23 October \u8211\'20\'13 as Fulton county district attorney \uc2 Fani Willis\uc2  had proposed:\par \par \uc2 enltrFulton Judge Scott McAfee laying out a very aggressive timetable for Chesebro's Fulton trial, with an Oct. 23, 2023 start date. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/uqOmqzuHRc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/uqOmqzuHRc}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Tamar Hallerman (@TamarHallerman) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/TamarHallerman/status/1694803223687598353?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 August 24, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 enltrPer McAfee's scheduling order:\par \par \uc2 Arraignments - Sept. 6\par \par \uc2 Discovery - by Sept. 20\par \par \uc2 Motions - by Sept. 27\par \par \uc2 Pretrial conference - Sept. 29\par \par \uc2 Motions hearing - TBD\par \par \uc2 Trial - Oct. 23\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Tamar Hallerman (@TamarHallerman) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/TamarHallerman/status/1694803508430618672?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 August 24, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 9.23pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.01pm BST\par \par \uc2 When \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  appears at the Rice Street jail in Atlanta this evening, the Guardian\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/hugo-lowell"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Hugo Lowell}}}\uc2  reports that he will be treated like any other defendant. That includes having his mugshot taken, and his height and weight recorded:\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  was expected to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/aug/24/trump-replaces-lawyer-hours-before-surrender-georgia-jail-reports"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 surrender at the Fulton county jail}}}\uc2  on Thursday evening on racketeering and conspiracy charges over his efforts to overturn the 2020 election results, yielding to the criminal justice process in Georgia that will involve him being processed like any other defendant.\par \par \uc2 The former president\u8217\'20\'19s arrival in Georgia follows {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/aug/24/republican-candidates-spectre-of-trump-haunts-debate"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a presidential debate}}}\uc2  featuring his main rivals for the 2024 Republican nomination, a race in which Trump remains the overwhelmingly dominant frontrunner despite his many legal troubles.\par \par \uc2 Trump had his legal team negotiate his booking to take place during the primetime viewing hours for the cable news networks, as he sought to discredit the charges and distract from the indignity of the surrender by turning it into a spectacle.\par \par \uc2 But Trump was expected to be booked by authorities without the special privileges afforded to him in his other criminal cases, being subject to a mugshot that he had desperately sought to avoid, having his fingerprints taken, as well as having his height and weight recorded.\par \par \uc2 Trump faced his fourth indictment since leaving office when he was charged in a 41-count indictment by the Fulton county district attorney, \uc2 Fani Willis\uc2 , last week, that described Trump and 18 allies as having engaged in a criminal enterprise to reverse his 2020 election defeat.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/aug/24/trump-surrender-georgia-jail-overturn-2020-election"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Trump to surrender at Georgia jail on charges he sought to overturn 2020 election}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.57pm BST\par \par \uc2 Trump departs resort to face arrest in Georgia\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  has left his Bedminster, New Jersey, resort for Georgia, where he is expected to be formally arrested this evening, CNN reports.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 9.02pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.48pm BST\par \par \uc2 Trump says to expect arrest at 7.30pm eastern\par \par \uc2 In {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://truthsocial.com/@realDonaldTrump/posts/110946087136303137"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a post on his Truth social account}}}\uc2 , \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  said he expected to be arrested in Georgia at 7.30pm eastern time, and fired off his typical string of insults at Fulton county district attorney \uc2 Fani Willis\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Here it is, in full:\par \par \uc2 231,000,000 Views, and still counting. The Biggest Video on Social Media, EVER, more than double the Super Bowl! But please excuse me, I have to start getting ready to head down to Atlanta, Georgia, where Murder and other Violent Crimes have reached levels never seen before, to get ARRESTED by a Radical Left, Lowlife District Attorney, \uc2 Fani Willis\uc2 , for A PERFECT PHONE CALL, and having the audacity to challenge a RIGGED & STOLEN ELECTION. THE EVIDENCE IS IRREFUTABLE! ARREST TIME: 7:30 P.M.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.32pm BST\par \par \uc2 Georgia authorities release Meadows mugshot\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s the mugshot for \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s former chief of staff \uc2 Mark Meadows\uc2 , which Georgia authorities released following his booking today:\par \par \uc2 Mark Meadows\uc2  was \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s chief of staff at the end of his term. Photograph: Fulton County Sheriff\u8217\'20\'19S Office/Reuters\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.26pm BST\par \par \uc2 John Eastman\u8217\'20\'19s bad week just got worse. A lawyer who advised \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  on his legal strategy to stop \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s election victory, Eastman was among those indicted in Georgia by district attorney \uc2 Fani Willis\uc2  for his attempt to tamper with the state\u8217\'20\'19s election.\par \par \uc2 On Tuesday, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/aug/22/scott-hall-georgia-election-2020-defendant-trump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 he was formally booked}}}\uc2  into the Fulton county jail, and Politico reports that today, the California bar is considering whether to revoke his license to practice law:\par \par \uc2 enltrHAPPENING NOW: John Eastman's disbarment proceedings are underway in California, even as his indictment is now pending in Georgia.\par \par \uc2 Currently on the stand: Matthew Seligman, an expert in the Electoral Count Act, who is explaning its provisions as Eastman looks on.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Kyle Cheney (@kyledcheney) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/kyledcheney/status/1694786334869569871?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 August 24, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 Eastman\u8217\'20\'19s name popped up repeatedly in the January 6 committee investigation last year, which discovered that {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/jun/16/trump-lawyer-john-eastman-presidential-pardon"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 he asked Trump for a pardon}}}\uc2  days after the attack on the Capitol.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.11pm BST\par \par \uc2 Interim summary\par \par \uc2 Hello US politics live blog readers, things are very busy at the Fulton county jail in Atlanta and are only going to get busier as more co-defendants in \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s Georgia election subversion case negotiate bail then turn themselves in \u8211\'20\'13 and the former US president is due there this evening to surrender himself. We\u8217\'20\'19re covering all this as it happens, so do stick with Guardian US.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s where things stand:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Mark Meadows\uc2 , \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s chief of staff at the White House, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/aug/24/trump-georgia-fulton-rally-republican-debate-politics-live-updates?page=with:block-64e79e8b8f08a1ac5546278c#block-64e79e8b8f08a1ac5546278c"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 turned himself in}}}\uc2  at the Fulton county jail in Atlanta, Georgia to face racketeering charges.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Jeff Clark, a former justice department attorney and a codefendant in the Georgia election subversion case, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/aug/24/trump-georgia-fulton-rally-republican-debate-politics-live-updates?page=with:block-64e795218f08a1ac55462735#block-64e795218f08a1ac55462735"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 struck}}}\uc2  a $100,00 bond agreement with Fulton county prosecutors.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Fani Willis\uc2 , Fulton county district attorney, has proposed for the Georgia racketeering (Rico) case against Trump and his 18 co-defendants to start on 23 October 2023, according to a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.documentcloud.org/documents/23926016-request-for-oct-23-trial-date"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 court filing}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Brad Raffensperger\uc2 , Georgia\u8217\'20\'19s secretary of state, has {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/aug/24/trump-georgia-fulton-rally-republican-debate-politics-live-updates?page=with:block-64e7768a8f08a1ac5546257d#block-64e7768a8f08a1ac5546257d"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 been subpoenaed}}}\uc2  to testify at a Monday hearing examining efforts by Meadows to move the Fulton county criminal case to federal court.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The Republican-ledHouse judiciary committee launched a congressional investigation into the Willis, over whether her prosecution of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/donaldtrump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Donald Trump}}}\uc2  is \u8220\'20\'1Cpolitically motivated\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.02pm BST\par \par \uc2 Mark Meadows\uc2  is trying to get his part of the Georgia organized crime case against him, \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  and others moved from state court to federal court and had hoped to be able to avoid having to surrender at the jail in Atlanta this week with his co-defendants.\par \par \uc2 Two days ago {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/aug/22/mark-meadows-asks-judge-to-block-arrest-georgia"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 he asked}}}\uc2  a federal court in an emergency motion to block his arrest, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://storage.courtlistener.com/recap/gov.uscourts.gand.319225/gov.uscourts.gand.319225.17.0.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 according to court documents}}}\uc2  filed on Tuesday. He asked the court to \u8220\'20\'1Cprotect\u8221\'20\'1D him from arrest before a Monday 28 August, hearing on his request to move the case out of the Fulton county superior court to the district court of northern {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/state-of-georgia"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Georgia}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Meadows is arguing that the charges against him concern his actions as an officer of the federal government. Trump is expected to argue likewise in due course.\par \par \uc2 In response, Fulton county district attorney {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/aug/14/donald-trump-prosecutor-fulton-county-georgia-district-attorney-fani-willis"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Fani Willis}}}\uc2  unequivocally {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/aug/22/mark-meadows-asks-judge-to-block-arrest-georgia"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 rejected}}}\uc2  the request, noting: \u8220\'20\'1CI am not granting any extensions\u8221\'20\'1D and that he was no different from any other defendant in a criminal case.\par \par \uc2 Willis indicated that if Meadows does not turn himself in by noon on Friday, he would be arrested, writing: \u8220\'20\'1CAt 12:30 pm on Friday I shall file warrants in the system.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Early Thursday afternoon, he surrendered to the jail to be booked.\par \par \uc2 The Fulton county district attorney, \uc2 Fani Willis\uc2 , speaks to the media after a grand jury brought back indictments against former president \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  and 18 of his allies in their attempt to overturn the state\u8217\'20\'19s 2020 election results, in Atlanta, Georgia. Photograph: Elijah Nouvelage/Reuters\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 8.39pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.45pm BST\par \par \uc2 Mark Meadows\uc2  has turned himself in at Fulton county jail in Atlanta, just under 24 hours before the deadline of noon Friday for all 19 defendants in the Georgia case to surrender, to face the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/commentisfree/2023/aug/15/trump-charges-fulton-county-white-house-odds"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 criminal charges}}}\uc2  against him\par \par \uc2 Like \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  and all 17 fellow co-defendants, Meadows is charged with being part of an organized crime racket in relation to working with others to overturn \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s victory in Georgia in the 2020 presidential election.\par \par \uc2 In official terms, he\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/aug/14/donald-trump-fulton-county-georgia-indictment-charges-pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 charged with}}}\uc2  violating the Georgia Racketeer Influenced and Corrupt Organizations Act (Rico) and \u8220\'20\'1Csolicitation of violation of oath by a public officer\u8221\'20\'1D, in the latter case being accused in the indictment of \u8220\'20\'1Cunlawfully soliciting, requesting and importuning Georgia secretary of state \uc2 Brad Raffensperger\uc2  \u8230\'20\'26 to engage in conduct constituting the felony offense\u8230\'20\'26by unlawfully altering, unlawfully adjusting and otherwise unlawfully influencing the certified returns for presidential electors for the November 3, 2020, election in Georgia\u8230\'20\'26\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 This, in short, related to efforts from Trump\u8217\'20\'19s mob to persuade Raffensperger to rustle up enough non-existent Republican votes falsely that it would give the-then president the win in the crucial state.\par \par \uc2 enltrFormer Trump White House chief of staff \uc2 Mark Meadows\uc2  has surrendered at the Fulton County Jail.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/iJOBgg63Ya"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/iJOBgg63Ya}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Keith Boykin (@keithboykin) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/keithboykin/status/1694781636523565227?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 August 24, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 7.58pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.18pm BST\par \par \uc2 Former White House chief of staff Meadows surrenders in Georgia\par \par \uc2 Mark Meadows\uc2 , \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s chief of staff at the White House, has just turned himself in at the Fulton county jail in Atlanta, Georgia.\par \par \uc2 He faces racketeering charges alongside Trump and 17 other co-defendants.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 7.20pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.00pm BST\par \par \uc2 Here are some of the latest images from the newswires taken at the Fulton county jail in Atlanta, Georgia, where \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  is expected to surrender this evening on racketeering and conspiracy charges.\par \par \uc2 Demonstrators gather outside the Fulton county jail in Atlanta, Georgia. Photograph: Anthony Stalcup/UPI/\uc2 Shutterstock\uc2  A man, calling himself \u8216\'20\'18hat man\u8217\'20\'19, stands near the entrance of Fulton county jail. Photograph: Brendan McDermid/Reuters Supporters of former president \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  and journalists gather in front of the Fulton county jail in Atlanta. Photograph: Ben Gray/AP Laurie Arbeiter holds signs outside the Fulton county jail. Photograph: Anthony Stalcup/UPI/\uc2 Shutterstock\uc2  Kurt Jantz, supporter of \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  stands near at the entrance of the Fulton county jail. Photograph: Dustin Chambers/Reuters\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 7.08pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.50pm BST\par \par \uc2 Trevian Kutti, a former publicist who was charged in the Georgia case in connection with the intimidation of an Atlanta election worker, has agreed to a $75,000 bond.\par \par \uc2 A Chicago-based publicist, Kutti allegedly threatened a Georgia election worker, Ruby Freeman, with jail if she did not say she participated in election fraud.\par \par \uc2 She faces three counts in the indictment: violation of Georgia\u8217\'20\'19s Rico Act, criminal conspiracy and influencing witnesses.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/aug/15/georgia-investigation-trump-fulton-county-who-to-know"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Georgia\u8217\'20\'19s election investigation: who are the main characters in Trump\u8217\'20\'19s case?}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 7.08pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.39pm BST\par \par \uc2 Former DoJ official Jeff Clark reaches $100,000 bond agreement\par \par \uc2 Jeff Clark, a former justice department attorney, has struck a $100,00 bond agreement with Fulton county prosecutors.\par \par \uc2 Clark\u8217\'20\'19s bail conditions include not communicating with witnesses and co-defendants, reporting to pretrial services by phone every month, surrendering by noon on Friday and not obstructing justice by intimidating witnesses.\par \par \uc2 From Politico\u8217\'20\'19s Kyle Cheney:\par \par \uc2 enltrAnd here is Jeff CLARK's bond order. Also set at $100,000 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/TIDJKdq0uG"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/TIDJKdq0uG}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Kyle Cheney (@kyledcheney) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/kyledcheney/status/1694760300250022044?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 August 24, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 6.48pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.32pm BST\par \par \uc2 Ahead of the surrender, \uc2 Donald Trump{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/aug/24/trump-georgia-fulton-rally-republican-debate-politics-live-updates?page=with:block-64e746528f081f06153f7b46#block-64e746528f081f06153f7b46"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 shook up his legal team}}}\uc2  and retained the top Georgia attorney Steven Sadow, who filed a notice of appearance with the Fulton county superior court as lead counsel, replacing Drew Findling. Trump\u8217\'20\'19s other lawyer in the case, Jennifer Little, is staying on.\par \par \uc2 The reason for the abrupt recalibration was unclear, and Trump\u8217\'20\'19s aides suggested it was unrelated to performance. Still, Trump has a record of firing lawyers who represented him during criminal investigations but were unable to stave off charges.\par \par \uc2 Findling was also unable to exempt Trump from having his mugshot taken, according to people familiar with the matter \u8211\'20\'13 something that personally irritated Trump, even though the Fulton county sheriff\u8217\'20\'19s office had always indicated they were uninterested in making such an accommodatioin.\par \par \uc2 A spokesperson for Trump did not immediately respond to a request for comment.\par \par \uc2 The other 18 co-defendants in the 2020 election subversion case appear to be receiving regular treatment based on online jail records for the former Trump election lawyer John Eastman and others, who had their height, weight and personal appearance made public.\par \par \uc2 Once the booking is complete, Trump was expected to be released immediately on conditions that include stringent witness intimidation restrictions that have not been put in place for his co-defendants, court filings show, until he is due back in state court for arraignment.\par \par \uc2 The Trump legal team could file a motion to remove the case to federal court before then, under a federal statute that allows for such venue changes if the case involves federal officials\u8217\'20\'19 actions taken \u8220\'20\'1Cunder color\u8221\'20\'1D of their office \u8211\'20\'13 as in, if it was part of official duties.\par \par \uc2 Trump could face major difficulties with that argument, however, since he would have to show that taking steps to change the outcome of the 2020 election in Georgia amounted to him acting in his official capacity as president, legal experts have said.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.22pm BST\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  was expected to leave this afternoon from his Bedminster club in New Jersey, where he spends his summers, and fly by private plane to Atlanta Hartsfield-Jackson airport.\par \par \uc2 He was then expected to travel into Atlanta by \uc2 US Secret Service\uc2  motorcade, a person familiar with the matter said.\par \par \uc2 The schedule will involve Trump arriving at the infamously decrepit Rice Street jail, located north-west of downtown Atlanta, in the early evening and the motorcade is expected to snake around into the jail premises down a road lined with dozens of TV cameras.\par \par \uc2 The strategy to turn the surrender into a made-for-television circus has been an effort to discredit the indictments, the person said, as well as to capitalize on the information void left by prosecutors after the events to foist his own spin on the charges.\par \par \uc2 To that end, once Trump is done with the booking process and returns directly to the airport, Trump is weighing delivering impromptu remarks to reporters there before boarding his plane as he liked to do when he was president talking to a pool of reporters, the person said.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.05pm BST\par \par \uc2 Trump prosecutor \uc2 Fani Willis\uc2  calls for Georgia election subversion trial to begin 23 October\par \par \uc2 Fulton county district attorney \uc2 Fani Willis\uc2  has proposed for the Georgia election subversion trial against \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  and his 18 co-defendants to start on 23 October 2023, according to a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.documentcloud.org/documents/23926016-request-for-oct-23-trial-date"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 court filing. }}}\par \par \uc2 The scheduling request by Willis came a day after one of Trump\u8217\'20\'19s co-defendants, Kenneth Chesebro, filed a demand for a speedy trial in the county superior court.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.58pm BST\par \par \uc2 Trump chief of staff \uc2 Mark Meadows\uc2  reaches $100,000 bond agreement in Georgia case\par \par \uc2 Mark Meadows\uc2 , former White House chief of staff for \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , has agreed to a $100,000 bond deal with the Fulton county district attorney\u8217\'20\'19s office, according to court documents.\par \par \uc2 Meadows was charged with two felony counts, including violating the Georgia Rico Act and solicitation of violation of oath from a public officer.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 5.58pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.43pm BST\par \par \uc2 Trump co-defendant \uc2 Mark Meadows\uc2  to argue for moving his Georgia case to federal court\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s more on Fulton county district attorney {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/aug/24/trump-georgia-fulton-rally-republican-debate-politics-live-updates?page=with:block-64e7768a8f08a1ac5546257d#block-64e7768a8f08a1ac5546257d"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Fani Willis\u8217\'20\'19 subpoenas}}}\uc2  for Georgia secretary of state, \uc2 Brad Raffensperger\uc2 , and investigator Francis Watson.\par \par \uc2 A federal judge last week ordered an \u8220\'20\'1Cevidentiary hearing\u8221\'20\'1D on a motion by \uc2 Mark Meadows\uc2 , the former White House chief of staff for \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , to remove the case to federal court. The hearing is expected to take place at 10am ET on Monday.\par \par \uc2 Meadows, who is a co-defendant alongside Trump in the Georgia election subversion case, has {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/aug/22/mark-meadows-asks-judge-to-block-arrest-georgia"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 sought to move his charges to federal court }}}\uc2  and push his Friday deadline to turn himself into Fulton county authorities, aruing the charges concern his actions as an officer of the federal government.\par \par \uc2 On Wednesday, Fulton county district attorney \uc2 Fani Willis\uc2  urged a judge to deny Meadows\u8217\'20\'19 \u8220\'20\'1Cmeritless\u8221\'20\'1D request to delay his arrest in the Georgia case. Willis rejected Meadows\u8217\'20\'19 request for an extension on the deadline, according to Meadows\u8217\'20\'19 emergency motion.\par \par \uc2 I am not granting any extensions. I gave 2 weeks for people to surrender themselves to the court. Your client is no different than any other criminal defendant in this jurisdiction. The two weeks was a tremendous courtesy.\par \par \uc2 Meadows was charged with two felony counts, including violating the Georgia Rico Act and solicitation of violation of oath from a public officer, according to Willis\u8217\'20\'19s indictment. Meadows was on the infamous phone call when Trump asked Raffensperger to \u8220\'20\'1Cfind\u8221\'20\'1D votes to overturn Biden\u8217\'20\'19s victory in the state.\par \par \uc2 He also received {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/sep/26/mark-meadows-text-messages-january-6-breach-book"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 hundreds of text messages}}}\uc2  on 6 January 2021 alerting him and the White House of escalating violence at the US Capitol and asking Trump to intervene.\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  walks with his chief of staff, \uc2 Mark Meadows\uc2 , in May 2020. Photograph: Mandel Ngan/AFP/Getty Images\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 5.46pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.34pm BST\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  is expected to leave his club in New Jersey later this afternoon with a coterie of aides and turn himself to Fulton county authorities this evening, the \uc2 Washington Post{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.washingtonpost.com/national-security/2023/08/24/trump-surrender-fulton-county-jail-georgia-indictment/#link-MYN2BYCACRDUJJEGMV76JW7JYE"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reported}}}\uc2 , citing sources.\par \par \uc2 Trump is not expected to deliver a speech, as he has done in the past after some of his previous indictments, the report says.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.21pm BST\par \par \uc2 Former Trump DoJ official Jeff Clark \u8217\'20\'19s lawyer has arrived at the Fulton county district attorney\u8217\'20\'19s office, apparently to negotiate bond conditions.\par \par \uc2 A federal judge denied Clark\u8217\'20\'19s motion to stay his surrender before noon tomorrow while he tries to have his case removed to federal court.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 6.05pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.00pm BST\par \par \uc2 While former president \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  was preparing to surrender at an Atlanta jail on Thursday, he was apparently also reconsidering his legal defense team.\par \par \uc2 Just hours before Trump is supposed to turn himself in, reports broke that he had shaken up his team. Criminal defense lawyer Steve Sadow is reportedly going to replace Trump\u8217\'20\'19s existing lawyer, Drew Findling, according to the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/2023/08/24/us/trump-georgia-lawyers.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 New York Times.}}}\par \par \uc2 Notably, Findling, alongside Jennifer Little and Marissa Goldberg, was key in negotiating Trump\u8217\'20\'19s $200,000 bond. Little will reportedly stay on the team.\par \par \uc2 The Guardian\uc2  has contacted Sadow for further comment.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 6.05pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.40pm BST\par \par \uc2 Law enforcement officers are on high alert at the Fulton county jail, where \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  is expected to turn himself to be processed later today.\par \par \uc2 Patrick Labat, left, sheriff of Fulton county walks next to the entrance of the Fulton county Jail. Photograph: Dustin Chambers/Reuters Law enforcement officers transport barricade near the entrance of the Fulton county Jail. Photograph: Dustin Chambers/Reuters Law enforcement officers sit on a vehicle near the entrance of the Fulton county Jail. Photograph: Ricardo Arduengo/Reuters\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 4.42pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.30pm BST\par \par \uc2 Georgia secretary of state \uc2 Brad Raffensperger\uc2  subpoenaed to testify in federal court\par \par \uc2 Brad Raffensperger\uc2 , Georgia\u8217\'20\'19s secretary of state, has been subpoenaed to testify at a Monday hearing examining efforts by the former White House chief of staff, \uc2 Mark Meadows\uc2 , to move the Fulton county criminal case to federal court, according to court filings.\par \par \uc2 Fulton county district attorney \uc2 Fani Willis\uc2  also subpoenaed Frances Watson, the chief investigator for Raffensperger during the 2020 election.\par \par \uc2 From Atlanta Journal-Constitution\u8217\'20\'19s Tamar Hallerman:\par \par \uc2 enltrBrad Raffensperger's subpoena also came through, a day after my report with {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/bluestein?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @bluestein}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/IoYPuE3IBG"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/IoYPuE3IBG}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Tamar Hallerman (@TamarHallerman) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/TamarHallerman/status/1694731517245771919?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 August 24, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 4.35pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.14pm BST\par \par \uc2 House Republicans open investigation into Fulton county DA \uc2 Fani Willis\par \par \uc2 The Republican-led House judiciary committee launched a congressional investigation into the Fulton county district attorney, \uc2 Fani Willis\uc2 , over whether her prosecution of \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  is \u8220\'20\'1Cpolitically motivated\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 In a letter to Willis announcing the investigation, House Judiciary chairman Jim Jordan demanded Willis turn over information and communications with the justice department and federal officials by 7 September. The letter states:\par \par \uc2 Ms. Willis\u8217\'20\'19s indictment and prosecution implicate substantial federal interests, and the circumstances surrounding her actions raise serious concerns about whether such actions are politically motivated.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 4.23pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.06pm BST\par \par \uc2 It was perhaps remarkable that the conversation between \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  and \uc2 Tucker Carlson\uc2  was taking place at all.\par \par \uc2 Just five months ago, Carlson was revealed to have said of Trump in a text message:\par \par \uc2 I hate him passionately.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe are very, very close to being able to ignore Trump most nights,\u8221\'20\'1D the then Fox News prime-time anchor said in a message to a colleague in early January 2021 as the former president continued a futile battle to remain in office. \u8220\'20\'1CI truly can\u8217\'20\'19t wait.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 But the two men set aside their differences to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/aug/23/donald-trump-tucker-carlson-interview"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 jointly take on their respective enemies \u8211\'20\'13}}}\uc2  Fox and the rest of the Republican primary field.\par \par \uc2 Despite the array of charges he faces for trying to rig the 2020 presidential election, Trump continued to maintain the false claim that it was stolen from him by the Democrats.\par \par \uc2 Trump also defended the crowd that gathered to hear him speak on 6 January 2021 immediately before the mass assault on Congress that shocked the US and the world and is now the subject of one of Trump\u8217\'20\'19s indictments. Trump suggested that he told the protesters to behave \u8220\'20\'1Cpeacefully and patriotically\u8221\'20\'1D but \u8220\'20\'1Ca very small group\u8221\'20\'1D went to the Capitol.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.57pm BST\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  suggested to \uc2 Tucker Carlson\uc2 , in a \uc2 Twitter\uc2  interview with the far-right former Fox News host staged to undermine the first Republican primary debate in Milwaukee, that he is concerned \u8220\'20\'1Cthe left\u8221\'20\'1D will try to kill him.\par \par \uc2 In a rambling interview, speckled with discussion of conspiracy theories from whether the billionaire sex offender \uc2 Jeffrey Epstein\uc2  was murdered in his jail cell to the role of federal agencies limiting the amount of water in washing machines, Trump took aim at critics on all sides in his traditional derisory fashion.\par \par \uc2 enltrTucker Carlson: \u8220\'20\'1CDo you think it\u8217\'20\'19s possible that [Jeffrey] Epstein was killed?\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Trump: \u8220\'20\'1CI think he probably committed suicide. He had a life with beautiful homes and beautiful everything and all of a sudden he\u8217\'20\'19s incarcerated\u8230\'20\'26\u8221\'20\'1D {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/9Q0UErmpOY"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/9Q0UErmpOY}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 The Recount (@therecount) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/therecount/status/1694518907523260455?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 August 24, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 In the 46-minute interview broadcast on \uc2 Twitter\uc2 , Carlson asked Trump if he is concerned \u8220\'20\'1Cthe left\u8221\'20\'1D, after impeaching and then indicting him, would try to kill him.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThey\u8217\'20\'19re savage animals. They are people that are sick, really sick,\u8221\'20\'1D Trump responded.\par \par \uc2 You have great people that are Democrats. Most of the people in our country are fantastic. And I\u8217\'20\'19m representing everybody \u8230\'20\'26 But I\u8217\'20\'19ve seen what they do.\par \par \uc2 Carlson, who is engaged in a protracted dispute with his former network after being taken off air, launched the interview five minutes before the Republican debate aired on Fox.\par \par \uc2 If that was an attempt to upstage both Trump\u8217\'20\'19s rivals in the 2024 election and Carlson\u8217\'20\'19s ex-employer, then it would appear to have been successful. The interview had more than 80m views on \uc2 Twitter\uc2  within two hours of being posted.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.44pm BST\par \par \uc2 Trump says he 'doesn't know' if the US is headed to civil war\par \par \uc2 Rather than attending the GOP debate, \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  chose to sit down for an interview with the former Fox News host \uc2 Tucker Carlson\uc2 , which was available on X, formerly known as \uc2 Twitter\uc2 , minutes before the debate began.\par \par \uc2 Trump cited his standing in the polls to justify skipping the debate, mocking his opponents\u8217\'20\'19 struggles to gain momentum in the race.\par \par \uc2 You see the polls that have come out, and I\u8217\'20\'19m leading by 50 and 60 points and some of them are at one and zero and two. And I\u8217\'20\'19m saying, do I sit there for an hour or two hours or whatever it\u8217\'20\'19s going to be and get harassed by people who shouldn\u8217\'20\'19t even be running for president?\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI just felt it would be more appropriate not to do the debate,\u8221\'20\'1D he added.\par \par \uc2 During his interview with Carlson, Trump suggested the US could see intensifying political violence and described the day of the January 6 2021 insurrection as one of \u8220\'20\'1Clove and unity\u8221\'20\'1D, according to a \uc2 Washington Post{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.washingtonpost.com/politics/2023/08/23/trump-tucker-carlson-interview/?pwapi_token=eyJ0eXAiOiJKV1QiLCJhbGciOiJIUzI1NiJ9..cs7tJExUPuIrSxxtLPfyblkRmmNHMiQAUwx2nmT0kgM"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  report.}}}\par \par \uc2 People in that crowd said it was the most beautiful day they ever experienced. There was love and unity. I have never seen such spirit and such passion and such love. And I\u8217\'20\'19ve also never seen, simultaneously and from the same people, such hatred at what they\u8217\'20\'19ve done to our country.\par \par \uc2 At the conclusion of the 46-minute interview, Carlson asked the former president if he believed the country was moving toward civil war. \u8220\'20\'1CDo you think it\u8217\'20\'19s possible that there\u8217\'20\'19s open conflict?\u8221\'20\'1D he asked. Trump replied:\par \par \uc2 I don\u8217\'20\'19t know.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 4.10pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.24pm BST\par \par \uc2 Republicans spar over post-Roe \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access in debate\par \par \uc2 Without the specter of Roe v Wade looming overhead, the eight Republican presidential hopefuls on last night\u8217\'20\'19s debate stage faced a new litmus test on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 : whether or not they support a nationwide ban on the procedure after 15 weeks of pregnancy.\par \par \uc2 The former vice-president \uc2 Mike Pence\uc2 , former Arkansas governor \uc2 Asa Hutchinson\uc2  and South Carolina senator Tim Scott all pledged to support a federal 15-week ban.\par \par \uc2 The question from the moderator Martha MacCallum had noted that \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  had consistently been a losing issue for Republicans in state ballots since the Dobbs decision.\par \par \uc2 Nevertheless just one candidate, the North Dakota governor, \uc2 Doug Burgum\uc2 , decisively rejected the idea that Congress ought to regulate \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access. Burgum, who signed North Dakota\u8217\'20\'19s six-week \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban in April, said the conservative mission to overturn Roe was predicated on the belief that states should be allowed to set their own rules on the procedure.\par \par \uc2 What is going to work in New York will never work in North Dakota and vice versa.\par \par \uc2 For decades, Roe v Wade offered Republican candidates a convenient boogeyman. The supreme court ruling was not just about \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  \u8211\'20\'13 swing state conservatives like Burgum could point to Roe as an example of federal overreach.\par \par \uc2 But Wednesday\u8217\'20\'19s debate {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/aug/24/republicans-abortion-stances-gop-debate"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 signaled a schism in the GOP\u8217\'20\'19s position on \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22 .}}}\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/aug/24/republicans-abortion-stances-gop-debate"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Republican candidates grapple with post-Roe positioning on \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22 }}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.34pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.06pm BST\par \par \uc2 Nikki Haley, the former governor of South Carolina and Republican presidential candidates, has performed well on \uc2 Google\uc2  search traffic since her appearance on the GOP primary debate stage last night, FiveThirtyEight\u8217\'20\'19s Nate Silver writes.\par \par \uc2 Tech entrepreneur \uc2 Vivek Ramaswamy\uc2 , who emerged in the absence of \uc2 Donald Trump{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/aug/24/trump-georgia-fulton-rally-republican-debate-politics-live-updates?page=with:block-64e7569c8f081f06153f7c42#block-64e7569c8f081f06153f7c42"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 as a surprise focus of the debate,}}}\uc2  is also likely to rise in the polls as a result of getting more media attention, Silver says.\par \par \uc2 enltrRamaswamy still isn't that well-known (~40% of Iowa caucusgoers didn't know enough to have an opinion in the NBC/DMR Iowa caucus poll) and it's fairly likely that he'll rise in the polls just for getting more media attention and that will in turn beget more attention.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Nate Silver (@NateSilver538) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/NateSilver538/status/1694685901899616471?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 August 24, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 enltrHaley also doing well on \uc2 Google\uc2  search traffic, which tbh I'd trust as much as anything else as an indicator of who "won". She may begin to get more attention from media and donors in the establishment-Republican-who-actually-has-a-chance? (but lol probably not) lane. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/2iUupMQdQJ"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/2iUupMQdQJ}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Nate Silver (@NateSilver538) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/NateSilver538/status/1694687369025200433?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 August 24, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.19pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.56pm BST\par \par \uc2 Who are the 18 other defendants charged in the Trump Georgia election case?\par \par \uc2 The Fulton county district attorney, \uc2 Fani Willis\uc2 , delivered a sweeping indictment earlier this month that charges \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , along with more than a dozen co-defendants, with 41 counts including racketeering, conspiracy, solicitation and filing false statements.\par \par \uc2 These are the other defendants charged in the indictment, which alleges a coordinated group effort to pressure Georgia officials into changing the outcome of the 2020 election.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://interactive.guim.co.uk/uploader/embed/2023/08/archive-zip/giv-13425DS3V01nPJs6K/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Interactive}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.49pm BST\par \par \uc2 Brian Tevis, an attorney representing \uc2 Rudy Giuliani\uc2  in Georgia, said he doesn\u8217\'20\'19t know who paid for the private plane that Giuliani flew on to Atlanta on Wednesday.\par \par \uc2 Tevis, a Georgia attorney who represented the former New York Mayor and Trump attorney in bond and surrender negotiations with the Fulton County district attorney\u8217\'20\'19s office, refused to discuss his client\u8217\'20\'19s finances during a CNN interview.\par \par \uc2 He also told Kaitlan Collins it is \u8220\'20\'1Cvery premature to be saying what is the defense going to be\u8221\'20\'1D when asked if Giuliani would be using his status as \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s lawyer as a defense in the Georgia election subversion case.\par \par \uc2 enltrBrian Tevis, the Georgia attorney who represented \uc2 Rudy Giuliani\uc2  in bond and surrender negotiations, says he doesn't know if he'll continue to represent him in this case and also doesn\u8217\'20\'19t know who paid for that private plane Giuliani took to Georgia. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/JoWfC4iYLC"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/JoWfC4iYLC}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Kaitlan Collins (@kaitlancollins) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/kaitlancollins/status/1694681546177839466?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 August 24, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.35pm BST\par \par \uc2 Nearly an hour into the first Republican debate in Milwaukee, Wisconsin, the Fox News hosts Martha MacCallum and Bret Baier asked the eight candidates on the stage whether they would still support \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  as the Republican presidential nominee if he were convicted of the charges he faces.\par \par \uc2 Six candidates \u8211\'20\'13 North Carolina\u8217\'20\'19s Governor \uc2 Doug Burgum\uc2 , Florida\u8217\'20\'19s Governor \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2 , the former \uc2 UN\uc2  Ambassador Nikki Haley, the former vice-president \uc2 Mike Pence\uc2 , the entrepreneur \uc2 Vivek Ramaswamy\uc2  and South Carolina\u8217\'20\'19s Senator Tim Scot t \u8211\'20\'13 indicated they would still support Trump. Only two candidates \u8211\'20\'13 the former New Jersey governor \uc2 Chris Christie\uc2  and former Arkansas governor \uc2 Asa Hutchinson\uc2  \u8211\'20\'13 said they would not.\par \par \uc2 Most of the candidates on stage raised their hands to say they\u8217\'20\'19d support \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  as the Republican nominee. Photograph: Win McNamee/Getty Images\par \par \uc2 The debate came one day before Trump was expected to surrender to authorities in Fulton county, Georgia, where he has been charged on 13 felony counts related to his efforts to overturn Biden\u8217\'20\'19s 2020 victory in the state. The former president faces 91 total felony counts across four criminal cases.\par \par \uc2 But a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cbsnews.com/news/trump-poll-indictments-2023-08-20/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 CBS News/YouGov survey}}}\uc2  compiled last week found that Trump now holds his largest polling lead to date, as he won the support of 62% of likely Republican primary voters. The survey showed Trump beating his next closest competitor, DeSantis, by 46 points, with every other candidate mired in the single digits.\par \par \uc2 With such stalwart support for Trump among the Republican base, it remains unclear how any of the participants in the Monday debate could capture the nomination. The electoral threat of nominating a twice-impeached former president, who now faces nearly 100 criminal charges, did not escape the attention of at least one debate participant.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe have to face the fact that Trump is the most disliked politician in America,\u8221\'20\'1D Haley said. \u8220\'20\'1CWe can\u8217\'20\'19t win a general election that way.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.23pm BST\par \par \uc2 Trump supporters gather outside Fulton county jail\par \par \uc2 Supporters of \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  are beginning to gather near the Fulton county jail in Atlanta, where the former president is expected to appear later today to surrender to authorities in connection with his attempts to reverse his 2020 election loss in Georgia.\par \par \uc2 Supporters of \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  hold a banner at the entrance of the Fulton County Jail, as he is expected to turn himself in to be processed after his Georgia indictment. Photograph: Dustin Chambers/Reuters Malcolm Davis from Rutledge, GA speaks to the media in Atlanta, Georgia. Photograph: Dustin Chambers/Reuters A vehicle and trailer drive by the Fulton County Jail. Photograph: Mike Stewart/AP\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.11pm BST\par \par \uc2 Vivek Ramaswamy\uc2 , the 38-year-old biotech entrepreneur running {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://projects.fivethirtyeight.com/polls/president-primary-r/2024/national/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 third in Republican polling}}}\uc2 , emerged in the absence of \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  as a surprise focus of the first debate of the Republican primary, showing scant respect for other candidates and drawing heavy fire in return.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe live in a dark moment,\u8221\'20\'1D Ramaswamy declaimed, in the distinctly Trumpian and conspiratorial fashion that has become a hallmark of his campaign.\par \par \uc2 Ramaswamy\u8217\'20\'19s bid for the Republican nomination has been hit by recent scandals over remarks that suggested sympathy for conspiracy theories around the 9/11 terrorist attacks and the January 6 assault on the Capitol. But he has sought to portray himself as a Trump-like outsider taking on the establishment with his extreme views.\par \par \uc2 All the other presidential candidates onstage in Milwaukee, Ramaswamy repeatedly said, were \u8220\'20\'1Cbought and paid for\u8221\'20\'1D by donors.\par \par \uc2 After all eight candidates declined to raise their hands when asked if they believed human behavior was causing the climate crisis, Ramaswamy jumped in, stridently rapping out:\par \par \uc2 Unlock American energy, drill, frack, burn coal, embrace nuclear.\par \par \uc2 Amid exchanges on crime, Ramaswamy attacked the former vice-president \uc2 Mike Pence\uc2 , seeming even to doubt {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=pUMqic2IcWA"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a Republican saint, Ronald Reagan}}}\uc2 , when he said: \u8220\'20\'1CSome others like you on this stage may have an, \u8216\'20\'18It\u8217\'20\'19s morning in America speech.\u8217\'20\'19 It is not morning in America.\par \par \uc2 We live in a dark moment and we have to confront the fact that we\u8217\'20\'19re in an internal sort of cold cultural civil war and we have to recognise that.\par \par \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2 , second to Trump for months but widely seen to be struggling, stood centre stage. But the rightwing Florida governor was often reduced to an onlooker as Ramaswamy threw rhetorical punches and others hit him back, making him a frequent center of the debate.\par \par \uc2 Read the full report by Martin Pengelly here.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/aug/23/vivek-ramaswamy-focus-republican-debate"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Combative Vivek Ramaswamy emerges as surprise focal point of GOP debate}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.04pm BST\par \par \uc2 In a Washington Post/University of Maryland {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.washingtonpost.com/climate-environment/2023/08/23/extreme-weather-climate-change-poll/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 poll}}}\uc2 , 35% of Republicans and Republican-leaning independents said they think the climate change is a major factor in the extreme heat that the US has experienced recently, compared with 85% of those who lean Democratic. Overall, nearly two-thirds of Americans who experienced extremely hot days said climate change was a major factor.\par \par \uc2 Young Republican voters, however, seem increasingly concerned about the climate crisis. A 2022 Pew {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.pewresearch.org/short-reads/2022/12/07/younger-evangelicals-in-the-u-s-are-more-concerned-than-their-elders-about-climate-change/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 poll}}}\uc2  found that 73% of Republicans aged 18-39 thought climate change was an extremely/very or somewhat serious issue.\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, the rightwing groups have been working to boost the fossil fuel industry while undermining the energy transition. Project 2025, a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.semafor.com/article/05/19/2023/the-heritage-foundation-is-looking-for-a-few-good-conservatives-to-deconstruct-the-administrative-state-in-2025"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 $22m}}}\uc2  endeavor by the climate-denying thinktank \uc2 the Heritage Foundation\uc2 , has developed a presidential proposal that lays out how a Republican president could dismantle US climate policy within their first 180 days in office.\par \par \uc2 The GOP candidates who\u8217\'20\'19ve held public office have already given voters a glimpse of how they might approach the climate crisis. The Florida governor, \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2 , has supported projects to build sea walls and improve drainage systems as Florida faces increasingly powerful hurricanes and storm surges, as well as threats from sea level rise. But he has refused to acknowledge the role of global heating on these disasters, scoffing at the \u8220\'20\'1Cpoliticization of the weather\u8221\'20\'1D and pushing bills {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://gizmodo.com/ron-desantis-signs-a-bill-that-mandates-cities-keep-usi-1847176182"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 banning}}}\uc2  Florida cities from adopting 100% clean energy goals. He also barred the state\u8217\'20\'19s pension fund from considering the climate crisis when making investment decisions.\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , who did not attend the debate, has done even more to impede climate action. As president, he rolled back nearly 100 climate regulations, according a \uc2 New York Times{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/interactive/2020/climate/trump-environment-rollbacks-list.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 tally}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Among the candidates who do support doing anything about the climate crisis, most think that thing should be carbon capture. Nikki Haley, who as US ambassador to the United Nations helped orchestrated the US withdrawal from the Paris agreement, has presented carbon capture technologies and tree planting as a way to keep burning fossil fuels while slowing the climate crisis.\par \par \uc2 The consensus among climate scientists is that while such technologies could be a tool in fighting global heating, an {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/environment/2023/jun/06/carbon-capture-and-storage-is-no-free-lunch-warns-climate-chief-hoesung-lee?utm_term=Autofeed&CMP=twt_gu&utm_medium&utm_source=Twitter#Echobox=1686068082"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 overreliance}}}\uc2  on them could cause the world to surpass climate tipping points.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.56pm BST\par \par \uc2 Unlike in recent election cycles, most Republican presidential hopefuls this time around didn\u8217\'20\'19t flat out deny that the climate crisis is real. But on the Fox News debate stage, they made clear that they\u8217\'20\'19re not interested in dwelling on the issues \u8211\'20\'13 or doing much about it.\par \par \uc2 On Tuesday night, the eight candidates were asked to raise their hands if they believed in the reality of human-caused global heating. They all punted.\par \par \uc2 enltrholy shit. Moderators ask for a show of hands of how many candidates believe in human-caused climate change. Not a single candidate raises their hand. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/Oi5IY8nAQ5"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/Oi5IY8nAQ5}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Aaron Rupar (@atrupar) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/atrupar/status/1694521481487609872?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 August 24, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 The Florida governor, \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2 , immediately derailed efforts to elicit a clear yes or no response. \u8220\'20\'1CLet\u8217\'20\'19s have this debate,\u8221\'20\'1D he said, before proceeding not to have it at all, instead criticising \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s response to the fires in Maui.\par \par \uc2 Vivek Ramaswamy\uc2 , a biotech entrepreneur, was notably the only candidate to full-throatedly deny climate science, making the unsubstantiated claim that \u8220\'20\'1Cmore people are dying due to bad climate change policies than they are due to actual climate change\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 There\u8217\'20\'19s no discernible trend of deaths linked to policies encouraging renewable energy. However, extreme heat \u8211\'20\'13 fueled by the climate crisis \u8211\'20\'13 killed about 1,500 people last year, according to \uc2 Centers for Disease Control and Prevention\uc2  records. Researchers estimate that the true figure is closer to 10,000 people every year.\par \par \uc2 Former \uc2 UN\uc2  ambassador Nikki Haley, on the other hand, said \u8220\'20\'1Cclimate change is real\u8221\'20\'1D but then pushed off all responsibility to take care of it on India and China. Both those countries have lower per capita carbon emissions than the US. And as of the latest figures, from 2021, no country had emitted more carbon dioxide since 1850 than the US.\par \par \uc2 The South Carolina senator Tim Scott didn\u8217\'20\'19t offer much in terms of solutions earlier, pointing a finger at the continent of Africa, as well as India and China. Africa accounts for one-fifth of the world\u8217\'20\'19s population and produces about 3% of global greenhouse gas emissions, according to the International Energy Association, while disproportionately experiencing the consequences of climate chaos. The US is responsible for about 14% of global emissions.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 1.58pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.47pm BST\par \par \uc2 Key takeaways from last night's Republican debate\par \par \uc2 Eight {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/republicans"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Republicans}}}\uc2  vying for the party nomination took the debate stage on Wednesday night in Milwaukee, Wisconsin, throwing punches over Ukraine, a federal \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban and more, hoping to increase their chances at defeating the no-show frontrunner.\par \par \uc2 Absent was \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , whose pre-taped interview with the rightwing media personality \uc2 Tucker Carlson\uc2  simultaneously published on \uc2 Twitter\uc2 , now known as X, and sought to siphon away screen time from the debate housed on Fox News, which famously ousted Carlson earlier this year.\par \par \uc2 But Trump\u8217\'20\'19s presence loomed over the debate, even as candidates seemed to somewhat hold back from criticizing the ex-president, as Fox debate moderator Bret Baier put it, \u8220\'20\'1Cthe elephant not in the room\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Here are eight key takeaways from the night:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/aug/24/republican-debate-key-takeaways-trump-ukraine-pence-desantis-ramaswamy"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Trump, Ukraine and a viral song: key takeaways from the Republican debate}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.38pm BST\par \par \uc2 During the first Republican debate on Wednesday, eight candidates attempted to cast themselves as viable alternatives to \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  while, for the most part, studiously ignoring the shadow of the doggedly popular former president who declined to appear on stage.\par \par \uc2 The Republicans alternatively railed on government excesses \u8211\'20\'13 promising, for example, to slash funding for federal programs \u8211\'20\'13 while debating the merits of a federal \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban and calling for an increasingly militarized southern border.\par \par \uc2 The debate was somewhat calmer without belligerent Trump, with the exception of outsider tech entrepreneur \uc2 Vivek Ramaswamy\uc2 , who clashed repeatedly with former vice-president \uc2 Mike Pence\uc2 , former New Jersey governor \uc2 Chris Christie\uc2  and Nikki Haley, the former governor of South Carolina. Other than his increasingly aggressive approach to immigration, \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2  \u8211\'20\'13 meant to be Trump\u8217\'20\'19s most likely challenger \u8211\'20\'13 remained relatively passive.\par \par \uc2 The debate opened with a focus on the economy, as Fox News moderators Bret Baier and Martha MacCallum played a clip of the viral conservative folk hit Rich Men North of Richmond, in which country artist Oliver Anthony describes his economic struggles while lamenting poor people \u8220\'20\'1Cmilkin\u8217\'20\'19 welfare\u8221\'20\'1D. The candidates launched into a brief discussion of the economy \u8211\'20\'13 the first and last point on which they appeared to entirely agree.\par \par \uc2 On the war in Ukraine, the Republicans diverged sharply in their view of the ideal role of US funding for the Ukrainian military. Ramaswamy, who accused supporters of Ukraine of neglecting \u8220\'20\'1Cpeople in Maui or the south side of Chicago\u8221\'20\'1D, drew sharp rebuke from Christie, who said that \u8220\'20\'1Cif we don\u8217\'20\'19t stand up to this kind of autocratic killing, we will be next\u8221\'20\'1D, describing in vivid detail Russia\u8217\'20\'19s bloody occupation of Ukraine. Pence echoed Christie\u8217\'20\'19s position, calling \uc2 Vladimir Putin\uc2  a \u8220\'20\'1Cdictator\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 The Republicans also used the discussion of the war in Ukraine to pivot to the topic of immigration, articulating a vision of a militarized southern US border. DeSantis, whose floundering campaign has suffered repeated false steps and who largely hung back during the debate, jumped into the fold on that topic.\par \par \uc2 When moderator MacCallum introduced the thorny question of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which has energized Democratic voters since Roe v Wade was overturned, the candidates raced to claim their anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  bona fides while splitting over the question of a federal ban.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/aug/24/republican-candidates-spectre-of-trump-haunts-debate"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Read the full report by Alice Herman here.}}}\par \par \uc2 Mike Pence\uc2  and \uc2 Vivek Ramaswamy\uc2  have a heated exchange at the Republican debate. Photograph: Brendan Smialowski/AFP/Getty Images\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/aug/24/republican-candidates-spectre-of-trump-haunts-debate"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Spectre of Trump haunts debate as candidates jostle for spotlight}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 1.38pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.30pm BST\par \par \uc2 What to expect when Trump turns himself in at Fulton county jail\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  is expected to surrender at the Fulton county jail on Thursday evening on racketeering and conspiracy charges over his efforts to overturn the results of the 2020 presidential election in the state of Georgia.\par \par \uc2 The surrender itself is expected to be mundane. At the Rice Street jail north-west of downtown Atlanta, where defendants charged in Fulton county are typically taken, the booking process involves a mugshot, fingerprinting and having height and weight recorded.\par \par \uc2 Trump asked his lawyers and the US secret service to get him an exemption from being photographed, according to sources, though it was not clear whether he will get special treatment. The Fulton county sheriff, Patrick Labat, has previously said Trump would be treated no differently.\par \par \uc2 The other 18 co-defendants in the 2020 election subversion case appear to be receiving regular treatment based on online jail records for the former Trump election lawyer John Eastman and others, who had their height, weight and personal appearance made public.\par \par \uc2 Once the booking is complete, Trump is expected to be released immediately on conditions that include stringent witness intimidation restrictions that have not been put in place for his co-defendants, court filings show, until he is due back in state court for arraignment.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.24pm BST\par \par \uc2 Some Maga fans are worried that {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/aug/24/trump-georgia-fulton-rally-republican-debate-politics-live-updates?page=with:block-64e7491d8f08590bcc98d075#block-64e7491d8f08590bcc98d075"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the pro-Donald Trump rally }}}\uc2  planned for today in Georgia is an \uc2 FBI\uc2  setup, according to an NBC {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nbcnews.com/politics/justice-department/maga-fans-think-trump-rally-atlanta-jail-fbi-setup-rcna101518"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 report. }}}\par \par \uc2 On both Truth Social and X, formerly known as \uc2 Twitter\uc2 , Trump supporters have allegedly voiced concern that undercover law enforcement officials and antifa activists were behind the protest.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWatch out for the \uc2 FBI\uc2  and antifa/blm to stir up a riot,\u8221\'20\'1D one user wrote. Another said: \u8220\'20\'1CBe careful, it could be a setup just like the J6.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The social media posts were highlighted by Advance Democracy, a nonpartisan research organization.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.20pm BST\par \par \uc2 A pro-Trump rally organized by the white nationalist conspiracy theorist Laura Loomer has been planned outside the Fulton county jail where \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  is expected to surrender to authorities later today.\par \par \uc2 Trump posted about the protest on his Truth Social platform on Wednesday, which has been planned for Thursday 10am Eastern time at the jail.\par \par \uc2 A Florida activist and failed political candidate who once described herself as a \u8220\'20\'1C {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cnn.com/2020/08/19/politics/laura-loomer-donald-trump-florida/index.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 proud Islamophobe}}}\uc2  \u8221\'20\'1D, Loomer received Trump\u8217\'20\'19s endorsement for a Republican House primary in 2020. She has been closely linked to Nick Fuentes, the white nationalist who, with the rapper Ye, controversially {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/nov/26/trump-nick-fuentes-dinner-reaction"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 dined with Trump}}}\uc2  last year.\par \par \uc2 enltrWaking up bright and early tomorrow to drive to Atlanta, Georgia from Florida!! See all of you there in front of the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/hashtag/FultonCountyJail?src=hash&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 #FultonCountyJail}}}\uc2  to support President \uc2 Donald J Trump\uc2  on Thursday, August 24!\par \par \uc2 See details below! ???????????????? {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/cuLrJTwkS2"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/cuLrJTwkS2}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Laura Loomer (@LauraLoomer) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/LauraLoomer/status/1694065197646852581?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 August 22, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.09pm BST\par \par \uc2 Steven Sadow, who has {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/aug/24/trump-georgia-fulton-rally-republican-debate-politics-live-updates?page=with:block-64e746528f081f06153f7b46#block-64e746528f081f06153f7b46"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  just been added}}}\uc2  to \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s Georgia legal defense team, is an Atlanta-based attorney whose website profile describes him as a \u8220\'20\'1Cspecial counsel for white collar and high profile defense\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI have been retained to represent President Trump in the Fulton County, Georgia case,\u8221\'20\'1D said Sadow, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://abcnews.go.com/Politics/trump-expected-shake-georgia-legal-team-ahead-surrender/story?id=102517057"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 according}}}\uc2  to ABC.\par \par \uc2 The President should never have been indicted. He is innocent of all the charges brought against him. We look forward to the case being dismissed or, if necessary, an unbiased, open minded jury finding the President not guilty. Prosecutions intended to advance or serve the ambitions and careers of political opponents of the President have no place in our justice system.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.05pm BST\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  shakes up legal team ahead of surrender\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  has shaken up his legal team just hours ahead of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/aug/24/trump-georgia-fulton-rally-republican-debate-politics-live-updates?page=with:block-64e73c5f8f08a1ac5546220b#block-64e73c5f8f08a1ac5546220b"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 his expected surrender}}}\uc2  to authorities in Fulton county on charges over his efforts to overturn the results of the 2020 presidential election in the state of Georgia.\par \par \uc2 Drew Findling is expected to depart the team and be replaced by Steven Sadow, a veteran criminal defense lawyer, the \uc2 New York Times{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/2023/08/24/us/trump-georgia-lawyers.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reported.}}}\par \par \uc2 Findling has served as lead attorney for Trump as it relates to the over two-year probe by the Fulton County district attorney, \uc2 Fani Willis\uc2 , into efforts by the former president and his allies to overturn the state\u8217\'20\'19s 2020 election results.\par \par \uc2 Another attorney, Jennifer Little, is expected to remain and work with Sadow, ABC {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://abcnews.go.com/Politics/trump-expected-shake-georgia-legal-team-ahead-surrender/story?id=102517057"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reported.}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 1.07pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.57pm BST\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  to surrender at Fulton county jail as Maga supporters plan Georgia rally\par \par \uc2 Good morning, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/us-politics"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 US politics}}}\uc2  blog readers. \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  is expected to surrender at the Fulton county jail in Atlanta today on racketeering and conspiracy charges over his efforts to overturn the results of the 2020 presidential election in the state of Georgia.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19ll be going to Atlanta, Georgia, on Thursday to be ARRESTED,\u8221\'20\'1D the former US president posted on his Truth Social platform earlier this week. The date was set during negotiations between Trump\u8217\'20\'19s lawyers and the Fulton county district attorney, \uc2 Fani Willis\uc2 , at her office on Monday.\par \par \uc2 Trump became a criminal defendant in a fourth case last week when a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/aug/14/donald-trump-georgia-indictment-2020-election"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 grand jury handed up a sprawling 41-count indictment}}}\uc2  that accused Trump and 18 co-defendants of engaging in a criminal enterprise and committing election fraud in trying to reverse his 2020 defeat. He has denied wrongdoing in Georgia and in three other indictments {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/jul/28/donald-trump-investigations-criminal-charges-tracker"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 which have produced a total of 91 criminal charges.}}}\par \par \uc2 On Wednesday, Trump {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://truthsocial.com/@realDonaldTrump/posts/110939996350255182"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 shared a screenshot}}}\uc2  of a tweet promoting a protest outside the Fulton county jail ahead of his expected surrender. The rally, promoted by the far-right activist Laura Loomer, is expected to begin at 10am Eastern time with attendees encouraged to bring their Trump-related flags, hats, shirts, signs and \u8220\'20\'1Clove\u8221\'20\'1D to support the former president.\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, Trump\u8217\'20\'19s shadow loomed large on the first Republican primary debate stage last night in Milwaukee, as eight candidates {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/aug/24/republican-candidates-spectre-of-trump-haunts-debate"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 attempted to cast themselves }}}\uc2  as viable alternatives to the former president. Despite his absence, they seemed to somewhat hold back from criticizing Trump, as Fox debate moderator Bret Baier put it, \u8220\'20\'1Cthe elephant not in the room\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020230824ej8o001mv\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
