\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Republican candidates grapple with post-Roe positioning on  \highlight22\uc2 abortion \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 Ava Sasani \par \uc2 926 \uc2 words\par \uc2 24 August 2023\par 16:14 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been a losing issue for GOP since end of federal right but Pence, Scott and Hutchinson urged tightening restrictions\par \par \uc2 Eight Republican presidential hopefuls clashed over the future of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access on Wednesday night in the first debate of the 2024 election cycle.\par \par \uc2 Without the specter of Roe v Wade looming overhead, the candidates faced a new litmus test on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 : whether or not they support a nationwide ban on the procedure after 15 weeks of pregnancy.\par \par \uc2 The former vice-president \uc2 Mike Pence\uc2 , the former Arkansas governor \uc2 Asa Hutchinson\uc2  and South Carolina Senator Tim Scott all pledged to support a federal 15-week ban.\par \par \uc2 The question from the moderator Martha MacCallum had noted that \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  had consistently been a losing issue for Republicans in state ballots since the Dobbs decision.\par \par \uc2 Nevertheless just one candidate, the North Dakota governor, \uc2 Doug Burgum\uc2 , decisively rejected the idea that Congress ought to regulate \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access.\par \par \uc2 Burgum, who signed North Dakota\u8217\'20\'19s six-week \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban in April, said the conservative mission to overturn Roe was predicated on the belief that states should be allowed to set their own rules on the procedure.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWhat is going to work in New York will never work in North Dakota and vice versa,\u8221\'20\'1D Burgum said.\par \par \uc2 For decades, Roe v Wade offered Republican candidates a convenient boogeyman. The supreme court ruling was not just about \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  \u8211\'20\'13 swing state conservatives like Burgum could point to Roe as an example of federal overreach.\par \par \uc2 But Wednesday\u8217\'20\'19s debate signaled a schism in the GOP\u8217\'20\'19s position on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 In a post-Roe landscape, one year after Senator \uc2 Lindsey Graham\uc2  first introduced a federal 15-week ban bill in Congress, Republicans were forced to choose between their purported support for states\u8217\'20\'19 rights and their opposition to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access.\par \par \uc2 Burgum was the lone voice that chose states\u8217\'20\'19 rights.\par \par \uc2 Pence and Scott, both evangelical Christians, said they support a 15-week ban because \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  is a \u8220\'20\'1Cmoral\u8221\'20\'1D question that necessitates federal intervention.\par \par \uc2 Scott said states like \u8220\'20\'1CCalifornia, New York and Illinois\u8221\'20\'1D should not be allowed to offer broad access to the procedure.\par \par \uc2 Pence said \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  was \u8220\'20\'1Cnot a states only issue, it\u8217\'20\'19s a moral issue\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 The former vice-president, who has centered \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  in his bid to court socially conservative voters, condemned his opponents for refusing to back a federal ban.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19m not new to this cause,\u8221\'20\'1D Pence said on Wednesday night. \u8220\'20\'1CCan\u8217\'20\'19t we have a minimum standard in every state in the nation?\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 In his opening remarks, Pence lauded the work of the Trump administration, which placed three conservative justices on the \uc2 US supreme court\uc2  and \u8220\'20\'1Cgave the people a new beginning for the right to life\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Pence also criticized the former South Carolina governor Nikki Haley, who suggested that it would be difficult to gain the requisite congressional support to pass a federal \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban.\par \par \uc2 Haley, the only woman on Wednesday\u8217\'20\'19s debate stage, said Republicans should instead pursue pragmatic legislative goals that could garner bipartisan support in Congress.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CLet\u8217\'20\'19s find consensus, can\u8217\'20\'19t we all agree that we should ban late-term abortions? Can\u8217\'20\'19t we all agree that we should encourage adoptions?\u8221\'20\'1D she said.\par \par \uc2 In his response, Pence directly addressed Haley: \u8220\'20\'1CConsensus is the opposite of leadership.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Susan B Anthony\uc2  Pro-Life America, a powerful anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  lobbying group, praised Pence, Hutchinson and Scott for offering \u8220\'20\'1Ca clear, bold case for national protections for the unborn at least by 15 weeks\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe position taken by candidates like \uc2 Doug Burgum\uc2 , that life is solely a matter for the states, is unacceptable for a nation founded on unalienable rights and for a presidential contender,\u8221\'20\'1D said Marjorie Dannenfelser, the group\u8217\'20\'19s president, in a statement on Wednesday night.\par \par \uc2 Last month, Dannenfelser issued a similar condemnation of the Florida governor, \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2 , for his reluctance to back a federal ban.\par \par \uc2 DeSantis has {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://apnews.com/article/florida-abortion-ban-approved-c9c53311a0b2426adc4b8d0b463edad1"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 supported bills restricting access to \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22 }}}\uc2  \u8211\'20\'13 including a six-week ban in his own state of Florida, but has stopped short of saying he would support a federal ban.\par \par \uc2 Dannenfelser said the Republican presidential candidate should \u8220\'20\'1Cwork to gather the votes necessary in Congress\u8221\'20\'1D to pass a national ban on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  after 15 weeks of pregnancy, adding that DeSantis\u8217\'20\'19s failure to support the ban was \u8220\'20\'1Cunacceptable\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThere are many pressing legislative issues for which Congress does not have the votes at the moment, but that is not a reason for a strong leader to back away from the fight,\u8221\'20\'1D she said in a statement last month.\par \par \uc2 On Wednesday night, Fox News moderators twice asked DeSantis to clarify his position on federal \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  restrictions, but the Florida governor refused to provide a direct answer.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19m going to stand on the side of life,\u8221\'20\'1D DeSantis said. \u8220\'20\'1CI understand Wisconsin is going to do it different than Texas, I understand Iowa and New Hampshire are going to be different, but I will support the cause of life as governor and as president.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Notably, \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  \u8211\'20\'13 the presumed GOP frontrunner \u8211\'20\'13 skipped Wednesday night\u8217\'20\'19s debate.\par \par \uc2 Earlier this year, Trump criticized DeSantis\u8217\'20\'19s position on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , calling Florida\u8217\'20\'19s six-week ban {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/jun/11/ron-desantis-trump-republican-2024"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1Ctoo harsh}}}\uc2  \u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 But the former president appears to share DeSantis\u8217\'20\'19s hesitations about the federal 15-week ban, dodging questions about the proposed restrictions since launching his re-election campaign in March.\par \par \uc2 The Guardian {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/apr/19/donald-trump-federal-abortion-ban-stance"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reported in April}}}\uc2  that Trump considers a federal \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban a losing proposition for Republicans, though his exact vision for the future of US \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access remains unclear.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020230824ej8o001rx\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
