\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Trump, Ukraine and a viral song: key takeaways from the Republican debate\b0\par\par\uc2 Mary Yang \par \uc2 1,387 \uc2 words\par \uc2 24 August 2023\par 14:32 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Former president and frontrunner was absent, but cast a long shadow over the eight presidential hopefuls\par \par \uc2 Eight Republicans vying for the party nomination took the debate stage on Wednesday night in Milwaukee, Wisconsin, throwing punches over Ukraine, a federal \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban and more, hoping to increase their chances at defeating the no-show frontrunner.\par \par \uc2 Absent was \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , whose pre-taped interview with the rightwing media personality \uc2 Tucker Carlson\uc2  simultaneously published on \uc2 Twitter\uc2 , now known as X, and sought to siphon away screen time from the debate housed on Fox News, which memorably ousted Carlson earlier this year.\par \par \uc2 But Trump\u8217\'20\'19s presence loomed over the debate, even as candidates seemed to somewhat hold back from criticizing the ex-president, as Fox debate moderator Bret Baier put it, \u8220\'20\'1Cthe elephant not in the room\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Here are eight key takeaways from the night:\par \par \uc2 A memorable opening with a viral song and jabs at\par \par \uc2 \u8216\'20\'18Bidenomics\par \par \uc2 \u8217\'20\'19\par \par \uc2 The debate kicked off with a question about a controversial conservative country song, Rich Men North of Richmond, whose lyricist complains about taxes and nods to conspiracy theories surrounding the crimes of \uc2 Jeffrey Epstein\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1COur country is in decline,\u8221\'20\'1D said \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2 , to whom the Fox News hosts Martha MacCallum and Bret Baier lobbed the first question. \u8220\'20\'1CWe need to send \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  back to his basement and reverse American decline.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Tim Scott touted his record of voting down government spending bills in the Senate, as well as his work on the 2017 Tax Cuts and Jobs Act, a Trump-era piece of legislation that cut taxes for corporations and wealthy individuals.\par \par \uc2 But Nikki Haley placed the blame on Republicans for spending exorbitantly during the pandemic, calling out Trump for increasing the national debt by $8tn and DeSantis, Scott and \uc2 Mike Pence\uc2  for voting to raise the national debt.\par \par \uc2 Energy independence was also a focus, with candidates broadly advocating for increasing domestic energy production.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CUnlock American energy. Drill, frack, burn, embrace nuclear,\u8221\'20\'1D said Ramaswamy, who later claimed that \u8220\'20\'1Cthe climate change agenda is a hoax\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Trump,\par \par \uc2 \u8216\'20\'18the elephant not in the room\par \par \uc2 \u8217\'20\'19\par \par \uc2 Although Trump was absent, hosts asked candidates to show where they stand on the ex-president.\par \par \uc2 Responding to a call for a show of hands by Baier, most candidates seemed to agree they would support Trump as president, even if he is convicted. Trump has amassed 91 felony counts in four criminal cases this year.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CSomeone\u8217\'20\'19s got to stop normalizing this conduct,\u8221\'20\'1D said Christie, who raised his hand briefly and begrudgingly and has been a loud critic of Trump. \u8220\'20\'1CWhether or not you believe the criminal charges are right or wrong. The conduct is beneath the office of the president of the United States.\u8221\'20\'1D His comments were met with boos from the audience.\par \par \uc2 Ramaswamy, who has defended Trump across all four indictments, continued to do so. He has repeatedly said he would pardon Trump as president and repeated that on the debate stage.\par \par \uc2 Haley added her derision: \u8220\'20\'1CTrump is the most disliked candidate in America. We can\u8217\'20\'19t win an election that way.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The candidates overall said they supported \uc2 Mike Pence\uc2  in his decision to refuse to stop the electoral certification, though Ramaswamy ardently defended Trump through the night and DeSantis refused to answer a question about whether he agreed Pence was right.\par \par \uc2 The war in Ukraine was a sticking point\par \par \uc2 Ramaswamy came out the strongest against increased aid to Ukraine, calling it a \u8220\'20\'1Cdisastrous\u8221\'20\'1D decision and a \u8220\'20\'1Cno-win war\u8221\'20\'1D. And DeSantis, who walked back earlier statements calling the war a \u8220\'20\'1Cterritorial dispute\u8221\'20\'1D, said : \u8220\'20\'1CI would have Europe pull their weight,\u8221\'20\'1D adding: \u8220\'20\'1CI think our support should be contingent on them doing it.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Haley, who served as US ambassador to the United Nations under Trump, delivered perhaps the strongest stance yet, calling Ukraine \u8220\'20\'1Ca pro-American country that was invaded by a thug\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Ramaswamy took a dig at Haley, wishing her \u8220\'20\'1Cwell\u8221\'20\'1D on her \u8220\'20\'1Cfuture career on the boards of \uc2 Lockheed\uc2  and \uc2 Raytheon\uc2 \u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Haley countered, saying that Ramaswamy would hand Ukraine to Russia and China and make America less safe. \u8220\'20\'1CYou have no foreign policy experience, and it shows,\u8221\'20\'1D Haley shot back at Ramaswamy, who said: \u8220\'20\'1CUkraine is not a priority for America.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Christie, who made a visit to the Ukrainian president, \uc2 Volodymyr Zelenskiy\uc2 , weeks earlier, took the opportunity to blast Trump, who has said the war in Ukraine isn\u8217\'20\'19t a vital interest. \u8220\'20\'1CThis is the \uc2 Vladimir Putin\uc2  who \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  called brilliant and a genius. If we don\u8217\'20\'19t stand up against this type of autocratic killing in the world, we will be next,\u8221\'20\'1D said Christie.\par \par \uc2 DeSantis would send troops to the\par \par \uc2 southern border\par \par \uc2 DeSantis said he would use lethal force at the US southern border to counter drug cartels entering the country and treat them as \u8220\'20\'1Cforeign terrorist organizations\u8221\'20\'1D. DeSantis also said he would divert funds from Ukraine to do so and vowed to send troops.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWhen these drug pushers are bringing fentanyl across the border, that\u8217\'20\'19s going to be the last thing they do. We\u8217\'20\'19re going to use force and we\u8217\'20\'19re going to leave them stone cold dead,\u8221\'20\'1D said DeSantis.\par \par \uc2 Scott echoed DeSantis\u8217\'20\'19s rhetoric, saying the southern border was the \u8220\'20\'1Cmost pressing need\u8221\'20\'1D when it comes to national security. He also laid out spending plans to complete Trump\u8217\'20\'19s border wall with $10bn, though he did not mention Trump. Hutchinson also agreed that he would use lethal force, nodding to his time as an undersecretary on border security for \uc2 George W Bush\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Candidates split over federal \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban\par \par \uc2 Each of the eight candidates have at some point identified themselves as anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  but differed over implementing a federal \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban.\par \par \uc2 Haley, the only woman on the debate stage, called herself \u8220\'20\'1Cunapologetically pro-life\u8221\'20\'1D but warned against \u8220\'20\'1Cdemonizing\u8221\'20\'1D the issue, hedging against a federal \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban. DeSantis, who signed into law a six-week ban in Florida saying he believes in a \u8220\'20\'1Cculture of life\u8221\'20\'1D, refused to answer whether he would approve a national ban.\par \par \uc2 Pence, an evangelical Christian who has been the most outspoken anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  candidate, said he would move to implement a national ban at \u8220\'20\'1Cwhen a baby is capable of feeling pain\u8221\'20\'1D though he did not explicitly describe that length.\par \par \uc2 Tim Scott also weighed in and said he would fight for a minimum 15-week ban on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 . Burgum, who signed into law a six-week ban in North Dakota, said he would not sign a federal \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban.\par \par \uc2 (Mostly) quiet on the climate\par \par \uc2 crisis\par \par \uc2 With the exception of Ramaswamy declaring \u8220\'20\'1Cthe climate change agenda\u8221\'20\'1D a \u8220\'20\'1Choax\u8221\'20\'1D, the candidates largely avoided a question about whether Republicans care about the climate crisis, a top issue among younger voters.\par \par \uc2 DeSantis dodged the question, which pointed to the Hawaii wildfires, attacking \u8220\'20\'1Ccorporate media\u8221\'20\'1D for treating Republicans and Democrats differently, claiming Biden was on a beach in Delaware during the disaster.\par \par \uc2 Haley was the only candidate to wholly assert that the climate crisis is real but said the onus should be on China and India to \u8220\'20\'1Creally lower their emissions\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Night of introductions\par \par \uc2 With the frontrunner absent, the lineup on the debate stage featured a bunch of relatively unknown faces.\par \par \uc2 In his first remarks, Ramaswamy didn\u8217\'20\'19t answer a question about the economy but instead said he guessed the audience would want to know \u8220\'20\'1CWho the heck is this skinny guy with a funny last name and what the heck is he doing in the middle of this debate stage?\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 That earned him a later attack from Christie, who said: \u8220\'20\'1CThe last person in one of these debates \u8230\'20\'26 who stood in the middle of the stage and said: \u8216\'20\'18What\u8217\'20\'19s a skinny guy with an odd last name doing up here\u8217\'20\'19 was \uc2 Barack Obama\uc2 , and I\u8217\'20\'19m afraid we\u8217\'20\'19re dealing with the same type of amateur.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Ramaswamy shot back: \u8220\'20\'1CCome on and give me a hug!... Give me that bear hug bro.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Scott, the only Black candidate on the debate stage, repeatedly brought up his back story, growing up in poverty and being raised by a single mom.\par \par \uc2 And Burgum, the governor of North Dakota who arrived at the debate after a trip to the ER earlier on Tuesday, mentioned at several points his \u8220\'20\'1Csmall-town\u8221\'20\'1D identity.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020230824ej8o000md\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
