\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Republicans feud over Trump,  \highlight22\uc2 abortion \highlight\uc2  and climate in first 2024 primary debate\b0\par\par\uc2 Joan E Greve \par \uc2 989 \uc2 words\par \uc2 24 August 2023\par 13:37 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Eight candidates gather in Milwaukee in hopes of catching up to former president in polls\par \par \uc2 Republican presidential candidates clashed over \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s legal woes during the first primary debate of the 2024 campaign season, underscoring the former president\u8217\'20\'19s absence from the event and casting a spotlight on his potential vulnerabilities in a general election rematch against \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Nearly an hour into the debate in Milwaukee, Wisconsin, the Fox News hosts Martha MacCallum and Bret Baier asked the eight candidates on the stage whether they would still support Trump as the Republican presidential nominee if he were convicted of the charges he faces. Six candidates \u8211\'20\'13 North Dakota\u8217\'20\'19s Governor \uc2 Doug Burgum\uc2 , Florida\u8217\'20\'19s Governor \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2 , the former \uc2 UN\uc2  ambassador Nikki Haley, the former vice-president \uc2 Mike Pence\uc2 , the entrepreneur \uc2 Vivek Ramaswamy\uc2  and South Carolina\u8217\'20\'19s Senator Tim Scott \u8211\'20\'13 indicated they would still support Trump. Only two candidates \u8211\'20\'13 the former New Jersey governor \uc2 Chris Christie\uc2  and former Arkansas governor \uc2 Asa Hutchinson\uc2  \u8211\'20\'13 said they would not.\par \par \uc2 Christie, a vocal critic of Trump, called on the fellow debate participants to \u8220\'20\'1Cstop normalizing this conduct\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWhether or not you believe that the criminal charges are right or wrong, the conduct is beneath the office of the president of the United States,\u8221\'20\'1D Christie said. When his criticism was met with some boos from the debate crowd, Christie added: \u8220\'20\'1CBooing is allowed, but it doesn\u8217\'20\'19t change the truth.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Ramaswamy jumped on Christie\u8217\'20\'19s comments, echoing Trump\u8217\'20\'19s complaints about the alleged politicization of federal law enforcement. \u8220\'20\'1CWe have to end the weaponization of justice in this country,\u8221\'20\'1D Ramaswamy said.\par \par \uc2 The debate came one day before Trump was expected to surrender to authorities in Fulton county, Georgia, where he has been charged on 13 felony counts related to his efforts to overturn Biden\u8217\'20\'19s 2020 victory in the state. The former president faces 91 total felony counts across four criminal cases.\par \par \uc2 But a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cbsnews.com/news/trump-poll-indictments-2023-08-20/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 CBS News/YouGov survey}}}\uc2  compiled last week found that Trump now holds his largest polling lead to date, as he won the support of 62% of likely Republican primary voters. The survey showed Trump beating his next closest competitor, DeSantis, by 46 points, with every other candidate mired in the single digits.\par \par \uc2 Rather than attending the debate, Trump chose to sit down for an interview with the former Fox News host \uc2 Tucker Carlson\uc2 , which was available on X, formerly known as \uc2 Twitter\uc2 , minutes before the debate began. Trump cited his standing in the polls to justify skipping the debate, mocking his opponents\u8217\'20\'19 struggles to gain momentum in the race.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CYou see the polls that have come out, and I\u8217\'20\'19m leading by 50 and 60 points and some of them are at one and zero and two. And I\u8217\'20\'19m saying, do I sit there for an hour or two hours or whatever it\u8217\'20\'19s going to be and get harassed by people who shouldn\u8217\'20\'19t even be running for president?\u8221\'20\'1D Trump told Carlson. \u8220\'20\'1CI just felt it would be more appropriate not to do the debate.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Although Trump\u8217\'20\'19s absence and his criminal charges shaped much of the debate, the candidates also sparred over key policy issues like \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  and climate change. Discussing federal \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  policy in the wake of the reversal of Roe v Wade, Pence praised a 15-week \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban as \u8220\'20\'1Can idea whose time has come\u8221\'20\'1D and DeSantis expressed pride over signing Florida\u8217\'20\'19s six-week \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban into law.\par \par \uc2 But Haley was more hesitant to embrace a potential federal ban, a proposal that is {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cbsnews.com/news/dobbs-roe-abortion-politics-opinion-poll-2023-06-22/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 widely unpopular}}}\uc2  with the American people. Describing herself as \u8220\'20\'1Cunapologetically pro-life\u8221\'20\'1D, Haley argued a federal ban would not pass Congress and called on Democrats and Republicans to \u8220\'20\'1Cfind consensus\u8221\'20\'1D on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access.\par \par \uc2 Discussing the climate crisis, Ramaswamy drew some boos from the debate crowd when he denied the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/environment/2021/aug/09/climate-crisis-unequivocally-caused-by-human-activities-says-ipcc-report"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 unequivocal truth}}}\uc2  of human-made climate change. \u8220\'20\'1CThe climate change agenda is a hoax,\u8221\'20\'1D Ramaswamy said.\par \par \uc2 Christie retorted: \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19ve had enough already tonight of a guy who sounds like ChatGPT.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 It was one of several insults directed at Ramaswamy, who has climbed into a distant {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://projects.fivethirtyeight.com/polls/president-primary-r/2024/national/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 third place}}}\uc2  in national polls. Mocking Ramaswamy\u8217\'20\'19s inexperience, Pence said: \u8220\'20\'1CNow is not the time for on-the-job training. We don\u8217\'20\'19t need to bring in a rookie.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Several other presidential candidates \u8211\'20\'13 including the rightwing commentator \uc2 Larry Elder\uc2 , the former Texas congressman \uc2 Will Hurd\uc2  and the mayor of Miami, \uc2 Francis Suarez\uc2  \u8211\'20\'13 failed to meet the \uc2 Republican National Committee\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s qualifications for the debate, leaving them out of the event and further diminishing their primary prospects. Hurd elected to live-tweet his reactions to the debate, and he criticized his opponents who said they would still support Trump in the event of a conviction.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CAnyone who raises their hand in support of \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  as our party\u8217\'20\'19s nominee even if convicted in a court of law is unfit to serve as president,\u8221\'20\'1D Hurd said.\par \par \uc2 But Trump\u8217\'20\'19s criminal charges appear to have only fortified his position as the frontrunner in the Republican presidential primary. According to the \uc2 CBS\uc2  poll, 73% of Trump\u8217\'20\'19s voters say they back the former president partly to \u8220\'20\'1Cshow support for his legal troubles\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 With such stalwart support for Trump among the Republican base, it remains unclear how any of the participants in the Monday debate could capture the nomination. The electoral threat of nominating a twice-impeached former president, who now faces nearly 100 criminal charges, did not escape the attention of at least one debate participant.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe have to face the fact that Trump is the most disliked politician in America,\u8221\'20\'1D Haley said. \u8220\'20\'1CWe can\u8217\'20\'19t win a general election that way.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8226\'20\'22 This article was amended on 24 August 2023. An earlier version incorrectly stated that \uc2 Doug Burgum\uc2  was the North Carolina governor.\par \par \uc2 David Smith contributed\par \par \uc2 reporting from Milwaukee\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020230824ej8o0008e\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
