\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Spectre of Trump haunts debate as candidates jostle for spotlight\b0\par\par\uc2 Alice Herman in Milwaukee, Wisconsin \par \uc2 1,012 \uc2 words\par \uc2 24 August 2023\par 13:19 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  and the southern border energized presidential hopefuls, while the war in Ukraine elicited divided opinions\par \par \uc2 During the first Republican debate on Wednesday, eight candidates attempted to cast themselves as viable alternatives to \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  while, for the most part, studiously ignoring the shadow of the doggedly popular former president who declined to appear on stage.\par \par \uc2 The Republicans alternatively railed on government excesses \u8211\'20\'13 promising, for example, to slash funding for federal programs \u8211\'20\'13 while debating the merits of a federal \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban and calling for an increasingly militarized southern border.\par \par \uc2 The debate was somewhat calmer without belligerent Trump, with the exception of the outsider tech entrepreneur \uc2 Vivek Ramaswamy\uc2 , who clashed repeatedly with former vice-president \uc2 Mike Pence\uc2 , former New Jersey governor \uc2 Chris Christie\uc2  and Nikki Haley, the former governor of South Carolina. Other than his increasingly aggressive approach to immigration, \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2  \u8211\'20\'13 meant to be Trump\u8217\'20\'19s most likely challenger \u8211\'20\'13 remained relatively passive.\par \par \uc2 The debate opened with a focus on the economy, as the Fox News moderators Bret Baier and Martha MacCallum played a clip of the viral conservative folk hit Rich Men North of Richmond, in which the country artist Oliver Anthony describes his economic struggles while lamenting poor people \u8220\'20\'1Cmilkin\u8217\'20\'19 welfare\u8221\'20\'1D. The candidates launched into a brief discussion of the economy \u8211\'20\'13 the first and last point on which they appeared to entirely agree.\par \par \uc2 On the war in Ukraine, the Republicans diverged sharply in their view of the ideal role of US funding for the Ukrainian military. Ramaswamy, who accused supporters of Ukraine of neglecting \u8220\'20\'1Cpeople in Maui or the south side of Chicago\u8221\'20\'1D, drew sharp rebuke from Christie, who said that \u8220\'20\'1Cif we don\u8217\'20\'19t stand up to this kind of autocratic killing, we will be next\u8221\'20\'1D, describing in vivid detail Russia\u8217\'20\'19s bloody occupation of Ukraine. Pence echoed Christie\u8217\'20\'19s position, calling \uc2 Vladimir Putin\uc2  a \u8220\'20\'1Cdictator\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI do not want to get to the point where we\u8217\'20\'19re sending our military resources abroad where we could be better using them here at home to protect our own borders,\u8221\'20\'1D replied Ramaswamy.\par \par \uc2 The Republicans also used the discussion of the war in Ukraine to pivot to the topic of immigration, articulating a vision of a militarized southern US border. DeSantis, whose floundering campaign has suffered repeated false steps and who largely hung back during the debate, jumped into the fold on that topic.\par \par \uc2 I\u8217\'20\'19m not gonna send troops to Ukraine, but I am gonna send them to our southern border\par \par \uc2 Ron DeSantis\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19m not gonna send troops to Ukraine, but I am gonna send them to our southern border,\u8221\'20\'1D said the Florida governor, adding that he would deploy \u8220\'20\'1Clethal force\u8221\'20\'1D to slow immigration and proposed sending troops across the border \u8220\'20\'1Con day one\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 When moderator MacCallum introduced the thorny question of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which has energized Democratic voters since Roe v Wade was overturned, the candidates raced to claim their anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  bona fides while splitting over the question of a federal ban.\par \par \uc2 DeSantis defended his hardline position on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  in Florida while invoking an odd story about a woman named Penny, who, he said, \u8220\'20\'1Csurvived multiple \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  attempts\u8221\'20\'1D and \u8220\'20\'1Cwas left discarded in a pan\u8221\'20\'1D. Haley, meanwhile, shied away from endorsing a federal ban, arguing that it would be challenging to find \u8220\'20\'1Cconsensus\u8221\'20\'1D on the issue.\par \par \uc2 Pence and the South Carolina senator Tim Scott endorsed a federal ban. \u8220\'20\'1CWe cannot let states like California, New York and Illinois have \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  on demand,\u8221\'20\'1D said Scott.\par \par \uc2 As predicted, the spectre of Trump haunted the GOP debate, even as the frontrunner sat the debate out, opting instead for a prerecorded interview with \uc2 Tucker Carlson\uc2  on X, the social media site formerly known as \uc2 Twitter\uc2 . When Fox News moderators asked which candidates would still support Trump if he is convicted in a court of law, Ramaswamy and Christie immediately clashed, with Ramaswamy accusing the government of using \u8220\'20\'1Cpolice force to indict its political opponents\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe more time we spend on this the less time they talk about issues you wanna talk about,\u8221\'20\'1D Baier admonished the crowd, which erupted in jeers when Christie accused Trump of engaging in \u8220\'20\'1Cconduct \u8230\'20\'26 beneath the office of president of the United States\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 In response to the question of whether Pence was justified in certifying the 2020 election, every candidate expressed support for the former vice-president \u8211\'20\'13 except DeSantis, who skirted the question, saying: \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s not about January 6 of 2021, it\u8217\'20\'19s about January 20, of 2025, when the next president is going to take office.\u8221\'20\'1D Pressed on the question, DeSantis said he had \u8220\'20\'1Cno beef\u8221\'20\'1D with Pence but declined to directly affirm Biden\u8217\'20\'19s victory in the 2020 election.\par \par \uc2 I don\u8217\'20\'19t think Trump\u8217\'20\'19s going down after this. I think he\u8217\'20\'19s gonna go up\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump Jr\par \par \uc2 For his part, Pence put a finer point on the subject: \u8220\'20\'1CThe American people deserve to know that Trump \u8230\'20\'26 asked me to put him over the constitution,\u8221\'20\'1D he said.\par \par \uc2 Outside the debate hall, a sweltering day gave way to a muggy night in Milwaukee, a Democratic stronghold, where voter turnout {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nbcnews.com/politics/2022-election/black-voter-turnout-declined-wisconsin-democrats-see-reversing-trend-k-rcna44778"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 efforts}}}\uc2  by grassroots groups like Bloc \u8211\'20\'13 Black Leaders Organizing Communities \u8211\'20\'13 can determine who wins statewide elections. The critical state has emerged as one of the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://apnews.com/article/wisconsin-battleground-state-presidential-election-8c8194948a51a7424fff1c8dd2b42a83"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 last}}}\uc2  true swing states in the country, delivering a narrow win to Biden in 2020 only after Trump won the state by a similarly thin margin in 2016. Underscoring the importance of the state, the \uc2 Republican National Committee\uc2  will return to Milwaukee in July 2024.\par \par \uc2 After the debate wrapped, a spirited \uc2 Donald Trump Jr\uc2  wandered through a small crowd of reporters, complaining that Fox News had not granted him access to the \u8220\'20\'1Cspin room\u8221\'20\'1D, where candidates gather after the debate, and talking up his father. \u8220\'20\'1CI don\u8217\'20\'19t think Trump\u8217\'20\'19s going down after this. I think he\u8217\'20\'19s gonna go up.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Trump is set to reclaim the spotlight on Thursday when he says he will voluntarily surrender himself at the Fulton county jail in Georgia.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020230824ej8o001b9\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
