\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Republican debate veers from  \highlight22\uc2 abortion \highlight\uc2  and fentanyl to Trump and Ukraine as Harris attacks \u8216\'20\'18extremist agenda\u8217\'20\'19 \u8211\'20\'13 as it happened\b0\par\par\uc2 Chris Stein US politics live blogger \par \uc2 8,595 \uc2 words\par \uc2 24 August 2023\par 04:21 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 This blog is now closed. You can read our latest stories about the debate below:Full report: GOP candidates clash on debate stage\u8216\'20\'18Savage animals\u8217\'20\'19: Trump attacks \u8216\'20\'18left\u8217\'20\'19 in Carlson interviewCombative \uc2 Vivek Ramaswamy\uc2  surprise focal point of debate\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.06am BST\par \par \uc2 Closing summary\par \par \uc2 The first debate of the Republican presidential primary season kicked off in Milwaukee, but the star of the show, \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , opted not to attend. He instead {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/aug/23/republican-presidential-debate-2023-candidates-trump-tucker-live-updates?page=with:block-64e6ace88f08319ad416c9e5#block-64e6ace88f08319ad416c9e5"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 sat for a prerecorded interview}}}\uc2  with conservative commentator \uc2 Tucker Carlson\uc2  that was posted to \uc2 Twitter\uc2  (recently renamed X) right as the Fox News-hosted debate began. On stage, the eight GOP candidates vying to overtake the ex-president in the polls, including Florida governor \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2 , entrepreneur \uc2 Vivek Ramaswamy\uc2  and former vice-president \uc2 Mike Pence\uc2 , made promises and pledges, while also engaging in a fair bit of bickering.\par \par \uc2 Here are the highlights:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Polls have recently shown a burst of support for Ramaswamy, even though he\u8217\'20\'19s never won an election. On the debate stage, he was savaged by the crowd of veteran politicians, with Chris Christie{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/aug/23/republican-presidential-debate-2023-candidates-trump-tucker-live-updates?page=with:block-64e6b4968f08319ad416ca1b#block-64e6b4968f08319ad416ca1b"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 comparing him to an AI}}}\uc2 , and Pence {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/aug/23/republican-presidential-debate-2023-candidates-trump-tucker-live-updates?page=with:block-64e6af848f08f3273b0850a1#block-64e6af848f08f3273b0850a1"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 calling him a \u8220\'20\'1Crookie\u8221\'20\'1D}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  divided the GOP candidates, with {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/aug/23/republican-presidential-debate-2023-candidates-trump-tucker-live-updates?page=with:block-64e6b53b8f08f3273b0850d9#block-64e6b53b8f08f3273b0850d9"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 some arguing}}}\uc2  the issue should be left up to the states to deal with.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Almost every candidate at the debate {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/aug/23/republican-presidential-debate-2023-candidates-trump-tucker-live-updates?page=with:block-64e6b9698f08f3273b0850f0#block-64e6b9698f08f3273b0850f0"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 said they would support Trump}}}\uc2  if he was the nominee, even if he was convicted of a crime. The only one who declined was Arkansas governor Asa Hutchinson. The \uc2 Republican National Committee\uc2 , however, had already made all who qualified for the debate sign a pledge to support the eventual nominee.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Ramaswamy stridently argued against providing more military aide to Ukraine, sparking {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/aug/23/republican-presidential-debate-2023-candidates-trump-tucker-live-updates?page=with:block-64e6bdd88f08f3273b085108#block-64e6bdd88f08f3273b085108"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 an argument with Pence}}}\uc2  and an admonishment from the moderators.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 DeSantis is polling in second place to Trump, but was surprisingly muted at the debate. When it came time to discuss border security, he piped up, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/aug/23/republican-presidential-debate-2023-candidates-trump-tucker-live-updates?page=with:block-64e6c2198f08f3273b085122#block-64e6c2198f08f3273b085122"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 vowing to leave}}}\uc2  drug traffickers \u8220\'20\'1Cstone cold dead\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 5.14am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.05am BST\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump Jr\uc2  compared Fox News to the Fulton county district attorney after he was blocked by security from entering the post-debate \u8220\'20\'1Cspin room\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Don Jr and fiancee Kimberly Guilfoyle were moving through press room when a burly security guard blocked their path and told them to go no further. \u8220\'20\'1CSo Fox is not letting us into the rest of the room, just so we\u8217\'20\'19re clear,\u8221\'20\'1D he told reporters, his voice trembling with emotion. \u8220\'20\'1CSo Fox is functioning like the Fulton county DA right now, trying to ban people from actually having discourse about politics.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Guilfoyle added: \u8220\'20\'1CHow un-American.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Don Jr, who has not appeared on Fox News for a year, continued: \u8220\'20\'1CProbably shouldn\u8217\'20\'19t surprise any of us, but that\u8217\'20\'19s what it is, and I\u8217\'20\'19ve been told by others that I would be able to go in \u8230\'20\'26 They\u8217\'20\'19re telling me right now, Fox won\u8217\'20\'19t let me into the spin room.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 He added: \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19\u8217\'20\'19m not allowed to go in there because the candidates that they\u8217\'20\'19ve been boosting while simultaneously trying to cut down Trump for the last two years didn\u8217\'20\'19t perform as they had hoped. So they can\u8217\'20\'19t have someone who can maybe be a representative of my father.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Don Jr talked to reporters in the main press area instead and defended his father\u8217\'20\'19s decision to skip the debate. \u8220\'20\'1CIf you\u8217\'20\'19re a political strategist and if you have a brain, if you have a 60-point lead dominating a field, you don\u8217\'20\'19t go into a setup.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Don Jr rated \uc2 Vivek Ramaswamy\uc2  as the winner of the debate and claimed that \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2  had the worst night. \u8220\'20\'1CHe sat there like a wallflower, basically got ambushed on all sides and everything that he said that actually got some applause was literally already Trump policy.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1C\u8216\'20\'18We use the military to fight the cartels. It\u8217\'20\'19s a threat to our nation.\u8217\'20\'19 That\u8217\'20\'19s Trump policy. \u8216\'20\'18Our nation is in decline, our nation\u8217\'20\'19s in decline, our nation\u8217\'20\'19s in decline\u8217\'20\'19 \u8211\'20\'13 literally from the Trump campaign website. He\u8217\'20\'19s not capable of those original thoughts so he takes an idea that works and tries to make it his own. But I didn\u8217\'20\'19t see a single idea, and again, I didn\u8217\'20\'19t see him prosecute the case of how he\u8217\'20\'19s going to beat \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 .\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 5.12am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.42am BST\par \par \uc2 Protesters gathered in Milwaukee as the Republican primary debate was held. Here are some of the latest images from the newswires:\par \par \uc2 People demonstrating against police violence as the GOP debate happens. Photograph: Pat A Robinson/ZUMA Press Wire/Shutterstock Protesters carrying a sign reading \u8216\'20\'18Stop trans genocide\u8217\'20\'19 march on the debate arena. Photograph: Pat A Robinson/ZUMA Press Wire/\uc2 Shutterstock\uc2  Hundreds of demonstrators gathered in Red Arrow Park before marching on the Republican primary debate. Photograph: Pat A Robinson/ZUMA Press Wire/Shutterstock Protesters parade outside as Republican presidential candidates participate in their first primary debate in Milwaukee. Photograph: Jonathan Ernst/Reuters\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 4.44am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.35am BST\par \par \uc2 Trump scorns GOP candidates who broke with him\par \par \uc2 He may have declined to participate, but \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  was clearly watching tonight\u8217\'20\'19s Republican debate.\par \par \uc2 The former president is unloading on candidates who criticized him over on {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://truthsocial.com/@realDonaldTrump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 his Truth Social account}}}\uc2 , including \uc2 Mike Pence\uc2  :\par \par \uc2 I never asked \uc2 Mike Pence\uc2  to put me above the Constitution. Who would say such a thing? A FAKE STORY!\par \par \uc2 Chris Christie\uc2 :\par \par \uc2 Chris Christie\uc2  was horrible tonight. He was booed at a level never seen before at such a debate. He should have walked off the stage - Nobody wanted to hear from him! DJT\par \par \uc2 And Asa Hutchinson, whose name he has taken to mispronouncing:\par \par \uc2 \u8216\'20\'18Aida\u8217\'20\'19 was a joke tonight. He\u8217\'20\'19s over!\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 4.48am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.23am BST\par \par \uc2 Harris attacks 'extremist agenda' as GOP debate wraps up\par \par \uc2 Tonight\u8217\'20\'19s Republican presidential primary debate has ended, and \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  has released a statement warning against the \u8220\'20\'1Cextremist agenda\u8221\'20\'1D she said was on display:\par \par \uc2 No one on stage \u8216\'20\'18won\u8217\'20\'19 tonight\u8217\'20\'19s debate. Instead, the American people heard how much they stand to lose from an extremist agenda.\par \par \uc2 One by one, each extremist Republican candidate laid out a vision for an America that is less fair, less free and less safe. These candidates want to raise costs for working families in order to benefit special interests and the ultra-wealthy. To gut social security and Medicare. To strip fundamental rights and basic freedoms from millions of people. And to reverse the Bidenomics strategy that has helped create 13m jobs, the strongest two years of small business creation in history, and record-low unemployment.\par \par \uc2 These extremists focus on unnecessary debates meant to divide our nation in hopes that the American public will not notice they have no affirmative agenda.\par \par \uc2 Back in Milwaukee, photos from the newswires indicate that the atmosphere onstage was more chummy than it appeared during commercial breaks.\par \par \uc2 Chris Christie\uc2  (left) \uc2 Mike Pence\uc2  (second from left), \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2  (center right) and \uc2 Vivek Ramaswamy\uc2  (right) chat during a break in the first debate of the GOP primary season. Photograph: Win McNamee/Getty Images\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 4.27am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.18am BST\par \par \uc2 DeSantis: 'We will reverse the decline of this country'\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThis is our time for choosing. We will send \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  back to his basement and we will reverse the decline of this country,\u8221\'20\'1D \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2  promised, referencing the now president\u8217\'20\'19s habit of spending a lot of time at home during the 2020 campaign, when Covid-19 was rife (Biden won nonetheless).\par \par \uc2 DeSantis continued:\par \par \uc2 I\u8217\'20\'19m a blue-collar kid. I work minimum wage jobs to be able to make ends meet. I understand the importance of the American dream. And I know how that slipped away from so many millions of Americans. We\u8217\'20\'19ll restore it.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 4.29am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.15am BST\par \par \uc2 Vivek Ramaswamy\uc2 : 'This is our moment to revive common ideals'\par \par \uc2 In his closing argument, \uc2 Vivek Ramaswamy\uc2  essentially repudiates his fellow millennials.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI was born in 1985 and I grew up into a generation where we were taught to celebrate our diversity and our differences and so much, that we forgot all of the ways we are really just the same as Americans, bound by a common set of ideals that set this nation into motion in 1776. And this is our moment to revive those common ideals.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Said ideals:\par \par \uc2 God is real. There are two genders. Fossil fuels are a requirements for human prosperity. Reverse racism is racism. An open border is not a border. Parents determined the education of their children. That nuclear family is the greatest form of governance known to man. Capitalism lifts us up from poverty. There are three branches of government, not four. And the US constitution, it is strongest guarantor of freedom in human history.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 4.20am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.11am BST\par \par \uc2 Mike Pence\uc2 : 'Different times call for different leadership'\par \par \uc2 Mike Pence\uc2  is in an awkward situation. He\u8217\'20\'19s trying to campaign on his accomplishments while serving under \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , but has also made clear he is no ally of his former boss.\par \par \uc2 He attempted to thread that difficult needle in his closing statement.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CDifferent times call for different leadership. The Republican party owes the American people the choice, proven leadership at the national level that knows how to move a conservative agenda forward. We proved in the Trump-Pence years you can turn this country around faster than you can imagine. And I have faith we will again because I have faith in the American people.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 4.19am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.08am BST\par \par \uc2 Haley: 'I will beat \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  and he knows that'\par \par \uc2 In her closing argument, Nikki Haley talked about her husband\u8217\'20\'19s latest military deployment, and promised to do \u8230\'20\'26 lots of things.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI will beat \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  and he knows that. I will strengthen our economy and we\u8217\'20\'19ll bring this inflation down. We will put transparency in the classroom. We will secure our borders, we will have the backs of our law enforcement and we will make sure we have a strong national security. And once again, we will make sure we have an America that is strong and proud,\u8221\'20\'1D Haley said.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 4.15am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.06am BST\par \par \uc2 Chris Christie\uc2 : 'I'm only one who has ever beaten Democratic incumbent'\par \par \uc2 Chris Christie\uc2  is from Democratic New Jersey, and argued that his ability to win the governor\u8217\'20\'19s office twice makes him the right man to beat \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19m the only one on this stage who has ever beaten the Democratic incumbent in election. I did it in a deep-blue state, being outspent three to one,\u8221\'20\'1D Christie said. \u8220\'20\'1CBeating a Democratic incumbent is not easy. The last Democratic incumbent president who was defeated was \uc2 Jimmy Carter\uc2 , and he was defeated by a conservative governor from a blue state who knew how to get results, who stood for the truth, who cared about accountability, and stood strong and hard against waste. Those are the very things that I did in my eight years as governor of New Jersey, and exactly what I\u8217\'20\'19ll do as president of the United States.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 4.15am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.03am BST\par \par \uc2 Tim Scott: 'If you're able-bodied in America, you work'\par \par \uc2 As he did when he kicked of his campaign in May, Tim Scott mixed reminiscence about his mother with rightwing messaging.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI had the good fortune to have a mom who worked 16-hour days, making sure we had food on our tables. She taught me that if you\u8217\'20\'19re able-bodied in America, you work, if you take out a loan, you pay it back, you commit a violent crime, you go to jail. And if God made you a man, you play sports against men,\u8221\'20\'1D the South Carolina senator said.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 4.14am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.00am BST\par \par \uc2 Hutchinson closing statement: 'New leadership that can bring bold ideas'\par \par \uc2 Asa Hutchinson asked voters to say no to \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 , and also to \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1COur nation is in trouble. It is in trouble because of failed leadership. And the solution is not four more years of \uc2 Joseph Biden\uc2 . The solution is not full more years of \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 . The solution is new leadership that can bring bold ideas to America and to bring out the best of America,\u8221\'20\'1D he said.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 4.15am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.58am BST\par \par \uc2 Now we\u8217\'20\'19re on to the closing arguments part of the debate, where candidates get to make their case without anybody interrupting them (a dynamic \uc2 Vivek Ramaswamy\uc2 , \uc2 Mike Pence\uc2  and \uc2 Chris Christie\uc2  all probably appreciate).\par \par \uc2 First up is \uc2 Doug Burgum\uc2 , who invoked the plains of his home state in promising to make Americans\u8217\'20\'19 lives better:\par \par \uc2 When I\u8217\'20\'19m on a horseback in the badlands of North Dakota, it looks like the horizon is just limitless. And when you can almost see beyond that horizon, you can see that this great country, our future is unlimited, but we\u8217\'20\'19ve got to focus on innovation, not regulation. We\u8217\'20\'19ve got to cut the red tape, we got to drive ourselves forward. The way we win the cold war with China is by growing our economy through innovation, and as [resident, I will bring out the best of America, I will improve every American life.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.52am BST\par \par \uc2 Ramaswamy blames single mothers for education struggles\par \par \uc2 American students {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/education/2022/sep/01/math-reading-scores-us-students-covid-pandemic-learning"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 are struggling to recover}}}\uc2  from the school closures and shift to remote learning Covid-19 caused, creating what some consider an \u8220\'20\'1Ceducation crisis\u8221\'20\'1D. The Republican candidates were asked how they\u8217\'20\'19d solve it, and \uc2 Vivek Ramaswamy\uc2 , who supports dismantling the education department and other parts of the federal government, said unmarried mothers were partially to blame.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CPart of the problem is we also have a federal government that pays single women more not to have a man in the house than to have a man in the house, contributing to an epidemic of fatherlessness. And I think that goes hand in glove with the education crisis as well because, we have to remember, education starts with the family and the nuclear family is the greatest form of governance known to mankind,\u8221\'20\'1D the entrepreneur said.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.53am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.46am BST\par \par \uc2 GOP candidates acknowledge climate change, but don't want to talk about it\par \par \uc2 Unlike in recent election cycles, when Republican candidates tended to completely reject the realities of global heating, most of the GOP presidential hopefuls (except \uc2 Vivek Ramaswamy\uc2  ) have at some point acknowledged that the climate crisis is real.\par \par \uc2 But almost all the candidates have indicated they\u8217\'20\'19re not interested in dwelling on the topic \u8211\'20\'13 or doing much to reduce greenhouse gas emissions or the use of fossil fuels.\par \par \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2  immediately derailed efforts to elicit a clear yes or no response from candidates on whether they believe in human-caused climate change. He said \u8220\'20\'1Clet\u8217\'20\'19s have the debate\u8221\'20\'1D before proceeding not to have the debate.\par \par \uc2 Ramaswamy was notably the only candidate to full-throatedly deny climate science, making the unsubstantiated claim that \u8220\'20\'1Cmore people are dying a bad climate change policies than they are of actual climate change.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Nikki Haley, on the other hand said \u8220\'20\'1Cclimate change is real\u8221\'20\'1D but then pushed off all responsibility to take care of it on India and China. Both those countries have lower per-capita carbon emissions than the US. And as of the latest figures, from 2021, no country had emitted more carbon dioxide since 1850 than the United States.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.49am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.43am BST\par \par \uc2 About halfway through the debate, candidates were asked whether they believe then vice-president \uc2 Mike Pence\uc2  did the right thing on January 6, when he refused Trump\u8217\'20\'19s efforts to sabotage the counting of electoral votes.\par \par \uc2 Most candidates resoundingly supported Pence\u8217\'20\'19s actions following the insurrection at the Capitol. \u8220\'20\'1CAbsolutely he did the right thing,\u8221\'20\'1D the South Carolina senator Tim Scott said. Nikki Haley agreed. \u8220\'20\'1CI do think \uc2 Mike Pence\uc2  did the right thing and I think we need to give him credit for it,\u8221\'20\'1D she said.\par \par \uc2 But Florida Governor \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2  avoided the question, instead choosing to rail on the \u8220\'20\'1Cweaponization\u8221\'20\'1D of federal agencies under the Biden administration. \u8220\'20\'1CThis election is not about January 6, 2021,\u8221\'20\'1D he said, adding that it\u8217\'20\'19s about January 2025, when the next president will take office.\par \par \uc2 Pressed by moderators to answer the question, DeSantis said: \u8220\'20\'1CMike did his duty. I have no beef with him.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Christie called out the Florida governor\u8217\'20\'19s lackluster support. \u8220\'20\'1C\uc2 Mike Pence\uc2  stood for the constitution and he deserves not grudging credit,\u8221\'20\'1D he said. \u8220\'20\'1CHe deserves our thanks as Americans for putting the constitution above personal and political pressure.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.45am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.39am BST\par \par \uc2 DeSantis promises to leave drug traffickers 'stone cold dead'\par \par \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2  has surprisingly hung back and stayed out of the fray during much of this debate, but jumped at the opportunity to articulate a vision of a militarized border with Mexico \u8211\'20\'13 repeatedly endorsing the use of \u8220\'20\'1Clethal force\u8221\'20\'1D to slow irregular migration.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19m not gonna send troops to Ukraine, but I am gonna send them to our southern border,\u8221\'20\'1D said the Florida governor. \u8220\'20\'1CWhen these drug pushers are bringing fentanyl across the border, that\u8217\'20\'19s going to be the last thing they do. We\u8217\'20\'19re going to use force and we\u8217\'20\'19re going to leave them stone cold dead.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.33am BST\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  wrapped up his interview with \uc2 Tucker Carlson\uc2  by warning of the threat of conflict in the US after saying that he expects the Democrats to steal the 2024 election from him.\par \par \uc2 The former president also described the crowd that stormed the Capitol on 6 January 2021 as full of \u8220\'20\'1Clove and unity\u8221\'20\'1D while appearing to justify the violence as the result of legitimate grievance.\par \par \uc2 Asked by Carlson if he thinks the country is headed to \u8220\'20\'1Ccivl war\u8221\'20\'1D and \u8220\'20\'1Copen conflict\u8221\'20\'1D, Trump said he didn\u8217\'20\'19t know but then added: \u8220\'20\'1CI can say this. There\u8217\'20\'19s a level of passion that I\u8217\'20\'19ve never seen. There\u8217\'20\'19s a level of hatred, that I\u8217\'20\'19ve never seen and that\u8217\'20\'19s probably a bad combination.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Carlson responded: \u8220\'20\'1CThat is a bad combination.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The remarks came after Trump defended the crowd that gathered to hear him speak on January 6. Trump suggested that he told the protestors to behave \u8220\'20\'1Cpeacefully and patriotically\u8221\'20\'1D but \u8220\'20\'1Ca very small group\u8221\'20\'1D went to the Capitol.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CPeople in that crowd said it was the most beautiful day they\u8217\'20\'19ve ever experienced. There was love in that crowd, and unity. I have never seen such spirit and such passion and such love. And I\u8217\'20\'19ve also never seen simultaneously, and from the same people, such hatred of what they\u8217\'20\'19ve done to our country,\u8221\'20\'1D he said.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.34am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.29am BST\par \par \uc2 Here are some scenes from Fiserv Forum in Milwaukee, site of tonight\u8217\'20\'19s Republican presidential debate:\par \par \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s makeup is touched up ahead of the debate. Photograph: Brendan Smialowski/AFP/Getty Images The former biotech executive \uc2 Vivek Ramaswamy\uc2  is seen debating on screens in the media filing center at the first Republican candidates\u8217\'20\'19 debate. Photograph: Jonathan Ernst/Reuters \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  is shown speaking on a video screen in the debate hall at the first Republican candidates\u8217\'20\'19 debate of the 2024 presidential election campaign. Photograph: Brian Snyder/Reuters\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.32am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.27am BST\par \par \uc2 Nikki Haley took possibly her strongest stance of the night in her rebuttal of \uc2 Vivek Ramaswamy\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s views on the Ukraine war.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe American president needs to have moral clarity,\u8221\'20\'1D she said. \u8220\'20\'1CWhen you look at the situation with Russia and Ukraine here you have a pro-American country that was invaded by a thug.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 She pointed out that \u8220\'20\'1Cless than 3.5% of our defense budget was given to Ukraine\u8221\'20\'1D and said the threat of Russia aligning further with China was a bigger threat than protecting the US defense budget.\par \par \uc2 She directly addressed Ramaswamy: \u8220\'20\'1CHe wants to hand Ukraine to Russia \u8230\'20\'26 you don\u8217\'20\'19t do that to friends.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CLook at what Putin did today \u8211\'20\'13 he killed Prigozhin,\u8221\'20\'1D she said. \u8220\'20\'1CYou are choosing a murderer over a pro-American country.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.30am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.24am BST\par \par \uc2 Pence, Ramaswamy squabble over Ukraine\par \par \uc2 Mike Pence\uc2  is a career politician who has made it all the way to the vice-president\u8217\'20\'19s office, while \uc2 Vivek Ramaswamy\uc2  has never been elected to anything. Nonetheless, their rivalry is among the most heated on the debate stage, and they engaged in a disagreement over aid to Ukraine.\par \par \uc2 Asked if he would support an increase in funding to Ukraine, Ramaswamy replied: \u8220\'20\'1CI would not, and I think that this is disastrous, protecting against an invasion across somebody else\u8217\'20\'19s border when we should use those same military resources to prevent across the invasion of our own southern border here in the United States.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Pence hit back. \u8220\'20\'1CLet me be clear, anybody that thinks we can\u8217\'20\'19t solve the problems here in the United States, and be the leader of the free world has a pretty small view of the greatest nation on Earth. We can do both,\u8221\'20\'1D he said. Addressing the entrepreneur: \u8220\'20\'1CBut, Vivek, if we do the giveaway that you want to give to Putin, to give him his land, it\u8217\'20\'19s not going to be too long before he rolls across a Nato border. And frankly, our men and women of our armed forces are going to have to go and fight him.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Then there was lots of cross-talk between the two men, who are one spot away from each other on the debate stage, and the moderators had to step in.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CHear this bell? That means your time\u8217\'20\'19s done,\u8221\'20\'1D said Bret Baier, pointing to a bell the moderators have been using to cut off the speakers. \u8220\'20\'1CSo, Mr Vice-President, we appreciate your aggressiveness here.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.29am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.17am BST\par \par \uc2 Tonight\u8217\'20\'19s debate is not just being watched on televisions across the US: the venue itself, in Milwaukee, Wisconsin, has attracted an august audience of political heavyweights, surrogates, reporters, observers, strategists, advisers, pollsters \u8230\'20\'26 and Nigel Farage.\par \par \uc2 Nigel Farage arrives at the debate hall in Milwaukee. Photograph: Jonathan Ernst/Reuters\par \par \uc2 Earlier, in his role as a host on GB News \u8211\'20\'13 sort of a British equivalent to Fox News, the host of tonight\u8217\'20\'19s debate \u8211\'20\'13 the former leader of the United Kingdom Independence Party (Ukip) and the Brexit Party offered a few thoughts.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/Nigel_Farage/status/1694437651372216496"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 One}}}\uc2 , with video of an interview with a Trump ally in the US House: \u8220\'20\'1CCongressman Byron Donalds is very impressive. One to watch.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/Nigel_Farage/status/1694467136209453471"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Another}}}\uc2 , in video of a conversation with a Trump adviser, \uc2 Jason Miller\uc2  : \u8220\'20\'1C\uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  sometimes will take your advice and other other times I\u8217\'20\'19ve no doubt he\u8217\'20\'19ll tell you your fortune, because that\u8217\'20\'19s the way he is with people.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Up to a point, Farage would know.\par \par \uc2 Our {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/andrewanthony"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Andrew Anthony}}}\uc2  has some thoughts on Farage, and particularly the rumbling scandal over where he was allowed to have a bank account, which led to the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/business/2023/aug/23/natwest-chief-alison-rose-pay-package-bank-nigel-farage-coutts"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 resignation}}}\uc2  of the chief executive of NatWest:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/commentisfree/2023/jul/29/give-nigel-farage-grievance-whip-up-storm-coutts"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 From Brexit to Coutts \u8211\'20\'13 has Nigel Farage become Britain\u8217\'20\'19s most influential politician? | Andrew Anthony}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.15am BST\par \par \uc2 Asked why he did not raise his hand when asked to do so if he will support \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  as the party\u8217\'20\'19s hypothetical nominee \u8211\'20\'13 even if he is convicted \u8211\'20\'13 the former Arkansas governor \uc2 Asa Hutchinson\uc2  said the Republican party needed to take a look in the mirror.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI did not raise my hand because there\u8217\'20\'19s an important issue we as a party have to face,\u8221\'20\'1D Hutchinson said.\par \par \uc2 He continued:\par \par \uc2 Well over a year ago, I said that \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  was morally disqualified from being president again as a result of what happened on January 6. More people are understanding the importance of that, including conservative legal scholars who says he may be disqualified under the 14th amendment from being president again, as a result of the insurrection. This is something that could disqualify him under our rules, and under the constitution. And so obviously, I\u8217\'20\'19m not going to support somebody who\u8217\'20\'19s been convicted of a serious felony, or who has (been disqualified) under our constitution, and that\u8217\'20\'19s consistent with our \uc2 RNC\uc2  rules, and I hope everybody would agree with that.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.20am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.12am BST\par \par \uc2 Tim Scott turned a question about Jan uary 6 into an attack on the Department of Justice, claiming that the agency was being weaponized under attorney general \uc2 Merrick Garland\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe need lady justice to wear a blindfold,\u8221\'20\'1D he said, citing a figure that only 17% of Americans have confidence in the department. His comments come as House Republicans and others have made strategic attacks on the Justice Department as it continues to investigate January 6, \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  and \uc2 Hunter Biden\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.14am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.09am BST\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s the moment the Republican candidates were asked to raise their hands if they would support \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  as the party\u8217\'20\'19s nominee, even if he was convicted in one of the trials he is facing:\par \par \uc2 enltrAsked directly at the debate if they\u8217\'20\'19d support \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  if he is convicted of a felony, 6 out of 8 Republican presidential candidates raise their hand. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/GbciS9sF6f"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/GbciS9sF6f}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 The Recount (@therecount) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/therecount/status/1694531303956521443?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 August 24, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.07am BST\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  has told \uc2 Tucker Carlson\uc2  that he is concerned his opponents will try to kill him in a rambling interview packed with conspiracy theories from whether \uc2 Jeffrey Epstein\uc2  was murdered to accusations that federal agencies are limiting the amount of water in washing machines.\par \par \uc2 Carlson asked Trump whether he was concerned that \u8220\'20\'1Cthe left\u8221\'20\'1D, after impeaching and then indicting him, would try and kill him.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThey\u8217\'20\'19re savage animals. They are people that are sick, really sick,\u8221\'20\'1D said Trump. \u8220\'20\'1CYou have great people that are Democrats. Most of the people in our country are fantastic. And I\u8217\'20\'19m representing everybody \u8230\'20\'26 But I\u8217\'20\'19ve seen what they do.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Trump took aim at his former attorney general Bill Barr. Carlson suggested to Trump that Barr had covered up the murder of the billionaire sex offender \uc2 Jeffrey Epstein\uc2  in a New York jail.\par \par \uc2 The former president didn\u8217\'20\'19t bite, saying he thought Epstein had probably killed himself but he took the opportunity to take a shot at Barr, accusing him of failing to properly investigate Trump\u8217\'20\'19s false allegations that he 2020 election was rigged.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CBarr became so petrified, so frightened of being impeached,\u8221\'20\'1D he said. \u8220\'20\'1CThey play a much rougher game, the left, the lunatics, and they were going to impeach Bill Barr and he was petrified.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.05am BST\par \par \uc2 That said, the Republican party has made participating in this debate conditional on the candidates supporting the party\u8217\'20\'19s eventual nominee.\par \par \uc2 That may be why \uc2 Chris Christie\uc2  raised his hand when asked if he would support \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , even if he is convicted. Asa Hutchinson did not raise his hand, tacitly violating that deal.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.15am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.03am BST\par \par \uc2 One of the more surprising candidates to raise their hands was \uc2 Chris Christie\uc2 , who from the start of the campaign has been a \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  critic.\par \par \uc2 But, when asked to elaborate on why he would still support Trump, Christie made clear he was not happy to do it. \u8220\'20\'1CSomeone\u8217\'20\'19s got to stop normalizing this conduct, okay. Whether or not you believe that the criminal charges are right or wrong, the conduct is beneath the office of president of the United States.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.05am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.01am BST\par \par \uc2 Almost all GOP candidates would support Trump as nominee, even if convicted\par \par \uc2 After a commercial break, the debate continued with the moderator Bret Baier asking the candidates to raise their hands if they would support \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  as the party\u8217\'20\'19s presidential nominee, even if he is convicted in one of the criminal cases he is facing.\par \par \uc2 The candidates with their hands raised. Photograph: Win McNamee/Getty Images\par \par \uc2 All candidates raised their hands, with the exception of the former Arkansas governor \uc2 Asa Hutchinson\uc2 . \uc2 Chris Christie\uc2  retracted his hand a moment after raising it and clarified that he was not really raising it.\par \par \uc2 Christie has deliberately positioned himself as the anti-Trump, almost the only Republican in a crowded field willing to directly take on and criticize the four-times-indicted frontrunner \u8211\'20\'13 despite being a former friend and ally.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.37am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.56am BST\par \par \uc2 The debate then turned to crime \u8211\'20\'13 an animating issue for American voters, but one that mayors and city councilmembers, not presidents and members of Congress, are best positioned to address.\par \par \uc2 Nonetheless, the Republican candidates weighed in on what they would do to tamp down on crime, which rose from historic lows nationwide after Covid-19 broke out in 2020.\par \par \uc2 Mike Pence\uc2  took on the politics of crime question with the usual Republican line. He said Democrats were focused on defunding police instead of making major cities safer. \u8220\'20\'1CDemocrats and liberal prosecutors continue to work out their fanciful agendas,\u8221\'20\'1D he said, and \u8220\'20\'1Cwhat we need is strong commitment to law enforcement\u8221\'20\'1D. He then used the question as a reason to talk about tax cuts passed by the Trump administration.\par \par \uc2 Vivek Ramaswamy\uc2  focused on worsening mental health, calling to bring back mental health institutions, and then parroted a new rightwing focus on attacking psychiatric medications. \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s not just drugging up people in those psychiatric institutions with Zoloft and Serequil,\u8221\'20\'1D he said, adding \u8220\'20\'1CThe reason we have that mental health epidemic is people are so hungry for purpose and meaning.\u8221\'20\'1D He said as president he would offer a \u8220\'20\'1Ctonal reset\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2  pointed to his record as Florida governor, saying crime was at a record low in the state, and then attacking progressive prosecutors for making communities elsewhere more dangerous. \u8220\'20\'1COne of the biggest reasons is because you have \uc2 George Soros\uc2  funding these radical leftwing district attorneys that get into office and they say they\u8217\'20\'19re not going to prosecute crimes they disagree with. The inmates are running the asylum!\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.05am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.47am BST\par \par \uc2 GOP candidates split on federal \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban\par \par \uc2 Prompted for their thoughts on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the Republican candidates differed over whether states should decide to restrict the procedure, or if they would push for a federal ban.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWhat is going tor work in New York is never going to work in North Dakota and vice versa,\u8221\'20\'1D said \uc2 Doug Burgum\uc2 , who as governor of North Dakota signed a strict \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban.\par \par \uc2 The former \uc2 UN\uc2  ambassador Nikki Haley took a similar tack. \u8220\'20\'1CWhen it comes to a federal ban, let\u8217\'20\'19s be honest with the American people... let\u8217\'20\'19s find consensus. Can\u8217\'20\'19t we all agree we should ban late term abortions? \u8230\'20\'26 Let\u8217\'20\'19s treat this like the respectful issue that it is.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2  was vague, telling the story of \u8220\'20\'1Ca lady in Florida named Penny. She survived multiple \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  attempts. She was left discarded in a pan. Fortunately, her grandmother saved her and brought her to a different hospital.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19m gonna stand on the side of life. Look, I understand Wisconsin is going to do it different than Texas. I understand Iowa and New Hampshire are going to do different, but I will support the cause of life as governor and as president,\u8221\'20\'1D DeSantis said.\par \par \uc2 Mike Pence\uc2  is one of the few candidates who from the start of his campaign called for a national ban, and repeated that tonight. \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19ve been a champion for life in Congress, a champion for life as governor and as vice-president,\u8221\'20\'1D he said. \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s not a state\u8217\'20\'19s only issue, it\u8217\'20\'19s a moral issue to accomplish.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.48am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.39am BST\par \par \uc2 Christie lays into Ramaswamy, saying he 'sounds like ChatGPT'\par \par \uc2 The former New Jersey governor \uc2 Chris Christie\uc2  is known for his sharp tongue, and on the debate stage he turned it loose on \uc2 Vivek Ramaswamy\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 He compared the first-time candidate, who is performing decently in the polls, to the former Democratic president \uc2 Barack Obama\uc2  \u8211\'20\'13 and not in a good way:\par \par \uc2 enltrChris Christie slams \uc2 Vivek Ramaswamy\uc2  at the GOP presidential debate: \u8220\'20\'1CI've have had enough already tonight of a guy who sounds like ChatGPT.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Christie also calls Ramaswamy "the same type of amateur" as \uc2 Barack Obama\uc2 . {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/OlgD9Yqvvz"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/OlgD9Yqvvz}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 The Recount (@therecount) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/therecount/status/1694523583349895629?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 August 24, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.43am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.36am BST\par \par \uc2 Responding to a video-recorded question from a young voter, the Republican candidates were asked to raise their hand if they believed humans were causing climate change.\par \par \uc2 It looked to be an awkward moment for the politicians, who belong to a party where many outright deny the scientific consensus that humans have caused the Earth\u8217\'20\'19s temperature to increase. Then, the Florida governor, \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2 , came to the rescue, as you can see in the clip below:\par \par \uc2 enltrGov. \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2  (R-FL) interrupts a hand-raise question at the GOP debate about whether the field of candidates acknowledges the existence of human-caused climate change, redirecting to criticism of President Biden:\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe\u8217\'20\'19re not schoolchildren, let\u8217\'20\'19s have the debate.\u8221\'20\'1D {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/ZoXjs3WeTS"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/ZoXjs3WeTS}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 The Recount (@therecount) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/therecount/status/1694522994108899493?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 August 24, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.38am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.28am BST\par \par \uc2 Ramaswamy: 'drill, frack, burn coal and embrace nuclear'\par \par \uc2 Fox News\u8217\'20\'19s two debate moderators, Martha MacCallum and Bret Baier, kicked off with questions about how the Republican candidates will improve the economy, which provoked a spat between the former vice-president \uc2 Mike Pence\uc2  and \uc2 Vivek Ramaswamy\uc2 , an entrepreneur who has never held elected office.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CYou\u8217\'20\'19ve got people on this stage that won\u8217\'20\'19t even talk about issues like social security and Medicare,\u8221\'20\'1D Pence said, then singled out Ramaswamy. \u8220\'20\'1CVivek, you recently said, a president can\u8217\'20\'19t do everything. Well, I\u8217\'20\'19ve got news for you, Vivek, I\u8217\'20\'19ve been in the hallway, I\u8217\'20\'19ve been in the West Wing and the president of the United States has to confront every crisis facing America.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThis isn\u8217\'20\'19t that complicated guys. Unlock American energy, drill, frack, burn coal and embrace nuclear,\u8221\'20\'1D Ramaswamy responded, as he embarked on a recitation of his economic policies. \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19m not sure I exactly understood \uc2 Mike Pence\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s comment \u8230\'20\'26 but for me, it\u8217\'20\'19s pretty simple. That\u8217\'20\'19s something that US president can do,\u8221\'20\'1D he said.\par \par \uc2 But the spat was not over. Pence went after Ramaswamy again: \u8220\'20\'1C\uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  has weakened this country at home and abroad. Now is not the time for on the job training. We don\u8217\'20\'19t need to bring in a rookie.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.35am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.20am BST\par \par \uc2 Ahead of the debate, Democratic leaders used the event as an opportunity to remind voters of the Republican Party\u8217\'20\'19s rightward shift since \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s time in the White House.\par \par \uc2 At a press conference this afternoon, \uc2 Democratic National Committee\uc2  chair \uc2 Jaime Harrison\uc2  described the Republican primary as \u8220\'20\'1Ca race to the bottom,\u8221\'20\'1D and as the candidates descended on Milwaukee, a plane circled downtown, trailing a sign reading \u8220\'20\'1CGOP 2024: A race for the extreme Maga base.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe\u8217\'20\'19re really hoping to use this as an opportunity to highlight the Maga extremism we\u8217\'20\'19re gonna see on the debate stage tonight,\u8221\'20\'1D Joe Oslund, a spokesperson for the Wisconsin Democratic Party, told the Guardian.\par \par \uc2 A fundraiser for the state party that launched today garnered more than $20,000 by 8.30pm ET.\par \par \uc2 Given Wisconsin\u8217\'20\'19s status as a key battleground state, the \uc2 RNC\uc2  chose Milwaukee as the site of the first debate and will return for its nominating convention next July.\par \par \uc2 In 2016, Trump won the state by more than 22,000 votes and in 2020, \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  defeated him by a similarly narrow margin. In an appeal for donations, the Wisconsin Democratic party chair, Ben Wikler, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/benwikler/status/1694365569049628780"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 described}}}\uc2  the state as \u8220\'20\'1Cthe home of the political nailbiter.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.27am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.08am BST\par \par \uc2 At the Republican debate, the first question of the night was about Rich Men North of Richmond. If you are wondering who they are, the Guardian\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/matthew-cantor"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Matthew Cantor}}}\uc2  has the answer:\par \par \uc2 In {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=sqSA-SY5Hro"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Rich Men North of Richmond}}}\uc2 , Oliver Anthony, a bushy-bearded former North Carolina factory worker, sings passionately about working hard for \u8220\'20\'1Cbullshit pay\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Armed with just a guitar and his powerful voice, he identifies the source of the problem: \u8220\'20\'1Crich men north of Richmond\u8221\'20\'1D \u8211\'20\'13 federal politicians \u8211\'20\'13 who \u8220\'20\'1Cwant to have total control\u8221\'20\'1D. The song laments homelessness \u8211\'20\'13 \u8220\'20\'1Cfolks in the street ain\u8217\'20\'19t got nothin\u8217\'20\'19 to eat\u8221\'20\'1D \u8211\'20\'13 and a national suicide crisis: \u8220\'20\'1CYoung men are putting themselves six feet in the ground / \u8217\'20\'19Cause all this damn country does is keep on kicking them down.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 So far, so resonant: the song has collected more than 12m views on \uc2 YouTube\uc2  alone, and on Tuesday afternoon, it sat at No 3 on Spotify\u8217\'20\'19s Top 50 \u8211\'20\'13 USA list.\par \par \uc2 But things start to feel a little less empathetic when Anthony starts complaining about \u8220\'20\'1Cthe obese milking welfare\u8221\'20\'1D, reasoning that \u8220\'20\'1Cif you\u8217\'20\'19re 5-foot-3 and you\u8217\'20\'19re 300 pounds / Taxes ought not to pay for your bags of fudge rounds\u8221\'20\'1D. We can all agree that politicians have caused many of America\u8217\'20\'19s problems; it\u8217\'20\'19s harder to argue that our country is being destroyed by short, overweight chocolate enthusiasts. He also rails against taxation, which he says means \u8220\'20\'1Cyour dollar ain\u8217\'20\'19t shit\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/music/2023/aug/16/rich-men-north-of-richmond-oliver-anthony"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Rich Men North of Richmond punches down. No surprise the right wing loves it}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.07am BST\par \par \uc2 Trump interview with \uc2 Tucker Carlson\uc2  starts airing five minutes before GOP debate\par \par \uc2 The former Fox News host \uc2 Tucker Carlson\uc2  launched his interview with \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  five minutes before the first Republican primary debate was to begin in Milwaukee in an attempt to sabotage both the former president\u8217\'20\'19s rivals in the 2024 election and their host, Carlson\u8217\'20\'19s former employer, Fox News.\par \par \uc2 Carlson opened the 46 minute interview with a question about why Trump wasn\u8217\'20\'19t at the Milwaukee debate.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CYou see the polls that have come out and I\u8217\'20\'19m leading by 50 and 60 points and some of them are at one and zero and two. And I\u8217\'20\'19m saying do I sit there for an hour or two hours or whatever it\u8217\'20\'19s going to be and get harassed by people who shouldn\u8217\'20\'19t even be running for president?\u8221\'20\'1D he said.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI just felt it would be more appropriate not to do the debate.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 It was perhaps remarkable that the conversation was taking place at all. Just five months ago it was revealed that Carlson said of Trump in a text message: \u8220\'20\'1CI hate him passionately.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe are very, very close to being able to ignore Trump most nights,\u8221\'20\'1D The then Fox News anchor said in a message to a colleague in early January 2021 as the former president continued a futile battle to remain in office. \u8220\'20\'1CI truly can\u8217\'20\'19t wait.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 But the two men set aside their differences to jointly take on their respective enemies \u8211\'20\'13 Fox and the rest of the Republican primary field.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.32am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.05am BST\par \par \uc2 First Republican debate begins\par \par \uc2 The first debate of the 2024 Republican presidential primary has kicked off in Milwaukee, Wisconsin.\par \par \uc2 Follow along here as we cover it live.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.03am BST\par \par \uc2 Doug Burgum\uc2  (left) on 11 August, before his leg injury. Photograph: Charlie Neibergall/AP\par \par \uc2 Onstage at the Republican presidential debate tonight is the governor of North Dakota, \uc2 Doug Burgum\uc2  \u8211\'20\'13 who almost didn\u8217\'20\'19t make it.\par \par \uc2 He has managed to make the event despite requiring crutches and wearing a boot after hurting his Achilles tendon while playing basketball.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19m in,\u8221\'20\'1D the 67-year-old rank outsider said in a tweet earlier, before his campaign confirmed his participation.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CDoug feels very strongly that his voice is necessary on the stage this evening, and has said he will fight through the pain and challenge standing in order to make that happen,\u8221\'20\'1D a statement said, as {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nbcnews.com/politics/2024-election/north-dakota-governor-doug-burgum-gop-debate-leg-injury-rcna101380"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reported}}}\uc2  by NBC News.\par \par \uc2 enltrI\u8217\'20\'19m in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/DZqLf3Yxik"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/DZqLf3Yxik}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 \uc2 Doug Burgum\uc2  (Text "DOUG" to 70177) (@DougBurgum) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/DougBurgum/status/1694456349055242604?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 August 23, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 Citing \u8220\'20\'1Csources close to Burgum\u8221\'20\'1D, NBC {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nbcnews.com/politics/2024-election/north-dakota-governor-doug-burgum-gop-debate-leg-injury-rcna101380"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 said}}}\uc2  he \u8220\'20\'1Csuffered a high-grade tear in a pickup basketball game with campaign staff\u8221\'20\'1D on Tuesday, and was admitted to a local emergency room.\par \par \uc2 Burgum himself {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cnn.com/2023/08/23/politics/doug-burgum-injured/index.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 told CNN}}}\uc2  : \u8220\'20\'1CI think the first piece of good news is tonight\u8217\'20\'19s not a dance contest. If this was Dancing with the Stars, I\u8217\'20\'19d be scratched from the competition. But it\u8217\'20\'19s a debate. We\u8217\'20\'19re standing at a podium for two hours and I may just have to cowboy up and we\u8217\'20\'19ll just get through it.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.01am BST\par \par \uc2 Tucker Carlson\uc2  releases interview with \uc2 Donald Trump\par \par \uc2 Just as the Republican presidential contenders took the debate stage in Milwaukee, the conservative commentator \uc2 Tucker Carlson\uc2  posted what looks to be the entirety of his interview with \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  :\par \par \uc2 enltrEp. 19 Debate Night with \uc2 Donald J Trump{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/ayPfII48CO"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/ayPfII48CO}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 \uc2 Tucker Carlson\uc2  (@TuckerCarlson) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/TuckerCarlson/status/1694513603251241143?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 August 24, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 Trump is skipping the debate, opting for the interview with Carlson instead. In April, Fox News, which is hosting tonight\u8217\'20\'19s encounter with the GOP candidates, booted Carlson off the air, and the conservative commentator has since tried to rebuild his audience on \uc2 Twitter\uc2  (also known as X).\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.02am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.56am BST\par \par \uc2 Republicans take the stage in Milwaukee as first presidential debate kicks off\par \par \uc2 The eight Republicans who have qualified for the first debate of the 2024 presidential primary process have taken the stage in Milwaukee.\par \par \uc2 Frontrunner \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  is not among them, having opted to sit for an interview with the conservative commentator \uc2 Tucker Carlson\uc2 . The debate stage is instead filled with candidates looking to oust him from the top of the polls, such as the Florida governor, \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2 , who is currently in second place {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://projects.fivethirtyeight.com/polls/president-primary-r/2024/national/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 in most surveys}}}\uc2 , as well as the entrepreneur \uc2 Vivek Ramaswamy\uc2 , who has seen some momentum in recent polling.\par \par \uc2 The former vice-president \uc2 Mike Pence\uc2 , Senator Tim Scott and the ex-\uc2 UN\uc2  ambassador Nikki Haley are among the other candidates still in the running who are onstage.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 1.57am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.40am BST\par \par \uc2 Preparations for the debate were entering the final stages on Wednesday, with the stage in Milwaukee set up well in advance of the candidates\u8217\'20\'19 arrival.\par \par \uc2 Here are some of the latest images coming to us from the newswires as Wisconsin\u8217\'20\'19s largest city prepared for the debate:\par \par \uc2 Supporters of \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  gather outside the Fiserv Forum in Milwaukee, Wisconsin. Photograph: Brendan Smialowski/AFP/Getty Images Demonstrators dressed as Trump and \uc2 Anthony Fauci\uc2 . Photograph: Jim Bourg/Reuters The arena before Republican candidates for president hold their first debate. Photograph: Mark Hertzberg/ZUMA Press Wire/\uc2 Shutterstock\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.27am BST\par \par \uc2 While Trump is a no-show, some of his family members and most fervent supporters did make it to the debate venue.\par \par \uc2 The former Arizona gubernatorial candidate Kari Lake, who, much like Trump, refuses to accept her election defeat last year, was seen talking to the ex-president\u8217\'20\'19s son Donald Jr outside the arena in Milwaukee:\par \par \uc2 Kari Lake, second from left, talks to group including \uc2 Donald Trump Jr\uc2 , outside the Fiserv Forum in Milwaukee. Photograph: Mike De Sisti/AP\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 1.28am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.15am BST\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s opponents for the Republican nomination took his announcement earlier this week that he would skip the debate in stride \u8211\'20\'13 at least publicly. But as the Guardian\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/martin-pengelly"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Martin Pengelly}}}\uc2  reported, the former president will nonetheless loom large over the debate stage:\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s rivals for the Republican presidential nomination reacted in mostly muted fashion to his declaration that he will skip all the party\u8217\'20\'19s primary debates, not just the first in Milwaukee on Wednesday.\par \par \uc2 Trump\u8217\'20\'19s team have strategized that as the overwhelming frontrunner, the former president would gain little from appearing on stage with his many rivals. At the same time, his legal team are probably wary Trump may be tempted to wade into subject matter at the heart of proliferating legal cases against him.\par \par \uc2 Andrew Romeo, a spokesperson for {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/ron-desantis"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Ron DeSantis}}}\uc2 , Trump\u8217\'20\'19s closest if distant rival, insisted: \u8220\'20\'1CNo one is entitled to this nomination, including \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 . You have to show up and earn it.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 But while Trump is betting that not showing up will not hurt him with voters \u8211\'20\'13 and that his son \uc2 Donald Trump Jr{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://thehill.com/homenews/campaign/4162343-trump-jr-gop-debate-media-surrogate/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 will prove}}}\uc2  an effective media surrogate in Milwaukee \u8211\'20\'13 DeSantis has a pressing need to earn support. With his campaign widely seen to be tanking, the hard-right Florida governor will take the stage in Wisconsin on Wednesday with serious work to do.\par \par \uc2 In a Sunday night post to his online platform, Truth Social, Trump {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.reuters.com/world/us/trump-says-he-wont-take-part-republican-debates-2023-08-21/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 cited}}}\uc2  a CBS News poll that gave him a 46-point national lead. Bragging of \u8220\'20\'1Clegendary numbers\u8221\'20\'1D, he said: \u8220\'20\'1CThe public knows who I am and what a successful presidency I had \u8230\'20\'26 I WILL THEREFORE NOT BE DOING THE DEBATES!\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/aug/21/trump-republican-debate-presidential-nomination"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Trump\u8217\'20\'19s shadow hangs over Republican debates even as he refuses to attend}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.01am BST\par \par \uc2 Trump to discuss debate skipping, indictments and 'civil war' in \uc2 Tucker Carlson\uc2  interview\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  is leading the Republican primary field, but rather than participate in tonight\u8217\'20\'19s debate, he sat for an interview with \uc2 Tucker Carlson\uc2  \u8211\'20\'13 a conservative commentator whose views are often aligned with the former president\u8217\'20\'19s.\par \par \uc2 Expect their interview, which airs on \uc2 Twitter\uc2  (also known as X) at 8.55pm ET, five minutes before the debate starts, to be a particularly friendly encounter. Carlson, who {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/media/2023/jun/24/fox-news-tucker-carlson-dispute"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 was booted from his primetime spot on Fox News }}}\uc2  earlier this year, has released a teaser that indicates he asked Trump about everything from his legal troubles to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/jun/27/jeffrey-epstein-doj-watchdog-negligence-misconduct"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the death of }}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/jun/27/jeffrey-epstein-doj-watchdog-negligence-misconduct"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Jeffrey Epstein}}}\uc2  :\par \par \uc2 enltrDonald Trump. \uc2 Tucker Carlson\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Debate Night in Bedminster\par \par \uc2 8:55pm ET {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/w8nGhOfEdv"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/w8nGhOfEdv}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 \uc2 Tucker Carlson\uc2  (@TuckerCarlson) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/TuckerCarlson/status/1694469568549237033?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 August 23, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 Carlson is getting back on his feet after Fox showed him the door without warning in April, and has opted to broadcast the interview on \uc2 Twitter\uc2 /X, which, since billionaire \uc2 Elon Musk\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s purchase last year, has become an increasingly friendly platform for the right. In the below video, Carlson says Trump approached him about doing the interview, seeking \u8220\'20\'1Ca far larger audience than he\u8217\'20\'19d receive on cable news\u8221\'20\'1D \u8211\'20\'13 which sure sounds like a dig at his former employer:\par \par \uc2 enltrHere\u8217\'20\'19s what\u8217\'20\'19s happening at 8:55pm ET. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/UZcgSnv6Nm"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/UZcgSnv6Nm}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 \uc2 Tucker Carlson\uc2  (@TuckerCarlson) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/TuckerCarlson/status/1694424270821068805?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 August 23, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 1.04am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.38am BST\par \par \uc2 For an idea of what the eight Republicans who qualified for the debate might say on stage, the Guardian\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/mary-yang"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Mary Yang}}}\uc2  has a comprehensive look at their stances on the major issues.\par \par \uc2 Such as \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access, the economy and the January 6 insurrection. Read it here:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/aug/22/republican-candidate-views-debate-desantis-ramaswamy-christie"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 From \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  to January 6: where each Republican candidate in the debate stands on big issues}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 12.43am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.20am BST\par \par \uc2 Everything you need to know about tonight's Republican debate\par \par \uc2 Fox News is hosting the first Republican primary debate, which begins at 9pm ET in Milwaukee.\par \par \uc2 Wisconsin is a perennial swing state that has lately become viewed as the \u8220\'20\'1Ctipping point\u8221\'20\'1D in determining the winner of presidential elections. Racially diverse and reliably Democratic, Milwaukee is its most populous city, but voters in its suburbs often play a major role in deciding elections. The debate will be held at the city\u8217\'20\'19s Fiserv Forum.\par \par \uc2 The Guardian\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/davidsmith"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 David Smith}}}\uc2  is in Milwaukee, and has this look at what tonight\u8217\'20\'19s debates mean for the city:\par \par \uc2 The Republican party faces an electability test on Wednesday when candidates including election deniers, climate deniers and anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  extremists take the debate stage in a city that rebukes them and a state they cannot afford to lose.\par \par \uc2 The first presidential primary debate will be held in Milwaukee, a racially diverse Democratic stronghold in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/wisconsin"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Wisconsin}}}\uc2 , a battleground that could decide who wins the White House in 2024.\par \par \uc2 Even without \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , who is {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/aug/23/donald-trump-republican-debate-tucker-carlson"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 skipping the primetime televised event}}}\uc2 , the juxtaposition between Republicans who have embraced his far-right agenda and their sceptical host city offers a preview of the party\u8217\'20\'19s struggle to broaden its appeal.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/aug/23/republican-debate-milwaukee-2024-election-trump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \u8216\'20\'18In enemy territory\u8217\'20\'19: first Republican debate descends on Democratic city}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 12.22am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.02am BST\par \par \uc2 Republicans set to joust in first presidential debate, sans Trump\par \par \uc2 Good evening, and welcome to our live coverage of the first Republican primary debate, which will feature all of the party\u8217\'20\'19s main presidential contenders \u8211\'20\'13 except for the frontrunner, \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 While his eight rivals slug it out on the debate stage in Milwaukee, Trump will sit down for an interview with far-right commentator \uc2 Tucker Carlson\uc2 , which will air at the same time.\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, in Georgia, the former president\u8217\'20\'19s co-defendants in the indictment filed by Fulton county prosecutor \uc2 Fani Willis\uc2  over their attempt to disrupt the 2020 election spent the day surrendering, including \uc2 Rudy Giuliani\uc2 , who turned himself in after posting a $150,000 bail.\par \par \uc2 The debate kicks off at 9pm eastern time on Fox News, and will feature the following candidates: Florida\u8217\'20\'19s governor \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2 , former New Jersey governor \uc2 Chris Christie\uc2 , South Carolina senator Tim Scott, entrepreneur \uc2 Vivek Ramaswamy\uc2 , Trump\u8217\'20\'19s ex-\uc2 UN\uc2  ambassador Nikki Haley and his former vice-president \uc2 Mike Pence\uc2 , and former Arkansas governor \uc2 Asa Hutchinson\uc2 . North Dakota governor \uc2 Doug Burgum\uc2  was supposed to be there, but just injured his leg at a baseball game and may not attend.\par \par \uc2 Follow along here as we cover it live.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020230824ej8n00007\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
