\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Trump Georgia case: Giuliani mugshot released as Meadows and Clark lose attempts to block arrest \u8211\'20\'13 as it happened\b0\par\par\uc2 Chris Stein US politics live blogger (now); Martin Pengelly, L\u233\'00\'E9onie Chao-Fong and Maya Yang (earlier) \par \uc2 11,101 \uc2 words\par \uc2 23 August 2023\par 23:23 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 This live blog is now closed. For all the latest updates from the first Republican primary debate, head to our dedicated debate blog :Republican debate without Trump \u8211\'20\'13 live updatesFull story: Giuliani surrenders at Fulton county\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.10am BST\par \par \uc2 Closing summary\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s co-defendants reported to the Fulton county jail in Georgia after being indicted last week by district attorney \uc2 Fani Willis\uc2  on charges related to their roles in trying to overturn the 2020 election. Among them was {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/aug/23/trump-giuliani-georgia-fulton-republican-debate-politics-live-updates?page=with:block-64e656d08f08d8698b4d223e#block-64e656d08f08d8698b4d223e"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Rudy Giuliani}}}\uc2  , the former New York City mayor and presidential candidate who advised Trump during his presidency, and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/aug/23/trump-giuliani-georgia-fulton-republican-debate-politics-live-updates?page=with:block-64e655e48f08f3273b084eae#block-64e655e48f08f3273b084eae"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Sidney Powell}}}\uc2  , another attorney for the ex-president. Authorities in Georgia {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/aug/23/trump-giuliani-georgia-fulton-republican-debate-politics-live-updates?page=with:block-64e672978f08d8698b4d2301#block-64e672978f08d8698b4d2301"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 released mugshots of all the defendants}}}\uc2  who have surrendered thus far, including Giuliani and Powell, both of whom were released. Separately, a federal judge {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/aug/23/trump-giuliani-georgia-fulton-republican-debate-politics-live-updates?page=with:block-64e67eb08f08f3273b084f9a#block-64e67eb08f08f3273b084f9a"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 turned down an attempt}}}\uc2  by defendants \uc2 Mark Meadows\uc2 , Trump\u8217\'20\'19s former White House chief of staff, and Jeff Clark, an ex-justice department official friendly to his false claims about his election defeat, to avoid their arrest in Fulton county. Both now have until Friday to report to jail.\par \par \uc2 This blog is about to close, but the blogging is far from finished. We are launching a separate blog dedicated to covering this evening\u8217\'20\'19s Republican presidential debate, as well as Trump\u8217\'20\'19s interview with \uc2 Tucker Carlson\uc2 . Follow along at the link here:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/aug/23/republican-presidential-debate-2023-candidates-trump-tucker-live-updates"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Republican debate live: Trump a no-show as eight presidential hopefuls will compete for spotlight}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.48pm BST\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s defense attorneys may be breathing a sigh of relief after the former president opted to skip the first debate of the Republican primaries. Why? \uc2 The Guardian\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/hugo-lowell"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Hugo Lowell}}}\uc2  has the answer:\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s decision to spurn the Republican primary debate on Wednesday in favor of a pretaped interview with \uc2 Tucker Carlson\uc2  solves the political question of how to inflict damage on the 2024 field, but it also eliminates concerns his remarks in the high-profile event could increase his legal exposure.\par \par \uc2 The former president confirmed over the weekend that he {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/aug/21/donald-trump-republican-debate-fox-news"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 would not attend the debate}}}\uc2  in Milwaukee, saying in a post on his Truth Social platform: \u8220\'20\'1CNew CBS poll, just out, has me leading the field by \u8216\'20\'18legendary\u8217\'20\'19 numbers \u8230\'20\'26 I WILL THEREFORE NOT BE DOING THE DEBATES.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Instead, Trump has settled on counter-programming the debate by having the interview he recorded with the former Fox News host air at the same time, with the aim of starving the other Republican presidential candidates of attention and publicly humiliating Fox News, which is hosting the debate with the \uc2 Republican National Committee\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The move to upstage the debate tackles Trump\u8217\'20\'19s political goals for his 2024 campaign, but it also quietly eliminates worries that Trump could deepen his legal jeopardy were he to be questioned about his four criminal cases by debate moderators or the other candidates.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/aug/23/donald-trump-republican-debate-tucker-carlson"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Trump\u8217\'20\'19s plan to skip debate shields him from legal exposure}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 11.54pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.24pm BST\par \par \uc2 Tucker Carlson releases teaser of Trump interview\par \par \uc2 Tucker Carlson\uc2  has just posted a short teaser of his interview with \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  that will air this evening at the same time as the first debate of the Republican primary \u8211\'20\'13 which the ex-president said he will not attend. You can watch the clip here:\par \par \uc2 enltrDonald Trump. \uc2 Tucker Carlson\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Debate Night in Bedminster\par \par \uc2 8:55pm ET {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/w8nGhOfEdv"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/w8nGhOfEdv}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 \uc2 Tucker Carlson\uc2  (@TuckerCarlson) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/TuckerCarlson/status/1694469568549237033?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 August 23, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 Carlson\u8217\'20\'19s still trying to find his feet after Fox News booted him earlier this year, but he remains an influential voice in rightwing media and Trumpworld, especially.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 11.26pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.07pm BST\par \par \uc2 The White House put out a statement about \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s pre recorded interview with the former Fox News host \uc2 Tucker Carlson\uc2 , the former president\u8217\'20\'19s choice of counter-programming to the Republican debate in Wisconsin tonight, a n event Trump is skipping while leading polling by around 40 points.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIn his softball \u8216\'20\'18interview\u8217\'20\'19 posting tonight, \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  will again make clear that he\u8217\'20\'19s running on the same extreme and deeply unpopular Maga [Make America great again] agenda the American people have rejected time and time again,\u8221\'20\'1D spokesperson Kevin Munoz said, in a statement {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://thehill.com/homenews/campaign/4167489-biden-campaign-bashes-trump-tucker-carlson-interview/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 first released to the Hill}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CInstead of explaining his broken promises to Wisconsin and the 13,000 \uc2 Foxconn\uc2  manufacturing jobs {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2020/dec/08/wisconsin-foxconn-factory-residents-displaced"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 that never were}}}\uc2 , we\u8217\'20\'19ll likely hear him double down on his most out-of-touch positions, including his support for wild, debunked conspiracy theories and a national \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban,\u8221\'20\'1D Munoz said.\par \par \uc2 (For {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2020/dec/08/wisconsin-foxconn-factory-residents-displaced"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 more}}}\uc2  on Trump, Wisconsin and \uc2 Foxconn\uc2 , the Taiwanese electronics giant, see below.)\par \par \uc2 Munoz also had words for the contenders on stage in Wisconsin, saying: \u8220\'20\'1CThat same extreme and unpopular agenda will be on display in Milwaukee later tonight by Maga Republican candidates doing their best impressions of \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 . The American people rejected these extreme ideas in 2018, 2020, and 2022 \u8211\'20\'13 and they will again in November 2024.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Polling regarding a notional general election rematch between Trump and \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  generally shows close contests.\par \par \uc2 Biden, who is on holiday in Nevada, briefly addressed the Republican debate earlier today. Asked if he was going to watch, he told reporters: \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19m going to try to see \u8211\'20\'13 get as much as I can, yes.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The pool report added: \u8220\'20\'1CAsked what his expectations were, he smiled broadly and laughed. \u8216\'20\'18I have none.\u8217\'20\'19\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1C\u8216\'20\'18Thank you all,\u8217\'20\'19 he added, and then walked to the car.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CHe was wearing a blue ballcap, aviators, and a teal sweater. He had what looked to be an iced coffee in his hand.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2020/dec/08/wisconsin-foxconn-factory-residents-displaced"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \u8216\'20\'18They demolished my house for this?\u8217\'20\'19 Residents outraged by the Foxconn factory that fizzled}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 11.13pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.52pm BST\par \par \uc2 Meadows and Clark lose in attempts to avoid surrender\par \par \uc2 Hugo Lowell reports:\par \par \uc2 Just in: A federal judge has denied former Trump White House chief of staff \uc2 Mark Meadows\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19 request for an emergency order to prevent his arrest at the Fulton county jail while he tries to have his case removed to federal court.\par \par \uc2 Furthermore:\par \par \uc2 A federal judge has denied former Trump Justice department official Jeff Clark\u8217\'20\'19s request for an emergency stay to avoid having to surrender at the Fulton county jail, after he filed to have his case removed to federal court. Clark has until Friday at noon to travel to Atlanta for booking.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 10.54pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.40pm BST\par \par \uc2 In a fundraising email to supporters, the South Carolina senator Tim Scott offers a (very basic) taste of what he might offer on the debate stage in Milwaukee tonight.\par \par \uc2 Tim Scott. Photograph: Cheney Orr/Reuters\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIf you had told 7-year-old Tim Scott he would one day be on a presidential debate stage, he would NOT believe you,\u8221\'20\'1D the email says.\par \par \uc2 Seven-year-old Tim might also not have believed that his grown-up self would take his debate stage bow with {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://projects.fivethirtyeight.com/polls/president-primary-r/2024/national/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 just 1% support}}}\uc2 , a mere 51 points behind the frontrunner, \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 . But I digress.\par \par \uc2 The email continues: \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19m a child of divorce. When I was 7, my mom, my older brother, and I moved into a two-bedroom rental house that we shared with my grandparents.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CMy Mama and Granddaddy told me you can be bitter or you can be better. You can be a victim or you can choose victory. Well Friend, I\u8217\'20\'19m ready to choose victory!\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CTonight, I\u8217\'20\'19ll share why the truth of my life disproves the Left\u8217\'20\'19s lies and why I believe America can do for anyone what she\u8217\'20\'19s done for me.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 What Scott might do in the primary remains of course to be seen. He has big support from the \uc2 Oracle\uc2  billionaire \uc2 Larry Ellison\uc2  and with a big debate performance, who knows.\par \par \uc2 But the signs are not particularly rosy, even when one zeroes in on Iowa, the first state to vote and one where evangelical Christians, a key Scott constituency, are strong.\par \par \uc2 Over the weekend, a major poll {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/2023/08/21/us/politics/trump-poll-rating.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 from NBC News and the Des Moines Register}}}\uc2  put the senator in third place. That was better than his position in national averages (linked to above). But though Scott had 9% support, \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2  of Florida had 19% and Trump \u8211\'20\'13 thrice-married and an adjudicated rapist yet still the No 1 choice for Christian conservatives \u8211\'20\'13 had 42%.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 10.56pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.21pm BST\par \par \uc2 Marjorie Taylor Greene\uc2 : my name is on a list for Trump VP\par \par \uc2 Our Washington bureau chief reports from Milwaukee, ahead of tonight\u8217\'20\'19s Republican debate \u8230\'20\'26\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  is missing from the first Republican primary debate but his supporters are not. Nine hours before kick-off, they were roving outside the venue wearing \u8220\'20\'1CMake America great again\u8221\'20\'1D caps and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/SmithInAmerica/status/1694383433382809855?s=20"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 brandishing signs}}}\uc2  mocking the Florida governor, \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Marjorie Taylor Greene\uc2 . Photograph: Jacquelyn Martin/AP\par \par \uc2 Some of the former president\u8217\'20\'19s allies in the \uc2 US Congress\uc2 , such as \uc2 Matt Gaetz\uc2  of Florida and \uc2 Marjorie Taylor Greene\uc2  of Georgia, are also here. Sitting in a hotel lobby, Greene told the Guardian that she backs Trump\u8217\'20\'19s decision to stay away.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI told him to skip it,\u8221\'20\'1D the far-right congresswoman and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.rollingstone.com/politics/politics-news/marjorie-taylor-greene-blames-internet-qanon-beliefs-1234657579/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 conspiracy theorist}}}\uc2  said. \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s a waste of his time.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CHe\u8217\'20\'19s winning by over 60%, poll after poll depending on what state you\u8217\'20\'19re looking at and the national poll. It\u8217\'20\'19s a complete waste of his time to step out on a stage and be the centre of the attacks when he has a four-year record as president that everybody wants back and none of those people on the stage have anything that they can compare to him.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 There has been speculation that Trump could choose Greene as his running mate.\par \par \uc2 She said: \u8220\'20\'1CWell, I\u8217\'20\'19d have to think about it and consider it. It\u8217\'20\'19s talked about frequently and I know my name is on a list but really my biggest focus right now is serving the district that elected me.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThat\u8217\'20\'19s of course a decision that President Trump has to make. I don\u8217\'20\'19t know who that person is going to be and I don\u8217\'20\'19t even think they\u8217\'20\'19re going to be on that debate stage. I\u8217\'20\'19ll argue that. But, of course, that\u8217\'20\'19s up to him. But I would be honoured and consider it. But my most important job is, of course, to serve the American people and I\u8217\'20\'19ll help him do whatever in any way I can.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Greene said the three Republicans she talks to most frequently are Trump, Kevin McCarthy, speaker of the House of Representatives, and James Comer, chairman of the House oversight committee. Do they all seem to be on the same page?\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CA lot of times, yeah. Not all the time but a lot of times. It just depends on the issue.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Trump is expected to surrender at the Fulton county jail on Thursday evening on racketeering and conspiracy charges, over his efforts to overturn the 2020 presidential election in Georgia. It is Greene\u8217\'20\'19s home state but she dismisses the sweeping indictment as \u8220\'20\'1Cgarbage\u8221\'20\'1D and has not read it.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI wouldn\u8217\'20\'19t waste five seconds of my time,\u8221\'20\'1D she said.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 12.19am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.01pm BST\par \par \uc2 Mugshots of \uc2 Rudy Giuliani\uc2  and co-defendants released by Fulton county\par \par \uc2 Booking pictures of those Trump aides and allies who have so far surrendered in Georgia have now been released.\par \par \uc2 Here is the official booking picture of Giuliani:\par \par \uc2 Rudy Giuliani\uc2  booking picture. Photograph: FULTON COUNTY SHERIFF'S OFFICE/AFP/Getty Images\par \par \uc2 Here are some for more of the co-defendants:\par \par \uc2 Sidney Powell\uc2 . Photograph: AP \uc2 Jenna Ellis\uc2 . Photograph: AP John Eastman. Photograph: Tiffany Turner/Fulton County Sheriff\u8217\'20\'19s Office Kenneth Chesebro. Photograph: AP\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 10.12pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.42pm BST\par \par \uc2 Some levity, of a sort, for those wanting a slightly different angle on what until relatively recently would have been the outlandish, outrageous prospect of a former US president being booked at an Atlanta jail on charges including racketeering and conspiracy, related to an attempt to overturn an election.\par \par \uc2 Bookies are {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.betonline.ag/sportsbook/futures-and-props/us-election/trump-indictment"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 offering}}}\uc2  punters the chance to bet on what \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s recorded weight will be when he surrenders at the Fulton County Jail tomorrow. As the Daily Beast {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.thedailybeast.com/you-can-bet-on-trumps-weight-ahead-of-his-surrender-to-fulton-county-jail"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 puts it}}}\uc2 , perennially pleasingly snarky\u8230\'20\'26\par \par \uc2 The line currently sits over/under 278.5lb, a far cry from the 244lb White House physician Sean Conley recorded for Trump {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cnn.com/2020/06/03/politics/donald-trump-annual-physical/index.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 in 2020}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 As the Beast also notes, part of punters\u8217\'20\'19 interest in the former president\u8217\'20\'19s avoirdupois is fueled by the purest schadenfreude, if I might overdo the pretentious italics. Trump, of course, has a habit of abusing his opponents, critics and enemies \u8211\'20\'13 see Christie, Chris and O\u8217\'20\'19Donnell, Rosie, passim \u8211\'20\'13 about their body mass index.\par \par \uc2 Trump\u8217\'20\'19s height will also be taken. His 2020 White House physical said he was 6ft 3in tall. There is speculation, widespread, that the truth is different:\par \par \uc2 enltrThere's been speculation -- and betting -- about Trump's weigh-in tomorrow. A related question: Will the deputies make him remove the lifts from his shoes before measuring his height? {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/dSDifJE3TD"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/dSDifJE3TD}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Jack Pitney (@jpitney) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/jpitney/status/1694401120930762924?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 August 23, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 9.43pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.24pm BST\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s a slightly fuller version of comments from \uc2 Rudy Giuliani\uc2 , the former New York mayor turned Trump attorney, after his surrender in Atlanta on charges including conspiracy and racketeering.\par \par \uc2 Speaking to reporters, and laughing as he did so, Giuliani said he was \u8220\'20\'1Cvery, very honoured to be involved in this case because this case is a fight for our way of life\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThis indictment is a travesty,\u8221\'20\'1D he said. \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s an attack on not just me, not just President [Donald] Trump, this is an attack on the American people. If this could happen to me, who is probably the most prolific prosecutor maybe in American history and the most effective mayor for sure, it can happen to you.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Giuliani was indeed a prolific prosecutor, back in New York before he became mayor and briefly, after leading New York on and after 9/11, dreamt of a rise to the White House.\par \par \uc2 As US attorney in Manhattan, he memorably cracked down on organised crime by using racketeering statutes.\par \par \uc2 It\u8217\'20\'19s safe to say his current predicament in relation to similar such statutes \u8230\'20\'26 has been noticed by quite a few observers.\par \par \uc2 I typed \u8220\'20\'1CGiuliani irony\u8221\'20\'1D into \uc2 Google\uc2 , and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://abcnews.go.com/US/perfect-irony-giuliani-faces-rico-charge-similar-popularized/story?id=102285953"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 this}}}\uc2  and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.msnbc.com/opinion/msnbc-opinion/sad-irony-fani-willis-flipping-rico-statute-rudy-giuliani-rcna100294"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 this}}}\uc2  and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/2023/08/18/opinion/rudy-giuliani-trump-authoritarianism.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 this}}}\uc2  came up. And {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://ny1.com/nyc/all-boroughs/politics/2023/08/16/rudy-giuliani-pioneered-using-rico-charges-to-take-on-the-mob--now-he-s-facing-a-charge-himself-in-georgia-election-case-donald-trump-andrew-kirtzman-america-s-mayor"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 more}}}\uc2 .\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/aug/22/michael-cohen-donald-trump-rudy-giuliani-legal-fees"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Here}}}\uc2 , meanwhile, is some further reading about what \uc2 Michael Cohen\uc2 , another Trump attorney who turned on his old boss after being sent to jail, had to say the other day about Trump, Giuliani and the concept of payment for legal services rendered \u8230\'20\'26\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/aug/22/michael-cohen-donald-trump-rudy-giuliani-legal-fees"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \u8216\'20\'18Donald\u8217\'20\'19s an idiot\u8217\'20\'19: Michael Cohen says Trump\u8217\'20\'19s rebuffing of Giuliani could backfire}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 9.30pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.05pm BST\par \par \uc2 Doug Burgum\uc2 , governor of North Dakota and GOP presidential candidate, said he will consult a physician before deciding if he will participate at tonight\u8217\'20\'19s debate, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/aug/23/trump-giuliani-georgia-fulton-republican-debate-politics-live-updates?page=with:block-64e61cdc8f08d8698b4d1f4f#block-64e61cdc8f08d8698b4d1f4f"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 after injuring his leg at a basketball game }}}\uc2  yesterday.\par \par \uc2 Speaking to CNN\u8217\'20\'19s Dana Bash, Burgum said his debate walkthrough went well despite tearing his achilles tendon.\par \par \uc2 enltr. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/DougBurgum?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @DougBurgum}}}\uc2  tells {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/DanaBashCNN?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @DanaBashCNN}}}\uc2  that his debate walkthrough went well despite tearing his Achilles tendon yesterday but says he\u8217\'20\'19s going to consult a physician before deciding if he will participate at tonight\u8217\'20\'19s Republican debate. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/J5r3P82HqC"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/J5r3P82HqC}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Greg Hughes (@newsbyhughes) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/newsbyhughes/status/1694422598220734529?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 August 23, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.58pm BST\par \par \uc2 Fulton County officials have released the mug shot of Kenneth Chesebro, the alleged architect of \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s fake electors plot.\par \par \uc2 Chesebro {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/aug/23/trump-giuliani-georgia-fulton-republican-debate-politics-live-updates?page=with:block-64e60a5f8f08d8698b4d1e64#block-64e60a5f8f08d8698b4d1e64"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 surrendered at the Fulton county jail }}}\uc2  earlier on Wednesday.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s the mug shot, as shared by \uc2 CBS\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19 Scott MacFarlane:\par \par \uc2 enltrNEW: Booking photo for Kenneth Chesebro in Fulton County, Georgia\par \par \uc2 Chesebro was also a figure in the House Jan 6 Select Committee probe, accused of drafting strategy to overturn election {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/jKbgZAf75B"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/jKbgZAf75B}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Scott MacFarlane (@MacFarlaneNews) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/MacFarlaneNews/status/1694435728090878319?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 August 23, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.53pm BST\par \par \uc2 Rudy Giuliani\uc2  claims he is being indicted because he was a lawyer for \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The former New York mayor accuses the \uc2 FBI\uc2  of having \u8220\'20\'1Cstole(n) my iCloud account the day that I began representing \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.49pm BST\par \par \uc2 Rudy Giuliani\uc2  says the Fulton county district office\u8217\'20\'19s case against him, \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  and his co-defendants is \u8220\'20\'1Can attack on the American people\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIf they can do this to me, they can do this to you,\u8221\'20\'1D he tells reporters.\par \par \uc2 Fulton county district attorney \uc2 Fani Willis\uc2  \u8220\'20\'1Cwill go down in American history for having conducted one of the worst attacks on the American constitution\u8221\'20\'1D, Giuliani says.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.45pm BST\par \par \uc2 Giuliani says he is 'very honored' to be involved in Georgia election subversion case\par \par \uc2 Rudy Giuliani\uc2  is speaking to reporters after he surrendered to authorities at the Fulton county jail on charges that he helped lead a racketeering enterprise and conspired to overturn the results of the 2020 presidential election in the state of Georgia.\par \par \uc2 Asked if he regretted attaching his name to \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , Giuliani replied:\par \par \uc2 I am very, very honoured to be involved in this because this case is a fight for our way of life.\par \par \uc2 This indictment is a travesty. It\u8217\'20\'19s an attack on not just me, not just President Trump, not just the people in this indictment, some of them I don\u8217\'20\'19t even know.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.42pm BST\par \par \uc2 Fulton county district attorney \uc2 Fani Willis\uc2  sharply rejected efforts by two of \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s co-defendants \u8211\'20\'13 former White House chief of staff \uc2 Mark Meadows\uc2  and Jeffrey Clark \u8211\'20\'13 to move their sprawling racketeering cases to federal court.\par \par \uc2 From my colleague Sam Levine:\par \par \uc2 enltrFulton county DA Fani Willis rebuts {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/JeffClarkUS?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @JeffClarkUS}}}\uc2  request to have a federal court halt his surrender in GA. "As inconvenient as modern air travel can admittedly be..." {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/ZQrZebyZhs"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/ZQrZebyZhs}}}\uc2  h/t {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/stphnfwlr?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @stphnfwlr}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/HktxSyycBe"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/HktxSyycBe}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Sam Levine (@srl) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/srl/status/1694428371428491571?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 August 23, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.38pm BST\par \par \uc2 Rudy Giuliani{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/aug/23/trump-giuliani-georgia-fulton-republican-debate-politics-live-updates?filterKeyEvents=false&page=with:block-64e610ec8f08319ad416c491#block-64e610ec8f08319ad416c491"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 left Manhattan in the morning }}}\uc2  to travel to Atlanta with his lead lawyer, John Esposito, on a private jet, though the source of the funding for the plane remains uncertain given Giuliani has struggled financially in the wake of mounting legal bills.\par \par \uc2 Giuliani\u8217\'20\'19s financial trouble stemming from having to retain lawyers for the congressional and federal criminal investigations into efforts to subvert the 2020 election results have become particularly acute in recent weeks, according to two people familiar with the matter.\par \par \uc2 The money problems have been exacerbated by Giuliani\u8217\'20\'19s recent setbacks in court \u8211\'20\'13 including in a defamation case against two Georgia election workers he falsely accused of stealing ballots \u8211\'20\'13 and the suspension of his law license over his election subversion efforts means he has few income streams.\par \par \uc2 The situation has led to Giuliani listing his Manhattan apartment for sale for more than $6m. He also travelled to \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s Mar-a-Lago club in April to ask the former president to help pay his legal bills after Trump rejected his earlier entreaties for support, the people said.\par \par \uc2 When that trip failed to convince Trump to have his Save America political action committee pay for Giuliani\u8217\'20\'19s legal bills, in the way that Trump has doled out $21m for aides\u8217\'20\'19 legal bills tied up in the criminal investigations, Giuliani\u8217\'20\'19s son Andrew made his own trip to see Trump.\par \par \uc2 Trump has never explained why he has consistently refused to help Giuliani, but people in his orbit point to Trump\u8217\'20\'19s complaints that Giuliani was defeated in almost every 2020 election lawsuit that he brought.\par \par \uc2 But the meeting with \uc2 Andrew Giuliani\uc2  appears to have helped, and Trump agreed to attend two fundraisers, the people said. Trump will host a $100,000-per-person fundraiser at his Bedminster club in New Jersey next month, according to an invitation reviewed by the \uc2 New York Times\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.35pm BST\par \par \uc2 Rudy Giuliani\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/aug/23/trump-giuliani-georgia-fulton-republican-debate-politics-live-updates?page=with:block-64e656d08f08d8698b4d223e#block-64e656d08f08d8698b4d223e"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  surrender to authorities}}}\uc2  at the Fulton county jail marks a jarring moment for Giuliani, a former federal prosecutor who made his name with aggressive racketeering cases, now facing a racketeering charge himself.\par \par \uc2 Alongside \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , Giuliani faces the most charges in the sprawling 41-count indictment handed up by a grand jury last week that described how he played a principal role in marshalling fake slates of electors among other schemes to reverse Trump\u8217\'20\'19s defeat in the 2020 election.\par \par \uc2 The bond for Giuliani was set at $150,000 after his lawyers met with the Fulton county district attorney \uc2 Fani Willis\uc2  earlier in the day. The amount was slightly less than the $200,000 bond for Trump but more than the $100,000 bond for another former Trump lawyer, \uc2 Sidney Powell\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.33pm BST\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  and his family are on vacation in Lake Tahoe.\par \par \uc2 The president, first lady and members of the Biden family \u8220\'20\'1Care taking a Pilates class followed by a spin class\u8221\'20\'1D, the White House said earlier.\par \par \uc2 AP\u8217\'20\'19s Seung Min Kim shared a photo of Biden after his pilates and spin classes:\par \par \uc2 enltrBiden, holding onto a post-workout drink after Pilates and spin at Pelodog, tells us of the plane crash in Russia:\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThere\u8217\'20\'19s not much that happens in Russia that Putin\u8217\'20\'19s not behind but I don\u8217\'20\'19t know enough to know the answer.\u8221\'20\'1D {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/yB2sPhqQ1W"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/yB2sPhqQ1W}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Seung Min Kim (@seungminkim) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/seungminkim/status/1694427630551101756?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 August 23, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 8.33pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.24pm BST\par \par \uc2 Democrats will be denied political oxygen on Wednesday night but hope to turn this to their advantage by framing all the Republican candidates as \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 -adjacent extremists.\par \par \uc2 At a press conference on the top floor of a downtown Milwaukee hotel, \uc2 Jaime Harrison\uc2 , chair of the \uc2 Democratic National Committee\uc2 , said:\par \par \uc2 Tonight, in prime time, Americans will have an opportunity to see in action the most extreme, the most divisive, the most chaotic slate of presidential candidates in history when these Maga 2024 Republicans take the debate stage here in Milwaukee, and I don\u8217\'20\'19t know if it\u8217\'20\'19s going to be a debate, but more like a circus.\par \par \uc2 They may try to differentiate themselves but the truth is that every single one of these candidates from \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  on down are extreme.\par \par \uc2 Harrison went on to list the candidates one by one, setting out their positions on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , pushing conspiracy theories and past associations with the Tea Party or Trump.\par \par \uc2 No matter who you pick, this group is as extreme as it gets. A bag full of Maga apples and they are all rotten. They are wildly out of step with the American people.\par \par \uc2 He attempted to draw a contrast between the two parties. \u8220\'20\'1CWe believe that our better days as a nation are ahead of us, not behind us. They believe that our better days are behind us and that is the difference in this election.\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  wakes up every day thinking about how to make the lives of the American people better. They wake up every day thinking about how do I get back in power? That is the difference between the Democratic party led by \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  and a Republican party led by Maga extremists.\par \par \uc2 Satya Rhodes-Conway\uc2 , the mayor of Madison, Wisconsin, accused Republicans of pushing a national \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban. \u8220\'20\'1CLet me be crystal clear about this: the 2024 Maga Republican presidential candidates are running on their extreme anti-choice records,\u8221\'20\'1D she said.\par \par \uc2 I\u8217\'20\'19m sure that they\u8217\'20\'19re going to talk about freedom on the debate stage tonight. But what about the freedom to make my own health care decisions? I guess that their version of freedom doesn\u8217\'20\'19t include women.\par \par \uc2 Rhodes-Conway added:\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s the bottom line: the American people don\u8217\'20\'19t want anything to do with their \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  bans. Voters in states all across this great country, including right here in Wisconsin, have made it clear that the craven \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  bans are wildly unpopular and out of step with the American public.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.18pm BST\par \par \uc2 Rudy Giuliani\uc2  has turned himself in at the Fulton county jail over charges tied to his efforts to help \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  overturn the 2020 presidential election.\par \par \uc2 The former New York City mayor and longtime Trump ally faces 13 charges that include racketeering, soliciting lawmakers to violate their oaths of office, making false statements and conspiracy counts dealing with the recruitment of fake electors.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s a look at the Fulton county jail records, as shared by NBC\u8217\'20\'19s Blayne Alexander:\par \par \uc2 enltrBREAKING: \uc2 Rudy Giuliani\uc2  has been booked into the Fulton County jail, according to jail records. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/CWBvLgMcwB"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/CWBvLgMcwB}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Blayne Alexander (@ReporterBlayne) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/ReporterBlayne/status/1694426201144643970?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 August 23, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.04pm BST\par \par \uc2 Rudy Giuliani\uc2  surrenders in elections racketeering case\par \par \uc2 Rudy Giuliani\uc2  has arrived at the Fulton county jail and surrendered to authorities, according to the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://justice.fultoncountyga.gov/PAJailManager/JailingDetail.aspx?JailingID=1472670"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 county sheriff\u8217\'20\'19s website.}}}\par \par \uc2 The former New York mayor and lawyer for \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  faces charges in the sprawling Georgia elections racketeering case. At a meeting earlier today with Fulton county district attorney \uc2 Fani Willis\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19 team, Giuliani\u8217\'20\'19s bond was set at $150,000.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19m feeling very, very good about it because I feel like I am defending the rights of all Americans, as I did so many times as a United States attorney,\u8221\'20\'1D Giuliani told reporters in New York this morning.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 8.08pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.55pm BST\par \par \uc2 Trump campaign attorney \uc2 Sidney Powell\uc2  surrenders to Fulton county authorities\par \par \uc2 Sidney Powell\uc2 , a lawyer for \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  heavily involved in efforts to overturn the 2020 election result, has surrendered to Fulton county authorities, according to county records.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 7.58pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.49pm BST\par \par \uc2 South Carolina\u8217\'20\'19s all-male highest court upholds six-week \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban\par \par \uc2 South Carolina \u8217\'20\'19s new all-male highest court on Wednesday reversed course on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights, upholding the state\u8217\'20\'19s strict six-week ban on the procedure.\par \par \uc2 The panel overrode an earlier decision in which the court decided a similar restriction was unconstitutional.\par \par \uc2 The court on Wednesday found that the state constitution\u8217\'20\'19s protection against \u8220\'20\'1Cunreasonable invasions of privacy\u8221\'20\'1D did not include a right to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , and that the state law was \u8220\'20\'1Cwithin the zone of reasonable policy decisions rationally related to the state\u8217\'20\'19s interest in protecting the unborn\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 A judge in May had put a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/may/26/south-carolina-abortion-ban-state-supreme-court-review"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 temporary halt}}}\uc2  to South Carolina\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/may/23/south-carolina-abortion-ban-six-weeks"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 new law banning}}}\uc2  most abortions around six weeks of pregnancy until the state supreme court could review the measure. The ruling at the time, by Judge Clifton Newman, came just about 24 hours after the state governor, \uc2 Henry McMaster\uc2 , signed the bill, and meant South Carolina reverted back to a ban at about 20 weeks after fertilization.\par \par \uc2 The new ruling is a blow to reproductive rights campaigners. On Wednesday, McMaster hailed the decision, issuing a statement saying:\par \par \uc2 The supreme court\u8217\'20\'19s ruling marks a historic moment in our state\u8217\'20\'19s history and is the culmination of years of hard work and determination by so many in our state to ensure that the sanctity of life is protected.\par \par \uc2 It went on:\par \par \uc2 With this victory, we protect the lives of countless unborn children and reaffirm South Carolina\u8217\'20\'19s place as one of the most pro-life states in America.\par \par \uc2 The decision was 4-1, with the chief justice, Donald Beatty, in the minority.\par \par \uc2 Caroline Sacerdote\uc2 , a staff attorney at the Center for Reproductive Rights who helped bring the lawsuit against the new six-week ban, said:\par \par \uc2 This decision is devastating not only because of the impact it will have on South Carolinians, but also because South Carolina is a critical state for access across the entire south-east region.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.44pm BST\par \par \uc2 Six defendants in Georgia election case have surrendered so far\par \par \uc2 The first six defendants in the Georgia election subversion case against \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  and 18 other defendants have been booked in the Fulton county jail so far.\par \par \uc2 The Fulton county district attorney, \uc2 Fani Willis\uc2 , who delivered the sweeping indictment last week, has given all 19 defendants until noon this Friday, 25 August, to voluntarily surrender.\par \par \uc2 The six defendants who have already been booked in the Fulton county jail are:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Scott Hall, a Georgia bail bondsman\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 John Eastman, a former Trump attorney\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Kenneth Chesebro, a pro-Trump attorney\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Cathy Latham, former chair of the Coffee county Republican party\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 David Shafer, Georgia GOP chair and fake elector\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Ray Smith, a former Trump attorney\par \par \uc2 Trump, whose bond has been set at $200,000 and was charged with 13 felony counts, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/aug/21/donald-trump-bond-set-fulton-county-georgia"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 said he plans to turn himself in}}}\uc2  on Thursday.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 7.44pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.27pm BST\par \par \uc2 Rudy Giuliani\uc2  reaches $150,000 bail agreement in Georgia election case\par \par \uc2 Rudy Giuliani\uc2  has reached a $150,000 bond agreement with the Fulton county district attorney\u8217\'20\'19s office.\par \par \uc2 From my colleague Hugo Lowell:\par \par \uc2 enltrNew: Former Trump lawyer \uc2 Rudy Giuliani\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s attorneys have agreed a $150,000 bond with the Fulton County DA\u8217\'20\'19s office\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Hugo Lowell (@hugolowell) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/hugolowell/status/1694415941147238910?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 August 23, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 Giuliani, the former New York mayor and Trump lawyer, faces 13 charges including racketeering, three counts of soliciting lawmakers to violate their oaths of office, three counts of making false statements and six conspiracy counts dealing with the recruitment of fake electors.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 7.32pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.22pm BST\par \par \uc2 Georgia Republican representative \uc2 Marjorie Taylor Greene\uc2  said that she will not vote to fund president \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s plan to expand global vaccine accessibility following the Covid-19 pandemic.\par \par \uc2 Greene, a fierce Biden critic, tweeted:\par \par \uc2 I will NOT vote to fund your COVID mental illness forcing masks and vaccines on anyone! Especially NOT children!\par \par \uc2 enltrDear President Psychopath,\par \par \uc2 You signed a resolution into law that stated the COVID-19 pandemic is OVER!!!!\par \par \uc2 I will NOT vote to fund your COVID mental illness forcing masks and vaccines on anyone!\par \par \uc2 Especially NOT children!\par \par \uc2 Investigate the VAERS reports & stop serving Big Pharma. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/O3k9Zz2Hnd"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/O3k9Zz2Hnd}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Rep. \uc2 Marjorie Taylor Greene\uc2 ???? (@RepMTG) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/RepMTG/status/1694127939061723450?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 August 22, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.01pm BST\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s co-defendant \uc2 Mark Meadows\uc2  has asked a federal court to block his arrest in Georgia.\par \par \uc2 Mary Yang reports:\par \par \uc2 Mark Meadows\uc2 , the former White House chief of staff for \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , has asked a federal court to block his arrest in an emergency motion, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://storage.courtlistener.com/recap/gov.uscourts.gand.319225/gov.uscourts.gand.319225.17.0.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 according to court documents}}}\uc2  filed on Tuesday.\par \par \uc2 Meadows, a named defendant in the sweeping election interference case against {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/donaldtrump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Donald Trump}}}\uc2  and 18 others in Fulton county, Georgia, has requested the case be moved to federal court, saying the charges concern his actions as an officer of the federal government.\par \par \uc2 Trump\u8217\'20\'19s legal team is also {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/aug/17/trump-georgia-indictment-trial-move-federal-court"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 expected to argue}}}\uc2  that the case should be moved to federal court because he was acting in the capacity of president.\par \par \uc2 In the Tuesday emergency motion, Meadows asked the court to \u8220\'20\'1Cprotect\u8221\'20\'1D him from arrest before a Monday, 28 August, hearing on his request to move the case out of the Fulton county superior court to the district court of northern {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/state-of-georgia"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Georgia}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 For the full story, click here:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/aug/22/mark-meadows-asks-judge-to-block-arrest-georgia"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Trump co-defendant Mark Meadows asks judge to block his arrest in Georgia }}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.48pm BST\par \par \uc2 Giuliani lawyers arrive at Fulton county DA building\par \par \uc2 Several lawyers of former \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  lawyer \uc2 Rudy Giuliani\uc2  have walked into the Fulton county district attorney building, according to \uc2 The Guardian\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s reporter Hugo Lowell.\par \par \uc2 enltrNew: Former Trump lawyer \uc2 Rudy Giuliani\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s local counsel Brian Tevis just walked into the Fulton County DA building\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Hugo Lowell (@hugolowell) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/hugolowell/status/1694398313917804691?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 August 23, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 enltrAlso currently in the Fulton County DA\u8217\'20\'19s office, per person familiar: Giuliani\u8217\'20\'19s other lawyer John Esposito, who travelled with him from New York\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Hugo Lowell (@hugolowell) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/hugolowell/status/1694404090812301785?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 August 23, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 6.52pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.36pm BST\par \par \uc2 Interim Summary\par \par \uc2 It is shortly past 1:30pm in Washington DC. Here is where the day\u8217\'20\'19s key events stand:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  \u8211\'20\'13 seeking to distract from the indignity of the surrender by turning things into a circus \u8211\'20\'13 in essence had his lawyers {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/aug/22/donald-trump-surrender-fulton-county-jail-thursday-night"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 negotiate the booking to take place on Thursday evening}}}\uc2  during the prime viewing hours for the cable news networks. Trump has posted on his Truth Social platform that he would be arrested on Thursday, but the primetime scheduling was finalized in recent days after his lawyers met with the Fulton county district attorney, \uc2 Fani Willis\uc2 , at her office on Monday.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 A plane carrying \uc2 Rudy Giuliani\uc2  has landed at Atlanta\u8217\'20\'19s Dekalb-Peachtree airport. The former New York mayor and lawyer for \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  is expected to surrender to face charges in the sprawling {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/state-of-georgia"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Georgia}}}\uc2  elections racketeering case later today.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 House speaker Kevin McCarthy said lawmakers could formally launch an impeachment inquiry into \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  next month when they return from summer recess. During an interview with Fox Business on Tuesday night, McCarthy said the Republican-led House will move forward with an impeachment inquiry if the Bidens do not \u8220\'20\'1Cprovide us the documents we\u8217\'20\'19re asking.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Misty Hampton, the former elections supervisor for Coffee county, has reached a $10,000 bond agreement with prosecutors in Fulton count, according to court documents. Hampton\u8217\'20\'19s bail conditions include not communicating with witnesses and co-defendants, reporting to pretrial services by phone every month and not obstructing justice by intimidating witnesses.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 A witness in the criminal case against \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  over his alleged mishandling of classified documents retracted \u8220\'20\'1Cprior false testimony\u8221\'20\'1D after switching lawyers last month and implicated the former president in new information, according to the justice department. The witness, a Trump employee identified elsewhere as Mar-a-Lago director of information technology, Yuscil Taveras, initially testified to a grand jury in Washington DC that he was unaware of any effort to erase surveillance video at the Florida property.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 North Dakota governor and Republican presidential hopeful \uc2 Doug Burgum\uc2  injured himself playing basketball on Tuesday, leaving in doubt his participation in the first Republican presidential debate tonight. Burgum, 67, was taken to a Milwaukee emergency room after injuring his leg while playing a game of pick-up basketball with his staff, CNN {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://edition.cnn.com/2023/08/23/politics/doug-burgum-injured/index.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reported,}}}\uc2  citing a source. He was discharged from the hospital the same day.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Fulton county officials released the first two booking photos of defendants in the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/state-of-georgia"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Georgia}}}\uc2  election subversion case against \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  and allies. John Eastman, who is alleged to have orchestrated the so-called fake elector plot that aimed to keep Trump in power after he lost the 2020 election, surrendered to authorities in Georgia on Tuesday. Scott Hall, a bail bondsman who is accused of a voting system breach in Georgia\u8217\'20\'19s Coffee county, was also booked in on Tuesday.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 6.40pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.23pm BST\par \par \uc2 In a quick pivot to the Russia-Ukraine war, the the Russian Civil Aviation Authority announced that \uc2 Yevgeny Prigozhin\uc2 , the leader of the Wagner mercenary group, was on the passenger list of a plane that crashed in the Tver region.\par \par \uc2 Our colleagues are bringing the latest updates on this story over at our Russia-Ukraine live blog which can be found here:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/live/2023/aug/23/russia-ukraine-war-live-updates-drones-downed-moscow"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Russia-Ukraine war live: Wagner leader Yevgeny Prigozhin onboard plane involved in fatal crash, Russian Civil Aviation authority says}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 6.37pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.11pm BST\par \par \uc2 Rudy Giuliani\uc2  is expected to meet with his attorneys at a local law office in Atlanta before a meeting with the Fulton county district attorney\u8217\'20\'19s office to discuss terms of a bond agreement, CNN {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://edition.cnn.com/politics/live-news/trump-indictment-georgia-election-08-23-23/h_7e4891a26a9d84fe19633c7181eeca17"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  reported.}}}\par \par \uc2 Giuliani\u8217\'20\'19s attorneys were seen entering a local law office after touching down in Atlanta, the report said.\par \par \uc2 The former New York mayor and Trump attorney, who {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/aug/23/trump-giuliani-georgia-fulton-republican-debate-politics-live-updates?page=with:block-64e6230d8f08f3273b084c4d#block-64e6230d8f08f3273b084c4d"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 landed in Georgia}}}\uc2  earlier this morning, is expected to surrender to authorities once a bond agreement is reached.\par \par \uc2 Giuliani faces 13 charges in the Georgia election subversion case, including racketeering, three counts of soliciting lawmakers to violate their oaths of office, three counts of making false statements and six conspiracy counts dealing with the recruitment of fake electors.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 6.41pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.02pm BST\par \par \uc2 House could launch Biden impeachment inquiry next month, says Kevin McCarthy\par \par \uc2 House speaker Kevin McCarthy said lawmakers could formally launch an impeachment inquiry into \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  next month when they return from summer recess.\par \par \uc2 During an interview with Fox Business on Tuesday night, McCarthy said the Republican-led House will move forward with an impeachment inquiry if the Bidens do not \u8220\'20\'1Cprovide us the documents we\u8217\'20\'19re asking\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIf they provide us the documents, there wouldn\u8217\'20\'19t be a need for an impeachment inquiry,\u8221\'20\'1D McCarthy said.\par \par \uc2 But if they withhold the documents and fight like they have now to not provide to the American public what they deserve to know, we will move forward with impeachment inquiry when we come back into session.\par \par \uc2 In July, McCarthy floated an impeachment inquiry into Biden over unproven claims of financial misconduct and his latest comments are the clearest signal yet that an inquiry could come soon in the House.\par \par \uc2 Republicans in Congress have ramped up investigations of Biden and his son \uc2 Hunter Biden\uc2 , particularly the younger Biden\u8217\'20\'19s business dealings.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 6.41pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.49pm BST\par \par \uc2 North Dakota governor and GOP presidential candidate \uc2 Doug Burgum\uc2  plans to appear on the debate stage tonight {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/aug/23/trump-giuliani-georgia-fulton-republican-debate-politics-live-updates?page=with:block-64e61cdc8f08d8698b4d1f4f#block-64e61cdc8f08d8698b4d1f4f"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 despite injuring his leg}}}\uc2  during a basketball game, \uc2 CBS\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19 Robert Costa reports.\par \par \uc2 Burgum, 67, was taken to a Milwaukee emergency room on Tuesday night and it was unclear if he would be able to stand for the two-hour debate.\par \par \uc2 enltrBurgum campaign source tells me the governor is planning to go to the \u8220\'20\'1Cwalk thru\u8221\'20\'1D this afternoon at the debate site despite his injury and ER visit\u8230\'20\'26 and has made clear to \uc2 RNC\uc2  he plans to be on stage tonight\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Robert Costa (@costareports) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/costareports/status/1694372883584192962?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 August 23, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.42pm BST\par \par \uc2 A Super Pac backing Florida governor \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2  was briefly suspended from X, formerly known as \uc2 Twitter\uc2 , hours before the first Republican presidential primary debate, according to reports.\par \par \uc2 Visitors to the \u8220\'20\'1CNever Back Down\u8221\'20\'1D \uc2 Twitter\uc2  account on Wednesday morning were greeted with a message stating \u8220\'20\'1CAccount suspended. \uc2 Twitter\uc2  suspends accounts that violate the \uc2 Twitter\uc2  Rules\u8221\'20\'1D. The account was later restored.\par \par \uc2 enltrAccount for {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/RonDeSantis?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @RonDeSantis}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/NvrBackDown24?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @NvrBackDown24}}}\uc2  super PAC suspended from X on {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/hashtag/GOPDebate?src=hash&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 #GOPDebate}}}\uc2  day. The reasons why are unknown at this writing.\par \par \uc2 Reporting by {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/AGGancarski?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @AGGancarski}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/nw3ia2ypvq"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/nw3ia2ypvq}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/hashtag/FlaPol?src=hash&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 #FlaPol}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/ZVDpGvWhGT"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/ZVDpGvWhGT}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Florida Politics (@Fla_Pol) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/Fla_Pol/status/1694357590166122941?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 August 23, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.31pm BST\par \par \uc2 My colleague David Smith is in Milwaukee today to cover the preparations for tonight\u8217\'20\'19s Republican primary debate.\par \par \uc2 enltrAt Fiserv Forum in Milwaukee for first Republican presidential primary debate: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/BO8meGpKZU"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/BO8meGpKZU}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 David Smith (@SmithInAmerica) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/SmithInAmerica/status/1694383433382809855?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 August 23, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.22pm BST\par \par \uc2 Former Coffee county elections supervisor Misty Hampton reaches $10,000 bail agreement\par \par \uc2 Misty Hampton, the former elections supervisor for Coffee county, has reached a $10,000 bond agreement with prosecutors in Fulton count, according to court documents.\par \par \uc2 Hampton\u8217\'20\'19s bail conditions include not communicating with witnesses and co-defendants, reporting to pretrial services by phone every month and not obstructing justice by intimidating witnesses.\par \par \uc2 Hampton was present when a \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 -aligned group sought to illegally access voting machines in search of fraud and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.washingtonpost.com/investigations/2022/09/20/coffee-county-georgia-cathy-latham/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 directed much of the group\u8217\'20\'19s search}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s a copy of the bond agreement, shared by Lawfare\u8217\'20\'19s Anna Bower:\par \par \uc2 enltrMisty Hampton, former Coffee County elections supervisor who was involved in unauthorized copying of voting systems, has bond set at $10,000. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/XwLFfwykks"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/XwLFfwykks}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Anna Bower (@AnnaBower) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/AnnaBower/status/1694379313385066889?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 August 23, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 5.50pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.15pm BST\par \par \uc2 Larry Elder\uc2 , the rightwing radio host who is running for the 2024 GOP presidential nomination, has threatened to file a complaint against the \uc2 Republican National Committee\uc2  (\uc2 RNC\uc2 ) if it does not reverse its decision to exclude him from participating in tonight\u8217\'20\'19s debate.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 RNC\uc2  announced on Tuesday that {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/aug/23/trump-giuliani-georgia-fulton-republican-debate-politics-live-updates?page=with:block-64e61cdc8f08d8698b4d1f4f#block-64e61cdc8f08d8698b4d1f4f"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 eight candidates had qualified}}}\uc2  for the Milwaukee debate, but that three candidates had fallen short: Miami mayor Francis S Suarez, businessman Perry Johnson, and Elder. All three had claimed to have met the donor and polling threshold.\par \par \uc2 In order to qualify for the first debate stage, the \uc2 RNC\uc2  required candidates to draw at least 40,000 individual donors and register at least 1% support in three national polls or in two national and two early state polls. Candidates were also required to sign a pledge to back the eventual winner of the GOP primary.\par \par \uc2 Posting to X, formerly known as \uc2 Twitter\uc2 , Elder said he intends to file an \uc2 FEC\uc2  complaint for violation of debate rules and illegal campaign contributions if the \uc2 RNC\uc2  does not reverse their decision by 2pm Central time.\par \par \uc2 enltrIf the \uc2 RNC\uc2  does not reverse their decision by 2pm CT and acknowledge that I met all criteria for entry into the presidential debate, I intend to file an \uc2 FEC\uc2  complaint for violation of debate rules and illegal campaign contributions.\par \par \uc2 FEC\uc2  rules governing debates are clear that\u8230\'20\'26 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/aKbFPOjy1k"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/aKbFPOjy1k}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 \uc2 Larry Elder\uc2  (@larryelder) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/larryelder/status/1694354593612763385?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 August 23, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 6.43pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.05pm BST\par \par \uc2 Prosecutors described the interaction with {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/aug/23/trump-giuliani-georgia-fulton-republican-debate-politics-live-updates?page=with:block-64e628618f08f3273b084ca2#block-64e628618f08f3273b084ca2"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  the witness who retracted \u8220\'20\'1Cfalse prior testimony\u8221\'20\'1D }}}\uc2  in the criminal case against \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  over the hoarding of classified documents in a filing that seeks a hearing in Florida about potential conflicts of interest involving the defense lawyer, Stanley Woodward, who also represents Trump valet Walt Nauta.\par \par \uc2 The filing states:\par \par \uc2 The target letter to Trump Employee 4 crystallized a conflict of interest arising from Mr Woodward\u8217\'20\'19s concurrent representation of Trump Employee 4 and Nauta.\par \par \uc2 They added:\par \par \uc2 Advising Trump Employee 4 to correct his sworn testimony would result in testimony incriminating Mr Woodward\u8217\'20\'19s other client, Nauta; but permitting Trump Employee 4\u8217\'20\'19s false testimony to stand uncorrected would leave Trump Employee 4 exposed to criminal charges for perjury.\par \par \uc2 enltrSpecial Counsel prosecutors explain this is the conflict of interested for lawyer Stanley Woodward, adding that Taveras flipped after switching lawyers and taking the Federal Public Defender. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/3PpBjChUMJ"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/3PpBjChUMJ}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Hugo Lowell (@hugolowell) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/hugolowell/status/1694108443781538199?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 August 22, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.56pm BST\par \par \uc2 The Republican party faces an electability test on Wednesday when candidates including election deniers, climate deniers and anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  extremists take the debate stage in a city that rebukes them and a state they cannot afford to lose.\par \par \uc2 The first presidential primary debate will be held in Milwaukee, a racially diverse Democratic stronghold in Wisconsin, a battleground that could decide who wins the White House in 2024.\par \par \uc2 Even without \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , who is {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/aug/23/donald-trump-republican-debate-tucker-carlson"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 skipping the primetime televised event}}}\uc2 , the juxtaposition between Republicans who have embraced his far-right agenda and their sceptical host city offers a preview of the party\u8217\'20\'19s struggle to broaden its appeal.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThis is a debate of bad ideas,\u8221\'20\'1D said {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/nov/04/wisconsin-republicans-racist-attack-ads-democrat-mandela-barnes"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Mandela Barnes}}}\uc2 , born and raised in Milwaukee and a former lieutenant governor of Wisconsin.\par \par \uc2 It\u8217\'20\'19s going to be a bunch of Maga extremists showing up in this city because Wisconsin is a critical state every election year. But regardless of how they perform, the reality is they are choosing a losing strategy of extremism and showing how out of touch they are with the people of this country and specifically people here in the city of Milwaukee.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/aug/23/republican-debate-milwaukee-2024-election-trump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Read the full report by the Guardian\u8217\'20\'19s Washington DC bureau chief, David Smith, here.}}}\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/aug/23/republican-debate-milwaukee-2024-election-trump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \u8216\'20\'18In enemy territory\u8217\'20\'19: first Republican debate descends on Democratic city}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.46pm BST\par \par \uc2 Mar-a-Lago witness \u8216\'20\'18retracted false testimony\u8217\'20\'19 to implicate Trump\par \par \uc2 A witness in the criminal case against \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  over his alleged mishandling of classified documents retracted \u8220\'20\'1Cprior false testimony\u8221\'20\'1D after switching lawyers last month and implicated the former president in new information, according to the justice department.\par \par \uc2 The witness, a Trump employee identified elsewhere as Mar-a-Lago director of information technology, Yuscil Taveras, initially testified to a grand jury in Washington DC that he was unaware of any effort to erase surveillance video at the Florida property.\par \par \uc2 Prosecutors said in a court filing on Tuesday that the witness after getting the new attorney \u8220\'20\'1Cimmediately \u8230\'20\'26 retracted his prior false testimony\u8221\'20\'1D and provided the justice department with information that helped form the basis of the revised indictment against Trump, his valet Walt Nauta, and a third defendant, Carlos De Oliveira.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.32pm BST\par \par \uc2 Rudy Giuliani\uc2  is expected to have traveled to Georgia with the former New York police commissioner Bernie Kerik, who is an unindicted co-conspirator in the Georgia election subversion case.\par \par \uc2 Kerik has been assisting Giuliani to find a lawyer to represent him, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/PaulaReidCNN/status/1694152724554654161"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 CNN reported}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Kerik, who is not a lawyer, has agreed to assist Giuliani at no cost through the first phase of the Georgia prosecution \u8212\'20\'14 including bond negotiations with the Fulton County district attorney\u8217\'20\'19s office and then surrendering to local authorities, the sources said.\par \par \uc2 Giuliani faces proliferating legal difficulties and expenses arising from work including searching for dirt on \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s political enemies, which stoked Trump\u8217\'20\'19s first impeachment, and challenging election results in states lost to \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The former New York mayor was forced to put his Manhattan flat on the market earlier this month to cover his soaring legal bills.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.22pm BST\par \par \uc2 Rudy Giuliani\uc2  lands in Atlanta to surrender to authorities\par \par \uc2 A plane carrying \uc2 Rudy Giuliani\uc2  has landed at Atlanta\u8217\'20\'19s Dekalb-Peachtree airport.\par \par \uc2 The former New York mayor and lawyer for \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  is expected to surrender to face charges in the sprawling Georgia elections racketeering case later today.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 5.33pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.11pm BST\par \par \uc2 Sidney Powell\uc2 , a lawyer for \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  heavily involved in efforts to overturn the 2020 election result, has struck a $100,000 bail agreement with prosecutors in Fulton count, according to court documents.\par \par \uc2 Powell\u8217\'20\'19s bail conditions include not communicating with witnesses and co-defendants, reporting to pretrial services by phone every month and not obstructing justice by intimidating witnesses.\par \par \uc2 From Politico\u8217\'20\'19s Kyle Cheney:\par \par \uc2 enltrUPDATE: Here is \uc2 Sidney POWELL\uc2 's $100,000 bond order: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/sfGJxuRQ8e"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/sfGJxuRQ8e}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Kyle Cheney (@kyledcheney) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/kyledcheney/status/1694351434534580257?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 August 23, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 4.11pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.59pm BST\par \par \uc2 Doug Burgum\uc2 's GOP debate attendance in doubt after leg injury\par \par \uc2 North Dakota governor and Republican presidential hopeful \uc2 Doug Burgum\uc2  injured himself playing basketball on Tuesday, leaving in doubt his participation in the first Republican presidential debate tonight.\par \par \uc2 Burgum, 67, was taken to a Milwaukee emergency room after injuring his leg while playing a game of pick-up basketball with his staff, CNN {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://edition.cnn.com/2023/08/23/politics/doug-burgum-injured/index.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reported,}}}\uc2  citing a source. He was discharged from the hospital the same day.\par \par \uc2 It is \u8220\'20\'1Cunclear if he will be able to stand\u8221\'20\'1D at the two-hour debate, which is set to begin at 9pm Eastern time on Wednesday, NBC {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cnbc.com/2023/08/23/burgum-injured-playing-basketball-may-have-to-skip-republican-debate.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reported.}}}\par \par \uc2 Burgum is one of eight candidates to meet the Republican national committee\u8217\'20\'19s qualifications for the first debate. The other seven are: Florida\u8217\'20\'19s governor \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2 , the former vice-president \uc2 Mike Pence\uc2 , former New Jersey governor \uc2 Chris Christie\uc2 , former South Carolina governor Nikki Haley, former Arkansas governor \uc2 Asa Hutchinson\uc2 , business entrepreneur \uc2 Vivek Ramaswamy\uc2 , and South Carolina senator Tim Scott.\par \par \uc2 Republican presidential candidate North Dakota Governor \uc2 Doug Burgum\uc2 . Photograph: Charlie Neibergall/AP\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 4.01pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.48pm BST\par \par \uc2 Rudy Giuliani\uc2  has retained counsel John Esposito and local counsel Brian Tevis to represent him against charges in Georgia, NBC {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nbcnews.com/politics/donald-trump/live-blog/trump-indictment-arrest-live-updates-rcna100651"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  reported.}}}\par \par \uc2 New York-based Esposito works at the law firm Aidala, Bertuna and Kamins and is a former Manhattan assistant district attorney.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.45pm BST\par \par \uc2 Trump to surrender during Thursday primetime hours to his benefit\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  \u8211\'20\'13 seeking to distract from the indignity of the surrender by turning things into a circus \u8211\'20\'13 in essence had his lawyers {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/aug/22/donald-trump-surrender-fulton-county-jail-thursday-night"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 negotiate the booking to take place on Thursday evening}}}\uc2  during the prime viewing hours for the cable news networks.\par \par \uc2 Trump has posted on his Truth Social platform that he would be arrested on Thursday, but the primetime scheduling was finalized in recent days after his lawyers met with the Fulton county district attorney, \uc2 Fani Willis\uc2 , at her office on Monday.\par \par \uc2 Trump returned to his instinct to maximize television ratings to his benefit for his surrender to authorities in Atlanta, the people said, and could extend the coverage of the proceedings by speaking afterwards in front of cameras and reporters.\par \par \uc2 The strategy to turn surrenders in each of his four criminal cases into spectacles has been an effort to discredit the indictments, as well as to capitalize on the information void left by prosecutors after such events to foist his own spin on the charges.\par \par \uc2 While he would prefer not to be charged, once indicted, Trump has moved to present himself as defiant and lament to his supporters that he supposedly is the victim of partisan investigations, for which he needs their political and financial support.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 4.02pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.32pm BST\par \par \uc2 Rudy Giuliani\uc2  has dined out for years on his aggressive use of Rico, the Racketeer Influenced and Corrupt Organizations Act, which he wielded with dramatic effect against New York mobsters in the 1980s.\par \par \uc2 For his pains, he was granted an award by the Italian government. Later, as New York City mayor, he turned his use of the anti-racketeering law into a vote-getter, presenting himself as the hero of Rico.\par \par \uc2 As an in-joke, he handed the keys of the city to the cast of the Sopranos. Then he went on Saturday Night Live and bragged about \u8220\'20\'1Csticking it to organised crime\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 He may not be laughing so loudly now.\par \par \uc2 Giuliani, \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  and 17 other co-defendants have been slapped with organised crime charges in Georgia under the state\u8217\'20\'19s Rico law, for allegedly having been part of a vast conspiracy to overturn the 2020 presidential election. The hero of Rico had been hoist with his own petard.\par \par \uc2 The irony that \uc2 Fani Willis\uc2 , the district attorney of Fulton county who is leading the prosecution, chose to hit the hero of Rico with a Rico rap has not been lost on Giuliani watchers. Appointed as US attorney for the southern district of New York in 1983, he did not so much invent the anti-racketeering law, which was enacted in 1970, as become an early adopter in its use against organised crime.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/aug/16/rudy-giuliani-rico-racketeering-georgia-indictment"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Giuliani championed organised crime act Rico. Now he\u8217\'20\'19s charged under it}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.23pm BST\par \par \uc2 Rudy Giuliani\uc2  is expected to travel to Georgia with the former New York police commissioner Bernie Kerik, who is an unindicted co-conspirator in the case.\par \par \uc2 CNN {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://edition.cnn.com/2023/08/23/politics/giuliani-fulton-county/index.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reported}}}\uc2  on Wednesday morning that Kerik, identified as co-conspirator No5 in the case, has been assisting Giuliani to find a lawyer to represent him.\par \par \uc2 Tim Parlatore, a lawyer representing Kerik, told CNN that he was \u8220\'20\'1Cnot sure\u8221\'20\'1D if Giuliani had yet found himself a Georgia-based lawyer, while noting that it would be normal to be required to have one, as part of bond arrangements when turning oneself in to face charges.\par \par \uc2 In early 2020, Trump {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nbcnews.com/news/us-news/trump-pardons-bernard-kerik-why-former-n-y-police-commissioner-n1138236"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pardoned}}}\uc2  Kerik for crimes including tax fraud and lying to investigators, for which Kerik had been {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://abcnews.go.com/Blotter/kerik-sentenced-years-prison/story?id=9875911"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 sentenced}}}\uc2  to four years in jail.\par \par \uc2 Later that year, Kerik worked with Giuliani on attempts to overturn \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s victory, a push which culminated in the deadly January 6 insurrection at the US Capitol as supporters of Trump violently tried but failed to ensure that Congress would not certify Biden\u8217\'20\'19s win.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.17pm BST\par \par \uc2 Rudy Giulian i was seen leaving his New York apartment building early on Wednesday. \u8220\'20\'1CI am going to Fulton country to comply with the law,\u8221\'20\'1D he said. \u8220\'20\'1CIf I plead today, I plead not guilty.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 He added that he would be photographed for a mugshot.\par \par \uc2 Isn\u8217\'20\'19t that nice? A mugshot for the man who probably put the worst criminals of the 20th century in jail. They\u8217\'20\'19re going to degrade themselves by doing a mugshot of me.\par \par \uc2 Unlike {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/aug/23/trump-giuliani-georgia-fulton-republican-debate-politics-live-updates?page=with:block-64e60fa78f08319ad416c48c#block-64e60fa78f08319ad416c48c"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the other defendants}}}\uc2  charged in the Georgia election subversion case, Giuliani plans to negotiate bond and turn himself all in the same day, CNN {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://edition.cnn.com/2023/08/23/politics/giuliani-fulton-county/index.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reported,}}}\uc2  citing sources.\par \par \uc2 The former New York mayor and Trump lawyer wants to complete the process before Trump arrives on Thursday, the report said.\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  is {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/aug/22/donald-trump-surrender-fulton-county-jail-thursday-night"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 expected to surrender}}}\uc2  at the Fulton county jail on Thursday evening.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.10pm BST\par \par \uc2 In remarks ahead of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/aug/23/trump-giuliani-georgia-fulton-republican-debate-politics-live-updates?page=with:block-64e610ec8f08319ad416c491#block-64e610ec8f08319ad416c491"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 his travel to Georgia }}}\uc2  to surrender at the Fulton county jail, \uc2 Rudy Giuliani\uc2  said he was feeling \u8220\'20\'1Cvery good\u8221\'20\'1D because he was \u8220\'20\'1Cdefending the rights of all Americans\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Giuliani told reporters in New York:\par \par \uc2 I\u8217\'20\'19m the same \uc2 Rudy Giuliani\uc2  that took down the mafia, that made New York City the safest city in America, that reduced crime more than any mayor in the history of any city anywhere.\par \par \uc2 I\u8217\'20\'19m fighting for justice \u8211\'20\'13 I have been from the first moment I represented \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , who has now been proven innocent several times.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.03pm BST\par \par \uc2 Rudy Giuliani\uc2  'feeling very good' as he heads to Georgia to surrender to authorities\par \par \uc2 Rudy Giuliani\uc2 , who served as \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s personal lawyer, said he was traveling to Georgia to surrender to face charges in the sprawling elections racketeering case.\par \par \uc2 Giulani is expected to travel to Georgia with former New York police commissioner Bernie Kerik, who is an unindicted co-conspirator in the case. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/PaulaReidCNN/status/1694152724554654161"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 CNN reported}}}\uc2  on Wednesday morning that Kerik, identified as co-conspirator No5 in the case, has been assisting Giuliani to find a lawyer to represent him.\par \par \uc2 Speaking in New York, Giuliani said:\par \par \uc2 I\u8217\'20\'19m going to Georgia and I\u8217\'20\'19m feeling very, very good about it because I feel like I\u8217\'20\'19m defending the rights of all Americans.\par \par \uc2 enltr\u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19m going to Georgia and I\u8217\'20\'19m feeling very, very good about it because I feel like I\u8217\'20\'19m defending the rights of all Americans.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Former Trump lawyer \uc2 Rudy Giuliani\uc2 , before he heads to Fulton County to surrender to authorities in the Georgia election interference indictment {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/AozTl4lHxF"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/AozTl4lHxF}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 The Recount (@therecount) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/therecount/status/1694342096415813975?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 August 23, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.09pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.58pm BST\par \par \uc2 Who are the 18 other defendants charged in the Trump Georgia election case?\par \par \uc2 The Fulton county district attorney, \uc2 Fani Willis\uc2 , delivered a sweeping indictment earlier this month that charges \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , along with more than a dozen co-defendants, with 41 counts including racketeering, conspiracy, solicitation and filing false statements.\par \par \uc2 These are the other defendants charged in the indictment, which alleges a coordinated group effort to pressure Georgia officials into changing the outcome of the 2020 election.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://interactive.guim.co.uk/uploader/embed/2023/08/archive-zip/giv-13425DS3V01nPJs6K/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Interactive}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.47pm BST\par \par \uc2 One individual stands out among the 18 \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  acolytes who were indicted in Georgia this week over their participation in the former president\u8217\'20\'19s alleged racketeering enterprise to overturn the 2020 election.\par \par \uc2 He is distinct not for his chutzpah and braggadocio \u8211\'20\'13 those qualities are trademarked by Trump. Instead he stands out for the opposite characteristics: his demure, scholarly demeanor that has left those who have known him utterly baffled by his eruption from a left-leaning attorney working in relative obscurity into a key figure in the glaring lights of a historic criminal prosecution.\par \par \uc2 Kenneth Chesebro is not your regular Trump guy. Yet Chesebro features heavily in Jack Smith\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.justice.gov/storage/US_v_Trump_23_cr_257.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 federal indictment}}}\uc2  of Trump and is centrally cast Fulton county district attorney \uc2 Fani Willis\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.washingtonpost.com/documents/1ccdf52e-1ba2-434c-93f8-2a7020293967.pdf?itid=lk_inline_manual_5"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 sprawling indictment}}}\uc2  in Georgia.\par \par \uc2 My colleague Ed Pilkington asks {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/aug/19/kenneth-chesebro-trump-georgia-indictment-fake-electors"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 how did this mild lawyer with a liberal past become the architect of Trump\u8217\'20\'19s election subversion scandal?}}}\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/aug/19/kenneth-chesebro-trump-georgia-indictment-fake-electors"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \u8216\'20\'18It baffles me\u8217\'20\'19: what drew a mild lawyer with a liberal past into Trump\u8217\'20\'19s election plot?}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.40pm BST\par \par \uc2 Trump attorneys Ray Smith and Kenneth Chesebro surrender in Georgia case\par \par \uc2 Kenneth Chesebro, the attorney who allegedly helped devise the fake elector scheme to subvert the 2020 presidential election, and Ray Smith, a Georgia lawyer who worked for Trump following the election, surrendered to Fulton county authorities today, according to jail records.\par \par \uc2 Chesebro has been {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/aug/15/georgia-investigation-trump-fulton-county-who-to-know"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 revealed to be}}}\uc2  one of the main architects of the fake electors scheme, which he described as a \u8220\'20\'1Cbold, controversial plan\u8221\'20\'1D. \uc2 The New York Times{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/2023/08/08/us/politics/trump-indictment-fake-electors-memo.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  obtained }}}\uc2  a copy of a memo from Chesebro to a Wisconsin attorney laying out a three-pronged plan to overturn election results in six states, including Georgia, and keep \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  in power.\par \par \uc2 Smith is accused of advising the alternate GOP electors who met at the state capital and cast votes for Trump and signed documents that falsely claimed Trump had won the election. Following the November 2020 election, Smith sent a letter to Georgia\u8217\'20\'19s Republican secretary of state, \uc2 Brad Raffensperger\uc2 , and submitted several affidavits.\par \par \uc2 Six of the 18 co-defendants charged alongside Trump in the Georgia election subversion case have now surrendered.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.42pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.31pm BST\par \par \uc2 'Fake electors' David Shafer and Cathy Latham surrender to Georgia authorities\par \par \uc2 Cathy Latham, the former chair of the Coffee county Republican party who is accused of being a fake elector, and former GOP chairman David Shafer, who is also accused of being a fake elector, surrendered and were booked at Fulton county jail early this morning.\par \par \uc2 Latham and Shafer, both of whom signed documents purporting to be valid 2020 presidential electors in Georgia, were released on bond, according to jail records. Shafter proceeded to share his mug shot on X, formerly known as \uc2 Twitter\uc2 :\par \par \uc2 enltrGood morning! {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/hashtag/NewProfilePicture?src=hash&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 #NewProfilePicture}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/EADF0zYSSH"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/EADF0zYSSH}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 David Shafer (@DavidShafer) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/DavidShafer/status/1694303972427763731?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 August 23, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.21pm BST\par \par \uc2 In December 2020, Trump attorney John Eastman reportedly helped orchestrate the plan for Georgia Republican electors to meet and sign a fraudulent certificate that said Trump won the election in what is now known as the fake electors scheme.\par \par \uc2 Eastman also drafted a six-point memo that directed the former vice-president \uc2 Mike Pence\uc2  to refuse to certify electoral votes on 6 January 2021.\par \par \uc2 Eastman, alongside \uc2 Rudy Giuliani\uc2 , spoke at a rally near the US Capitol on the day of the insurrection where he spread baseless claims of election fraud. Kenneth Chesebro, another Trump attorney who worked closely with Eastman, Trump and Giuliani to halt the electoral certification and is a named defendant, was also at the Capitol that day.\par \par \uc2 After Trump\u8217\'20\'19s 2020 loss, bail bondsman Scott Hall allegedly sought illegal access to voting machines in Coffee county, Georgia, to search for evidence they were rigged.\par \par \uc2 According to the indictment, he allegedly traveled to the Coffee county elections office to copy voter data from \uc2 Dominion Voting Systems\uc2  machines, which was a breach of privacy and unlawful.\par \par \uc2 Hall was charged alongside the Coffee county officials Misty Hampton and Cathy Latham, as well as Trump-aligned attorney \uc2 Sidney Powell\uc2 , for \u8220\'20\'1Cwillfully and unlawfully tampering with electronic ballot markers and tabulating machines\u8221\'20\'1D, which was an act of conspiracy to commit election fraud.\par \par \uc2 Hall also placed several phone calls to the individuals who were involved with intimidating Georgia poll workers to allegedly coerce false testimony about election security, according to the indictment.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.16pm BST\par \par \uc2 First mug shots released in Trump Georgia election case\par \par \uc2 Fulton county officials released the first two booking photos of defendants in the Georgia election subversion case against \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  and allies.\par \par \uc2 John Eastman, who is alleged to have orchestrated the so-called fake elector plot that aimed to keep Trump in power after he lost the 2020 election, surrendered to authorities in Georgia on Tuesday.\par \par \uc2 Scott Hall, a bail bondsman who is accused of a voting system breach in Georgia\u8217\'20\'19s Coffee county, was also booked in on Tuesday.\par \par \uc2 enltrFulton County Sheriff's Office has released mug shots for John Eastman and Scott Hall. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/EWrOWpJTf4"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/EWrOWpJTf4}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 The Recount (@therecount) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/therecount/status/1694329950885564767?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 August 23, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.12pm BST\par \par \uc2 The first two defendants in the Georgia election subversion case against \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  and 18 other defendants were booked in at the Fulton county jail on Tuesday.\par \par \uc2 Scott Hall, an Atlanta-area bail bondsman, was booked at the Rice Street jail on Tuesday. John Eastman, a Trump attorney and allegedly one of the main architects of Trump\u8217\'20\'19s plan to halt the certification of Biden\u8217\'20\'19s victory, also voluntarily turned himself in later on Tuesday morning.\par \par \uc2 enltrJohn Eastman, after turning himself in over his Georgia election interference case indictment, vows to contest \u8220\'20\'1Cevery count of the indictment\u8221\'20\'1D:\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI am confident that when the law is faithfully applied in this proceeding, all of my co-defendants and I will be fully vindicated.\u8221\'20\'1D {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/Dlsvrn4YHj"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/Dlsvrn4YHj}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 The Recount (@therecount) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/therecount/status/1694056034879320361?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 August 22, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 Hall was charged with seven felony counts, including six criminal conspiracy charges and with violating the Rico Act. His bond is set at $10,000, according to a \u8220\'20\'1Cconsent bond order\u8221\'20\'1D posted to the Fulton county court\u8217\'20\'19s website on Monday.\par \par \uc2 Eastman was charged with nine felony counts, including criminal conspiracy, solicitation, filing false documents and violating the Rico Act. Eastman\u8217\'20\'19s bond is set at $100,000.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.01pm BST\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  to turn himself in to Georgia authorities on Thursday night\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  is expected to surrender at the Fulton county jail on Thursday evening on racketeering and conspiracy charges over his efforts to overturn the results of the 2020 presidential election in the state of Georgia, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/aug/22/donald-trump-surrender-fulton-county-jail-thursday-night"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 according to two people briefed on the matter.}}}\par \par \uc2 Trump has posted on his Truth Social platform that he would be arrested on Thursday, but the prime-time scheduling was finalized in recent days after his lawyers met with the Fulton county district attorney, \uc2 Fani Willis\uc2 , at her office on Monday.\par \par \uc2 The surrender itself is expected to be mundane. At the Rice Street jail north-west of downtown Atlanta, where defendants charged in Fulton county are typically taken, the booking process involves a mug shot, fingerprinting and having height and weight recorded.\par \par \uc2 Trump asked his lawyers and the US secret service to get him an exemption from being photographed, the people said, though it was not clear whether he will get special treatment. The Fulton county sheriff, Patrick Labat, has previously said Trump would be treated no differently.\par \par \uc2 The other 18 co-defendants in the 2020 election subversion case appear to be receiving regular treatment based on online jail records for the former Trump election lawyer John Eastman and others, who had their height, weight and personal appearance made public.\par \par \uc2 Once the booking is complete, Trump is expected to be released immediately on conditions that include stringent witness intimidation restrictions that have not been put in place for his co-defendants, court filings show, until he is due back in state court for arraignment.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.57pm BST\par \par \uc2 Former Trump attorney \uc2 Rudy Giuliani\uc2 , who is {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/aug/23/trump-giuliani-georgia-fulton-republican-debate-politics-live-updates?page=with:block-64e5f6a88f08d8698b4d1d61#block-64e5f6a88f08d8698b4d1d61"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 expected to surrender}}}\uc2  to Fulton county jail later today, will have a lawyer with a Georgia license to represent him during the bond negotiations, CNN {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://edition.cnn.com/2023/08/23/politics/giuliani-fulton-county/index.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reported,}}}\uc2  citing a source.\par \par \uc2 Giuliani is believed to be traveling to Georgia with the former New York police commissioner, Bernie Kerik, who has been working with the former mayor to help him find a Georgia lawyer to represent him in this case, according to the report.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 1.57pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.48pm BST\par \par \uc2 Rudy Giuliani\uc2  expected to surrender at Fulton county jail\par \par \uc2 Good morning, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/us-politics"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 US politics}}}\uc2  blog readers. The New York mayor turned Trump attorney \uc2 Rudy Giuliani\uc2  is expected to surrender at the Fulton county jail on Wednesday on charges he acted as \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s chief co-conspirator in a plot to subvert the 2020 presidential election, according to reports.\par \par \uc2 Sources {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://edition.cnn.com/2023/08/23/politics/giuliani-fulton-county/index.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 told}}}\uc2  CNN that Giuliani wants to get it all done before Trump comes to Georgia. The former president is expected to turn himself in on Thursday evening, the \uc2 Guardian{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/aug/22/donald-trump-surrender-fulton-county-jail-thursday-night"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reported on Tuesday. }}}\uc2  Giuliani is expected to travel to the state with former New York police commissioner Bernie Kerik who has been working to help the former mayor find a Georgia lawyer to represent him in this case.\par \par \uc2 Fulton county district attorney \uc2 Fani Willis\uc2  has set a deadline of noon on Friday for Trump and his 18 co-defendants to turn themselves in on charges that they acted together as a \u8220\'20\'1Ccriminal organisation\u8221\'20\'1D as part of a vast conspiracy to overturn the 2020 presidential election.\par \par \uc2 Several have already voluntarily turned themselves in \u8211\'20\'13 on Tuesday, Scott Hall, an Atlanta-area bail bondsman, and John Eastman, a Trump attorney and allegedly one of the main architects of Trump\u8217\'20\'19s plan to halt the certification of Biden\u8217\'20\'19s victory, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/aug/22/scott-hall-georgia-election-2020-defendant-trump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 were booked in at the Rice Street jail.}}}\uc2  Trump \u8220\'20\'1Celectors\u8221\'20\'1D David Shafer and Cathy Latham also surrendered early Wednesday, according to court records.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s what else we\u8217\'20\'19re watching today:\par \par \uc2 Eight Republican presidential hopefuls will gather in Milwaukee, Wisconsin, tonight to take part in the first 2024 Republican primary debate.\par \par \uc2 The eight candidates scheduled to appear are: Florida\u8217\'20\'19s governor \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2 , the former vice-president \uc2 Mike Pence\uc2 , former New Jersey governor \uc2 Chris Christie\uc2 , North Dakota\u8217\'20\'19s governor \uc2 Doug Burgum\uc2 , former South Carolina governor Nikki Haley, former Arkansas governor \uc2 Asa Hutchinson\uc2 , business entrepreneur \uc2 Vivek Ramaswamy\uc2 , and South Carolina senator Tim Scott.\par \par \uc2 The debate begins at 9pm Eastern time. We will be following it live on this blog.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020230823ej8n001jv\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
