\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 South Carolina\u8217\'20\'19s all-male highest court upholds six-week  \highlight22\uc2 abortion \highlight\uc2  ban\b0\par\par\uc2 Ava Sasani and agencies \par \uc2 929 \uc2 words\par \uc2 23 August 2023\par 18:35 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Panel overrode earlier decision in which top court decided a similar restriction was unconstitutional\par \par \uc2 South Carolina\u8217\'20\'19s new all-male highest court on Wednesday reversed course on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights, upholding the state\u8217\'20\'19s strict six-week ban on the procedure.\par \par \uc2 The panel overrode an earlier decision in which the court decided a similar restriction was unconstitutional.\par \par \uc2 The court on Wednesday found that the state constitution\u8217\'20\'19s protection against \u8220\'20\'1Cunreasonable invasions of privacy\u8221\'20\'1D did not include a right to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , and that the state law was \u8220\'20\'1Cwithin the zone of reasonable policy decisions rationally related to the state\u8217\'20\'19s interest in protecting the unborn\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 A judge in May had put a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/may/26/south-carolina-abortion-ban-state-supreme-court-review"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 temporary halt}}}\uc2  to South Carolina\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/may/23/south-carolina-abortion-ban-six-weeks"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 new law banning}}}\uc2  most abortions around six weeks of pregnancy until the state supreme court could review the measure.\par \par \uc2 The ruling at the time, by Judge Clifton Newman, came just about 24 hours after the state governor, \uc2 Henry McMaster\uc2 , signed the bill, and meant {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/south-carolina"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 South Carolina}}}\uc2  reverted back to a ban at about 20 weeks after fertilization.\par \par \uc2 The new ruling is a blow to reproductive rights campaigners. On Wednesday, McMaster hailed the decision, issuing a statement saying: \u8220\'20\'1CThe supreme court\u8217\'20\'19s ruling marks a historic moment in our state\u8217\'20\'19s history and is the culmination of years of hard work and determination by so many in our state to ensure that the sanctity of life is protected.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 It went on: \u8220\'20\'1CWith this victory, we protect the lives of countless unborn children and reaffirm South Carolina\u8217\'20\'19s place as one of the most pro-life states in America.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The decision was 4-1, with the chief justice, Donald Beatty, in the minority.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThis decision is devastating not only because of the impact it will have on South Carolinians, but also because South Carolina is a critical state for access across the entire south-east region,\u8221\'20\'1D said \uc2 Caroline Sacerdote\uc2 , a staff attorney at the Center for Reproductive Rights who helped bring the lawsuit against the new six-week ban.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThis morning, our clients had patients coming in from Texas, Louisiana, Mississippi, patients who had traveled overnight to access critical, essential healthcare.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Because of Wednesday\u8217\'20\'19s ruling, Sacerdote said providers had to turn away those patients to adhere to the six-week ban.\par \par \uc2 Greenville Women\u8217\'20\'19s Clinic, one of just three \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  providers in South Carolina, had a full waiting room of patients seeking the procedure on Wednesday morning, according to Sacerdote.\par \par \uc2 It is unclear how \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights supporters will battle the latest six-week ban in South Carolina.\par \par \uc2 During last year\u8217\'20\'19s special legislative session on the original six-week ban, South Carolina Republican lawmakers continually refused to create a ballot measure that would ask voters if they support the right to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 . Unlike states such as Ohio and Michigan, South Carolina does not give citizens the power to create their own ballot measures. Only the legislature can create a ballot measure on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Vicki Ringer, the director of public affairs for Planned Parenthood South Atlantic, said South Carolina lawmakers were afraid to pose the question of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access directly to voters.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThey have seen, just like we all have, all of these states that have put \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  on the ballot, the people have come out in droves to support safe, legal \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 ,\u8221\'20\'1D Ringer said in a press conference on Wednesday.\par \par \uc2 The South Carolina legislature also has the power to select the justices on the state\u8217\'20\'19s high court.\par \par \uc2 Catherine Humphreville, an attorney with \uc2 Planned Parenthood\uc2 , said the South Carolina supreme court upheld the six-week ban despite striking down \u8220\'20\'1Ca nearly identical law\u8221\'20\'1D in January.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe only thing that changed since January is the makeup of the court,\u8221\'20\'1D Humphreville said.\par \par \uc2 The reversal in today\u8217\'20\'19s ruling signals a new court that will \u8220\'20\'1Cdo the bidding of anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  politicians\u8221\'20\'1D, according to Humphreville.\par \par \uc2 When the state legislature passed the hotly contested bill in May, the vote went mostly along party lines, with the notable exception of the state senate\u8217\'20\'19s five female members \u8211\'20\'13 three Republicans, a Democrat and an independent \u8211\'20\'13 who all opposed it.\par \par \uc2 The new law came after the state supreme court in January struck down a previous \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  law, by a 3-2 vote.\par \par \uc2 However, the author of that ruling, Justice Kaye Hearn, has since retired. South Carolina\u8217\'20\'19s Republican legislature in February replaced Hearn, who was the sole woman on the five-member court, with Justice Garrison Hill, who voted to uphold the new law on Wednesday.\par \par \uc2 Justice John Few also switched his vote, finding that the new law addressed gaps in the old one by explaining the legislature\u8217\'20\'19s rationale more fully and by requiring health insurance plans to cover contraception.\par \par \uc2 Beatty, in dissent, said the new law was essentially the same as the previous one that the court had struck down and that the court should have followed its earlier finding.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CToday\u8217\'20\'19s result will surely weigh heavily upon the public and our state\u8217\'20\'19s medical professionals, in light of the threat of criminal penalties placed upon practitioners and the serious harm that could occur to women who could be denied reproductive healthcare during this uncertainty,\u8221\'20\'1D he wrote.\par \par \uc2 The win for anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  lobby and ultra-conservative legislators in the state general assembly came just over a year after the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2022/jun/24/roe-v-wade-overturned-abortion-summary-supreme-court"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 US supreme court overturned}}}\uc2  the federal right to seek an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the US when it struck down {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/roe-v-wade"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Roe v Wade}}}\uc2 , giving power to the individual states to legislate on the matter.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020230823ej8n001rz\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
