\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 US appeals court upholds restrictions on  \highlight22\uc2 abortion \highlight\uc2  pill access\b0\par\par\uc2 Gloria Oladipo \par \uc2 518 \uc2 words\par \uc2 16 August 2023\par 20:22 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Ruling prevents mifepristone being prescribed by non-doctors or shipped by mail but does not order drug off market\par \par \uc2 A US appeals court ruled on Wednesday to limit access to the \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  pill mifepristone, returning to regulations that were in place in several years ago, but will not be taking the medication off the market.\par \par \uc2 The US court of appeals for the fifth circuit decided that the \uc2 Food and Drug Administration\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s (\uc2 FDA\uc2 ) previous regulations for mifepristone were unlawful, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.reuters.com/world/us/us-appeals-court-rules-restrict-abortion-pill-use-2023-08-16/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Reuters reported}}}\uc2 . The \uc2 FDA\uc2  had ruled that the \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  pill could be taken at a later stage in pregnancy (70 days into pregnancy versus 49 days), shipped via mail, and could be prescribed from medical professionals who are not doctors.\par \par \uc2 This latest ruling does not order the pill to be taken off the market, compared to a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cbsnews.com/news/federal-judge-halts-fda-approval-of-abortion-pill-mifepristone/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 preliminary ruling }}}\uc2  that suspended the drug\u8217\'20\'19s \uc2 FDA\uc2  approval. But the decision does eliminate the ability to obtain the \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  pill online or through other methods of sale that were approved post 2016.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThis means that, until final judgment, Mifeprex will remain available to the public under the conditions for use that existed in 2016,\u8221\'20\'1D {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/JoeDudekJD/status/1691880371158237344"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the court said}}}\uc2 , referring to the \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  medication\u8217\'20\'19s brand name.\par \par \uc2 Mifepristone, along with the pill misoprostol, is medication used for abortions procedures. The pill is used in more than half of US abortions and is approved for use in the first 10 weeks of pregnancy, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.washingtonpost.com/politics/2023/08/16/abortion-pill-mifepristone-court-ruling-appeal/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the Washington Post reported}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The ruling will not have an immediate impact on mifepristone, with the medication remaining available under current regulations.\par \par \uc2 The challenge against the \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  pill {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/may/17/abortion-pill-ruling-mifepristone-fifth-circuit-supreme-court-explained#:~:text=In%20late%20April%2C%20the%20supreme,groups%20targeting%20the%20pill%20continues.&text=The%20lawsuit%20is%20the%20most,Wade%20was%20overturned%20in%202022."}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 began in November }}}\uc2  when a case was brought against the \uc2 FDA\uc2  by Alliance for Hippocratic Medicine, a group of anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  medical practitioners.\par \par \uc2 In a lawsuit filed in Amarillo, Texas, the Alliance for Hippocratic Medicine, a Catholic faith organization, argued that the \uc2 FDA\uc2  had ignored safety concerns regarding minors when it approved mifepristone and overstepped its regulatory authority. The \uc2 FDA\uc2  sharply defended its approval of the medication, noting rigorous safety reviews of the pill.\par \par \uc2 In April, a Texas federal judge ruled with the Alliance for Hippocratic Medicine and issued an injunction for the \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  medication, revoking decades-old \uc2 FDA\uc2  approval of mifepristone.\par \par \uc2 The availability of mifepristone was protected via an emergency order from the supreme court in April that maintains the pill\u8217\'20\'19s availability during the appeals process.\par \par \uc2 The most recent decision will likely be appealed to the supreme court for review. The continued legal battle over mifepristone is one of the most significant \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights cases since {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/commentisfree/2023/jun/23/roe-v-wade-overturned-abortion"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the overturn of Roe v Wade }}}\uc2  last June.\par \par \uc2 Since the overturning of Roe v Wade, an increasing number of states have attempted to restrict access to mifepristone.\par \par \uc2 Republican lawmakers have also attempted to curtail access to the medication on the federal level. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/jul/25/republicans-abortion-pill-mail-law"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 In July}}}\uc2 , a Republican-supported spending bill included several provisions that would stop access to the pill via the mail nationwide and would curtail \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights.\par \par \uc2 At least 20 states {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/interactive/2022/us/abortion-laws-roe-v-wade.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 have also issued}}}\uc2  total or near-total bans on abortions.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020230816ej8g002h1\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
