\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Prosecutors charge \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  and 18 others with election interference crimes \u8211\'20\'13 as it happened\b0\par\par\uc2 Helen Sullivan (now) with Maanvi Singh and L\u233\'00\'E9onie Chao-Fong (earlier) \par \uc2 14,118 \uc2 words\par \uc2 15 August 2023\par 13:12 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 This blog is now closed. You can read all the latest developments in our latest blog:Trump indictment \u8211\'20\'13 live updatesRead the full story here\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.22am BST\par \par \uc2 We\u8217\'20\'19re closing this blog now, thanks for following along. Here is our full report on the indictment:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/aug/14/donald-trump-georgia-indictment-2020-election"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Donald Trump and allies indicted in Georgia over bid to reverse 2020 election loss}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.18am BST\par \par \uc2 The Fulton county indictment represents a crucial turning point in a drama that has been unfolding since Biden was declared the winner of Georgia in November 2020. Two statewide recounts in Georgia confirmed Biden defeated Trump by roughly 12,000 votes, making him the first Democratic presidential nominee to win the state since 1992. The victory was heralded as a landmark achievement for Democrats, particularly the Black voters who make up much of the party\u8217\'20\'19s base in Georgia.\par \par \uc2 Kendra Davenport Cotton, chief executive officer at the New Georgia Project Action Fund, emphasized that the validity of Biden\u8217\'20\'19s win in Georgia had been determined beyond question long before Trump\u8217\'20\'19s indictment. But the charges against Trump reassert the electoral power of the multiracial coalition that carried Biden to victory.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe believe facts. Biden won the 2020 race because Georgia voters showed up and showed out in record breaking numbers,\u8221\'20\'1D Cotton said. \u8220\'20\'1CThe folks that I work with here at NGP Action Fund have always known the power of Georgia voters and have always known what Georgia voters are capable of \u8211\'20\'13 especially Black, brown and young voters.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/aug/14/donald-trump-georgia-indictment-analysis-fani-willis-2020-election"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Trump\u8217\'20\'19s Georgia charges are a win for voting rights leaders}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.12am BST\par \par \uc2 After nearly three years, two statewide recounts and a violent attack on the US Capitol, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/donaldtrump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Donald Trump}}}\uc2  is finally facing criminal charges over his relentless campaign to overturn \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s 2020 victory in the battleground state of Georgia.\par \par \uc2 On Monday, the former president and his allies were indicted on a total of 41 counts in Fulton county, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/state-of-georgia"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Georgia}}}\uc2 , where the district attorney, \uc2 Fani Willis\uc2 , has been investigating the former president and his associates since 2021. The 13 charges against Trump himself include racketeering, forgery and perjury. News of the Georgia indictment came less than two weeks after Trump pleaded not guilty to a separate set of federal charges stemming from special counsel Jack Smith\u8217\'20\'19s investigation into the January 6 attack and 2020 election subversion efforts.\par \par \uc2 For the voting rights leaders who worked tirelessly to deliver Democratic wins in Georgia, Trump\u8217\'20\'19s indictment in Fulton county marked a clear rebuke of his extensive efforts to disenfranchise the state\u8217\'20\'19s voters, reaffirming the sanctity and the power of the ballot.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThis indictment is a win for voting rights and democracy because it strengthens our ability to defend it from its most imminent threat: \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 ,\u8221\'20\'1D said Xakota Espinoza, a spokesperson for the Georgia-based voting rights group Fair Fight. \u8220\'20\'1CIt is critical that we send a message that our democracy is sacrosanct, whether it is at the ballot box or courthouse.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/aug/14/donald-trump-georgia-indictment-analysis-fani-willis-2020-election"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Trump\u8217\'20\'19s Georgia charges are a win for voting rights leaders}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.05am BST\par \par \uc2 Summary\par \par \uc2 Phew. What a day. Here is what happened:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 A grand jury in Georgia has issued an indictment accusing \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  of efforts to overturn his 2020 election loss to Democrat \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Prosecutors brought 41 counts against Trump and his associates, including forgery and racketeering, which is used to target members of organized crime groups.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The defendants were indicted on charges of violating Georgia\u8217\'20\'19s Racketeer Influenced and Corrupt Organizations (Rico) Act. The act essentially allows prosecutors to link together different crimes committed by different people and bring criminal charges against a larger criminal enterprise. The law requires prosecutors to show the existence of a criminal enterprise that has committed at least two underlying crimes.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Prosecutors charged 18 people in addition to Trump, including \uc2 Mark Meadows\uc2 , Trump\u8217\'20\'19s former White House chief of staff, and lawyers \uc2 Rudy Giuliani\uc2  and John Eastman.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Fulton county district attorney \uc2 Fani Willis\uc2  said that all 19 defendants would be tried at the same time and that she would be asking for a trial within the next six months.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Willis said she was \u8220\'20\'1Cgiving the defendants the opportunity to voluntarily surrender no later than Friday the 25th day of August at noon.\u8221\'20\'1D This is the normal procedure. Trump will (most likely) arrive, be processed, and will plead not guilty.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Asked about accusations that the charges are politically motivated, Willis said, \u8220\'20\'1CI make decisions in this office based on facts and the law\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 This is the fourth time that Trump has been indicted. But this case is different because Trump cannot interfere in the case, even if he is elected president in 2024, and cannot issue a pardon.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The Trump campaign has responded to the indictment, saying, \u8220\'20\'1CPresident Trump will continue to power through this unprecedented abuse of power\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 A news conference featuring district attorney Fani T Willis is expected to take place after the indictment is released.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The court {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/aug/14/trump-2020-election-georgia-charges-update"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 briefly posted a document on its website earlier on Monday}}}\uc2  listing several felony charges against Trump, but quickly removed it without explanation. Willis\u8217\'20\'19s office said at the time no charges had been filed and declined further comment.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Over the course of a two-year investigation, Willis has examined Trump\u8217\'20\'19s alleged efforts to pressure state leaders to reverse his 11,000-vote loss to Democrat \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  in the state and organise a slate of illegitimate electors to undermine the process of formalising Biden\u8217\'20\'19s victory. She has also looked into an alleged attempt by Trump\u8217\'20\'19s allies to manipulate voting equipment in rural Coffee county.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Trump has denied any wrongdoing and accuses Fulton county district attorney \uc2 Fani Willis\uc2 , an elected Democrat, of being politically motivated.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Trump, 77, has been criminally indicted three times so far this year, including once by US special counsel Jack Smith on charges of trying to overturn his election defeat. He has long dismissed the many investigations, including two impeachments, he has faced in his years in politics as a politically motivated \u8220\'20\'1Cwitch-hunt\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 5.08am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.57am BST\par \par \uc2 What did \uc2 Fani Willis\uc2  say?\par \par \uc2 Fulton county district attorney \uc2 Fani Willis\uc2  has just finished addressing the media, after a grand jury\u8217\'20\'19s decision to indict former US president \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  and 18 others on election interference charges.\par \par \uc2 Here were the main points:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The 19 defendants will be tried together.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The Fulton county DA\u8217\'20\'19s office will be proposing a trial date within the next six months.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Asked about accusations that the charges are politically motivated, Willis said, \u8220\'20\'1CI make decisions in this office based on facts and the law\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Willis said she was \u8220\'20\'1Cgiving the defendants the opportunity to voluntarily surrender no later than Friday the 25th day of August at noon.\u8221\'20\'1D This is the normal procedure. Trump will (most likely) arrive, be processed, and will plead not guilty.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe state\u8217\'20\'19s role in this process is essential to the functioning of our democracy,\u8221\'20\'1D Willis said.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The indictment includes 41 felony counts.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 4.59am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.50am BST\par \par \uc2 Defendants will be tried together\par \par \uc2 A moment earlier Willis was asked whether those named in the indictment would be tried together.\par \par \uc2 Asked whether she would try the defendants together, she responded with a question.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CDo I intend to try the 19 defendants named in this case?\u8221\'20\'1D she asked, emphasising the number \u8220\'20\'1Cnineteen\u8221\'20\'1D, before answering: \u8220\'20\'1CYes,\u8221\'20\'1D she said bluntly.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 4.57am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.47am BST\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI make decisions in this office based on facts and the law,\u8221\'20\'1D she says, when asked about accusations that the charges are politically motivated.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.46am BST\par \par \uc2 Willis proposing trial date within next six months\par \par \uc2 Willis is being asked about trial dates. She is asked whether she would like to try Trump first \u8211\'20\'13 though this is the fourth indictment.\par \par \uc2 She does not care about being first, she says, but she will be proposing a trial date within the next six months.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.45am BST\par \par \uc2 Willis will now take questions, \u8220\'20\'1Cprior to going to sleep\u8221\'20\'1D, she says.\par \par \uc2 Rico charges involve time you have to serve, she says in response to a question: \u8220\'20\'1CIt is not a probated sentence\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 4.53am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.43am BST\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI am giving the defendants the opportunity to voluntarily surrender no later than Friday the 25th day of August at noon,\u8221\'20\'1D says Willis.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 4.53am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.42am BST\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe state\u8217\'20\'19s role in this process is essential to the functioning of our democracy,\u8221\'20\'1D Willis says.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.41am BST\par \par \uc2 Some of the acts took place in other jurisdictions, she says, but are being included here.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.41am BST\par \par \uc2 Every individual named is charged with one count of violating Georgia\u8217\'20\'19s Rico act, she says.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CSpecifically, the participants in association took various actions in Georgia and elsewhere to block the [results] of the vote,\u8221\'20\'1D she says.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 4.52am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.39am BST\par \par \uc2 Fulton county district attorney \uc2 Fani Willis\uc2  speaks\par \par \uc2 Fulton county district attorney \uc2 Fani Willis\uc2  is speaking now.\par \par \uc2 The prosecutors and investigators worked diligently on the case, she says.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe indictment includes 41 felony counts and is 97 pages long. Please remember that everyone charged \u8230\'20\'26 is presumed innocent,\u8221\'20\'1D she says.\par \par \uc2 She then lists the names of those charged:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 ,\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Rudolph Giuliani\uc2 ,\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 John Eastman,\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Mark Meadows\uc2 ,\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Kenneth Chesebro,\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Jeffrey Clark,\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Jenna Ellis,\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Ray Stallings Smith III,\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Robert Cheeley,\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Michael a. Roman,\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 David Shafer,\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Shawn Still,\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Stephen Lee,\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Harrison Floyd,\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Trevian c. Kutti,\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Sidney Powell\uc2 ,\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Cathleen Latham,\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Scott Hall,\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Misty Hampton\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.36am BST\par \par \uc2 Why is this case different?\par \par \uc2 The Georgia case is different because Trump cannot interfere in the case, even if he is president, and cannot issue a pardon.\par \par \uc2 This is the second case that has sought any kind of criminal accountability for his attempt to overturn the election. It is the fourth time Trump has been charged with a crime this year.\par \par \uc2 Earlier in August, Jack Smith, the special counsel for the justice department, filed four federal charges against Trump for trying to overturn the election. Trump has pleaded not guilty to those charges, and Smith has moved to set a trial date for 2 January. If Trump were elected president while the case was still pending, he would almost certainly move to fire Smith and get rid of the charges. He could also theoretically pardon himself if he has been convicted.\par \par \uc2 But he cannot issue a pardon in this case.\par \par \uc2 In June, Smith charged Trump with illegally retaining national defense information under the Espionage Act and obstructing the government\u8217\'20\'19s attempt to retrieve the documents. Trump pleaded not guilty.\par \par \uc2 In March, Trump was charged with 34 felony counts of falsifying business records in Manhattan. Those charges are connected to a $130,000 payment he made to Stormy Daniels, a pornstar, with whom he is alleged to have had an extramarital affair. \uc2 Michael Cohen\uc2 , Trump\u8217\'20\'19s attorney at the time, paid the money to Daniels through a shell company and Trump\u8217\'20\'19s reimbursed him, cataloguing it as a legal expense. \uc2 Alvin Bragg\uc2 , the Manhattan district attorney, said that amounted to falsifying business records. Trump has pleaded not guilty.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 4.48am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.32am BST\par \par \uc2 What is the Georgia Rico Act?\par \par \uc2 Trump and eighteen others have been indicted on charges of violating Georgia\u8217\'20\'19s Racketeer Influenced and Corrupt Organizations (Rico) Act.\par \par \uc2 The act essentially allows prosecutors to link together different crimes committed by different people and bring criminal charges against a larger criminal enterprise. The law requires prosecutors to show the existence of a criminal enterprise that has committed at least two underlying crimes.\par \par \uc2 Prosecutors have long used the federal Rico act to go after the mafia. But Georgia\u8217\'20\'19s version is even more expansive than the federal statute. It allows prosecutors in the state to bring racketeering charges if a defendant attempts or solicits a crime, even if they don\u8217\'20\'19t bring charges for those crimes itself.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.29am BST\par \par \uc2 What is this case about?\par \par \uc2 While we wait to hear from Fulton county district attorney \uc2 Fani Willis\uc2 , here is a refresher on what the case is about.\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  lost {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/state-of-georgia"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Georgia}}}\uc2  in the 2020 presidential election. After the election, Trump and his allies made an aggressive push to invalidate the election results in Georgia as part of an effort to overturn the election results.\par \par \uc2 On 2 January 2021, Trump called \uc2 Brad Raffensperger\uc2 , the Republican who serves as Georgia\u8217\'20\'19s top election official, and asked him to overturn the election. \u8220\'20\'1CAll I want to do is this. I just want to find 11,780 votes, which is one more than we have because we won the state,\u8221\'20\'1D {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/jan/03/trump-georgia-raffensperger-call-biden-washington-post"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Trump said to Raffensperger on the call}}}\uc2 . Raffensperger refused.\par \par \uc2 The call came as Trump and allies, including \uc2 Rudy Giuliani\uc2 , were spreading outlandish lies about the election in Georgia in order to seed doubt about the results. Most notably, Giuliani and others {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://apnews.com/article/giuliani-georgia-election-workers-lawsuit-false-statements-afc64a565ee778c6914a1a69dc756064"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 amplified misleading surveillance video}}}\uc2  from State Farm Arena they claimed showed election workers taking ballots out from under a table and counting them after observers left for the evening. The claim was false \u8211\'20\'13 counting had not stopped for the evening when the ballots were tallied.\par \par \uc2 Just as he did in other swing states, Trump {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/aug/05/trump-fake-electors-georgia"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 convened a slate of fake electors}}}\uc2  in Georgia. The group of 16 people met discreetly in the Georgia capitol in December 2020 and signed on to a certificate affirming Trump\u8217\'20\'19s victory that was sent {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.americanoversight.org/american-oversight-obtains-seven-phony-certificates-of-pro-trump-electors"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 to the National Archives}}}\uc2 . Some involved in the scheme have said they merely believed they were preserving Trump\u8217\'20\'19s options amid pending litigation. The alternate slate of electors, both in Georgia and elsewhere, would later become a lynchpin of Trump\u8217\'20\'19s effort to overturn the election.\par \par \uc2 One of those fake electors, Cathy Latham, also was involved in a separate incident in which Trump allies {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.americanoversight.org/american-oversight-obtains-seven-phony-certificates-of-pro-trump-electors"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 obtained unauthorized access}}}\uc2  to Dominion voting equipment. On 7 January 2021, Latham helped a firm hired by the Trump campaign get access to voting equipment in Coffee county, a rural county 200 miles south-east of Atlanta. The data was uploaded to a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.washingtonpost.com/investigations/2022/10/28/coffee-county-election-voting-machines/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 password-protected site}}}\uc2 , where other election deniers could download it as they sought to prove the baseless allegation that Dominion voting machines had been rigged and cost Trump the election.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 4.52am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.26am BST\par \par \uc2 Trump indictment: what we know so far\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 A grand jury in Georgia has issued an indictment accusing \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  of efforts to overturn his 2020 election loss to Democrat \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Prosecutors brought 41 counts against Trump and his associates, including forgery and racketeering, which is used to target members of organized crime groups.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Prosecutors charged 18 other people, including \uc2 Mark Meadows\uc2 , Trump\u8217\'20\'19s former White House chief of staff, and lawyers \uc2 Rudy Giuliani\uc2  and John Eastman.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The Trump campaign has responded to the indictment, saying, \u8220\'20\'1CPresident Trump will continue to power through this unprecedented abuse of power\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 A news conference featuring district attorney Fani T Willis is expected to take place after the indictment is released.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The court {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/aug/14/trump-2020-election-georgia-charges-update"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 briefly posted a document on its website earlier on Monday}}}\uc2  listing several felony charges against Trump, but quickly removed it without explanation. Willis\u8217\'20\'19s office said at the time no charges had been filed and declined further comment.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Over the course of a two-year investigation, Willis has examined Trump\u8217\'20\'19s alleged efforts to pressure state leaders to reverse his 11,000-vote loss to Democrat \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  in the state and organise a slate of illegitimate electors to undermine the process of formalising Biden\u8217\'20\'19s victory. She has also looked into an alleged attempt by Trump\u8217\'20\'19s allies to manipulate voting equipment in rural Coffee county.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Trump has denied any wrongdoing and accuses Fulton county district attorney \uc2 Fani Willis\uc2 , an elected Democrat, of being politically motivated.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Trump, 77, has been criminally indicted three times so far this year, including once by US special counsel Jack Smith on charges of trying to overturn his election defeat. He has long dismissed the many investigations, including two impeachments, he has faced in his years in politics as a politically motivated \u8220\'20\'1Cwitch-hunt\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 4.42am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.23am BST\par \par \uc2 Here is the moment that Fulton County Superior Court Judge Robert McBurney received the indictment documents earlier:\par \par \uc2 Fulton County Superior Court Judge Robert McBurney receives documents on 14 August 2023 in Atlanta, Georgia. Photograph: Megan Varner/Getty Images\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.18am BST\par \par \uc2 You can read the full indictment {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.documentcloud.org/documents/23909543/23sc188947-criminal-indictment.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 here}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Nineteen people have been indicted by the grand jury, including \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The defendants are:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 ,\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Rudolph Giuliani\uc2 ,\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 John Eastman,\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Mark Meadows\uc2 ,\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Kenneth Chesebro,\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Jeffrey Clark,\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Jenna Ellis,\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Ray Stallings Smith III,\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Robert Cheeley,\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Michael a. Roman,\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 David Shafer,\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Shawn Still,\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Stephen Lee,\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Harrison Floyd,\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Trevian c. Kutti,\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Sidney Powell\uc2 ,\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Cathleen Latham,\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Scott Hall,\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Misty Hampton\par \par \uc2 They are charged with violating the Georgia Rico (racketeer influenced and corrupt organizations) act.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 4.26am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.08am BST\par \par \uc2 We are expecting Fulton county district attorney \uc2 Fani Willis\uc2 , who led the investigation, to address the media shortly: cameras are trained on the podium.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.05am BST\par \par \uc2 The Trump campaign has responded to the indictment, saying, \u8220\'20\'1CPresident Trump will continue to power through this unprecedented abuse of power\u8221\'20\'1D and accusing Fulton county district attorney \uc2 Fani Willis\uc2 , an elected Democrat, of being part of the \u8220\'20\'1CDeranged Democrat Prosecutor Club\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 The statement is attributed to Karoline Leavitt, spokesperson for Make America Great Again Inc.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.02am BST\par \par \uc2 Here is a screenshot of the documents showing the names of Trump and others:\par \par \uc2 enltrBREAKING: \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  and others indicted on criminal charges in Fulton County, Georgia {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/GTI4H9sWT4"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/GTI4H9sWT4}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Anna Bower (@AnnaBower) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/AnnaBower/status/1691281787979210752?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 August 15, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.59am BST\par \par \uc2 Trump indicted for a fourth time\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  and several allies have been indicted in Georgia, accused of scheming to illegally overturn his 2020 election loss in the state. It\u8217\'20\'19s the fourth criminal case to be brought against the former president and the second to allege that he tried to subvert the results of the vote.\par \par \uc2 The Fulton county grand jury indictment of Trump follows a two-year investigation ignited by a January 2021 phone call in which the then-president suggested that Georgia\u8217\'20\'19s Republican secretary of state could help him \u8220\'20\'1Cfind 11,780 votes\u8221\'20\'1D needed to reverse his narrow loss to Democrat \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 4.07am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.56am BST\par \par \uc2 The indictment is 98 pages and includes Trump\u8217\'20\'19s name, as well as several others, including \uc2 Rudy Giuliani\uc2 , Don Eastman, \uc2 Mark Meadows\uc2 , Geoffrey Clark, Ray Smith and Robert Cheeley, CNN reports.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 4.00am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.55am BST\par \par \uc2 Indictment unsealed and Trump reportedly indicted\par \par \uc2 The documents have been unsealed, CNN reports, and show that \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  has been indicted for a fourth time.\par \par \uc2 The Guardian\uc2  has not confirmed this yet.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.56am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.53am BST\par \par \uc2 Hillary Clinton\uc2 : 'I don't know that anybody should be satisfied'\par \par \uc2 Hillary Clinton\uc2  has spoken to Rachel Maddow about the election interference case, NBC reports.\par \par \uc2 Clinton said that she feels, \u8220\'20\'1Cprofound sadness\u8221\'20\'1D that Trump has faced indictments \u8220\'20\'1Cthat went right to the heart of whether or not our democracy would survive.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 She continued:\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI hope that we won\u8217\'20\'19t have accountability just for \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , and if there are others named in these indictments along with him for their behavior, but we\u8217\'20\'19ll also have accountability for a political party that has just thrown in with all of the lies and the divisiveness and the lack of any conscience about what was being done to the country,\u8221\'20\'1D she said.\par \par \uc2 She was asked whether she felt any satisfaction, and replied:\par \par \uc2 enltrHillary Clinton tells {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/maddow?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @maddow}}}\uc2  re: Trump indictments in GA:\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI don't know that anybody should be satisfied. This is a terrible moment for our country, to have a former president accused of these terribly important crimes. The only satisfaction may be that the system is working.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Sahil Kapur (@sahilkapur) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/sahilkapur/status/1691263380961587200?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 August 15, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.47am BST\par \par \uc2 At least one of the indictments related to Trump case\par \par \uc2 At least one of the 10 indictments is related to the election investigation, CNN reports, and the indictments are expected to be unsealed shortly.\par \par \uc2 It is possible that multiple people are named on one indictment.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.57am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.42am BST\par \par \uc2 Grand jury has been empaneled for weeks, hearing multiple cases\par \par \uc2 The Guardian\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s Hugo Lowell has pointed out that the grand jury has been meeting for weeks, and has heard evidence in a number of cases.\par \par \uc2 What does mean? Well, the grand jury returned 10 indictments, but those have not been made public. What it means is that some of those indictments may be for other cases.\par \par \uc2 The grand jury may have voted on multiple cases today.\par \par \uc2 So there are two possibilities:\par \par \uc2 1. 10 different indictments of different individuals in the Trump 2020 election interference case\par \par \uc2 2. One or more indictments related to the Trump 2020 election interference case, and others related to other cases\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.36am BST\par \par \uc2 There is no requirement that defendants are given advance notice of an indictment, or told before the indictments are made public, the \uc2 New York Times\uc2  notes, \u8220\'20\'1Cand there is no indication that they have informed any defense lawyers in the Trump case\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.34am BST\par \par \uc2 While we wait for the indictments to be made public, here is our full report on what happened today:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/aug/14/donald-trump-georgia-indictment-2020-election"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Georgia grand jury returns indictments in Trump 2020 election inquiry}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.26am BST\par \par \uc2 Here is video of a representative from the Fulton Country clerk\u8217\'20\'19s office carrying the indictment paperwork \u8211\'20\'13 the paperwork we are hoping will be made public shortly \u8211\'20\'13 out of the court for processing:\par \par \uc2 enltrHere\u8217\'20\'19s the representative from the Fulton County Superior Court Clerk\u8217\'20\'19s office carrying the indictments unsealed today out of the courtroom, and back towards the clerk\u8217\'20\'19s office for processing. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/NBCNews?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @NBCNews}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/3SdnG97RGM"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/3SdnG97RGM}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Gary Grumbach (@GaryGrumbach) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/GaryGrumbach/status/1691270721249464320?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 August 15, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.21am BST\par \par \uc2 Snap analysis\par \par \uc2 Anthony Michael Kreis, a law professor at \uc2 Georgia State University\uc2 , noted that Georgia\u8217\'20\'19s Rico statute was a favourite tool for the Fulton county district attorney, referencing the 2014 Atlanta public schools trial where teachers and officials conspired to cheat on standardised tests.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI think the 2020 election aftermath and attempts to overthrow the election are very similar to that, where there\u8217\'20\'19s just a lot of moving parts and a lot of different actors,\u8221\'20\'1D he said.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThey all don\u8217\'20\'19t necessarily have the same degree of information as all the others do. They all don\u8217\'20\'19t get together and say, \u8216\'20\'18Let\u8217\'20\'19s do this unlawful thing\u8217\'20\'19 but they know they\u8217\'20\'19re part of a machine that\u8217\'20\'19s doing something they shouldn\u8217\'20\'19t,\u8221\'20\'1D Kreis explained.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.16am BST\par \par \uc2 The Trump campaign has released a statement calling Fulton county district attorney \uc2 Fani Willis\uc2 , an elected Democrat, a \u8220\'20\'1Crabid partisan\u8221\'20\'1D \u8211\'20\'13 and the indictments \u8220\'20\'1Cbogus\u8221\'20\'1D. The statement is long and continues in that vein.\par \par \uc2 Instead, you can read our profile of Willis, by Jewel Wicker. Here is a short exerpt:\par \par \uc2 In early 2021 Willis had just been elected district attorney when she announced plans to investigate Trump. She took office by unseating her former boss, who had served as the DA in Georgia\u8217\'20\'19s most populous county (which includes the state\u8217\'20\'19s capital, Atlanta) for six terms, or 23 years.\par \par \uc2 Her investigation has focused on Trump\u8217\'20\'19s efforts to subvert the will of Georgia\u8217\'20\'19s voters, including his campaign\u8217\'20\'19s plot to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/aug/05/trump-fake-electors-georgia"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 assemble a slate of fake electors}}}\uc2  and Trump\u8217\'20\'19s phone call to Georgia\u8217\'20\'19s Republican secretary of state, \uc2 Brad Raffensperger\uc2 , asking him to \u8220\'20\'1Cfind 11,780 votes\u8221\'20\'1D, which would make him the winner over \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  in the state.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 You can read the full profile here:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/aug/14/donald-trump-prosecutor-fulton-county-georgia-district-attorney-fani-willis"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \u8216\'20\'18He\u8217\'20\'19s going to be very surprised\u8217\'20\'19: Georgia DA Fani Willis prepares to face off with Trump}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.11am BST\par \par \uc2 Snap analysis\par \par \uc2 Charges against Trump would mark significant legal peril for him, since the charges come at the state level and he would not be able to undo any potential convictions through measures such as a self-pardon or appointing a partisan attorney general even if he was re-elected president in 2024.\par \par \uc2 In recent months, the district attorney\u8217\'20\'19s office identified multiple general and state election law violations by Trump and Republican operatives as they sought to subvert the 2020 election, from pressuring state officials to organizing fake slates of electors to breaching voting machines.\par \par \uc2 The prosecutors examined whether there was scope {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://viewer.gutools.co.uk/us-news/2023/jul/21/georgia-trump-charges-fraud-election-2020"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 to construct racketeering charges from the outset}}}\uc2 , hiring experts on the Rico law (Racketeer Influenced and Corrupt Organizations Act) in Georgia, which is more expansive than its federal counterpart and requires only the showing of an \u8220\'20\'1Cinterrelated pattern of activity\u8221\'20\'1D of a criminal enterprise.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.02am BST\par \par \uc2 An Atlanta-area grand jury returned 10 indictments on Monday night, according to the cover page for the charging papers, in the investigation of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://viewer.gutools.co.uk/us-news/donaldtrump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Donald Trump\u8217\'20\'19s}}}\uc2  efforts to subvert the 2020 election in Georgia.\par \par \uc2 The specific charges and the names of the defendants were not immediately clear. The indictments were walked over to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://viewer.gutools.co.uk/us-news/state-of-georgia"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Georgia}}}\uc2  superior court judge Robert McBurney, who did not make public any of the contents of the indictments.\par \par \uc2 But the high-profile investigation led by Fulton county district attorney \uc2 Fani Willis\uc2  is widely expected to result in charges against Trump and multiple allies, especially given the nature of the witnesses summoned to testify to the grand jury on Monday.\par \par \uc2 The witnesses included former Georgia lieutenant governor Geoff Duncan and the reporter George Chidi, who had initially been scheduled to testify on Tuesday but were summoned to appear a day early, a move that signalled the prosecutors wanted to wrap proceedings the same day.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.56am BST\par \par \uc2 If you\u8217\'20\'19re just joining us: the \u8220\'20\'1Cworst case scenario\u8221\'20\'1D for when we will know who has been indicted (including whether former US President \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  has been indicted for the fourth time) is at midnight, Fulton county court clerk Che Alexander told reporters earlier.\par \par \uc2 It is currently almost 10pm in Fulton county, Georgia, where the indictment documents are being processed in the clerk\u8217\'20\'19s office.\par \par \uc2 We could know any time from now until then who the grand jury has voted to indict.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.58am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.45am BST\par \par \uc2 Neal Katyal\uc2 , a professor of law at \uc2 Georgetown University\uc2 , has posted {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/neal_katyal/status/1691260726793699329?s=20"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 more about the indictments}}}\uc2  on \uc2 Twitter\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Just to be clear, however: the \uc2 Guardian\uc2  has not verified the below. We do not know for certain whether Trump has been indicted (or, in other words, that the 10 indictments are \u8220\'20\'1Cvery very bad news for Trump\u8221\'20\'1D):\par \par \uc2 Katyal says:\par \par \uc2 The Georgia Indictments say there were zero \u8216\'20\'18no bills.\u8217\'20\'19 That means that the Grand Jury decided to indict in all cases that the DA (the prosecutor) sought. This is very very bad news for Trump, and likely others in his circle.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.48am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.38am BST\par \par \uc2 A reminder: the case stems from a 2 January 2021, phone call in which Trump urged Georgia\u8217\'20\'19s top election official, \uc2 Brad Raffensperger\uc2 , to \u8220\'20\'1Cfind\u8221\'20\'1D enough votes to reverse his narrow loss in the state. Raffensperger declined to do so.\par \par \uc2 Experts agree that in Trump\u8217\'20\'19s conclusive 2020 defeat by \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 , there was no widespread electoral fraud in Georgia or any other state.\par \par \uc2 Trump is also facing 78 criminal charges in three other indictments, over:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Hush-money payments to the adult film star Stormy Daniels\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Retention of classified documents\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Election subversion at the federal level\par \par \uc2 Despite his unprecedented legal jeopardy, Trump dominates Republican primary polling as the first televised debate nears at the end of this month, my colleague Martin Pengelly {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/aug/14/trump-2020-election-georgia-charges-update"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reported}}}\uc2  earlier.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.46am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.34am BST\par \par \uc2 Georgia grand jury indictment: What we know so far\par \par \uc2 Here is the latest, via AP:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The grand jury in Georgia investigating \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s attempts to overturn his 2020 election loss returned several criminal indictments on Monday, although it was unclear whether the charges involved the former president.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Officials with the Fulton county court handed the indictment to judge Robert McBurney, but did not make them public.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Media accounts showed images of a cover sheet saying the grand jury had returned 10 indictments, but did not say who was indicted or what charges were filed.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Fulton county court clerk Che Alexander told reporters it could take her office up to three hours to process the indictments, after they were accepted by the judge.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 A news conference featuring district attorney Fani T Willis is expected to take place after the indictment is released.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The court {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/aug/14/trump-2020-election-georgia-charges-update"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 briefly posted a document on its website earlier on Monday}}}\uc2  listing several felony charges against Trump, but quickly removed it without explanation. Willis\u8217\'20\'19s office said at the time no charges had been filed and declined further comment.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Over the course of a two-year investigation, Willis has examined Trump\u8217\'20\'19s alleged efforts to pressure state leaders to reverse his 11,000-vote loss to Democrat \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  in the state and organise a slate of illegitimate electors to undermine the process of formalising Biden\u8217\'20\'19s victory. She has also looked into an alleged attempt by Trump\u8217\'20\'19s allies to manipulate voting equipment in rural Coffee county.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Trump has denied any wrongdoing and accuses Fulton county district attorney \uc2 Fani Willis\uc2 , an elected Democrat, of being politically motivated.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Trump, 77, has been criminally indicted three times so far this year, including once by US special counsel Jack Smith on charges of trying to overturn his election defeat. He has long dismissed the many investigations, including two impeachments, he has faced in his years in politics as a politically motivated \u8220\'20\'1Cwitch-hunt\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.28am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.30am BST\par \par \uc2 As we await news of who precisely has been indicted, Republican senator \uc2 Lindsey Graham\uc2  has said on Fox news: \u8220\'20\'1CThe American people can decide whether they want him to be president or not. This should be decided at the ballot box, not a bunch of liberal jurisdictions trying to put the man in jail.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThey\u8217\'20\'19re weaponizing the law in this country, they\u8217\'20\'19re trying to take \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  down and this is setting a bad precedent,\u8221\'20\'1D he continued.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.39am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.27am BST\par \par \uc2 NBC\u8217\'20\'19s Gary Grumbach has outlined exactly what happened at the court over the last half hour:\par \par \uc2 At 8:58pm, a rep from Fulton County Superior Court Clerk\u8217\'20\'19s office, a representative from the Fulton County District Attorney\u8217\'20\'19s office and several representatives from the \uc2 Fulton County Sheriff\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s office walked into courtroom 8D \u8211\'20\'13 Superior Court Judge Robert McBurney\u8217\'20\'19s courtroom.\par \par \uc2 The District Attorney\u8217\'20\'19s office representative was holding a stack of papers. They were greeted by the Judge, who said \u8216\'20\'18is it evening or night?\u8217\'20\'19 when the representative from the DA\u8217\'20\'19s office said \u8216\'20\'18Good evening.\u8217\'20\'19\par \par \uc2 McBurney went through every indictment \u8211\'20\'13 it appeared there were multiple \u8211\'20\'13 making sure they were all signed and the various forms were properly filled out. He asked the DA\u8217\'20\'19s rep \u8216\'20\'18Everything went as it should have in front of the grand jury?\u8217\'20\'19 The DA\u8217\'20\'19s rep said, \u8220\'20\'1CYes your honor.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The Judge did not read anything aloud from the indictment. McBurney then handed the indictments to the Clerk\u8217\'20\'19s office representative, as he instructed her to maintain custody of the indictments. She departed the courtroom, en route to the Clerk\u8217\'20\'19s office to file the indictment\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.23am BST\par \par \uc2 MSNBC correspondent Blayne Alexander has posted a picture of the certification that the grand jury indictments were returned in open court, and that there were 10 indictments.\par \par \uc2 enltrBIG FLAG: a Fulton County grand jury has returned 10 indictments. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/CharlieGileNBC?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @CharlieGileNBC}}}\uc2  snapped this photo at the clerk\u8217\'20\'19s office.\par \par \uc2 We are awaiting names and details. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/IwGVxsck80"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/IwGVxsck80}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Blayne Alexander (@ReporterBlayne) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/ReporterBlayne/status/1691254200422764544?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 August 15, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.19am BST\par \par \uc2 It is 9.20 pm in Fulton county, Georgia.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.42am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.18am BST\par \par \uc2 If you\u8217\'20\'19re just joining us, the grand jury at Fulton County, Georgia has returned 10 indictments. Court remained open past 5pm \u8211\'20\'13 and is still open, with reporters and court staff prepared to work through the night.\par \par \uc2 The clark confirmed that the grand jury has voted to indict 10 people. But, the clark said that processing, stamping and making the indictment documents public could take three hours, CNN reports. But it may be only an hour.\par \par \uc2 We do not know who has been indicted.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.13am BST\par \par \uc2 So it is now a question of who has been indicted. It is not clear.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.12am BST\par \par \uc2 What does 10 indictments mean?\par \par \uc2 There could be one or multiple people in each indictment, but it is likely this means that a minimum of ten people have been charged in these indictments, CNN reports.\par \par \uc2 The grand jury votes yes or no on each indictment, by majority vote (12 of 23 jurors).\par \par \uc2 But the grand jury has been hearing multiple cases over the last few weeks. So there is a possibility that jurors voted on multiple indictments this evening \u8211\'20\'13 and that not all of the 10 indictments are related to the Trump 2020 election interference case.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.45am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.09am BST\par \par \uc2 Grand jury returns 10 indictments\par \par \uc2 The grand jury has returned 10 indictments, the Guardian\u8217\'20\'19s Hugo Lowell reports from the courtroom.\par \par \uc2 enltrNEW: Fulton County grand jury returned 10 indictments today in the Trump case, per cover page filed with clerk\u8217\'20\'19s office\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Hugo Lowell (@hugolowell) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/hugolowell/status/1691255539223941120?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 August 15, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.09am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.06am BST\par \par \uc2 The paperwork \u8211\'20\'13 a large stack of papers \u8211\'20\'13 have now been walked back to the clerk\u8217\'20\'19s office for the next stage of processing.\par \par \uc2 This document may be the indictment \u8211\'20\'13 but it may not be. We should know shortly.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.09am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.04am BST\par \par \uc2 We are expecting a dozen or so defendants to be indicted, if the grand jury has voted to indict. The defendants include former US president \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 If Trump is indicted this will be his fourth indictment.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.02am BST\par \par \uc2 Judge Robert McBurney checks document\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CEverything went as it should have?\u8221\'20\'1D Judge Robert McBurney asks. He hands the documents back to the clerk, who agrees to take custody of them.\par \par \uc2 The document will now be docketed and will become available to the public any moment.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.41am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.59am BST\par \par \uc2 Indictment handed to the judge\par \par \uc2 The indictment is being handed to the judge. He is now looking at it.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.57am BST\par \par \uc2 We\u8217\'20\'19re not yet sure of how a potential indictment will be processed today (in the court or behind closed doors), but things appear to be moving quickly so we should have news any minute.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.56am BST\par \par \uc2 Different judges handle this stage of proceedings differently, CNN reports. Sometimes indictments are processed behind closed doors, sometimes they are processed in court in front of the public.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 1.57am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.54am BST\par \par \uc2 At the moment \u8220\'20\'1Ceveryone is going to the places they need to be to process a potential indictment\u8221\'20\'1D, CNN reports.\par \par \uc2 Court is back in session and reporters are waiting for word from the grand jury. We have yet to hear whether the grand jury has any findings.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 1.57am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.53am BST\par \par \uc2 Fulton county sheriff Patrick Labat enters courtroom\par \par \uc2 Judge Robert McBurney tells the courtroom: \u8220\'20\'1CThe convoy is mobile,\u8221\'20\'1D presumably referring to the grand jury return being walked over from the grand jury room inside the Fulton county DA\u8217\'20\'19s office to the courthouse.\par \par \uc2 The Fulton county sheriff Patrick Labat just entered the courtroom.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 1.54am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.51am BST\par \par \uc2 The New York Times\uc2  has quoted McBurney, who earlier reportedly offered potato crisps to hungry reporters, as saying, \u8220\'20\'1CDid anyone leave early? Everyone stayed? I was tempted.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.49am BST\par \par \uc2 Judge Robert McBurney enters courtroom\par \par \uc2 My colleague Hugo Lowell is in the courtroom at Fulton county, Georgia. He says that judge Robert McBurney has just returned to the courtroom, where 50 reporters are waiting for the grand jury to return from voting.\par \par \uc2 McBurney is the duty judge who will preside over any grand jury returns today.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 1.52am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.46am BST\par \par \uc2 Judge Robert McBurney just entered the courtroom.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.38am BST\par \par \uc2 Grand jury voting on whether to indict \uc2 Donald Trump\par \par \uc2 The Guardian\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s Hugo Lowell, who is in Georgia, has confirmed that the grand jury is currently voting on whether to indict Trump:\par \par \uc2 enltrConfirming that the Fulton County grand jury is currently voting on indictments in the Trump 2020 case, per people familiar\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Hugo Lowell (@hugolowell) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/hugolowell/status/1691245551612821505?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 August 15, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 1.41am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.35am BST\par \par \uc2 Where things stand\par \par \uc2 Hello, this is Helen Sullivan taking over our live updates of the election subversion investigation into \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 As my colleague Maanvi Singh noted, we understand that the grand jury is currently voting on whether to indict Trump over election fraud charges.\par \par \uc2 The jury in Fulton county, Georgia, has spent the day and much of the evening hearing from witnesses.\par \par \uc2 Prosecutors have presented evidence to the grand jury as they push toward a likely indictment, the Associated Press reports.\par \par \uc2 Trump is also facing 78 criminal charges in three other indictments, over:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Hush-money payments to the adult film star Stormy Daniels\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Retention of classified documents\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Election subversion at the federal level\par \par \uc2 Despite his unprecedented legal jeopardy, Trump dominates Republican primary polling as the first televised debate nears at the end of this month, my colleague Martin Pengelly {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/aug/14/trump-2020-election-georgia-charges-update"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reported}}}\uc2  earlier.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 1.52am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.09am BST\par \par \uc2 Grand jury reportedly voting on election fraud charges\par \par \uc2 It appears the grand jury is voting on the election fraud charges.\par \par \uc2 enltrBreaking on {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/MSNBC?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @MSNBC}}}\uc2  : The Fulton County grand jury is voting NOW.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Kyle Griffin (@kylegriffin1) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/kylegriffin1/status/1691239763594887169?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 August 15, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 1.21am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.42am BST\par \par \uc2 The Fulton county district attorney appears determined to finish presenting evidence in the Trump case to the grand jury tonight, according to multiple people familiar \u8211\'20\'13 meaning indictments could come tonight.\par \par \uc2 Inside the courthouse, people are currently having dinner. Judge Robert McBurney, who is the duty judge presiding over any grand jury returns, tells reporters he\u8217\'20\'19s been informed he needs to stay for another hour.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 12.58am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.40am BST\par \par \uc2 Georgia DA Fani Willis prepares to face off with Trump\par \par \uc2 Willis is {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/aug/08/trump-2020-election-fulton-county-charges-next-week"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 expected to ask}}}\uc2  a grand jury this week to indict former president \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  and others for their attempts to overturn the election. The announcement of criminal charges, part of a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/jul/21/georgia-trump-charges-fraud-election-2020"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 sprawling racketeering case}}}\uc2 , will be the culmination of more than two years of work.\par \par \uc2 In early 2021, Willis had just been elected district attorney when she announced plans to investigate Trump. She took office by unseating her former boss, who had served as the DA in Georgia\u8217\'20\'19s most populous county (which includes the state\u8217\'20\'19s capital, Atlanta) for six terms, or 23 years.\par \par \uc2 Her investigation has focused on Trump\u8217\'20\'19s efforts to subvert the will of Georgia\u8217\'20\'19s voters, including his campaign\u8217\'20\'19s plot to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/aug/05/trump-fake-electors-georgia"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 assemble a slate of fake electors}}}\uc2  and Trump\u8217\'20\'19s phone call to Georgia\u8217\'20\'19s Republican secretary of state, \uc2 Brad Raffensperger\uc2 , asking him to \u8220\'20\'1Cfind 11,780 votes\u8221\'20\'1D, which would make him the winner over \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  in the state.\par \par \uc2 In her first term as DA \u8211\'20\'13 and amid ongoing conversations about criminal justice reform in Georgia and beyond \u8211\'20\'13 Willis has not only prepared to face off with a former president and his legal team, she\u8217\'20\'19s also been tough on crime in a number of other ways, too.\par \par \uc2 Read more:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/aug/14/donald-trump-prosecutor-fulton-county-georgia-district-attorney-fani-willis"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \u8216\'20\'18He\u8217\'20\'19s going to be very surprised\u8217\'20\'19: Georgia DA Fani Willis prepares to face off with Trump}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.08am BST\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  case tracker: where does each investigation stand?\par \par \uc2 Twice impeached and now arrested and indicted three times. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/donaldtrump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Donald Trump}}}\uc2  faces serious criminal charges in New York, Florida and Washington over a hush-money scheme during the 2016 election, his alleged mishandling of classified documents and his efforts to overturn the 2020 election.\par \par \uc2 As Trump prepares for those cases to go to trial, the former president is simultaneously reeling from a verdict that found him liable for sexual abuse and defamation toward writer E Jean Carroll. A {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/new-york"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 New York}}}\uc2  jury awarded Carroll, who accused Trump of assaulting her in 1996, $5m in damages.\par \par \uc2 And more criminal charges could be on the way for Trump in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/state-of-georgia"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Georgia}}}\uc2 . Here is where each case against Trump stands:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/jul/28/donald-trump-investigations-criminal-charges-tracker"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  Donald Trump case tracker: where does each investigation stand?}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 12.23am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.51pm BST\par \par \uc2 The Fulton county grand jury is still hearing from witnesses.\par \par \uc2 It\u8217\'20\'19s unclear when we will hear about charges. Judge Robert McBurney appeared before reporters briefly, but did not indicate whether the presentation of charges would happen tonight.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 12.24am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.44pm BST\par \par \uc2 A two-page docket, which appeared to have been posted on the Fulton county court website and then removed, has set of a flurry of speculation this afternoon. The Reuters news agency cited that docket in a story that charges against \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  had been filed. But the agency later revised the report, saying that the Georgia was \u8220\'20\'1Cset to charge\u8221\'20\'1D the former president.\par \par \uc2 The Fulton county clerk said the court had \u8220\'20\'1Clearned of a fictitious document that has been circulated online\u8221\'20\'1D, an apparent reference to the Reuters report on the docket that detailed racketeering and conspiracy charges against Trump.\par \par \uc2 More clarity is expected to come at 5pm local time.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 12.24am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.14pm BST\par \par \uc2 George Chidi, the independent journalist who was subpoenaed to appear before the Fulton county grand jury, was just seen entering the courthouse where he is expected to testify.\par \par \uc2 Journalist George Chidi prepares to enter the Fulton county Courthouse, Monday, 14 August 2023 in Atlanta. Photograph: Ben Gray/AP\par \par \uc2 Chidi had previously written for {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://theintercept.com/2023/07/31/trump-georgia-grand-jury-subpoena/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 The Intercept}}}\uc2  about how he happened upon \u8220\'20\'1Ca semi-clandestine meeting of Republicans pretending to be Georgia\u8217\'20\'19s official electors in December 2020\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 He had testified about the experience once already, to a separate special grand jury that was investigating election interference in an advisory capacity. Today he is expected to explain what he witnessed once again, to the new grand jury this week.\par \par \uc2 He wrote for The Intercept:\par \par \uc2 I went to Georgia\u8217\'20\'19s state Capitol on December 14, 2020, to watch the solemn and usually forgettable ritual casting of electoral votes. As \uc2 Stacey Abrams\uc2  led the Democratic delegation upstairs, Republicans sat in a reserved room on the Capitol\u8217\'20\'19s second floor to prepare a competing \u8212\'20\'14 and potentially illegal \u8212\'20\'14 slate of their own.\par \par \uc2 The Republicans threw me out of the room moments after I entered, camera phone in hand, going live on \uc2 Facebook\uc2 . When I asked what kind of gathering they were having, they told me it was an \u8220\'20\'1Ceducation meeting.\u8221\'20\'1D As it turns out, \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s election team had sent an email the previous night, instructing the group to maintain \u8220\'20\'1C {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/jun/07/trump-campaign-fake-georgia-electors-email"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 complete secrecy}}}\uc2 .\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Election madness wasn\u8217\'20\'19t incipient in 2020; it was happening all around us. And I get thrown out of a lot of places. So I didn\u8217\'20\'19t think much about it beyond tweeting a still from the \uc2 Facebook\uc2  Live, asking my friends to identify the people in the picture.\par \par \uc2 But because I was lied to and thrown out, it confirmed that the legislators were acting in secret, that they didn\u8217\'20\'19t want the press or public to know what they were doing. That specific bit of information has apparently been important enough to ask me to convey it to a grand jury \u8212\'20\'14 again.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 12.26am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.58pm BST\par \par \uc2 Judge in Trump hush-money case won't recuse himself\par \par \uc2 The judge in \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s Manhattan {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/mar/31/trump-stormy-daniels-affair-hush-money-indictment"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 hush-money criminal case }}}\uc2  has rejected the former president\u8217\'20\'19s demand to step aside, denying defense claims that he\u8217\'20\'19s biased against the Republican election front-runner because he\u8217\'20\'19s given cash to Democrats and his daughter is a party consultant, the Associated Press writes.\par \par \uc2 The agency further reports:\par \par \uc2 New York Judge Juan Manuel Merchan acknowledged in a ruling that he made several small donations to Democratic causes during the 2020 campaign, including $15 to Trump\u8217\'20\'19s Democratic rival, \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 , but said he is certain of his \u8220\'20\'1Cability to be fair and impartial.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Removing himself from the case, which is due to go to trial next March, \u8220\'20\'1Cwould not be in the public interest,\u8221\'20\'1D Merchan wrote. His six-page ruling echoed a state court ethics panel\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://nycourts.gov/legacyhtm/ip/judicialethics/opinions/23-54.htm"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 recent opinion}}}\uc2  that endorsed his continued involvement in the Trump case.\par \par \uc2 The decision on recusal was entirely up to Merchan. There is so far no comment from Trump lawyers or the prosecutor, the Manhattan district attorney.\par \par \uc2 Trump {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/apr/04/donald-trump-charges-34-felony-counts"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pleaded not guilty}}}\uc2  in April {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/global/video/2023/apr/04/donald-trump-appears-in-court-to-plead-not-guilty-to-hush-money-charge-video"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 in Manhattan}}}\uc2  to 34 felony counts of falsifying business records. The charges relate to hush-money payments made during the 2016 campaign to bury allegations that he had extramarital sexual encounters. He has denied wrongdoing.\par \par \uc2 Trump\u8217\'20\'19s lawyers {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://apnews.com/article/donald-trump-criminal-case-judge-merchan-d0e54b546043e0497b5c04e78b505d6a"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 wanted Merchan off the case}}}\uc2  in part because his daughter, Loren, is a political consultant whose firm has worked for some of Trump\u8217\'20\'19s Democratic rivals and because, they contend, he acted inappropriately by involving himself in plea negotiations last year for Trump\u8217\'20\'19s longtime finance chief, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/aug/18/allen-weisselberg-trump-organization-pleads-guilty-tax-fraud"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Allen Weisselberg}}}\uc2  . Merchan said he previously rejected that argument when asked to exit the \uc2 Trump Organization\uc2  case.\par \par \uc2 Merchan said in his ruling that Trump\u8217\'20\'19s lawyers had \u8220\'20\'1Cfailed to demonstrate that there exists concrete, or even realistic reasons for recusal to be appropriate, much less required on these grounds.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  appears with his lawyer Todd Blanche by video conferencing before Justice Juan Merchan during a hearing before his trial over charges that he falsified business records to conceal money paid to silence porn star Stormy Daniels in 2016, in Manhattan state court in New York, May 23, 2023. Photograph: Jane Rosenberg/Reuters\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.28pm BST\par \par \uc2 Summary of the day so far\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The indictment of \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  over his attempted election subversion in Georgia loomed closer as prosecutors began presenting to a grand jury in Atlanta on Monday. The Fulton county district attorney, \uc2 Fani Willis\uc2 , is expected early this week to seek multiple charges against more than a dozen defendants that could include the former president, sources {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/aug/14/donald-trump-charges-georgia-2020-us-election-overturn-interference"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  told the Guardian.}}}\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 A former Democratic state senator, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/aug/14/donald-trump-indictment-latest-updates-georgia-election-charges-fulton-county?page=with:block-64da63938f08b5423cbd8567#block-64da63938f08b5423cbd8567"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Jen Jordan,}}}\uc2  former Democratic state representative, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/aug/14/donald-trump-indictment-latest-updates-georgia-election-charges-fulton-county?page=with:block-64da6db98f0868b14259289b#block-64da6db98f0868b14259289b"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Bee Nguyen,}}}\uc2  and \uc2 Gabriel Sterling\uc2 , a top official in the office of the Georgia secretary of state, were seen at the Fulton county courthouse.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Former Georgia Lt Gov Geoff Duncan and independent journalist George Chidi, both expected to appear on Tuesday at the Fulton County grand jury hearing, are {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/aug/14/donald-trump-indictment-latest-updates-georgia-election-charges-fulton-county?page=with:block-64da6f828f0868b1425928a9#block-64da6f828f0868b1425928a9"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 set to testify on Monday instead. }}}\uc2  Chidi said the change was because prosecutors are \u8220\'20\'1Cmoving faster than they thought\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 A two-page docket report posted to the Fulton county court website indicated {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/aug/14/donald-trump-indictment-latest-updates-georgia-election-charges-fulton-county?page=with:block-64da688d8f08b5423cbd8586#block-64da688d8f08b5423cbd8586"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 charges against Trump}}}\uc2  including racketeering, conspiracy and false statements. The appearance of the report set off a flurry of news media activity, but then the document vanished. A spokesperson for the district attorney said reports \u8220\'20\'1Cthat those charges were filed [are] inaccurate. Beyond that we cannot comment.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Trump appeared to warn former Georgia lieutenant governor, Geoff Duncan, against testifying before the Fulton County grand jury in the state\u8217\'20\'19s 2020 election investigation. The former president\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/aug/14/donald-trump-indictment-latest-updates-georgia-election-charges-fulton-county?page=with:block-64da431a8f08e1f5a10e8202#block-64da431a8f08e1f5a10e8202"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Truth Social post}}}\uc2  came days after the US district judge \uc2 Tanya Chutkan\uc2 , who is overseeing Trump\u8217\'20\'19s January 6 case in Washington DC, warned against making \u8220\'20\'1Cinflammatory statements\u8221\'20\'1D that could intimidate witnesses in that trial.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Democratic presidential candidate \uc2 Robert F Kennedy Jr\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s campaign {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/aug/14/donald-trump-indictment-latest-updates-georgia-election-charges-fulton-county?page=with:block-64da3bb98f08b5423cbd834c#block-64da3bb98f08b5423cbd834c"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  tried to walk back on comments}}}\uc2  he made in support of a nationwide \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  restriction after the first three months of pregnancy.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Lawyers for \uc2 Hunter Biden\uc2 , the son of President \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  who has been under a years-long federal investigation over failing to pay taxes and, separately, illegally possessing a gun, said that part of the plea deal which unexpectedly fell apart in July {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/aug/14/donald-trump-indictment-latest-updates-georgia-election-charges-fulton-county?page=with:block-64da7afe8f08e1f5a10e84ac#block-64da7afe8f08e1f5a10e84ac"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 remains \u8220\'20\'1Cvalid and binding\u8221\'20\'1D}}}\uc2 , in a Sunday court filing.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The US navy became {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/aug/14/donald-trump-indictment-latest-updates-georgia-election-charges-fulton-county?page=with:block-64da4ce28f08e1f5a10e82b9#block-64da4ce28f08e1f5a10e82b9"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the third branch of the military }}}\uc2  to no longer have a Senate-confirmed leader for the first time in history, as Republican senator Tommy Tuberville continues his blockade on military nominations over the Pentagon\u8217\'20\'19s \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  policy.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.12pm BST\par \par \uc2 Lawyers for \uc2 Hunter Biden\uc2 , the son of President \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  who has been under a years-long federal investigation over failing to pay taxes and, separately, illegally possessing a gun, said that part of the plea deal which unexpectedly fell apart in July remains \u8220\'20\'1Cvalid and binding\u8221\'20\'1D, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://storage.courtlistener.com/recap/gov.uscourts.ded.82797/gov.uscourts.ded.82797.27.0.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 in a Sunday court filing}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Federal prosecutors, led by US attorney David Weiss, had on Friday {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://storage.courtlistener.com/recap/gov.uscourts.ded.82797/gov.uscourts.ded.82797.25.0.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 asked the court to cancel its request}}}\uc2  that the two sides reach a renewed agreement on the deal \u8220\'20\'1Csince there is no longer a plea agreement or diversion agreement for the Court to consider\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 But \uc2 Hunter Biden\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s lawyers said the guilty pleas were \u8220\'20\'1Cseparate and independent\u8221\'20\'1D from the diversion agreement that is set to drop his felony gun charges after two years. They said the diversion agreement was executed at the July hearing even as the overall deal collapsed and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/hunter-biden"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Hunter Biden}}}\uc2  intends to abide by its terms.\par \par \uc2 The court has \u8220\'20\'1Cacknowledged in its filings agreeing to the public disclosure of the Plea and Diversion Agreements \u8211\'20\'13 that the parties have a valid and binding bilateral Diversion Agreement\u8221\'20\'1D, \uc2 Hunter Biden\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s lawyers wrote in their Sunday filing, responding to prosecutors\u8217\'20\'19 Friday motion.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.05pm BST\par \par \uc2 Republican presidential candidate \uc2 Vivek Ramaswamy\uc2  has accused Fulton County of being \u8220\'20\'1Cdownright pathetic\u8221\'20\'1D after a list of criminal charges in Georgia against \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  briefly appeared on its website before it was removed.\par \par \uc2 enltrHere we go again: another disastrous Trump indictment. It\u8217\'20\'19s downright pathetic that Fulton County publicly posted the indictment on its website even before the grand jury had finished convening. Since the four prosecutions against Trump are using novel & untested legal theories,\u8230\'20\'26 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/LOYkGcCgm5"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/LOYkGcCgm5}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 \uc2 Vivek Ramaswamy\uc2  (@VivekGRamaswamy) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/VivekGRamaswamy/status/1691149756272095248?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 August 14, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.54pm BST\par \par \uc2 A judge presiding over grand jury deliberations in Fulton County has said cameras will be allowed into the courtroom if \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  is indicted this week.\par \par \uc2 Fulton County superior court judge Robert McBurney was quoted by the Messenger as saying:\par \par \uc2 If a grand jury presents an indictment, that\u8217\'20\'19s usually in the afternoon, and you can film and photograph that.\par \par \uc2 Unlike federal or Manhattan courts, where Trump appeared for his three previous arraignments, Georgia law requires that cameras be allowed into judicial proceedings with a judge\u8217\'20\'19s approval, according to NBC.\par \par \uc2 Open courtrooms \u8220\'20\'1Care an indispensable element of an effective and respected judicial system\u8221\'20\'1D, the Georgia supreme court stated in a 2018 order.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.45pm BST\par \par \uc2 Experts agree that in \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s conclusive 2020 defeat by \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  there was no widespread electoral fraud in Georgia or any other state.\par \par \uc2 The federal {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/aug/01/trump-indictment-full-text-2020-election-jan-6"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 indictment}}}\uc2  secured by the special counsel Jack Smith this month contained extensive evidence that Trump was repeatedly told as much but advanced his lie regardless.\par \par \uc2 In Atlanta on Monday, prosecutors began presenting to a grand jury.\par \par \uc2 A former Democratic state senator, Jen Jordan, told reporters as she left the Fulton county courthouse she was questioned for about 40 minutes. News outlets reported that a former Democratic state representative, Bee Nguyen, and \uc2 Gabriel Sterling\uc2 , a top official in the office of the Georgia secretary of state, were seen arriving too.\par \par \uc2 Nguyen and Jordan attended state legislative hearings in December 2020, during which the former New York mayor turned Trump attorney \uc2 Rudy Giuliani\uc2  and other aides made false claims of widespread fraud in Georgia.\par \par \uc2 The Trump lawyer John Eastman appeared during at least one of those hearings, saying the election had not been held in compliance with Georgia law and lawmakers should appoint a new slate of electors.\par \par \uc2 Sterling and the Georgia secretary of state, \uc2 Brad Raffensperger\uc2 , pushed back against allegations of widespread problems. Both are {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/republicans"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Republicans}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 On 2 January 2021, Trump called Raffensperger to say officials should help \u8220\'20\'1Cfind\u8221\'20\'1D the votes he needed to beat Biden. The release of a recording of that call prompted Willis to open her investigation.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.25pm BST\par \par \uc2 Georgia grand jury witnesses to testify today because prosecutors 'moving faster' than anticipated\par \par \uc2 Former Georgia Lt Gov Geoff Duncan and independent journalist George Chidi are expected to testify today before the Fulton county grand jury hearing the \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  2020 election subversion case.\par \par \uc2 Chidi, who was scheduled to appear Tuesday before the grand jury, said he will instead testify today because prosecutors are \u8220\'20\'1Cmoving faster than they thought\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 enltrChange of plans. I'm going to court today. They're moving faster than they thought.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 George Chidi (find me on Threads and \uc2 Substack\uc2 ) (@neonflag) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/neonflag/status/1691145633892020236?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 August 14, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 Duncan was also scheduled to appear in front of the grand jury, but an official with direct knowledge of Duncan\u8217\'20\'19s hearing told the Atlanta Journal-Constitution that he will now meet with grand jurors on Monday.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 1.00am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.11pm BST\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s the full statement by former state representative Bee Nguyen, who {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/aug/14/donald-trump-indictment-latest-updates-georgia-election-charges-fulton-county?page=with:block-64da63938f08b5423cbd8567#block-64da63938f08b5423cbd8567"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 confirmed }}}\uc2  she testified to a Fulton County grand jury hearing the \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  2020 election subversion case earlier today.\par \par \uc2 From the Atlanta Journal-Constitution\u8217\'20\'19s Patricia Murphy:\par \par \uc2 enltrFormer state Rep. Bee Nguyen, who was running for Secretary of State as a Democrat in the aftermath of the 2020 elections, released a statement about her testimony today. Her entire campaign was about protecting democracy for the future. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/hashtag/gapol?src=hash&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 #gapol}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/3MtLbqPeb7"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/3MtLbqPeb7}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Patricia Murphy (@MurphyAJC) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/MurphyAJC/status/1691148044450803732?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 August 14, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.54pm BST\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s a copy of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/aug/14/donald-trump-indictment-latest-updates-georgia-election-charges-fulton-county?page=with:block-64da5cc98f08e1f5a10e83a2#block-64da5cc98f08e1f5a10e83a2"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the document }}}\uc2  that the Fulton County court reportedly published on their website before taking it down without explanation, which listed several criminal charges against \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  related to his attempts to overturn his 2020 election defeat in Georgia.\par \par \uc2 The document was dated today, 14 August, and named Trump as the defendant. The charges listed in the document include:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Violation Of The Georgia Rico (Racketeer Influenced And Corrupt Organizations) Act\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Solicitation Of Violation Of Oath By Public Officer\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Conspiracy To Commit Impersonating A Public Officer\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Conspiracy To Commit Forgery in the First Degree\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Conspiracy To Commit False Statements and Writings\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Conspiracy To Commit Filing False Documents\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Filing False Documents\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Solicitation of Violation of Oath By Public Officer\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 False Statements And Writings\par \par \uc2 enltrthis document was posted online by the fulton county georgia DA\u8217\'20\'19s office and then quickly taken down. defendant: donald trump {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/rv1jrbXp77"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/rv1jrbXp77}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 jack queen (@jackqueen_) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/jackqueen_/status/1691135829941407745?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 August 14, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.39pm BST\par \par \uc2 Two former Georgia state lawmakers testify to Fulton County grand jury\par \par \uc2 Former Democratic state representative for Georgia Bee Nguyen has confirmed that she testified on Monday to the Fulton County grand jury hearing the \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  2020 election subversion case.\par \par \uc2 enltrEx-Georgia State Rep. Bee Nguyen confirms that she testified this morning before the Fulton County grand jury:\par \par \uc2 "When I took my oath of office in 2017, I swore my allegiance to our Constitution and promised to protect and defend out State and our country."\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Kyle Griffin (@kylegriffin1) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/kylegriffin1/status/1691134057894105098?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 August 14, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 Earlier we {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/aug/14/donald-trump-indictment-latest-updates-georgia-election-charges-fulton-county?page=with:block-64da549b8f08e1f5a10e8312#block-64da549b8f08e1f5a10e8312"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reported}}}\uc2  that former state senator Jen Jordan testified before the Fulton County grand jury for about 40 minutes on Monday.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 6.43pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.31pm BST\par \par \uc2 The Atlanta Journal-Constitution\u8217\'20\'19s Tamar Hallerman, who has been reporting from the Fulton County courthouse, writes that the district attorney\u8217\'20\'19s office confirms no indictments have yet been made in the Trump election interference case.\par \par \uc2 enltrI am standing in the Fulton courthouse and just spoke to the DA\u8217\'20\'19s office. NO INDICTMENTS yet in the Trump election interference case\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Tamar Hallerman (@TamarHallerman) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/TamarHallerman/status/1691134101250625537?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 August 14, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.24pm BST\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s more on {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/aug/14/donald-trump-indictment-latest-updates-georgia-election-charges-fulton-county?page=with:block-64da5cc98f08e1f5a10e83a2#block-64da5cc98f08e1f5a10e83a2"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 that Reuters report}}}\uc2  that said the state of Georgia appeared set to charge \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  with a variety of charges, including racketeering, conspiracy and false statements.\par \par \uc2 According to Reuters, the Fulton County court\u8217\'20\'19s website briefly posted a document appearing to detail several criminal charges against Trump, before taking the document down without explanation.\par \par \uc2 The two-page document cited the \u8220\'20\'1CViolation Of The Georgia Rico (Racketeer Influenced And Corrupt Organizations) Act\u8221\'20\'1D, \u8220\'20\'1CSolicitation Of Violation Of Oath By Public Officer\u8221\'20\'1D, \u8220\'20\'1CConspiracy To Commit False Statements and Writings\u8221\'20\'1D and \u8220\'20\'1CConspiracy To Commit Forgery in the First Degree\u8221\'20\'1D among other charges listed, Reuters said.\par \par \uc2 The document was dated 14 August and named the former president, the news agency said.\par \par \uc2 A spokesperson for the DA\u8217\'20\'19s office responded:\par \par \uc2 The Reuters report that those charges were filed is inaccurate. Beyond that we cannot comment.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.10pm BST\par \par \uc2 Georgia court publishes then removes docket of charges against \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  - report\par \par \uc2 The Fulton County district attorney\u8217\'20\'19s office said no charges have been filed yet against in the case investigating \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  and others for their attempts to overturn the 2020 election.\par \par \uc2 It comes after Reuters reported that the state of Georgia appeared set to charge Trump with a variety of charges, including racketeering, conspiracy and false statements.\par \par \uc2 The Reuters report cited a two-page docket report posted to the Fulton County court\u8217\'20\'19s website, which it said is no longer available on the court\u8217\'20\'19s website.\par \par \uc2 enltrThis is NOT true. I just spoke with the DA\u8217\'20\'19s office {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/hashtag/gapol?src=hash&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 #gapol}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/vgPK6bSD1s"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/vgPK6bSD1s}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Tamar Hallerman (@TamarHallerman) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/TamarHallerman/status/1691130975806279699?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 August 14, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 6.37pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.47pm BST\par \par \uc2 Fulton county district attorney \uc2 Fani Willis\uc2  is {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/aug/08/trump-2020-election-fulton-county-charges-next-week"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 expected to ask}}}\uc2  a grand jury this week to indict \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  and others for their attempts to overturn the election. The announcement of criminal charges, part of a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/jul/21/georgia-trump-charges-fraud-election-2020"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 sprawling racketeering case}}}\uc2 , will be the culmination of more than two years of work.\par \par \uc2 In early 2021, Willis had just been elected district attorney when she announced plans to investigate Trump.\par \par \uc2 Her investigation has focused on Trump\u8217\'20\'19s efforts to subvert the will of Georgia\u8217\'20\'19s voters, including his campaign\u8217\'20\'19s plot to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/aug/05/trump-fake-electors-georgia"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 assemble a slate of fake electors}}}\uc2  and Trump\u8217\'20\'19s phone call to Georgia\u8217\'20\'19s Republican secretary of state, \uc2 Brad Raffensperger\uc2 , asking him to \u8220\'20\'1Cfind 11,780 votes\u8221\'20\'1D, which would make him the winner over \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  in the state.\par \par \uc2 In her first term as DA \u8211\'20\'13 and amid ongoing conversations about criminal justice reform in Georgia and beyond \u8211\'20\'13 Willis has not only prepared to face off with a former president and his legal team, she\u8217\'20\'19s also been tough on crime in a number of other ways, too.\par \par \uc2 Since running for office, the Democratic official has made no apologies for being a liberal with {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/2023/02/02/magazine/fani-willis-trump.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 conservative-leaning views}}}\uc2  on criminal justice or the fact that she was endorsed and received funding from a police union during her campaign.\par \par \uc2 As DA, she\u8217\'20\'19s indicted Grammy-award winning rapper Young Thug and his music collective under Georgia\u8217\'20\'19s racketeering statute, fought appeals from teachers she previously prosecuted during a high-profile standardized test cheating scandal, and sought the death penalty for a man who murdered four women during a shooting spree that targeted Asian spas in metro Atlanta.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/aug/14/donald-trump-prosecutor-fulton-county-georgia-district-attorney-fani-willis"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \u8216\'20\'18He\u8217\'20\'19s going to be very surprised\u8217\'20\'19: Georgia DA Fani Willis prepares to face off with Trump}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.26pm BST\par \par \uc2 Georgia former state senator Jen Jordan, who was spotted earlier at the Fulton County courthouse, testified on Monday before a grand jury investigating \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s alleged efforts to overturn the state\u8217\'20\'19ss 2020 election results.\par \par \uc2 Jordan told the Atlanta Journal Constitution\u8217\'20\'19s Tamar Hallerman that she testified to the grand jury for about 40 minutes.\par \par \uc2 enltrJordan declined to say much about her testimony, but when I asked about this probe entering the indictment phase she responded, "it's about time." {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/hashtag/gapol?src=hash&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 #gapol}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Tamar Hallerman (@TamarHallerman) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/TamarHallerman/status/1691109239589068801?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 August 14, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.16pm BST\par \par \uc2 Defense secretary \uc2 Lloyd Austin\uc2 , during a relinquishment ceremony for retiring chief of naval operations Adm Mike Gilday, criticized Republican senator Tommy Tuberville \u8217\'20\'19s ongoing hold on senior military promotions.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CBecause of this blanket hold, starting today, for the first time in the history of the \uc2 Department of Defense\uc2 , three of our military services are operating without Senate-confirmed leaders,\u8221\'20\'1D Austin said.\par \par \uc2 This is unprecedented, it is unnecessary, and it is unsafe.\par \par \uc2 Austin did not name Tuberville in his speech, but he called on the Senate to confirm \u8220\'20\'1Call of our superbly qualified military nominees\u8221\'20\'1D, as the US navy became the third branch of the military to no longer have a Senate-confirmed leader.\par \par \uc2 He added:\par \par \uc2 This sweeping hold is undermining America\u8217\'20\'19s military readiness. It\u8217\'20\'19s hindering our ability to retain our very best officers. And it\u8217\'20\'19s upending the lives of far too many American military families.\par \par \uc2 enltr\u8220\'20\'1CThree of our military services are operating without Senate-confirmed leaders. This is unprecedented, it is unnecessary, and it is unsafe.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Defense Sec. \uc2 Lloyd Austin\uc2  shares \u8220\'20\'1Cpainful milestone\u8221\'20\'1D at relinquishment of office ceremony for Chief of Naval Operations Adm. Mike Gilday {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/zKxhwPi55M"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/zKxhwPi55M}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 The Recount (@therecount) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/therecount/status/1691100116399124480?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 August 14, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.52pm BST\par \par \uc2 The US navy became the third branch of the military to no longer have a Senate-confirmed leader for the first time in history, as Republican senator Tommy Tuberville continues his blockade on military nominations over the Pentagon\u8217\'20\'19s \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  policy.\par \par \uc2 The Navy, Army and Marine Corps are now all without a confirmed leader, after retiring chief of naval operations Adm Mike Gilday gave up command on Monday.\par \par \uc2 enltrOne more down as CNO Gilday relinquished command this morning.\par \par \uc2 Defense Secretary \uc2 Lloyd Austin\uc2  said today this is the first time in DOD history three services are without a Senate-confirmed chief. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/2tbO6A5Wry"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/2tbO6A5Wry}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Haley Britzky (@halbritz) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/halbritz/status/1691111893232963584?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 August 14, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 Since February, Tuberville has been protesting Pentagon policy that allows service members to travel for \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  care if their state does not provide it. His method is to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/aug/08/tommy-tuberville-senate-block-military-promotions-abortion"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 place a hold on all promotions }}}\uc2  to senior ranks that are subject to Senate confirmation, usually a pro forma process carried out with unanimous consent.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.34pm BST\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s primary rivals are preparing for the possibility that the former president and Republican nomination frontrunner will attend the first GOP presidential primary debate next week, according to a report.\par \par \uc2 The campaigns of four of the eight candidates who say they have qualified for the Republican national committe\u8217\'20\'19s (\uc2 RNC\uc2 ) 23 August debate in Milwaukee {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nbcnews.com/politics/2024-election/gop-candidates-prepare-possibility-trump-first-debate-rcna99351"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 told}}}\uc2  NBC they are holding debate prep sessions as if Trump will be there.\par \par \uc2 A fifth candidate, former South Carolina governor Nikki Haley, said she expects Trump to be at the debate.\par \par \uc2 Trump has been threatening to skip the debate for months, but last week insisted he hasn\u8217\'20\'19t \u8220\'20\'1Ctotally ruled it out\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 5.04pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.24pm BST\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/aug/14/donald-trump-indictment-latest-updates-georgia-election-charges-fulton-county?page=with:block-64da431a8f08e1f5a10e8202#block-64da431a8f08e1f5a10e8202"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Truth Social post}}}\uc2  on Monday warning former Georgia lieutenant governor, Geoff Duncan, against testifying before the Fulton County grand jury, comes days after the federal judge presiding over a separate Trump case {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/aug/11/trump-trial-date-sooner-warns-judge-tanya-chutkan"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 warned inflammatory remarks from the former president would push her to schedule the trial sooner.}}}\par \par \uc2 US district court judge \uc2 Tanya Chutkan\uc2  said on Friday that she would take every step to safeguard the integrity of proceedings and to avoid tainting the potential jury pool.\par \par \uc2 The admonition came as she ruled on Trump\u8217\'20\'19s requests to have fewer restrictions in a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://storage.courtlistener.com/recap/gov.uscourts.dcd.258149/gov.uscourts.dcd.258149.28.0_5.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 protective order}}}\uc2  that will govern what evidence turned over to his lawyers in the discovery process the former president could share publicly.\par \par \uc2 Broadly speaking, Chutkan ruled that Trump was free to share \u8220\'20\'1Cnon-sensitive materials\u8221\'20\'1D as designated by prosecutors, but narrowed the scope so closely that it could ultimately amount to only a pyrrhic victory. Chutkan also ended up rejecting the majority of Trump\u8217\'20\'19s other requests.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/aug/11/trump-trial-date-sooner-warns-judge-tanya-chutkan"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  Inflammatory remarks could speed up 2020 election trial, judge warns Trump}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 5.09pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.14pm BST\par \par \uc2 Trump appears to warn former Lt Gov Geoff Duncan against testifying to Georgia grand jury\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  appeared to warn former Georgia lieutenant governor, Geoff Duncan, against testifying before the Fulton County grand jury in the state\u8217\'20\'19s 2020 election investigation.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI am reading reports that failed former Lt. Governor of Georgia, Jeff Duncan, will be testifying before the Fulton County Grand Jury,\u8221\'20\'1D Trump posted on Truth Social today.\par \par \uc2 Trump added:\par \par \uc2 He shouldn\u8217\'20\'19t. I barely know him but he was, right from the beginning of this Witch Hunt, a nasty disaster for those looking into the Election Fraud that took place in Georgia.\par \par \uc2 His post came days after the US district judge \uc2 Tanya Chutkan\uc2 , who is overseeing Trump\u8217\'20\'19s January 6 case in Washington DC, warned against making \u8220\'20\'1Cinflammatory statements\u8221\'20\'1D that could intimidate witnesses in that trial.\par \par \uc2 Duncan confirmed he had been asked to testify before the grand jury on Tuesday hearing evidence of alleged meddling in the 2020 presidential election.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CRepublicans should never let honesty be mistaken for weakness,\u8221\'20\'1D Duncan tweeted.\par \par \uc2 enltrI can confirm that I have been requested to testify before the Fulton County grand jury on Tuesday. I look forward to answering their questions around the 2020 election.\par \par \uc2 Republicans should never let honesty be mistaken for weakness. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/3j73O1kLNj"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/3j73O1kLNj}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Geoff Duncan (@GeoffDuncanGA) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/GeoffDuncanGA/status/1690432894789971968?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 August 12, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 4.21pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.05pm BST\par \par \uc2 The US will send Ukraine a new military aid package worth around $200m, secretary of state \uc2 Antony Blinken\uc2  announced.\par \par \uc2 The latest security aid package includes air defense munitions, artillery rounds, anti-armor capabilities, and additional mine-clearing equipment, according to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.state.gov/additional-u-s-security-assistance-for-ukraine-9/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the statement}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 For more updates on Russia\u8217\'20\'19s war in Ukraine, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/live/2023/aug/14/russia-ukraine-war-live-strikes-on-odesa-leave-three-injured-zelenskiy-promises-justice-for-deadly-attack-on-kherson#top-of-blog"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 please follow our live blog. }}}\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/live/2023/aug/14/russia-ukraine-war-live-strikes-on-odesa-leave-three-injured-zelenskiy-promises-justice-for-deadly-attack-on-kherson"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Russia-Ukraine war live: strikes on Odesa leave three injured; rouble falls to 16-month low against dollar}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.56pm BST\par \par \uc2 After five years, the US attorney pursuing \uc2 Hunter Biden\uc2  has only been able to file tax and unlawful gun possession charges \u8211\'20\'13 and that shouldn\u8217\'20\'19t change just because the prosecutor has been {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/aug/11/hunter-biden-special-counsel-investigation-merrick-garland"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 named special counsel}}}\uc2  in the case, the lawyer for the president\u8217\'20\'19s son has said.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIf anything changes from his conclusion \u8230\'20\'26 the question [that] should be asked [is] what infected the process that was not the facts and the law?\u8221\'20\'1D \uc2 Hunter Biden\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s attorney, Abbe Lowell, said on \uc2 CBS\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s Face the Nation on Sunday. Lowell also said: \u8220\'20\'1CThere\u8217\'20\'19s no new evidence to be found.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1COnly thing that will change is the scrutiny on some of the charges.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 enltrHunter Biden's attorney Abbe Lowell says while U.S. attorney David Weiss has been appointed special counsel, "he's the same person he's been for the last five years."\par \par \uc2 "If anything changes from his conclusion...what infected the process that was not the facts and the law?" {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/uQANuFDdm2"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/uQANuFDdm2}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Face The Nation (@FaceTheNation) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/FaceTheNation/status/1690758821000482818?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 August 13, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 Lowell\u8217\'20\'19s remarks came after the US attorney in Delaware who has been investigating \uc2 Hunter Biden\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s business dealings, David Weiss, received an appointment on Thursday to become special counsel over the case.\par \par \uc2 The US attorney general, \uc2 Merrick Garland\uc2 , has said Weiss told him days earlier that \u8220\'20\'1Cin his judgment, his investigation [had] reached a stage at which he should continue his work as a special counsel, and he asked to be appointed\u8221\'20\'1D. Garland added that he granted the request of Weiss \u8211\'20\'13 who was appointed to his post by \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s presidential predecessor \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  \u8211\'20\'13 having concluded that it was \u8220\'20\'1Cin the public interest\u8221\'20\'1D to do so.\par \par \uc2 Yet Garland\u8217\'20\'19s justification did little to dampen a political firestorm in Washington DC. Weiss\u8217\'20\'19s probe into Biden\u8217\'20\'19s son is set to continue on a track that is parallel to special counsel investigations into Trump \u8211\'20\'13 the Republican frontrunner to challenge Biden in the 2024 race for the White House \u8211\'20\'13 which have produced a multitude of criminal charges against him.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 5.42pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.43pm BST\par \par \uc2 Robert F Kennedy Jr\uc2  walks back on supporting three-month federal \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban\par \par \uc2 Democratic presidential candidate \uc2 Robert F Kennedy Jr\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s campaign on Sunday evening tried to walk back on comments he made earlier in the day in support of a nationwide \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  restriction after the first three months of pregnancy.\par \par \uc2 In an interview at the Iowa State Fair, Kennedy told NBC News that he believes \u8220\'20\'1Ca decision to abort a child should be up to the women during the first three months of life\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Asked if he would sign a federal ban on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  after 15 weeks or 21 weeks of pregnancy if he were elected president, he said \u8220\'20\'1Cyes, three months\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Once a child is viable, outside the womb, I think then the state has an interest in protecting the child.\par \par \uc2 But in a later statement, Kennedy\u8217\'20\'19s campaign team said he had \u8220\'20\'1Cmisunderstood\u8221\'20\'1D the reporter\u8217\'20\'19s questions, citing a \u8220\'20\'1Ccrowded\u8221\'20\'1D and \u8220\'20\'1Cnoisy\u8221\'20\'1D exhibit hall at the fair.\par \par \uc2 The statement continued:\par \par \uc2 Mr Kennedy\u8217\'20\'19s position on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  is that it is always the woman\u8217\'20\'19s right to choose. He does not support legislation banning \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 In response, NBC reporter Ali Vitali shared a transcript of the full exchange and said she asked her questions multiple times to make sure the presidential candidate understood the subject.\par \par \uc2 enltrHere\u8217\'20\'19s the full exchange with Kennedy, in which I ask the questions multiple times to make sure we\u8217\'20\'19re understanding- even at one point saying I was surprised by the stance.\par \par \uc2 Full story here and video TK: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/NHWNhlaLL5"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/NHWNhlaLL5}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/t9NbrnqRG4"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/t9NbrnqRG4}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/U9FBPDNY2A"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/U9FBPDNY2A}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Ali Vitali (@alivitali) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/alivitali/status/1690890657655590913?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 August 14, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.33pm BST\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  case tracker: where does each investigation stand?\par \par \uc2 Twice impeached and now arrested and indicted three times. \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  faces serious criminal charges in New York, Florida and Washington over a hush-money scheme during the 2016 election, his alleged mishandling of classified documents and his efforts to overturn the 2020 election.\par \par \uc2 As Trump prepares for those cases to go to trial, the former president is simultaneously reeling from a verdict that found him liable for sexual abuse and defamation toward writer E Jean Carroll. A New York jury awarded Carroll, who accused Trump of assaulting her in 1996, $5m in damages.\par \par \uc2 And more criminal charges could be on the way for Trump in Georgia as early as this week.\par \par \uc2 Here is where each case against Trump stands:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/jul/28/donald-trump-investigations-criminal-charges-tracker"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  Donald Trump case tracker: where does each investigation stand?}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.20pm BST\par \par \uc2 Prosecutors investigating \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s efforts to overturn the 2020 election results in Georgia have gathered evidence directly connecting members of the former president\u8217\'20\'19s legal team to the voting system breach in Coffee County, according to a report.\par \par \uc2 Prosecutors have {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/aug/11/trump-georgia-voting-machine-charges-fulton"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 taken a special interest}}}\uc2  in the breach of voting machines in Coffee county by Trump allies because of the brazen nature of the operation and the possibility that Trump was aware that his allies intended to covertly gain access to the machines.\par \par \uc2 In a series of particularly notable incidents, forensics experts hired by Trump allies copied data from virtually every part of the voting system, which is used statewide in Georgia, before uploading them to a password-protected website that could be accessed by 2020 election deniers.\par \par \uc2 Investigators are in possession of text messages and emails indicating the breach was a top-down push by Trump\u8217\'20\'19s team to access sensitive voting software, CNN {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://edition.cnn.com/2023/08/13/politics/coffee-county-georgia-voting-system-breach-trump/index.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reported, }}}\uc2  citing sources.\par \par \uc2 Six days before pro-Trump operatives gained unauthorized access to voting systems, the local elections official who allegedly helped facilitate the breach shared a \u8220\'20\'1Cwritten invitation\u8221\'20\'1D to attorneys working for Trump, according to the report.\par \par \uc2 Investigators have also probed the involvement of Trump\u8217\'20\'19s then attorneys, \uc2 Rudy Giuliani\uc2  and \uc2 Sidney Powell\uc2 , the sources said.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/aug/11/trump-georgia-voting-machine-charges-fulton"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Trump allies face potential charges in Georgia over voting machine breaches}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.07pm BST\par \par \uc2 Georgia former state senator Jen Jordan has been spotted at the Fulton County courthouse today, according to NBC.\par \par \uc2 Jordan had been expected to testify before a grand jury as part of the Georgia prosecutor\u8217\'20\'19s investigation into \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s alleged efforts to overturn his election loss in the state.\par \par \uc2 enltrSpotted at the Fulton County courthouse: Former GA Senator Jen Jordan, who was subpoenaed by Willis. She asked security for directions to the DA\u8217\'20\'19s office.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Charlie Gile (@CharlieGileNBC) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/CharlieGileNBC/status/1691072910465609729?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 August 14, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.51pm BST\par \par \uc2 The indictment that the Fulton County district attorney, Fanis Willis, may bring against \uc2 Donald Trump{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/aug/14/donald-trump-charges-georgia-2020-us-election-overturn-interference"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 as early as this week }}}\uc2  could be the most sprawling case against the former president in response to his efforts to remain in power after losing the 2020 election.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1C I think people are going to be surprised at the level of preparedness and the level of sophistication of the prosecution,\u8221\'20\'1D Clint Rucker, a former prosecutor in Fulton County, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://apnews.com/article/trump-georgia-election-investigation-fani-willis-indictment-32bfdd2cca9d3184056836b208a78379"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 told AP.}}}\par \par \uc2 He added that he was not surprised the investigation has taken so long. While Willis is likely to let her team of prosecutors handle the trial, he said there was no question that she is calling the shots.\par \par \uc2 When she says stuff like, \u8216\'20\'18We\u8217\'20\'19re ready to go,\u8217\'20\'19 that\u8217\'20\'19s not being braggadocious'. It\u8217\'20\'19s her saying pretty much to anybody who\u8217\'20\'19s interested, \u8216\'20\'18Look, we\u8217\'20\'19re ready.\u8217\'20\'19\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.39pm BST\par \par \uc2 Who is \uc2 Fani Willis\uc2 ?\par \par \uc2 The synopsis for a \uc2 Fani Willis\uc2  biopic would probably go something like this:\par \par \uc2 In Fulton county, the first Black woman to serve as district attorney takes on an unlikely case. Willis grew up attending court with her father, a defense attorney and Black Panther. Now, she sits on the opposite side of the courtroom, hoping to indict a former president who sought to overturn election results and often espoused white supremacist rhetoric while doing so.\par \par \uc2 The film\u8217\'20\'19s montage would pull from real life, depicting a determined, unflappable Willis relentlessly poring over documents, leading her team through the long work hours and security risks that come with bringing an indictment against an often inflammatory former president, even as national attention on the case reached a groundswell.\par \par \uc2 We\u8217\'20\'19d watch her face {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nbcnews.com/politics/politics-news/fulton-county-da-fani-willis-shares-racist-threat-trump-probe-nears-co-rcna97515"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 racist threats}}}\uc2  and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.ajc.com/politics/derogatory-and-false-fulton-da-denies-rumors-circulated-by-trump/YSB6RC7KXZG25COURJFHDA5SGM/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 unsubstantiated rumors of misconduct}}}\uc2 , but she\u8217\'20\'19d refuse to back down from the task at hand. She\u8217\'20\'19d advocate for what she believed to be right even when it wasn\u8217\'20\'19t popular. She\u8217\'20\'19d appear in press conferences and in media interviews delivering stern {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nbcnews.com/meet-the-press/meetthepressblog/fulton-county-da-expect-subpoenas-trump-associates-rcna36948"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 soundbites}}}\uc2  such as: \u8220\'20\'1CLady justice is actually blind. This is the reality. If you come into my community and you commit a crime, you deserve to be held responsible.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 According to some of Willis\u8217\'20\'19s colleagues who have worked with her over more than 20 years, all of this would be an accurate depiction of the district attorney.\par \par \uc2 Defense attorney Brian Steel has known Willis her entire career and says she\u8217\'20\'19s both \u8220\'20\'1Cextremely honest\u8221\'20\'1D and \u8220\'20\'1Cextremely hard working\u8221\'20\'1D. Atlanta NAACP president Gerald Griggs described her as \u8220\'20\'1Ctransparent\u8221\'20\'1D, a \u8220\'20\'1Czealous advocate for the state\u8221\'20\'1D and the \u8220\'20\'1Cbest trial attorney\u8221\'20\'1D in the Fulton county district attorney\u8217\'20\'19s office. He said:\par \par \uc2 What you see on TV is authentic to who she really is.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/aug/14/donald-trump-prosecutor-fulton-county-georgia-district-attorney-fani-willis"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Read the Guardian\u8217\'20\'19s full profile of Willis here. }}}\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/aug/14/donald-trump-prosecutor-fulton-county-georgia-district-attorney-fani-willis"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \u8216\'20\'18He\u8217\'20\'19s going to be very surprised\u8217\'20\'19: Georgia DA Fani Willis prepares to face off with Trump}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.44pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.23pm BST\par \par \uc2 The district attorney\u8217\'20\'19s office in Georgia has spent more than two years investigating whether \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  and his allies interfered in the 2020 election in Georgia, including impaneling a special grand jury that made it more straightforward to compel evidence from recalcitrant witnesses.\par \par \uc2 Unlike in the federal system, grand juries in the state of Georgia need to already be considering an indictment when they subpoena documents and testimony. By using a special grand jury, prosecutors can collect evidence without the pressure of having to file charges.\par \par \uc2 The special grand jury in the Trump investigation heard evidence for roughly seven months and recommended indictments of more than a dozen people including the former president himself, its forewoman strongly suggested in interviews with multiple news outlets.\par \par \uc2 Trump\u8217\'20\'19s legal team sought last month to invalidate the work of the special grand jury and have the Fulton county district attorney, \uc2 Fani Willis\uc2 , disqualified from proceedings, but the Georgia supreme court rejected the motion, ruling that Trump lacked \u8220\'20\'1Ceither the facts or the law necessary to mandate Ms Willis\u8217\'20\'19s disqualification\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 From his Bedminster club in New Jersey, where Trump spends his summers, the former president unleashed a wave of personal attacks against Willis ahead of what would be his fourth indictment after most recently being charged by special counsel Jack Smith with conspiring to subvert the 2020 election.\par \par \uc2 Trump posted on his Truth Social platform that Willis was \u8220\'20\'1Cracist\u8221\'20\'1D and treated gang members with \u8220\'20\'1Ckid gloves\u8221\'20\'1D \u8211\'20\'13 two accusations without any merit, especially given her office last week prosecuted members of the PDE gang in Atlanta with a Rico charge and street gang terrorism.\par \par \uc2 Fulton County District Attorney \uc2 Fani Willis\uc2 . Photograph: John Bazemore/AP\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.14pm BST\par \par \uc2 In the weeks after the 2020 presidential election, \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  and his allies kicked off an aggressive pressure campaign in an attempt to overturn the election results in six swing states where certified results declared \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  the winner.\par \par \uc2 Nowhere was the effort more acute than in Georgia, which became the consuming focus of the former president and his allies, according to a \uc2 Washington Post{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.washingtonpost.com/national-security/interactive/2023/trump-georgia-election-investigation/?itid=ap_amygardner"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 report }}}\uc2  today. Those close to Trump pushed state officials to identify fraud that would cast Biden\u8217\'20\'19s victory in doubt, it writes.\par \par \uc2 In the process, they personally targeted individual election workers with false claims of cheating, unleashing waves of threats, and amplified conspiracy theories about rigged machines that persist today. In the end, after Trump sought to use every lever of power to overturn the results, top state Republicans stood in his way, refusing to buckle under the pressure.\par \par \uc2 Some of the most fantastical claims of fraud came directly from Trump and his allies, \u8220\'20\'1Cwho amplified baseless accusations on conservative media and unleashed new waves of outlandish tips from rank-and-file Republicans\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 The former president\u8217\'20\'19s accusations also turned election workers in Georgia and other states into targets of harassment and threats.\par \par \uc2 They spread false claims that thousands of mail ballots should be discarded because of questionable signatures, that a mother-daughter team of election workers in Atlanta had triple-tallied counterfeit votes, that voting machines had been programmed to flip votes from one candidate to another.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.59pm BST\par \par \uc2 What charges could \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  face in Georgia election case?\par \par \uc2 For the purposes of the Trump case, prosecutors in Georgia will be required to show an \u8220\'20\'1Cinterrelated pattern of activity by and through the [public] office\u8221\'20\'1D predicated on at least two \u8220\'20\'1Cqualifying\u8221\'20\'1D or predicate crimes drawn from a list of specific statutes.\par \par \uc2 The prosecutors on the Trump case have developed evidence of a pattern of racketeering activity that could lead to a Rico charge based on predicates of influencing witnesses and computer trespass, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/jul/21/georgia-trump-charges-fraud-election-2020"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the Guardian has previously reported}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Among the election law charges that prosecutors have been examining: criminal solicitation to commit election fraud through seeking a public or political officer to fail to perform duties and seeking to destroy, deface or delay the delivery of ballots; and conspiracy to commit election fraud.\par \par \uc2 The prosecutors have also developed evidence for the previously unreported state election law charges of intentional interference with performance of election duties, the people said, as well as general criminal solicitation, which is not part of the Georgia election law statutes.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.51pm BST\par \par \uc2 In anticipation of charges against \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  and his allies related to his efforts to overturn the 2020 election results in Georgia, local law enforcement last week started to increase security around the building that contains the Fulton county district attorney\u8217\'20\'19s office and Georgia superior court, closing off roads and installing temporary barricades.\par \par \uc2 The district attorney, \uc2 Fani Willis\uc2 , had instructed most of her staff to work remotely through the first weeks of August as a safety precaution, and the public area inside the building for days has been taken over by deputies from the Fulton county sheriff\u8217\'20\'19s office.\par \par \uc2 Fulton County Sheriff officers block off a street in front of the Fulton County Courthouse in Atlanta, Georgia. Photograph: Joe Raedle/Getty Images A Fulton County Sheriff K-9 officer secures the area around the Fulton County Courthouse in Atlanta, Georgia. Photograph: Joe Raedle/Getty Images\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.39pm BST\par \par \uc2 Georgia prosecutors prepare to face off with \uc2 Donald Trump\par \par \uc2 Good morning, US politics blog readers. The Fulton county district attorney investigating \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s efforts to overturn the 2020 election results in Georgia is {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/aug/14/donald-trump-charges-georgia-2020-us-election-overturn-interference"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 expected to seek multiple charges}}}\uc2  against more than a dozen defendants, including the former president, this week.\par \par \uc2 The timeline for when the district attorney, \uc2 Fani Willis\uc2 , would present evidence to a grand jury came into sharper relief over the weekend after prosecutors summoned the former Georgia lieutenant governor, Geoff Duncan, and reporter George Chidi to testify on Tuesday.\par \par \uc2 The presentation is {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/aug/08/trump-2020-election-fulton-county-charges-next-week"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 expected to take two days}}}\uc2 , to a grand jury that meets Mondays and Tuesdays. In Georgia, it is typical for prosecutors to ask a grand jury to return indictments the same day. The notifications are the clearest indication that the prosecutors intend to charge the former president this week.\par \par \uc2 Prosecutors have identified roughly seven statutes of the Georgia state criminal code \u8211\'20\'13 including a racketeering charge, election law crimes as well as other non-election law crimes \u8211\'20\'13 with which to charge more than a dozen defendants in a sprawling indictment, the Guardian {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/aug/14/donald-trump-charges-georgia-2020-us-election-overturn-interference"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reported today,}}}\uc2  citing sources.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s what else we\u8217\'20\'19re watching today:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 10.30am Eastern time:President \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  will depart Rehoboth Beach, Delaware, for the White House.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 1pm: Biden and vice president \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  will have lunch.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 3pm.White House press secretary \uc2 Karine Jean-Pierre\uc2  will brief the press.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The House and Senate are out.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 1.43pm BST\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020230814ej8e001ed\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
