\par\par \uc2 World news\par \b \uc2 Girl, 13, gives birth after she was raped and denied  \highlight22\uc2 abortion \highlight\uc2  in Mississippi\b0\par\par\uc2 Lauren Aratani \par \uc2 949 \uc2 words\par \uc2 14 August 2023\par 20:14 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 The nearest \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  clinic \u8211\'20\'13 in Chicago \u8211\'20\'13 was too far away and too expensive for her mother to provide her with the procedure\par \par \uc2 A 13-year-old girl in Mississippi gave birth to a boy after she was raped as well as impregnated by a stranger \u8211\'20\'13 and then was unable to get an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , according to a Time magazine {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://time.com/6303701/a-rape-in-mississippi/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 report}}}\uc2  published on Monday.\par \par \uc2 The mother of the girl, who uses the pseudonym Ashley in the report, was looking to get an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  for her daughter but was told the closest {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/abortion"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22 }}}\uc2  provider was in Chicago \u8211\'20\'13 a drive of more than nine hours from their home in Clarksdale, Mississippi.\par \par \uc2 Ashley\u8217\'20\'19s mother, referred to as Regina in the report, told Time that the cost of getting an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  in Chicago was too expensive when considering the price of travel, taking time off work and getting the \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  for her daughter.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI don\u8217\'20\'19t have the funds for all this,\u8221\'20\'1D Regina told Time.\par \par \uc2 The report is the latest in a series of horrific personal accounts that have surfaced after the \uc2 US supreme court\uc2  overturned the nationwide \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access rights which had been established by the Roe v Wade precedent. Since the decision, titled Dobbs v Jackson Women\u8217\'20\'19s Health Organization, 14 state laws banning \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  have gone into effect, according to the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://reproductiverights.org/maps/abortion-laws-by-state/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Center for Reproductive Rights}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The women\u8217\'20\'19s health clinic that was at the center of the case was the last \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  provider in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/mississippi"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Mississippi}}}\uc2  until it closed last summer after the Dobbs decision.\par \par \uc2 Last summer, just a week after the ruling, a local newspaper in Ohio {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/jul/03/ohio-indiana-abortion-rape-victim"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reported}}}\uc2  that a 10-year-old who was raped had to travel to Indiana for an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  because of restrictions in her state. A man was found {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2023/jul/06/nine-year-old-child-rape-victim-abortion-indiana-ohio-life-sentence"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 guilty}}}\uc2  last month of raping and impregnating the girl in that case, and he received a sentence of life imprisonment.\par \par \uc2 Other stories detail how women {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.npr.org/2023/05/22/1177425651/texas-women-sue-abortion"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 nearly died}}}\uc2  because doctors had to wait until their life was at risk to perform an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  \u8211\'20\'13 or that many women now have to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/sep/14/louisiana-woman-skull-less-fetus-new-york-abortion"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 travel long distances}}}\uc2  to get any kind of reproductive healthcare. An {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.pbs.org/newshour/politics/a-year-after-fall-of-roe-v-wade-25-million-women-live-in-states-with-abortion-bans-or-restrictions"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 estimated}}}\uc2  25 million women ages 15 to 33 live in states that have \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  restrictions.\par \par \uc2 With respect to Monday\u8217\'20\'19s Time report, Ashley discovered she was pregnant after her mother took her to the hospital for uncontrollable vomiting. Regina noticed that Ashley was behaving differently, staying in her room when she used to enjoy going outside to record TikTok dances. Upon receiving bloodwork showing Ashley was pregnant, the hospital contacted the police.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWhat have you been doing?\u8221\'20\'1D a nurse asked Ashley at that time, according to the report. The hospital ultimately directed Ashley to the Clarksdale Women\u8217\'20\'19s Clinic, which provides OB-GYN services. The clinic did not respond to requests from the Guardian for comment.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt was surreal for her,\u8221\'20\'1D Dr Erica Balthrop, Ashley\u8217\'20\'19s physician, told Time. \u8220\'20\'1CShe just had no clue.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Before Dobbs, Balthrop could have directed Regina to a Memphis \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  clinic that was a 90-minute drive north, or to Jackson Women\u8217\'20\'19s Health, which is a 2.5-hour drive south. But Mississippi \u8211\'20\'13 along with all the states surrounding it \u8211\'20\'13 has banned \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Mississippi, along with many other states that also ban abortions, technically make exceptions for when the pregnancy is from rape or is life-threatening. But abortions granted under these exceptions are {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.kff.org/womens-health-policy/issue-brief/a-review-of-exceptions-in-state-abortions-bans-implications-for-the-provision-of-abortion-services/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 extremely rare}}}\uc2  and poorly tracked.\par \par \uc2 In January, the \uc2 New York Times{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/interactive/2023/01/21/us/abortion-ban-exceptions.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reported}}}\uc2  that Mississippi made two exceptions since the state\u8217\'20\'19s \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban went into effect. The state requires that a rape be reported to law enforcement in order to qualify for a legal \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Two out of three sexual assault cases in the US are not reported to the police, according to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.google.com/search?q=rainn&oq=rainn&aqs=chrome..69i57j46i199i433i465i512j46i131i433i512j0i131i433i512j46i512j69i60l3.1063j1j4&sourceid=chrome&ie=UTF-8"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Rainn}}}\uc2 , or the Rape, Abuse & Incest National Network, an anti-sexual assault nonprofit. Even if an exception is made, a person must travel out of their state to get an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  procedure if their state bans it.\par \par \uc2 The laws exacerbate longstanding health inequalities in Mississippi, where Black women are four times more likely to die from pregnancy-related complications compared with white women, according to the state\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://msdh.ms.gov/page/resources/19612.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 health department}}}\uc2 . According to the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.guttmacher.org/report/characteristics-us-abortion-patients-2014"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Guttmacher Institute}}}\uc2 , 60% of women who seek abortions are people of color and about half live below the federal poverty line.\par \par \uc2 Regina said she filed a complaint with the Clarksdale police department after she learned Ashley was pregnant. She told Time that her daughter ultimately opened up about what happened: a man came into their front yard while she was making TikToks outside while her uncle and sibling were inside and assaulted her. Ashley said she did not know who the man was and that no one witnessed the attack.\par \par \uc2 The police department confirmed to Time that a report had been filed. But the agency declined to comment publicly on the case since it involved a minor.\par \par \uc2 After 39 weeks of pregnancy, Ashley gave birth to a boy, whom they nicknamed Peanut. Ashley told Time the birth was \u8220\'20\'1Cpainful\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThis situation hurts the most because it was an innocent child doing what children do, playing outside, and it was my child,\u8221\'20\'1D Regina told Time. \u8220\'20\'1CIt still hurts, and is going to always hurt.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Information and support for anyone affected by rape or sexual abuse issues is available from the following organisations. In the US, Rainn offers support on 800-656-4673. In the UK, Rape Crisis offers support on 0808 500 2222. In Australia, support is available at 1800Respect (1800 737 732). Other international helplines can be found at ibiblio.org/rcip/internl.html\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020230814ej8e002bi\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
