\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Trump investigation: special counsel Jack Smith obtained search warrant for \uc2 Twitter\uc2  account \u8211\'20\'13 as it happened\b0\par\par\uc2 L\u233\'00\'E9onie Chao-Fong (now) and Maya Yang (earlier) \par \uc2 7,471 \uc2 words\par \uc2 11 August 2023\par 09:03 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 This blog has now closed. Read our latest story here\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.02pm BST\par \par \uc2 Closing summary\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s a recap of today\u8217\'20\'19s developments:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The US special counsel who is investigating \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  obtained a search warrant for the former president\u8217\'20\'19s \uc2 Twitter\uc2  account, and the social media platform delayed complying, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/aug/09/twitter-fined-contempt-trump-case"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a court filing }}}\uc2  on Wednesday showed. The delay in compliance prompted a federal judge to hold \uc2 Twitter\uc2  in contempt and fine it $350,000, the filing showed.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 A previously unseen internal memo from the 2020 Trump campaign {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/aug/09/previously-unseen-memo-details-trump-plot-subvert-election-results"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 describes in detail}}}\uc2  the plot by \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  and his lawyers to subvert election results in six states, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/2023/08/08/us/politics/trump-indictment-fake-electors-memo.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 according to a copy}}}\uc2  obtained by \uc2 The New York Times\uc2 . The {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://int.nyt.com/data/documenttools/chesebro-dec-6-memo/ce55d6abd79c2c71/full.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 memo}}}\uc2  describes a three-pronged plan to prevent Congress from certifying \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s victory on 6 January 2020, that involved coordinating with Republican electors and campaign attorneys in six states, as well as \uc2 Mike Pence\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The Fulton county district attorney investigating \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s efforts to overturn the 2020 election results in the state of Georgia is {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/aug/09/trump-secret-memo-2020-election-indictments-biden-energy-live-updates?page=with:block-64d3dc568f082ff528844691#block-64d3dc568f082ff528844691"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 expected to seek more than a dozen indictments}}}\uc2  when she presents her case before a grand jury next week, according to a report. The prosecutors in the office of district attorney \uc2 Fani Willis\uc2  completed its internal reviews for criminal charges in the Trump case weeks ago, and could present evidence to a grand jury and ask it to return indictments as early as next Tuesday, the \uc2 Guardian{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/aug/08/trump-2020-election-fulton-county-charges-next-week"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  reported }}}\uc2  on Tuesday.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The judge presiding over \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s election subversion case, US district judge \uc2 Tanya Chutkan\uc2 , has s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/aug/09/trump-secret-memo-2020-election-indictments-biden-energy-live-updates?page=with:block-64d39d628f082ff5288442b8#block-64d39d628f082ff5288442b8"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 et a date for a hearing}}}\uc2  on a proposed protective order by prosecutors. The protective order, if granted, will govern how evidence is handled in the case. The order, requested last Friday by special counsel Jack Smith \u8217\'20\'19s team, asks for Trump to be prohibited from publicly sharing evidence in the case during the discovery phase.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The California US senator \uc2 Dianne Feinstein\uc2 , 90, was hospitalized on Tuesday evening {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/aug/09/dianne-feinstein-hospital-fall"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 after suffering a fall }}}\uc2  in her home, a spokesperson said. \u8220\'20\'1CSenator Feinstein briefly went to the hospital yesterday afternoon as a precaution after a minor fall in her home,\u8221\'20\'1D a spokesperson said in a statement. \u8220\'20\'1CAll of her scans were clear and she returned home.\u8221\'20\'1D At 90, Feinstein is the oldest serving US senator.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2 , the Republican governor of Florida, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/aug/09/desantis-suspends-orlando-democrat-prosecutor-monique-worrell"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 suspended the top prosecutor}}}\uc2  in Orlando on Wednesday, claiming \u8220\'20\'1Cdereliction of duty\u8221\'20\'1D on crime. In {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wesh.com/article/desantis-monique-worrell-suspension/44774085"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 return}}}\uc2 , the prosecutor said DeSantis, a candidate for the Republican presidential nomination, was a \u8220\'20\'1Cweak dictator\u8221\'20\'1D acting undemocratically and for political reasons.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 A respected conservative judge who advised the former Republican vice-president \uc2 Mike Pence\uc2  not to attempt to overturn the 2020 election {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/aug/09/anti-trump-judge-conservative-republican-party"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 believes }}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/aug/09/anti-trump-judge-conservative-republican-party"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Donald Trump}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/aug/09/anti-trump-judge-conservative-republican-party"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  has destroyed the Republican party. }}}\uc2  \u8220\'20\'1CAmerican democracy simply cannot function without two equally healthy and equally strong political parties,\u8221\'20\'1D J Michael Luttig{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cnn.com/2023/08/09/politics/michael-luttig-conservative-judge-republicans-cnntv/index.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 told CNN on Wednesday}}}\uc2 . \u8220\'20\'1CSo today, in my view, there is no Republican party to counter the Democratic party in the country.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.36pm BST\par \par \uc2 J Michael Luttig{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cnn.com/2023/08/09/politics/michael-luttig-conservative-judge-republicans-cnntv/index.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 told CNN}}}\uc2  :\par \par \uc2 A political party is a collection and assemblage of individuals who share a set of beliefs and principles and policy views about the United States of America. Today, there is no such shared set of beliefs and values and principles or even policy views as within the Republican party for America.\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , he said, was a danger \u8220\'20\'1Cmore so today\u8221\'20\'1D than last year, when Luttig testified to the House January 6 committee.\par \par \uc2 A respected conservative judge who was {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/2006/05/10/washington/11luttigcnd.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 considered}}}\uc2  for the supreme court under \uc2 George W Bush\uc2 , Luttig made a tremendous impact with his January 6 testimony.\par \par \uc2 Speaking on primetime television, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/video/2022/jun/16/ex-federal-judge-luttig-pence-obeying-trump-constitutional-crisis-video"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Luttig said}}}\uc2  :\par \par \uc2 I believe that had Vice-President Pence obeyed the orders from his president \u8230\'20\'26 and declared \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  the next president of the United States \u8230\'20\'26 [he] would have plunged America into what I believe would have been tantamount to a revolution, within a constitutional crisis.\par \par \uc2 On Wednesday, Luttig {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cnn.com/2023/08/09/politics/michael-luttig-conservative-judge-republicans-cnntv/index.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 also told CNN}}}\uc2  he did not think Trump could avoid conviction for election subversion.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe evidence is overwhelming that the former president knew full well that he had lost the election,\u8221\'20\'1D he said.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 8.37pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.23pm BST\par \par \uc2 A respected conservative judge who advised the former Republican vice-president \uc2 Mike Pence\uc2  not to attempt to overturn the 2020 election believes \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  has destroyed the Republican party.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CAmerican democracy simply cannot function without two equally healthy and equally strong political parties,\u8221\'20\'1D \uc2 J Michael Luttig{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cnn.com/2023/08/09/politics/michael-luttig-conservative-judge-republicans-cnntv/index.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 told CNN on Wednesday}}}\uc2 . \u8220\'20\'1CSo today, in my view, there is no Republican party to counter the Democratic party in the country.\par \par \uc2 And for that reason, American democracy is in grave peril.\par \par \uc2 American democracy has by most measures been in grave peril since 6 January 2021, the day Pence, as vice-president, took Luttig\u8217\'20\'19s advice and refused to attempt to block congressional certification of \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s election win.\par \par \uc2 A mob Trump told to \u8220\'20\'1Cfight like hell\u8221\'20\'1D attacked the Capitol, some chanting for Pence to be hanged. The effort failed but nine deaths have been linked to the riot, including law enforcement suicides. More than a thousand people have been charged and hundreds convicted, some with seditious conspiracy.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.05pm BST\par \par \uc2 A cousin of Elvis Presley is the Democratic candidate for governor in Mississippi, after winning his primary unopposed on Tuesday.\par \par \uc2 The general election will be held on 7 November. The Democrat, \uc2 Brandon Presley\uc2 , said he would advocate for people who struggle to make ends meet. He will face the current Republican governor, \uc2 Tate Reeves\uc2 , who defeated two first-time candidates, John Witcher, a physician, and David Hardigree, a military veteran.\par \par \uc2 Mississippi is one of three states holding races for governor this year. Despite Republicans holding all statewide offices for 20 years, the \uc2 Democratic Governors Association\uc2  chair, \uc2 Phil Murphy\uc2  of New Jersey, has predicted a Democrat could win.\par \par \uc2 In his hometown, Nettleton, Presley took the stage at his victory party to See See Rider, a song Elvis Presley often used as walk-on music. The candidate said he would not sing, though.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe\u8217\'20\'19re trying to get votes,\u8221\'20\'1D Presley said. \u8220\'20\'1CWe\u8217\'20\'19re not trying to lose them.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/aug/09/brandon-presley-elvis-cousin-democrat-mississippi-governor"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Read the full story here.}}}\par \par \uc2 Brandon Presley\uc2  at the Neshoba County Fair in Philadelphia, Mississippi on 27 July 2023. Photograph: Rogelio V Solis/AP\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/aug/09/brandon-presley-elvis-cousin-democrat-mississippi-governor"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Elvis Presley\u8217\'20\'19s cousin is Democratic candidate for Mississippi governor}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 8.05pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.50pm BST\par \par \uc2 The US special counsel who is investigating \uc2 Donald Trump{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/aug/09/trump-secret-memo-2020-election-indictments-biden-energy-live-updates?filterKeyEvents=false&page=with:block-64d3c1688f0884de6f41780f#block-64d3c1688f0884de6f41780f"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 obtained a search warrant }}}\uc2  for the former president\u8217\'20\'19s \uc2 Twitter\uc2  account, and the social media platform delayed complying, a court filing on Wednesday showed.\par \par \uc2 The delay in compliance prompted a federal judge to hold \uc2 Twitter\uc2  in contempt and fine it $350,000, the filing showed.\par \par \uc2 The filing says the team of US special counsel Jack Smith obtained a search warrant in January directing \uc2 Twitter\uc2 , which recently rebranded to X, to produce \u8220\'20\'1Cdata and records\u8221\'20\'1D related to Trump\u8217\'20\'19s \uc2 Twitter\uc2  account as well as a non-disclosure agreement prohibiting \uc2 Twitter\uc2  from disclosing the search warrant.\par \par \uc2 The filing says prosecutors got the search warrant after a court \u8220\'20\'1Cfound probable cause to search the \uc2 Twitter\uc2  account for evidence of criminal offenses\u8221\'20\'1D. The court found that disclosing the warrant could risk that Trump would \u8220\'20\'1Cwould seriously jeopardize the ongoing investigation\u8221\'20\'1D by giving him \u8220\'20\'1Can opportunity to destroy evidence, change patterns of behavior\u8221\'20\'1D, according to the filing.\par \par \uc2 Twitter\uc2  objected to the non-disclosure agreement, saying four days after the compliance deadline that it would not produce any of the account information, according to the ruling. The judges wrote that \uc2 Twitter\uc2  \u8220\'20\'1Cdid not question the validity of the search warrant\u8221\'20\'1D but argued that the non-disclosure agreement was a violation of the first amendment and wanted the court to assess the legality of the agreement before it handed any information over.\par \par \uc2 The delay in compliance prompted a lower court to \uc2 Twitter\uc2  in contempt, and on Wednesday, the federal court in Washington upheld that decision.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.41pm BST\par \par \uc2 Fulton county prosecutors to seek more than a dozen indictments in Trump case - report\par \par \uc2 The Fulton county district attorney investigating \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s efforts to overturn the 2020 election results in the state of Georgia is expected to seek more than a dozen indictments when she presents her case before a grand jury next week, according to a report.\par \par \uc2 The prosecutors in the office of district attorney \uc2 Fani Willis\uc2  completed its internal reviews for criminal charges in the Trump case weeks ago, and could present evidence to a grand jury and ask it to return indictments as early as next Tuesday, the \uc2 Guardian{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/aug/08/trump-2020-election-fulton-county-charges-next-week"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  reported }}}\uc2  on Tuesday.\par \par \uc2 Willis has been eyeing conspiracy and racketeering charges, which would allow her to bring more than a dozen indictments against multiple defendants, CNN {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://edition.cnn.com/2023/08/09/politics/trump-georgia-fani-willis-dozen-indictments/index.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reported, }}}\uc2  citing sources.\par \par \uc2 In the Trump investigation, prosecutors have developed evidence to pursue a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/jul/21/georgia-trump-charges-fraud-election-2020"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 sprawling racketeering case}}}\uc2  that is predicated on a statute about influencing witnesses and computer trespass by Trump operatives in Coffee county, the \uc2 Guardian\uc2  has previously reported.\par \par \uc2 The extent of Trump\u8217\'20\'19s legal jeopardy remains unclear. But the racketeering statute in Georgia is especially expansive and attempts to solicit or coerce certain activity \u8211\'20\'13 for instance, Trump\u8217\'20\'19s call to the secretary of state, \uc2 Brad Raffensperger\uc2  \u8211\'20\'13 could be included in the indictment.\par \par \uc2 The district attorney\u8217\'20\'19s office has also {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/jul/25/trump-georgia-investigation-fulton-county-prosecutors"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 weighed several state election law charges}}}\uc2 , including: criminal solicitation to commit election fraud and conspiracy to commit election fraud, as well as solicitation of a public or political officer to fail to perform their duties and solicitation to destroy, deface or remove ballots.\par \par \uc2 The district attorney\u8217\'20\'19s office has spent more than two years investigating whether Trump and his allies interfered in the 2020 election in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/state-of-georgia"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Georgia}}}\uc2 , including impaneling a special grand jury that made it more straightforward to compel evidence from recalcitrant witnesses.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.27pm BST\par \par \uc2 A group of LGBTQ+ veterans have filed a lawsuit against the defense department and defense secretary \uc2 Lloyd Austin\uc2  over their discharge status and the use of language that \u8220\'20\'1Cidentifies their actual or perceived sexual orientation as the reason for their discharge\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 The class action {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://static1.squarespace.com/static/64c94be754e1a62dc1a0d8c9/t/64d2e4c25ca281066283ffde/1691542722745/LGBTQ+Vets+-+Complaint.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  lawsuit}}}\uc2  was filed on Tuesday on behalf of five veterans in the US district court of the northern district of California.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CLGBTQ+ veterans are entitled to relief from the government\u8217\'20\'19s ongoing discrimination through the removal of separation narratives and codes that identify their sexual orientation, modification of codes that prevent re-enlistment, and upgrades to their discharge statuses as needed,\u8221\'20\'1D the lawsuit said.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CRequiring LGBTQ+ veterans to first bear the stigma and discriminatory effects of carrying indicators of sexual orientation on their [discharge papers] and then navigate a broken record correction process to seek resolution violates their constitutional rights to equal protection, informational privacy, property, and due process protected by the Fourteenth and Fifth Amendments to the US Constitution,\u8221\'20\'1D it added.\par \par \uc2 The lawsuit comes 13 years after the repeal of \u8220\'20\'1CDon\u8217\'20\'19t ask, don\u8217\'20\'19t tell\u8221\'20\'1D in the military.\par \par \uc2 Despite its repeal, the lawsuit alleges that the government has taken no steps to \u8220\'20\'1Ccorrect this discrimination systematically.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CInstead, it directs LGBTQ+ veterans to a pre-existing record correction and discharge upgrade process to individually request modification of their records. This widely criticized process requires veterans to initiate lengthy individual actions (including the extended process of obtaining military records) and demands that veterans prove discrimination occurred, even though the government has already conceded both the discriminatory nature of its policies and the pernicious effects,\u8221\'20\'1D it said.\par \par \uc2 \u8226\'20\'22 This post was amended on 10 August 2023 to clarify language related to the nature of the complaint by the LBTQ+ veterans.\par \par \uc2 On July 26, 2017, after a series of tweets by President \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , which proposed to ban transgender people from military service, thousands of New Yorkers took the streets of in opposition. Thousands of transgender soldiers are currently serving in all branches of the United States Armed forces. Photograph: Pacific Press/LightRocket/Getty Images\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 10.03am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.04pm BST\par \par \uc2 J. Michael Luttig\uc2 , a prominent retired judge and adviser to former vice president \uc2 Mike Pence\uc2  said that \u8220\'20\'1Cthere is no Republican party.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 In an {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://edition.cnn.com/2023/08/09/politics/michael-luttig-conservative-judge-republicans-cnntv/index.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 interview}}}\uc2  with CNN on Wednesday, Luttig, who has issued harsh criticisms towards \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  over his alleged involvement in the 2021 Capitol Hill riots and advised Pence to not overturn the 2020 election results, said:\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CAmerican democracy simply cannot function without two equally healthy and equally strong political parties. So today, in my view, there is no Republican party to counter the Democratic party in the country\u8230\'20\'26And for that reason, American democracy is in grave peril.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Luttig, who in June published an op-ed in the \uc2 New York Times\uc2  and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/2023/06/25/opinion/trump-republican-party.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 criticized}}}\uc2  \u8220\'20\'1CRepublican\u8217\'20\'19s\u8217\'20\'19 spineless support\u8221\'20\'1D towards Trump, went on to criticize the Republican party, saying:\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CA political party is a collection and assemblage of individuals who share a set of beliefs and principles and policy views about the United States of America. Today, there is no such shared set of beliefs and values and principles or even policy views as within the Republican Party for America.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Luttig was a the former judge on the 4th US circuit court of appeals and was a key witness in the January 6 hearings.\par \par \uc2 Last year, during his {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=pTDQDwUyeBg&ab_channel=PBSNewsHour"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 testimony,}}}\uc2  he said efforts to overturn the election results were \u8220\'20\'1Ctantamount to a revolution.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 7.08pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.45pm BST\par \par \uc2 Former GOP operative Anton Lazzaro has been sentenced to 21 years in prison following his conviction of giving teenage girls gifts, alcohol and money in return for sex.\par \par \uc2 Lazzaro was handed the sentencing on Wednesday after he was found guilty in March of seven counts involving \u8220\'20\'1Ccommercial sex acts\u8221\'20\'1D with five 15 to 16-year old girls in 2020. Lazzaro was 30 years old at the time.\par \par \uc2 The Associated Press reports US district judge Patrick Schiltz saying that Lazzaro only showed sympathy to two individuals throughout the trial \u8211\'20\'13 "to himself and \uc2 Jeffrey Epstein\uc2 ,\u8221\'20\'1D the late disgraced financier and convicted sex offender.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s almost as if Mr. Lazzaro set up a sex trafficking assembly line,\u8221\'20\'1D Schiltz said, adding that he was struck by the \u8220\'20\'1Csoulless, almost mechanical nature\u8221\'20\'1D of how he took advantage of the girls.\par \par \uc2 On Wednesday, one of the victims spoke in court, saying, \u8220\'20\'1CI still see him in my nightmares, in my panic attacks, in men in their thirties. \u8230\'20\'26 Putting Tony behind bars will save so many girls.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 A mother of another different victim told Lazzaro, \u8220\'20\'1CThe damage you caused my daughter, mentally and emotionally, you didn\u8217\'20\'19t just cause that damage to her. You caused it to me and my family and all these victims and all of their families,\u8221\'20\'1D she said. \u8220\'20\'1CYou stand up here and you don\u8217\'20\'19t even care. You\u8217\'20\'19re justifying your actions. \u8230\'20\'26 I hope you rot in hell,\u8221\'20\'1D the Associated Press reports.\par \par \uc2 This booking photo released by Sherburne County Jail shows Anton Lazzaro. The formerly well-connected GOP donor convicted of giving teenage girls gifts, alcohol and money in exchange for sex was sentenced Wednesday, Aug. 9, 2023, to 21 years in prison. Photograph: Sherburne County Jail/AP\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.29pm BST\par \par \uc2 Prosecutors seeking to obtain a search warrant for \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s \uc2 Twitter\uc2  account \u8220\'20\'1Cfaced difficulties\u8221\'20\'1D when it first attempted to serve \uc2 Twitter\uc2  with the warrant and nondisclosure order, according to the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.documentcloud.org/documents/23903693/redactedopinion.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  court documents. }}}\par \par \uc2 The filing says that \uc2 Twitter\uc2  objected to producing any of the account information on 1 February 2023, four days after the compliance deadline. The filing states:\par \par \uc2 Twitter\uc2  informed the government that it would not comply with the warrant until the district court assessed the legality of the nondisclosure order.\par \par \uc2 A day later, \uc2 Twitter\uc2  filed a motion to vacate or modify the nondisclosure order, it says.\par \par \uc2 In its motion challenging the nondisclosure order, \uc2 Twitter\uc2  argued that the order violated the company\u8217\'20\'19s First Amendment right to communicate with its subscriber, former President Trump. The company asserted that compliance with the warrant before resolution of the motion to vacate or modify the nondisclosure order would preclude the former President from asserting executive privilege to shield communications made using his \uc2 Twitter\uc2  account.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.14pm BST\par \par \uc2 According to newly revealed {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.documentcloud.org/documents/23903693/redactedopinion.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  court documents}}}\uc2 , \uc2 Twitter\uc2  was barred from notifying anyone that a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/aug/09/trump-secret-memo-2020-election-indictments-biden-energy-live-updates?page=with:block-64d3c1688f0884de6f41780f#block-64d3c1688f0884de6f41780f"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 search warrant had been obtained}}}\uc2  for \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s \uc2 Twitter\uc2  account.\par \par \uc2 The special counsel\u8217\'20\'19s office sought the warrant in January 2023 as part of its investigation into the former president\u8217\'20\'19s efforts to overturn the 2020 presidential election.\par \par \uc2 The filing says special counsel Jack Smith obtained a search warrant directing \uc2 Twitter\uc2  to produce \u8220\'20\'1Cdata and records\u8221\'20\'1D related to Trump\u8217\'20\'19s \uc2 Twitter\uc2  account. The filing says the court \u8220\'20\'1Cfound probable cause to search the \uc2 Twitter\uc2  account for evidence of criminal offenses\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 The court \u8220\'20\'1Cfound that there were \u8216\'20\'18reasonable grounds to believe\u8217\'20\'19 that disclosing the warrant to former President Trump \u8216\'20\'18would seriously jeopardize the ongoing investigation\u8217\'20\'19 by giving him \u8216\'20\'18an opportunity to destroy evidence, change patterns of behavior, [or] notify confederates\u8217\'20\'19\u8221\'20\'1D, the filing writes.\par \par \uc2 The district court also concluded the non-disclosure order was necessary because it \u8220\'20\'1Cfound reason to believe that the former President would \u8216\'20\'18flee from prosecution\u8217\'20\'19\u8221\'20\'1D, it says.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 6.19pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.54pm BST\par \par \uc2 Special counsel Jack Smith obtained search warrant for \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s \uc2 Twitter\uc2  account\par \par \uc2 Special counsel Jack Smith sought and obtained a search warrant for \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s \uc2 Twitter\uc2  account as part of his criminal investigation of the former president, according to newly revealed {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.documentcloud.org/documents/23903693/redactedopinion.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  court documents.}}}\par \par \uc2 Twitter\uc2 , now known as X, initially delayed production of the materials required by the search warrant, which resulted in a federal judge holding the company in contempt and levying a $350,000 fine.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 7.45pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.46pm BST\par \par \uc2 Democratic Senate majority leader \uc2 Chuck Schumer\uc2  released a statement following the news that California senator \uc2 Dianne Feinstein\uc2 , 90, was {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/aug/09/dianne-feinstein-hospital-fall"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 hospitalized on Tuesday evening after suffering a fall in her home.}}}\par \par \uc2 Schumer said:\par \par \uc2 I spoke with Sen. Feinstein this morning. She said she suffered no injuries and briefly went to the hospital as a precaution. I\u8217\'20\'19m glad she is back home now and is doing well.\par \par \uc2 From HuffPost\u8217\'20\'19s Igor Bobic:\par \par \uc2 enltrSchumer statement: \u8220\'20\'1CI spoke with Sen. Feinstein this morning. She said she suffered no injuries and briefly went to the hospital as a precaution. I\u8217\'20\'19m glad she is back home now and is doing well.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Igor Bobic (@igorbobic) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/igorbobic/status/1689311750737338381?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 August 9, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.34pm BST\par \par \uc2 Rudy Giuliani\uc2  claims \u8216\'20\'18dog ate my homework\u8217\'20\'19 in \uc2 Smartmatic\uc2  case, lawyers say\par \par \uc2 A voting machine company behind a $2.7bn defamation lawsuit over lies about the 2020 election said \uc2 Rudy Giuliani\uc2  was using excuses like \u8220\'20\'1Cthe dog ate my homework\u8221\'20\'1D to avoid the discovery process.\par \par \uc2 Lawyers for Smartmartic wrote:\par \par \uc2 The dog ate my homework.\u8217\'20\'19 \u8216\'20\'18I have to wash my hair.\u8217\'20\'19 \u8216\'20\'18I can\u8217\'20\'19t go out, I\u8217\'20\'19m sick.\u8217\'20\'19 Since the dawn of time, people have made up excuses to avoid doing things they do not want to do.\par \par \uc2 This is exactly what Giuliani has done here.\par \par \uc2 The former New York mayor turned personal attorney to \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , 79, is named alongside Fox News in the lawsuit, which follows a defamation suit Fox News settled for $787.5m with \uc2 Dominion Voting Systems\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 In the \uc2 Smartmatic\uc2  case, in Monday court filings {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://edition.cnn.com/2023/08/08/media/smartmatic-rudy-giuliani/index.html#:~:text=Smartmatic%20claims%20Giuliani%20only%20produced,have%20to%20wash%20my%20hair"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 first reported by CNN}}}\uc2 , lawyers expressed frustration over trying to get Giuliani to turn over relevant records.\par \par \uc2 They said:\par \par \uc2 For months, Giuliani has made up excuses to get out of his discovery obligations \u8230\'20\'26 To date, Giuliani has not produced a single non-public document responsive to the discovery requests \uc2 Smartmatic\uc2  issued 14 months ago.\par \par \uc2 The company asked a New York judge to force Giuliani to turn over materials.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 5.42pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.20pm BST\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights group \uc2 Naral Pro-Choice America\uc2  said in a statement after {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/aug/09/trump-secret-memo-2020-election-indictments-biden-energy-live-updates?page=with:block-64d3ba9a8f0884de6f4177ae#block-64d3ba9a8f0884de6f4177ae"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  Ohio voters rejected a proposal}}}\uc2  that would have made it considerably harder to amend the state constitution:\par \par \uc2 Ohioans\u8217\'20\'19 support for \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access and reproductive freedom was never in question. From defeating Issue 1 tonight to submitting nearly twice the amount of signatures needed to get a measure protecting \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access on the ballot in November, Ohio voters have made clear that they will settle for nothing less than reproductive freedom for all.\par \par \uc2 Senator \uc2 Sherrod Brown\uc2 , a Democrat facing what is expected to be one of the toughest re-election bids next year, also praised the defeat of the amendment.\par \par \uc2 enltrBy rejecting Issue 1, Ohioans rejected special interests and demanded that democracy remain where it belongs \u8212\'20\'14 in the hands of voters, not the rich and powerful.\par \par \uc2 That is what has always guided me. I am proud to stand with Ohioans in this fight.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 \uc2 Sherrod Brown\uc2  (@SherrodBrown) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/SherrodBrown/status/1689071920132599808?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 August 9, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 The issue underscores the continued political salience of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  since the supreme court overturned Roe v Wade last year. Campaigns linked to protecting \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights in politically competitive states, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/aug/03/kansas-abortion-vote-state-constitution"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 like a referendum Kansas}}}\uc2  and a supreme court race in Wisconsin, have been {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/apr/04/wisconsin-supreme-court-election-results"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 incredibly successful}}}\uc2 . \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights have prevailed in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nbcnews.com/politics/elections/ohio-issue-one-reject-loss-abortion-rights-ballot-measure-rcna98842"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 all seven states }}}\uc2  where they have been on the ballot since last year.\par \par \uc2 The rejection also comes as activists are drafting a constitutional amendment that would strip lawmakers of their power to draw district lines and turn it over to a citizen-led commission instead. Last year, Ohio Republicans ignored repeated orders from the supreme court to draw maps that were not severely distorted to their advantage.\par \par \uc2 The rejection is a major win for the One Person, One Vote campaign, a broad coalition of good-government, labor and environmental groups that aggressively campaigned across the state urging people to reject the amendment. The contest was expected to be a low-turnout midsummer affair, but turnout actually surged during the election. The result is also a blow to \uc2 Richard Uihlein\uc2 , a GOP megadonor, who spent millions trying to get the amendment to pass.\par \par \uc2 Rachael Belz, CEO of Ohio Citizen Action, which worked to reject the amendment, said:\par \par \uc2 When they forced Issue 1 on to the ballot, they awakened a sleeping giant and unleashed a movement. And that movement isn\u8217\'20\'19t going away tomorrow. It will continue to build and grow and to carry us through to victories in November and beyond. We thank Ohio voters for doing their homework and for going out to vote \u8216\'20\'18no\u8217\'20\'19 on Issue 1.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.13pm BST\par \par \uc2 Ohio voters reject measure in victory for \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights supporters\par \par \uc2 Ohio voters on Tuesday rejected a proposal that would have made it considerably harder to amend the state constitution in a major win for reproductive rights and democracy advocates in the state.\par \par \uc2 The result means that Ohio will keep its current process for amending the state constitution in place. The procedure first requires voters to collect a certain number of signatures from at least 44 of the state\u8217\'20\'19s 88 counties to send an amendment proposal to the ballot and then a simple majority to pass it.\par \par \uc2 Issue 1, the proposal under consideration, would have made both of those steps harder. It would have required voters to collect signatures in all 88 counties and then required a supermajority of 60% to pass it.\par \par \uc2 US president \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  said of the result: \u8220\'20\'1Cdemocracy won\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 It was the first time since 1926 that Ohio voters cast ballots on a proposed constitutional amendment in August. Republicans, who control the state legislature, rushed the measure to the ballot in an effort to make it harder to pass a referendum to protect \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights that\u8217\'20\'19s set for this fall.\par \par \uc2 With a little over half of the vote counted, the \u8220\'20\'1Cno\u8221\'20\'1D vote led 59% to 41%. A majority vote would have been needed to approve the amendment, which was not possible given votes left to be counted, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://apnews.com/article/ohio-abortion-rights-constitutional-amendment-special-election-227cde039f8d51723612878525164f1a"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the Associated Press projected}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.00pm BST\par \par \uc2 At 90, \uc2 Dianne Feinstein\uc2 , who was {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/aug/09/trump-secret-memo-2020-election-indictments-biden-energy-live-updates?filterKeyEvents=false&page=with:block-64d3a0fe8f082ff5288442d8#block-64d3a0fe8f082ff5288442d8"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 hospitalized on Tuesday evening}}}\uc2  after suffering a fall in her home, is the oldest serving US senator.\par \par \uc2 She has said she will retire at the end of her term next year. The race to succeed her is heating up, the former House intelligence chair Adam Schiff competing with two other representatives, \uc2 Katie Porter\uc2  and Barbara Lee.\par \par \uc2 But continued health problems have stoked {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/commentisfree/2023/apr/15/clinging-to-power-does-not-make-dianne-feinstein-a-feminist-hero"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 calls}}}\uc2  for Feinstein {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/may/29/dianne-feinstein-democrats-divided-health-questions"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 to step aside sooner}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Earlier this year, Feinstein was absent from Congress for nearly three months while suffering from shingles. Since her return, she has sometimes appeared frail and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/may/16/dianne-feinstein-says-hasnt-been-gone-from-senate"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 confused}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The Chronicle {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.sfchronicle.com/politics/article/feinstein-hospitalized-after-fall-18287088.php"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 said}}}\uc2  Feinstein had been due to attend an event celebrating the city\u8217\'20\'19s cable cars on 2 August, but had missed it after developing a cough.\par \par \uc2 The first woman to be mayor of San Francisco, Feinstein was {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.feinstein.senate.gov/public/index.cfm/biography"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 elected}}}\uc2  to the \uc2 US Senate\uc2  in 1992. Between 2017 and 2021, she led Democrats on the judiciary committee.\par \par \uc2 She is not the only prominent US politician to face questions about her age and health.\par \par \uc2 The 81-year-old Republican leader in the Senate, \uc2 Mitch McConnell\uc2 , has suffered a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/jul/27/mitch-mcconnell-freeze-press-conference-fall-age"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 number of falls}}}\uc2  and last month {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/jul/26/mitch-mcconnell-press-conference"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 froze during remarks to reporters}}}\uc2 , prompting both expressions of concern and calls for him to step down.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.53pm BST\par \par \uc2 Responding to her suspension by Florida governor \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2 , state attorney Monique Worrell said the move was \u8220\'20\'1Csimply a smokescreen\u8221\'20\'1D for DeSantis\u8217\'20\'19 \u8220\'20\'1Cfailing and disastrous presidential campaign\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Worrell said:\par \par \uc2 Under this tyranny, elected officials can be removed simply for political purposes and by a whim of the governor. No matter how you feel about me, you should not be OK with that.\par \par \uc2 enltr\u8220\'20\'1CThis is simply a smokescreen for \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2 ' failing and disastrous presidential campaign.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 State Attorney Monique Worrell (D) slams Gov. \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2  (R-FL) for suspending her from office {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/7RDZczg64W"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/7RDZczg64W}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 The Recount (@therecount) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/therecount/status/1689295628038193152?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 August 9, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.39pm BST\par \par \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2  suspends elected Florida state attorney Monique Worrell\par \par \uc2 Florida governor \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2  suspended the Orlando-area state attorney, Monique Worrell, accusing her of under-prosecuting criminals in her jurisdiction.\par \par \uc2 Worrell, a Democratic elected official who took office in 2021, was suspended for \u8220\'20\'1Cdereliction of duty\u8221\'20\'1D on crime, DeSantis announced at a press conference in Tallahassee.\par \par \uc2 An executive order signed by DeSantis and secretary of state Cord Byrd accused Worrell of \u8220\'20\'1Csystematically\u8221\'20\'1D allowing criminals to evade incarceration and pursuing lenient sentences and declining to prosecute certain charges.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CProsecutors do have a certain amount of discretion about what cases to bring and which cases to not,\u8221\'20\'1D DeSantis said.\par \par \uc2 But what this state attorney has done is abuse that discretion and effectively nullified certain laws in the state of Florida that breaches her duties that she owes to the people of Florida under our state constitution, and provides the basis for the suspension.\par \par \uc2 The decision marks the second time DeSantis has suspended a democratically elected prosecutor from office. Both have been Democrats.\par \par \uc2 Last year, the Florida governor suspended Hillsborough county state attorney, Andrew Warren, after Warren said he would not enforce state restrictions on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  or gender-related surgery.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 4.51pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.25pm BST\par \par \uc2 The {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/aug/09/trump-secret-memo-2020-election-indictments-biden-energy-live-updates?page=with:block-64d3ab498f0877b51bef9b72#block-64d3ab498f0877b51bef9b72"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 previously unseen internal memo}}}\uc2  from the 2020 Trump campaign describes a three-pronged plan to prevent Congress from certifying \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s victory on 6 January 2020, that involved coordinating with Republican electors and campaign attorneys in six states, as well as \uc2 Mike Pence\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 It also emphasized the importance of the participation by \u8220\'20\'1Call six states\u8221\'20\'1D and \u8220\'20\'1Cmessaging about this being a routine measure\u8221\'20\'1D as well as \u8220\'20\'1Clogistics\u8221\'20\'1D regarding what is now known as the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/aug/05/trump-fake-electors-georgia"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 fake electors scheme}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The letter was written by Kenneth Chesebro, an attorney associated with \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , and addressed to a Wisconsin lawyer, James R Troupis, the lead attorney for the Trump campaign in Wisconsin, who oversaw the fake electors scheme in his state.\par \par \uc2 Troupis filed a lawsuit in December 2020 asking the Wisconsin supreme court to throw out hundreds of thousands of absentee ballots, saying they violated voting requirements. The court ultimately rejected the lawsuit.\par \par \uc2 Chesebro wrote to Troupis that \u8220\'20\'1Cit seems feasible\u8221\'20\'1D the Trump campaign could subvert Biden\u8217\'20\'19s victory. His plan would \u8220\'20\'1Cforce the Members of Congress, the media, and the American people to focus on the substantive evidence of illegal election and counting activities in the six contested States, provided three things happen\u8221\'20\'1D. He then lays out those three steps, describing a plan in detail.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.20pm BST\par \par \uc2 Secret memo shows Trump campaign knew fake elector scheme was likely to fail\par \par \uc2 An {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/aug/09/trump-secret-memo-2020-election-indictments-biden-energy-live-updates?page=with:block-64d381948f0884de6f41747b#block-64d381948f0884de6f41747b"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  internal Trump campaign memo}}}\uc2  by Kenneth Chesebro, a lawyer allied with \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , reveals new details about how the former president and his team initiated the plan to interfere with the electoral college process and install fake GOP electors in multiple states after losing the 2020 presidential election.\par \par \uc2 The 6 December 2020 memo, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/aug/09/trump-secret-memo-2020-election-indictments-biden-energy-live-updates?page=with:block-64d38d118f082ff5288441e7#block-64d38d118f082ff5288441e7"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 made public }}}\uc2  on Tuesday by the \uc2 New York Times\uc2 , shows how Chesebro laid out the plan to put forth slates of Republican electors in seven key swing states that Trump had lost.\par \par \uc2 The document, which federal prosecutors described as a \u8220\'20\'1Cfraudulent elector memo\u8221\'20\'1D, revealed that Chesebro proposed the appointment of fake electors, and detailed a \u8220\'20\'1Cmessaging\u8221\'20\'1D strategy to portray them as evidence if legislatures later concluded Trump as the victor in those states.\par \par \uc2 In the memo, Chesebro {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/aug/09/trump-secret-memo-2020-election-indictments-biden-energy-live-updates?page=with:block-64d38d118f082ff5288441e7#block-64d38d118f082ff5288441e7"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 acknowledges}}}\uc2  that he is suggesting a \u8220\'20\'1Cbold, controversial strategy\u8221\'20\'1D that the supreme court would \u8220\'20\'1Clikely\u8221\'20\'1D ultimately reject. He argues that the plan would focus attention on claims of voter fraud and \u8220\'20\'1Cbuy the Trump campaign more time to win litigation that would deprive Biden of electoral votes and/or add to Trump\u8217\'20\'19s column\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 The memo was referenced in the four-count indictment against Trump by a Washington DC grand jury last month. The indictment identifies, but does not name, Chesebro as a co-conspirator in Trump\u8217\'20\'19s alleged conspiracy to obstruct certification of the 2020 election.\par \par \uc2 In separate, previously seen emails, Chesebro had also suggested having then-vice president \uc2 Mike Pence\uc2  open and count the electoral votes alone. Pence would then certify the fake electors\u8217\'20\'19 votes, even though Biden would have won the state, according to the plan.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 4.31pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.52pm BST\par \par \uc2 There has been open debate within the Democratic party over whether Senator \uc2 Dianne Feinstein\uc2 , 90, whose health and cognitive abilities have come into question after a two-and-a-half-month absence due to shingles and other medical complications, should resign.\par \par \uc2 Questions over Feinstein\u8217\'20\'19s ability to effectively represent California, the most populous US state, have been a sensitive issue for Democrats going back years. As her diminishing health plays out in the public eye there is a renewed urgency to the situation. Riding out her term in absentia until retirement next year is also not a viable option, with Feinstein the tie-breaking vote on the Senate judiciary committee, which holds confirmation hearings for judicial nominees, and effectively the only person who can ensure that \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s picks for judges go through.\par \par \uc2 Feinstein\u8217\'20\'19s compounding health issues and status as the oldest member of Congress now present Democrats with a complex problem that has pitted several prominent members of Congress against each other, as several lawmakers issued calls in recent weeks for Feinstein to step down.\par \par \uc2 California Democrats, who voted her into office six times, are increasingly divided over whether she should continue to serve. More than 60 progressive organizations {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://docs.google.com/document/u/0/d/1U08lf60hSoWXXdibHZ9BSipogVfTh2E4kjKEVxB1LEA/mobilebasic"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 called}}}\uc2  on her to step down \u8211\'20\'13 noting that the 39 million constituents she represents deserve \u8220\'20\'1Cconstant representation\u8221\'20\'1D. It hasn\u8217\'20\'19t helped that the senator has physically {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.latimes.com/california/newsletter/2023-05-24/as-staff-shield-feinstein-from-the-press-a-picture-really-is-worth-a-thousand-words-essential-california"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 shielded}}}\uc2  herself from her constituents and the press, dismissing questions about her health and ability to serve.\par \par \uc2 Feinstein\u8217\'20\'19s eventual return to Washington on 10 May only prompted a new round of debate and news coverage, after she arrived looking exceedingly frail and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://slate.com/news-and-politics/2023/05/dianne-feinstein-health-return-to-senate.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 appeared confused}}}\uc2  by reporters\u8217\'20\'19 questions about her absence. Feinstein suffered more complications from her illness than previously disclosed, the \uc2 New York Times{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/2023/05/18/us/politics/feinstein-illness-shingles-senate.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reported}}}\uc2 , including post-shingles encephalitis and a condition known as Ramsay Hunt syndrome which causes facial paralysis.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/may/29/dianne-feinstein-democrats-divided-health-questions"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Read the full story here.}}}\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/may/29/dianne-feinstein-democrats-divided-health-questions"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Democrats\u8217\'20\'19 Dianne Feinstein dilemma: party split over senator\u8217\'20\'19s diminishing health }}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.46pm BST\par \par \uc2 California senator \uc2 Dianne Feinstein\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/aug/09/trump-secret-memo-2020-election-indictments-biden-energy-live-updates?page=with:block-64d3a0fe8f082ff5288442d8#block-64d3a0fe8f082ff5288442d8"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  latest medical setback}}}\uc2  comes days after she reportedly handed power of attorney over to her daughter.\par \par \uc2 Katherine, a former San Francisco judge, is said to have been given power of attorney over her mother amid an ongoing dispute regarding her late husband \uc2 Richard Blum\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s estate, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/2023/08/03/us/feinstein-husband-estate-family-fortune.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 according }}}\uc2  to the \uc2 New York Times\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.29pm BST\par \par \uc2 Senator \uc2 Dianne Feinstein\uc2  hospitalized after fall\par \par \uc2 Senator \uc2 Dianne Feinstein\uc2  was hospitalized after tripping and falling in her San Francisco home, according to multiple reports.\par \par \uc2 The 90-year-old Democratic senator was taken to a nearby hospital and returned home on Tuesday night, TMZ {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tmz.com/2023/08/09/senator-dianne-feinstein-hospitalized-trip-fall-shingles-health-san-francisco/?adid=social-tw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reported.}}}\par \par \uc2 Feinstein\u8217\'20\'19s spokesperson {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.sfchronicle.com/politics/article/feinstein-hospitalized-after-fall-18287088.php"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  told}}}\uc2  the San Francisco Chronicle that she spent an hour or two in the hospital. Her scans were clear, he added.\par \par \uc2 Feinstein has struggled with her health in recent years. She was absent from the Senate for two-and-a-half-months due to shingles and other medical complications.\par \par \uc2 Senator \uc2 Dianne Feinstein\uc2  at a confirmation hearing Wednesday, 12 July 2023, on Capitol Hill in Washington. Photograph: Mariam Zuhaib/AP\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 5.00pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.15pm BST\par \par \uc2 Judge schedules Friday hearing on protective order in January 6 case\par \par \uc2 The judge presiding over \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s election subversion case, US district judge \uc2 Tanya Chutkan\uc2 , has set a date for a hearing on a proposed protective order by prosecutors.\par \par \uc2 The protective order, if granted, will govern how evidence is handled in the case. The order, requested last Friday by special counsel Jack Smith \u8217\'20\'19s team, asks for Trump to be prohibited from publicly sharing evidence in the case during the discovery phase.\par \par \uc2 The decision to schedule the hearing for Friday morning comes a day after the special counsel\u8217\'20\'19s office and Trump\u8217\'20\'19s legal team filed dueling motions over the proposed protective order.\par \par \uc2 Trump is not required to be present at the Friday hearing in Washington DC, Chutkan said.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.18pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.43pm BST\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  last week {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/aug/04/trump-court-arraignment-power-dynamics-january-6"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pleaded not guilty}}}\uc2  to charges that he conspired to overturn the results of the 2020 election by conspiring to block Congress from confirming \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s victory over him. He also pleaded not guilty to charges that he obstructed the certification by directing his supporters to descend on the Capitol on the day of the January 6 attack.\par \par \uc2 He is also accused of \u8211\'20\'13 and has pleaded not guilty to \u8211\'20\'13 scheming to disrupt the election process and deprive Americans of their right to have their votes counted.\par \par \uc2 John Lauro slammed the indictment as politically motivated and full of holes. He said:\par \par \uc2 This is what\u8217\'20\'19s called a Swiss cheese indictment \u8211\'20\'13 so many holes that we\u8217\'20\'19re going to be identifying.\par \par \uc2 Lauro suggested that his side would argue that Trump\u8217\'20\'19s actions were protected by his constitutional right to free speech as well as presidential immunity.\par \par \uc2 Taking aim at Biden, the Democratic incumbent, Lauro added:\par \par \uc2 This is the first time in history that a sitting president has used his justice department to go after a political opponent to knock him out of a race that creates grave constitutional problems.\par \par \uc2 Lauro confirmed that he planned to file a motion to dismiss the conspiracy charges, as well as another to transfer the case from Washington DC\u8217\'20\'19s federal courthouse to one in West Virginia, a state where Trump won 69% of the votes in 2020, his second largest margin of victory in a state after Wyoming.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe would like a diverse venue and diverse jury to have an expectation that will reflect the characteristics of the American people,\u8221\'20\'1D he said. \u8220\'20\'1CI think West Virginia would be an excellent venue.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Lauro was brought on to Trump\u8217\'20\'19s legal team in mid-July. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.washingtonpost.com/history/2023/08/04/trump-indictment-john-lauro-tim-donaghy/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  He has defended a string of controversial clients }}}\uc2  who include Dewayne Allen Levesque \u8211\'20\'13 manager of the Pink Pony nightclub in Florida who was acquitted of charges of racketeering, conspiracy, and aiding and abetting prostitution \u8211\'20\'13 and the disgraced NBA referee Tim Donaghy, who admitted to taking payoffs from bookies in exchange for a one-year, three-month prison sentence.\par \par \uc2 Trump will not accept a plea deal in the criminal conspiracy charges, Lauro told \uc2 CBS\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.29pm BST\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s attorney has suggested that \uc2 Mike Pence\uc2  could help his former boss fight off the 2020 election-related criminal conspiracy charges against Trump, claiming that the former vice-president would be the \u8220\'20\'1Cbest witness\u8221\'20\'1D for the defence.\par \par \uc2 In an interview with \uc2 CBS\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s Face the Nation on Sunday, attorney John Lauro played down differences between the former president and Pence\u8217\'20\'19s accounts of what happened in the run up to the 6 January 2021 certification of \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s victory over Trump, whose supporters attacked the US Capitol that day.\par \par \uc2 Asked on Face the Nation whether he feared that Pence would be called as a prosecution witness in the case, Lauro said: \u8220\'20\'1CNo, no in fact, the vice-president will be our best witness.\par \par \uc2 There was a constitutional disagreement between the vice-president [Pence] and president Trump, but the bottom line is never, never in our country\u8217\'20\'19s history, as those kinds of disagreements have been prosecuted criminally. It\u8217\'20\'19s unheard of.\par \par \uc2 Earlier on Sunday, Pence \u8211\'20\'13 who is running against Trump for the 2024 Republican presidential nomination \u8211\'20\'13 told \uc2 CBS\uc2  that he {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/aug/06/mike-pence-trump-interview"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 had \u8220\'20\'1Cno plans\u8221\'20\'1D to testify}}}\uc2  for the prosecution. But he did not rule it out. In response to Lauro\u8217\'20\'19s assertion last week that all Trump did was ask him to pause the certification, Pence said: \u8220\'20\'1CThat\u8217\'20\'19s not what happened.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 President \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  and Vice President \uc2 Mike Pence\uc2  attend a campaign rally at Cherry Capital airport in Traverse City, Michigan, 2 November 2020. Photograph: Carlos Barr\u237\'00\'EDa/Reuters\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.19pm BST\par \par \uc2 The Fulton county district attorney\u8217\'20\'19s office investigating \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s efforts to overturn the 2020 election results in the state of Georgia has been issuing summons to witnesses to testify before the grand jury, as part of the final presentation by prosecutors that is expected to take just a couple of days before they ask the grand jury to return an indictment, according to two people familiar with the matter.\par \par \uc2 Charges stemming from the Trump investigation could come as early as next Tuesday if the presentment starts on Monday, the people said. That dovetails with a timeline inferred from district attorney \uc2 Fani Willis\uc2  instructing her staff to move to remote work during that period because of security concerns, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/may/19/georgia-2020-election-inuiry-charges-july"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the Guardian has previously reported}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The district attorney\u8217\'20\'19s office has spent more than two years investigating whether Trump and his allies interfered in the 2020 election in Georgia, including impaneling a special grand jury that made it more straightforward to compel evidence from recalcitrant witnesses.\par \par \uc2 Unlike in the federal system, grand juries in the state of Georgia need to already be considering an indictment when they subpoena documents and testimony. By using a special grand jury, prosecutors can collect evidence without the pressure of having to file charges.\par \par \uc2 The special grand jury in the Trump investigation heard evidence for roughly seven months and recommended indictments of more than a dozen people including the former president himself, its forewoman strongly suggested in interviews with multiple news outlets.\par \par \uc2 Trump\u8217\'20\'19s legal team sought last month to invalidate the work of the special grand jury and have Willis disqualified from proceedings, but the Georgia supreme court rejected the motion, ruling that Trump lacked \u8220\'20\'1Ceither the facts or the law necessary to mandate Ms Willis\u8217\'20\'19s disqualification\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.14pm BST\par \par \uc2 Fulton county prosecutors to seek new 2020 election charges next week\par \par \uc2 The Fulton county district attorney investigating \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s efforts to overturn the 2020 election results in the state of Georgia is expected to present evidence to a grand jury and ask it to return indictments as early as next Tuesday, according to two people familiar with the matter.\par \par \uc2 The prosecutors in the office of district attorney \uc2 Fani Willis\uc2  completed its internal reviews for criminal charges in the Trump case weeks ago, the people said. The review process, to identify any weakness with the case, is typically seen as the final step before charges are filed.\par \par \uc2 Willis has also privately indicated to her senior staff that the prosecutors on the Trump case were sufficiently prepared that they could go to trial tomorrow, the people said.\par \par \uc2 In the Trump investigation, prosecutors have developed evidence to pursue a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/jul/21/georgia-trump-charges-fraud-election-2020"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 sprawling racketeering case}}}\uc2  that is predicated on a statute about influencing witnesses and computer trespass by Trump operatives in Coffee county, the \uc2 Guardian\uc2  has previously reported.\par \par \uc2 The extent of Trump\u8217\'20\'19s legal jeopardy remains unclear. But the racketeering statute in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/state-of-georgia"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Georgia}}}\uc2  is especially expansive and attempts to solicit or coerce certain activity \u8211\'20\'13 for instance, Trump\u8217\'20\'19s call to the secretary of state, \uc2 Brad Raffensperger\uc2  \u8211\'20\'13 could be included in the indictment.\par \par \uc2 The district attorney\u8217\'20\'19s office has also {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/jul/25/trump-georgia-investigation-fulton-county-prosecutors"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 weighed several state election law charges}}}\uc2 , including: criminal solicitation to commit election fraud and conspiracy to commit election fraud, as well as solicitation of a public or political officer to fail to perform their duties and solicitation to destroy, deface or remove ballots.\par \par \uc2 Willis originally suggested charging decisions were \u8220\'20\'1Cimminent\u8221\'20\'1D in January, but the timetable has been repeatedly delayed after a number of Republicans who sought to help Trump stay in power as so-called fake electors accepted immunity deals as the investigation neared its end.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.00pm BST\par \par \uc2 The {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/aug/09/trump-secret-memo-2020-election-indictments-biden-energy-live-updates?page=with:block-64d381948f0884de6f41747b#block-64d381948f0884de6f41747b"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 newly disclosed memo}}}\uc2  by Trump lawyer Kenneth Chesebro includes a strategy to explain why pro-Trump electors were meeting in states where \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  was declared the winner, the Times {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/2023/08/08/us/politics/trump-indictment-fake-electors-memo.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reported.}}}\par \par \uc2 Chesebro wrote:\par \par \uc2 I believe that what can be achieved on Jan. 6 is not simply to keep Biden below 270 electoral votes. It seems feasible that the vote count can be conducted so that at no point will Trump be behind in the electoral vote count unless and until Biden can obtain a favorable decision from the Supreme Court upholding the Electoral Count Act as constitutional, or otherwise recognizing the power of Congress (and not the president of the Senate) to count the votes.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.49pm BST\par \par \uc2 Secret Trump memo laid out plan to overturn election\par \par \uc2 Good morning, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/us-politics"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 US politics}}}\uc2  blog readers. A lawyer allied with former president \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  initially pitched the now-infamous plan to use fake electors in swing states to subvert the 2020 election results as \u8220\'20\'1Ca bold, controversial strategy\u8221\'20\'1D that the supreme court would \u8220\'20\'1Clikely\u8221\'20\'1D reject, according to a secret memo.\par \par \uc2 Federal prosecutors are portraying the memo, dated 6 December 2020 and written by Kenneth Chesebro, as a crucial link in how the Trump team\u8217\'20\'19s efforts to keep him in power evolved into a criminal conspiracy, according to a \uc2 New York Times{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/2023/08/08/us/politics/trump-indictment-fake-electors-memo.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 report. }}}\uc2  The existence of the memo came to light in last week\u8217\'20\'19s indictment of Trump.\par \par \uc2 Chesebro, identified as \u8220\'20\'1Cco-conspirator 5\u8221\'20\'1D in the federal indictment of Trump, reportedly argued that the plan would focus attention on claims of voter fraud and \u8220\'20\'1Cbuy the Trump campaign more time to win litigation that would deprive Biden of electoral votes and/or add to Trump\u8217\'20\'19s column\u8221\'20\'1D. He wrote in the memo:\par \par \uc2 I recognize that what I suggest is a bold, controversial strategy, and that there are many reasons why it might not end up being executed on Jan. 6. But as long as it is one possible option, to preserve it as a possibility it is important that the Trump-Pence electors cast their electoral votes on Dec. 14.\par \par \uc2 The document, described by prosecutors as the \u8220\'20\'1Cfraudulent elector memo\u8221\'20\'1D, provides new details about how the plan originated and was discussed behind the scenes. The memo show the plan was a criminal plot to engineer \u8220\'20\'1Ca fake controversy that would derail the proper certification of Biden as president-elect\u8221\'20\'1D, prosecutors said.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s what else we\u8217\'20\'19re watching today:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 3pm EST: President \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  will speak about his administration\u8217\'20\'19s clean energy and manufacturing investments in Albuquerque.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 5.55pm EST : Biden will fly to Salt Lake city.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The House and Senate are out.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020230809ej89001xr\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
