\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Prosecutors ask for 2 January start date for Trump 2020 election interference case \u8211\'20\'13 as it happened\b0\par\par\uc2 L\u233\'00\'E9onie Chao-Fong \par \uc2 7,401 \uc2 words\par \uc2 10 August 2023\par 21:07 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Federal prosecutors say they estimate it will take four to six weeks to present their case against former US presidentFull story: Trump and valet plead not guilty to new document charges\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.39pm BST\par \par \uc2 Closing summary\par \par \uc2 Hello again, US politics live blog readers, it\u8217\'20\'19s been a lively day in political news, which we do our best to bring you as it happens. There will be more live coverage on Friday but, for now, this blog is closing.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s where things stand:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  has {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/aug/10/trump-documents-indictment-valet-property-manager-mar-a-lago-biden-live-updates?page=with:block-64d542d08f089cdb327cd6b9#block-64d542d08f089cdb327cd6b9"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 lodged an appeal}}}\uc2  against the dismissal of his defamation lawsuit against the New York writer E Jean Carroll.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The US supreme court{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/aug/10/trump-documents-indictment-valet-property-manager-mar-a-lago-biden-live-updates?page=with:block-64d53f3f8f0808267411c58f#block-64d53f3f8f0808267411c58f"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 has agreed}}}\uc2  to hear a challenge by \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s administration to the legality of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/society/2018/sep/30/theyre-drug-dealers-in-armani-suits-executives-draw-focus-amid-us-epidemic"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 OxyContin maker}}}\uc2 Purdue Pharma\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s bankruptcy settlement that {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/society/2023/may/30/purdue-pharma-sackler-family-protected-from-opioid-lawsuits"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 would shield}}}\uc2  its owners, the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2019/jul/26/sacklers-opioids-purdue-pharma-oxycontin-opioids"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Sackler family}}}\uc2 , from lawsuits.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The Biden administration{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/aug/10/trump-documents-indictment-valet-property-manager-mar-a-lago-biden-live-updates?page=with:block-64d53d148f0808267411c57a#block-64d53d148f0808267411c57a"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 asked Congress}}}\uc2  for $13bn in emergency defense aid to Ukraine and an additional $8bn for humanitarian support, plus money to replenish the US federal disaster funds and fortify the US-Mexico border, in a package worth $40bn.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The House oversight committee {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/aug/10/trump-documents-indictment-valet-property-manager-mar-a-lago-biden-live-updates?page=with:block-64d531d68f089cdb327cd643#block-64d531d68f089cdb327cd643"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 intends to}}}\uc2  subpoena \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  and \uc2 Hunter Biden\uc2  amid its ongoing investigation into the Biden family\u8217\'20\'19s business dealings.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Federal prosecutors{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/aug/10/trump-documents-indictment-valet-property-manager-mar-a-lago-biden-live-updates?page=with:block-64d527088f0808267411c4c3#block-64d527088f0808267411c4c3"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 asked a judge}}}\uc2  to set a 2 January trial date for former president \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  in the case related to his efforts to overturn the results of the 2020 election.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Joe Manchin, West Virginia\u8217\'20\'19s Democratic US Senator, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/aug/10/trump-documents-indictment-valet-property-manager-mar-a-lago-biden-live-updates?page=with:block-64d5252a8f0808267411c49f#block-64d5252a8f0808267411c49f"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 said he\u8217\'20\'19s}}}\uc2  \u8220\'20\'1Cthinking seriously\u8221\'20\'1D about becoming an independent.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s valet,Walt Nauta,{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/aug/10/trump-documents-indictment-valet-property-manager-mar-a-lago-biden-live-updates?page=with:block-64d4fa438f08646765674f61#block-64d4fa438f08646765674f61"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pleaded not guilty}}}\uc2  in Florida court to conspiring with the former president to obstruct the investigation into his possession of classified documents at his Mar-a-Lago estate.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Supreme CourtJustice \uc2 Clarence Thomas{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/aug/10/trump-documents-indictment-valet-property-manager-mar-a-lago-biden-live-updates?page=with:block-64d4f0558f08d13e612ef311#block-64d4f0558f08d13e612ef311"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 received}}}\uc2  \u8216\'20\'18unprecedented\u8217\'20\'19 number of gifts from billionaire friends, according to a new report detailing even more largesse than previously revealed that has been showered upon the bench\u8217\'20\'19s most conservative member.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 9.46pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.10pm BST\par \par \uc2 Trump appeals dismissal of defamation claim v E Jean Carroll\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  has lodged an appeal against the dismissal of his defamation lawsuit against the New York writer E Jean Carroll, Reuters reports.\par \par \uc2 The development comes just {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/aug/07/donald-trump-rape-language-e-jean-carroll"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 three days after}}}\uc2  the former US president {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://storage.courtlistener.com/recap/gov.uscourts.nysd.543790/gov.uscourts.nysd.543790.200.0.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 lost}}}\uc2  his counterclaim for defamation against E Jean Carroll, the writer against whom he was found liable for sexual abuse and defamation, and fined $5m.\par \par \uc2 Carroll also continues to pursue a separate defamation case against him.\par \par \uc2 E Jean Carroll leaving the Manhattan courthouse after a jury found Trump liable for sexual assault and defamation. Photograph: Derek French/\uc2 Shutterstock\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 9.31pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.57pm BST\par \par \uc2 Supreme Court to take case over OxyContin maker\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 US supreme court\uc2  has agreed to hear a challenge by \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s administration to the legality of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/society/2018/sep/30/theyre-drug-dealers-in-armani-suits-executives-draw-focus-amid-us-epidemic"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 OxyContin maker}}}\uc2 Purdue Pharma\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s bankruptcy settlement that {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/society/2023/may/30/purdue-pharma-sackler-family-protected-from-opioid-lawsuits"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 would shield}}}\uc2  its owners from the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2019/jul/26/sacklers-opioids-purdue-pharma-oxycontin-opioids"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Sackler family}}}\uc2  from lawsuits over their role in the country\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/news/2018/nov/08/the-making-of-an-opioid-epidemic"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 opioid epidemic}}}\uc2 , Reuters reports.\par \par \uc2 The court also paused bankruptcy proceedings concerning Purdue and its affiliates and said in a brief order that it would hold oral arguments in December in the administration\u8217\'20\'19s appeal of a lower court\u8217\'20\'19s ruling upholding the settlement. The court\u8217\'20\'19s new term begins in October.\par \par \uc2 Purdue\u8217\'20\'19s owners under the settlement would receive immunity in exchange for paying up to $6bn to settle thousands of lawsuits filed by states, hospitals, people who had become addicted and others who have sued the Stamford, Connecticut-based company over its misleading marketing of OxyContin.\par \par \uc2 At issue is whether US bankruptcy law allows Purdue\u8217\'20\'19s restructuring to include legal protections for the Sackler family, who have not filed for personal bankruptcy.\par \par \uc2 Purdue filed for Chapter 11 bankruptcy protection from creditors in 2019 to address its debts, nearly all of which stemmed from thousands of lawsuits alleging that OxyContin helped kickstart an opioid epidemic that has caused more than 500,000 US overdose deaths over two decades.\par \par \uc2 Fake pill bottles with messages about OxyContin maker \uc2 Purdue Pharma\uc2 . Photograph: Seth Wenig/AP\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 9.56pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.48pm BST\par \par \uc2 Biden asks Congress for more cash for Ukraine, climate, border\par \par \uc2 The Biden administration on Thursday asked Congress to provide more than $13bn in emergency defense aid to Ukraine and an additional $8bn for humanitarian support through the end of the year, another massive infusion of cash as {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://apnews.com/hub/russia-ukraine"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the Russian invasion}}}\uc2  wears on and Ukraine pushes {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://apnews.com/article/russia-ukraine-war-counteroffensive-major-push-12334bbee83b608221dafced4727369e"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a counteroffensive}}}\uc2  against the Kremlin\u8217\'20\'19s deeply entrenched forces, the Associated Press writes.\par \par \uc2 The package includes $12bn to replenish the US federal disaster funds at home after a deadly climate season of heat and storms and funds to bolster the enforcement at the southern border with Mexico, including money to curb the flow of deadly fentanyl. All told, it\u8217\'20\'19s a $40bn package.\par \par \uc2 While {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://apnews.com/article/biden-europe-congress-government-and-politics-bddc8fc02afcc2a072bbdd388dc1a658"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the last such request}}}\uc2  from the White House for Ukraine funding was easily approved in 2022, there\u8217\'20\'19s a different dynamic this time.\par \par \uc2 A political divide on the issue has grown, with the Republican-led House facing enormous pressure to demonstrate support for the party\u8217\'20\'19s leader, \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , who has been very skeptical of the war. Meanwhile, American support for the effort has been slowly softening.\par \par \uc2 White House budget director \uc2 Shalanda Young\uc2 , in a letter to House speaker Kevin McCarthy, urged swift action to follow through on the US \u8220\'20\'1Ccommitment to the Ukrainian peoples\u8217\'20\'19 defense of their homeland and to democracy around the world\u8221\'20\'1D as well as other needs.\par \par \uc2 The request was crafted with an eye to picking up support from Republicans, as well as Democrats, particularly with increased domestic funding around border issues \u8211\'20\'13 a top priority for the GOP, which has been highly critical of the Biden administration\u8217\'20\'19s approach to halting the flow of migrants crossing from Mexico.\par \par \uc2 Still, the price tag of $40bn may be too much for Republicans who are fighting to slash, not raise, federal outlays.\par \par \uc2 Senate majority leader and New York Senator \uc2 Chuck Schumer\uc2  said:\par \par \uc2 The latest request from the Biden administration shows America\u8217\'20\'19s continued commitment to helping Americans here at home and our friends abroad. We hope to join with our Republican colleagues this fall to avert an unnecessary government shutdown and fund this critical emergency supplemental request.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 9.23pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.38pm BST\par \par \uc2 Continuing on the issue of Jack Smith requesting a 2 January 2024 trial date for \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  over the former president\u8217\'20\'19s efforts to subvert the 2020 election while he was still in office:\par \par \uc2 On Thursday in a court filing, the government also noted that Trump\u8217\'20\'19s legal team had known about the facts of the case for at least a year after prosecutors first contacted them in June 2022 and one of the lawyers involved in that initial outreach, presumably Evan Corcoran, was at Trump\u8217\'20\'19s arraignment.\par \par \uc2 It also argued that Trump\u8217\'20\'19s lawyers were wrong to characterize the Speedy Trial Act, which broadly mandates criminal cases to go to trial promptly, as existing for the benefit of the defendant and therefore allowing Trump to seek delays if he chooses.\par \par \uc2 The speedy trial rules in fact exist to protect the rights of the public as well as the defendant, prosecutors wrote, citing an opinion from {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://casetext.com/case/us-v-gambino-22"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 United States v Gambino}}}\uc2  that found: \u8220\'20\'1CThe public is the loser when a criminal trial is not prosecuted expeditiously, as suggested by the aphorism, \u8216\'20\'18justice delayed is justice denied\u8217\'20\'19.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 But the draft schedule proposed by the government, that would see evidence turned over to Trump through discovery completed by the end of August and jury selection at the start of December, is almost certain to be delayed because of complicating factors.\par \par \uc2 The prosecution unexpectedly disclosed in a footnote that they intended to use classified information at trial, which means his case will be tried according to the time-consuming steps laid out in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://viewer.gutools.co.uk/us-news/2023/jun/28/trump-classified-documents-trial-delayed-spring-2024"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the Classified Information Procedures Act}}}\uc2 , or Cipa.\par \par \uc2 Cipa essentially requires the defense to disclose what classified information they want to use at trial in advance, so the courts can decide whether to add restrictions. If the government feels the restrictions aren\u8217\'20\'19t enough, they can decide whether they still want to continue with the case.\par \par \uc2 While Cipa established a mechanism through which the government can safely charge cases involving classified documents, the series of steps that have to be followed means it takes longer to get to trial compared with regular criminal cases without national security implications.\par \par \uc2 A \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  supporter outside the E Barrett Prettyman federal courthouse in Washington DC. Photograph: Bonnie Cash/UPI/\uc2 Shutterstock\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 8.56pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.30pm BST\par \par \uc2 In asking the judge overseeing the criminal case against {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://viewer.gutools.co.uk/us-news/donaldtrump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Donald Trump}}}\uc2  over his efforts to subvert the 2020 election to schedule the trial for the start of January 2024, the written filing from prosecutors in the office of special counsel Jack Smith set an aggressive timeline.\par \par \uc2 Trump\u8217\'20\'19s lawyers are expected to seek substantial delay, according to a person close to the former president.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CA January 2 trial date would vindicate the public\u8217\'20\'19s strong interest in a speedy trial,\u8221\'20\'1D prosecutors wrote. \u8220\'20\'1CIt is difficult to imagine a public interest stronger than the one in this case in which the defendant \u8211\'20\'13 the former President of the United States \u8211\'20\'13 is charged with three criminal conspiracies.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://storage.courtlistener.com/recap/gov.uscourts.dcd.258148/gov.uscourts.dcd.258148.23.0_1.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 eight-page filing}}}\uc2  submitted to US district court judge \uc2 Tanya Chutkan\uc2 , who will hear arguments from both sides about the scope of the protective order in the case on Friday, argued it gave sufficient time to Trump to prepare a defense.\par \par \uc2 Last week, Trump pleaded not guilty to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://viewer.gutools.co.uk/us-news/2023/aug/01/donald-trump-charged-2020-election"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 charges filed in federal district court in Washington}}}\uc2  that he conspired to defraud the United States, conspired to obstruct an official proceeding, obstructed an official proceeding, and engaged in a conspiracy against rights.\par \par \uc2 Among other things, the government said Trump\u8217\'20\'19s legal team already appeared to know what arguments they intended to make at trial and what pre-trial motions they intended to file and therefore were in a position to quickly go to trial.\par \par \uc2 The prosecutors, for instance, sought to use the television appearances from Trump lawyer John Lauro \u8211\'20\'13 where he discussed potential legal defenses and the possibility of filing a motion to change the trial venue to West Virginia \u8211\'20\'13 against him.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt appears that defense counsel is already planning which motions the defendant will file,\u8221\'20\'1D prosecutors said in one footnote. \u8220\'20\'1COn \uc2 CBS\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s Face the Nation on August 6, 2023, Mr Lauro stated, \u8216\'20\'18We\u8217\'20\'19re going to be identifying and litigating a number of motions that we\u8217\'20\'19re going to file.\u8217\'20\'19\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 More of this report in the next post.\par \par \uc2 Special counsel Jack Smith speaks to the media on 1 August 2023, in Washington. Photograph: J Scott Applewhite/AP\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 8.44pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.00pm BST\par \par \uc2 House GOP to 'subpoena the Bidens', says oversight committee chair\par \par \uc2 James Comer, the Republican chair of the House oversight committee, said his committee will eventually move to subpoena \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  and \uc2 Hunter Biden\uc2  amid its ongoing investigation into the Biden family\u8217\'20\'19s business dealings.\par \par \uc2 Comer, speaking on Fox Business on Thursday, said:\par \par \uc2 This is always going to end with the Bidens coming in front of the committee. We are going to subpoena the family.\par \par \uc2 He added:\par \par \uc2 We know that this is going to end up in court when we subpoena the Bidens. So we\u8217\'20\'19re putting together a case and I think we\u8217\'20\'19ve done that very well.\par \par \uc2 His comments came a day after the House oversight committee {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/aug/10/trump-documents-indictment-valet-property-manager-mar-a-lago-biden-live-updates?page=with:block-64d50bd48f0808267411c305#block-64d50bd48f0808267411c305"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 issued a memo}}}\uc2  laying out their intention to accuse \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  of corruption even without direct evidence that he financially benefited from foreign business dealings by his son. The memo outlined millions of dollars in foreign funds paid to \uc2 Hunter Biden\uc2  and his former associates while his father was vice-president, but it did not show a direct payment to \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 8.13pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.39pm BST\par \par \uc2 National security council spokesperson Adrienne Watson confirmed that the five Americans detained by Iran had been moved to house arrest, and said negotiations for their release were continuing.\par \par \uc2 Watson described the transfer as \u8220\'20\'1Can encouraging step\u8221\'20\'1D \u8211\'20\'13 but adding that they should never have been detained in the first place. She said:\par \par \uc2 We will not rest until they are all back home in the United States. Until that time, negotiations for their eventual release remain ongoing and are delicate. We will, therefore, have little in the way of details to provide about the state of their house arrest or about our efforts to secure their freedom.\par \par \uc2 The Iranian Americans include businessmen Siamak Namazi, 51, and Emad Shargi, 58, as well as environmentalist Morad Tahbaz, 67, who also has British nationality, said Jared Genser, a lawyer who represents Namazi. The identity of the other two US citizens has not been made public.\par \par \uc2 Freeing the five would remove a major irritant between the US and Iran, though the nations remain at odds on issues from the Iranian nuclear program to Tehran\u8217\'20\'19s support for Shia militias in nations such as Iraq and Lebanon.\par \par \uc2 Namazi, who in 2016 was convicted of espionage-related charges the United States has rejected as baseless, has been detained by Iran for more than seven years. His father, Baquer, was allowed to leave Iran in October for medical treatment after being detained on similar charges also rejected by Washington.\par \par \uc2 Iranian-American businessman Siamak Namazi, one of the US dual citizens now under house arrest in Iran. Photograph: Reuters\par \par \uc2 Tahbaz was arrested in 2018 and sentenced to 10 years in prison for \u8220\'20\'1Cassembly and collusion against Iran\u8217\'20\'19s national security\u8221\'20\'1D and working for the United States as a spy. Shargi was convicted of espionage in 2020 and also sentenced to 10 years.\par \par \uc2 Iranian Americans, whose US citizenship is not recognized by Tehran, are often pawns between the two nations, which are at odds over issues including Iran\u8217\'20\'19s expanding nuclear program.\par \par \uc2 In February, NBC News reported Washington and Tehran were holding indirect talks exploring a prisoner exchange and the transfer of billions of dollars of Iranian funds in South Korean banks currently blocked by US sanctions. If transferred, those funds could only be spent for humanitarian purposes.\par \par \uc2 Any transfer could draw Republican criticism that \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  had effectively paid a ransom for the US citizens and that Iran using that money for humanitarian purposes could free up funds for its nuclear program or to support militias in nations such as Iraq, Lebanon and Yemen.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 8.16pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.27pm BST\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  is likely to oppose {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/aug/10/trump-documents-indictment-valet-property-manager-mar-a-lago-biden-live-updates?page=with:block-64d527088f0808267411c4c3#block-64d527088f0808267411c4c3"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the schedule proposed}}}\uc2  by special counsel Jack Smith in the latest court filing.\par \par \uc2 The former president\u8217\'20\'19s lawyers have already suggested they will try to slow things down, citing the complexity of the case and Trump\u8217\'20\'19s crowded legal and political schedule.\par \par \uc2 Trump\u8217\'20\'19s legal team is due to respond by next Thursday. US district judge \uc2 Tanya Chutkan\uc2  has indicated she will make a decision on the trial date at a 28 August hearing.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 8.16pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.12pm BST\par \par \uc2 Prosecutors propose 2 January trial date for Trump 2020 election interference case\par \par \uc2 Federal prosecutors asked a judge to set a 2 January trial date for former president \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  in the case related to his efforts to overturn the results of the 2020 election.\par \par \uc2 In {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://storage.courtlistener.com/recap/gov.uscourts.dcd.258148/gov.uscourts.dcd.258148.23.0_1.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 court documents,}}}\uc2  prosecutors with special counsel Jack Smith \u8217\'20\'19s team said they want the case before US district judge \uc2 Tanya Chutkan\uc2  to move to trial swiftly in Washington\u8217\'20\'19s federal court. Prosecutors estimate that it will take four to six weeks to present their case.\par \par \uc2 This trial date, and the proposed schedule outlined below, would give the defendant time to review the discovery in this case and prepare a defense, and would allow the Court and parties to fully litigate any pre-trial legal issues.\par \par \uc2 The team added:\par \par \uc2 Most importantly, a January 2 trial date would vindicate the public\u8217\'20\'19s strong interest in a speedy trial\u8212\'20\'14an interest guaranteed by the Constitution and federal law in all cases, but of particular significance here, where the defendant, a former president, is charged with conspiring to overturn the legitimate results of the 2020 presidential election, obstruct the certification of the election results, and discount citizens\u8217\'20\'19 legitimate votes.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.04pm BST\par \par \uc2 Senator Joe Manchin 'seriously' considering leaving Democratic party\par \par \uc2 West Virginia senator Joe Manchin, who has yet to decide whether to run for reelection next year or wage a long-shot third party bid for president, said he\u8217\'20\'19s \u8220\'20\'1Cthinking seriously\u8221\'20\'1D about becoming an independent.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19m thinking seriously,\u8221\'20\'1D Manchin told West Virginia radio host Hoppy Kercheval on Thursday. He added:\par \par \uc2 I have to have peace of mind, basically. The brand has become so bad. The D brand and R brand... You\u8217\'20\'19ve heard me say a million times, I am not a Washington Democrat.\par \par \uc2 Asked how seriously he was about becoming an independent, Manchin said he has \u8220\'20\'1Cbeen thinking about that for quite some time\u8221\'20\'1D and that he wanted to \u8220\'20\'1Cmake sure that my voice is truly an independent voice\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Manchin, who earlier this year described himself as an independent Democrat, has been dropping hints for months that he might switch to become an independent. On Thursday, he said he was not yet ready to make an announcement about his future with the Democratic party immediately. \u8220\'20\'1CWhen I get ready to make a decision, I\u8217\'20\'19ll come see you,\u8221\'20\'1D he told Kercheval.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 7.05pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.37pm BST\par \par \uc2 Five US dual citizens detained in Iran moved out of prison to house arrest\par \par \uc2 The US and Iran have reached an agreement to win the freedom of five imprisoned Americans in exchange for several jailed Iranians and about $6bn in Iranian government assets blocked under US sanctions, according to reports.\par \par \uc2 Five Iranian-Americans were transferred from prison to house arrest, according to a lawyer for one of the prisoners. Jared Genser, counsel to Siamak Namazi, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://edition.cnn.com/2023/08/10/politics/americans-released-from-iranian-prison-house-arrest/index.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 told}}}\uc2  CNN the move was an \u8220\'20\'1Cimportant development\u8221\'20\'1D, adding:\par \par \uc2 While I hope this will be the first step to their ultimate release, this is at best the beginning of the end and nothing more.\par \par \uc2 In addition to Namazi, Emad Sharghi, Morad Tahbaz, and two others whose names have not been made public, were moved from Tehran\u8217\'20\'19s notorious Evin Prison, and are anticipated to be held at a hotel under guard by Iranian officials, until they are allowed to board a plane.\par \par \uc2 The Biden administration has been engaged in negotiations to try to secure the release of the Americans from Iran, a country with which it does not have diplomatic relations.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 7.36pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.20pm BST\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been on the ballot in seven US states since the supreme court overturned Roe v Wade on 24 June 2022 and in each instance, anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  advocates have lost, according to a NBC {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nbcnews.com/politics/elections/abortion-rights-won-every-election-roe-v-wade-overturned-rcna99031"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 report. }}}\par \par \uc2 In some instances, voters have approved state constitutional amendments protecting \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights. In others, they\u8217\'20\'19ve rejected measures that would weaken protections or make explicit in the state constitution that \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights are not protected.\par \par \uc2 On Tuesday, Ohio voters {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/aug/08/ohio-issue-1-rejected-state-constitution"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 rejected a proposal}}}\uc2  that would have made it considerably harder to amend the state constitution in a major win for reproductive rights and democracy advocates in the state.\par \par \uc2 Campaigns linked to protecting \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights in politically competitive states, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/aug/03/kansas-abortion-vote-state-constitution"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 like a referendum in Kansas}}}\uc2  and a supreme court race in Wisconsin, have been {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/apr/04/wisconsin-supreme-court-election-results"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 incredibly successful}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.11pm BST\par \par \uc2 Biden approves disaster declaration for Hawaii\par \par \uc2 President \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  has approved a disaster declaration for Hawaii, following wildfires on the island that have left at least 36 people dead.\par \par \uc2 Federal funding was made available Thursday morning for affected residents in Maui county, according a statement about the declaration.\par \par \uc2 Along with the declaration, Biden also ordered that federal aid be used to supplement local recovery efforts for areas impacted by the wildfires.\par \par \uc2 Such funding can be used for grants for temporary housing, loans to cover uninsured property that was damaged, and in other ways to support recovery on the island.\par \par \uc2 Please do follow {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/aug/10/hawaii-fires-wildfires-lahaina-maui-death-toll-latest-updates?filterKeyEvents=false&page=with:block-64d4a6168f0877b51befa3c9#block-64d4a6168f0877b51befa3c9"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 our live coverage of the devastating wildfires in Hawaii.}}}\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/aug/10/hawaii-fires-wildfires-lahaina-maui-death-toll-latest-updates"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Hawaii fires: Biden approves disaster declaration amid fears Maui death toll could rise \u8211\'20\'13 latest updates}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.58pm BST\par \par \uc2 Security around the federal judge overseeing \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s January 6 case has reportedly increased at the Washington DC courthouse where the case will be tried.\par \par \uc2 US district judge \uc2 Tanya Chutkan\uc2  was seen on Thursday walking into the cafeteria inside the E Barrett Prettyman courthouse while accompanied by US marshals, NBC {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nbcnews.com/politics/donald-trump/security-bolstered-judge-overseeing-trump-election-case-rcna99221"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reported}}}\uc2 . She was seen returning to her chambers accompanied by some of the marshals.\par \par \uc2 Chutkan was observed as recently as last week walking around the building without security. CNN first {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://edition.cnn.com/2023/08/07/politics/security-judge-tanya-chutkan-trump-january-6/index.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  reported }}}\uc2  the heightened security for Chutkan, who was randomly assigned to Trump\u8217\'20\'19s case after he was indicted last week.\par \par \uc2 In a post on Truth Social earlier this week, Trump called on Chutkan to be recused from the case, arguing that \u8220\'20\'1Cthere is no way I can get a fair trial\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.32pm BST\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  had already indicated he would plead not guilty to the expanded set of charges after the former president\u8217\'20\'19s legal team submitted a court filing waiving his right to appear at the arraignment in person.\par \par \uc2 The filing read:\par \par \uc2 I have received a copy of the Indictment and the plea is NOT GUILTY to the charged offense(s).\par \par \uc2 At his {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/jun/13/trump-arraignment-not-guilty-charges-mar-a-lago-documents-court"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 initial arraignment}}}\uc2  in June, Trump pleaded not guilty to 37 federal counts, including 31 violations of the Espionage Act, over his alleged mishandling of classified documents after leaving the White House in 2021.\par \par \uc2 According to Smith\u8217\'20\'19s indictment, Trump intentionally withheld dozens of classified documents from federal officials even after a subpoena was issued to recover the materials from Mar-a-Lago. Some of those documents included information on America\u8217\'20\'19s nuclear programs, the US military\u8217\'20\'19s vulnerabilities and the White House\u8217\'20\'19s plans for retaliation in the event of an attack.\par \par \uc2 The former president appears to have been aware of the illegality of retaining the documents, as recordings obtained by the special counsel show Trump acknowledging he could no longer declassify information after leaving office.\par \par \uc2 The judge overseeing the case, US district court judge Aileen Cannon, has set a trial date of May 2024.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 6.07pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.24pm BST\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s valet, Walt Nauta, and Carlos De Oliveira, the property manager of Trump\u8217\'20\'19s Mar-a-Lago estate, appeared in court in Ft Pierce, Florida on Thursday in charges stemming from the former president\u8217\'20\'19s alleged mishandling of classified documents.\par \par \uc2 The hearing came two weeks after special counsel Jack Smith filed his superseding indictment adding De Oliveira as a codefendant in the case and outlining further charges against Trump and Nauta.\par \par \uc2 De Oliveira faces four federal criminal charges, including making false statements and conspiring to obstruct justice. Smith\u8217\'20\'19s superseding indictment alleges that Trump engaged in a scheme with Nauta and De Oliveira to wipe a server containing Mar-a-Lago surveillance footage that was subpoenaed by prosecutors and showed boxes of classified documents being removed from the storage room.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.14pm BST\par \par \uc2 House Republicans issued a memo on Wednesday laying out their intention to accuse \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  of corruption even without direct evidence that he financially benefited from foreign business dealings by his son, \uc2 Hunter Biden\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The 19-page memo outlines \u8220\'20\'1Cnew information obtained in the [Oversight] Committee\u8217\'20\'19s investigation into the Biden family\u8217\'20\'19s influence peddling schemes\u8221\'20\'1D, according to House oversight committee chair, James Comer, including more than $20m in payments from \u8220\'20\'1Cforeign sources\u8221\'20\'1D to shell companies controlled by \uc2 Hunter Biden\uc2  and his associates. As with the previous two memos released by Comer this year, it does not show a direct payment to \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The memo states:\par \par \uc2 President Biden\u8217\'20\'19s defenders purport a weak defense by asserting the Committee must show payments directly to the President to show corruption. This is a hollow claim no other American would be afforded if their family members accepted foreign payments or bribes. Indeed, the law recognizes payments to family members to corruptly influence others can constitute a bribe.\par \par \uc2 The memo marks a clear shift in House Republicans\u8217\'20\'19 strategy and could signal that House GOPs are gearing up to launch an impeachment inquiry into the president this fall, Punchbowl reported.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CUp to this point, Republicans haven\u8217\'20\'19t tied any official actions by Biden as vice president to the money received by \uc2 Hunter Biden\uc2 , other family members or their business associates. The Republicans\u8217\'20\'19 basic thrust is that there has to be corruption or something illegal going on because it all seems so sordid,\u8221\'20\'1D it writes.\par \par \uc2 Republicans have sought to use testimony from Devon Archer, a former associate of \uc2 Hunter Biden\uc2 , to prove wrongdoing by father and son. Speaking behind closed doors to members of the committee last week, Archer testified that \uc2 Hunter Biden\uc2  sold the illusion of access to his father and that he was \u8220\'20\'1Cnot aware of any\u8221\'20\'1D wrongdoing by \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 In a statement following its release, White House spokesperson Ian Sams described the memo as \u8220\'20\'1Cfull of years-old \u8216\'20\'18news,\u8217\'20\'19 innuendo, and misdirection \u8211\'20\'13 but notably missing, yet again, is any connection to President Biden\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Comer, in a statement on Wednesday, said Republicans \u8220\'20\'1Cwill continue to follow the money trail and obtain witness testimony to determine whether foreign actors targeted the Bidens, President Biden is compromised or corrupt, and our national security is threatened.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.03pm BST\par \par \uc2 Videos that compare climate activists to Nazis, portray solar and wind energy as environmentally ruinous and claim that current global heating is part of natural long-term cycles will be made available to young schoolchildren in Florida, after the state approved their use in its public school curriculum.\par \par \uc2 Slickly-made animations by the Prager University Foundation, a conservative group that produces materials on science, history, gender and other topics widely criticized as distorting the truth, will be allowed to be shown to children in kindergarten to fifth grade after being adopted by \uc2 Florida\u8217\'20\'19s department of education\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Teachers who use the materials \u8220\'20\'1Cwill not be reprimanded, cannot be pushed back on about it, we are approved on the curriculum\u8221\'20\'1D, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.prageru.com/video/parent-alert-prageru-kids-is-now-approved-curriculum-in-florida-schools"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 said}}}\uc2  Jill Simonian, director of outreach at PragerU Kids, the youth arm of the organization. \u8220\'20\'1CMore states are following. Florida \u8211\'20\'13 I\u8217\'20\'19m applauding. This is step in the right direction.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 But experts who have studied the videos and other PragerU output have warned that many of Florida\u8217\'20\'19s 3 million public schoolchildren risk being exposed to a form of rightwing indoctrination that conforms to the worldview of the organization\u8217\'20\'19s funders but bears little resemblance to reality.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/aug/10/florida-ron-desantis-climate-vidoes-school-curriculum"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Read the full story here.}}}\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/aug/10/florida-ron-desantis-climate-vidoes-school-curriculum"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Videos denying climate science approved by Florida as state curriculum}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 6.31pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.39pm BST\par \par \uc2 Michigan fake electors for \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  arraigned on felony charges\par \par \uc2 Sixteen Michigan Republicans who acted as fake electors for \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  in 2020 have pleaded not guilty to felony charges including forgery and conspiracy to commit election forgery.\par \par \uc2 The group were hit with state charges last month and accused of submitting false certificates that confirmed they were legitimate electors despite \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s victory in Michigan.\par \par \uc2 Nine of the defendants were arraigned on the state charges at a virtual court hearing in Lansing on Thursday, CNN {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://edition.cnn.com/2023/08/10/politics/michigan-fake-elector-arraignments/index.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reported.}}}\uc2  The other seven defendants had already pleaded not guilty in the past few weeks.\par \par \uc2 The group includes the head of the Republican national committee\u8217\'20\'19s chapter in Michigan, Kathy Berden, as well as the former co-chair of the Michigan Republican Party, Meshawn Maddock, and Shelby township clerk Stan Grot. The top charges carry a maximum penalty of 14 years in prison.\par \par \uc2 In announcing the felony charges last month, Michigan\u8217\'20\'19s attorney general Dana Nessel, a Democrat, said:\par \par \uc2 The false electors\u8217\'20\'19 actions undermined the public\u8217\'20\'19s faith in the integrity of our elections and, we believe, also plainly violated the laws by which we administer our elections in Michigan.\par \par \uc2 The defendants were released on a $1,000 bond. The next hearing in the case is scheduled for 18 August.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.20pm BST\par \par \uc2 A Florida attorney, Donnie Murrell, sat by Mar-a-Lago property manager Carlos De Oliveira before US magistrate judge Shaniek Mills Maynard in the Florida courtroom on Thursday, but he had not yet filed a notice of appearance in the case.\par \par \uc2 Murrell told the judge that he hoped to do so by Friday afternoon after ironing out some details, and that it was \u8220\'20\'1Cclose to being handled\u8221\'20\'1D, NBC reported.\par \par \uc2 Murrell asked to have De Oliveira be arraigned on August 25, when there is already a pre-trial hearing scheduled, but Maynard rejected that request.\par \par \uc2 De Oliveira and his co-defendant, Trump valet Walt Nauta, arrived at the courthouse this morning separately. Nauta pleaded not guilty to conspiring with the former president in the latest charges through his lawyer. The report says:\par \par \uc2 Asked if he understood the charges, Trump\u8217\'20\'19s aide, speaking softly, said that he did. \u8216\'20\'18Thank you, your honor,\u8217\'20\'19 Nauta responded when the judge wished him a good day.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 4.22pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.01pm BST\par \par \uc2 Trump valet pleads not guilty to latest charges in classified documents case\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s valet, Walt Nauta, appeared before a judge in federal court in Fort Pierce, Florida, and pleaded not guilty to conspiring with the former president to obstruct the investigation into his possession of classified documents at his Mar-a-Lago estate.\par \par \uc2 Nauta\u8217\'20\'19s co-defendant and Mar-a-Lago maintenance worker, Carlos De Oliveira, was also due to be arraigned on Thursday on charges including conspiracy to obstruct justice in the case brought by special counsel Jack Smith.\par \par \uc2 But De Oliveira was again unable to enter a plea because he has not yet secured a local attorney, which is required under local court rules. He is now scheduled to be arraigned on 15 August.\par \par \uc2 The magistrate judge also formally accepted the latest not guilty plea of Trump, who in a court filing last week waived his notice of appearance at the arraignment.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.53pm BST\par \par \uc2 US supreme court\uc2  justice \uc2 Clarence Thomas\uc2  has been embroiled in ethics scandals for months following bombshell revelations by \uc2 ProPublica\uc2 , which included how Thomas repeatedly accepted luxury vacations such as a $500,000 trip to Indonesia in 2019 from Harlan Crow, a billionaire businessman, Republican donor and longtime friend.\par \par \uc2 Thomas, \uc2 Samuel Alito\uc2  and the Trump-appointed \uc2 Neil Gorsuch\uc2  \u8211\'20\'13 all conservative hardliners on the supreme court \u8211\'20\'13 have {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/law/2023/jul/12/us-supreme-court-justices-ethics-rules-controversy-explain"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 fallen foul of recent ethics disputes.}}}\par \par \uc2 As a result, many Democrats have called for tighter ethics rules for the supreme court\u8217\'20\'19s justices, who {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/may/02/republicans-democrats-supreme-court-ethics-rules"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 they say}}}\uc2  lack conduct rules that are comparable to other federal authorities.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/law/2023/jul/12/us-supreme-court-justices-ethics-rules-controversy-explain"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 What ethical controversies are US supreme court justices facing?}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.43pm BST\par \par \uc2 The latest \uc2 ProPublica{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.propublica.org/article/clarence-thomas-other-billionaires-sokol-huizenga-novelly-supreme-court"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  report }}}\uc2  expands upon the publication\u8217\'20\'19s previous investigation into \uc2 Clarence Thomas\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s relationship with conservative billionaire Harlan Crow.\par \par \uc2 Crow\uc2  was revealed to have treated Thomas and his wife to extravagant vacations, private jet flights, gifts, tuition payments, and even the purchase of his mother\u8217\'20\'19s house in Georgia.\par \par \uc2 The latest investigation reveals a pattern of gifts to Thomas from Crow and three other wealthy benefactors: David Sokol, a former top executive at \uc2 Berkshire Hathaway\uc2 , Paul \u8220\'20\'1CTony\u8221\'20\'1D Novelly, an oil baron, and the late billionaire H. Wayne Huizenga.\par \par \uc2 The total value of the undisclosed trips they\u8217\'20\'19ve given Thomas since 1991, the year he was appointed to the court, is likely in the millions, according to the report.\par \par \uc2 Huizenga, who died in 2018, is believed to be Thomas\u8217\'20\'19 first \u8220\'20\'1Cbillionaire benefactor\u8221\'20\'1D, sending his personal private plane to fly the justice to South Florida at least twice, the report says.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.27pm BST\par \par \uc2 Justice \uc2 Clarence Thomas\uc2  received 'unprecedented' number of gifts from billionaire friends - report\par \par \uc2 US supreme court\uc2  justice \uc2 Clarence Thomas\uc2  has received dozens of luxury vacations, private jet flights and other gifts from his wealthy friends, according to a new \uc2 ProPublica{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.propublica.org/article/clarence-thomas-other-billionaires-sokol-huizenga-novelly-supreme-court"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 report}}}\uc2  that goes beyond the publication\u8217\'20\'19s previous reporting about Thomas\u8217\'20\'19 relationship with GOP mega donor Harlan Crow.\par \par \uc2 Thomas has received a series of gifts from a \u8220\'20\'1Ccadre of industry titans and ultrawealthy executives\u8221\'20\'1D during his three decades on the supreme court, the report says, including:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CAt least 38 destination vacations, including a previously unreported voyage on a yacht around the Bahamas\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Twenty-six private jet flights and eight helicopter flights\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 A dozen VIP passes to professional and college sporting events, \u8220\'20\'1Ctypically perched in the skybox\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Two stays at luxury resorts in Florida and Jamaica\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 A standing invitation \u8220\'20\'1Cto an uber-exclusive golf club overlooking the Atlantic coast\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Thomas appears to have violated the law by failing to disclose flights, yacht cruises and expensive sports tickets, the report says, citing ethics experts. The pattern also \u8220\'20\'1Cexposes consistent violations of judicial norms\u8221\'20\'1D, current and former federal judges appointed by both parties told the publication.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIn my career I don\u8217\'20\'19t remember ever seeing this degree of largesse given to anybody,\u8221\'20\'1D said Jeremy Fogel, a former federal judge who served for years on the judicial committee that reviews judges\u8217\'20\'19 financial disclosures. \u8220\'20\'1CI think it\u8217\'20\'19s unprecedented.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 US supreme court\uc2  associate Justice \uc2 Clarence Thomas\uc2 . Photograph: Evelyn Hockstein/Reuters\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.28pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.04pm BST\par \par \uc2 If \uc2 Donald Trump{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/aug/10/trump-documents-indictment-valet-property-manager-mar-a-lago-biden-live-updates?page=with:block-64d4e9ca8f08cea93c07b532#block-64d4e9ca8f08cea93c07b532"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 does decide}}}\uc2  to attend the first GOP presidential debate on 23 August, here are the candidates he will likely share the stage with:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Florida governor \uc2 Ron DeSantis\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 South Carolina Tim Scott\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Former South Carolina governor Nikki Haley\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Former New Jersey governor \uc2 Chris Christie\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Entrepreneur \uc2 Vivek Ramaswamy\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 North Dakota governor \uc2 Doug Burgum\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Former vice president \uc2 Mike Pence\par \par \uc2 To qualify for the debate, candidates need to satisfy polling and donor requirements set by the Republican national committee: at least 1% in three high-quality national polls or a mix of national and early-state polls, between 1 July and 21 August, and a minimum of 40,000 donors, with 200 in 20 or more states.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.54pm BST\par \par \uc2 Trump says he won't sign loyalty pledge ahead of first GOP debate\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  said he will not sign the loyalty pledge required by the Republican national committee (\uc2 RNC\uc2 ) for candidates to participate in the first GOP primary debate this month.\par \par \uc2 Trump, in a \uc2 Newsmax\uc2  interview on Wednesday, said:\par \par \uc2 I wouldn\u8217\'20\'19t sign the pledge. Why would I sign a pledge if there are people on there that I wouldn\u8217\'20\'19t have. I wouldn\u8217\'20\'19t have certain people as somebody that I would endorse.\par \par \uc2 He declined to specify which candidates he would not support, but he said he \u8220\'20\'1Ccan name three or four people that I wouldn\u8217\'20\'19t support for president\u8221\'20\'1D. Trump specifically criticized Florida governor \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2 , former New Jersey governor \uc2 Chris Christie\uc2  and former Arkansas governor \uc2 Asa Hutchinson\uc2  during the course of the interview.\par \par \uc2 Trump said he would announce next week whether he will attend the 23 August debate in Milwaukee. The \uc2 RNC\uc2  has said candidates must sign a pledge stating that they will support the eventual party nominee in 2024, in order to participate in the primary debate.\par \par \uc2 The former president has repeatedly indicated that he may skip the debate but on Wednesday said he had not \u8220\'20\'1Ctotally ruled it out\u8221\'20\'1D. \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19ve actually gotten very good marks on debating talents,\u8221\'20\'1D he said.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.35pm BST\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  was charged with three additional counts in the case surrounding his alleged mishandling of classified documents after leaving the White House late last month.\par \par \uc2 The former president has been charged with one additional count of willful retention of national defense information and two additional obstruction counts, according to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://storage.courtlistener.com/recap/gov.uscourts.flsd.648652/gov.uscourts.flsd.648652.85.0_2.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 court documents.}}}\par \par \uc2 The superseding indictment also charges Trump, his aides Carlos De Oliveira and Walt Nauta with two new obstruction counts stemming from allegations that they attempted to delete surveillance camera footage last summer at Mar-a-Lago.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.13pm BST\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/aug/09/trump-lawyers-request-classified-documents-mar-a-lago"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 The filing,}}}\uc2  submitted to US district court judge Aileen Cannon, was the latest twist in the back-and-forth negotiation between \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  and prosecutors in the office of special counsel Jack Smith over the protective order governing the use of what gets turned over in discovery.\par \par \uc2 Since Trump was charged with retaining national security materials, including US nuclear secrets and plans for US retaliation in the event of an attack, his case will be tried according to the time-consuming steps laid out in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/jun/28/trump-classified-documents-trial-delayed-spring-2024"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the Classified Information Procedures Act}}}\uc2 , or Cipa.\par \par \uc2 The rules require Cannon, under Cipa section 3, to issue a protective order before prosecutors can start the discovery process whereby they turn over to the defense all of the materials they intend to use at trial, just like in any other criminal case.\par \par \uc2 According to the rules, Trump\u8217\'20\'19s lawyers can challenge the protective order and ask the judge to extend access to Trump himself. Last month, Trump did ask to be able to review the classified discovery materials himself, and prosecutors agreed to his request.\par \par \uc2 The remaining sticking point, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://storage.courtlistener.com/recap/gov.uscourts.flsd.648653/gov.uscourts.flsd.648653.84.0_3.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 according to an earlier filing by prosecutors}}}\uc2 , has been where Trump will be allowed to review those materials.\par \par \uc2 Trump had sought permission to discuss the classified documents with his lawyers at both his Bedminster club in New Jersey, where he spends his summers, and his Mar-a-Lago club in Florida, where the indictment against him says he hoarded the national security papers.\par \par \uc2 But prosecutors objected to the final request, noting that they were unaware of any previous case where defendants were allowed to discuss classified information in a private residence and that it was inconsistent with the law.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThere is no basis for the defendant\u8217\'20\'19s request,\u8221\'20\'1D prosecutors wrote last month.\par \par \uc2 It is particularly striking that he seeks permission to do so in the very location at which he is charged with wilfully retaining the documents charged in this case.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.08pm BST\par \par \uc2 Trump requests to review classified documents at Mar-a-Lago ahead of trial\par \par \uc2 Lawyers for \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  asked a federal judge on Wednesday to approve the re-establishment of an ultra-secure facility at his Mar-a-Lago club to review classified documents produced to him in discovery, an audacious request without precedent in national security cases.\par \par \uc2 The request essentially would give Trump the freedom to discuss and review the same classified documents he has been charged with illegally retaining in the same location where the alleged crimes took place.\par \par \uc2 Trump\u8217\'20\'19s lawyers suggested the re-establishment of a sensitive compartmented information facility, often called a \u8220\'20\'1CScif\u8221\'20\'1D, at Mar-a-Lago in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://storage.courtlistener.com/recap/gov.uscourts.flsd.648652/gov.uscourts.flsd.648652.104.0.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 an 11-page filing}}}\uc2  that argued Trump\u8217\'20\'19s schedule and security requirements made it impossible for him to make regular trips to such a facility at a courthouse.\par \par \uc2 The Scif at Mar-a-Lago that existed during the Trump presidency was removed after Trump left office in January 2021. Although the case has elements that are novel, reconstructing a Scif for a private citizen because of their former office would be unprecedented.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.59pm BST\par \par \uc2 Federal prosecutors last month expanded the indictment against \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  for retaining national security documents and obstructing the government\u8217\'20\'19s efforts to retrieve them.\par \par \uc2 The former president was accused of attempting to destroy evidence and inducing someone else to destroy evidence, as well as an additional count under the Espionage Act for retaining a classified document about US plans to attack Iran that he discussed on tape at his Bedminster club in New Jersey.\par \par \uc2 The expanded indictment added a new section titled \u8220\'20\'1CThe Attempt to Delete Security Camera Footage\u8221\'20\'1D that alleged in detail how Trump engaged in a scheme with his valet, Walt Nauta, and Mar-a-Lago club maintenance worker, Carlos De Oliveira, to wipe a server containing surveillance footage that prosecutors subpoenaed which showed boxes of classified documents being removed from the storage room.\par \par \uc2 According to the indictment, Trump seemingly instructed Nauta to unexpectedly travel to Mar-a-Lago to have the tapes destroyed. Nauta then enlisted the help of De Oliveira, and they walked to a security booth where the camera angles were displayed on monitors before walking down to the cameras and pointing them out with flashlights.\par \par \uc2 The following week, De Oliveira asked the director of IT at Mar-a-Lago, described as \u8220\'20\'1CTrump Employee 4\u8221\'20\'1D but understood to be Yuscil Taveras, how long surveillance footage was stored for and then told him \u8220\'20\'1Cthe boss\u8221\'20\'1D wanted the server deleted.\par \par \uc2 When the director of IT replied that he did not know how to delete the server and suggested De Oliveira ask the security supervisor at the \uc2 Trump Organization\uc2 , De Olivera again insisted that \u8220\'20\'1Cthe boss\u8221\'20\'1D wanted the server deleted, the indictment said.\par \par \uc2 For months, prosecutors in the office of the special counsel have viewed the surveillance footage at Mar-a-Lago as key to the case because it showed Nauta removing boxes of classified documents out of the storage room just before Trump\u8217\'20\'19s lawyer was scheduled to search for any classified documents after receiving a subpoena.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.21pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.47pm BST\par \par \uc2 Trump's co-defendants back in court to face charges in classified documents case\par \par \uc2 Good morning, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/us-politics"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 US politics}}}\uc2  blog readers. The property manager of \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s Mar-a-Lago estate and a personal aide to the former president are due back in federal court in Florida on Thursday to face charges in the case regarding the mishandling of classified documents, after federal prosecutors expanded the indictment against Trump late last month.\par \par \uc2 Carlos De Oliveira, the Florida property manager, is scheduled to be arraigned in Fort Pierce before a magistrate judge on charges including conspiracy to obstruct justice in the case brought by special counsel Jack Smith. Thursday\u8217\'20\'19s arraignment will be the first time De Oliveira enters a plea in the case. The maintenance worker was charged in a superseding indictment last month but had not yet found a Florida-based attorney to represent him, as required by the court. He was released on $100,000 personal surety bond.\par \par \uc2 Walt Nauta, Trump\u8217\'20\'19s valet, is expected to enter a plea for a second time after he was charged alongside the former president earlier this summer. He pleaded not guilty to the charges he faced in the original indictment.\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  was also scheduled to be arraigned today on the new charges, which includes allegations that he schemed with De Oliveira and Nauta to try to delete Mar-a-Lago security footage sought by investigators, as well as new counts of obstruction and willful retention of national defense information.\par \par \uc2 But the former president submitted a waiver of appearance for Thursday\u8217\'20\'19s arraignment and entered a plea of not guilty. His filing said:\par \par \uc2 I have received a copy of the Indictment and the plea ls NOT GUILTY to the charged offense(s).\par \par \uc2 Nauta and De Oliveira are due to be arraigned at a hearing at 10am eastern time before US magistrate judge Shaniek Mills Maynard.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s what else we\u8217\'20\'19re watching today:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 1:45pmEST: President \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  is in Utah, where he will join veterans and families to discuss the Promise to Address Comprehensive Toxics (Pact) Act. He will visit the George E Wahlen Department of Veterans Affairs Medical Center to mark the first anniversary of the law that is delivering the largest expansion of veterans benefits in decades.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 2:30pm: Biden will attend a campaign lunch.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 4:25pm: Biden is due to leave Salt Lake City to return to Washington.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The House and Senate are out.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.00pm BST\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020230810ej8a001v3\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
