\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  links Grand Canyon national monument to fight against climate change \u8211\'20\'13 as it happened\b0\par\par\uc2 Chris Stein US politics live blogger \par \uc2 5,640 \uc2 words\par \uc2 8 August 2023\par 20:03 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 This blog has now closed. Read our latest story on Biden\u8217\'20\'19s national monument here\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.00pm BST\par \par \uc2 Closing summary\par \par \uc2 Democrats and Republicans are closely watching a special election in Ohio that could indicate if voters, even in red states, are willing to protect \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access. Buckeye state residents are considering {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/aug/08/trump-jan-6-ohio-abortion-vote-republican-biden-latest-news?page=with:block-64d232b38f083b553df029e6#block-64d232b38f083b553df029e6"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Issue 1}}}\uc2 , a GOP-backed measure that would make it more difficult to change the state constitution, which reproductives rights advocates are {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/aug/08/trump-jan-6-ohio-abortion-vote-republican-biden-latest-news?page=with:block-64d240048f088246c33073c2#block-64d240048f088246c33073c2"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 asking voters to do in November to ensure \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  remains legal}}}\uc2 . Today\u8217\'20\'19s election is viewed as a test of whether the issue, which so animated voters in last year\u8217\'20\'19s midterm elections and was seen as one reason why Democrats nationwide performed better than expected, remains as potent as it once was. Polls close in Ohio at 7.30pm eastern time.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s what else happened today:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/aug/08/trump-jan-6-ohio-abortion-vote-republican-biden-latest-news?page=with:block-64d28abc8f0890cce121a820#block-64d28abc8f0890cce121a820"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 established}}}\uc2  a new national monument around the Grand Canyon, linking the decision to his fight against climate change.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 If Issue 1 is approved in Ohio, election-day turnout will likely be crucial, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/aug/08/trump-jan-6-ohio-abortion-vote-republican-biden-latest-news?page=with:block-64d24f3f8f083b553df02b50#block-64d24f3f8f083b553df02b50"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a top political analyst says}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2  is {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/aug/08/trump-jan-6-ohio-abortion-vote-republican-biden-latest-news?page=with:block-64d2531a8f083b553df02b90#block-64d2531a8f083b553df02b90"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 replacing his campaign manager}}}\uc2  in an effort to jump-start his floundering presidential bid.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The Washington DC grand jury that last week indicted Donald Trump{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/aug/08/trump-jan-6-ohio-abortion-vote-republican-biden-latest-news?page=with:block-64d25b2c8f0890cce121a5b7#block-64d25b2c8f0890cce121a5b7"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 is continuing its work}}}\uc2 , for reasons that remain unknown.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Addressing a rally in New Hampshire, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/aug/08/trump-jan-6-ohio-abortion-vote-republican-biden-latest-news?page=with:block-64d295d58f088246c3307813#block-64d295d58f088246c3307813"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Trump made light}}}\uc2  of the multiple criminal indictments filed against him, saying they helped him in the polls.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.55pm BST\par \par \uc2 Below is a map of Baaj Nwaavjo I\u8217\'20\'19tah Kukveni-Ancestral Footprints of the Grand Canyon National Monument, which \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  established today.\par \par \uc2 The new areas are around the national park situated in northern Arizona, and outlined in green:\par \par \uc2 The Baaj Nwaavjo I\u8217\'20\'19tah Kukveni-Ancestral Footprints of the Grand Canyon National Monument, outlined in green. Photograph: Stephanie Smith, Grand Canyon Trust\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.43pm BST\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile in Ohio, voting is ongoing in the special election over Issue 1, which would raise the bar to amend the state\u8217\'20\'19s constitution through the ballot box, as \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights advocates {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2023/feb/21/ohio-abortion-referendum-paperwork-filed"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 hope voters will do later this year}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 It may only be one state of 50, but nonetheless expect today\u8217\'20\'19s election to be viewed as a litmus test for how important the issue of reproductive rights is to Americans, more than a year after the supreme court overturned Roe v Wade.\par \par \uc2 A {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cnn.com/2023/08/08/politics/cnn-poll-abortion-electoral-litmus-test-supreme-court/index.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 CNN poll released today}}}\uc2  indicates that voters nationwide do indeed remain fired up by the court\u8217\'20\'19s decision, which overturned nearly 50 years of precedent and allowed states to ban \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  completely. The share of those surveyed disapproving of the decision was 64%, the same as it was a year ago, CNN says.\par \par \uc2 After a draft of the court\u8217\'20\'19s decision was leaked in May 2022, the network\u8217\'20\'19s pollsters found that 26% of respondents would only vote for a candidate who shared their view on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 . That number is now up to 29% in the latest survey, according to CNN.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.24pm BST\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  is in New Hampshire, an early voting state in the Republican primaries, where he is basking in his status as the frontrunner for the nomination.\par \par \uc2 The former president is an avid poll watcher, and is clearly relishing {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://projects.fivethirtyeight.com/polls/president-primary-r/2024/national/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the noticeable uptick}}}\uc2  in his public support ever since the first criminal indictments again him became public earlier this year:\par \par \uc2 enltr\u8220\'20\'1CEvery time you get indicted, I like to check the polls. One more indictment and I think this election is over!\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  touts his poll numbers after indictments during a speech in New Hampshire {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/9ljiVryjz7"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/9ljiVryjz7}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 The Recount (@therecount) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/therecount/status/1688992557118726144?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 August 8, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.03pm BST\par \par \uc2 Among those who joined \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  for his speech at the Grand Canyon was \uc2 Kyrsten Sinema\uc2 , the Arizona senator who last year left the Democratic party to be an independent:\par \par \uc2 enltrIn the front row for President \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 's in Red Butte, AZ-- Democratic-turned-Independent Arizona Senator \uc2 Kyrsten Sinema\uc2 . {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/ALmXeqKJ1N"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/ALmXeqKJ1N}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 DJ Judd (@DJJudd) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/DJJudd/status/1688980373965791232?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 August 8, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 Sinema has had a tortured relationship with Biden and many Democrats, particularly progressives. When Democrats controlled the Senate in 2021 and 2022 by just a single vote, Sinema acted to block proposals that would have increased taxes on the wealthy, voted against raising the minimum wage and protected the filibuster, which requires most legislation to pass with at least 60 votes.\par \par \uc2 She is up for re-election next year, though she has not said if she will stand for another term. Today, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://emersoncollegepolling.com/arizona-2024-senator-kyrsten-sinemas-independent-candidacy-could-help-democrats-for-u-s-senate/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Emerson College released polling}}}\uc2  showing that if Sinema is on the ballot, she will probably pull support from the Republican candidate \u8211\'20\'13 not whoever the Democrats nominate. If that trend holds, it will be good news for Biden\u8217\'20\'19s allies, who are defending several Senate seats in red or swing states next year, and can only afford to lose one and maintain their majority in the chamber.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.40pm BST\par \par \uc2 Biden links Grand Canyon national monument to fight against climate change\par \par \uc2 As he announced {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/environment/2023/aug/08/biden-grand-canyon-new-national-monument"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a new million-acre national monument}}}\uc2  around the Grand Canyon, \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  connected the move to his fights against climate change and rightwing culture war policies.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI made a commitment as president to prioritize respect for the tribal sovereignty and self determination, to honor the solemn promises the United States made to tribal nations, to fulfill federal trust and treaty obligations,\u8221\'20\'1D Biden said.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CAt a time when some seek to ban books and bury history, we\u8217\'20\'19re making it clear that we can\u8217\'20\'19t just choose to learn only what we want to know. We should learn everything that\u8217\'20\'19s good or bad, the truth about who we are as a nation. That\u8217\'20\'19s what great nations do.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The new Baaj Nwaavjo I\u8217\'20\'19tah Kukveni Grand Canyon national monument is the homeland for several tribes, and includes the headwaters of the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/may/22/colorado-river-states-california-arizona-nevada"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 drought-stricken}}}\uc2  Colorado river.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CPreserving these lands is good not only for Arizona but for the planet. It\u8217\'20\'19s good for the economy, it\u8217\'20\'19s good for the soul of the nation, and I believe \u8230\'20\'26 to my core it\u8217\'20\'19s the right thing to do. But there\u8217\'20\'19s more work ahead to combat the existential threat of climate change,\u8221\'20\'1D Biden said.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 8.45pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.23pm BST\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 , who {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.presidency.ucsb.edu/statistics/data/presidential-news-conferences"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 is lagging his predecessors}}}\uc2  when it comes to giving news conferences and interviews to reporters, has sat for a one-on-0ne with the \uc2 Weather Channel\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The network said its interview airs tomorrow, and will concern climate change:\par \par \uc2 enltrEXCLUSIVE: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/POTUS?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @POTUS}}}\uc2  sits down with \uc2 The Weather Channel\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/StephanieAbrams?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @StephanieAbrams}}}\uc2  to discuss our changing planet.\par \par \uc2 Join us WEDNESDAY from 6 a.m. - noon ET on air and on our TV app: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/Feaf8zTBxX"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/Feaf8zTBxX}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/W8JegkTisT"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/W8JegkTisT}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 \uc2 The Weather Channel\uc2  (@weatherchannel) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/weatherchannel/status/1688901016689971200?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 August 8, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 Expect the president to talk about the Inflation Reduction Act, both in that interview and in his speech today at the Grand Canyon. Signed about a year ago, the measure is the first piece of federal legislation intended to address climate change.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.59pm BST\par \par \uc2 Few places in America are more beautiful than the Grand Canyon, which those aboard Air Force One got a good view of when \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  arrived yesterday:\par \par \uc2 Air Force One over the Grand Canyon, before landing in Arizona. Photograph: Jonathan Ernst/Reuters\par \par \uc2 According to the White House, the president will in a few minutes speak from the Red Butte Airfield, an abandoned facility that local broadcaster KPNX calls {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.12news.com/article/travel/president-biden-speaks-in-arizona-tuesday-5-things-to-know/75-9eaec4ed-7f9f-4fb5-a8de-aabd11c843fb"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1Cone of Arizona\u8217\'20\'19s hidden gems\u8221\'20\'1D}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.40pm BST\par \par \uc2 Biden moves to protect Grand Canyon from uranium mining\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  is spending today in Arizona, where at 2pm eastern time he will announce that he is designating about one million acres around the Grand Canyon as a national monument, which will also protect it from uranium mining.\par \par \uc2 The Guardian\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/maanvi-singh"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Maanvi Singh}}}\uc2  and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/mary-yang"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Mary Yang}}}\uc2  have more:\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  will designate a \u8220\'20\'1Cnearly 1m acres\u8221\'20\'1D expanse around the Grand Canyon as a new national monument, protecting the region from future uranium mining.\par \par \uc2 The designation, which Biden is expected to announce on Tuesday comes after years-long lobbying by tribal leaders and local environmentalists to block mining projects that they say would damage the Colorado River watershed and important cultural sites.\par \par \uc2 The new Baaj Nwaavjo I\u8217\'20\'19tah Kukveni Grand Canyon national monument encompasses the headwaters of the Colorado River, as well as the habitat of the endangered California condor. It is also the homeland of several tribes. Baaj Nwaavjo means \u8220\'20\'1Cwhere tribes roam\u8221\'20\'1D for the Havasupai tribe and I\u8217\'20\'19tah Kukveni means \u8220\'20\'1Cour footprints\u8221\'20\'1D for the Hopi tribe.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CEstablishing the Baaj Nwaavjo I\u8217\'20\'19tah Kukveni \u8211\'20\'13 Ancestral Footprints of the Grand Canyon National Monument honors our solemn promise to Tribal Nations to respect sovereignty, preserves America\u8217\'20\'19s iconic landscapes for future generations, and advances my commitment to protect and conserve at least 30% of our nation\u8217\'20\'19s land and waters by 2030,\u8221\'20\'1D Biden said in a statement.\par \par \uc2 In 2012, the Obama administration had {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.washingtonpost.com/news/energy-environment/wp/2017/12/12/federal-appeals-court-upholds-obama-era-uranium-mining-ban-around-grand-canyon-tuesday-but-allows-nearby-mine-to-open/?itid=lk_inline_manual_38"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 blocked new mining on federal land in the area}}}\uc2  \u8211\'20\'13 but the protections are due to expire by 2023. The new designation would protect the area in perpetuity. Mining industry officials have said they will attempt to challenge the decision.\par \par \uc2 Congress has been exploring new laws to boost national uranium production and enrichment, in an effort to reduce the US\u8217\'20\'19s dependence on Russian imports.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/environment/2023/aug/08/biden-grand-canyon-new-national-monument"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Biden to designate 1m acres around Grand Canyon a national monument}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 6.50pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.21pm BST\par \par \uc2 The supreme court\u8217\'20\'19s grant of a Biden administration request to reinstate its regulations on ghost guns while a legal challenge continues came about after a split among the six-member conservative majority.\par \par \uc2 Conservatives \uc2 Brett Kavanaugh\uc2 , \uc2 Neil Gorsuch\uc2 , \uc2 Samuel Alito\uc2  and \uc2 Clarence Thomas\uc2  dissented, while \uc2 Amy Coney Barrett\uc2  and \uc2 John Roberts\uc2  joined with the court\u8217\'20\'19s three liberals in allowing the regulations to remains in place, at least for now, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://news.bloomberglaw.com/us-law-week/bidens-ghost-gun-rule-can-stay-in-effect-supreme-court-says"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Bloomberg News reports}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Expect further litigating over the rules, which \uc2 Bloomberg\uc2  reports were put in place by the Biden administration to stop gun violence, only to be challenged in court:\par \par \uc2 The ATF rule subjects gun kits to the same federal requirements as fully assembled firearms, meaning dealers must include serial numbers, conduct background checks and keep records of transactions.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt isn\u8217\'20\'19t extreme. It\u8217\'20\'19s just basic common sense,\u8221\'20\'1D Biden said when he announced the rule at a White House event last year.\par \par \uc2 US District Judge \uc2 Reed O\u8217\'20\'19Connor\uc2  tossed out the regulation, and a three-judge panel of the 5th US Circuit Court of Appeals had left the core of his ruling in force while it considers the administration\u8217\'20\'19s appeal on an expedited basis. All four lower court judges are Republican appointees.\par \par \uc2 Alito last week temporarily blocked O\u8217\'20\'19Connor\u8217\'20\'19s order while the high court decided how to handle the case.\par \par \uc2 The key legal issue is whether gun kits can be classified as \u8220\'20\'1Cfirearms\u8221\'20\'1D under a 1968 law that imposes requirements on dealers. The administration contends that kits qualify as firearms because the law covers items that can \u8220\'20\'1Creadily be converted\u8221\'20\'1D into functional weapons. The disputed weapons can be assembled by almost anyone in as little as 20 minutes, US Solicitor General \uc2 Elizabeth Prelogar\uc2  said in court papers.\par \par \uc2 The rule is being challenged by a collection of manufacturers, dealers, individuals and gun-rights groups. They say the administration is trying to change a 50-year-old understanding of the 1968 Gun Control Act.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.02pm BST\par \par \uc2 US Supreme Court\uc2  backs Biden curbs on "ghost guns"\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 US Supreme Court\uc2  has just granted a request by \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s administration to reinstate - at least for now - a federal regulation aimed at reining in privately made firearms called \u8220\'20\'1C {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/aug/24/us-ghost-guns-new-rules-untraceable"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 ghost guns}}}\uc2  \u8221\'20\'1D that are difficult for law enforcement to trace, Reuters reports.\par \par \uc2 The news agency further writes:\par \par \uc2 The justices put on hold a July 5 decision by US District Judge \uc2 Reed O\u8217\'20\'19Connor\uc2  in Fort Worth, Texas that had blocked the 2022 rule nationwide pending the administration\u8217\'20\'19s appeal.\par \par \uc2 O\u8217\'20\'19Connor found that the administration exceeded its authority under a 1968 federal law called the Gun Control Act in implementing the rule relating to ghost guns, firearms that are privately assembled and lack the usual serial numbers required by the federal government.\par \par \uc2 The rule, issued by the \uc2 Bureau of Alcohol, Tobacco, Firearms and Explosives\uc2  (ATF) in 2022 to target the rapid proliferation of the homemade weapons, bans \u8220\'20\'1Cbuy build shoot\u8221\'20\'1D kits without serial numbers that individuals can get online or at a store without a background check. The kits can be quickly assembled into a working firearm.\par \par \uc2 The rule clarified that ghost guns qualify as \u8220\'20\'1Cfirearms\u8221\'20\'1D under the federal Gun Control Act, expanding the definition of a firearm to include parts and kits that may be readily turned into a gun. It required serial numbers and that manufacturers and sellers be licensed. Sellers under the rule also must run background checks on purchasers prior to a sale.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/commentisfree/2023/jun/22/alitos-wrongdoing-makes-a-supreme-court-ethics-overhaul-an-imperative"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Conservative}}}\uc2  Justice {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/law/2023/jun/21/samuel-alito-undisclosed-gifts-billionaire-paul-singer-supreme-court"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Samuel Alito}}}\uc2 , who handles emergency matters arising from a group of states including Texas, on July 28 temporarily blocked O\u8217\'20\'19Connor\u8217\'20\'19s decision to give the justices time to decide how to proceed.\par \par \uc2 The administration on July 27 asked the justices to halt O\u8217\'20\'19Connor\u8217\'20\'19s ruling that invalidated a Justice Department restriction on the sale of ghost gun kits while it appeals to the New Orleans-based 5th U.S. Circuit Court of Appeals.\par \par \uc2 The administration said that allowing the O\u8217\'20\'19Connor\u8217\'20\'19s ruling to stand would enable an \u8220\'20\'1Cirreversible flow of large numbers of untraceable ghost guns into our nation\u8217\'20\'19s communities.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Supreme Court Justice \uc2 Samuel Alito\uc2 , featured in the center of a campaign sign held up by Nikki Tran of Washington on May 3, 2022, less than 24 hours after the unprecedented leak of the draft opinion that overturned Roe v Wade, which was confirmed the following month. Photograph: Jacquelyn Martin/AP\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 6.05pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.50pm BST\par \par \uc2 Who is James Uthmeier, Florida governor \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s newly-designated campaign manager for the Republican\u8217\'20\'19s presidential bid?\par \par \uc2 Another youthful face now at the head of extremist DeSantis\u8217\'20\'19s campaign, Uthmeier was gubernatorial chief of staff after being DeSantis\u8217\'20\'19s general counsel, but he\u8217\'20\'19s also a former senior adviser to \uc2 Wilbur Ross\uc2 , a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/news/2017/nov/05/trump-commerce-secretary-wilbur-ross-business-links-putin-family-paradise-papers"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 controversial}}}\uc2  commerce secretary {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2019/sep/09/wilbur-ross-sharpiegate-alabama-resignation"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 in the Trump}}}\uc2  administration.\par \par \uc2 enltr??BREAKING: \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2  has replaced his presidential campaign manager, Generra Peck, with his gubernatorial office's chief of staff, James Uthmeier.\par \par \uc2 This latest shakeup comes after the DeSantis shed his staff in mid-July.\par \par \uc2 It\u8217\'20\'19s apparent that a shakeup was needed with DeSantis\u8230\'20\'26 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/0LAdaivf31"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/0LAdaivf31}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 I Meme Therefore I Am ???? (@ImMeme0) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/ImMeme0/status/1688939388724449283?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 August 8, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 Reuters further reports that:\par \par \uc2 It is unclear what direction Uthmeier will take the DeSantis campaign as its new manager. He has relatively little experience with campaigns or electoral politics in general.\par \par \uc2 The latest shakeup fits into a historical pattern for DeSantis, said Whit Ayres, a Republican operative who was DeSantis\u8217\'20\'19 pollster when he ran for Florida governor in 2018. \u8220\'20\'1CThis is par for the course for DeSantis\u8217\'20\'19 campaigns. He\u8217\'20\'19s run for Congress three times, and for governor twice. He had different campaign staff for all five campaigns. It is very difficult to run for president the first time if you have nobody around you who has presidential experience,\u8221\'20\'1D he added.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.28pm BST\par \par \uc2 Florida governor Ron DeSanti s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/aug/08/trump-jan-6-ohio-abortion-vote-republican-biden-latest-news?page=with:block-64d2531a8f083b553df02b90#block-64d2531a8f083b553df02b90"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 has replaced}}}\uc2  the campaign manager of his bid to win the 2024 Republican nomination for US president, Generra Peck, four days after Robert Bigelow, the biggest individual donor to a group supporting the DeSantis candidacy, told Reuters he would not donate more money unless the governor changes his approach because \u8220\'20\'1Cextremism isn\u8217\'20\'19t going to get you elected,\u8221\'20\'1D the news agency reports. The new campaign manager will be close adviser James Uthmeier.\par \par \uc2 Reuters further reports:\par \par \uc2 Bigelow said he had told Peck, who he called \u8220\'20\'1Ca very good campaign manager,\u8221\'20\'1D that DeSantis needed to be more moderate to have a chance.\par \par \uc2 Asked how Peck reacted, Bigelow said, laughing: \u8220\'20\'1CThere was a long period of silence where I thought maybe she had passed out. But I think she took it all in.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 DeSantis is running second in the race for the Republican nomination to face Democratic President \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  in the November 2024 election, but has been sinking in opinion polls for months. The latest Reuters/\uc2 Ipsos\uc2  poll put his national support at just 13%, far behind former President Trump, at 47%.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CJames Uthmeier has been one of Governor DeSantis\u8217\'20\'19 top advisors for years and he is needed where it matters most: working hand in hand with Generra Peck and the rest of the team to put the governor in the best possible position to win this primary and defeat \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 ,\u8221\'20\'1D Romeo, the communications director, said in a statement.\par \par \uc2 DeSantis had been facing increasing pressure from donors to change tack in recent months as he continued to drop in the polls and he burned through cash at a faster-than-expected rate.\par \par \uc2 Dan Eberhart\uc2 , a prominent Republican donor, suggested that the move was still too tepid.\par \par \uc2 DeSantis faces a crucial moment on August 23 in Milwaukee, Wisconsin, at the first Republican debate of the 2024 campaign. \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  has said he plans to skip the debate, which would make DeSantis the focus of attacks from other candidates.\par \par \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2  looks into the crowd after speaking as supporters of former US president \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  hold up signs during a barbecue fundraiser in Cedar Rapids, Iowa, on Sunday. Photograph: Joseph Cress/\uc2 USA TODAY NETWORK\uc2 /Reuters\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 5.30pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.58pm BST\par \par \uc2 The day so far\par \par \uc2 Democrats and Republicans are closely watching a special election in Ohio that could indicate if voters, even in red states, are willing to protect \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access. Buckeye state residents are considering {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/aug/08/trump-jan-6-ohio-abortion-vote-republican-biden-latest-news?page=with:block-64d232b38f083b553df029e6#block-64d232b38f083b553df029e6"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Issue 1}}}\uc2 , a GOP-backed measure that would make it more difficult to change the state constitution, which reproductives rights advocates are {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/aug/08/trump-jan-6-ohio-abortion-vote-republican-biden-latest-news?page=with:block-64d240048f088246c33073c2#block-64d240048f088246c33073c2"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 asking voters to do in November to ensure \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  remains legal}}}\uc2 . Today\u8217\'20\'19s election is viewed as a test of whether the issue, which so animated voters in last year\u8217\'20\'19s midterm elections and was seen as one reason why Democrats nationwide performed better than expected, remains as potent as it once was. Polls close in Ohio at 7.30pm eastern time.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s what else is going on today:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 If Issue 1 is approved in Ohio, election-day turnout will likely be crucial, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/aug/08/trump-jan-6-ohio-abortion-vote-republican-biden-latest-news?page=with:block-64d24f3f8f083b553df02b50#block-64d24f3f8f083b553df02b50"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a top political analyst says}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2  is {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/aug/08/trump-jan-6-ohio-abortion-vote-republican-biden-latest-news?page=with:block-64d2531a8f083b553df02b90#block-64d2531a8f083b553df02b90"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 replacing his campaign manager}}}\uc2  in an effort to jump-start his floundering presidential bid.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The Washington DC grand jury that last week indicted Donald Trump{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/aug/08/trump-jan-6-ohio-abortion-vote-republican-biden-latest-news?page=with:block-64d25b2c8f0890cce121a5b7#block-64d25b2c8f0890cce121a5b7"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 is continuing its work}}}\uc2 , for reasons that remain unknown.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.42pm BST\par \par \uc2 About a year ago, former \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  adviser \uc2 Peter Navarro\uc2  was {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/jun/03/peter-navarro-indicted-trump-adviser-capitol-attack-inquiry"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 indicted for defying a subpoena}}}\uc2  issued by the congressional committee investigating the January 6 attack.\par \par \uc2 Navarro\u8217\'20\'19s case still has not been resolved, and Politico reports that in a filing today, the ex-president\u8217\'20\'19s ally is seeking to further delay his trial:\par \par \uc2 enltrPeter NAVARRO subpoenaed Trump spokeswoman Liz HARRINGTON to appear at an Aug. 28 hearing ahead of his Sept. 5 criminal contempt trial \u8212\'20\'14 only to learn she\u8217\'20\'19s due to give birth on Aug. 29.\par \par \uc2 Now he wants to delay the hearing *and* the trial (which has already been delayed 9 months) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/a2MhGiHRM8"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/a2MhGiHRM8}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Kyle Cheney (@kyledcheney) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/kyledcheney/status/1688873100685856768?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 August 8, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 4.43pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.29pm BST\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s trial over the election subversion plot is a long way off, and the Guardian\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/hugo-lowell"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Hugo Lowell}}}\uc2  reports that his lawyers are currently wrangling with prosecutors over what evidence the former president can share publicly:\par \par \uc2 Federal prosecutors asked a federal judge to reject {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/donaldtrump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Donald Trump\u8217\'20\'19s}}}\uc2  request for fewer restrictions over how he can publicly share evidence in the case involving his efforts to subvert the 2020 election, arguing the former president was seeking to abuse the discovery process.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe defendant seeks to use the discovery material to litigate this case in the media,\u8221\'20\'1D prosecutors {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://storage.courtlistener.com/recap/gov.uscourts.dcd.258149/gov.uscourts.dcd.258149.15.0_1.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 wrote in an eight-page brief}}}\uc2  on Monday. \u8220\'20\'1CBut that is contrary to the purpose of criminal discovery, which is to afford defendants the ability to prepare for and mount a defense in court.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The court filings, submitted to the US district court judge \uc2 Tanya Chutkan\uc2 , who is overseeing the case, highlighted comments made over the weekend by Trump\u8217\'20\'19s lawyer John Lauro about the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/aug/06/trump-attorney-pence-election-conspiracy-trial"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 former vice-president Mike Pence being a potential witness}}}\uc2  to stress the importance of strict restrictions.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThis district\u8217\'20\'19s rules prohibit defense counsel from doing precisely what he has stated he intends to do with discovery if permitted: publicize, outside of court, details of this case, including the testimony of anticipated witnesses,\u8221\'20\'1D prosecutors wrote.\par \par \uc2 Trump has characterized the indictment, charging him with four felonies over his attempt to obstruct the congressional certification of \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s election win on 6 January 2021 and overturn the results of the 2020 election, as a political witch-hunt and infringing on his first amendment rights.\par \par \uc2 To that end, his lawyers filed a brief earlier on Monday asking the judge to issue a less restrictive protective order, a routine step in criminal cases to ensure evidence turned over to defendants in discovery is used to help construct a defense and not to chill witnesses.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/aug/07/trump-evidence-witness-transcripts-january-6"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Prosecutors seek to prevent Trump from sharing January 6 case evidence}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.14pm BST\par \par \uc2 Trump grand jury continues work in Washington DC\par \par \uc2 CNN reports that the grand jury which last week indicted \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  on charges {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/aug/03/trump-arraignment-indictment-jan-6-2020-election"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 related to his failed effort to overturn the 2020 election}}}\uc2  has returned to work in Washington DC:\par \par \uc2 enltrThe grand jury that handed up an indictment against Trump last week is meeting again today at the federal courthouse in Washington, DC.\par \par \uc2 This indicates the investigation into election interference is ongoing.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Casey Gannon (@caseyagannon) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/caseyagannon/status/1688898955055091713?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 August 8, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 It\u8217\'20\'19s unclear what evidence prosecutors may be presenting to the jurors.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.58pm BST\par \par \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2  is trying everything to turn his campaign around, including proposing {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/aug/04/ron-desantis-slitting-throats-federal-jobs-president-campaign#:~:text=%E2%80%9COn%20bureaucracy%2C%20you%20know%2C,wants%20to%20protect%20its%20own.%E2%80%9D"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1Cslitting throats\u8221\'20\'1D}}}\uc2  and, most recently, deploying tactics used in the Iraq war on the US border, the Guardian\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/martin-pengelly"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Martin Pengelly}}}\uc2  reports:\par \par \uc2 The rightwing Florida governor and 2024 presidential hopeful {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/ron-desantis"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Ron DeSantis}}}\uc2  has sparked controversy by outlining a hardline border policy of deadly force despite acknowledging that drug traffickers could be difficult to distinguish from migrants crossing into the US.\par \par \uc2 DeSantis, whose ailing campaign has failed to cut into the lead of the Republican frontrunner, \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , said that under his direction as president, US law enforcement on the lookout for drugs would not mistakenly use lethal force on migrants because US agents would have \u8220\'20\'1Crules of engagement\u8221\'20\'1D similar to police or US forces in war zones like Iraq.\par \par \uc2 In {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nbcnews.com/politics/2024-election/ron-desantis-of-course-trump-lost-2020-election-rcna98200"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 an NBC interview}}}\uc2  broadcast on Monday night, the Republican Florida governor was asked about a campaign-trail promise: \u8220\'20\'1CIf cartels are trying to run product into this country, they\u8217\'20\'19re going to end up {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.foxnews.com/politics/desantis-vows-use-deadly-force-border-stop-cartel-operatives-stone-cold-dead"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 stone-cold dead}}}\uc2 .\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CHow do you know you\u8217\'20\'19re using deadly force against the right people?\u8221\'20\'1D his interviewer, Dasha Burns, asked.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CSame way a police officer would know,\u8221\'20\'1D DeSantis said. \u8220\'20\'1CSame way somebody operating in Iraq would know.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/aug/08/desantis-claims-agents-can-tell-traffickers-from-migrants-in-call-for-deadly-force"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 DeSantis claims agents can tell traffickers from migrants in call for deadly force}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.39pm BST\par \par \uc2 DeSantis replaces top manager in effort to shore up flailing campaign - report\par \par \uc2 Florida governor \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s once-promising campaign for the Republican presidential nomination {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/aug/04/ron-desantis-donor-super-pac-florida"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 is not looking so hot}}}\uc2 , and today, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://themessenger.com/politics/desantis-new-campaign-manager-exclusive"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 The Messenger reports}}}\uc2  he will replace a top staffer with a veteran from his administration.\par \par \uc2 From The Messenger\u8217\'20\'19s exclusive:\par \par \uc2 In his third staff shakeup in less than a month, Florida Gov. \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2  replaced his embattled presidential campaign manager with one of his most trusted, and most conservative, advisers: his gubernatorial office\u8217\'20\'19s chief of staff, James Uthmeier.\par \par \uc2 Outgoing campaign manager Generra Peck will remain as chief strategist on the campaign as part of the restructuring. Peck guided DeSantis\u8217\'20\'19s blowout reelection bid last year, but she quickly became the subject of criticism from DeSantis advisers and donors in mid-July after his presidential campaign stalled and money dried up.\par \par \uc2 The campaign then twice {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://themessenger.com/politics/ron-desantiss-campaign-crashes-into-reality"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  cut staff and expenses}}}\uc2  and retooled DeSantis\u8217\'20\'19s press strategy to make him more available to the mainstream media.\par \par \uc2 But {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://themessenger.com/politics/biggest-desantis-donor-says-no-more-money-until-changes-are-made"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 donors}}}\uc2  and some outside advisers weren\u8217\'20\'19t satisfied, leading DeSantis last week to ask Uthmeier to diagnose problems with the campaign and see if he could fix them. Ultimately, it led the governor to ask Uthmeier to take the job.\par \par \uc2 Uthmeier shies away from calling the reshuffling a \u8220\'20\'1Creboot.\u8221\'20\'1D It\u8217\'20\'19s a despised word in the campaign, where advisers prefer to call this the last campaign \u8220\'20\'1Creload\u8221\'20\'1D \u8212\'20\'14 and say they\u8217\'20\'19re going to win, despite the naysayers and early polling.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CPeople have written Governor DeSantis\u8217\'20\'19s obituary many times,\u8221\'20\'1D Uthmeier said in a written statement to The Messenger. \u8220\'20\'1CFrom his race against establishment primary candidate Adam Putnam, to his victory over legacy media-favored candidate \uc2 Andrew Gillum\uc2  [in 2018], to his twenty point win over \uc2 Charlie Crist\uc2  [in 2022], Governor DeSantis has proven that he knows how to win. He\u8217\'20\'19s breaking records on fundraising and has a supporting super PAC with $100 million in the bank and an incredible ground game. Get ready.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.22pm BST\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s what Kyle Kondik, managing editor of political newsletter Sabato\u8217\'20\'19s Crystal Ball, will be assessing today to determine which way Ohio voters are leaning on Issue 1:\par \par \uc2 enltrIn re: Issue 1 in Ohio today, remember from past elections that the early/absentee vote (which will come out first after polls close at 7:30) will almost certainly overstate how Dem the electorate is (or, in this case, the size of the "no" advantage on this issue)\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Kyle Kondik (@kkondik) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/kkondik/status/1688909601398550529?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 August 8, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 enltrIF this thing is close - not a given - a few counties I'll be watching are Wood (south of Toledo, Bowling Green); Portage (Kent State, east of Akron), and Erie (Sandusky). Wood has been a recent bellwether; Erie and Portage are old pieces of the D coalition that have reddened\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Kyle Kondik (@kkondik) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/kkondik/status/1688910432164274176?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 August 8, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 enltrseems clear that the GOP needs a big Election Day turnout today. Some of the big counties post live turnout if curious - what GOP is looking for is for Election Day to eventually swamp the vote cast early\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Kyle Kondik (@kkondik) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/kkondik/status/1688911088665219072?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 August 8, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.01pm BST\par \par \uc2 Ahead of the Ohio special election today, \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  foes were out on the streets of Cincinnati, encouraging people to vote yes on Issue 1:\par \par \uc2 A sign asking Ohioans to vote in support of Issue 1 sits above another sign advocating against \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights on 20 July in Cincinnati. Photograph: Patrick Orsagos/AP\par \par \uc2 Here are scenes from across the state today, as voters head to the polls:\par \par \uc2 Voters come and go at the Beachwood Community Center in Beachwood, Ohio during the special election on Issue 1. Photograph: David Petkiewicz/AP A man arrives at the Brooklyn Senior Community Center, in Brooklyn, Ohio to vote on Issue 1. Photograph: David Petkiewicz/AP\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.42pm BST\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  is not explicitly on the ballot today in Ohio, nor is redistricting. Rather, the question before Buckeye state voters concerns whether to make it harder to get measures that would undermine Republican policies on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  and redistricting onto ballots in the future. Yes, that is kind of confusing, but fortunately for us, the Guardian\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/ava-sasani"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Ava Sasani}}}\uc2  is here with an explainer that should answer all your questions:\par \par \uc2 On Tuesday, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/ohio"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Ohio}}}\uc2  will hold a special election that could make it harder for the state\u8217\'20\'19s voters to amend their own constitution.\par \par \uc2 Republican lawmakers in May approved \u8220\'20\'1CIssue 1,\u8221\'20\'1D a proposal that would raise the threshold required to pass any future ballot measure amending Ohio\u8217\'20\'19s constitution from a simple majority to 60% of voters.\par \par \uc2 Voting \u8220\'20\'1Cyes\u8221\'20\'1D on Issue 1 would make it more difficult for Ohio citizens to amend the state constitution, raising the threshold to 60% of all voters. The change would be effective immediately.\par \par \uc2 Voting \u8220\'20\'1Cno\u8221\'20\'1D on Issue 1 would keep the current method of creating and passing a citizen-led state constitutional amendment. Since 1912, Ohio has allowed a simple majority of voters to approve constitutional amendments through ballot questions.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/aug/08/ohio-special-election-issue-1-abortion-rights"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Republicans pushed a special election in Ohio \u8211\'20\'13 what does it mean for \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  rights?}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.22pm BST\par \par \uc2 Both \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights and democracy at stake in Ohio election\par \par \uc2 If voters today approve Issue 1, the Republican-backed measure that would make it harder to change Ohio\u8217\'20\'19s state constitution via the popular vote, the impacts will extend beyond \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights.\par \par \uc2 While Issue 1\u8217\'20\'19s passage would make it much more difficult for a constitutional amendment protecting access to the procedure to qualify for the November ballot, it would also help the state\u8217\'20\'19s Republican lawmakers protect their political power. How? \uc2 The Guardian\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/sam-levine"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Sam Levine}}}\uc2  explains:\par \par \uc2 Currently, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/ohio"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Ohio}}}\uc2  requires activists to get a certain number of signatures on petitions, both statewide and in 44 of 88 counties, to send an amendment to the ballot. In each of the 44 counties, the total number of signatures needs to be equivalent to 5% of the vote in that county in the last gubernatorial race. Statewide, the total has to be equivalent to 10% of the same.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.ohiosos.gov/globalassets/elections/2023/spec/issuereport.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Issue 1}}}\uc2 , the only question on Tuesday\u8217\'20\'19s ballot, would make that process considerably harder. It would require supporters to get the signatures in all 88 counties and then obtain a 60% supermajority for an amendment to pass.\par \par \uc2 The vote comes just three months before Ohio is to rule on a constitutional amendment to protect \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights in November. Republicans have {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.statenews.org/government-politics/2023-06-06/larose-says-issue-1-is-100-about-stopping-possible-abortion-amendment"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 openly said}}}\uc2  that Issue 1 is an attempt {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/AndrewJTobias/status/1603130384744534016?s=20&t=VwO_MBEHrPVV-CIASKq2UA"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 to block}}}\uc2  the \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  measure from passing.\par \par \uc2 The vote is also an effort to preserve Republican political power in Ohio. Activists in the state are crafting a constitutional amendment that would strip state lawmakers of their ability to draw electoral districts and hand it over to an independent commission instead. Last year, Republicans {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.whio.com/news/local/ohio-supreme-court-rejects-gop-drawn-statehouse-maps-5th-time/G5O7V3AMGRGKHGRVO6UB67YMUE/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 repeatedly ignored rebukes}}}\uc2  from the supreme court calling for the redrawing of district lines because they were too distorted in favor of Republicans. Republicans eventually ran out the clock, preserved their supermajority in the state legislature, and then used that supermajority to refer Issue 1 to the ballot.\par \par \uc2 Polling has been limited and it is difficult to predict the results of a ballot referendum. The average of three polls, all of which have slightly different wording, have shown 35% of Ohioans support the change, 45% oppose it, and 20% aren\u8217\'20\'19t sure, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://fivethirtyeight.com/features/ohio-issue-1-abortion-ballot-measures/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 according to FiveThirtyEight.}}}\uc2  Similar measures to raise the threshold for constitutional amendments in other states have failed in recent years, the outlet noted.\par \par \uc2 If the measure passes, opponents say, it would effectively institute minority rule in Ohio. Supporters say it should be harder for citizens to amend the state constitution. That argument is not supported by data \u8211\'20\'13 roughly 75% of the citizen-initiated constitutional amendments over the last century have failed. Ohio also allows the legislature to send constitutional amendments to the ballot and voters have approved 106 out of 157 since 1914, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cleveland.com/news/2023/07/how-hard-is-it-to-amend-ohios-constitution-how-do-other-states-do-it-key-questions-and-answers-for-state-issue-1.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 according to cleveland.com}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/aug/08/ohio-issue-1-constitution-amendment"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Ohioans vote in election that could determine future of majority rule}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.00pm BST\par \par \uc2 Ohio votes in proxy battle over \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights\par \par \uc2 Good morning, US politics blog readers. The state of Ohio is holding an unusual special election in the middle of the summer today, where voters are being asked what seems like a fairly innocuous question: should the bar for changing the state constitution via a ballot initiative be raised to 60% support, from its current simple majority? But the measure, which would also increase the number of signatures required for campaigners to get an initiative on the ballot, is, in fact, a Republican-backed attempt to undermine a constitutional amendment protecting \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access that is expected to go to voters in November. If the measure up for consideration today, known as Issue 1, succeeds, it could make it much more difficult for the \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  amendment to qualify for the ballot.\par \par \uc2 Republicans dominate the state government in right-leaning Ohio, and even before Roe v Wade was overturned, passed a law restricting the procedure after six weeks of pregnancy, though its implementation is {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/oct/07/ohio-court-blocks-six-week-abortion-ban-indefinitely"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 currently blocked by a judge\u8217\'20\'19s ruling}}}\uc2 . But {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/aug/03/kansas-abortion-vote-state-constitution"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 even in red states}}}\uc2 , reproductive rights advocates and their Democratic allies have seen success in protecting \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  at the ballot box, and they\u8217\'20\'19re hoping to repeat that today.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s what else is going on:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Mike Pence\uc2  said he has qualified to appear on the stage when the first Republican presidential debate is hosted on 23 August.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  is in Arizona, where {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://apnews.com/article/grand-canyon-monument-biden-tribes-1fa3d27c48651e2dc844c9c49a0cd14f"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 he will designate}}}\uc2  a new national monument near the Grand Canyon intended to protect the national park from mining.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Legal wrangling continues in \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s case over the attempts to overturn the 2020 election, with {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/aug/07/trump-evidence-witness-transcripts-january-6"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the judge yesterday ordering}}}\uc2  a hearing to consider prosecutors\u8217\'20\'19 request for limits on what information the former president can share publicly.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020230808ej88001ml\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
