\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Judge dismisses Trump\u8217\'20\'19s countersuit against E Jean Carroll that claimed she defamed him \u8211\'20\'13 as it happened\b0\par\par\uc2 Aben\u233\'00\'E9 Clayton (now); Chris Stein, US politics live blogger, and Martin Pengelly (earlier) \par \uc2 6,683 \uc2 words\par \uc2 7 August 2023\par 22:10 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 This live blog is now closed. You can read our full report about Trump\u8217\'20\'19s countersuit being thrown out here:Judge says E Jean Carroll allegation Trump raper her is \u8216\'20\'18substantially true\u8217\'20\'19\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.06pm BST\par \par \uc2 Summary\par \par \uc2 That\u8217\'20\'19s all for today\u8217\'20\'19s live blog. Here are some of the biggest news events of the day:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Attorneys for \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  filed a response to federal prosecutors request for a protective order. In it, Trump\u8217\'20\'19s lawyers ask that the judge reject the request.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s attempt to countersue E Jean Carroll, the advice columnist who won a $5m civil judgment earlier this year after a jury found he sexually abused her, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/aug/07/trump-social-post-jan-6-biden-desantis-2024-latest-news?page=with:block-64d118318f08d95cff6be874#block-64d118318f08d95cff6be874"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 was rejected by a judge}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Ron DeSantis{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/aug/07/trump-social-post-jan-6-biden-desantis-2024-latest-news?page=with:block-64d0f4778f08e5e4127d08c9#block-64d0f4778f08e5e4127d08c9"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 again rejected}}}\uc2  Trump\u8217\'20\'19s false claims about the 2020 election in an interview, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/aug/07/trump-social-post-jan-6-biden-desantis-2024-latest-news?page=with:block-64d0f8c28f08d95cff6be6ed#block-64d0f8c28f08d95cff6be6ed"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 drawing insults}}}\uc2  from a spokeswoman for the former president.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Aileen Cannon, the federal judge overseeing Trump\u8217\'20\'19s trial over the Mar-a-Lago documents, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/aug/07/trump-social-post-jan-6-biden-desantis-2024-latest-news?page=with:block-64d1005c8f08e5e4127d0969#block-64d1005c8f08e5e4127d0969"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 appeared to disclose}}}\uc2  an ongoing grand jury investigation in a court filing.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Ohio{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/aug/07/trump-social-post-jan-6-biden-desantis-2024-latest-news?page=with:block-64d114808f08e5e4127d0a71#block-64d114808f08e5e4127d0a71"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 will tomorrow}}}\uc2  vote on whether to raise the bar to amend the state constitution, part of a GOP-backed attempt to undermine a forthcoming ballot initiative to protect \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s our latest story on Trump\u8217\'20\'19s countersuit against E Jean Carroll being thrown out by a judge:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/aug/07/donald-trump-rape-language-e-jean-carroll"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Judge says E Jean Carroll allegation Trump raped her is \u8216\'20\'18substantially true\u8217\'20\'19 in court dismissal }}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 11.08pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.50pm BST\par \par \uc2 Key event\par \par \uc2 Attorneys for \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  have filed a response to a protective order requested by federal prosecutors in the former president\u8217\'20\'19s indictment for allegedly attempting to overturn the 2020 election.\par \par \uc2 The requested order is based on a a statement Trump made Friday: \u8220\'20\'1CIF YOU GO AFTER ME, I\u8217\'20\'19M COMING AFTER YOU!\u8221\'20\'1D Trump, however, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/aug/07/trump-social-post-jan-6-biden-desantis-2024-latest-news?page=with:block-64d1059e8f08e5e4127d0990#block-64d1059e8f08e5e4127d0990"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 argued}}}\uc2  he was just exercising his right to free speech.\par \par \uc2 Trump\u8217\'20\'19s lawyers argue that the former president\u8217\'20\'19s first amendment right is at risk of being restricted by the \uc2 US government\uc2  and the Biden administration during the election season, the response reads. Trump\u8217\'20\'19s legal team wants US district court judge \uc2 Tanya Chutkan\uc2 , who is overseeing Trump\u8217\'20\'19s election conspiracy case, to reject the order, describing it as \u8220\'20\'1Coverly broad\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Protective orders are common in criminal cases, but federal prosecutors said it is \u8220\'20\'1Cparticularly important in this case\u8221\'20\'1D because Trump has posted on social media about \u8220\'20\'1Cwitnesses, judges, attorneys, and others associated with legal matters pending against him\u8221\'20\'1D, the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://apnews.com/article/trump-election-capitol-riot-indictment-protective-order-71cd642e876c47fff4e1283c15f8ca01"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Associated Press reported}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 10.56pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.05pm BST\par \par \uc2 Hello, I am Aben\u233\'00\'E9 Clayton, a west coast reporter taking over the blog from my colleague Chris.\par \par \uc2 I\u8217\'20\'19ll be keeping an eye on the clock as Trump\u8217\'20\'19s attorneys the 5pm eastern time deadline for \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s attorneys response {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/aug/07/trump-social-post-jan-6-biden-desantis-2024-latest-news?page=with:block-64d0e1ec8f08e5e4127d07c4#block-64d0e1ec8f08e5e4127d07c4"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  to a request}}}\uc2  for a protective order in the January 6 case from special counsel Jack Smith, over a statement Trump made Friday: \u8220\'20\'1CIF YOU GO AFTER ME, I\u8217\'20\'19M COMING AFTER YOU!\u8221\'20\'1D Trump, however, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/aug/07/trump-social-post-jan-6-biden-desantis-2024-latest-news?page=with:block-64d1059e8f08e5e4127d0990#block-64d1059e8f08e5e4127d0990"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 argued}}}\uc2  he was just exercising his right to free speech.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.59pm BST\par \par \uc2 There\u8217\'20\'19s no telling when it might happen, but \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  could very well soon be indicted by a grand jury in Georgia\u8217\'20\'19s Fulton county for his campaign\u8217\'20\'19s attempt to overturn \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s victory in the state three years ago.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/jul/25/trump-georgia-investigation-fulton-county-prosecutors"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 All signs point to Trump}}}\uc2  being among those targeted by \uc2 Fani Willis\uc2 , the Atlanta-area district attorney investigating the election subversion effort by the former president and his allies. She has said a decision on who to bring charges against will be made before September.\par \par \uc2 CNN reported today that the street outside the Fulton county courthouse has been closed to the public in advance of the expected indictment:\par \par \uc2 enltrPolice in Atlanta have closed the street in front of the Fulton County Courthouse ahead of a possible indictment of \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 DA Fani Willis has said she will announce a charging decision by Sept. 1 in the probe of Trump's efforts to overturn his 2020 loss in Georgia. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/MnE7MlMvuW"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/MnE7MlMvuW}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 The Recount (@therecount) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/therecount/status/1688595189407924307?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 August 7, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.44pm BST\par \par \uc2 A battle is brewing between the Biden administration and America\u8217\'20\'19s electrical utilities, the Guardian\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/dharna-noor"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Dharna Noor}}}\uc2  and Floodlight\u8217\'20\'19s Kristi Swartz report. At issue are policies intended to cut down on greenhouse gas emissions, but which the utilities argue are too strict and complicated to carry out:\par \par \uc2 The main lobbying group for US electric utilities plans to oppose a Biden administration proposal to curb greenhouse gas emissions from existing gas power plants, raising questions about the industry\u8217\'20\'19s commitment to reducing planet-heating pollution.\par \par \uc2 The pushback will put the \uc2 Edison Electric Institute\uc2  (\uc2 EEI\uc2 ) out of step with many of its members\u8217\'20\'19 stated commitments to cut emissions, critics say. It also runs counters to the US voters\u8217\'20\'19 political views based on {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.dataforprogress.org/blog/2023/8/7/voters-support-the-epas-proposed-rules-on-coal-and-gas-fired-power-plants"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 new polling}}}\uc2  shared exclusively with the Guardian and Floodlight.\par \par \uc2 The power plant rules, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/environment/2023/may/11/new-rules-us-fossil-fuel-power-plant-emissions"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 first proposed}}}\uc2  in May, would force power providers to clean up certain large coal- and gas-fired plants, either by installing new greener technologies or shutting the projects down. The \uc2 Environmental Protection Agency\uc2  (\uc2 EPA\uc2 ) is asking states and utilities to submit plans on how they choose to limit those emissions within 24 months of the rules\u8217\'20\'19 final approval.\par \par \uc2 Public comments must be submitted by 8 August.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/aug/07/us-utilities-gas-power-plants-lobbying-eei-epa"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 US utilities oppose Biden efforts to make gas power plants cleaner }}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.29pm BST\par \par \uc2 The Guardian\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/chrismcgreal"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Chris McGreal}}}\uc2  has taken a closer look at the argument, made by many Republicans, of a link between asylum seekers and America\u8217\'20\'19s struggles with fentanyl, and finds that the rhetoric does not match the facts:\par \par \uc2 Republican politicians have been accused of exploiting the tragedy of America\u8217\'20\'19s fentanyl crisis by blaming {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/joebiden"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Joe Biden}}}\uc2  for the rising death toll, and linking it to his immigration policies and populist anger over the US\u8217\'20\'19s troubled southern border.\par \par \uc2 Critics say Republican leaders are guilty of a cynical political ploy by misrepresenting an increase in asylum seekers as a cause of the serious problem of cross-border drug smuggling driving a huge US public health crisis.\par \par \uc2 Fentanyl kills about 70,000 Americans a year. It is the leading cause of record drug overdose deaths in the US and the primary cause of death among adults under the age of 45.\par \par \uc2 The synthetic opioid, usually made from chemicals manufactured in China and put together in Mexico, is popular with drug cartels because it is many times more powerful than other narcotics and so requires smaller quantities, which are easier to smuggle than heroin or cocaine.\par \par \uc2 It is then laced into other drugs to boost their power and value. But because small amounts of the narcotic as so strong, fentanyl has driven up the number of accidental overdoses and deaths.\par \par \uc2 The Republicans\u8217\'20\'19 push to blame the Biden administration follows record seizures of fentanyl at the US\u8217\'20\'19s south-western frontier. Customs and Border Protection (CBP) has discovered {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cbp.gov/newsroom/stats/drug-seizure-statistics"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 three times}}}\uc2  as much of the drug so far this year as during the same period in 2022. If seizures continue at that rate, CBP is on course to confiscate enough fentanyl in 2023 to kill close to a billion people \u8211\'20\'13 and that is almost certainly only a fraction of the drug smuggled into the US.\par \par \uc2 The Republican party claims this is evidence that \u8220\'20\'1Ccartels have operational control of the border\u8221\'20\'1D. The speaker of the House of Representatives, Kevin McCarthy, tied the sharp increase in fentanyl seizures and deaths to the record number of undocumented migrants entering the US last year, and blamed the White House for letting them in. So did Congresswoman Mary Miller when she claimed that Biden and the homeland security secretary, Alejandro Mayorkas, \u8220\'20\'1Copened our borders and flooded our streets with fentanyl\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 When \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2  was looking for someone to blame for the escalating death toll from the supercharged opioid his eye naturally fell on Biden.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/aug/07/republicans-fentanyl-biden-asylum-seekers-cynicism"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Republicans accused of cynical ploy in blaming fentanyl crisis on Biden}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.11pm BST\par \par \uc2 When special counsel Jack Smith indicted \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  last week over the failed plot to overturn the 2020 election, he {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/aug/03/trump-arraignment-indictment-jan-6-2020-election"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 referenced the actions of six co-conspirators}}}\uc2 , but did not name them.\par \par \uc2 However, one of them is believed to be John Eastman, who served as Trump\u8217\'20\'19s attorney and was an architect of the legal strategy intended to stop \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  from entering the White House.\par \par \uc2 He\u8217\'20\'19s in the midst of defending his law license in California, where legal authorities have accused him of violating a number of ethics rules by participating in the election subversion attempt. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.politico.com/news/2023/08/07/eastman-trump-disbarment-postpone-00110131"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Politico reports today}}}\uc2  that Eastman is seeking to have the disbarment proceedings postponed, because he is worried he may soon face criminal charges:\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1C[R]ecent developments in the investigation have renewed and intensified [Eastman\u8217\'20\'19s] concerns that the federal government might bring charges against him,\u8221\'20\'1D his attorneys Randall Miller and Zachary Mayer {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.documentcloud.org/documents/23901160-sbc-23-o-30029-respondents-motion-for-abatement-of-state-bar-disciplinary-proceeding-declaration-of-zachary-mayer"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 wrote in an Aug. 4 filing}}}\uc2  posted to the court\u8217\'20\'19s public docket on Monday.\par \par \uc2 Miller said the growing concern about criminal charges might prompt Eastman to assert his Fifth Amendment rights during disbarment proceedings. The Fifth Amendment generally allows people to refuse to provide testimony that could be used against them. But invoking the Fifth Amendment in the disbarment proceedings would jeopardize Eastman\u8217\'20\'19s ability to defend his law license, his lawyers wrote.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1C[Eastman] requests that the Court exercise its discretion to stay the State Bar\u8217\'20\'19s disciplinary proceeding against him pending resolution of a parallel criminal investigation being conducted by Special Counsel Jack Smith and any trial or other proceedings that may result from that investigation,\u8221\'20\'1D Miller and Mayer wrote.\par \par \uc2 Bar discipline authorities {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.politico.com/news/2023/06/11/john-eastman-disbarment-trial-trump-00101407"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 have charged Eastman}}}\uc2  with multiple violations of professional rules and ethics \u8212\'20\'14 as well as the law \u8212\'20\'14 in his effort to upend the certified results of the 2020 election. Eastman\u8217\'20\'19s bar discipline trial began in June \u8212\'20\'14 and he had even testified for several hours without asserting his Fifth Amendment rights. But it was postponed to late August after the proceedings ran longer than the initially anticipated two weeks.\par \par \uc2 Eastman is asking that the proceedings be postponed yet again until the resolution of Smith\u8217\'20\'19s newly filed criminal case \u8212\'20\'14 in which Trump is, at least so far, the only defendant. If the disciplinary judge, Yvette Roland, denies that request, Eastman is asking her for a three-month delay to see whether he has been charged by then.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.49pm BST\par \par \uc2 In recent months, several supreme court justices {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/law/2023/jul/12/us-supreme-court-justices-ethics-rules-controversy-explain"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 have been the subject of media reports}}}\uc2  outlining ties between them and parties with interests in their cases.\par \par \uc2 And while most of the justices scrutinized have belonged to the court\u8217\'20\'19s six-member conservative majority, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://apnews.com/article/supreme-court-sotomayor-book-sales-ethics-colleges-b2cb93493f927f995829762cb8338c02"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the Associated Press last month reported}}}\uc2  that liberal justice \uc2 Sonia Sotomayor\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s staff have prodded institutions where she appears to buy her book.\par \par \uc2 In an opinion article {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.washingtonpost.com/opinions/2023/08/07/sotomayor-book-festival-mississippi-ethics/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 published today in the Washington Post}}}\uc2 , Margaret McMullan, an organizer of the Mississippi Book Festival, published her account of inviting Sotomayor to speak in 2019 \u8211\'20\'13 noting that the justice turned down a modest stipend and didn\u8217\'20\'19t seem that interested in selling her book:\par \par \uc2 Subsequent emails and phone conversations were similar. No, Le said, the justice did not need us to provide lunch or dinner. No, she could not accept the $250 stipend.\par \par \uc2 Did Le urge me to buy more books? No. She did ask whether we wanted any of the copies of \u8220\'20\'1CMy Beloved World\u8221\'20\'1D to be in Spanish. In fact, we did, and I hadn\u8217\'20\'19t thought to order them.\par \par \uc2 When Sotomayor came to Jackson, we had her speaking in the sanctuary at Galloway Memorial United Methodist Church, the church where Eudora Welty once worshiped. Backstage, Sotomayor smiled when she saw my clipboard of questions. She helped me with my tote bag full of books. She then clapped her hands together and said something like, \u8220\'20\'1COkay. Here\u8217\'20\'19s what we\u8217\'20\'19re going to do.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 In addition to our planned onstage interview, she said, she wanted the freedom to go off-script. \u8220\'20\'1CThey\u8217\'20\'19re children,\u8221\'20\'1D I recall her saying. \u8220\'20\'1CI want to be sure I get to their questions.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CPerfect,\u8221\'20\'1D I said.\par \par \uc2 She concludes:\par \par \uc2 There very well might be a culture of poor ethical conduct in the Supreme Court, but there is no moral equivalency between justices accepting rides on private jets to vacation with friends who had cases before the court and Sotomayor talking about her books and her life to a crowd of mesmerized young readers.\par \par \uc2 The standard royalty rate for authors is {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://publishdrive.com/what-is-the-typical-royalty-rate-for-an-author.html#:~:text=Generally%2C%20the%20standard%20royalty%20rates,70%25%20with%20self%2Dpublishing.&text=That%27s%20right."}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 less than 10 percent of the sales price}}}\uc2 . I don\u8217\'20\'19t know anything about Sotomayor\u8217\'20\'19s deal with her publishers, but 10 percent would make her cut of the 1,500 books our foundation purchased approximately $2,250 \u8212\'20\'14 for which she had to fly to Mississippi and give two presentations. During the hottest month of the year.\par \par \uc2 Was that a bribe? You be the judge.\par \par \uc2 It\u8217\'20\'19s not the first time someone who knows the justices has spoken out to defend their ethics. Harlan Crow, the billionaire and Republican donor who was reported to have taken conservative justice \uc2 Clarence Thomas\uc2  on luxury trips, has given {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theatlantic.com/ideas/archive/2023/05/harlan-crow-clarence-thomas-relationship/674092/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 multiple}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.dallasnews.com/news/2023/04/17/harlan-crow-theres-nothing-wrong-with-my-friendship-with-clarence-thomas/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 interviews}}}\uc2  in which he denied there being anything improper about their relationship.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.22pm BST\par \par \uc2 There have been reports of long lines in Ohio as early voting has surged ahead of a closely watched special election on Tuesday that could {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/aug/06/ohio-issue-1-vote-democracy-future-republicans"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 make it harder}}}\uc2  to amend the state constitution:\par \par \uc2 enltrOne of Ohio\u8217\'20\'19s many voting restrictions backed by Republicans means that counties can only have one early voting location regardless of population size.\par \par \uc2 So heavily Dem Franklin County\u8217\'20\'19s 1.3 million people get one location just like heavily GOP Vinton County\u8217\'20\'19s 13,000 people {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/A15aXrTS5i"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/A15aXrTS5i}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Stephen Wolf (@PoliticsWolf) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/PoliticsWolf/status/1688541877161611265?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 August 7, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 Ohioans are voting on Issue 1, a proposal that would require signatures in all 88 counties as well as a 60% supermajority to amend the state constitution.\par \par \uc2 Currently, voters need to collect 5% of the gubernatorial vote in all 44 counties to send a constitutional amendment to the ballot, which must win a simple statewide majority to pass. Republicans are seeking to change the rules ahead of a referendum to protect \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights this fall.\par \par \uc2 Republicans placed the special election on the ballot in August, hoping it would be a low-turnout affair. But turnout has been extremely strong \u8211\'20\'13 nearly 600,000 people have cast ballots so far. For more than a decade, Ohio Republicans {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://civilrights.org/edfund/resource/statement-of-mike-brickner-on-voting-rights-and-election-administration-in-ohio/#"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 have only allowed}}}\uc2  counties to have one in-person early voting site. That restriction can create a bottleneck in the more populous counties in the state, which tend to be Democratic-leaning.\par \par \uc2 A {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/jan/18/activists-sue-ohio-republican-voting-access-restrictions"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 new law}}}\uc2  enacted by Republicans this year also imposes additional hurdles to voting early. The measure eliminated early voting on the Monday before election day, typically one of the busiest days, instead extending the hours on other available days. It also gave voters less time to request a mail-in ballot and only allows counties to offer a single ballot drop box, which must be available in front of the boards of elections.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.04pm BST\par \par \uc2 Robert Reich\uc2 : Will Trump be jailed before trial?\par \par \uc2 Our columnist \uc2 Robert Reich\uc2  considers \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s characteristic disregard for the instructions of a judge, in the aftermath of his arraignment on charges related to his attempted election subversion, and whether federal authorities will take the logical next step\u8230\'20\'26\par \par \uc2 At \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s arraignment for trying to overturn the result of the 2020 election, magistrate judge Moxila A Upadhyaya warned him he could be taken into custody if he violated the conditions of his release, including attempting to influence jurors or intimidate future witnesses.\par \par \uc2 The judge said: \u8220\'20\'1CYou have heard your conditions of release. It is important you comply. You may be held pending trial in this case if you violate the conditions of release.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 She asked: \u8220\'20\'1CDo you understand these warnings and consequence, sir? Are you prepared to comply?\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Trump responded: \u8220\'20\'1CYes.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 But not 24 hours later, Trump posted on social media a message that could be understood as an attempt to influence potential jurors or retaliate against any witness prepared to testify against him. He wrote: \u8220\'20\'1CIF YOU GO AFTER ME, I\u8217\'20\'19M COMING AFTER YOU!\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 On Friday evening, prosecutors from the office of special counsel Jack Smith asked the court for a protective order to stop Trump from making public any of the information they were about to deliver to his lawyers under the discovery phase of the upcoming criminal trial, such as the names of witnesses who will testify against him.\par \par \uc2 On Saturday, the presiding judge in the case, \uc2 Tanya Chutkan\uc2 , ordered that Trump\u8217\'20\'19s lawyers respond to the prosecutor\u8217\'20\'19s request by 5pm Monday.\par \par \uc2 All through the weekend, Trump continued to threaten potential witnesses.\par \par \uc2 On Sunday he called Jack Smith \u8220\'20\'1Cderanged\u8221\'20\'1D, and accused the special counsel of waiting to bring the case until \u8220\'20\'1Cright in the middle\u8221\'20\'1D of his election campaign.\par \par \uc2 In another post he asserted that he would never get a \u8220\'20\'1Cfair trial\u8221\'20\'1D with Chutkan and jurors from Washington DC.\par \par \uc2 These statements directly violate the conditions of Trump\u8217\'20\'19s release pending trial.\par \par \uc2 They also could inflame Trump supporters, thereby endangering those who are trying to administer justice, such as Smith and Chutkan, as well as potential witnesses.\par \par \uc2 It\u8217\'20\'19s going to get a lot worse unless Chutkan \u8211\'20\'13 on her own initiative or at the urging of prosecutors \u8211\'20\'13 orders Trump\u8217\'20\'19s lawyers to show cause why his release pending trial should not be revoked, in light of his repeated violation of the conditions of his release.\par \par \uc2 Read the whole piece\u8230\'20\'26\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/commentisfree/2023/aug/07/will-donald-trump-be-jailed-before-trial"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Will Donald Trump be jailed before his trial? | Robert Reich}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.41pm BST\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  has completed one of the less onerous presidential duties: welcoming to the White House a champion team from major league sports.\par \par \uc2 It was the \uc2 Houston Astros\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19 turn today, having won the World Series last year. The pool reporter, Sabrina Siddiqui (of the Wall Street Journal but formerly {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/sabrina-siddiqui"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 of this parish}}}\uc2  ), informs us that a collection of Texas notables also attended, among them Lena Hidalgo, the judge of Harris county, and David Martin, mayor pro-tem of Houston.\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  is presented with a jersey while hosting the \uc2 Houston Astros\uc2  to celebrate their 2022 World Series victory. Photograph: Mandel Ngan/AFP/Getty Images\par \par \uc2 No word yet if Biden mentioned the impending Rugby World Cup, and how he thinks {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/sport/2023/mar/17/joe-biden-backs-ireland-six-nations-england"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 his beloved Ireland}}}\uc2  might do. Of course, he in all likelihood did not. But rest assured, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/sport/2021/jul/23/joe-biden-rugby-fan-mlr-ireland-all-blacks-syracuse-law-school"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 this reporter}}}\uc2  \u8211\'20\'13 if perhaps no one else in the entire Washington or even global press corps \u8211\'20\'13 will continue to try to find out.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.22pm BST\par \par \uc2 Indictments of \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  regarding his attempt to overturn the 2020 election and his retention of classified information are \u8220\'20\'1Cexquisite \u8230\'20\'26 beautiful and intricate\u8221\'20\'1D, the former House speaker \uc2 Nancy Pelosi{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://nymag.com/intelligencer/2023/08/how-nancy-pelosi-long-game-led-to-trumps-indictment.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 said}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Nancy Pelosi\uc2 . Photograph: Derek French/\uc2 Shutterstock\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe indictments against the president are exquisite,\u8221\'20\'1D Pelosi, 83 and a regular antagonist of the 77-year-old former president, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://nymag.com/intelligencer/2023/08/how-nancy-pelosi-long-game-led-to-trumps-indictment.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 told New York magazine}}}\uc2  in an interview published today.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThey\u8217\'20\'19re beautiful and intricate, and they probably have a better chance of conviction than anything that I would come up with.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Pelosi\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://nymag.com/intelligencer/2023/08/how-nancy-pelosi-long-game-led-to-trumps-indictment.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 words to New York magazine}}}\uc2  seemed likely to prompt a response from Trump, with whom she frequently clashed when she was speaker and he was in the Oval Office. In one high-profile incident, in February 2020, Pelosi famously tore up a Trump speech, after his State of the Union address.\par \par \uc2 Pelosi also {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://nymag.com/intelligencer/2023/08/how-nancy-pelosi-long-game-led-to-trumps-indictment.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 told the magazine}}}\uc2  that if Trump were to win the Republican nomination and the 2024 election against \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 , \u8220\'20\'1Cit would be a criminal enterprise in the White House\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CDon\u8217\'20\'19t even think of that,\u8221\'20\'1D she said. \u8220\'20\'1CDon\u8217\'20\'19t think of the world being on fire. It cannot happen, or we will not be the United States of America.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Trump has \u8211\'20\'13 unsurprisingly \u8211\'20\'13 been in a somewhat combative mood.\par \par \uc2 Last week, Pelosi {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://viewer.gutools.co.uk/us-news/2023/aug/04/donald-trump-scared-puppy-nancy-pelosi"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 told MSNBC}}}\uc2  Trump looked like a \u8220\'20\'1Cscared puppy\u8221\'20\'1D when he arrived in court in Washington to face four charges related to his attempt to overturn the 2020 election.\par \par \uc2 Trump, who has previously called Pelosi \u8220\'20\'1Ccrazy\u8221\'20\'1D and an \u8220\'20\'1Canimal\u8221\'20\'1D, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.newsweek.com/donald-trump-snaps-back-nancy-pelosi-over-mean-comments-1817796"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 denied}}}\uc2  being scared.\par \par \uc2 He also called the former speaker \u8220\'20\'1Creally quite vicious \u8230\'20\'26 a Wicked Witch \u8230\'20\'26 a sick and demented psycho who will someday live in HELL!\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.03pm BST\par \par \uc2 The day so far\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s attempt to countersue E Jean Carroll, the advice columnist who won a $5m civil judgment earlier this year after a jury found he sexually abused her, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/aug/07/trump-social-post-jan-6-biden-desantis-2024-latest-news?page=with:block-64d118318f08d95cff6be874#block-64d118318f08d95cff6be874"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 was rejected by a judge}}}\uc2 . But the former president\u8217\'20\'19s lawyers are no doubt keeping busy ahead of a 5pm eastern time deadline {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/aug/07/trump-social-post-jan-6-biden-desantis-2024-latest-news?page=with:block-64d0e1ec8f08e5e4127d07c4#block-64d0e1ec8f08e5e4127d07c4"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 to respond to a request}}}\uc2  for a protective order in the January 6 case from special counsel Jack Smith, over a statement Trump made Friday: \u8220\'20\'1CIF YOU GO AFTER ME, I\u8217\'20\'19M COMING AFTER YOU!\u8221\'20\'1D Trump, however, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/aug/07/trump-social-post-jan-6-biden-desantis-2024-latest-news?page=with:block-64d1059e8f08e5e4127d0990#block-64d1059e8f08e5e4127d0990"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 argued}}}\uc2  he was just exercising his right to free speech.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s what else has happened today so far:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Ron DeSantis{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/aug/07/trump-social-post-jan-6-biden-desantis-2024-latest-news?page=with:block-64d0f4778f08e5e4127d08c9#block-64d0f4778f08e5e4127d08c9"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 again rejected}}}\uc2  Trump\u8217\'20\'19s false claims about the 2020 election in an interview, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/aug/07/trump-social-post-jan-6-biden-desantis-2024-latest-news?page=with:block-64d0f8c28f08d95cff6be6ed#block-64d0f8c28f08d95cff6be6ed"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 drawing insults}}}\uc2  from a spokeswoman for the former president.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Aileen Cannon, the federal judge overseeing Trump\u8217\'20\'19s trial over the Mar-a-Lago documents, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/aug/07/trump-social-post-jan-6-biden-desantis-2024-latest-news?page=with:block-64d1005c8f08e5e4127d0969#block-64d1005c8f08e5e4127d0969"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 appeared to disclose}}}\uc2  an ongoing grand jury investigation in a court filing.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Ohio{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/aug/07/trump-social-post-jan-6-biden-desantis-2024-latest-news?page=with:block-64d114808f08e5e4127d0a71#block-64d114808f08e5e4127d0a71"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 will tomorrow}}}\uc2  vote on whether to raise the bar to amend the state constitution, part of a GOP-backed attempt to undermine a forthcoming ballot initiative to protect \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.41pm BST\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s legal troubles have made plenty of news, but are they causing his supporters to change their minds? \uc2 The Guardian\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/chrismcgreal"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Chris McGreal}}}\uc2  has a reality check from Iowa, the first state to vote in the GOP primary process:\par \par \uc2 From his corner of rural Iowa, Neil Shaffer did more than his fair share to put {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/donaldtrump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Donald Trump}}}\uc2  in the White House and to try to keep him there.\par \par \uc2 Shaffer oversaw the biggest swing of any county in the US from \uc2 Barack Obama\uc2  to Trump in 2016, and increased the then president\u8217\'20\'19s share of the vote four years later. But the chair of the Howard county Republican party is not enthusiastic at the prospect of yet another Trump presidential campaign, and he blames the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/democrats"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Democrats}}}\uc2  for driving it.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CHonestly, the Democrats are shooting themselves in the foot with these prosecutions,\u8221\'20\'1D he said. \u8220\'20\'1CWhy is Trump doing so well? Because people feel like they are piling on him. If this is the Democrats\u8217\'20\'19 effort to make him look bad, it hasn\u8217\'20\'19t. It\u8217\'20\'19s probably going to make him the [Republican] nominee and, honestly, he may win the general election again. And then whose fault would it be?\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 After {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/aug/03/trump-arraignment-indictment-jan-6-2020-election"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pleading not guilty}}}\uc2  on Thursday to federal charges over his attempts to steal the 2020 presidential election, Trump denounced the indictment as \u8220\'20\'1Ca persecution of a political opponent\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIf you can\u8217\'20\'19t beat him, you persecute him or you prosecute him,\u8221\'20\'1D he said.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/aug/06/donald-trump-iowa-republicans-2024-election"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \u8216\'20\'18These people are diehard\u8217\'20\'19: Iowa Trump supporters shrug off indictments}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 5.42pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.22pm BST\par \par \uc2 Judge tosses Trump countersuit against E Jean Carroll\par \par \uc2 A judge has thrown out \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s countersuit against advice columnist E Jean Carroll, who earlier this year won a $5m defamation judgment against the former president after a jury found he sexually abused her:\par \par \uc2 enltrJUST IN: Trump's counterclaim against E. Jean Carroll has been *dismissed* by Judge Kaplan. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/BAUsk2lfdE"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/BAUsk2lfdE}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/GdyVaZ0UoR"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/GdyVaZ0UoR}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Kyle Cheney (@kyledcheney) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/kyledcheney/status/1688582423309623296?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 August 7, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 Trump {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/jun/28/trump-sues-e-jean-carroll-for-defamation-over-comments"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 responded by filing a counterclaim}}}\uc2  against Carroll, arguing she defamed him by saying he raped her. That claim was rejected by judge Lewis Kaplan, who said the former president\u8217\'20\'19s contention did not add up.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.11pm BST\par \par \uc2 Ohio to vote on GOP-backed attempt to undercut \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  measure by changing rules\par \par \uc2 After the supreme court overturned Roe v Wade last year, \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights advocates in Ohio succeeded in collecting enough signatures to put a measure on the November ballot that will enshrine access to the procedure in the state constitution.\par \par \uc2 Republican lawmakers in the state, who support \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  restrictions passed into law prior to the supreme court\u8217\'20\'19s decision, then moved to change the rules for amending Ohio\u8217\'20\'19s constitution, with a ballot measure that will be voted on in a special election to be held tomorrow.\par \par \uc2 As the Guardian\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/sam-levine"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Sam Levine}}}\uc2  reports, it\u8217\'20\'19s a big moment for democracy in the state that will have reverberations beyond just \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights:\par \par \uc2 An under-the-radar election in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/ohio"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Ohio}}}\uc2  on Tuesday has quietly emerged as one of the most high-stakes stress tests for American democracy in recent years.\par \par \uc2 The question Ohio voters will decide on 8 August is simple: how easy should it be to amend the state constitution? Like {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://ballotpedia.org/Initiated_constitutional_amendment"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 17}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://ballotpedia.org/Initiated_constitutional_amendment"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 other states}}}\uc2 , Ohio allows citizens to place constitutional amendments on the statewide ballot if they get a certain number of signatures and more than 50% of the statewide vote. The process has been in place for more than a century in Ohio, and in November, voters will use it to decide whether to protect \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights.\par \par \uc2 In May, Republicans who control the state legislature {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/may/23/ohio-abortion-rights-republican-ballot-super-majority"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 abruptly sent a proposal}}}\uc2  to the ballot called Issue 1 that would make it much harder to change the constitution. If approved, a constitutional amendment would need 60% of the vote to pass instead of a simple majority. It would also make it significantly harder for citizens to even propose a constitutional amendment, requiring signatures from 5% of the voters in all of Ohio\u8217\'20\'19s 88 counties (the state currently requires organizers to get signatures in 44).\par \par \uc2 In May, Republicans who control the state legislature {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/may/23/ohio-abortion-rights-republican-ballot-super-majority"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 abruptly sent a proposal}}}\uc2  to the ballot called Issue 1 that would make it much harder to change the constitution. If approved, a constitutional amendment would need 60% of the vote to pass instead of a simple majority. It would also make it significantly harder for citizens to even propose a constitutional amendment, requiring signatures from 5% of the voters in all of Ohio\u8217\'20\'19s 88 counties (the state currently requires organizers to get signatures in 44).\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/aug/06/ohio-issue-1-vote-democracy-future-republicans"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 The election that could determine the future of democracy in Ohio}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 5.13pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.41pm BST\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, the Washington DC federal court has made public the document \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  signed following his arraignment last Thursday in which he agreed to the conditions of his release:\par \par \uc2 enltrNEW DOC: Here is \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 's signature on the conditions of his release\par \par \uc2 (including the pledge not to tamper with or retaliate against witnesses/victims/informants or officers of the court) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/gcC6ncySCB"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/gcC6ncySCB}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/ZGrSnEY7Ta"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/ZGrSnEY7Ta}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Kyle Cheney (@kyledcheney) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/kyledcheney/status/1688572394410057730?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 August 7, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 enltrAnd here's the part about not communicating with other witnesses in the case unless counsel is present. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/gcC6ncySCB"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/gcC6ncySCB}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/U1xHWQaSl8"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/U1xHWQaSl8}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Kyle Cheney (@kyledcheney) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/kyledcheney/status/1688572908321288192?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 August 7, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 You can find the entire document {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.documentcloud.org/documents/23901070-conditions"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 here}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.24pm BST\par \par \uc2 As part of his defense against charges related to attempting to overturn the 2020 election, \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s attorney John Lauro has mulled asking for the trial to be moved \u8211\'20\'13 perhaps to West Virginia.\par \par \uc2 The Mountain State is also one of the most Trump-friendly: the then-president carried it by nearly 69% three years ago, his second-biggest win nationwide, after Wyoming. \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 , meanwhile, won Washington DC, where the charges were filed and where the trial will currently take place, by a whopping 92%.\par \par \uc2 But {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.politico.com/news/2023/08/07/trump-judge-chutkan-transfer-venue-00110094"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Politico reports}}}\uc2  that federal judges, including \uc2 Tanya Chutkan\uc2 , who is presiding over the January 6 case, are unlikely to grant a change of venue for the proceedings. Here\u8217\'20\'19s why:\par \par \uc2 At the heart of Chutkan\u8217\'20\'19s analysis \u8212\'20\'14 like most of her colleagues\u8217\'20\'19 as well \u8212\'20\'14 is a rejection of Trump\u8217\'20\'19s premise. Just because a juror is affiliated with one political party \u8212\'20\'14 and even opposes the political views of someone facing charges \u8212\'20\'14 does not mean they are incapable of setting aside those views to judge a case based on evidence and facts.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CPeople in this country have strong views \u8230\'20\'26 we expect people to have opinions. And one of the things \u8212\'20\'14 it\u8217\'20\'19s fine to have an opinion,\u8221\'20\'1D Chutkan {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.documentcloud.org/documents/23900940-chutlantranscript9282022"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 said in September 2022}}}\uc2 , swatting aside defendant Russell Alford\u8217\'20\'19s bid to relocate his Jan. 6 case. \u8220\'20\'1CBut what I\u8217\'20\'19m going to be instructing the jury is \u8216\'20\'18can you put aside your opinion and adjudge the defendant based on the evidence?\u8217\'20\'19 And it\u8217\'20\'19s amazing how, I have found, how seriously jurors take that charge. And what we\u8217\'20\'19re looking for is not people without opinions; what we\u8217\'20\'19re looking for is people who are able to put aside their opinion and focus their decision solely on the evidence presented in this courtroom.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The protection for prosecutors and defendants concerned about juror bias is typically a thorough vetting process \u8212\'20\'14 known as \u8220\'20\'1Cvoir dire\u8221\'20\'1D \u8212\'20\'14 in which the judge and lawyers get to grill potential jurors under oath about their background, views and experiences, screening out those who might be incapable of deciding the case fairly. This process has helped seat jurors in other politically explosive recent cases, including the seditious conspiracy trials of leaders of the Oath Keepers and Proud Boys, who were charged with helping orchestrate and exacerbate the Jan. 6 attack.\par \par \uc2 Often, predictions about rampant bias in the jury pool are put to rest after interviews reveal jurors with diverse political viewpoints, little knowledge of the cases or issues present and no preconceived notions about the defendants or their potential guilt or innocence. And courts uniformly prefer to wait for this process to play out before considering a venue transfer.\par \par \uc2 Courts\u8217\'20\'19 overwhelming reluctance to relocate trials is rooted in the Sixth Amendment\u8217\'20\'19s guarantee for \u8220\'20\'1Ca speedy and public trial, by an impartial jury of the State and district wherein the crime shall have been committed.\u8221\'20\'1D Appellate courts have repeatedly found that venue transfers are justified only in the most extreme circumstances \u8212\'20\'14 and even then only after an extensive voir dire has proven it impossible to seat a fair jury. Those circumstances include a tiny jury pool \u8212\'20\'14 much smaller than Washington\u8217\'20\'19s 600,000-plus population of potential jurors \u8212\'20\'14 and pretrial publicity that uniquely taints that particular district.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.03pm BST\par \par \uc2 Trump cites speech rights in opposing protective order\par \par \uc2 Ahead of an afternoon deadline for his lawyers to respond to a request from special counsel Jack Smith for {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/aug/05/donald-trump-threatening-social-media-post-flagged-by-prosecutors-in-court-filing"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a protective order}}}\uc2  in the January 6 case, \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  said such a ruling would infringe on his free speech rights.\par \par \uc2 From his {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://truthsocial.com/@realDonaldTrump/posts/110848767329986697"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Truth social account}}}\uc2  :\par \par \uc2 No, I shouldn\u8217\'20\'19t have a protective order placed on me because it would impinge upon my right to FREE SPEECH. Deranged Jack Smith and the Department of Injustice should, however, because they are illegally \u8220\'20\'1Cleaking\u8221\'20\'1D all over the place!\par \par \uc2 The former president\u8217\'20\'19s attorneys have until 5pm eastern time to respond to the request from Smith, who asked for the protective order after Trump on Friday wrote, \u8220\'20\'1CIF YOU GO AFTER ME, I\u8217\'20\'19M COMING AFTER YOU!\u8221\'20\'1D on Truth.\par \par \uc2 Smith wants Trump\u8217\'20\'19s attorneys barred from publicly sharing \u8220\'20\'1Csensitive\u8221\'20\'1D materials including grand jury transcripts obtained during the January 6 case\u8217\'20\'19s pre-trial motions.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.37pm BST\par \par \uc2 Judge in Trump documents case appears to disclose ongoing grand jury investigation\par \par \uc2 Aileen Cannon, the federal judge presiding over \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s trial on charges related to keeping classified documents at his Mar-a-Lago resort, appeared to disclose an ongoing grand jury investigation in a court filing today, the Guardian\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/hugo-lowell"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Hugo Lowell}}}\uc2  reports:\par \par \uc2 enltrNEW on Trump classified docs: US judge Aileen Cannon appears to disclose that Special Counsel is using an \u8220\'20\'1Cout-of-district grand jury to continue to investigate and/or to seek post-indictment hearings\u8221\'20\'1D \u8212\'20\'14 and strikes two filings by prosecutors {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/dSElatjEZY"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/dSElatjEZY}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Hugo Lowell (@hugolowell) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/hugolowell/status/1688553014901059584?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 August 7, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 Cannon was appointed to the bench by Trump, and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/jun/14/trump-judge-miami-aileen-cannon-arraignment-indictment"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 faced scrutiny last year}}}\uc2  for a decision in an earlier stage of the Mar-a-Lago case that some legal experts viewed as favorable to the former president, and which was later overturned by an appeals court.\par \par \uc2 Cannon\u8217\'20\'19s is presiding over Trump\u8217\'20\'19s trial in Florida on charges brought by special counsel Jack Smith, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/jun/08/trump-mar-a-lago-case-explainer"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 who alleges}}}\uc2  the former president illegally stored classified documents at his Mar-a-Lago resort, and conspired to hide them from government officials sent to retrieve them.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.18pm BST\par \par \uc2 In response to the charges filed against him over January 6, \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s lawyers have argued the former president did not know that he indeed lost the 2020 election. But as the Guardian\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/hugo-lowell"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Hugo Lowell}}}\uc2  reports, that defense may not be enough to stop prosecutors from winning a conviction:\par \par \uc2 Included in the indictment last week against {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/donaldtrump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Donald Trump}}}\uc2  for his efforts to subvert the 2020 presidential election was a count of obstructing an official proceeding \u8211\'20\'13 the attempt to stop the vote certification in Congress on the day his supporters mounted the January 6 Capitol attack.\par \par \uc2 The count is notable, because \u8211\'20\'13 based on a review of previous judicial rulings in other cases where the charge has been brought \u8211\'20\'13 it may be one where prosecutors will not need to prove Trump knew he lost the election, as the former president\u8217\'20\'19s legal team has repeatedly claimed.\par \par \uc2 The obstruction of an official proceeding statute has four parts, but in Trump\u8217\'20\'19s case what is at issue is the final element: whether the defendant acted corruptly.\par \par \uc2 The definition of \u8220\'20\'1Ccorruptly\u8221\'20\'1D is currently under review by the US court of appeals for the DC circuit in the case titled {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://storage.courtlistener.com/recap/gov.uscourts.cadc.39016/gov.uscourts.cadc.39016.1218509547.0.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 United States v Robertson}}}\uc2 . Yet previous rulings by district court judges and a different three-judge panel in the DC circuit in an earlier case suggest how it will apply to Trump.\par \par \uc2 In short: even with the most conservative interpretation, prosecutors at trial may not need to show that Trump knew his lies about 2020 election fraud to be false, or that the ex-president knew he had lost to \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThere\u8217\'20\'19s no need to prove that Trump knew he lost the election to establish corrupt intent,\u8221\'20\'1D said Norman Eisen, special counsel to the House judiciary committee in the first Trump impeachment.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe benefit under the statute is the presidency itself \u8211\'20\'13 and Trump clearly knew that without his unlawful actions, Congress was going to certify Biden as the winner of the election. That\u8217\'20\'19s all the corrupt intent you need,\u8221\'20\'1D Eisen said.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/aug/07/trump-belief-2020-election-may-not-matter-obstruction-charge"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Prosecutors may not need to show that Trump knew he had lost the election}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.01pm BST\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s team has clearly been paying attention to \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s NBC News interview, with a spokeswoman attacking the Florida governor for his comments dismissing the ex-president\u8217\'20\'19s false claims about his 2020 election loss:\par \par \uc2 enltrIf you think \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  got 81 million votes, you\u8217\'20\'19re an idiot\par \par \uc2 If you\u8217\'20\'19re just saying that, you\u8217\'20\'19re either a coward or corrupt\par \par \uc2 Either way it\u8217\'20\'19s disqualifying {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/vGWe5LAhG5"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/vGWe5LAhG5}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Liz Harrington (@realLizUSA) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/realLizUSA/status/1688545048797872129?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 August 7, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.43pm BST\par \par \uc2 Speaking of Republican presidential candidates, NBC News scored a sit-down interview with Florida governor \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2 , and got him to again say that his chief rival \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  lost the 2020 election.\par \par \uc2 DeSantis, whose {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/aug/04/ron-desantis-donor-super-pac-florida"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 campaign for the White House is in troubled waters}}}\uc2 , had been vague on the issue until last week, when he started saying publicly that he did not believe the former president\u8217\'20\'19s false claims about his election loss.\par \par \uc2 Here he is saying it again, on NBC:\par \par \uc2 enltrGov. \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2  (R-FL): "Of course he lost."\par \par \uc2 NBC News' Dasha Burns: \u8220\'20\'1CTrump lost the 2020 election?\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 DeSantis: "\uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 's the president. But the issue is, I think what people in the media and elsewhere, they want to act like somehow this was just like the perfect election. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/hzL7oNKCrz"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/hzL7oNKCrz}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 The Recount (@therecount) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/therecount/status/1688518634744766464?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 August 7, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.25pm BST\par \par \uc2 Pence emerges as potential witness in Trump January 6 trial\par \par \uc2 In his final days as vice-president, \uc2 Mike Pence\uc2  faced pressure from \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  to go along with his plan to disrupt \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s election victory. Pence refused his then-boss\u8217\'20\'19s request, and the two running mates are now foes, but could Pence potentially be a witness in the trial on the federal charges brought against Trump over the election subversion plot?\par \par \uc2 In {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/aug/06/mike-pence-trump-interview"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 an interview with CBS News}}}\uc2  broadcast over the weekend, Pence, who is running for the Republican presidential nomination, said he has \u8220\'20\'1Cno plans to testify\u8221\'20\'1D, but added \u8220\'20\'1Cpeople can be confident we\u8217\'20\'19ll obey the law. We\u8217\'20\'19ll respond to the call of the law, if it comes and we\u8217\'20\'19ll just tell the truth.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Far from being worried about what Trump\u8217\'20\'19s former deputy might have to say about him, the former president\u8217\'20\'19s attorney John Lauro said his legal team would welcome Pence\u8217\'20\'19s testimony.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe vice-president will be our best witness,\u8221\'20\'1D {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/aug/06/trump-attorney-pence-election-conspiracy-trial"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Lauro said}}}\uc2  in a Sunday appearance on \uc2 CBS\uc2 , though he didn\u8217\'20\'19t exactly say why he felt that way. \u8220\'20\'1CThere was a constitutional disagreement between the vice-president [Pence] and president Trump, but the bottom line is never, never in our country\u8217\'20\'19s history, as those kinds of disagreements have been prosecuted criminally. It\u8217\'20\'19s unheard of.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.05pm BST\par \par \uc2 Trump faces deadline to respond to prosecutors' request for protection after warning 'I\u8217\'20\'19m coming after you'\par \par \uc2 Good morning, US politics blog readers. Mere days have passed since special counsel Jack Smith indicted \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  for his failed effort to reverse his 2020 election loss, but the two sides are already battling over what the former president can say and do. On Friday, Trump wrote \u8220\'20\'1CIF YOU GO AFTER ME, I\u8217\'20\'19M COMING AFTER YOU!\u8221\'20\'1D, prompting Smith\u8217\'20\'19s prosecutors to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/aug/05/donald-trump-threatening-social-media-post-flagged-by-prosecutors-in-court-filing"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 request a protective order}}}\uc2  that would restrict what the former president\u8217\'20\'19s legal team can share publicly, saying it is necessary to guard people involved in the case against retaliation.\par \par \uc2 Trump\u8217\'20\'19s lawyers have until 5pm eastern time today to respond. It\u8217\'20\'19s an early salvo in what is expected to be the lengthy process Smith\u8217\'20\'19s case is expected to take, and which will undoubtedly hang over the 2024 election, where Trump is currently the frontrunner. Either way, the former president has not been shy about sharing his thoughts regarding the unprecedented criminal charges leveled against him, and do not be surprised if today is no different.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s what else is happening:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Voters in Ohio are {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/aug/06/ohio-issue-1-vote-democracy-future-republicans"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 gearing up to decide}}}\uc2  on Tuesday whether to approve a Republican-backed proposal that will raise the bar for changing the state\u8217\'20\'19s constitution. What this is really about is a ballot initiative scheduled to be put to a vote in November that would enshrine \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  protections in the state\u8217\'20\'19s laws, but which would face a much more difficult road to passage if tomorrow\u8217\'20\'19s vote succeeds.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2 , the Florida governor whose presidential campaign appears to be floundering, just {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nbcnews.com/politics/2024-election/ron-desantis-of-course-trump-lost-2020-election-rcna98200"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 sat down for an interview with NBC News}}}\uc2 , where, among other things, he reiterated that he believed Trump lost the 2020 election.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  is hosting World Series winners the \uc2 Houston Astros\uc2  at the White House today, before heading to the Grand Canyon.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.08pm BST\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020230807ej870020l\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
