\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  expects indictment \u8216\'20\'18any day now\u8217\'20\'19 in 2020 election subversion case \u8211\'20\'13 as it happened\b0\par\par\uc2 L\u233\'00\'E9onie Chao-Fong (now) and Chris Stein (earlier) \par \uc2 6,918 \uc2 words\par \uc2 31 July 2023\par 23:10 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 The blog is now closed, but you can read more about \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s swirling legal peril here.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.00am BST\par \par \uc2 Closing summary\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s a recap of today\u8217\'20\'19s developments:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 A judge in Georgia {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/jul/31/trump-investigations-aide-hunter-biden-republicans-desantis-politics-live-updates?page=with:block-64c7be6a8f086b325af62c18#block-64c7be6a8f086b325af62c18"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 turned down an attempt}}}\uc2  by \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  to stop Fulton county district attorney \uc2 Fani Willis\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s investigation into his efforts to overturn the 2020 election result in the state. Over the weekend, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/jul/31/trump-investigations-aide-hunter-biden-republicans-desantis-politics-live-updates?page=with:block-64c7c53c8f086b325af62c6c#block-64c7c53c8f086b325af62c6c"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Willis said}}}\uc2  she could announce charges in the case anytime between now and the first day of September.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Trump said he expected he could be indicted {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/jul/31/trump-investigations-aide-hunter-biden-republicans-desantis-politics-live-updates?page=with:block-64c7f1c88f086b325af62f07#block-64c7f1c88f086b325af62f07"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1Cany day now\u8221\'20\'1D}}}\uc2  as part of special counsel Jack Smith\u8217\'20\'19s investigation into the January 6 insurrection. Smith has been looking into Trump\u8217\'20\'19s efforts to remain in office following his 2020 election defeat to \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 . Federal prosecutors have assembled evidence to charge Trump with three crimes, the \uc2 Guardian{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/jul/20/donald-trump-january-6-grand-jury-deadline"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  has reported}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Carlos De Oliveira, the property manager of Trump\u8217\'20\'19s Mar-a-Lago estate, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/jul/31/trump-investigations-aide-hunter-biden-republicans-desantis-politics-live-updates?page=with:block-64c7ef7d8f08db2904abd7c0#block-64c7ef7d8f08db2904abd7c0"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 made his first court appearance}}}\uc2  on Monday on charges in the classified documents case against the former president. De Oliveira was added last week to the indictment with Trump and the ex-president\u8217\'20\'19s valet, Walt Nauta, and faces charges including conspiracy to obstruct justice and lying to investigators.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 A month out from the first debate of the Republican presidential primary, \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s domination of the field increases with each poll. On Monday, the first 2024 survey from the \uc2 New York Times\uc2  and Siena College {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/jul/31/trump-investigations-aide-hunter-biden-republicans-desantis-politics-live-updates?page=with:block-64c817ee8f085120bb1daaac#block-64c817ee8f085120bb1daaac"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 put Trump at 54% support. }}}\uc2  His closest challenger, \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2 , was at 17%. No one else \u8211\'20\'13 including \uc2 Mike Pence\uc2 , Tim Scott and Nikki Haley \u8211\'20\'13 was higher than 3%.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 House Republicans announced an investigation into {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/jul/26/why-hunter-biden-plea-deal-fell-apart"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the deal reached between Hunter Biden and the justice department}}}\uc2  that would have seen the president\u8217\'20\'19s son plead guilty to tax charges and enter a diversion agreement to resolve a gun charge.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 A former business partner of \uc2 Hunter Biden\uc2  told the House oversight committee on Monday that Hunter sought to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/jul/31/trump-investigations-aide-hunter-biden-republicans-desantis-politics-live-updates?page=with:block-64c828f48f085120bb1dab18#block-64c828f48f085120bb1dab18"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 create an \u8220\'20\'1Cillusion of access\u8221\'20\'1D}}}\uc2  to his fatherJoe Biden to impress clients and business associates, but he insisted the then vice-president was never directly involved in any deals, according to Democratic Representative Dan Goldman.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 But the Republican chair of the House oversight committee, James Comer, said Archer\u8217\'20\'19s testimony {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/jul/31/trump-investigations-aide-hunter-biden-republicans-desantis-politics-live-updates?page=with:block-64c82ea38f086b325af6308e#block-64c82ea38f086b325af6308e"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1Cconfirms Joe Biden lied }}}\uc2  to the American people when he said he had no knowledge about his son\u8217\'20\'19s business dealings and was not involved\u8221\'20\'1D. Republican representative Andy Biggs, who attended the interview, told reporters: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/jul/31/trump-investigations-aide-hunter-biden-republicans-desantis-politics-live-updates?page=with:block-64c828f48f085120bb1dab18#block-64c828f48f085120bb1dab18"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI think we should do an impeachment inquiry.\u8221\'20\'1D}}}\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  decided to keep the US Space Command headquarters in Colorado, rather than move it Alabama. The move deals a blow to the economy of a deeply Republican state whose senator Tommy Tuberville has lately been blocking hundreds of military promotions in protest of defense department policies intended to help service members obtain abortions. There is {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/jul/31/trump-investigations-aide-hunter-biden-republicans-desantis-politics-live-updates?page=with:block-64c8114d8f08db2904abd8b8#block-64c8114d8f08db2904abd8b8"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 no indication yet}}}\uc2  that Biden\u8217\'20\'19s decision has anything to do with Tuberville\u8217\'20\'19s blockade.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 A Massachusetts district attorney called for a federal investigation into Florida governor \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s efforts to transport migrants by plane across state lines. In a letter to attorney general \uc2 Merrick Garland\uc2 , Cape and Islands district attorney Robert Galibois {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/jul/31/trump-investigations-aide-hunter-biden-republicans-desantis-politics-live-updates?page=with:block-64c8369c8f086b325af630a8#block-64c8369c8f086b325af630a8"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 asked the justice department}}}\uc2  to investigate a September 2022 incident in which 49 immigrants were transported from Texas to Martha\u8217\'20\'19s Vineyard.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 A super PAC backing Democratic presidential candidate \uc2 Robert F Kennedy Jr\uc2  raised $6.47m in July, according to a press release from American Values 2024. The press release noted that American Values 2024 has {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/jul/31/trump-investigations-aide-hunter-biden-republicans-desantis-politics-live-updates?page=with:block-64c81ca38f08db2904abd915#block-64c81ca38f08db2904abd915"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 received donations from both Democrats and Republicans,}}}\uc2  including the Trump mega donor Timothy Mellon, Democratic Party donor Abby Rockefeller, and Gavin de Becker, a security consultant close to \uc2 Jeff Bezos\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.37pm BST\par \par \uc2 A Massachusetts district attorney called for a federal investigation into Florida governor \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s efforts to transport migrants by plane across state lines.\par \par \uc2 In a letter to attorney general \uc2 Merrick Garland\uc2 , Cape and Islands district attorney Robert Galibois asked the justice department to investigate a September 2022 incident in which 49 immigrants were transported from Texas to Martha\u8217\'20\'19s Vineyard.\par \par \uc2 Galibois asked the DoJ to investigate allegations that the migrants were misled into getting on the planes.\par \par \uc2 Subsequent reporting and public statements also indicate that Florida Governor \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2  and his administration planned, initiated, funded with taxpayer monies, and executed this enterprise.\par \par \uc2 He added:\par \par \uc2 My office posits that, due to the interstate transportation of these migrants, this alleged scheme remains available for federal prosecution.\par \par \uc2 California governor \uc2 Gavin Newsom\uc2  has also called on the justice department to probe Florida over the flights.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.04pm BST\par \par \uc2 The chair of the House oversight committee, James Comer, has released a statement after \uc2 Hunter Biden\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s former business partner {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/jul/31/trump-investigations-aide-hunter-biden-republicans-desantis-politics-live-updates?page=with:block-64c828f48f085120bb1dab18#block-64c828f48f085120bb1dab18"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Devon Archer}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/jul/31/trump-investigations-aide-hunter-biden-republicans-desantis-politics-live-updates?page=with:block-64c828f48f085120bb1dab18#block-64c828f48f085120bb1dab18"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  testified before the committee }}}\uc2  on Monday.\par \par \uc2 During his closed-door interview, Archer said \uc2 Hunter Biden\uc2  sought to create an \u8220\'20\'1Cillusion of access\u8221\'20\'1D to his father while doing business in Ukraine but that \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  played no role in any deals, according to Democratic representative Dan Goldman, who attended the interview.\par \par \uc2 But Comer said Archer\u8217\'20\'19s testimony \u8220\'20\'1Cconfirms \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  lied to the American people when he said he had no knowledge about his son\u8217\'20\'19s business dealings and was not involved\u8221\'20\'1D. The then vice-president \u8220\'20\'1Cwas \u8216\'20\'18the brand\u8217\'20\'19 that his son sold around the world to enrich the Biden family\u8221\'20\'1D, he said.\par \par \uc2 The statement goes on to say:\par \par \uc2 Why did \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  lie to the American people about his family\u8217\'20\'19s business dealings and his involvement? It begs the question what else he is hiding from the American people. The House Committee on Oversight and Accountability will continue to follow the Bidens\u8217\'20\'19 money trail and interview witnesses to determine whether foreign actors targeted the Bidens, President Biden is compromised and corrupt, and our national security is threatened.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 11.22pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.44pm BST\par \par \uc2 Hunter Biden\uc2  sold 'illusion of access' to his father, says former business partner\par \par \uc2 Devon Archer, a former business partner of \uc2 Hunter Biden\uc2 , said Hunter sought to create an \u8220\'20\'1Cillusion of access\u8221\'20\'1D to his father \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  to impress clients and business associates, but he insisted the then vice-president was never directly involved in any deals.\par \par \uc2 The Republican-led House oversight committee conducted a more than-five hour interview with Archer as part of its expanding congressional inquiry into the Biden family businesses.\par \par \uc2 The interview focused on the 2010s, when \uc2 Hunter Biden\uc2  sat on the board of the Ukraine energy company \uc2 Burisma\uc2  and his father was vice-president under President \uc2 Barack Obama\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Both Republican and Democratic lawmakers inside the closed-door interview said Archer testified that over the span of 10 years, \uc2 Hunter Biden\uc2  put his father on the phone around 20 times while in the company of associates but \u8220\'20\'1Cnever once spoke about any business dealings\u8221\'20\'1D, AP reported.\par \par \uc2 Democratic Representative Dan Goldman told reporters that Archer testified that Hunter sold the \u8220\'20\'1Cillusion of access\u8221\'20\'1D to his father and \u8220\'20\'1Ctried to get credit for things that [Hunter] had nothing to do with\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 But Republican representative Andy Biggs, who has co-sponsored legislation to impeach Biden, said Archer\u8217\'20\'19s testimony implicated the president and quoted the witness as saying \uc2 Burisma\uc2  could not have survived without the \u8220\'20\'1CBiden brand\u8221\'20\'1D. He told reporters:\par \par \uc2 I think we should do an impeachment inquiry.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.13pm BST\par \par \uc2 The Susan B Anthony List, the nation\u8217\'20\'19s leading anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  group, called Florida governor and GOP presidential candidate \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19 failure to support federal \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  restrictions \u8220\'20\'1Cunacceptable\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 DeSantis signed into law a controversial six-week \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban in Florida in April. In a recent interview with Megyn Kelly, DeSantis was asked if he would support \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  bans at the federal level.\par \par \uc2 He replied:\par \par \uc2 I\u8217\'20\'19ve been a pro-life governor. I\u8217\'20\'19ll be a pro-life president and I\u8217\'20\'19ll come down on the side of life.\par \par \uc2 DeSantis added that he would \u8220\'20\'1Cbe a leader with the bully pulpit to help local communities and states advance the cause of life but he avoided answering if he would enact a federal \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban.\par \par \uc2 In response, Marjorie Dannenfelser, president of the Susan B Anthony Pro-Life America group, criticized DeSantis, saying that \u8220\'20\'1Ca pro-life president has a duty to protect the lives of all Americans\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Dannenfelser said in a statement:\par \par \uc2 Gov. DeSantis\u8217\'20\'19s dismissal of this task is unacceptable to prolife voters. A consensus is already formed. Intensity for it is palpable and measurable.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.53pm BST\par \par \uc2 A super PAC backing Democratic presidential candidate \uc2 Robert F Kennedy Jr\uc2  raised $6.47m in July, according to a press release from American Values 2024.\par \par \uc2 The press release noted that American Values 2024 has received donations from both Democrats and Republicans, including the Trump mega donor Timothy Mellon, Democratic Party donor Abby Rockefeller, and Gavin de Becker, a security consultant close to \uc2 Jeff Bezos\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Mellon said in the press release:\par \par \uc2 The fact that Kennedy gets so much bipartisan support tells me two things: that he\u8217\'20\'19s the one candidate who can unite the country and root out corruption and that he\u8217\'20\'19s the one Democrat who can win in the general election.\par \par \uc2 The super PAC said it raised $6.47m in July, bringing its total fundraising for Kennedy to about $16.82m.\par \par \uc2 About $5m of that haul came during his testimony in front of the House judiciary select subcommittee on the weaponization of the federal government, according to the press release.\par \par \uc2 Kennedy\u8217\'20\'19s appearance before the House subcommittee on 20 July came days after he told reporters at a press dinner that Covid-19 had been \u8220\'20\'1Cethnically targeted\u8221\'20\'1D at Caucasians and Black people, while Ashkenazi Jews and Chinese people had greater immunity.\par \par \uc2 The false claim was enthusiastically embraced by neo-Nazi groups, while being condemned by scientists and Jewish organizations.\par \par \uc2 Robert F Kennedy, Jr., testifies before a House Judiciary Select Subcommittee on the Weaponization of the Federal Government hearing on Capitol Hill in Washington. Photograph: Patrick Semansky/AP\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.33pm BST\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  is demanding Republican support for impeaching \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  over corruption allegations against \uc2 Hunter Biden\uc2 , the president\u8217\'20\'19s surviving son.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CAny Republican that doesn\u8217\'20\'19t act on Democrat fraud should be immediately primaried and get out,\u8221\'20\'1D Trump told a rally in Erie, Pennsylvania, on Saturday.\par \par \uc2 Republicans {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://pressgallery.house.gov/member-data/party-breakdown"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 hold the US House}}}\uc2 , where impeachment would start, by just five seats. GOP members in Democratic areas seem likely to suffer at the polls next year.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIf they\u8217\'20\'19re not willing to do it,\u8221\'20\'1D Trump said, \u8220\'20\'1Cwe\u8217\'20\'19ve got a lot of good, tough {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/republicans"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Republicans}}}\uc2  around.\par \par \uc2 People are going to run against \u8217\'20\'19em, and people are going to win. And they\u8217\'20\'19re going to get my endorsement every single time. They\u8217\'20\'19re going to win \u8217\'20\'19cause we win almost every race when we endorse.\par \par \uc2 Factcheckers dispute that. Surveying the 2022 midterms, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/2022/12/06/us/politics/trump-candidate-endorsement-georgia.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the New York Times said}}}\uc2  : \u8220\'20\'1CMr Trump endorsed more than 250 candidates, and his 82% success rate is, on the surface, impressive. But the vast majority of those endorsements were of incumbents and heavy favorites to win.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The paper added:\par \par \uc2 In the 36 most competitive House races \u8230\'20\'26 Mr Trump endorsed candidates in five contests. All five lost.\par \par \uc2 Trump\u8217\'20\'19s influence on key Senate races won by Democrats has been widely discussed.\par \par \uc2 In Pennsylvania, Trump also called for {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.washingtonpost.com/politics/2023/07/29/trump-ukraine-congress-hunter-biden/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 conditioning aid to Ukraine}}}\uc2  in its war with Russia on White House cooperation with investigations of \uc2 Hunter Biden\uc2 . Trump\u8217\'20\'19s own first impeachment was for withholding aid to Ukraine in an attempt to uncover dirt on the Bidens. Pundits noted the irony.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CSo much for denying the quid pro quo, as he did in 2019,\u8221\'20\'1D {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/peterbakernyt/status/1685834963193651200"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 said}}}\uc2  Peter Baker, the Times\u8217\'20\'19 chief White House correspondent.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.24pm BST\par \par \uc2 A month out from the first debate of the Republican presidential primary, \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s domination of the field increases with each poll.\par \par \uc2 On Monday, the first 2024 survey from {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/2023/07/31/us/politics/2024-poll-nyt-siena-trump-republicans.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the New York Times and Siena College}}}\uc2  put Trump at 54% support. His closest challenger, \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2 , was at 17%. No one else \u8211\'20\'13 including \uc2 Mike Pence\uc2 , Tim Scott and Nikki Haley \u8211\'20\'13 was higher than 3%.\par \par \uc2 DeSantis\u8217\'20\'19s hard-right campaign is widely seen to be out of fuel and on a glide path to destruction. Trump dominates early voting states and in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://projects.fivethirtyeight.com/polls/president-primary-r/2024/national/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 national averages}}}\uc2  leads the Florida governor by more than 30 points.\par \par \uc2 Fani Willis\uc2 , the district attorney of Fulton county, Georgia, is \u8220\'20\'1C {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cnn.com/2023/07/30/politics/fulton-county-fani-willis-trump-investigation/index.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 ready to go}}}\uc2  \u8221\'20\'1D with indictments in her investigation of Trump\u8217\'20\'19s election subversion. In Washington, the special counsel Jack Smith is expected to add charges regarding election subversion to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cnn.com/interactive/2023/06/politics/annotated-trump-indictment-dg/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 40 counts already filed}}}\uc2  over the former president\u8217\'20\'19s retention of classified records.\par \par \uc2 Trump already faces {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/apr/02/donald-trump-escalate-attacks-against-manhattan-da"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 34 criminal charges}}}\uc2  in New York over hush-money payments to the porn star Stormy Daniels. Referring to Trump being ordered to pay $5m after being found liable for sexual abuse and defamation against the writer E Jean Carroll, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.washingtonpost.com/politics/2023/07/19/trump-carroll-judge-rape/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a judge recently said}}}\uc2  Carroll proved Trump raped her. Lawsuits over Trump\u8217\'20\'19s business affairs continue.\par \par \uc2 Heading for trials in primary season, Trump denies wrongdoing and claims political persecution. But his chaos-agent campaign, which {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://abcnews.go.com/US/trump-hell-run-convicted-sentenced-responds-security-footage/story?id=101773573"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 he has said}}}\uc2  he will not abandon even if convicted and sentenced, does not just threaten the national peace. It threatens his own party.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.00pm BST\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  just decided to keep the US Space Command headquarters in Colorado, rather than move it Alabama, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://apnews.com/article/space-command-biden-colorado-alabama-382b12b57733848fd1d083227aefa0bf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the Associated Press reports}}}\uc2 . And, surprising as it might seem, Biden\u8217\'20\'19s decision may soon be caught up in the debate over \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access.\par \par \uc2 First, a recap: \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  created Space Force in 2019, and near the end of his presidency ordered it moved from its temporary home in Colorado Springs, Colorado to Huntsville, Alabama. Biden has now reversed that decision, dealing a blow to the economy of a deeply Republican state whose senator Tommy Tuberville has lately been blocking hundreds of military promotions {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/jul/24/ommy-tuberville-abortion-militarty-promotions-democrats-letter"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 in protest of defense department policies}}}\uc2  intended to help service members obtain abortions.\par \par \uc2 While there is no indication yet that Biden\u8217\'20\'19s decision has anything to do with Tuberville\u8217\'20\'19s blockade, the president has personally decried the senator\u8217\'20\'19s campaign, calling it \u8220\'20\'1Cridiculous\u8221\'20\'1D and saying it threatens the military\u8217\'20\'19s readiness.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s more on the decision, from the AP:\par \par \uc2 The officials said Biden was convinced by the head of Space Command, Gen. James Dickinson, who argued that moving his headquarters now would jeopardize military readiness. Dickinson\u8217\'20\'19s view, however, was in contrast to Air Force leadership, who studied the issue at length and determined that relocating to Huntsville, Alabama, was the right move.\par \par \uc2 The officials spoke on condition of anonymity to discuss the decision ahead of the announcement.\par \par \uc2 The president, they said, believes that keeping the command in Colorado Springs would avoid a disruption in readiness that the move would cause, particularly as the U.S. races to compete with China in space. And they said Biden firmly believes that maintaining stability will help the military be better able to respond in space over the next decade.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.42pm BST\par \par \uc2 House Republicans launch inquiry into Hunter Biden plea deal\par \par \uc2 House Republicans have announced an investigation into {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/jul/26/why-hunter-biden-plea-deal-fell-apart"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the deal reached between }}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/jul/26/why-hunter-biden-plea-deal-fell-apart"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Hunter Biden}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/jul/26/why-hunter-biden-plea-deal-fell-apart"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  and the justice department}}}\uc2  that would have seen the president\u8217\'20\'19s son plead guilty to tax charges and enter a diversion agreement to resolve a gun charge.\par \par \uc2 Biden was expected to formally accept the agreement with prosecutors during a federal court hearing in Delaware last week, but judge Maryellen Noreika objected to portions of the deal and ordered the two sides to renegotiate it and present it to her at a future date.\par \par \uc2 Republicans have for years accused the president\u8217\'20\'19s son of corruption, and since it was announced have called the plea agreement a \u8220\'20\'1Csweetheart deal\u8221\'20\'1D. In a letter to attorney general \uc2 Merrick Garland\uc2 , the Republican chairs of the House judiciary, ways and means and oversight committees demand a range of documents and explanations from the justice department.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe Department\u8217\'20\'19s unusual plea and pretrial diversion agreements with Mr. Biden raise serious concerns \u8212\'20\'14 especially when combined with recent whistleblower allegations \u8212\'20\'14 that the Department has provided preferential treatment toward Mr. Biden in the course of its investigation and proposed resolution of his alleged criminal conduct,\u8221\'20\'1D the committee chairs write. Earlier this month, the House oversight committee heard from two \uc2 Internal Revenue Service\uc2  agents {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.axios.com/2023/07/19/hunter-biden-joe-ziegler-whistleblower-irs-doj"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 who claimed politicization}}}\uc2  of the Hunter Biden investigation, despite statements from the \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  -appointed US attorney who led the case that he had the ultimate authority to bring charges.\par \par \uc2 The letter marks the latest instance of the House GOP using the chamber\u8217\'20\'19s powers to investigate the Biden administration. Since the start of the year, it has launched investigations into topics including the \u8220\'20\'1Cweaponization\u8221\'20\'1D of the federal government under the Biden administration, and the state and federal prosecutions targeting Trump.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.16pm BST\par \par \uc2 A small group of progressive lawmakers led by Vermont Senator \uc2 Bernie Sanders\uc2  on Monday {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.sanders.senate.gov/press-releases/news-sanders-markey-merkley-and-warren-send-letter-to-attorney-general-urging-doj-to-bring-lawsuits-against-the-fossil-fuel-industry/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 urged}}}\uc2  the United States to bring lawsuits against the fossil fuel industry for its alleged efforts to sow doubt about the climate crisis.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe actions of \uc2 ExxonMobil\uc2 , Shell, and potentially other fossil fuel companies represent a clear violation of federal racketeering laws, truth in advertising laws, consumer protection laws, and potentially other laws, and the Department must act swiftly to hold them accountable for their unlawful actions,\u8221\'20\'1D reads the letter, which was also signed by Democratic senators \uc2 Ed Markey\uc2  and Elizabeth Warren of Massachusetts and \uc2 Jeff Merkley\uc2  of Oregon.\par \par \uc2 The letter, addressed to attorney general \uc2 Merrick Garland\uc2 , references the well-documented climate misinformation campaign waged over decades by oil and gas companies, and the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/jun/07/climate-crisis-big-oil-lawsuits-constitution"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 dozens of lawsuits}}}\uc2  filed by states, municipalities, and the District of Columbia about that campaign.\par \par \uc2 The letter was sent as swaths of the United States bake under sweltering temperatures. This summer\u8217\'20\'19s record-breaking heatwaves in America and southern Europe, which have put tens of millions of people under heat advisories, would have been \u8220\'20\'1Cvirtually impossible\u8221\'20\'1D without climate change, according to a recent {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.npr.org/2023/07/25/1189901992/a-new-study-looks-at-the-role-climate-change-is-playing-in-current-heat-waves"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 study}}}\uc2  by scientists at World Weather Attribution.\par \par \uc2 The senators also implore the Department of Justice, the \uc2 Federal Trade Commission\uc2  and other law enforcement agencies to file their own lawsuits against parties who participated in climate deception, and request a meeting with Garland.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe polluters must pay,\u8221\'20\'1D the senators wrote.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.00pm BST\par \par \uc2 Andy Biggs, a rightwing Republican member of the oversight committee, said Devon Archer revealed that \uc2 Hunter Biden\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s family name helped Ukrainian natural gas firm \uc2 Burisma\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s business.\par \par \uc2 That\u8217\'20\'19s according to Punchbowl News:\par \par \uc2 enltrAndy Biggs says Devon Archer told Oversight, "'\uc2 Burisma\uc2  would have gone out of business sooner if the Biden brand had not been invoked. People would be intimidated to really mess with \uc2 Burisma\uc2  because of the Biden family brand.'"\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Max Cohen (@maxpcohen) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/maxpcohen/status/1686083459163230208?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 July 31, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 Fox News reports a unnamed source saying the same:\par \par \uc2 enltr1) From a source familiar with the transcribed interview with former \uc2 Hunter Biden\uc2  business partner Devon Archer.\par \par \uc2 Archer testified there was value of adding \uc2 Hunter Biden\uc2  to \uc2 Burisma\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s board was \u8220\'20\'1Cthe brand.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Chad Pergram (@ChadPergram) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/ChadPergram/status/1686082659850555392?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 July 31, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 enltr5) Archer testified that \uc2 Hunter Biden\uc2  put then-Vice President \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  on the speakerphone during business meetings, over 20 times. Archer testified that \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  was put on the phone to sell \u8220\'20\'1Cthe brand.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Chad Pergram (@ChadPergram) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/ChadPergram/status/1686082666444050432?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 July 31, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 It is unclear if Biden actually participated in the meetings, or just took the calls to speak with his son, as Democratic congressman Dan Goldman, who attended the interview with Archer, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/jul/31/trump-investigations-aide-hunter-biden-republicans-desantis-politics-live-updates?page=with:block-64c7fe848f086b325af62f87#block-64c7fe848f086b325af62f87"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 characterized the conversations}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 However, Punchbowl reports Biggs said Archer had no knowledge of an unverified bribery allegation against Joe and \uc2 Hunter Biden\uc2  that was reported to the \uc2 FBI\uc2 :\par \par \uc2 enltrAndy Biggs says that Devon Archer didn\u8217\'20\'19t know anything at all about the Joe and \uc2 Hunter Biden\uc2  bribery allegation contained in the FD-1023 form\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Max Cohen (@maxpcohen) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/maxpcohen/status/1686081796377575424?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 July 31, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.45pm BST\par \par \uc2 Following the Republican-led House oversight committee\u8217\'20\'19s interview with Devon Archer, a former business partner of \uc2 Hunter Biden\uc2 , a Democratic lawmaker on the committee downplayed the president involvement in his son\u8217\'20\'19s business.\par \par \uc2 Archer testified that Hunter would call up \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  during business meetings in the period when they served on the board of Ukrainian natural gas company \uc2 Burisma\uc2 , but only for \u8220\'20\'1Ccasual conversation,\u8221\'20\'1D Democratic congressman and committee member Dan Goldman said, Punchbowl News reports.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe witness was very, very consistent, that none of those conversations ever had to do with any business dealings or transactions,\u8221\'20\'1D Goldman said, adding that Hunter and \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  spoke frequently.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1C[Biden] says hello to someone that he sees his son with. What is he supposed to say? \u8216\'20\'18Hi, son. No, I\u8217\'20\'19m not gonna say hello to the other people at the table or the other people on the phone.\u8217\'20\'19\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s more of Goldman\u8217\'20\'19s comments to the press:\par \par \uc2 enltr\u8220\'20\'1CThe only evidence we have right now of any official action by President Biden in connection to \uc2 Hunter Biden\uc2 's business interests is bad for \uc2 Hunter Biden\uc2 's business interests.\u8220\'20\'1C\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Rep. Dan Goldman (D-NY) gives an update on House Oversight's closed-door meeting with Devon Archer {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/5dt7Brhfjv"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/5dt7Brhfjv}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 The Recount (@therecount) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/therecount/status/1686080844081795072?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 July 31, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.22pm BST\par \par \uc2 Several Republican presidential candidates have vowed that, in the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/jul/31/trump-investigations-aide-hunter-biden-republicans-desantis-politics-live-updates?page=with:block-64c7cf9e8f086b325af62ccf#block-64c7cf9e8f086b325af62ccf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 as-of-now unlikely scenario}}}\uc2  that they are elected to the White House next year, they would pardon \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 . But as the Guardian\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/ramon-antonio-vargas"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Ramon Antonio Vargas}}}\uc2  reports, former Arkansas governor Asa Hutchinson is trying to distinguish himself by promising to do no such thing:\par \par \uc2 Former Arkansas governor {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/apr/02/asa-hutchinson-announces-candidacy-for-republican-presidential-nomination"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Asa Hutchinson}}}\uc2  has said it is \u8220\'20\'1Cinappropriate\u8221\'20\'1D for some of his fellow Republican presidential hopefuls to publicly discuss potentially pardoning \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , who is their party\u8217\'20\'19s frontrunner for its 2024 nomination despite his mounting criminal charges.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CAnybody who promises pardons during a presidential campaign is not serving our system of justice well,\u8221\'20\'1D Hutchinson said Sunday on \uc2 CBS\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s Face the Nation. \u8220\'20\'1CAnd it\u8217\'20\'19s inappropriate.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The remarks from Hutchinson cut a stark contrast with {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/jul/30/republican-criticizes-trump-2024-campaign"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 comments from other Republicans}}}\uc2  in the running for the presidency, who said they would pardon Trump if they eventually defeated the Democratic incumbent, \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 .\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/jul/30/mitch-mcconnell-nikki-haley-health-concerns"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Nikki Haley}}}\uc2 , once South Carolina\u8217\'20\'19s governor and the Trump White House\u8217\'20\'19s United Nations ambassador, has said she would be inclined to pardon the former president if she won the election to help the country \u8220\'20\'1Cmove forward\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.02pm BST\par \par \uc2 Former New York city police commissioner Bernard Kerik, a leading Trump ally, will meet with special counsel Jack Smith in the coming days as part of the federal investigation into efforts to overturn the 2020 election.\par \par \uc2 Kerik\u8217\'20\'19s attorney {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cnn.com/2023/07/30/politics/bernie-kerik-special-counsel-trump-giuliani/index.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  told}}}\uc2  CNN on Sunday that the special counsel\u8217\'20\'19s office will meet with Kerik and his lawyers \u8220\'20\'1Cin about a week\u8221\'20\'1D to discuss efforts taken by former Trump lawyer \uc2 Rudy Giuliani\uc2  to investigate potential election fraud in the wake of the 2020 election. He said:\par \par \uc2 We have a meeting scheduled in about a week with the special counsel\u8217\'20\'19s office to talk about a lot of the efforts that the Giuliani team was taking at the time to investigate fraud, and that\u8217\'20\'19s really going to get into, you know, the core of whether they can charge somebody with having corrupt intent.\par \par \uc2 The meeting will come after Kerik {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/jul/24/rudy-giuliani-bernie-kerik-trump-documents-jack-smith-capitol-attack"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  turned over thousands of pages of documents}}}\uc2  to the special counsel\u8217\'20\'19s office connected to the debunked voter fraud claims made by Trump and Giuliani.\par \par \uc2 In early 2020, Trump {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nbcnews.com/news/us-news/trump-pardons-bernard-kerik-why-former-n-y-police-commissioner-n1138236"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pardoned}}}\uc2  Kerik for crimes including tax fraud and lying to investigators, for which Kerik had been {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://abcnews.go.com/Blotter/kerik-sentenced-years-prison/story?id=9875911"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 sentenced}}}\uc2  to four years in jail. Later that year, Kerik worked with Giuliani on attempts to overturn \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s victory, a push which culminated in the failed but deadly January 6 attack on Congress.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 7.04pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.44pm BST\par \par \uc2 Trump expects to be indicted \u8216\'20\'18any day now\u8217\'20\'19 on January 6 charges\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  said he expects he could be indicted \u8220\'20\'1Cany day now\u8221\'20\'1D as part of special counsel Jack Smith \u8217\'20\'19s investigation into the January 6 insurrection.\par \par \uc2 Smith has been looking into Trump\u8217\'20\'19s efforts to remain in office following his 2020 election defeat to \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 . Federal prosecutors have assembled evidence to charge Trump with three crimes, the \uc2 Guardian{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/jul/20/donald-trump-january-6-grand-jury-deadline"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  has reported: }}}\uc2  obstruction of an official proceeding, conspiracy to defraud the United States, and a statute that makes it unlawful to conspire to violate civil rights.\par \par \uc2 Trump, posting to Truth Social on Monday, wrote:\par \par \uc2 I assume that an Indictment from Deranged Jack Smith and his highly partisan gang of Thugs, pertaining to my \u8220\'20\'1CPEACEFULLY & PATRIOTICALLY Speech, will be coming out any day now, as yet another attempt to cover up all of the bad news about bribes, payoffs, and extortion, coming from the Biden \u8216\'20\'18camp.\u8217\'20\'19 This seems to be the way they do it. ELECTION INTERFERENCE! PROSECUTORIAL MISCONDUCT!\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 7.07pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.34pm BST\par \par \uc2 Carlos De Oliveira, the Mar-a-Lago property manager and third co-defendant in the special counsel\u8217\'20\'19s classified documents case, declined to answer questions as he left the Miami courthouse.\par \par \uc2 De Oliveira was escorted by federal agents and his attorney, John Irving, who said it was time for the justice department \u8220\'20\'1Cto put their money where their mouth is\u8221\'20\'1D after charging his client.\par \par \uc2 De Oliveira was added as a third defendant in \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s complicated classified documents indictment on Thursday. He faces charges such as trying to obstruct justice, concealing records and documents, and making false statements to the \uc2 FBI\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 De Oliveira, 56, was a valet, maintenance worker and more recently a property manager at Trump\u8217\'20\'19s resort, Mar-a-Lago, according to the superseding {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.documentcloud.org/documents/23889238-trump-superseeding-indictment"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 indictment}}}\uc2 . The indictment said De Oliveira helped Trump\u8217\'20\'19s personal valet, Walt Nauta, move 30 boxes of documents, from Trump\u8217\'20\'19s residence to a storage room, and asked the person responsible for surveillance at the resort to delete the footage on behalf of Trump. He was also accused of draining the resort pool to flood the rooms that contained surveillance footage.\par \par \uc2 When the \uc2 FBI\uc2  discovered the documents at Mar-a-Lago in August 2022, Trump {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/jul/28/carlos-de-oliveira-mar-a-lago-trump-documents-indictment"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  allegedly called De Oliveira}}}\uc2  and said he would get him an attorney.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.27pm BST\par \par \uc2 Trump co-defendant Carlos De Oliveira makes first court appearance\par \par \uc2 Carlos De Oliveira, the property manager of \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19 s Mar-a-Lago estate, made his first appearance in a Miami courtroom on Monday as part of the special counsel\u8217\'20\'19s investigation into the former president\u8217\'20\'19s alleged mishandling of classified documents.\par \par \uc2 During the roughly 10-minute hearing, De Oliveira, the third and newest co-defendant in Trump\u8217\'20\'19s classified documents case, heard the charges against him and received pre-trial orders. He was unable to enter a plea because he had failed to secure local counsel.\par \par \uc2 Chief Magistrate Judge Edwin Torres granted an extension request, and the arraignment is now scheduled to take place on 10 August at the federal courthouse in Fort Pierce, Florida. De Oliveira was released on a $100,000 bond pending trial.\par \par \uc2 De Oliveira was indicted on Thursday on four charges, including conspiracy to obstruct justice and making false statements to the \uc2 FBI\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Trump and his longtime valet, Walt Nauta, were charged in the classified documents case last month and face additional counts in the indictment that charged De Oliveira. Both Trump and Nauta have pleaded not guilty to the initial charges.\par \par \uc2 Mar-a-Lago worker Carlos De Oliveira (L) and his attorney John Irvine (R) arrive at the James Lawrence King Federal Justice Building to arraign for connection with special counsel Jack Smith\u8217\'20\'19s classified documents case in Miami, Florida. Photograph: Anadolu Agency/Getty Images\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.07pm BST\par \par \uc2 The day so far\par \par \uc2 A judge in Georgia {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/jul/31/trump-investigations-aide-hunter-biden-republicans-desantis-politics-live-updates?page=with:block-64c7be6a8f086b325af62c18#block-64c7be6a8f086b325af62c18"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 turned down an attempt}}}\uc2  by \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  to stop Fulton county district attorney \uc2 Fani Willis\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s investigation into his efforts to overturn the 2020 election result in the state. Over the weekend, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/jul/31/trump-investigations-aide-hunter-biden-republicans-desantis-politics-live-updates?page=with:block-64c7c53c8f086b325af62c6c#block-64c7c53c8f086b325af62c6c"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Willis said}}}\uc2  she could announce charges in the case anytime between now and the first day of September. Meanwhile, a former business partner of \uc2 Hunter Biden{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/jul/31/trump-investigations-aide-hunter-biden-republicans-desantis-politics-live-updates?page=with:block-64c7ca4f8f086b325af62cad#block-64c7ca4f8f086b325af62cad"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reported}}}\uc2  for an interview with the Republican-led House oversight committee, as the GOP {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/jul/31/trump-investigations-aide-hunter-biden-republicans-desantis-politics-live-updates?page=with:block-64c7aaa58f086b325af62b18#block-64c7aaa58f086b325af62b18"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 toys with the idea}}}\uc2  of starting impeachment proceedings against \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  when they return from their August recess.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s what else has happened today:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Trump is in a historically good position to win the Republican presidential primary, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/jul/31/trump-investigations-aide-hunter-biden-republicans-desantis-politics-live-updates?page=with:block-64c7e2c08f085120bb1da897#block-64c7e2c08f085120bb1da897"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 CNN concludes}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 At a weekend rally in Pennsylvania, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/jul/31/trump-investigations-aide-hunter-biden-republicans-desantis-politics-live-updates?page=with:block-64c7db9e8f08db2904abd65c#block-64c7db9e8f08db2904abd65c"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Trump called for}}}\uc2  stopping aid to Ukraine until the government helps prove alleged corruption by the Biden family.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s once-promising presidential campaign {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/jul/31/trump-investigations-aide-hunter-biden-republicans-desantis-politics-live-updates?page=with:block-64c7d5408f086b325af62d19#block-64c7d5408f086b325af62d19"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 is suffering}}}\uc2  from both Republican defections and his own missteps.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.39pm BST\par \par \uc2 A {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cnn.com/2023/07/30/politics/trump-second-term-president-election-2024/index.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 CNN analysis published on Sunday}}}\uc2  finds \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s poll numbers add up to a commanding lead in the Republican primary, and any candidate who manages to overcome it would essentially be making history.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s the gist of their findings:\par \par \uc2 Trump is not only in a historically strong position for a nonincumbent to win the Republican nomination, but he is in a better position to win the general election than at any point during the 2020 cycle and almost at any point during the 2016 cycle.\par \par \uc2 No one in Trump\u8217\'20\'19s current polling position in the modern era has lost an open presidential primary that didn\u8217\'20\'19t feature an incumbent. He\u8217\'20\'19s pulling in more than 50% of support in the national primary polls, i.e., more than all his competitors combined.\par \par \uc2 Three prior candidates in open primaries were pulling in more than half the vote in primary surveys in the second half of the calendar year before the election: Democrat \uc2 Al Gore\uc2  and Republican \uc2 George W. Bush\uc2  in 2000 and Democrat \uc2 Hillary Clinton\uc2  in 2016. Gore remains the only nonincumbent to win every single presidential nominating contest, while Bush and Clinton never lost their national polling advantage in their primaries.\par \par \uc2 Today, Trump\u8217\'20\'19s closest primary competitor, Florida Gov. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cnn.com/2023/07/27/politics/ron-desantis-byron-donalds-black-history-education/index.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Ron DeSantis}}}\uc2 , has fallen below 20% nationally. No other contender is at or above 10%. This makes the margin between Trump and the rest of the field north of 30 points on average.\par \par \uc2 A look back at past polls does show candidates coming back from deficits greater than 10 points to win the nomination, but none greater than 30 points at this point. In fact, the biggest comebacks when you average all the polls in the second half of the year before the election top out at about 20 points (Democrats George McGovern in 1972, \uc2 Jimmy Carter\uc2  in 1976 and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cnn.com/politics/presidency/barack-obama"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Barack Obama}}}\uc2  in 2008).\par \par \uc2 CNN also finds that polls taken thus far show Trump mounting a dangerous challenge to \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 , though with the election more than a year away, there are plenty of chances for that to change:\par \par \uc2 What should arguably be more amazing is that despite most Americans {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://abcnews.go.com/Politics/majority-americans-trump-illegal-poll/story?id=98430435"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 agreeing that}}}\uc2  Trump\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://poll.qu.edu/poll-release?releaseid=3874"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 two indictments}}}\uc2  thus far were warranted, he remains competitive in a potential rematch with {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cnn.com/politics/joe-biden"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 President Joe Biden}}}\uc2 . A poll out last week from {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://law.marquette.edu/poll/wp-content/uploads/2023/07/MLSPSC15ToplinesRV.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Marquette University Law School}}}\uc2  had Biden and Trump tied percentage-wise (with a statistically insignificant few more respondents choosing Trump).\par \par \uc2 The Marquette poll is one of a number of surveys showing Trump either tied or ahead of Biden. The {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://projects.fivethirtyeight.com/polls/president-general/national/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 ABC News/Washington Post poll}}}\uc2  has published three surveys of the matchup between the two, and Trump has come out ahead \u8211\'20\'13 albeit within the margin of error \u8211\'20\'13 every time. Other pollsters have shown Biden only narrowly ahead.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 5.40pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.19pm BST\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  during his Saturday rally in Erie, Pennsylvania. Photograph: Joed Viera/AFP/Getty Images\par \par \uc2 Over the weekend, \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  held a rally in Pennsylvania, a swing state crucial to winning the White House, and made a demand that will be familiar to those who remember his stint as president.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.washingtonpost.com/politics/2023/07/29/trump-ukraine-congress-hunter-biden/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 The Washington Post reports}}}\uc2  that Trump said: \u8220\'20\'1CCongress should refuse to authorize a single additional shipment of our depleted weapons stockpiles \u8230\'20\'26 to Ukraine until the \uc2 FBI\uc2 , DOJ and \uc2 IRS\uc2  hand over every scrap of evidence they have on the Biden Crime Family\u8217\'20\'19s corrupt business dealings.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 It wasn\u8217\'20\'19t that far removed from his actions in 2019 when, as president, he blocked aid to Ukraine then, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2020/jan/24/trump-impeachment-trial-democrats-focus"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 on a phone call with }}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2020/jan/24/trump-impeachment-trial-democrats-focus"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Volodymyr Zelenskiy}}}\uc2  , tried to get the Ukrainian president to cooperate with his administration in investigating \uc2 Hunter Biden\uc2 . That led to Democrats, who then controlled the House, impeaching Trump, though he was ultimately acquitted by the GOP-controlled Senate.\par \par \uc2 Much has changed in the intervening three-plus years. Republicans now control the House, and Democrats the Senate, while \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  is in the White House and Trump is just a candidate. But some things aren\u8217\'20\'19t so different. Republicans seem willing to use their House majority to impeach Biden, but his conviction appears likely to be turned down by the Senate \u8211\'20\'13 a reversal of the dynamics that played out three years ago. Russia\u8217\'20\'19s aggression in Ukraine has, of course, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/live/2023/jul/31/russia-ukraine-war-live-zelenskiy-moscow-kyiv-saudia-arabia-summit"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 become worse}}}\uc2 , but as his comments this weekend make clear, Trump seems ready to use the nation as a pawn for his political designs.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 5.59pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.40pm BST\par \par \uc2 One of the biggest surprises of the presidential campaign season thus far is the flame-out of \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s presidential campaign. The Florida governor has raked in cash, secured endorsements and bent the state legislature to his will, all in service to his presidential aspirations, but is getting defeated handily by \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  in the polls. From Miami, the Guardian\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/richardluscombe"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Richard Luscombe}}}\uc2  looks into why:\par \par \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2  is facing growing backlash in Florida as his presidential campaign {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/jul/25/ron-desantis-president-campaign-staff-cuts"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 flails across the country}}}\uc2 . Analysts and political opponents are seeing signs of a tail-off in his support, and evidence of Republicans recoiling at his extremist positions on slavery, education, \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  and immigration.\par \par \uc2 Hints at a shift in his standing came towards the end of the recently concluded legislative session in his home state, when several Republican lawmakers defied the governor by voting against new laws {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.politico.com/news/2023/04/12/florida-republicans-against-abortion-ban-00091744"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 restricting abortions}}}\uc2  or expanding his {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.newsweek.com/florida-ron-desantis-disney-republican-1796985"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 feud with Disney}}}\uc2 . They passed anyway.\par \par \uc2 But observers say the strength of the resistance appears to have gathered pace since DeSantis\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/may/25/what-happened-ron-desantis-us-presidential-campaign-launch-twitter-elon-musk"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 glitch-ridden presidential campaign launch}}}\uc2  in May, and subsequent missteps on the stump.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/jul/31/ron-desantis-presidential-campaign-florida-republicans"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 DeSantis fatigue grows among Florida Republicans as 2024 campaign falters}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.17pm BST\par \par \uc2 This morning, the \uc2 New York Times\uc2  and Siena College {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/2023/07/31/us/politics/2024-poll-nyt-siena-trump-republicans.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 released a poll}}}\uc2  that confirms \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s popularity among Republicans, despite the legal troubles facing him.\par \par \uc2 The former president is far and away the frontrunner for the party\u8217\'20\'19s presidential nomination, with 54% support the survey finds. His closest competitor is Florida governor \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2 , but even that\u8217\'20\'19s a generous description, because the poll has him at a measly 17%. No other candidate cracks double-digit support, or even comes close. \uc2 Mike Pence\uc2 , Tim Scott and Nikki Haley all poll at 3%.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.51pm BST\par \par \uc2 Hunter Biden\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s former business partner Devon Archer has arrived for his interview with the Republican-led House oversight committee.\par \par \uc2 As CBS News reports, he declined to answer questions from reporters:\par \par \uc2 enltrFormer \uc2 Hunter Biden\uc2  business partner Devon Archer arrives for transcribed interview GOP-led house oversight. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/CBS_Herridge?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @CBS_Herridge}}}\uc2  \u8220\'20\'1CWhat will you tell congressional investigators about \uc2 Hunter Biden\uc2 's business deals?"\par \par \uc2 Devon Archer: \u8220\'20\'1CNo comment.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Herridge: "Are White House denials about\u8230\'20\'26 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/YsXKtSvWW7"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/YsXKtSvWW7}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Catherine Herridge (@CBS_Herridge) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/CBS_Herridge/status/1686024083845025793?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 July 31, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.31pm BST\par \par \uc2 Over the weekend, Fulton county district attorney \uc2 Fani Willis\uc2  told Atlanta\u8217\'20\'19s WXIA that her office was \u8220\'20\'1Cready to go\u8221\'20\'1D when it comes to deciding charges in the long-running investigation into the attempt by \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  and his allies to overturn the 2020 election.\par \par \uc2 Willis reiterated that charging decisions will be announced by the first day of September. Here are her full comments:\par \par \uc2 enltr"The work is accomplished. We've been working for 2.5 years. We're ready to go."\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Fulton County DA \uc2 Fani Willis\uc2  reaffirmed she will announce charging decisions by September 1 in her investigation into \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 /his allies in Georgia {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/1iM4d0rrpi"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/1iM4d0rrpi}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 The Recount (@therecount) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/therecount/status/1686000636347695104?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 July 31, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.44pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.10pm BST\par \par \uc2 Judge denies Trump attempt to block potential prosecution in Georgia\par \par \uc2 A superior court judge in Georgia has rejected an attempt by \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  to derail district attorney \uc2 Fani Willis\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s investigation into his campaign to overturn the 2020 election result in the state.\par \par \uc2 The ruling by judge Robert McBurney is in response to a motion Trump filed in March {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.washingtonpost.com/nation/2023/03/20/trump-georgia-grand-jury/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 seeking to block}}}\uc2  a grand jury report ordered by Willis and stop it from being used in any prosecutions. Willis has said that indictments in the case could come anytime between now and the end of August.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe movants\u8217\'20\'19 asserted \u8216\'20\'18injuries\u8217\'20\'19 that would open the doors of the courthouse to their claims are either insufficient or else speculative and unrealized. They are insufficient because, while being the subject (or even target) of a highly publicized criminal investigation is likely an unwelcome and unpleasant experience, no court ever has held that that status alone provides a basis for the courts to interfere with or halt the investigation,\u8221\'20\'1D McBurney wrote.\par \par \uc2 He added that the request to block the report\u8217\'20\'19s use \u8220\'20\'1Cis not what either statutory or case law generally allows\u8221\'20\'1D, and also rejected Trump\u8217\'20\'19s request that Willis be removed from the case.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.10pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.43pm BST\par \par \uc2 Lawyer rejects GOP speculation that justice department wants former \uc2 Hunter Biden\uc2  business partner in jail before testimony\par \par \uc2 Last year, \uc2 Hunter Biden\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s former business partner Devon Archer {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.justice.gov/usao-sdny/pr/devon-archer-sentenced-year-and-day-prison-fraudulent-issuance-and-sale-more-60-million"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 was sentenced to a year in prison}}}\uc2  on fraud charges unrelated to his dealings with the president\u8217\'20\'19s son. Archer has yet to turn himself in, but on Saturday, the justice department wrote to the judge handling his case and asked that a date be scheduled for Archer to begin his sentence.\par \par \uc2 The following day, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://youtu.be/lHKYdpZ1Z24?t=12"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 on Fox News}}}\uc2 , James Comer, the Republican chair of the House oversight committee, said it was \u8220\'20\'1Codd\u8221\'20\'1D that prosecutors would request Archer report to prison just before he was scheduled to meet with the panel\u8217\'20\'19s investigators.\par \par \uc2 Comer and fellow GOP lawmakers have long insinuated that the justice department is covering up for the Biden family, but Matthew Schwartz, an attorney for Archer, rejected the chair\u8217\'20\'19s allegation.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe are aware of speculation that the Department of Justice\u8217\'20\'19s weekend request to have Mr. Archer report to prison is an attempt by the Biden administration to intimidate him in advance of his meeting with the House Oversight Committee on Monday,\u8221\'20\'1D Schwartz said in a statement {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cnn.com/2023/07/31/politics/devon-archer-house-testimony/index.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 obtained by CNN}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CTo be clear, Mr. Archer does not agree with that speculation. In any case, Mr. Archer will do what he has planned to do all along, which is to show up on Monday and to honestly answer the questions that are put to him by the Congressional investigators.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.44pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.15pm BST\par \par \uc2 Amid impeachment threats, House GOP to question \uc2 Hunter Biden\uc2 's former business partner\par \par \uc2 Good morning, US politics blog readers. \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  is on vacation and House and Senate lawmakers are on their August recess, but not everyone in Congress is taking a holiday. Investigators with the Republican-led House oversight committee will today sit down for an interview with Devon Archer, the former business partner of \uc2 Hunter Biden\uc2 . The committee has taken the lead in the GOP\u8217\'20\'19s quest to prove corruption on the part of the Bidens, and while we may not find out what Archer told them for weeks to come, the ultimate goals of the GOP\u8217\'20\'19s investigation may soon become clear.\par \par \uc2 In recent days, top Republicans, including speaker of the House Kevin McCarthy, have openly mused about impeaching the president. No such inquiry would start till September, when their break is over, and, at this point, impeachment looks more political than practical: with the Senate in Democratic hands, the chances of Biden being removed from the White House are slim to none. House GOP has, however, not yet definitively said if they\u8217\'20\'19ll go through with it, but expect to hear plenty of saber rattling in the weeks to come.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s what else is happening today:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2 , whose presidential campaign at this point appears to be well off the rails, sits down for an interview with Fox News that will air at 6pm eastern time.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  spoke with ABC News in an interview that will air at 7pm eastern time, though portions of her remarks have already been broadcast.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 A \uc2 New York Times\uc2 /Siena poll{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/2023/07/31/us/politics/2024-poll-nyt-siena-trump-republicans.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 has found}}}\uc2  what almost all the other polls before it have found: \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  is the frontrunner for the Republican presidential nomination.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020230731ej7v001h4\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
