\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Trump, DeSantis and top Republican candidates share stage at Iowa event \u8211\'20\'13 as it happened\b0\par\par\uc2 Aben\u233\'00\'E9 Clayton (now); L\u233\'00\'E9onie Chao-Fong and Chris Stein politics live blogger (earlier) \par \uc2 7,012 \uc2 words\par \uc2 29 July 2023\par 02:25 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Most of the party\u8217\'20\'19s 13 candidates for the presidential nomination in the early voting state attend the 2023 Lincoln Dinner fundraiser\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.16am BST\par \par \uc2 Lincoln Dinner concludes\par \par \uc2 After more than two hours of speeches mainly centered on trans healthcare, the southern border and \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the Lincoln Dinner put on by Iowa\u8217\'20\'19s Republicans, has concluded.\par \par \uc2 Thirteen speakers took to the podium to lay out their ideas about what is wrong with America and how they, as presidential hopefuls, had the answers to conservative gripes.\par \par \uc2 Few took direct jabs at each other and rather directed their criticisms at Democratic policies and boogeymen like the indoctrination of children and stripping of rights from parents.\par \par \uc2 The former Arkansas governor Asa Hutchinson mentioned the many lawsuits former president \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  is facing and \uc2 Will Hurd\uc2 , a lesser-known candidate from Texas, said explicitly that Tump was running for president to stay out of prison. That comment was met with loud boos from the ballroom audience.\par \par \uc2 Trump, who spoke last and continues to dominate in the polls despite his numerous legal liabilities, pulled no punches when calling out his main opponent, \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2 , the governor of Florida. He continuously mispronounced his name, called out his opposition to ethanol production and argued that the Florida governor was lagging behind in the polls.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI wouldn\u8217\'20\'19t take a chance on that one,\u8221\'20\'1D Trump said of DeSantis.\par \par \uc2 While, he made it a point to tell the Iowa audience about his policies on trans people in sports and tariffs he imposed on China, the former president made no mention of the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/jul/28/donald-trump-investigations-criminal-charges-tracker"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 litany of charges}}}\uc2  he is facing.\par \par \uc2 The only Republican candidate absent from the dinner was \uc2 Chris Christie\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Read the rest of the Guardian\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/jul/28/iowa-trump-desantis-scott-lincoln-dinner"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 coverage of the dinner here}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.22am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.31am BST\par \par \uc2 Most of the Republican speakers at tonight\u8217\'20\'19s Lincoln Dinner did not take aim at any of their peers, but \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , who just left the podium to cheers, took several jabs at \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 He continuously mispronounced his name, called out his opposition to ethanol production and argued that the Florida governor was lagging behind in the polls.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI wouldn\u8217\'20\'19t take a chance on that one,\u8221\'20\'1D Trump said of DeSantis.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.41am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.45am BST\par \par \uc2 Will Hurd\uc2 , a former US representative from Texas and lesser-known candidate in the Republican race, left the stage to the sound of boos after he said that \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  is running for president just to stay out prison.\par \par \uc2 enltrFormer Texas Rep. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/WillHurd?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @WillHurd}}}\uc2  was up next.\par \par \uc2 He went after frontrunner {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/realDonaldTrump?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @realDonaldTrump}}}\uc2  in blunt terms.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1C\uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  is running to stay out of prison.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 [Boos]\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI know the truth is hard. But if we elect \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , we are giving \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  four more years in the White House\u8230\'20\'26\u8221\'20\'1D {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/iQmeNsGF6W"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/iQmeNsGF6W}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Taylor Popielarz (@TaylorPopielarz) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/TaylorPopielarz/status/1685088342877061120?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 July 29, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 1.53am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.31am BST\par \par \uc2 At the podium now is former vice-president \uc2 Mike Pence\uc2 . He opens his speech by calling out what he sees as \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s failing at the border and pro-choice stance.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1C\uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  has been a disaster for America,\u8221\'20\'1D he tells the crowd.\par \par \uc2 In addition to standard conservative talking points on the national debt and national security, he also vowed to implement a ban on trans people in the military.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 1.39am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.19am BST\par \par \uc2 We\u8217\'20\'19re approaching the halfway point of tonight\u8217\'20\'19s Lincoln Dinner in Iowa. So far, six Republican candidate hopefuls have given their spiel on their plans for the nation. They are:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Nikki Haley\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Asa Hutchinson\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Ron DeSantis\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Tim Scott\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Perry Johnson\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Doug Burgum\par \par \uc2 Each speaker has called out salient issues in today\u8217\'20\'19s culture wars like \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access, healthcare for transgender children and ethnic studies in schools.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 1.38am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.53am BST\par \par \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2 , governor of Florida, a potential Republican ticket frontrunner, just left the stage. He emphasized the policies that have allowed the state to \u8220\'20\'1Cbeat the left\u8217\'20\'19s agenda\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 He also vowed to deploy the military to the southern border and use \u8220\'20\'1Cdeadly force\u8221\'20\'1D on cartels.\par \par \uc2 DeSantis\u8217\'20\'19 assaults on transgender healthcare, \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access and ethnic studies and LGBTQ+ education have been well-documented. In May, the \uc2 Guardian\uc2  published a story where wide minority groups warned of what the damage his presidency could do to the nation.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/may/25/florida-groups-america-white-house-ron-desantis"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Read that piece here.}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 1.38am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.33am BST\par \par \uc2 Nikki Haley, the former governor of South Carolina was the first presidential hopeful to address the Lincoln Dinner audience.\par \par \uc2 She emphasized the nation\u8217\'20\'19s $32tn debt as well as the economic struggles facing many American families. She also took an unsurprising aim at the Biden administration, claiming that a 2024 win for Biden will mean that \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  is really the one winning the election.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 1.38am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.22am BST\par \par \uc2 Iowa governor \uc2 Kim Reynolds\uc2  just stepped off of the Lincoln Dinner stage. During her speech she touted the state\u8217\'20\'19s supermajority and passage of conservative education and \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  policies. She told the dinner audience:\par \par \uc2 We\u8217\'20\'19re empowering parents and protecting life.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Earlier this month state legislators voted to ban most abortions after six weeks of pregnancy, a time before most people know they are pregnant.\par \par \uc2 Read more on {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/jul/12/iowa-passes-six-week-abortion-ban#:~:text=A%20similar%20six%2Dweek%20ban,constitutionally%20protected%20right%20in%20Iowa."}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the decision here}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 1.38am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.16am BST\par \par \uc2 I\u8217\'20\'19m Aben\u233\'00\'E9 Clayton, reporting from the west coast.\par \par \uc2 The Lincoln Dinner, put on by Iowa\u8217\'20\'19s Republican Party is underway.\par \par \uc2 All of the Republican candidates for president, except \uc2 Chris Christie\uc2 , will deliver speeches of up to 10min to the ballroom audience.\par \par \uc2 Up first were Jeff Kaufman a state representative and \uc2 Kim Reynolds\uc2 , the governor of Iowa.\par \par \uc2 I\u8217\'20\'19ll be posting updates from the dinner here.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 12.25am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.58pm BST\par \par \uc2 At the Iowa Republican party\u8217\'20\'19s 2023 Lincoln Dinner fundraiser, the super PAC backing \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2  has set up baseballs to throw at cans of Bud Light.\par \par \uc2 From the \uc2 New York Times\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19 Shane Goldmacher:\par \par \uc2 enltrIn hospitality suite at Iowa GOP dinner, the DeSantis super PAC has set up baseballs to throw at Bud Light cans, per pic from NBD {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/dvuR45pshs"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/dvuR45pshs}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Shane Goldmacher (@ShaneGoldmacher) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/ShaneGoldmacher/status/1685059915251863552?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 July 28, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.51pm BST\par \par \uc2 Trump, DeSantis and top Republican candidates to share stage at Iowa event\par \par \uc2 Every major Republican presidential candidate will share a stage in the early voting state of Iowa tonight, as \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  continues to dominate in the polls despite his numerous legal liabilities.\par \par \uc2 Most of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/ng-interactive/2023/jun/17/2024-presidential-candidates-biden-trump-republicans-democrats"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the 13 candidates}}}\uc2  will appear at the Iowa Republican party\u8217\'20\'19s 2023 Lincoln Dinner fundraiser, giving them an opportunity to address donors and local party leaders with less than six months left before the state\u8217\'20\'19s crucial caucuses.\par \par \uc2 The lineup of confirmed speakers for tonight are:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Ron DeSantis\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Mike Pence\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Nikki Haley\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Tim Scott\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Vivek Ramaswamy\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Asa Hutchinson\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Larry Elder\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Perry Johnson\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Doug Burgum\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Francis Suarez\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Ryan Binkley\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Will Hurd\par \par \uc2 The event is scheduled to begin at 7pm ET. We will be following it live here on the blog.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 12.19am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.39pm BST\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.documentcloud.org/documents/23889238-trump-superseeding-indictment"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Along with two new charges}}}\uc2  of obstruction of justice, there was another new count of retaining classified material. Special counsel Jack Smith describes a July 2021 incident in which \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  bragged about a \u8220\'20\'1Cplan of attack\u8221\'20\'1D against another country in an interview at his golf resort in Bedminster, New Jersey.\par \par \uc2 The former president then waved around the classified documents to his guests: a writer, publisher and two Trump staff members who all lacked security clearances \u8220\'20\'1CThis is secret information,\u8221\'20\'1D he said, according to a recording cited in the documents, claiming that, \u8220\'20\'1Cas president I could have declassified it\u8221\'20\'1D \u8211\'20\'13 but he had not.\par \par \uc2 The indictment says the document was returned to the federal government on 17 January 2022, which is the date Trump provided 15 boxes of records to the National Archives.\par \par \uc2 Trump now faces 40 criminal counts in the classified documents case alone. \uc2 Ty Cobb\uc2 , a former Trump White House lawyer, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/jul/28/trump-lawyer-charges-1000-years-mar-a-lago"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 told CNN}}}\uc2  :\par \par \uc2 I think this original indictment was engineered to last a thousand years and now this superseding indictment will last an antiquity. This is such a tight case, the evidence is so overwhelming.\par \par \uc2 The new charges were made public hours after Trump said his lawyers met with justice department officials investigating his attempts to overturn his 2020 election loss to \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 , in a sign that another set of criminal charges could come soon.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.30pm BST\par \par \uc2 Video from \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s Mar-a-Lago estate in Florida would play a significant role in the investigation because, prosecutors say, it shows his valet, Walt Nauta, moving boxes of documents in and out of a storage room \u8211\'20\'13 including a day before an \uc2 FBI\uc2  visit to the property \u8211\'20\'13 at Trump\u8217\'20\'19s direction.\par \par \uc2 According to the indictment, Nauta met Mar-a-Lago property manager Carlos De Oliveira at Mar-a-Lago on 25 June 2022. They went to a security guard booth where surveillance video is displayed on monitors and walked with a torch through a tunnel where the storage room was located, observing and pointing out surveillance cameras.\par \par \uc2 Two days later, according to the indictment, De Oliveira walked through a basement tunnel with a Trump employee to a small room known as an \u8220\'20\'1Caudio closet\u8221\'20\'1D. The two men had a conversation supposed to \u8220\'20\'1Cremain between the two of them\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 De Oliveira asked how many days the server retained footage. De Oliveira allegedly told the employee that \u8220\'20\'1Cthe boss\u8221\'20\'1D wanted the server deleted and asked: \u8220\'20\'1CWhat are we going to do?\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The indictment asserts that Trump called De Oliveira before and after the incident, and that Nauta and De Oliveira were also in contact.\par \par \uc2 Prosecutors further allege that, during a voluntary interview with the \uc2 FBI\uc2  last January, De Oliveira lied when he said he \u8220\'20\'1Cnever saw nothing\u8221\'20\'1D with regard to boxes at Mar-a-Lago.\par \par \uc2 De Oliveira was added to the indictment, charged with obstruction and false statements related to that \uc2 FBI\uc2  interview. This could impact the trial date, currently set for May next year, by which stage the Republican nomination may well have been decided.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.17pm BST\par \par \uc2 A tunnel lit by torchlight. An attempt to delete incriminating camera footage. A \u8220\'20\'1Cboss\u8221\'20\'1D whose orders must be obeyed. And all to no avail.\par \par \uc2 The latest criminal charges against \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , the former US president, conjure images of the hapless {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/jun/05/watergate-50th-anniversary-john-dean-interview"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Watergate burglars}}}\uc2  or a mob movie with elements of farce.\par \par \uc2 But while they deepen Trump\u8217\'20\'19s legal perils, analysts say, they will only harden his determination to regain the White House as his best chance of staying out of jail. Opinion polls show he remains the runaway frontrunner for the Republican nomination in 2024.\par \par \uc2 Trump, who left office in January 2021, pleaded not guilty in Miami last month to federal charges of unlawfully retaining classified government documents at his Mar-a-Lago estate in Florida and obstructing justice. Prosecutors allege that he put some of America\u8217\'20\'19s most sensitive national security secrets at risk.\par \par \uc2 On Thursday they updated the indictment by accusing the former president of scheming with his valet, Walt Nauta, and a Mar-a-Lago property manager, Carlos De Oliveira, to hide surveillance footage from federal investigators after they issued a subpoena for it.\par \par \uc2 It was left to others to dwell on the irony of Trump, who spent much of the 2016 campaign savaging rival \uc2 Hillary Clinton\uc2  for {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.fbi.gov/news/press-releases/statement-by-fbi-director-james-b-comey-on-the-investigation-of-secretary-hillary-clinton2019s-use-of-a-personal-e-mail-system"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 deleting emails}}}\uc2  from a computer server as secretary of state, now standing accused of trying to delete security footage at his home.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.01pm BST\par \par \uc2 The US is expected to announce a new military aid package to Taiwan worth $345m, according to US officials, a move that is likely to anger China.\par \par \uc2 The package includes man-portable air defense systems, or Manpads, intelligence and surveillance capabilities, firearms and missiles, AP reported, citing sources.\par \par \uc2 Congress authorized up to $1bn worth of Presidential Drawdown Authority weapons aid for Taiwan in the 2023 budget.\par \par \uc2 The latest package would be in addition to nearly $19bn in military sales of F-16s and other weapons systems that the US has approved to Taiwan.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.38pm BST\par \par \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2  suggests he would pardon Trump if elected\par \par \uc2 Florida governor \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2  indicated he would consider pardoning \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  if he is elected president, a day after the former president {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/jul/27/trump-mar-a-lago-classified-documents-case-carlos-de-oliveira"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 was indicted on additional charges}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 In an interview on the Megyn Kelly show, DeSantis was asked if he would commit to pardoning Trump on any federal charges. He replied:\par \par \uc2 Well, what I\u8217\'20\'19ve said is very simple. I\u8217\'20\'19m going to do what\u8217\'20\'19s right for the country. I don\u8217\'20\'19t think it would be good for the country to have an almost 80-year-old former president go to prison. It doesn\u8217\'20\'19t seem like it would be a good thing.\par \par \uc2 And I look at like, you know, \uc2 Ford\uc2  pardoned Nixon, took some heat for it, but at the end of the day, it\u8217\'20\'19s like, do we want to move forward as a country? Or do we want to be mired in these past controversies?\par \par \uc2 DeSantis previously said that, if elected, he would consider pardoning people involved in the January 6 insurrection, including Trump.\par \par \uc2 enltrDeSantis, asked whether he\u8217\'20\'19d pardon Trump on any federal charges against him, says in part:\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI'm going to do what's right for the country. I don't think it would be good for the country to have an almost 80 year old former president go to prison\u8230\'20\'26\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/PCqEjpp2CY"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/PCqEjpp2CY}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Shelby Talcott (@ShelbyTalcott) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/ShelbyTalcott/status/1684932187337134081?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 July 28, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 10.48pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.01pm BST\par \par \uc2 Republican representative John James of Michigan weighed in on the debate over Florida\u8217\'20\'19s controversial new curriculum standards for Black history, which include the contention that some Black people benefited from being enslaved.\par \par \uc2 James criticized \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2 , the Florida governor also running for the GOP presidential nomination, for supporting the new standards that require Florida teachers to tell middle school students people enslaved in the US developed skills that \u8220\'20\'1Ccould be applied for their personal benefit\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Posting to \uc2 Twitter\uc2 , James said DeSantis should \u8220\'20\'1Cput the shovel down\u8221\'20\'1D if he found himself \u8220\'20\'1Cin a deep hole\u8221\'20\'1D, and that the Florida governor was \u8220\'20\'1Cnow so far from the Party of Lincoln that your [Education] board is re-writing history\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 It comes after DeSantis accused his GOP rival and the only Black Republican in the \uc2 US Senate\uc2 , Tim Scott, of laundering Democratic talking points after {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/jul/28/tim-scott-ron-desantis-florida-slavery-teaching"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the South Carolina senator said slavery was \u8220\'20\'1Cdevastating\u8221\'20\'1D. }}}\par \par \uc2 Addressing DeSantis, James wrote:\par \par \uc2 There are only five black Republicans in Congress and you\u8217\'20\'19re attacking two of them\par \par \uc2 enltr. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/RonDeSantis?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @RonDeSantis}}}\uc2 , #1: slavery was not CTE! Nothing about that 400 years of evil was a \u8220\'20\'1Cnet benefit\u8221\'20\'1D to my ancestors. #2: there are only five black Republicans in Congress and you\u8217\'20\'19re attacking two of them.\par \par \uc2 My brother in Christ\u8230\'20\'26 ??????? if you find yourself in a deep hole put the shovel\u8230\'20\'26 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/9DGZw4BI0o"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/9DGZw4BI0o}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 John James (@JohnJamesMI) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/JohnJamesMI/status/1685020441692225536?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 July 28, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.33pm BST\par \par \uc2 Democrat congressman \uc2 Dean Phillips\uc2  weighs primary run against Biden\par \par \uc2 Dean Phillips\uc2 , a moderate Democrat congressman representing Minnesota, is considering a potential 2024 primary challenge against \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 , according to multiple reports.\par \par \uc2 Phillips will meet with Democrat donors next week in New York about a potential long-shot primary challenge. The news was first {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.politico.com/news/magazine/2023/07/28/2024-presidential-contest-candidates-biden-trump-00108685"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reported}}}\uc2  by Politico, then Phillips {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cnn.com/2023/07/28/politics/dean-phillips-2024/index.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 confirmed}}}\uc2  his meeting to CNN.\par \par \uc2 Phillips has said publicly he does not believe Biden should run for reelection. In an {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.minnpost.com/elections/2022/07/phillips-democrats-need-new-generation-of-leadership-not-biden-in-2024/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 interview}}}\uc2  last year, he said the country \u8220\'20\'1Cwould be well served by a new generation of compelling, well-prepared, dynamic Democrats to step up\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Politico writes:\par \par \uc2 Phillips, who\u8217\'20\'19s in his third term representing suburban Minneapolis, has drawn attention from contributors by both denouncing the \u8220\'20\'1CNo Labels\u8221\'20\'1D attempt to field a third-party ticket and calling for a contested Democratic primary next year. A former executive, he\u8217\'20\'19s also the sort of pro-business social moderate with private sector experience who corporate leaders usually pine for in a presidential candidate.\par \par \uc2 Phillips, 54, is highly unlikely to mount a primary challenge unless Biden\u8217\'20\'19s health worsens or his political standing drops precipitously, I\u8217\'20\'19m told, and does not want to further weaken the president.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.59pm BST\par \par \uc2 Congress has a lot on its plate when it gets back to work in September.\par \par \uc2 Among its most important tasks is agreeing on a number of funding bills, ahead of a 30 September deadline after which the \uc2 US government\uc2  could shut down if the legislation is not passed.\par \par \uc2 But Republicans are also {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/jul/25/mccarthy-biden-impeachment-inquiry-fox-news"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 openly mulling}}}\uc2  whether to impeach \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  over allegations of corruption. It\u8217\'20\'19s possible the effort would succeed in the House, where the GOP has a majority, but there is almost no chance at this point of the Democratic-controlled Senate voting to convict the president.\par \par \uc2 Biden appears to be taking the threat in stride. In a speech earlier today, he turned the impeachment push into a laugh line:\par \par \uc2 enltrPresident Biden: \u8220\'20\'1CThe \uc2 Washington Post\uc2  suggested Republicans may have to find something else to criticize me for, now that inflation is coming down. Maybe they\u8217\'20\'19ll decide to impeach me because it\u8217\'20\'19s coming down. I don't know. I love that one.\u8221\'20\'1D {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/IFwNVCo7DY"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/IFwNVCo7DY}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 The Recount (@therecount) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/therecount/status/1684986596548849683?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 July 28, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 9.20pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.49pm BST\par \par \uc2 Congress is on recess for the next few weeks, which is likely a relief for the Senate pages who recently got screamed at by a House Republican. The Associated Press has the story:\par \par \uc2 A freshman Republican congressman from Wisconsin yelled and cursed at high school-aged Senate pages during a late-night tour of the Capitol this week, eliciting a bipartisan rebuke from Senate leaders.\par \par \uc2 Derrick Van Orden, who represents western Wisconsin\u8217\'20\'19s third district, used a profanity to describe the young pages as lazy and another to order them off the floor of the Capitol Rotunda on Wednesday night, according to PunchBowl News. The pages were lying down to take photos, according to the publication.\par \par \uc2 In a statement responding to the report, Van Orden doubled down.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI have long said our nation\u8217\'20\'19s Capitol is a symbol of the sacrifice our servicemen and women have made for this country and should never be treated like a frat house common room,\u8221\'20\'1D Van Orden said.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/jul/28/republican-derrick-van-orden-pages-capitol-wisconsin"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Republican congressman rebuked by senators for swearing at young pages}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.29pm BST\par \par \uc2 Fortunately for \uc2 Samuel Alito\uc2 , legislation to force the supreme court to adopt an ethics code appears to lack the votes for enactment.\par \par \uc2 A week ago, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/jul/20/trump-testimony-january-6-case-biden-epa-us-politics-live?filterKeyEvents=false&page=with:block-64b981d68f087edb1f3ee8db#block-64b981d68f087edb1f3ee8db"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the Senate judiciary committee approved}}}\uc2  the Supreme Court Ethics, Recusal, and Transparency Act, which, in addition to mandating the justices outline their ethics rules, would create a mechanism to investigate violations of the code, force justices to explain publicly why they are recusing themselves from cases and improve requirements for transparency and disclosure.\par \par \uc2 But while Democrats were able to get the bill through the judiciary committee with a simple majority, it appears to have no Republican supporters, as {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/may/02/republicans-democrats-supreme-court-ethics-rules"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a hearing on the proposal made clear}}}\uc2 , nixing its chances of clearing the 60-vote majority needed to pass most legislation in the Senate. There have also been no indications that the GOP, which controls the House, would consider the bill.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.06pm BST\par \par \uc2 Conservative justice Alito says Congress has no authority to impose ethics code on supreme court\par \par \uc2 Conservative supreme court justice \uc2 Samuel Alito\uc2  told {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/samuel-alito-the-supreme-courts-plain-spoken-defender-precedent-ethics-originalism-5e3e9a7?st=yaf444fmb8q9vd1"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the Wall Street Journal}}}\uc2  that he does not believe Congress has the authority to impose a code of ethics on the nation\u8217\'20\'19s highest court.\par \par \uc2 His comments came amid {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/law/2023/may/28/supreme-court-sheldon-whitehouse-ethics-reform"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a push by Senate Democrats}}}\uc2  to pass legislation forcing the nation\u8217\'20\'19s highest court to adopt an ethics regulations in response to a series of media reports {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/law/2023/jul/12/us-supreme-court-justices-ethics-rules-controversy-explain"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 revealing entanglements}}}\uc2  between the justices and parties with interests in their cases.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI know this is a controversial view, but I\u8217\'20\'19m willing to say it,\u8221\'20\'1D Alito told the Journal\u8217\'20\'19s editorial board, which typically takes conservative positions, in an interview. \u8220\'20\'1CNo provision in the constitution gives them the authority to regulate the supreme court \u8211\'20\'13 period.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 He added that \u8220\'20\'1CCongress did not create the supreme court\u8221\'20\'1D but demurred when asked if his colleagues agreed. \u8220\'20\'1CI don\u8217\'20\'19t know that any of my colleagues have spoken about it publicly, so I don\u8217\'20\'19t think I should say. But I think it is something we have all thought about.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Alito also reflected on mounting criticism of the court\u8217\'20\'19s legitimacy from the left, after the six-justice conservative majority overturned Roe v Wade, expanded the ability for people to carry concealed weapons, allowed businesses to turn away LGBTQ+ people and banned race-conscious college admissions {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/law/2023/jul/01/us-supreme-court-rulings-what-does-it-mean-affirmative-action-lgbtq-student-debt"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 in recent decisions}}}\uc2 . He wondered if something comparable to the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2021/nov/27/integration-public-schools-massive-resistance-virginia-1950s"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1Cmassive resistance\u8221\'20\'1D}}}\uc2  seen in Virginia beginning in the 1950s to court rulings ordering desegregation might emerge in opposition to the supreme court today.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIf we\u8217\'20\'19re viewed as illegitimate, then disregard of our decisions becomes more acceptable and more popular. So you can have a revival of the massive resistance that occurred in the South after Brown,\u8221\'20\'1D he said, referring to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/education/2022/jul/15/us-schools-segregated-race-class-analysis"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the landmark school desegregation case}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 8.09pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.39pm BST\par \par \uc2 From Georgia, the Guardian\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/justin-glawe"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Justin Glawe}}}\uc2  brings us a story that illustrates how \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s lies about the 2020 election are affecting voting even in the smallest communities:\par \par \uc2 A rural {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/state-of-georgia"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Georgia}}}\uc2  elections office run by Republicans who promote falsehoods about the 2020 election approved a motion on Monday to institute automatic hand recounts for all future elections.\par \par \uc2 The decision will require elections staff in Spalding county to hand-count each ballot, then compare those vote totals with totals reached by voting tabulation machines provided by the secretary of state. Hand counts slow certification of election results and are less reliable than tabulations carried out by machines.\par \par \uc2 In introducing the measure, Republican board member James Newland cited false claims about widespread voter fraud.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/jul/28/georgia-republican-election-hand-count-ballot"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Republican promoters of election fraud falsehoods approve ballot hand-counts }}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.17pm BST\par \par \uc2 After Texas\u8217\'20\'19s Republican governor deployed razor wire and buoys to keep migrants from crossing into the state from Mexico, the Guardian\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/erum-salam"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Erum Salam}}}\uc2  spoke to a Democratic state senator about what the new border policy means. Here\u8217\'20\'19s what he had to say:\par \par \uc2 The rightwing governor of Texas, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/greg-abbott"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Greg Abbott}}}\uc2 , is conducting a border policy that is \u8220\'20\'1Ccriminal\u8221\'20\'1D and \u8220\'20\'1Cinhumane\u8221\'20\'1D by deploying razor wire and a huge floating buoy in the Rio Grande, a top Texas Democrat has told the Guardian.\par \par \uc2 Abbott has earned widespread condemnation from civil rights groups and immigration activists for his actions on the border and been accused of pushing a policy that is racist and inflammatory. The \uc2 US Department of Justice\uc2  has sued over the issue \u8211\'20\'13 though Abbott is currently defying the federal government and not changing tack.\par \par \uc2 Allegations have also surfaced of border officers being instructed to withhold water in extreme heat, and push children \u8220\'20\'1Cback into the water to go to Mexico\u8221\'20\'1D from a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cbsnews.com/texas/news/read-full-email-texas-dps-trooper-sent-concerns-alleged-inhumane-handling-migrants/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 leaked email}}}\uc2  sent from a state trooper in the border city of Eagle Pass, Texas.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/jul/28/texas-governor-condemned-razor-wire-buoy-us-mexico-border"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Texas Senate hopeful decries governor\u8217\'20\'19s \u8216\'20\'18criminal, inhumane\u8217\'20\'19 razor-wire barrier}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.57pm BST\par \par \uc2 Abigail Spanberger\uc2 , a third-term Democrat congresswoman representing Virginia, has told multiple people she will run for governor in 2025, according to a Politico {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.politico.com/news/2023/07/28/spanberger-future-00108756"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  report.}}}\par \par \uc2 Spanberger and one of her top aides has told several Democrats that she is planning to bid for the governor\u8217\'20\'19s mansion that Republican governor Glenn Youngkin will vacate in 2025, the report says, citing sources.\par \par \uc2 That decision could have major implications for Richmond and for Washington, where she would open up a critical battleground seat if she opts not to run for reelection next year.\par \par \uc2 Youngkin won the seat in 2021 in what was {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/nov/02/glenn-youngkin-wins-virginia-governor-election-result"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a shock defeat }}}\uc2  for the Democrats. The battle in Virginia was seen as a litmus test of Biden\u8217\'20\'19s presidency one year after he won the White House.\par \par \uc2 Rep. \uc2 Abigail Spanberger\uc2  of Virginia. Photograph: Anna Moneymaker/Getty Images\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.37pm BST\par \par \uc2 A voting rights group in Florida filed a lawsuit against the rightwing governor and presidential candidate \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2 , saying his administration created a maze of bureaucratic and sometimes {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/jan/12/florida-police-man-arrest-voter-fraud-body-camera"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 violent}}}\uc2  obstacles to discourage formerly incarcerated citizens from exercising their right to vote.\par \par \uc2 Florida voters in 2018 overwhelmingly passed a constitutional referendum, called amendment 4, that lifted the state\u8217\'20\'19s lifetime voting ban for people with felony convictions.\par \par \uc2 Yet what ensued in the years since 2018 was an aggressive campaign, led by DeSantis, to sow confusion and fear among formerly incarcerated people. The Florida Rights Restoration Coalition (FRRC), which championed amendment 4, said state officials have continued to disenfranchise 1.4 million Florida residents \u8211\'20\'13 roughly a quarter of the state\u8217\'20\'19s eligible Black voters.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWho is the public supposed to rely on to determine voter eligibility?\u8221\'20\'1D said the FRRC\u8217\'20\'19s executive director, Desmond Meade.\par \par \uc2 We\u8217\'20\'19re saying that it is the responsibility of the state. The law says it is the responsibility of the state.\par \par \uc2 DeSantis appears to disagree. The lawsuit, resubmitted on Friday by the FRRC, comes a year after the Florida governor ordered the arrests of dozens of people who participated in the 2020 election, including people who had been issued voter registration cards from the Florida department of state.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/jul/28/ron-desantis-sued-voting-rights-group"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Read the full story here.}}}\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/jul/28/ron-desantis-sued-voting-rights-group"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Ron DeSantis sued over bid to restrict voting rights for people with past convictions}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.25pm BST\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  signed an executive order on Friday to implement military justice reforms aimed at strengthening how the military handles serious military crimes, including sexual assault cases.\par \par \uc2 The change to the Uniform Code of Military Justice transfers key decision-making authorities on the prosecution of sexual assault and other violent crimes outside the military chain of command and to independent military attorneys.\par \par \uc2 The order officially implements changes passed by Congress in 2022 aimed at strengthening protections for service members, who were often at the mercy of their commanders to decide whether to take their assault claims seriously.\par \par \uc2 AP reports:\par \par \uc2 Members of Congress, frustrated with the growing number of sexual assaults in the military, fought with defense leaders for several years over the issue. They argued that commanders at times were willing to ignore charges or incidents in their units to protect those accused of offenses and that using independent lawyers would beef up prosecutions. Military leaders balked, saying it could erode commanders\u8217\'20\'19 authority.\par \par \uc2 In a call with reporters previewing the executive order, senior administration officials said it was the most sweeping change to the military legal code since it was created in 1950. An official said:\par \par \uc2 These changes follow decades tireless efforts by survivors, advocates and members of Congress to strengthen the military justice systems response to gender-based violence.\par \par \uc2 enltrToday, I signed an Executive Order strengthening how our military handles sexual assault and serious offenses.\par \par \uc2 Ending gender-based violence has been a priority for me throughout my career.\par \par \uc2 This represents a turning point for survivors of gender-based violence in the military. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/zJ0ixMn3xZ"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/zJ0ixMn3xZ}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 President Biden (@POTUS) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/POTUS/status/1684974581990268936?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 July 28, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 6.31pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.03pm BST\par \par \uc2 The day so far\par \par \uc2 Washington is reacting in a completely predictable fashion to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/jul/28/trump-classified-documents-charges-indictment-jan-6-politics-live-updates?page=with:block-64c3c4ad8f08db2904abb654#block-64c3c4ad8f08db2904abb654"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the new charges}}}\uc2  brought against \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  yesterday over the government secrets discovered at Mar-a-Lago. While {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/jul/28/trump-classified-documents-charges-indictment-jan-6-politics-live-updates?page=with:block-64c3c89e8f086b325af60e50#block-64c3c89e8f086b325af60e50"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 his detractors}}}\uc2  say he should end his presidential campaign over the allegations, which one former Trump White House lawyer {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/jul/28/trump-classified-documents-charges-indictment-jan-6-politics-live-updates?page=with:block-64c3bf428f08db2904abb5f9#block-64c3bf428f08db2904abb5f9"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 called \u8220\'20\'1Ctight\u8221\'20\'1D}}}\uc2 , the former president remains defiant, and Republican House speaker Kevin McCarthy {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/jul/28/trump-classified-documents-charges-indictment-jan-6-politics-live-updates?page=with:block-64c3e4c08f086b325af61082#block-64c3e4c08f086b325af61082"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 gave no indication}}}\uc2  that his crucial support was wavering.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s what else has happened today so far:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Trump remains the frontrunner for the Republican presidential nomination, and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/jul/28/trump-classified-documents-charges-indictment-jan-6-politics-live-updates?page=with:block-64c3d9e08f08db2904abb82d#block-64c3d9e08f08db2904abb82d"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 polls are beginning to show}}}\uc2  a pronounced drop in support for Florida governor \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2 , and an uptick in voters interested in first-time candidate \uc2 Vivek Ramaswamy\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Mitch McConnell{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/jul/28/trump-classified-documents-charges-indictment-jan-6-politics-live-updates?page=with:block-64c3ee8c8f08db2904abb97a#block-64c3ee8c8f08db2904abb97a"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 does not plan to}}}\uc2  step down as the leader of the Senate Republicans, at least not in this Congress, a spokesperson said, despite {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/jul/28/trump-classified-documents-charges-indictment-jan-6-politics-live-updates?page=with:block-64c3e56f8f08db2904abb8ef#block-64c3e56f8f08db2904abb8ef"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 this week\u8217\'20\'19s health scare}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 A former federal prosecutor{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/jul/28/trump-classified-documents-charges-indictment-jan-6-politics-live-updates?page=with:block-64c3cd128f08db2904abb705#block-64c3cd128f08db2904abb705"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 told CNN}}}\uc2  the new charges against Trump may be an indication special counsel Jack Smith does not believe the Mar-a-Lago case will be resolved before next year\u8217\'20\'19s election.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 6.05pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.40pm BST\par \par \uc2 A spokesperson for \uc2 Mitch McConnell\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s office said he will stay as the Senate Republican leader through the 2024 election, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.reuters.com/world/us/us-senate-republican-leader-mcconnell-plans-stay-post-through-current-congress-2023-07-28/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Reuters reports}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CHe plans to serve his full term in the job they overwhelmingly elected him to do,\u8221\'20\'1D the spokesperson said, referring to GOP senators. McConnell\u8217\'20\'19s current term representing Kentucky in the Senate runs through 2026, and the spokesperson did not address his plans beyond the current Congress, which ends in the first days of January 2025.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.17pm BST\par \par \uc2 Over in the Senate, the fallout continues from \uc2 Mitch McConnell\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s health scare earlier this week. \uc2 The Guardian\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/martin-pengelly"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Martin Pengelly}}}\uc2  reports one Republican senator said \u8211\'20\'13 albeit anonymously \u8211\'20\'13 that McConnell should step down as the party\u8217\'20\'19s leader in the chamber:\par \par \uc2 Mitch McConnell\uc2 , the 81-year-old Republican leader in the \uc2 US Senate\uc2  who suffered a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/jul/27/mitch-mcconnell-freeze-press-conference-fall-age"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 public health scare}}}\uc2  this week, should step down from the role he has filled since 2007, an unnamed GOP senator {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nbcnews.com/politics/congress/gop-senators-express-anxieties-mitch-mcconnells-health-rcna96706"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 said}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 McConnell, from Kentucky, remains \u8220\'20\'1Cintellectually sharp\u8221\'20\'1D on \u8220\'20\'1Ca whole host of issues including baseball\u8221\'20\'1D, the anonymous senator {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nbcnews.com/politics/congress/gop-senators-express-anxieties-mitch-mcconnells-health-rcna96706"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 told NBC News}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 But they added: \u8220\'20\'1CPeople think that he\u8217\'20\'19s not hearing well. I think that he is just not processing.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 At a news conference on Capitol Hill on Wednesday, McConnell stopped talking mid-sentence, standing mutely for 23 seconds until he was led away from reporters.\par \par \uc2 He returned to say: \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19m fine.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/jul/28/mitch-mcconnell-freezing-speech-health"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Mitch McConnell should step down as Senate minority leader after freezing, GOP senator says}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.57pm BST\par \par \uc2 McCarthy downplays concerns over new Trump charges\par \par \uc2 CNN managed to track down Republican speaker of the House Kevin McCarthy at the Capitol to ask him if he was concerned about the new charges against \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The short version of the speaker\u8217\'20\'19s answer, as you will see from the clip below, is that he is not:\par \par \uc2 enltrSpeaker McCarthy weighs in for first time on new charges filed against Trump alleging obstruction in docs probe. Asked if he had concerns with that and Trump allegedly seeking deletion of surveillance video.\par \par \uc2 "What concerns me," he says, is Biden's mishandling of classified docs {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/LJc0N6dYNU"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/LJc0N6dYNU}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Manu Raju (@mkraju) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/mkraju/status/1684953581349167104?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 July 28, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 McCarthy\u8217\'20\'19s comments are not much of a surprise. While he hasn\u8217\'20\'19t formally made an endorsement in the 2024 presidential campaign, he has long striven to stay on the good side of the former president, who has many allies among House Republicans.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 6.44pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.37pm BST\par \par \uc2 Speaking of \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2 , his support for controversial new standards regarding teaching about slavery in Florida have become fodder for a rival on the Republican campaign trail, the Associated Press reports:\par \par \uc2 The South Carolina senator Tim Scott criticized {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/ron-desantis"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Ron DeSantis}}}\uc2 , the Florida governor also running for the Republican presidential nomination, for supporting new standards that require Florida teachers to tell middle school students people enslaved in the US developed skills that \u8220\'20\'1Ccould be applied for their personal benefit\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWhat slavery was really about was separating families, about mutilating humans and even raping their wives,\u8221\'20\'1D Scott, the only Black Republican in the \uc2 US Senate\uc2 , told reporters on Thursday after a town hall event in Ankeny, Iowa.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt was just devastating. So I would hope that every person in our country \u8211\'20\'13 and certainly running for president \u8211\'20\'13 would appreciate that.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/jul/28/tim-scott-ron-desantis-florida-slavery-teaching"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Tim Scott criticizes Ron DeSantis for Florida teaching guidelines on slavery}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.19pm BST\par \par \uc2 That said, polls give little indication that the prosecutions of \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  are affecting his standing among Republicans.\par \par \uc2 Glance at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://projects.fivethirtyeight.com/polls/president-primary-r/2024/national/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 aggregator FiveThirtyEight}}}\uc2  and you\u8217\'20\'19ll see the former president remains the campaign\u8217\'20\'19s frontrunner, as he has for months, including before he was {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/mar/30/donald-trump-indicted-stormy-daniels-hush-money"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 first indicted by Manhattan district attorney }}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/mar/30/donald-trump-indicted-stormy-daniels-hush-money"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Alvin Bragg}}}\uc2  . Trump leads the race with 52.4% support, a big improvement from the 43.4% support he was receiving at the start of the year.\par \par \uc2 Despite all his money and endorsements, Florida governor \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2  remains in a distant second place with 15.5% support, and if you look closely, you can see a sharp drop in his poll numbers in the most recent surveys. If there is anything new on this graph, it\u8217\'20\'19s the apparent momentum of first-time candidate \uc2 Vivek Ramaswamy\uc2 , who looks to be heading into a solid third place.\par \par \uc2 As an example, an \uc2 Ohio Northern University\uc2  poll that wrapped up on Wednesday shows him in second place among Republican voters in that state, beating DeSantis:\par \par \uc2 enltr2024 Ohio Republican Primary:\par \par \uc2 Trump 64%\par \par \uc2 Ramaswamy 12%\par \par \uc2 DeSantis 9%\par \par \uc2 Pence 6%\par \par \uc2 Haley 3%\par \par \uc2 Christie 2%\par \par \uc2 Hutchinson 1%\par \par \uc2 Ohio Northern University\uc2 , 7/17-26 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/sn585Hp39P"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/sn585Hp39P}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Political Polls (@Politics_Polls) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/Politics_Polls/status/1684919487076704256?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 July 28, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.53pm BST\par \par \uc2 Despite his bluster, \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  appears to be in serious legal trouble, and all indications point to it getting worse.\par \par \uc2 He has already been indicted by Manhattan district attorney \uc2 Alvin Bragg\uc2  for allegedly falsifying business records in the state, and by special counsel Jack Smith on federal charges related to stashing classified government materials at Mar-a-Lago.\par \par \uc2 But with both Smith and other prosecutors continuing to investigate Trump, don\u8217\'20\'19t be surprised if he finds himself the target of more indictments in the weeks and months to come. To keep track of them all, \uc2 The Guardian\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/joan-greve"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Joan E Greve}}}\uc2  and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/andrew-witherspoon"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Andrew Witherspoon}}}\uc2  have put together this handy explainer:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/jul/18/donald-trump-what-how-many-criminal-charges"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Donald Trump\u8217\'20\'19s legal problems: where does each case stand?}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.33pm BST\par \par \uc2 Trump again says he will not drop out of 2024 race despite new charges\par \par \uc2 In an interview with conservative radio host John Fredericks today, \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  reiterated that he would stay in the presidential race despite the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/jul/27/trump-mar-a-lago-classified-documents-case-carlos-de-oliveira"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 expanding indictment}}}\uc2  against him over the Mar-a-Lago documents:\par \par \uc2 enltrPresident Trump says indictments will never stop his campaign for POTUS!\par \par \uc2 Watch {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/jfradioshow?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @jfradioshow}}}\uc2  exclusive interview with {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/hashtag/PresidentTrump?src=hash&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 #PresidentTrump}}}\uc2  LIVE NOW!\par \par \uc2 Watch LIVE? {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/aeKhZCtVbe"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/aeKhZCtVbe}}}\par \par \uc2 Watch {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/hashtag/AmericanSunrise?src=hash&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 #AmericanSunrise}}}\uc2  with {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/edhenry?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @edhenry}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/mrsflorida2016?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @mrsflorida2016}}}\uc2  & {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/TBatesNews?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @TBatesNews}}}\uc2  ??: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/SGNOcrAlVc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/SGNOcrAlVc}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/HBN8nRayWK"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/HBN8nRayWK}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Real America's Voice (RAV) (@RealAmVoice) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/RealAmVoice/status/1684908152578293760?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 July 28, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 The new charges announced yesterday concern an attempt by Trump to delete surveillance footage of boxes of classified documents being moved out of a room at Mar-a-Lago. In today\u8217\'20\'19s interview, Trump denied any wrongdoing, saying \u8220\'20\'1CThese were security tapes. We handed them over to them\u8221\'20\'1D, according to Reuters.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.16pm BST\par \par \uc2 On CNN, a former federal prosecutor said the new charges against \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  in the Mar-a-Lago case indicate special counsel Jack Smith does not believe the matter will be resolved before the 2024 presidential election.\par \par \uc2 The case is currently set for trial in May 2024, but Renato Mariotti told the network it\u8217\'20\'19s likely to be pushed back:\par \par \uc2 enltr"This is not something you do if you're trying to get this done quickly before the [2024] election."\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Former federal prosecutor Renato Mariotti says superseding indictment in the classified docs case against \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  shows Jack Smith doesn't think he will get a speedy trial {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/336N1fHTHP"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/336N1fHTHP}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 The Recount (@therecount) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/therecount/status/1684916202391404544?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 July 28, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.55pm BST\par \par \uc2 John Bolton\uc2  reiterates call for Trump to end White House campaign\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s one-time national security adviser \uc2 John Bolton\uc2  is now among his many Republican foes. This morning, Bolton reiterated his call for the former president to end his White House campaign after the new charges against him:\par \par \uc2 enltrI called for Trump to end his presidential candidacy after the first Federal indictment and do so again now after the second one. It is more "obstruction of justice as a way of life": Trump's pure selfishness and self-interest - not regard for principle or country. America will\u8230\'20\'26\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 \uc2 John Bolton\uc2  (@AmbJohnBolton) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/AmbJohnBolton/status/1684891589041127424?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 July 28, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 4.50pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.39pm BST\par \par \uc2 As the Guardian\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/hugo-lowell"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Hugo Lowell}}}\uc2  and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/maanvi-singh"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Maanvi Singh}}}\uc2  report, special counsel Jack Smith has both leveled new charges against Trump, and indicted a third person over the secret government materials found at Mar-a-Lago:\par \par \uc2 Federal prosecutors on Thursday expanded the indictment against {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/donaldtrump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Donald Trump}}}\uc2  for retaining national security documents and obstructing the government\u8217\'20\'19s efforts to retrieve them, unveiling new charges against him and an employee over an attempt to destroy surveillance footage.\par \par \uc2 The new charges \u8211\'20\'13 filed by the special counsel Jack Smith in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/florida"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Florida}}}\uc2  \u8211\'20\'13 were outlined in a superseding indictment that named Mar-a-Lago club maintenance worker Carlos De Oliveira as the third co-defendant in the case. Trump\u8217\'20\'19s valet Walt Nauta was previously indicted for obstruction with the former president last month.\par \par \uc2 Trump\u8217\'20\'19s legal exposure in the classified documents case grew after he was accused of attempting to destroy evidence and inducing someone else to destroy evidence, as well as an additional count under the Espionage Act for retaining a classified document about US plans to attack Iran that he discussed on tape at his Bedminster club in New Jersey.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/jul/27/trump-mar-a-lago-classified-documents-case-carlos-de-oliveira"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Trump faces more charges in classified documents case as second aide named}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.22pm BST\par \par \uc2 Former Trump lawyer says evidence 'overwhelming' in Mar-a-Lago case\par \par \uc2 A former lawyer for \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  who represented him in an earlier special counsel investigation has warned that the evidence revealed by Jack Smith in the Mar-a-Lago case is \u8220\'20\'1Coverwhelming\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Ty Cobb\uc2  represented Trump during a period early in his presidency when he was being investigated by special counsel \uc2 Robert Mueller\uc2  for alleged ties to Russia, which ultimately did not amount to the type of scandal the then-president\u8217\'20\'19s detractors hoped would sink his administration.\par \par \uc2 But Cobb told CNN today that the charges in the Mar-a-Lago case brought by Smith, who was named a special counsel last year, are different. \uc2 The Guardian\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/martin-pengelly"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Martin Pengelly}}}\uc2  reports on why:\par \par \uc2 A former Trump White House lawyer said the evidence against the former president over his handling of classified documents was now \u8220\'20\'1Coverwhelming\u8221\'20\'1D and would \u8220\'20\'1Clast an antiquity\u8221\'20\'1D, after {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/jul/27/trump-mar-a-lago-classified-documents-case-carlos-de-oliveira"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 new charges were filed}}}\uc2  in the case on Thursday.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI think this original indictment was engineered to last a thousand years and now this superseding indictment will last an antiquity,\u8221\'20\'1D \uc2 Ty Cobb\uc2  told CNN. \u8220\'20\'1CThis is such a tight case, the evidence is so overwhelming.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 In June, the special counsel Jack Smith {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/jun/09/trump-indictment-what-does-it-mean-what-happens-next-explainer-charges"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 indicted}}}\uc2  Trump on 37 counts regarding his handling of classified records after leaving the White House.\par \par \uc2 On Thursday, in a superseding indictment filed in a Florida court, four more charges were outlined. A second Trump staffer, the Mar-a-Lago maintenance worker Carlos De Oliveira, was charged, alongside Walt Nauta, Trump\u8217\'20\'19s valet. Nauta previously pleaded {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/jul/06/trump-valet-walt-nauta-not-guilty-arraignment-mar-a-lago"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 not guilty}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/jul/28/trump-lawyer-charges-1000-years-mar-a-lago"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Ex-Trump lawyer says evidence against him \u8216\'20\'18overwhelming\u8217\'20\'19 in Mar-a-Lago case}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.02pm BST\par \par \uc2 Trump legal peril increases with new charges\par \par \uc2 Good morning, US politics blog readers. \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  is squarely in the cross hairs of federal prosecutors, who yesterday {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/jul/27/trump-mar-a-lago-classified-documents-case-carlos-de-oliveira"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 added new charges}}}\uc2  to the indictment brought against him in June for allegedly hiding classified documents at his Mar-a-Lago resort. It is also possible that today, special counsel Jack Smith will unveil a new indictment against the former president related to his actions on January 6. Last week, Trump said he had received a letter formally telling him he was a target in the investigation and yesterday, his lawyers attended a meeting at Smith\u8217\'20\'19s offices \u8211\'20\'13 both signs that an indictment could be near.\par \par \uc2 No former president has faced the sort of legal problems Trump is in, but there are also no signs yet that they\u8217\'20\'19ve dented his standing among Republicans. He continues to lead polls among the party\u8217\'20\'19s presidential candidates, and plans to spend this weekend rallying supporters in Erie, Pennsylvania. We\u8217\'20\'19ll see if Washington has anything to say about the ongoing investigations against him today.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s what else is happening:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Congress has left town for its summer break, but only after the Senate passed a version of a crucial defense funding bill without the contentious provisions over \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , transgender care and other culture ware issues that the House inserted in its version. This legislation must pass, and expect a big fight over it when lawmakers get back to work in September.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 All the main Republican candidates, including Trump, \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2 , Tim Scott and \uc2 Mike Pence\uc2  will this evening speak at the Iowa GOP\u8217\'20\'19s Lincoln Dinner.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  is heading up to Maine to promote his economic record, before flying to Delaware for a weekend on the beach.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020230728ej7s001ux\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
FF
