\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Republicans target  \highlight22\uc2 abortion \highlight\uc2  pill access as government shutdown threat looms\b0\par\par\uc2 Nick Robins-Early \par \uc2 799 \uc2 words\par \uc2 25 July 2023\par 18:34 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 House GOP seeks to end availability of mifepristone by mail and cut billions in low-income food benefits as part of budget fight\par \par \uc2 A Republican-backed spending bill threatens to end national access to mail-order \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  pills and cut billions from the Supplemental Nutrition Assistance Program (Snap) that provides low-income families with food benefits.\par \par \uc2 The legislation is part of a spate of appropriations bills that lawmakers will debate this month, and which Congress must reach a decision on by the end of September in order to pass a budget for the 2024 fiscal year and avoid a federal shutdown. It was {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.axios.com/2023/05/19/house-fda-funding-abortion-tobacco"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 already approved}}}\uc2  by a House appropriations subcommittee in May, while being condemned by Democrats and causing internal rifts among Republicans. Republicans have added several provisions to the bill that would have wide-ranging effects on reproductive rights, health policy and benefits.\par \par \uc2 The food and agriculture spending bill is the latest front in the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2023/apr/30/republicans-divided-abortion-democrats-united-2024-election"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 rightwing campaign}}}\uc2  against reproductive rights. In the year since the supreme court overturned Roe v Wade, Republicans have passed bills in more than a dozen states that ban or severely restrict \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access. Ending access to mail-order pills that induce abortions {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.washingtonpost.com/politics/2023/07/19/doctors-northeast-launch-abortion-pill-pipeline-into-states-with-bans/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 would complicate and limit efforts}}}\uc2  from \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights groups and physicians to provide care for people in states with \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  bans.\par \par \uc2 Specifically, the bill would reverse a 2021 Food and Drug Administration policy that allowed people to get the \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 -inducing drug mifepristone \u8211\'20\'13 which can be used up to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.kff.org/womens-health-policy/fact-sheet/the-availability-and-use-of-medication-abortion/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 10 weeks}}}\uc2  after conception \u8211\'20\'13 through the mail rather than via in-person visits to providers. The \uc2 FDA\uc2  had temporarily lifted restrictions on the drug during the Covid-19 pandemic, before later {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/2021/12/16/health/abortion-pills-fda.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 making those changes permanent}}}\uc2 . But the drug, which is widely used for {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.npr.org/2023/04/10/1169033855/abortion-pill-mifepristone-ruling"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  and can also be used for managing miscarriages}}}\uc2 , has been the center of legal challenges and rightwing attempts to prevent its use ever since.\par \par \uc2 House Republicans\u8217\'20\'19 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://appropriations.house.gov/sites/republicans.appropriations.house.gov/files/documents/FY24%20Agriculture%2C%20Rural%20Development%2C%20Food%20and%20Drug%20Administration%2C%20and%20Related%20Agencies%20-%20Bill%20Summary_0.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 messaging on the bill}}}\uc2  claims that their provision \u8220\'20\'1Creins in wasteful Washington spending\u8221\'20\'1D and \u8220\'20\'1Cprotects the lives of unborn children\u8221\'20\'1D. The bill would also decrease the Snap benefit program \u8211\'20\'13 formerly known as food stamps \u8211\'20\'13 by $32bn compared with 2023 levels, as well as prevent the health and human services department from putting limits on the maximum amount of nicotine in cigarettes.\par \par \uc2 The approaching fight over spending bills has echoes of the standoff over {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.washingtonpost.com/business/2023/05/25/debt-ceiling-no-deal/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 debt ceiling negotiations}}}\uc2  earlier this year, when Democrats accused Republicans of holding the government hostage in an attempt to exact sweeping cuts to federal programs. Hardline Republicans similarly pushed to shift their party towards far-right policies during those negotiations as well.\par \par \uc2 Democrats are eager to prevent a government shutdown such as the one in 2018 during the Trump administration that left about 800,000 government workers without pay and lasted longer than any previous closure in US history. But {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://rollcall.com/2023/07/18/house-democrats-look-for-lines-in-the-sand-on-farm-bill/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 some have called for establishing red lines}}}\uc2  around what compromises they are willing to make, with a number of House Democrats such as the Massachusetts representative \uc2 Jim McGovern\uc2  pushing back against attempts to cut Snap funding and other conservative provisions in recent legislation. House Democrats previously {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.axios.com/pro/health-care-policy/2023/06/14/house-appropriations-fda-bill"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 tried to add two amendments}}}\uc2  to the food and agriculture spending bill that would have eliminated the anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  provision, but both failed.\par \par \uc2 Several Republicans have also spoken out against the food and agriculture bill, including the New York representative \uc2 Marc Molinaro\uc2 , {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.politico.com/news/2023/07/24/health-policy-bill-gop-00107455"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 who told Politico}}}\uc2  he will vote against the legislation if it comes to the floor. Molinaro, along with another New York Republican lawmaker, previously denounced a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/2023/04/07/health/abortion-pills-ruling-texas.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 conservative Texas judge\u8217\'20\'19s ruling}}}\uc2  that threatened to remove \uc2 FDA\uc2  approval of mifepristone.\par \par \uc2 Molinaro\u8217\'20\'19s opposition to the bill highlights a rift within the Republican party over just how far to push an anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  agenda that has {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/jun/24/republicans-abortion-electoral-backlash-roe-v-wade"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 proven nationally unpopular}}}\uc2  and contributed to electoral losses in many states.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  policy has divided the GOP as hard-right Republicans, as well as powerful Christian conservative activist groups, have demanded far-reaching bans on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access. Others, such as the South Carolina Republican Nancy Mace, have warned that Republicans need to \u8220\'20\'1Cread the room\u8221\'20\'1D on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  or face defeat in elections.\par \par \uc2 The Republican speaker of the House, Kevin McCarthy, has meanwhile been left scrambling to manage the different factions of his party as votes on must-pass appropriations bills loom. In addition to limiting \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access and benefits, far-right Republicans have {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/2023/07/12/us/politics/defense-bill-republicans-ukraine-war.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 sought to use spending bills to greatly reduce}}}\uc2  military aid to Ukraine in its fight against the Russian invasion.\par \par \uc2 An {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.npr.org/2023/04/26/1171863775/poll-americans-want-abortion-restrictions-but-not-as-far-as-red-states-are-going"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 NPR/PBS NewsHour/Marist poll}}}\uc2  from earlier this year saw that support for \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access was at an all-time high, and included a finding that about one-third of Republicans also broadly back the right to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020230725ej7p002e9\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
