\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Iowa Republicans pass six-week  \highlight22\uc2 abortion \highlight\uc2  ban\b0\par\par\uc2 Nick Robins-Early and agencies \par \uc2 689 \uc2 words\par \uc2 25 July 2023\par 15:31 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Legislation is latest in raft of anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  laws passed in states across the country since supreme court overturned Roe v Wade\par \par \uc2 Iowa\u8217\'20\'19s state legislature voted on Tuesday night to ban most abortions after around six weeks of pregnancy, a time before most people know they are pregnant.\par \par \uc2 Republican lawmakers, which hold a majority in both the Iowa house and senate, passed the anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  bill after the governor, \uc2 Kim Reynolds\uc2 , called a special session to seek a vote on the ban.\par \par \uc2 The bill passed with exclusively Republican support in a rare, one-day legislative burst lasting more than 14 hours.\par \par \uc2 The legislation will take immediate effect after the governor signs it on Friday and will prohibit abortions after the first sign of cardiac activity \u8211\'20\'13 usually around six weeks, with some exceptions for cases of rape or incest. It will allow for abortions up until 20 weeks of pregnancy only under certain conditions of medical emergency. Abortions in the state were previously allowed up to 20 weeks.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe Iowa supreme court questioned whether this legislature would pass the same law they did in 2018, and today they have a clear answer,\u8221\'20\'1D Reynolds said in a statement. \u8220\'20\'1CThe voices of Iowans and their democratically elected representatives cannot be ignored any longer, and justice for the unborn should not be delayed.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The legislation is the latest in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/interactive/2022/us/abortion-laws-roe-v-wade.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a raft of anti-\b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  laws}}}\uc2  passed in states across the country since the supreme court overturned Roe v Wade last year, ending the nationwide constitutional right to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 . A number of states, including a swath of the southern US, have passed full bans on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  without exceptions for cases of rape or incest.\par \par \uc2 Preparations were already under way to quickly file legal challenges in court and get the measure blocked, once Reynolds signs it into law.\par \par \uc2 A similar six-week ban that the legislature passed in 2018 was blocked by the state\u8217\'20\'19s supreme court one year later. Since that decision, however, Roe has been overturned and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://apnews.com/article/abortion-health-iowa-supreme-court-government-and-politics-0074e14defa4a6699e65d921f0edbc58"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a more conservative court ruled}}}\uc2  that \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  is no longer a constitutionally protected right in Iowa. The court was split 3-3 last month on whether to remove the block on the 2018 law, a deadlock which resulted in Reynolds seeking to pass new legislation in a special session this week.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe ACLU of Iowa, \uc2 Planned Parenthood\uc2  and the Emma Goldman Clinic remain committed to protecting the reproductive rights of Iowans to control their bodies and their lives, their health and their safety \u8211\'20\'13 including filing a lawsuit to block this reckless, cruel law,\u8221\'20\'1D the ACLU of Iowa\u8217\'20\'19s executive director, Mark Stringer, said in a statement.\par \par \uc2 In the meantime, Planned Parenthood North Central States has said it will refer patients out of state if they\u8217\'20\'19re scheduled for abortions in the next few weeks. The organization, the largest \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  provider in the state, will continue to provide care to patients who present before cardiac activity is detected.\par \par \uc2 As state lawmakers debated the bill, crowds of protesters gathered in the capitol rotunda in support of reproductive rights and chanted \u8220\'20\'1Cvote them out\u8221\'20\'1D at Republican legislators. A Des Moines Register/Mediacom Iowa {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.desmoinesregister.com/story/news/politics/iowa-poll/2022/10/23/iowa-poll-abortion-laws-fetal-heartbeat-ban-roe-v-wade/69563125007/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 survey from last year}}}\uc2  showed that around 61% of Iowans were generally in favor of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access, a number that tracks with nationwide beliefs about the right to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 During a public hearing on Tuesday before the vote, lawmakers heard from advocates both for and against the bill who gave brief statements in the chambers. A range of medical professionals and reproductive rights activists urged the legislature to reconsider the bill, warning that it would cause immense societal harm, reduce bodily autonomy and prevent physicians from caring for patients.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CYou would be forcing a woman to a lifelong obligation which affects her education, career, family and community,\u8221\'20\'1D Amy Bingaman, an obstetrician and gynecologist, told lawmakers.\par \par \uc2 Advocates of the bill, many from Christian organizations and hardline anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  activist groups, thanked lawmakers during the hearing and touted the bill as a victory for their movement.\par \par \uc2 The Associated Press contributed to this report\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020230725ej7p00290\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
