\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Tearful Texas doctor recalls being forced to travel out of state for  \highlight22\uc2 abortion \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 Maya Yang \par \uc2 1,026 \uc2 words\par \uc2 21 July 2023\par 12:55 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Austin Dennard unable to obtain \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  in home state because of confusion surrounding exceptions under restrictive Texas ban\par \par \uc2 Emotional testimonies from women and doctors continued into the second day of court hearings on the confusion surrounding exceptions under Texas\u8217\'20\'19s restrictive \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban.\par \par \uc2 On Thursday, Austin Dennard, an OB-GYN doctor herself, delivered a tearful testimony as she recounted her experiences of being forced to travel out of state for an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  due to a nonviable pregnancy.\par \par \uc2 Eleven weeks into the pregnancy last year, Dennard, who is pregnant again, learned that her baby had anencephaly, a rare and fatal condition affecting the development of the brain and can also pose a serious health risk to the mother. Explaining the condition, Dennard {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/ReproRights/status/1682106656975384578?s=20"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  said}}}\uc2  that babies \u8220\'20\'1Csurvive seconds, minutes \u8230\'20\'26 maybe a day. They essentially struggle for air until they pass away.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Due to a cardiac heartbeat, Dennard was unable to obtain an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  in Texas and thus had to look elsewhere for an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI felt like my pregnancy was not my own, that it belonged to the state, because I no longer had a choice of what I could do. I felt abandoned. I couldn\u8217\'20\'19t believe that after spending my entire life in the state, being a sixth generation Texan, practicing medicine in the state, that the state had completely turned their back on me,\u8221\'20\'1D Dennard said.\par \par \uc2 She went on to describe her experience of obtaining an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  out of state, which she described as \u8220\'20\'1Cvery safe\u8221\'20\'1D and \u8220\'20\'1Clasted no more than 10 minutes\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI was able to walk out of that clinic and get on an airplane and come home, which I feel very lucky for, but emotionally, the \u8230\'20\'26 recovery is quite longer. As I\u8217\'20\'19m sure everyone can tell from listening to the plaintiffs, that grief really never goes away,\u8221\'20\'1D Dennard testified as she wept.\par \par \uc2 Upon being asked whether she considered going public with her story earlier, Dennard said: \u8220\'20\'1CI did. At first, my husband and I thought about it.\u8221\'20\'1D However, she later decided against it out of \u8220\'20\'1Cfear that our professional careers \u8230\'20\'26 and that the safety of my family could be compromised.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CFrankly, I think so soon after the \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , I was in a very fragile state, more fragile than I am now, and I don\u8217\'20\'19t think I was ready to risk putting myself out there for fear that some really bad things could happen as a repercussion.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Nevertheless, Dennard explained her ultimate decision to join more than a dozen women in the lawsuit filed on behalf of them by the \uc2 Center for Reproductive Rights\uc2  against the state. The lawsuit, which does not seek to repeal Texas\u8217\'20\'19s highly restrictive \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  laws, is seeking clarification on which situations fall under the \u8220\'20\'1Cmedical emergency\u8221\'20\'1D exception in Texas\u8217\'20\'19s \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  bans.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CJoining this lawsuit, I feel, has been a wonderfully productive way to try to make change for the women in Texas so that we can help each other regain the rights that we deserve for our bodies,\u8221\'20\'1D said Dennard.\par \par \uc2 Dennard\u8217\'20\'19s appearance follows {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/jul/20/texas-women-pregnancy-abortion-ban"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 testimonies}}}\uc2  from three other women on Wednesday who each described their own harrowing experiences of being denied abortions in the state despite their life-threatening pregnancies.\par \par \uc2 In another testimony on Thursday, Ali Raja, an emergency medicine physician at Massachusetts general hospital, described the confusing language surrounding exceptions under Texas\u8217\'20\'19s \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  bans.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CMy opinion is that the laws as they\u8217\'20\'19re currently written \u8211\'20\'13 the medical exceptions \u8211\'20\'13 they\u8217\'20\'19re confusing and that confusion and lack of clarity is keeping physicians from being able to exercise their good faith judgment in the treatment of patients,\u8221\'20\'1D Raja {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://abcnews.go.com/US/doctors-testify-confusion-surrounding-texas-abortion-bans/story?id=101521408"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 said.}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt \u8230\'20\'26 is pretty evident that the fact is that the consequences of those laws are severe personally to the physicians themselves. And as a consequence of that \u8230\'20\'26 in patients where there is a gray zone and there\u8217\'20\'19s a lack of clarity, they are going to err on the side of not treating,\u8221\'20\'1D he added.\par \par \uc2 Following Thursday\u8217\'20\'19s hearing, one of CRR\u8217\'20\'19s attorneys, Nick Kabat, told the Guardian \u8220\'20\'1Cthere wasn\u8217\'20\'19t a dry eye in the courtroom\u8221\'20\'1D during the harrowing testimonies.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWhat this \u8230\'20\'26 demonstrated is that Texas\u8217\'20\'19s \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  bans are harming women across the state. The state [is] trying to tie [doctors\u8217\'20\'19] hands and stop them from providing the care that they were trained to do,\u8221\'20\'1D Kabat added.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe fight has begun and we want people to be aware that these things are happening and we\u8217\'20\'19re not going to shut up about it until something is done about it,\u8221\'20\'1D he said.\par \par \uc2 Speaking to the Guardian, Angela Vasquez-Giroux, vice-president of communications and research at Naral Pro-Choice America, one of the country\u8217\'20\'19s largest reproductive rights organizations, said that to her, the biggest takeaway is that \u8220\'20\'1Cnone of this had to happen\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CEvery single thing that every one of these women in the lawsuit and testifying these last few days have experienced and told us about \u8211\'20\'13 it\u8217\'20\'19s a direct result of the policies that were written and passed and are now being enforced by Republicans in Texas. These are also the blueprint for the horrific laws that we\u8217\'20\'19re seeing passed and being enforced around the country,\u8221\'20\'1D Vasquez-Giroux said.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s cruel, it\u8217\'20\'19s inhumane and it\u8217\'20\'19s state-sanctioned and state-enforced torture, having to wait until you\u8217\'20\'19re almost dead to get basic treatment. It\u8217\'20\'19s inexcusable,\u8221\'20\'1D she added.\par \par \uc2 Vasquez-Giroux also pushed back against one of the state\u8217\'20\'19s attorneys who {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/jul/20/texas-women-pregnancy-abortion-ban"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  said}}}\uc2  the lawsuit stems merely from the notion that the women \u8220\'20\'1Csimply do not like Texas\u8217\'20\'19s restrictions on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 \u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CNumerically, she\u8217\'20\'19s correct. Eighty per cent of people do not like these restrictions on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  \u8230\'20\'26 but really, this is another facet of the desperation and the underhandedness of the Republican party and anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  extremists.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThey see someone who has suffered so much trying to build their family and carry to term a child they desperately wanted and their answer is, \u8216\'20\'18You just don\u8217\'20\'19t like me,\u8217\'20\'19 like that\u8217\'20\'19s their takeaway. That\u8217\'20\'19s sickening and pathetic.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020230721ej7l000xq\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
