\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Supreme court ethics: Senate committee approves new rules as fresh \uc2 Clarence Thomas\uc2  claims emerge \u8211\'20\'13 as it happened\b0\par\par\uc2 L\u233\'00\'E9onie Chao-Fong (now) and Gloria Oladipo (earlier) \par \uc2 7,012 \uc2 words\par \uc2 20 July 2023\par 20:10 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Rules passed along party lines; conservative nonprofits reportedly orchestrated a $1.8m PR campaign to defend supreme court justice\u8226\'20\'22 This blog is now closed. To read more about \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  click here\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.00pm BST\par \par \uc2 Summary of the day\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s a recap of today\u8217\'20\'19s developments:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  faced a deadline of midnight on Thursday to say if he would appear before a Washington grand jury convened by the special counsel Jack Smith to consider federal charges over his election subversion and incitement of the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/jan/09/us-capitol-insurrection-white-supremacist-terror"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 attack on Congress}}}\uc2  on 6 January 2021.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Prosecutors had assembled evidence to charge Trump with three crimes, the Guardian {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/jul/19/trump-investigation-three-federal-crimes-january-6"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reported }}}\uc2  late on Wednesday, citing two people familiar with the matter. They were: obstruction of an official proceeding, conspiracy to defraud the United States, and an unusual statute that makes it unlawful to conspire to violate civil rights.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 A federal grand jury investigating Trump\u8217\'20\'19s efforts to overturn the 2020 election has heard testimony from an aide who was with the former president for much of the day on 6 January 2021. William Russell was asked to appear on Thursday after making previous grand jury appearances. A data expert who worked on the 2020 election was {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/jul/20/trump-testimony-january-6-case-biden-epa-us-politics-live?page=with:block-64b9852d8f087edb1f3ee8f1#block-64b9852d8f087edb1f3ee8f1"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 also reportedly scheduled}}}\uc2  to appear before a grand jury.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 House speaker Kevin McCarthy has denied he privately promised Trump that he would get legislation passed that would erase Trump\u8217\'20\'19s two impeachments. According to a Politico report, in return for delaying an endorsement for Trump\u8217\'20\'19s 2024 president election, McCarthy {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/jul/20/trump-testimony-january-6-case-biden-epa-us-politics-live?page=with:block-64b94bed8f081d44d14a5671#block-64b94bed8f081d44d14a5671"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pledged that he would get the House to vote}}}\uc2  to expunge both impeachments against the former president. The outlet said McCarthy had promised to do so before Congress leaves for an August recess.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The Democratic-led Senate judiciary committee voted to advance a supreme court ethics reform bill that would tighten financial disclosures and bolster recusal requirements for justices. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/jul/20/trump-testimony-january-6-case-biden-epa-us-politics-live?page=with:block-64b981d68f087edb1f3ee8db#block-64b981d68f087edb1f3ee8db"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 The vote}}}\uc2  was along party lines, with Republicans adamantly opposed. The panel vote came after months of scrutiny on the court over {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/law/2023/jul/12/us-supreme-court-justices-ethics-rules-controversy-explain"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 ethical controversies}}}\uc2  supreme court justices have been involved in.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Conservative non-profit groups steered by the rightwing legal activist, \uc2 Leonard Leo\uc2 , {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/jul/20/trump-testimony-january-6-case-biden-epa-us-politics-live?page=with:block-64b954168f081d44d14a56f5#block-64b954168f081d44d14a56f5"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reportedly orchestrated}}}\uc2  a $1.8m public relations campaign to defend and celebrate supreme court justice, \uc2 Clarence Thomas\uc2 , after he faced renewed scrutiny over his past misconduct claims.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Democratic presidential candidate \uc2 Robert F Kennedy Jr{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/jul/20/trump-testimony-january-6-case-biden-epa-us-politics-live?page=with:block-64b958f78f08ff360bcb1615#block-64b958f78f08ff360bcb1615"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 defended himself}}}\uc2  against accusations of racism and antisemitism at a hearing on alleged \u8220\'20\'1Cweaponization\u8221\'20\'1D of the federal government. Kennedy {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/jul/17/robert-f-kennedy-jr-covid-condemned"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 provoked anger }}}\uc2  last week when he was filmed falsely suggesting that the coronavirus could have been \u8220\'20\'1Cethnically targeted\u8221\'20\'1D to spare Ashkenazi Jews and Chinese people. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/jul/17/robert-f-kennedy-jr-covid-condemned"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 A report seen by the Guardian }}}\uc2  said Kennedy has a long history of racism, antisemitism and xenophobia.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 9.02pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.53pm BST\par \par \uc2 Florida Governor \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2  backed Senator Tommy Tuberville\u8217\'20\'19s months-long blockade on military nominations over the Pentagon\u8217\'20\'19s \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  policy, saying that the policy would \u8220\'20\'1Cgo out the window\u8221\'20\'1D if he became president.\par \par \uc2 Asked by radio host \uc2 Hugh Hewitt\uc2  if he thinks Tuberville should release his hold, DeSantis replied: \u8220\'20\'1CNo I don\u8217\'20\'19t.\u8221\'20\'1D He added:\par \par \uc2 The military\u8217\'20\'19s policy is not following US law. They are using tax dollars. They\u8217\'20\'19re funding \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  tourism, which is not an appropriate thing for the military to be doing.\par \par \uc2 He said:\par \par \uc2 Day one as commander-in-chief, that policy will go out the window.\par \par \uc2 Tuberville, the Republican senator for Alabama, mounted his obstruction effort earlier this year. He is seeking the end of \uc2 Department of Defense\uc2  policy that provides paid time off and covers travel costs for servicewomen and dependents in need of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  services.\par \par \uc2 Tuberville\u8217\'20\'19s blockade has so far impacted nearly 300 military promotions, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://thehill.com/homenews/senate/4107551-desantis-backs-tubervilles-military-holds/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 according }}}\uc2  to the Hill. The Pentagon has said more than 650 leadership positions could be vacant by the end of the year.\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  and the US defense secretary, \uc2 Lloyd Austin\uc2 , said last week that the senator\u8217\'20\'19s hold is {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/jul/13/pentagon-chief-republian-senator-tommy-tuberville"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 jeopardising US national security.}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.38pm BST\par \par \uc2 Texas women who were denied abortions took the stand and delivered harrowing testimonies of their experiences of carrying life-threatening pregnancies as a result of the state\u8217\'20\'19s highly restrictive \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  laws.\par \par \uc2 The women are part of a lawsuit filed in March by the \uc2 Center for Reproductive Rights\uc2 , which is seeking clarification on which situations fall under the \u8220\'20\'1Cmedical emergency\u8221\'20\'1D exception in Texas\u8217\'20\'19s \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  bans. The lawsuit appears to be the first of its kind where women who were denied abortions are suing a state since the supreme court overturned Roe v Wade last year.\par \par \uc2 During Wednesday\u8217\'20\'19s hearing, plaintiff Samantha Casiano delivered an emotional testimony about being forced to give birth to a baby who died four hours later as a result of a fatal birth defect.\par \par \uc2 Twenty weeks into her pregnancy, Casiano discovered that her baby had anencephaly, a rare condition in which parts of the baby\u8217\'20\'19s skull and brain are missing. Casiano said that doctors informed her that they were unable to perform an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the state and that she was instead given funeral home information.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI felt like I was abandoned,\u8221\'20\'1D Casiano said.\par \par \uc2 I had this funeral home paper and this is just supposed to be a scan day.\par \par \uc2 Casiano went on to describe her thought processes upon learning about her baby\u8217\'20\'19s defect, telling the court that she considered getting an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  out of state but was also afraid of losing her job or being jailed. She said:\par \par \uc2 I felt like I was imprisoned in my own body.\par \par \uc2 At one point, as Casiano read aloud a doctor\u8217\'20\'19s note about her high-risk pregnancy, she became overwhelmed and vomited during the hearing. Following a recess, Casiano returned to the stand and said that recalling the events \u8220\'20\'1Cjust makes my body remember, and it just reacts\u8221\'20\'1D. She added:\par \par \uc2 I now have a psychiatrist \u8230\'20\'26 I now vomit a lot more. I\u8217\'20\'19ve never vomited before like that, ever, before my pregnancy. My body\u8217\'20\'19s never reacted that way.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/jul/20/texas-women-pregnancy-abortion-ban"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Read the full story here.}}}\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/jul/20/texas-women-pregnancy-abortion-ban"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Texas women give harrowing testimony on impact of extreme \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  ban}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 8.46pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.22pm BST\par \par \uc2 Stanley Woodward, a lawyer representing {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/jul/20/trump-testimony-january-6-case-biden-epa-us-politics-live?page=with:block-64b9852d8f087edb1f3ee8f1#block-64b9852d8f087edb1f3ee8f1"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  Trump aide }}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/jul/20/trump-testimony-january-6-case-biden-epa-us-politics-live?page=with:block-64b9852d8f087edb1f3ee8f1#block-64b9852d8f087edb1f3ee8f1"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 William Russell}}}\uc2 , told a judge he was delayed because his client \u8211\'20\'13 who he didn\u8217\'20\'19t name \u8211\'20\'13 was being asked questions before a grand jury that involved questions of executive privilege.\par \par \uc2 From Politico\u8217\'20\'19s Kyle Cheney:\par \par \uc2 enltrNOTABLE: Woodward was reluctant to reveal this in open court. McFadden asked him if that was due to grand jury secrecy rules. And Woodward said yes.\par \par \uc2 McFadden then said he would absolve Woodward of any secrecy requirements so he could explain his belated appearance.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Kyle Cheney (@kyledcheney) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/kyledcheney/status/1682097712743735297?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 July 20, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 8.31pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.10pm BST\par \par \uc2 A federal grand jury investigating \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s efforts to overturn the 2020 election is hearing testimony from an aide who was with the former president for much of the day on 6 January 2021.\par \par \uc2 William Russell, a former White House aide who continued to work for Trump after he left office, was at a federal courthouse in Washington to testify before the grand jury convened by special counsel Jack Smith.\par \par \uc2 Russell was asked to appear on Thursday after making previous grand jury appearances, the \uc2 Washington Post{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.washingtonpost.com/national-security/2023/07/20/former-aide-expected-before-grand-jury-trump-faces-possible-charges/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reported}}}\uc2 . According to the paper, a data expert who worked on the 2020 election was also scheduled to appear before a grand jury.\par \par \uc2 In addition, Smith\u8217\'20\'19s team are reportedly in the process of scheduling a grand jury appearance by Bernard Kerik, a former New York city police commissioner who worked with Trump attorney \uc2 Rudy Giuliani\uc2  in the effort to overturn the election results.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.54pm BST\par \par \uc2 Senate committee approves new supreme court ethics rules\par \par \uc2 The Democratic-led Senate judiciary committee voted to advance a supreme court ethics reform bill that would tighten financial disclosures and bolster recusal requirements for justices.\par \par \uc2 The vote, championed by Senate judiciary chair Dick Durbin and Senator Sheldon Whitehouse, was 11-10 along party lines, with Republicans adamantly opposed.\par \par \uc2 The bill would demand the court create a code within 180 days and establish rules on recusals related to potential conflicts of interest and disclosure of gifts and travel.\par \par \uc2 The legislation has little chance to make it through the full Senate and in a divided Congress.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.35pm BST\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/jul/18/donald-trump-what-how-many-criminal-charges"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Donald Trump\u8217\'20\'19s court dates}}}\uc2  are set to clash with the Republican primary calendar. The former president faces three civil trials in New York, one to begin in October and two in January.\par \par \uc2 The clash is raising extraordinary and unprecedented questions about the logistical, legal and political challenges of various trials unfolding against the backdrop of a presidential campaign, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/2023/07/20/us/politics/trump-trials-2024-campaign.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 according}}}\uc2  to the \uc2 New York Times\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The paper cites Bruce Green, a \uc2 Fordham University\uc2  professor and former prosecutor, as saying:\par \par \uc2 The courts will have to decide how to balance the public interest in having expeditious trials against Trump\u8217\'20\'19s interest and the public interest in his being able to campaign so that the democratic process works. That\u8217\'20\'19s a type of complexity that courts have never had to deal with before.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.22pm BST\par \par \uc2 In polling averages for the Republican primary, \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  leads by {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://projects.fivethirtyeight.com/polls/president-primary-r/2024/national/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 about 30 points}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 He has maintained that lead {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/jul/18/donald-trump-what-how-many-criminal-charges"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 even while facing}}}\uc2  34 criminal charges in New York, over hush-money payments to the porn star Stormy Daniels ; 37 federal charges over his retention of classified documents; the prospect of state and federal indictments over his election subversion; a $5m fine after being held liable for sexual abuse and defamation against the writer E Jean Carroll; and ongoing investigations of his business affairs. Denying all wrongdoing, Trump has pleaded not guilty to all criminal charges.\par \par \uc2 Nonetheless, polling regarding a notional general election {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.realclearpolitics.com/epolls/2024/president/us/general_election_desantis_vs_biden-7967.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 shows}}}\uc2  him in a close race with \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 . Earlier this week, Miles Taylor, who was a US homeland security official when in 2018 he wrote a famous anonymous \uc2 New York Times\uc2  column warning of Trump\u8217\'20\'19s unfitness for office, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/books/2023/jul/18/miles-taylor-whistleblower-trump-biden-interview"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 told the Guardian}}}\uc2  Trump could yet return to the White House.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThere\u8217\'20\'19s been a number of polls that show the ex-president beating \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  by several points,\u8221\'20\'1D Taylor {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/books/2023/jul/18/miles-taylor-whistleblower-trump-biden-interview"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 said}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 It would be hubris to say, \u8216\'20\'18Oh, no, we would beat him again a second time.\u8217\'20\'19 Actually, I don\u8217\'20\'19t think that. If the election was held today, I think \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  would defeat \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 , and that really concerns me.\par \par \uc2 Taylor also pointed to the supine nature of the Republican party, saying McCarthy, the House speaker, \u8220\'20\'1Cthought Trump was a buffoon and a danger and I\u8217\'20\'19m sure Kevin still thinks that privately\u8221\'20\'1D but is unwilling, or unable, to move in any way against him. Taylor said:\par \par \uc2 Those people publicly, because they\u8217\'20\'19re afraid, are still supporting the man. That collective anonymity is putting us in pretty seriously great danger.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.18pm BST\par \par \uc2 House speaker Kevin McCarthy privately promised \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  to hold a vote on expunging the former president\u8217\'20\'19s two impeachments, the first in 2019 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/trump-impeachment"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 for withholding}}}\uc2  military aid in an attempt to extract political dirt from Ukraine, the second {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/trump-impeachment-2021"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 for inciting}}}\uc2  the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/us-capitol-breach"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Capitol attack}}}\uc2 , Politico {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.politico.com/playbook"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reported}}}\uc2  on this morning.\par \par \uc2 But a vote to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/jul/20/trump-testimony-january-6-case-biden-epa-us-politics-live?filterKeyEvents=false&page=with:block-64b94bed8f081d44d14a5671#block-64b94bed8f081d44d14a5671"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 expunge Trump\u8217\'20\'19s impeachments }}}\uc2  would not be guaranteed to succeed.\par \par \uc2 Republicans control the House {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://about.bgov.com/brief/balance-of-power-republican-majority-in-the-house/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 by a very slim majority}}}\uc2 . Two sitting GOP congressmen, D avid Valadao of California and \uc2 Dan Newhouse\uc2  of Washington state, voted to impeach Trump over the Capitol riot. Republicans in swing districts, particularly in heavily Democratic north-eastern states, already face uphill fights to keep their seats.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.06pm BST\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  faced a deadline of midnight on Thursday to say if he would appear before a Washington grand jury convened by the special counsel Jack Smith to consider federal charges over his election subversion and incitement of the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/jan/09/us-capitol-insurrection-white-supremacist-terror"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 attack on Congress}}}\uc2  on 6 January 2021.\par \par \uc2 Late on Wednesday, citing two people familiar with the matter, the \uc2 Guardian{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/jul/19/trump-investigation-three-federal-crimes-january-6"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reported}}}\uc2  that prosecutors had assembled evidence to charge Trump with three crimes.\par \par \uc2 They were: obstruction of an official proceeding, conspiracy to defraud the United States, and an unusual statute that makes it unlawful to conspire to violate civil rights.\par \par \uc2 Obstruction of an official proceeding is {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/2023/07/18/us/politics/target-letter-trump-obstruction-fraud-charges.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 punishable}}}\uc2  by up to 20 years in prison. Conspiracy to defraud the United States carries a maximum five-year sentence. The civil rights charge is {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.justice.gov/crt/statutes-enforced-criminal-section#:~:text=A%20conviction%20carries%20a%20statutory,of%20years%20or%20for%20life."}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 punishable}}}\uc2  by up to 10 years in prison.\par \par \uc2 By Thursday afternoon, all indications were that Trump would not agree to testify.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.00pm BST\par \par \uc2 Biden also took jabs at Alabama senator Tommy Tuberville in his speech, as Tuberville has blocked consideration for about 200 military promotions.\par \par \uc2 While speaking in Philadelphia about his infrastructure agenda, Biden referred to Tuberville without naming the senator: \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19m glad the senator is coming along around on the infrastructure law but I\u8217\'20\'19m not going to let up until he comes around on the critical military nominations as well.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 enltrBiden pokes at Tuberville in his remarks in Philadephia: \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19m glad the senator is coming along around on the infrastructure law but I\u8217\'20\'19m not going to let up until he comes around on the critical military nominations as well.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 AlexGangitano (@AlexGangitano) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/AlexGangitano/status/1682081139484139533?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 July 20, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 Biden has previously attacked Tuberville over the stalled nominations. The senator has blocked the nominations to protest the Pentagon\u8217\'20\'19s policy on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/jul/13/pentagon-chief-republian-senator-tommy-tuberville"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Biden attacks \u8216\'20\'18ridiculous\u8217\'20\'19 Republican senator for blocking military picks}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 7.01pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.39pm BST\par \par \uc2 During his speech, Biden also took an opportunity to criticize Trump, who is a candidate in the 2024 presidential election.\par \par \uc2 Biden was discussing wind energy projects, which he has supported for their ability to create clean energy and produce jobs.\par \par \uc2 During the speech, Biden noted that \u8220\'20\'1Cwindmills do not cause cancer\u8221\'20\'1D, mocking a claim made by Trump in 2019.\par \par \uc2 enltrBiden takes dig at Trump during his speech in Philadephia: \u8220\'20\'1Cnot withstandling what the other guy said, windmills do not cause cancer.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Trump in 2019 claimed that the noise from a windmill causes cancer.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 AlexGangitano (@AlexGangitano) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/AlexGangitano/status/1682077898017046545?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 July 20, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.20pm BST\par \par \uc2 Biden says Wall Street 'didn't build the middle class' in Bidenomics remarks in Philadelphia\par \par \uc2 Biden is in Philadelphia now, delivering remarks on his plans to grow the US economy under his Bidenomics plan.\par \par \uc2 Biden began his remarks by acknowledging mass flooding in Bucks County, Pennsylvania.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe idea that there is not global warming cannot be denied by anyone anymore,\u8221\'20\'1D Biden said.\par \par \uc2 Biden emphasized that his plan for the economy is to strength the middle class.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI often say, and I mean this sincerely, Wall street [has] good folks down there, but they didn\u8217\'20\'19t build the middle class. They didn\u8217\'20\'19t build America.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Biden emphasized the 13m jobs that have been added in two and half years, including nearly 500,000 in Pennsylvania.\par \par \uc2 Biden also noted that unemployment is down, along with inflation, as the rising price of goods and services have impacted many across the country.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 6.38pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.55pm BST\par \par \uc2 The Republican-led House oversight committee will hold a hearing on UFOs, officially called unidentified aerial phenomena (UAPs), next week, according to congressman Tim Burchett.\par \par \uc2 The committee hearing, spearheaded by Burchett, will investigate the increase in sightings of UAPs and their impact on national security.\par \par \uc2 It comes after a former intelligence community official alleged that the \uc2 US government\uc2  has a covert program focused on recovering debris from crashed, non-human origin spacecraft, according to a Debrief {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://thedebrief.org/intelligence-officials-say-u-s-has-retrieved-non-human-craft/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 report. }}}\par \par \uc2 The former intelligence official, David Grusch, will testify at the hearing along with two former Navy pilots, including one who recorded a widely seen video of a UAP near his fighter jet.\par \par \uc2 Burchett and Representative Anna Paulina Luna said members of Congress have been \u8220\'20\'1Cstonewalled\u8221\'20\'1D by military officials when they\u8217\'20\'19ve asked for details on UAPs, including their possible origins. Burchett said:\par \par \uc2 This is ridiculous folks. Either they do exist or they don\u8217\'20\'19t exist. They keep telling us they don\u8217\'20\'19t exist, but they block every opportunity for us to get a hold of the information to prove that they do exist.\par \par \uc2 And we\u8217\'20\'19re gonna get to the bottom of that dadgummit. Whatever the truth may be. We\u8217\'20\'19re done with the coverup.\par \par \uc2 enltrOversight hearing on UAPs: July 26th, 10:00amEST.\par \par \uc2 Witnesses: David Grusch, David Fravor, Ryan Graves.\par \par \uc2 Full press conference: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/5UUZjKPmSP"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/5UUZjKPmSP}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/otldAPjn0b"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/otldAPjn0b}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Rep. Tim Burchett (@RepTimBurchett) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/RepTimBurchett/status/1682045566321057792?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 July 20, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.26pm BST\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  is in Philadelphia today to talk \u8220\'20\'1CBidenomics\u8221\'20\'1D and tout his administration\u8217\'20\'19s efforts to boost clean energy manufacturing and create union jobs.\par \par \uc2 As the president launches his 2024 re-election campaign, the White House hopes to revamp the messaging on the president\u8217\'20\'19s economic performance {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/jul/01/joe-biden-bidenomics-2024-reelection-economy"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 with a series of speeches, memos and the term \u8220\'20\'1CBidenomics\u8221\'20\'1D.}}}\par \par \uc2 Biden will visit the Philadelphia Shipyard for a steel-cutting ceremony to mark the construction of a union-built vessel that will be used to help build offshore windfarms.\par \par \uc2 President \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  walks to greet onlookers after disembarking Air Force One at \uc2 Philadelphia International Airport\uc2  in Philadelphia, Pennsylvania. Photograph: Mandel Ngan/AFP/Getty Images\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 5.43pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.11pm BST\par \par \uc2 Robert F Kennedy Jr\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s appearance before the House judiciary select subcommittee on the weaponization of the federal government came despite requests from outside groups to disinvite him after {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/jul/17/robert-f-kennedy-jr-covid-condemned"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 his recent remarks.}}}\par \par \uc2 Republicans are eager to elevate Kennedy, a long-shot Democratic candidate for president and heir to the famous political family.\par \par \uc2 A watchdog group asked the panel\u8217\'20\'19s chairman, Jim Jordan, to drop the invitation to Kennedy after he falsely claimed that Covid-19 was engineered to target some ethnic groups and spare others.\par \par \uc2 Jordan said that while he disagreed with Kennedy\u8217\'20\'19s remarks, he was not about to drop him from the panel, AP reported. Speaker Kevin McCarthy took a similar view, saying he did not want to censor Kennedy.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 5.27pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.06pm BST\par \par \uc2 RFK Jr uses House panel appearance to deny accusations of racism and antisemitism\par \par \uc2 Democratic presidential candidate \uc2 Robert F Kennedy Jr\uc2  defended himself against accusations of racism and antisemitism at a hearing on alleged \u8220\'20\'1Cweaponization\u8221\'20\'1D of the federal government.\par \par \uc2 Kennedy, speaking before the House judiciary select subcommittee on the weaponization of the federal government, said \u8220\'20\'1Cno evidence\u8221\'20\'1D exists that he is antisemitic and that the attacks that have been made on him in recent days have been intended to keep him quiet.\par \par \uc2 Kennedy {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/jul/17/robert-f-kennedy-jr-covid-condemned"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 provoked anger last week }}}\uc2  when he was filmed falsely suggesting that the coronavirus could have been \u8220\'20\'1Cethnically targeted\u8221\'20\'1D to spare Ashkenazi Jews and Chinese people. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/jul/17/robert-f-kennedy-jr-covid-condemned"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 A report seen by the Guardian }}}\uc2  said Kennedy has a long history of racism, antisemitism and xenophobia.\par \par \uc2 enltr"I wanna say this while I'm on the record that in my entire life... I have never uttered a phrase that was either racist or antisemetic."\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 \uc2 Robert F Kennedy Jr\uc2 . testifying before the House Judiciary Weaponization of the Federal Government Subcommittee {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/h29XsmSYbt"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/h29XsmSYbt}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 The Recount (@therecount) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/therecount/status/1682024809134444547?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 July 20, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 5.27pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.46pm BST\par \par \uc2 Conservative nonprofit groups steered by the rightwing legal activist, \uc2 Leonard Leo\uc2 , reportedly orchestrated a $1.8m public relations campaign to defend and celebrate supreme court justice, \uc2 Clarence Thomas\uc2 , after he faced renewed scrutiny over his past misconduct claims.\par \par \uc2 According to a \uc2 Washington Post{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.washingtonpost.com/investigations/2023/07/20/leonard-leo-clarence-thomas-paoletta/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  report,}}}\uc2  Leo, a hugely influential figure {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/apr/06/leonard-leo-watchdog-complaint-investigation"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 said to have been}}}\uc2  the chief curator of supreme court nominees when \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  was president, was the architect of a years-long \u8220\'20\'1Ccoordinated and sophisticated\u8221\'20\'1D campaign that included advertising aimed at boosting flattering content in online searches, promotion for a laudatory film, and websites and \uc2 Twitter\uc2  accounts celebrating his career.\par \par \uc2 The paper writes:\par \par \uc2 The 25th anniversary of \uc2 Clarence Thomas\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s confirmation to the Supreme Court was approaching \u8212\'20\'14 a moment that would draw attention to his accomplishments on the bench but also to the misconduct claims that had nearly derailed his rise. Among the wave of retrospective accounts set to come out that year, 2016, was a star-studded HBO film dramatically recounting \uc2 Anita Hill\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s sexual harassment allegations.\par \par \uc2 That spring, a flurry of opinion articles defending Thomas and railing against the film appeared in news outlets, penned by a D.C. lawyer who had worked in the George H.W. Bush White House during the confirmation. Websites celebrating Thomas\u8217\'20\'19s career \u8212\'20\'14 and attacking his onetime accuser \u8212\'20\'14 popped up. And on \uc2 Twitter\uc2 , a new account using the name \u8220\'20\'1CJustice Thomas Fan Account\u8221\'20\'1D began serving up flattering commentary.\par \par \uc2 \u8216\'20\'18Justice Thomas: The most open & personable of Justices, intimate in sharing his feelings, easily moved to laughter,\u8217\'20\'19 read one early tweet on the account.\par \par \uc2 The campaign, led by Leo, shows how the judicial activist has continued to exert influence in support of conservative justices after helping them secure lifetime appointments, the report says.\par \par \uc2 Leonard Leo\uc2  in this 2016 photo, as then vice-president of the \uc2 Federalist Society\uc2 . Photograph: Carolyn Kaster/AP\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.28pm BST\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 UN\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s security council will meet in New York tomorrow over the \u8220\'20\'1Chumanitarian consequences\u8221\'20\'1D of Russia\u8217\'20\'19s withdrawal from a deal that allowed the safe Black Sea export of Ukraine grain for the past year, according to Britain\u8217\'20\'19s \uc2 UN\uc2  mission.\par \par \uc2 enltr?? {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/hashtag/BREAKING?src=hash&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 #BREAKING}}}\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 UN Security Council\uc2  will meet tomorrow at 10am for a briefing on Ukraine.\par \par \uc2 The Council will discuss the humanitarian consequences of Russia\u8217\'20\'19s interruption of the Black Sea Grain Initiative. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/hashtag/UNSC?src=hash&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 #UNSC}}}\uc2  ???????? {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/jKEEeV2nR0"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/jKEEeV2nR0}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 UK at the \uc2 UN\uc2  ???????? (@UKUN_NewYork) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/UKUN_NewYork/status/1682034525126418439?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 July 20, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 For more live updates on Russia\u8217\'20\'19s war in Ukraine, head over to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/live/2023/jul/20/russia-ukraine-war-live-updates-deaths-reported-mykolaiv-strikes-missiles-odesa-targeted#top-of-blog"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 our excellent Russia-Ukraine war blog. }}}\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/live/2023/jul/20/russia-ukraine-war-live-updates-deaths-reported-mykolaiv-strikes-missiles-odesa-targeted"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Russia-Ukraine war live: UN security council to meet over \u8216\'20\'18humanitarian consequences\u8217\'20\'19 of grain deal collapse}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.17pm BST\par \par \uc2 Kevin McCarthy denies report he privately promised Trump to expunge impeachments\par \par \uc2 House speaker Kevin McCarthy has denied he privately promised former president \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  that he would get legislation passed that would erase Trump\u8217\'20\'19s two impeachments.\par \par \uc2 According to a Politico {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.politico.com/news/2023/07/20/kevin-mccarthy-donald-trump-impeachment-expunge-promise-00107236"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 report, }}}\uc2  Trump was outraged at McCarthy for withholding his endorsement of his presidential run in the 2024 election. In an interview last month, McCarthy expressed doubt that Trump was the \u8220\'20\'1Cstrongest\u8221\'20\'1D candidate to defeat \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  and win back the White House next year.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CHe needs to endorse me \u8211\'20\'13 today!\u8221\'20\'1D Trump is said to have fumed to his staff on his way to a campaign event in New Hampshire. McCarthy called Trump to apologize after the interview, claiming he misspoke, sources {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cnn.com/2023/07/20/politics/kevin-mccarthy-expunging-trump-impeachments/index.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  told }}}\uc2  CNN at the time.\par \par \uc2 In return for delaying that endorsement, according to Politico, McCarthy pledged that he would get the House to vote to expunge both impeachments against the former president. The outlet said McCarthy had promised to do so before Congress leaves for an August recess. Recess begins in less than two weeks.\par \par \uc2 In 2019, a Democrat-controlled House voted to impeach Trump for abuse of power and obstruction of Congress after he asked Ukraine to investigate his presidential election rival, \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 , and his son on unsubstantiated corruption accusations.\par \par \uc2 The House impeached Trump for a second time in 2021 for his actions ahead of the deadly January 6 attack on the US Capitol by his supporters. The Senate acquitted him both times, thanks to the votes of Republicans. McCarthy voted against impeaching Trump both times.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThere\u8217\'20\'19s no deal,\u8221\'20\'1D McCarthy told a reporter in the Capitol on Thursday, Reuters reported.\par \par \uc2 House Speaker Kevin McCarthy denied he privately promised \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  that he would get legislation passed that would erase Trump\u8217\'20\'19s two impeachments. Photograph: Leah Millis/Reuters\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 4.37pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.47pm BST\par \par \uc2 The South Carolina senator \uc2 Lindsey Graham\uc2 , the top Republican on the Senate judiciary committee, accused Democrats of trying to \u8220\'20\'1Cdestroy\u8221\'20\'1D the supreme court and said the ethics bill \u8220\'20\'1Cis an assault on the court itself\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Congress should stay out of the court\u8217\'20\'19s business, Graham said.\par \par \uc2 enltrJUST NOW:\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CCongress needs to stay out of the Supreme Court\u8217\'20\'19s business.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/LindseyGrahamSC?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @LindseyGrahamSC}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Senate Republicans (@SenateGOP) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/SenateGOP/status/1681758763852636162?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 July 19, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 Opening the committee meeting, Senate judiciary chair Dick Durbin said the legislation would be a \u8220\'20\'1Ccrucial first step\u8221\'20\'1D in restoring confidence in the court.\par \par \uc2 Graham vowed, in response, that \u8220\'20\'1Call of us are going to vote no\u8221\'20\'1D. From NBC\u8217\'20\'19s Sahil Kapur:\par \par \uc2 enltrSenate Judiciary Committee is now considering the Whitehouse-Durbin bill to bolster ethics, disclosure and recusal rules for Supreme Court justices.\par \par \uc2 Durbin says it's a "crucial first step in restoring confidence in the court."\par \par \uc2 Graham trashes it, vows all Republicans vote no.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Sahil Kapur (@sahilkapur) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/sahilkapur/status/1682026167426244608?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 July 20, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 4.05pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.34pm BST\par \par \uc2 What ethical controversies are \uc2 US supreme court\uc2  justices facing?\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s a rundown of the ethical controversies supreme court justices have been involved in.\par \par \uc2 Real estate transactions\par \par \uc2 Clarence Thomas\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s friend Harlan Crow, the Texas Republican billionaire mega-donor, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.propublica.org/article/clarence-thomas-harlan-crow-real-estate-scotus"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 bought three properties}}}\uc2  that the conservative justice and his family owned, including Thomas\u8217\'20\'19s childhood home in Savannah, Georgia, where Thomas\u8217\'20\'19s mother still lives. \uc2 Crow\uc2  made significant renovations, cleared blight and let Thomas\u8217\'20\'19s mother live there rent-free. The cost was more than $100,000 but was not disclosed.\par \par \uc2 Justice \uc2 Neil Gorsuch\uc2  sold a 40-acre property he co-owned in rural Colorado after he became a justice, Politico {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.politico.com/news/2023/04/25/neil-gorsuch-colorado-property-sale-00093579"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reported}}}\uc2 . \uc2 Brian Duffy\uc2 , the chief executive of \uc2 Greenberg Traurig\uc2 , which has had more than 20 cases before the supreme court, bought the property in 2017. Gorsuch disclosed the sale and reportedly made between $250,000 and $500,000, but he left blank the buyer\u8217\'20\'19s identity.\par \par \uc2 School support\par \par \uc2 Crow paid thousands of dollars in private school tuition for two boarding schools that Thomas\u8217\'20\'19s great-nephew attended, \uc2 ProPublica{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.propublica.org/article/clarence-thomas-harlan-crow-private-school-tuition-scotus"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reported}}}\uc2 . The transaction was not disclosed.\par \par \uc2 An investigation by the Associated Press revealed how colleges and universities attract supreme court justices to campuses as a way to generate donations for institutions, raising ethical concerns around a court that, unlike other government agencies, does not have a formal code of conduct. The visits have resulted in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://apnews.com/article/supreme-court-teaching-paradise-travel-46c7d9ed41a5fabc5c64579b45abdd98"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 all-expenses-paid teaching opportunities}}}\uc2  and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://apnews.com/article/supreme-court-sotomayor-book-sales-ethics-colleges-b2cb93493f927f995829762cb8338c02"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 book sales}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Money to partners\par \par \uc2 The Republican activist \uc2 Leonard Leo{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.washingtonpost.com/investigations/2023/05/04/leonard-leo-clarence-ginni-thomas-conway/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 paid}}}\uc2  Thomas\u8217\'20\'19s wife, Ginni, $25,000 for polling services in January 2012, telling the Republican pollster Kellyanne Conway to make \u8220\'20\'1Cno mention of Ginni\u8221\'20\'1D, the \uc2 Washington Post\uc2  reported. It\u8217\'20\'19s unclear whether that is a direct ethical concern for \uc2 Clarence Thomas\uc2  but it may constitute a conflict of interest.\par \par \uc2 Ginni, who also {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.npr.org/2022/09/29/1125886442/ginni-thomas-wife-supreme-court-justice-testifies-jan-6"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 attended}}}\uc2  the January 6 attack at the Capitol, reportedly {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.npr.org/2022/09/29/1125886442/ginni-thomas-wife-supreme-court-justice-testifies-jan-6"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 exchanged text messages}}}\uc2  with the then White House chief of staff \uc2 Mark Meadows\uc2 , encouraging him to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://apnews.com/article/biden-politics-united-states-government-fraud-mark-meadows-c734294e2810f1240ea7ed1cbf675760"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 support }}}\uc2  then president \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s false election fraud claims aimed at subverting the results of his 2020 electoral defeat. The Judicial Education Project, a law firm tied to Leo, filed a brief to the supreme court in the landmark case that eventually gutted the Voting Rights Act not long after the payment was made.\par \par \uc2 Roberts\u8217\'20\'19 wife, Jane Sullivan Roberts, ran a legal recruiting firm that raised ethical concerns since she made millions of dollars in commissions from placing lawyers at firms, some of which appeared before the court. \uc2 The New York Times{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/2023/01/31/us/john-roberts-jane-sullivan-roberts.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 obtained}}}\uc2  a letter from a former colleague of Roberts to the US justice department and Congress inquiring about the connection.\par \par \uc2 Luxury trips\par \par \uc2 For more than two decades, Thomas accepted millions of dollars\u8217\'20\'19 worth of luxury trips on private planes and \u8220\'20\'1Csuperyachts\u8221\'20\'1D, and vacations from his friend Crow without reporting them on financial disclosure forms, \uc2 ProPublica{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.propublica.org/article/clarence-thomas-scotus-undisclosed-luxury-travel-gifts-crow"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reported}}}\uc2 . \uc2 Crow\uc2  has said that he did not attempt to influence Thomas politically or legally nor did he discuss pending supreme court cases. Thomas said he was told he was not required to disclose the trips. Notably, a company linked to Crow was involved in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.bloomberg.com/news/articles/2023-04-24/clarence-thomas-friend-harlan-crow-had-business-before-the-supreme-court#xj4y7vzkg"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 at least one case}}}\uc2  before the \uc2 US supreme court\uc2 , \uc2 Bloomberg\uc2  reported. Thomas did not recuse himself from the case.\par \par \uc2 Justice \uc2 Samuel Alito{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.propublica.org/article/samuel-alito-luxury-fishing-trip-paul-singer-scotus-supreme-court"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reportedly}}}\uc2  took a private jet to an all-expenses-covered fishing trip to Alaska, paid for by the hedge fund billionaire and conservative mega-donor \uc2 Paul Singer\uc2 . NPR {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.npr.org/2023/06/28/1183337280/supreme-court-ethics-financial-disclosures-possible-conflicts-of-interest"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reports}}}\uc2  that Singer has been involved in 10 appeals to the supreme court. In an unprecedented move, Alito {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/propublica-misleads-its-readers-alito-gifts-disclosure-alaska-singer-23b51eda"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 defended himself}}}\uc2  in an op-ed in the Wall Street Journal, declaring he did not have to recuse himself and followed what he \u8220\'20\'1Cunderstood to be standard practice\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.24pm BST\par \par \uc2 Senate committee to vote on supreme court ethics reform\par \par \uc2 The Senate judiciary committee is expected to vote today on a bill that would require the supreme court to adopt a code of ethics.\par \par \uc2 Senate Democrats have called for a measure to establish a code of conduct for the supreme court justices similar to those that other government agencies must follow.\par \par \uc2 The bill, unlikely to pass in a divided Congress, would demand the court create a code within 180 days and establish rules on recusals related to potential conflicts of interest and disclosure of gifts and travel.\par \par \uc2 The panel vote comes after months of scrutiny on the court over {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/law/2023/jul/12/us-supreme-court-justices-ethics-rules-controversy-explain"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 ethical controversies}}}\uc2  supreme court justices have been involved in.\par \par \uc2 Senate judiciary committee chair, Dick Durbin, said this week:\par \par \uc2 Just about every week now, we learn something new and deeply troubling about the justices serving on the supreme court, the highest court in the land in the United States, and their conduct outside the courtroom.\par \par \uc2 Let me tell you, if I or any member of the Senate failed to report an all-expense paid luxury getaway or if we used our government staff to help sell books we wrote, we\u8217\'20\'19d be in big trouble.\par \par \uc2 The bill would need at least nine GOP votes to pass, and Republicans appear united against it, arguing that the legislation would undermine the separation of powers and \u8220\'20\'1Cdestroy\u8221\'20\'1D the court.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.06pm BST\par \par \uc2 Trump\u8217\'20\'19s legal problems: where does each case stand?\par \par \uc2 Twice impeached and now twice arrested and indicted. \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  faces serious charges in New York and Florida over a hush-money scheme during the 2016 election and his alleged mishandling of classified documents.\par \par \uc2 And more criminal charges could be on the way for Trump in Georgia and Washington DC. Here is where each case against Trump stands:\par \par \uc2 Classified documents case in Florida\par \par \uc2 Status: Trump pleaded not guilty; trial scheduled for August\par \par \uc2 default\par \par \uc2 Charges: 31 counts of willful retention of national defense information under the Espionage Act, conspiracy to obstruct justice and false statements and representations, among others\par \par \uc2 Hush-money case in New York\par \par \uc2 Status: Trump pleaded not guilty; trial forthcoming\par \par \uc2 default\par \par \uc2 Charges: 34 felony charges of falsifying business records\par \par \uc2 January 6 case in Washington\par \par \uc2 Status: Subpoenas issued by grand jury\par \par \uc2 default\par \par \uc2 Potential charges against Trump: Obstruction of an official proceeding, conspiracy to defraud the government and incitement of an insurrection\par \par \uc2 2020 election meddling case in Georgia\par \par \uc2 Status: Grand jury report finished; charging decisions expected this summer\par \par \uc2 default\par \par \uc2 Potential charges against Trump: Election code violations\par \par \uc2 E Jean Carroll lawsuits in New York\par \par \uc2 Status: First lawsuit going to trial; second lawsuit on appeal\par \par \uc2 default\par \par \uc2 Allegations against Trump: Defamation and sexual abuse\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/jul/18/donald-trump-what-how-many-criminal-charges"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Read the full story here. }}}\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/jul/18/donald-trump-what-how-many-criminal-charges"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Donald Trump\u8217\'20\'19s legal problems: where does each case stand?}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.59pm BST\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  has said he has {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/jul/20/trump-testimony-january-6-case-biden-epa-us-politics-live?page=with:block-64b9306c8f08ff360bcb13ad#block-64b9306c8f08ff360bcb13ad"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 until midnight tonight}}}\uc2  to testify before the federal grand jury deciding whether to indict him over his efforts to overturn the 2020 election.\par \par \uc2 Targets of criminal investigations rarely speak to grand juries, as they are usually advised by their attorneys to not take up invitations to meet with the grand jury because any statements provided in that setting could be used to help build a case against them in the event that they\u8217\'20\'19re charged.\par \par \uc2 Trump has not exercised that right in the two other criminal cases in which he\u8217\'20\'19s been charged, Politico\u8217\'20\'19s Kyle Cheney {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.politico.com/news/2023/07/18/trump-says-hes-received-a-target-letter-from-special-counsel-jack-smiths-jan-6-investigators-00106776"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 writes. }}}\par \par \uc2 enltrLots of anticipation at the federal courthouse in DC today \u8212\'20\'14 Trump, of course, is not expected to show up but high likelihood of grand jury activity today as Jan. 6 probe nears charging stage.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Kyle Cheney (@kyledcheney) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/kyledcheney/status/1682008671151112192?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 July 20, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.50pm BST\par \par \uc2 Recent witnesses who have appeared before the grand jury investigating \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s efforts to overturn the 2020 election were reportedly asked about the former president\u8217\'20\'19s state of mind surrounding the January 6 insurrection.\par \par \uc2 Federal prosecutors asked multiple former senior Trump White House officials to speak to Trump\u8217\'20\'19s mindset in the days and weeks after losing the 2020 election, leading up to 6 January, according to a New York Times {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/2023/07/13/us/politics/kushner-grand-jury-trump.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  report. }}}\par \par \uc2 Witnesses including Trump\u8217\'20\'19s son-in-law, \uc2 Jared Kushner\uc2 , were asked if he had privately acknowledged that he had lost the election, it said. Kushner is understood to have said that it was his impression that Trump truly believed the election was stolen.\par \par \uc2 The line of questioning suggested prosecutors were trying to determine if Trump acted with corrupt intent as he sought to remain in power, the paper said.\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  and his son-in-law \uc2 Jared Kushner\uc2  in the Oval Office of the White House. Photograph: Andrew Caballero-Reynolds/AFP/Getty Images\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.36pm BST\par \par \uc2 January 6 grand jury to hear testimony from Trump aide\par \par \uc2 A federal grand jury investigating \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s efforts to overturn the 2020 election will hear testimony from an aide who was with the former president for much of the day on 6 January 2021, according to multiple reports.\par \par \uc2 William Russell, a former White House aide who now works for Trump\u8217\'20\'19s presidential campaign, is scheduled to testify before the grand jury convened by special counsel Jack Smith, both {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cnn.com/2023/07/20/politics/trump-grand-jury-analysis/index.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 CNN}}}\uc2  and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nbcnews.com/politics/justice-department/trump-grand-jury-hear-testimony-aide-was-jan-6-rcna94998"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 NBC }}}\uc2  reported.\par \par \uc2 Russell, who has previously testified before the grand jury, served in the Trump White House as a special assistant to the president and deputy director of advance, before moving to Florida to work as an aid to Trump after he left office.\par \par \uc2 Multiple former senior Trump White House officials have testified before the grand jury in the special counsel\u8217\'20\'19s investigation into the January 6 insurrection. Among those who have testified {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/jul/13/jared-kushner-testify-grand-jury"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  are Trump\u8217\'20\'19s son-in-law}}}\uc2  and former White House senior adviser, \uc2 Jared Kushner\uc2 , and former top Trump aide, \uc2 Hope Hicks\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 In April, \uc2 Mike Pence\uc2  testified for seven hours behind closed doors, meaning the details of what he told the prosecutors in the case remain uncertain.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 7.41pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.26pm BST\par \par \uc2 What {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/jul/20/trump-testimony-january-6-case-biden-epa-us-politics-live?page=with:block-64b934358f08ff360bcb13f6#block-64b934358f08ff360bcb13f6"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the potential charges}}}\uc2  means for Trump is unclear.\par \par \uc2 Prosecutors have been examining various instances of Trump pressuring officials like his former vice-president \uc2 Mike Pence\uc2 , but Trump\u8217\'20\'19s efforts to obstruct the transfer of power could also be construed as conspiring to defraud voters more generally.\par \par \uc2 The other two statutes, meanwhile, suggest a core part of the case against Trump is focused on the so-called fake electors scheme and the former president\u8217\'20\'19s efforts to use the fake slates in a conspiracy to stop the congressional certification of \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s election win on 6 January 2021.\par \par \uc2 The target letter did not cite any seditious conspiracy, incitement of insurrection or deprivation of rights under color of law \u8211\'20\'13 other areas for which legal experts have suggested Trump could have legal risk.\par \par \uc2 Last year, the House select committee that investigated the Capitol attack concluded that Trump committed multiple crimes in an attempt to reverse his 2020 defeat to \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 , including conspiracy to defraud the United States and obstruction of an official proceeding.\par \par \uc2 The committee issued symbolic criminal referrals to the justice department, although at that point the justice department had since stepped up its criminal investigation with the addition of new prosecutors in spring 2022 before they were folded into the special counsel\u8217\'20\'19s office.\par \par \uc2 House investigators also concluded that there was evidence for prosecutors to charge Trump with conspiracy to defraud and obstruction of an official proceeding. They also issued referrals for incitement of insurrection, which was not listed in the target letter.\par \par \uc2 Should prosecutors charge Trump in the federal January 6 investigation, the case could go to trial much more quickly than the Mar-a-Lago classified documents case \u8211\'20\'13 before the 2024 election \u8211\'20\'13 because pre-trial proceedings would not be delayed by rules governing national security materials.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.22pm BST\par \par \uc2 Trump under investigation for civil rights conspiracy in January 6 inquiry\par \par \uc2 Federal prosecutors investigating \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s efforts to overturn the 2020 election results have evidence to charge the former president with three crimes, including section 241 of the US legal code that makes it unlawful to conspire to violate civil rights, two people familiar with the matter said.\par \par \uc2 The potential charges detailed in a target letter sent to Trump by prosecutors from the office of special counsel Jack Smith, who also charged Trump with retaining classified documents last month, was the clearest signal of an imminent indictment.\par \par \uc2 Prosecutors appear to have evidence to charge Trump with obstruction of an official proceeding and conspiracy to defraud the United States based on the target letter, two statutes that the House select committee examining the January 6 Capitol attack issued criminal referrals for last year.\par \par \uc2 The target letter to Trump identified a previously unconsidered third charge, the sources said. That is {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.justice.gov/crt/statutes-enforced-criminal-section#:~:text=18%20U.S.C.%20%C2%A7%20241&text=Section%20241%20makes%20it%20unlawful,having%20exercised%20such%20a%20right."}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 section 241 of title 18 of the US code}}}\uc2 , which makes it unlawful to conspire to threaten or intimidate a person in the \u8220\'20\'1Cfree exercise\u8221\'20\'1D of any right or privilege under the \u8220\'20\'1CConstitution or laws of the United States\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 The statute, enacted to protect the civil rights of Black voters targeted by white supremacy groups after the US civil war, is unusual because it is typically used by prosecutors in law enforcement misconduct and hate crime prosecutions, though its use has expanded in recent years.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.16pm BST\par \par \uc2 Deadline looms for Trump to appear before January 6 grand jury\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  has until Thursday midnight to respond to special counsel Jack Smith and tell his office whether he will appear before a grand jury in the justice department\u8217\'20\'19s investigation into efforts to overturn the 2020 election results.\par \par \uc2 A letter sent to Trump by prosecutors from Smith\u8217\'20\'19s office on Sunday identified the former president as a \u8220\'20\'1Ctarget\u8221\'20\'1D in the probe into the January 6 insurrection, Trump posted to his Truth Social website on Tuesday. He wrote:\par \par \uc2 Deranged Jack Smith, the prosecutor with \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s DOJ, sent a letter \u8230\'20\'26 stating that I am a TARGET of the January 6th Grand Jury investigation, and giving me a very short 4 days to report to the Grand Jury, which almost always means an Arrest and an Indictment.\par \par \uc2 People who receive target letters from federal authorities are usually advised by their attorneys to not take up invitations to meet with the grand jury because any statements provided in that setting could be used to help build a case against them in the event that they\u8217\'20\'19re charged.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.57pm BST\par \par \uc2 Trump quietly adds new lawyer as he faces potential indictment in January 6 case\par \par \uc2 Good morning, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/us-politics"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 US politics}}}\uc2  blog readers. The former president, \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , has quietly added a criminal defense attorney to his legal team as he faces a potential indictment in the justice department\u8217\'20\'19s investigation into the January 6 insurrection.\par \par \uc2 Attorney John Lauro, who has also represented Trump attorneys Christina Bobb and Alina Habba, is joining Trump\u8217\'20\'19s legal team alongside Todd Blanche, according to sources, CNN {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cnn.com/2023/07/19/politics/john-lauro-attorney-trump-january-6/index.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reported}}}\uc2  late on Wednesday.\par \par \uc2 Lauro will be solely focused on special counsel Jack Smith \u8217\'20\'19s investigation into Trump\u8217\'20\'19s efforts to remain in office following his 2020 election defeat to \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 , including the deadly 6 January 2021 riot in which his supporters overran the Capitol building in Washington DC.\par \par \uc2 Federal prosecutors have evidence to charge the former president with three crimes, including section 241 of the US legal code that makes it unlawful to conspire to violate civil rights, the Guardian {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/jul/19/trump-investigation-three-federal-crimes-january-6"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reported last night,}}}\uc2  citing two people familiar with the matter.\par \par \uc2 Trump faces being charged with obstruction of an official proceeding and conspiracy to defraud the United States, two statutes that the House select committee examining the January 6 Capitol attack issued criminal referrals for last year.\par \par \uc2 The target letter also identified a previously unconsidered third charge, the sources said. That is {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.justice.gov/crt/statutes-enforced-criminal-section#:~:text=18%20U.S.C.%20%C2%A7%20241&text=Section%20241%20makes%20it%20unlawful,having%20exercised%20such%20a%20right."}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 section 241 of title 18 of the US code}}}\uc2 , which makes it unlawful to conspire to threaten or intimidate a person in the \u8220\'20\'1Cfree exercise\u8221\'20\'1D of any right or privilege under the \u8220\'20\'1CConstitution or laws of the United States\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 The potential charges detailed in a target letter sent to Trump by prosecutors from Smith\u8217\'20\'19s office, who also charged Trump with retaining classified documents last month, was the clearest signal of an imminent indictment.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s what else we\u8217\'20\'19re watching today:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 9am ET: \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  will get his daily intelligence briefing.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 9am ET: The House will hold a hearing on online censorship. Democratic presidential hopeful, Robert F Kennedy, is expected to testify.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 10am ET: The Senate will meet to resume consideration of an \uc2 EPA\uc2  nomination and the NDAA.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 10.20am ET: Biden will leave for Joint Base Andrews, where he will fly to Philadelphia.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 10.45am ET: House Minority Leader \uc2 Hakeem Jeffries\uc2  will hold his weekly news conference.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 1pm ET: Biden will speak about \u8220\'20\'1CBidenomics\u8221\'20\'1D. He will depart Philadelphia to return to the White House in the afternoon.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.22pm BST\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020230720ej7k001me\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
