\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 \u8216\'20\'18The future of  \highlight22\uc2 abortion \highlight\uc2  is tenuous\u8217\'20\'19: relief and fear in Iowa as ban blocked\b0\par\par\uc2 Mary Yang \par \uc2 781 \uc2 words\par \uc2 20 July 2023\par 16:12 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Rights groups and their lawyers have challenged \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  bans in many states and some rulings have led to a gray areas in law\par \par \uc2 Obtaining an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  after six weeks of pregnancy, before most know they are pregnant, was a crime in Iowa \u8211\'20\'13 for a weekend.\par \par \uc2 On Friday afternoon, \uc2 Kim Reynolds\uc2 , the Iowa governor, a Republican, signed a law banning the procedure after six weeks, at which point doctors begin detecting cardiac activity in an embryo, with narrow exceptions at an evangelical conference. \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  providers immediately {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/jul/17/iowa-six-week-abortion-ban-lawsuit-filed"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 filed a lawsuit}}}\uc2  seeking a temporary injunction and an Iowa judge approved it on Monday.\par \par \uc2 Reproductive rights groups and their legal teams welcomed the temporary block \u8211\'20\'13 but with caution, as state lawmakers could challenge the ruling in court.\par \par \uc2 ??\u8220\'20\'1CWe are deeply relieved that the court granted this relief so essential healthcare in Iowa can continue,\u8221\'20\'1D said Abbey Hardy-Fairbanks, the medical director at the Emma Goldman Clinic, in a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.aclu-ia.org/en/press-releases/iowa-court-temporarily-blocks-six-week-abortion-ban"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 joint statement}}}\uc2  with the \uc2 ACLU\uc2  and \uc2 Planned Parenthood\uc2  after the ruling Monday. \u8220\'20\'1CWe are also acutely aware that the relief is only pending further litigation and the future of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  in Iowa remains tenuous and threatened.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Reynolds, who called a rare special legislative session to pass the six-week ban, signaled her crusade {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://governor.iowa.gov/press-release/2023-07-17/gov-reynolds-statement-injunction-heartbeat-law"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 in a brief statement}}}\uc2  released shortly after the Monday ruling: \u8220\'20\'1CThe \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  industry\u8217\'20\'19s attempt to thwart the will of Iowans and the voices of their elected representatives continues today, but I will fight this all the way to the Iowa supreme court,\u8221\'20\'1D she said.\par \par \uc2 The legal back and forth over \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  in Iowa has mirrored court battles in other states, where reproductive rights groups and their lawyers have taken a number of approaches to challenge \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  bans under state law. Since the supreme court overturned Roe v Wade, 25 states have tried to implement either a complete or \u8220\'20\'1Cpre-viability\u8221\'20\'1D ban, according to a \uc2 Kaiser Family Foundation\uc2  (KFF) tracker. The bans are currently blocked by courts in seven states.\par \par \uc2 In Nebraska \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  providers and the \uc2 ACLU\uc2  are challenging the state\u8217\'20\'19s 12-week ban, which \uc2 Jim Pillen\uc2 , the governor, signed into law in May. Plaintiffs Planned Parenthood of the Heartland and Sarah Traxler, an OB-GYN, are seeking a temporary injunction on the law, which also bans gender-affirming surgery for people under 19, saying it {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.aclunebraska.org/sites/default/files/574_singe_subject_lawsuit.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 violated the state constitution}}}\uc2  by lumping together two unrelated bills.\par \par \uc2 And in Wisconsin, where clinics are no longer performing abortions after an 1849 law making \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  a felony in nearly all cases took effect last May, the attorney general, \uc2 Josh Kaul\uc2 , a Democrat, is suing to repeal the ban. A judge ruled in July that the lawsuit could continue after a defendant, a conservative Wisconsin attorney, moved to dismiss the case.\par \par \uc2 But legal battles have led to uncertainty for \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  providers and those seeking \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  care.\par \par \uc2 Over the last year, 20% of OB-GYNs have felt constraints on their ability to provide care for miscarriages and other pregnancy-related medical emergencies, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.kff.org/womens-health-policy/report/a-national-survey-of-obgyns-experiences-after-dobbs/#:~:text=Nationally%2C%20one%20in%20five%20office,in%20ten%20OBGYNs%20(40%25)."}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 according}}}\uc2  to a KFF survey conducted in May. That figure doubled in states where \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  is banned.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CProviders have stopped providing things preemptively because they\u8217\'20\'19re afraid about their criminal liability or they\u8217\'20\'19ve actually moved out of the state,\u8221\'20\'1D said \uc2 Laurie Sobel\uc2 , an associate director for women\u8217\'20\'19s health policy at KFF. \u8220\'20\'1CThere\u8217\'20\'19s a lot in the middle that poses burdens and challenges to people seeking \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  care.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Varied restrictions over contraceptives and \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  methods across states have further complicated access to care since the Dobbs ruling, Sobel said.\par \par \uc2 More than two-thirds of OB-GYNs nationwide said they understand the circumstances under which \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  is legal in the state they practice very well while just 45% of OBGYNs in states where \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  is restricted by gestational limits said so, according to the survey by KFF.\par \par \uc2 In Iowa, the last ruling that set a clear standard for how to review \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  cases was in 2015, according to Sally Frank, a professor at Drake University Law School and an expert on Iowa\u8217\'20\'19s \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  law. In that case, the Iowa supreme court used the standard of \u8220\'20\'1Cundue burden\u8221\'20\'1D to rule that a ban on televisits to obtain \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  pills violated the state constitution.\par \par \uc2 If the state appeals the judge\u8217\'20\'19s ruling and the lawsuit goes up to the Iowa supreme court, justices will need to decide whether to use the 2015 undue burden test, which favors reproductive rights groups, or set a new standard, said Frank.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe thing about \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  is you can ban it, but that doesn\u8217\'20\'19t mean it\u8217\'20\'19s going to stop,\u8221\'20\'1D said Frank.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020230720ej7k0018q\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
