\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 White House condemns \uc2 Robert Kennedy Jr\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s Covid claims as \u8216\'20\'18vile\u8217\'20\'19 \u8211\'20\'13 as it happened\b0\par\par\uc2 L\u233\'00\'E9onie Chao-Fong (now) and Joanna Walters (earlier) \par \uc2 7,028 \uc2 words\par \uc2 17 July 2023\par 23:09 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Karine Jean-Pierre\uc2  leads denunciation of Democrat\u8217\'20\'19s remarksWhite House ends months-long Netanyahu snub\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.00am BST\par \par \uc2 Summary of the day\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s a recap of today\u8217\'20\'19s developments:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Family members of Democratic presidential hopeful \uc2 Robert Kennedy Jr\uc2  joined {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/jul/17/manchin-third-party-biden-trump-2024-live-updates?page=with:block-64b5adfa8f0820b061204be7#block-64b5adfa8f0820b061204be7"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the White House}}}\uc2 in condemning his \u8220\'20\'1Cdeplorable\u8221\'20\'1D claim that Covid-19 was engineered to target some ethnic groups and spare others. The former attorney and nephew of \uc2 John F Kennedy{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/jul/17/robert-f-kennedy-jr-covid-condemned"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 made the extraordinary assertion}}}\uc2  during a recent dinner in New York city, saying the virus was \u8220\'20\'1Ctargeted to attack Caucasians and Black people\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Democratic Senator \uc2 Joe Manchin\uc2  and Republican former Utah governor \uc2 Jon Huntsman{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/jul/17/manchin-third-party-biden-trump-2024-live-updates?page=with:block-64b5c1378f0820b061204c65#block-64b5c1378f0820b061204c65"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 repeatedly dodged questions }}}\uc2  on whether they would run on a third-party ticket in the 2024 presidential election under the No Labels movement. The pair appeared at the group No Labels\u8217\'20\'19 town hall meeting to co-headline the organization\u8217\'20\'19s \u8220\'20\'1Ccommonsense\u8221\'20\'1D policy platform release, the first in a series of events that the group says it will hold as the 2024 presidential election takes shape.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Manchin\u8217\'20\'19s appearance at the No Labels event on Monday has fueled speculation that he is considering a run for the presidency. If he ran for the presidency as a No Labels candidate, it could not only {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/jul/17/manchin-third-party-biden-trump-2024-live-updates?page=with:block-64b54c128f08de0be01a5bef#block-64b54c128f08de0be01a5bef"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 split the Democratic vote }}}\uc2  in a way that gives the White House to the Republicans in 2024 but also hands the party his crucial seat in what is currently a finely-balanced Senate where the Democrats have a very narrow majority.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 An Iowa judge has temporarily blocked the state\u8217\'20\'19s new \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban from taking effect, just days after Governor \uc2 Kim Reynolds\uc2  signed the measure into law. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/jul/17/manchin-third-party-biden-trump-2024-live-updates?page=with:block-64b5b3958f0820b061204c08#block-64b5b3958f0820b061204c08"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  The move }}}\uc2  restores access to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  in Iowa for up to 20 weeks of pregnancy while the courts assess the new law\u8217\'20\'19s constitutionality. Meanwhile, Democratic Senator \uc2 Chris Murphy\uc2  of Connecticut warned that it is {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/jul/17/manchin-third-party-biden-trump-2024-live-updates?page=with:block-64b56eb88f0820b0612049c7#block-64b56eb88f0820b0612049c7"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1C100% certain\u8221\'20\'1D }}}\uc2  that the Republicans will pass a national \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban if they win Congress next year.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 House {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/democrats"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Democrats}}}\uc2  plan to unveil a resolution to formally censure Republican congressman George Santos for lying to voters about his education, work history and family background. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/jul/17/manchin-third-party-biden-trump-2024-live-updates?page=with:block-64b577128f08de0be01a5e70#block-64b577128f08de0be01a5e70"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 The resolution}}}\uc2  from Representative \uc2 Ritchie Torres\uc2  will be privileged, meaning that the Republican-controlled House must act on it. Santos has \u8220\'20\'1Cdisgraced [Congress], and the institution should speak with one voice against his misconduct,\u8221\'20\'1D said Torres.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Republican presidential candidate \uc2 Vivek Ramaswamy\uc2  announced {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/jul/17/manchin-third-party-biden-trump-2024-live-updates?page=with:block-64b567db8f0820b061204970#block-64b567db8f0820b061204970"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a list of candidates}}}\uc2  he would nominate to the supreme court if he were elected, including Senator Ted Cruz of Texas and Senator \uc2 Mike Lee\uc2  of Utah as possible nominees for the nation\u8217\'20\'19s top court.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Iowa Governor \uc2 Kim Reynolds{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/jul/17/manchin-third-party-biden-trump-2024-live-updates?page=with:block-64b590dd8f08742a26fe9261#block-64b590dd8f08742a26fe9261"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 dodged a question}}}\uc2  about whether she would be Florida Governor \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s running mate if he won the Republican presidential primary. DeSantis, at a fundraising event on Saturday, told reporters that he would consider Reynolds as a pick for vice president if he won the GOP nomination.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Ohio secretary of state \uc2 Frank LaRose\uc2  formally announced his candidacy for \uc2 US Senate\uc2 , becoming the third prominent Republican hoping to challenge Democratic incumbent \uc2 Sherrod Brown\uc2  in 2024. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/jul/17/manchin-third-party-biden-trump-2024-live-updates?page=with:block-64b57e9d8f08742a26fe91a7#block-64b57e9d8f08742a26fe91a7"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Ohio\u8217\'20\'19s Senate race}}}\uc2  looks to be one of the most competitive in the country next year, alongside races in Arizona, Montana and West Virginia. The state backed Trump in the 2016 and 2020 elections.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 A leading environmental group has hit out at US climate envoy \uc2 John Kerry\uc2  over comments he made rejecting calls for the US {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/jul/17/manchin-third-party-biden-trump-2024-live-updates?page=with:block-64b58e3a8f08742a26fe9253#block-64b58e3a8f08742a26fe9253"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 to pay climate reparations}}}\uc2  to developing countries affected by climate-change fueled disasters.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  has invited Israeli prime minister, \uc2 Benjamin Netanyahu\uc2 , to Washington for an official visit, according to a statement from Netanyahu\u8217\'20\'19s office. The {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/jul/17/manchin-third-party-biden-trump-2024-live-updates?page=with:block-64b581838f08de0be01a5ee5#block-64b581838f08de0be01a5ee5"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  phone call between the two leaders}}}\uc2  took place as Israeli president, \uc2 Isaac Herzog\uc2 , is traveling to Washington for meetings with Biden and to address a joint address to Congress.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The chair of the US Congressional Progressive Caucus apologized for calling Israel a \u8220\'20\'1Cracist state\u8221\'20\'1D. \u8220\'20\'1CI offer my apologies to those who I have hurt with my words,\u8221\'20\'1D \uc2 Pramila Jayapal\uc2  of Washington state {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/jul/17/manchin-third-party-biden-trump-2024-live-updates?page=with:block-64b55fb08f0820b06120490a#block-64b55fb08f0820b06120490a"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 said}}}\uc2  in a statement on Sunday.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.44pm BST\par \par \uc2 Joe Manchin\uc2  refuses to rule out third-party run for president\par \par \uc2 Democratic Senator \uc2 Joe Manchin\uc2  and Republican former Utah governor \uc2 Jon Huntsman\uc2  repeatedly dodged questions on whether they would run on a third-party ticket in the 2024 presidential election under the No Labels movement.\par \par \uc2 Manchin and \uc2 Huntsman\uc2  appeared at an event hosted by the bipartisan group in New Hampshire to unveil their platform, called Common Sense.\par \par \uc2 The event at Saint Anselm College in Manchester was described as the first public opportunity to highlight the group\u8217\'20\'19s policies.\par \par \uc2 Asked if he would consider \uc2 Huntsman\uc2  as a potential running mate on a unity ticket, Manchin said people were \u8220\'20\'1Cputting the cart ahead of the horse\u8221\'20\'1D and that the pair were there \u8220\'20\'1Cto make sure the American people have an option\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 He dismissed concerns that his candidacy could serve as a \u8220\'20\'1Cspoiler\u8221\'20\'1D to \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  that could help \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  become president.\par \par \uc2 I\u8217\'20\'19ve never been in any race I\u8217\'20\'19ve ever spoiled, I\u8217\'20\'19ve been in races to win. And if I get in a race, I\u8217\'20\'19m gonna win. I haven\u8217\'20\'19t made a decision.\par \par \uc2 enltrAt a No Labels event in New Hampshire, Sen. \uc2 Joe Manchin\uc2  (D-WV) says he \u8220\'20\'1Chasn\u8217\'20\'19t made decision\u8221\'20\'1D on a 2024 independent run but rejects the idea he\u8217\'20\'19d be a spoiler.\par \par \uc2 "I\u8217\'20\'19ve never been in any race I\u8217\'20\'19ve ever spoiled, I\u8217\'20\'19ve been in races to win. And if I get in a race, I\u8217\'20\'19m gonna win." {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/SYGJ9JXC6Y"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/SYGJ9JXC6Y}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 The Recount (@therecount) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/therecount/status/1681055870988300291?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 July 17, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 Asked what his party affiliation is, Manchin said he was \u8220\'20\'1Cthe most independent Democrat you\u8217\'20\'19ve ever met\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.14pm BST\par \par \uc2 In an {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/BarackObama/status/1680927869021696005/photo/1"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 open letter to American librarians}}}\uc2 , Barack Obama has criticised \u8220\'20\'1Cprofoundly misguided\u8221\'20\'1D rightwing efforts to ban books from libraries in public schools.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CSome of the books that shaped my life \u8211\'20\'13 and the lives of so many others \u8211\'20\'13 are being challenged by people who disagree with certain ideas or perspectives,\u8221\'20\'1D the former president {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/BarackObama/status/1680927869021696005/photo/1"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 wrote}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 It\u8217\'20\'19s no coincidence that these \u8216\'20\'18banned books\u8217\'20\'19 are often written by or feature people of colour, Indigenous people, and members of the LGBTQ+ community.\par \par \uc2 Obama\u8217\'20\'19s letter on Monday supported {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://uniteagainstbookbans.org/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Unite Against Book Bans}}}\uc2 , a campaign led by the \uc2 American Library Association\uc2  (ALA).\par \par \uc2 Obama also appeared in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tiktok.com/@kankakeepubliclibrary/video/7256781675802283306?lang=en"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a TikTok video}}}\uc2  posted by the Kankakee Public Library, from Illinois, which has found success with viral videos.\par \par \uc2 The 44th president appeared at the end of the short video, which otherwise featured staff reading books subject to bans or attempted bans. Obama was shown reading and sipping from a library-branded mug. More videos are set to be released.\par \par \uc2 The ALA has {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.ala.org/news/press-releases/2023/03/record-book-bans-2022"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 found}}}\uc2  that in US public schools last year, \u8220\'20\'1Ca record 2,571 unique titles were targeted for censorship\u8221\'20\'1D, often by parent-led groups, \u8220\'20\'1Ca 38% increase from the 1,858 unique titles targeted for censorship in 2021\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1COf those titles, the vast majority were written by or about members of the LGBTQ+ community and people of colour,\u8221\'20\'1D it adds.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.03pm BST\par \par \uc2 House Speaker Kevin McCarthy said Republicans will move forward with a scheduled hearing featuring \uc2 Robert Kennedy Jr\uc2  after the Democratic presidential hopeful was {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/jul/17/robert-f-kennedy-jr-covid-condemned"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  condemned}}}\uc2  for falsely claiming that Covid-19 was engineered to target some ethnic groups and spare others.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI disagree with everything he said,\u8221\'20\'1D McCarthy told reporters. But he rejected calls by Democrats to cancel Kennedy\u8217\'20\'19s public appearance on Thursday before a Republican-controlled House committee.\par \par \uc2 The hearing we\u8217\'20\'19re going to have this week is about censorship. I don\u8217\'20\'19t think censoring somebody is the answer here.\par \par \uc2 enltrSeconds after condemning purported Democratic anti-semitism, Kevin McCarthy defends House Republicans inviting RFK Jr to testify before Congress despite his anti-semitic remarks because "I don't think censoring somebody is actually the answer here" {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/yx5DscxSy8"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/yx5DscxSy8}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Aaron Rupar (@atrupar) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/atrupar/status/1681009313467203585?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 July 17, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.52pm BST\par \par \uc2 Close Kennedy family members weighing in reflects the growing outrage at Democratic presidential hopeful \uc2 Robert Kennedy Jr\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s words, which he tried to disavow on Monday in a statement sent to the Guardian by his campaign staff.\par \par \uc2 The statement reads:\par \par \uc2 The New York Post story is mistaken. I have never, ever suggested that the Covid-19 virus was engineered to \u8216\'20\'18spare Jews,\u8217\'20\'19 and I unequivocally reject this disgusting and outlandish conspiracy theory.\par \par \uc2 New York Post reporter Jon Levine exploited this off-the-record conversation to smear me as an antisemite. This cynical maneuver is consistent with the mainstream media playbook to discredit me as a crank - and by association, to discredit revelations of genuine corruption and collusion.\par \par \uc2 Separate messages {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/jul/17/robert-f-kennedy-jr-covid-condemned"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 sent to the Guardian}}}\uc2  purportedly from Kennedy\u8217\'20\'19s personal email address cite Wikipedia links to press articles about the plausibility of ethnically-targeted bioweapons.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe study is solid, and not at all controversial,\u8221\'20\'1D one of the messages says of a research paper by the \uc2 British Medical Association\uc2 , {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/science/2004/oct/28/thisweekssciencequestions.weaponstechnology"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reported by the Guardian}}}\uc2  in 2004, that \u8220\'20\'1Crogue scientists\u8221\'20\'1D could develop bioweapons designed to target certain ethnic groups based on their genetic differences.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.40pm BST\par \par \uc2 Iowa judge temporarily blocks state's \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban\par \par \uc2 An Iowa judge has temporarily blocked the state\u8217\'20\'19s new \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban from taking effect on Monday, just days after Governor \uc2 Kim Reynolds\uc2  signed the measure into law.\par \par \uc2 Polk County District Court Judge Joseph Seidlin ruled that {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/jul/17/manchin-third-party-biden-trump-2024-live-updates?page=with:block-64b5725a8f08742a26fe90ee#block-64b5725a8f08742a26fe90ee"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a lawsuit by \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  providers}}}\uc2  is likely to succeed, and the temporary injunction will remain in place for the duration of the lawsuit.\par \par \uc2 The move restores access to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  in Iowa for up to 20 weeks of pregnancy while the courts assess the new law\u8217\'20\'19s constitutionality.\par \par \uc2 Last week, Iowa lawmakers passed a six-week ban on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  in a rare special legislative session, called by Governor Reynolds, who signed the bill on Friday afternoon.\par \par \uc2 The law would ban almost all abortions once cardiac activity can be detected, which is usually six weeks into a pregnancy and before many women know they are pregnant. Prior to the law, \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  was legal in the state up to 22 weeks of pregnancy.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.29pm BST\par \par \uc2 West Virginia Senator \uc2 Joe Manchin\uc2  is {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nolabels.org/commonsense"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 speaking}}}\uc2  at an event hosted by the moderate group No Labels, fueling speculation that he could run on a third-party ticket for the presidency.\par \par \uc2 Manchin has not declared whether he will run, but it\u8217\'20\'19s difficult to see how his flirtation with No Labels would amount to a serious candidacy, according to a Vox {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.vox.com/2024-elections/2023/7/17/23797895/joe-manchin-third-party-2024-election-no-labels-joe-biden"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 report.}}}\par \par \uc2 It\u8217\'20\'19s true that many Democrats don\u8217\'20\'19t want Biden to run again, and many Republicans say the same of Trump, who is the current GOP frontrunner. But while 2024 may shape up to be the rematch no one asked for, third-party candidates don\u8217\'20\'19t have a successful track record in the US, and there\u8217\'20\'19s no indication a third-party candidate would be able to launch a credible challenge to either party\u8217\'20\'19s nominee this time. If Manchin or another third-party candidate runs, they would probably lose badly.\par \par \uc2 They might, however, get enough support among moderates to derail Biden in states that he narrowly won in 2020, despite No Labels co-chair Joe Lieberman\u8217\'20\'19s assurances that his group is not looking to get in the race for a \u8220\'20\'1Cspoiler.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 10.30pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.13pm BST\par \par \uc2 The White House\u8217\'20\'19s press secretary, \uc2 Karine Jean-Pierre\uc2 , described Robert F Kennedy\u8217\'20\'19s comments that Covid-19 was \u8220\'20\'1Cethnically targeted\u8221\'20\'1D to spare Ashkenazi Jews and Chinese people as false\u8221\'20\'1D and \u8220\'20\'1Cvile\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe claims made on that tape is false,\u8221\'20\'1D she said during a press briefing earlier this afternoon.\par \par \uc2 It is vile, and they put our fellow Americans in danger.\par \par \uc2 enltrWhite House Press Secretary \uc2 Karine Jean-Pierre\uc2  condemns RFK Jr.\u8217\'20\'19s comments that COVID -19 was \u8220\'20\'1Cethnically targeted\u8221\'20\'1D to spare Jewish and Chinese people:\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe claims made on that tape is false. It is vile. They put our fellow Americans in danger.\u8221\'20\'1D {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/ANyTEqePGN"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/ANyTEqePGN}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 The Recount (@therecount) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/therecount/status/1681038699864227840?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 July 17, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 She declined to discuss Kennedy directly, citing the legal constraints on the administration\u8217\'20\'19s ability to address campaign matters. But she warned that the presidential candidate\u8217\'20\'19s remarks amounted to encouraging racist theories around the virus.\par \par \uc2 If you think about the racist and antisemitic conspiracy theories that come out of saying those type of things, it\u8217\'20\'19s an attack on our fellow citizens.\par \par \uc2 And so it\u8217\'20\'19s important that we essentially speak out when we hear those claims more broadly.\par \par \uc2 She also cited a statement from the \uc2 American Jewish Committee\uc2  that called Kennedy\u8217\'20\'19s claims \u8220\'20\'1C {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/jul/17/manchin-third-party-biden-trump-2024-live-updates?page=with:block-64b587098f0820b061204aee#block-64b587098f0820b061204aee"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 deeply offensive\u8221\'20\'1D }}}\uc2  and reflective of \u8220\'20\'1Csome of the most abhorrent antisemitic conspiracy theories throughout history.\u8221\'20\'1D Jean-Pierre added:\par \par \uc2 This is something that this president, and this whole administration, is going to stand against.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 10.13pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.07pm BST\par \par \uc2 Former Utah governor \uc2 Jon Huntsman\uc2 , who is due to speak at this evening\u8217\'20\'19s No Labels event in New Hampshire, has insisted it is \u8220\'20\'1Cnot a campaign\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 enltrFmr. Gov. \uc2 Jon Huntsman\uc2  (R-UT) this AM to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/scrippsnews?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @scrippsnews}}}\uc2  in Manchester, NH: No Labels event tonight at St. Anselm is "not a campaign"\par \par \uc2 Huntsman\uc2  tells me he is NOT weighing a third party presidential run. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/2qh5bOxRGJ"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/2qh5bOxRGJ}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Nathaniel Reed (@ReedReports) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/ReedReports/status/1680982947397091336?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 July 17, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.00pm BST\par \par \uc2 Iowa Governor \uc2 Kim Reynolds\uc2  dodged a question about whether she would be Florida Governor \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s running mate if he won the Republican presidential primary.\par \par \uc2 DeSantis, at a fundraising event on Saturday, told reporters that he would consider Reynolds as a pick for vice president if he won the GOP nomination.\par \par \uc2 Asked about DeSantis\u8217\'20\'19s comments, Reynolds told Fox\u8217\'20\'19s Ainsley Earhardt:\par \par \uc2 I appreciate the comments. But look, I\u8217\'20\'19m so focused. We are implementing a boldest universal school choice plan in the country. I just called a special session last week. This last week we passed the fetal heartbeat bill, and I actually cut state government and I cut 21 agencies from my Cabinet and we\u8217\'20\'19re implementing our alignment bill.\par \par \uc2 She added:\par \par \uc2 So I\u8217\'20\'19m busy working on being governor of the great state of Iowa and I\u8217\'20\'19m already working on cutting taxes again next year. So that\u8217\'20\'19s my focus right now.\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  last week expressed his frustration with Reynolds for declining to endorse a candidate early in the race. In a post to Truth Social, Trump wrote:\par \par \uc2 I opened up the Governor position for \uc2 Kim Reynolds\uc2 , & when she fell behind, I ENDORSED her, did big Rallies, & she won. Now, she wants to remain \u8216\'20\'18NEUTRAL.\u8217\'20\'19 I don\u8217\'20\'19t invite her to events! DeSanctus down 45 points!\par \par \uc2 DeSantis, speaking on Saturday, also dismissed Trump\u8217\'20\'19s criticism of Reynolds, saying:\par \par \uc2 I thought the attacks on her were totally, totally out of hand and totally unnecessary.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.44pm BST\par \par \uc2 Joe Kennedy III\uc2 , a former congressman from Massachusetts and nephew of Robert F Kennedy Jr, has publicly distanced himself from his {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/jul/17/manchin-third-party-biden-trump-2024-live-updates?page=with:block-64b587098f0820b061204aee#block-64b587098f0820b061204aee"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  uncle\u8217\'20\'19s latest comments.}}}\par \par \uc2 enltrMy uncle\u8217\'20\'19s comments were hurtful and wrong. I unequivocally condemn what he said.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 \uc2 Joe Kennedy III\uc2  (@joekennedy) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/joekennedy/status/1681023900459704321?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 July 17, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 Robert F Kennedy\u8217\'20\'19s sister, Kerry Kennedy, has also {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/jul/17/manchin-third-party-biden-trump-2024-live-updates?page=with:block-64b596a78f08742a26fe9280#block-64b596a78f08742a26fe9280"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 sharply criticised}}}\uc2  his remarks about Covid.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.30pm BST\par \par \uc2 A leading environmental group has hit out at US climate envoy \uc2 John Kerry\uc2  over comments he made rejecting calls for the US to pay climate reparations to developing countries affected by climate-change fueled disasters.\par \par \uc2 On Friday, at a congressional hearing on the state department\u8217\'20\'19s climate agenda, Kerry said that \u8220\'20\'1Cunder no circumstances\u8221\'20\'1D would the US meet reparations demands. However, the US has previously committed to contributing to a \u8220\'20\'1Closs and damages\u8221\'20\'1D fund for developing countries that does not involve statements of liability.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe are disappointed and angered by this news, but not surprised, because \uc2 John Kerry\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s words are just the latest example of Kerry and the US refusing to back up their vague claims for US support in global climate progress with real, substantive action,\u8221\'20\'1D {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://350.org/press-release/kerry-reparations/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 said }}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://350.org/press-release/kerry-reparations/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Jeff Ordower}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://350.org/press-release/kerry-reparations/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 , North America director of the climate advocacy group 350.0rg.}}}\par \par \uc2 Ordower added that Kerry and president Biden \u8220\'20\'1Chave tried to walk a tightrope of limited culpability: they talk a big game about \u8220\'20\'1Cinterconnected nations\u8221\'20\'1D and \u8220\'20\'1Cthe need for a fossil fuel phasedown,\u8221\'20\'1D but shied away \u8220\'20\'1Cwhen it comes to \u8220\'20\'1Cput their words into practice.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The criticism comes as Kerry met with Chinese counterpart \uc2 Xie Zhenhua\uc2  in Beijing to urge joint action to cut methane emissions and coal-fired power.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIn the next three days we hope we can begin taking some big steps that will send a signal to the world about the serious purpose of China and the United States to address a common risk, threat, challenge to all of humanity created by humans themselves,\u8221\'20\'1D Kerry said, according to Reuters.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt is toxic for both Chinese and for Americans and for people in every country on the planet.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The US climate envoy\u8217\'20\'19s comments came as temperature records in the US, Europe and China are coming close to being broken this week, alongside intense rain and flooding in other areas that are collectively pushing climate change issue to the top of the global political agenda.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.20pm BST\par \par \uc2 Claims made by RFK Jr on Covid 'vile' \u8211\'20\'13 White House\par \par \uc2 White House press secretary \uc2 Karine Jean-Pierre\uc2  has taken the chance to condemn {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/jul/17/manchin-third-party-biden-trump-2024-live-updates?page=with:block-64b58d448f0820b061204b33#block-64b58d448f0820b061204b33"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 remarks}}}\uc2  made by presidential hopeful Robert F Kennedy Jr after a video surfaced of him making false claims that Covid-19 was {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/jul/17/manchin-third-party-biden-trump-2024-live-updates?page=with:block-64b587098f0820b061204aee#block-64b587098f0820b061204aee"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1Cethnically targeted\u8221\'20\'1D}}}\uc2  to attack certain ethnic groups.\par \par \uc2 Kennedy, the infamous conspiracy theorist, famous scion and rogue candidate for the Democratic presidential nomination hit the headlines at the weekend after it emerged that he said at a press event in New York City last week that the coronavirus is a genetically engineered bioweapon that may have been \u8220\'20\'1Cethnically targeted\u8221\'20\'1D to spare Ashkenazi Jews and Chinese people, the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://nypost.com/2023/07/15/rfk-jr-says-covid-was-ethnically-targeted-to-spare-jews/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 New York Post reported}}}\uc2  at the weekend.\par \par \uc2 Kennedy is garnering loud and swift criticism, including from members of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/jul/17/manchin-third-party-biden-trump-2024-live-updates?page=with:block-64b596a78f08742a26fe9280#block-64b596a78f08742a26fe9280"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 his own family}}}\uc2 . The White House was asked about it during the press briefing today and Jean-Pierry called Kennedy\u8217\'20\'19s remarks not just \u8220\'20\'1Cfalse\u8221\'20\'1D but also \u8220\'20\'1Cvile\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 The White House press secretary \uc2 Karine Jean-Pierre\uc2  speaks during the daily briefing at the White House today. Photograph: Chris Kleponis/\uc2 EPA\par \par \uc2 The briefing is ongoing. Oh! It just wrapped up.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 9.30pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.02pm BST\par \par \uc2 The US is not in a position to attribute the overnight attack that damaged the road bridge linking Crimea to southern Russia, the White House has stated on Monday.\par \par \uc2 The White House daily media briefing is still underway and press secretary \uc2 Karine Jean-Pierre\uc2  is taking questions now. But a little earlier, National Security Council spokesman John Kirby was at the podium and his part of the briefing mainly focused on foreign policy and overseas news.\par \par \uc2 Kirby was not prepared to commit to naming the perpetrator of the attack on the bridge. We\u8217\'20\'19ve been covering this topic in our {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/live/2023/jul/17/russia-ukraine-war-live-crimean-bridge-emergency-traffic-stops-explosion?page=with:block-64b57aa48f08742a26fe917a#block-64b57aa48f08742a26fe917a"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Ukraine war live blog}}}\uc2 , but that is closing now. It will be back on Tuesday.\par \par \uc2 Russian president \uc2 Vladimir Putin\uc2  has attributed the overnight attack to Ukraine {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/live/2023/jul/17/russia-ukraine-war-live-crimean-bridge-emergency-traffic-stops-explosion?page=with:block-64b57aa48f08742a26fe917a#block-64b57aa48f08742a26fe917a"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 and said}}}\uc2  that his forces are preparing a response.\par \par \uc2 You can read the Guardian\u8217\'20\'19s full report on this topic {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2023/jul/17/kharkiv-mayor-dismisses-russian-claims-terrorism-crimea-kerch-bridge-attack"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 here}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.33pm BST\par \par \uc2 RFK's sister condemns Covid remarks\par \par \uc2 Robert F Kennedy\u8217\'20\'19s sister is among those who have sharply criticised his remarks about Covid.\par \par \uc2 Kerry Kennedy wrote on \uc2 Twitter\uc2 : \u8220\'20\'1CI strongly condemn my brother\u8217\'20\'19s deplorable and untruthful remarks last week about Covid being engineered for ethnic targeting.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 enltrI STRONGLY condemn my brother's deplorable and untruthful remarks last week about Covid being engineered for ethnic targeting. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/9YCag7JtHm"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/9YCag7JtHm}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Kerry Kennedy (@KerryKennedyRFK) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/KerryKennedyRFK/status/1680998094413115393?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 July 17, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.56pm BST\par \par \uc2 Democrats were quick to distance themselves from presidential hopeful Robert F Kennedy Jr after a video surfaced of him making false claims that Covid-19 was {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/jul/17/manchin-third-party-biden-trump-2024-live-updates?page=with:block-64b587098f0820b061204aee#block-64b587098f0820b061204aee"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1Cethnically targeted\u8221\'20\'1D}}}\uc2  to attack certain ethnic groups.\par \par \uc2 Kennedy\u8217\'20\'19s comments included \u8220\'20\'1Creprehensible anti-semitic and anti-Asian comments aimed at perpetuating harmful and debunked racist tropes, the Democratic congressional campaign committee said in a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://dccc.org/dccc-statement-on-rfk-jr-s-reprehensible-comments/#:~:text=%E2%80%9CLast%20week%2C%20RFK%20Jr.,in%20the%20strongest%20possible%20terms.%E2%80%9D"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  statement. }}}\par \par \uc2 The Democratic presidential candidate\u8217\'20\'19s attempt to repurpose fringe-right conspiracy theories is not new for his candidacy, the \uc2 Washington Post{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.washingtonpost.com/politics/2023/07/17/rfk-covid-democrats/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reported}}}\uc2 . The paper compares Kennedy\u8217\'20\'19s remarks to how \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  offered a conspiratorial right-wing worldview to Republican primary voters in 2015.\par \par \uc2 It\u8217\'20\'19s not surprising that the party\u8217\'20\'19s institutions and leaders would take this tack; the Democratic Party is keenly attuned to racist stereotypes and antisemitism. But it is also not much of a burden. Kennedy\u8217\'20\'19s support in the primary is not particularly robust relative to the incumbent president, and his long-standing conspiratorial rhetoric has not been effective at building a constituency. The party is certainly eager that it doesn\u8217\'20\'19t.\par \par \uc2 Compare the response here with the Republican Party\u8217\'20\'19s response to \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  in 2015. The chairman of the party then, Reince Priebus, didn\u8217\'20\'19t excoriate Trump\u8217\'20\'19s repeated rhetoric about criminal immigrants on social media. The party doesn\u8217\'20\'19t appear to have done so either [\u8230\'20\'26] For the GOP, Trump\u8217\'20\'19s controversial comments were already accepted by a large segment of its base, which is why his candidacy quickly gained traction.\par \par \uc2 There is an interesting question inherent to the Kennedy situation for the Democratic Party: How accountable is it for the espoused views of one of its candidates for the presidential nomination? What is it about Kennedy that demands a response at all? Is it his name? Because he\u8217\'20\'19s getting more than zero percent in polls? Is it simply that Kennedy affords Democrats an opportunity to reinforce who they are relative to what he presents?\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.43pm BST\par \par \uc2 West Virginia Senator \uc2 Joe Manchin\uc2 , who is set to headline the No Labels event in New Hampshire later today, is arguably the most conservative Democratic senator.\par \par \uc2 Manchin has not declared yet whether he will run for reelection to his Senate seat. He has told reporters that he will wait until late this year before announcing whether he will run.\par \par \uc2 Should Manchin seek another term, he would face a serious challenge from Governor \uc2 Jim Justice\uc2 , who is seeking the Republican nomination in the Senate race. \uc2 West Virginia\uc2  has been leaning heavily Republican, having overwhelmingly voted for \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  in 2016 and 2020.\par \par \uc2 Manchin has at times complicated legislative initiatives being pushed by his party leaders, Reuters reported. But Democratic leaders have treaded softly as Manchin also has been key to the party holding on to its Senate majority.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.33pm BST\par \par \uc2 Robert F Kennedy Jr condemned for spreading conspiracy theory that Covid-19 was 'ethnically targeted'\par \par \uc2 Democratic presidential candidate Robert F Kennedy Jr faced widespread criticism over the weekend after a video surfaced of him making false claims that Covid-19 was \u8220\'20\'1Cethnically targeted\u8221\'20\'1D to attack certain ethnic groups while sparing Ashkenazi Jews and Chinese people.\par \par \uc2 The New York Post on Saturday originally {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://nypost.com/2023/07/15/rfk-jr-says-covid-was-ethnically-targeted-to-spare-jews/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 published}}}\uc2  a clip of Kennedy\u8217\'20\'19s conspiracy theory comments, made during a recent dinner in New York City. In the recording, Kennedy can be heard making a series of false and misleading claims, including saying:\par \par \uc2 Covid-19 is targeted to attack Caucasians and Black people. The people who are most immune are Ashkenazi Jews and Chinese.\par \par \uc2 Kennedy is also heard saying:\par \par \uc2 We don\u8217\'20\'19t know whether it was deliberately targeted or not but there are papers out there that show the racial or ethnic differential and impact.\par \par \uc2 Ted Deutch\uc2 , CEO of the \uc2 American Jewish Committee\uc2 , said Kennedy\u8217\'20\'19s comments are \u8220\'20\'1Cdeeply offensive and incredibly dangerous\u8221\'20\'1D in a tweet on Saturday.\par \par \uc2 The Anti-Defamation League told multiple outlets that Kennedy\u8217\'20\'19s comment \u8220\'20\'1Cfeeds into sinophobic and antisemitic conspiracy theories about Covid-19 that we have seen evolve over the last three years.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Democratic national committee chair \uc2 Jaime Harrison\uc2  condemned Kennedy\u8217\'20\'19s remarks and said they do not reflect the views of the party.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 7.47pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.06pm BST\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  has invited Israeli prime minister, \uc2 Benjamin Netanyahu\uc2 , to Washington for an official visit, according to a statement from Netanyahu\u8217\'20\'19s office.\par \par \uc2 The two leaders shared a \u8220\'20\'1Clong and warm\u8221\'20\'1D conversation where they discussed curbing threats from Iran and its proxies and strengthening the alliance between the two countries, the Israeli statement said.\par \par \uc2 The invitation comes more than seven months after Netanyahu was sworn in as prime minister. The delay was viewed as a major snub from Biden, as most Israeli prime ministers had already received an invitation to the White House this far into their terms.\par \par \uc2 The phone call between the two leaders took place as Israeli president, \uc2 Isaac Herzog\uc2 , is traveling to Washington for meetings with Biden and to address a joint address to Congress.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.53pm BST\par \par \uc2 Ohio secretary of state \uc2 Frank LaRose\uc2  formally announced his candidacy for \uc2 US Senate\uc2  today, becoming the third prominent Republican hoping to challenge Democratic incumbent \uc2 Sherrod Brown\uc2  in 2024.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s official: I\u8217\'20\'19m running,\u8221\'20\'1D LaRose said on \uc2 Twitter\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 I\u8217\'20\'19m on a mission to give back to the state that has given me so much. To continue to serve the country I love and fight to protect the values we share. That\u8217\'20\'19s why I\u8217\'20\'19m running to serve as your next United States senator.\par \par \uc2 enltrIt's official: I'm running. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/YEs89T9uU4"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/YEs89T9uU4}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 \uc2 Frank LaRose\uc2  (@FrankLaRose) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/FrankLaRose/status/1680883793140350976?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 July 17, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 LaRose, Ohio\u8217\'20\'19s secretary of state since 2019, is the third major candidate to jump into the primary to take on Brown. He follows Bernie Moreno, a businessman running with \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s encouragement, and state senator \uc2 Matt Dolan\uc2 , whose family owns the \uc2 Cleveland Guardians\uc2  baseball team.\par \par \uc2 Ohio\u8217\'20\'19s Senate race looks to be one of the most competitive in the country next year, alongside races in Arizona, Montana and West Virginia. The state backed Trump in the 2016 and 2020 elections.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.43pm BST\par \par \uc2 New York mayor \uc2 Eric Adams\uc2  has appointed Edward Caban as the first Hispanic officer to lead the city\u8217\'20\'19s police department in its 178-year history.\par \par \uc2 Adams announced the appointment of Caban, 55, in a morning news conference outside the 40th Precinct in the South Bronx, where Caban began his career as an officer in 1991.\par \par \uc2 Caban had been instrumental to the \uc2 NYPD\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s efforts to decrease crime after the Covid-19 pandemic, Mayor Adams said, noting that major crimes are down across the city this summer. He added:\par \par \uc2 Commissioner Caban is truly one of New York\u8217\'20\'19s finest, a leader who understands the importance of both safety and justice.\par \par \uc2 enltrEdward Caban is sworn in as the first Latino officer to lead the \uc2 New York Police Department\uc2  in its 177-year history. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/6Kpj9fgHQj"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/6Kpj9fgHQj}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 The Recount (@therecount) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/therecount/status/1680953299363680258?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 July 17, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 Caban stepped in as acting police chief after the surprise resignation of \uc2 Keechant Sewell\uc2 , the first woman to lead the department, last month.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.30pm BST\par \par \uc2 Florida governor and 2024 Republican presidential candidate \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2  has reduced campaign staff as his campaign has struggled to meet fundraising goals.\par \par \uc2 Fewer than 10 staffers were laid off, according to an anonymous staffer, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.politico.com/news/2023/07/15/desantis-campaign-sheds-staff-amid-cash-crunch-00106485"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reported}}}\uc2  Politico. The staffers were involved in event planning and may be picked up by the pro-DeSantis super Pac Never Back Down. Two senior campaign advisers, Dave Abrams and Tucker Obenshain, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.politico.com/news/2023/07/14/two-senior-desantis-advisers-are-leaving-to-help-run-outside-effort-00106422"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 left}}}\uc2  the campaign this past week to assist a pro-DeSantis nonprofit group.\par \par \uc2 Sources within the campaign reported an internal assessment that the campaign hired too many staffers too early.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThey never should have brought so many people on; the burn rate was way too high,\u8221\'20\'1D said one Republican source familiar with the campaign\u8217\'20\'19s thought process to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nbcnews.com/politics/2024-election/ron-desantis-fires-roughly-dozen-staffers-campaign-shake-rcna94470"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 NBC News}}}\uc2 . \u8220\'20\'1CPeople warned the campaign manager but she wanted to hear none of it.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 More shake-ups within the campaign are expected in the coming weeks after two months on the presidential campaign, with DeSantis still lagging substantially in second place behind former president {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/donaldtrump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Donald Trump}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Even in DeSantis\u8217\'20\'19s home state of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/florida"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Florida}}}\uc2 , Trump still has a 20-point lead over the governor, according to a recent \uc2 Florida Atlantic University\uc2  poll.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.22pm BST\par \par \uc2 House Democrats plan resolution to censure George Santos\par \par \uc2 House Democrats plan to unveil a resolution to formally censure Republican congressman George Santos for lying to voters about his education, work history and family background.\par \par \uc2 The resolution from Representative \uc2 Ritchie Torres\uc2  will be privileged, meaning that the Republican-controlled House must act on it, NBC News {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nbcnews.com/politics/congress/democrats-prepare-vote-censure-rep-george-santos-rcna94681"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  reported. }}}\par \par \uc2 The measure faces long odds of passing in the House, but Democrats believe forcing a vote will help maintain political pressure on Republican leaders who have stood by the embattled New York congressman in the face of a 13-count federal indictment, the \uc2 New York Times{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/2023/07/17/nyregion/george-santos-censure-democrats.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reported. }}}\par \par \uc2 Santos has \u8220\'20\'1Cdisgraced [Congress], and the institution should speak with one voice against his misconduct,\u8221\'20\'1D said Torres, who wrote the resolution.\par \par \uc2 US congressman George Santos of New York. Photograph: J Scott Applewhite/AP\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 6.58pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.56pm BST\par \par \uc2 Lawsuit filed in Iowa to block Republicans\u8217\'20\'19 six-week \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  providers in Iowa have filed a lawsuit to block state Republicans\u8217\'20\'19 latest attempt to ban the procedure after six weeks of pregnancy, before most people even know they are pregnant.\par \par \uc2 Last week, Iowa lawmakers passed a six-week ban on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  in a rare special legislative session, called by Governor \uc2 Kim Reynolds\uc2 , who signed the bill on Friday afternoon. The law takes immediate effect, further shrinking the options available to people seeking abortions in the midwest. Reynolds said on Friday:\par \par \uc2 In a rare and historic special session, the Iowa legislature voted for a second time to reject the inhumanity of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  and pass the fetal heartbeat law.\par \par \uc2 The move to restrict \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  in Iowa came less than one month after a deadlocked state supreme court blocked enforcement of a near-identical six-week ban. Reproductive justice advocates across the country condemned Reynolds\u8217\'20\'19 decision to call a special session on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CEvery dirty trick in the book is being used to pass these extremely unpopular \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  bans,\u8221\'20\'1D said \uc2 Kimberly Inez McGuire\uc2 , executive director of Unite for Reproductive & Gender Equity (Urge), a progressive advocacy group that supports \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/jul/17/iowa-six-week-abortion-ban-lawsuit-filed"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Read the full story here.}}}\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/jul/17/iowa-six-week-abortion-ban-lawsuit-filed"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Lawsuit filed in Iowa to block Republicans\u8217\'20\'19 six-week \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  ban}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 6.35pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.44pm BST\par \par \uc2 Democratic Senator \uc2 Chris Murphy\uc2  of Connecticut has warned that it is \u8220\'20\'1C100% certain\u8221\'20\'1D that the Republicans will pass a national \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban if they win Congress next year.\par \par \uc2 Murphy, tweeting this morning, was responding to the approval in the Republican-led House of Representatives of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/jul/14/republicans-house-defense-bill-abortion-lgbt-rights-diversity"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a huge defense bill}}}\uc2  that includes amendments overturning the Pentagon\u8217\'20\'19s policies on covering \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  services for the military. He said:\par \par \uc2 If you didn\u8217\'20\'19t know already, if Republicans win control of the House and Senate in 2024, they are going to pass a national \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban. It\u8217\'20\'19s 100% certain. Just so we\u8217\'20\'19re clear about the stakes.\par \par \uc2 enltrIf you didn\u8217\'20\'19t know already, if Republicans win control of the House and Senate in 2024, they are going to pass a national \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban. It\u8217\'20\'19s 100% certain.\par \par \uc2 Just so we\u8217\'20\'19re clear about the stakes. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/Nq8ItTDq6D"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/Nq8ItTDq6D}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 \uc2 Chris Murphy\uc2  ?? (@ChrisMurphyCT) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/ChrisMurphyCT/status/1680920611005014016?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 July 17, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.27pm BST\par \par \uc2 Republican presidential candidate \uc2 Vivek Ramaswamy\uc2  announced a list of candidates he would nominate to the supreme court if he were elected.\par \par \uc2 Ramaswamy\u8217\'20\'19s list includes Senator Ted Cruz of Texas and Senator \uc2 Mike Lee\uc2  of Utah as possible nominees for the nation\u8217\'20\'19s top court, as well as federal judges behind the contentious rulings on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  pills and \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s airplane mask mandate.\par \par \uc2 The list makes Ramaswamy the first in the GOP\u8217\'20\'19s field to itemize his possible top judicial appointments. \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  in the 2016 primary released his own list of possible appointments to the high court.\par \par \uc2 In an interview, Ramaswamy said he was releasing the list of possible appointments to show voters where he stood. He said:\par \par \uc2 It\u8217\'20\'19s important, when you\u8217\'20\'19re asking voters to select the next president of the United States, that you be as transparent as you can about what you\u8217\'20\'19re going to do.\par \par \uc2 Ramaswamy remains a long shot to be the Republican nominee, Axios {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.axios.com/2023/07/17/ramaswamy-supreme-court-picks-conservative"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 writes, }}}\uc2  but his list signals that as president he\u8217\'20\'19d seek to bend the court further to the right.\par \par \uc2 Republican presidential candidate businessman \uc2 Vivek Ramaswamy\uc2 . Photograph: Charlie Neibergall/AP\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.06pm BST\par \par \uc2 No Labels says presidential candidates will have full autonomy over platform\par \par \uc2 The bipartisan No Labels group has said any presidential candidates nominated at next year\u8217\'20\'19s convention will have full autonomy to create their own policy platforms.\par \par \uc2 This means that the group\u8217\'20\'19s Common Sense\u8221\'20\'1D document, released over the weekend and outlining broad statements of principle, is little more than a starting point to spur more debate.\par \par \uc2 The 63-page {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.commonsensemajority.org/_files/ugd/9f0726_a8092681d4cc40ae8623b98b83d3853d.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  document}}}\uc2  claims to be a \u8220\'20\'1Cblueprint for where America\u8217\'20\'19s common sense majority wants the country to go.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 Washington Post{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.washingtonpost.com/politics/2023/07/15/no-labels-platform/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reports:}}}\par \par \uc2 Many of the proposals in the No Labels plan are long-standing ideas that have not yet found majority support in Washington: a bipartisan deficit reduction commission that would produce a plan that Congress had to vote on without amendment. Tort restructuring to restrict medical malpractice lawsuits. More price transparency for hospital bills, and patent restructuring to encourage generic biologic drug production.\par \par \uc2 Other proposals have for years been blocked in the \uc2 U.S. Senate\uc2 , like a plan for universal background checks for gun purchases, a plan to ban gun purchases by anyone under the age of 21 and a plan to provide a path to citizenship for undocumented migrants brought to the United States as children.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 6.59pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.47pm BST\par \par \uc2 West Virginia Senator \uc2 Joe Manchin\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s decision to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/jul/17/manchin-third-party-biden-trump-2024-live-updates?page=with:block-64b540c88f08742a26fe8e2c#block-64b540c88f08742a26fe8e2c"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 headline an event}}}\uc2  for No Labels is causing a stir among Democrats who are worried that he might declare a third-party presidential run.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CJoe is America\u8217\'20\'19s biggest political tease,\u8221\'20\'1D Democrat Senator \uc2 Dick Durbin{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://thehill.com/homenews/senate/4098396-manchin-stokes-speculation-with-no-labels-event/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  told}}}\uc2  The Hill.\par \par \uc2 I trust that he\u8217\'20\'19ll make a judgment to run for reelection in West Virginia. I hope he will.\par \par \uc2 Polls show a third-party bid by a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/jul/17/manchin-third-party-biden-trump-2024-live-updates?page=with:block-64b54c128f08de0be01a5bef#block-64b54c128f08de0be01a5bef"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 No Labels candidate}}}\uc2  could create a real headache for \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 . The Hill cited Senator \uc2 Chris Van Hollen\uc2  as saying:\par \par \uc2 It\u8217\'20\'19s pretty clear that a No Labels candidate would help reelect \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , and I hope anybody who considers it recognizes that that\u8217\'20\'19s a very possible outcome.\par \par \uc2 That path is not a path to winning. It\u8217\'20\'19s a path to spoiling the election for \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  and electing \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.36pm BST\par \par \uc2 The chair of the US Congressional Progressive Caucus apologised for calling Israel a \u8220\'20\'1Cracist state\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI offer my apologies to those who I have hurt with my words,\u8221\'20\'1D \uc2 Pramila Jayapal\uc2  of Washington state {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/RepJayapal/status/1680679681446559746/photo/1"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 said}}}\uc2  in a statement on Sunday.\par \par \uc2 The day before, at Netroots Nation, a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.politico.com/news/2023/07/14/netroots-nation-2023-00106429"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 progressive event}}}\uc2  in Chicago, Jayapal addressed a group of pro-Palestinian protesters. She said:\par \par \uc2 As somebody that\u8217\'20\'19s been in the streets and has participated in a lot of demonstrations, I think I want you to know that we have been fighting to make it clear that Israel is a racist state.\par \par \uc2 Jayapal also said \u8220\'20\'1Cthe Palestinian people deserve self-determination and autonomy\u8221\'20\'1D and that \u8220\'20\'1Cthe dream of a two-state solution is slipping away from us\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Pramila Jayapal\uc2  speaks in Washington DC on 24 May. Photograph: Anadolu Agency/Getty Images\par \par \uc2 Republican and pro-Israel groups {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/rncresearch/status/1680327553586741248?s=46&utm_source=Sailthru&utm_medium=email&utm_campaign=7/17/23%20%20Punchbowl%20News%20AM&utm_term=Punchbowl%20AM%20and%20Active%20Subscribers%20from%20Memberful%20Combined"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 seized}}}\uc2  on the comments. Ahead of a week in which the president of Israel, \uc2 Isaac Herzog\uc2 , will {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.jpost.com/israel-news/article-750270"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 address Congress}}}\uc2 , Democratic House leaders also rebuked Jayapal.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIsrael is not a racist state,\u8221\'20\'1D a statement from the leaders {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/JakeSherman/status/1680722926767685633/photo/1"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 said}}}\uc2 , noting the \u8220\'20\'1Cuniquely special relationship\u8221\'20\'1D between the US and Israel.\par \par \uc2 Democratic leaders also said they \u8220\'20\'1Cstrongly support[ed] Israel\u8217\'20\'19s right to exist as a homeland for the Jewish people\u8221\'20\'1D while remaining \u8220\'20\'1Cfirmly committed to a robust two-state solution where Israel and the Palestinian people can live side-by-side in peace and prosperity\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/jul/17/pramila-jayapal-israel-racist-state-apology"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Read the full story here.}}}\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/jul/17/pramila-jayapal-israel-racist-state-apology"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  Progressive US congresswoman apologises for calling Israel \u8216\'20\'18racist state\u8217\'20\'19}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.58pm BST\par \par \uc2 The bipartisan No Labels group is building up a head of steam as it hopes to field a \u8220\'20\'1Cunity\u8221\'20\'1D candidate for the 2024 presidential election, and it\u8217\'20\'19s described as {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/2023/05/19/us/politics/no-labels-president-manchin.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 well-funded}}}\uc2  even though it\u8217\'20\'19s not clear where a lot of the money is coming from.\par \par \uc2 But will it fall between two stools? An analysis piece in the \uc2 New York Times\uc2  assesses that the group has, in effect, something for everyone to like \u8211\'20\'13 or dislike\u8230\'20\'26..\par \par \uc2 The {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/2023/07/15/us/politics/no-labels-presidential-run.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 newspaper reports}}}\uc2  :\par \par \uc2 A new {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.commonsensemajority.org/_files/ugd/9f0726_a8092681d4cc40ae8623b98b83d3853d.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 political platform focused on cooperative governance}}}\uc2  by the bipartisan group No Labels has something for everyone to embrace \u8212\'20\'14 and just as much for both sides to reject.\par \par \uc2 For example, the government must stop \u8220\'20\'1Creleasing\u8221\'20\'1D undocumented migrants into the country, it maintains. But the government must also broaden legal immigration channels and offer a path to citizenship to those brought to the country as children.\par \par \uc2 Or this one: The constitutional right to bear arms is inviolable but must be tempered with universal background checks and age restrictions on the purchase of military-style semiautomatic rifles.\par \par \uc2 Then there is this: A woman must have a right to control her reproductive health, but that right has to be balanced with society\u8217\'20\'19s obligation to safeguard human life.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/2023/05/19/us/politics/no-labels-president-manchin.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 No Labels\u8217\'20\'19 possible third-party challenge}}}\uc2  for the presidency next year has drawn fire from liberals, centrists and even some members of Congress who support the group\u8217\'20\'19s principles but fear that their efforts \u8212\'20\'14 based on the seemingly high-minded ideals of national unity \u8212\'20\'14 could greatly damage President Biden\u8217\'20\'19s re-election campaign and hand the White House back to \uc2 Donald J. Trump\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 But at an event on Monday, the group will formally release what it calls a \u8220\'20\'1Ccommon sense\u8221\'20\'1D proposal for a centrist White House, in hopes of shifting the conversation from the politics of its potential presidential bid to the actual policies that it believes can unite the country and temper the partisanship of the major party nominees. If the ideas do not take political flight, or if one or both of the parties adopt many of the proposals the group\u8217\'20\'19s leaders say no challenge will be necessary.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.28pm BST\par \par \uc2 Democrats fear \uc2 Joe Manchin\uc2 , No Labels could hand White House back to Trump\par \par \uc2 West Virginia Senator \uc2 Joe Manchin\uc2  is headlining today at the event in New Hampshire organized by No Labels, the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/apr/25/arizona-third-parties-2024-elections"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 third party outfit}}}\uc2  that promotes itself as \u8220\'20\'1Cmiddle of the road\u8221\'20\'1D or \u8220\'20\'1Ccommon sense\u8221\'20\'1D and hopes to get on the ballot in 50 states for the 2024 presidential election with a \u8220\'20\'1Cunity ticket\u8221\'20\'1D, much to the Democratic Party\u8217\'20\'19s chagrin.\par \par \uc2 No Labels has {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.bostonglobe.com/2023/07/17/nation/no-labels-new-hampshire-third-party-joe-manchin/?event=event12"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 been around}}}\uc2  for more than a decade but is coming closer to full disrupter status now, despite being little known or understood outside political insiders.\par \par \uc2 Manchin has not declared yet whether he will run for reelection.\par \par \uc2 If he ran for the presidency as a No Labels candidate, it could not only split the Democratic vote in a way that gives the White House to the Republicans in 2024 but also hands the party his crucial seat in what is currently a finely-balanced Senate where the Democrats have a very narrow majority.\par \par \uc2 Manchin will appear today alongside former Utah governor and Republican presidential candidate \uc2 Jon Huntsman\uc2 , at St Anselm College in the first of a series of so-called common sense town halls No Labels is hosting, the Hill {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://thehill.com/homenews/senate/4098396-manchin-stokes-speculation-with-no-labels-event/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reports}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Joe Manchin\uc2  (left) talks with right-wing Alabama Senator Tommy Tuberville on Capitol Hill on July 11, 2023. Photograph: Kevin Wurm/Reuters\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.07pm BST\par \par \uc2 Joe Manchin\uc2  appearance at 'No Labels' event to stoke turmoil\par \par \uc2 Good morning, US politics live blog readers, there\u8217\'20\'19s a lot of action outside of Washington, DC, today \u8211\'20\'13 although still involving national politics and, specifically, the 2024 presidential election. Here\u8217\'20\'19s what\u8217\'20\'19s on the agenda:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 No Labels, the moderate group angling to get a foothold as a third party presidential force in US politics, is {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cnn.com/2023/07/17/politics/joe-manchin-new-hampshire-third-party/index.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 meeting in New Hampshire}}}\uc2  today and \uc2 Joe Manchin\uc2 , West Virginia\u8217\'20\'19s conservative Democratic US Senator, is taking part in a town hall. The Democratic Party worries that if Manchin, who\u8217\'20\'19s up for re-election, decided to run for president {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.bostonglobe.com/2023/05/05/nation/how-joe-manchin-could-upend-the-2024-presidential-race/?p1=Article_Inline_Text_Link"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 on a No Labels ticket}}}\uc2 , it would upend the 2024 election, split the Democratic vote and hand the White Houses back to \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 White House press secretary \uc2 Karine Jean-Pierre\uc2  is scheduled to conduct the daily media briefing in the West Wing at 3pm ET.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s apparent appetite for greater authoritarianism in the US if he is in power will translate in 2025 if he\u8217\'20\'19s won the White House into a plan for a \u8220\'20\'1Csweeping expansion of presidential power over the machinery of government, reshaping the structure of the executive branch to concentrate far greater authority directly in his hands,\u8221\'20\'1D {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/2023/07/17/us/politics/trump-plans-2025.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 according to the New York Times}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 US climate envoy \uc2 John Kerry\uc2  is {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/environment/2023/jul/17/us-climate-envoy-kerry-meets-chinese-counterpart-amid-record-heat"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 in Beijing}}}\uc2  meeting his Chinese counterpart, as both countries grapple with record high temperatures and punishing heatwaves driven by the human-caused climate crisis. We are currently running an extreme weather live blog and you can follow all the weather and climate developments {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/environment/live/2023/jul/17/europe-heatwave-2023-us-asia-heat-extreme-severe-weather-fires-flash-floods-flooding-record-breaking-heat-wave-stress-temperature-red-alert-climate-crisis"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 here}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020230717ej7h001mo\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
