\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Lawsuit filed in Iowa to block Republicans\u8217\'20\'19 six-week  \highlight22\uc2 abortion \highlight\uc2  ban\b0\par\par\uc2 Ava Sasani \par \uc2 994 \uc2 words\par \uc2 17 July 2023\par 13:46 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  providers filed suit after state legislature\u8217\'20\'19s recent special session in which restriction was passed with governor\u8217\'20\'19s blessing\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  providers in Iowa have filed a lawsuit to block state Republicans\u8217\'20\'19 latest attempt to ban the procedure after six weeks of pregnancy, before most people even know they are pregnant.\par \par \uc2 Last week, Iowa lawmakers passed a six-week ban on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  in a rare special legislative session, called by Governor \uc2 Kim Reynolds\uc2 , who signed the bill on Friday afternoon. The law takes immediate effect, further shrinking the options available to people seeking abortions in the midwest.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIn a rare and historic special session, the Iowa legislature voted for a second time to reject the inhumanity of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  and pass the fetal heartbeat law,\u8221\'20\'1D Reynolds said on Friday.\par \par \uc2 The move to restrict \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  in Iowa came less than one month after a deadlocked state supreme court blocked enforcement of a near-identical six-week ban. Reproductive justice advocates across the country condemned Reynolds\u8217\'20\'19 decision to call a special session on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CEvery dirty trick in the book is being used to pass these extremely unpopular \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  bans,\u8221\'20\'1D said \uc2 Kimberly Inez McGuire\uc2 , executive director of Unite for Reproductive & Gender Equity (Urge), a progressive advocacy group that supports \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThey don\u8217\'20\'19t want to do it in the light of day, that\u8217\'20\'19s why we\u8217\'20\'19re seeing these special sessions, that\u8217\'20\'19s why we\u8217\'20\'19re seeing bans passed in the middle of the night,\u8221\'20\'1D she added.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  providers in Iowa said they were unsurprised that the state GOP used a unique legislative tool for the sole purpose of restricting reproductive freedom. Francine Thompson, executive director of the Emma Goldman Clinic \u8211\'20\'13 one of two \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  providers in Iowa and a plaintiff in the new lawsuit \u8211\'20\'13 said the ban\u8217\'20\'19s passage was expected yet appalling.\par \par \uc2 She said there was a cruel irony to the timing of the governor\u8217\'20\'19s announcement of the special session, which came just after Independence Day, \u8220\'20\'1Ca day we typically associate with celebrating our freedom from oppressive and tyrannical governments\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Staff at the Emma Goldman Clinic spent hours this week on the phones with nervous patients confused by the legal status of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  in Iowa.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CSince Dobbs, the phone lines are always jammed,\u8221\'20\'1D Thompson said. \u8220\'20\'1CThe most recent calls are not really in an attempt to get seen before the law goes into effect, but are clients seeking information to wade through the chaos of rapidly changing access and the myriad of restrictions in surrounding states.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The six-week ban is confusing, in part, because it closely resembles a 2018 law that was blocked by an Iowa district judge years before Roe v Wade was overturned. Earlier this year, Reynolds asked the Iowa supreme court to reverse the district judge\u8217\'20\'19s decision. The state justices split 3-3, leaving the lower court\u8217\'20\'19s order in place, meaning the 2018 ban remains unenforceable.\par \par \uc2 The lawsuit against the new six-week ban is expected to reach the Iowa supreme court, which last year ruled that the state constitution does not guarantee the right to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 But last month, the 3-3 deadlock happened after one justice, Dana Oxley, opted to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.brennancenter.org/our-work/analysis-opinion/justices-spar-over-judicial-and-legislative-power-iowa-abortion-ruling"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 recuse herself}}}\uc2  from the case because of a conflict of interest with her old law firm. It is unclear if Justice Oxley will recuse herself again, causing another split ruling.\par \par \uc2 Iowa Republican lawmakers might not care about the outcome of the legal battle. They win political points with their core, conservative voter base simply by reconvening at the state capital to pass an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CBecause of gerrymandering, Iowa Republicans aren\u8217\'20\'19t really worried about losing to a Democrat, but they are at a real risk of being primaried,\u8221\'20\'1D said Mary Ziegler, a law professor at \uc2 University of California, Davis\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 If the ban is struck down, Republicans can blame the courts, a convenient boogeyman in the tug-of-war over state \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  law. The good-faith attempt to pass a six-week ban is enough to reassure anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  lobbying groups and socially conservative donors.\par \par \uc2 Ziegler said ideological posturing is especially important for Governor Reynolds ahead of the Iowa caucus, which helps select the Republican presidential nominee. Reynolds\u8217\'20\'19 endorsement could therefore change the future of her party.\par \par \uc2 But first, Ziegler said, the governor \u8220\'20\'1Cneeds to prove her conservative credentials\u8221\'20\'1D on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Reynolds signed the ban at the Family Leadership Summit, a gathering of evangelical Christians and social conservatives in Des Moines. The event attracted 2024 Republican presidential hopefuls such as Florida\u8217\'20\'19s governor, \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2 , and the former vice-president \uc2 Mike Pence\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Just as Reynolds was signing the six-week ban, attorneys for \uc2 Planned Parenthood\uc2  and the Emma Goldman Clinic asked an Iowa judge to temporarily block the six-week ban from taking effect while litigation proceeds. That decision is expected this week.\par \par \uc2 Dr Emily Boevers, an Iowa OB-GYN at one of the state\u8217\'20\'19s last remaining rural hospitals, braced for an anxious weekend. She volunteers her weekends providing \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  care at the \uc2 Planned Parenthood\uc2  clinic in Iowa City, though she does not offer abortions in her everyday work at the hospital.\par \par \uc2 Boevers is one of two OB-GYNs in her home county \u8211\'20\'13 the other is expected to retire this fall. She is worried that the six-week ban could drive doctors in her specialty out of Iowa, worsening the region\u8217\'20\'19s existing shortage of maternal healthcare providers.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CNorth of me, there is not another hospital for 50 miles,\u8221\'20\'1D said Boevers.\par \par \uc2 She said the criminalization of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  brings \u8220\'20\'1Ca level of hostility towards obstetric care in all its components\u8221\'20\'1D that will \u8220\'20\'1Cinvariably harm\u8221\'20\'1D the already dwindling OB-GYN workforce in Iowa.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CForcing experts in women\u8217\'20\'19s health to withhold care from our patients, it goes against many of our moral codes,\u8221\'20\'1D Boevers said. \u8220\'20\'1CAs an obstetrician-gynecologist, I trust my patients to make the best decision for their situation.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020230717ej7h0013f\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
