\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Republican congresswoman accused of hypocrisy for anti- \highlight22\uc2 abortion \highlight\uc2  vote\b0\par\par\uc2 Richard Luscombe \par \uc2 622 \uc2 words\par \uc2 15 July 2023\par 15:13 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Nancy Mace calls measure to block reimbursement of travel costs for military seeking procedure \u8216\'20\'18asshole move\u8217\'20\'19 then votes for it\par \par \uc2 The fallout from the decision by House Republicans to include a divisive anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  measure in Friday\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/jul/14/republicans-house-defense-bill-abortion-lgbt-rights-diversity"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 defense spending vote }}}\uc2  has snared the South Carolina congresswoman Nancy Mace, who has been accused of hypocrisy for voting for it.\par \par \uc2 On Thursday, Mace, who has frequently been {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://abcnews.go.com/Politics/nancy-mace-republicans-lose-huge-middle-ground-abortion/story?id=98777224"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 at odds with her party }}}\uc2  over its \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  stance, launched a profanity-laced tirade apparently against the inclusion of an amendment that would block the reimbursement of travel costs for military members who seek the procedure.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s an asshole move, an asshole amendment,\u8221\'20\'1D she told aides in an elevator, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.politico.com/newsletters/huddle/2023/07/14/a-hole-abortion-vote-roils-gops-defense-bill-plans-00106329"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 according to Politico }}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe should not be taking this fucking vote, man. Fuck.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 She voted for it anyway. Then in an appearance on Friday night on CNN Primetime she struggled to explain herself, attempting to portray herself as consistent on the issue of opposing reimbursements for elective surgeries for those in the military, while claiming that servicewomen would still be able to get an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CNothing in here would prohibit a woman from traveling out of state to follow state law,\u8221\'20\'1D Mace said, reported {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.thedailybeast.com/gop-rep-nancy-mace-flip-flops-on-asshole-abortion-bill-just-travel"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 by the Daily Beast }}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CSo I think that\u8217\'20\'19s, you know, a really important message. Nothing would prohibit her from being able to do that. There are no limits on her travel.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Pressed by the host, Kaitlan Collins, who used Mace\u8217\'20\'19s own words to question why Republicans were being \u8220\'20\'1Cassholes\u8221\'20\'1D to women, and pointing out access to an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  for a woman stationed in Texas was more difficult than for one in New York, the congresswomen admitted she was uncomfortable.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI did not like the idea of this amendment. These are not issues that I believe we should be voting on right now without some consideration of what we can do to protect women and show that we\u8217\'20\'19re pro-women, which has been my frustration for the better part of the last seven months,\u8221\'20\'1D she said.\par \par \uc2 Mace went further in an appearance on Fox News on Friday night, suggesting that her party\u8217\'20\'19s control of the House could be threatened by its position on issues such as \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  that do not align with public sentiment.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe vast majority of Americans aren\u8217\'20\'19t with us,\u8221\'20\'1D she said.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CNinety per cent of America is somewhere in the middle, especially on women\u8217\'20\'19s rights, and we have to show that even if we\u8217\'20\'19re pro-life, we care about women, and we\u8217\'20\'19ve yet to do that this year.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CInstead of playing these games with whatever woke means, whatever the flavor of the day for woke is that day, we\u8217\'20\'19ve got to be balanced to show that we actually care about women.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe can do both at the same time. And with my colleagues that are forcing some of these votes on these amendments, it makes it very difficult for us to hold on to the majority.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The defense bill, which passed the House 219-210 mostly on party lines, included other controversial amendments covering healthcare costs for transgender service members and diversity initiatives.\par \par \uc2 The bill is seen as dead on arrival in the Senate, where Democrats hold the majority, and another example of rightwingers in Republican ranks exerting their influence over the House speaker, Kevin McCarthy, in an attempt to change a number of the Biden administration\u8217\'20\'19s policy goals.\par \par \uc2 Mace told Fox: \u8220\'20\'1CEvery single Democrat knows that if there\u8217\'20\'19s an amendment they don\u8217\'20\'19t like, it\u8217\'20\'19s going to get tossed out in the Senate. So this is really just sort of political gamesmanship, political theater.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020230715ej7f001e1\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
