\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s legal team urges Georgia court to block 2020 election investigation \u8211\'20\'13 as it happened\b0\par\par\uc2 Chris Stein US politics live blogger \par \uc2 4,939 \uc2 words\par \uc2 14 July 2023\par 20:04 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Lawyers for former US president ask Georgia\u8217\'20\'19s highest court to prevent district attorney from prosecuting him\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.03pm BST\par \par \uc2 Closing summary\par \par \uc2 Republicans and Democrats in Congress are on a collision course after rightwing lawmakers inserted provisions targeting Pentagon policies on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access, transgender care and diversity into a must-pass defense spending bill that {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/jul/14/tucker-carlson-presidential-forum-missing-trump-defense-bill-republicans-abortion-latest?page=with:block-64b163b78f08ce64897ecd9a#block-64b163b78f08ce64897ecd9a"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 cleared the House}}}\uc2  this morning. Democrats are {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/jul/14/tucker-carlson-presidential-forum-missing-trump-defense-bill-republicans-abortion-latest?page=with:block-64b19aad8f080a06e306006d#block-64b19aad8f080a06e306006d"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 outraged}}}\uc2  that the GOP used the measure, which usually attracts bipartisan support, to push culture war goals, but there\u8217\'20\'19s no word yet on what will become of the legislation when it arrives in the Senate, where \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s allies rule the roost and are unlikely to support attempts to prevent service members from accessing abortions services or gender-affirming care. Expect to hear lots more about this in the days to come.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s what else happened today:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Tucker Carlson\uc2  might be unemployed, but that apparently {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/jul/14/tucker-carlson-presidential-forum-missing-trump-defense-bill-republicans-abortion-latest?page=with:block-64b167268f08df28470046f2#block-64b167268f08df28470046f2"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 has not changed}}}\uc2  his views on US support to Ukraine, as he made clear in an exchange with GOP presidential contender and senator Tim Scott.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Mike Pence\uc2  tried to explain to a rightwing crowd in Iowa why he did not go along with \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s wishes on January 6. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/jul/14/tucker-carlson-presidential-forum-missing-trump-defense-bill-republicans-abortion-latest?page=with:block-64b18b5c8f080a06e305ffcd#block-64b18b5c8f080a06e305ffcd"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 It did not go well}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Speaking of Trump, his lawyers {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/jul/14/tucker-carlson-presidential-forum-missing-trump-defense-bill-republicans-abortion-latest?page=with:block-64b18fc38f08df28470049b8#block-64b18fc38f08df28470049b8"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 are trying}}}\uc2  to stop Atlanta-area prosecutor \uc2 Fani Willis\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s investigation of his campaign to overturn the 2020 election result in Georgia.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 A federal appeals court panel{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/jul/14/tucker-carlson-presidential-forum-missing-trump-defense-bill-republicans-abortion-latest?page=with:block-64b19e308f08df2847004a2e#block-64b19e308f08df2847004a2e"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 blocked a judge\u8217\'20\'19s ruling}}}\uc2  that prevented some Biden administration officials from holding talks with social media companies intended to fight misinformation.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Four House Democrats from swing districts{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/jul/14/tucker-carlson-presidential-forum-missing-trump-defense-bill-republicans-abortion-latest?page=with:block-64b177408f08df284700484c#block-64b177408f08df284700484c"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 crossed party lines}}}\uc2  to support the defense funding bill, while four conservative Republicans opposed it, with one saying it was too expensive.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.59pm BST\par \par \uc2 Former US vice president \uc2 Mike Pence\uc2  earlier at the \uc2 Tucker Carlson\uc2 -anchored event in Iowa, reiterated his disapproval of \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s encouragement on January 6, 2021, of protesters to seek the overturning of the 2020 election results.\par \par \uc2 Having already {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/jul/14/tucker-carlson-presidential-forum-missing-trump-defense-bill-republicans-abortion-latest?page=with:block-64b18b5c8f080a06e305ffcd#block-64b18b5c8f080a06e305ffcd"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 defended his refusal}}}\uc2  to block the certification by the \uc2 US Congress\uc2  of \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s victory, Pence gladly repeated for the highly-pro-Trump crowd his assertions that he\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/CNN/status/1593070517019254785"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 made before}}}\uc2  that Trump\u8217\'20\'19s exhortations (and tweets) on January 6 exhorting the crowd to take action to keep him in office were reckless.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CTrump\u8217\'20\'19s words that day were reckless\u8230\'20\'26whatever his intentions in that moment, it endangered me, my family and everyone else in the Capitol,\u8221\'20\'1D Pence said.\par \par \uc2 He added, as the audience remained eerily quiet: \u8220\'20\'1CThe law will hold him accountable.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 He later added, perhaps in a desperate attempt to win more warmth from the crowd: \u8220\'20\'1CAnd \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  will have no right to overturn the election when we beat them in 2024.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Tucker Carlson\uc2  (left) and \uc2 Mike Pence\uc2  (right) at an event in Des Moines earlier today. Photograph: Charlie Neibergall/AP\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.35pm BST\par \par \uc2 The now-stayed federal judge\u8217\'20\'19s ruling restricting how some Biden administration officials may interact with social media companies was evidence of a \u8220\'20\'1Cweaponization of the court\u8221\'20\'1D that benefits pedalers of misinformation, an expert on combating such lies told the \uc2 Guardian\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/edpilkington"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Ed Pilkington}}}\uc2  earlier this month:\par \par \uc2 Restricting the ability of the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/biden-administration"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Biden administration}}}\uc2  to work with social media companies in countering online conspiracy theories is a \u8220\'20\'1Cweaponisation of the court system\u8221\'20\'1D that could devastate the fight against misinformation ahead of the 2024 presidential election, a leading expert has warned.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/media/2023/may/19/fox-news-lawsuit-nina-jankowicz"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Nina Jankowicz}}}\uc2 , a specialist in disinformation campaigns, told the Guardian that an injunction imposed by a federal judge on Tuesday against key federal agencies and officials blocking their communication with tech platforms could unleash false information in critical areas of public life. She said that election denialism and anti-vaccine propaganda could be the beneficiaries.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThis is a weaponisation of the court system. It is an intentional and purposeful move to disrupt the work that needs to be done ahead of the 2024 election, and it\u8217\'20\'19s really chilling,\u8221\'20\'1D she said.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/jul/05/biden-social-media-injunction-lawsuit"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Limits on Biden officials working with social media firms a \u8216\'20\'18weaponisation of the court\u8217\'20\'19 \u8211\'20\'13 expert}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.17pm BST\par \par \uc2 Appeals court stays ruling restricting talks between Biden administration, social media firms\par \par \uc2 A federal appeals court has stayed {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/jul/04/judge-restricts-white-house-communications-with-social-media-companies"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a judge\u8217\'20\'19s ruling from earlier this month}}}\uc2  that put limits on how certain White House officials could interact with social media companies, Reuters reports.\par \par \uc2 The lower court\u8217\'20\'19s ruling in response to a lawsuit from Republican attorneys general in Louisiana and Missouri {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/jul/05/biden-social-media-injunction-lawsuit"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 complicated efforts}}}\uc2  by the Biden administration to work with platforms like \uc2 Facebook\uc2 , \uc2 Twitter\uc2  and \uc2 YouTube\uc2  to address misinformation around elections and the Covid-19 pandemic.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s Reuters reporting from when the lower court\u8217\'20\'19s ruling was first handed down on what it means for the fight against conspiracy theories:\par \par \uc2 The ruling said \uc2 US government\uc2  agencies like the \uc2 Department of Health and Human Services\uc2  and the \uc2 FBI\uc2  could not talk to social media companies for \u8220\'20\'1Cthe purpose of urging, encouraging, pressuring, or inducing in any manner the removal, deletion, suppression, or reduction of content containing protected free speech\u8221\'20\'1D under the free speech clause of the first amendment to the US constitution.\par \par \uc2 A White House official said the US justice department was reviewing the order and will evaluate its options.\par \par \uc2 The order also mentioned by name officials, including the secretary of the \uc2 Department of Homeland Security\uc2 , Alejandro Mayorkas, and Jen Easterly, who heads the \uc2 Cybersecurity and Infrastructure Security Agency\uc2 , in its restrictions.\par \par \uc2 Judge Terry Doughty, in an order filed with the US district court for the western district of Louisiana, made some exceptions for communications between government officials and the companies, including to warn about risks to national security and about criminal activity.\par \par \uc2 The injunction was {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.washingtonpost.com/technology/2023/07/04/biden-social-lawsuit-missouri-louisiana/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 first reported by}}}\uc2  the \uc2 Washington Post\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Tuesday\u8217\'20\'19s order marks a win for Republicans who had sued the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/biden-administration"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Biden administration}}}\uc2 , saying it was using the coronavirus health crisis and the threat of misinformation as an excuse to curb views that disagreed with the government.\par \par \uc2 US officials have said they were aiming to tamp down misinformation about Covid vaccines to curb preventable deaths.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.00pm BST\par \par \uc2 Democratic and Republican lawmakers have plenty to say about the defense spending bill that just passed the House, with one GOP congressman saying his party wanted to use the legislation to align the military\u8217\'20\'19s policies with \u8220\'20\'1Ctraditional America\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Here are Tim Burchett \u8217\'20\'19s comments to CNN:\par \par \uc2 enltrTim Burchett, Republican of Tennessee, on the social policy changes in the defense bill. "When we are getting away from what traditional America believes, traditional America is not going to play ball with you." {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/jRZ2Y7Vurj"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/jRZ2Y7Vurj}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Manu Raju (@mkraju) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/mkraju/status/1679925874613731342?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 July 14, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 Then there\u8217\'20\'19s the ever-puzzling Nancy Mace, a Republican congresswoman from South Carolina who does not seemed pleased with the bill\u8217\'20\'19s provisions barring the Pentagon from paying for service members to travel for abortions, but voted for it anyway:\par \par \uc2 enltrNancy Mace, who voted for defense bill and amendment nixing Pentagon \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  policy: "If we want to show America that we come together and that we care about women, then we got to stop being assholes to women." {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/esxHkSVTq6"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/esxHkSVTq6}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Manu Raju (@mkraju) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/mkraju/status/1679924121109397505?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 July 14, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.39pm BST\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s attorneys are attempting to disrupt Fulton county district attorney \uc2 Fani Willis\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s investigation into the campaign to overturn the 2020 election result in Georgia days after she impaneled two grand juries specifically tasked with deciding who should face charges in her inquiry. Here\u8217\'20\'19s coverage from the Guardian\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/martin-pengelly"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Martin Pengelly}}}\uc2  of that development, from Tuesday:\par \par \uc2 A grand jury selected in Georgia on Tuesday is expected to say whether {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/donaldtrump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Donald Trump}}}\uc2  and associates should face criminal charges over their attempt to overturn the former president\u8217\'20\'19s defeat by \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  in the 2020 election.\par \par \uc2 The district attorney of Fulton county, \uc2 Fani Willis\uc2 , has {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/apr/25/trump-georgia-prosecutor-charges-fani-willis"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 indicated}}}\uc2  she expects to obtain indictments between the end of July and the middle of August. Trump also faces possible federal charges over his election subversion, culminating in his incitement of the deadly January 6 attack on Congress.\par \par \uc2 Trump already {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/jul/11/trump-classified-documents-trial-after-2024-election"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 faces trials}}}\uc2  on 71 criminal charges: 34 in New York over hush money payments to the porn star Stormy Daniels and 37 in Florida, from federal prosecutors and regarding his {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/jul/11/trump-classified-documents-trial-after-2024-election"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 retention of classified documents}}}\uc2  after leaving office.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/jul/11/georgia-jury-trump-2020-criminal-charges-lost-election-overturn"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Georgia grand jury selected in Trump case over attempt to overturn 2020 defeat}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.13pm BST\par \par \uc2 Trump team urges Georgia court to block election investigation\par \par \uc2 Lawyers for former US president \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  are asking Georgia\u8217\'20\'19s highest court to prevent the district attorney who has been investigating his actions in the wake of the 2020 election from prosecuting him and to throw out a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://apnews.com/article/trump-georgia-election-investigation-grand-jury-documents-40535dd2b4401e804af515229c6c2d68"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 special grand jury report}}}\uc2  that is part of the inquiry, the Associated Press reports.\par \par \uc2 AP writes:\par \par \uc2 Fulton County District Attorney \uc2 Fani Willis\uc2  has been investigating since early 2021 whether Trump and his allies broke any laws as they tried to overturn his narrow election loss in Georgia to Democrat \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 . She {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://apnews.com/article/trump-georgia-election-investigation-fani-willis-d6191037a8993d653686e679bf5e8ea5"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 has suggested}}}\uc2  that she is likely to seek charges in the case from a grand jury next month.\par \par \uc2 Trump\u8217\'20\'19s Georgia legal team on Friday filed similar petitions in the Georgia Supreme Court and Fulton County Superior Court naming Willis and Fulton County Superior Court Judge Robert McBurney, who oversaw the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://apnews.com/article/donald-trump-georgia-a66edf8ccbf51924b76d7a4e7fcd1e16"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 special grand jury}}}\uc2 , as respondents. A spokesperson for Willis declined to comment. McBurney did not immediately respond to an email seeking comment.\par \par \uc2 Trump\u8217\'20\'19s legal team \u8212\'20\'14 \uc2 Drew Findling\uc2 , Jennifer Little and Marissa Goldberg \u8212\'20\'14 acknowledged that the filings are unusual but necessary given the tight time frame. Willis has indicated she will use the special grand jury report to seek an indictment \u8220\'20\'1Cwithin weeks, if not days.\u8221\'20\'1D Two new regular grand juries {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://apnews.com/article/trump-georgia-election-investigation-grand-jury-0cfd32492da81697879b8c8ac00f8c83#:~:text=ATLANTA%20(AP)%20%E2%80%94%20A%20grand,2020%20election%20loss%20in%20Georgia."}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 were seated this week}}}\uc2 , and one is likely to hear the case.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CEven in an extraordinarily novel case of national significance, one would expect matters to take their normal procedural course within a reasonable time,\u8221\'20\'1D the filings say. \u8220\'20\'1CBut nothing about these processes have been normal or reasonable. And the all-but-unavoidable conclusion is that the anomalies below are because Petitioner is President \uc2 Donald J. Trump\uc2 .\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.08pm BST\par \par \uc2 GOP crowd underwhelmed as Pence defends Jan 6 stance\par \par \uc2 The sound of silence. Or, to be fair, the whisper of sporadic applause. That\u8217\'20\'19s what just greeted {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/mike-pence"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Mike Pence}}}\uc2  when he again defended his refusal on January 6, 2021, to refuse to block the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/jan/06/congress-certify-election-biden-republicans-object"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 certification by Congress}}}\uc2  of \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s victory over \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The presidential candidate did not impress the right-wing crowd at \uc2 Tucker Carlson\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s event when he said: \u8220\'20\'1CI did my duty\u8221\'20\'1D and upheld the US constitution, after thousands of extreme Trump supporters had invaded the US Capitol in a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/books/2022/oct/02/michael-fanone-capitol-attack-officer-kevin-mccarthy-republicans-trump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 deadly insurrection}}}\uc2  as they tried to overturn {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/ng-interactive/2020/nov/24/us-election-results-2020-joe-biden-defeats-donald-trump-to-win-presidency"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Trump\u8217\'20\'19s defeat}}}\uc2  in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2020/nov/13/us-election-most-secure-history-voter-fraud-false-claim"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the 2020 election}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 A few hands clap. This is hardly surprising, but very interesting to hear live.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s important that we hold those accountable that perpetrated acts of violence in our nation\u8217\'20\'19s Capitol,\u8221\'20\'1D he said, to almost total silence in the hall. He quickly added that there needed to be more vigor in prosecuting people who ended up rioting during the Black Lives Matter protests of 2020. That drew cheers.\par \par \uc2 Carlson asked Pence: \u8220\'20\'1CDo you think the last election was fair?\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 In short, Pence indicated he did. He noted that there were some irregularities and that changes made by states to voting procedures as a result of the Covid-19 pandemic undermined public confidence in the system. But he noted that there were recounts and lawsuits and in the end, in terms of the votes \u8220\'20\'1Cstates certified and courts upheld and ultimately we were able to establish that\u8221\'20\'1D nothing \u8220\'20\'1Cwould change the outcome of the election in any way,\u8221\'20\'1D adding: \u8220\'20\'1CI knew I had to do my duty that day\u8221\'20\'1D when he endorsed the certification of Biden\u8217\'20\'19s victory, in the early hours of January 7, 2021.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.23pm BST\par \par \uc2 Former US vice president \uc2 Mike Pence\uc2  has taken the stage at the event in Iowa hosted by \uc2 Tucker Carlson\uc2 , as he eyes a comeback after being fired from Fox News, a forum together with Blaze Media feature Republican presidential candidates \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2 , Tim Scott, Nikki Haley, \uc2 Vivek Ramaswamy\uc2  and Asa Hutchinson.\par \par \uc2 Pence begins by slamming Biden economic policy, Biden policies at the US-Mexico border and celebrating the Iowa {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/jul/12/iowa-passes-six-week-abortion-ban"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 legislature passing}}}\uc2  a ban on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  after six weeks of pregnancy, when many people don\u8217\'20\'19t even know they\u8217\'20\'19re pregnant.\par \par \uc2 Pence noted the bill will be signed into law later today by Iowa governor \uc2 Kim Reynolds\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Now Pence is talking about the insurrection by extremist supporters of \uc2 Donald Trump{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/us-capitol-breach"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 at the US Capitol}}}\uc2  on January 6, 2021. More in a moment.\par \par \uc2 Mike Pence\uc2  (right) answers questions from event host \uc2 Tucker Carlson\uc2  (left) in Des Moines today. Photograph: Scott Olson/Getty Images\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 6.40pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.13pm BST\par \par \uc2 Interim summary\par \par \uc2 Hello again, US politics live blog readers, it\u8217\'20\'19s been a lively morning and there is more action to come, on Capitol Hill and elsewhere.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s where things stand:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Tucker Carlson\uc2  has been one of the most prominent public skeptics of America\u8217\'20\'19s support for Ukraine\u8217\'20\'19s defense against the Russian invasion, and he\u8217\'20\'19s carrying on in this bent at the event he\u8217\'20\'19s hosting today. \u8220\'20\'1CWhy not force a peace?\u8221\'20\'1D {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/jul/14/tucker-carlson-presidential-forum-missing-trump-defense-bill-republicans-abortion-latest?page=with:block-64b167268f08df28470046f2#block-64b167268f08df28470046f2"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 he asked}}}\uc2  GOP presidential candidate Tim Scott today.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The House{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/jul/14/tucker-carlson-presidential-forum-missing-trump-defense-bill-republicans-abortion-latest?page=with:block-64b163b78f08ce64897ecd9a#block-64b163b78f08ce64897ecd9a"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 approved}}}\uc2  the annual defense bill that rightwing Republicans packed with culture war amendments, including provisions blocking the Pentagon\u8217\'20\'19s policies on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , gender-affirming care and diversity.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The White House today {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/jul/14/tucker-carlson-presidential-forum-missing-trump-defense-bill-republicans-abortion-latest?page=with:block-64b157778f08df28470045a2#block-64b157778f08df28470045a2"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 announced}}}\uc2  it had forgiven $39bn in student loan debt held by 804,000 borrowers after making fixes to a program intended to provide relief for certain people who had been paying for 20 years or more.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 House Democrats accused GOP of \u8216\'20\'18extreme and reckless legislative joyride\u8217\'20\'19 in defense bill. In a joint statement, House minority leader \uc2 Hakeem Jeffries\uc2 , whip Katherine Clark and caucus chair \uc2 Pete Aguilar\uc2  encouraged their members to vote against the NDAA, saying \u8220\'20\'1Cextreme MAGA {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/republicans"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Republicans}}}\uc2  have chosen to hijack\u8221\'20\'1D legislation that is typically passed with bipartisan support.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.32pm BST\par \par \uc2 After House conservatives packed it with culture war amendments, this year\u8217\'20\'19s National Defense Authorization Act (NDAA) passed by a party line vote \u8211\'20\'13 with a few exceptions.\par \par \uc2 Democrats generally opposed the legislation, while Republicans approved it, except for the following crossover votes, as compiled by CNN:\par \par \uc2 enltrCrossover votes in House\u8217\'20\'19s defense bill, which was approved 219-210\par \par \uc2 Four Republican NO votes:\par \par \uc2 Andy Biggs (AZ)\par \par \uc2 Ken Buck\uc2  (CO)\par \par \uc2 Eli Crane (AZ)\par \par \uc2 Tom Massie (KY\par \par \uc2 Four Democratic YES votes:\par \par \uc2 Jared Golden (ME)\par \par \uc2 Donald Davis (NC)\par \par \uc2 Gabriel Vasquez (NM)\par \par \uc2 Marie Glusenkamp Perez (WA)\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Manu Raju (@mkraju) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/mkraju/status/1679883377728446467?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 July 14, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 The four Democrats who voted for it all hail from swing districts, while the four Republicans who opposed it are generally seen as belonging to the party\u8217\'20\'19s right wing.\par \par \uc2 Among the Republican opponents was Colorado\u8217\'20\'19s \uc2 Ken Buck\uc2 , who in a statement cited the legislation\u8217\'20\'19s price tag as the reason he voted against it:\par \par \uc2 enltrMy statement on my vote against the NDAA???? {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/DttHtK85Ij"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/DttHtK85Ij}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Rep. \uc2 Ken Buck\uc2  (@RepKenBuck) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/RepKenBuck/status/1679882656329154566?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 July 14, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.11pm BST\par \par \uc2 Republican House speaker Kevin McCarthy condemned congressman Eli Crane for using {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/jul/14/tucker-carlson-presidential-forum-missing-trump-defense-bill-republicans-abortion-latest?page=with:block-64b1518d8f08df284700452a#block-64b1518d8f08df284700452a"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 an outdated and offensive term}}}\uc2  to refer to African Americans on the House floor:\par \par \uc2 enltrSpeaker Kevin McCarthy, when asked about Rep. Eli Crane (R-AZ) referring to \u8220\'20\'1Ccolored people\u8221\'20\'1D on the House floor Thursday:\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThat's not acceptable. I'll take him at his word that he misspoke. I have never heard him use that before, so you would have to ask him about that.\u8221\'20\'1D {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/8JvkImjHb5"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/8JvkImjHb5}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 The Recount (@therecount) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/therecount/status/1679884435368427520?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 July 14, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 Politico reports that Crane has apologized for using the language:\par \par \uc2 enltrRep. Eli Crane tells me he deeply regrets using the words \u8220\'20\'1Ccolored people\u8221\'20\'1D on the House floor yesterday.\par \par \uc2 Says he misspoke and is sorry that his words hurt people and is mad at himself that it has blown back on his team.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Olivia Beavers (@Olivia_Beavers) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/Olivia_Beavers/status/1679872576124776449?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 July 14, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.51pm BST\par \par \uc2 McCarthy says Republicans 'keep our promises' after passing defense bill\par \par \uc2 Back at the Capitol, Republican speaker of the House Kevin McCarthy is clearly pleased that the chamber passed the National Defense Authorization Act:\par \par \uc2 enltrHouse Speaker Kevin McCarthy touts Republicans passing the National Defense Authorization Act:\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI'm sorry to disappoint you, that Republicans continue to keep our promises.\u8221\'20\'1D {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/20NHPVGx5I"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/20NHPVGx5I}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 The Recount (@therecount) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/therecount/status/1679876525179518977?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 July 14, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 But the battle is not over. Thanks to McCarthy\u8217\'20\'19s alliance with far-right lawmakers in his caucus, the annual bill setting the Pentagon\u8217\'20\'19s budget is packed with culture war provisions such as bans on the department\u8217\'20\'19s policies of reimbursing travel expenses related to abortions, and on providing gender-affirming care to transgender service members.\par \par \uc2 We haven\u8217\'20\'19t heard too much yet from the Senate\u8217\'20\'19s Democratic leaders about these provisions, but don\u8217\'20\'19t be surprised if they declare their opposition to the bill, setting the stage for a major showdown between the two parties in the days and even weeks to come.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 6.28pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.32pm BST\par \par \uc2 Tucker Carlson\uc2  keeps up anti-Ukraine bent in interview with GOP contenders Republican presidential candidate and South Carolina senator Tim Scott (right) speaks during the Family Leadership Summit as moderator \uc2 Tucker Carlson\uc2  (left) looks on. Photograph: Charlie Neibergall/AP\par \par \uc2 During his time on Fox News, and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/media/2023/jun/07/tucker-carlson-twitter-first-show"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 even after}}}\uc2  the conservative network unceremoniously booted him off the airwaves, \uc2 Tucker Carlson\uc2  has been one of the most prominent public skeptics of America\u8217\'20\'19s support for Ukraine\u8217\'20\'19s defense against the Russian invasion.\par \par \uc2 Today, Carlson is interviewing several GOP presidential contenders at the Family Leadership Summit in Des Moines, Iowa. First up was senator Tim Scott, who was quizzed by Carlson on why Washington should continue supporting Ukraine.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CAre you concerned that we\u8217\'20\'19re moving, as we seem to be toward war with Russia?\u8221\'20\'1D Carlson asked, pointing to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.defense.gov/News/News-Stories/Article/Article/3458135/biden-approves-mobilization-of-reserves-to-support-eucom/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 an announcement from the Pentagon yesterday}}}\uc2  that it would call up new reserves for a long-running operation to deter threats against \uc2 Nato\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s eastern flank.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CAmerica\u8217\'20\'19s national, vital interest is degrading the Russian military. When we degrade the Russian military, we make sure that our home front is safer, and that our Nato ally partners that would cause us to send soldiers over is safe,\u8221\'20\'1D Scott replied.\par \par \uc2 But Carlson was dubious. \u8220\'20\'1CWhy not force a peace?\u8221\'20\'1D he asked Scott.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CHow would you do that?\u8221\'20\'1D the senator replied. Carlson then went on to call Ukraine \u8220\'20\'1Ca client state of the United States\u8221\'20\'1D and insist \u8220\'20\'1Cwithout American backing, there\u8217\'20\'19s no Ukraine\u8221\'20\'1D, implying that America could force Kyiv to the negotiating table with Russia.\par \par \uc2 His comments did not appear to sway Scott. \u8220\'20\'1CI think the faster we get the peace, the better off we are. What we don\u8217\'20\'19t want to do from my perspective is allow ourselves to ask for a premature peace that cannot be achieved.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 4.33pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.08pm BST\par \par \uc2 House passes defense bill with conservative amendments on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , transgender care\par \par \uc2 The House has just approved the annual defense bill that rightwing Republicans packed with culture war amendments, including provisions blocking the Pentagon\u8217\'20\'19s policies on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , gender-affirming care and diversity.\par \par \uc2 The vote was mostly party line, with almost all Republicans supporting the measure and most Democrats voting against it, breaking with the tradition of the bill, which sets out the defense department\u8217\'20\'19s yearly budget, passing with bipartisan support:\par \par \uc2 enltrThe House passed H.R. 2670 \u8211\'20\'13 National Defense Authorization Act for Fiscal Year 2024 by a vote of 219-210. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/OB8qJR5HjL"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/OB8qJR5HjL}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 House Press Gallery (@HouseDailyPress) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/HouseDailyPress/status/1679868236135899136?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 July 14, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 It now must be approved by the Senate, where the Democratic majority is unlikely to support any of the rightwing amendments included by the House GOP.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.55pm BST\par \par \uc2 A big question hanging over the 2024 presidential race is when \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s criminal trial over the classified documents found at Mar-a-Lago will be resolved. As the Guardian\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/hugo-lowell"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Hugo Lowell}}}\uc2  reports, prosecutors are trying to fend off an attempt by the former president\u8217\'20\'19s lawyers to delay the proceedings:\par \par \uc2 Federal prosecutors asked the judge presiding over the Mar-a-Lago classified documents case on Thursday to reject {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/donaldtrump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Donald Trump\u8217\'20\'19s}}}\uc2  request that any trial should not take place until after the 2024 presidential election and reset the trial date for December.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThere is no basis in law or fact for proceeding in such an indeterminate and open-ended fashion, and the defendants provide none,\u8221\'20\'1D the prosecutors wrote in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://storage.courtlistener.com/recap/gov.uscourts.flsd.648652/gov.uscourts.flsd.648652.76.0.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 an 11-page court filing}}}\uc2  that sharply attacked Trump\u8217\'20\'19s arguments.\par \par \uc2 The dueling requests from Trump and the justice department present an early test for the US district court judge Aileen Cannon, a Trump appointee who is under heightened scrutiny for previously issuing favorable rulings to the former president during the criminal investigation.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/jul/13/donald-trump-trial-delay-prosecutors-object"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Justice department says \u8216\'20\'18no basis\u8217\'20\'19 to delay Trump\u8217\'20\'19s classified documents trial}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.36pm BST\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile in the Senate, the Guardian\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/adam-gabbatt"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Adam Gabbatt}}}\uc2  reports that a recently arrived lawmaker has finally given up his quest to publicly defend white nationalism:\par \par \uc2 Politicians typically enter office with a variety of interests, goals and focuses.\par \par \uc2 A wave of progressive Democrats were elected in 2018 with the stated goal of bringing universal healthcare to the US. Franklin Delano Roosevelt promised to lead the country out of the Great Depression with the New Deal. \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  wanted to build a wall, \u8220\'20\'1Cdrain the swamp\u8221\'20\'1D, and force people {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=giU4TyVJ7v8"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 to say}}}\uc2  \u8220\'20\'1CMerry Christmas\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Tommy Tuberville, the Republican senator from Alabama, has taken a different tack.\par \par \uc2 In a series of interviews and statements in recent months, he has invested his political capital in an attempt to defend white nationalism, and white nationalists, in what one anti-racist group called a \u8220\'20\'1Cdeeply disturbing\u8221\'20\'1D crusade \u8211\'20\'13 one that only appeared to come to an end this week, after condemnation from his Republican colleagues.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/jul/14/republican-senator-tommy-tuberville-white-natiomalists"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Republican senator finally ends crusade to defend white nationalists }}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.16pm BST\par \par \uc2 Biden administration forgives $39bn in student loan debt\par \par \uc2 The White House today announced it had forgiven $39bn in student loan debt held by 804,000 borrowers after making fixes to a program intended to provide relief for certain people who had been paying for 20 years or more.\par \par \uc2 The move comes after the supreme court last month blocked \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  from implementing his plan to relieve hundreds of billions of dollars in federal student loans. The president vowed to come up with an alternative program, but the effort is expected to take months to implement.\par \par \uc2 The student loan forgiveness announced today is separate from that, but in a statement, \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  said it was part of the administration\u8217\'20\'19s effort to address the high levels of debt many Americans take on to fund their education:\par \par \uc2 President \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  and I are committed to delivering relief to student loan debt borrowers to help them move forward with their lives \u8211\'20\'13 whether they want to start a family, buy a home, or become an entrepreneur. Today, we are taking another historic step by forgiving $39 billion in student loan debt for 804,000 borrowers who have been paying down their debts for 20 years or more and should qualify for relief. Instead, many were placed into forbearance by loan servicers in violation of the rules, and others did not get appropriate credit for their monthly payments. Addressing these harmful practices and reducing student loan debt has been a priority throughout my career. As California Attorney General, I won $1 billion for defrauded veterans and students by taking on predatory for-profit colleges.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.52pm BST\par \par \uc2 During last night\u8217\'20\'19s NDAA amendment vote on the House floor, congressman Eli Crane, a rightwing Republican and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.facebook.com/EliCraneAZ/posts/181411810895584/?paipv=0&eav=AfaHcct-eh54cr8qUEgum2XQKhFZzl0_lOyBMCgeFLOmeiiP8JksKLgOzkwEfE6h4tM&_rdr"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 promoter of baseless conspiracy theories}}}\uc2  about the 2020 election, used outdated and offensive language to refer to African Americans.\par \par \uc2 Crane\u8217\'20\'19s comment came during debate over an amendment he proposed to stop the defense department \u8220\'20\'1Cfrom making participation in training or support for certain race-based concepts a requirement for hiring, promotion, or retention of individuals\u8221\'20\'1D. That provision was among those included in the bill.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s a clip of the Crane\u8217\'20\'19s words, and the reaction:\par \par \uc2 enltrWow. Republicans are just openly calling my colleagues \u8220\'20\'1Ccolored people\u8221\'20\'1D on the House Floor now.\par \par \uc2 They\u8217\'20\'19re bringing amendments to the floor to stop bases named after confederate traitors from getting new names.\par \par \uc2 The GOP is not even hiding the racism anymore. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/7bRMjbi00O"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/7bRMjbi00O}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Rep. \uc2 Jim McGovern\uc2  (@RepMcGovern) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/RepMcGovern/status/1679634603387019264?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 July 13, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 Democrat \uc2 Joyce Beatty\uc2  was the lawmaker who demanded Crane\u8217\'20\'19s comment be stricken from the record, a request that was granted. Here\u8217\'20\'19s what she had to say about the episode:\par \par \uc2 enltr(1/2) I am still in utter shock and disbelief that a Republican uttered the words \u8216\'20\'18colored people\u8217\'20\'19 in reference to African-American service members who sacrifice their lives for our freedom. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/lOxpkt5HSR"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/lOxpkt5HSR}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Rep. \uc2 Joyce Beatty\uc2  (@RepBeatty) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/RepBeatty/status/1679651733251805186?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 July 14, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 enltr(2/2) I will not tolerate such racist and repugnant words in the House Chamber or anywhere in the Congress. That\u8217\'20\'19s why I asked that those words be stricken from the record, which was done so by unanimous consent.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Rep. \uc2 Joyce Beatty\uc2  (@RepBeatty) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/RepBeatty/status/1679651739664785411?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 July 14, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.16pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.29pm BST\par \par \uc2 House Democrats accuse GOP of 'extreme and reckless legislative joyride' in defense bill\par \par \uc2 In a joint statement released on Thursday evening, Democratic House minority leader \uc2 Hakeem Jeffries\uc2 , whip Katherine Clark and caucus chair \uc2 Pete Aguilar\uc2  encouraged their members to vote against the NDAA, saying \u8220\'20\'1Cextreme MAGA Republicans have chosen to hijack\u8221\'20\'1D legislation that is typically passed with bipartisan support.\par \par \uc2 Democrats are particularly incensed by amendments pushed by the GOP\u8217\'20\'19s right wing that would prevent the Pentagon from reimbursing service members who travel for abortions, and bar a healthcare program from paying for gender-affirming care. Other Republican amendments that made it into a bill include bans on diversity, equity and inclusion initiatives, and on defense department schools teaching that America is \u8220\'20\'1Ca fundamentally racist country\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s their full statement:\par \par \uc2 Extreme MAGA Republicans have chosen to hijack the historically bipartisan National Defense Authorization Act to continue attacking reproductive freedom and jamming their right-wing ideology down the throats of the American people.\par \par \uc2 House Republicans have turned what should be a meaningful investment in our men and women in uniform into an extreme and reckless legislative joyride. The bill undermines a woman\u8217\'20\'19s freedom to seek \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  care, targets the rights of LGBTQ+ servicemembers and bans books that should otherwise be available to military families.\par \par \uc2 House Democrats will always put people over politics to protect our national security. We will vote no on final passage of this bill.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.15pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.07pm BST\par \par \uc2 Far-right Republicans use defense spending to target \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , transgender care\par \par \uc2 Good morning, US politics blog readers. Every year for the last 50 or so, Congress passes the National Defense Authorization Act (NDAA) outlining the defense department\u8217\'20\'19s annual budget, but this year\u8217\'20\'19s bill is looking to be especially contentious. Yesterday, rightwing Republicans, with speaker of the House Kevin McCarthy\u8217\'20\'19 s blessing, succeeded in adding amendments to the legislation blocking the Pentagon from paying travel expenses for employees seeking abortions out of states, and another barring a healthcare program for the armed forces from providing gender-affirming care.\par \par \uc2 The House is expected to vote on final passage of the act around 10.30am eastern time today, but the amendments have sparked a revolt among Democrats, who are telling their lawmakers not to support it. And even if it passes Congress\u8217\'20\'19s lower chamber, it still needs to be approved by the Senate, where \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s allies have a majority and are unlikely to be friendly to conservative attempts to shoehorn culture war priorities into such crucial legislation. There will be plenty of news on this today, but one thing that can be said now is that this battle represents the latest consequence of the far right\u8217\'20\'19s sway in the GOP, which only took control of the House at the start of this year.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s what else is going on today:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Tucker Carlson\uc2 , eyeing a comeback after being fired from Fox News, will at 10am host a forum together with Blaze Media feature Republican presidential candidates \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2 , Tim Scott, Nikki Haley, \uc2 Vivek Ramaswamy\uc2  and Asa Hutchinson.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Biden is taking it easy today after a long week visiting \uc2 Nato\uc2  allies in Europe, with no public events or press briefing scheduled.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The state of American democracy: not good, according to a new poll from {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://apnews.com/article/poll-democracy-partisanship-trump-biden-trust-221f2b4f6cf9805f766c9a8395b9539d"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 The Associated Press-NORC Center for Public Affairs Research}}}\uc2 . A troubling one in 10 people surveyed give it high marks, with the rest saying America\u8217\'20\'19s system of government isn\u8217\'20\'19t doing a good job representing their interests.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020230714ej7e001pg\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
