\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Confuse and mislead: US anti- \highlight22\uc2 abortion \highlight\uc2  groups\u8217\'20\'19 strategy to soften extreme bans\b0\par\par\uc2 Ava Sasani \par \uc2 825 \uc2 words\par \uc2 13 July 2023\par 16:25 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Critics decry \u8216\'20\'18vague language and misinformation\u8217\'20\'19 as \uc2 Susan B Anthony\uc2  claims US does not have true \u8216\'20\'18bans\u8217\'20\'19 since exceptions exist\par \par \uc2 In the year since the \uc2 US supreme court\uc2  ruled there is no constitutional right to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  movement is still struggling to define a cohesive vision of post-Roe America.\par \par \uc2 Now they are employing a new strategy: use confusing or misleading language to repackage and soften the more extreme types of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  restrictions.\par \par \uc2 A recent example appeared in the Hill, where Marjorie Dannenfelser, president of Susan B Anthony Pro-Life America, one of the most powerful anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  groups in the country, wrote an opinion column arguing that the United States does not actually have any \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  \u8220\'20\'1Cbans\u8221\'20\'1D. Even states with the strictest \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  laws have some \u8220\'20\'1Cexceptions\u8221\'20\'1D, Dannenfelser wrote, so there are no true \u8220\'20\'1Cbans\u8221\'20\'1D on the procedure.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  movement is fueled by vague language and misinformation,\u8221\'20\'1D said Rachel O\u8217\'20\'19Leary Carmona, the executive director of Women\u8217\'20\'19s March. \u8220\'20\'1CThe more they obfuscate, the more successful they are, because when their agenda comes to light and is understood by voters, they do not win.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Today, 14 states have \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  bans that do not offer any exceptions for cases of rape or incest.\par \par \uc2 Republican infighting has slowed the anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  movement\u8217\'20\'19s progress in states such as {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/may/23/south-carolina-abortion-ban-six-weeks"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 South Carolina}}}\uc2 , where the conservative legislature was and remains split on questions the American public broadly agrees on, such as whether \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  bans should include exceptions {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.pewresearch.org/religion/2022/05/06/americas-abortion-quandary/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 for rape or incest victims.}}}\par \par \uc2 The problems facing the anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  movement intensified last fall, when midterm voters turned out in favor of reproductive rights, opting to protect \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access in states such as Michigan, Kentucky, Kansas and California. Even before the election, conservative state lawmakers were apprehensive on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  after the demise of Roe.\par \par \uc2 The journalists Dannenfelser addresses in her opinion piece spent {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/series/a-year-without-roe"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the past year}}}\uc2  documenting the way \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  bans \u8211\'20\'13 even those with exceptions for the life of the mother \u8211\'20\'13 are effectively useless when doctors fear prosecution for misinterpreting the law.\par \par \uc2 In March, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2023/mar/07/texas-abortion-women-lawsuit-ban"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 five women sued Texas}}}\uc2  after suffering severe health complications during pregnancy. The state\u8217\'20\'19s overlapping \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  bans were supposed to allow for the procedure in cases where the pregnancy risks substantial harm to the mother\u8217\'20\'19s health. But the law also imposes strict penalties on doctors \u8211\'20\'13 hundreds of thousands of dollars in fines and up to 99 years in jail for providing \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  care. Doctors\u8217\'20\'19 reasonable fear of misinterpreting the law, the Texas women said, interrupted their ability to obtain life-saving abortions.\par \par \uc2 The Texas case is not rare. In August, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/2022/08/19/us/politics/louisiana-abortion-law.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  a Louisiana woman}}}\uc2  was denied \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  care, even though her baby had no chance of survival, and continuing the pregnancy would jeopardize her own health. In December, an Idaho woman shared {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tiktok.com/@geekynerdbitch/video/7176785510982176046?is_copy_url=1&is_from_webapp=v1"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 on TikTok}}}\uc2  that she had been bleeding out for 19 days before she received miscarriage treatment.\par \par \uc2 Dannenfelser is probably aware of these stories, O\u8217\'20\'19Leary Carmona said. The anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  movement knows that \u8220\'20\'1Cexceptions\u8221\'20\'1D are not workable in hospitals and doctors\u8217\'20\'19 offices.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CBut they don\u8217\'20\'19t care about real people. They know what they\u8217\'20\'19re doing when they use this kind of language,\u8221\'20\'1D O\u8217\'20\'19Leary Carmona told the Guardian. \u8220\'20\'1CThis misinformation, making suggestions about what is and isn\u8217\'20\'19t a ban, that\u8217\'20\'19s a real threat that should be taken very seriously.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Twisting the term \u8220\'20\'1Cban\u8221\'20\'1D helps win the support of people who might feel uneasy about a law that prohibits all abortions.\par \par \uc2 O\u8217\'20\'19Leary Carmona said confusing language and misinformation are longstanding strategies used by conservative thinktanks and lobby groups to make extreme political goals, including sweeping \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  bans, appear more palatable to the general public.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 National Right to Life Committee\uc2 , a leading anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  advocacy group, is credited for a recent Idaho law that created the term {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/jul/12/idaho-abortion-lawsuit-minors"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1C\b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  trafficking\u8221\'20\'1D}}}\uc2 . In April, Idaho passed legislation requiring any person under 18 to get permission from a parent or guardian before traveling out of state to have an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 . Any person who violates the law could be charged for \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  \u8220\'20\'1Ctrafficking\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt is disgusting to label access to healthcare as trafficking,\u8221\'20\'1D said Tai Simpson of the Indigenous Idaho Alliance, one of the plaintiffs behind a lawsuit challenging the Idaho statute.\par \par \uc2 In June last year, before the court ruling on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  was announced, Jim Bopp, general counsel for the \uc2 National Right to Life Committee\uc2 , released a memo outlining potential legislation that could be pursued {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nrlc.org/wp-content/uploads/NRLC-Post-Roe-Model-Abortion-Law-FINAL-1.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1Cin the event Roe v Wade is overturned\u8221\'20\'1D}}}\uc2 . Part of that document included a sample bill outlining the term \u8220\'20\'1C\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  trafficking\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Simpson said Idaho \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  opponents used Bopp\u8217\'20\'19s language to gain support for a controversial bill that grappled with the constitutional question of the right to interstate travel.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThey are misusing \u8216\'20\'18trafficking\u8217\'20\'19 to create fear where no fear needs to exist, to create a crime where no crime exists,\u8221\'20\'1D she said.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020230713ej7d001p6\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
