\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Trump documents trial judge sets first hearing; Georgia grand jury set to weigh 2020 election charges \u8211\'20\'13 as it happened\b0\par\par\uc2 L\u233\'00\'E9onie Chao-Fong \par \uc2 5,368 \uc2 words\par \uc2 11 July 2023\par 20:06 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Aileen Cannon sets 18 July for hearing as ex-US president asks for trial delay; grand jury to decide if Trump has case to answer on election interferenceTrump asks for documents trial delay until after 2024 US election\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.02pm BST\par \par \uc2 Summary of the day\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s a recap of today\u8217\'20\'19s developments:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 A grand jury selected in Georgia on Tuesday is expected to decide later this summer whether \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  and associates will face criminal charges over their attempt to overturn the former president\u8217\'20\'19s defeat by \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  in the 2020 election. The district attorney of Fulton county, \uc2 Fani Willis\uc2 , has {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/apr/25/trump-georgia-prosecutor-charges-fani-willis"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 indicated}}}\uc2  she expects to obtain indictments between the end of July and the middle of August.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The federal judge overseeing the case involving former Trump\u8217\'20\'19s handling of classified documents after leaving office has agreed to delay an upcoming hearing in the case. The hearing, originally scheduled for 14 July, will now occur on {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/jul/11/trump-georgia-grand-jury-biden-nato-ukraine-politics-live-updates?page=with:block-64ad5ef78f08ce64897ea233#block-64ad5ef78f08ce64897ea233"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 18 July.}}}\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Trump asked the federal judge overseeing the Mar-a-Lago classified documents case to indefinitely postpone setting a trial date in court filings and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/jul/11/trump-classified-documents-trial-after-2024-election"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 suggested,}}}\uc2  at a minimum, that any scheduled trial should not take place until after the 2024 presidential election.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s pick to become the country\u8217\'20\'19s top military officer, Gen Charles \u8220\'20\'1CCQ\u8221\'20\'1D Brown, warned senators that an indefinite blockade of senior officer promotions {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/jul/11/trump-georgia-grand-jury-biden-nato-ukraine-politics-live-updates?page=with:block-64adae238f08ce64897ea6cb#block-64adae238f08ce64897ea6cb"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 could have a far-reaching impact}}}\uc2  across the US armed forces.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Alabama senator Tommy Tuberville has {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/jul/11/trump-georgia-grand-jury-biden-nato-ukraine-politics-live-updates?page=with:block-64ada0938f080a06e305d58c#block-64ada0938f080a06e305d58c"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  tripled down on his belief}}}\uc2  that not all white nationalists should be labelled as \u8220\'20\'1Cracists\u8221\'20\'1D, just a day after he said the definition of a \u8220\'20\'1Cwhite nationalist\u8221\'20\'1D {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/jul/11/trump-georgia-grand-jury-biden-nato-ukraine-politics-live-updates?page=with:block-64ad81498f080a06e305d3bd#block-64ad81498f080a06e305d3bd"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 was a matter of \u8220\'20\'1Copinion\u8221\'20\'1D. }}}\uc2  Tuberville was \u8220\'20\'1Cwrong, wrong, wrong\u8221\'20\'1D, Senate majority leader \uc2 Chuck Schumer\uc2  said, while Senate Republican leader \uc2 Mitch McConnell\uc2  said {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/jul/11/trump-georgia-grand-jury-biden-nato-ukraine-politics-live-updates?page=with:block-64ada4f08f08ce64897ea673#block-64ada4f08f08ce64897ea673"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  \u8220\'20\'1Cwhite supremacy is simply unacceptable}}}\uc2  in the military and in our whole country.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Supreme court justice \uc2 Sonia Sotomayor\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s staff pressed public institutions, including colleges and libraries, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/jul/11/trump-georgia-grand-jury-biden-nato-ukraine-politics-live-updates?page=with:block-64ad8ca58f08ce64897ea555#block-64ad8ca58f08ce64897ea555"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 to buy copies of her books}}}\uc2  when she traveled there for speaking engagements, according to an AP report.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The House rules committee held a hearing on the $874bn annual defense policy bill, known as the National Defense Authorization Act (NDAA). {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/jul/11/trump-georgia-grand-jury-biden-nato-ukraine-politics-live-updates?page=with:block-64ad6be18f080a06e305d25c#block-64ad6be18f080a06e305d25c"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 More than 1,500 amendments }}}\uc2  were filed to the bill, and Speaker Kevin McCarthy will {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/jul/11/trump-georgia-grand-jury-biden-nato-ukraine-politics-live-updates?page=with:block-64ad65e88f08ce64897ea2b2#block-64ad65e88f08ce64897ea2b2"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 need to navigate }}}\uc2  between the demands of his most conservative members and the need for Democratic votes in order to get a bill ultimately signed into law.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Former Fox News host \uc2 Tucker Carlson\uc2  will host the first GOP presidential forum for the 2024 primary season this week, but {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/jul/11/trump-georgia-grand-jury-biden-nato-ukraine-politics-live-updates?page=with:block-64ad762f8f080a06e305d301#block-64ad762f8f080a06e305d301"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  notably missing }}}\uc2  from the lineup is the current GOP frontrunner, former president \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The Secret Service will {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/jul/11/trump-georgia-grand-jury-biden-nato-ukraine-politics-live-updates?page=with:block-64adaacb8f08df2847002064#block-64adaacb8f08df2847002064"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 provide a briefing}}}\uc2  to Congress on the discovery of cocaine at the White House on Thursday.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 A US thinktank chief who accuses \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  of China-linked corruption involving his son, \uc2 Hunter Biden\uc2 , and who has been presented by Republicans as a \u8220\'20\'1Cmissing\u8221\'20\'1D witness against the president, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/jul/11/gal-luft-biden-china-agent-charged"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 was charged with China-linked offenses }}}\uc2  including failing to register as a foreign agent, arms trafficking and violations of sanctions on Iran.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 9.06pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.40pm BST\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s pick to become the country\u8217\'20\'19s top military officer warned senators that an indefinite blockade of senior officer promotions could have a far-reaching impact across the US armed forces.\par \par \uc2 Testifying at his Senate armed services committee confirmation hearing to be the joint chiefs of staff, Gen Charles \u8220\'20\'1CCQ\u8221\'20\'1D Brown, the outgoing air force chief of staff, said \u8220\'20\'1Cwe will lose talent\u8221\'20\'1D as a result of the prolonged hold on general and flag officers.\par \par \uc2 Brown made the remarks shortly after being questioned by Republican senator Tommy Tuberville, who has used a Senate procedure to put a hold on hundreds of military nominations from moving forward in protest of Pentagon \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  policies. An aide to Tuberville said his block would also apply to Brown, Reuters reported.\par \par \uc2 US air force\uc2  Gen Charles Brown Jr. attends a \uc2 US Senate\uc2  hearing on his nomination to be chairman of the Joint Chiefs of Staff. Photograph: Kevin Wurm/Reuters\par \par \uc2 Brown also said that the inability of senior officers to take new assignments created a \u8220\'20\'1Cchain of events\u8221\'20\'1D that affects junior officers as well as military families.\par \par \uc2 Democrats including Senator Elizabeth Warren have slammed Tuberville for punishing uniformed military leaders who were not responsible for the policy on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  travel that he was protesting. Warren said:\par \par \uc2 If the senator from Alabama continues his reckless action, he will soon be holding 650 leaders who have served their country honorably hostage.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 8.47pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.20pm BST\par \par \uc2 The Secret Service will provide a briefing to Congress on the discovery of cocaine at the White House, Axios is reporting.\par \par \uc2 The meeting between Secret Service representatives and the Republican-controlled House oversight committee will take place at 10am EST on Thursday, according to two sources familiar with the plan.\par \par \uc2 House oversight chair James Comer sent a letter to the Secret Service director last week requesting a briefing after cocaine was found at the White House.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 8.21pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.06pm BST\par \par \uc2 A grand jury selected in Georgia that is expected to decide later this summer whether \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  and associates will face charges over their attempt to overturn the 2020 election has been formally sworn in after a three-hour selection process in Atlanta.\par \par \uc2 enltrThe Georgia grand jury that is expected to consider charges against \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  and his Republican allies' efforts to overturn the 2020 election was formally sworn in Tuesday afternoon after a three-hour selection process in Atlanta, per {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/MarshallCohen?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @MarshallCohen}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Kaitlan Collins (@kaitlancollins) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/kaitlancollins/status/1678830765293858829?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 July 11, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.54pm BST\par \par \uc2 The Senate Republican leader, \uc2 Mitch McConnell\uc2 , was asked if he has concerns that Senator Tommy Tuberville {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/jul/11/trump-georgia-grand-jury-biden-nato-ukraine-politics-live-updates?page=with:block-64ada0938f080a06e305d58c#block-64ada0938f080a06e305d58c"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 has a \u8220\'20\'1Chard time\u8221\'20\'1D denouncing white nationalism}}}\uc2 , especially in the military.\par \par \uc2 McConnell replied:\par \par \uc2 White supremacy is simply unacceptable in the military and in our whole country.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.41pm BST\par \par \uc2 Alabama senator Tommy Tuberville has tripled down on his belief that not all white nationalists should be labelled as \u8220\'20\'1Cracists\u8221\'20\'1D, just a day after he said the definition of a \u8220\'20\'1Cwhite nationalist\u8221\'20\'1D was a matter of \u8220\'20\'1Copinion\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Tuberville, in an interview with ABC News\u8217\'20\'19 Rachel Scott, was asked why he continued to insist that a white nationalist \u8220\'20\'1Cto me is an American\u8221\'20\'1D. He replied:\par \par \uc2 Listen, I\u8217\'20\'19m totally against racism. And if Democrats want to say that white nationalists are racist, I\u8217\'20\'19m totally against that, too.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CBut that\u8217\'20\'19s not a Democratic definition,\u8221\'20\'1D Scott said. Tuberville responded:\par \par \uc2 Well that\u8217\'20\'19s your definition. My definition is racism is bad.\par \par \uc2 Scott noted that the definition of a white nationalist is someone believing \u8220\'20\'1Cthe white race is superior to all other races\u8221\'20\'1D and asked, \u8220\'20\'1CDo you believe that white nationalists are racist?\u8221\'20\'1D He replied:\par \par \uc2 Yes, if that\u8217\'20\'19s what a racist is, yes.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 7.44pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.30pm BST\par \par \uc2 Potential grand jurors were questioned for about two hours before Fulton county judge Robert McBurney announced who were chosen, CBS News reported.\par \par \uc2 There will be two concurrent grand juries that will be made up of 16 to 23 people and up to three alternates as part of the process.\par \par \uc2 One group will meet on Mondays and Tuesdays. The other will meet Thursdays and Fridays. Of the 23 Fulton County residents chosen for the grand jury, a majority, 12, would need to vote in favor of an indictment.\par \par \uc2 Fulton county district attorney \uc2 Fani Willis\uc2  is expected to present her case before one of the two new grand juries being seated today.\par \par \uc2 Ed Garland, a local attorney, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.ajc.com/politics/grand-jurors-who-will-consider-trump-charges-to-be-selected-tuesday/R7RXC2GUFRB5JLHKKRE5LX4IZ4/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 told the Atlanta Journal-Constitution}}}\uc2  the jurors selected would face an \u8220\'20\'1Cawesome responsibility\u8221\'20\'1D that \u8220\'20\'1Cno other group of Georgia citizens has ever dealt with \u8211\'20\'13 the potential indictment of a former president\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Garland added:\par \par \uc2 This is a case that has been saturated in the media with political overtones, so it is imperative for them to be fair and impartial and for our judicial system to live up to its ideals.\par \par \uc2 At the courthouse, McBurney reminded reporters of the sensitivity of proceedings. \u8220\'20\'1CIt would not go well if any of [the jurors\u8217\'20\'19] pictures appear in any of your outlets,\u8221\'20\'1D he said.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.10pm BST\par \par \uc2 The Turkish president, Recep \uc2 Tayyip Erdogan\uc2 , meets with President \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  during a Nato leaders summit in Vilnius, Lithuania. Photograph: Turkish Presidential Press Office/Reuters\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 7.21pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.41pm BST\par \par \uc2 A grand jury selected in Georgia on Tuesday is expected to decide later this summer whether \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  and associates will face criminal charges over their attempt to overturn the former president\u8217\'20\'19s defeat by \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  in the 2020 election.\par \par \uc2 The district attorney of Fulton county, \uc2 Fani Willis\uc2 , has {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/apr/25/trump-georgia-prosecutor-charges-fani-willis"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 indicated}}}\uc2  she expects to obtain indictments between the end of July and the middle of August. Trump also faces possible federal charges over his election subversion, culminating in his incitement of the deadly January 6 attack on Congress.\par \par \uc2 Trump faces trials on 71 criminal charges: 34 in New York over hush money payments to the porn star Stormy Daniels and 37 in Florida, from federal prosecutors and regarding his retention of classified documents after leaving office.\par \par \uc2 Trump\u8217\'20\'19s legal jeopardy does not stop there. In a civil case in New York, he was fined about $5m after being found liable for sexual abuse and defamation against the writer E Jean Carroll. Another civil case, concerning Trump\u8217\'20\'19s business practices, continues in New York.\par \par \uc2 The grand jury selection for the Fulton county case comes at a febrile moment in US society. Denying all wrongdoing and claiming political persecution, Trump remains the clear frontrunner for the Republican nomination to face Biden again at the polls next year.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 6.43pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.28pm BST\par \par \uc2 Supreme court justice Sotomayor's staff pushed colleges and libraries to buy her books - report\par \par \uc2 Supreme court justice \uc2 Sonia Sotomayor\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s staff pressed public institutions, including colleges and libraries, to buy copies of her books when she traveled there for speaking engagements, according to an AP {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://apnews.com/article/supreme-court-sotomayor-book-sales-ethics-colleges-b2cb93493f927f995829762cb8338c02"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 report.}}}\par \par \uc2 Documents obtained by the AP show Sotomayor\u8217\'20\'19s taxpayer-funded staff suggesting a library in Oregon in 2019 that it did not order enough copies of her book for attendees at an event that would feature the justice. According to AP, the staffer wrote:\par \par \uc2 For an event with 1,000 people and they have to have a copy of Just Ask to get into the line, 250 books is definitely not enough. Families purchase multiples and people will be upset if they are unable to get in line because the book required is sold out.\par \par \uc2 AP also identified similar instances at other institutions, including \uc2 Clemson University\uc2 , \uc2 Michigan State University\uc2 , and. \uc2 University of California, Davis\par \par \uc2 For members of Congress or members of the executive branch, this sort of arrangement is illegal. But because the supreme court has no formal code of ethics, such practices are legal.\par \par \uc2 In a statement to AP, the court said staffers \u8220\'20\'1Cassist the Justices in complying with judicial ethics guidance\u8221\'20\'1D for visits, including surrounding their books.\par \par \uc2 Sotomayor has disclosed earnings of at least $3.7m from book sales since she joined the court in 2009, AP noted.\par \par \uc2 Supreme Court Justice \uc2 Sonia Sotomayor\uc2  addresses attendees of an event promoting her new children's book "Just Ask!" in 2019. Photograph: John Amis/AP\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 6.32pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.56pm BST\par \par \uc2 Every member of the Michigan Republican congressional delegation is backing \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s bid to return to the White House, his presidential campaign said.\par \par \uc2 Representatives Jack Bergman, Bill Huizenga, John James, Lisa McClain, John Moolenaar and \uc2 Tim Walberg\uc2  will also serve on Trump\u8217\'20\'19s \u8220\'20\'1C2024 Michigan federal leadership team\u8221\'20\'1D, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/jonathanoosting/status/1678775245371736066"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 according to the campaign}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 enltrTrump just announced his leadership team in Michigan and it looks to be more House members than have endorsed DeSantis in all of Congress. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/Go13diQWWT"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/Go13diQWWT}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 @andykaczynski on Threads (@KFILE) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/KFILE/status/1678787427316408321?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 July 11, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 6.08pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.44pm BST\par \par \uc2 A US thinktank chief who accuses \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  of China-linked corruption involving his son, \uc2 Hunter Biden\uc2 , and who has been presented by Republicans as a \u8220\'20\'1Cmissing\u8221\'20\'1D witness against the president, was charged with China-linked offenses including failing to register as a foreign agent, arms trafficking and violations of sanctions on Iran.\par \par \uc2 Gal Luft, 57 and a dual US-Israeli citizen, is co-director of the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://www.iags.org/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Institute for the Analysis of Global Security}}}\uc2  (IAGS), based in Maryland, near Washington.\par \par \uc2 He was charged on Monday in absentia, having skipped bail in Cyprus in April while awaiting extradition.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.justice.gov/usao-sdny/pr/us-attorney-announces-charges-against-co-director-think-tank-acting-unregistered"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Announcing}}}\uc2  the charges, \uc2 Damian Williams\uc2 , US attorney for the southern district of New York, said Luft \u8220\'20\'1Cengaged in multiple, serious criminal schemes.\par \par \uc2 He subverted foreign agent registration laws in the United States to seek to promote Chinese policies by acting through a former high-ranking \uc2 US government\uc2  official; he acted as a broker in deals for dangerous weapons and Iranian oil; and he told multiple lies about his crimes to law enforcement.\par \par \uc2 The charges seemed guaranteed to infuriate Republicans in Congress seeking to use \uc2 Hunter Biden\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s troubled personal life and business dealings in attacks on his father, potentially including attempts by rightwingers in the House to bring about impeachment proceedings.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/jul/11/gal-luft-biden-china-agent-charged"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Read the full story here.}}}\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/jul/11/gal-luft-biden-china-agent-charged"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \u8216\'20\'18Missing witness\u8217\'20\'19 who accuses Biden of China corruption charged with being China agent}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.30pm BST\par \par \uc2 Senate majority leader \uc2 Chuck Schumer\uc2  slammed Senator Tommy Tuberville for \u8220\'20\'1Cfanning the flames of bigotry and intolerance\u8221\'20\'1D after Tuberville said the definition of a \u8220\'20\'1Cwhite nationalist\u8221\'20\'1D was a matter of \u8220\'20\'1Copinion\u8221\'20\'1D during a television interview last night.\par \par \uc2 During the interview with CNN\u8217\'20\'19s Kaitlan Collins, Tuberville was asked to clarify his prior comments on whether white nationalists should be barred from serving in the US military. \u8220\'20\'1CIf people think that a white nationalist is a racist, I agree with that,\u8221\'20\'1D he said.\par \par \uc2 Collins noted that, by definition, a white nationalist is \u8220\'20\'1Csomeone who believes that the white race is superior to other races\u8221\'20\'1D. Tuberville replied: \u8220\'20\'1CWell, that\u8217\'20\'19s some people\u8217\'20\'19s opinion.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 My opinion of a white nationalist, if someone wants to call them white nationalist, to me, is an American. It\u8217\'20\'19s an American.\par \par \uc2 Now if that white nationalist is a racist, I\u8217\'20\'19m totally against anything that they want to do because I am 110% against racism.\par \par \uc2 enltrThat moment in which Sen. Tommy Tuberville admits he does not know what it means to be a white nationalist, and then goes on to defend them.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIf somebody wants to call them white nationalist, to me, it's an American.\u8221\'20\'1D {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/J4CEIEoVk9"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/J4CEIEoVk9}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 \uc2 Gavin Newsom\uc2  (@GavinNewsom) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/GavinNewsom/status/1678782552046440448?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 July 11, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 Tuberville was \u8220\'20\'1Cwrong, wrong, wrong\u8221\'20\'1D, Schumer said today, adding that \u8220\'20\'1Cthe definition of white nationalism is not a matter of opinion\u8221\'20\'1D. Schumer added:\par \par \uc2 For the Senator from Alabama to obscure the racist nature of white nationalism is indeed very, very dangerous.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 6.07pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.13pm BST\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  has declared a state of emergency in Vermont, where torrential rainfall has triggered life-threatening flash floods.\par \par \uc2 The declaration allows for the \uc2 Federal Emergency Management Agency\uc2  (Fema) to provide aid to the state amid the flash flooding.\par \par \uc2 Cars under water during flooding from the Winooski river that inundated Montpelier, Vermont. Photograph: John Lazenby/Alamy Stock Photo/Alamy Live News.\par \par \uc2 The National Weather Service has issued flash flood warnings and advisories across Vermont from the Massachusetts line north to the Canadian border. In the south and west, states were blistering under a worsening heatwave, as the US embarked on another {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/jul/10/us-weather-floods-heatwave-climate-crisis-alerts"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 week of extreme weather}}}\uc2  and experts warned that the human-caused climate crisis is driving the record-breaking conditions.\par \par \uc2 You can follow the latest extreme weather news from across the US {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/live/2023/jul/11/weather-latest-updates-flooding-heat-temperatures-us"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 on our live blog.}}}\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/live/2023/jul/11/weather-latest-updates-flooding-heat-temperatures-us"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Extreme US weather live: fears Vermont dam could overflow and worsen flooding; 42m under heat advisory across south}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 5.39pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.54pm BST\par \par \uc2 At least one of the far-right lawmakers on the House rules committee, Ralph Norman of South Carolina, said he planned to oppose {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/jul/11/trump-georgia-grand-jury-biden-nato-ukraine-politics-live-updates?page=with:block-64ad65e88f08ce64897ea2b2#block-64ad65e88f08ce64897ea2b2"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  the }}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/jul/11/trump-georgia-grand-jury-biden-nato-ukraine-politics-live-updates?page=with:block-64ad65e88f08ce64897ea2b2#block-64ad65e88f08ce64897ea2b2"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 defense authorization bill.}}}\par \par \uc2 Norman, a Freedom Caucus member, told CNN he was concerned the bill did not go far enough to target \u8220\'20\'1Cwoke\u8221\'20\'1D Pentagon policies, and won\u8217\'20\'19t receive the amendment votes to change that.\par \par \uc2 Another conservative member of the panel, Chip Roy of Texas, said \u8220\'20\'1Cthere are still glaring issues at the DOD that it needs to address in order to receive my support\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 4.59pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.42pm BST\par \par \uc2 Tucker Carlson\uc2  to host first GOP presidential forum \u8211\'20\'13 without \uc2 Donald Trump\par \par \uc2 Former Fox News host \uc2 Tucker Carlson\uc2  will host the first GOP presidential forum for the 2024 primary season this week, just weeks before the \uc2 Republican National Committee\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s (\uc2 RNC\uc2 ) first debate in Milwaukee, Wisconsin.\par \par \uc2 The event in Iowa will feature Carlson speaking one-on-one with Florida Governor \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2 , former South Carolina Governor Nikki Haley, businessman \uc2 Vivek Ramaswamy\uc2 , Senator Tim Scott of South Carolina, and former vice-president \uc2 Mike Pence\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 enltrGet notified for Friday's event here: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/tPIrAMIso1"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/tPIrAMIso1}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/l2LSmQNGtA"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/l2LSmQNGtA}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 TheBlaze (@theblaze) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/theblaze/status/1678515766419767301?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 July 10, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 But notably missing from the lineup is the current GOP frontrunner, former president \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 A Trump campaign spokesperson {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://thehill.com/media/4090653-tucker-carlson-hosting-first-gop-presidential-forum-without-trump/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 told}}}\uc2  the Hill:\par \par \uc2 Unfortunately there is a scheduling conflict and the President will be in Florida this weekend headlining the premier national young voter conference with Turning Point Action conference while DeSantis is nowhere to be found.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 4.52pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.31pm BST\par \par \uc2 Few Republicans are highly confident that votes will be counted accurately in next year\u8217\'20\'19s presidential election, according to a new poll.\par \par \uc2 The poll, conducted by Associated Press and NORC Center for Public Affairs Research, found that only 22% of Republicans have high confidence that votes in the upcoming presidential election will be counted accurately, compared with 71% of Democrats.\par \par \uc2 While Democrats\u8217\'20\'19 confidence in elections has risen in recent years, the opposite is true for Republicans. Overall, the poll found that fewer than half of Americans \u8211\'20\'13 44% \u8211\'20\'13 have \u8220\'20\'1Ca great deal\u8221\'20\'1D or \u8220\'20\'1Cquite a bit\u8221\'20\'1D of confidence that the votes in the next presidential election will be counted accurately.\par \par \uc2 The results suggest years of sustained attacks against elections by former president \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  and his allies have taken a toll, AP writes.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 4.52pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.17pm BST\par \par \uc2 As California considers implementing large-scale reparations for Black residents affected by the legacy of slavery, the state has also become the focus of the nation\u8217\'20\'19s divisive reparations conversation, drawing the backlash of conservatives criticizing the priorities of a \u8220\'20\'1Cliberal\u8221\'20\'1D state.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CReparations for Slavery? California\u8217\'20\'19s Bad Idea Catches On,\u8221\'20\'1D commentator Jason L Riley {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/reparations-for-slavery-californias-bad-idea-catches-on-reform-new-york-race-7398e5d1"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 wrote}}}\uc2  in the Wall Street Journal, as New York approved {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://apnews.com/article/reparations-slavery-new-york-commission-4f3eef7de52e149f64432dd929720b79"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a commission}}}\uc2  to study the idea. In the \uc2 Washington Post\uc2 , conservative columnist George F Will {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.washingtonpost.com/opinions/2023/06/07/california-reparations-silliness/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 said}}}\uc2  the state\u8217\'20\'19s debate around reparations adds to a \u8220\'20\'1Cplague of solemn silliness\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Roughly two-thirds of Americans oppose the idea of reparations, according to 2021 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.umass.edu/news/article/umass-amherstwcvb-poll-finds-nearly-half?_gl=1*rjqh2s*_ga*MTQ4MzE5MDI0LjE2NjgwMjE2MjE.*_ga_21RLS0L7EB*MTY2ODc4OTUzMS41LjEuMTY2ODc4OTcwMC4wLjAuMA..&_ga=2.180216236.968932827.1668789532-148319024.1668021621"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 polling}}}\uc2  from the \uc2 University of Massachusetts Amherst\uc2  and 2022 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.pewresearch.org/short-reads/2022/11/28/black-and-white-americans-are-far-apart-in-their-views-of-reparations-for-slavery/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 polling}}}\uc2  from the \uc2 Pew Research Center\uc2 . Both found that more than 80% Black respondents support some kind of compensation for the descendants of slaves, while a similar majority of white respondents opposed. \uc2 Pew\uc2  found that roughly two-thirds of Hispanics and Asian Americans opposed, as well.\par \par \uc2 But in California, there\u8217\'20\'19s greater support. Both the state\u8217\'20\'19s Reparations Task Force \u8211\'20\'13 which released its 1,100-page final report and recommendations {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://oag.ca.gov/ab3121/report"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 to the public}}}\uc2  on 29 June \u8211\'20\'13 and a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://bunchecenter.ucla.edu/wp-content/uploads/sites/112/2023/05/Draft-reparations-report-FINAL_05.22.23.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 University of California, Los Angeles study}}}\uc2  found that roughly two-thirds of Californians are in favor of some form of reparations, though residents are divided on what they should be.\par \par \uc2 When delving into the reasons why people resist, Tatishe Nteta, who directed the UMass poll, expected feasibility or the challenges of implementing large programs to top the list, but this wasn\u8217\'20\'19t the case.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWhen we ask people why they oppose, it\u8217\'20\'19s not about the cost. It\u8217\'20\'19s not about logistics. It\u8217\'20\'19s not about the impossibility to place a monetary value on the impact of slavery,\u8221\'20\'1D said Nteta, provost professor of political science at the \uc2 University of Massachusetts Amherst\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 It is consistently this notion that the descendants of slaves do not deserve these types of reparations.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/jul/11/california-historic-reparations-black-residents"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Read the full story here.}}}\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/jul/11/california-historic-reparations-black-residents"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  California faces backlash as it weighs historic reparations for Black residents}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.05pm BST\par \par \uc2 More than 1,5000 amendments were filed to the FY2024 defense authorization bill, which is projected to hit the House floor this week. At issue is whether the House will take up the hard-right amendments, with the weight falling once again on Speaker Kevin McCarthy.\par \par \uc2 Some of the most closely watched amendments relate to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , diversity, equity and inclusion (DEI) funding, and transgender troops, according to Politico\u8217\'20\'19s Playbook.\par \par \uc2 McCarthy will need to navigate between the demands of his most conservative members \u8211\'20\'13 three of whom serve on the House rules committee \u8211\'20\'13 and the need for Democratic votes in order to get a bill ultimately signed into law, Playbook writes. It continues:\par \par \uc2 In the past, House leaders typically have told the hard right to pound sand, knowing they weren\u8217\'20\'19t going to vote for the final bill anyway. But after pissing off conservatives during the debt limit standoff, McCarthy looks poised to make a different calculation this time.\par \par \uc2 Facing heavy criticism from the House Freedom Caucus and other conservatives, McCarthy is under pressure to give on a number of high-profile issues touching defense policy, Punchbowl News writes. It says:\par \par \uc2 Every \u8216\'20\'18culture war\u8217\'20\'19 provision from the Freedom Caucus that\u8217\'20\'19s added to the base legislation will cost Democratic votes. It will also make GOP moderates unhappy.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.38pm BST\par \par \uc2 The House rules committee is scheduled to mark up the FY2024 defense authorization bill, the annual bill setting Pentagon priorities and policies, today.\par \par \uc2 The bill, which is expected to hit the floor later this week, has been signed into law 60 years straight. But this year, Speaker Kevin McCarthy and GOP leaders are confronting a legislative landmine as the far-right {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/jan/05/house-republicans-voting-against-mccarthy-speaker"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 House Freedom Caucus}}}\uc2  push for dozens of proposed changes to the legislation.\par \par \uc2 Adam Smith\uc2 , the head Democrat on the House armed services committee, said he was worried about a flurry of \u8220\'20\'1Cextreme right-wing amendments\u8221\'20\'1D attached to the bill and that he wasn\u8217\'20\'19t \u8220\'20\'1Cremotely\u8221\'20\'1D confident the bill will pass this week.\par \par \uc2 Smith {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.washingtonpost.com/politics/2023/07/10/congress-returns-with-lots-do-little-time-do-it/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 told}}}\uc2  the \uc2 Washington Post\uc2  he was concerned about GOP measures on \u8220\'20\'1C\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , guns, the border, and social policy and equity issues\u8221\'20\'1D. Without the controversial amendments, Smith predicted that well over 300 House members would vote for the bill. With them, \u8220\'20\'1Cyou lose most, if not all, Democrats,\u8221\'20\'1D he told Politico\u8217\'20\'19s Playbook.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.40pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.12pm BST\par \par \uc2 Iowa \u8217\'20\'19s state legislature is holding a special session on Tuesday as it plans to vote on a bill that would ban most abortions at around six weeks of pregnancy, when most people don\u8217\'20\'19t yet know they are pregnant.\par \par \uc2 The state is the latest in the country to vote on legislation restricting reproductive rights after the overturning of Roe v Wade last year, which ended the nationwide constitutional right to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Iowa\u8217\'20\'19s Republican governor, \uc2 Kim Reynolds\uc2 , called for the special session last week, vowing to \u8220\'20\'1Ccontinue to fight against the inhumanity of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 \u8221\'20\'1D and calling the \u8220\'20\'1Cpro-life\u8221\'20\'1D movement against reproductive rights \u8220\'20\'1Cthe most important human rights cause of our time\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Lawmakers in the GOP-controlled legislature will debate {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.legis.iowa.gov/legislation/BillBook?ba=HSB255&ga=90"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 House Study Bill 255}}}\uc2 , which was released on Friday and seeks to prohibit abortions at the first sign of cardiac activity except in certain cases such as rape or incest.\par \par \uc2 Iowa\u8217\'20\'19s house, senate and governor\u8217\'20\'19s office are all Republican-controlled, and the bill faces few hurdles from being passed.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/jul/11/iowa-six-week-abortion-ban"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Read the full story here.}}}\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/jul/11/iowa-six-week-abortion-ban"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Republican-controlled Iowa legislature to vote on six-week \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  ban}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.57pm BST\par \par \uc2 Judge sets first hearing on Trump classified documents case for 18 July\par \par \uc2 The first hearing before US District Judge Aileen Cannon in the federal criminal case against \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  will be on 18 July, according to a court order.\par \par \uc2 enltrJust in: Federal judge in classified docs case schedules Section 2 hearing \u8212\'20\'14 to determine timings going forward for the classified discovery portion of the pre-trial prep \u8212\'20\'14 for July 18\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Hugo Lowell (@hugolowell) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/hugolowell/status/1678757436893675523?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 July 11, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.52pm BST\par \par \uc2 Trump {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/jun/08/donald-trump-charged-retention-classified-documents"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 was charged}}}\uc2  with retention of national defense information, including US nuclear secrets and plans for US retaliation in the event of an attack, which means his case will be tried under the rules laid out in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/jun/28/trump-classified-documents-trial-delayed-spring-2024"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the Classified Information Procedures Act, or Cipa}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Cipa provides a mechanism for the government to charge cases involving classified documents without risking the \u8220\'20\'1Cgraymail\u8221\'20\'1D problem, where the defense threatens to reveal classified information at trial, but the steps that have to be followed mean it takes longer to get to trial.\par \par \uc2 The process includes the government turning over all of the classified information they want to use to the defense in discovery, like any other criminal case, in addition to the non-classified discovery that is done in a separate process.\par \par \uc2 Trump\u8217\'20\'19s lawyers argued the amount of discovery \u8211\'20\'13 the government is making the material available in batches because there is so much evidence and it has not finished processing everything that came from search warrants \u8211\'20\'13 meant that they could not know how long the process would take.\par \par \uc2 Trump\u8217\'20\'19s lawyers wrote:\par \par \uc2 From a practical manner, the volume of discovery and the Cipa logistics alone make plain that the government\u8217\'20\'19s requested schedule is unrealistic.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.44pm BST\par \par \uc2 Trump asks for classified documents trial to take place after 2024 election\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  asked the federal judge overseeing the Mar-a-Lago {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/jun/08/trump-mar-a-lago-case-explainer"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 classified documents case}}}\uc2  to indefinitely postpone setting a trial date in court filings on Monday and suggested, at a minimum, that any scheduled trial should not take place until after the 2024 presidential election.\par \par \uc2 The papers submitted by Trump\u8217\'20\'19s lawyers in response to the US justice department\u8217\'20\'19s motion to hold the trial this December made clear the former president\u8217\'20\'19s aim to delay proceedings as their guiding strategy \u8211\'20\'13 the case may be dropped if Trump wins the election.\par \par \uc2 The filing said:\par \par \uc2 The court should, respectfully, before establishing any trial date, allow time for development of further clarity as to the full nature and scope of the motions that will be filed.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.06pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.37pm BST\par \par \uc2 Fulton county district attorney \uc2 Fani Willis\uc2  launched the investigation in early 2021, after \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  tried to overturn his election defeat in Georgia by calling \uc2 Brad Raffensperger\uc2 , Georgia\u8217\'20\'19s secretary of state, and suggesting the state\u8217\'20\'19s top elections official could help him \u8220\'20\'1Cfind 11,780 votes\u8221\'20\'1D, just enough needed to beat \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The investigation expanded to include an examination of a slate of Republican fake electors, phone calls by Trump and others to Georgia officials in the weeks after the 2020 election and unfounded allegations of widespread election fraud made to state lawmakers, according to AP.\par \par \uc2 About a year into her investigation, Willis asked for a special grand jury. At the time, she said she needed the panel\u8217\'20\'19s subpoena power to compel testimony from witnesses who had refused to cooperate without a subpoena. In a January 2022 letter to Fulton county superior court chief judge, Christopher Brasher, Willis wrote that Raffensperger, who she called an \u8220\'20\'1Cessential witness\u8221\'20\'1D, had \u8220\'20\'1Cindicated that he will not participate in an interview or otherwise offer evidence until he is presented with a subpoena by my office\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 That special grand jury was seated in May 2022, and released in January after completing its work. The panel issued subpoenas and heard testimony from 75 witnesses, ranging from some of Trump\u8217\'20\'19s most prominent allies to local election workers, before drafting a final report with recommendations for Willis.\par \par \uc2 Portions of that report that were released in February said jurors believed that \u8220\'20\'1Cone or more witnesses\u8221\'20\'1D committed perjury and urged local prosecutors to bring charges. The panel\u8217\'20\'19s foreperson {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/feb/22/trump-election-2020-grand-jury-georgia"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 said in media interviews}}}\uc2  later that they recommended indicting numerous people, but she declined to name names.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/feb/22/trump-election-2020-grand-jury-georgia"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \u8216\'20\'18A big freaking deal\u8217\'20\'19: the grand jury that investigated Trump election pressure}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.39pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.12pm BST\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s a bit {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/jul/11/trump-georgia-grand-jury-biden-nato-ukraine-politics-live-updates?page=with:block-64ad47918f08df2847001abb#block-64ad47918f08df2847001abb"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 more}}}\uc2  on the grand jury being seated today in Atlanta, Georgia, that will probably consider charges against \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  and his Republican allies for their efforts to overturn the 2020 election.\par \par \uc2 The new grand jury term begins today in Fulton county, and two panels will be selected at the downtown Atlanta courthouse, each made up of 16 to 23 people and up to three alternates. One of these panels is expected to handle the Trump investigation.\par \par \uc2 Fulton County Superior Court Judge Robert McBurney will preside over today\u8217\'20\'19s court proceedings, CNN reported. McBurney oversaw the special grand jury that previously collected evidence in the Trump investigation, and he is also expected to oversee the grand jury tasked with making charging decisions in the case.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.20pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.54pm BST\par \par \uc2 Grand jury handling 2020 election case against Trump and allies to be selected in Georgia\par \par \uc2 Good morning, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/us-politics"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 US politics}}}\uc2  blog readers. A grand jury being seated today in Atlanta is expected to consider charges against former President \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  and his Republican allies for their efforts to overturn the 2020 election.\par \par \uc2 Fulton county district attorney \uc2 Fani Willis\uc2  launched the investigation in early 2021, shortly after Trump tried to overturn his loss by calling Georgia\u8217\'20\'19s secretary of state, \uc2 Brad Raffensperger\uc2 , and suggested the state\u8217\'20\'19s top elections official could help him \u8220\'20\'1Cfind 11,780 votes\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 A special grand jury previously issued subpoenas and heard testimony from about 75 witnesses, which included Trump advisers, his former attorneys, White House aides, and Georgia officials. That panel drafted a final report with recommendations for Willis.\par \par \uc2 The new grand jury term begins today in Fulton county, which includes most of Atlanta and some suburbs. Fulton County Superior Court Judge Robert McBurney will swear-in two grand juries, one of which is expected to hear evidence in the Georgia elections case.\par \par \uc2 Willis, an elected Democrat, is expected to present her case before one of two new grand juries being seated. The panel won\u8217\'20\'19t be deciding guilt, only if Willis has enough evidence to move her case forward and who should face indictment. Willis has previously indicated that final decisions could come next month.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s what else we\u8217\'20\'19re watching today:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  is meeting with other \uc2 Nato\uc2  leaders in Vilnius, Lithuania, where Russia\u8217\'20\'19s war in Ukraine will top the agenda.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The House rules committee is scheduled to mark up the FY2024 defense authorization bill today. The legislation is set to hit the floor later this week, with final passage currently envisioned for Friday.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The House will meet at noon and at 2pm will take up multiple bills, with last votes expected at 6.30pm\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The Senate will meet at 10am and vote on several nominations throughout the day. There will be classified all-senators briefing with defense and intelligence officials on how AI is used for national security purposes.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.46pm BST\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020230711ej7b001ju\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
