\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 US mother pleads guilty to giving daughter  \highlight22\uc2 abortion \highlight\uc2  pills and burying fetus\b0\par\par\uc2 Guardian staff and agency \par \uc2 432 \uc2 words\par \uc2 11 July 2023\par 13:03 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Jesssica Burgess of Nebraska admits to providing \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  after 20 weeks and tampering with human skeletal remains\par \par \uc2 A Nebraska mother has pleaded guilty to giving her 17-year-old daughter pills for an illegal \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  last year and helping to burn and bury the fetus.\par \par \uc2 Under a plea agreement, Jessica Burgess, 42, of Norfolk, admitted to providing an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  after 20 weeks of gestation, false reporting and tampering with human skeletal remains. Charges of concealing the death of another person and \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  by someone other than a licensed physician were dismissed.\par \par \uc2 Burgess was accused of helping her then-17-year-old daughter, Celeste Burgess, end her pregnancy. Madison county district court documents show she ordered \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  pills on the internet.\par \par \uc2 After the teen aborted the 29-week-old fetus, the two burned the remains and buried them in a field north of Norfolk in north-eastern Nebraska. Authorities later found the burned fetus.\par \par \uc2 Madison county attorney Joe Smith has said it is the first time he has charged anyone with illegally performing an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  after 20 weeks, a restriction that was passed in 2010. In May, the Republican governor, \uc2 Jim Pillen\uc2 , signed a 12-week \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban.\par \par \uc2 After pleading guilty last Friday, Jessica Burgess is set for sentencing on 22 September. Two of the counts against her are felonies, one is a misdemeanor.\par \par \uc2 Celeste Burgess, now 18, was charged as an adult and pleaded guilty in May to removing, concealing or abandoning a dead body. She is scheduled to be sentenced on 20 July. She faces up to two years in prison.\par \par \uc2 Via \uc2 Facebook\uc2  messages, the two discussed terminating the pregnancy and plans to destroy the evidence. The messages, which law enforcement acquired using a search warrant, were detailed in court documents.\par \par \uc2 Last summer, a man pleaded no contest to a misdemeanor for helping the women bury the fetus on his parents\u8217\'20\'19 land.\par \par \uc2 Last June, the conservative-dominated \uc2 US supreme court{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2022/jun/24/roe-v-wade-overturned-abortion-summary-supreme-court"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 struck down}}}\uc2  the national right to an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the US, upending almost 50 years of precedent after overturning {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/roe-v-wade"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Roe v Wade}}}\uc2  as part of the Dobbs v Jackson Women\u8217\'20\'19s Health Organization case.\par \par \uc2 It has {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/series/a-year-without-roe"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 sparked a year}}}\uc2  of protest, political backlash and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/aug/03/kansas-abortion-rights-referendum-reaction"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 some surprises}}}\uc2  by pro-choice campaigners {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/nov/11/abortion-midterm-elections-republicans-women-voters"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 and voters}}}\uc2  and more incidents of extreme difficulties for women wanting or needing to access \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The power on {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/ng-interactive/2023/jun/24/abortion-rights-roe-v-wade-photo-essay"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  rights}}}\uc2  passed to the individual states, some of which have enshrined {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2022/nov/09/vermont-abortion-vote-first-us-state-constitution"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 protections}}}\uc2 , while others have {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2023/apr/13/florida-six-week-abortion-ban-republicans"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 heavily restricted}}}\uc2  or all but {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/ng-interactive/2023/jun/22/abortion-ban-politicians-who-voted-for-restrictions-who-are-they-men-women"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 banned the procedure}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020230710ej7a002xr\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
