\par\par \uc2 World news\par \b \uc2 Man gets life sentence for raping girl, nine, forced to leave Ohio for  \highlight22\uc2 abortion \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 Maya Yang \par \uc2 492 \uc2 words\par \uc2 10 July 2023\par 15:26 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Gerson Fuentes found guilty in case that dominated headlines when girl had to travel to Indiana for procedure banned in Ohio\par \par \uc2 The man found guilty of raping and impregnating a nine-year-old Ohio girl who later traveled to Indiana for an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been sentenced to life in prison.\par \par \uc2 On Wednesday afternoon, 28-year-old Gerson Fuentes appeared at the Franklin county court of common pleas in Columbus, Ohio, where he entered a plea agreement which will allow him to be eligible to seek probation after 25 years. If granted parole, Fuentes would also have to register as a tier 3 sex offender and will have a lifetime of in-person verification every 90 days.\par \par \uc2 Last July, Fuentes was arrested and charged with raping the child in a case that dominated nationwide headlines after the girl, who turned 10 shortly after, was then {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/jul/03/ohio-indiana-abortion-rape-victim"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 forced}}}\uc2  to travel to neighboring Indiana for an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  due to Ohio\u8217\'20\'19s six-week \u8220\'20\'1Ctrigger ban\u8221\'20\'1D at the time which came into effect after the \uc2 US supreme court\uc2  overturned Roe v Wade last year.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/jul/14/man-charged-10-year-old-abortion-rightwing-media-indiana-ohio"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 According to}}}\uc2  a police investigator who testified at a hearing last year, Fuentes, who is from Guatemala and living in Columbus, Ohio, had confessed to raping the girl at least twice.\par \par \uc2 The case went on to gain further attention after the Indiana state attorney general launched an investigation into Caitlin Bernard, the doctor who performed the \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  on the child victim. The attorney general, Todd Rokita, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.in.gov/apps/pla/litigation/viewer.aspx?id=21742"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 accused}}}\uc2  Bernard of violating state law by not reporting the child\u8217\'20\'19s abuse and violating patient privacy protections, despite Bernard\u8217\'20\'19s refusal to discuss specific details of the victim\u8217\'20\'19s case and identity.\par \par \uc2 In response, Bernard {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.indystar.com/story/news/health/2023/04/21/indiana-ag-todd-rokita-drops-dr-bernards-lawsuit-against-himself/70140254007/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 sued}}}\uc2  Rokita, accusing him of causing her reputation \u8220\'20\'1Cirreparable harm\u8221\'20\'1D. Last November, Rokita asked a state medical board to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/2022/11/30/us/indiana-attorney-general-abortion-doctor.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 discipline}}}\uc2  Bernard.\par \par \uc2 Following the \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , Bernard became the center of a political firestorm after rightwing media {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/jul/14/man-charged-10-year-old-abortion-rightwing-media-indiana-ohio"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 called}}}\uc2  the story \u8220\'20\'1Cnot true\u8221\'20\'1D and a \u8220\'20\'1Clie\u8221\'20\'1D. At one point, a Republican commentator {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/jul/14/man-charged-10-year-old-abortion-rightwing-media-indiana-ohio"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 said}}}\uc2  \u8220\'20\'1Cthere is no proof\u8221\'20\'1D that the victim even \u8220\'20\'1Cexists\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, Joe Biden condemned the case of the child victim, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.washingtonpost.com/politics/2022/07/08/biden-abortion-10-year-old-rape-victim/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 saying}}}\uc2  last year: \u8220\'20\'1CShe was forced to have to travel out of the state to Indiana to seek to terminate the pregnancy and maybe save her life \u8230\'20\'26 Ten years old \u8211\'20\'13 10 years old! \u8211\'20\'13 raped, six weeks pregnant, already traumatized, was forced to travel to another state.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 In May, the Indiana state medical board {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/may/26/indiana-abortion-ruling-caitlin-bernard-medical-license"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 ruled}}}\uc2  that it will allow Bernard to continue practicing in Indiana and that she will not have to lose her license. It also found Bernard not guilty of violating reporting requirements about child abuse in the case. However, the board did rule that Bernard violated patient privacy laws in discussing the case with the media. It ultimately voted to issue a letter of reprimand to Bernard and fines of $3,000.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020230706ej760010c\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
