\par\par \uc2 Opinion\par \b \uc2 Biden has reminded us yet again that he\u8217\'20\'19s a weak and lukewarm ally of  \highlight22\uc2 abortion \highlight\uc2  rights\b0\par\par\uc2 Moira Donegan \par \uc2 1,286 \uc2 words\par \uc2 29 June 2023\par 16:32 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 At a recent fundraiser he said he\u8217\'20\'19s \u8216\'20\'18not big on\u8217\'20\'19 \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 . It\u8217\'20\'19s not pro-choice activists who are out of step with the mainstream; it\u8217\'20\'19s Joe Biden\par \par \uc2 A closed-door fundraiser for the very wealthy is a place where a lot of politicians really shine. Among their fellow elites, surrounded by people like them who like them \u8211\'20\'13 and are giving them money \u8211\'20\'13 Democrats and Republicans alike often become their truest selves. They drop the flesh-pressing affectations, the focused-group soundbites, the stiff smiles. They become something they\u8217\'20\'19re usually not: honest.\par \par \uc2 Honest is what Biden was at a similar fundraiser in tony Chevy Chase, Maryland, this past Tuesday, when he told a crowd of his wealthy supporters that he was personally ambivalent about \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights. \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19m a practicing Catholic. I\u8217\'20\'19m not big on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 ,\u8221\'20\'1D the president said. Nevertheless, he claimed that the compromise Roe v Wade decision on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  \u8220\'20\'1Cgot it right\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Biden\u8217\'20\'19s reassertion of his own discomfort with \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  came just three days after the first anniversary of the \uc2 US supreme court\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s Dobbs decision, which eliminated the \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  right. In the year since women lost the constitutional right that the president says he is not \u8220\'20\'1Cbig on\u8221\'20\'1D, the bans that snapped into effect have had life-changing \u8211\'20\'13 life-ruining \u8211\'20\'13 effects for thousands.\par \par \uc2 Women have been forced to carry for months babies that cannot live outside the womb, which they have {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cnn.com/2023/05/02/health/florida-abortion-term-pregnancy/index.html#:~:text=A%20Florida%20woman%2C%20unable%20to,%2C%E2%80%9D%20said%20Dorbert%2C%2033."}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 had to watch die}}}\uc2  after agonizing moments or hours of life. Women and girls have been forced to flee their home states to get abortions after being {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.pbs.org/newshour/politics/indiana-doctor-defends-actions-in-10-year-old-rape-victims-abortion"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 impregnated through rape}}}\uc2 . Women have {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://abcnews.go.com/US/tennessee-woman-gets-emergency-hysterectomy-after-doctors-deny/story?id=99457461"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 lost their organs}}}\uc2  to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  bans, needing emergency hysterectomies to save their lives after incomplete miscarriages or cesarean scar pregnancies. Others have been drafted into exercises in morbid futility, forced to carry fetuses that lack major organs, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nbcnews.com/news/us-news/louisiana-woman-carrying-fetus-skull-seek-abortion-another-state-rcna45005"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 such as heads}}}\uc2 , in a new reality that has been {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.thenation.com/article/society/abortion-bans-torture-cruelty/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 likened to torture}}}\uc2 . Other women have been forced to become {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.npr.org/sections/health-shots/2023/04/25/1171851775/oklahoma-woman-abortion-ban-study-shows-confusion-at-hospitals"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 sicker and sicker}}}\uc2  \u8211\'20\'13 suffering, risking their lives, and incurring permanent damage to their bodies in order to be made ill enough that \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  might become legally permissible.\par \par \uc2 Many more women have been stripped of control over their lives \u8211\'20\'13 denied healthcare, denied the ability to plan their families, denied the freedom to choose the course of their own lives, for the sake of retrograde, bigoted and punitive conceptions of gender and sexuality held by others. And all American women, along with many trans people, have been degraded and humiliated by \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  bans, relegated to a lesser class of adult citizenship, informed that they are not permitted to control their own fates.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  data project {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://societyfp.org/research/wecount/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 WeCount}}}\uc2  suggests that there were 25,640 fewer legal abortions in America in the year following Dobbs. That number does not account for the number of women \u8211\'20\'13 the unlucky ones \u8211\'20\'13 who received care only after their pregnancies sickened them to the brink of death. And it doesn\u8217\'20\'19t account for the women \u8211\'20\'13 the lucky ones, as these things go \u8211\'20\'13 who were able to flee their home states and subject themselves to the indignity and burden of traveling for care. So the number is conservative. But still, it represents a staggering injustice: 25,640 violations of human rights; 25,640 people who deserved better.\par \par \uc2 Throughout the past year, members of the Biden administration, and President Biden in particular, have been largely absent from this unfolding catastrophe. They have not taken on an expansive view of executive authority in attempts to restore \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights; they have not pressed allies in Congress to advance pro-choice legislation; they have not been willing to challenge, even tentatively, an anti-choice federal judiciary that is wildly expanding its interpretations of its own power.\par \par \uc2 They are not even willing to do the one thing that the president has the unquestioned authority to do: use the bully pulpit to express solidarity with American women, to grieve for their lost health, futures and dignity, and to rally Americans to the increasingly popular pro-choice cause. Joe Biden has abdicated leadership on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the loss of which is causing untold suffering, and which will define life prospects for a generation of women. Because he finds it distasteful. Because he\u8217\'20\'19s not \u8220\'20\'1Cbig on\u8221\'20\'1D it.\par \par \uc2 It is not Catholicism that makes Joe Biden unwilling to issue a full-throated support of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights. It is sexism\par \par \uc2 Lest this seem like an ungenerous reading of a well-intended gaffe, it should be noted that an unwillingness to advocate for \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights has been a recurring theme of his career. \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  is a test that Joe Biden has failed every single time that history has called him to it. His paeans to his Catholic faith as cover for his unwillingness to champion \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  also ring false: most American Catholics {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.americamagazine.org/politics-society/2022/06/06/poll-us-catholics-disagree-church-abortion-lgbt-243108"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 support \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  rights}}}\uc2 . And as Jamie Manson, the president of \uc2 Catholics for Choice\uc2 , pointed out, the church also fiercely opposes marriage equality, which the president has long championed. It is not Catholicism that makes Joe Biden unwilling to issue a full-throated support of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights. It is sexism.\par \par \uc2 Until it became {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/2019/06/06/us/politics/joe-biden-hyde-amendment.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a political liability}}}\uc2  for him in the 2020 midterm cycle, Biden was among one of the last leading Democrats to support the Hyde Amendment, a 1976 provision that forbade federal funding for abortions, and which, because of its ban on Medicaid coverage of the procedure, made Roe\u8217\'20\'19s protection of the \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  right largely moot for poor women almost as soon as it was achieved. Biden\u8217\'20\'19s assertion that \u8220\'20\'1CRoe got it right,\u8221\'20\'1D is both disingenuous to this long-held position, which curtailed Roe\u8217\'20\'19s protections, and also a sign of how indifferent and uninterested he has been in the insights of pro-choice activists, who have long argued that Roe was insufficient in its protections for \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , inadequate in its argument for the right on privacy, rather than liberty and equality, grounds, and too diminished by subsequent attacks on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access that were pursued by rabidly anti-choice Republicans and allowed by cowardly \u8220\'20\'1Cpro-choice\u8221\'20\'1D Democrats who never had the courage of their campaign promises.\par \par \uc2 But an indifference to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights activists from Biden is no surprise: after the Dobbs decision, while his administration fumbled and tried to change the subject from their own incompetence and lack of preparation, it was not those who had conspired and schemed for decades against Roe who the Biden administration blamed, and it was not those who had snatched women\u8217\'20\'19s rights away that they demonized. It was pro-choice activists.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CJoe Biden\u8217\'20\'19s goal in responding to Dobbs is not to satisfy some activists who have consistently been out of step with the mainstream of the Democratic party,\u8221\'20\'1D his then-communications director, \uc2 Kate Bedingfield\uc2 , {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.thecut.com/2022/07/joe-biden-white-house-dobbs-response-awful.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 sneered}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Mission accomplished: pro-choice activists are not satisfied with Joe Biden. But \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  is a salient issue, one that is only growing more popular, and more electorally persuasive, every day. In light of the post-Dobbs political reality, Joe Biden\u8217\'20\'19s unwillingness to give unqualified support to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights is not just morally cowardly; it\u8217\'20\'19s also politically irresponsible. Republicans are running from the issue, and the Biden campaign is declining to attack them on it. Voters are rallying around \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights, and the Biden campaign is declining to lead them.\par \par \uc2 The time for apologetic, defensive, partial non-defenses of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights is over, and America\u8217\'20\'19s newly mobilized pro-choice majority knows it. It\u8217\'20\'19s not the activists who are out of step with the mainstream of the Democratic party. It\u8217\'20\'19s Joe Biden.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Moira Donegan is a Guardian US columnist\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020230629ej6t0028m\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
