\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Biden puts  \highlight22\uc2 abortion \highlight\uc2  rights at center of campaign on Roe reversal anniversary\b0\par\par\uc2 Maya Yangand agencies \par \uc2 883 \uc2 words\par \uc2 26 June 2023\par 11:28 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 President announces executive order to boost access to contraception as Republicans call for national restrictions\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/joebiden"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Joe Biden}}}\uc2  on Friday put reproductive rights squarely in the middle of his 2024 re-election campaign as the US president hosted a rally based around defending \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights, notched three high-profile endorsements from groups dedicated to the issue, and announced an executive order aimed at boosting access to contraception.\par \par \uc2 The moves came in stark contrast to the Republican field of candidates, many of whom were attending the Faith & Freedom Coalition annual conference in Washington DC.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  has become a tough issue for Republicans because most Americans support the right to an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  after the conservative-dominated \uc2 US supreme court\uc2  last year axed the federal right to terminate a pregnancy.\par \par \uc2 Nonetheless, former vice-president \uc2 Mike Pence\uc2  on Friday doubled down on his hardline stance in a speech calling for national restrictions on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  \u8211\'20\'13 a position seen as unlikely to win much wide support. Pence\u8217\'20\'19s former boss \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  will address the same conference on Saturday and has in recent weeks sought to take a less extreme stance.\par \par \uc2 Biden and the Democrats, meanwhile, are on the attack on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , pointing out the huge loss of reproductive freedoms for millions of women since the US\u8217\'20\'19s highest court overturned the landmark Roe v Wade decision that had protected \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  freedoms.\par \par \uc2 Biden and Vice-President \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  on Friday were being endorsed by \uc2 Planned Parenthood Action Fund\uc2 , Naral Pro-Choice America and Emily\u8217\'20\'19s List. The groups are throwing their early support behind the re-election effort in part to highlight the importance of the issue for Democrats heading into the election year, the groups\u8217\'20\'19 leaders told the Associated Press.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI think that President Biden has been an incredibly valuable partner, along with Vice-President Harris, in fighting back against the onslaught of attacks that we have seen,\u8221\'20\'1D said \uc2 Alexis McGill Johnson\uc2 , president and chief executive of \uc2 Planned Parenthood Action Fund\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Biden and fellow Democrats have already seen the power of the issue: a majority of Americans want legalized \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  nationwide. In the lead-up to the 2022 midterm elections, many political pundits dismissed the issue, but it was among the top concerns for voters, who consistently rejected efforts to restrict \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the states when given the chance.\par \par \uc2 Biden\u8217\'20\'19s campaign manager, Julie Chavez Rodriguez, said the president and the vice-president were proud to have earned the support of the groups. Since the decision last year by the supreme court, \u8220\'20\'1Cwe have seen the horrifying impact that the extreme Maga agenda has on women\u8217\'20\'19s health,\u8221\'20\'1D she said, referring to Trump\u8217\'20\'19s \u8220\'20\'1CMake America Great Again\u8221\'20\'1D slogan.\par \par \uc2 Biden has said he will work to protect reproductive health care, including enshrining \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights in federal law. He is expected to convey that message in remarks on Friday at a rally with the first lady, Jill Biden, Harris and the second gentleman, Doug Emhoff.\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, Biden\u8217\'20\'19s executive order aims to strengthen access to contraception, a growing concern for Democrats after some conservatives have signaled a willingness to push beyond \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  into regulation of contraception. In 2017, nearly 65% \u8211\'20\'13 or 46.9 million \u8211\'20\'13 of the 72.2 million girls and women age 15 to 49 in the US used a form of contraception.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.whitehouse.gov/briefing-room/statements-releases/2023/06/23/fact-sheet-president-biden-issues-executive-order-on-strengthening-access-to-contraception/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 In a statement}}}\uc2 , Biden highlighted reproductive health as a top priority of his administration in the wake of the Dobbs v Jackson Women\u8217\'20\'19s Health Organization ruling from the conservative-led court that reversed Roe v Wade.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CContraception is an essential component of reproductive health care that has only become more important in the wake of Dobbs and the ensuing crisis in women\u8217\'20\'19s access to healthcare,\u8221\'20\'1D Biden said.\par \par \uc2 Biden is seeking to strengthen access to \u8220\'20\'1Caffordable, high-quality contraception and family planning services\u8221\'20\'1D, the statement added. It\u8217\'20\'19s his third executive order on reproductive health care access since the Dobbs ruling.\par \par \uc2 The measures include expanding access and services through Medicaid, improving coverage of contraception through Medicare and seeking ways to compel private health insurance companies to provide contraception and family planning services as needed.\par \par \uc2 The consequences of restricting \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access in America have quickly moved beyond ending an unwanted pregnancy into miscarriage and pregnancy care in general.\par \par \uc2 Women in states with tight restrictions are increasingly unable to access care for pregnancy-related complications. Doctors facing criminal charges if they provide abortions are increasingly afraid to care for patients who aren\u8217\'20\'19t sick enough yet to be considered treatable.\par \par \uc2 Over the last year 22 US states have passed either a ban or highly restrictive policies on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 . Other states, though, have expanded access to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  care. The Biden administration has brought together leaders from all 50 states to talk strategy on how to expand access and work together to help people in more restrictive states.\par \par \uc2 Most of the states with severe \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  restrictions are also states that have a high maternal mortality rate and higher rates of stillbirth and miscarriage. Black women are disproportionately affected \u8211\'20\'13 they are more than three times more likely to die from pregnancy-related causes than white women, according to the \uc2 US Centers for Disease Control and Prevention\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The Associated Press contributed to this story\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020230626ej6q0023g\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
